(5008, 1299, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long, well polished staff with a fantastic diamond attached.', '<p><i>A long, well polished staff with a fantastic diamond attached.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5009, 1299, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Gem staffs are used to cast sorcery spells. Generally, use of the staff to cast such spells involves a right-click and activation on some type of target that is within a certain acceptable range. The player must have access to the spells to be used with the staff in addition to having the ruby staff itself. Gem staffs cannot be improved or repaired, and their quality level is unimportant to function. They do not take damage from using spells, however.', '<ul><li>Gem staffs are used to cast sorcery spells. Generally, use of the staff to cast such spells involves a right-click and activation on some type of target that is within a certain acceptable range. The player must have access to the spells to be used with the staff in addition to having the ruby staff itself.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gem staffs cannot be improved or repaired, and their quality level is unimportant to function. They do not take damage from using spells, however.</li></ul>', 1),
(5010, 1299, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'Gem staffs are not considered melee weapons in Wurm and subsequently cause the player to use unarmed combat when they are equipped during melee combat situations. As such, they do not take damage from combat. A 37ql star gem and an 89ql staff combine to make a 51ql gem staff at 10 skill level in alchemy and 24 in natural substances. Further testing is needed for additional production details.', '<ul><li>Gem staffs are not considered melee weapons in Wurm and subsequently cause the player to use unarmed combat when they are equipped during melee combat situations. As such, they do not take damage from combat.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>A 37ql star gem and an 89ql staff combine to make a 51ql gem staff at 10 skill level in alchemy and 24 in natural substances. Further testing is needed for additional production details.</li></ul>', 2),
(5011, 1299, 'Additional Images', 'Additional_Images', '', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rubystaffunequipped.jpg\"><img alt=\"Rubystaffunequipped.jpg\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/f7/Rubystaffunequipped.jpg/800px-Rubystaffunequipped.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/f7/Rubystaffunequipped.jpg/1200px-Rubystaffunequipped.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/f7/Rubystaffunequipped.jpg/1600px-Rubystaffunequipped.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(5012, 1299, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Sorcery Emerald staff Sapphire staff Opal staff Diamond staff', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Sorcery\" title=\"Sorcery\">Sorcery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Emerald_staff\" title=\"Emerald staff\">Emerald staff</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sapphire_staff\" title=\"Sapphire staff\">Sapphire staff</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Opal_staff\" title=\"Opal staff\">Opal staff</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Diamond_staff\" title=\"Diamond staff\">Diamond staff</a></li></ul>', 4),
(5028, 1306, 'Description', 'Description', 'Walking on Slate slabs is the fastest way of travelling (up to 17.3Km/h). Slate slabs can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 Body strength . Paving with slate slabs is fairly difficult compared to other pavements due to the simple fact that it requires slate slab . Slate slabs have the chance of decaying if not walked upon for an extended period of time.', '<p>Walking on Slate slabs is the fastest way of travelling (up to 17.3Km/h). Slate slabs can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a>. Paving with slate slabs is fairly difficult compared to other pavements due to the simple fact that it requires <a href=\"/index.php/Slate_slab\" title=\"Slate slab\">slate slab</a>. \n</p>\n<p>Slate slabs have the chance of decaying if not walked upon for an extended period of time. \n</p>', 0),
(5029, 1306, 'Making Slate slabs', 'Making_Slate_slabs', 'Activate a slate slab Right-click a tile of packed dirt and select Pave .', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Slate_slab\" title=\"Slate slab\">slate slab</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> and select <i><a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">Pave</a></i>.</li></ol>', 1),
(5030, 1306, 'Destroying Slate slabs', 'Destroying_Slate_slabs', 'Activate a shovel Right-click a tile of slate slabs and select Destroy Pavement .', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of slate slabs and select <i>Destroy Pavement</i>.</li></ol>', 2),
(5031, 1306, 'Messages', 'Messages', 'You need to be stronger to destroy pavement. 20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement. You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first. 10+ Digging is required to remove pavement. You need to be stronger to dig on roads. 20+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.', '<dl><dt>You need to be stronger to destroy pavement.</dt>\n<dd>20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first.</dt>\n<dd>10+ Digging is required to remove pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You need to be stronger to dig on roads.</dt>\n<dd>20+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.</dd></dl>', 3),
(5032, 1306, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Slate slab paving: Lichen', '<ul><li>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Slate slab paving: <a href=\"/index.php/Lichen\" title=\"Lichen\">Lichen</a></li></ul>', 4),
(5033, 1306, 'Alternatives', 'Alternatives', 'Alternative pavements include gravel , stone slabs , marble slabs , round cobblestone , rough cobblestone and cobblestone .', '<p>Alternative pavements include <a href=\"/index.php/Gravel\" title=\"Gravel\">gravel</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_slabs\" title=\"Stone slabs\">stone slabs</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Marble_slabs\" title=\"Marble slabs\">marble slabs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Round_cobblestone\" title=\"Round cobblestone\">round cobblestone</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rough_cobblestone\" title=\"Rough cobblestone\">rough cobblestone</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Cobblestone\" title=\"Cobblestone\">cobblestone</a>.\n</p>', 5),
(5035, 1208, 'Description', 'Description', 'A flat and square marble slab.  It is about your length and width. Marble slabs are used for building marble slab floors as well as roads, walkways, and highways.', '<p>A flat and square marble slab.  It is about your length and width. \n</p>\n<p>Marble slabs are used for building <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_slab_floor\" title=\"Marble slab floor\">marble slab floors</a> as well as roads, walkways, and highways.\n</p>', 0),
(5036, 1208, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Upon failure, 8 kg. of marble shards are consumed.', '<ul><li>Upon failure, 8 kg. of <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_shards\" title=\"Marble shards\">marble shards</a> are consumed.</li></ul>', 1),
(5060, 1314, 'Description', 'Description', 'A heavy lump of black glossy adamantine.', '<p><i>A heavy lump of black glossy adamantine.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5061, 1314, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Adamantine lumps are obtained as rewards from the Hota Battlecamp . Also, at the end of Epic scenarios, the winning God will sometimes inflict terraforming events upon the territories of opposing kingdoms, such as large trenches, towers of dirt and volcanos. Around these changes, boulders appear which can be mined for glimmersteel and adamantine. Can also be obtained at the end of a rift .', '<ul><li>Adamantine lumps are obtained as rewards from the <a href=\"/index.php/Hota_Battlecamp\" title=\"Hota Battlecamp\">Hota Battlecamp</a>.</li>\n<li>Also, at the end of Epic scenarios, the winning God will sometimes inflict terraforming events upon the territories of opposing kingdoms, such as large trenches, towers of dirt and volcanos. Around these changes, boulders appear which can be mined for glimmersteel and adamantine.</li>\n<li>Can also be obtained at the end of a <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">rift</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(5062, 1314, 'Enchanting', 'Enchanting', 'Will be faster to use if enchanted with Wind of ages . Skill experience boost if enchanted with Circle of cunning Enchantments on adamantine lumps will degrade over time. You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one with the enchanted lump activated.', '<ul><li>Will be faster to use if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_ages\" title=\"Wind of ages\">Wind of ages</a>.</li>\n<li>Skill experience boost if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Circle_of_cunning\" title=\"Circle of cunning\">Circle of cunning</a></li>\n<li>Enchantments on adamantine lumps will degrade over time.</li>\n<li>You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one with the enchanted lump activated.</li></ul>', 2),
(5063, 1314, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(5064, 1314, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See List of adamantine products See metal products list for more items that can be made from adamantine.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Adamantine_products\" title=\"Category:Adamantine products\">List of adamantine products</a></li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from adamantine.</li></ul>', 4),
(5080, 1319, 'Description', 'Description', 'This statue is the prize of a Hota tournament.', '<p><i>This statue is the prize of a Hota tournament.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5081, 1319, 'Use', 'Use', 'Storage Container Optional Light, causing slow heating of contents in and on statue Aesthetic Value Note : Lit statues will slowly heat their contents.  Never put a flammable object into or on a lit statue ... it will be destroyed after some time.', '<ul><li>Storage Container</li>\n<li>Optional Light, causing slow heating of contents in and on statue</li>\n<li>Aesthetic Value</li></ul>\n<p><b>Note : Lit statues will slowly heat their contents.  Never put a flammable object into or on a lit statue ... it will be destroyed after some time.</b>\n</p>', 1),
(5082, 1319, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'They appear at the alliance capitals token after winning the HotA . Can be planted. When attempting to plant, if the statue is activated, you will get the message: \"Needs to be on the ground.\" They do not decay when carried in inventory or kept on-deed. Only one statue can be loaded into a rowboat or sailboat. There is a random chance of winning different statues at the HotA. They contain 5 glimmersteel and adamantine lumps when won. They can contain a medallion when won, sometimes more than one if multiple participants. The color of the light will be red unless the alliance that wins has more than 30 wins If the alliance has more than 30 wins, the light\'s color will vary The material of the statue will vary based on the number of alliance wins When lit, they will slowly heat their contents. (Good for food; Very bad for flammable items). This can be useful for keeping branding irons hot.', '<ul><li>They appear at the alliance capitals token after winning the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/HotA\" title=\"HotA\">HotA</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be planted.\n<ul><li>When attempting to plant, if the statue is activated, you will get the message: \"Needs to be on the ground.\"</li></ul></li>\n<li>They do not decay when carried in inventory or kept on-deed.</li>\n<li>Only one statue can be loaded into a rowboat or sailboat.</li>\n<li>There is a random chance of winning different statues at the HotA.</li>\n<li>They contain 5 glimmersteel and adamantine lumps when won.</li>\n<li>They can contain a medallion when won, sometimes more than one if multiple participants.</li>\n<li>The color of the light will be red unless the alliance that wins has more than 30 wins\n<ul><li>If the alliance has more than 30 wins, the light\'s color will vary</li></ul></li>\n<li>The material of the statue will vary based on the number of alliance wins</li>\n<li>When lit, they will slowly heat their contents. (Good for food; Very bad for flammable items). This can be useful for keeping branding irons hot.</li></ul>', 2),
(5083, 1319, 'Types of Statues', 'Types_of_Statues', 'There are 11 different HotA statues, as shown below. Statue Image Statue Image Bull vs Bear Sol Demon Dog vs Boar Dragon vs Man Lady of the lake Man vs Bear NoGump Scorpion Deer Wolf vs Bison Woman vs Snake (Anaconda)', '<p>There are 11 different HotA statues, as shown below.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"90\">Statue</th>\n<th>Image</th>\n<th>Statue</th>\n<th>Image\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bull vs Bear\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:BullVsBear.jpg\"><img alt=\"BullVsBear.jpg\" data-file-height=\"903\" data-file-width=\"821\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"220\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4d/BullVsBear.jpg/200px-BullVsBear.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/4d/BullVsBear.jpg/300px-BullVsBear.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/4d/BullVsBear.jpg/400px-BullVsBear.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sol_Demon\" title=\"Sol Demon\">Sol Demon</a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Demon.jpg\"><img alt=\"Demon.jpg\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"601\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"254\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7f/Demon.jpg/200px-Demon.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7f/Demon.jpg/300px-Demon.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7f/Demon.jpg/400px-Demon.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dog vs Boar\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:DogVsBoar.jpg\"><img alt=\"DogVsBoar.jpg\" data-file-height=\"743\" data-file-width=\"755\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"197\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/55/DogVsBoar.jpg/200px-DogVsBoar.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/55/DogVsBoar.jpg/300px-DogVsBoar.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/55/DogVsBoar.jpg/400px-DogVsBoar.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td>Dragon vs Man\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Dragon.jpg\"><img alt=\"Dragon.jpg\" data-file-height=\"1019\" data-file-width=\"823\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"248\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Dragon.jpg/200px-Dragon.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Dragon.jpg/300px-Dragon.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/bb/Dragon.jpg/400px-Dragon.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Lady_of_the_lake\" title=\"Lady of the lake\">Lady of the lake</a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LadyoftheLake.jpg\"><img alt=\"LadyoftheLake.jpg\" data-file-height=\"642\" data-file-width=\"273\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"470\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/0e/LadyoftheLake.jpg/200px-LadyoftheLake.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/0/0e/LadyoftheLake.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td>Man vs Bear\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:ManVsBear.jpg\"><img alt=\"ManVsBear.jpg\" data-file-height=\"708\" data-file-width=\"764\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"185\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c2/ManVsBear.jpg/200px-ManVsBear.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c2/ManVsBear.jpg/300px-ManVsBear.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c2/ManVsBear.jpg/400px-ManVsBear.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/NoGump\" title=\"NoGump\">NoGump</a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Nogump.jpg\"><img alt=\"Nogump.jpg\" data-file-height=\"575\" data-file-width=\"629\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"183\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c5/Nogump.jpg/200px-Nogump.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c5/Nogump.jpg/300px-Nogump.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c5/Nogump.jpg/400px-Nogump.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Scorpion\" title=\"Scorpion\">Scorpion</a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:ScorpionHota.jpg\"><img alt=\"ScorpionHota.jpg\" data-file-height=\"717\" data-file-width=\"896\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"160\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/ScorpionHota.jpg/200px-ScorpionHota.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/ScorpionHota.jpg/300px-ScorpionHota.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7b/ScorpionHota.jpg/400px-ScorpionHota.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Deer\" title=\"Deer\">Deer</a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Stag.jpg\"><img alt=\"Stag.jpg\" data-file-height=\"763\" data-file-width=\"512\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"298\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Stag.jpg/200px-Stag.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Stag.jpg/300px-Stag.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/bb/Stag.jpg/400px-Stag.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td>Wolf vs Bison\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:WolfVsBison.jpg\"><img alt=\"WolfVsBison.jpg\" data-file-height=\"822\" data-file-width=\"898\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"183\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e1/WolfVsBison.jpg/200px-WolfVsBison.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e1/WolfVsBison.jpg/300px-WolfVsBison.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e1/WolfVsBison.jpg/400px-WolfVsBison.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Woman vs Snake (Anaconda)\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:AnacondaHota.PNG\"><img alt=\"AnacondaHota.PNG\" data-file-height=\"589\" data-file-width=\"488\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"241\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/68/AnacondaHota.PNG/200px-AnacondaHota.PNG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/68/AnacondaHota.PNG/300px-AnacondaHota.PNG 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/68/AnacondaHota.PNG/400px-AnacondaHota.PNG 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3),
(5084, 1319, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Hota Battlecamp Statues', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hota_Battlecamp\" title=\"Hota Battlecamp\">Hota Battlecamp</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li></ul>', 4),
(5085, 1320, 'Description', 'Description', 'This medallion is the prize of a Hota tournament. It has the head of a (statue it came from) on it.', '<p><i>This medallion is the prize of a Hota tournament. It has the head of a (statue it came from) on it.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5086, 1320, 'Use', 'Use', 'None', '<ul><li>None</li></ul>', 1),
(5087, 1320, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Random prize inside a hota statue. They currently have no model. They can be worn around the neck. More than one can be won at a time.', '<ul><li>Random prize inside a hota statue.</li>\n<li>They currently have no model.</li>\n<li>They can be worn around the neck.</li>\n<li>More than one can be won at a time.</li></ul>', 2),
(5088, 1320, 'Types of Medallion Designs', 'Types_of_Medallion_Designs', 'Demon Nymph Dog Bear Bull Pheasant', '<ul><li>Demon</li>\n<li>Nymph</li>\n<li>Dog</li>\n<li>Bear</li>\n<li>Bull</li>\n<li>Pheasant</li></ul>', 3),
(5089, 1320, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Hota Battlecamp Hota statue', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hota_Battlecamp\" title=\"Hota Battlecamp\">Hota Battlecamp</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hota_statue\" title=\"Hota statue\">Hota statue</a></li></ul>', 4),
(5090, 1321, 'Current Title', 'Current_Title', 'Arch Mage Yggdrasil the Beast [Fearless Dragonslayer]', '<p>Arch Mage Yggdrasil the Beast [Fearless Dragonslayer] \n</p>', 0),
(5091, 1321, 'Nature', 'Nature', 'A veteran player, and well experienced. Always willing to help, even if he can\'t.\nMischievous and merry, this player can oft be found having a laugh in global chat. Extremely welcoming to newcomers, known to go the extra mile to help new users.', '<p>A veteran player, and well experienced. Always willing to help, even if he can\'t.\nMischievous and merry, this player can oft be found having a laugh in global chat.\n</p>\n<p>Extremely welcoming to newcomers, known to go the extra mile to help new users.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(5092, 1321, 'Goals', 'Goals', 'Reaching the final step on the path of insanity\nCollecting all the sorcery items', '<p>Reaching the final step on the path of insanity\nCollecting all the sorcery items\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(5093, 1321, 'Wurm Online', 'Wurm_Online', 'Began wurm as a villager of New Dawn Village on Golden Valley . After building the villages beginnings he disappeared from the world. Months later he returned to its ruins, meeting two wurmians who\'d become very important in his future. Rillian and Jenica . The three of them formed a triumvirate of power,  as they expanded upon the remains of New Dawn Village. In a few months it had grown to a large hub, to the extent of being trusted with bears by the GM\'s. Elarian First Age Yggdrasil yet again went missing and reappeared on the now desecrated and ravaged Golden Valley. Due in part to a mass exodus to the island of Independence . Deciding to exile himself for the destruction of the village he arrived in Independence, and to his surprise found Rillian within the village of Elarial . The age concluded with the resignation of Quarry over his inactivity and a poor choice he made resulting in most of the villagers leaving. Elarian Second Age During this period, Elarial witnessed it\'s greatest expansion. Yggdrasil has rose to co-mayor and spent his time establishing trade routes and exclusive contracts. While Rillian handled administration, expanding the physical property and maintaining it. Elarial now expanded now across multiple deeds, not counting it\'s numerious allies and trade relations. Elarial Elarial Harbor Elarial Gardens Elarial Heights Elarial Retreat End of the Second Age The end of second age came as Elarials villagers disappeared. Rillian and Yggdrasil were alone in Elarial for some time. The deeds were falling into disrepair. Several village construction plans were started far earlier than planned with failed results. The biggest was a rush to complete a colossal market consisting of 144 merchants with port access, in attempt to wrestle power from Freedom Market . Nearing the end, Yggdrasil commissioned and built a boat bridge (then largest ever made) crossing the inner sea from Elarial Harbor, hoping in vein to draw in visitors. While the plan failed, it has created a permanent memorial to the late Elarial. Elarian Third Age During the recent Elarian age, Yggdrasil sought to reestablish Elarian glory. Founding the Elarial Consortium, he drove to create a kingdom on Independance. A group of alliances grouping together to increase prosperity and safety among their numbers. These plans were abandoned and Elarial fell into ruin and disbanded Luin First Age Year 1104 Disheartened by the decay of Elarial, he made a short trip to Deliverance where he constructed a small rowboat to travel to Release where he joined the Harvestmoon Lagoon Alliance. \nMet with friendly faces, Yggdrasil made the choice to let the past go and move on. This was set in stone with the founding of Luin, a large deed situated on an isthmus in the north east corner of Release. As of Year 1127, Luin continues to stand strong.', '<p>Began wurm as a villager of New Dawn Village on <a href=\"/index.php/Golden_Valley\" title=\"Golden Valley\">Golden Valley</a>. After building the villages beginnings he disappeared from the world. Months later he returned to its ruins, meeting two <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wurmian\" title=\"Wurmian\">wurmians</a> who\'d become very important in his future. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rillian\" title=\"Rillian\">Rillian</a> and <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Jenica&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Jenica (page does not exist)\">Jenica</a>. The three of them formed a triumvirate of power,  as they expanded upon the remains of New Dawn Village. In a few months it had grown to a large hub, to the extent of being trusted with bears by the GM\'s. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>Elarian First Age</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nYggdrasil yet again went missing and reappeared on the now desecrated and ravaged Golden Valley. Due in part to a mass exodus to the island of <a href=\"/index.php/Independence\" title=\"Independence\">Independence</a>. Deciding to exile himself for the destruction of the village he arrived in Independence, and to his surprise found Rillian within the village of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Elarial\" title=\"Elarial\">Elarial</a>. The age concluded with the resignation of <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Quarry&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Quarry (page does not exist)\">Quarry</a> over his inactivity and a poor choice he made resulting in most of the villagers leaving. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>Elarian Second Age</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nDuring this period, Elarial witnessed it\'s greatest expansion. Yggdrasil has rose to co-mayor and spent his time establishing trade routes and exclusive contracts. While Rillian handled administration, expanding the physical property and maintaining it. Elarial now expanded now across multiple deeds, not counting it\'s numerious allies and trade relations.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Elarial\" title=\"Elarial\">Elarial</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Elarial_Harbor&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Elarial Harbor (page does not exist)\">Elarial Harbor</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Elarial_Gardens&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Elarial Gardens (page does not exist)\">Elarial Gardens</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Elarial_Heights&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Elarial Heights (page does not exist)\">Elarial Heights</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Elarial_Retreat&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Elarial Retreat (page does not exist)\">Elarial Retreat</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n<b>End of the Second Age</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe end of second age came as Elarials villagers disappeared. Rillian and Yggdrasil were alone in Elarial for some time. The deeds were falling into disrepair. Several village construction plans were started far earlier than planned with failed results. The biggest was a rush to complete a colossal market consisting of 144 merchants with port access, in attempt to wrestle power from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Market\" title=\"Freedom Market\">Freedom Market</a>. \n</p>\n<p>Nearing the end, Yggdrasil commissioned and built a boat bridge (then largest ever made) crossing the inner sea from Elarial Harbor, hoping in vein to draw in visitors. While the plan failed, it has created a permanent memorial to the late Elarial. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b> Elarian Third Age </b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nDuring the recent Elarian age, Yggdrasil sought to reestablish Elarian glory. Founding the Elarial Consortium, he drove to create a kingdom on Independance. A group of alliances grouping together to increase prosperity and safety among their numbers. \n</p>\n<p>These plans were abandoned and Elarial fell into ruin and disbanded \n</p>\n<p><b> Luin First Age </b>\nYear 1104\n</p>\n<p>Disheartened by the decay of Elarial, he made a short trip to Deliverance where he constructed a small rowboat to travel to Release where he joined the Harvestmoon Lagoon Alliance. \nMet with friendly faces, Yggdrasil made the choice to let the past go and move on. This was set in stone with the founding of Luin, a large deed situated on an isthmus in the north east corner of Release. \n</p>\n<p>As of Year 1127, Luin continues to stand strong.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(5094, 1321, 'Wurm Unlimited', 'Wurm_Unlimited', 'Former Emperor of the Horde of the Summoned, and Sicko of the Path of Insanity on the former Primordial server. No longer active on WU', '<p>Former Emperor of the Horde of the Summoned, and Sicko of the <a href=\"/index.php/Path_of_Insanity\" title=\"Path of Insanity\">Path of Insanity</a> on the former Primordial server.\n</p>\n<p>No longer active on WU\n</p>', 4),
(5095, 1321, 'Trivia & Quotes', 'Trivia_.26_Quotes', 'Used to catapult animal corpses at Boston. If he\'s running, you should be as well. As of Alpha 1.0.0, is nolonger stuffed with fluff. \"Look what I can do\" -  Last words before immediately being killed by a dragon Has been struck by Poseidon\'s lightning and lived. Has an unhealthy love for cavebugs. Has been kissed by Enki. Rumor has it, if you speak his name 3 times at night into a mirror. He will arrive and fix your highways.', '<ul><li>Used to catapult animal corpses at Boston.</li>\n<li>If he\'s running, you should be as well.</li>\n<li>As of Alpha 1.0.0, is nolonger stuffed with fluff.</li>\n<li>\"Look what I can do\" -  Last words before immediately being killed by a dragon</li>\n<li>Has been struck by Poseidon\'s lightning and lived.</li>\n<li>Has an unhealthy love for cavebugs.</li>\n<li>Has been kissed by Enki.</li>\n<li>Rumor has it, if you speak his name 3 times at night into a mirror. He will arrive and fix your highways.</li></ul>', 5),
(5096, 1322, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sell is a feature that allows you to sell low-value items to Traders , Personal merchants , and settlement tokens for a small amount of iron.', '<p>Sell is a feature that allows you to sell low-value items to <a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">Traders</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Personal_merchant\" title=\"Personal merchant\">Personal merchants</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement_token\" title=\"Settlement token\">settlement tokens</a> for a small amount of iron.\n</p>', 0),
(5097, 1322, 'How it Works', 'How_it_Works', '1) Move to stand beside a trader, a merchant, or a token (does not have to be your own deed). 2) Activate the item you wish to sell by double-clicking it. 3) Right-click the trader, merchant, or token and select the \'Sell\' option; this triggers a 3-second timer. (must be on foot, not mounted to see the sell option) 4) Your money is added automatically to your bank account.', '<p>1) Move to stand beside a trader, a merchant, or a token (does not have to be your own deed).\n</p>\n<p>2) Activate the item you wish to sell by double-clicking it.\n</p>\n<p>3) Right-click the trader, merchant, or token and select the \'Sell\' option; this triggers a 3-second timer. (must be on foot, not mounted to see the sell option)\n</p>\n<p>4) Your money is added automatically to your bank account.\n</p>', 1),
(5098, 1322, 'Limitations', 'Limitations', 'Items are given an iron value when sold. This is equivalent to 1 iron per 10ql plus 1 iron; minimum being 1 iron for a 0-9ql item. You can earn up to 500 iron (the equivalent of 5 copper) per hour by selling items in this way. When you hit the maximum limit, you\'ll get the message: \"You have sold your quota for now.\" Once you get this message, you will be able to sell again one hour after you sold your first item. Certain items cannot be sold this way, including starter items, liquids, scraps, dirt, clay, needles, stone shards, branches, and nails.', '<ul><li>Items are given an iron value when sold. This is equivalent to 1 iron per 10ql plus 1 iron; minimum being 1 iron for a 0-9ql item.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can earn up to 500 iron (the equivalent of 5 copper) per hour by selling items in this way. When you hit the maximum limit, you\'ll get the message: \"You have sold your quota for now.\"<br/> Once you get this message, you will be able to sell again one hour after you sold your first item.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Certain items cannot be sold this way, including starter items, liquids, scraps, dirt, clay, needles, stone shards, branches, and nails.</li></ul>', 2),
(5099, 1322, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'Further discussion of the sell feature can be found at the City Hall section of the Wurm Online Forum: http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/87796-money-distribution-improvements/', '<p>Further discussion of the sell feature can be found at the City Hall section of the Wurm Online Forum: <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/87796-money-distribution-improvements/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/87796-money-distribution-improvements/</a>\n</p>', 3),
(5100, 1322, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Personal merchant Settlement token Trader', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Personal_merchant\" title=\"Personal merchant\">Personal merchant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Settlement_token\" title=\"Settlement token\">Settlement token</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">Trader</a></li></ul>', 4),
(5101, 1296, 'Description', 'Description', 'A flowerbed is a decorative structure that can be built on tile borders .', '<p>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">flowerbed</a> is a decorative structure that can be built on <a href=\"/index.php/Tile_border\" title=\"Tile border\">tile borders</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(5102, 1296, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To create a flowerbed, you need to have all materials in your inventory. Activate a flower, right-click a tile border and select \" Plant flowerbed \". All materials will be consumed at once. The flowerbed can not be improved, use materials as high quality as possible to make it last. You can water a flowerbed with any container that holds water to reduce its decay. When creating at least one side must not be paved. \"You cannot plant a flowerbed there.\" They do not take damage on settlements.', '<ul><li>To create a flowerbed, you need to have all materials in your inventory.</li>\n<li>Activate a flower, right-click a tile border and select \"<i>Plant flowerbed</i>\".</li>\n<li>All materials will be consumed at once.</li>\n<li>The flowerbed can not be improved, use materials as high quality as possible to make it last.</li>\n<li>You can water a flowerbed with any container that holds water to reduce its decay.</li>\n<li>When creating at least one side must not be paved. \"You cannot plant a flowerbed there.\"</li>\n<li>They do not take damage on settlements.</li></ul>', 1),
(5103, 1296, 'Images', 'Images', 'Variety of flowerbeds Orange-Red : Yellow : Blue : Greenish-Yellow : White : Purple : White-Dotted :', '<table align=\"center\" border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"5\" style=\"text-align:center; style=\">\n<caption>Variety of flowerbeds\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr style=\"background-color:#a6a290;\">\n<th>Orange-Red :\n</th>\n<th>Yellow :\n</th>\n<th>Blue :\n</th>\n<th>Greenish-Yellow :\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Orangered_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Orangered flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"287\" data-file-width=\"924\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"62\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/76/Orangered_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Orangered_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/76/Orangered_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Orangered_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/76/Orangered_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Orangered_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Yellow_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Yellow flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"308\" data-file-width=\"913\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"67\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/32/Yellow_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Yellow_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/32/Yellow_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Yellow_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/32/Yellow_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Yellow_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Blue_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Blue flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"923\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"61\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/28/Blue_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Blue_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/28/Blue_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Blue_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/28/Blue_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Blue_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Greenishyellow flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"926\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"59\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/34/Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/34/Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/34/Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Greenishyellow_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr style=\"background-color:#a6a290;\">\n<th>White :\n</th>\n<th>Purple :\n</th>\n<th>White-Dotted :\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:White_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"White flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"253\" data-file-width=\"904\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"56\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/cf/White_flowerbed.jpg/200px-White_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/cf/White_flowerbed.jpg/300px-White_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/cf/White_flowerbed.jpg/400px-White_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Purple_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Purple flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"251\" data-file-width=\"906\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"55\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/dd/Purple_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Purple_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/dd/Purple_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Purple_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/dd/Purple_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Purple_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg\"><img alt=\"Whitedotted flowerbed.jpg\" data-file-height=\"272\" data-file-width=\"908\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"60\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d2/Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg/200px-Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d2/Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg/300px-Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/d2/Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg/400px-Whitedotted_flowerbed.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(5104, 1288, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see an high iron fence.', '<p><i>You see an high iron fence. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(5105, 1288, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(5106, 1288, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair High iron fence with stone brick. Each stone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, the iron fence bars will turn rusty in color. High iron fence gates cannot be built in arched walls, iron fence gates can.', '<ul><li>Repair High iron fence with stone brick. Each stone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, the iron fence bars will turn rusty in color.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>High iron fence gates cannot be built in arched walls, <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_fence_gate\" title=\"Iron fence gate\">iron fence gates</a> can.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(5107, 1288, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(5108, 1325, 'Description', 'Description', 'Temples are mission structures requiring high Masonry skill.\nTemples now act as light sources, and are always lit. The color of the lighting can be changed like that of a lamp (this requires 5 kg of dye).', '<p><b>Temples</b> are <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mission_structures\" title=\"Category:Mission structures\">mission structures</a> requiring high <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">Masonry</a> skill.\nTemples now act as light sources, and are always lit. The color of the lighting can be changed like that of a lamp (this requires 5 kg of dye).\n</p>', 0),
(5109, 1325, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Mission structures , for more information on mission structures in general.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mission_structures\" title=\"Category:Mission structures\">Mission structures</a>, for more information on mission structures in general.</li></ul>', 1),
(5110, 1329, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'The default is O or ESC . This may be changed by binding a key to MAIN_MENU or STOP_OR_MAIN_MENU , which will also stop your actions and toggle the main menu. Main menu', '<p>The default is <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120109\">.mw-parser-output .key{border:1px solid #aaa;border-radius:2px;box-shadow:1px 2px 2px #ddd;background-color:#f9f9f9;background-image:linear-gradient(to top,#eee,#f9f9f9,#eee);padding:1px 3px;font-family:inherit;font-size:0.85em}</style>\n<span class=\"key\">O</span> or <link href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r120109\" rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\"/>\n<span class=\"key\">ESC</span>. This may be changed by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bind\" title=\"Bind\">binding</a> a key to <b>MAIN_MENU</b> or <b>STOP_OR_MAIN_MENU</b>, which will also stop your actions and toggle the main menu.\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Main_menu.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"266\" data-file-width=\"446\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"179\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/47/Main_menu.png/300px-Main_menu.png\" srcset=\"/images/4/47/Main_menu.png 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Main_menu.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Main menu</div></div></div>', 0),
(5111, 1329, 'Options', 'Options', 'Character A drag and drop paper doll of your body and equipment. Inventory Character\'s inventory Skills Displays the character\'s skills. Map Displays the in-game map. Valrei map Displays the in-game Valrei map. Console Opens the game console for advanced commands and settings. Settings Opens the Settings window. Note: This is not an in-game window and may open behind the game. Hud settings Opens a second window with more toggles, see below. Support Opens the support ticket window. Wiki search Opens the Wiki search window, allowing you to search the wiki from in-game. Quit Exits the game.', '<dl><dt><a href=\"/index.php/Character_window\" title=\"Character window\">Character</a></dt>\n<dd>A drag and drop paper doll of your body and equipment.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">Inventory</a></dt>\n<dd>Character\'s inventory</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Skills\" title=\"Skills\">Skills</a></dt>\n<dd>Displays the character\'s skills.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/World_map\" title=\"World map\">Map</a></dt>\n<dd>Displays the in-game map.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Valrei_map\" title=\"Valrei map\">Valrei map</a></dt>\n<dd>Displays the in-game Valrei map.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Console\" title=\"Console\">Console</a></dt>\n<dd>Opens the game console for advanced commands and settings.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settings\" title=\"Settings\">Settings</a></dt>\n<dd>Opens the Settings window. Note: This is not an in-game window and may open behind the game.</dd>\n<dt>Hud settings</dt>\n<dd>Opens a second window with more toggles, see below.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Support_window\" title=\"Support window\">Support</a></dt>\n<dd>Opens the support ticket window.</dd>\n<dt>Wiki search</dt>\n<dd>Opens the Wiki search window, allowing you to search the wiki from in-game.</dd>\n<dt>Quit</dt>\n<dd>Exits the game.</dd></dl>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(5112, 1329, 'Hud Settings', 'Hud_Settings', 'Achievement Window Displays achievements and your character\'s progress with them. Chat window Main chat window. Compass Must have a compass in your inventory. When settled, displays your current heading. Debug timing Opens the Debug Info window. Event window Event window with Friend \'s list and status bar Fight window Fight options window Healthbar Health and information window Menu bar Displays the current key bindings for ESC and F1 to F12 Mission progress A compact window showing mission progress. Mission details Shows specifics about current missions . Statistics Shows client statistics. Target window Shows current target for combat. Select bar Shows what is selected and provides quick keys for some actions. (Ironwood Skin only) Timers Preset timers and custom timers. Toolbelt Must have a toolbelt equipped. Can hotkey items and tools by dragging to the toolbelt. Character window Displays a 3D model view of your character, without the drag and drop paper doll. Skill tracker Displays skill progress. Quickbar Button bar with actions, such as Climbing , Stealth , and toggles for Faithful and Lawful . Notification Displays the in-game tutorial, Book of Wisdom , and any tutorial notifications. Crafting Shows the crafting window. Status effects Shows current status effects as icons on the HUD. Spell effects Shows list of current spell effects. Read more: Interface and controls | Client | Key bindings', '<dl><dt><a href=\"/index.php/Achievements\" title=\"Achievements\">Achievement Window</a></dt>\n<dd>Displays achievements and your character\'s progress with them.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Chat\" title=\"Chat\">Chat window</a></dt>\n<dd>Main chat window.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Compass\" title=\"Compass\">Compass</a></dt>\n<dd>Must have a compass in your inventory. When settled, displays your current heading.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Debug_info\" title=\"Debug info\">Debug timing</a></dt>\n<dd>Opens the Debug Info window.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Interface_and_controls#Event_window\" title=\"Interface and controls\">Event window</a></dt>\n<dd>Event window with <a href=\"/index.php/Friend\" title=\"Friend\">Friend</a>\'s list and status bar</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fight window</a></dt>\n<dd>Fight options window</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Healthbar\" title=\"Healthbar\">Healthbar</a></dt>\n<dd>Health and information window</dd>\n<dt>Menu bar</dt>\n<dd>Displays the current key bindings for <link href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r120109\" rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\"/></dd></dl>\n<p><span class=\"key\">ESC</span> and <link href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r120109\" rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\"/>\n<span class=\"key\">F1</span> to <link href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r120109\" rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\"/>\n<span class=\"key\">F12</span>\n</p>\n<dl><dt>Mission progress</dt>\n<dd>A compact window showing mission progress.</dd>\n<dt>Mission details</dt>\n<dd>Shows specifics about current <a href=\"/index.php/Mission\" title=\"Mission\">missions</a>.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Client_statistics\" title=\"Client statistics\">Statistics</a></dt>\n<dd>Shows client statistics.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Target\" title=\"Target\">Target window</a></dt>\n<dd>Shows current target for combat.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Select_bar\" title=\"Select bar\">Select bar</a></dt>\n<dd>Shows what is selected and provides quick keys for some actions. (Ironwood Skin only)</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Timers\" title=\"Timers\">Timers</a></dt>\n<dd>Preset timers and custom timers.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Toolbelt\" title=\"Toolbelt\">Toolbelt</a></dt>\n<dd>Must have a toolbelt equipped. Can hotkey items and tools by dragging to the toolbelt.</dd>\n<dt>Character window</dt>\n<dd>Displays a 3D model view of your character, without the drag and drop paper doll.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Skill_tracker\" title=\"Skill tracker\">Skill tracker</a></dt>\n<dd>Displays skill progress.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Quickbar\" title=\"Quickbar\">Quickbar</a></dt>\n<dd>Button bar with actions, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Climbing\" title=\"Climbing\">Climbing</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a>, and toggles for <a href=\"/index.php/Faithful\" title=\"Faithful\">Faithful</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Lawful\" title=\"Lawful\">Lawful</a>.</dd>\n<dt>Notification</dt>\n<dd>Displays the in-game tutorial, <a href=\"/index.php/Book_of_Wisdom\" title=\"Book of Wisdom\">Book of Wisdom</a>, and any tutorial notifications.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Crafting\" title=\"Crafting\">Crafting</a></dt>\n<dd>Shows the crafting window.</dd>\n<dt>Status effects</dt>\n<dd>Shows current status effects as icons on the HUD.</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"/index.php/Spell_effects\" title=\"Spell effects\">Spell effects</a></dt>\n<dd>Shows list of current spell effects.</dd></dl>\n<p><b>Read more:</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Interface_and_controls\" title=\"Interface and controls\">Interface and controls</a> | <a href=\"/index.php/Client\" title=\"Client\">Client</a> | <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Key_binding\" title=\"Key binding\">Key bindings</a>\n</p>', 2),
(5113, 1331, 'Description', 'Description', 'Shrines are mission structures requiring Carpentry skill. The shrine, like most buildable mission structures, provides various criteria for the location and terrain of its construction as a part of the mission briefing.  A 5x5 flat, slabbed area is required for before building the shrine, as well as a certain area of map and various other criteria that sometimes appear (must be greater than 100 steps up, some X must be within Y tiles - i.e. some fruit trees or bushes must be within 5 tiles, etc.). Like most epic mission structures, it can be started with a bit of clay on a slab.  Success chance appears to be around 50%, and it did not appear that any materials were consumed or damaged on failure. The unfinished shrine does have a model, unlike the temple and some other buildable mission structures that appear as a question mark bag.  In the unfinished state it is approximately the size of a pile of items.', '<p><b>Shrines</b> are <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mission_structures\" title=\"Category:Mission structures\">mission structures</a> requiring <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill.\n</p>\n<p>The shrine, like most buildable mission structures, provides various criteria for the location and terrain of its construction as a part of the mission briefing.  A 5x5 flat, slabbed area is required for before building the shrine, as well as a certain area of map and various other criteria that sometimes appear (must be greater than 100 steps up, some X must be within Y tiles - i.e. some fruit trees or bushes must be within 5 tiles, etc.).  \n</p>\n<p>Like most epic mission structures, it can be started with a bit of clay on a slab.  Success chance appears to be around 50%, and it did not appear that any materials were consumed or damaged on failure.\n</p>\n<p>The unfinished shrine does have a model, unlike the temple and some other buildable mission structures that appear as a question mark bag.  In the unfinished state it is approximately the size of a pile of items.\n</p>', 0),
(5114, 1331, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Mission structures , for more information on mission structures in general.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mission_structures\" title=\"Category:Mission structures\">Mission structures</a>, for more information on mission structures in general.</li></ul>', 1),
(5151, 1340, 'Description', 'Description', 'A round flask containing liquid with a really funny strong smell. Maybe something equally fun will happen if you quaff it? A yellow potion is an item given as part of the Legacy loyalty bonus program that provides gifts to players who purchase premium time in consecutive months.', '<p><i>A round flask containing liquid with a really funny strong smell. Maybe something equally fun will happen if you quaff it?</i>\n</p>\n<p>A yellow potion is an item given as part of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Legacy_loyalty_bonus\" title=\"Legacy loyalty bonus\">Legacy loyalty bonus</a> program that provides gifts to players who purchase <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> time in consecutive months.\n</p>', 0),
(5152, 1340, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To drink it, right-click the potion and select Use , at which point, the potion will promptly transform the player into a random creature or object. The duration of the effect depends on the quality of the potion, and the quality of the potion depends on how many times and how long a player has been premium. Taking damage , embarking on a vehicle or animal, or sitting on furniture will dispel the effect. The player\'s camera view height is relative to the item or creature they transform into. For example, transformed into potted flowers, the player\'s view will then be very close to the ground. Yellow potions do not decay when stored anywhere on an active deed.', '<ul><li>To drink it, right-click the potion and select <b>Use</b>, at which point, the potion will promptly transform the player into a random creature or object.</li>\n<li>The duration of the effect depends on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the potion, and the quality of the potion depends on how many times and how long a player has been premium.</li>\n<li>Taking <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a>, embarking on a vehicle or animal, or sitting on furniture will dispel the effect.</li>\n<li>The player\'s camera view height is relative to the item or creature they transform into. For example, transformed into potted flowers, the player\'s view will then be very close to the ground.</li>\n<li>Yellow potions do not decay when stored anywhere on an active deed.</li></ul>', 1),
(5153, 1340, 'Possible Transformations', 'Possible_Transformations', 'Bear Black wolf Goblin Large barrel Pheasant Pile of items Pottery flowerpot with flowers Skeleton Son of Nogump Spectre Zombie', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bear\" title=\"Bear\">Bear</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_wolf\" title=\"Black wolf\">Black wolf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Goblin\" title=\"Goblin\">Goblin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">Large barrel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pheasant\" title=\"Pheasant\">Pheasant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_items\" title=\"Pile of items\">Pile of items</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_flowerpot\" title=\"Pottery flowerpot\">Pottery flowerpot</a> with flowers</li>\n<li>Skeleton</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Son_of_Nogump\" title=\"Son of Nogump\">Son of Nogump</a></li>\n<li>Spectre</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Zombie\" title=\"Zombie\">Zombie</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5154, 1342, 'Description', 'Description', 'This wolf-like creature is unnaturally big and clumsy. The Worg seems finicky and nervous, which makes it unpredictable and dangerous to deal with.', '<p><i>This wolf-like creature is unnaturally big and clumsy. The Worg seems finicky and nervous, which makes it unpredictable and dangerous to deal with.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5155, 1342, 'Summoning the Worg', 'Summoning_the_Worg', '\'Summon Worg\' is a spell permanently granted to players by single use of the Valrei item, green tome of magic . To summon the worg, activate gem staff, right-click the ground, and click Summon Worg. The \'Summon Worg\' spell costs 500 karma. Upon summoning, the appearing worg will be traited as an \"Aged\" worg. The Worg will be tamed, respondent only to its summoner\'s commands, upon being summoned. Currently, players are only able to gather the power to summon a worg for 24 real-life hours. After this period, the worg will die and go back into the ether. It is possible to breed two worgs, but due to the 24-hour limitation, a baby worg has yet to be documented in this plane of existence. Worgs can be led by rope.', '<ul><li>\'Summon Worg\' is a spell permanently granted to players by single use of the Valrei item, <a href=\"/index.php/Green_tome_of_magic\" title=\"Green tome of magic\">green tome of magic</a>.</li>\n<li>To summon the worg, activate gem staff, right-click the ground, and click Summon Worg.</li>\n<li>The \'Summon Worg\' spell costs 500 karma.</li>\n<li>Upon summoning, the appearing worg will be traited as an \"Aged\" worg.</li>\n<li>The Worg will be tamed, respondent only to its summoner\'s commands, upon being summoned.</li>\n<li>Currently, players are only able to gather the power to summon a worg for 24 real-life hours. After this period, the worg will die and go back into the ether.</li>\n<li>It is possible to breed two worgs, but due to the 24-hour limitation, a baby worg has yet to be documented in this plane of existence.</li>\n<li>Worgs can be led by rope.</li></ul>', 1),
(5156, 1343, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fairly large wagon designed to be dragged by four animals.', '<p><i>A fairly large wagon designed to be dragged by four animals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5157, 1343, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A wagon is a vehicle that requires 21 mind logic to command, and 23 body strength is needed to use the load cargo function. A wagon can carry one passenger, at the very back of the wagon. Can be secured with a small or large padlock . Can\'t be dragged (must have a minimum of 2 animals hitched to it to move), but can be hauled .', '<p>A wagon is a vehicle that requires 21 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to command, and 23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> is needed to use the <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">load cargo</a> function. \n</p>\n<ul><li>A wagon can carry one passenger, at the very back of the wagon.</li>\n<li>Can be secured with a small or large <a href=\"/index.php/Padlock\" title=\"Padlock\">padlock</a>.</li>\n<li>Can\'t be dragged (must have a minimum of 2 animals hitched to it to move), but can be <a href=\"/index.php/Haul\" title=\"Haul\">hauled</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(5158, 1343, 'Hitchable Creatures', 'Hitchable_Creatures', 'Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a wagon. Brown bears when tamed , young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Bulls Bisons Donkeys Hell horse , young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Horses Mules Trolls when dominated , young and adolescent Unicorns when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Weta when on Jackal', '<p>Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a wagon.  \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">Brown bears</a> when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tame\" title=\"Tame\">tamed</a>, young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">Bulls</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bisons</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Donkey\" title=\"Donkey\">Donkeys</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">Hell horse</a>, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horses</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mule\" title=\"Mule\">Mules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Trolls</a> when <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">dominated</a>, young and adolescent</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">Unicorns</a> when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weta\" title=\"Weta\">Weta</a> when on Jackal</li></ul>', 2),
(5159, 1343, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'At least 40 fine carpentry is required to create as well as to continue building a wagon. However, the quality of the materials (i.e. planks etc) also plays a large part in chance of success (higher ql = higher creation chance). The QL of additional components plays a major role in the attach chance, especially at lower fine carpentry skill levels. Using starting components with too low QL may result in a wagon being uncraftable, even with sufficient Fine Carpentry level. Last wood piece determines wood type.', '<ul><li>At least 40 fine carpentry is required to create as well as to continue building a wagon. However, the quality of the materials (i.e. planks etc) also plays a large part in chance of success (higher ql = higher creation chance). The QL of additional components plays a major role in the attach chance, especially at lower fine carpentry skill levels.\n<ul><li>Using starting components with too low QL may result in a wagon being uncraftable, even with sufficient <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fine_Carpentry\" title=\"Fine Carpentry\">Fine Carpentry</a> level.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Last wood piece determines wood type.</li></ul>', 3),
(5160, 1343, 'Capacity', 'Capacity', 'A wagon normally holds the maximum of 100 items directly in the hold, however, the total capacity of a wagon can be increased by stacking other containers , such as large crates , inside. Wagons can hold 20 small crates (3000 items), or  27 rafts , or 12 large crates (3600 items), or 16 \"10% reduced size runed\" large crates (4800 items). Can hold 1 forge and 2 creature cages . Can be loaded with ~65 felled trees, or up to around 75 when runed. A runed wagon can fit 1 bulk storage bin or 1 food storage bin plus 2 large crates . A wagon can hold 9 bee hives without being runed. See the Container page for more information.', '<p>A wagon normally holds the maximum of 100 items directly in the hold, however, the total capacity of a wagon can be increased by stacking other <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">containers</a>, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a>, inside. \n</p>\n<ul><li>Wagons can hold 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">small crates</a> (3000 items), or  27 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Raft\" title=\"Raft\">rafts</a>, or 12 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a> (3600 items), or 16 \"10% reduced size runed\" <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a> (4800 items).</li>\n<li>Can hold 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a> and 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">creature cages</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be loaded with ~65 felled trees, or up to around 75 when runed.</li>\n<li>A runed wagon can fit 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a> or 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">food storage bin</a> plus 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a>.</li>\n<li>A wagon can hold 9 <a href=\"/index.php/Bee_hive\" title=\"Bee hive\">bee hives</a> without being runed.</li>\n<li>See the <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">Container</a> page for more information.</li></ul>', 4),
(5161, 1343, 'Loadable Items', 'Loadable_Items', '(Not an exhaustive list)\nNote: You must be embarked as commander in order to be able to load things. Right click them and load them. Bed Beehive Forge Oven Smelter Kiln Floor loom Large barrel Large crate Small crate Ornate fountain Planter rack Small cart Statue Bow rack Weapon rack Coffin Bench Large dining table Archery target Armour stand Saddle rack Shield rack Hitching post Chicken coop When Runed Only Bulk storage bin Food storage bin large cart *Only on PVE servers', '<p>(Not an exhaustive list)\nNote: You must be embarked as commander in order to be able to load things. Right click them and load them.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">Bed</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Beehive\" title=\"Beehive\">Beehive</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Oven</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">Smelter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">Kiln</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Floor_loom\" title=\"Floor loom\">Floor loom</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">Large barrel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ornate_fountain\" title=\"Ornate fountain\">Ornate fountain</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Planter_rack\" title=\"Planter rack\">Planter rack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">Small cart</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Statue\" title=\"Statue\">Statue</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bow_rack\" title=\"Bow rack\">Bow rack</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Weapon_rack\" title=\"Weapon rack\">Weapon rack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Coffin\" title=\"Coffin\">Coffin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bench\" title=\"Bench\">Bench</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_dining_table\" title=\"Large dining table\">Large dining table</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery_target\" title=\"Archery target\">Archery target</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour_stand\" title=\"Armour stand\">Armour stand</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Saddle_rack\" title=\"Saddle rack\">Saddle rack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shield_rack\" title=\"Shield rack\">Shield rack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hitching_post\" title=\"Hitching post\">Hitching post</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Chicken_coop\" title=\"Chicken coop\">Chicken coop</a></li></ul>\n<p><b>When Runed Only</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">Food storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a> *Only on PVE servers</li></ul>', 5),
(5162, 1343, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Bisons have a speed bonus when dragging wagons making them faster than horses when hitched to a wagon. Ebony black draft horses have a slight pulling speed boost over other colors. The wood cannot be dyed with dye , but it can be colored a random color with an adamantine rune of Jackal. Wagons created in the various kingdoms will display the colors specific to each kingdom similar to kingdom banners , but the fabric itself cannot be dyed further. Can be loaded into all ships larger than small sailing boat with the exception of a Cog. Requires the equivalent of approximately 39 large crates of space to be loaded. A vehicle’s quality helps offset the weight in a vehicle, this effect starts at above 30 quality and will reduce the weight penalty up to 3x at 100 quality.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bisons</a> have a speed bonus when dragging wagons making them faster than <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a> when hitched to a wagon.</li>\n<li>Ebony black draft <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Horses\" title=\"Horses\">horses</a> have a slight pulling speed boost over other colors.</li>\n<li>The wood cannot be dyed with <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>, but it can be colored a random color with an adamantine <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a> of Jackal.</li>\n<li>Wagons created in the various <a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom\" title=\"Kingdom\">kingdoms</a> will display the colors specific to each kingdom similar to <a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom_banner\" title=\"Kingdom banner\">kingdom banners</a>, but the fabric itself cannot be dyed further.</li>\n<li>Can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Load\" title=\"Load\">loaded</a> into all <a href=\"/index.php/Ship\" title=\"Ship\">ships</a> larger than <a href=\"/index.php/Small_sailing_boat\" title=\"Small sailing boat\">small sailing boat</a> with the exception of a Cog.</li>\n<li>Requires the equivalent of approximately 39 large crates of space to be loaded.</li>\n<li>A vehicle’s quality helps offset the weight in a vehicle, this effect starts at above 30 quality and will reduce the weight penalty up to 3x at 100 quality.</li></ul>', 6),
(5163, 1343, 'Wagon Styles', 'Wagon_Styles', 'Wagons from PVP Kingdoms have different designs on the cloth portion and are sometimes considered collectors editions. If a kingdom changes their designs, current wagons will change to that new design.', '<p>Wagons from PVP Kingdoms have different designs on the cloth portion and are sometimes considered collectors editions. If a kingdom changes their designs, current wagons will change to that new design. \n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n<a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Wagons.jpg\"><img alt=\"Wagons.jpg\" data-file-height=\"976\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"976\" src=\"/images/2/23/Wagons.jpg\" width=\"1920\"/></a>\n</p>\n</div>', 7),
(5164, 1344, 'Description', 'Description', 'Expel the darkness with this +2 lantern, gives +4 to jollyness checks during winter. A lantern like any other, but requires candles to stay lit.\nSnow lanterns of 99 ql were given to premium players as a Christmas gift in 2013.\nSome premium players received an 80 ql Snow lantern as a Christmas gift in 2022.', '<p><i>Expel the darkness with this +2 lantern, gives +4 to jollyness checks during winter.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A lantern like any other, but requires candles to stay lit.\nSnow lanterns of 99 ql were given to premium players as a Christmas gift in 2013.\nSome premium players received an 80 ql Snow lantern as a Christmas gift in 2022.\n</p>', 0),
(5165, 1344, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To Light: Activate a steel and flint , right-click the snow lantern, and select \"Light\". To Refill: Activate a candle , right-click the lantern, and select \"Fill\".', '<p><b>To Light:</b> Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_and_flint\" title=\"Steel and flint\">steel and flint</a>, right-click the snow lantern, and select \"Light\".\n</p>\n<p><b>To Refill:</b> Activate a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Candles\" title=\"Candles\">candle</a>, right-click the lantern, and select \"Fill\".\n</p>', 1),
(5166, 1344, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'The number of candles needed to refill the lantern is dependent upon the quality of the candles. When the lantern is full, you will get an event message to that effect. Snow lanterns do not appear to decay when left outside of inventory, on-deed. On-deed, snow lanterns stay lit for approximately 6 real-life months once initially filled and lit. Research is still pending with regard to this exact time and if candle quality also contributes. Snow lanterns cannot be dyed.', '<ul><li>The number of candles needed to refill the lantern is dependent upon the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the candles.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>When the lantern is full, you will get an event message to that effect.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Snow lanterns do not appear to decay when left outside of inventory, on-deed.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>On-deed, snow lanterns stay lit for approximately 6 real-life months once initially filled and lit. Research is still pending with regard to this exact time and if candle quality also contributes.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Snow lanterns cannot be dyed.</li></ul>', 2),
(5167, 1344, 'History', 'History', 'Snow lanterns were given to premium players as a Christmas gift in 2013.', '<p>Snow lanterns were given to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> players as a Christmas gift in 2013.\n</p>', 3),
(5173, 1294, 'Description', 'Description', 'A clay flowerpot hardened by fire.', '<p><i>A clay flowerpot hardened by fire.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5174, 1294, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'In order to plant flowers in it, activate your flowers and select \"plant flowers\" on the flowerpot.', '<ul><li>In order to plant flowers in it, activate your flowers and select \"plant flowers\" on the flowerpot.</li></ul>', 1),
(5175, 1294, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot be improved. Cannot be repaired, unless there are flowers in it, then repairing can be done by use of \"watering\" them, which can be accomplished by filling a container with water, then activating the container and right-clicking on the pot for \"water plant\". Uses 0.1ℓ of water to water the plants. Gives gardening skill for watering. Quality is determined by the average of both the flower and the pot combined. Flowerpots with flowers in them can now be emptied by activating shovel or trowel , right-clicking the item, and clicking \"Empty,\" which will put the appropriate type of flower bouquet in the player\'s inventory.', '<ul><li>Cannot be improved.</li>\n<li>Cannot be repaired, unless there are flowers in it, then repairing can be done by use of \"watering\" them, which can be accomplished by filling a container with water, then activating the container and right-clicking on the pot for \"water plant\".</li>\n<li>Uses 0.1ℓ of water to water the plants.</li>\n<li>Gives <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">gardening</a> skill for watering.</li>\n<li>Quality is determined by the average of both the flower and the pot combined.</li>\n<li>Flowerpots with flowers in them can now be emptied by activating <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a>, right-clicking the item, and clicking \"Empty,\" which will put the appropriate type of flower bouquet in the player\'s inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(5176, 1294, 'Messages', 'Messages', '[03:29:53] You start watering the flowers. [03:30:02] You successfully watered the flowers, they look healthier.', '<p>[03:29:53] You start watering the flowers.\n</p>\n<p>[03:30:02] You successfully watered the flowers, they look healthier.\n</p>', 3),
(5177, 1294, 'Images', 'Images', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Flowerpots.jpg\" title=\"Seven pottery flowerpot with different flowers on them as labelled.\"><img alt=\"Seven pottery flowerpot with different flowers on them as labelled.\" data-file-height=\"388\" data-file-width=\"1800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"108\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/5f/Flowerpots.jpg/500px-Flowerpots.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/5f/Flowerpots.jpg/750px-Flowerpots.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/5f/Flowerpots.jpg/1000px-Flowerpots.jpg 2x\" width=\"500\"/></a>\n</p>', 4),
(5181, 1349, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a patch of well maintained lawn.', '<p><i>You see a patch of well maintained lawn.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5182, 1349, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Lawn is created by first cutting grass short and then activating scissors and Right Click > Nature > Trim grass on the tile. \"You start to trim the grass to lawn length.\" \"You trim the grass to look like a lawn.\"', '<p>Lawn is created by first cutting <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a> short and then activating <a href=\"/index.php/Scissors\" title=\"Scissors\">scissors</a> and <b>Right Click &gt; Nature &gt; Trim grass</b> on the tile.\n</p>\n<p>\"You start to trim the grass to lawn length.\"\n</p>\n<p>\"You trim the grass to look like a lawn.\"\n</p>', 1),
(5183, 1349, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Lawn tiles are simply for decoration and no nature actions may be used upon them: Flowers and sprouts may not be planted. Animals cannot graze on the lawn. A tree or bush may be turned into lawn by first cutting the grass with a sickle and then cutting with scissors . A shovel can be used to pack or dig which will destroy the Lawn. Lawn cannot be made into enchanted grass . Leaves do not display in autumn. On deed, lawn will not decay; on perimeter and off-deed; lawn will decay and return to short grass. Mineral debris Resource nodes can spawn on lawn.', '<ul><li>Lawn tiles are simply for decoration and no nature actions may be used upon them:</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><a href=\"/index.php/Flower\" title=\"Flower\">Flowers</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a> may not be planted.</dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">Animals</a> cannot graze on the lawn.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bush\" title=\"Bush\">bush</a> may be turned into lawn by first cutting the grass with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> and then cutting with <a href=\"/index.php/Scissors\" title=\"Scissors\">scissors</a>.</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> can be used to pack or dig which will destroy the Lawn.</li>\n<li>Lawn cannot be made into <a href=\"/index.php/Enchanted_grass\" title=\"Enchanted grass\">enchanted grass</a>.</li>\n<li>Leaves do not display in autumn.</li>\n<li>On deed, lawn will not decay; on perimeter and off-deed; lawn will decay and return to short grass.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on lawn.</li></ul>', 2),
(5186, 1351, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small crate made from planks, primarily used to transport goods.', '<p><i>A small crate made from planks, primarily used to transport goods.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5187, 1351, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Requires 10 carpentry to create. The plank\'s QL determines the success chance. The crate\'s wood type is dictated by the type of plank you attach last. Prevents decay of its contents similar to bulk storage bin and food storage bins . Items that fit in bulk or food storage bins also fit in crates. A small crate can hold up to 150 items, regardless of individual item volume and the crate itself, empty or otherwise, has a volume of 1,000.  This creates the vision that the crate is bigger on the inside than it is on the outside as the volume of 150 dirt alone, for example, way exceeds that of the crate. May be \'Hauled Up\' to upper floors of buildings, and \'Hauled Down\', but to haul down you must be on the same floor opening as the crate, and not below it. To haul up, you must be on the floor opening above the crate. Hauling only works on floor openings with ladders and not with stairs or gaps in the floor. May be loaded while full or empty, but cannot be picked up to the inventory regardless. Loading requires 23 body strength . Small crates aren\'t efficient for transporting items with a volume of less than 6.66 since the 150 of these items would take up a lot less volume in a smaller container than that of the crate, for example seeds in satchels . 5% of each of the stored items are lost every 28 days. This loss does not apply to containers on a deed with more than 28 days of upkeep left. Can be stored in a crate rack . Ownership changes to the last character to unload the crate, so if you are given a crate you must load it (into, for example, a large cart ) and unload it before you can rename it.', '<ul><li>Requires 10 <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> to create.</li>\n<li>The plank\'s QL determines the success chance.</li>\n<li>The crate\'s wood type is dictated by the type of plank you attach last.</li>\n<li>Prevents decay of its contents similar to <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">food storage bins</a>.</li>\n<li>Items that fit in bulk or food storage bins also fit in crates.</li>\n<li>A small crate can hold up to 150 items, regardless of individual item <a href=\"/index.php/Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> and the crate itself, empty or otherwise, has a volume of 1,000.  This creates the vision that the crate is bigger on the inside than it is on the outside as the volume of 150 <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_dirt\" title=\"Pile of dirt\">dirt</a> alone, for example, way exceeds that of the crate.</li>\n<li>May be \'Hauled Up\' to upper floors of buildings, and \'Hauled Down\', but to haul down you must be on the same floor opening as the crate, and not below it. To haul up, you must be on the floor opening above the crate.</li>\n<li>Hauling only works on floor openings with ladders and not with stairs or gaps in the floor.</li>\n<li>May be <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">loaded</a> while full or empty, but cannot be picked up to the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> regardless.\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Load\" title=\"Load\">Loading</a> requires 23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Small crates aren\'t efficient for transporting items with a volume of less than 6.66 since the 150 of these items would take up a lot less volume in a smaller container than that of the crate, for example seeds in <a href=\"/index.php/Satchel\" title=\"Satchel\">satchels</a>.</li>\n<li>5% of each of the stored items are lost every 28 days. This loss does not apply to containers on a deed with more than 28 days of upkeep left.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Crate_rack\" title=\"Crate rack\">crate rack</a>.</li>\n<li>Ownership changes to the last character to unload the crate, so if you are given a crate you must load it (into, for example, a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>) and unload it before you can rename it.</li></ul>', 1),
(5188, 1351, 'Vehicle Load Capacity', 'Vehicle_Load_Capacity', 'Vehicle Quantity Large cart 5 Wagon 20 Cog 51 Corbita 85 Knarr 75 Caravel 100', '<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"90\">Vehicle</th>\n<th>Quantity\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large cart</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cog</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">51\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">Corbita</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">85\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">Knarr</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">75\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Caravel\" title=\"Caravel\">Caravel</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">100\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(5189, 1351, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Large crate Crate rack Bulk storage bin Food storage bin', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crate_rack\" title=\"Crate rack\">Crate rack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">Food storage bin</a></li></ul>', 3),
(5190, 1352, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large crate made from planks, primarily used to transport goods.', '<p><i>A large crate made from planks, primarily used to transport goods.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5191, 1352, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A large crate can hold up to 300 items, regardless of individual item volume . The crate itself, empty or otherwise, has a volume of 1,728.  This creates the vision that the crate is bigger on the inside than it is on the outside as the volume of 300 dirt alone, for example, way exceeds that of the crate. Requires 60 carpentry to create (and continue), 23% chance with a 1 QL plank. The plank\'s QL affects the success chance. Can be stored in vehicles and can also be stored in a crate rack by moving from a vehicle\'s cargo hold to the crate rack. Cannot be taken and held directly in player inventory. Prevents decay of its contents similar to bulk storage bin and food storage bins . Items that fit in bulk or food storage bins also fit in crates. May be \'hauled Up\' to upper floors of buildings, and \'hauled Down\', but to haul down you must be on the same floor opening as the crate, and not below it. To haul up, you must be on the floor opening above the crate. Hauling only works on floor openings with ladders and not with stairs or gaps in the floor. May be loaded while full or empty, but cannot be picked up to the inventory regardless. Loading requires 23 body strength . Large crates aren\'t efficient for transporting items with a volume of less than 5.76 since the 300 of these items would take up a lot less volume in a smaller container than that of the crate, for example seeds in satchels . 5% of each of the stored items are lost every 28 days. This loss does not apply to containers on a deed with more than 28 days of upkeep left. Ownership changes to the last character to unload the crate, so if you are given a crate you must load it (into, for example, a large cart ) and unload it before you can rename it.', '<ul><li>A large crate can hold up to 300 items, regardless of individual item <a href=\"/index.php/Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a>. The crate itself, empty or otherwise, has a volume of 1,728.  This creates the vision that the crate is bigger on the inside than it is on the outside as the volume of 300 <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_dirt\" title=\"Pile of dirt\">dirt</a> alone, for example, way exceeds that of the crate.</li>\n<li>Requires 60 <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> to create (and continue), 23% chance with a 1 QL plank.</li>\n<li>The plank\'s QL affects the success chance.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in vehicles and can also be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Crate_rack\" title=\"Crate rack\">crate rack</a> by moving from a vehicle\'s cargo hold to the crate rack.</li>\n<li>Cannot be taken and held directly in player inventory.</li>\n<li>Prevents decay of its contents similar to <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">food storage bins</a>.</li>\n<li>Items that fit in bulk or food storage bins also fit in crates.</li>\n<li>May be \'hauled Up\' to upper floors of buildings, and \'hauled Down\', but to haul down you must be on the same floor opening as the crate, and not below it. To haul up, you must be on the floor opening above the crate.</li>\n<li>Hauling only works on floor openings with ladders and not with stairs or gaps in the floor.</li>\n<li>May be <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">loaded</a> while full or empty, but cannot be picked up to the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> regardless.\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Load\" title=\"Load\">Loading</a> requires 23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Large crates aren\'t efficient for transporting items with a volume of less than 5.76 since the 300 of these items would take up a lot less volume in a smaller container than that of the crate, for example seeds in <a href=\"/index.php/Satchel\" title=\"Satchel\">satchels</a>.</li>\n<li>5% of each of the stored items are lost every 28 days. This loss does not apply to containers on a deed with more than 28 days of upkeep left.</li>\n<li>Ownership changes to the last character to unload the crate, so if you are given a crate you must load it (into, for example, a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>) and unload it before you can rename it.</li></ul>', 1),
(5192, 1352, 'Vehicle Load Capacity', 'Vehicle_Load_Capacity', 'Vehicle Quantity Large cart 3 Wagon 12 Cog 29 Corbita 49 Knarr 43 Caravel 62 Wagoner container 20', '<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"90\">Vehicle</th>\n<th>Quantity\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large cart</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">12\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cog</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">Corbita</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">49\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">Knarr</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">43\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Caravel\" title=\"Caravel\">Caravel</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">62\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wagoner_container\" title=\"Wagoner container\">Wagoner container</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">20\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(5193, 1352, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Small crate Bulk storage bin Food storage bin Crate rack', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">Food storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crate_rack\" title=\"Crate rack\">Crate rack</a></li></ul>', 3),
(5194, 1353, 'Description', 'Description', 'A brazier made from metal.', '<p><i>A brazier made from metal.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5195, 1353, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Сan be made of any metal (see images below). See brazier bowl recipe list in-game. brazier bowl must be at least glowing from hot while creation. brazier stand may not be hot. brazier bowl determines resulting material. Can be continued while in the inventory or on the ground. Quality of the brazier stand affects creation chance, brazier bowl quality has no effect. brazier bowl is damaged on a failure to create, brazier stand is damaged on a failure to attach. Uses 0.21kg lump to improve. 0.21kg is lost on a failure to improve.', '<ul><li>Сan be made of any metal (see images below). See <a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">brazier bowl</a> recipe list in-game.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">brazier bowl</a> must be at least glowing from hot while creation.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_stand\" title=\"Brazier stand\">brazier stand</a> may not be hot.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">brazier bowl</a> determines resulting material.</li>\n<li>Can be continued while in the inventory or on the ground.</li>\n<li>Quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_stand\" title=\"Brazier stand\">brazier stand</a> affects creation chance, <a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">brazier bowl</a> quality has no effect.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">brazier bowl</a> is damaged on a failure to create, <a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_stand\" title=\"Brazier stand\">brazier stand</a> is damaged on a failure to attach.</li>\n<li>Uses 0.21kg lump to improve. 0.21kg is lost on a failure to improve.</li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(5196, 1353, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Braziers may be powered by olive oil or tar (0.13kg). The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate. Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below. Braziers are stationary light sources that require higher skill and more materials than street lamps. They can be planted much like a sign and can be picked up by the planter only. You need 10 digging skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 effective quality . Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to decay or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally. There\'s no limit to how many decorative lamps you can plant. When planted on a deed , braziers will be automatically lit during night and unlit during the day. They respond to manual control though, and when snuffed, will stay dark at night. This is also true after planting, so you need fuel to light them the first time. On-deed lamps do not need refueling. Will fit inside a non-runed mailbox.', '<ul><li>Braziers may be powered by <a href=\"/index.php/Olive_oil\" title=\"Olive oil\">olive oil</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a> (0.13kg).</li>\n<li>The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate.</li>\n<li>Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below.</li>\n<li>Braziers are stationary light sources that require higher skill and more materials than street lamps. They can be planted much like a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Signs\" title=\"Category:Signs\">sign</a> and can be picked up by the planter only.</li>\n<li>You need 10 digging skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Effective_quality\" title=\"Effective quality\">effective quality</a>.</li>\n<li>Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally.</li>\n<li>There\'s no limit to how many decorative lamps you can plant.</li>\n<li>When planted on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">deed</a>, braziers will be automatically lit during night and unlit during the day. They respond to manual control though, and when snuffed, will stay dark at night. This is also true after planting, so you need fuel to light them the first time. On-deed lamps do not need refueling.</li>\n<li>Will fit inside a non-runed mailbox.</li></ul>', 2),
(5197, 1353, 'Decorative lamp types', 'Decorative_lamp_types', 'Brazier pillar Candelabra Small brazier', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_pillar\" title=\"Brazier pillar\">Brazier pillar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Candelabra\" title=\"Candelabra\">Candelabra</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Small brazier</a></li></ul>', 3),
(5198, 1353, 'Images', 'Images', 'Gold, electrum, silver, bronze (left to right) Iron, lead, steel (left to right) Copper, tin, brass, zinc (left to right) Glimmersteel, adamantine, empyrean, seryll (left to right)', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:502px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:GESB.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"340\" data-file-width=\"1519\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"112\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/GESB.png/500px-GESB.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/GESB.png/750px-GESB.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1a/GESB.png/1000px-GESB.png 2x\" width=\"500\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:GESB.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Gold, electrum, silver, bronze (left to right)</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:502px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:ILS.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"397\" data-file-width=\"1268\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"157\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1e/ILS.png/500px-ILS.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1e/ILS.png/750px-ILS.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1e/ILS.png/1000px-ILS.png 2x\" width=\"500\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:ILS.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Iron, lead, steel (left to right)</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:502px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:CTBZ.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"419\" data-file-width=\"1646\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"127\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/8d/CTBZ.png/500px-CTBZ.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/8d/CTBZ.png/750px-CTBZ.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/8d/CTBZ.png/1000px-CTBZ.png 2x\" width=\"500\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:CTBZ.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Copper, tin, brass, zinc (left to right)</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:602px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gaes.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"400\" data-file-width=\"1637\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"147\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/9e/Gaes.png/600px-Gaes.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/9e/Gaes.png/900px-Gaes.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/9/9e/Gaes.png/1200px-Gaes.png 2x\" width=\"600\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gaes.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Glimmersteel, adamantine, empyrean, seryll (left to right)</div></div></div>', 4),
(5199, 1354, 'Description', 'Description', 'A stand for braziers.', '<p><i>A stand for braziers.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5200, 1354, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Lump ql does not affect creation chance. Each attempt uses 0.04kg of copper on failure to create. Max creation quality is limited by max lump quality.', '<ul><li>Lump ql does not affect creation chance.</li>\n<li>Each attempt uses 0.04kg of copper on failure to create.</li>\n<li>Max creation quality is limited by max lump quality.</li></ul>', 1),
(5201, 1354, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Small brazier Brazier bowl', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_brazier\" title=\"Small brazier\">Small brazier</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_bowl\" title=\"Brazier bowl\">Brazier bowl</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5202, 1355, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bowl for a small brazier .', '<p>A bowl for a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_brazier\" title=\"Small brazier\">small brazier</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(5203, 1355, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Requires 30 Jewelry smithing to create and uses 0.15kg lump to improve.', '<ul><li>Requires 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a> to create and uses 0.15kg lump to improve.</li></ul>', 1),
(5204, 1355, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Small brazier Brazier stand', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_brazier\" title=\"Small brazier\">Small brazier</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_stand\" title=\"Brazier stand\">Brazier stand</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5209, 1357, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cart designed to transport ships over land.', '<p>A cart designed to transport <a href=\"/index.php/Ship\" title=\"Ship\">ships</a> over land.\n</p>', 0),
(5210, 1357, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Ship transporters require 15 fine carpentry to start and continue building. 0.50 kg log weight is used up when using a log to improve a ship transporter. 20.1 mind logic is needed to command the ship transporter. For security, the ship transporter can be locked with a large padlock Unfinished and finished ships can both be loaded onto the transporter. Will not hold anything but ships. Will not load moored ships or ships you aren\'t allowed to command. Can be dragged as well as have 2 animals hitched to it. Cannot be loaded on a ship. 23 body strength is needed to use the load cargo function. However, in order to load a ship which itself is loaded with cargo, additional body strength is needed depending on that extra weight. For example, a corbita loaded with 1000kg of iron lumps amongst 3 large and 1 small crates will then require 25.4 body strength in order to load onto a ship transporter.', '<ul><li>Ship transporters require 15 <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a> to start and continue building.</li>\n<li>0.50 kg log weight is used up when using a log to improve a ship transporter.</li>\n<li>20.1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> is needed to command the ship transporter.</li>\n<li>For security, the ship transporter can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_padlock\" title=\"Large padlock\">large padlock</a></li>\n<li>Unfinished and finished ships can both be loaded onto the transporter.</li>\n<li>Will not hold anything but ships.</li>\n<li>Will not load moored ships or ships you aren\'t allowed to command.</li>\n<li>Can be dragged as well as have 2 animals hitched to it.</li>\n<li>Cannot be loaded on a ship.</li>\n<li>23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> is needed to use the <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">load cargo</a> function. However, in order to load a ship which itself is loaded with cargo, additional body strength is needed depending on that extra weight. For example, a <a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">corbita</a> loaded with 1000kg of iron lumps amongst 3 large and 1 small crates will then require 25.4 body strength in order to load onto a ship transporter.</li></ul>', 1),
(5211, 1357, 'Hitchable Creatures', 'Hitchable_Creatures', 'Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a cart or wagon. Brown bears when tamed , young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Bulls Bisons Donkeys Hell horse , young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Horses Mules Trolls when dominated , young and adolescent Unicorns when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Weta when on Jackal', '<p>Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a cart or wagon.  \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">Brown bears</a> when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tame\" title=\"Tame\">tamed</a>, young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">Bulls</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bisons</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Donkey\" title=\"Donkey\">Donkeys</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">Hell horse</a>, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horses</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mule\" title=\"Mule\">Mules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Trolls</a> when <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">dominated</a>, young and adolescent</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">Unicorns</a> when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weta\" title=\"Weta\">Weta</a> when on Jackal</li></ul>', 2),
(5212, 1361, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bowl for a brazier.', '<p>A bowl for a brazier.\n</p>', 0),
(5213, 1361, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Requires 30 Jewelry smithing to create, prior to 30 the option does not appear. At 30 Jewelry smithing with a 50ql Large Anvil the creation chance is 28% At 40 Jewelry smithing with a 70ql Large Anvil the creation chance is 61% On failure you lose 10% (0.5kg) of the lump.', '<ul><li>Requires 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a> to create, prior to 30 the option does not appear.</li>\n<li>At 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a> with a 50ql <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Anvil\" title=\"Large Anvil\">Large Anvil</a> the creation chance is 28%</li>\n<li>At 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a> with a 70ql <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Anvil\" title=\"Large Anvil\">Large Anvil</a> the creation chance is 61%</li>\n<li>On failure you lose 10% (0.5kg) of the lump.</li></ul>', 1),
(5214, 1361, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Brazier pillar', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_pillar\" title=\"Brazier pillar\">Brazier pillar</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5220, 1365, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick black bear rug.', '<p><i>A thick black bear rug.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5221, 1365, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Requires 30 leatherworking to create. Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.', '<ul><li>Requires 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leatherworking</a> to create.</li>\n<li>Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.</li></ul>', 1),
(5222, 1365, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Fur can be combined to make the rug as long as it still says black bear fur (activate the black bear fur to combine). 0.30 kg of the fur is lost with each failed creation attempt.', '<ul><li>Fur can be combined to make the rug as long as it still says black bear fur (activate the black bear fur to combine).</li>\n<li>0.30 kg of the fur is lost with each failed creation attempt.</li></ul>', 2),
(5223, 1366, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick mountain lion rug.', '<p><i>A thick mountain lion rug.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5224, 1366, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Requires 30 leatherworking to create. Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.', '<ul><li>Requires 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leatherworking</a> to create.</li>\n<li>Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.</li></ul>', 1),
(5225, 1367, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick brown bear rug.', '<p><i>A thick brown bear rug.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5226, 1367, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Requires 30 leatherworking to create. Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.', '<ul><li>Requires 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leatherworking</a> to create.</li>\n<li>Quality of the rug depends on salt quality.</li></ul>', 1),
(5227, 1367, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Fur can be combined to make the rug as long as it still says brown bear fur (activate the brown bear fur to combine). 0.30 kg of the fur is lost with each failed creation attempt.', '<ul><li>Fur can be combined to make the rug as long as it still says brown bear fur (activate the brown bear fur to combine).</li>\n<li>0.30 kg of the fur is lost with each failed creation attempt.</li></ul>', 2),
