(5745, 1519, 'Description', 'Description', 'A stone slab on two bricks. It looks very inviting. A bench is a decorative item made out of stone bricks , clay , and a slab . Can be created using stone brick , marble brick , sandstone brick , or slate brick .', '<p><i>A stone slab on two bricks. It looks very inviting.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Bench\" title=\"Bench\">bench</a> is a decorative <a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">item</a> made out of <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone bricks</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a>, and a <a href=\"/index.php/Slab\" title=\"Slab\">slab</a>. Can be created using <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">marble brick</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Sandstone_brick\" title=\"Sandstone brick\">sandstone brick</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Slate_brick\" title=\"Slate brick\">slate brick</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(5746, 1519, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'The quality of the brick affects your success chance. The stone slab affects the initial quality of the resulting bench. On failure, the stone brick and the stone slab each take 1.00 damage. Clay can be combined into larger lumps and it will only add 2kg per continue. Must be on the floor to continue building.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the brick affects your success chance.</li>\n<li>The stone slab affects the initial quality of the resulting bench.</li>\n<li>On failure, the stone brick and the stone slab each take 1.00 damage.</li>\n<li>Clay can be combined into larger lumps and it will only add 2kg per continue.</li>\n<li>Must be on the floor to continue building.</li></ul>', 1),
(5747, 1519, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be loaded. Cannot be picked up after completing, but can be pushed/pulled and rotated. Cannot have items placed on it.', '<ul><li>Can be loaded.</li>\n<li>Cannot be picked up after completing, but can be pushed/pulled and rotated.</li>\n<li>Cannot have items placed on it.</li></ul>', 2),
