(5947, 1579, 'Description', 'Description', 'A playful dolphin. They have been known to defend sailors in distress from their natural enemy, the shark.', '<p><i>A playful dolphin. They have been known to defend sailors in distress from their natural enemy, the shark.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5948, 1579, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Dolphins are not caught by fishing, but can be fought and killed like other animals. Dolphins are considered monsters.', '<ul><li>Dolphins are not caught by fishing, but can be fought and killed like other animals.</li>\n<li>Dolphins are considered monsters.</li></ul>', 1),
(5949, 1580, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a weird beast with eight legs. You have heard scary rumours that larger variants sometimes attack ships.', '<p><i>This is a weird beast with eight legs. You have heard scary rumours that larger variants sometimes attack ships.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5950, 1580, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Butchering can produce an octopus ink sac, which is used to make black ink . These octopuses are not caught by fishing, but can be fought in the water like other animals. For the octopus that is caught with a fishing rod , see octopus (fishing) .', '<ul><li>Butchering can produce an octopus ink sac, which is used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Black_ink\" title=\"Black ink\">black ink</a>.</li>\n<li>These octopuses are not caught by fishing, but can be fought in the water like other animals. For the octopus that is caught with a <a href=\"/index.php/Fishing_rod\" title=\"Fishing rod\">fishing rod</a>, see <a href=\"/index.php/Octopus_(fishing)\" title=\"Octopus (fishing)\">octopus (fishing)</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(5951, 1576, 'Description', 'Description', 'It is a Stone brick support.', '<p><i>It is a Stone brick support.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5952, 1576, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This structure\'s foundation and ballast material will vary based on the calculated amount of extensions. Brick supports are 9 meters tall Brick extensions are 3 meters tall each A support can be made for any type of bridge: marble, pottery, rendered, rounded stone, sandstone, slate, or stone brick. The support will include a number of extension - depending of the total size of the bridge The support will include 0, 1 or 2 walls - depending of the total width of the bridge.', '<ul><li>This structure\'s foundation and ballast material will vary based on the calculated amount of extensions.</li>\n<li>Brick supports are 9 meters tall</li>\n<li>Brick extensions are 3 meters tall each</li>\n<li>A support can be made for any type of bridge: marble, pottery, rendered, rounded stone, sandstone, slate, or stone brick.</li>\n<li>The support will include a number of extension - depending of the total size of the bridge</li>\n<li>The support will include 0, 1 or 2 walls - depending of the total width of the bridge.</li></ul>', 1),
(5953, 1576, 'Images', 'Images', 'Highlighted Section = Brick bridge support', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 340px\"><div style=\"width: 340px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 338px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bridgesupport.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"869\" data-file-width=\"979\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/fb/Bridgesupport.png/507px-Bridgesupport.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/fb/Bridgesupport.png/761px-Bridgesupport.png 1.5x, /images/f/fb/Bridgesupport.png 2x\" width=\"338\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 318px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Highlighted Section = Brick bridge support\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
