be loaded by the \"owner\" of the item, i.e. whoever originally dropped it.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>', 4);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(5971, 1587, 'Description', 'Description', 'An ingenious device which turns rough wool into yarn. The Spinning wheel is a tool used to create yarn from wool .', '<p><i>An ingenious device which turns rough wool into yarn.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>Spinning wheel</b> is a tool used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Yarn\" title=\"Yarn\">yarn</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wool\" title=\"Wool\">wool</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(5972, 1587, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate the wool, right-click on the wheel and select create > resources .', '<p>Activate the wool, right-click on the wheel and select <b>create</b> &gt; <b>resources</b>.\n</p>', 1),
(5973, 1587, 'Notes', 'Notes', '30 fine carpentry skill is required to start a spinning wheel. The quality of the small wheel affects the success chance when creating. The unfinished version must be on the floor in order to be continued. The last wooden piece determines the wood type. They cannot be mailed.', '<ul><li>30 <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a> skill is required to start a spinning wheel.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Small_wheel\" title=\"Small wheel\">small wheel</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The unfinished version must be on the floor in order to be continued.</li>\n<li>The last wooden piece determines the wood type.</li>\n<li>They cannot be mailed.</li></ul>', 2),
(5974, 1295, 'Description', 'Description', 'A gravestone to mark the final resting place of someone important.', '<p><i>A gravestone to mark the final resting place of someone important.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(5975, 1295, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A gravestone is a decorative item that can be used to bury a corpse . With a shovel and gravestone in your inventory, activate the gravestone and right-click the corpse on the ground. The corpse will be buried and the gravestone planted in its place.  By activating a stone chisel , an inscription may be made by right-clicking the planted gravestone. Once planted it, cannot be picked up or improved . Can only be moved and turned with the Move right-click options. When dropped, it lays flat on the ground. The default name of the planted gravestone is that of the buried corpse. However, it may be renamed. Maximum inscription length is 2 characters for every 1 full quality of the gravestone. The markings on the stone translate to: respawn alreadi . It is spelled with an i because there is no y in the Futhark language. The gravestone must be bashed to be removed. Repairing requires no specific activated item. Can be created using stone , marble , sandstone , or slate .', '<ul><li>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">gravestone</a> is a decorative item that can be used to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bury\" title=\"Bury\">bury</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Corpse\" title=\"Corpse\">corpse</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>With a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> and gravestone in your inventory, activate the gravestone and right-click the corpse on the ground. The corpse will be buried and the gravestone planted in its place.  By activating a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>, an inscription may be made by right-clicking the planted gravestone.</li>\n<li>Once planted it, cannot be picked up or <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improved</a>.</li>\n<li>Can only be moved and turned with the <i>Move</i> right-click options.</li>\n<li>When dropped, it lays flat on the ground.</li>\n<li>The default name of the planted gravestone is that of the buried corpse. However, it may be renamed.</li>\n<li>Maximum inscription length is 2 characters for every 1 full quality of the gravestone.</li>\n<li>The markings on the stone translate to: <i>respawn alreadi</i>. It is spelled with an <i>i</i> because there is no <i>y</i> in the Futhark language.</li>\n<li>The gravestone must be bashed to be removed.</li>\n<li>Repairing requires no specific activated item.</li>\n<li>Can be created using <a href=\"/index.php/Stone\" title=\"Stone\">stone</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Marble\" title=\"Marble\">marble</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Sandstone_brick\" title=\"Sandstone brick\">sandstone</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Slate\" title=\"Slate\">slate</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(5979, 1444, 'Description', 'Description', '', '', 0),
(5980, 1444, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You must be a follower of Magranon to create, but anyone can continue this item, with increased difficulty for those who do not follow Magranon. Unlike the non-god colossus , this needs a color rune (adamantine of Jackal) instead of craftable dye.', '<ul><li>You must be a follower of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> to create, but anyone can continue this item, with increased difficulty for those who do not follow Magranon.</li>\n<li>Unlike the non-god <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">colossus</a>, this needs a color <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a> (adamantine of Jackal) instead of craftable dye.</li></ul>', 1),
(5981, 1444, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Colossus Colossus of Fo Colossus of Vynora Colossus of Libila', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">Colossus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Fo\" title=\"Colossus of Fo\">Colossus of Fo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Vynora\" title=\"Colossus of Vynora\">Colossus of Vynora</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Libila\" title=\"Colossus of Libila\">Colossus of Libila</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5982, 1443, 'Description', 'Description', 'A grand statue depicting the avatar of the benevolent diety Vynora.', '<p><i>A grand statue depicting the avatar of the benevolent diety Vynora.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(5983, 1443, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You must be a follower of Vynora to create, but anyone can continue this item, with increased difficulty for those who do not follow Vynora. Unlike the non-god colossus , this needs a color rune (adamantine of Jackal) instead of craftable dye.', '<ul><li>You must be a follower of <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> to create, but anyone can continue this item, with increased difficulty for those who do not follow Vynora.</li>\n<li>Unlike the non-god <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">colossus</a>, this needs a color <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a> (adamantine of Jackal) instead of craftable dye.</li></ul>', 1),
(5984, 1443, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Colossus Colossus of Magranon Colossus of Fo Colossus of Libila', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">Colossus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Magranon\" title=\"Colossus of Magranon\">Colossus of Magranon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Fo\" title=\"Colossus of Fo\">Colossus of Fo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Libila\" title=\"Colossus of Libila\">Colossus of Libila</a></li></ul>', 2),
(5985, 1592, 'Description', 'Description', 'A piece of wool cloth, about an arm length square. A square piece of wool cloth is made from yarn .', '<p><i>A piece of wool cloth, about an arm length square.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>square piece of wool cloth</b> is made from <a href=\"/index.php/Yarn\" title=\"Yarn\">yarn</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(5986, 1592, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Clothes Patchwork pants Common wool hat Foresters wool hat Squire wool cap Peasant wool cap Brown bear helm Furniture Royal lounge chaise Tapestries Cavalry motif tapestry Festivities motif tapestry Battle of Kyara tapestry Green tapestry Beige tapestry Orange tapestry Tapestry of Faeldray Tapestry of Mclavin Tapestry of Ehizellbob Tapestry of Evening', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Clothes\" title=\"Clothes\">Clothes</a>\n<dl><dd><a href=\"/index.php/Patchwork_pants\" title=\"Patchwork pants\">Patchwork pants</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Common_wool_hat\" title=\"Common wool hat\">Common wool hat</a></dd>\n<dd><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Foresters_wool_hat\" title=\"Foresters wool hat\">Foresters wool hat</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Squire_wool_cap\" title=\"Squire wool cap\">Squire wool cap</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Peasant_wool_cap\" title=\"Peasant wool cap\">Peasant wool cap</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear_helm\" title=\"Brown bear helm\">Brown bear helm</a></dd></dl></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Furniture\" title=\"Furniture\">Furniture</a>\n<dl><dd><a href=\"/index.php/Royal_lounge_chaise\" title=\"Royal lounge chaise\">Royal lounge chaise</a></dd></dl></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry\" title=\"Tapestry\">Tapestries</a>\n<dl><dd><a href=\"/index.php/Cavalry_motif_tapestry\" title=\"Cavalry motif tapestry\">Cavalry motif tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Festivities_motif_tapestry\" title=\"Festivities motif tapestry\">Festivities motif tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Battle_of_Kyara_tapestry\" title=\"Battle of Kyara tapestry\">Battle of Kyara tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Green_tapestry\" title=\"Green tapestry\">Green tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Beige_tapestry\" title=\"Beige tapestry\">Beige tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Orange_tapestry\" title=\"Orange tapestry\">Orange tapestry</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry_of_Faeldray\" title=\"Tapestry of Faeldray\">Tapestry of Faeldray</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry_of_Mclavin\" title=\"Tapestry of Mclavin\">Tapestry of Mclavin</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry_of_Ehizellbob\" title=\"Tapestry of Ehizellbob\">Tapestry of Ehizellbob</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry_of_Evening\" title=\"Tapestry of Evening\">Tapestry of Evening</a></dd></dl></li></ul>', 1),
(5987, 1592, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the floor loom affects the success chance.', '<p>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Floor_loom\" title=\"Floor loom\">floor loom</a> affects the success chance.\n</p>', 2),
(5988, 1593, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fluffy ball of yarn, incorrect use may be fatal. WARNING: Do not leave unattended near cats!', '<p><i>A fluffy ball of yarn, incorrect use may be fatal. WARNING: Do not leave unattended near cats!</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(5989, 1593, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Yarn may be turned into a square piece of wool cloth which may then be used to create clothes and tapestry .', '<ul><li>Yarn may be turned into a <a href=\"/index.php/Square_piece_of_wool_cloth\" title=\"Square piece of wool cloth\">square piece of wool cloth</a> which may then be used to create <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Clothes\" title=\"Clothes\">clothes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Tapestry\" title=\"Tapestry\">tapestry</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(5999, 1597, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'Main window Options This page explains how to use the Skill tracker window.  To activate the tracker enter the in-game options screen (default key is Esc ), click Tools then More to open HUD Settings and select Skill tracker .  The skill tracker allows players to monitor specific skills in a less obtrusive way than having the Skills window open.  Up to 100 skills over 10 pages may be tracked, including the characteristics and religion hierarchies. Selecting skills Right click the tracker and select Skill tracker options , this pop-up allows the selection of which skills to track for the currently activated page.  From the drop-down menus the player can select which skills to display, in order, to what decimal place they\'d like to see changes and whether or not to activate (show) that particular skill in the window.  The lower-most checkbox, Show progress to next level , when checked will change the progress bar to show just that, rather than progress to 100 as default.  Clicking Ok will confirm any changes on the currently displayed page. Right click on the tracker again and select Save skill tracker to ensure that the choices made are locked in place.  Alternatively the Save to... sub-menu may be used to save to an alternative page. Changing pages Open up the context menu on the tracker and select Next skill tracker , Previous skill tracker or Load skill tracker to pick another page.  The above process may then be repeated to set tracking of different skill-sets. Skill tracker name You can change the name of your 10 skill tracker setups via the skill tracker options function. Select Skill tracker options , then edit the name in the Skill tracker name box.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Skill_tracker.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"356\" data-file-width=\"328\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"326\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7c/Skill_tracker.png/300px-Skill_tracker.png\" srcset=\"/images/7/7c/Skill_tracker.png 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Skill_tracker.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Main window</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Skill_tracker_options.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"513\" data-file-width=\"700\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"220\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/80/Skill_tracker_options.png/300px-Skill_tracker_options.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/80/Skill_tracker_options.png/450px-Skill_tracker_options.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/80/Skill_tracker_options.png/600px-Skill_tracker_options.png 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Skill_tracker_options.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Options</div></div></div>\n<p>This page explains how to use the Skill tracker window.  To activate the tracker enter the in-game options screen (default key is <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120109\">.mw-parser-output .key{border:1px solid #aaa;border-radius:2px;box-shadow:1px 2px 2px #ddd;background-color:#f9f9f9;background-image:linear-gradient(to top,#eee,#f9f9f9,#eee);padding:1px 3px;font-family:inherit;font-size:0.85em}</style>\n<span class=\"key\">Esc</span>), click <b>Tools</b> then <b>More</b> to open <b>HUD Settings</b> and select <b>Skill tracker</b>.  The skill tracker allows players to monitor specific skills in a less obtrusive way than having the <a href=\"/index.php/Skills\" title=\"Skills\">Skills</a> window open.  Up to 100 skills over 10 pages may be tracked, including the <a href=\"/index.php/Characteristics\" title=\"Characteristics\">characteristics</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religion</a> hierarchies.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Selecting_skills\">Selecting skills</span></h3>\n<p><b>Right click</b> the tracker and select <b>Skill tracker options</b>, this pop-up allows the selection of which skills to track for the currently activated page.  From the drop-down menus the player can select which skills to display, in order, to what decimal place they\'d like to see changes and whether or not to activate (show) that particular skill in the window.  The lower-most checkbox, <b>Show progress to next level</b>, when checked will change the progress bar to show just that, rather than progress to 100 as default.  Clicking <b>Ok</b> will confirm any changes on the currently displayed page.\n</p>\n<p>Right click on the tracker again and select <b>Save skill tracker</b> to ensure that the choices made are locked in place.  Alternatively the <b>Save to...</b> sub-menu may be used to save to an alternative page.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Changing_pages\">Changing pages</span></h3>\n<p>Open up the context menu on the tracker and select <b>Next skill tracker</b>, <b>Previous skill tracker</b> or <b>Load skill tracker</b> to pick another page.  The above process may then be repeated to set tracking of different skill-sets.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Skill_tracker_name\">Skill tracker name</span></h3>\n<p>You can change the name of your 10 skill tracker setups via the skill tracker options function. Select <b>Skill tracker options</b>, then edit the name in the <b>Skill tracker name</b> box.\n</p>', 0),
(6000, 1597, 'Tips', 'Tips', 'Priests For priests the Favor skill could be placed on a tracker to see the current deviation from the player\'s maximum.  This would provide a more detailed view of favor than what\'s currently available on the healthbar , at least without needing to hover over anything for information.', '<p><b>Priests</b>\n</p>\n<dl><dd>For <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> the <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">Favor</a> skill could be placed on a tracker to see the current deviation from the player\'s maximum.  This would provide a more detailed view of favor than what\'s currently available on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Healthbar\" title=\"Healthbar\">healthbar</a>, at least without needing to hover over anything for information.</dd></dl>', 1),
(6001, 1597, 'Keybinds', 'Keybinds', 'As with the the toolbelt there are key bindings to quickly change and save tracking pages.  These are also available to change in the launcher settings . Keybind Description NEXT_SKILL_TRACKER Loads the next tracker page in sequence. PREV_SKILL_TRACKER Loads the previous tracker page in sequence. SAVE_SKILL_TRACKER Saves the current setup on the currently selected page. SAVE_SKILL_TRACKER# Saves the current setup on tracker window #.  Note that tracker window 1 is actually #=0, unlike the toolbelt. LOAD_SKILL_TRACKER# Loads tracker window #.  Note that tracker window 1 is actually #=0, unlike the toolbelt.', '<p>As with the the <a href=\"/index.php/Toolbelt\" title=\"Toolbelt\">toolbelt</a> there are <a href=\"/index.php/Key_bindings\" title=\"Key bindings\">key bindings</a> to quickly change and save tracking pages.  These are also available to change in the launcher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settings\" title=\"Settings\">settings</a>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"220\"><b>Keybind</b>\n</th>\n<th width=\"900\"><b>Description</b>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">NEXT_SKILL_TRACKER\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">Loads the next tracker page in sequence.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">PREV_SKILL_TRACKER\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">Loads the previous tracker page in sequence.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">SAVE_SKILL_TRACKER\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">Saves the current setup on the currently selected page.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">SAVE_SKILL_TRACKER#\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">Saves the current setup on tracker window #.  Note that tracker window 1 is actually #=0, unlike the toolbelt.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">LOAD_SKILL_TRACKER#\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">Loads tracker window #.  Note that tracker window 1 is actually #=0, unlike the toolbelt.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(6002, 1598, 'Description', 'Description', 'A curved wooden chair with a footrest.', '<p><i>A curved wooden chair with a footrest.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6003, 1598, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used as decoration.', '<ul><li>Used as decoration.</li></ul>', 1),
(6004, 1598, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Skill Requirement: 40 Fine Carpentry. Can not be loaded Can be picked up by hand.', '<ul><li>Skill Requirement: 40 Fine Carpentry.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded</li>\n<li>Can be picked up by hand.</li></ul>', 2),
(6005, 1599, 'Description', 'Description', 'Feel like the captain of a dragon ship while leaning back comfortably.', '<p><i>Feel like the captain of a dragon ship while leaning back comfortably.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6006, 1599, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Skill Requirement: 70 Fine Carpentry. Can be loaded in a wagon, but not a large cart. Can be picked up by hand. Does not fit in a mailbox, including one runed for size. Wood type is determined by the last wood piece attached.', '<ul><li>Skill Requirement: 70 Fine Carpentry.</li>\n<li>Can be loaded in a wagon, but not a large cart.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up by hand.</li>\n<li>Does not fit in a mailbox, including one runed for size.</li>\n<li>Wood type is determined by the last wood piece attached.</li></ul>', 1),
(6007, 1601, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see an barred wall', '<p><i>You see an barred wall </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6008, 1601, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6009, 1601, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone barred wall . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone barred wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6010, 1601, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6011, 1601, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6012, 1601, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6013, 1602, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall', '<p><i>You see a wall </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6014, 1602, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6015, 1602, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone wall . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6016, 1602, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone wall . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_wall\" title=\"Stone wall\">Stone wall</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6017, 1602, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6018, 1602, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6019, 1603, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see an arched wall opening', '<p><i>You see an arched wall opening </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6020, 1603, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6021, 1603, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone arched wall . Continuation requires at least 1 stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone arched wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6022, 1603, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the stone arched wall . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Stone arched wall\">stone arched wall</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6023, 1603, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a stone brick before improving it. Activate a stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6024, 1603, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6025, 1604, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door', '<p><i>You see a door </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6026, 1604, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob (for example trolls ) or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob (for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>) or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(6027, 1604, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 2),
(6028, 1604, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone door . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone door</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 3),
(6029, 1604, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone door . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_door\" title=\"Stone door\">Stone door</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 4),
(6030, 1604, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(6031, 1604, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 6),
(6032, 1605, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door', '<p><i>You see a door </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6033, 1605, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6034, 1605, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone double door . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone double door</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6035, 1605, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone double door . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_double_door\" title=\"Stone double door\">Stone double door</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6036, 1605, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6037, 1605, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6038, 1606, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door', '<p><i>You see a door </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6039, 1606, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob (for example trolls ) or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob (for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>) or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(6040, 1606, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 2),
(6041, 1606, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone portcullis . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone portcullis</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 3),
(6042, 1606, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone portcullis (wall) . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Stone portcullis (wall)\">Stone portcullis (wall)</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 4);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(6043, 1606, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(6044, 1606, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 6),
(6045, 1607, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a window', '<p><i>You see a window </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6046, 1607, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6047, 1607, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone window . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone window</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6048, 1607, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone window . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_window\" title=\"Stone window\">Stone window</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6049, 1607, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6050, 1607, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6051, 1554, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Although rope bridges can be only one tile wide, they function as any other bridge and can be passed over by large carts and wagons . Uses ropemaking skill. See skill requirements for exact levels. Unlike other bridges, rope bridges sag down in the middle, sagging less when the planner has more body strength . This can make them impractical over shallow areas, or between areas with significant difference in height. Rope Bridge sag (3%-12%) Body Strength Sag % 1 12 10 11 20 10 30 9 40 8 50 7 60 6 70 5 80 4 90 3', '<ul><li>Although rope bridges can be only one tile wide, they function as any other bridge and can be passed over by <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large carts</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagons</a>.</li>\n<li>Uses <a href=\"/index.php/Ropemaking\" title=\"Ropemaking\">ropemaking</a> skill. See <a href=\"/index.php/Bridge#Skill_Requirements\" title=\"Bridge\">skill requirements</a> for exact levels.</li>\n<li>Unlike other bridges, rope bridges sag down in the middle, sagging less when the planner has more <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>. This can make them impractical over shallow areas, or between areas with significant difference in height.</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<caption>Rope Bridge sag (3%-12%)\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Body Strength</th>\n<th>Sag %\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>12\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>11\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>10\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>9\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>7\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>80</td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>3\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 0),
(6052, 1554, 'Construction--Parts of the Bridge', 'Construction--Parts_of_the_Bridge', 'Rope bridge crown The center parts of a rope bridge. It is a bridge crown made of rope. Total items required 10 planks 6 mooring ropes 4 cordage ropes Rope bridge abutment The section of the bridge that connects to the ground. A structure made with rope and built to support the lateral pressure of a span of a rope bridge. Total items required 10 planks 4 logs 2 thick ropes 6 mooring ropes 4 cordage ropes Rope bridge double abutment Only used for one tile rope bridges. It is a bridge abutment made of rope.  This section is only used for one tile long rope bridges. Total items required 10 planks 8 logs 4 thick ropes 8 mooring ropes 4 cordage ropes', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rope_bridge_crown\">Rope bridge crown</span></h3>\n<p>The center parts of a rope bridge. <i>It is a bridge crown made of rope.</i>\n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>10 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>6 <a href=\"/index.php/Mooring_rope\" title=\"Mooring rope\">mooring ropes</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Cordage_rope\" title=\"Cordage rope\">cordage ropes</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rope_bridge_abutment\">Rope bridge abutment</span></h3>\n<p>The section of the bridge that connects to the ground. <i>A structure made with rope and built to support the lateral pressure of a span of a rope bridge.</i>\n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>10 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Thick_rope\" title=\"Thick rope\">thick ropes</a></li>\n<li>6 <a href=\"/index.php/Mooring_rope\" title=\"Mooring rope\">mooring ropes</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Cordage_rope\" title=\"Cordage rope\">cordage ropes</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rope_bridge_double_abutment\">Rope bridge double abutment</span></h3>\n<p>Only used for one tile rope bridges. <i>It is a bridge abutment made of rope.  This section is only used for one tile long rope bridges.</i>\n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>10 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>8 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Thick_rope\" title=\"Thick rope\">thick ropes</a></li>\n<li>8 <a href=\"/index.php/Mooring_rope\" title=\"Mooring rope\">mooring ropes</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Cordage_rope\" title=\"Cordage rope\">cordage ropes</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(6053, 1554, 'Images', 'Images', 'Example of a Rope Bridge', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Ropebridge.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e9/Ropebridge.jpg/800px-Ropebridge.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e9/Ropebridge.jpg/1200px-Ropebridge.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e9/Ropebridge.jpg/1600px-Ropebridge.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 514px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Example of a Rope Bridge\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(6054, 1554, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Bridge Ropemaking', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bridge\" title=\"Bridge\">Bridge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ropemaking\" title=\"Ropemaking\">Ropemaking</a></li></ul>', 3),
(6055, 1609, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'The select bar will display information and actions available to the player depending on which item is currently activated and what item of the world has been clicked upon. To activate the select bar, enter the in-game options screen (default key is Esc) and select Select bar .', '<p>The select bar will display information and actions available to the player depending on which item is currently <a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">activated</a> and what item of the world has been clicked upon. To activate the select bar, enter the in-game options screen (default key is Esc) and select <b>Select bar</b>. \n</p>', 0),
(6056, 1609, 'Additional Usage Notes', 'Additional_Usage_Notes', '(The example image shows the options available when clicking on a cave floor with a pickaxe activated. Notice The examine option, the eye, will always be visible for all selected objects. Next, there is track , mine , prospect , flatten, and pray .) Typically, most options available from the right-click interface will show up in the select bar as descriptive icons. The order of actions in the context menu also corresponds to the order of selected bar buttons. Right-clicking anywhere in the select bar will open the context menu, helpful for when tiles or objects are out of sight. It is important to also note, however, that if the player is too far from the object they are trying to interact with, an action may not be possible, even if it\'s displayed here or on the context menu. Below the object name is a small progress bar and below that is a health bar. To the right of these bars are: an empty box, a button for left-clicking to open the context menu , and a button for toggling the visibility of hotkey text which is bound to a button.  Finally, the last button allows for hiding the quick buttons, making the window slightly smaller. NB: The hotkey text will show up if a key is bound to the select button via SELECT_BUTTON_# . When selecting a creature, or player, its current health is also displayed. To move the window, simply click and drag any portion of the bar which is not a button.  To hide or lock the window, move the mouse pointer to the very extreme edge of the bar - the far right appears to be the easiest location - and right-click and select (Un)Lock or (Un)Hide. Common interactions without items activated include open, repair, take, embark, and so forth. Items in an inventory or container cannot be interacted with via the select bar.', '<div class=\"floatright\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Selectbar.png\"><img alt=\"Selectbar.png\" data-file-height=\"79\" data-file-width=\"277\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"79\" src=\"/images/4/47/Selectbar.png\" width=\"277\"/></a></div>\n<p>(The example image shows the options available when clicking on a cave floor with a pickaxe activated. Notice The <a href=\"/index.php/Examine\" title=\"Examine\">examine</a> option, the eye, will always be visible for all selected objects. Next, there is <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Track\" title=\"Track\">track</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mine\" title=\"Mine\">mine</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Prospect\" title=\"Prospect\">prospect</a>, flatten, and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pray\" title=\"Pray\">pray</a>.)  \n</p>\n<ul><li>Typically, most options available from the right-click interface will show up in the select bar as descriptive icons. The order of actions in the <a href=\"/index.php/Context_menu\" title=\"Context menu\">context menu</a> also corresponds to the order of selected bar buttons.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Right-clicking anywhere in the select bar will open the context menu, helpful for when tiles or objects are out of sight. It is important to also note, however, that if the player is too far from the object they are trying to interact with, an action may not be possible, even if it\'s displayed here or on the context menu.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Below the object name is a small progress bar and below that is a health bar. To the right of these bars are: an empty box, a button for left-clicking to open the <a href=\"/index.php/Context_menu\" title=\"Context menu\">context menu</a>, and a button for toggling the visibility of hotkey text which is bound to a button.  Finally, the last button allows for hiding the quick buttons, making the window slightly smaller.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd>NB: The hotkey text will show up if a key is bound to the select button via <a href=\"/index.php/Key_bindings#SelectBar\" title=\"Key bindings\">SELECT_BUTTON_#</a>.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>When selecting a creature, or player, its current health is also displayed.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"floatright\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Select_bar_creature.jpg\"><img alt=\"Select bar creature.jpg\" data-file-height=\"87\" data-file-width=\"279\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"87\" src=\"/images/f/f1/Select_bar_creature.jpg\" width=\"279\"/></a></div>\n<ul><li>To move the window, simply click and drag any portion of the bar which is not a button.  To hide or lock the window, move the mouse pointer to the very extreme edge of the bar - the far right appears to be the easiest location - and right-click and select (Un)Lock or (Un)Hide.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Common interactions without items activated include open, repair, take, embark, and so forth.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Items in an inventory or container cannot be interacted with via the select bar.</li></ul>', 1),
(6063, 1611, 'Description', 'Description', 'A movable wall made from planks, this will block most arrows and also provide some protection against hot oil.', '<p><i>A movable wall made from planks, this will block most arrows and also provide some protection against hot oil.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6064, 1611, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Automatically snaps to closest tile border player is facing. Can be placed on existing walls. Minimum 10 carpentry to create and continue. Carries a creator tag. Weak against mauling attacks. Can\'t be picked up or loaded into a vehicle, even when unfinished. Any movement requires right-click->move and you may only move it when behind it. Players and creatures may NOT travel through siege shields and they act like a normal fence/wall. Cannot be repaired or improved once planted.', '<ul><li>Automatically snaps to closest tile border player is facing.</li>\n<li>Can be placed on existing walls.</li>\n<li>Minimum 10 carpentry to create and continue.</li>\n<li>Carries a creator tag.</li>\n<li>Weak against mauling attacks.</li>\n<li>Can\'t be picked up or loaded into a vehicle, even when unfinished.</li>\n<li>Any movement requires right-click-&gt;move and you may only move it when behind it.</li>\n<li>Players and creatures may NOT travel through siege shields and they act like a normal fence/wall.</li>\n<li>Cannot be repaired or improved once planted.</li></ul>', 1),
(6065, 1612, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a large mount suited for placing large weapons on.', '<p><i>This is a large mount suited for placing large weapons on.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6066, 1612, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in the creation of ballistas . Can be dyed, but this will not show up when combined into a ballista.', '<ul><li>Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Ballista\" title=\"Ballista\"> ballistas</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be dyed, but this will not show up when combined into a ballista.</li></ul>', 1),
(6067, 1613, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pole fastened in chains lies here.', '<p><i>A pole fastened in chains lies here.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6068, 1613, 'Turret Types', 'Turret_Types', 'A Strange device becomes one of four elemental turrets when cast upon with Courier or Dark messenger under specific circumstances. The basic device is simply ornamental. Strange device - The un-cast default item. Acid turret - Cast inside caves . Frost turret - Cast near water . Fire turret - Cast near a glowing item or by lava . Lightning turret - Cast high upon a mountain. Healing turret - Spawned within active rifts.', '<p>A Strange device becomes one of four elemental turrets when cast upon with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">Courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> under specific circumstances. The basic device is simply ornamental.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Strange device</a> - The un-cast default item.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\" title=\"Acid turret\">Acid turret</a> - Cast inside <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">caves</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\" title=\"Frost turret\">Frost turret</a> - Cast near <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\" title=\"Fire turret\">Fire turret</a> - Cast near a <a href=\"/index.php/Temperature\" title=\"Temperature\">glowing item</a> or by <a href=\"/index.php/Lava\" title=\"Lava\">lava</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\" title=\"Lightning turret\">Lightning turret</a> - Cast high upon a mountain.</li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Healing_turret&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Healing turret (page does not exist)\">Healing turret</a> - Spawned within active rifts.</li></ul>', 1),
(6069, 1613, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Turrets only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they can still be created but are purely decorative, unless spawned as part of an active rift . Needs 40 fine carpentry skill to start. Can be picked up. But will not fit into a large cart or wagon . Cannot be dyed with dye, but can be dyed with a color rune . Turret type depends on the circumstances upon where the cast occurs. A converted device must first be dispelled in order to improve on the item quality or cast. Courier / Dark messenger can\'t shatter a strange device.', '<ul><li>Turrets only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they can still be created but are purely decorative, unless spawned as part of an active <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">rift</a>.</li>\n<li>Needs 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a> skill to start.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up. But will not fit into a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a>.</li>\n<li>Cannot be dyed with dye, but can be dyed with a color <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a>.</li>\n<li>Turret type depends on the circumstances upon where the cast occurs.</li>\n<li>A converted device must first be <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">dispelled</a> in order to improve on the item <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> or cast.</li>\n<li>Courier / Dark messenger can\'t shatter a strange device.</li></ul>', 2),
(6070, 1613, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', 'Strange device Acid turret Frost turret Fire turret Lightning turret', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 136.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Strange_device.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"333\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/205px-Strange_device.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/308px-Strange_device.png 1.5x, /images/6/60/Strange_device.png 2x\" width=\"137\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 117px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Strange device</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 141.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Acid_turret.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"894\" data-file-width=\"842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/212px-Acid_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/318px-Acid_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/424px-Acid_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"142\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 122px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\" title=\"Acid turret\">Acid turret</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 110px\"><div style=\"width: 110px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 108px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Frost_turret.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"551\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/162px-Frost_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/244px-Frost_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/324px-Frost_turret.png 2x\" width=\"108\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 88px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\" title=\"Frost turret\">Frost turret</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 146px\"><div style=\"width: 146px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 144px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Fire_turret.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"673\" data-file-width=\"647\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/216px-Fire_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/325px-Fire_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/433px-Fire_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"144\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 124px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\" title=\"Fire turret\">Fire turret</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 118.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Lightning_turret.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"797\" data-file-width=\"631\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/178px-Lightning_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/267px-Lightning_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/356px-Lightning_turret.png 2x\" width=\"119\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 99px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\" title=\"Lightning turret\">Lightning turret</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(6075, 1615, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long dart with a four-sided pyramidal head which will pierce even thick shields. This is used as ammunition for a ballista .', '<p><i>A long dart with a four-sided pyramidal head which will pierce even thick shields.</i>\n</p>\n<p>This is used as ammunition for a <a href=\"/index.php/Ballista\" title=\"Ballista\">ballista</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(6076, 1615, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality dart head increases your creation chance. The dart will be of the same wood type as the shaft. The material of the dart head has no effect on the dart.', '<ul><li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> dart head increases your creation chance.</li>\n<li>The dart will be of the same wood type as the shaft.</li>\n<li>The material of the dart head has no effect on the dart.</li></ul>', 1),
(6077, 1616, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality small anvil increases your creation chance. Failure creating causes 0.02 kg of lump to be consumed. The quality of the dart head later affects your chance at creating the ballista dart.', '<ul><li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> small anvil increases your creation chance.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> creating causes 0.02 kg of lump to be consumed.</li>\n<li>The quality of the dart head later affects your chance at creating the ballista dart.</li></ul>', 0),
(6078, 1617, 'Description', 'Description', 'The trebuchet is a huge frightening machine designed to haul devastating rocks long distances. You need to put a lot of rocks or ore into it as counterweights.', '<p><i>The trebuchet is a huge frightening machine designed to haul devastating rocks long distances. You need to put a lot of rocks or ore into it as counterweights.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6079, 1617, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To aim a trebuchet, you must load mineable materials into the counterweight, similar to how catapults are cranked. The default firing angle is 45 degrees, which can be changed with a range of 5-85 degrees. Skill requirement: Fine carpentry 80. Cannot be loaded, but must be pushed to its location. Starting power is determined by the loaded amount. Power is directly related to starting velocity. Arc of the projectile is checked along it for any walls, floors, bridges or fences it hits. Otherwise the projectile will travel the full arc until it hits the ground. Projectiles will have a maximum of 20 damage per shot.', '<ul><li>To aim a trebuchet, you must load mineable materials into the counterweight, similar to how <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Catapult\" title=\"Catapult\">catapults</a> are cranked. The default firing angle is 45 degrees, which can be changed with a range of 5-85 degrees.</li>\n<li>Skill requirement: <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">Fine carpentry</a> 80.</li>\n<li>Cannot be loaded, but must be pushed to its location.</li>\n<li>Starting power is determined by the loaded amount. Power is directly related to starting velocity.</li>\n<li>Arc of the projectile is checked along it for any walls, floors, bridges or fences it hits. Otherwise the projectile will travel the full arc until it hits the ground.</li>\n<li>Projectiles will have a maximum of 20 damage per shot.</li></ul>', 1),
(6080, 1617, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a trebuchet: War machines > Trebuchets Mind > Mind logic When creating a trebuchet: Carpentry > Fine carpentry', '<p>When using a trebuchet:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/War_machines\" title=\"War machines\">War machines</a> &gt; Trebuchets</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a trebuchet:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">Fine carpentry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(6081, 1617, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Bombadier at 50 skill Gravel Chucker at 70 skill Siege Lord at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Bombadier at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Gravel Chucker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Siege Lord at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(6082, 1618, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a very quick easy barrier construction made from a log and lots of shafts.', '<p><i>This is a very quick easy barrier construction made from a log and lots of shafts.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6083, 1618, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to deal piercing damage to enemy players when walked across, similar to thorn bushes.', '<ul><li>Used to deal piercing damage to enemy players when walked across, similar to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Thorn\" title=\"Thorn\">thorn</a> bushes.</li></ul>', 1),
(6084, 1618, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Doesn\'t deal damage on PvE servers, or block passage. Doesn\'t break after use. Takes up a tile akin to bulk storage bin and bed . Cannot be moved once created. Building distance is the same tile the barrier will appear on, dealing damage to builder (on PVP only). Minimum 5 carpentry to create and continue', '<ul><li>Doesn\'t deal damage on PvE servers, or block passage.</li>\n<li>Doesn\'t break after use.</li>\n<li>Takes up a tile akin to <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">bed</a>.</li>\n<li>Cannot be moved once created.</li>\n<li>Building distance is the same tile the barrier will appear on, dealing damage to builder (on PVP only).</li>\n<li>Minimum 5 carpentry to create and continue</li></ul>', 2),
(6093, 1621, 'Description', 'Description', 'Inside this building live fanatic guards who spend all their time awake shooting arrows at every enemy in sight. Archery towers on PvP servers will shoot arrows at enemy players. On the Freedom Isles PvE servers, they are purely decorative. The shooting range for a Archery tower is 10-15 tiles and the range and speed will also increase based on the quality.', '<p><i>Inside this building live fanatic guards who spend all their time awake shooting arrows at every enemy in sight.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Archery towers</a> on PvP servers will shoot arrows at enemy players. On the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Isles\" title=\"Freedom Isles\">Freedom Isles</a> PvE servers, they are purely decorative.\n</p>\n<p>The shooting range for a <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Archery tower</a> is 10-15 tiles and the range and speed will also increase based on the quality. \n</p>', 0),
(6094, 1621, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'At least 40 fine carpentry is required to create, as well as to continue building an archery tower. Have to be built at least 20 tiles apart (19 tiles between them) from another archery tower. Needs to be built on a flat tile. Can not be built in a cave. They can be created on the same tiles as guard towers . Automatically centers on the tile it\'s created on. Can not be picked up. Attaching of materials is done on the same tile the unfinished tower is occupying When the last piece is attached, the tower will complete one tile away in the direction the builder is facing. Planning ahead is therefore recommended. (10/10/21 Just created a tower, it remained on the tile I was building it on and also standing in). They will shoot based on their line of sight. On PvP servers, it only functions within kingdom influence. On PvP servers, they require no ammo to shoot, but the arrows can not be picked up. On PvP servers, their arrows can be blocked by shields .', '<ul><li>At least 40 fine carpentry is required to create, as well as to <a href=\"/index.php/Unfinished_item\" title=\"Unfinished item\">continue</a> building an archery tower.</li>\n<li>Have to be built at least 20 tiles apart (19 tiles between them) from another archery tower.</li>\n<li>Needs to be built on a <a href=\"/index.php/Slope\" title=\"Slope\">flat</a> tile.</li>\n<li>Can not be built in a cave.</li>\n<li>They can be created on the same tiles as <a href=\"/index.php/Guard_tower\" title=\"Guard tower\">guard towers</a>.</li>\n<li>Automatically centers on the tile it\'s created on.</li>\n<li>Can not be picked up.</li>\n<li>Attaching of materials is done on the same tile the unfinished tower is occupying</li>\n<li>When the last piece is attached, the tower will complete one tile away in the direction the builder is facing. Planning ahead is therefore recommended. (10/10/21 Just created a tower, it remained on the tile I was building it on and also standing in).</li>\n<li>They will shoot based on their line of sight.</li>\n<li>On PvP servers, it only functions within kingdom influence.</li>\n<li>On PvP servers, they require no ammo to shoot, but the arrows can not be picked up.</li>\n<li>On PvP servers, their arrows can be blocked by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shields</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(6095, 1622, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by acid spirits.', '<p><i>A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by acid spirits.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6096, 1622, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Acid turrets are strange devices that have been cast upon with courier or Dark messenger while inside of a cave . They cause damage to nearby enemies.', '<p>Acid turrets are <a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\" title=\"Strange device\">strange devices</a> that have been cast upon with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> while inside of a <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">cave</a>. They cause damage to nearby enemies.\n</p>', 1),
(6097, 1622, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative. Must be 10 tiles away from another turret. Range of fire is ~8 tiles. Attack may be blocked with a shield . Can not be loaded on a large cart , wagon . Can be picked up. In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first dispelled . Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.', '<ul><li>Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative.</li>\n<li>Must be 10 tiles away from another turret.</li>\n<li>Range of fire is ~8 tiles.</li>\n<li>Attack may be blocked with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a>.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded on a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up.</li>\n<li>In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">dispelled</a>.</li>\n<li>Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.</li></ul>', 2),
(6098, 1622, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', 'Default Acid Frost Fire Lightning', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 136.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"333\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/205px-Strange_device.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/308px-Strange_device.png 1.5x, /images/6/60/Strange_device.png 2x\" width=\"137\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 117px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Default\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 141.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"894\" data-file-width=\"842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/212px-Acid_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/318px-Acid_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/424px-Acid_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"142\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 122px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Acid\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 110px\"><div style=\"width: 110px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 108px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"551\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/162px-Frost_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/244px-Frost_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/324px-Frost_turret.png 2x\" width=\"108\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 88px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Frost\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 146px\"><div style=\"width: 146px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 144px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"673\" data-file-width=\"647\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/216px-Fire_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/325px-Fire_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/433px-Fire_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"144\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 124px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Fire\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 118.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"797\" data-file-width=\"631\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/178px-Lightning_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/267px-Lightning_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/356px-Lightning_turret.png 2x\" width=\"119\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 99px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lightning\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(6099, 1623, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by frost spirits.', '<p><i>A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by frost spirits.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6100, 1623, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Frost turrets are strange devices that have been cast upon with courier or Dark messenger while near water . They cause damage to nearby enemies.', '<p>Frost turrets are <a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\" title=\"Strange device\">strange devices</a> that have been cast upon with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> while near <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>. They cause damage to nearby enemies.\n</p>', 1),
(6101, 1623, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative. Must be 10 tiles away from another turret. Range of fire is ~8 tiles. Attack may be blocked with a shield . Can not be loaded on a large cart , wagon . Can be picked up. In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first dispelled . Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.', '<ul><li>Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative.</li>\n<li>Must be 10 tiles away from another turret.</li>\n<li>Range of fire is ~8 tiles.</li>\n<li>Attack may be blocked with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a>.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded on a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up.</li>\n<li>In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">dispelled</a>.</li>\n<li>Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.</li></ul>', 2),
(6102, 1623, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', 'Default Acid Frost Fire Lightning', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 136.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"333\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/205px-Strange_device.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/308px-Strange_device.png 1.5x, /images/6/60/Strange_device.png 2x\" width=\"137\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 117px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Default\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 141.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"894\" data-file-width=\"842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/212px-Acid_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/318px-Acid_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/424px-Acid_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"142\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 122px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Acid\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 110px\"><div style=\"width: 110px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 108px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"551\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/162px-Frost_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/244px-Frost_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/324px-Frost_turret.png 2x\" width=\"108\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 88px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Frost\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 146px\"><div style=\"width: 146px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 144px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"673\" data-file-width=\"647\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/216px-Fire_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/325px-Fire_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/433px-Fire_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"144\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 124px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Fire\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 118.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"797\" data-file-width=\"631\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/178px-Lightning_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/267px-Lightning_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/356px-Lightning_turret.png 2x\" width=\"119\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 99px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lightning\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(6103, 1624, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by fire spirits.', '<p><i>A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by fire spirits.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6104, 1624, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Fire turrets are strange devices that have been cast upon with courier or Dark messenger while near lava or an item that is glowing from the heat . They cause damage to nearby enemies.', '<p>Fire turrets are <a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\" title=\"Strange device\">strange devices</a> that have been cast upon with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> while near <a href=\"/index.php/Lava\" title=\"Lava\">lava</a> or an item that is <a href=\"/index.php/Temperature\" title=\"Temperature\">glowing from the heat</a>. They cause damage to nearby enemies.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(6105, 1624, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative. Must be 10 tiles away from another turret. Range of fire is ~8 tiles. Attack may be blocked with a shield . Can not be loaded on a large cart , wagon Can be picked up. In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first dispelled . Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.', '<ul><li>Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative.</li>\n<li>Must be 10 tiles away from another turret.</li>\n<li>Range of fire is ~8 tiles.</li>\n<li>Attack may be blocked with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a>.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded on a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a></li>\n<li>Can be picked up.</li>\n<li>In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">dispelled</a>.</li>\n<li>Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.</li></ul>', 2),
(6106, 1624, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', 'Default Acid Frost Fire Lightning', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 136.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"333\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/205px-Strange_device.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/308px-Strange_device.png 1.5x, /images/6/60/Strange_device.png 2x\" width=\"137\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 117px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Default\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 141.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"894\" data-file-width=\"842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/212px-Acid_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/318px-Acid_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/424px-Acid_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"142\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 122px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Acid\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 110px\"><div style=\"width: 110px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 108px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"551\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/162px-Frost_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/244px-Frost_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/324px-Frost_turret.png 2x\" width=\"108\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 88px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Frost\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 146px\"><div style=\"width: 146px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 144px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"673\" data-file-width=\"647\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/216px-Fire_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/325px-Fire_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/433px-Fire_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"144\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 124px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Fire\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 118.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"797\" data-file-width=\"631\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/178px-Lightning_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/267px-Lightning_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/356px-Lightning_turret.png 2x\" width=\"119\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 99px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lightning\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(6107, 1625, 'Descripton', 'Descripton', 'A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by lightning spirits.', '<p><i>A pole in chains floats here. It seems inhabited by lightning spirits.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6108, 1625, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Lightning turrets are strange devices that have been cast upon with courier or Dark messenger while high upon a mountain. They cause damage to nearby enemies.', '<p>Lightning turrets are <a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\" title=\"Strange device\">strange devices</a> that have been cast upon with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> while high upon a mountain. They cause damage to nearby enemies.\n</p>', 1),
(6109, 1625, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative. Must be 10 tiles away from another turret. Range of fire is ~8 tiles. Attack may be blocked with a shield . Can not be loaded on a large cart , wagon . Can be picked up. In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first dispelled . Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.', '<ul><li>Only function on PvP servers. On PvE Freedom servers, they are purely decorative.</li>\n<li>Must be 10 tiles away from another turret.</li>\n<li>Range of fire is ~8 tiles.</li>\n<li>Attack may be blocked with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a>.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded on a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up.</li>\n<li>In order to improve or re-cast upon they must be first <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">dispelled</a>.</li>\n<li>Turret range (Up to 5x their base range at 100ql) and rate of fire (up to 33% faster at 100ql) will increase based on quality.</li></ul>', 2),
(6110, 1625, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', 'Default Acid Frost Fire Lightning', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 138.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 136.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Strange_device\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"333\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/205px-Strange_device.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/60/Strange_device.png/308px-Strange_device.png 1.5x, /images/6/60/Strange_device.png 2x\" width=\"137\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 117px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Default\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 143.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 141.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"894\" data-file-width=\"842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/212px-Acid_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/318px-Acid_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/78/Acid_turret.jpg/424px-Acid_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"142\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 122px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Acid\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 110px\"><div style=\"width: 110px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 108px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"764\" data-file-width=\"551\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/162px-Frost_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/244px-Frost_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/ac/Frost_turret.png/324px-Frost_turret.png 2x\" width=\"108\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 88px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Frost\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 146px\"><div style=\"width: 146px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 144px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"673\" data-file-width=\"647\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/216px-Fire_turret.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/325px-Fire_turret.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Fire_turret.jpg/433px-Fire_turret.jpg 2x\" width=\"144\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 124px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Fire\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 120.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 118.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Lightning_turret\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"797\" data-file-width=\"631\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/178px-Lightning_turret.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/267px-Lightning_turret.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/ff/Lightning_turret.png/356px-Lightning_turret.png 2x\" width=\"119\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 99px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lightning\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(6123, 1628, 'Description', 'Description', 'A more robust wool cap commonly used by squires.', '<p><i>A more robust wool cap commonly used by squires.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6124, 1628, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A minimum of 25 cloth tailoring skill is required to create the Squire wool cap. Hats replace armour pieces to the head and do not provide any protection.', '<ul><li>A minimum of 25 cloth tailoring skill is required to create the Squire wool cap.</li>\n<li>Hats replace <a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armour</a> pieces to the head and do not provide any protection.</li></ul>', 1),
(6125, 1628, 'Variants', 'Variants', 'There are five variants of the squire wool hat, regular, blue, green, yellow, and red. These are all created from the finished base hat and colored raw dying materials. They may not be colored by using pre-made dye. To color a hat it needs to first be dipped in water ; activate water from a container in the inventory and on the base hat right click > create .  The table below shows all materials required to create a dyed hat, including the initial water. Color Water 1 kg Cochineal Copper lump Iron lump Tannin Woad Blue 1 2 Brown 3 3 2 1 Dark 1 1 1 Green 1 1 Red 1 2 Yellow 2 2 1 Gallery Squire wool cap Blue squire wool cap Green squire wool cap Red squire wool cap Yellow squire wool cap', '<p>There are five variants of the squire wool hat, regular, blue, green, yellow, and red. These are all created from the finished base hat and colored raw dying materials. They may not be colored by using pre-made dye.\n</p>\n<p>To color a hat it needs to first be dipped in <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>; activate water from a <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">container</a> in the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> and on the base hat <b>right click</b> &gt; <b>create</b>.  The table below shows all materials required to create a dyed hat, including the initial water.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th height=\"17\" width=\"90\">Color\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a> 1 kg\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Cochineal\" title=\"Cochineal\">Cochineal</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper lump</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">Iron lump</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Tannin\" title=\"Tannin\">Tannin</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Woad\" title=\"Woad\">Woad</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Blue\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Brown\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Dark\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Green\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Red\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Yellow\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 198.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 198.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 196.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Squire_wool_cap.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"160\" data-file-width=\"126\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/c/c0/Squire_wool_cap.png\" width=\"197\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 177px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Squire wool cap\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 208.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 206.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Blue_squire_wool_cap.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"270\" data-file-width=\"223\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/e/e8/Blue_squire_wool_cap.png\" width=\"207\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 187px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Blue squire wool cap\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 203.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 203.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 201.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green_squire_wool_cap.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"276\" data-file-width=\"222\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/f/f7/Green_squire_wool_cap.png\" width=\"202\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 182px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Green squire wool cap\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 209.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 209.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 207.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Red_squire_wool_cap.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"269\" data-file-width=\"223\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/b/bc/Red_squire_wool_cap.png\" width=\"208\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 188px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Red squire wool cap\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 197.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 197.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 195.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Yellow_squire_wool_cap.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"290\" data-file-width=\"227\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/5/51/Yellow_squire_wool_cap.png\" width=\"196\"/></