(6178, 1650, 'Effective ql curve', 'Effective_ql_curve', 'Weapons up to quality 70 have an effective ql curve. Actual QL Effective QL 1 20 10 34.7 20 43.6 30 50.4 40 56.1 50 61.2 60 65.8 70 70 80 80 90 90 100 100', '<p>Weapons up to quality 70 have an effective ql curve. \n</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Actual QL\n</th>\n<th>Effective QL\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>34.7\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>43.6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>50.4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>56.1\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>61.2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>65.8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>70\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>80</td>\n<td>80\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>90\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>100\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(6179, 1650, 'Notes', 'Notes', '*Weapon statistics for bows are those used when wielding the bow in melee combat, not when using it for actual archery .', '<ul><li>*Weapon statistics for bows are those used when wielding the bow in melee combat, not when using it for actual <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(6180, 1651, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small serious gnome stands here ready for christmas. You can barely make out the signature of its maker,  \'Rolf\'.\'', '<p><i>A small serious gnome stands here ready for christmas.</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>You can barely make out the signature of its maker,  \'Rolf\'.\'</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6181, 1651, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These limited edition gnomes were sold on http://www.playerauctions.com/ in 2014. There were only 200 made. Each of these gnomes has Rolf\'s personal signature. Green cap gnomes were gifted with a base quality of 99.0. Their caps glow a bright green. They are supposed to have a secret purpose. Further research and documentation is needed regarding this special purpose as well as with regard to its decay/non-decay properties.', '<ul><li>These limited edition gnomes were sold on <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.playerauctions.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.playerauctions.com/</a> in 2014. There were only 200 made.</li>\n<li>Each of these gnomes has <a href=\"/index.php/User:Rolf\" title=\"User:Rolf\">Rolf\'s</a> personal signature.</li>\n<li>Green cap gnomes were gifted with a base quality of 99.0.</li>\n<li>Their caps glow a bright green.</li>\n<li>They are supposed to have a secret purpose. Further research and documentation is needed regarding this special purpose as well as with regard to its decay/non-decay properties.</li></ul>', 1),
(6182, 1651, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Garden gnome', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Garden_gnome\" title=\"Garden gnome\">Garden gnome</a></li></ul>', 2),
(6183, 1652, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall.', '<p><i>You see a wall. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6184, 1652, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 wooden beam in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Timber framed balcony .', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beam</a>  in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Timber framed balcony</b>.</li></ul>', 1),
(6185, 1652, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 2),
(6186, 1652, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a plank before improving it. Activate a plank , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the plank is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(6187, 1652, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Timber framed wall Timber framed door Timber framed double door Timber framed window Timber framed balcony Timber framed jetty Timber framed arched wall Timber framed arch left Timber framed arch right Timber framed T arch', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_wall\" title=\"Timber framed wall\">Timber framed wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_door\" title=\"Timber framed door\">Timber framed door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_double_door\" title=\"Timber framed double door\">Timber framed double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_window\" title=\"Timber framed window\">Timber framed window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Timber framed balcony</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_jetty\" title=\"Timber framed jetty\">Timber framed jetty</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arched_wall\" title=\"Timber framed arched wall\">Timber framed arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arch_left\" title=\"Timber framed arch left\">Timber framed arch left</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arch_right\" title=\"Timber framed arch right\">Timber framed arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_T_arch\" title=\"Timber framed T arch\">Timber framed T arch</a></li></ul>', 4),
(6188, 1653, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a window.', '<p><i>You see a window. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6189, 1653, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Plank and 1 Large nails in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Wooden wide window . Continuation requires at least 1 plank in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">Plank</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">Large nails</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Wooden wide window</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> in your inventory.</li></ul>', 1),
(6190, 1653, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 2),
(6191, 1653, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a plank before improving it. Activate a plank , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the plank is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(6192, 1653, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Wooden wall Wooden door Wooden double door Wooden window Wooden wide window Wooden portcullis Wooden canopy Wooden arch Wooden T arch Wooden arch right Wooden arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_wall\" title=\"Wooden wall\">Wooden wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_door\" title=\"Wooden door\">Wooden door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_double_door\" title=\"Wooden double door\">Wooden double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_window\" title=\"Wooden window\">Wooden window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Wooden wide window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_portcullis\" title=\"Wooden portcullis\">Wooden portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_canopy\" title=\"Wooden canopy\">Wooden canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch\" title=\"Wooden arch\">Wooden arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_T_arch\" title=\"Wooden T arch\">Wooden T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_right\" title=\"Wooden arch right\">Wooden arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_left\" title=\"Wooden arch left\">Wooden arch left</a></li></ul>', 4),
(6193, 1654, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall.', '<p><i>You see a wall. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6194, 1654, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 wooden beam in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Timber framed jetty .', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beam</a>  in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Timber framed jetty</b>.</li></ul>', 1),
(6195, 1654, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 2),
(6196, 1654, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a plank before improving it. Activate a plank , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the plank is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(6197, 1654, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Timber framed wall Timber framed door Timber framed double door Timber framed window Timber framed balcony Timber framed jetty Timber framed arched wall Timber framed arch left Timber framed arch right Timber framed T arch', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_wall\" title=\"Timber framed wall\">Timber framed wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_door\" title=\"Timber framed door\">Timber framed door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_double_door\" title=\"Timber framed double door\">Timber framed double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_window\" title=\"Timber framed window\">Timber framed window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_balcony\" title=\"Timber framed balcony\">Timber framed balcony</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Timber framed jetty</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arched_wall\" title=\"Timber framed arched wall\">Timber framed arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arch_left\" title=\"Timber framed arch left\">Timber framed arch left</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arch_right\" title=\"Timber framed arch right\">Timber framed arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_T_arch\" title=\"Timber framed T arch\">Timber framed T arch</a></li></ul>', 4),
(6198, 1655, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door.', '<p><i>You see a door. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6199, 1655, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob, for example trolls , or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob, for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>, or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(6200, 1655, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Plank and 1 Large nails in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Wooden canopy . Continuation requires at least 1 plank in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">Plank</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">Large nails</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Wooden canopy</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6201, 1655, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6202, 1655, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a plank before improving it. Activate a plank , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the plank is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6203, 1655, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Wooden wall Wooden door Wooden double door Wooden window Wooden wide window Wooden portcullis Wooden canopy Wooden arch Wooden T arch Wooden arch right Wooden arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_wall\" title=\"Wooden wall\">Wooden wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_door\" title=\"Wooden door\">Wooden door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_double_door\" title=\"Wooden double door\">Wooden double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_window\" title=\"Wooden window\">Wooden window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_wide_window\" title=\"Wooden wide window\">Wooden wide window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_portcullis\" title=\"Wooden portcullis\">Wooden portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Wooden canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch\" title=\"Wooden arch\">Wooden arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_T_arch\" title=\"Wooden T arch\">Wooden T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_right\" title=\"Wooden arch right\">Wooden arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_left\" title=\"Wooden arch left\">Wooden arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6204, 1656, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see an oriel', '<p><i>You see an oriel </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6205, 1656, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6206, 1656, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Stone oriel . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Stone oriel</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6207, 1656, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'Pliers are used for modifying the wall into its trimless version, the Plain stone oriel . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Remove Decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Pliers\" title=\"Pliers\">Pliers</a> are used for modifying the wall into its trimless version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_oriel\" title=\"Plain stone oriel\">Plain stone oriel</a>.  <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Remove Decorations</b>.</li>\n<li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6208, 1656, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6209, 1656, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Stone wall Stone door Stone portcullis Stone window Stone oriel Stone double door Stone T arch Stone arch right Stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_wall\" title=\"Stone wall\">Stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_door\" title=\"Stone door\">Stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Stone portcullis (wall)\"> Stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_window\" title=\"Stone window\">Stone window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_double_door\" title=\"Stone double door\">Stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_T_arch\" title=\"Stone T arch\">Stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_arch_right\" title=\"Stone arch right\">Stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_arch_left\" title=\"Stone arch left\">Stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6210, 1657, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see an oriel.', '<p><i>You see an oriel. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(6211, 1657, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(6212, 1657, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Plain stone oriel . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Plain stone oriel</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(6213, 1657, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'A hammer or mallet can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the Stone oriel . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Add decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> can be used for modifying the wall into its trimmed version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_oriel\" title=\"Stone oriel\">Stone oriel</a>. <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Add decorations</b>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(6214, 1657, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(6215, 1657, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Plain stone wall Plain stone window Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain narrow stone window Plain stone portcullis Plain stone barred wall Plain stone arched wall Plain stone T arch Plain stone arch right Plain stone arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_window\" title=\"Plain stone window\">Plain stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_door\" title=\"Plain stone door\">Plain stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_double_door\" title=\"Plain stone double door\">Plain stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Plain stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_narrow_stone_window\" title=\"Plain narrow stone window\">Plain narrow stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_portcullis\" title=\"Plain stone portcullis\">Plain stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Plain stone barred wall\">Plain stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Plain stone arched wall\">Plain stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Plain stone T arch\">Plain stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Plain stone arch right\">Plain stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Plain stone arch left\">Plain stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(6216, 1658, 'New Client', 'New_Client', 'Non-fatal Debug Messages Logging to <wurm installation path>\\console.log This is the location of the console.log PBuffer support true - Are OpenGL pixel buffers (PBuffers) enabled Windows XP Operating System Using ATI workaround of dispatching display() on event thread This is logged by JOGL if you have an ATI video card. Gui initialized Operating system Windows XP (arch: x86, version: 5.1) - Details of the Operating System, as seen by the JVM. System.getProperty(\"os.name\"), System.getProperty(\"os.arch\") and System.getProperty(\"os.version\"). Java version 1.5.0 the Java version. System.getProperty(\"java.version\"). Java vendor Sun Microsystems Inc. ( http://java.sun.com/ ) : Who made the JVM? System.getProperty(\"java.vendor\") and System.getProperty(\"java.vendor.url\"). Wurm version 1.1.4a : Version of the Wurm Client JOGL version 1.1.0-b06 : Version of JOGL . net.java.games.jogl.Version.getVersion(). OpenGL vendor ATI Technologies Inc. : Who made your Video card & driver.  gL.glGetString(GL.GL_VENDOR). OpenGL renderer RADEON X800 : Video card model. Make sure that this does not refer to MESA software renderer as you will have problems running Wurm without hardware acceleration. gl.glGetString(GL.GL_RENDERER). OpenGL version <Driver OpenGL version> WinXP Release. gl.glGetString(GL.GL_VERSION). OpenGL extensions A list of OpenGL extensions supported by your video card & driver. gl.glGetString(GL.GL_EXTENSIONS). The following OpenGL extensions are required: GL_ARB_window_pos GL_ARB_multitexture There may be others as well. Colorbits 5, 6, 5, 0 : GL.GL_RED_BITS, GL.GL_GREEN_BITS, GL.GL_BLUE_BITS, GL.GL_ALPHA_BITS Stencilbits 8 : GL.GL_STENCIL_BITS Depthbits 24 : GL.GL_DEPTH_BITS Texture units 3 : Number of OpenGL textures supported by the video card GL.GL_MAX_TEXTURE_UNITS. This must be at least 2 or Wurm will not run. Running autorun.bsh Starting the autorun.bsh Sending login woot Trying to logon to the server Login ok Welcome back, CharacterName! Wurm has been waiting for you. : Log on was successful Using ATI workaround of dispatching display() on event thread ATI JOGL workaround PBuffer inited OpenGL PBuffer has been successfully initialised Exceptions java.io.FileNotFoundException: <path>console.log (Access is denied) at java.io.FileOutputStream.open(Native method)\n<snip>\nFailed to open <path>console.log This is logged to the wurm console (press F1) if the client cannot create console.log; in this case the console.log file already existed and was \"read only\". See my suggestion in the Forums: http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?p=28803 Unable to enumerate pixel formats of window using wglGetPixelFormatAttribivARB Crash!\nnet.java.games.jogl.GLException: Unable to enumerate pixel formats of window using wglGetPixelFormatAttribivARB: 127\nat net.java.games.jogl.impl.windows.WindowsGLContext.choosePixelFormatAndCreateContext(WindowsGLContext.java:412)\nat net.java.games.jogl.impl.windows.WindowsOnscreenGLContext.create(WindowsOnscreenGLContext.java:211)\nat net.java.games.jogl.impl.windows.WindowsGLContext.makeCurrent(WindowsGLContext.java:135)\nat net.java.games.jogl.impl.windows.WindowsOnscreenGLContext.makeCurrent(WindowsOnscreenGLContext.java:110)\nat net.java.games.jogl.impl.GLContext.invokeGL(GLContext.java:254)\nat net.java.games.jogl.GLCanvas.displayImpl(GLCanvas.java:208)\nat net.java.games.jogl.GLCanvas.display(GLCanvas.java:75)\nat class.dZ.run(SourceFile:93)\nat java.lang.Thread.run(Unknown Source) This is probably a Video card / video driver problem. http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=2069 http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=2052 http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=2001 WGL_ARB_pixel_format adds functions to WGL that allow the application to query pixel format attributes and choose from a list of supported pixel formats. The primary use of this extension is in conjunction with WGL_ARB_pbuffer in order to test whether a pixel format can be used for a pbuffer. For full details, consult the WGL_ARB_pixel_format spec . Look at Delphi3D´s list of graphics cards that support this extension. Crash: GL_ARB_window_pos not found. Either your graphics card is too old, or you need to update your drivers. Your video driver does not support the OpenGL extension GL_ARB_window_pos, which is required in order to run the Wurm client. Refer to the wurmonline front page for links to new drivers. For full details, consult the GL_ARB_window_pos spec . Look at Delphi3D´s list of graphics cards that support this extension. Crash: No multitexture support found. No multitexture support found.\nEither your graphics card is too old, or you need to update your drivers. Minimum requirements not met. This occurs when your card/driver does not support the GL_ARB_multitexture OpenGL extension. GL_ARB_multitexture is part of OpenGL 1.2.1 and higher. Look at Delphi3D´s list of graphics cards that support this extension.\nRefer to the wurmonline front page for links to new drivers. Crash: No z-buffer found. No z-buffer found.\nEither your graphics card is too old, or you need to update your drivers. Minimum requirements not met. Crash: Found jogl <version number> instead of <required version number> This is usually caused by having manually installed an old version of jogl. To fix it, simply delete the manually installed jogl, and restart Wurm Online. Where <version number> is an unsupported version of JOGL and <required version number> is the only version of JOGL supported by the Wurm client. java.util.ConcurrentModificationException Crash! This occurs when two threads are trying to update the same Java Collection. This can occur when you dragging and dropping items, or other people are changing the same item somewhere. Crash (hard): Error starting Wurm Online UnsatisfiedLinkError : linux Crash (hard): Error starting Wurm Online\njava.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError /home/lxuser/.java/.deployment/javaws/cache/http/Dw