ay send it to an undesired floor.</li>\n<li>You cannot use haul up or haul down with a staircase.</li></ul>', 1),
(6747, 1751, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Openings Marble slab staircase Stone brick staircase Slate slab staircase Pottery brick staircase Spiral staircase Stone slab staircase Standalone staircase', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Openings\" title=\"Category:Openings\">Category:Openings</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_slab_staircase\" title=\"Marble slab staircase\">Marble slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick_staircase\" title=\"Stone brick staircase\">Stone brick staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Slate_slab_staircase\" title=\"Slate slab staircase\">Slate slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick_staircase\" title=\"Pottery brick staircase\">Pottery brick staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spiral_staircase\" title=\"Spiral staircase\">Spiral staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_slab_staircase\" title=\"Stone slab staircase\">Stone slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Standalone_staircase\" title=\"Standalone staircase\">Standalone staircase</a></li></ul>', 2),
(6750, 947, 'Scenario description', 'Scenario_description', 'Scenarios are only active on the epic servers. On Valrei , the deities compete for a number of rare items. One such competition is a scenario. When a deity has found the number of items required to win the scenario (usually half) and brought them to the target location, the scenario is won and ends.\nThe god will then give your side bonuses or the enemy sides penalties. These bonuses and penalties can be terraforming events, volcanos, meteors, skill bonuses etc.', '<p>Scenarios are only active on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Epic\" title=\"Epic\">epic</a> servers.\n</p>\n<p>On <a href=\"/index.php/Valrei_(moon)\" title=\"Valrei (moon)\">Valrei</a>, the <a href=\"/index.php/Gods\" title=\"Gods\"> deities</a> compete for a number of rare items. One such competition is a scenario. When a deity has found the number of items required to win the scenario (usually half) and brought them to the target location, the scenario is won and ends.\nThe god will then give your side bonuses or the enemy sides penalties. These bonuses and penalties can be terraforming events, volcanos, meteors, skill bonuses etc.\n</p>', 0),
(6751, 947, 'Valrei map', 'Valrei_map', 'You can follow the progress of the deities on the in-game Valrei map or on the official twitter feed reflecting the progress of the gods.', '<p>You can follow the progress of the deities on the in-game <a href=\"/index.php/Valrei_map\" title=\"Valrei map\">Valrei map</a> or on the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://twitter.com/#!/valreimoon\" rel=\"nofollow\">official twitter feed</a> reflecting the progress of the gods.\n</p>', 1),
(6752, 947, 'Deity movement & Missions explanation', 'Deity_movement_.26_Missions_explanation', 'On a normal hexagon a deity will move once every 3 days if not assisted by players. The deity will move when the move timer is up, and doing more than one mission will reduce the time to move. There are slow and trap tiles that will increase movement timer, and trap tiles may cost the deity some vitality. A deity will give the players missions that they can complete to help the deity. Two missions are required to be finished for a deity to receive help.  Doing missions may give the deity a small strength or vitality buff as well.\nThe missions are designed to be performed by a number of players based on the current active “base kingdom”  (HOTS, MR and JK as template) population on a server in order to succeed. Sometimes the task will be too hard though, and sometimes it will require only one player to perform something simple on a remote location. Participants in missions will receive 20 minutes of sleep bonus , added to an amount of sleep bonus proportional with their participation, with a maximum of 30 minutes.  They will also get 1 battlerank, and karma/scenario points proportional to the amount of help given towards completing the mission.  Just helping complete it will give the karma/scenario points, the mission only has to be completed for the sleep bonus and battlerank. When a deity loses a fight against another deity or immortal, it will drop any collectibles in its possession and respawn at its home square. Some hexagons will offer strength or vitality buffs. The mission spawn time and expire time are in your own timezone. New mission will spawn when the previous mission is either completed or expires.', '<p>On a normal hexagon a deity will move once every 3 days if not assisted by players. The deity will move when the move timer is up, and doing more than one mission will reduce the time to move. There are slow and trap tiles that will increase movement timer, and trap tiles may cost the deity some vitality.\n</p>\n<p>A deity will give the players <a href=\"/index.php/Mission\" title=\"Mission\">missions</a> that they can complete to help the deity. Two missions are required to be finished for a deity to receive help.  Doing missions may give the deity a small strength or vitality buff as well.\nThe missions are designed to be performed by a number of players based on the current active “base kingdom”  (HOTS, MR and JK as template) population on a server in order to succeed. Sometimes the task will be too hard though, and sometimes it will require only one player to perform something simple on a remote location.\n</p>\n<p>Participants in missions will receive 20 minutes of <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a>, added to an amount of <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a> proportional with their participation, with a maximum of 30 minutes.  They will also get 1 battlerank, and karma/scenario points proportional to the amount of help given towards completing the mission.  Just helping complete it will give the karma/scenario points, the mission only has to be completed for the sleep bonus and battlerank.\n</p>\n<p>When a deity loses a fight against another deity or immortal, it will drop any collectibles in its possession and respawn at its home square.\n</p>\n<p>Some hexagons will offer strength or vitality buffs.\n</p>\n<p>The mission spawn time and expire time are in your own timezone.\n</p>\n<p>New mission will spawn when the previous mission is either completed or expires.\n</p>', 2),
(6753, 947, 'Spell effect bonuses', 'Spell_effect_bonuses', 'Deities will give out certain spell effects when they have received help. They can also remove these spell effects from the opposing gods.  These are based on your kingdom\'s deity, not the religion you follow. Spirit Stamina: Stamina regain is faster Spirit Fervor: Gives 1 CR Spirit Favor: Favour regain is faster', '<p>Deities will give out certain spell effects when they have received help. They can also remove these spell effects from the opposing gods.  These are based on your kingdom\'s deity, not the religion you follow.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Spirit Stamina: Stamina regain is faster</li>\n<li>Spirit Fervor: Gives 1 CR</li>\n<li>Spirit Favor: Favour regain is faster</li></ul>', 3),
(6754, 947, 'Deities allegiances', 'Deities_allegiances', 'Magranon will assist MR and any PMKs using the MR template Fo and Vynora will assist JK and any PMKs using the JK template Libila will assist the BL and any PMKs using the BL template', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> will assist <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/MR\" title=\"MR\">MR</a> and any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PMK\" title=\"PMK\">PMKs</a> using the MR template</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> will assist <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/JK\" title=\"JK\">JK</a> and any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PMK\" title=\"PMK\">PMKs</a> using the JK template</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> will assist the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/BL\" title=\"BL\">BL</a> and any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PMK\" title=\"PMK\">PMKs</a> using the BL template</li></ul>', 4),
(6755, 947, 'Immortals', 'Immortals', 'Immortals are other creatures living on Valrei. Some are friendly to the deities. Nogump the Dirty, a fairly friendly giant whose stupidity makes him a bit dangerous. Friend of Vynora. Jackal is the ally of Magranon. He’s a trickster and apparently looks quite a bit like a Jackal. Jackal is also a moon you can see from ingame. The Deathcrawler is an undead creature who looks like a giant crayfish with a mummified human-like head. The Dirtmaw Giant is a slobbering, aggressive giant whose main goal in life is to trample things and keep his plains flat. Walnut is also called the Treekeeper. His home holds a cherrytree whose berries give the power of immortality, which is what gives him his nickname. Pharmakos, aka The Expelled, is the ally of Libila. He is a tall, pale creature with parchment-like skin who spends his time with alchemy and mystical experiments. The Scavenger is a black beast who roams the Wintertree Hills, searching for and devouring any sort of living or dead meat that enters the region.', '<p>Immortals are other creatures living on Valrei. Some are friendly to the deities.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Nogump the Dirty, a fairly friendly giant whose stupidity makes him a bit dangerous. Friend of Vynora.</li>\n<li>Jackal is the ally of Magranon. He’s a trickster and apparently looks quite a bit like a Jackal. Jackal is also a moon you can see from ingame.</li>\n<li>The Deathcrawler is an undead creature who looks like a giant crayfish with a mummified human-like head.</li>\n<li>The Dirtmaw Giant is a slobbering, aggressive giant whose main goal in life is to trample things and keep his plains flat.</li>\n<li>Walnut is also called the Treekeeper. His home holds a cherrytree whose berries give the power of immortality, which is what gives him his nickname.</li>\n<li>Pharmakos, aka The Expelled, is the ally of Libila. He is a tall, pale creature with parchment-like skin who spends his time with alchemy and mystical experiments.</li>\n<li>The Scavenger is a black beast who roams the Wintertree Hills, searching for and devouring any sort of living or dead meat that enters the region.</li></ul>', 5),
(6756, 947, 'Source tokens', 'Source_tokens', 'Source tokens can be collected by the deities to boost their attacks on other deities', '<p>Source tokens can be collected by the deities to boost their attacks on other deities\n</p>', 6),
(6777, 1757, 'Description', 'Description', 'A hard, sharp piece of rock fastened to a short shaft.', '<p><i>A hard, sharp piece of rock fastened to a short shaft.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6778, 1757, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Either a crude knife or a carving knife can be used to carve a crude shaft from a branch . Only a carving knife can create a shaft from a log ; a crude knife will not work. Either a crude knife or a stone chisel can be used to create a Crude axe head from at stone shards .', '<ul><li>Either a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">crude knife</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a> can be used to carve a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shaft\" title=\"Crude shaft\">crude shaft</a> from a <a href=\"/index.php/Branch\" title=\"Branch\">branch</a>.</li>\n<li>Only a <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a> can create a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> from a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a>; a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">crude knife</a> will not work.</li>\n<li>Either a crude knife or a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a> can be used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe_head\" title=\"Crude axe head\">Crude axe head</a> from at <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(6779, 1757, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A crude axe of stone can be made from simple rummaged and foraged materials if you have lost your iron hatchet . Cannot be improved or repaired.', '<ul><li>A <b>crude axe</b> of stone can be made from simple <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">rummaged and foraged</a> materials if you have lost your iron <a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">hatchet</a>.</li>\n<li>Cannot be improved or repaired.</li></ul>', 2),
(6780, 1757, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Crude tools Crude knife Crude pickaxe Crude shovel', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_tools\" title=\"Crude tools\">Crude tools</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">Crude knife</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\">Crude pickaxe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">Crude shovel</a></li></ul>', 3),
(6785, 1760, 'Description', 'Description', 'A piece of hard stone roughly shaped into an axe blade.', '<p><i>A piece of hard stone roughly shaped into an axe blade.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(6786, 1760, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a crude axe when attached to a crude shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe\" title=\"Crude axe\">crude axe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shaft\" title=\"Crude shaft\">crude shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(6792, 1763, 'Description', 'Description', 'A developing size 5 Village not far from Newtown and Riverside .  Developed by, and for new players, to help them learn the game, skills and a trade.', '<p>A developing size 5 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village\" title=\"Village\">Village</a> not far from Newtown and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Riverside\" title=\"Riverside\">Riverside</a>.  Developed by, and for new players, to help them learn the game, skills and a trade.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(6793, 1763, 'Area Map', 'Area_Map', '', '<p><img alt=\"Lochside.jpg\" src=\"http://thomas.belandi.be/Lochside.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 1),
(6794, 1763, 'Applications', 'Applications', 'We have a starter area nearby.  Applicants for citizenship will be asked to work there.  Those showing enthusiasm and hard work will be invited to become citizens .  Players not invited to become citizens are welcome to continue in the area, and trade with the village.', '<p>We have a starter area nearby.  Applicants for <a href=\"/index.php/Citizen\" title=\"Citizen\">citizenship</a> will be asked to work there.  Those showing enthusiasm and hard work will be invited to become <a href=\"/index.php/Citizen\" title=\"Citizen\">citizens</a>.  Players not invited to become <a href=\"/index.php/Citizen\" title=\"Citizen\">citizens</a> are welcome to continue in the area, and trade with the village.\n</p>', 2),
(6795, 1763, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Shade', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Shade</a>\n</p>', 3),
(6796, 1763, 'Elders', 'Elders', '', '', 4),
(6797, 1763, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Ysildur Naamah Danka Karmien Purp Frangellica Thaneofcawdor Shadak', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Ysildur</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Naamah</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Danka</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Karmien\" title=\"Player:Karmien\">Karmien</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Purp\" title=\"Player:Purp\">Purp</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Frangellica\" title=\"Player:Frangellica\">Frangellica</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Thaneofcawdor\" title=\"Player:Thaneofcawdor\">Thaneofcawdor</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Shadak</a></li></ul>', 5),
(6798, 1763, 'Stores', 'Stores', 'Lochside Gift Shoppe - Selling Ash, Pottery and Wooden goods. Lochside Pawn Shoppe - Selling miscellaneous tools and supplies. Lochside Garden Centre - Coming Soon. Farm Supplies - Coming Soon. Ironmongery - Coming Soon.', '<p>Lochside Gift Shoppe - Selling Ash, Pottery and Wooden goods.\n</p>\n<p>Lochside Pawn Shoppe - Selling miscellaneous tools and supplies.\n</p>\n<p>Lochside Garden Centre - Coming Soon.\n</p>\n<p>Farm Supplies - Coming Soon.\n</p>\n<p>Ironmongery - Coming Soon.\n</p>', 6),
(6799, 1763, 'Alliances', 'Alliances', 'PM Shade to discuss.', '<p>PM Shade to discuss.\n</p>', 7),
(6800, 1764, 'Helheim', 'Helheim', '\"If you stare into an abyss long enough, the abyss will stare back.\"', '<p>\"If you stare into an abyss long enough, the abyss will stare back.\"\n</p>', 0),
(6801, 1764, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Mortal Council Doctorchaos Commonenemy Kingen Citizens Kimble Substance Alts Bait Tay Tylerdun', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Mortal\" title=\"User:Mortal\">Mortal</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Council\">Council</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Doctorchaos</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Commonenemy\" title=\"User:Commonenemy\">Commonenemy</a></li>\n<li>Kingen</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Kimble</li>\n<li>Substance</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alts\">Alts</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Bait</li>\n<li>Tay</li>\n<li>Tylerdun</li></ul>', 1),
(6802, 1764, 'Basic Info', 'Basic_Info', 'Now recruiting. You will need to assist in whatever ways you can. Send a PM to any one of us. Striving to be a major force in the HotS kingdom.', '<p>Now recruiting. You will need to assist in whatever ways you can. Send a PM to any one of us. Striving to be a major force in the HotS kingdom.\n</p>', 2),
(6803, 1765, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Beauturkey Zusker Soltanis Charger Grimbark Ysidro Fazz Lyshep Breygor Madlink Aurorafaith Shaughn Dazt', '<ul><li>Beauturkey</li>\n<li>Zusker</li>\n<li>Soltanis</li>\n<li>Charger</li>\n<li>Grimbark</li>\n<li>Ysidro</li>\n<li>Fazz</li>\n<li>Lyshep</li>\n<li>Breygor</li>\n<li>Madlink</li>\n<li>Aurorafaith</li>\n<li>Shaughn</li>\n<li>Dazt</li></ul>', 0),
(6804, 1766, 'Settlement token', 'Settlement_token', 'There is a sundial and a compass on top of the token. The settlement token is the center of a settlement . There you can read the latest news and information, check the directions from the sundial compass on top, as well as modify your town\'s rules and settings and manage its citizens and guards etc. You can also allocate your bank account at the token to store both money and items (max 5). If you have money in your bank account, you can withdraw it at any settlement token. \nYou can also purchase game time under Manage player payments: 30 days of playing time for 10 silver.\nIf you try to manage your bank (open the item storage) at another token, it asks whether you want to transfer the items there, but the move takes some time to take effect.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Settlement_token_Sundial.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"532\" data-file-width=\"577\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"277\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/56/Settlement_token_Sundial.png/300px-Settlement_token_Sundial.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/56/Settlement_token_Sundial.png/450px-Settlement_token_Sundial.png 1.5x, /images/5/56/Settlement_token_Sundial.png 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Settlement_token_Sundial.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>There is a sundial and a compass on top of the token.</div></div></div>\n<p>The settlement token is the center of a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">settlement</a>. There you can read the latest news and information, check the directions from the sundial compass on top, as well as modify your town\'s rules and settings and manage its citizens and guards etc.\n</p>\n<p>You can also allocate your <a href=\"/index.php/Bank_account\" title=\"Bank account\">bank account</a> at the token to store both <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Money\" title=\"Money\">money</a> and items (max 5). If you have money in your bank account, you can withdraw it at any settlement token. \nYou can also purchase game time under Manage player payments: 30 days of playing time for 10 silver.\nIf you try to manage your bank (open the item storage) at another token, it asks whether you want to transfer the items there, but the move takes some time to take effect.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(6805, 1766, 'Actions', 'Actions', 'Settlement Add to Upkeep This is where you can add to your monthly upkeep from the money in your bank. Area History Announcements about founding and disbanding of villages on your server, as well as slayings of uniques on your server and rift openings. Disband settlement Only select this option if you want to disband your village. Info This tells you the size of the deed, how many guards it has, the amount of upkeep and how long the upkeep will last. Manage windows These windows allow you to change your village permissions . Resize This window allows you to resize your village. Show Village Plan This brings up a 2d plan of your village, which can be exported to use in Deed Planner. Settlement History This tells you who has joined and left the village, who contributed to upkeep and how much they added. Area History This shows a history of deed founding and disbanding, possibly across the entire server. Twitter settings The mayor can configure Twitter settings for your village here. Bank Manage Opens a blank window that lets you drop ingame money into it to be added to your ingame bank account.\nYou generally need to use the website shop to buy premium time, though you can also buy referrals from players or use a token to buy a month for 10 ingame silver. Withdraw Money Lets you withdraw ingame coins from your ingame bank account. Manage Player Payments Here you can buy premium time as long as you have at least 10 silver in your ingame bank account. Select premium rewards This option opens the Marks shop . Reimbursements This option allows you to access any reimbursements that you are entitled for not letting your premium run out, also known as Legacy loyalty bonuses . This program is no longer active, but you may still have unclaimed items from before the Marks shop was launched. Sell This allows you to sell low quality items for iron coins. See Sell for more information. This option will only show up when you have a sellable item activated.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Settlement\">Settlement</span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Add_to_Upkeep\">Add to Upkeep</span></h4>\n<p>This is where you can add to your monthly upkeep from the money in your bank. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Area_History\">Area History</span></h4>\n<p>Announcements about <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement#Founding\" title=\"Settlement\">founding</a> and disbanding of villages on your server, as well as slayings of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Uniques\" title=\"Uniques\">uniques</a> on your server and <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">rift</a> openings. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Disband_settlement\">Disband settlement</span></h4>\n<p>Only select this option if you want to <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement#Disbanding\" title=\"Settlement\">disband</a> your village. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Info\">Info</span></h4>\n<p>This tells you the size of the deed, how many guards it has, the amount of upkeep and how long the upkeep will last.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Manage_windows\">Manage windows</span></h4>\n<p>These windows allow you to change your <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement\" title=\"Permissions\"> village permissions</a>.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resize\">Resize</span></h4>\n<p>This window allows you to <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement#Resizing\" title=\"Settlement\">resize</a> your village. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Show_Village_Plan\">Show Village Plan</span></h4>\n<p>This brings up a 2d plan of your village, which can be exported to use in Deed Planner. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Settlement_History\">Settlement History</span></h4>\n<p>This tells you who has joined and left the village, who contributed to upkeep and how much they added.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Area_History_2\">Area History</span></h4>\n<p>This shows a history of deed founding and disbanding, possibly across the entire server.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Twitter_settings\">Twitter settings</span></h4>\n<p>The mayor can configure Twitter settings for your village here. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bank\">Bank</span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Manage\">Manage</span></h4>\n<p>Opens a blank window that lets you drop ingame money into it to be added to your ingame bank account.\nYou generally need to use the website shop to buy premium time, though you can also buy referrals from players or use a token to buy a month for 10 ingame silver.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Withdraw_Money\">Withdraw Money</span></h4>\n<p>Lets you withdraw ingame coins from your ingame bank account.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Manage_Player_Payments\">Manage Player Payments</span></h4>\n<p>Here you can buy premium time as long as you have at least 10 silver in your ingame bank account.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Select_premium_rewards\">Select premium rewards</span></h3>\n<p>This option opens the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Marks_shop\" title=\"Marks shop\">Marks shop</a>. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Reimbursements\">Reimbursements</span></h3>\n<p>This option allows you to access any reimbursements that you are entitled for not letting your premium run out, also known as <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Legacy_loyalty_bonus\" title=\"Legacy loyalty bonus\">Legacy loyalty bonuses</a>. This program is no longer active, but you may still have unclaimed items from before the Marks shop was launched. \n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sell\">Sell</span></h4>\n<p>This allows you to sell low quality items for iron coins. See <a href=\"/index.php/Sell\" title=\"Sell\">Sell</a> for more information. This option will only show up when you have a sellable item activated.\n</p>', 1),
(6806, 1768, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'Gummo is a small village of Mol-Rehan . and gate of Wild server to MR-Home server. We provide free QL50+ meal and high QL Iron,Copper,Silver,Gold,Tin,Lead for all Mol-Rehan players.', '<p>Gummo is a small village of <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a>. and gate of Wild server to MR-Home server.<br/>\nWe provide free QL50+ meal and high QL Iron,Copper,Silver,Gold,Tin,Lead for all Mol-Rehan players.\n</p>', 0),
(6807, 1768, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Mimiga - [Digger] [Excavater] [Handyman] [Lumberjack] [Mason] [Miner] [Prime Minester] Citizens Bekku - [Farmer] Champion of Fo Ciocc - [Caterer] [Trollslayer] Kaityo in Gold1 Myon - [Miner] Champion of Magranon Namelesscity - [Blacksmith] [Carpenter] [Digger] [Excavater] [Handyman] [Miner] [Trollslayer] Xneo - Yuyuko - Priest of Vynora Trader Rikako', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Mimiga - [Digger] [Excavater] [Handyman] [Lumberjack] [Mason] [Miner] [Prime Minester]</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Bekku - [Farmer] <i>Champion of <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a></i></li>\n<li>Ciocc - [Caterer] [Trollslayer] <i>Kaityo in Gold1</i></li>\n<li>Myon - [Miner] <i>Champion of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a></i></li>\n<li>Namelesscity - [Blacksmith] [Carpenter] [Digger] [Excavater] [Handyman] [Miner] [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li>Xneo -</li>\n<li>Yuyuko - <i>Priest of <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a></i></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trader\">Trader</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Rikako</li></ul>', 1),
(6808, 1768, 'External Links', 'External_Links', 'Wurm Oukoku', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmoukoku.blogsite.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wurm Oukoku</a>\n</p>', 2),
(6809, 1769, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Raffeh - Mayor [Digger][Trollslayer]', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Raffeh\" title=\"User:Raffeh\">Raffeh</a> - Mayor [Digger][Trollslayer]</li></ul>', 0),
(6810, 1769, 'Elders', 'Elders', 'Ztricky - Elder [Trollslayer][Mason] Darius - Elder [Miner][Blacksmith]', '<ul><li>Ztricky - Elder [Trollslayer][Mason]</li>\n<li>Darius - Elder [Miner][Blacksmith]</li></ul>', 1),
(6811, 1769, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Jonglen - Citizen Jaurz - Citizen AlexGodis - Priest of Vynora [Digger][Trollslayer]', '<ul><li>Jonglen - Citizen</li>\n<li>Jaurz - Citizen</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Alexgodis\" title=\"Player:Alexgodis\">AlexGodis</a> - Priest of Vynora [Digger][Trollslayer]</li></ul>', 2),
(6812, 1769, 'Merchants', 'Merchants', 'Coming soon.', '<p>Coming soon.\n</p>', 3),
(6813, 1770, 'Ebony Veil', 'Ebony_Veil', '.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .s-abandonedbox{border-color:#000;background-color:#EEE;text-align:center} Abandoned settlement This settlement has been abandoned, disbanded, or otherwise removed from the world of Wurm. Ebony Veil We Are Coming. Size 15 Village Mayor Marienara Population Classified Allies Crystal Lake Harbours Keep Hell\'s Kitchen Hellstone Helmsdeep Kalaburz No Rest For The Wicked Ombos Our Fort Sealand The Link The Shroud Enemies Jenn Kellon Emperor of The Horde of the Summoned Daolin (Member of EV) Officers of The Horde of the Summoned Armsmaster: Assasin: Posteh Bloodwhisperer: Chief of the Cabal: Mortal Dancer: Khainegomm (Member of EV) Harbinger:  (Member of Sealand) Mistress: Mirjam Main Thug: Tiu Party Fixer: Eir Seer: Wwiiol (Member of EV) Shaman: Wwiiol (Member of EV) Politics High Consul (Mayor) Marienara Consul (Elders) Daolin Doral Dracneir Eir Tiu Nimto Sizewell Zarwin Zerobyte Patricians (Senior Citizens) Barakus Ironfist', '<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120370\">.mw-parser-output .s-abandonedbox{border-color:#000;background-color:#EEE;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"boxstyle s-abandonedbox\">\n<p><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Abandoned_settlements\" title=\"Category:Abandoned settlements\">Abandoned settlement</a></b>\n</p><p>This settlement has been abandoned, disbanded, or otherwise removed from the world of Wurm.\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n<img alt=\"EVHOTS.png\" src=\"http://i29.photobucket.com/albums/c254/kasei10/EVHOTS.png\"/>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120115\">.mw-parser-output .settlement-highlight-row{background-color:#006400;color:#FFFFFF}</style>\n</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"1\" class=\"wikitable\" style=\"float:right; margin:1em; width:200px;\">\n<caption><b>Ebony Veil</b> <br/> <i>We Are Coming.</i>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p><b>Size 15</b> <b>Village</b>\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"settlement-highlight-row\">Mayor\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Marienara\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"settlement-highlight-row\">Population\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Classified\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"settlement-highlight-row\">Allies\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<ul><li>Crystal Lake</li>\n<li>Harbours Keep</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hell%27s_Kitchen\" title=\"Hell\'s Kitchen\">Hell\'s Kitchen</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hellstone\" title=\"Hellstone\">Hellstone</a></li>\n<li>Helmsdeep</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Kalaburz\" title=\"Kalaburz\">Kalaburz</a></li>\n<li>No Rest For The Wicked</li>\n<li>Ombos</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Our_Fort\" title=\"Our Fort\">Our Fort</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sealand\" title=\"Sealand\">Sealand</a></li>\n<li>The Link</li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=The_Shroud&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"The Shroud (page does not exist)\">The Shroud</a></li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"settlement-highlight-row\">Enemies\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p>Jenn Kellon\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Emperor_of_The_Horde_of_the_Summoned\">Emperor of The Horde of the Summoned</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daolin\" title=\"Player:Daolin\">Daolin</a> (Member of EV)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Officers_of_The_Horde_of_the_Summoned\">Officers of The Horde of the Summoned</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Armsmaster:</li>\n<li>Assasin: <a href=\"/index.php/User:Posteh\" title=\"User:Posteh\">Posteh</a></li>\n<li>Bloodwhisperer:</li>\n<li>Chief of the Cabal: <a href=\"/index.php/User:Mortal\" title=\"User:Mortal\">Mortal</a></li>\n<li>Dancer: Khainegomm (Member of EV)</li>\n<li>Harbinger:  (Member of Sealand)</li>\n<li>Mistress: <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mirjam\" title=\"Player:Mirjam\">Mirjam</a></li>\n<li>Main Thug: <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Tiu\" title=\"Player:Tiu\">Tiu</a></li>\n<li>Party Fixer: <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Eir\" title=\"Player:Eir\">Eir</a></li>\n<li>Seer: <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Wwiiol\" title=\"Player:Wwiiol\">Wwiiol</a> (Member of EV)</li>\n<li>Shaman: <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Wwiiol\" title=\"Player:Wwiiol\">Wwiiol</a> (Member of EV)</li></ul>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Politics\">Politics</span></h1>\n<h3><span id=\"High_Consul_(Mayor)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"High_Consul_.28Mayor.29\">High Consul (Mayor)</span></h3>\n<p>Marienara\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Consul_(Elders)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Consul_.28Elders.29\">Consul (Elders)</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daolin\" title=\"Player:Daolin\">Daolin</a></li>\n<li>Doral</li>\n<li>Dracneir</li>\n<li>Eir</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Tiu\" title=\"Player:Tiu\">Tiu</a></li>\n<li>Nimto</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sizewell\" title=\"Player:Sizewell\">Sizewell</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zarwin\" title=\"Player:Zarwin\">Zarwin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Zerobyte\" title=\"User:Zerobyte\">Zerobyte</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Patricians_(Senior_Citizens)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Patricians_.28Senior_Citizens.29\">Patricians (Senior Citizens)</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Barakus\" title=\"User:Barakus\">Barakus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ironfist\" title=\"Player:Ironfist\">Ironfist</a></li></ul>', 0),
(6814, 1771, 'Elin\'s Legacy', 'Elin.27s_Legacy', 'Elin\'s Legacy is a size 11 settlement in the south of Freedom. It\'s located SSE of the south entrance of the Crystal Canal. The settlement is currently made up out of the main fort with a kitchen, a barracks, a smithing & tailoring building and an animal pen. On the norhtside of the main fort is a harbor area with storage facility, docks, shipwright and an inn . The inn houses four beds which are rentable for 1 copper. In the northwest corner is small bit of farmland to ensure a steady supply of cooking ingredients. On the south side of the fort just outside the gate is a small chapel dedicated to Vynora , a silver altar is located within the building. This chapel is only a few tiles removed from the 2 tile highway. The east side and west side of the fort are being reworked as of 16/08/10. A cog was completed for use by the village on 5-5-2010', '<p>Elin\'s Legacy is a size 11 settlement in the south of Freedom. It\'s located SSE of the south entrance of the Crystal Canal.\n</p>\n<p>The settlement is currently made up out of the main fort with a kitchen, a barracks, a smithing &amp; tailoring building and an animal pen. <br/>\nOn the norhtside of the main fort is a harbor area with storage facility, docks, shipwright and an <a href=\"/index.php/Inn\" title=\"Inn\">inn</a>. The inn houses four beds which are rentable for 1 copper.<br/>\nIn the northwest corner is small bit of farmland to ensure a steady supply of cooking ingredients.<br/>\nOn the south side of the fort just outside the gate is a small chapel dedicated to <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>, a silver altar is located within the building. This chapel is only a few tiles removed from the 2 tile highway.<br/><br/>\nThe east side and west side of the fort are being reworked as of 16/08/10. <br/>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">cog</a> was completed for use by the village on 5-5-2010\n</p>', 0),
(6815, 1771, 'Current projects', 'Current_projects', 'Creation of small islands in the lake (1 finished) Dredging the harbor to better facilitate large ships (First dock and exit done, second one still requires dregging) Removal of farmland, raising the freed up area and extending the fort.', '<ul><li>Creation of small islands in the lake (1 finished)</li>\n<li>Dredging the harbor to better facilitate large ships (First dock and exit done, second one still requires dregging)</li>\n<li>Removal of farmland, raising the freed up area and extending the fort.</li></ul>', 1),
(6816, 1771, 'Members', 'Members', 'Infy: co-founder Ghostless: Citizen Elin: Priestess of Vynora', '<ul><li>Infy: co-founder</li>\n<li>Ghostless: Citizen</li>\n<li>Elin: Priestess of Vynora</li></ul>', 2),
(6817, 1772, 'About Elysian Fields', 'About_Elysian_Fields', 'Elysian Fields is a s10 Village located in an inlet on the south eastern coast of the freedom map. It is owned by Artashes and primarily designed by Mithika . The fields produce a great deal of farm crop and this is a site dedicated to the breeding, taming and care of animals. There is an Inn with beds and meals are typically available for passing travelers. This is a great stop to make if you are on your way to visit the red dragon located at Elysian Heights. Elysian Fields disbanded in 2011.', '<p>Elysian Fields is a s10 Village located in an inlet on the south eastern coast of the freedom map. It is owned by Artashes and primarily designed by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:LeveDara\" title=\"User:LeveDara\">Mithika</a>. The fields produce a great deal of farm crop and this is a site dedicated to the breeding, taming and care of animals. \n</p>\n<p>There is an Inn with beds and meals are typically available for passing travelers. This is a great stop to make if you are on your way to visit the red dragon located at Elysian Heights.\n</p>\n<p>Elysian Fields disbanded in 2011.\n</p>', 0),
(6818, 1772, 'The Deed', 'The_Deed', '', '<p><img alt=\"elysianlayout.jpg\" src=\"http://chalicekin.com/wurm/elysianlayout.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 1),
(6819, 1773, 'Description', 'Description', 'Erika is a Size 5 Jenn-Kellon Homestead located on the Wild server somewhere. Erika Anthem http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h8vZsmXUFAg', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Erika\" title=\"Erika\">Erika</a> is a Size 5 <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">Homestead</a> located on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wild\" title=\"Wild\">Wild</a> server somewhere.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><b>Erika Anthem</b>\n</p><p><a class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h8vZsmXUFAg\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h8vZsmXUFAg</a>\n</p>\n</center>', 0),
(6820, 1773, 'Towns Members', 'Towns_Members', 'Erika Finegentlemen', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Erika\">Erika</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Finegentlemen\" title=\"Player:Finegentlemen\">Finegentlemen</a></li></ul>', 1),
