(6920, 1815, 'Battles On Previous Maps', 'Battles_On_Previous_Maps', 'Siege of Merkamanost - Goldv1 Battle for the White Light - Final Beta', '<ul><li>Siege of Merkamanost - <i><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cataclysm\" title=\"Cataclysm\">Goldv1</a></i></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Battle_for_the_White_Light\" title=\"Battle for the White Light\">Battle for the White Light</a> - <i>Final Beta</i></li></ul>', 2),
(6921, 1815, 'Ancient LO', 'Ancient_LO', 'Libilian Outlawz', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Libilian_Outlawz\" title=\"Libilian Outlawz\">Libilian Outlawz</a></li></ul>', 3),
(6922, 1816, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'Originally a size 5 homestead deed carved out the side of a small mountain, Little Harbor was intended to be a cargo port for the land locked village of Rat Point. Over time the borders were expanded and when the Freedom servers opened to free players, Little Harbor experienced a surge in growth and became a village of it\'s own. Though this time has passed, a few remain who call it home. Little Harbor is designed to exploit the beauty of the landscape, with much of it\'s structure hidden from view by gentle slopes and trees allowed to grow freely. The docks are off-deed and available for public use, and a public road leads up through Little Harbor into the mountains and valley beyond.', '<p>Originally a size 5 homestead deed carved out the side of a small mountain, Little Harbor was intended to be a cargo port for the land locked village of Rat Point. Over time the borders were expanded and when the Freedom servers opened to free players, Little Harbor experienced a surge in growth and became a village of it\'s own. Though this time has passed, a few remain who call it home. Little Harbor is designed to exploit the beauty of the landscape, with much of it\'s structure hidden from view by gentle slopes and trees allowed to grow freely. The docks are off-deed and available for public use, and a public road leads up through Little Harbor into the mountains and valley beyond. \n</p>', 0),
(6923, 1816, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Mayor Beanbag Deed holder. Carpenter, Blacksmith, Mason, Miner, Excavator, Farmer. Elders Markesilvers Harbormaster. Shipwright, Cook, Tailor, Farmer. Randazzo Village Administrator. Fisherman, Scout, Forager, Miner, Digger.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Beanbag\" title=\"User:Beanbag\">Beanbag</a>  Deed holder. Carpenter, Blacksmith, Mason, Miner, Excavator, Farmer.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Markesilvers</a>  Harbormaster. Shipwright, Cook, Tailor, Farmer.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Randazzo</a>  Village Administrator. Fisherman, Scout, Forager, Miner, Digger.</li></ul>', 1),
(6924, 1816, 'Recruiting', 'Recruiting', 'Little Harbor is not currently looking for new villagers.', '<p>Little Harbor is not currently looking for new villagers.\n</p>', 2),
(6925, 1817, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'Lupus Pactum is a Undeeded Village located on the Wild Server\nWe are situated on Spider Island and have people joining our Village all the time\nWe always have a good time, Be it working, just messing, and just talking to friends\nTheres always something to do around the Village. We are accepting members all the Time and we have food and water to feed them all, so why not swing by and take a look, lots of work to be done, and theres something to do for everyone!', '<p>Lupus Pactum is a Undeeded Village located on the Wild Server\nWe are situated on Spider Island and have people joining our Village all the time\nWe always have a good time, Be it working, just messing, and just talking to friends\nTheres always something to do around the Village.\n</p>\n<p>We are accepting members all the Time and we have food and water to feed them all, so why not swing by and take a look, lots of work to be done, and theres something to do for everyone!\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(6926, 1817, 'Rules', 'Rules', 'Do not Steal From the Village', '<p>Do not Steal From the Village\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(6927, 1817, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'Walls We need to make defenses, the Walls will be out next step Harbor Well Boats will be released soon, so lets get a head start and make a Harbor, The harbor will have a Beach area and maybe have a shack that will serve nice Drinks\nThe Boats will help us get our Resources alot easier, and trade Weapons and other things, This could open up a lot of Oppotunities for us', '<p><b>Walls</b>\n</p>\n<p>We need to make defenses, the Walls will be out next step<b></b>\n</p>\n<p><b>Harbor</b>\n</p>\n<p>Well Boats will be released soon, so lets get a head start and make a Harbor, The harbor will have a Beach area and maybe have a shack that will serve nice Drinks\nThe Boats will help us get our Resources alot easier, and trade Weapons and other things, This could open up a lot of Oppotunities for us\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(6928, 1817, 'Ranks and Members', 'Ranks_and_Members', 'The Village is made up of Ranks, These Ranks will get you to places you need, If your just starting out, you may not have access to certain places a Noble could, so you gotta work up and get the Privledges 1) King: Tbot 2) Noble: Faunze Milp/Smbh 3) Warchief: skiyootlaroso Facepunchrider 4) Higher Villager: Viperguy 5) Villager: Raksard 6) Peasant: Bassclef Anthraxa Stickmaus Alucardx Allyhax Foxhound Stratoss Fernando Kinver Waerlock', '<p>The Village is made up of Ranks, These Ranks will get you to places you need, If your just starting out, you may not have access to certain places a Noble could, so you gotta work up and get the Privledges\n</p>\n<p><b>1) King:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Tbot\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>2) Noble:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Faunze\n</p>\n<p>Milp/Smbh\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><b>3) Warchief:</b>\n</p>\n<p>skiyootlaroso\n</p>\n<p>Facepunchrider\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>4) Higher Villager:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Viperguy\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><b>5) Villager:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Raksard\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><b>6) Peasant:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Bassclef\n</p>\n<p>Anthraxa\n</p>\n<p>Stickmaus\n</p>\n<p>Alucardx\n</p>\n<p>Allyhax\n</p>\n<p>Foxhound\n</p>\n<p>Stratoss\n</p>\n<p>Fernando\n</p>\n<p>Kinver\n</p>\n<p>Waerlock\n</p>', 3),
(6929, 1818, 'Description', 'Description', 'Marnimark on Water is a two-man village and will more than likely stay that way. Situated on the hillside downstream from Reborn west from Samling , down the fjord/lake/river. Useful Buildings Kitchen Blacksmith Craft House Armoury Storhouse Resources Iron Lead Tin Politics Non-confrontational, however will defend land from griefers. Freedom rule breakers will be reported. Founders Marni Greasemark Citizens Not recruiting. Tradeskills TBA.', '<p><b>Marnimark on Water</b> is a two-man village and will more than likely stay that way. Situated on the hillside downstream from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Reborn\" title=\"Reborn\">Reborn</a> west from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Samling\" title=\"Samling\">Samling</a>, down the fjord/lake/river.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Useful_Buildings\">Useful Buildings</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Kitchen</li>\n<li>Blacksmith</li>\n<li>Craft House</li>\n<li>Armoury</li>\n<li>Storhouse</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Iron_vein\" title=\"Iron vein\">Iron</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lead_vein\" title=\"Lead vein\">Lead</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tin_vein\" title=\"Tin vein\">Tin</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Politics\">Politics</span></h3>\n<p>Non-confrontational, however will defend land from griefers. Freedom rule breakers will be reported.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Founders\">Founders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Marni\" title=\"Player:Marni\">Marni</a></li>\n<li>Greasemark</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Not recruiting.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tradeskills\">Tradeskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li>TBA.</li></ul>', 0),
(6930, 1819, 'Marshy Cove', 'Marshy_Cove', 'The Community of Marshy Cove was founded by Mercutio of Jenn-Kellon. It is located just east of Scorpion Stone , along the coastline. We believe in making the most of the area we live in. which means that we do not waste space by making mansions and unnecessary large buildings. We each have our own private area which is only a single tile house with three tiles of personal yard. There is no need for anything bigger because of community buildings for storage, smithing and farming. Each member has their own ovens that will be improved to 20 quality if requested. If interested in joining Marshy Cove, contact Mercutio ingame or Forum PM Tybalt.', '<p><b></b>\n</p>\n<p>The Community of Marshy Cove was founded by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mercutio\" title=\"Player:Mercutio\"> Mercutio</a> of Jenn-Kellon. It is located just east of <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Scorpion_stone_(village)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Scorpion stone (village) (page does not exist)\">Scorpion Stone</a>, along the coastline. \n</p>\n<p>We believe in making the most of the area we live in. which means that we do not waste space by making mansions and unnecessary large buildings. We each have our own private area which is only a single tile house with three tiles of personal yard. There is no need for anything bigger because of community buildings for storage, smithing and farming. Each member has their own ovens that will be improved to 20 quality if requested. If interested in joining Marshy Cove, contact Mercutio ingame or Forum PM Tybalt.\n<b></b>\n</p>', 0),
(6931, 1819, 'What We Offer.', 'What_We_Offer.', '20+ Quality Community Forge 20+ Quality Community Large Anvil Access to Community Dairy Farm Access to Community Farms Community Mines with all Veins but Silver and Zinc(Access to Silver and Zinc near by.) 20 Quality Raw Materials for Improving Fine Fishing Rods Available for use upon Request Clay in Local Area Tar in Local Area Nice Covered Dock for Fishing and Shipbuilding', '<p><b></b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>20+ Quality Community Forge</li>\n<li>20+ Quality Community Large Anvil</li>\n<li>Access to Community Dairy Farm</li>\n<li>Access to Community Farms</li>\n<li>Community Mines with all Veins but Silver and Zinc(Access to Silver and Zinc near by.)</li>\n<li>20 Quality Raw Materials for Improving</li>\n<li>Fine Fishing Rods Available for use upon Request</li>\n<li>Clay in Local Area</li>\n<li>Tar in Local Area</li>\n<li>Nice Covered Dock for Fishing and Shipbuilding</li></ul>\n<p><b></b>\n</p>', 1),
(6932, 1819, 'Community Rules.', 'Community_Rules.', 'Everyone gets 2x2 Personal Area, that is all. Houses are not to be over one tile in size. No Slave Labor. Help with community where you can. No Building, Terraforming, Paving or Cutting local trees without discussing plans with Mercutio or Kepler. No Hoarding, of anything. If you have more than you can use in a reasonable time, share with the community. No Animal Abuse. If you can\'t take care of an animal, you don\'t need it. Also no beating the cows. Have Fun, it is after all the reason we are all here.', '<p><b></b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Everyone gets 2x2 Personal Area, that is all. Houses are not to be over one tile in size.</li>\n<li>No Slave Labor.</li>\n<li>Help with community where you can.</li>\n<li>No Building, Terraforming, Paving or Cutting local trees without discussing plans with Mercutio or Kepler.</li>\n<li>No Hoarding, of anything. If you have more than you can use in a reasonable time, share with the community.</li>\n<li>No Animal Abuse. If you can\'t take care of an animal, you don\'t need it. Also no beating the cows.</li>\n<li>Have Fun, it is after all the reason we are all here.</li></ul>', 2),
(6933, 1820, 'History', 'History', 'It was dark. Sounds of creatures were heard from all around. Two excited explorers left the landmass of the home of Jenn-Kellon and left for an island of contested space, a wild island. It was a day from then that they had setup camp and begun to construct a settlement, a fort, to defend themselves from Horde of the Summoned. Miriel Advert', '<p>It was dark. Sounds of creatures were heard from all around. Two excited explorers left the landmass of the home of Jenn-Kellon and left for an island of contested space, a wild island. It was a day from then that they had setup camp and begun to construct a settlement, a fort, to defend themselves from Horde of the Summoned.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www12.asphost4free.com/FortFN/Miriel_Tower.swf\" rel=\"nofollow\">Miriel Advert</a>\n</p>', 0),
(6934, 1820, 'Deed', 'Deed', 'We have no deed as yet.', '<p>We have no deed as yet.\n</p>', 1),
(6935, 1820, 'Resources', 'Resources', 'We have a clay area, access to iron, tin and gold with more metal prospected. We are located next to a lemon forest with plenty of pines around. The deed area is on the side of a mountain with a safe path leading up to it. The area is perfect for building defences on.', '<p>We have a clay area, access to iron, tin and gold with more metal prospected. We are located next to a lemon forest with plenty of pines around. The deed area is on the side of a mountain with a safe path leading up to it. The area is perfect for building defences on.\n</p>', 2),
(6936, 1820, 'Location / Screenshots', 'Location_.2F_Screenshots', 'View from south side of deed area:', '<p>View from south side of deed area:\n<img alt=\"MirielView5.jpg\" src=\"http://www12.asphost4free.com/FortFN/Images/MirielView5.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 3),
(6937, 1820, 'Population', 'Population', 'abandonded', '<dl><dd>abandonded</dd></dl>', 4),
(6938, 1822, 'The Village', 'The_Village', 'New Eden is a beautiful Jenn-Kellon village located within the vast lands of the Wild server. We have large amounts of open land and resources such as iron, copper, zinc, silver, gold, peat, wood, tar, and clay at our disposal. As well as bountiful amounts of wild animals and fish. New Eden is a wonderful village for any player coming from Golden Valley, looking for a safe and nice place to call home, or any experienced players desiring a village to reside in and grow.', '<p>New Eden is a beautiful Jenn-Kellon village located within the vast lands of the Wild server. We have large amounts of open land and resources such as iron, copper, zinc, silver, gold, peat, wood, tar, and clay at our disposal. As well as bountiful amounts of wild animals and fish. New Eden is a wonderful village for any player coming from Golden Valley, looking for a safe and nice place to call home, or any experienced players desiring a village to reside in and grow.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(6939, 1822, 'Citizenship', 'Citizenship', 'To join the village, you need to first contact one of the Templar. You will be evaluated by the council and if you are cleared, you will either be told the location of the village, or be brought to the village. Upon your approval of joining by the Templar, you will be admitted as a Citizen of New Eden. As a Citizen of New Eden, all we ask is that you contribute to helping the village, with projects and maintenance, and do your share to better it while you\'re here. In return, we will give you good food, clean water, and a safe place to sleep. We hope you enjoy it here in New Eden, and would love to have you!', '<p>To join the village, you need to first contact one of the Templar. You will be evaluated by the council and if you are cleared, you will either be told the location of the village, or be brought to the village. Upon your approval of joining by the Templar, you will be admitted as a Citizen of New Eden.\n</p>\n<p>As a Citizen of New Eden, all we ask is that you contribute to helping the village, with projects and maintenance, and do your share to better it while you\'re here. In return, we will give you good food, clean water, and a safe place to sleep. We hope you enjoy it here in New Eden, and would love to have you!\n</p>', 1),
(6940, 1822, 'Templar', 'Templar', '- Typhlix (Lord) - Jaegar - Tynathat - Acurapassion', '<p>- <b><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Typhlix\" title=\"Player:Typhlix\">Typhlix</a> (Lord)</b>\n</p>\n<p>- <b>Jaegar</b>\n</p>\n<p>- <b>Tynathat</b>\n</p>\n<p>- <b><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Acurapassion\" title=\"Player:Acurapassion\">Acurapassion</a></b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(6941, 1822, 'Citizens Past and Present', 'Citizens_Past_and_Present', '- \' Adrego \' - \'Ajmac\' - \'Alvin\' - \' Arieon \' - \' Bacheaven \' - \'Bruce\' - \' Chewius \' - \' Decoy \' - \' Elistremal \' - \' Fewtyl \' - \'Icezeppo\' - \' Jayzen \' - \' Jenuv \' - \' Lute \' - \'Lynksis\' - \' Malimoo \' - \' Mannerius \' - \' Ragadorn \' - \' Soleca \' - \'Timy\' - \'Ttex\' - \' Zaramoth \'', '<p>- \'<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Adrego\" title=\"Player:Adrego\">Adrego</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Ajmac\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Alvin\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Arieon\" title=\"Player:Arieon\">Arieon</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Bacheaven\" title=\"Player:Bacheaven\">Bacheaven</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Bruce\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Chewius\" title=\"Player:Chewius\">Chewius</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Decoy\" title=\"Player:Decoy\">Decoy</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Elistremal\" title=\"Player:Elistremal\">Elistremal</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Fewtyl\" title=\"Player:Fewtyl\">Fewtyl</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Icezeppo\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jayzen\" title=\"Player:Jayzen\">Jayzen</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jenuv\" title=\"Player:Jenuv\">Jenuv</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Lute\" title=\"Player:Lute\">Lute</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Lynksis\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Malimoo\" title=\"Player:Malimoo\">Malimoo</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Mannerius\" title=\"Player:Mannerius\">Mannerius</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Ragadorn\" title=\"Player:Ragadorn\">Ragadorn</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Soleca\" title=\"Player:Soleca\">Soleca</a>\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Timy\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'Ttex\'\n</p>\n<p>- \'<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zaramoth\" title=\"Player:Zaramoth\">Zaramoth</a>\'\n</p>', 3),
(6942, 1822, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Created by: Acurapassion, edited by Typhlix', '<p><img alt=\"NewEdenLandscapecopy.png\" src=\"http://i37.photobucket.com/albums/e77/04rsxs/NewEdenLandscapecopy.png\"/>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Created by: Acurapassion, edited by Typhlix\n</p>', 4),
(6947, 1825, 'The Story so Far.', 'The_Story_so_Far.', 'many a month ago... there was a place named Vagrant... It was peaceful, many people lived there, and it was a happy place, but one day all the water ran dry and people moved away, leaving a small barren landscape behind them... one person decided to make a small yet triumphant stand though, his name was traslogan... Traslogan journeyed to First Light in search of new people in search of adventure in the land of riches, and there he found durr. Both of them were eager and willing to find a land where the lakes run free and the land runs wild, and they journeyed all over the Golden Valley, and finally found a stretch of water, and many miles of endless forest and flat landscapes... they named this place New Vagrant ... People from far and near journeyed into New Vagrant... seeing opportunity and settling down in the housing that durr and traslogan had made, after a few short months the village prospered, becoming big enough to be visible on a map of the Golden Valley. there were new places in the village like storage buildings, public farmland, and smithies and cookeries. But in the end... the bros...an old enemy of wurm...famous for destroying the natural beauty of the world...they came... ravaging the landscape... destroying what paradise the villagers had made for themselves. the villagers left, Durr left, Lotan left, everyone left expect traslogan who held out until the last minute, where traslogan officially retired from mayorship and retired to Bottleneck Bay. A third Vagrant in the Golden Valley has been established by Lotan, who originated from New Vagrant. It\'s name is Vagrant Hill, set on top of a mesa only minutes away from the debris of New Vagrant. But now, after months of recovering... Traslogan has rose up again, he has rallied Durr, Cragos, Donovar and Glyde... Together the 5 of them are journeying to The Freedom Isles... To establish Vagrant over there... The Journey has been hard.                                                                       \nEncounters have been rough.                                                                                    \nBut Vagrant has prevailed.                                                                                                             \nA new era begins... The era of New Vagrant II Vagrant Shall live on... So Long as there is one Vagrant-Man standing, he shall charge forward to make another Vagrant. - Paterso', '<p>many a month ago... there was a place named Vagrant... It was peaceful, many people lived there, and it was a happy place, but one day all the water ran dry and people moved away, leaving a small barren landscape behind them... one person decided to make a small yet triumphant stand though, his name was traslogan...\n</p>\n<p>Traslogan journeyed to First Light in search of new people in search of adventure in the land of riches, and there he found durr. Both of them were eager and willing to find a land where the lakes run free and the land runs wild, and they journeyed all over the Golden Valley, and finally found a stretch of water, and many miles of endless forest and flat landscapes... they named this place <i>New Vagrant</i>...\n</p>\n<p>People from far and near journeyed into New Vagrant... seeing opportunity and settling down in the housing that durr and traslogan had made, after a few short months the village prospered, becoming big enough to be visible on a map of the Golden Valley. there were new places in the village like storage buildings, public farmland, and smithies and cookeries.\n</p>\n<p>But in the end... the bros...an old enemy of wurm...famous for destroying the natural beauty of the world...they came... ravaging the landscape... destroying what paradise the villagers had made for themselves. the villagers left, Durr left, Lotan left, everyone left expect traslogan who held out until the last minute, where traslogan officially retired from mayorship and retired to Bottleneck Bay.\n</p>\n<p>A third Vagrant in the Golden Valley has been established by Lotan, who originated from New Vagrant. It\'s name is Vagrant Hill, set on top of a mesa only minutes away from the debris of New Vagrant.\n</p>\n<p>But now, after months of recovering... Traslogan has rose up again, he has rallied Durr, Cragos, Donovar and Glyde... Together the 5 of them are journeying to The Freedom Isles... To establish Vagrant over there...\n</p>\n<p>The Journey has been hard.                                                                       \nEncounters have been rough.                                                                                    \nBut Vagrant has prevailed.                                                                                                             \nA new era begins... The era of New Vagrant II    \n</p>\n<p><i>Vagrant Shall live on... So Long as there is one Vagrant-Man standing, he shall charge forward to make another Vagrant.</i> - Paterso\n</p>', 0),
(6948, 1825, 'So whats happening now?', 'So_whats_happening_now.3F', 'Since the absence of  Traslogan, New Vagrant has practically left the wurm world and is a very quiet village...but it still lurks there in kinoss bay... New Vagrant is currently recruiting as it currently has well enough space to manage many, many more villagers.', '<p>Since the absence of  Traslogan, New Vagrant has practically left the wurm world and is a very quiet village...but it still lurks there in kinoss bay...\n</p>\n<p>New Vagrant is currently recruiting as it currently has well enough space to manage many, many more villagers.\n</p>', 1),
(6949, 1825, 'Where exactly is New Vagrant now?', 'Where_exactly_is_New_Vagrant_now.3F', 'New Vagrant is disbanded.', '<p>New Vagrant is disbanded.\n</p>', 2),
(6950, 1825, 'past and present mayors', 'past_and_present_mayors', 'Vagrant:Straggler:Missing:presumed dead or went premium New Vagrant:Durr(now known as myriad):Unknown: No Reply Via Forum or Game in over 8 months Vagrant Hill:Lotan:Alive and Well: Ragequitted. New Vagrant(Original&Freedom):Traslogan:Alive and Well:Resides at Traslogan\'s Retreat New Vagrant(Freedom) : Lappen & Draconis - Current Mayors', '<p>Vagrant:Straggler:Missing:presumed dead or went premium\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nNew Vagrant:Durr(now known as myriad):Unknown: No Reply Via Forum or Game in over 8 months              \n</p>\n<p><br/>         \nVagrant Hill:Lotan:Alive and Well: Ragequitted.\n</p>\n<p>New Vagrant(Original&amp;Freedom):Traslogan:Alive and Well:Resides at <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Traslogan%27s_Retreat\" title=\"Traslogan\'s Retreat\">Traslogan\'s Retreat</a>\n</p>\n<p>New Vagrant(Freedom) : Lappen &amp; Draconis - Current Mayors\n</p>', 3),
(6951, 1825, 'Villagers of New Vagrant', 'Villagers_of_New_Vagrant', 'Traslogan - Founder (Rumoured to think of wurm as a Doner Kebab)    - left New Vagrant Renegade(Command&Conquer...duh?!) Berks(Sorry...No Comment.) Lappen(Good ol lappen) - Mayor Tarakona(tara...whatta?) Leverloos(flush...) Draconis(Dragons anonymous) - Mayor', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Traslogan\" title=\"Player:Traslogan\">Traslogan</a> - Founder (Rumoured to think of wurm as a Doner Kebab)    - left New Vagrant        \n</p>\n<p>Renegade(Command&amp;Conquer...duh?!)\n</p>\n<p>Berks(Sorry...No Comment.)\n</p>\n<p>Lappen(Good ol lappen) - Mayor\n</p>\n<p>Tarakona(tara...whatta?)\n</p>\n<p>Leverloos(flush...)\n</p>\n<p>Draconis(Dragons anonymous) - Mayor\n</p>', 4),
(6952, 1825, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Coming along soon :)', '<p>Coming along soon :)\n</p>', 5),
(6953, 1826, 'The Story so Far.', 'The_Story_so_Far.', 'many a month ago... there was a place named Vagrant... It was peaceful, many people lived there, and it was a happy place, but one day all the water ran dry and people moved away, leaving a small barren landscape behind them... one person decided to make a small yet triumphant stand though, his name was traslogan... Traslogan journeyed to First Light in search of new people in search of adventure in the land of riches, and there he found durr. Both of them were eager and willing to find a land where the lakes run free and the land runs wild, and they journeyed all over the Golden Valley, and finally found a stretch of water, and many miles of endless forest and flat landscapes... they named this place New Vagrant ... People from far and near journeyed into New Vagrant... seeing opportunity and settling down in the housing that durr and traslogan had made, after a few short months the village prospered, becoming big enough to be visible on a map of the Golden Valley. there were new places in the village like storage buildings, public farmland, and smithies and cookeries. But in the end... the bros...an old enemy of wurm...famous for destroying the natural beauty of the world...they came... ravaging the landscape... destroying what paradise the villagers had made for themselves. the villagers left, Durr left, Lotan left, everyone except traslogan left until the last minute, where traslogan officially retired from mayorship and retired to Bottleneck Bay. A third Vagrant in the Golden Valley has been established by Lotan, who originated from New Vagrant. It\'s name is Vagrant Hill, set on top of a mesa only minutes away from the debris of New Vagrant. But now, after months of recovering... Traslogan has rose up again, he has rallied Durr, Cragos, Donovar and Glyde... Together the 5 of them are journeying to The Freedom Isles... To establish Vagrant over there... Vagrant Shall live on... So Long as there is one Vagrant-Man standing, he shall charge forward to make another Vagrant. - Paterso', '<p>many a month ago... there was a place named Vagrant... It was peaceful, many people lived there, and it was a happy place, but one day all the water ran dry and people moved away, leaving a small barren landscape behind them... one person decided to make a small yet triumphant stand though, his name was traslogan...\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\"> Traslogan</a> journeyed to First Light in search of new people in search of adventure in the land of riches, and there he found durr. Both of them were eager and willing to find a land where the lakes run free and the land runs wild, and they journeyed all over the Golden Valley, and finally found a stretch of water, and many miles of endless forest and flat landscapes... they named this place <i><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/New_Vagrant\" title=\"New Vagrant\">New Vagrant</a></i>...\n</p>\n<p>People from far and near journeyed into New Vagrant... seeing opportunity and settling down in the housing that durr and traslogan had made, after a few short months the village prospered, becoming big enough to be visible on a map of the Golden Valley. there were new places in the village like storage buildings, public farmland, and smithies and cookeries.\n</p>\n<p>But in the end... the bros...an old enemy of wurm...famous for destroying the natural beauty of the world...they came... ravaging the landscape... destroying what paradise the villagers had made for themselves. the villagers left, Durr left, Lotan left, everyone except traslogan left until the last minute, where traslogan officially retired from mayorship and retired to Bottleneck Bay.\n</p>\n<p>A third Vagrant in the Golden Valley has been established by Lotan, who originated from New Vagrant. It\'s name is Vagrant Hill, set on top of a mesa only minutes away from the debris of New Vagrant.\n</p>\n<p>But now, after months of recovering... Traslogan has rose up again, he has rallied Durr, Cragos, Donovar and Glyde... Together the 5 of them are journeying to The Freedom Isles... To establish Vagrant over there...\n</p>\n<p><i>Vagrant Shall live on... So Long as there is one Vagrant-Man standing, he shall charge forward to make another Vagrant.</i> - Paterso\n</p>', 0),
(6954, 1826, 'past and present mayors', 'past_and_present_mayors', 'Vagrant:Straggler:Missing:presumed dead or went premium New Vagrant:Traslogan:Alive and Well:Retired from mayorship: resides in at GlitterDale Lake with a small group of players. New Vagrant:Durr:Gone:left Wurm due to griefing:Rumoured to have gone premium or to have stopped playing altogether. Vagrant Hill:Lotan:Alive and Well:Still current mayor', '<p>Vagrant:Straggler:Missing:presumed dead or went premium\n</p>\n<p><br/>                \nNew Vagrant:Traslogan:Alive and Well:Retired from mayorship: resides in at GlitterDale Lake with a small group of players.                     \n</p>\n<p>New Vagrant:Durr:Gone:left Wurm due to griefing:Rumoured to have gone premium or to have stopped playing altogether.                \n</p>\n<p><br/>         \nVagrant Hill:Lotan:Alive and Well:Still current mayor\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(6955, 1826, 'Villagers(those who are either still in a Vagrant or were once in a Vagrant)', 'Villagers.28those_who_are_either_still_in_a_Vagrant_or_were_once_in_a_Vagrant.29', 'Straggler(mayor)(Mr.nochaos) Lotan(mayor)(sits back and enjoys the ride) Traslogan(mayor)(Rumoured to think of wurm as a Doner Kebab) Durr(mayor)(Mr.NO MORE GRIEFAHS!!!) Kyuuka(likes fishing white sharks in wurm) Wolves(The 1-man-band) Cheese(The silent one...) Godmon(The Repairman) Mrice(the lemon-lover) Hevet(the Mystery dude) Arrowwind(The Rat Trainer) Maleficus(The Dude who nicked the kleptomaniac title lol) ClayTonic(Sorry...No description...)', '<p>Straggler(mayor)(Mr.nochaos)\n</p>\n<p>Lotan(mayor)(sits back and enjoys the ride)          \n</p>\n<p>Traslogan(mayor)(Rumoured to think of wurm as a Doner Kebab)            \n</p>\n<p>Durr(mayor)(Mr.NO MORE GRIEFAHS!!!)\n</p>\n<p>Kyuuka(likes fishing white sharks in wurm)\n</p>\n<p>Wolves(The 1-man-band)           \n</p>\n<p>Cheese(The silent one...)             \n</p>\n<p>Godmon(The Repairman)           \n</p>\n<p>Mrice(the lemon-lover)          \n</p>\n<p>Hevet(the Mystery dude)             \n</p>\n<p>Arrowwind(The Rat Trainer)          \n</p>\n<p>Maleficus(The Dude who nicked the kleptomaniac title lol)       \n</p>\n<p>ClayTonic(Sorry...No description...)\n</p>', 2),
(6956, 1827, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Mayor Jaybudd Dwarf Jaiden Dwarf Jolinar Dwarf Werid Dwarf Whimsy', '<ul><li>Mayor <a href=\"/index.php/User:Jaybudd\" title=\"User:Jaybudd\">Jaybudd</a></li>\n<li>Dwarf <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jaiden\" title=\"Player:Jaiden\">Jaiden</a></li>\n<li>Dwarf <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Jolinar\" title=\"Player:Jolinar\">Jolinar</a></li>\n<li>Dwarf Werid</li>\n<li>Dwarf <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Whimsy\" title=\"Player:Whimsy\">Whimsy</a></li></ul>', 0),
(6957, 1827, 'History', 'History', 'June \'09 Tuscany Port is founded.  Eventually, the original 11x11 is flattened. January \'10 The 21x21 land area that encompasses the initial area of Nist Akath is completed, with special thanks to Traxx of Pheonix Enterprises . February \'10 The new deed changes are put in place. Tuscany Port as such is disbanded and replaced with Nist Akath. Alliance is formed with Pheonix Enterprises . Jaiden joins the village. March \'10 Jaybudd , overseer, takes a vacation from Wurm. Deed silently remains. May \'10 Jaybudd returns.  Nothing major is changed. June \'10 Alliances with Mallorn Estate and Saltwater Farm formed. Jolinar joins the village. July \'10 Mallorn Estate disbanded. Werid joins the village. Whimsy joins the village. April \'11 Disbanded.', '<p>June \'09<br/>\nTuscany Port is founded.  Eventually, the original 11x11 is flattened.<br/>\n<br/>\nJanuary \'10<br/>\nThe 21x21 land area that encompasses the initial area of Nist Akath is completed, with special thanks to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Traxx\" title=\"Player:Traxx\">Traxx</a> of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pheonix_Enterprises\" title=\"Pheonix Enterprises\">Pheonix Enterprises</a>.<br/>\n<br/>\nFebruary \'10<br/>\nThe new deed changes are put in place.  <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tuscany_Port\" title=\"Tuscany Port\">Tuscany Port</a> as such is disbanded and replaced with Nist Akath.<br/>\nAlliance is formed with <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pheonix_Enterprises\" title=\"Pheonix Enterprises\">Pheonix Enterprises</a>.<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jaiden\" title=\"Player:Jaiden\">Jaiden</a> joins the village.<br/>\n<br/>\nMarch \'10<br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Jaybudd\" title=\"User:Jaybudd\">Jaybudd</a>, overseer, takes a vacation from Wurm.<br/>\nDeed silently remains.<br/>\n<br/>\nMay \'10<br/>\nJaybudd returns.  Nothing major is changed.<br/>\n<br/>\nJune \'10<br/>\nAlliances with Mallorn Estate and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Saltwater_Farm\" title=\"Saltwater Farm\">Saltwater Farm</a> formed.<br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Jolinar\" title=\"Player:Jolinar\">Jolinar</a> joins the village.<br/>\n<br/>\nJuly \'10<br/>\nMallorn Estate disbanded.<br/>\nWerid joins the village.<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Whimsy\" title=\"Player:Whimsy\">Whimsy</a> joins the village.<br/>\n</p>\n<p>April \'11<br/>\nDisbanded.<br/>\n</p>', 1),
(6958, 1827, 'Useful Links', 'Useful_Links', 'Sketchup Model Screenshots', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/jaybud4/wurm-online/nist-akath-sketchup\" rel=\"nofollow\">Sketchup Model</a><br/>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/jaybud4/wurm-online/nist-akath\" rel=\"nofollow\">Screenshots</a>\n</p>', 2),
