(7226, 1906, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'Coming soon :P', '<p>Coming soon :P<br/>\n</p>', 3),
(7227, 1906, 'History and Events', 'History_and_Events', 'Dec 14, 2006 22:38 GMT - The village of Sturmgeist has just been founded by Tfugl. Jan 9, 2007 16:23 GMT - Under the rule of Tfugl, Sturmgeist has formed an alliance with Northern Light. Citizens rejoice! Feb 2, 2007 18:24 GMT - Under the rule of Tfugl, Sturmgeist has been disbanded and the town people has moved to Northern Light. Citizens rejoice!', '<p>Dec 14, 2006 22:38 GMT - The village of Sturmgeist has just been founded by Tfugl.<br/>\nJan 9, 2007 16:23 GMT - Under the rule of Tfugl, Sturmgeist has formed an alliance with Northern Light. Citizens rejoice!<br/>\nFeb 2, 2007 18:24 GMT - Under the rule of Tfugl, Sturmgeist has been disbanded and the town people has moved to Northern Light. Citizens rejoice!<br/>\n</p>', 4),
(7228, 1909, 'History', 'History', 'SweC-village #1 (2005-08-05 - 2005-08-11) Events: 2005-02-28 20:46 Keit suggests the game \"Wurm Online\" on the SweC forums. It all started here. ( Swedishphoenix \'s notes: It actually took about 6 months untill somebody answered in this thread. Despite the late entry, this thread would become the biggest one about Wurm Online on the forums.) 2005-08-05 22:10 Nienithaur finds the perfect place for the first SweC-village. It was a bit NE from the whitelight, near Eir\'s fortress. 2005-08-11 13:46 Xerbee declares the village to be dead. The vets left and let the n00bs play around in the ruins. The village lived for 6 days. The cause of the death was because there were 30+ members, food was sparse, chat filled with noobs asking for help, and complete chaos.\nBrallan helped to take over the village and try to get it functional again. The rest of the story is clouded... Misc. info: Deed: No Members: 30+ http://www.fsson.com/wurm (First website or forums for the village. Dead link.) Most of the swedish vets came or had a connection to this village. Antondaslayer (?), Mazarinkid (?), Xerbee , Brallan, Nischka, Angry and more... Source: http://www.sweclockers.com/forum/showthread.php?s=&threadid=426747 SweC-village #2 (2006-02-25 - 2006-) Events: 2006-02-20 16:23 One year later Hypre suggests to try again with a village. 2006-02-25 00:00 The village was started. Zalmanusa found a nice place north of the old avalon treefarm (NW from NT). 2006-03-03 07:28 Rotab logs on and finds himself trapped in our mine. Apparently some Blacklighters have raided the camp and sealed the mine. Ran suggests to build a tower or move. Many new players started, so they stayed for a while at the old camp. 2006-03-03 22:13 Xerbee suggests to move to Cape Fear, near South Port. The crew, Reservdel ( Mongo ), Xerbee , Ran, Hypre and Rotab started moving with our carts towards the new village. When they arrived they thought it over, and they did not like the new place. 2006-03-04 15:44 Xerbee says that he and 5 others will go to Toni \'s old place and get money for a deed. The result would become the same as the first village; the vets would leave the n00bs all by themselves in the ruins of the village. 2006-03-04 19:37 The legendary Swedishphoenix starts to play the game, and joins the village fast. He started to make some basic wooden tools and planks. Rotab , Reservdel ( Mongo ), Pellefan and VeoRinr were the first villagers he met, and 2 of them would become some of his closest friends... 2006-03-05 15:22 The second BL-raid takes place. \"<Fryking>BL raidar er!! kom in och försvara fanan förihelvete!\" 2006-03-05 18:40 The first \"big\" impact on the village. Now the vets are planning their \"escape\" for Toni\'s village. They want to cloud it from the other villagers by going on a seperate IRC-channel, and telling everyone in the old channel to keep quiet about it. But the noble CerpA takes a screenshot and posts on the forums. More and more, the village stared to break down. 2006-03-08 15:28 Midiland (possibly RPGprayer\'s alt) tells everyone on the forums that we have a mole in the village. \"Someone has to die then\". Swedishphoenix took on the job as secret detective and would soon reveal the mole. 2006-03-10 22:08 3:rd BL-raid started. Malvada, Heven, Erwtje, Fusspawn, Robinhawkins and Inacron were present during the raid. This started to get serious, they had several hyenas, our forge got a rotting touch spell, 4 houses were smashed down and raided, our cow got killed and resurrected as a zombie, almost all resources were stolen, aswell as all the items. Malvada \"traced\" my IP and \"hacked\" himself into our IRC-channel. He got a fat ban on Swedishphoenix \'s request though. (Several weeks after gold, malvado told Swedishphoenix that he got the IRC-adress from the mole, and not hacked the channel.) After the raid, Midiland claims that Swedishphoenix is the mole. This got punched down fast by Rotab . According to him, Swedishphoenix \'s mission was to kill Xerbee and Ran for being tyrants. After some research, Swedishphoenix found out that RPGprayer was the mole. He had also converted to BL during the raid.', '<h3><span id=\"SweC-village_#1_(2005-08-05_-_2005-08-11)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"SweC-village_.231_.282005-08-05_-_2005-08-11.29\">SweC-village #1 (2005-08-05 - 2005-08-11)</span></h3>\n<p><b>Events:</b>\n</p>\n<p><b>2005-02-28 20:46</b> Keit suggests the game \"Wurm Online\" on the SweC forums. It all started here. (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a>\'s notes: It actually took about 6 months untill somebody answered in this thread. Despite the late entry, this thread would become the biggest one about Wurm Online on the forums.)<br/>\n<b>2005-08-05 22:10</b> Nienithaur finds the perfect place for the first SweC-village. It was a bit NE from the whitelight, near Eir\'s fortress.<br/>\n<b>2005-08-11 13:46</b> Xerbee declares the village to be dead. The vets left and let the n00bs play around in the ruins. The village lived for 6 days. The cause of the death was because there were 30+ members, food was sparse, chat filled with noobs asking for help, and complete chaos.\nBrallan helped to take over the village and try to get it functional again. The rest of the story is clouded...\n</p>\n<p><b>Misc. info:</b><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Deed: No<br/>\nMembers: 30+<br/>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.fsson.com/wurm\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.fsson.com/wurm</a> (First website or forums for the village. Dead link.)\n</p>\n<p>Most of the swedish vets came or had a connection to this village. <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Antondaslayer\" title=\"Player:Antondaslayer\">Antondaslayer</a> (?), Mazarinkid (?), <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xerbee\" title=\"Player:Xerbee\">Xerbee</a>, Brallan, Nischka, Angry and more...\n</p>\n<p><b>Source:</b><br/>\n<a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.sweclockers.com/forum/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=426747\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.sweclockers.com/forum/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=426747</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"SweC-village_#2_(2006-02-25_-_2006-)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"SweC-village_.232_.282006-02-25_-_2006-.29\">SweC-village #2 (2006-02-25 - 2006-)</span></h3>\n<p><b>Events:</b>\n</p>\n<p><b>2006-02-20 16:23</b> One year later Hypre suggests to try again with a village.<br/>\n<b>2006-02-25 00:00</b> The village was started. Zalmanusa found a nice place north of the old avalon treefarm (NW from NT).<br/>\n<b>2006-03-03 07:28</b> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Rotab\" title=\"User:Rotab\">Rotab</a> logs on and finds himself trapped in our mine. Apparently some Blacklighters have raided the camp and sealed the mine. Ran suggests to build a tower or move. Many new players started, so they stayed for a while at the old camp.<br/>\n<b>2006-03-03 22:13</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xerbee\" title=\"Player:Xerbee\">Xerbee</a> suggests to move to Cape Fear, near South Port. The crew, Reservdel (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mongo\" title=\"Player:Mongo\">Mongo</a>), <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xerbee\" title=\"Player:Xerbee\">Xerbee</a>, Ran, Hypre and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Rotab\" title=\"User:Rotab\">Rotab</a> started moving with our carts towards the new village. When they arrived they thought it over, and they did not like the new place.<br/>\n<b>2006-03-04 15:44</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xerbee\" title=\"Player:Xerbee\">Xerbee</a> says that he and 5 others will go to <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Toni\" title=\"Player:Toni\">Toni</a>\'s old place and get money for a deed. The result would become the same as the first village; the vets would leave the n00bs all by themselves in the ruins of the village.<br/>\n<b>2006-03-04 19:37</b> The legendary <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> starts to play the game, and joins the village fast. He started to make some basic wooden tools and planks. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Rotab\" title=\"User:Rotab\">Rotab</a>, Reservdel (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mongo\" title=\"Player:Mongo\">Mongo</a>), Pellefan and VeoRinr were the first villagers he met, and 2 of them would become some of his closest friends...<br/>\n<b>2006-03-05 15:22</b> The second BL-raid takes place. \"&lt;Fryking&gt;BL raidar er!! kom in och försvara fanan förihelvete!\"<br/>\n<b>2006-03-05 18:40</b> The first \"big\" impact on the village. Now the vets are planning their \"escape\" for Toni\'s village. They want to cloud it from the other villagers by going on a seperate IRC-channel, and telling everyone in the old channel to keep quiet about it. But the noble CerpA takes a screenshot and posts on the forums. More and more, the village stared to break down.<br/>\n<b>2006-03-08 15:28</b> Midiland (possibly RPGprayer\'s alt) tells everyone on the forums that we have a mole in the village. \"Someone has to die then\". <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> took on the job as secret detective and would soon reveal the mole.<br/>\n<b>2006-03-10 22:08</b> 3:rd BL-raid started. Malvada, Heven, Erwtje, Fusspawn, Robinhawkins and Inacron were present during the raid. This started to get serious, they had several hyenas, our forge got a rotting touch spell, 4 houses were smashed down and raided, our cow got killed and resurrected as a zombie, almost all resources were stolen, aswell as all the items. Malvada \"traced\" my IP and \"hacked\" himself into our IRC-channel. He got a fat ban on <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a>\'s request though. (Several weeks after gold, malvado told <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> that he got the IRC-adress from the mole, and not hacked the channel.)<br/>\nAfter the raid, Midiland claims that <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> is the mole. This got punched down fast by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Rotab\" title=\"User:Rotab\">Rotab</a>. According to him, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a>\'s mission was to kill <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xerbee\" title=\"Player:Xerbee\">Xerbee</a> and Ran for being tyrants.<br/>\nAfter some research, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> found out that RPGprayer was the mole. He had also converted to BL during the raid.\n</p>', 0),
(7229, 1909, 'Info', 'Info', 'The (5:th) Swec-village was bought by Steffe and founded by Swedishphoenix . Deed size: 5 Towers: 2, 40 ql Democracy: No Trader : No Personal Merchant : 1. Stationed outside The Swec-village, currently selling basic tools and compasses. Deity: Vynora - IRC-channel: #swec-wurm @ quakenet.org Forums: http://www.orjans.se/alex/wurm/', '<p>The (5:th) Swec-village was bought by Steffe and founded by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Deed size: 5<br/>\nTowers: 2, 40 ql<br/>\nDemocracy: No<br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">Trader</a>: No<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Personal_Merchant\" title=\"Personal Merchant\">Personal Merchant</a>: 1. Stationed outside The Swec-village, currently selling basic tools and compasses.<br/>\nDeity: <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a><br/>\n-<br/>\nIRC-channel: #swec-wurm @ quakenet.org<br/>\nForums: <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.orjans.se/alex/wurm/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.orjans.se/alex/wurm/</a><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7230, 1909, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Swedishphoenix - Mayor [ Digger , Smith (Specializes in: Blacksmithing, Armoursmithing), Miner ] Steffe - Co-mayor [ Carpenter , Lumberjack, Mason ( Reserve )] Swedishtiger - Citizen [Farmer, Carpenter ( Reserve ), Mason ( Reserve )] Rotab - Citizen [Jack of all Trades] Shaka - Citizen [Smith (Specializes in: Blacksmithing , Weaponsmithing), Carpenter ( Reserve )] Ganova - Citizen [ Currently inactive ] Moru - Citizen [Cook, Mason, Farmer, Chain armour smith] Ulfpain - Citizen [ Prospector , Coalmaker, Smith (Specializes in: Plate armour smithing)] Swecwurm - Writ-holder [ Only serves as an alt, holding the writs of the village. ] Soon-to-be Villagers Robfox - Elder [ Digger , Goldsmith, Carpenter , Lumberjack] Maloken - ? [ Digger ] Tosti - ? [ Miner , Chain armour smith] Bold text indicates achieved title in the skill/job.', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a> - Mayor [<b>Digger</b>, Smith (Specializes in: Blacksmithing, Armoursmithing), <b>Miner</b>]<br/>\nSteffe - Co-mayor [<b>Carpenter</b>, Lumberjack, Mason (<i>Reserve</i>)]<br/>\nSwedishtiger - Citizen [Farmer, Carpenter (<i>Reserve</i>), Mason (<i>Reserve</i>)]<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Rotab\" title=\"User:Rotab\">Rotab</a> - Citizen [Jack of all Trades]<br/>\nShaka - Citizen [Smith (Specializes in: <b>Blacksmithing</b>, Weaponsmithing), Carpenter (<i>Reserve</i>)]<br/>\nGanova - Citizen [<i>Currently inactive</i>]<br/>\nMoru - Citizen [Cook, Mason, Farmer, Chain armour smith]<br/>\nUlfpain - Citizen [<b>Prospector</b>, Coalmaker, Smith (Specializes in: Plate armour smithing)]<br/>\nSwecwurm - Writ-holder [<i>Only serves as an alt, holding the writs of the village.</i>]<br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Soon-to-be_Villagers\"><i>Soon-to-be Villagers</i></span></h3>\n<p>Robfox - Elder [<b>Digger</b>, Goldsmith, <b>Carpenter</b>, Lumberjack]<br/>\nMaloken - ? [<b>Digger</b>]<br/>\nTosti - ? [<b>Miner</b>, Chain armour smith]<br/>\n</p>\n<p><i>Bold text indicates achieved title in the skill/job.</i>\n</p>', 2),
(7231, 1909, 'Allies', 'Allies', 'Homesteads: Aurifex Ficis - Robfox Nangijala - Tegel Slottstradgarden - Maloken Villages : None', '<p><b>Homesteads:</b><br/>\n<i>Aurifex Ficis</i> - Robfox<br/>\n<i>Nangijala</i> - Tegel<br/>\n<i>Slottstradgarden</i> - Maloken<br/>\n</p>\n<p><b>Villages</b>:<br/>\n<i>None</i><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(7232, 1909, 'Enemies', 'Enemies', 'Enemy towns: None KOS list: Redmercury - Attacked Swedishphoenix \'s pet lion. Auras - Do I really have to explain why?', '<p><b>Enemy towns:</b><br/>\n<i>None<br/></i>\n</p>\n<p><b>KOS list:<br/></b>\n<i>Redmercury</i> - Attacked <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Swedishphoenix\" title=\"Player:Swedishphoenix\">Swedishphoenix</a>\'s pet lion.<br/>\n<i>Auras</i> - Do I really have to explain why?<br/>\n</p>', 4),
(7233, 1909, 'Resources', 'Resources', 'The Swec-village is located in the middle of two mineral zones, gold and iron. The Swec-village has 6 Iron Veins and 2 Gold Veins , all normal ql. Copper and zinc zones are not far from the village either. A 3x3 tar field is just at the beach of the village. Pine , birch and oak trees are plentyful in the forests. Clay is in 2 directions from the village, one very close and one a bit further away, towards Newtown.', '<p>The Swec-village is located in the middle of two mineral zones, gold and iron. The Swec-village has 6 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron_Vein\" title=\"Iron Vein\">Iron Veins</a> and 2 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gold_Vein\" title=\"Gold Vein\">Gold Veins</a>, all normal ql. <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_vein\" title=\"Copper vein\">Copper</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_vein\" title=\"Zinc vein\">zinc</a> zones are not far from the village either.<br/> \nA 3x3 <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a> field is just at the beach of the village.<br/> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pine\" title=\"Pine\">Pine</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Birch\" title=\"Birch\">birch</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">oak</a> trees are plentyful in the forests.<br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">Clay</a> is in 2 directions from the village, one very close and one a bit further away, towards Newtown.<br/>\n</p>', 5),
(7234, 1909, 'Town map', 'Town_map', '[ [1] ] Note: Because of the attack on upl.silentwhisper.net the town map cannot be viewed (the host is down). I still have the map though, and it will be updated and uploaded when I have time.', '<p>[<a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://files.upl.silentwhisper.net/upload5/by1.PNG\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>]<br/>\n<i>Note: Because of the attack on upl.silentwhisper.net the town map cannot be viewed (the host is down). I still have the map though, and it will be updated and uploaded when I have time.</i>\n</p>', 6),
(7235, 1909, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'On their way. For real this time. Interested in joining our village? Please sign up on the SweC-forums first (www.sweclockers.com) since we only accept members of SweC at this time.', '<p><i>On their way. For real this time.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/>\n<i>Interested in joining our village? Please sign up on the SweC-forums first (www.sweclockers.com) since we only accept members of SweC at this time.</i>\n</p>', 7),
(7237, 1911, 'The Lost Town', 'The_Lost_Town', 'Valley of cursed souls is a lost town, rumored to not have been discovered yet on the strange wild place that is libilas homeworld.\nPerhaps in a future it might ressurect to past glory.', '<p>Valley of cursed souls is a lost town, rumored to not have been discovered yet on the strange wild place that is libilas homeworld.\nPerhaps in a future it might ressurect to past glory.\n</p>\n<hr/>', 0),
(7238, 1912, 'OWNED BY DEVILS PEAK', 'OWNED_BY_DEVILS_PEAK', 'Mayor Sgmw', '<ul><li>Mayor Sgmw</li></ul>', 0),
(7239, 1912, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Leila And any other white lighter that wants to join.', '<ul><li>Leila</li></ul>\n<p>And any other white lighter that wants to join.\n</p>', 1),
(7240, 1912, 'Buildings', 'Buildings', 'The Sgmw\'s house - trader john', '<ul><li>The Sgmw\'s house - <a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">trader john</a></li></ul>', 2),
(7241, 1912, 'Location', 'Location', 'It is directly under the white light\nway to Newtown from White templars is about 2Km SSW', '<p>It is directly under the white light\nway to Newtown from White templars is about 2Km SSW\n</p>', 3),
(7242, 1912, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'COMING SOON!', '<p>COMING SOON!\n</p>', 4),
(7243, 1913, 'Location', 'Location', 'Tiergarden is located on the Wild Server, in proximity with the Isle of the White Dragon.\nNOTE: It no longer exists. It has now been disbanded.', '<p>Tiergarden is located on the Wild Server, in proximity with the Isle of the White Dragon.\nNOTE: It no longer exists. It has now been disbanded.\n</p>', 0),
(7244, 1913, 'History', 'History', 'Tiergardens location was found by Eddy, Telsist, Borny, and Seto; a few kilometers from Leersum and the white light. The Jenn-Kellon Tower was built with the help from all towns members and then the deed was planted. Although Tiergarden was founded in a prime location rich with resources, the invading black light forces had easy access to the location due to a road from Leersum leading to Tiergarden\'s front gate. After successfully defending against multiple BL raids, ranging in size from 3-7 attackers, the remaining citizens of Tiergarden decided it was necessary to leave Tiergarden and make residence off the beaten path to allow proper training in order to properly fight the Libilian menace. Tiergarden was sold to a fellow WL then disbanded a month later.', '<p>Tiergardens location was found by Eddy, Telsist, Borny, and Seto; a few kilometers from Leersum and the white light. The Jenn-Kellon Tower was built with the help from all towns members and then the deed was planted. Although Tiergarden was founded in a prime location rich with resources, the invading black light forces had easy access to the location due to a road from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leersum\" title=\"Leersum\">Leersum</a> leading to Tiergarden\'s front gate. After successfully defending against multiple BL raids, ranging in size from 3-7 attackers, the remaining citizens of Tiergarden decided it was necessary to leave Tiergarden and make residence off the beaten path to allow proper training in order to properly fight the Libilian menace.\n<br/><i>Tiergarden was sold to a fellow WL then disbanded a month later.</i>\n</p>', 1),
(7245, 1913, 'Current Members', 'Current_Members', 'None - disbanded', '<p>None - disbanded\n</p>', 2),
(7246, 1913, 'Previous Citizens', 'Previous_Citizens', 'Eddy Telsist Borny Seto Stuckey Ace Snappy Sempar Vark Zeus', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Eddy\" title=\"Player:Eddy\">Eddy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Telsist\" title=\"Player:Telsist\">Telsist</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Borny\" title=\"Player:Borny\">Borny</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Seto\" title=\"Player:Seto\">Seto</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Stuckey\" title=\"User:Stuckey\">Stuckey</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ace\" title=\"Player:Ace\">Ace</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Snappy\" title=\"Player:Snappy\">Snappy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Sempar\" title=\"Player:Sempar\">Sempar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Vark\" title=\"Player:Vark\">Vark</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeus\" title=\"Player:Zeus\">Zeus</a></li></ul>', 3),
(7247, 1913, 'Allies', 'Allies', 'Greater Havens Independent Settlers Sanctuary Isle Due to the selling of Tiergarden, these alliances may not be valid.', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Greater_Havens\" title=\"Greater Havens\">Greater Havens</a>\n<br/><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Independent_Settlers&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Independent Settlers (page does not exist)\">Independent Settlers</a>\n<br/>Sanctuary Isle\n<br/><i>Due to the selling of Tiergarden, these alliances may not be valid.</i>\n</p>', 4),
(7248, 1913, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'Tiergarden: White Dragon:', '<ul><li>Tiergarden:</li></ul>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm290uj9.jpg\" src=\"http://img175.imageshack.us/img175/4168/wurm290uj9.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>White Dragon:</li></ul>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm291kg6.jpg\" src=\"http://img175.imageshack.us/img175/1898/wurm291kg6.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 5),
(7249, 1917, 'Town Information', 'Town_Information', 'Founded by Planeteer on the day of Awakening in week 3 of the Snake\'s starfall in the year of 1001.', '<p>Founded by Planeteer on the day of Awakening in week 3 of the Snake\'s starfall in the year of 1001.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
