(7330, 1943, 'For sale', 'For_sale', 'Dirt We export many products. Ask us ingame and we\'ll try and organize a deal for you.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">Dirt</a></li>\n<li>We export many products. Ask us ingame and we\'ll try and organize a deal for you.</li></ul>', 4),
(7331, 1943, 'Animalkeep Farms', 'Animalkeep_Farms', 'Animalkeep is currently in the process of building a large farming complex. We are looking for seeds and animals to buy, so please contact us if you\'re willing to sell any!', '<p>Animalkeep is currently in the process of building a large farming complex. We are looking for seeds and animals to buy, so please contact us if you\'re willing to sell any!\n</p>', 5),
(7332, 1943, 'Animalkeep Contractors', 'Animalkeep_Contractors', 'We also source out labor - we\'re willing to work purely for food but pay is negotiable. Contact us ingame.', '<p>We also source out labor - we\'re willing to work purely for food but pay is negotiable. Contact us ingame.\n</p>', 6),
(7333, 1943, 'External links', 'External_links', 'Animalkeep website', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://animalkeep.webs.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">Animalkeep website</a></li></ul>', 7),
(7341, 1945, 'Description', 'Description', 'A size 10 village deed which existed during the summer of 2007. It was located far to the north of Newtown, connected by Public Highway . The village was founded by Cauthon , who provided all 100 silver coins for the deed, for members of the Penny Arcade forums. It is on a lake, affectionately called North Lake or Arcadian Lake, and had much more clay than it needed. After the people of Penny Arcade lost interest and the money ran out, the houses and items slowly rotted. Those who did not stop playing or who started playing months later can be found at Arcadia Bay or Mount Awesome.', '<p>A size 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village_deed\" title=\"Village deed\">village deed</a> which existed during the summer of 2007. It was located far to the north of Newtown, connected by Public <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">Highway</a>. The village was founded by <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Cauthon</a>, who provided all 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Silver_coin\" title=\"Silver coin\">silver coins</a> for the deed, for members of the Penny Arcade forums. It is on a lake, affectionately called North Lake or Arcadian Lake, and had much more <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> than it needed.\n</p>\n<p>After the people of Penny Arcade lost interest and the money ran out, the houses and items slowly rotted. Those who did not stop playing or who started playing months later can be found at <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arcadia_Bay\" title=\"Arcadia Bay\">Arcadia Bay</a> or Mount Awesome.\n</p>', 0),
(7342, 1945, 'People', 'People', 'Mayor Kazhiim Elders Thorgot - Head carpenter - Carpenter , former priest Infinity - Digger , Blacksmith , Farmer, Cook Jaedlyn - Hunter Loras - Smith Citizens Zanetheinsane - Founder of Mount Awesome - Excavator , Mason , Handyman , Lumberjack , Blacksmith teslas Zahrkon - Tower builder Akinos Arguss Arkis Baham Becoming Celethang Cycophant Darklyre Downer Draeven fallaxdraco Giacomo Griffball Grrn Ishallriseagain Iskatel Jothki KidDynamic LastAndroid Limitbreakerx Pil Rhesus Ryke SirCarcass Suriko Taliosfalcon Thatguybob Ursus Utsanomiko Vaen Webguy Wergalf Wombatpa Xinrius', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Kazhiim</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Thorgot\" title=\"Player:Thorgot\">Thorgot</a> - Head carpenter - <b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Carpenter\" title=\"Carpenter\">Carpenter</a></b>, former priest</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Infinity\" title=\"Player:Infinity\">Infinity</a> - <b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Digger\" title=\"Digger\">Digger</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Blacksmith\" title=\"Blacksmith\">Blacksmith</a></b>, Farmer, Cook</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jaedlyn\" title=\"Player:Jaedlyn\">Jaedlyn</a> - Hunter</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Loras\" title=\"Player:Loras\">Loras</a> - Smith</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zanetheinsane\" title=\"Player:Zanetheinsane\">Zanetheinsane</a> - Founder of Mount Awesome - <b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Excavator\" title=\"Excavator\">Excavator</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mason\" title=\"Mason\">Mason</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Handyman\" title=\"Handyman\">Handyman</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lumberjack\" title=\"Lumberjack\">Lumberjack</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Blacksmith\" title=\"Blacksmith\">Blacksmith</a></b></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Teslas\" title=\"Player:Teslas\">teslas</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zahrkon\" title=\"Player:Zahrkon\">Zahrkon</a> - Tower builder</li>\n<li>Akinos</li>\n<li>Arguss</li>\n<li>Arkis</li>\n<li>Baham</li>\n<li>Becoming</li>\n<li>Celethang</li>\n<li>Cycophant</li>\n<li>Darklyre</li>\n<li>Downer</li>\n<li>Draeven</li>\n<li>fallaxdraco</li>\n<li>Giacomo</li>\n<li>Griffball</li>\n<li>Grrn</li>\n<li>Ishallriseagain</li>\n<li>Iskatel</li>\n<li>Jothki</li>\n<li>KidDynamic</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:LastAndroid\" title=\"Player:LastAndroid\">LastAndroid</a></li>\n<li>Limitbreakerx</li>\n<li>Pil</li>\n<li>Rhesus</li>\n<li>Ryke</li>\n<li>SirCarcass</li>\n<li>Suriko</li>\n<li>Taliosfalcon</li>\n<li>Thatguybob</li>\n<li>Ursus</li>\n<li>Utsanomiko</li>\n<li>Vaen</li>\n<li>Webguy</li>\n<li>Wergalf</li>\n<li>Wombatpa</li>\n<li>Xinrius</li></ul>', 1),
(7343, 1945, 'Directions', 'Directions', 'Head north from Newtown over the land bridge across the lake. Follow the highway past Vean\'s place. The highway veers west. Turn right (north) on the highway instead of continuing west to Noriyah. Follow the road until you reach Arcadia.', '<p>Head north from Newtown over the land bridge across the lake. Follow the highway past Vean\'s place. The highway veers west. Turn right (north) on the highway instead of continuing west to Noriyah. Follow the road until you reach Arcadia.\n</p>', 2),
(7344, 1946, 'Description', 'Description', 'A size 5 village on an island, founded on July 3rd 2008 at 8:17 PM. Created by players of Arcadia , with much help from Mount Awesome. A current-ish list of tasks and related information can be found AB_todo|here.', '<p>A size 5 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village_deed\" title=\"Village deed\">village</a> on an island, founded on July 3rd 2008 at 8:17 PM. Created by players of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arcadia\" title=\"Arcadia\">Arcadia</a>, with much help from Mount Awesome.\n</p>\n<p>A current-ish list of tasks and related information can be found AB_todo|here.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(7345, 1946, 'People', 'People', 'Leaders Momarr Tamorlane Acting MoMayor Citizens Arcadia Momarr Tamorlane Stydracos Lepidopterist Low Activity / New Players / Gone But Not Forgotten Fonjo MIA Synold MIA Ferrat MIA Fanaticalist MIA LastAndroid Gone But Not Forgotten Rainadoo (Murderer) Incarcerated Darknigh Climbing the Mountain Mouserecoil Traitor Jeriktelorian KOS Is there a wildcard command for this thing?', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Leaders\">Leaders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Momarr\" title=\"Player:Momarr\">Momarr</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tamorlane\" title=\"Player:Tamorlane\">Tamorlane</a> Acting MoMayor</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Arcadia\" title=\"Player:Arcadia\">Arcadia</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Momarr\" title=\"Player:Momarr\">Momarr</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tamorlane\" title=\"Player:Tamorlane\">Tamorlane</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Stydracos\" title=\"Player:Stydracos\">Stydracos</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Lepidopterist</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Low_Activity_/_New_Players_/_Gone_But_Not_Forgotten\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Low_Activity_.2F_New_Players_.2F_Gone_But_Not_Forgotten\">Low Activity / New Players / Gone But Not Forgotten</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Fongo\" title=\"Player:Fongo\">Fonjo</a> MIA</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Synold</a> MIA</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Ferrat\" title=\"Player:Ferrat\">Ferrat</a> MIA</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Fanaticalist</a> MIA</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:LastAndroid\" title=\"Player:LastAndroid\">LastAndroid</a> Gone But Not Forgotten</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Rainadoo\" title=\"Player:Rainadoo\">Rainadoo</a> (Murderer) Incarcerated</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Darknigh\" title=\"Player:Darknigh\">Darknigh</a> Climbing the Mountain</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mouserecoil\" title=\"Player:Mouserecoil\">Mouserecoil</a> Traitor</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Jeriktelorian</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"KOS\">KOS</span></h3>\n<p>Is there a wildcard command for this thing?\n</p>', 1),
(7346, 1946, 'Directions', 'Directions', 'Southwest area of map, swim or sail south from Ahkenaten .', '<p>Southwest area of map, swim or sail south from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ahkenaten\" title=\"Ahkenaten\">Ahkenaten</a>.\n</p>', 2),
(7347, 1946, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Though Arcadia Bay is still very much a work in progress, we are happy to show some of what we have accomplished so far. Here is the heart of Arcadia Bay, where the deed is actually placed.  Citizens refer to this area as \"The Mound\": And another view: Southwest of the mound is our main source of crops, the Plantation: On the backside of our lake, you can see the Mound off to the north in a very picturesque setting: And finally, a view of the rapidly growing neighborhood southeast of the Mound where many of the citizens reside:', '<p>Though Arcadia Bay is still very much a work in progress, we are happy to show some of what we have accomplished so far.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nHere is the heart of Arcadia Bay, where the deed is actually placed.  Citizens refer to this area as \"The Mound\":\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"mound1.png\" src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v521/bigdookie/mound1.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nAnd another view:\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"mound2.png\" src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v521/bigdookie/mound2.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nSouthwest of the mound is our main source of crops, the Plantation:\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"plantrear.png\" src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v521/bigdookie/plantrear.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nOn the backside of our lake, you can see the Mound off to the north in a very picturesque setting:\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"lake.png\" src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v521/bigdookie/lake.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nAnd finally, a view of the rapidly growing neighborhood southeast of the Mound where many of the citizens reside:\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"eastside.png\" src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v521/bigdookie/eastside.png\"/>\n</p>', 3),
(7348, 1947, 'History', 'History', 'Once upon a time, a small band of warriors, Agrue , The Lord Templar , and Gunner joined the ranks of the ancient island fortress of Saint Minas . Instantly recognizing its insolence and feeble nature, they destroyed Saint Minas and convinced its followers to leave the tyrannical grip Fullkontact had held over the beautiful city. They moved to West island to ensure the tyrant Fullkontact would never return again, and to contain the evil to Aeldell , a word meaning \"Prison of great evils\" in the ancient tongue.', '<p>Once upon a time, a small band of warriors, <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Agrue</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Lordtemplar\" title=\"Player:Lordtemplar\">The Lord Templar</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Gunner\" title=\"Player:Gunner\">Gunner</a> joined the ranks of the ancient island fortress of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Saint_Minas\" title=\"Saint Minas\">Saint Minas</a>. Instantly recognizing its insolence and feeble nature, they destroyed Saint Minas and convinced its followers to leave the tyrannical grip <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Fullkontact\" title=\"Player:Fullkontact\">Fullkontact</a> had held over the beautiful city. They moved to West island to ensure the tyrant Fullkontact would never return again, and to contain the evil to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Aeldell\" title=\"Aeldell\">Aeldell</a>, a word meaning \"Prison of great evils\" in the ancient tongue.\n</p>', 0),
(7349, 1947, 'Recruitment', 'Recruitment', 'If you can make it here, you\'re in. We\'re currently recruiting.\nFor more information, visit http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=2964.0', '<p>If you can make it here, you\'re in. We\'re currently recruiting.\nFor more information, visit <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=2964.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=2964.0</a>\n</p>', 1),
(7350, 1947, 'Alliances', 'Alliances', 'If you wish to become an ally, talk to Lord Templar or Gunner.', '<p>If you wish to become an ally, talk to Lord Templar or Gunner.\n</p>', 2),
(7351, 1947, 'People', 'People', 'Mayors of Azarad\'s Hold Lord Templar Gunner Citizens of Azarad\'s Hold Azmodeus Babygirl Bernhardo Fukajin Huntar Raoth Ember Nell', '<h3><span id=\"Mayors_of_Azarad\'s_Hold\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayors_of_Azarad.27s_Hold\">Mayors of Azarad\'s Hold</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Lordtemplar\" title=\"Player:Lordtemplar\">Lord Templar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Gunner\" title=\"Player:Gunner\">Gunner</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Citizens_of_Azarad\'s_Hold\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens_of_Azarad.27s_Hold\">Citizens of Azarad\'s Hold</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Azmodeus</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Babygirl</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Bernhardo\" title=\"Player:Bernhardo\">Bernhardo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Fukajin</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Huntar\" title=\"Player:Huntar\">Huntar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Raoth</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Ember\" title=\"Player:Ember\">Ember</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Nell\" title=\"Player:Nell\">Nell</a></li></ul>', 3),
(7352, 1947, 'External links', 'External_links', 'Azarad Hold\'s Current Progress Village Recruit Thread', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://noxhub.net/templar/wurm/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Azarad Hold\'s Current Progress</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=2964.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Village Recruit Thread</a></li></ul>', 4),
(7353, 1948, 'History of BoS', 'History_of_BoS', 'As remembered by the inhabitants. The story of BoS actually starts without any of its current members, with a fellow by the name Amader. He, in turn, attracted Solver to the game and Einnel, Daash, Theacke, Madboy, Rmt and Tottman were soon to follow. The site where we all settled down was dubbed Wolf Hill (first incarnation), due to the frequency of said lupine at the site, even though it was too close to Serenity Port for an actual deed to be planted without permission. We asked for that from the Serenity Port mayor, but were rudely denied and so eventually we packed up and left for other lands. Amader, together with his RL friend Madonna, went separate ways from the rest of us and settled in the far north while the rest of us finally found ourselves at a tranquil bay in the south, approximately SSW of Mesa Verde, where we settled down and founded the Bay of Swedes in December 2007. Bay of Swedes (second incarnation) was the name of our community, as most of us wanted their own homestead deed and founded them separately. With time, our reputation on the Home server grew and our gathering became widely known. During this time some of our members stopped playing, but most remained. Several ambitious projects were attempted, and some even completed ;), and by the end of its time the bay had been transformed into a lush park of walkways, flower fields and oak tree groves. Supplies of Champ enchanted tools and iron lumps in QL70-95 were never a problem with the close connections we had with others (for example Udgaard). It was not ruled by a single individual, such as a mayor, but instead held together by a sense of friendship and camaraderie. The founders where Daash , Einnel , Gustavl, Lillmad , Madboy , Rmt , Solver , Theacke and Tottman . They regularly came together to work on larger projects. The members started out with the thought of independent places in the bay. Before the KvK raid where implemented most members of BoS had some kind of deed. Villages size 5( Kendra : Solver and Oppboga: Madboy ). Homestead size 5(Arboga: Tottman , Fellingsbro:Minimad, Guldsmedshyttan : Rmt , Magrathea: Daash and Nora:Aske).  One decided to stay undeeded(Einnels mansion: Einnel ). When Rolf implemented KvK raids, we realized that none of the deeds were suited for defense since they were built to have easy access and look good. Instead of demolishing and rebuilding all the deeds we joined forces in founding a new size 10 village and naming it Fort BoS. From an Island of 5x6 tiles it was enlarged into a 19x19 tiles flat area. We then built a tower in the middle and Ql80 walls around the edge. With no land bridge, boats became our transportation between main land and the island. One week before the freedom server opened, the remaining members each packed a boat and traveled south. We made camp on an island on the outskirts of the map waiting for the border to open. On opening day we all set sail looking for a new place to plant the BoS concept. We found an island suitable for our needs, and named it BoS Island BoS Featured A Colossus looking down on the bay. Highway leading directly to NT. It was considered a public 2-tile cobblestone road with gravel on the sides, completely free from towers. A nice looking port with docks for both large and small ships/boats. All roads in BoS were 2 or 3-tile wide, but these, unlike the NT road, were NOT public roads . Most of the settlements were close to water and encompassed the complete coastline of the bay. It had all the regular convenient resources available, such as clay, peat and ores. BoS Allies Mesa Verde - Lilbear Aegis - Riverboy Tenakill - Asidecay and Becket Udgaard - Mith , Anthon (main supplier of iron and rock shards)', '<p>As remembered by the inhabitants. \n</p>\n<p>The story of BoS actually starts without any of its current members, with a fellow by the name Amader. He, in turn, attracted Solver to the game and Einnel, Daash, Theacke, Madboy, Rmt and Tottman were soon to follow. The site where we all settled down was dubbed Wolf Hill (first incarnation), due to the frequency of said lupine at the site, even though it was too close to Serenity Port for an actual deed to be planted without permission. We asked for that from the Serenity Port mayor, but were rudely denied and so eventually we packed up and left for other lands. \n</p>\n<p>Amader, together with his RL friend Madonna, went separate ways from the rest of us and settled in the far north while the rest of us finally found ourselves at a tranquil bay in the south, approximately SSW of Mesa Verde, where we settled down and founded the Bay of Swedes in December 2007. \n</p>\n<p>Bay of Swedes (second incarnation) was the name of our community, as most of us wanted their own homestead deed and founded them separately. With time, our reputation on the Home server grew and our gathering became widely known. During this time some of our members stopped playing, but most remained. Several ambitious projects were attempted, and some even completed ;), and by the end of its time the bay had been transformed into a lush park of walkways, flower fields and oak tree groves. Supplies of Champ enchanted tools and iron lumps in QL70-95 were never a problem with the close connections we had with others (for example Udgaard). \n</p>\n<p><br/>\nIt was not ruled by a single individual, such as a mayor, but instead held together by a sense of friendship and camaraderie. The founders where <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daash\" title=\"Player:Daash\">Daash</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Einnel\" title=\"Player:Einnel\">Einnel</a>, Gustavl, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Lillmad\" title=\"Player:Lillmad\">Lillmad</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Madboy\" title=\"Player:Madboy\">Madboy</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Rmt\" title=\"Player:Rmt\">Rmt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Solver\" title=\"Player:Solver\">Solver</a>, Theacke and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tottman\" title=\"Player:Tottman\">Tottman</a>. They regularly came together to work on larger projects.  \n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe members started out with the thought of independent places in the bay. Before the KvK raid where implemented most members of BoS had some kind of deed. Villages size 5(<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Kendra\" title=\"Kendra\">Kendra</a>:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Solver\" title=\"Player:Solver\">Solver</a> and Oppboga:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Madboy\" title=\"Player:Madboy\">Madboy</a>). Homestead size 5(Arboga:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tottman\" title=\"Player:Tottman\">Tottman</a>, Fellingsbro:Minimad, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Guldsmedshyttan\" title=\"Guldsmedshyttan\">Guldsmedshyttan</a>:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Rmt\" title=\"Player:Rmt\">Rmt</a>, Magrathea:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daash\" title=\"Player:Daash\">Daash</a> and Nora:Aske).  One decided to stay undeeded(Einnels mansion:<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Einnel\" title=\"Player:Einnel\">Einnel</a>). \n</p>\n<p><br/>\nWhen Rolf implemented KvK raids, we realized that none of the deeds were suited for defense since they were built to have easy access and look good. Instead of demolishing and rebuilding all the deeds we joined forces in founding a new size 10 village and naming it Fort BoS. From an Island of 5x6 tiles it was enlarged into a 19x19 tiles flat area. We then built a tower in the middle and Ql80 walls around the edge. With no land bridge, boats became our transportation between main land and the island.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nOne week before the freedom server opened, the remaining members each packed a boat and traveled south. We made camp on an island on the outskirts of the map waiting for the border to open. On opening day we all set sail looking for a new place to plant the BoS concept. We found an island suitable for our needs, and named it <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/BoS_Island\" title=\"BoS Island\">BoS Island</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"BoS_Featured\">BoS Featured</span></h3>\n<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">Colossus</a> looking down on the bay.</li>\n<li>Highway leading directly to NT. It was considered a public 2-tile cobblestone road with gravel on the sides, completely free from towers.</li>\n<li>A nice looking port with docks for both large and small ships/boats.</li>\n<li>All roads in BoS were 2 or 3-tile wide, but these, unlike the NT road, were <b>NOT public roads</b>.</li>\n<li>Most of the settlements were close to water and encompassed the complete coastline of the bay.</li>\n<li>It had all the regular convenient resources available, such as clay, peat and ores.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"BoS_Allies\">BoS Allies</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Mesa Verde - Lilbear</li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Aegis&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Aegis (page does not exist)\">Aegis</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Riverboy\" title=\"Player:Riverboy\">Riverboy</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tenakill\" title=\"Tenakill\">Tenakill</a> - <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Asidecay\" title=\"Player:Asidecay\">Asidecay</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Becket\" title=\"Player:Becket\">Becket</a></li>\n<li>Udgaard - <a href=\"/index.php/User:Mith\" title=\"User:Mith\">Mith</a>, Anthon (main supplier of iron and rock shards)</li></ul>', 0),
(7356, 1950, 'Past Citizens/Guests', 'Past_Citizens.2FGuests', 'Citizens Anayyatta Letac Baalel Goppend MattyK Cannonfodder Desoan Artiph Drazak Spyeddie (Was Anayyatta\'s son\'s account.) Kamie Dragonhead Guests Glass Nayballs Naturesown Internetdude Ulviirala', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens_2\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Anayyatta</li>\n<li>Letac</li>\n<li>Baalel</li>\n<li>Goppend</li>\n<li>MattyK</li>\n<li>Cannonfodder</li>\n<li>Desoan</li>\n<li>Artiph</li>\n<li>Drazak</li>\n<li>Spyeddie <i> (Was Anayyatta\'s son\'s account.) </i></li>\n<li>Kamie</li>\n<li>Dragonhead</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Guests\">Guests</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Glass</li>\n<li>Nayballs</li>\n<li>Naturesown</li>\n<li>Internetdude</li>\n<li>Ulviirala</li></ul>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(7357, 1950, 'Alts', 'Alts', 'Benie - Alt of Misterangry. Bennie - Alt of Misterangry. Benietwo - Alt of Misterangry. Ctrlaltdelete - Alt of Misterangry. Holds the deed for the Shipyard. Priest of Vynora . Mrangry - Alt of Misterangry. Spyeddie - Alt of Anayyatta. Panoramia Shipyard', '<ul><li>Benie - Alt of Misterangry.</li>\n<li>Bennie - Alt of Misterangry.</li>\n<li>Benietwo - Alt of Misterangry.</li>\n<li>Ctrlaltdelete - Alt of Misterangry. Holds the deed for the Shipyard. Priest of <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>.</li>\n<li>Mrangry - Alt of Misterangry.</li>\n<li>Spyeddie - Alt of Anayyatta.</li></ul>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Panoramia\">Panoramia</span></h1>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://benniebay.beniesbuilds.com/shipyardpanoramia.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\">Shipyard</a>\n</p>', 1),
(7364, 1954, 'About', 'About', 'Founded and maintained by Maluraq.  Previously known as [Maluraq\'s Hideoutw] (the \'w\' was a typo). Ethario of [Woodlands Hunting] very helpfully maintained the property in between deeds.', '<p>Founded and maintained by Maluraq.  Previously known as [Maluraq\'s Hideoutw] (the \'w\' was a typo).\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Ethario\" title=\"Player:Ethario\">Ethario</a> of [Woodlands Hunting] very helpfully maintained the property in between deeds.\n</p>', 0),
(7365, 1954, 'Visitors', 'Visitors', 'Visitors are welcome and beds can be rented if desired.  Much prime hunting ground on steppe and in forested areas available nearby.', '<p>Visitors are welcome and beds can be rented if desired.  Much prime hunting ground on steppe and in forested areas available nearby.\n</p>', 1),
(7366, 1954, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Location is well-landscaped and can support additional players should they wish to assist in costs of upgrading to village status.', '<p>Location is well-landscaped and can support additional players should they wish to assist in costs of upgrading to village status.\n</p>', 2),
(7367, 1954, 'Layout', 'Layout', 'Special thanks to the mapper tool .', '<p><img alt=\"cedarhillmonastery_local.png\" src=\"http://mikebabcock.ca/gaming/wurmonline/cedarhillmonastery_local.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p>Special thanks to the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jenn001.game.wurmonline.com/mapper/map.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">mapper tool</a>.\n</p>', 3),
(7368, 1954, 'Directions', 'Directions', 'Contact me in-game for directions if you\'d like to visit', '<p>Contact me in-game for directions if you\'d like to visit\n</p>', 4),
(7369, 1955, 'Disbanded', 'Disbanded', 'Chalice was disbanded on April 9th 2009 due to the Village not being intended to face KVK concerns. Due to the vulnerable village design it was decided that it was not worth the effort of altering the area for defense.', '<p>Chalice was disbanded on April 9th 2009 due to the Village not being intended to face KVK concerns. Due to the vulnerable village design it was decided that it was not worth the effort of altering the area for defense. \n</p>', 0),
(7370, 1955, 'Existance', 'Existance', 'The concept of Chalice is of an open and casual feeling village design while maintaining a high degree of symmetry. Using the Mapper I was able to plan the basic idea fairly easily. Creating three tiers starting at water level and raising up to xx at its top level the village provides a tidy example of what can be done with terraforming while still utilizing the space efficiently. The name is a reference to a sphere of magic (the chalice of osiomax) created for use in the aD&D tabletop rpg and the building names reflect the general concepts of this. In this case visitors may find the names a bit strange which may add a sense of mystery to the town. The village itself is not inhabited by villagers though visitors may use beds in the inn and two guests houses provide beds for those that come to assist with deed construction or local projects. With this in mind the only citizens on the deed are Sppt and Raidsoft(and his priest alt Dynok) along with the deed holder Levex(alt of Levedara). Also citizens are Wossoo and Miggy though they are primarily residents of the wild server city of Kyara . None of these project members however live on the deed full time. 1 Depths - Stone - Boat house, storing construction items relevant to shipbuilding. 2 Oblivion - Stone - The Inn which holds 6 beds priced at 25i to rent. 3 The Chalice - Wood - Central storage and Private trader. 4 Devour - Wood - Cookhouse and Cloth tailoring. 5 Division - Stone - Merchant building. 6 Fallacies - Stone - Alchemy and Leather working shop. 7 Voidforge - Wood - Smithy & Carpentry storage. 8 Hole in the Wall - Wood - Guesthouse complete with bed & private yard. 9 Void in the Space - Wood - Guesthouse complete with bed & private yard. 10 Throne - Stone - Mansion complete with bed, dining arrangement, personal work spaces and balcony. 11 Mantle - Stone - Mansion complete with bed, dining arrangement, personal work spaces and balcony.', '<p>The concept of Chalice is of an open and casual feeling village design while maintaining a high degree of symmetry. Using the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tools\" title=\"Tools\">Mapper</a> I was able to plan the basic idea fairly easily. Creating three tiers starting at water level and raising up to xx at its top level the village provides a tidy example of what can be done with terraforming while still utilizing the space efficiently. \n</p>\n<p>The name is a reference to a sphere of magic (the chalice of osiomax) created for use in the aD&amp;D tabletop rpg and the building names reflect the general concepts of this. In this case visitors may find the names a bit strange which may add a sense of mystery to the town. The village itself is not inhabited by villagers though visitors may use beds in the inn and two guests houses provide beds for those that come to assist with deed construction or local projects. With this in mind the only citizens on the deed are Sppt and Raidsoft(and his priest alt Dynok) along with the deed holder Levex(alt of Levedara). Also citizens are Wossoo and Miggy though they are primarily residents of the wild server city of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Kyara\" title=\"Kyara\">Kyara</a>. None of these project members however live on the deed full time. \n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"chalicelayout.jpg\" src=\"http://draconicspires.com/wurm/chalicelayout.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>1 Depths - Stone - Boat house, storing construction items relevant to shipbuilding.</li>\n<li>2 Oblivion - Stone - The Inn which holds 6 beds priced at 25i to rent.</li>\n<li>3 The Chalice - Wood - Central storage and Private trader.</li>\n<li>4 Devour - Wood - Cookhouse and Cloth tailoring.</li>\n<li>5 Division - Stone - Merchant building.</li>\n<li>6 Fallacies - Stone - Alchemy and Leather working shop.</li>\n<li>7 Voidforge - Wood - Smithy &amp; Carpentry storage.</li>\n<li>8 Hole in the Wall - Wood - Guesthouse complete with bed &amp; private yard.</li>\n<li>9 Void in the Space - Wood - Guesthouse complete with bed &amp; private yard.</li>\n<li>10 Throne - Stone - Mansion complete with bed, dining arrangement, personal work spaces and balcony.</li>\n<li>11 Mantle - Stone - Mansion complete with bed, dining arrangement, personal work spaces and balcony.</li></ul>', 1),
(7371, 1955, 'Location', 'Location', 'Chalice is approximate 1 hour and 15 minutes walk/swim from Newtown if one chooses a good route. This is much hastened if one owns a boat and docks on the western shore. Close to its north western corner is the homestead of Among the Hills, owned by Martinus and to the South across the lake is Norgarde, a homestead owned by Starshaker. Extrusion has planted his own size 5 homestead, Semper Fidelis to the South West, and created the following local area map.', '<p>Chalice is approximate 1 hour and 15 minutes walk/swim from Newtown if one chooses a good route. This is much hastened if one owns a boat and docks on the western shore. Close to its north western corner is the homestead of Among the Hills, owned by Martinus and to the South across the lake is Norgarde, a homestead owned by Starshaker. Extrusion has planted his own size 5 homestead, Semper Fidelis to the South West, and created the following local area map.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"chalicelocal.jpg\" src=\"http://draconicspires.com/wurm/images/chalicelocal.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 2),
(7372, 1955, 'Contributors', 'Contributors', 'Levedara - Deed owner, primary designer. General terraforming and construction. Raidsoft - General design help, Terraforming & Construction. Rockcliff - Tool donations, crop donations & food - Special thanks to Uzetaab , Annette & Keyos . Dashiva - Food & Basic tools. Martinus - Digging, dirt delivery & general building supplies. Trinexx - Digging. Miggy - Carpentry, floorboards, and building supplies. Thorgot - Carpentry, boat supplies and floorboards. Sppt - Masonry and general construction.', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:LeveDara\" title=\"User:LeveDara\">Levedara</a> - Deed owner, primary designer. General terraforming and construction.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Raidsoft\" title=\"Player:Raidsoft\">Raidsoft</a> - General design help, Terraforming &amp; Construction.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rockcliff\" title=\"Rockcliff\">Rockcliff</a> - Tool donations, crop donations &amp; food - Special thanks to <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Uzetaab\" title=\"Player:Uzetaab\">Uzetaab</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Annette\" title=\"Player:Annette\">Annette</a> &amp; <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Keyos\" title=\"Player:Keyos\">Keyos</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Dashiva\" title=\"Player:Dashiva\">Dashiva</a> - Food &amp; Basic tools.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Martinus</a> - Digging, dirt delivery &amp; general building supplies.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Trinexx\" title=\"Player:Trinexx\">Trinexx</a> - Digging.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Miggy\" title=\"Player:Miggy\">Miggy</a> - Carpentry, floorboards, and building supplies.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Thorgot\" title=\"Player:Thorgot\">Thorgot</a> - Carpentry, boat supplies and floorboards.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Sppt\" title=\"Player:Sppt\">Sppt</a> - Masonry and general construction.</li></ul>', 3),
(7373, 1955, 'Allied with', 'Allied_with', 'Rockcliff', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rockcliff\" title=\"Rockcliff\">Rockcliff</a></li></ul>', 4),
(7374, 1956, 'Where On The Map Are We?', 'Where_On_The_Map_Are_We.3F', 'We are on the north coast. Here\'s a map', '<p>We are on the north coast. Here\'s a map\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"rawrzmappz.jpg\" src=\"http://i21.photobucket.com/albums/b291/overkill2005/rawrzmappz.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 0),
(7375, 1956, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Overkill (Miner,Mason,Digger,Handyman,Lumberjack)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Overkill\" title=\"Player:Overkill\">Overkill</a> <b>(Miner,Mason,Digger,Handyman,Lumberjack)</b></li></ul>', 1),
(7376, 1956, 'Elders', 'Elders', 'Prokiller', '<ul><li>Prokiller</li></ul>', 2),
(7377, 1956, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Codom (Priest) Ols Ilyana Namelesscake Roflkittens Verlix', '<ul><li>Codom (Priest)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ols\" title=\"Player:Ols\">Ols</a></li>\n<li>Ilyana</li>\n<li>Namelesscake</li>\n<li>Roflkittens</li>\n<li>Verlix</li></ul>', 3),
(7378, 1956, 'Allied with', 'Allied_with', 'Iron\'s Paradise Common Denominator Farmstead Bake Sale Common Denominator Seaport', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron%27s_Paradise\" title=\"Iron\'s Paradise\">Iron\'s Paradise</a></li>\n<li>Common Denominator Farmstead Bake Sale</li>\n<li>Common Denominator Seaport</li></ul>', 4),
(7379, 1956, 'Enemies', 'Enemies', 'Phoenix Enterprises', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Phoenix_Enterprises\" title=\"Phoenix Enterprises\">Phoenix Enterprises</a></li></ul>', 5),
(7380, 1957, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'A size 10 village along the northern west coast. It is west of Garden of Gods near Oakvale a bit north.', '<p>A size 10 village along the northern west coast. It is west of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Garden_of_Gods\" title=\"Garden of Gods\">Garden of Gods</a> near Oakvale a bit north.\n</p>', 0),
(7381, 1957, 'Inhabitants', 'Inhabitants', 'Elders Citizens', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>', 1),
(7382, 1957, 'Additional Info', 'Additional_Info', '\"Copperblazes is not recruiting at the moment.\" - Delamore', '<p>\"Copperblazes is not recruiting at the moment.\" - Delamore\n</p>', 2),
(7383, 1959, 'History', 'History', 'The village farms were originally leveled and fenced by Crossbow, who had an undeeded house and workshop in the valley.  He was assisted by Bikerduck and Iambob, from the early Oakvale holding just south of Aegis.  Crossbow also opened a moderate sized mine with zinc and iron veins, and most critically, access to the water table.  He also planted groves of birch, maple, and olives in the hollow west of the farm, as well as a mixed herb garden closer to his buildings.  When Crossbow left Wurm, he gave his buildings and farmlands to Urman who had maintained the areas during several long absences.  After he left, Crossbow’s buildings were replaced and the new buildings were labeled “Crossbow Farms” in recognition of his lasting efforts. Urman expanded the stone-fenced farmlands, and planted and fenced extensive tree farms.  He also improved the paths leading to the north (to Aegis) and east (to an area known as Miller’s Tower and to Newtown), with well graded paved roads.  The roads have a distinctive pattern of 4 cobble tiles and 1 gravel tile for visibility.  Most of the paths were bordered with camellia bushes for the alchemy ingredients.  Urman also built a guard tower to protect the bottom of the valley. The deed that is currently at Crossbow Farms was originally placed by Larken at the village of Forest’s Edge, which was about 90 tiles south of the current farm.  Forest’s Edge included Larken, his wife Stcheryl, and a few friends.  When Stcheryl became disinterested in Wurm, Urman bought the village from Larken, who moved further into the wilderness and eventually moved to Wild.  When creature spawns were introduced, a crocodile spawn appeared on the deeded area at Forest Edge.  No one lived at the village, but it was used as a local chat channel.  The deed was pulled from Forest Edge and placed at Crossbow Farms during the amnesty when the Mol Rehan home server was opened.', '<p>The village farms were originally leveled and fenced by Crossbow, who had an undeeded house and workshop in the valley.  He was assisted by Bikerduck and Iambob, from the early Oakvale holding just south of Aegis.  Crossbow also opened a moderate sized mine with zinc and iron veins, and most critically, access to the water table.  He also planted groves of birch, maple, and olives in the hollow west of the farm, as well as a mixed herb garden closer to his buildings.  When Crossbow left Wurm, he gave his buildings and farmlands to Urman who had maintained the areas during several long absences.  After he left, Crossbow’s buildings were replaced and the new buildings were labeled “Crossbow Farms” in recognition of his lasting efforts.\n</p>\n<p>Urman expanded the stone-fenced farmlands, and planted and fenced extensive tree farms.  He also improved the paths leading to the north (to Aegis) and east (to an area known as Miller’s Tower and to Newtown), with well graded paved roads.  The roads have a distinctive pattern of 4 cobble tiles and 1 gravel tile for visibility.  Most of the paths were bordered with camellia bushes for the alchemy ingredients.  Urman also built a guard tower to protect the bottom of the valley.  \n</p>\n<p>The deed that is currently at Crossbow Farms was originally placed by Larken at the village of Forest’s Edge, which was about 90 tiles south of the current farm.  Forest’s Edge included Larken, his wife Stcheryl, and a few friends.  When Stcheryl became disinterested in Wurm, Urman bought the village from Larken, who moved further into the wilderness and eventually moved to Wild.  When creature spawns were introduced, a crocodile spawn appeared on the deeded area at Forest Edge.  No one lived at the village, but it was used as a local chat channel.  The deed was pulled from Forest Edge and placed at Crossbow Farms during the amnesty when the Mol Rehan home server was opened.\n</p>', 0),
(7384, 1959, 'Members', 'Members', 'Urman - Ally and Owner', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Urman\" title=\"Player:Urman\">Urman</a> - Ally and Owner</li></ul>', 1),
(7385, 1960, 'Notice: Under Construction!', 'Notice:_Under_Construction.21', 'Notice This section is currently under construction Read more on the current events page', '<div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Important_Icon.png\"><img alt=\"Important Icon.png\" data-file-height=\"64\" data-file-width=\"64\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"50\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/13/Important_Icon.png/50px-Important_Icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/1/13/Important_Icon.png 1.5x\" width=\"50\"/></a></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"\">\n</span></h3>\n<p>Notice This section is currently under construction\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<small><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Current_events\" title=\"Current events\">Read more on the current events page</a></small>\n</p>', 0),
(7386, 1960, 'Description', 'Description', 'At moment Crystal Cove is saving up for a size 10 village Villagers #Deyrka\n     #Drenx\n     #Davieg\n     #Dave\n     #NavyDT\n     #Walkerboh\n     #Anonymousbro\n     #Retha', '<p>At moment Crystal Cove is saving up for a size 10 village\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Villagers\">Villagers</span></h3>\n<pre>     #Deyrka\n     #Drenx\n     #Davieg\n     #Dave\n     #NavyDT\n     #Walkerboh\n     #Anonymousbro\n     #Retha\n</pre>', 1),
(7387, 1961, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'Cydonia is a group of adventurers who love to have fun it\'s as simple as that. Our village is located on an isle at the southernmost regions of wurm. Our village is settled in a small cove where we have plenty of resources, including peat not 20 tiles behind the village.', '<p>Cydonia is a group of adventurers who love to have fun it\'s as simple as that.\n</p>\n<p>Our village is located on an isle at the southernmost regions of wurm. Our village is settled in a small cove where we have plenty of resources, including peat not 20 tiles behind the village.\n</p>', 0),
(7388, 1961, 'Rules', 'Rules', 'These are our village rules which everyone must abide by. Stealing from anyone weather it be a new player or someone you hate is strictly prohibited and will result in banishment. No fighting with other players unless we are at war or they attack you first. Other than that just have fun, it\'s a game.', '<p>These are our village rules which everyone must abide by.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Stealing from anyone weather it be a new player or someone you hate is strictly prohibited and will result in banishment.</li>\n<li>No fighting with other players unless we are at war or they attack you first.</li></ul>\n<p>Other than that just have fun, it\'s a game.\n</p>', 1),
(7389, 1961, 'Ranking', 'Ranking', 'Our ranking system is quite simple. There is the elder council who are the leaders of our village. Then there are knights that are our citizens. And lastly there are our squires, who are new players to the village who havn\'t gained our trust entirely.', '<p>Our ranking system is quite simple. There is the elder council who are the leaders of our village. Then there are knights that are our citizens. And lastly there are our squires, who are new players to the village who havn\'t gained our trust entirely.\n</p>', 2),
(7390, 1961, 'Cydonians', 'Cydonians', 'Elder Council Syrinx (Fighter / Mason / Leatherworker) Knights Themesticles (Vynorian Priest) Squires', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elder_Council\">Elder Council</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Syrinx\" title=\"Player:Syrinx\">Syrinx</a> (Fighter / Mason / Leatherworker)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Knights\">Knights</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Themesticles</a> (Vynorian Priest)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Squires\">Squires</span></h3>', 3),
(7391, 1961, 'We are recruiting', 'We_are_recruiting', 'If you would like to join the ranks of Cydonia please private message Syrinx in game or on the fourms.', '<p>If you would like to join the ranks of Cydonia please private message Syrinx in game or on the fourms.\n</p>', 4),
(7392, 1962, 'History', 'History', 'Daevon has been found 25 January 2009.', '<p>Daevon has been found 25 January 2009.\n</p>', 0),
(7393, 1962, 'News', 'News', 'We Search for people who want to join us. We offer 2x3 or 2x2 house (you decide), nice steppe, clay and sand close, exotic tree and bushes and nice community.', '<p>We Search for people who want to join us. We offer 2x3 or 2x2 house (you decide), nice steppe, clay and sand close, exotic tree and bushes and nice community.\n</p>', 1),
(7394, 1962, 'People', 'People', 'Mayors Polan - King Cookier Danypos - Lord Cookie  co-mayor Citizens Wertiumx - Citizen Alts Cookiemonster - priest alt', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayors\">Mayors</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Polan\" title=\"Player:Polan\">Polan</a> - King Cookier</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Danypos\" title=\"Player:Danypos\">Danypos</a> - Lord Cookie  co-mayor</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Wertiumx</a> - Citizen</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alts\">Alts</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Cookiemonster - priest alt</li></ul>', 2),
(7395, 1963, 'Anyone', 'Anyone', 'Collect any discarded tools and items on the ground and place in the Storage Shed, please try to combine same items such as wood scraps into about 20kg to 30kg pieces for future fuel for ovens and forges. Think of things to add to this list.', '<ul><li>Collect any discarded tools and items on the ground and place in the Storage Shed, please try to combine same items such as wood scraps into about 20kg to 30kg pieces for future fuel for ovens and forges.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Think of things to add to this list.</li></ul>', 0),
(7396, 1963, 'Carpentry', 'Carpentry', 'Make planks and store them into the storage shed, DO NOT PLACE THEM INTO YOUR HOUSE LOCKED UP!! Repair any house walls and fences.', '<ul><li>Make planks and store them into the storage shed,<b>DO NOT PLACE THEM INTO YOUR HOUSE LOCKED UP!!</b></li>\n<li>Repair any house walls and fences.</li></ul>', 1),
(7397, 1963, 'Digging', 'Digging', 'Keep terraforming the land east. create flat land and easy to walk up ramps.', '<ul><li>Keep terraforming the land east. create flat land and easy to walk up ramps.</li></ul>', 2),
(7398, 1963, 'Healing and First Aid', 'Healing_and_First_Aid', 'Needs more information on were items are.', '<ul><li>Needs more information on were items are.</li></ul>', 3),
(7399, 1963, 'Kitchen/Food', 'Kitchen.2FFood', 'We need new cooks to help lesson the load. Meals are great, but casseroles help too. The kitchen needs the following items: Meat (fish), vegetables, foraged items, kindling, and scraps or logs for burning. Also pottery items if anyone wants to do that.', '<ul><li>We need new cooks to help lesson the load. Meals are great, but casseroles help too.</li></ul>\n<p>The kitchen needs the following items: Meat (fish), vegetables, foraged items, kindling, and scraps or logs for burning.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Also pottery items if anyone wants to do that.</li></ul>', 4),
(7400, 1963, 'Masonry', 'Masonry', 'Repair any stone fences. Make slabs out of decaying shards. Make bricks. Lots and Lots of Bricks, place them in the shed.', '<ul><li>Repair any stone fences.</li>\n<li>Make slabs out of decaying shards.</li>\n<li>Make bricks. Lots and Lots of Bricks, place them in the shed.</li></ul>', 5),
(7401, 1963, 'Mining', 'Mining', 'Do not open any more mines. Try to mine existing shafts if possible. Shards may need to be mined, ask around. Extend the main mine with the forge deeper.', '<ul><li>Do not open any more mines. Try to mine existing shafts if possible.</li>\n<li>Shards may need to be mined, ask around.</li>\n<li>Extend the main mine with the forge deeper.</li></ul>', 6),
(7402, 1963, 'Smithing', 'Smithing', 'Smelt iron or other metals laying around. Make tools for new players.', '<ul><li>Smelt iron or other metals laying around.</li>\n<li>Make tools for new players.</li></ul>', 7),
(7403, 1963, 'Shipbuilding', 'Shipbuilding', 'Only thing I can think of, would be to extend the 1 tile \"dock\" in front of our land. Other than that we need nothing here.', '<ul><li>Only thing I can think of, would be to extend the 1 tile \"dock\" in front of our land. Other than that we need nothing here.</li></ul>', 8),
(7404, 1963, 'Tailoring', 'Tailoring', 'Do we even do this?', '<ul><li>Do we even do this?</li></ul>', 9),
(7405, 1963, 'Woodcutting and Forestry', 'Woodcutting_and_Forestry', 'Don\'t cut down oaks, willows, or olive trees. Pines can all die. Cut old and very old trees. If there are felled trees that aren\'t being used then make Charcoal pile . Try to find sprouts for oaks or other trees.', '<ul><li>Don\'t cut down oaks, willows, or olive trees. Pines can all die. Cut old and very old trees.</li>\n<li>If there are felled trees that aren\'t being used then make <a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal_pile\" title=\"Charcoal pile\">Charcoal pile</a>.</li>\n<li>Try to find sprouts for oaks or other trees.</li></ul>', 10),
(7406, 1963, 'Jobs needed completion', 'Jobs_needed_completion', '120 planks are needed for Boxxybabe\'s new home. Also are 12 large iron nails.', '<ul><li>120 planks are needed for Boxxybabe\'s new home.</li>\n<li>Also are 12 large iron nails.</li></ul>', 11),
(7407, 1963, 'Suspected Thief', 'Suspected_Thief', 'Please if you do not see the \"Awesome Manta\" boat by the front please IMMEDIATELY type /dev Someone has stolen BoxxyBabe\'s boat, Awesome Manta!', '<ul><li>Please if you do not see the \"Awesome Manta\" boat by the front please IMMEDIATELY type /dev Someone has stolen BoxxyBabe\'s boat, Awesome Manta!</li></ul>', 12),
(7408, 1963, 'Other Information', 'Other_Information', 'Do not build anywhere near the town or other people without permission. If in doubt, ask. We also need a premium person to break some stone fences and one fence gate. If you would like to add stuff to this, please PM (/t Boxxybabe) and with what sections and information.', '<ul><li>Do not build anywhere near the town or other people without permission.\n<ul><li>If in doubt, ask.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li>We also need a premium person to break some stone fences and one fence gate.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If you would like to add stuff to this, please PM (/t Boxxybabe) and with what sections and information.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 13),
(7409, 1963, 'How to contact us', 'How_to_contact_us', 'Please either visit our irc channel or PM either Meis, or prosak in game. [1]', '<p>Please either visit our irc channel or PM either Meis, or prosak in game.\n<a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"irc://irc.heavenlyplace.net/dirtville\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>\n</p>', 14),
(7410, 1964, 'Donners Pass', 'Donners_Pass', 'Carved out of the bedrock of Wurm this high mountain village is surrounded by the majestic peaks overlooking Newtown and the surrounding waters. Founded in the first days of gold Donner\'s Pass has evolved from a modest size 5 homestead into the size 10 village of today. This is in no small part to our hardworking citizens, camaraderie as well as our shared desire to master the terrain. \n    The rugged landscape and the story of Donner Pass pays homage to the challenges faced in simply surviving Wurm. Sol\'s Keep DP Ascension, our first expansion sits perched high atop the great peak and serves as a lookout post. \n\n    If fellowship, a bit of work and domination of a landscape sound like fun feel free to contact us...we look forward to seeing you!', '<p>   Carved out of the bedrock of Wurm this high mountain village is surrounded by the majestic peaks overlooking Newtown and the surrounding waters. Founded in the first days of gold Donner\'s Pass has evolved from a modest size 5 homestead into the size 10 village of today. This is in no small part to our hardworking citizens, camaraderie as well as our shared desire to master the terrain. \n    The rugged landscape and the story of Donner Pass pays homage to the challenges faced in simply surviving Wurm. Sol\'s Keep DP Ascension, our first expansion sits perched high atop the great peak and serves as a lookout post. \n\n    If fellowship, a bit of work and domination of a landscape sound like fun feel free to contact us...we look forward to seeing you!\n\n\n</p>', 0),
(7411, 1964, 'Information', 'Information', 'Trader Euthenia (*the Greek spirit of prosperity) Size 10 village deed . Located on the mountain east SE of Newtown Donners Pass is building a training facility. Beds for rent', '<p>Trader Euthenia (*the Greek spirit of prosperity)<br/>\nSize 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village_Deeds\" title=\"Village Deeds\">village deed</a>.<br/>\nLocated on the mountain east SE of Newtown<br/>\nDonners Pass is building a training facility. Beds for rent<br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7412, 1964, 'How to apply for Donners Pass', 'How_to_apply_for_Donners_Pass', 'Basically we take on new people as and when they ask. They will be set up in the brand new NT side of DP. DP now has a NT side which is closer to Newtown and is open for the newer people of Donners Pass. To apply for a place in Donners Pass, PM one of the following people.... Beowulf - Mayor Bradow - Elder Mith - Elder Or you can PM one of these people and they will get back to you with information ASAP.... Diamond Legionare Rune', '<p>Basically we take on new people as and when they ask. They will be set up in the brand new NT side of DP.<br/>\nDP now has a NT side which is closer to Newtown and is open for the newer people of Donners Pass.<br/>\n</p>\n<p>To apply for a place in Donners Pass, PM one of the following people....<br/>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Beowulf\" title=\"User:Beowulf\">Beowulf</a> - Mayor <br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Bradow\" title=\"User:Bradow\">Bradow</a>  - Elder <br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Mith\" title=\"User:Mith\">Mith</a>   - Elder\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nOr you can PM one of these people and they will get back to you with information ASAP....<br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Diamond\" title=\"User:Diamond\">Diamond</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Legionare\" title=\"User:Legionare\">Legionare</a><br/>\nRune<br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7413, 1964, 'Members', 'Members', 'Elders Beowulf -Mayor Bradow Mith Claw Tukster Legionaire Guild Masters Helge -Tailor Guild Tukster -Wood Guild Rune -Painting Guild Guildings Legionaire Members Arunsun Bogart Diamond KeyKeeper', '<p>Elders\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Beowulf\" title=\"User:Beowulf\">Beowulf</a> -Mayor<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Bradow\" title=\"User:Bradow\">Bradow</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Mith\" title=\"User:Mith\">Mith</a><br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Claw&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Claw (page does not exist)\">Claw</a><br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Tukster&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Tukster (page does not exist)\">Tukster</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Legionaire\" title=\"User:Legionaire\">Legionaire</a><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Guild Masters\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Helge\" title=\"User:Helge\">Helge</a> -Tailor Guild<br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Tukster&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Tukster (page does not exist)\">Tukster</a> -Wood Guild<br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Rune&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Rune (page does not exist)\">Rune</a> -Painting Guild<br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nGuildings\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Legionaire\" title=\"User:Legionaire\">Legionaire</a><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nMembers\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Arunsun&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Arunsun (page does not exist)\">Arunsun</a><br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Bogart&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Bogart (page does not exist)\">Bogart</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Diamond\" title=\"User:Diamond\">Diamond</a><br/>\n<a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:KeyKeeper&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:KeyKeeper (page does not exist)\">KeyKeeper</a><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(7414, 1964, 'Website', 'Website', 'Donners Pass Homepage', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.helges.dk/dp//\" rel=\"nofollow\">Donners Pass Homepage</a>\n</p>', 4),
(7415, 1964, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'Donners Pass Awaiting more pictures', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:172px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mountain.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"113\" data-file-width=\"618\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"31\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7e/Mountain.jpg/170px-Mountain.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7e/Mountain.jpg/255px-Mountain.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7e/Mountain.jpg/340px-Mountain.jpg 2x\" width=\"170\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mountain.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Donners Pass</div></div></div>\n<p><i>Awaiting more pictures</i><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<br/>\n</p>', 5),
(7416, 1964, 'Alliances', 'Alliances', 'Sol\'s Keep DP Ascension(expansion) OldGuard Pupanox', '<p>Sol\'s Keep DP Ascension(expansion)<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/OldGuard\" title=\"OldGuard\">OldGuard</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pupanox\" title=\"Pupanox\">Pupanox</a><br/>\n</p>', 6),
(7417, 1965, 'Location', 'Location', 'Northeastern side of Bearback Lake. Just South of the road to Rockcliff. Direction to Dragon Forest from NewTown Getting to Dragon Forest is easy. Just go West from Newtown and follow what is known as the Bearback Highway until you get to the old crossroads. Make a left and go south, passing the sign to Rockcliff. 30 seconds after you pass it, look for the entrance on your right. Dragon Forest is quite the cozy homestead, and has the largest clay bed on the lake, just north of the homestead. Dragon Forest started out as Benie\'s Homestead, and grew ever since. It was once a beautiful place. But sadly, it\'s lost it\'s beauty due to it\'s owner constantly changing it because he\'s never happy.', '<p>Northeastern side of Bearback Lake. Just South of the road to Rockcliff.\n<img alt=\"Road_to_Dragon_Forest.png\" src=\"http://beniesbuilds.com/img/Wurm/Road_to_Dragon_Forest.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><i>Direction to Dragon Forest from NewTown</i>\n</p>\n<p>Getting to Dragon Forest is easy. Just go West from Newtown and follow what is known as the Bearback Highway until you get to the old crossroads. Make a left and go south, passing the sign to Rockcliff. 30 seconds after you pass it, look for the entrance on your right.\n</p>\n<p>Dragon Forest is quite the cozy homestead, and has the largest clay bed on the lake, just north of the homestead.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nDragon Forest started out as Benie\'s Homestead, and grew ever since. It was once a beautiful place. But sadly, it\'s lost it\'s beauty due to it\'s owner constantly changing it because he\'s never happy.\n</p>', 0),
(7418, 1966, 'Location', 'Location', 'Located southeast of Bennie Bay', '<p>Located southeast of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bennie_Bay\" title=\"Bennie Bay\">Bennie Bay</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7419, 1968, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Xallo', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xallo\" title=\"Player:Xallo\">Xallo</a></li></ul>', 0),
(7420, 1968, 'Allied with', 'Allied_with', 'Iron\'s Paradise Port Isengard', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron%27s_Paradise\" title=\"Iron\'s Paradise\">Iron\'s Paradise</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Port_Isengard\" title=\"Port Isengard\">Port Isengard</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7421, 1969, 'President', 'President', 'Jimmi [Lumberjack], [Carpenter], [Miner], [Digger], [Trollslayer], [Keeper of Faith] ///  Locksmith , Coal-maker, allround', '<p><b>Jimmi</b> [Lumberjack], [Carpenter], [Miner], [Digger], [Trollslayer], [Keeper of Faith] ///  Locksmith , Coal-maker, allround\n</p>', 0),
(7422, 1969, 'Captain', 'Captain', 'Addamm [Carpenter], [Lumberjack], [Digger], [Trollslayer], [Renowned Carpenter], ///  Armour Smith , allround Shereff', '<p><b>Addamm</b> [Carpenter], [Lumberjack], [Digger], [Trollslayer], [Renowned Carpenter], ///  Armour Smith , allround <br/>\n<b>Shereff</b>\n<br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7423, 1969, 'Elders', 'Elders', 'Uberbear /// Blacksmith , Sprout Picker', '<p><br/>\n<b>Uberbear</b> /// Blacksmith , Sprout Picker\n<br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7424, 1969, 'Citiziens', 'Citiziens', 'Jot [Mason] [Digger] [Trollslayer] [Caterer] [Carpenter]  /// Cook, Farmer, Mason Robbinman [Trollslayer]              /// Weaponsmith, Miner Jonjon /// Shieldsmith Dannypos /// Armoursmith Knux /// Digger Yagamilight', '<p><br/>\n<b>Jot</b> [Mason] [Digger] [Trollslayer] [Caterer] [Carpenter]  /// Cook, Farmer, Mason<br/>\n<b>Robbinman</b> [Trollslayer]              /// Weaponsmith, Miner<br/>\n<b>Jonjon</b>                               /// Shieldsmith<br/>\n<b>Dannypos</b>                             /// Armoursmith<br/>\n<b>Knux</b>                                 /// Digger<br/>\n<b>Yagamilight</b><br/>\n<br/>\n</p>', 3),
(7425, 1971, 'History', 'History', 'Green Oaks was founded on the 7th day of the Snakes Starfall in the year 989.', '<p>Green Oaks was founded on the 7th day of the Snakes Starfall in the year 989.\n</p>', 0),
(7426, 1971, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Lords KingdarkX Killerslug Citizens Melodycat Villagers Usafpararescue', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lords\">Lords</span></h3>\n<p>KingdarkX\n</p>\n<p>Killerslug\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p>Melodycat\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Villagers_2\">Villagers</span></h3>\n<p>Usafpararescue\n</p>', 1),
(7427, 1971, 'Facilities', 'Facilities', 'Many of the Green Oaks facilities are for citizens only, but some are for villagers. Pen Green Oaks has a cattle pen for citizens that currently has 2 cows & 2 calves. Because of a nearby spawn, this number is likely to increase. Mine The mine currently has a copper vein & two zinc veins. In the smithy we have a 60ql forge along with all the tools for imping and finishing smithing items. Towers We are currently constructing a tower near the mine and pen Spawns Nearby; There a pig, deer, wolf, bear and scorpian spawns. On the steppe there are troll, wolf, mountain lion, wildcat, bear, dog and cow spawns.', '<p>Many of the Green Oaks facilities are for citizens only, but some are for villagers.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Pen\">Pen</span></h3>\n<p>Green Oaks has a cattle pen for citizens that currently has 2 cows &amp; 2 calves. Because of a nearby spawn, this number is likely to increase.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mine\">Mine</span></h3>\n<p>The mine currently has a copper vein &amp; two zinc veins.\n</p>\n<p>In the smithy we have a 60ql forge along with all the tools for imping and finishing smithing items.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Towers\">Towers</span></h3>\n<p>We are currently constructing a tower near the mine and pen\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Spawns\">Spawns</span></h3>\n<p>Nearby; There a pig, deer, wolf, bear and scorpian spawns. On the steppe there are troll, wolf, mountain lion, wildcat, bear, dog and cow spawns.\n</p>', 2),
(7433, 1976, 'Members', 'Members', 'Urman - Ally and Owner', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Urman\" title=\"Player:Urman\">Urman</a> - Ally and Owner</li></ul>', 0),
(7434, 1977, 'Description', 'Description', 'You will found the city on the north west coast flanked from a small forest, the most land around are tundra.', '<p>You will found the city on the north west coast flanked from a small forest, the most land around are tundra.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"HerosOfLevedara.jpg\" src=\"http://i435.photobucket.com/albums/qq76/Margoe_images/HerosOfLevedara.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 0),
(7435, 1977, 'Services', 'Services', 'We are offer travelers if the ask friendly, free refreshment and healing.\nThere alsow a hotel near the habour with cosy beds to sleep in.\nIf you need anything, like new tools, or only some tools imped, wa are allways happy to help. We will start alsow a trading center at the city where player can sell and buy there stuff.', '<p>We are offer travelers if the ask friendly, free refreshment and healing.\nThere alsow a hotel near the habour with cosy beds to sleep in.\nIf you need anything, like new tools, or only some tools imped, wa are allways happy to help.\n</p>\n<p>We will start alsow a trading center at the city where player can sell and buy there stuff.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7436, 1977, 'Trading', 'Trading', 'The city sell: healing covers, first aid bandage (rags, cloths, shets), tools, weapons, chain armor, shields, farming stuff and food. The city buy: Hide, butcherd stuff for healing covers.', '<p>The city sell: healing covers, first aid bandage (rags, cloths, shets), tools, weapons, chain armor, shields, farming stuff and food.\n</p>\n<p>The city buy: Hide, butcherd stuff for healing covers.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7437, 1977, 'Rules', 'Rules', 'Do not build or teraform in a 100 title range from the city token! (especial don\'t destroy the tundra!!) Do not beg citizens for free items if they have already said no Chat rules apply within the local range. Follow the chat rules. Treat players with respect in the local area. Keep confrontations to private messages. Remain calm, have fun', '<ol><li>Do not build or teraform in a 100 title range from the city token! (especial don\'t destroy the tundra!!)</li>\n<li>Do not beg citizens for free items if they have already said no</li>\n<li>Chat rules apply within the local range. Follow the chat rules.</li>\n<li>Treat players with respect in the local area. Keep confrontations to private messages.</li>\n<li>Remain calm, have fun</li></ol>', 3),
(7438, 1978, 'Description and history', 'Description_and_history', 'Hidden Village was a size 5 village in the middle northern area on Jenn-Kellon home at 43, 26 on the Gold 2 Village Roadmap. The last known mayor was Houston. The village features a mountain-like scheme, lovely terraformed on a hillside, but noone could tell who originally built it. It\'s most likely to be the creators of Shore haven that stood at the exact same spot Hidden Village was founded after the abandonment of Shore haven.', '<p>Hidden Village was a size 5 village in the middle northern area on <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Home\" title=\"Home\">home</a> at 43, 26 on the Gold 2 Village Roadmap. The last known mayor was Houston.\n</p>\n<p>The village features a mountain-like scheme, lovely terraformed on a hillside, but noone could tell who originally built it. It\'s most likely to be the creators of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shore_haven\" title=\"Shore haven\">Shore haven</a> that stood at the exact same spot <b>Hidden Village</b> was founded after the abandonment of Shore haven.\n</p>', 0),
(7439, 1978, 'Location', 'Location', 'The area is rich with resources, everything within only a couple of minutes of travelling. A couple of mines have been tunneled into the mountains, supplying people with all kinds of ore and prebuild high quality forges . The nearby Scorpion Lake is rich with fish and habitated a raging scorpion stone by its tar pit, giving the lake its name. The scorpion tunnel, now partially caved in, passed by the lake to connect Hidden Village with Rosewood Manor in order to get to the closest clay resource at Sanctum . The huge peat field to the south at Fire Lake and the mossy area to the east completes the resource list and makes it a most desirable location.', '<p>The area is rich with resources, everything within only a couple of minutes of travelling. A couple of mines have been <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">tunneled</a> into the mountains, supplying people with all kinds of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">ore</a> and prebuild high <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>.\n</p>\n<p>The nearby Scorpion Lake is rich with <a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a> and habitated a <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_conditions\" title=\"Animal conditions\">raging</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Lair\" title=\"Lair\">scorpion stone</a> by its tar pit, giving the lake its name. The scorpion tunnel, now partially caved in, passed by the lake to connect <b>Hidden Village</b> with Rosewood Manor in order to get to the closest <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> resource at <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sanctum\" title=\"Sanctum\">Sanctum</a>.\n</p>\n<p>The huge <a href=\"/index.php/Peat\" title=\"Peat\">peat</a> field to the south at Fire Lake and the <a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">mossy</a> area to the east completes the resource list and makes it a most desirable location.\n</p>', 1),
(7440, 1979, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'Horsedog Cove is the capital village of Horsedog Nation . The cove is a size 10 village built inside of a natural cove on the North West corner of the Jenn-Kellon home server overlooking the west ocean.', '<p>Horsedog Cove is the capital village of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Horsedog_Nation\" title=\"Horsedog Nation\">Horsedog Nation</a>.\n</p>\n<p>The cove is a size 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village\" title=\"Village\">village</a> built inside of a natural cove on the North West corner of the Jenn-Kellon home server overlooking the west ocean.\n</p>', 0),
(7441, 1979, 'Inhabitants', 'Inhabitants', 'Risky Avanel Bobthebanker Botwo Esclavo Hitch Kaimaera Tanith Taylordmule Thedave Kosh', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Risky</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Avanel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Bobthebanker</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Botwo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Esclavo</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Hitch\" title=\"Player:Hitch\">Hitch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Kaimaera</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Tanith\" title=\"Player:Tanith\">Tanith</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Taylordmule</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Thedave</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Kosh</a></li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(7442, 1979, 'Current Projects', 'Current_Projects', 'Horsedog Cove has started its beatification and deed reclamation project. As an aging working village, the Horsedog Cove Deed and surrounding area has been neglected while other Horsedog Nation projects were being completed.  . We are now going back and fixing some issues that have been ignored for too long. Horsedog Cove was originally settled as a size five village and later expanded to a size 10.  The first order of business will be to flat raise all the deeded land to a level usable state in order to reclaim deeded property for the village expansion Both the South and North ramps will be expanded to two tile ramps and will match the tetris slap/cobblestone Horsedog Nation standard road textures. The back road connecting the two ramps will be widened to two tiles The main road though the city center will be also widened to two tiles We will shorten the animal pen to reclaim the on deed property and bring the level of the entire area to the standard Horsedog grade Demolish and Rebuild the Horsedog Bar and Grill on the new reclaimed pen land Build a large on deed storage house New player housing on deed and to the south off deed General trimming and pruning on and surrounding the deed. Horsedog Training Center, a major off deed expansion will be built to the South East of the cove.  The training center will be a dedicated area used to level up fighting related skills.  Some ideas include: Area for training archery Training dummy ground New animal pens separated by the use of the particular animals/monsters A hunting lodge and common ground to share stories and strategies and beds for fight related sleep bonus. A tiered arena with spectator seating for fighting tournaments with monsters and PVP sparing', '<p>Horsedog Cove has started its beatification and deed reclamation project.  \n</p>\n<p>As an aging working village, the Horsedog Cove Deed and surrounding area has been neglected while other Horsedog Nation projects were being completed.  . We are now going back and fixing some issues that have been ignored for too long.  \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Horsedog Cove was originally settled as a size five village and later expanded to a size 10.  The first order of business will be to flat raise all the deeded land to a level usable state in order to reclaim deeded property for the village expansion</li>\n<li>Both the South and North ramps will be expanded to two tile ramps and will match the tetris slap/cobblestone Horsedog Nation standard road textures.</li>\n<li>The back road connecting the two ramps will be widened to two tiles</li>\n<li>The main road though the city center will be also widened to two tiles</li>\n<li>We will shorten the animal pen to reclaim the on deed property and bring the level of the entire area to the standard Horsedog grade</li>\n<li>Demolish and Rebuild the Horsedog Bar and Grill on the new reclaimed pen land</li>\n<li>Build a large on deed storage house</li>\n<li>New player housing on deed and to the south off deed</li>\n<li>General trimming and pruning on and surrounding the deed.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\nHorsedog Training Center, a major off deed expansion will be built to the South East of the cove.  The training center will be a dedicated area used to level up fighting related skills.  Some ideas include:\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Area for training archery</li>\n<li>Training dummy ground</li>\n<li>New animal pens separated by the use of the particular animals/monsters</li>\n<li>A hunting lodge and common ground to share stories and strategies and beds for fight related sleep bonus.</li>\n<li>A tiered arena with spectator seating for fighting tournaments with monsters and PVP sparing</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7443, 1979, 'Screen Shots', 'Screen_Shots', 'An overview of the Cove at night', '<p><img alt=\"wurm338.jpg\" src=\"http://www.acidstar.com/spot/wurm/wurm338.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p>An overview of the Cove at night\n</p>', 3),
(7444, 1980, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'Horsedog Vineyard is a member homestead of the Horsedog Nation . HDV was Founded on the day of the Ant in week 1 of the Bear\'s starfall in the year 988 (Saturday April 27\'th 2008) by Evilspot. The vineyard is a size five homestead stationed atop a flattened mesa on the North West corner of the Jenn-Kellon home server.  The mesa and homestead are to the North East of Horsedog Cove .', '<p>Horsedog Vineyard is a member <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Homestead\" title=\"Homestead\">homestead</a> of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Horsedog_Nation\" title=\"Horsedog Nation\">Horsedog Nation</a>.  \n</p>\n<p>HDV was Founded on the day of the Ant in week 1 of the Bear\'s starfall in the year 988 (Saturday April 27\'th 2008) by Evilspot.\n</p>\n<p>The vineyard is a size five <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Homestead\" title=\"Homestead\">homestead</a> stationed atop a flattened mesa on the North West corner of the Jenn-Kellon home server.  The mesa and homestead are to the North East of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Horsedog_Cove\" title=\"Horsedog Cove\">Horsedog Cove</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(7445, 1980, 'Inhabitants', 'Inhabitants', 'Evilspot', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Evilspot\" title=\"Player:Evilspot\">Evilspot</a>\n</p>', 1),
(7446, 1980, 'Current Projects', 'Current_Projects', 'Horsedog Vineyard is still under heavy construction: The mesa is still in the process of flat raising to reclaim more land to accommodate the space needed for the designed build out. Only 1/5th of the grape vineyard has been planted. Gravel paving the packed dirt spacers in the wine field The maple tree farm is still in the clearing and planting phase.', '<p><b>Horsedog Vineyard is still under heavy construction:</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>The mesa is still in the process of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Flattening\" title=\"Flattening\">flat raising</a> to reclaim more land to accommodate the space needed for the designed build out.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Only 1/5th of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grape\" title=\"Grape\">grape</a> vineyard has been planted.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gravel paving the packed dirt spacers in the wine field</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Maple\" title=\"Maple\">maple</a> tree farm is still in the clearing and planting phase.</li></ul>', 2),
(7447, 1980, 'Wine Purchase', 'Wine_Purchase', 'Currently all of our wine vintages are ageing and not for sell.', '<p>Currently all of our wine vintages are ageing and not for sell.\n</p>', 3),
(7448, 1980, 'Screen Shots', 'Screen_Shots', 'A view from inside the vineyard An older shot from on top the mesa.  The Mesa is still being flat raised.', '<p><img alt=\"wurm335.jpg\" src=\"http://www.acidstar.com/spot/wurm/wurm335.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p>A view from inside the vineyard\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm283.jpg\" src=\"http://www.acidstar.com/spot/wurm/wurm283.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p>An older shot from on top the mesa.  The Mesa is still being flat raised.\n</p>', 4),
(7449, 1981, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Ironfist', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ironfist\" title=\"Player:Ironfist\">Ironfist</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7450, 1981, 'Allied with', 'Allied_with', 'Alphabetical Order Catan Common Denominator Elitewarrior\'s Home Eagle Breeze Port Isengard Tuscany Pointe Valenwood Home Port', '<p>Alphabetical Order\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Catan\" title=\"Catan\">Catan</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Common_Denominator\" title=\"Common Denominator\">Common Denominator</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Elitewarrior%27s_Home\" title=\"Elitewarrior\'s Home\">Elitewarrior\'s Home</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Eagle_Breeze\" title=\"Eagle Breeze\">Eagle Breeze</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Port_Isengard\" title=\"Port Isengard\">Port Isengard</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Tuscany_Pointe&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Tuscany Pointe (page does not exist)\">Tuscany Pointe</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Valenwood_Home_Port\" title=\"Valenwood Home Port\">Valenwood Home Port</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7451, 1981, 'Location', 'Location', '100 tiles east of Port Isengard at the home west border.\nGold 2 Village Roadmap X12/Y12', '<p>100 tiles east of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Port_Isengard\" title=\"Port Isengard\">Port Isengard</a> at the home west border.\nGold 2 Village Roadmap X12/Y12\n</p>', 2),
(7452, 1982, 'Ironfist\'s Manson', 'Ironfist.27s_Manson', 'Ironfist\'s Manson was the 3rd Homestead of Ironfist .\nFeel free to loot what you see ;) Location Ironfist\'s Manson is located at the coast between New Southport and Mystery Glade. I desided to move to the homeserver west border to be more close to the wild ore.\nThe name of the new homestead is Iron\'s Paradise.', '<p><img alt=\"wurm026sp5.jpg\" src=\"http://img151.imageshack.us/img151/108/wurm026sp5.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p>Ironfist\'s Manson was the 3rd Homestead of <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ironfist\" title=\"Player:Ironfist\">Ironfist</a>.\nFeel free to loot what you see ;)\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Location\">Location</span></h5>\n<p>Ironfist\'s Manson is located at the coast between <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/wiki/index.php/New_Southport\" rel=\"nofollow\">New Southport</a> and Mystery Glade.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>I desided to move to the homeserver west border to be more close to the wild ore.\nThe name of the new homestead is Iron\'s Paradise.\n</p>', 0),
(7453, 1983, 'Description', 'Description', 'Nature is a parent skill that has various subskills:', '<p><b>Nature</b> is a parent <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> that has various subskills:\n</p>', 0),
(7454, 1983, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Nature Subskills Animal husbandry - Breeding and grooming animals . Animal taming - Making an animal a pet. Botanizing - Looking for different kind of herbs . Farming - Planting, farming, and harvesting fields and crops. Fishing - Catching fish . Foraging - Searching for edible things in the grass. Forestry - Cutting sprouts , pruning, and harvesting trees and bushes. Gardening - Planting trees , bushes , and flowers as well as collecting herbs and spices from pottery planters . Meditating - Relaxing and focusing your body and mind on a meditation rug Milking - Milking cows , bisons or sheep . Papyrusmaking - Creating papyrus sheets from reed fibre and paper sheet from wood pulps .', '<ul><li>Nature</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">Animal husbandry</a> - Breeding and grooming <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Animal_taming\" title=\"Animal taming\">Animal taming</a> - Making an animal a pet.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> - Looking for different kind of <a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">herbs</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Farming</a> - Planting, farming, and harvesting fields and crops.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fishing\" title=\"Fishing\">Fishing</a> - Catching <a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> - Searching for edible things in the grass.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a> - Cutting <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a>, pruning, and harvesting trees and bushes.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">Gardening</a> - Planting <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bushes\" title=\"Bushes\">bushes</a>, and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Flowers\" title=\"Flowers\">flowers</a> as well as collecting <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Herbs\" title=\"Herbs\">herbs</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spices\" title=\"Spices\">spices</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\">pottery planters</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Meditating\" title=\"Meditating\">Meditating</a> - Relaxing and focusing your body and mind on a <a href=\"/index.php/Meditation_rug\" title=\"Meditation rug\">meditation rug</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Milking\" title=\"Milking\">Milking</a> - Milking <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cows\" title=\"Cows\">cows</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">bisons</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">sheep</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Papyrusmaking\" title=\"Papyrusmaking\">Papyrusmaking</a> - Creating <a href=\"/index.php/Papyrus_sheet\" title=\"Papyrus sheet\">papyrus sheets</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_fibre\" title=\"Reed fibre\">reed fibre</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Paper_sheet\" title=\"Paper sheet\">paper sheet</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_pulp\" title=\"Wood pulp\">wood pulps</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(7455, 1983, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Ecologist at 50 skill Treehugger at 70 skill Druidkin at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Ecologist at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Treehugger at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Druidkin at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(7456, 1984, 'General Info', 'General_Info', 'Ivalice was founded on the Home server by a group of players who had departed Serenity Port as a result of displeasure over the leadership displayed there. The group built the town and lived there for a period of about 1-2 months, during which they were brought into the limelight as the center of drama on the home server, as shown here and here . After the White Dragon was slain in their backyard, the core members then relocated to the Wild server , joining the Blacklighters and forming the village of Darkwoods . Ivalice has been disbanded and is being allowed to decay naturally. It is located near Maple Bay and Brimstone and is about an hour north of the un-deeded settlement of Atlantis and the old SP. It is an interesting sight for any traveler, though dangerous, as much of the wildlife has moved in after the citizens left.', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ivalice\" title=\"Ivalice\">Ivalice</a> was founded on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Home\" title=\"Home\">Home</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Server\" title=\"Server\">server</a> by a group of players who had departed <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Serenity_Port&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Serenity Port (page does not exist)\">Serenity Port</a> as a result of displeasure over the leadership displayed there. The group built the town and lived there for a period of about 1-2 months, during which they were brought into the limelight as the center of drama on the home server, as shown <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=14117\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a> and <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=14406\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a>. After the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/White_Dragon\" title=\"White Dragon\">White Dragon</a> was slain in their backyard, the core members then relocated to the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wild\" title=\"Wild\">Wild</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Server\" title=\"Server\">server</a>, joining the <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighters</a> and forming the village of <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Darkwoods&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Darkwoods (page does not exist)\">Darkwoods</a>.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ivalice\" title=\"Ivalice\">Ivalice</a> has been disbanded and is being allowed to decay naturally. It is located near <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Maple_Bay&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Maple Bay (page does not exist)\">Maple Bay</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Brimstone\" title=\"Brimstone\">Brimstone</a> and is about an hour north of the un-deeded settlement of Atlantis and the old SP. It is an interesting sight for any traveler, though dangerous, as much of the wildlife has moved in after the citizens left.\n</p>', 0),
(7457, 1984, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Chromega Elders Amara Crimsonmori Cross Zarwin Citizens Advisor Agentusp Animal (formerly Dridje ) Blackknight Ceselb Chaoticone Draugwyn Eon Fieron Glennc Glenskunk Humbard Siege Willithesm Zimfire', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Chromega\" title=\"User:Chromega\">Chromega</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Amara\" title=\"Player:Amara\">Amara</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Crimsonmori\" title=\"Player:Crimsonmori\">Crimsonmori</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Cross\" title=\"User:Cross\">Cross</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zarwin\" title=\"Player:Zarwin\">Zarwin</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Wossoo\" title=\"Player:Wossoo\">Advisor</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Agentusp\" title=\"Player:Agentusp\">Agentusp</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Animal\" title=\"Player:Animal\">Animal</a> (formerly <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Dridje</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Wossoo\" title=\"Player:Wossoo\">Blackknight</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Ceselb</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Chaoticone\" title=\"Player:Chaoticone\">Chaoticone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Draugwyn\" title=\"Player:Draugwyn\">Draugwyn</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Eon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fieron\" title=\"Player:Fieron\">Fieron</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Glenn\" title=\"Player:Glenn\">Glennc</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Glenskunk\" title=\"Player:Glenskunk\">Glenskunk</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Humbard</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Siege\" title=\"Player:Siege\">Siege</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Agentusp\" title=\"Player:Agentusp\">Willithesm</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zimfire\" title=\"Player:Zimfire\">Zimfire</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7458, 1985, 'Description', 'Description', 'Jewelspar is a small town of active, dedicated, players who strive for high skills and, above all, a friendly community. It disbanded on 30th December 2007 at 14:13 (GMT).', '<p>Jewelspar is a small town of active, dedicated, players who strive for high skills and, above all, a friendly community. It disbanded on 30th December 2007 at 14:13 (GMT).\n</p>', 0),
(7459, 1985, 'Mayoress', 'Mayoress', 'Dizzybot', '<p>Dizzybot\n</p>', 1),
(7460, 1985, 'History', 'History', 'In the beginning there was Newtown, a brave settlement founded by the first to visit the lands of Wurm. Shortly after the initial huge wave of refugees settlements began sprouting everywhere, one particular hamlet drew much attention. This town grew under the banner Old Town and was a very powerful regiment of strict leadership with dedicated townsfolk. Within days the town had grown so famous, for it\'s numerous kills, it had become the most hated in all of Wurm. As the town grew and the problems slipped in it simply shattered. The town was divided by a desire for warfare, half longed for a peaceful existence in the beauty of Wurm while the other roared for battle. The city finally disbanded and so Jewelspar was born. The peaceful village of skilled craftspeople exists many miles from the site of Old Town and, as desired, it is in a place of beauty.', '<p>In the beginning there was Newtown, a brave settlement founded by the first to visit the lands of Wurm. Shortly after the initial huge wave of refugees settlements began sprouting everywhere, one particular hamlet drew much attention. This town grew under the banner Old Town and was a very powerful regiment of strict leadership with dedicated townsfolk. Within days the town had grown so famous, for it\'s numerous kills, it had become the most hated in all of Wurm. As the town grew and the problems slipped in it simply shattered. The town was divided by a desire for warfare, half longed for a peaceful existence in the beauty of Wurm while the other roared for battle. The city finally disbanded and so Jewelspar was born. The peaceful village of skilled craftspeople exists many miles from the site of Old Town and, as desired, it is in a place of beauty.\n</p>', 2),
(7461, 1985, 'Area', 'Area', 'Jewelspar nestles between two mountains besides a vast lake and dense forest.', '<p>Jewelspar nestles between two mountains besides a vast lake and dense forest.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"jewelsparew4.jpg\" src=\"http://img412.imageshack.us/img412/9950/jewelsparew4.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 3),
(7462, 1985, 'Trade', 'Trade', 'Jewelspar has much to offer to those willing to trade; Everything from a lock-pick or lock to high quality tools.\nTo trade PM one of the following: Dizzybot Zarnibuddha Pidgeon Ignition', '<p>Jewelspar has much to offer to those willing to trade; Everything from a lock-pick or lock to high quality tools.\nTo trade PM one of the following:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dizzybot</li>\n<li>Zarnibuddha</li>\n<li>Pidgeon</li>\n<li>Ignition</li>\n</ul>', 4),
(7463, 1988, 'Members', 'Members', 'KillerOfBleh -=- Mayor', '<p>KillerOfBleh -=- Mayor\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(7464, 1988, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', '360 Degree Panoramic', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.jonathanedgecombe.com/panoramic.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">360 Degree Panoramic</a>\n</p>', 1),
(7465, 1989, 'Description', 'Description', 'Khazad Ered, home of the Dwarf Xeniphi . Set atop the Dwarf Mountain (previously known as Moss Mountain) a size 5 homestead that upon desertion was a splendour to behold. Within close distance of Rockcliff and former Infinity , may be reached by the Stairway to Heaven provided by Hrundi and the yet and forever unfinished road & tunnel.', '<p>Khazad Ered, home of the Dwarf <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xeniphi\" title=\"Player:Xeniphi\">Xeniphi</a>. Set atop the Dwarf Mountain (previously known as Moss Mountain) a size 5 homestead that upon desertion was a splendour to behold. Within close distance of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rockcliff\" title=\"Rockcliff\">Rockcliff</a> and former <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Infinity&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Infinity (page does not exist)\">Infinity</a>, may be reached by the Stairway to Heaven provided by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Hrundi\" title=\"Player:Hrundi\">Hrundi</a> and the yet and forever unfinished road &amp; tunnel.\n</p>', 0),
(7466, 1989, 'Information', 'Information', 'Contact Xeniphi', '<p>Contact <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xeniphi\" title=\"Player:Xeniphi\">Xeniphi</a>\n</p>', 1),
(7467, 1990, 'Where Are We?', 'Where_Are_We.3F', 'We are currently located just south east of Validus. The map coordinates are 79,27 on the X/Y axis.', '<p>We are currently located just south east of Validus.\n</p>\n<p>The map coordinates are 79,27 on the X/Y axis.\n</p>', 0),
(7468, 1990, 'Mayor', 'Mayor', 'Jenki (priest:Vynora) Likia Titles: Woodcutter Taissia (priest:Fo)', '<ul><li>Jenki (priest:Vynora)</li>\n<li>Likia Titles: Woodcutter</li>\n<li>Taissia (priest:Fo)</li></ul>', 1),
(7469, 1990, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Ghosted Titles: Miner,Digger,Woodcutter,Carpenter,Mason,TrollSlayer,And Handyman XxosirisxX (priest:Vynora) Oris (priest:Fo) Akasallia Titles: Carpenter Uristmcminer Titles: Carpenter, Digger, TrollSlayer Mollyz Lasertrold Titles: Prospector,Digger, Excavator Garrett Yuniko Yoinko MoonlightZelda Avenar Naglfar Titles: Ageless Queequeg Waffel Anirind Cartmann', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ghosted\" title=\"Player:Ghosted\">Ghosted</a> Titles: Miner,Digger,Woodcutter,Carpenter,Mason,TrollSlayer,And Handyman</li>\n<li>XxosirisxX (priest:Vynora)</li>\n<li>Oris (priest:Fo)</li>\n<li>Akasallia Titles: Carpenter</li>\n<li>Uristmcminer Titles: Carpenter, Digger, TrollSlayer</li>\n<li>Mollyz</li>\n<li>Lasertrold Titles: Prospector,Digger, Excavator</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Garrett\" title=\"Player:Garrett\">Garrett</a></li>\n<li>Yuniko</li>\n<li>Yoinko</li>\n<li>MoonlightZelda</li>\n<li>Avenar</li>\n<li>Naglfar Titles: Ageless</li>\n<li>Queequeg</li>\n<li>Waffel</li>\n<li>Anirind</li>\n<li>Cartmann</li></ul>', 2),
(7470, 1990, 'Trade', 'Trade', 'What we wish to buy: High ql ore (all ore 50+ql) Contact Akasallia\nRopes (mooring ropes,cordage ropes, and thick ropes) Contact Uristmcminer What we are selling: Boats (all) Contact Uristmcminer', '<p><i></i>\n<b>What we wish to buy:</b><i></i>\n</p>\n<p>High ql ore (all ore 50+ql) Contact Akasallia\nRopes (mooring ropes,cordage ropes, and thick ropes) Contact Uristmcminer\n</p>\n<p><b>What we are selling:</b>\nBoats (all) Contact Uristmcminer\n</p>', 3),
(7471, 1990, 'Priest Services', 'Priest_Services', 'Here is a list of the enchants we offer: List of Vynora spells available: Bless (This is cast on gold and silver alters to \"activate\" them with the power of Vynora.) Opulence (This is cast on food to make you eat less) Wind of Ages (This is cast on tools to give you a better/faster timer) * Aura of Shared Pain (This is cast on Armour to inflict damage when you take some. {Example: You attack a pig and he hits you. Your armour will then hurt him in the same place and do a portion of the damage}) Vynora\'s  Touch (This is cast on armour and will help protect you from demise spells.) ** Mend (This is cast on pelts and non-repair objects to repair them) Circle of Cunning (This is cast on tools/weapons for increased skill gain.) * Vessel (This is cast on gems to \"store\" favor for future use. Just a little side note but when \"vessled\" it stores 2x the priest\'s faith {depending on gem ql}) Flaming Arua (This is cast on weapons to aflict extra damage to your opponent.) Self Healer\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit trolls) ** Animal\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit \"animals\".) ** Libila\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Libila) ** Fo\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Fo) ** Magranon\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Magranon) ** Dragon\'s Demise (This gives a 10% bonus to hit a dragon) ** List of Fo spells available: Fo\'s Hand (This is cast on armour to protect followers of Fo against demise spells) ** Bless (This is cast on gold and silver alters to \"activate\" them with the power of FO.) Morning Fog (This is cast on player/animals to protect them from thorns. It wears off after going through them.) Refresh (This spell is cast on players to restore stamina. Cure Light (This spell is cast on wounds to heal light damage) Cure Medium (This spell is cast on wounds to heal medium damage) Cure Serious (This spell is cast on wounds to heal a lot of damage) Courier (This spell is cast on \"mailboxes\" to enable them to ship stuff) ** Anything marked with this must be cast on 70+ql tools/weapons/armour. * This spell WILL NOT affect dredges or weapons!', '<p><b>Here is a list of the enchants we offer:</b>\n</p>\n<p><b>List of Vynora spells available:</b>\n</p>\n<p><i>Bless</i> (This is cast on gold and silver alters to \"activate\" them with the power of Vynora.)\n</p>\n<p><i>Opulence</i> (This is cast on food to make you eat less)\n</p>\n<p><i>Wind of Ages</i> (This is cast on tools to give you a better/faster timer) *\n</p>\n<p><i>Aura of Shared Pain</i> (This is cast on Armour to inflict damage when you take some. {Example: You attack a pig and he hits you. Your armour will then hurt him in the same place and do a portion of the damage})\n</p>\n<p><i>Vynora\'s  Touch</i> (This is cast on armour and will help protect you from demise spells.) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Mend</i> (This is cast on pelts and non-repair objects to repair them)\n</p>\n<p><i>Circle of Cunning</i> (This is cast on tools/weapons for increased skill gain.) * \n<i> Vessel</i> (This is cast on gems to \"store\" favor for future use. Just a little side note but when \"vessled\" it stores 2x the priest\'s faith {depending on gem ql})\n</p>\n<p><i>Flaming Arua</i> (This is cast on weapons to aflict extra damage to your opponent.) \n</p>\n<p><i>Self Healer\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit trolls) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Animal\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit \"animals\".) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Libila\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Libila) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Fo\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Fo) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Magranon\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit followers of Magranon) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Dragon\'s Demise</i> (This gives a 10% bonus to hit a dragon) **\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>List of Fo spells available:</b>\n</p>\n<p><i>Fo\'s Hand</i> (This is cast on armour to protect followers of Fo against demise spells) **\n</p>\n<p><i>Bless</i> (This is cast on gold and silver alters to \"activate\" them with the power of FO.) \n</p>\n<p><i>Morning Fog</i> (This is cast on player/animals to protect them from thorns. It wears off after going through them.)\n</p>\n<p><i>Refresh</i> (This spell is cast on players to restore stamina.\n</p>\n<p><i>Cure Light</i> (This spell is cast on wounds to heal light damage)\n</p>\n<p><i>Cure Medium</i> (This spell is cast on wounds to heal medium damage)\n</p>\n<p><i>Cure Serious</i> (This spell is cast on wounds to heal a lot of damage)\n</p>\n<p><i>Courier</i> (This spell is cast on \"mailboxes\" to enable them to ship stuff)\n</p>\n<ul><li>** Anything marked with this must be cast on 70+ql tools/weapons/armour.</li>\n<li>* This spell WILL NOT affect dredges or weapons!</li></ul>', 4),
