(7749, 2102, 'Active Members', 'Active_Members', 'Kalel, Volatar, Lois, Lemmymtrhd, Commissarsirk, Anti, Cyrax, Waldnir, Tastycube.', '<p>Kalel, Volatar, Lois, Lemmymtrhd, Commissarsirk, Anti, Cyrax, Waldnir, Tastycube.\n</p>', 0),
(7750, 2103, 'Description', 'Description', 'Glitterdale , or its settlement token , was the starting point of the new players who started the game as Mol-Rehan characters. Glitterdale has two public traders , six guides , and two bartenders .', '<p><b>Glitterdale</b>, or its <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement_token\" title=\"Settlement token\">settlement token</a>, was the starting point of the new players who started the game as <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a> characters. Glitterdale has two public <a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">traders</a>, six <a href=\"/index.php/Guide\" title=\"Guide\">guides</a>, and two <a href=\"/index.php/Bartender\" title=\"Bartender\">bartenders</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(7751, 2103, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Glitterdale maps', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Astronomy_and_geography#Golden_Valley_Server\" title=\"Astronomy and geography\">Glitterdale maps</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7752, 2104, 'Village Locations', 'Village_Locations', 'Sunset Valley Lower Sunset Valley Main The Harbour The Cavern The Tunnel The Mine The North Farm The Buried Willow', '<ul><li>Sunset Valley Lower</li>\n<li>Sunset Valley Main</li>\n<li>The Harbour</li>\n<li>The Cavern</li>\n<li>The Tunnel</li>\n<li>The Mine</li>\n<li>The North Farm</li>\n<li>The Buried Willow</li></ul>', 0),
(7753, 2104, 'Community Projects', 'Community_Projects', 'Fencing SV Lower (Completed) Fencing SV Main (Completed) Headquarters (Completed) Coastal road (Under Construction) North farm (Under Construction) Harbour Gate houses Farm moat (Under Construction) More settlement boats +Ql30 rope tool House all citizens', '<ul><li>Fencing SV Lower <b> (Completed)</b></li>\n<li>Fencing SV Main <b> (Completed)</b></li>\n<li>Headquarters <b> (Completed)</b></li>\n<li>Coastal road <b> (Under Construction)</b></li>\n<li>North farm <b> (Under Construction)</b></li>\n<li>Harbour</li>\n<li>Gate houses</li>\n<li>Farm moat <b> (Under Construction)</b></li>\n<li>More settlement boats</li>\n<li>+Ql30 rope tool</li>\n<li>House all citizens</li></ul>', 1),
(7754, 2104, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Garrasion (Founder) Radioprotector (Founder) Teefy Vilnayin (Elder) Roach Noobpwner Genii Thehuntergatherer Bman Thor Crimsonflames If you wish to join Sunset Valley you must find us on your own and then we will review your possible integration into the community.\nThanks to Strawberry for creating our wiki.', '<ul><li>Garrasion <b>(Founder)</b></li>\n<li>Radioprotector <b>(Founder)</b></li>\n<li>Teefy</li>\n<li>Vilnayin <b>(Elder)</b></li>\n<li>Roach</li>\n<li>Noobpwner</li>\n<li>Genii</li>\n<li>Thehuntergatherer</li>\n<li>Bman</li>\n<li>Thor</li>\n<li>Crimsonflames</li></ul>\n<p>If you wish to join Sunset Valley you must find us on your own and then we will review your possible integration into the community.\nThanks to Strawberry for creating our wiki.\n</p>', 2),
(7762, 2106, 'Inactive Members', 'Inactive_Members', 'Strike Azog Rhaen Aengus Disciple Aeperdeper Arialynx Nemor Jhandar How to join us While we are an undeeded settlement, we would love for you to actually be accepted by us to build near us, otherwise we will lure bears to you everyday. That being said, in order for you to join us you will need to contact any one of the mayors, and request to join. Almost always we accept somebody, seeing as this is the newbie server that we play on. What we can offer We currently are in the process of building a community warehouse, with supplies for anyone to have. Of course, everything will be locked in chests so that we can control how much of something somebody can get. Inside will be a high QL forge along with a high QL oven. How to find us From Glitterdale or First Light 1) Follow amnesty road until you get to HOTS lake. 2) Go counter-clockwise around the lake until you get to us. Screenshots Click on the links next to the descriptions to see the \"hi-res\" images. A \"birds-eye\" view of our village from the village Outlaws . [1] A frontal view of the village, with a little glimpse of Outlaws at the top-left of the screenshot. [2]', '<p>Strike\n</p>\n<p>Azog\n</p>\n<p>Rhaen\n</p>\n<p>Aengus\n</p>\n<p>Disciple\n</p>\n<p>Aeperdeper\n</p>\n<p>Arialynx\n</p>\n<p>Nemor\n</p>\n<p>Jhandar\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_join_us\">How to join us</span></h1>\n<p>While we <i>are</i> an undeeded settlement, we would love for you to actually be accepted by us to build near us, otherwise we will lure bears to you everyday. That being said, in order for you to join us you will need to contact any one of the mayors, and request to join. Almost always we accept somebody, seeing as this is the newbie server that we play on.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"What_we_can_offer\">What we can offer</span></h1>\n<p>We currently are in the process of building a community warehouse, with supplies for anyone to have. Of course, everything will be locked in chests so that we can control how much of something somebody can get. Inside will be a high <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> forge along with a high <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> oven.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_find_us\">How to find us</span></h1>\n<p><b>From <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Glitterdale\" title=\"Glitterdale\">Glitterdale</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/First_Light\" title=\"First Light\">First Light</a></b>\n</p>\n<p>1) Follow amnesty road until you get to <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">HOTS</a> lake.\n</p>\n<p>2) Go counter-clockwise around the lake until you get to us.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Screenshots\">Screenshots</span></h1>\n<p><b>Click on the links next to the descriptions to see the \"hi-res\" images.</b>\n</p>\n<p>A \"birds-eye\" view of our village from the village <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Outlaw%27s_Village\" title=\"Outlaw\'s Village\">Outlaws</a>. <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://img9.imageshack.us/img9/9638/wurm200904062043.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm200904062043thumb.png\" src=\"http://img9.imageshack.us/img9/5594/wurm200904062043thumb.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p>A frontal view of the village, with a little glimpse of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Outlaw%27s_Village\" title=\"Outlaw\'s Village\">Outlaws</a> at the top-left of the screenshot.<a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://img19.imageshack.us/img19/5200/yewfrontview.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">[2]</a>\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"yewfrontviewthumb.png\" src=\"http://img19.imageshack.us/img19/1985/yewfrontviewthumb.png\"/>\n</p>', 0),
(7767, 2112, 'Location', 'Location', 'Aegis is located just to the East of Samling (The Newtown of Freedom) along the Freedom Road. Current Projects We are currently farming, mining, building our houses, and transporting the dirt from the pit we dug to get to the rock layer. (250 dirt down, first iron mine so far reported.) Residents Alistar (Mayor) Radnor (Writholder) Blalt Fredyc Secos Adamb Wisteria Librarian Johan Vydagen Spiderhawk Achroite Apocadawg Dominikk Shadowex Huntera Achroite Fredyc Kyellan Longbeard Vashous Alluraprime Ephemeral Enemies Linkdead Beanbagg Village Plan Village Plan Village Website Village Website', '<p>Aegis is located just to the East of Samling (The Newtown of Freedom) along the Freedom Road.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Current_Projects\">Current Projects</span></h3>\n<p>We are currently farming, mining, building our houses, and transporting the dirt from the pit we dug to get to the rock layer. (250 dirt down, first iron mine so far reported.)\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Residents\">Residents</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Alistar (Mayor)</li>\n<li>Radnor (Writholder)</li>\n<li>Blalt</li>\n<li>Fredyc</li>\n<li>Secos</li>\n<li>Adamb</li>\n<li>Wisteria</li>\n<li>Librarian</li>\n<li>Johan</li>\n<li>Vydagen</li>\n<li>Spiderhawk</li>\n<li>Achroite</li>\n<li>Apocadawg</li>\n<li>Dominikk</li>\n<li>Shadowex</li>\n<li>Huntera</li>\n<li>Achroite</li>\n<li>Fredyc</li>\n<li>Kyellan</li>\n<li>Longbeard</li>\n<li>Vashous</li>\n<li>Alluraprime</li>\n<li>Ephemeral</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Enemies\">Enemies</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Linkdead</li>\n<li>Beanbagg</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Plan\">Village Plan</span></h3>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img15.imageshack.us/img15/4317/wallsh.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\">Village Plan</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Website\">Village Website</span></h3>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://aegis.renscreations.com/?page_id=2\" rel=\"nofollow\">Village Website</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7768, 2114, 'Guild Masters:', 'Guild_Masters:', 'Rycory: Master of Stables Nikolaius: Master of Bard Hall', '<ul><li>Rycory: Master of Stables</li>\n<li>Nikolaius: Master of Bard Hall</li></ul>', 0),
(7769, 2114, 'Guild Members:', 'Guild_Members:', '', '', 1),
(7770, 2114, 'Citizenry:', 'Citizenry:', 'Cryogenisist Kam Endorsements Al\'Saius openly recommends trade with any of the following merchants/shops: Stone Harbor Crafts Ultimarus Trading Company Build-A-Blade Armoury Cliff Side Exports', '<ul><li>Cryogenisist</li>\n<li>Kam</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Endorsements\">Endorsements</span></h3>\n<p>Al\'Saius openly recommends trade with any of the following merchants/shops:\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=57387.0%7C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Stone Harbor Crafts</a>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=56934.0%7C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Ultimarus Trading Company</a>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=58927.0%7C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Build-A-Blade Armoury</a>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=55468.0%7C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Cliff Side Exports</a>\n</p>', 2),
(7771, 2115, 'Description', 'Description', 'We are located west of Samling on the edge of the large mountain. Access is by land bridge to the coastal walkway, or by boat. Useful Buildings Avalon Market\nBuying and selling tba', '<p>We are located west of Samling on the edge of the large mountain. Access is by land bridge to the coastal walkway, or by boat.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Useful_Buildings\">Useful Buildings</span></h3>\n<p>Avalon Market\nBuying and selling tba\n</p>', 0),
(7772, 2115, 'Avalon', 'Avalon', 'Avalon was first started as the mystic sister village of Mist, way back in early beta in the map called the \"Religion Map\". This map was the first introduction of religion to wurm. Originally founded by Barakus, Avalon survived numerous maps and still survives today under the Mayorship of Barakus. Over the years there have been some usurpers that on occasion have taken advantage of map change to gain control of Avalon, but patience prevailed and it is once again back in its founders hands. Avalon will always be strong and support our sister city of Mist.\nLong may Avalon prosper.', '<p>Avalon was first started as the mystic sister village of Mist, way back in early beta in the map called the \"Religion Map\". This map was the first introduction of religion to wurm. Originally founded by Barakus, Avalon survived numerous maps and still survives today under the Mayorship of Barakus. Over the years there have been some usurpers that on occasion have taken advantage of map change to gain control of Avalon, but patience prevailed and it is once again back in its founders hands.\n</p>\n<p>Avalon will always be strong and support our sister city of Mist.\nLong may Avalon prosper.\n</p>', 1),
(7773, 2115, 'Merchandise', 'Merchandise', 'None yet.', '<p>None yet.\n</p>', 2),
(7774, 2117, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'A plateau rising out of the hillside west of Darkenstone along the highway from it to Insanity.  We have a beautiful view of the lakes in the middle of the map, and the various mountains of Freedom.  Please feel free to check in on our Merchant for any supplies you need in your travels, or just stop in at our public fountain and mailbox and enjoy the view. Originally a solo effort by Maluraq , since finishing the basic teraforming of the deed and creating the highway up from the bay, new members were invited to join and work independently on their skills or whims while helping wherever possible with the needs of the deed.', '<p>A plateau rising out of the hillside west of Darkenstone along the highway from it to Insanity.  We have a beautiful view of the lakes in the middle of the map, and the various mountains of Freedom.  Please feel free to check in on our Merchant for any supplies you need in your travels, or just stop in at our public fountain and mailbox and enjoy the view.\n</p>\n<p>Originally a solo effort by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Maluraq\" title=\"Player:Maluraq\">Maluraq</a>, since finishing the basic teraforming of the deed and creating the highway up from the bay, new members were invited to join and work independently on their skills or whims while helping wherever possible with the needs of the deed.\n</p>', 0),
(7775, 2117, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'Single-lane ramp up the mountain to the peak Docking area for ships Development of Copper Cliffs at mountain\'s peak Guard towers at the four corners of the mountain\'s peak Planting steppe on mountainside Completed Flat-raising of deed on hillside Two-lane highway from the water at the bay to the deed Guard towers along highway for visitor safety Cave canal for easy passage from Samling to IHSH and Oreo regions', '<dl><dd>Single-lane ramp up the mountain to the peak</dd>\n<dd>Docking area for ships</dd>\n<dd>Development of <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_settlement\" title=\"Undefined settlement\">Copper Cliffs</a> at mountain\'s peak</dd>\n<dd>Guard towers at the four corners of the mountain\'s peak</dd>\n<dd>Planting steppe on mountainside</dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed\">Completed</span></h3>\n<dl><dd>Flat-raising of deed on hillside</dd>\n<dd>Two-lane highway from the water at the bay to the deed</dd>\n<dd>Guard towers along highway for visitor safety</dd>\n<dd>Cave canal for easy passage from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Samling\" title=\"Samling\">Samling</a> to IHSH and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oreo\" title=\"Oreo\">Oreo</a> regions</dd></dl>', 1),
(7776, 2117, 'Local Mapping', 'Local_Mapping', 'Some local mapping of the roads and deed location, please ignore grass/water, they\'re not accurate.', '<p>Some local mapping of the roads and deed location, please ignore grass/water, they\'re not accurate.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"bhe_roadmap.png\" src=\"http://mikebabcock.ca/gaming/wurmonline/freedom/bhe_roadmap.png\"/>\n</p>', 2),
(7777, 2117, 'The View', 'The_View', '', '<p><img alt=\"BHE_view_panorama_tn.jpg\" src=\"http://mikebabcock.ca/gaming/wurmonline/freedom/BHE_view_panorama_tn.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 3),
(7778, 2117, 'Exports and Productivity', 'Exports_and_Productivity', 'Blacksmithing products up to 75ql, specializing in lamps Cotton products such as sheets, sails and even cloth armour on request', '<ul><li>Blacksmithing products up to 75ql, specializing in lamps</li>\n<li>Cotton products such as sheets, sails and even cloth armour on request</li></ul>', 4),
(7779, 2117, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Mayor Maluraq Teraforming guru and benevolent dictator', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Maluraq\" title=\"Player:Maluraq\">Maluraq</a> Teraforming guru and benevolent dictator</li></ul>', 5),
(7780, 2117, 'Recruiting', 'Recruiting', 'If you are a crafter or worker interested in joining a peaceful village, please message Maluraq on the forums or in-game.\nThere is no forced labour or required hours, it is simply required that you try to get along with your fellow villagers.', '<p>If you are a crafter or worker interested in joining a peaceful village, please message Maluraq on the forums or in-game.\nThere is no forced labour or required hours, it is simply required that you try to get along with your fellow villagers.\n</p>', 6),
(7781, 2120, 'Nearby', 'Nearby', 'There are 2 public mines by Blossom. The first is to the North of the token. The second public mine is in the nearby Settlement of Boat Port. \nTo the North of Blossom is Blossom Market, where traders often gather.', '<p>There are 2 public mines by Blossom. The first is to the North of the token. The second public mine is in the nearby Settlement of Boat Port. \nTo the North of Blossom is Blossom Market, where traders often gather.\n</p>', 0),
(7782, 2121, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold = Title Mayor: Surtr - [Tim the Toolman] , [Lumberjack] , [Dragonslayer] , [Blacksmith] , [Renowned Blacksmith] , [Handyman] , [Shieldsmith] , [Farmer] , [Excavator] , [Carpenter] , [Mason] , [Prime Minester] , [Digger] , [Miner] , [High Mason] , [Soldier] , [Landshaper] , [Trollslayer] , [Repairman] , [Caterer] , [Mercenary] , [Body Builder] , [Sculptor] Currently working Villagers Jebraltix, [Trollslayer] Insano Calvinoph Harvick - Priest of Magranon, [Padre] Abbydo - Priestess of Vynora, [Mystic] , [Norn] Freya - Priestess of Fo , [Norn]', '<p><b>Bold</b> = Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor:\">Mayor:</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Surtr\" title=\"Player:Surtr\">Surtr</a> - <b>[Tim the Toolman]</b>, <b>[Lumberjack]</b>, <b>[Dragonslayer]</b>, <b>[Blacksmith]</b>, <b>[Renowned Blacksmith]</b>, <b>[Handyman]</b>, <b>[Shieldsmith]</b>, <b>[Farmer]</b>, <b>[Excavator]</b>, <b>[Carpenter]</b>, <b>[Mason]</b>, <b>[Prime Minester]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Miner]</b>, <b>[High Mason]</b>, <b>[Soldier]</b>, <b>[Landshaper]</b>, <b>[Trollslayer]</b>, <b>[Repairman]</b>, <b>[Caterer]</b>, <b>[Mercenary]</b>, <b>[Body Builder]</b>, <b>[Sculptor]</b></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_working_Villagers\">Currently working Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Jebraltix, <b>[Trollslayer]</b></li>\n<li>Insano</li>\n<li>Calvinoph</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Harvick - Priest of Magranon,  <b>[Padre]</b></li>\n<li>Abbydo - Priestess of Vynora, <b>[Mystic]</b>, <b>[Norn]</b></li>\n<li>Freya - Priestess of Fo ,  <b>[Norn]</b></li></ul>', 0),
(7783, 2121, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', '', '<p><img alt=\"wurm201009242010.png\" src=\"http://i656.photobucket.com/albums/uu281/dndsparks/Boondock/wurm201009242010.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Boondock_Cur_8_29.png\" src=\"http://i656.photobucket.com/albums/uu281/dndsparks/Boondock/Boondock_Cur_8_29.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7784, 2121, 'External Links', 'External_Links', '(Coming soon...)', '<ul><li>(Coming soon...)</li></ul>', 2),
(7785, 2122, 'Description', 'Description', 'Think big or your not a BoS Member BoS Island is the third incarnation of a team effort of several IRL swedish friends. The village was founded by Aske , Daash , Madboy , Minimad , Rmt , Solver and Tottman during the first hours in the initial wave of settlers that arrived to the land of Independence.', '<p><b>Think big or your not a BoS Member</b>\n</p>\n<p>BoS Island is the third incarnation of a team effort of several IRL swedish friends. The village was founded by <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Aske</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daash\" title=\"Player:Daash\">Daash</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Madboy\" title=\"Player:Madboy\">Madboy</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Minimad\" title=\"Player:Minimad\">Minimad</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Rmt\" title=\"Player:Rmt\">Rmt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Solver\" title=\"Player:Solver\">Solver</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tottman\" title=\"Player:Tottman\">Tottman</a> during the first hours in the initial wave of settlers that arrived to the land of Independence. \n</p>', 0),
(7786, 2122, 'Buildings', 'Buildings', '7 large private villas with adjacent patch of land that the owner is free to use as he/she see fit. 1 well equipped large kitchen that can also serve as the village community center. 1 Guest house of considerable size. A fully functional wishing well, both water and enchanted. Two merchant houses with high ql merchandise A Harbour with piers for bigger ships and a marina for smaller crafts', '<ul><li>7 large private villas with adjacent patch of land that the owner is free to use as he/she see fit.</li>\n<li>1 well equipped large kitchen that can also serve as the village community center.</li>\n<li>1 Guest house of considerable size.</li>\n<li>A fully functional wishing well, both water and enchanted.</li>\n<li>Two merchant houses with high ql merchandise</li>\n<li>A Harbour with piers for bigger ships and a marina for smaller crafts</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7787, 2122, 'Politics', 'Politics', 'Government The combined group effort that today is known as BoS Island is not ruled by a single individual, such as a mayor, but instead is held together by a sense of friendship and comraderie. The inhabitants regulary comes together to work on larger projects.\nFrom time to time the group has been known to temporarly invite friends and travelers to live as citizens in the village, or to invite honorary citizens. People invited in this way do not have a vote when deciding issues that concern the citizenry, but they will of course listen to their input. Language use People of many ages inhabit the island, and the languages spoken most frequently are swedish and english. Regular chat regulations are naturally being followed, however the inhabitants wish to apologize beforehand to the non-swedish speakers that happen to pass by if they feel left out of the loop when swedish is being spoken.', '<p><b>Government</b>\n</p>\n<p>The combined group effort that today is known as BoS Island is not ruled by a single individual, such as a mayor, but instead is held together by a sense of friendship and comraderie. The inhabitants regulary comes together to work on larger projects.\nFrom time to time the group has been known to temporarly invite friends and travelers to live as citizens in the village, or to invite honorary citizens. People invited in this way do not have a vote when deciding issues that concern the citizenry, but they will of course listen to their input.\n</p>\n<p><b>Language use</b>\n</p>\n<p>People of many ages inhabit the island, and the languages spoken most frequently are swedish and english. Regular chat regulations are naturally being followed, however the inhabitants wish to apologize beforehand to the non-swedish speakers that happen to pass by if they feel left out of the loop when swedish is being spoken.\n</p>', 2),
(7788, 2122, 'History', 'History', 'As remembered by the inhabitants. The story of BoS actually starts without any of its current members, with a fellow by the name Amader who had been playing on and off for a long time on the Jenn-kellon Home server. He, in turn, attracted Solver to the game and Einnel, Daash, Theacke, Madboy, Rmt and Tottman were soon to follow. The site where we all settled down was dubbed Wolf Hill, due to the frequence of said lupine at the site, even though it was too close to Serenity Port for an actual deed to be planted without permission. We asked for that from the Serenity Port mayor, but were rudely denied and so eventually we packed up and left for other lands. Amader, together with his RL friend Madonna, went seperate ways from the rest of us and settled in the far north while the rest of us finally found ourselves at a tranquil bay in the south, approximately SSW of Mesa Verde, where we settled down and founded the Bay of Swedes . Bay of Swedes was the name of our community, as most of us wanted their own homestead deed and founded them seperately. With time, our reputation on the Home server grew and our gathering became widely known. During this time some of our members stopped playing, but most remained. Several ambitious projects were attempted, and some even completed ;), and by the end of its time the bay had been transformed into a lush park of walkways, flower fields and oak tree groves. With the advent of the Freedom server, and imminent closure of Home, the people of BoS packed up their bags and moved once more. Since we now had ships, the process was a bit easier this time. Arriving in freedom (09-06-17), we came upon a suitable island to the northeast of the main continent and swiftly claimed it as our own. This time we established a deed right away to cement our hold over the island. Since it wasn\'t an actual bay, we named it \"BoS island\" in honor of our past and the reputation it held. Time went by and we started to settle in, taming the area and mining caves in search of the treasured ores. This arrangement worked for a couple of weeks until opinions clashed and some of us decided to move and settle down near our old friend Riverboy(alt Lilbear). We started to make room for us and putting down our own deeds. Right about this time the concept of breeding was introduced in the game. As a result the numbers of wild animals decreased rapidly, and as such hunting became a dreary prospect indeed. So when the portals between freedom and wild opened up 09-10-22, some of us took the chance and used it. Almost completely empty of all gear when we arrived on the other side, we were met up by a couple of players that took us in. See BoS as HOTS . Nearly all of our members left for wild that day, leaving only Aske and Daash left on Freedom. Even though we\'ve branched on different servers, we are still one community and linked together.', '<p>As remembered by the inhabitants.\n</p>\n<p>The story of BoS actually starts without any of its current members, with a fellow by the name Amader who had been playing on and off for a long time on the Jenn-kellon Home server. He, in turn, attracted Solver to the game and Einnel, Daash, Theacke, Madboy, Rmt and Tottman were soon to follow. The site where we all settled down was dubbed Wolf Hill, due to the frequence of said lupine at the site, even though it was too close to Serenity Port for an actual deed to be planted without permission. We asked for that from the Serenity Port mayor, but were rudely denied and so eventually we packed up and left for other lands.\n</p>\n<p>Amader, together with his RL friend Madonna, went seperate ways from the rest of us and settled in the far north while the rest of us finally found ourselves at a tranquil bay in the south, approximately SSW of Mesa Verde, where we settled down and founded the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bay_of_Swedes\" title=\"Bay of Swedes\">Bay of Swedes</a>.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bay_of_Swedes\" title=\"Bay of Swedes\">Bay of Swedes</a> was the name of our community, as most of us wanted their own homestead deed and founded them seperately. With time, our reputation on the Home server grew and our gathering became widely known. During this time some of our members stopped playing, but most remained. Several ambitious projects were attempted, and some even completed ;), and by the end of its time the bay had been transformed into a lush park of walkways, flower fields and oak tree groves.\n</p>\n<p>With the advent of the Freedom server, and imminent closure of Home, the people of BoS packed up their bags and moved once more. Since we now had ships, the process was a bit easier this time. Arriving in freedom (09-06-17), we came upon a suitable island to the northeast of the main continent and swiftly claimed it as our own. This time we established a deed right away to cement our hold over the island. Since it wasn\'t an actual bay, we named it \"BoS island\" in honor of our past and the reputation it held.\n</p>\n<p>Time went by and we started to settle in, taming the area and mining caves in search of the treasured ores. This arrangement worked for a couple of weeks until opinions clashed and some of us decided to move and settle down near our old friend Riverboy(alt Lilbear). We started to make room for us and putting down our own deeds. Right about this time the concept of breeding was introduced in the game. As a result the numbers of wild animals decreased rapidly, and as such hunting became a dreary prospect indeed.\n</p>\n<p>So when the portals between freedom and wild opened up 09-10-22, some of us took the chance and used it. Almost completely empty of all gear when we arrived on the other side, we were met up by a couple of players that took us in. See <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/BoS_as_HOTS\" title=\"BoS as HOTS\">BoS as HOTS</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Nearly all of our members left for wild that day, leaving only <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Aske</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daash\" title=\"Player:Daash\">Daash</a> left on Freedom. Even though we\'ve branched on different servers, we are still one community and linked together.\n</p>', 3),
(7789, 2122, 'Village External Links', 'Village_External_Links', 'http://www.wurmonline.se', '<p><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.se\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.se</a>\n</p>', 4),
(7790, 2124, 'Byzantium', 'Byzantium', 'Founded in 1015 by Chewius, and expatriot of Jenn Kellon on the east side of Crystal Canal. Like its historical namesake, Byzantium lies on an important waterway and is at the crossroads of important trade routes in southern central Freedom Isle. There is a templar to keep out criminals and tower consripts to fend of beasts, making it a safe place to live. The village has grown into the largest in the canal area. view from Bearshark Overlook', '<p>Founded in 1015 by Chewius, and expatriot of Jenn Kellon on the east side of Crystal Canal. Like its historical namesake, Byzantium lies on an important waterway and is at the crossroads of important trade routes in southern central Freedom Isle. There is a templar to keep out criminals and tower consripts to fend of beasts, making it a safe place to live. The village has grown into the largest in the canal area.\n<img alt=\"wurm201108191748.jpg\" src=\"http://i1004.photobucket.com/albums/af169/chewius/wurm201108191748.jpg\"/>\nview from Bearshark Overlook\n</p>', 0),
(7791, 2124, 'Moonshine Bay', 'Moonshine_Bay', 'The colonial outpost of Byzantium on Deliverance.', '<p>The colonial outpost of Byzantium on Deliverance.\n</p>', 1),
(7792, 2124, 'Key buildings and facilities', 'Key_buildings_and_facilities', 'Foundry - close to the mine ramp and place for metal smithing and other crafting, storage for bulk materials Shipyard- on the bay beside the docks. A convenient place for building ships or offloading cargo. Mines- main mine down ramp from the foundry has iron copper and lead veins. 2nd mine along the shore with lead. The Barn - near the farmlands. Storage for food and materials, convenient location for crafting non metal items. Stables - field for village horses and cows and other non aggressive creatures. Cafe - house for cooking and food storage. Bazaar- facility for merchants. (Now moved to the canal side) 1 so far, anyone is welcome. Spirit cottage - at village plaza near the token (70) cast Trader - on sight, may need to ask for access.', '<ul><li>Foundry - close to the mine ramp and place for metal smithing and other crafting, storage for bulk materials</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Shipyard- on the bay beside the docks. A convenient place for building ships or offloading cargo.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Mines- main mine down ramp from the foundry has iron copper and lead veins. 2nd mine along the shore with lead.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The Barn - near the farmlands. Storage for food and materials, convenient location for crafting non metal items.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Stables - field for village horses and cows and other non aggressive creatures.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cafe - house for cooking and food storage.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Bazaar- facility for merchants. (Now moved to the canal side) 1 so far, anyone is welcome.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Spirit cottage - at village plaza near the token (70) cast</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Trader - on sight, may need to ask for access.</li></ul>', 2),
(7793, 2124, 'Resources', 'Resources', 'Important ores including iron and lead and copper are in on deed mine, we maintain tree farms and an almost completed island for controlled but open access to clay. We also have access to silver and tar. Growing cow and deer herds will provide meat and hides.', '<p>Important ores including iron and lead and copper are in on deed mine, we maintain tree farms and an almost completed \n</p>\n<p>island for controlled but open access to clay. We also have access to silver and tar. Growing cow and deer \n</p>\n<p>herds will provide meat and hides.\n</p>', 3),
(7794, 2124, 'Transportation', 'Transportation', 'By sea: Likely the easiest way to get to Byzantium for most people. From The Howel and Freedom Market via Freedom Harbor cross Crystal Lake southward to the canal. Can also be easily reached from the southern sea. By land: Road infrastructure in these parts is limited due to steep mountains across the canal though a main high way leads to Byzantium from Free Bears to the south and new roads are being made to connect with Avocano.', '<p>By sea: Likely the easiest way to get to Byzantium for most people. From The Howel and Freedom Market via Freedom\n</p>\n<p>Harbor cross Crystal Lake southward to the canal. Can also be easily reached from the southern sea.\n</p>\n<p>By land: Road infrastructure in these parts is limited due to steep mountains across the canal though a main high \n</p>\n<p>way leads to Byzantium from Free Bears to the south and new roads are being made to connect with Avocano.\n</p>', 4),
(7795, 2124, 'Recruiting, villagers and housing', 'Recruiting.2C_villagers_and_housing', 'We are welcoming any constructive players experienced or not. We just like to have a good time. You\'re welcome to help with village projects or do your own thing. There is good area for hunting nearby as well. While the village population grows there is plenty of room for individual housing if desired or room at the two inns if all you want is a bed and a chest.', '<p>We are welcoming any constructive players experienced or not. We just like to have a good time. You\'re welcome to \n</p>\n<p>help with village projects or do your own thing. There is good area for hunting nearby as well. While the village \n</p>\n<p>population grows there is plenty of room for individual housing if desired or room at the two inns if all you \n</p>\n<p>want is a bed and a chest.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm201106271709.jpg\" src=\"http://i1004.photobucket.com/albums/af169/chewius/wurm201106271709.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 5),
(7796, 2126, 'Description', 'Description', 'Carisann is Kinda New was found last year in November there is still alot to do in carisann\nwe accept new and old players and we have great members in carisann.', '<p>Carisann is Kinda New was found last year in November there is still alot to do in carisann\nwe accept new and old players and we have great members in carisann.\n</p>', 0),
(7797, 2126, 'Location', 'Location', 'We are Located a 28x 37y in between Elarial and Halcyon', '<p>We are Located a 28x 37y in between Elarial and Halcyon\n</p>', 1),
(7798, 2126, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Sethisles (Mayor) Delamr(Elder) Unknown', '<ul><li>Sethisles (Mayor)</li>\n<li>Delamr(Elder)</li>\n<li>Unknown</li></ul>', 2),
(7799, 2126, 'Old Citizens', 'Old_Citizens', 'Jellyman(IS BACK) Kalak (Inactivity) Cothdor (Inactivity) Thane (Inactivity) Clowny (Quit)', '<ul><li>Jellyman(IS BACK)</li>\n<li>Kalak (Inactivity)</li>\n<li>Cothdor (Inactivity)</li>\n<li>Thane (Inactivity)</li>\n<li>Clowny (Quit)</li></ul>', 3),
(7800, 2126, 'Recruitment', 'Recruitment', 'At the Moment we are recruiting people new or old.', '<p>At the Moment we are recruiting people new or old.\n</p>', 4),
(7801, 2126, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'Peir(Complete) Guard Tower(Complete) Farm(Unfinished) Barracks(Done) Storage(Done) Making Peir Longer(Unfinished) Workshop(Unfinished) Little Farms(Complete) Animal Pens(Complete) Kitchen(Complete) Warehouse(Unfinished) Armoury (Unfinished) Church (Unfinished) Colossus (Unfinished)', '<ul><li>Peir(Complete)</li>\n<li>Guard Tower(Complete)</li>\n<li>Farm(Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Barracks(Done)</li>\n<li>Storage(Done)</li>\n<li>Making Peir Longer(Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Workshop(Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Little Farms(Complete)</li>\n<li>Animal Pens(Complete)</li>\n<li>Kitchen(Complete)</li>\n<li>Warehouse(Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Armoury (Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Church (Unfinished)</li>\n<li>Colossus (Unfinished)</li></ul>', 5),
(7802, 2126, 'Features', 'Features', 'We Have Alot of Clay outside by the peir we have a clay workshop with bsb\'s and stuff also sand aswel!\nPublic Trader', '<p>We Have Alot of Clay outside by the peir we have a clay workshop with bsb\'s and stuff also sand aswel!\nPublic Trader\n</p>', 6),
(7803, 2126, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Coming Soon.', '<p>Coming Soon.\n</p>', 7),
(7804, 2126, 'Mine', 'Mine', 'He have a Private mine for villagers only and in that mine\nwe have Iron Silver Lead (: also a forge by 2 iron veins also we have a troll statue xD', '<p>He have a Private mine for villagers only and in that mine\nwe have Iron Silver Lead (: also a forge by 2 iron veins also we have a troll statue xD\n</p>', 8),
(7805, 2128, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'Cliff Side is a quaint little gem on the North coast overlooking the sea. Cliff Side was originally a Homestead created by Felthanne , but after the deed changes it became a village. The deed is of a multi-tiered design with 100 tiles of farm fields, multiple ondeed houses (with room for more), a large church, inn (with a visiting stables), and a building that houses our exports. Cliff Side has it\'s own village website ( http://www.cliffside.co ). Village History October 9th 2009 [20:09:39] It is 00:33:27 on Wrath day in week 4 of the starfall of Dancers in the year of 1000. [20:09:39] The homestead of Cliff Side has just been founded by Felthanne. Feburary 10th 2010 Expanded from a size 5 homestead to a size 12 village. August 15th 2010 Expanded from size 12 village to a size 16 village. November 26th 2010 Expanded from a size 16 village to a size 19 village. May 11th 2011 Expanded from a size 19 village to a size 20 village. Resources Water Clay (Few minutes away by foot or boat) Tar Sand Large Cave Iron Copper Gold Silver Lead Tin', '<ul><li>Cliff Side is a quaint little gem on the North coast overlooking the sea.</li>\n<li>Cliff Side was originally a Homestead created by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Felthanne\" title=\"Player:Felthanne\">Felthanne</a>, but after the deed changes it became a village.</li>\n<li>The deed is of a multi-tiered design with 100 tiles of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Farm\" title=\"Farm\">farm</a> fields, multiple ondeed houses (with room for more), a large church, inn (with a visiting stables), and a building that houses our exports.</li>\n<li>Cliff Side has it\'s own village website (<a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.cliffside.co\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.cliffside.co</a>).</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_History\">Village History</span></h3>\n<ul><li>October 9th 2009\n<ul><li>[20:09:39] It is 00:33:27 on Wrath day in week 4 of the starfall of Dancers in the year of 1000.</li>\n<li>[20:09:39] The homestead of Cliff Side has just been founded by Felthanne.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li>Feburary 10th 2010\n<ul><li>Expanded from a size 5 homestead to a size 12 village.</li></ul></li>\n<li>August 15th 2010\n<ul><li>Expanded from size 12 village to a size 16 village.</li></ul></li>\n<li>November 26th 2010\n<ul><li>Expanded from a size 16 village to a size 19 village.</li></ul></li>\n<li>May 11th 2011\n<ul><li>Expanded from a size 19 village to a size 20 village.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Water</li>\n<li>Clay (Few minutes away by foot or boat)</li>\n<li>Tar</li>\n<li>Sand</li>\n<li>Large Cave\n<ul><li>Iron</li>\n<li>Copper</li>\n<li>Gold</li>\n<li>Silver</li>\n<li>Lead</li>\n<li>Tin</li></ul></li></ul>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(7806, 2128, 'Village Recruitment', 'Village_Recruitment', 'Village Recruitment Status: Open Recruiting Instructions If you would like to become a citizen of Cliff Side please PM Felthanne via the forums ( Here ) or in-game. Alternatively you could visit our website and post on our forums here . Village Rules All Village rules are on the our village website. Village Members Chancellor Felthanne Senator Leader Jpiolho Senators Skrrp Yasgur Equestrians Tds Citizens Updated: Sept. 7th 2014 Sashy Davinton Losty Xtigermanx Sangraff Stubbsfield Projects Projects Undertaken Cliff Side Farm Completed Projects Cliff Side Cooking Guild Guard Tower Comprehensive remodeling. Future Projects Colossi And a bunch of others!', '<div align=\"center\">\n<table style=\"border:2px solid Black; -moz-border-radius:10px; text-align:left; background: #EE8\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"background: #EE8; padding: 0.2em; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 1.5em; text-align:center;\">Village Recruitment Status: <b>Open Recruiting</b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div align=\"left\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Instructions\">Instructions</span></h3>\n<ul><li>If you would like to become a citizen of Cliff Side please PM Felthanne via the forums (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?action=pm;sa=send;u=7945%7CClick\" rel=\"nofollow\">Here</a>) or in-game.</li>\n<li>Alternatively you could visit our website and post on our forums <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.cliffside.co/\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Rules\">Village Rules</span></h3>\n<ul><li>All Village rules are on the our village website.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Members\">Village Members</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chancellor\">Chancellor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Felthanne\" title=\"Player:Felthanne\">Felthanne</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Senator_Leader\">Senator Leader</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jpiolho\" title=\"Player:Jpiolho\">Jpiolho</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Senators\">Senators</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Player:Skrrp&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Player:Skrrp (page does not exist)\">Skrrp</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Yasgur\" title=\"Player:Yasgur\">Yasgur</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equestrians\">Equestrians</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Player:Tds&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Player:Tds (page does not exist)\">Tds</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p>Updated: Sept. 7th 2014\n</p>\n<ul><li>Sashy</li>\n<li>Davinton</li>\n<li>Losty</li>\n<li>Xtigermanx</li>\n<li>Sangraff</li>\n<li>Stubbsfield</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects\">Projects</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects_Undertaken\">Projects Undertaken</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Cliff Side Farm</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed_Projects\">Completed Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Cliff Side Cooking Guild</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Guard_Tower\" title=\"Guard Tower\">Guard Tower</a></li>\n<li>Comprehensive remodeling.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Future_Projects\">Future Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Colossi</li>\n<li>And a bunch of others!</li></ul></div></div>', 1),
(7807, 2128, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Chancellor Felthanne Senator Leader Jpiolho Senators Skrrp Yasgur Equestrians Tds Citizens Updated: Sept. 7th 2014 Sashy Davinton Losty Xtigermanx Sangraff Stubbsfield', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chancellor\">Chancellor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Felthanne\" title=\"Player:Felthanne\">Felthanne</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Senator_Leader\">Senator Leader</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Jpiolho\" title=\"Player:Jpiolho\">Jpiolho</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Senators\">Senators</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Player:Skrrp&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Player:Skrrp (page does not exist)\">Skrrp</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Yasgur\" title=\"Player:Yasgur\">Yasgur</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equestrians\">Equestrians</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Player:Tds&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Player:Tds (page does not exist)\">Tds</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p>Updated: Sept. 7th 2014\n</p>\n<ul><li>Sashy</li>\n<li>Davinton</li>\n<li>Losty</li>\n<li>Xtigermanx</li>\n<li>Sangraff</li>\n<li>Stubbsfield</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7808, 2128, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'Projects Undertaken Cliff Side Farm Completed Projects Cliff Side Cooking Guild Guard Tower Comprehensive remodeling. Future Projects Colossi And a bunch of others!', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects_Undertaken\">Projects Undertaken</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Cliff Side Farm</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed_Projects\">Completed Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Cliff Side Cooking Guild</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Guard_Tower\" title=\"Guard Tower\">Guard Tower</a></li>\n<li>Comprehensive remodeling.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Future_Projects\">Future Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Colossi</li>\n<li>And a bunch of others!</li></ul>', 3),
(7809, 2129, 'Village History', 'Village_History', 'September 6th 2010 [14:53:24] It is 08:50:16 on day of Awakening in week 4 of the starfall of Fires in the year of 1008. [14:53:24] The settlement of Cliff Side Port has just been founded by Offe.', '<ul><li>September 6th 2010\n<ul><li>[14:53:24] It is 08:50:16 on day of Awakening in week 4 of the starfall of Fires in the year of 1008.</li>\n<li>[14:53:24] The settlement of Cliff Side Port has just been founded by Offe.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(7810, 2129, 'Miscellaneous', 'Miscellaneous', 'Home of the Cliff Side Cooking Guild If interested in storing your boat here, please contact Felthanne ingame or via the forums.', '<ul><li>Home of the Cliff Side Cooking Guild</li>\n<li>If interested in storing your boat here, please contact Felthanne ingame or via the forums.</li></ul>', 1),
(7811, 2130, 'Village History', 'Village_History', 'August 17th 2011 [19:18:30] It is 01:34:32 on day of Awakening in week 3 of the starfall of Dancers in the year of 1016. [19:18:30] The settlement of Cliff Side Suburbs has just been founded by Alfansor. Has been disbanded due to lack of new villagers.', '<ul><li>August 17th 2011\n<ul><li>[19:18:30] It is 01:34:32 on day of Awakening in week 3 of the starfall of Dancers in the year of 1016.</li>\n<li>[19:18:30] The settlement of Cliff Side Suburbs has just been founded by Alfansor.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>Has been disbanded due to lack of new villagers.\n</p>', 0),
(7812, 2130, 'Miscellaneous', 'Miscellaneous', 'All houses are owned by villagers of Cliff Side', '<ul><li>All houses are owned by villagers of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cliff_Side\" title=\"Cliff Side\">Cliff Side</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7813, 2131, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'Coast of death is a fairly new settlement and we already have a great group of villagers which work as a awesome team! The settlement is slowly coming along and already starting some of the main features of our village. Still much work to be done, best get cracking! At the time being the settlement size is only 20 I believe, I will be expanding the settlement size as soon as I the money to afford it. Coast of Death is located just South-West of Nyrada (14x - 36y) on the map. Village creation [00:41:37] It is 22:06:43 on day of Sleep in week 2 of the starfall of the Digging in the year of 1012. [00:41:37] The settlement of Coast Of Death has just been founded by Deathrow. Resources Water Clay (Few minutes away by foot or boat) Tar Sand Small Cave Iron Copper (Across the lake)', '<ul><li>Coast of death is a fairly new <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settlements\" title=\"Settlements\">settlement</a> and we already have a great group of villagers which work as a awesome team! The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settlements\" title=\"Settlements\">settlement</a> is slowly coming along and already starting some of the main features of our village. Still much work to be done, best get cracking!</li>\n<li>At the time being the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settlements\" title=\"Settlements\">settlement</a> size is only 20 I believe, I will be expanding the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settlements\" title=\"Settlements\">settlement</a> size as soon as I the money to afford it.</li>\n<li>Coast of Death is located just South-West of <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_settlement\" title=\"Undefined settlement\">Nyrada</a> (14x - 36y) on the map.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_creation\">Village creation</span></h3>\n<ul><li>[00:41:37] It is 22:06:43 on day of Sleep in week 2 of the starfall of the Digging in the year of 1012.\n<ul><li>[00:41:37] The settlement of Coast Of Death has just been founded by Deathrow.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Water</li>\n<li>Clay (Few minutes away by foot or boat)</li>\n<li>Tar</li>\n<li>Sand</li>\n<li>Small Cave\n<ul><li>Iron\n<ul><li>Copper (Across the lake)</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>', 0),
(7814, 2131, 'Village Recruitment', 'Village_Recruitment', 'Village Recruitment Status: Not Recruiting. Instructions If you would like to become a citizen of Coast of Death please PM DeathRow via the forums( Here ) or in-game. Coast of Death is a friendly community and we would like to see all new recruits get along with all current villagers (This does apply to current villagers getting along with new recruits). Village Rules Village Language: English only please. Respect all villagers/locals. Respect all villagers property (No Stealing!). All i can think off for now :D. Village Members Mayor DeathRow - [Troll Slayer] Co-Mayor BlackFox Village Elder Twinsen - [Troll Slayer] , [Digger] Citizens Ninja Duck Eighters Gdwrules Kresyffert Seveners Binglek Odkrywca Projects Projects Undertaken Lower Village Area (Half complete) Upper Village Area Docks Farm Land Completed Projects Future Projects Colossus Guard Tower Animal Pens Inn Altars Mail Box Merchants', '<div align=\"center\">\n<table style=\"border:2px solid Black; -moz-border-radius:10px; text-align:left; background: #EE8\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"background: #EE8; padding: 0.2em; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 1.5em; text-align:center;\">Village Recruitment Status: <b>Not Recruiting.</b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div align=\"left\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Instructions\">Instructions</span></h3>\n<ul><li>If you would like to become a citizen of Coast of Death please PM DeathRow via the forums(<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?action=pm;sa=send;u=7945%7CClick\" rel=\"nofollow\">Here</a>) or in-game.</li>\n<li>Coast of Death is a friendly community and we would like to see all new recruits get along with all current villagers (This does apply to current villagers getting along with new recruits).</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Rules\">Village Rules</span></h3>\n<ol><li>Village Language: English only please.</li>\n<li>Respect all villagers/locals.</li>\n<li>Respect all villagers property (No Stealing!).</li>\n<li>All i can think off for now :D.</li></ol>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Members\">Village Members</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:DeathRow\" title=\"Player:DeathRow\">DeathRow</a> - <b>[Troll Slayer]</b></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Co-Mayor\">Co-Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li>BlackFox</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Elder\">Village Elder</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Twinsen\" title=\"Player:Twinsen\">Twinsen</a> - <b>[Troll Slayer]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Ninja Duck</li>\n<li>Eighters</li>\n<li>Gdwrules</li>\n<li>Kresyffert</li>\n<li>Seveners</li>\n<li>Binglek</li>\n<li>Odkrywca</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects\">Projects</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects_Undertaken\">Projects Undertaken</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Lower Village Area (Half complete)</li>\n<li>Upper Village Area</li>\n<li>Docks</li>\n<li>Farm Land</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed_Projects\">Completed Projects</span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Future_Projects\">Future Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Colossus</li>\n<li>Guard Tower</li>\n<li>Animal Pens</li>\n<li>Inn</li>\n<li>Altars</li>\n<li>Mail Box</li>\n<li>Merchants</li></ul></div></div>', 1),
(7815, 2131, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Mayor DeathRow - [Troll Slayer] Co-Mayor BlackFox Village Elder Twinsen - [Troll Slayer] , [Digger] Citizens Ninja Duck Eighters Gdwrules Kresyffert Seveners Binglek Odkrywca', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:DeathRow\" title=\"Player:DeathRow\">DeathRow</a> - <b>[Troll Slayer]</b></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Co-Mayor\">Co-Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li>BlackFox</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Elder\">Village Elder</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Twinsen\" title=\"Player:Twinsen\">Twinsen</a> - <b>[Troll Slayer]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Ninja Duck</li>\n<li>Eighters</li>\n<li>Gdwrules</li>\n<li>Kresyffert</li>\n<li>Seveners</li>\n<li>Binglek</li>\n<li>Odkrywca</li></ul>', 2),
(7816, 2131, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'Projects Undertaken Lower Village Area (Half complete) Upper Village Area Docks Farm Land Completed Projects Future Projects Colossus Guard Tower Animal Pens Inn Altars Mail Box Merchants', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects_Undertaken\">Projects Undertaken</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Lower Village Area (Half complete)</li>\n<li>Upper Village Area</li>\n<li>Docks</li>\n<li>Farm Land</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed_Projects\">Completed Projects</span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Future_Projects\">Future Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Colossus</li>\n<li>Guard Tower</li>\n<li>Animal Pens</li>\n<li>Inn</li>\n<li>Altars</li>\n<li>Mail Box</li>\n<li>Merchants</li></ul>', 3),
(7817, 2132, 'Description', 'Description', 'Coeurebene is a small village currently inhabited by Tymst and Aiwelin.\nThe village is under construction and only consist of a small warehouse, a shipyard, two farms and an animal pen at the moment.', '<p><b>Coeurebene</b> is a small village currently inhabited by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Tymst\" title=\"User:Tymst\">Tymst</a> and Aiwelin.\nThe village is under construction and only consist of a small warehouse, a shipyard, two farms and an animal pen at the moment.\n</p>', 0),
(7818, 2132, 'Position', 'Position', 'The village is situated in the south of Independence, north of Raven\'s wood , south of Sheerfall and east of Woodbank.', '<p>The village is situated in the south of Independence, north of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Raven%27s_wood\" title=\"Raven\'s wood\">Raven\'s wood</a>, south of Sheerfall and east of Woodbank.\n</p>', 1),
(7819, 2132, 'Production', 'Production', 'We\'re currently building some boat to launch a business.', '<p>We\'re currently building some boat to launch a business.\n</p>', 2),
(7820, 2135, 'Village information', 'Village_information', 'Location 40x, 31y\nBudding Village, Hiring new players. We supply a 6x10 tile location that is yours to do with what you want. We have 4 jobs. Wall maintenance, Digging, Farming, and Fishing/Hunting. While you are trying to figure out what you want to do in game. We provide a Cart with tools that help you in which ever you choose to do. For the best information contact Rebmac, but also reachable is Amiti (his wife) or Lanaya. Master Carpenter: Kathnelakr Master Ship builder: Kathnelakr Fo Priest: Amiti Mag Priest: TotalDarkness Vyn Priest: TeraLynn Master Blacksmith: Master Hunter/fighter: Amiti Master Farmer: Teralynn Master Cook: Amiti (more jobs available)', '<p>Location 40x, 31y\nBudding Village, Hiring new players. We supply a 6x10 tile location that is yours to do with what you want. We have 4 jobs. Wall maintenance, Digging, Farming, and Fishing/Hunting. While you are trying to figure out what you want to do in game. We provide a Cart with tools that help you in which ever you choose to do.\n</p>\n<p>For the best information contact Rebmac, but also reachable is Amiti (his wife) or Lanaya.\n</p>\n<p>Master Carpenter: Kathnelakr                  \n</p>\n<p>Master Ship builder: Kathnelakr\n</p>\n<p>Fo Priest: Amiti\n</p>\n<p>Mag Priest: TotalDarkness\n</p>\n<p>Vyn Priest: TeraLynn\n</p>\n<p>Master Blacksmith:\n</p>\n<p>Master Hunter/fighter: Amiti\n</p>\n<p>Master Farmer: Teralynn\n</p>\n<p>Master Cook: Amiti\n</p>\n<p>(more jobs available)\n</p>', 0),
(7821, 2135, 'Jobs', 'Jobs', 'While living in our village is free, we do ask that one of 4 jobs is done. These jobs are currently Wall Maintenance, Digging, Farming/Animal maintenance and Fishing/Hunting. Wall Maintenance, You\'re responsible for the improvement, and repair of stone, or wood walls/fences. This also includes mining rock shards, and cutting bricks according to the master miner\'s plans. If you do a good enough job, you will also be entrusted with the building/planning of new walls. Digging: You\'re responsible for digging clay/tar/dirt and sand. Mostly Tar will be the #1 need, with Clay and sand coming a close second. Dirt will only be needed if an area needs flattened. Farming/Animal maintenance. Under direction you will be given a section of farm to watch over, make sure it\'s farmed, / weeded, and if anything needs harvested, you alert a harvester (Amiti or Lanaya currently). Tending to the animals can be done at any time, making sure food is on the ground for pigs/dogs/hens, and all the animals that can be groomed are. Fishing/Hunting: You will be given tools of the trade, fishing is a pole and a cart to drag the fish around in. Hunting is armor/weapons, and either a hunting party, or if you wish to go it alone, then a prayer and some bandages. Your main goal is to bring meat back so we all get good quality meals. Each job is easy to do for beginners (maybe not hunting) and will work those basic skills up that either require you to build something or work on something. All we require is an hour each log in, work on a section, say in village chat which section you\'re working and what you\'re doing (which will get checked) after that you are free to do what you wish.', '<p>While living in our village is free, we do ask that one of 4 jobs is done. These jobs are currently Wall Maintenance, Digging, Farming/Animal maintenance and Fishing/Hunting.\n</p>\n<p>Wall Maintenance, You\'re responsible for the improvement, and repair of stone, or wood walls/fences. This also includes mining rock shards, and cutting bricks according to the master miner\'s plans. If you do a good enough job, you will also be entrusted with the building/planning of new walls.\n</p>\n<p>Digging: You\'re responsible for digging clay/tar/dirt and sand. Mostly Tar will be the #1 need, with Clay and sand coming a close second. Dirt will only be needed if an area needs flattened.\n</p>\n<p>Farming/Animal maintenance. Under direction you will be given a section of farm to watch over, make sure it\'s farmed, / weeded, and if anything needs harvested, you alert a harvester (Amiti or Lanaya currently). Tending to the animals can be done at any time, making sure food is on the ground for pigs/dogs/hens, and all the animals that can be groomed are.\n</p>\n<p>Fishing/Hunting: You will be given tools of the trade, fishing is a pole and a cart to drag the fish around in. Hunting is armor/weapons, and either a hunting party, or if you wish to go it alone, then a prayer and some bandages. Your main goal is to bring meat back so we all get good quality meals.\n</p>\n<p>Each job is easy to do for beginners (maybe not hunting) and will work those basic skills up that either require you to build something or work on something. All we require is an hour each log in, work on a section, say in village chat which section you\'re working and what you\'re doing (which will get checked) after that you are free to do what you wish.\n</p>', 1),
(7822, 2135, 'Tasks to complete', 'Tasks_to_complete', 'Flatten slums Mine path from upper to lower mine Finish walls west side Flatten tar road/create fence for back of farm to tar (Remove back farm wall, raise road, rebuild back farm wall with fence at tar) Repair/ Imp all walls Create carts and tools for new villagers Open recruitment for villagers who are willing to do a job. We have a Team Speak Server, and are active when speaking.', '<ol><li>Flatten slums</li>\n<li>Mine path from upper to lower mine</li>\n<li>Finish walls west side</li>\n<li>Flatten tar road/create fence for back of farm to tar (Remove back farm wall, raise road, rebuild back farm wall with fence at tar)</li>\n<li>Repair/ Imp all walls</li>\n<li>Create carts and tools for new villagers</li></ol>\n<p>Open recruitment for villagers who are willing to do a job.\n</p>\n<p>We have a Team Speak Server, and are active when speaking.\n</p>', 2),
(7823, 2136, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'Dannebro is a small village created by Xquizen and the village is still under construction...', '<p>Dannebro is a small village created by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xquizen\" title=\"Player:Xquizen\">Xquizen</a> and the village is still under construction...\n</p>', 0),
(7824, 2136, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Mayor Xquizen Village Elder Arvenn Citizens Roack Belmek', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xquizen\" title=\"Player:Xquizen\">Xquizen</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Village_Elder\">Village Elder</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Arvenn\" title=\"Player:Arvenn\">Arvenn</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Roack\" title=\"Player:Roack\">Roack</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Belmek\" title=\"Player:Belmek\">Belmek</a></li></ul>', 1),
(7825, 2139, 'Canal History', 'Canal_History', 'Was the first major canal project undertaken on the Freedom Isles. Allowing passage to the center of the map for hundreds of settlers. The Darkenstone Canal deed was placed during the server\'s opening day on June 17th, 2009 at coords 28x,17y. The village of Darkenstone has relocated several times to different areas of the server. Was primarily constructed and cared for by Aureate from 2009 to 2013. The canal underwent some major remodeling in 2012. Early days of the Darkenstone Canal in late 2009. Darkenstone Canal in Aug 2013.', '<ul><li>Was the first major canal project undertaken on the Freedom Isles. Allowing passage to the center of the map for hundreds of settlers.</li>\n<li>The Darkenstone Canal deed was placed during the server\'s opening day on June 17th, 2009 at coords 28x,17y.</li>\n<li>The village of Darkenstone has relocated several times to different areas of the server.</li>\n<li>Was primarily constructed and cared for by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Aureate\" title=\"Player:Aureate\">Aureate</a> from 2009 to 2013.</li>\n<li>The canal underwent some major remodeling in 2012.</li></ul>\n<p>Early days of the Darkenstone Canal in late 2009.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm200907101017.jpg\" src=\"http://i201.photobucket.com/albums/aa211/Persephon/Wurm/wurm200907101017.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p>Darkenstone Canal in Aug 2013.\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"canal2013_zps270c2d5e.jpg\" src=\"http://i201.photobucket.com/albums/aa211/Persephon/Wurm/canal2013_zps270c2d5e.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 0),
(7826, 2140, 'Please don\'t edit with out first talking to Zachariah', 'Please_don.27t_edit_with_out_first_talking_to_Zachariah', '', '', 0),
(7827, 2140, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'Dawnstar is a new settlement established on January 19, 2014. Took over a preexisting deed named Apple Valley. We are located in the Freedom Isle cluster on The Celebration server. On the map we are located at 5x and 22y. The northern coast of the Median Isle island. We like to think that Dawnstar is a place of learning. We are very enthusiastic about inviting new players to our village. We are very tolerant with followings of all the deities. But we do not tolerate trolls. If you troll you will be put on the KOS list. We have a full functioning guard tower that will attack upon request, as well. The village is abundant with many fresh tall oak trees. We also have many helpful resources on the deed and a full dock.', '<p>Dawnstar is a new settlement established on January 19, 2014. Took over a preexisting deed named Apple Valley.\n</p>\n<p>We are located in the Freedom Isle cluster on The Celebration server. On the map we are located at 5x and 22y. The northern coast of the Median Isle island. \n</p>\n<p>We like to think that Dawnstar is a place of learning. We are very enthusiastic about inviting new players to our village. We are very tolerant with followings of all the deities. But we do not tolerate trolls. If you troll you will be put on the KOS list. We have a full functioning guard tower that will attack upon request, as well.\n</p>\n<p>The village is abundant with many fresh tall oak trees. We also have many helpful resources on the deed and a full dock. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(7828, 2140, 'Important People', 'Important_People', 'Mayor -Edircka', '<ul><li><b>Mayor</b>-Edircka</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7829, 2140, 'Motto and beliefs', 'Motto_and_beliefs', 'Friends welcome enemies too..........as long as you are dead. We like to believe that Dawnstar is a place of learning. We like to teach new players how to work Wurm and how to survive. Then we give them the reigns and they go from there.', '<p>Friends welcome enemies too..........as long as you are dead. \n</p>\n<p>We like to believe that Dawnstar is a place of learning. We like to teach new players how to work Wurm and how to survive. Then we give them the reigns and they go from there.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(7830, 2140, 'Local Laws', 'Local_Laws', 'Allies MAY NOT do the following within the settlement limits Picking up items that do not belong to you is considered theft and will be punished Build Cut down trees Expand the settlement Farm fields Hire guards Invite other people to be citizens Lock fence and wall gates Decide what is on this list Mine Pass any locked fence Dig, flatten, level, and pack Ally! You MAY, however, do the following within the city limits Fish Everything else Citizens you MAY NOT do the following within the city limits Destroy houses, fences, and walls Hire guards Invite other people to become citizens Decide what is on this list Citizens you MAY, however, do the following within the city limits Build Cut down trees Cut down old trees Expand the settlement Farm fields Lock fences and wall gates Mine Fish Dig, flatten, level, and pack Note: City officials may have other permissions', '<p><b>Allies MAY NOT do the following within the settlement limits</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Picking up items that do not belong to you is considered theft and will be punished</li>\n<li>Build</li>\n<li>Cut down trees</li>\n<li>Expand the settlement</li>\n<li>Farm fields</li>\n<li>Hire guards</li>\n<li>Invite other people to be citizens</li>\n<li>Lock fence and wall gates</li>\n<li>Decide what is on this list</li>\n<li>Mine</li>\n<li>Pass any locked fence</li>\n<li>Dig, flatten, level, and pack</li></ul>\n<p><b>Ally! You MAY, however, do the following within the city limits</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Fish</li>\n<li>Everything else</li></ul>\n<p><b>Citizens you MAY NOT do the following within the city limits</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Destroy houses, fences, and walls</li>\n<li>Hire guards</li>\n<li>Invite other people to become citizens</li>\n<li>Decide what is on this list</li></ul>\n<p><b>Citizens you MAY, however, do the following within the city limits</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Build</li>\n<li>Cut down trees</li>\n<li>Cut down old trees</li>\n<li>Expand the settlement</li>\n<li>Farm fields</li>\n<li>Lock fences and wall gates</li>\n<li>Mine</li>\n<li>Fish</li>\n<li>Dig, flatten, level, and pack</li></ul>\n<p><b>Note: City officials may have other permissions</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(7831, 2140, 'Allies', 'Allies', 'We are in The Misfits alliance. The alliance consists of: Amish Paradise Awsomesaucia Bio Dome Dawnstar Dragonstone Castle Enlightenment Flopper\'s Farm Greenville Hilltop Jotunheimr Kynesgrove Lake Placid Le Mons Pledge Misfit Market Mountain Top Mountain View Northern Awsomesaucia Nova Port Pax Le Mons Schadenfreude Hamlet Stormwind Sunrise Bay The Greenhouse The Silver Dollar Pub Tinman Tinmann Vanaheimr Verdian City Vista Point Whitewolf Watch Subject to change', '<p>We are in The Misfits alliance. \n</p>\n<p>The alliance consists of:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Amish Paradise</li>\n<li>Awsomesaucia</li>\n<li>Bio Dome</li>\n<li>Dawnstar</li>\n<li>Dragonstone Castle</li>\n<li>Enlightenment</li>\n<li>Flopper\'s Farm</li>\n<li>Greenville</li>\n<li>Hilltop</li>\n<li>Jotunheimr</li>\n<li>Kynesgrove</li>\n<li>Lake Placid</li>\n<li>Le Mons Pledge</li>\n<li>Misfit Market</li>\n<li>Mountain Top</li>\n<li>Mountain View</li>\n<li>Northern Awsomesaucia</li>\n<li>Nova Port</li>\n<li>Pax Le Mons</li>\n<li>Schadenfreude Hamlet</li>\n<li>Stormwind</li>\n<li>Sunrise Bay</li>\n<li>The Greenhouse</li>\n<li>The Silver Dollar Pub</li>\n<li>Tinman</li>\n<li>Tinmann</li>\n<li>Vanaheimr</li>\n<li>Verdian City</li>\n<li>Vista Point</li>\n<li>Whitewolf Watch</li></ul>\n<p><i>Subject to change</i>\n</p>', 5),
(7832, 2140, 'Pictures of around the deed', 'Pictures_of_around_the_deed', 'Bellow are a few pictures of around the settlement followed by a brief description: This is our big field located on deed. We allow all citizens to farm on said field and this is also were we store livestock (ie. horses, cows, bulls, etc.) This is the main entrance from the docks. This is a front view of the main entrance and the docks. This is a picture of the guard tower on deed. So there is a highly functioning guard tower that will help you upon request. This is just one of the many fully gown oaks on the deed. We ask please don\'t cut them down. This is a picture of the workshop available to all citizens. As you can see shown by the person (unknown) working in front of it. Please come and visit or stay for a while it doesn\'t matter Information that precedes is subject to change. -- Zachariah ( talk ) 15:10, 29 January 2014 (CET)', '<p>Bellow are a few pictures of around the settlement followed by a brief description:\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Feild.jpg\"><img alt=\"Feild.jpg\" data-file-height=\"471\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"471\" src=\"/images/b/bb/Feild.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is our big field located on deed. We allow all citizens to farm on said field and this is also were we store livestock (ie. horses, cows, bulls, etc.)</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Front_Gate.jpg\"><img alt=\"Front Gate.jpg\" data-file-height=\"472\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"472\" src=\"/images/d/dd/Front_Gate.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is the main entrance from the docks.</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Front.jpg\"><img alt=\"Front.jpg\" data-file-height=\"471\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"471\" src=\"/images/7/70/Front.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is a front view of the main entrance and the docks.</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Guard_Tower.jpg\"><img alt=\"Guard Tower.jpg\" data-file-height=\"471\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"471\" src=\"/images/6/62/Guard_Tower.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is a picture of the guard tower on deed. So there is a highly functioning guard tower that will help you upon request.</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Oak.jpg\"><img alt=\"Oak.jpg\" data-file-height=\"472\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"472\" src=\"/images/9/9a/Oak.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is just one of the many fully gown oaks on the deed. We ask please don\'t cut them down.</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Working_Community.jpg\"><img alt=\"Working Community.jpg\" data-file-height=\"471\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"471\" src=\"/images/0/08/Working_Community.jpg\" width=\"800\"/></a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is a picture of the workshop available to all citizens. As you can see shown by the person (unknown) working in front of it.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\nPlease come and visit or stay for a while it doesn\'t matter \n</p>\n<p><b>Information that precedes is subject to change.</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>--<a href=\"/index.php/User:Zachariah\" title=\"User:Zachariah\">Zachariah</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/User_talk:Zachariah\" title=\"User talk:Zachariah\">talk</a>) 15:10, 29 January 2014 (CET)\n</p>', 6),
(7833, 2143, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold = Title Mayor: Staticcling - [Trollslayer] Currently working Villagers Yela Located just East of PCG Freedom Village', '<p><b>Bold</b> = Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor:\">Mayor:</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Staticcling\" title=\"Player:Staticcling\">Staticcling</a> - <b>[Trollslayer]</b></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_working_Villagers\">Currently working Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Yela\" title=\"Player:Yela\">Yela</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\nLocated just East of PCG Freedom Village\n</p>', 0),
(7834, 2144, 'Background Stuff', 'Background_Stuff', 'a village (4 cool ppl n stuf)', '<p>a village (4 cool ppl n stuf)\n</p>', 0),
(7835, 2144, 'Roster n Stuff', 'Roster_n_Stuff', 'classified', '<p>classified\n</p>', 1),
(7836, 2144, 'more stuff', 'more_stuff', 'this section wasn\'t needed', '<p>this section wasn\'t needed\n</p>', 2),
(7847, 2148, 'Description', 'Description', 'Echelon is located on a small to medium Island in the Southwestern Section of Freedom, called Seris Isle, unofficially it is termed Black Pearl island. There is no \"mountain\" on Seris Isle, but it is lucky enough to be volcanically formed so rock is right under the soil layer. The deed is lucky enough to have an ondeed mine with a current Ironvein count of 8. There is also Lead, Zinc and Copper detected on the island. It also has a few spawns on the island along with a wide mixture of trees and clay. The main feature of the island is the smallest Volcano on Freedom which has yet to spawn any Fiends to date. New or experienced players will find a place for themselves in our community and there is room for any kind of player with projects regularly cropping up.', '<p>Echelon is located on a small to medium Island in the Southwestern Section of Freedom, called Seris Isle, unofficially it is termed Black Pearl island. There is no \"mountain\" on Seris Isle, but it is lucky enough to be volcanically formed so rock is right under the soil layer. The deed is lucky enough to have an ondeed mine with a current Ironvein count of 8. There is also Lead, Zinc and Copper detected on the island. It also has a few spawns on the island along with a wide mixture of trees and clay. The main feature of the island is the smallest Volcano on Freedom which has yet to spawn any Fiends to date. New or experienced players will find a place for themselves in our community and there is room for any kind of player with projects regularly cropping up.\n</p>', 0),
(7848, 2148, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold = Title Mayor: Xzalander Currently working Villagers Xzalander Active Villagers in their own sub-deeds Currently In-Active Villagers', '<p><b>Bold</b> = Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor:\">Mayor:</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Xzalander</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_working_Villagers\">Currently working Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Xzalander</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Active_Villagers_in_their_own_sub-deeds\">Active Villagers in their own sub-deeds</span></h4>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_In-Active_Villagers\">Currently In-Active Villagers</span></h4>', 1),
(7849, 2148, 'Village Projects', 'Village_Projects', 'Round T\'World The first project initiated, which is to be completed in four to five parts. Part One is complete but is currently being held back until Part Two is nearing completion. \nLike most this is a sailing round the world trip, but with in person interviews at large, popular and well known towns and villages. Currently Visited Locations Xanadu The Academy Of Enlightenment New Brovegas Akhenaten New Eminence Next Planned Area Freebears The Elysian Bay The Dark Citadel Project is on hold. WANTED: Reporters for the Round T\'World Project. The Colossus Shrine The Colossus Shrine Planning Thread This second project is still in the planning phase and has yet to begin construction. It is designed to be a tall spire which plateaus into a ring of land with a raised centre. On each compass point will be constructed a Colossi. The raised centre will most likely be a viewing area with all three Prayer Altars. Contributions in planning and eventual construction is appreciated and on deed support for food, bed and water will be provided for contributors.', '<h3><span id=\"Round_T\'World\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Round_T.27World\">Round T\'World</span></h3>\n<p>The first project initiated, which is to be completed in four to five parts. Part One is complete but is currently being held back until Part Two is nearing completion. \nLike most this is a sailing round the world trip, but with <b>in person interviews</b> at large, popular and well known towns and villages.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_Visited_Locations\">Currently Visited Locations</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Xanadu</li>\n<li>The Academy Of Enlightenment</li>\n<li>New Brovegas</li>\n<li>Akhenaten</li>\n<li>New Eminence</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Next_Planned_Area\">Next Planned Area</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Freebears</li>\n<li>The Elysian Bay</li>\n<li>The Dark Citadel</li></ul>\n<p><b>Project is on hold.</b>\n<b>WANTED:</b> Reporters for the Round T\'World Project. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Colossus_Shrine\">The Colossus Shrine</span></h3>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=39568.msg380167#%20msg380167\" rel=\"nofollow\">The Colossus Shrine Planning Thread</a> <br/>\nThis second project is still in the planning phase and has yet to begin construction. It is designed to be a tall spire which plateaus into a ring of land with a raised centre. On each compass point will be constructed a Colossi. The raised centre will most likely be a viewing area with all three Prayer Altars.\n</p>\n<p>Contributions in planning and eventual construction is appreciated and on deed support for food, bed and water will be provided for contributors.\n</p>', 2),
(7850, 2149, 'First Age', 'First_Age', 'Location 33-35y - 27-29x. 37y, 24x Elarial was a consortium settlement founded on the coast of Dragon Fang mountain on the Independence server. It consisted of \"Elarial, Elarial Heights, Elarial Harbor, Hillside, Elarial gardens, and Elarial Island Retreat\". Construction plans for Elarial included a massive highway that ended in an elaborate 144 stall market, in a bid to wrestle control from Freedom Market. Elarial\'s Harbormaster and Seraphim, Yggdrasil. Commissioned and paid for an extensive boat bridge crossing the inner sea. Due to economic collapse, and over extension of assets. Elarial eventually collapsed due to intense repair, and upkeep costs. Along with decreased morale, due to territorial claims with neighboring Sutherland Shire. Elarial\'s region of control was the square area of 33-35y, 27-29x. With controlling interest in a small island located at 37y, 24x. Elarial contributed to the construction of Crystal Pastures, and is survived by it\'s massive terraforming projects and boat bridge.', '<p>Location 33-35y - 27-29x. 37y, 24x\n</p>\n<p>Elarial was a consortium settlement founded on the coast of Dragon Fang mountain on the Independence server. It consisted of \"Elarial, Elarial Heights, Elarial Harbor, Hillside, Elarial gardens, and Elarial Island Retreat\". Construction plans for Elarial included a massive highway that ended in an elaborate 144 stall market, in a bid to wrestle control from Freedom Market. \n</p>\n<p>Elarial\'s Harbormaster and Seraphim, Yggdrasil. Commissioned and paid for an extensive boat bridge crossing the inner sea. \n</p>\n<p>Due to economic collapse, and over extension of assets. Elarial eventually collapsed due to intense repair, and upkeep costs. Along with decreased morale, due to territorial claims with neighboring Sutherland Shire. \n</p>\n<pre>  Elarial\'s region of control was the square area of 33-35y, 27-29x.\n</pre>\n<p>With controlling interest in a small island located at 37y, 24x.\n</p>\n<p>Elarial contributed to the construction of Crystal Pastures, and is survived by it\'s massive terraforming projects and boat bridge.\n</p>', 0),
(7851, 2151, 'Location', 'Location', 'Click here to view location on WurmWalker .', '<p>Click <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmwalker.110mb.com/map.php?x=1770&amp;y=3674\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a> to view location on <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmwalker.110mb.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\">WurmWalker</a>.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(7852, 2151, 'About Exile\'s Gate', 'About_Exile.27s_Gate', 'Founded on October 11, 2010 by ForeverSkyz .\nPredecessor of Lock Haven , our first Freedom settlement. Exile\'s Gate is a size 35 by 62 in all direction (71 x 125 tiles) village, covers a total of 8,875 tiles of land. Exile\'s Gate boasts 150+ tall walls surrounding an inclosed town, sunk in 100 dirt steep, with unique gates at the entry points. The main landing off the Southern ocean breaks way into two 30 tile 300 dirt steep ramparts soaring into the bay facing the west. Expanding a total of 8,875 tiles with water fronts, and main road that leads straight to Freedom Market .', '<p>Founded on October 11, 2010 by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:ForeverSkyz\" title=\"Player:ForeverSkyz\">ForeverSkyz</a>.\nPredecessor of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lock_Haven\" title=\"Lock Haven\">Lock Haven</a>, our first Freedom settlement.\n</p>\n<p>Exile\'s Gate is a size 35 by 62 in all direction (71 x 125 tiles) village, covers a total of 8,875 tiles of land. \n</p>\n<p>Exile\'s Gate boasts 150+ tall walls surrounding an inclosed town, sunk in 100 dirt steep, with unique gates at the entry points.\n</p>\n<p>The main landing off the Southern ocean breaks way into two 30 tile 300 dirt steep ramparts soaring into the bay facing the west.\n</p>\n<p>Expanding a total of 8,875 tiles with water fronts, and main road that leads straight to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Market\" title=\"Freedom Market\">Freedom Market</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(7853, 2151, 'Achievements', 'Achievements', 'Colossus of Exile\'s Gate - Completion date: December 23, 2010 Marks the exact one year anniversary of ForeverSkyz arrival on Freedom .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">Colossus</a> of Exile\'s Gate - Completion date: December 23, 2010</li></ul>\n<p>Marks the exact one year anniversary of <a href=\"/index.php/Player:ForeverSkyz\" title=\"Player:ForeverSkyz\">ForeverSkyz</a> arrival on <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a>.\n</p>', 2),
(7854, 2151, 'External Link', 'External_Link', 'Exile\'s Gate official website - [link removed]', '<p>Exile\'s Gate official website - [link removed]\n</p>', 3),
(7855, 2154, 'Description', 'Description', 'The few odd travelers that have claimed to have seen it can\'t remember how they got there. However, all of them agree that it is a mystical place of great beauty and riches. We are located at north west of Crystal Lake just east of Fang mountain. Useful Buildings None yet but we will open a 2x2 house with forge,oven,beds,free meals for the travelers Resources Water lots Clay just north of village (currently still under water at dredge level but few days before it is at dig level) Nearby but not very near Tar,Rock,Iron Politics Citizens of Fisherman\'s Retreat mostly keep to themselves. There had been no sightings for almost two centuries until Discon and Judgemaik visited some old friends on Wild. It is not clear why but it seems that they are here to stay.\nEveryone is welcomed to pass by and feel the hospitality of this place. Its a place for travelers to rest and find some peace before they start their venture again. Religion Vynora Fo', '<p>The few odd travelers that have claimed to have seen it can\'t remember how they got there. However, all of them agree that it is a mystical place of great beauty and riches.\n</p>\n<p>We are located at north west of Crystal Lake just east of Fang mountain.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Useful_Buildings\">Useful Buildings</span></h3>\n<p>None yet but we will open a 2x2 house with forge,oven,beds,free meals for the travelers\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Water lots</li>\n<li>Clay just north of village (currently still under water at dredge level but few days before it is at dig level)</li>\n<li>Nearby but not very near Tar,Rock,Iron</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Politics\">Politics</span></h3>\n<p>Citizens of Fisherman\'s Retreat mostly keep to themselves. There had been no sightings for almost two centuries until <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Discon\" title=\"Player:Discon\">Discon</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Judgemaik\" title=\"Player:Judgemaik\">Judgemaik</a> visited some old friends on Wild. It is not clear why but it seems that they are here to stay.\nEveryone is welcomed to pass by and feel the hospitality of this place. Its a place for travelers to rest and find some peace before they start their venture again.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Religion\">Religion</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a></li></ul>', 0),
(7856, 2154, 'People of Avalon', 'People_of_Avalon', 'Founders Judgemaik [ Keeper of Faith ][ Trollslayer ][ Miner ] Discon [ Keeper of Faith ][ Trollslayer ][ Digger ] Citizens Maya [ Keeper of Faith ] Pending Vynora priesthood Tradeskills None yet Allies', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Founders\">Founders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Judgemaik\" title=\"Player:Judgemaik\">Judgemaik</a> [<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Keeper_of_Faith\" title=\"Keeper of Faith\">Keeper of Faith</a></b>][<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trollslayer\" title=\"Trollslayer\">Trollslayer</a></b>][<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Miner\" title=\"Miner\">Miner</a></b>]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Discon\" title=\"Player:Discon\">Discon</a> [<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Keeper_of_Faith\" title=\"Keeper of Faith\">Keeper of Faith</a></b>][<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trollslayer\" title=\"Trollslayer\">Trollslayer</a></b>][<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Digger\" title=\"Digger\">Digger</a></b>]</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Maya\" title=\"Player:Maya\">Maya</a> [<b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Keeper_of_Faith\" title=\"Keeper of Faith\">Keeper of Faith</a></b>] Pending <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> priesthood</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tradeskills\">Tradeskills</span></h3>\n<p>None yet\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Allies\">Allies</span></h3>', 1),
(7857, 2154, 'Paintings', 'Paintings', 'None yet.', '<p>None yet.\n</p>', 2),
(7864, 2158, 'Description', 'Description', 'Gallifrey is no longer an existing village. Telvanni and Atropos have moved to a new location and started Lantea .', '<p>Gallifrey is no longer an existing village. Telvanni and Atropos have moved to a new location and started <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lantea\" title=\"Lantea\">Lantea</a>.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(7865, 2158, 'Location', 'Location', 'On the edge of the vast northeastern tundra/steppe. Settled right near the woods. Giving a rather large hunting ground to all sorts of fighters. To get to us please PM Telvanni or Atropos in game.', '<p>On the edge of the vast northeastern tundra/steppe. Settled right near the woods. Giving a rather large hunting ground to all sorts of fighters. To get to us please PM Telvanni or Atropos in game.\n</p>', 1),
(7866, 2158, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Mayor Telvanni Elders Atropos', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Telvanni\" title=\"Player:Telvanni\">Telvanni</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Atropos\" title=\"Atropos\">Atropos</a></li></ul>', 2),
(7867, 2158, 'Recruiting', 'Recruiting', 'While we are not actively recruiting if you would like to join PM Telvanni on the forums or message Atropos or Telvanni in game and we will see what we can do.', '<p>While we are not actively recruiting if you would like to join PM Telvanni on the forums or message Atropos or Telvanni in game and we will see what we can do.\n</p>', 3),
(7868, 2158, 'Coming Soon', 'Coming_Soon', 'We are working on our skills to provide a public service. Telvanni is working on weapon smithing. We plan on placing a merchant in the freedom market that will be selling weapons of all types and any types of tools that could be required to start your own place. Atropos is still deciding on what to do but when we she knows what she wants to do we will be adding that to the list of items that we are going to be offering.', '<p>We are working on our skills to provide a public service. Telvanni is working on weapon smithing. We plan on placing a merchant in the freedom market that will be selling weapons of all types and any types of tools that could be required to start your own place. Atropos is still deciding on what to do but when we she knows what she wants to do we will be adding that to the list of items that we are going to be offering.\n</p>', 4),
(7869, 2159, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold - Title Mayor Loxie - Digger Co-Mayor Arthlo - Educated Full Citizens Recruits Arghablarg - None Lastwill - None Esteemed Friends These friends have helped Gem Cove or our individual citizens in one way or another. Selfless players we enjoy spending time with! Darkregis Eyerobot Foreverskyz Noct Vion Zalifear Zefin', '<p><b>Bold</b> - Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Loxie\" title=\"Player:Loxie\">Loxie</a> - Digger</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Co-Mayor\">Co-Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Arthlo\" title=\"Player:Arthlo\">Arthlo</a> - Educated</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Full_Citizens\">Full Citizens</span></h4>\n<ul><li class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Recruits\">Recruits</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Arghablarg\" title=\"Player:Arghablarg\">Arghablarg</a> - None</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Lastwill\" title=\"Player:Lastwill\">Lastwill</a> - None</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Esteemed_Friends\">Esteemed Friends</span></h4>\n<p>These friends have helped Gem Cove or our individual citizens in one way or another. Selfless players we enjoy spending time with!\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Darkregis\" title=\"Player:Darkregis\">Darkregis</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Eyerobot\" title=\"Player:Eyerobot\">Eyerobot</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Foreverskyz\" title=\"Player:Foreverskyz\">Foreverskyz</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Noct\" title=\"Player:Noct\">Noct</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Vion\" title=\"Player:Vion\">Vion</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Zalifear\" title=\"Player:Zalifear\">Zalifear</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Zefin\" title=\"Player:Zefin\">Zefin</a></li></ul>', 0),
(7870, 2159, 'Current Projects', 'Current_Projects', 'Terraforming East Hill Rejuvinate Docks and Decorate Merchant Square \"Living Lighthouse\" Collossus of Gem Cove', '<ul><li>Terraforming East Hill</li>\n<li>Rejuvinate Docks and Decorate</li>\n<li>Merchant Square</li>\n<li>\"Living Lighthouse\"</li>\n<li>Collossus of Gem Cove</li></ul>', 1),
(7871, 2159, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Coming Soon!', '<p>Coming Soon!\n</p>', 2),
(7872, 2160, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'Gmantwelve\'s Hermit Farm was made purely for Gmantwelve to live alone. Little did he know that he would find it hard to work on his own so he made this thread so he would not go crazy. The lot is also deeded. The farm has grown largely since it\'s first development with a pen and 4 additional houses, it is prospering well. Villagers Currently only three people live in Gmantwelve\'s Hermit Farm. Brqqq gmantwelve Mutsu Projects Project Lol \'R\' Us - Creating a Collossus named Lol \'R\' Us where the Landbridge was once going to be. Location and Pictures Map', '<p>Gmantwelve\'s Hermit Farm was made purely for <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/wiki/index.php?title=User:Gmantwelve\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gmantwelve</a> to live alone. Little did he know that he would find it hard to work on his own so he made <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=50252.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">this thread</a> so he would not go crazy. The lot is also deeded. <br/>\nThe farm has grown largely since it\'s first development with a pen and 4 additional houses, it is prospering well.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Villagers\">Villagers</span></h3>\n<p>Currently only three people live in Gmantwelve\'s Hermit Farm.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Brqqq</li>\n<li>gmantwelve</li>\n<li>Mutsu</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Projects\">Projects</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Project Lol \'R\' Us - Creating a Collossus named Lol \'R\' Us where the Landbridge was once going to be.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Location_and_Pictures\">Location and Pictures</span></h3>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img840.imageshack.us/img840/6599/mapxv.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\">Map</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7873, 2160, 'History', 'History', 'On the 25th of February, 2011, Gmantwelve decided to settle in the area by a lake right next to The Western Wall. From there, Gmantwelve developed a small house with a small farm behind it. A couple days later, Gmantwelve added a Deed to the settlement to keep his crops safe from bypassing scavangers. Shortly after the deed, Gmantwelve made a thread (See Overview) asking for people to join his settlement. 3rd of March, 2011 - Deed was founded 4th-10th of March, 2011 - Allied with Kystan 11th of March, 2011 - DragonKnight is recruited from Kchat. He assist in making the landbridge. 12th of March, 2011 - Alfansor is recruited after PMing Gmantwelve on the forums. He was the chef and fisherman. 16th of March, 2011 - Alfansor leaves the village to join Wild. We have no food supply other than Gmantwelve\'s crops. Due to being banned on the Wiki, a small portion of important dates are lost. (Up yours, Manny!)', '<p>On the 25th of February, 2011, Gmantwelve decided to settle in the area by a lake right next to The Western Wall. From there, Gmantwelve developed a small house with a small farm behind it. A couple days later, Gmantwelve added a Deed to the settlement to keep his crops safe from bypassing scavangers. Shortly after the deed, Gmantwelve made a thread (See Overview) asking for people to join his settlement.\n</p>\n<ul><li>3rd of March, 2011 - Deed was founded</li>\n<li>4th-10th of March, 2011 - Allied with Kystan</li>\n<li>11th of March, 2011 - DragonKnight is recruited from Kchat. He assist in making the landbridge.</li>\n<li>12th of March, 2011 - Alfansor is recruited after PMing Gmantwelve on the forums. He was the chef and fisherman.</li>\n<li>16th of March, 2011 - Alfansor leaves the village to join Wild. We have no food supply other than Gmantwelve\'s crops.</li>\n<li>Due to being banned on the Wiki, a small portion of important dates are lost. (Up yours, Manny!)</li></ul>', 1),
(7874, 2162, 'Bulletin Board', 'Bulletin_Board', 'Job available - digging.  no haul reqd.  10c per 100 dirt.  see Urman', '<ul><li>Job available - digging.  no haul reqd.  10c per 100 dirt.  see Urman</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(7875, 2162, 'Members', 'Members', 'Urman - Owner/Mayor Baggins Yalin Capella - Vynora priest wannabe Fobro - Fo priest alt (inactive)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Urman\" title=\"Player:Urman\">Urman</a> - Owner/Mayor</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Baggins\" title=\"Player:Baggins\">Baggins</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Yalin\" title=\"Player:Yalin\">Yalin</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Capella\" title=\"Player:Capella\">Capella</a> - Vynora priest wannabe</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Fobro</a> - Fo priest alt (inactive)</li></ul>', 1),
