(7971, 2193, 'Map', 'Map', 'Not pixel-perfect but a good estimate of the layout', '<table style=\"border:1px solid #BBB;margin:.2em\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><img alt=\"NL.png\" src=\"http://i971.photobucket.com/albums/ae196/Moru2/NL.png\"/>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><i>Not pixel-perfect but a good estimate of the layout</i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3),
(7972, 2193, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Early dawn at Northern Light and the forges are already lit.', '<table style=\"border:1px solid #BBB;margin:.2em\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><img alt=\"northern_light_dawn.jpg\" src=\"http://i971.photobucket.com/albums/ae196/Moru2/northern_light_dawn.jpg\"/>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><i>Early dawn at Northern Light and the forges are already lit.</i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 4),
(7973, 2194, 'The Story of NorthSide Haven', 'The_Story_of_NorthSide_Haven', 'NorthSide Haven was founded after Traslogan disbanded Traslogan\'s Retreat and he seeked out a new place for a village. This led to him sailing around the north coast until he found the spot that NSH is situated upon. From there, Traslogan and Paterso began construction of NorthSide Haven, starting with it\'s first farm and progressing to rows of housing.\nSo far NorthSide Haven has seen tremendous progress, with a welcome inn setup and many houses signifying plentiful space, and farms in abundance to prevent the village going hungry. NorthSide Haven slowly but surely turns into the Haven that it was destined to be', '<p>NorthSide Haven was founded after <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\">Traslogan</a> disbanded <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Traslogan%27s_Retreat\" title=\"Traslogan\'s Retreat\">Traslogan\'s Retreat</a> and he seeked out a new place for a village. This led to him sailing around the north coast until he found the spot that NSH is situated upon. From there, Traslogan and Paterso began construction of NorthSide Haven, starting with it\'s first farm and progressing to rows of housing.\nSo far NorthSide Haven has seen tremendous progress, with a welcome inn setup and many houses signifying plentiful space, and farms in abundance to prevent the village going hungry. NorthSide Haven slowly but surely turns into the Haven that it was destined to be\n</p>', 0),
(7974, 2194, 'NSH Recruitment', 'NSH_Recruitment', 'NSH is currently recruiting at the moment, you can visit our Forums [1] and post a recruitment application in the village hall section or message Traslogan, or you can PM traslogan in-game. Or heck, just come over to NSH and hope we\'re online!', '<p>NSH is currently recruiting at the moment, you can visit our Forums<a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://z15.invisionfree.com/NorthSide_Haven/index.php?\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a> and post a recruitment application in the village hall section or message Traslogan, or you can PM traslogan in-game. Or heck, just come over to NSH and hope we\'re online!\n</p>', 1),
(7975, 2194, 'Current Villagers', 'Current_Villagers', 'Traslogan - Mayor - The one in charge Paterso - Elder - The Alt of the Mayor and the Recruiter of the mobs Astralknight - Villager - Astroboy....duuhh?! ;) Tiranic - Villager - he be a sinkin\' Nyack - Villager - And a nick nack paddy wack..... Insano - Villager - The asylum resident Bezki - Villager - Buzkill! Polemidas - villager - WoW boss?', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\">Traslogan</a> - <b>Mayor</b> - The one in charge\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\">Paterso</a> - <b>Elder</b> - The Alt of the Mayor and the Recruiter of the mobs\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Astralknight</a> - <b>Villager</b> - Astroboy....duuhh?! ;)\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Tiranic</a> - <b>Villager</b> - he be a sinkin\'\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Nyack\" title=\"Player:Nyack\">Nyack</a> - <b>Villager</b> - And a nick nack paddy wack.....\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Insano\" title=\"Player:Insano\">Insano</a> - <b>Villager</b> - The asylum resident\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Bezki</a> - <b>Villager</b> - Buzkill!\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Polemidas</a> - <b>villager</b> - WoW boss?\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(7976, 2194, 'Pictures of NorthSide Haven', 'Pictures_of_NorthSide_Haven', '', '<p><img alt=\"wurm201106112312_2.jpg\" src=\"http://i1214.photobucket.com/albums/cc488/Traslogan/wurm201106112312_2.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<img alt=\"wurm201106112309_1.jpg\" src=\"http://i1214.photobucket.com/albums/cc488/Traslogan/wurm201106112309_1.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<img alt=\"wurm201105062139.jpg\" src=\"http://i1214.photobucket.com/albums/cc488/Traslogan/wurm201105062139.jpg\"/>\n</p>', 3),
(7977, 2195, 'Description', 'Description', 'Gardening is a skill , which is used for and raised via: Planting sprouts , hedges , flowers , thatch , and mixed grass . Watering potted flowers and flowerbeds . Cutting grass to obtain mixed grass or hay , picking flowers, and gathering reed or kelp . Planting and picking from herb planters . Improving trellises using carpentry tools. Gardening does not include sowing seeds for farming .', '<p><b>Gardening</b> is a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a>, which is used for and raised via:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Planting <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hedge\" title=\"Hedge\">hedges</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Flowers\" title=\"Flowers\">flowers</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Thatch\" title=\"Thatch\">thatch</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Mixed_grass\" title=\"Mixed grass\">mixed grass</a>.</li>\n<li>Watering <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_flowerpot\" title=\"Pottery flowerpot\">potted flowers</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Flowerbed\" title=\"Flowerbed\"> flowerbeds</a>.</li>\n<li>Cutting grass to obtain <a href=\"/index.php/Mixed_grass\" title=\"Mixed grass\">mixed grass</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hay\" title=\"Hay\">hay</a>, picking flowers, and gathering <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_tile\" title=\"Reed tile\">reed</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Kelp\" title=\"Kelp\">kelp</a>.</li>\n<li>Planting and picking from <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\"> herb planters</a>.</li>\n<li>Improving <a href=\"/index.php/Trellis\" title=\"Trellis\">trellises</a> using carpentry tools.</li></ul>\n<p>Gardening does not include sowing <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seed\" title=\"Seed\">seeds</a> for <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(7978, 2195, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Gardening can be done while moving, so long as you do not move too far away (two tiles) from the tile you are currently working on. When choosing \"Plant Naturally\" in ground tiles for sprouts, each individual tile has one specific location where the sprout will be planted, and it doesn\'t change no matter how many times you replant sprouts. Level 15 gardeners can mouse over flower, grass, reed, and steppe tiles up to 1 tile away to determine the height and flower type. This range extends by 1 tile for every additional 15 skill (e.g. 2 tiles at 30 skill, 3 tiles at 45 skill). Level 30 gardeners can mouse over tiles up to 2 tiles away. This range continues to increase by 1 tile for every 15 points of skill. Level 50 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout, and you can almost feel it start sucking nutrition from the earth.\" when planting a sprout. Level 60 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout, and you get a weird feeling that the plant thanks you.\" when planting a sprout, and the level 50 message when planting a flower. Level 80 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout. As you see the plant bow you hear the voice in your head of hundreds of plants thanking you.\" when planting a sprout, and \"You plant the bouquet of [color] flowers, and you see them perform an almost unnoticable bow. Or was it the wind?\" when planting flowers. Level 90 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout. As you see the plant bow you hear the voice in your head of hundreds of plants thanking you.\" when planting a sprout, and \"You plant the bouquet of [color] flowers. As you see them bow you hear their thankful tiny voices in your head.\" when planting flowers.', '<ul><li>Gardening can be done while moving, so long as you do not move too far away (two tiles) from the tile you are currently working on.</li>\n<li>When choosing \"Plant Naturally\" in ground tiles for sprouts, each individual tile has one specific location where the sprout will be planted, and it doesn\'t change no matter how many times you replant sprouts.</li>\n<li>Level 15 gardeners can mouse over flower, grass, reed, and steppe tiles up to 1 tile away to determine the height and flower type. This range extends by 1 tile for every additional 15 skill (e.g. 2 tiles at 30 skill, 3 tiles at 45 skill).</li>\n<li>Level 30 gardeners can mouse over tiles up to 2 tiles away. This range continues to increase by 1 tile for every 15 points of skill.</li>\n<li>Level 50 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout, and you can almost feel it start sucking nutrition from the earth.\" when planting a sprout.</li>\n<li>Level 60 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout, and you get a weird feeling that the plant thanks you.\" when planting a sprout, and the level 50 message when planting a flower.</li>\n<li>Level 80 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout. As you see the plant bow you hear the voice in your head of hundreds of plants thanking you.\" when planting a sprout, and \"You plant the bouquet of [color] flowers, and you see them perform an almost unnoticable bow. Or was it the wind?\" when planting flowers.</li>\n<li>Level 90 gardeners get the message \"You plant the sprout. As you see the plant bow you hear the voice in your head of hundreds of plants thanking you.\" when planting a sprout, and \"You plant the bouquet of [color] flowers. As you see them bow you hear their thankful tiny voices in your head.\" when planting flowers.</li></ul>', 1),
(7979, 2195, 'Harvesting', 'Harvesting', 'To harvest, activate a sickle , right-click the trellis , and click Harvest . Trellises can only be harvested when mature or older, and must be in season . Examining the trellis will tell you if it\'s ready to be harvested, almost ready, or is in season but has been harvested already. With enough skill, hovering the mouse over it will also tell you if it can be harvested. The amount of goods harvested depends on the player\'s gardening skill level and the age of the trellis: 1 below 26 skill 2 at 26 skill 3 at 53 skill 4 at 80 skill', '<ul><li>To harvest, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>, right-click the <a href=\"/index.php/Trellis\" title=\"Trellis\">trellis</a>, and click <i>Harvest</i>. Trellises can only be harvested when mature or older, and must be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seasons\" title=\"Seasons\">in season</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Examining the <a href=\"/index.php/Trellis\" title=\"Trellis\">trellis</a> will tell you if it\'s ready to be harvested, almost ready, or is in season but has been harvested already. With enough skill, hovering the mouse over it will also tell you if it can be harvested.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The amount of goods harvested depends on the player\'s gardening skill level and the age of the trellis:\n<ul><li>1 below 26 skill</li>\n<li>2 at 26 skill</li>\n<li>3 at 53 skill</li>\n<li>4 at 80 skill</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(7980, 2195, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Nature > Gardening Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Nature\" title=\"Nature\">Nature</a> &gt; Gardening</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 3),
(7981, 2195, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Greenthumbs at 50 skill Gardener at 70 skill Jiko Enkai Zenji at 90 skill Flower Power at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Greenthumbs at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Gardener at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Jiko Enkai Zenji at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Flower Power at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(7982, 2195, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Forestry Farming', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Farming</a></li></ul>', 5),
(7983, 2196, 'Oak Point', 'Oak_Point', 'Oak Point is located about 15 minutes south of Samling on the Freedom server. Supplying the whole of Freedom with High Quality enchanted tools and armor at very reasonable prices!! If you wish to visit Oak Point, see the Community Map', '<p>Oak Point is located about 15 minutes south of Samling on the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> server.\n</p>\n<p>Supplying the whole of Freedom with High Quality enchanted tools and armor at very reasonable prices!!\n</p>\n<p>If you wish to visit Oak Point, see the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=21270.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Community Map</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7984, 2196, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Ghosted - Tanner , Excavator , High Mason , Famer , Handyman , Prime Minester , Lumberjack , Blacksmith , Carpenter XxosirisxX - Devout , Priest of Vynora Oris - Priest of Fo Candymountia - Blacksmith , Miner Avatarjtc Aragonii Wulfgar Capenter TheGodofWurm Coffeeman Celtarific', '<ul><li>Ghosted - <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">Tanner</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">Excavator</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">High Mason</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Famer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Handyman</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Prime Minester</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">Lumberjack</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_smithing\" title=\"Black smithing\">Blacksmith</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpenter</a></li>\n<li>XxosirisxX - <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">Devout</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Priest of Vynora</a></li>\n<li>Oris - <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Priest of Fo</a></li>\n<li>Candymountia - <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_smithing\" title=\"Black smithing\">Blacksmith</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Miner</a></li>\n<li>Avatarjtc</li>\n<li>Aragonii</li>\n<li>Wulfgar <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Capenter</a></li>\n<li>TheGodofWurm</li>\n<li>Coffeeman</li>\n<li>Celtarific</li></ul>', 1),
(7985, 2196, 'Trading', 'Trading', 'Blacksmithing - Up to 60ql Tools Weaponsmithing - Up to 20ql Weapons Studded Leather - Up to 60ql Armour Jewelry - Up to 30ql Shields - Up to 20ql Carpentry - Up to 55ql Ores and Rockshards - Up to 70ql Forum Thread for Oak Point Priest Services', '<ul><li>Blacksmithing - Up to 60ql Tools</li>\n<li>Weaponsmithing - Up to 20ql Weapons</li>\n<li>Studded Leather - Up to 60ql Armour</li>\n<li>Jewelry - Up to 30ql</li>\n<li>Shields - Up to 20ql</li>\n<li>Carpentry - Up to 55ql</li>\n<li>Ores and Rockshards - Up to 70ql</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=22332.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Forum Thread</a>\nfor Oak Point Priest Services\n</p>', 2),
(7986, 2197, 'Oreo', 'Oreo', 'Oreo is located slightly west of the center of the Freedom server. Supplying the whole of Freedom with High Quality enchanted tools and armour at very reasonable prices!! If you wish to visit Oreo, see the Community Map', '<p>Oreo is located slightly west of the center of the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> server.\n</p>\n<p>Supplying the whole of Freedom with High Quality enchanted tools and armour at very reasonable prices!!\n</p>\n<p>If you wish to visit Oreo, see the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img190.imageshack.us/img190/1267/freedomh.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">Community Map</a>\n</p>', 0),
(7987, 2197, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Drega - Master Tanner , Able Shieldsmith , Excavator , Mason , Famer , Handywoman , Repairwoman , Dragon Slayer . Tantrum - Master Blacksmith , Prime Minester , Excavator , Mason , Handyman , Dragon Slayer . Rosie - Renowned Goldsmith , Animal Trainer , Tailor . Whitewidow - Priest of Vynora .', '<ul><li>Drega - <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">Master Tanner</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Shield_smithing\" title=\"Shield smithing\">Able Shieldsmith</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">Excavator</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">Mason</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Famer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Handywoman</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">Repairwoman</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Titles#Special_titles\" title=\"Titles\">Dragon Slayer</a>.</li>\n<li>Tantrum - <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_smithing\" title=\"Black smithing\">Master Blacksmith</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Prime Minester</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">Excavator</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">Mason</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Handyman</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Titles#Special_titles\" title=\"Titles\">Dragon Slayer</a>.</li>\n<li>Rosie - <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Renowned Goldsmith</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">Animal Trainer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">Tailor</a>.</li>\n<li>Whitewidow - <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Priest of Vynora</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(7988, 2197, 'Old Citizens', 'Old_Citizens', 'Pombear - Champion of Vynora . Chumpeh - Champion of Vynora .', '<ul><li>Pombear - <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Champion of Vynora</a>.</li>\n<li>Chumpeh - <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Champion of Vynora</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(7989, 2197, 'Trading', 'Trading', 'Blacksmithing - Up to 90ql Tools Weaponsmithing - Up to 40ql Weapons Studded Leather - Up to 90ql Armour Jewelry - Up to 50ql Shields - Up to 70ql Carpentry - Up to 50ql Ores and Rockshards - Up to 70ql Forum Thread for Oreo Tool Trade', '<ul><li>Blacksmithing - Up to 90ql Tools</li>\n<li>Weaponsmithing - Up to 40ql Weapons</li>\n<li>Studded Leather - Up to 90ql Armour</li>\n<li>Jewelry - Up to 50ql</li>\n<li>Shields - Up to 70ql</li>\n<li>Carpentry - Up to 50ql</li>\n<li>Ores and Rockshards - Up to 70ql</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=21628.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Forum Thread</a>\nfor Oreo Tool Trade\n</p>', 3),
(7990, 2198, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold = Title Mayor: Digiseer - [Digger] , [Miner] , [Mason] , [Handyman] , [Excavator] . [Blacksmith] Currently working Villagers Enrago MetalAngel Lance Veerserif Staticcling Yela Active Villagers in their own sub-deeds The Distant But Jovial Landowner Mthec - [Farmer] , [Crofter] , [Handyman] , [Tim the Toolman] , [Trollslayer] , [Digger] , [Excavator] , [Miner] , [Prime Minester] , [Gardener] , [Smith] Tropical Aldabest - [Carpenter] , [Renowned Carpenter] , [Digger] , [Harbormaster] , [Tailor] Ironwood Grove Shadethedruid - [Digger] , [Miner] , [Handyman] Silvercliff Sanctuary Shadetheranger Charybdis Isle Prospero Currently In-Active Villagers Akkumage - [Padre] Graham Hughesy KGB Bishopcrane', '<p><b>Bold</b> = Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor:\">Mayor:</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Digiseer\" title=\"Player:Digiseer\">Digiseer</a> - <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Miner]</b>, <b>[Mason]</b>, <b>[Handyman]</b>, <b>[Excavator]</b>. <b>[Blacksmith]</b></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_working_Villagers\">Currently working Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Enrago\" title=\"Player:Enrago\">Enrago</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:MetalAngel\" title=\"Player:MetalAngel\">MetalAngel</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Lance\" title=\"Player:Lance\">Lance</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Veerserif\" title=\"Player:Veerserif\">Veerserif</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Staticcling\" title=\"Player:Staticcling\">Staticcling</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Yela\" title=\"Player:Yela\">Yela</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Active_Villagers_in_their_own_sub-deeds\">Active Villagers in their own sub-deeds</span></h4>\n<ul><li>The Distant But Jovial Landowner\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mthec\" title=\"Player:Mthec\">Mthec</a> - <b>[Farmer]</b>, <b>[Crofter]</b>, <b>[Handyman]</b>, <b>[Tim the Toolman]</b>, <b>[Trollslayer]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Excavator]</b>, <b>[Miner]</b>, <b>[Prime Minester]</b>, <b>[Gardener]</b>, <b>[Smith]</b></li></ul></li>\n<li>Tropical\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Aldabest\" title=\"Player:Aldabest\">Aldabest</a> - <b>[Carpenter]</b>, <b>[Renowned Carpenter]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Harbormaster]</b>, <b>[Tailor]</b></li></ul></li>\n<li>Ironwood Grove\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Shadethedruid\" title=\"Player:Shadethedruid\">Shadethedruid</a> - <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Miner]</b>, <b>[Handyman]</b></li></ul></li>\n<li>Silvercliff Sanctuary\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Shadetheranger\" title=\"Player:Shadetheranger\">Shadetheranger</a></li></ul></li>\n<li>Charybdis Isle\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Prospero\" title=\"Player:Prospero\">Prospero</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_In-Active_Villagers\">Currently In-Active Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Akkumage\" title=\"Player:Akkumage\">Akkumage</a> - <b>[Padre]</b></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Graham\" title=\"Player:Graham\">Graham</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Hughesy\" title=\"Player:Hughesy\">Hughesy</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:KGB\" title=\"Player:KGB\">KGB</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Bishopcrane\" title=\"Player:Bishopcrane\">Bishopcrane</a></li></ul>', 0),
(7991, 2198, 'Village Achievements', 'Village_Achievements', 'The Failossus A Colossus built on ridge near the village, hense named due to the lack of control the village has upon it. The Lighthouse The Lighthouse is located on a small island beside the docks with a penned Champion Lava Spider providing the light. The Village Zoo Currently hosting: A Champion Troll , Champion Wolf , Champion Black Bear and a Champion Scorpion . Al\'s House An achievement of how much rubbish can fit inside a single building.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Failossus\">The Failossus</span></h3>\n<p>A Colossus built on ridge near the village, hense named due to the lack of control the village has upon it.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Lighthouse\">The Lighthouse</span></h3>\n<p>The Lighthouse is located on a small island beside the docks with a penned Champion <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lava_Spider\" title=\"Lava Spider\">Lava Spider</a> providing the light.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Village_Zoo\">The Village Zoo</span></h3>\n<p>Currently hosting: A Champion <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Troll</a>, Champion <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wolf\" title=\"Wolf\">Wolf</a>, Champion <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_Bear\" title=\"Black Bear\">Black Bear</a> and a Champion <a href=\"/index.php/Scorpion\" title=\"Scorpion\">Scorpion</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Al\'s_House\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Al.27s_House\">Al\'s House</span></h3>\n<p>An achievement of how much rubbish can fit inside a single building.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(7992, 2199, 'History', 'History', 'Pheonix Enterprises was and still is a vision of Lando. It was his idea to make a construction company to do work for other players in exchange for money. It started in Gold1 before Wurmageddon as He owned Pitstop then on the road to Cliffside (correct me if im wrong Lando). I used to live in the shire which was just a undeeded spot between Riverside and a HS that was just a farm. I used to teach new players the ropes and the idea was to form a work crew for various project. After the crash Lando wanted to continue this goal and Noyst, Thoth, Mannifestation, Lando and I ( and one other..name escapes me) formed Pheonix Enterprises on the Noth shore of the lake on a tree and spider filled mountain slope. Things were harder as we all had zero skills to start with but over time we leveled farm1, planted a few crops and were underway. Iron was hard to find at first and we made Trinity Mines up on that mountain and made a rough ramp up to it. My deed guards didnt get a rest up there fighting of scorps and wolfs. I think our first job was to make 1000 motar for Vean from the clay pit up on the steppes. I had 4 Mason skill and Nos and Lando were around 12. 30 percent success isnt a fun thing but we managed to get it done and dragged back to Veans. The Next was a job of on some island east which was a 30 minute swim from NT. I got dragged along as I had 30 Carpentry and could plan the building but it was kind of fun killing a load of trees (yes Oaks too ) but we managed to get some oak sprouts and cedar that we planted on farm1 for protection. The only tree types there were lemon, maple and Pine at the time so this was a real gain for the area. The Willow tree in farm1 came from the Lost valley area where lando had arranged use of a mine there that had silver in it. The village grew slowly and we got a job on wild building Kyara\'s dirt walls. I think everyone left to go over there to earn some cash and i stayed behind for a month digging the upper terrace down and farming. We were getting kinda bored so we decided to build the Northern Highway landbridge. Alot of work by a small team of Binary, Bald, Qex lando and i with the aid of anyone wanting to dig dirt for cash. 40000 dirt later and a huge hole in wurm it was completed. Would have been alot easier had we known about fountain carts back then. Rest most of you know.. The Northern Highway project. The establishment of the road HS\'s Trinity, Sronghold and Timesink, the mad push to the coast and the setting up Of Pheonix North Port. Qex\'s beautiful HS on the NE coast made us push a road across 300 tiles of forest just to see his place... Then they introduced ships which made it redundant.. although we did have loads of fun hunting that road and the Desert Outpost. Alot of hours went into developing PNP to its size with its large farms and connections to the sea and wild. But many pleasant memories go with it and alot of friends that grew bored and frustrated with the game. Now we are on Freedom and have started a new village with some of Wurms most dedicated and skilled players.. Only time will tell if we succeed in making it a great place to live. --Traxx, Mayor of PE', '<p>Pheonix Enterprises was and still is a vision of Lando. It was his idea to make a construction company to do work for other players in exchange for money. It started in Gold1 before Wurmageddon as He owned Pitstop then on the road to Cliffside (correct me if im wrong Lando). I used to live in the shire which was just a undeeded spot between Riverside and a HS that was just a farm. I used to teach new players the ropes and the idea was to form a work crew for various project.\n</p>\n<p>After the crash Lando wanted to continue this goal and Noyst, Thoth, Mannifestation, Lando and I ( and one other..name escapes me) formed Pheonix Enterprises on the Noth shore of the lake on a tree and spider filled mountain slope. Things were harder as we all had zero skills to start with but over time we leveled farm1, planted a few crops and were underway. Iron was hard to find at first and we made Trinity Mines up on that mountain and made a rough ramp up to it. My deed guards didnt get a rest up there fighting of scorps and wolfs.\n</p>\n<p>I think our first job was to make 1000 motar for Vean from the clay pit up on the steppes. I had 4 Mason skill and Nos and Lando were around 12. 30 percent success isnt a fun thing but we managed to get it done and dragged back to Veans. The Next was a job of on some island east which was a 30 minute swim from NT. I got dragged along as I had 30 Carpentry and could plan the building but it was kind of fun killing a load of trees (yes Oaks too ) but we managed to get some oak sprouts and cedar that we planted on farm1 for protection. The only tree types there were lemon, maple and Pine at the time so this was a real gain for the area.\n</p>\n<p>The Willow tree in farm1 came from the Lost valley area where lando had arranged use of a mine there that had silver in it.\n</p>\n<p>The village grew slowly and we got a job on wild building Kyara\'s dirt walls. I think everyone left to go over there to earn some cash and i stayed behind for a month digging the upper terrace down and farming. \n</p>\n<p>We were getting kinda bored so we decided to build the Northern Highway landbridge. Alot of work by a small team of Binary, Bald, Qex lando and i with the aid of anyone wanting to dig dirt for cash. 40000 dirt later and a huge hole in wurm it was completed. Would have been alot easier had we known about fountain carts back then.\n</p>\n<p>Rest most of you know.. The Northern Highway project. The establishment of the road HS\'s Trinity, Sronghold and Timesink, the mad push to the coast and the setting up Of Pheonix North Port. Qex\'s beautiful HS on the NE coast made us push a road across 300 tiles of forest just to see his place... Then they introduced ships which made it redundant.. although we did have loads of fun hunting that road and the Desert Outpost.\n</p>\n<p>Alot of hours went into developing PNP to its size with its large farms and connections to the sea and wild. But many pleasant memories go with it and alot of friends that grew bored and frustrated with the game.\n</p>\n<p>Now we are on Freedom and have started a new village with some of Wurms most dedicated and skilled players.. Only time will tell if we succeed in making it a great place to live.\n</p>\n<p>--Traxx, Mayor of PE\n</p>', 0),
(7993, 2199, 'Directions', 'Directions', 'We are located in the South-West of Independence at coordinates 12x57y.\nClick here for a map.', '<p>We are located in the South-West of Independence at coordinates 12x57y.\nClick <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://noizeviolation.com/wurm/Freedom_map.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a> for a map.\n</p>', 1),
