(8042, 2216, 'Early History of Stonehaven', 'Early_History_of_Stonehaven', 'Stonehaven was founded by Xzovy The Magnificent in the early summer of 2010. It was only by a great feat of Herculean effort that Xzovy was able to carve one of Freedom\'s steepest mountains into the noble plateau that now holds Stonehaven. Elegantly situated, between the Inner Sea and the forest, we consider Stonehaven to be one of the Seven Wonders of Freedom. Shortly after Xzovy carved the mountain down to size, actually it was more like a small hill, he was joined by his friend Bensmithbensmith, an eager, if still-wet-behind-the-ears, noob. It was this combination of dogged determination and innocence that drew Xianruflux, at this time an Elder of The Academy, to visit their deed. After a few trips to Stonehaven it was clear to Xianruflux that if these two were to make a reality of their dream they would need his help and thus a partnership was born. Xzovy, our political conscience, suggested we become an Isocracy ( http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isocracy ) and after not more than a few of his long winded lectures Ben and Xian gave in. Once that issue was settled and the village motto confirmed: Free, Equal, Happy; we got down to the hard work of assisting Xzovy to create his dream. The weeks and months passed in blissful peace as we settled into our new home surrounded by good neighbours and ample resources, until the accident. It was late one night in the early fall when Xzovy and Xianruflux heard the screams. After much searching we finally discovered Bensmithbensmith deep in a mine. He was unable to move and suffering from a nasty crafting accident which left him catatonic. Weeks of rehabilitation followed but to no avail, Bensmithbensmith remained unable to focus and lost concentration easily. We even brought a priest to the deed to minister to his wounds. Although she remains at Stonehaven as our spiritual leader, Qvmmruvi, was unable to return our friend to his preaccident state. Eventually he succumbed to his injuries and we lost him. To this day the deed remains divided on the subject of minecrafting - safe, or not safe...', '<p>Stonehaven was founded by Xzovy The Magnificent in the early summer of 2010. It was only by a great feat of Herculean effort that Xzovy was able to carve one of Freedom\'s steepest mountains into the noble plateau that now holds Stonehaven. Elegantly situated, between the Inner Sea and the forest, we consider Stonehaven to be one of the Seven Wonders of Freedom. Shortly after Xzovy carved the mountain down to size, actually it was more like a small hill, he was joined by his friend Bensmithbensmith, an eager, if still-wet-behind-the-ears, noob. It was this combination of dogged determination and innocence that drew Xianruflux, at this time an Elder of The Academy, to visit their deed. After a few trips to Stonehaven it was clear to Xianruflux that if these two were to make a reality of their dream they would need his help and thus a partnership was born. \n</p>\n<p>Xzovy, our political conscience, suggested we become an Isocracy (<a class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isocracy\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isocracy</a>) and after not more than a few of his long winded lectures Ben and Xian gave in. Once that issue was settled and the village motto confirmed: Free, Equal, Happy; we got down to the hard work of assisting Xzovy to create his dream.\n</p>\n<p>The weeks and months passed in blissful peace as we settled into our new home surrounded by good neighbours and ample resources, until the accident. It was late one night in the early fall when Xzovy and Xianruflux heard the screams. After much searching we finally discovered Bensmithbensmith deep in a mine. He was unable to move and suffering from a nasty crafting accident which left him catatonic. Weeks of rehabilitation followed but to no avail, Bensmithbensmith remained unable to focus and lost concentration easily. We even brought a priest to the deed to minister to his wounds. Although she remains at Stonehaven as our spiritual leader, Qvmmruvi, was unable to return our friend to his preaccident state. Eventually he succumbed to his injuries and we lost him. To this day the deed remains divided on the subject of minecrafting - safe, or not safe...\n</p>', 0),
(8043, 2216, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Xianruflux - Deedholder/Mayor - Blacksmith and Primeminester Xzovy - Founder - Carpenter, Digger, and Mason Qvmmruvi - Priestess Lilnellie - Innkeeper Bensmithbensmith - Retired', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Xianruflux\" title=\"Player:Xianruflux\">Xianruflux</a> - Deedholder/Mayor - Blacksmith and Primeminester</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Xzovy</a> - Founder - Carpenter, Digger, and Mason</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Qvmmruvi</a> - Priestess</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Lilnellie</a> - Innkeeper</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Bensmithbensmith</a> - Retired</li></ul>', 1),
(8044, 2216, 'External Resources', 'External_Resources', 'Stonehaven Forums Recruitment Thread - Wurm Forums', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://stonehaven.freeforums.org\" rel=\"nofollow\">Stonehaven Forums</a>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=48416.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Recruitment Thread - Wurm Forums</a>\n</p>', 2),
(8045, 2217, 'Location', 'Location', 'Stonewall Abbey is located in the west of the Freedom Isles. It is north of Appleby Town, south of Garden of the Gods, west of Eve of Insanity, east of Kystran. On the Freedom Map it is at the coordinates of 21y, 14x. It was abandoned at 2011/03/18.', '<p>Stonewall Abbey is located in the west of the Freedom Isles. It is north of Appleby Town, south of Garden of the Gods, west of Eve of Insanity, east of Kystran. On the Freedom Map it is at the coordinates of 21y, 14x.\n</p>\n<p>It was abandoned at 2011/03/18.\n</p>', 0),
(8046, 2217, 'Active Villagers(Last updated: 2011/03/15)', 'Active_Villagers.28Last_updated:_2011.2F03.2F15.29', 'Mayors Taxfrog Vice-mayors Picasso High Command Mooney Citizens Bicas Mushmellow', '<ul><li>Mayors\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Taxfrog\" title=\"Player:Taxfrog\">Taxfrog</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Vice-mayors\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Picasso\" title=\"Player:Picasso\">Picasso</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li>High Command\n<ul><li>Mooney</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Citizens\n<ul><li>Bicas</li>\n<li>Mushmellow</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(8047, 2218, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'The majority of the villagers are premium players, however Storm\'s End recruits all kinds of players; new and veteran.  Below is a list of some of the more active players and veteran players with some of their proficiencies. Slickshot - King - Renowned carpenter and builder of the village, as well as an armoursmith and bowmaker. Joykill - Hand of the King - Co-owner and the \"jack of all trades\" of the village.  Proficient in mining, digging, farming, fighting, and leatherworking. Gorgonkain - Villager - The prominent breeder in the village, proficient in animal husbandry and dying on long adventures. Kolbuingen - Villager - Another \"jack of all trades\" skilled in building, mining, blacksmithing, fighting and donating of upkeep.', '<p>The majority of the villagers are premium players, however <b>Storm\'s End</b> recruits all kinds of players; new and veteran.  Below is a list of some of the more active players and veteran players with some of their proficiencies.\n</p>\n<ul><li><b><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Slickshot\" title=\"Player:Slickshot\">Slickshot</a></b> - <i>King</i> - Renowned carpenter and builder of the village, as well as an armoursmith and bowmaker.</li>\n<li><b>Joykill</b> - <i>Hand of the King</i> - Co-owner and the \"jack of all trades\" of the village.  Proficient in mining, digging, farming, fighting, and leatherworking.</li>\n<li><b>Gorgonkain</b> - <i>Villager</i> - The prominent breeder in the village, proficient in animal husbandry and dying on long adventures.</li>\n<li><b>Kolbuingen</b> - <i>Villager</i> - Another \"jack of all trades\" skilled in building, mining, blacksmithing, fighting and donating of upkeep.</li></ul>', 0),
(8048, 2218, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', '', '<p><img alt=\"1mb8XU1.jpg\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/1mb8XU1.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8049, 2218, 'Services and Community Buildings', 'Services_and_Community_Buildings', 'Mailbox near settlement token. Tempest Workshop Bows, weapons, tools, leather items for sale. Elfsong Tavern Public access to forges, oven, loom and beds. Sept of Vynora Church with a Vynora alter emitting a large domain.  Sermons are held here often. Grand Steppe Hunting Lodge - affiliation The lodge is affiliated with Storm\'s End and is located in the Grand Steppe, protected by the deed Haven . Public access to forge, oven, beds and a merchant selling weapons for hunting.', '<ul><li><i>Mailbox near settlement token.</i></li>\n<li><b>Tempest Workshop</b>\n<ul><li>Bows, weapons, tools, leather items for sale.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Elfsong Tavern</b>\n<ul><li>Public access to forges, oven, loom and beds.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Sept of Vynora</b>\n<ul><li>Church with a Vynora alter emitting a large domain.  Sermons are held here often.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Grand Steppe Hunting Lodge</b> - <i>affiliation</i>\n<ul><li>The lodge is affiliated with <i>Storm\'s End</i> and is located in the Grand Steppe, protected by the deed <i><b>Haven</b></i>.</li>\n<li>Public access to forge, oven, beds and a merchant selling weapons for hunting.</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(8050, 2219, 'Description', 'Description', 'Large (size 45x45) village located on Sunrise Lake in the southeastern lake of Celebration. Check out our recruitment ad .', '<p>Large (size 45x45) village located on Sunrise Lake in the southeastern lake of Celebration. \n</p>\n<p>Check out our <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/62891-sunrise-bay-recruiting-on-celebration/\" rel=\"nofollow\">recruitment ad</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(8051, 2219, 'Events', 'Events', '', '', 1),
(8052, 2219, 'Merchants and Trade', 'Merchants_and_Trade', 'Name Owner Details Forum Post Cloth Tailoring - Merchant in Amish Paradise Market Claies Shipbuilding, Ropes, Carpentry and masonry bulk orders Garnetstar', '<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"5\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"text-align:left;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Owner</th>\n<th>Details</th>\n<th>Forum Post\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cloth Tailoring - Merchant in Amish Paradise Market</td>\n<td>Claies\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shipbuilding, Ropes, Carpentry and masonry bulk orders</td>\n<td>Garnetstar\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>', 2),
(8053, 2219, 'People', 'People', 'Mayor Claies - [Community Assistant] , [Digger] , Citizens Garnetstar - [Harbormaster] , [Carpenter] , [Digger] , [Farmer] , [Mason] , [Trollslayer] Ezreal - [Miner] Luapnor Tree - [Miner] Divus - [Carpenter] Laiwyn', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Claies\" title=\"Player:Claies\">Claies</a> - <b>[Community Assistant]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b>,</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Garnetstar\" title=\"User:Garnetstar\">Garnetstar</a> - <b>[Harbormaster]</b>,<b>[Carpenter]</b>, <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Farmer]</b>, <b>[Mason]</b>, <b>[Trollslayer]</b></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Ezreal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Ezreal (page does not exist)\">Ezreal</a> - <b>[Miner]</b></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Luapnor&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Luapnor (page does not exist)\">Luapnor</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Tree&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Tree (page does not exist)\">Tree</a> - <b>[Miner]</b></li>\n<li><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Divus&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Divus (page does not exist)\">Divus</a> - <b>[Carpenter]</b></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Laiwyn\" title=\"User:Laiwyn\">Laiwyn</a></li></ul>', 3),
(8054, 2222, 'History', 'History', 'Tenakill was originally founded on JK home, it\'s page during that era can be found here . Tenakill\'s location on JK home was initially scouted by Becket . Tenakill\'s location on Independence was scouted by Asidecay and Magen It is 17:10:15 on day of the Wurm in week 2 of the starfall of the Digging in the year of 998. The village of Tenakill has just been founded by Asidecay.', '<ul><li>Tenakill was originally founded on JK home, it\'s page during that era can be found <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tenakill_(JK-h)\" title=\"Tenakill (JK-h)\">here</a>.</li>\n<li>Tenakill\'s location on JK home was initially scouted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Becket\" title=\"Player:Becket\">Becket</a>. <br/>Tenakill\'s location on Independence was scouted by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Asidecay\" title=\"Player:Asidecay\">Asidecay</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Magen\" title=\"Player:Magen\">Magen</a></li>\n<li>It is 17:10:15 on day of the Wurm in week 2 of the starfall of the Digging in the year of 998.<br/> The village of Tenakill has just been founded by Asidecay.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(8055, 2222, 'Location', 'Location', 'Tenakill is located on the mid-west coast of the Independence server of the Freedom Isles . The location on Mystecore\'s map is 7x, 42y. We have submitted a map of our area to the Project FRAM|FRAM project, hopefully it will be added soon. Until then, here is our copy:', '<p>Tenakill is located on the mid-west coast of the <a href=\"/index.php/Independence\" title=\"Independence\">Independence</a> server of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Isles\" title=\"Freedom Isles\">Freedom Isles</a>.<br/> \nThe location on <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://gmapuploader.com/iframe/LaHd0n8GMx\" rel=\"nofollow\">Mystecore\'s map</a> is 7x, 42y.\n</p>\n<p>We have submitted a map of our area to the Project FRAM|FRAM project, hopefully it will be added soon. Until then, here is our copy:<br/>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img130.imageshack.us/img130/6276/mapupdateo.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"mapupdateo.th.png\" src=\"http://img130.imageshack.us/img130/6276/mapupdateo.th.png\"/></a>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8056, 2222, 'Goods and Services', 'Goods_and_Services', 'Tenakill offers goods, wares and services on their either their merchants located at Freedom Market or by special order. Have a look at the thread over in the forums for availability and pricing.', '<p>Tenakill offers goods, wares and services on their either their merchants located at <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Market\" title=\"Freedom Market\">Freedom Market</a> or by special order. Have a look at the thread over in the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=43726.0%7CWurm\" rel=\"nofollow\">forums</a> for availability and pricing.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(8057, 2222, 'Images', 'Images', '', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img838.imageshack.us/img838/3466/wurm2009101223591.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm2009101223591.th.png\" src=\"http://img838.imageshack.us/img838/3466/wurm2009101223591.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img638.imageshack.us/img638/529/wurm200910190011.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm200910190011.th.png\" src=\"http://img638.imageshack.us/img638/529/wurm200910190011.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img185.imageshack.us/img185/9908/wurm200912250239.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm200912250239.th.png\" src=\"http://img185.imageshack.us/img185/9908/wurm200912250239.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img803.imageshack.us/img803/1382/wurm200912290422.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm200912290422.th.png\" src=\"http://img803.imageshack.us/img803/1382/wurm200912290422.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img834.imageshack.us/img834/6342/wurm201007080350.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm201007080350.th.png\" src=\"http://img834.imageshack.us/img834/6342/wurm201007080350.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img69.imageshack.us/img69/9092/wurm2010100521501.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm2010100521501.th.png\" src=\"http://img69.imageshack.us/img69/9092/wurm2010100521501.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img543.imageshack.us/img543/1238/wurm201010270056.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm201010270056.th.png\" src=\"http://img543.imageshack.us/img543/1238/wurm201010270056.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img812.imageshack.us/img812/3349/wurm2010102619312.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm2010102619312.th.png\" src=\"http://img812.imageshack.us/img812/3349/wurm2010102619312.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img138.imageshack.us/img138/9342/wurm201010270057.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm201010270057.th.png\" src=\"http://img138.imageshack.us/img138/9342/wurm201010270057.th.png\"/></a>\n<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://img225.imageshack.us/img225/5662/wurm201010292113.png\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"wurm201010292113.th.png\" src=\"http://img225.imageshack.us/img225/5662/wurm201010292113.th.png\"/></a>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(8058, 2222, 'Population', 'Population', 'Mayors Asidecay - [Bodybuilder], [Soldier], [Digger], [Excavator], [Land Shaper], [Smith], [Tinker], [Goldsmith], [Blacksmith], [Renowned Blacksmith], [Master Blacksmith], [Mason], [High Mason], [Miner], [Prime Minester], [Lumberjack], [Timberman], [Axeman], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Fletcher], [Tailor], [Handyman], [Tim the Toolman], [Repairman], [Farmer], [Crofter], [Gardener], [Greenthumbs], [Forester], [Trollslayer] Becket - [Bodybuilder], [Soldier], [Mercenary], [Mason], [High Mason], [Master Mason], [Miner], [Prime Minester], [Mastermine], [Digger], [Excavator], [Land Shaper], [Blacksmith], [Renowned Blacksmith], [Goldsmith], [Lumberjack], [Axeman], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Harbormaster], [Handyman], [Tim the Toolman], [Repairman], [Gardener], [Farmer], [Crofter], [Greenthumbs], [Caterer], [Trollslayer] Magen - [Cook], [Caterer], [Iron Chef], [Animal Trainer], [Beast Speaker], [Tanner], [High Tanner], [Lumberjack], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Blacksmith], [Bowmaker], [Mason], [Trollslayer], [Miner], [Handywoman], [Gardener], [Farmer], [Digger], [Excavator] Officers Paulscott Pacer Citizens Lizzee Itumatra Mianna Truxtun - Vynoran Priest Gogogetem Tima Fullmetal Recruits None', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayors\">Mayors</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Asidecay\" title=\"Player:Asidecay\">Asidecay</a> - [Bodybuilder], [Soldier], [Digger], [Excavator], [Land Shaper], [Smith], [Tinker], [Goldsmith], [Blacksmith], [Renowned Blacksmith], [Master Blacksmith], [Mason], [High Mason], [Miner], [Prime Minester], [Lumberjack], [Timberman], [Axeman], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Fletcher], [Tailor], [Handyman], [Tim the Toolman], [Repairman], [Farmer], [Crofter], [Gardener], [Greenthumbs], [Forester], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Becket\" title=\"Player:Becket\">Becket</a> - [Bodybuilder], [Soldier], [Mercenary], [Mason], [High Mason], [Master Mason], [Miner], [Prime Minester], [Mastermine], [Digger], [Excavator], [Land Shaper], [Blacksmith], [Renowned Blacksmith], [Goldsmith], [Lumberjack], [Axeman], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Harbormaster], [Handyman], [Tim the Toolman], [Repairman], [Gardener], [Farmer], [Crofter], [Greenthumbs], [Caterer], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Magen\" title=\"Player:Magen\">Magen</a> - [Cook], [Caterer], [Iron Chef], [Animal Trainer], [Beast Speaker], [Tanner], [High Tanner], [Lumberjack], [Carpenter], [Renowned Carpenter], [Blacksmith], [Bowmaker], [Mason], [Trollslayer], [Miner], [Handywoman], [Gardener], [Farmer], [Digger], [Excavator]</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Officers\">Officers</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Paulscott</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Pacer\" title=\"Player:Pacer\">Pacer</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Lizzee</li>\n<li>Itumatra</li>\n<li>Mianna</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Truxtun\" title=\"Player:Truxtun\">Truxtun</a> - Vynoran Priest</li>\n<li>Gogogetem</li>\n<li>Tima</li>\n<li>Fullmetal</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Recruits\">Recruits</span></h3>\n<p>None\n</p>', 4),
(8059, 2224, 'Village Info', 'Village_Info', 'Founded in May 2010 on the Freedom-Independence server. NOT in any way what-so-ever affiliated with the former Dark Citadel , Horde of the Summoned deed, on the Wild server.', '<p>Founded in May 2010 on the Freedom-Independence server.\n</p>\n<p><b>NOT</b> in any way what-so-ever affiliated with the former <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Dark_Citadel&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Dark Citadel (page does not exist)\">Dark Citadel</a>, Horde of the Summoned deed, on the Wild server.\n</p>', 0),
(8060, 2224, 'Members', 'Members', 'Darkmalice', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Darkmalice</a></li></ul>', 1),
(8061, 2227, 'Introduction & Info', 'Introduction_.26_Info', 'Founded in late April 2011, Tiger Den is a small village which is more to be considered a homestead (No more homesteads, all deeds are officially villages.) It is not a village that is officially recruiting, it is a small area that I can truly call home. Whenever I am online, I am working on it, and no one tells me what to do with it, the benefits of having a deed :) Of course, mine, and the villagers. I can\'t take the credit for this place. It is located at 33y 20x (It is on the Community Map) just by Waterside. This does not mean we are not welcoming, please, come visit and chat and hang out! However, griefers will receive -100 reputation and be automatically killed by the guards, naturally. This village is here so I can use being a mayor to help me further increase my game experience, give me a place to grind, and have a place where I can put what I want where I want, and have no one complain about me messing up their stuff. It\'s a great place! The area has a problem with strong hostile creatures, namely Huge Spiders, bears, and trolls. I plan to take down every single lair soon.', '<p>Founded in late April 2011, Tiger Den is a small village which is more to be considered a homestead (No more homesteads, all deeds are officially villages.) It is not a village that is officially recruiting, it is a small area that I can truly call home. Whenever I am online, I am working on it, and no one tells me what to do with it, the benefits of having a deed :) Of course, mine, and the villagers. I can\'t take the credit for this place. It is located at 33y 20x (It is on the Community Map) just by Waterside. This does not mean we are not welcoming, please, come visit and chat and hang out! However, griefers will receive -100 reputation and be automatically killed by the guards, naturally. This village is here so I can use being a mayor to help me further increase my game experience, give me a place to grind, and have a place where I can put what I want where I want, and have no one complain about me messing up their stuff. It\'s a great place! The area has a problem with strong hostile creatures, namely Huge Spiders, bears, and trolls. I plan to take down every single lair soon.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(8062, 2227, 'Story', 'Story', 'It\'s a funny story. I was wandering as a nomad when I came across this place. It was deeded, and owned by Nownowson. He was kind and helped me out, and I sailed over to Halcyon which I joined but got kicked out. So I wandered a long time, then just left the game seeing no progress. then just took a break from the game seeing no progress. I told a real life friend about Wurm (Thecuriouscat), and got them to join. So, seeing something fun was happening now, I started playing. We wandered around then finally, seeing the center island is too populated, sailed back over to that place with the helpful village. Thing is, I didn\'t know I had gone back to the same area of the village. I had, as a matter of fact, forgotten that village. And I stumbled across a little flat spot that looked perfect for a house. I then logged off for the night, and when I got back on, prepared to get to work. But suddenly, I found out why it was flat. I turned and looked. I hadn\'t noticed it, but this was the remains of that helpful village. All the houses were gone, and the fences were around 40 DMG. It was like a chill down my spine. That village that was thriving and helpful only a month ago was abandoned, and I had unwittingly stumbled upon it. I started making the house, when I just one day decided to deed the whole place. So the legend of that helpful village lives on. It was kind of passed down to me in a way. Because if you ever need help, we\'re a real helpful village!', '<p>It\'s a funny story. I was wandering as a nomad when I came across this place. It was deeded, and owned by Nownowson. He was kind and helped me out, and I sailed over to Halcyon which I joined but got kicked out. So I wandered a long time, then just left the game seeing no progress. then just took a break from the game seeing no progress. I told a real life friend about Wurm (Thecuriouscat), and got them to join. So, seeing something fun was happening now, I started playing. We wandered around then finally, seeing the center island is too populated, sailed back over to that place with the helpful village. Thing is, I didn\'t know I had gone back to the same area of the village. I had, as a matter of fact, forgotten that village. And I stumbled across a little flat spot that looked perfect for a house. I then logged off for the night, and when I got back on, prepared to get to work. But suddenly, I found out why it was flat. I turned and looked. I hadn\'t noticed it, but this was the remains of that helpful village. All the houses were gone, and the fences were around 40 DMG. It was like a chill down my spine. That village that was thriving and helpful only a month ago was abandoned, and I had unwittingly stumbled upon it. I started making the house, when I just one day decided to deed the whole place. So the legend of that helpful village lives on. It was kind of passed down to me in a way. Because if you ever need help, we\'re a real helpful village!\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8063, 2227, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Xtigermanxx Trollslayer - Mayor (Village Fighter) Thecuriouscat - Elder Appelstrudel - Villager (Village Cook) Purgman - Villager', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Xtigermanxx\" title=\"Xtigermanxx\">Xtigermanxx</a> <b>Trollslayer</b> - Mayor (Village Fighter)\n</p>\n<p>Thecuriouscat - Elder\n</p>\n<p>Appelstrudel - Villager (Village Cook)\n</p>\n<p>Purgman - Villager\n</p>', 2),
(8064, 2228, 'Members', 'Members', 'Uranoz - Terraformer/Blacksmith/Farmer/Chief (Leader) Gitoro - Carpentry/Woodcutter/Miner (Officer) Troels - Miner Tedarus - Miner/Masonry/Carpentry/Woodcutter', '<ul><li>Uranoz - Terraformer/Blacksmith/Farmer/Chief (Leader)</li>\n<li>Gitoro - Carpentry/Woodcutter/Miner (Officer)</li>\n<li>Troels - Miner</li>\n<li>Tedarus - Miner/Masonry/Carpentry/Woodcutter</li></ul>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(8065, 2228, 'To do', 'To_do', 'As Timberberg Harbour is still under construction, we still have some jobs to do.. And for people who want to help they are always welcome to come by and ask if we need help!\nHere is a list of jobs to do: Plan our dock (0%) Terraform dock (~1%) Build boat building house (0%) Build our Small Sailing Boat (~50%) - Gitoro is slowly working on this Make downward ramp to dock (~45%) - Uranoz is slowly working on this Build sleeping barracks (~65%) - Tedarus is making great progress here Build cooking house (0%) Build private storage (0%) - Is the next house we are going to work on, already making large chests Make floorboards to houses (0%) Make stone slabs to houses (0%)', '<p>As Timberberg Harbour is still under construction, we still have some jobs to do.. And for people who want to help they are always welcome to come by and ask if we need help!\nHere is a list of jobs to do:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Plan our dock <b>(0%)</b></li>\n<li>Terraform dock <b>(~1%)</b></li>\n<li>Build boat building house <b>(0%)</b></li>\n<li>Build our Small Sailing Boat <b>(~50%)</b> - <i>Gitoro is slowly working on this</i></li>\n<li>Make downward ramp to dock <b>(~45%)</b> - <i>Uranoz is slowly working on this</i></li>\n<li>Build sleeping barracks <b>(~65%)</b> - <i>Tedarus is making great progress here</i></li>\n<li>Build cooking house <b>(0%)</b></li>\n<li>Build private storage <b>(0%)</b> - <i>Is the next house we are going to work on, already making large chests</i></li>\n<li>Make floorboards to houses <b>(0%)</b></li>\n<li>Make stone slabs to houses <b>(0%)</b></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8066, 2228, 'Future', 'Future', 'As soon as we got the coins we are going to upgrade our deed from Homestead to Village.', '<p>As soon as we got the coins we are going to upgrade our deed from Homestead to Village.\n</p>', 2),
(8067, 2229, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Bold = Title Mayor: Battlepants - [Lots] Currently Active Villagers Aeper Elshar - [Digger] , [Excavator] , [Trollslayer] , [Carpenter] Shyel [Trollslayer] Sparkyrich Inactive Villagers + Alts Chillywilly Figs Gurkin Longinus Muni Synapse', '<p><b>Bold</b> = Title\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor:\">Mayor:</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Battlepants\" title=\"Player:Battlepants\">Battlepants</a> - <b>[Lots]</b></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Currently_Active_Villagers\">Currently Active Villagers</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Aeper</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Elshar\" title=\"Player:Elshar\">Elshar</a> - <b>[Digger]</b>, <b>[Excavator]</b>, <b>[Trollslayer]</b>, <b>[Carpenter]</b></li>\n<li>Shyel <b>[Trollslayer]</b></li>\n<li>Sparkyrich</li></ul>\n<h4><span id=\"Inactive_Villagers_+_Alts\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inactive_Villagers_.2B_Alts\">Inactive Villagers + Alts</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Chillywilly</li>\n<li>Figs</li>\n<li>Gurkin</li>\n<li>Longinus</li>\n<li>Muni</li>\n<li>Synapse</li></ul>', 0),
(8068, 2232, 'Location', 'Location', 'Freedom Southmost point of the Inner Sea, due south of Freedom Market Dock', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> Southmost point of the Inner Sea, due south of Freedom Market Dock\n</p>', 0),
(8069, 2232, 'Description', 'Description', 'Built on a hillside and terraformed into the sea.', '<p>Built on a hillside and terraformed into the sea.\n</p>', 1),
(8070, 2232, 'Trade', 'Trade', 'Merchants will be here when I get to that. None in Freedom Market.', '<p>Merchants will be here when I get to that. None in Freedom Market.\n</p>', 2),
(8071, 2232, 'History', 'History', 'The Beginning', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Beginning\">The Beginning</span></h3>', 3),
(8072, 2232, 'Leaders', 'Leaders', 'Tritus [Founder & Mayor]', '<ul><li><b>Tritus</b> [Founder &amp; Mayor]</li></ul>', 4),
(8073, 2232, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Angua Svelte Trimin', '<ul><li>Angua</li>\n<li>Svelte</li>\n<li>Trimin</li></ul>', 5),
(8074, 2232, 'Credits', 'Credits', 'Kalborn and Wraithglow as reliable paid diggers who provided about 50% of the dirt required for the sea reclamation.', '<p>Kalborn and Wraithglow as reliable paid diggers who provided about 50% of the dirt required for the sea reclamation.\n</p>', 6),
(8075, 2233, 'About', 'About', 'Tyrian Bay was named after the scrolling shooter arcade game , Tyrian. \nThe towns purpose is to graduly become a research center, dedicated to providing the WurmWiki with facts about the game not yet provided. \"Tyrian Bay is still under construction and does not yet own a Settlement Token\". All players looking to pursue and help finalize the knowledge base of the WurmWiki or perhaps anyone looking for a safe haven may find a place at Tyrian\". All players are expected to treat one another with respect and are to be independent, with regards to maintaining their own lifestyle. The people of Tyrian are mature and sensible. We allow free speech, but we as a town keep our thoughts to ourselves. Religion The people of Tyrian follow no God in particular, however Vynora shrines may be located around the Bay. \"If anything, we believe in SCIENCE\".', '<p>Tyrian Bay was named after the <i>scrolling shooter arcade game</i>, Tyrian. \nThe towns purpose is to graduly become a research center, dedicated to providing the WurmWiki with facts about the game not yet provided. \"Tyrian Bay is still under construction and does not yet own a Settlement Token\". All players looking to pursue and help finalize the knowledge base of the WurmWiki or perhaps anyone looking for a safe haven may find a place at Tyrian\". All players are expected to treat one another with respect and are to be independent, with regards to maintaining their own lifestyle.\n</p>\n<p>The people of Tyrian are mature and sensible. We allow free speech, but we as a town keep our thoughts to ourselves.\n</p>\n<center><img alt=\"TyrianSCIENCE-1.png\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r307/mallaboro/TyrianSCIENCE-1.png\"/></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Religion\">Religion</span></h3>\n<p>The people of Tyrian follow no God in particular, however Vynora shrines may be located around the Bay. \"If anything, we believe in SCIENCE\".\n</p>', 0),
(8076, 2233, 'Location', 'Location', 'Directions Freedom , South of Etheral Dawn Map Will be displayed once the settlement token is placed. Town Design', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Directions\">Directions</span></h4>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a>, South of <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_settlement\" title=\"Undefined settlement\">Etheral Dawn</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Map\">Map</span></h3>\n<p>Will be displayed once the settlement token is placed.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Town_Design\">Town Design</span></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"key.png\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r307/mallaboro/key.png\"/>\n</p>\n<center><img alt=\"mainpng-1.png\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r307/mallaboro/mainpng-1.png\"/> <img alt=\"main2png-1.png\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r307/mallaboro/main2png-1.png\"/></center>', 1),
(8077, 2233, 'Members', 'Members', 'Civilians Zinglon - Mayor , cook and terraformer. Ninjabomberman - Carpenter, ship builder, mason. Mallaboro - Miner, blacksmith, carpenter, farmer. Zulop - Miner, blacksmith.', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Civilians\">Civilians</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Zinglon</a> - <b>Mayor</b>, cook and terraformer.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Ninjabomberman</a> - Carpenter, ship builder, mason.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Mallaboro\" title=\"User:Mallaboro\">Mallaboro</a> - Miner, blacksmith, carpenter, farmer.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Zulop</a> - Miner, blacksmith.</li></ul>', 2),
(8078, 2233, 'Research Contributions', 'Research_Contributions', 'Information on a subject Wood scraps Fighting_Skill_Tips Details on... Max speed on cobblestone in full cotton set Alternative requirement to making a Chain Jacket Theories on factors on luck', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Information_on_a_subject\">Information on a subject</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wood_scraps\" title=\"Wood scraps\">Wood scraps</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fighting_Skill_Tips\" title=\"Fighting Skill Tips\">Fighting_Skill_Tips</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Details_on...\">Details on...</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Max speed on cobblestone in full cotton set</li>\n<li>Alternative requirement to making a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_Jacket\" title=\"Chain Jacket\">Chain Jacket</a></li>\n<li>Theories on factors on luck</li></ul>', 3),
(8079, 2235, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'We are located in the bay on the South East corner of the project FRAM|map of the freedom server .  We are a friendly group willing to help out our neighbors when we are available to do so. This village went through a name change during the deed changes and is now known as: Unified Republic of the Red Star.', '<p>We are located in the bay on the South East corner of the project FRAM|map of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_server\" title=\"Freedom server\">freedom server</a>.  We are a friendly group willing to help out our neighbors when we are available to do so.\n</p>\n<p><b></b>\nThis village went through a name change during the deed changes and is now known as:  <b>Unified Republic of the Red Star.</b>\n<b></b>\n</p>', 0),
(8080, 2235, 'Key Members', 'Key_Members', 'Pentax Pilot Ayesha Agra Other Members of Interest Infrared Sobokan danneskjolk - Magranon Priest in training Magic Priest Alts URRSemperor - Magranon Priest Folker - Fo Priest HeadLune - Vynora Priest', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Pentaxpilot\" title=\"Player:Pentaxpilot\">Pentax Pilot</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ayesha\" title=\"Player:Ayesha\">Ayesha</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Agra\" title=\"Player:Agra\">Agra</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_Members_of_Interest\">Other Members of Interest</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Infrared\" title=\"Player:Infrared\">Infrared</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sobokan\" title=\"Player:Sobokan\">Sobokan</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Danneskjolk\" title=\"Player:Danneskjolk\">danneskjolk</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> Priest in training</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Magic\" title=\"Player:Magic\">Magic</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Priest_Alts\">Priest Alts</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:URRSEmperor\" title=\"Player:URRSEmperor\">URRSemperor</a>  -  <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> Priest</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Folker\" title=\"Player:Folker\">Folker</a>  -  <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> Priest</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:HeadLune\" title=\"Player:HeadLune\">HeadLune</a>  -  <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> Priest</li></ul>', 1),
(8081, 2235, 'Nearby Resources', 'Nearby_Resources', 'Clay Moss Tar Multiple Iron Veins Zinc located directly on a bay with sea access and our own personal lake', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">Clay</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">Moss</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">Tar</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron_Vein\" title=\"Iron Vein\">Multiple Iron Veins</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Zinc\" title=\"Zinc\">Zinc</a></li>\n<li>located directly on a bay with sea access and our own personal lake</li></ul>', 2),
(8082, 2235, 'External Links', 'External_Links', 'Main Web Page', '<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://urrsvillage.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Main Web Page</a>\n</p>', 3),
(8083, 2237, 'Background', 'Background', 'Ussta Delmah was a size 5 homestead on the western coast of Mol-Rehan Home , the great lands of Johen King . It was founded on wrath day in week 4 of the starfall of diamonds in the year of 994 by Ulviirala . It was disbanded on the day of tears in week 3 of the starfall of the saw in the year of 998 due to the impending doom on Mol-Rehan Home and was to be reestablished on luck day in week 2 of the starfall of the digging in the year of 998 on the island Flamgra\'in in the northeastern area of the map.', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ussta_Delmah\" title=\"Ussta Delmah\">Ussta Delmah</a> was a size 5 <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">homestead</a> on the western coast of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan_Home\" title=\"Mol-Rehan Home\">Mol-Rehan Home</a>, the great lands of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Johen_King\" title=\"Johen King\">Johen King</a>. It was founded on wrath day in week 4 of the <a href=\"/index.php/Wurm_Universe\" title=\"Wurm Universe\">starfall</a> of diamonds in the year of 994 by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ulviirala\" title=\"Player:Ulviirala\">Ulviirala</a>.\n</p>\n<p>It was disbanded on the day of tears in week 3 of the starfall of the saw in the year of 998 due to the impending doom on Mol-Rehan Home and was to be reestablished on luck day in week 2 of the starfall of the digging in the year of 998 on the island Flamgra\'in in the northeastern area of the map.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(8084, 2237, 'Design', 'Design', 'A map of the construction plans. All of the perimeter was carefully planned, staying true to the not all-flat plzkthx and extraordinary building plans initiatives taken by its proprietor. With the Jatha\'la beldraein d\'ussta delmah , Ussta Delmah features a three-rooms house on a small elevation. It is the main house on the homestead utilized for living, storage, and crafting. It has two 2x3 rooms, and a 2x2 room, all in all 21 usable tiles , enclosed by 34 sturdy stone walls . The path to the entrance is diagonal and elevated at the edges, paved with stone slabs representing teeth, hence why it is called The Jaw . The Beldraen del quivveden d\'ussta delmah is a small 2 by 2 wooden house of somewhat good quality , serving as a suitable doss for guests and travellers. It features plenty of room for storage and a bed for sleeping comfortably. The western perimeter is mainly flat, the corners on the eastern side a rolling upwards with a gentle 4/4 slope , suitable for farming and for integrating the place into the landscape without a sudden abyss along the edges.', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Usstadelmahdesign.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"751\" data-file-width=\"751\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Usstadelmahdesign.jpg/300px-Usstadelmahdesign.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Usstadelmahdesign.jpg/450px-Usstadelmahdesign.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c8/Usstadelmahdesign.jpg/600px-Usstadelmahdesign.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Usstadelmahdesign.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>A map of the construction plans.</div></div></div>\n<p>All of the <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">perimeter</a> was carefully planned, staying true to the <i>not all-flat plzkthx</i> and <i>extraordinary building plans</i> initiatives taken by its proprietor. \n</p>\n<p>With the <i>Jatha\'la beldraein d\'ussta delmah</i>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ussta_Delmah\" title=\"Ussta Delmah\">Ussta Delmah</a> features a three-rooms <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/House_(general)\" title=\"House (general)\">house</a> on a small elevation. It is the main house on the homestead utilized for living, storage, and crafting. It has two 2x3 rooms, and a 2x2 room, all in all 21 usable <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>, enclosed by 34 sturdy <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_wall\" title=\"Stone wall\">stone walls</a>. The path to the entrance is diagonal and elevated at the edges, paved with <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_slab\" title=\"Stone slab\">stone slabs</a> representing teeth, hence why it is called <i>The Jaw</i>.\n</p>\n<p>The <i>Beldraen del quivveden d\'ussta delmah</i> is a small 2 by 2 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_house\" title=\"Wooden house\">wooden house</a> of somewhat good <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, serving as a suitable doss for guests and travellers. It features plenty of room for storage and a <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">bed</a> for sleeping comfortably.\n</p>\n<p>The western perimeter is mainly flat, the corners on the eastern side a rolling upwards with a gentle 4/4 <a href=\"/index.php/Slope\" title=\"Slope\">slope</a>, suitable for <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a> and for integrating the place into the landscape without a sudden abyss along the edges.\n</p>', 1),
(8085, 2237, 'Environment', 'Environment', 'Ussta Delmah does not have many resources in its perimeter apart from a few harvestable trees and a few types of tree that are rather rare on Flamgra\'in. A small part of the deed is used as farmland , growing grains , cotton , wemp plants , and a few vegetables . Within save walls, completely on-deed (not perimeter) Ussta Delmah also accommodates cattle , horses , and deer on the grassy areas. Connected to the shore with a short and straight road, a shipyard and docks, deep enough to harbour even the greatest ships. The latest addition is the Oakmeal Inn adjacent to the docks and open for everyone.', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ussta_Delmah\" title=\"Ussta Delmah\">Ussta Delmah</a> does not have many resources in its perimeter apart from a few harvestable trees and a few types of tree that are rather rare on Flamgra\'in. A small part of the deed is used as <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farmland</a>, growing <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grain\" title=\"Grain\">grains</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Cotton\" title=\"Cotton\">cotton</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_plants\" title=\"Wemp plants\">wemp plants</a>, and a few <a href=\"/index.php/Vegetables\" title=\"Vegetables\">vegetables</a>. Within save walls, <b>completely on-deed</b> (not perimeter) <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ussta_Delmah\" title=\"Ussta Delmah\">Ussta Delmah</a> also accommodates <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cattle\" title=\"Cattle\">cattle</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Deer\" title=\"Deer\">deer</a> on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grassy</a> areas.\n</p>\n<p>Connected to the shore with a short and straight road, a <a href=\"/index.php/Ship\" title=\"Ship\">shipyard</a> and docks, deep enough to harbour even the greatest ships. The latest addition is <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ussta_Delmah#The_Oakmeal_Inn\" title=\"Ussta Delmah\">the Oakmeal Inn</a> adjacent to the docks and open for everyone.\n</p>', 2),
(8086, 2238, 'About the village', 'About_the_village', 'The village sits on the shore of a beautiful bay, The Bay of Bears, and is bordered to its west by woodland, to its east and north by the bay, and to the south by the main highway to Newtown. Three sides of the village, western, southern and eastern, are protected by tall stone walls ; the Northern side of the village is open to the bay. The village has been built on the faint remnants of previous occupation, but to accommodate the new larger settlement land has been reclaimed from the lake and a small hillock has been brought down to lake level with one tier. This reclamation has included the construction of a small harbour and a fishing pier that reaches out beyond the village boundary into deeper water. Buildings The village it self is only half constructed. Two residences have been completed in the south-western corner of the village and are home to the Mayor and Becky. In addition, there is a village store, a workshop next to the forge, a small shed and Fore Paws Village Shop. This shop is located by the front gate and is home to a Public Trader , though from time to time we restrict access. The shop is accessible to travellers and local residents without the need to enter the village front gate, though during transactions they are safe within the village boundary and are subject to the protection of the Spirit Guards . Around the harbour area there are now several stone houses and two wooden cottages, plus some storage. Resources The village has a large internal farm area growing Pumpkins , Potatos , Cereals , Corn , Wemp and Cotton - all with good success. We also have 1 large farm area across the road from the Village on Pine Lake, and another a little further down which is a community project for the Bears of Wurm. We have access to a large mine with 5 iron veins . This mine has also broken through into older working which gave us some cave bug issues - gallantly eradicated by Syrinx and Terasar. Fishing is good and we have plentiful Cherry , Lemon and Olive trees in the area. We are also cultivating oak in the nurseries and cedar and Birch. Access Front Gate The front gate to the village is situated one third along the southern wall, on the main highway heading east. The gate is indented into the wall two tiles so that visitors have access to the Kingdom Trader, when open. There is no automatic entrance to the village through this gate as it is nominally for the use of Citizens only. Visitors are recommended to use the East harbour Gate or arrive at the harbour by water. The east gate is signposted farther along. East Gate The East Gate is situated in the eastern wall near the lake and is the main public access. Follow the main highway heading east along the wall and turn left towards the lake at the south-eastern corner. Follow the path down to the lake. Visitors are welcome to this gate which is kept unlocked at all times. Here one has access to the harbour and the good fishing available from the pier and the harbour wall. This also give access to the village token which is just by the village farm. Forest Gate The Forest or West Gate is located in the western wall at the extreme north-western corner. This gate gives access to the forest. This gate is for citizens only and is kept locked. Harbour Visitors are welcome to arrive at the village from the lake and land at the small harbour. Like the East Gate, this access is open at all times. Safety Zone We have built into our walls safety zones by indenting two of the gates, the Front Gate and the East Gate, by one tile. However, we have also added a more effective safety zone into the south western corner of our walls. This zone, also known as the killing zone, is not only overlooked by the Tower, but is also protected by the village Spirit Guards. As it is a corner, it is possible to run across the corner of our boundary and lure gullible crocodiles and spiders into the trap. We will be adding a donation barrel for travellers who make use of our guards in this way. Please donate however much you like from the bounty gained from butchering the now dead beast. We think this is a fair trade for the traveller facilitating themselves of our overpaid guards. Please bury any resulting corpses - especially your own!', '<p>The village sits on the shore of a beautiful bay, The Bay of Bears, and is bordered to its west by woodland, to its east and north by the bay, and to the south by the main highway to Newtown. Three sides of the village, western, southern and eastern, are protected by <a href=\"/index.php/Tall_stone_wall\" title=\"Tall stone wall\">tall stone walls</a>; the Northern side of the village is open to the bay.\n</p>\n<p>The village has been built on the faint remnants of previous occupation, but to accommodate the new larger settlement land has been reclaimed from the lake and a small hillock has been brought down to lake level with one tier. This reclamation has included the construction of a small harbour and a fishing pier that reaches out beyond the village boundary into deeper water.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Buildings\">Buildings</span></h3>\n<p>The village it self is only half constructed. Two residences have been completed in the south-western corner of the village and are home to the Mayor and Becky. In addition, there is a village store, a workshop next to the forge, a small shed and Fore Paws Village Shop. This shop is located by the front gate and is home to a <a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">Public Trader</a>, though from time to time we restrict access. The shop is accessible to travellers and local residents without the need to enter the village front gate, though during transactions they are safe within the village boundary and are subject to the protection of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spirit_guards\" title=\"Spirit guards\">Spirit Guards</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Around the harbour area there are now several stone houses and two wooden cottages, plus some storage.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span></h3>\n<p>The village has a large internal farm area growing <a href=\"/index.php/Pumpkin\" title=\"Pumpkin\">Pumpkins</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Potato\" title=\"Potato\">Potatos</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oat\" title=\"Oat\">Cereals</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Corn\" title=\"Corn\">Corn</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_plants\" title=\"Wemp plants\">Wemp</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Cotton\" title=\"Cotton\">Cotton</a> - all with good success. We also have 1 large farm area across the road from the Village on Pine Lake, and another a little further down which is a community project for the Bears of Wurm. \n</p>\n<p>We have access to a large <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mine\" title=\"Mine\">mine</a> with 5 <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ore\" title=\"Iron ore\">iron veins</a>. This mine has also broken through into older working which gave us some <a href=\"/index.php/Cave_bug\" title=\"Cave bug\">cave bug</a> issues - gallantly eradicated by Syrinx and Terasar.\n</p>\n<p>Fishing is good and we have plentiful <a href=\"/index.php/Cherry\" title=\"Cherry\">Cherry</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lemon\" title=\"Lemon\">Lemon</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Olive\" title=\"Olive\">Olive</a> trees in the area. We are also cultivating oak in the nurseries and cedar and Birch.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Access\">Access</span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Front_Gate\">Front Gate</span></h4>\n<p>The front gate to the village is situated one third along the southern wall, on the main highway heading east. The gate is indented into the wall two tiles so that visitors have access to the Kingdom Trader, when open. There is no automatic entrance to the village through this gate as it is nominally for the use of Citizens only. Visitors are recommended to use the East harbour Gate or arrive at the harbour by water. The east gate is signposted farther along.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"East_Gate\">East Gate</span></h4>\n<p>The East Gate is situated in the eastern wall near the lake and is the main public access. Follow the main highway heading east along the wall and turn left towards the lake at the south-eastern corner. Follow the path down to the lake. Visitors are welcome to this gate which is kept unlocked at all times. Here one has access to the harbour and the good fishing available from the pier and the harbour wall. This also give access to the village token which is just by the village farm.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Forest_Gate\">Forest Gate</span></h4>\n<p>The Forest or West Gate is located in the western wall at the extreme north-western corner. This gate gives access to the forest. This gate is for citizens only and is kept locked.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Harbour\">Harbour</span></h4>\n<p>Visitors are welcome to arrive at the village from the lake and land at the small harbour. Like the East Gate, this access is open at all times.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Safety_Zone\">Safety Zone</span></h3>\n<p>We have built into our walls safety zones by indenting two of the gates, the Front Gate and the East Gate, by one tile. However, we have also added a more effective safety zone into the south western corner of our walls. This zone, also known as the killing zone, is not only overlooked by the Tower, but is also protected by the village Spirit Guards. As it is a corner, it is possible to run across the corner of our boundary and lure gullible crocodiles and spiders into the trap.\n</p>\n<p>We will be adding a donation barrel for travellers who make use of our guards in this way. Please donate however much you like from the bounty gained from butchering the now dead beast. We think this is a fair trade for the traveller facilitating themselves of our overpaid guards.\n</p>\n<p>Please bury any resulting corpses - especially your own!\n</p>', 0),
(8087, 2238, 'Residents', 'Residents', 'Founder Gurubear Who is now to be found in a very small bay on Independence. Mayor Tealc Citizens In no fixed order ... Andrea Aroundthehorn Beneldorla Benoen Blofield Brattygirl Burningrubber Conger Dangron Elenadia Elwood Erelafay Fenrir Greatphoenix Hatstrosity Hilti Hokimu |Kamie Ladybird Lokia Lolabelle Lureman Maxian Morieta Neoss Nmds Palepu Patro Qob Royster Seleano Splashed Windee Woodchuck And maybe you? Updated 20th April', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Founder\">Founder</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Gurubear\" title=\"Player:Gurubear\">Gurubear</a> Who is now to be found in a very small bay on Independence.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tealc\" title=\"Player:Tealc\">Tealc</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p>In no fixed order ...\n</p>\n<ul><li>Andrea</li>\n<li>Aroundthehorn</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Beneldorla\" title=\"Player:Beneldorla\">Beneldorla</a></li>\n<li>Benoen</li>\n<li>Blofield</li>\n<li>Brattygirl</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Burningrubber</a></li>\n<li>Conger</li>\n<li>Dangron</li>\n<li>Elenadia</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Elwood\" title=\"Player:Elwood\">Elwood</a></li>\n<li>Erelafay</li>\n<li>Fenrir</li>\n<li>Greatphoenix</li>\n<li>Hatstrosity</li>\n<li>Hilti</li>\n<li>Hokimu</li>\n<li>|Kamie</li>\n<li>Ladybird</li>\n<li>Lokia</li>\n<li>Lolabelle</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Lureman\" title=\"Player:Lureman\">Lureman</a></li>\n<li>Maxian</li>\n<li>Morieta</li>\n<li>Neoss</li>\n<li>Nmds</li>\n<li>Palepu</li>\n<li>Patro</li>\n<li>Qob</li>\n<li>Royster</li>\n<li>Seleano</li>\n<li>Splashed</li>\n<li>Windee</li>\n<li>Woodchuck</li></ul>\n<p>And maybe you?\n</p>\n<p>Updated 20th April\n</p>', 1),
(8088, 2238, 'Fishing', 'Fishing', 'The village boasts two prime fishing points, both accessible to the public as well as citizens. The pier stretches out 4 tiles beyond the village boundary into relatively deep water. However, fishing from this point does not require very high skills. As it is beyond the village boundary, visitors can safely drop anything they wish without worries of not being able to pick them up again. However, we would ask that no structure is put up on the pier as this needs to be kept for all to use. The main harbour wall, just by the east wall, is another prime location for fishing. Again, a small strip of tiles is outside the village boundary. One note: the lake is home to several bears who like to quietly float up to our lake side border and amuse themselves by eating fishermen. Do keep an eye out for these cheerful creatures and avoid fishing in thick fog.', '<p>The village boasts two prime fishing points, both accessible to the public as well as citizens.\n</p>\n<p>The pier stretches out 4 tiles beyond the village boundary into relatively deep water. However, fishing from this point does not require very high skills. As it is beyond the village boundary, visitors can safely drop anything they wish without worries of not being able to pick them up again. However, we would ask that no structure is put up on the pier as this needs to be kept for all to use.\n</p>\n<p>The main harbour wall, just by the east wall, is another prime location for fishing. Again, a small strip of tiles is outside the village boundary.\n</p>\n<p>One note: the lake is home to several bears who like to quietly float up to our lake side border and amuse themselves by eating fishermen. Do keep an eye out for these cheerful creatures and avoid fishing in thick fog.\n</p>', 2),
(8089, 2238, 'Notes for Visitors', 'Notes_for_Visitors', 'The Village of Small Bears is a very relaxed company of people, as is the community of which it is part, However, we have a couple of guidelines for visitors and potential settlers alike: No Stealing Please take any rubbish with you No fighting Please be a little careful of some subject matters and language - we are a mixed community of young and old Come and say hello - don\'t just use the trader when it is obvious people are around and about and say nothing. If you have accidentally spawned in the middle of the village, refrain from attacking it just because you are too idiotic to realise that Wurm does not stand still and wait for you for months on end. Look surprised, be cheerful, and move on. Have fun. We are not some overwhelming organisation, nor are we tied in knots by long lists of crazy rules; the mayor is quite simply too old for all that. We always remember that this is just a game.', '<p>The Village of Small Bears is a very relaxed company of people, as is the community of which it is part, \n</p>\n<p>However, we have a couple of guidelines for visitors and potential settlers alike:\n</p>\n<ul><li>No Stealing</li>\n<li>Please take any rubbish with you</li>\n<li>No fighting</li>\n<li>Please be a little careful of some subject matters and language - we are a mixed community of young and old</li>\n<li>Come and say hello - don\'t just use the trader when it is obvious people are around and about and say nothing.</li>\n<li>If you have accidentally spawned in the middle of the village, refrain from attacking it just because you are too idiotic to realise that Wurm does not stand still and wait for you for months on end. Look surprised, be cheerful, and move on.</li>\n<li>Have fun. We are not some overwhelming organisation, nor are we tied in knots by long lists of crazy rules; the mayor is quite simply too old for all that. We always remember that this is just a game.</li></ul>', 3),
(8090, 2238, 'Future Plans', 'Future_Plans', 'Well, whatever next? The Village of the Small Bears has grown much over the last year. It\'s harbour boasts many boats, we have built two giant colossi, a pier has been constructed, and the beach and the shore frontage are being finished as I type. But things should not stay like that, and the Founder, he of many a wild and furry idea, will soon be putting pen to paper and designing another great task for the busy citizens. Watch this space!', '<p>Well, whatever next?\n</p>\n<p>The Village of the Small Bears has grown much over the last year. It\'s harbour boasts many boats, we have built two giant colossi, a pier has been constructed, and the beach and the shore frontage are being finished as I type.\n</p>\n<p>But things should not stay like that, and the Founder, he of many a wild and furry idea, will soon be putting pen to paper and designing another great task for the busy citizens. \n</p>\n<p>Watch this space!\n</p>', 4),
(8091, 2238, 'How to find us', 'How_to_find_us', 'The village is only a few minutes away from Newtown and is simple to locate. Head east from Newtown over the half completed land bridge across the lake. Turn left on the eastern shore and follow the path up the side of the hill. Continue on the path over the hill and down the other side. At the junction, as the main highway turns left towards Serene Bear Landing, continue straight on down the hill following the smaller path; the path widens again after a few hundred meters. The Village of Small Bears will come into your sight on the left hand side of the road behind the long tall stone walls.', '<p>The village is only a few minutes away from Newtown and is simple to locate. Head east from Newtown over the half completed land bridge across the lake. Turn left on the eastern shore and follow the path up the side of the hill. Continue on the path over the hill and down the other side. At the junction, as the main highway turns left towards Serene Bear Landing, continue straight on down the hill following the smaller path; the path widens again after a few hundred meters. The Village of Small Bears will come into your sight on the left hand side of the road behind the long tall stone walls.\n</p>', 5),
(8092, 2238, 'Recruiting Citizens', 'Recruiting_Citizens', 'We are keen to encourage and help any and all players that want to settle down to this rather laid back and Zen type of existence round Bear Bay. There is plenty of land available to build on, or you may be interested in moving into one of the vacant properties in the village itself. If you wish to become a citizen, all we ask is that you are prepared to join in with the various projects and to help others both in and around the village. We are looking especially for players who are prepared to give a long term commitment to the village and the community around Bear Bay. We are closely associated with Serene Bear Landing on the other side of the bay and are considering joint projects with their mayor, Sillyma. If you are interested in applying for citizenship, please come and talk to Tealc, or PM him in game.', '<p>We are keen to encourage and help any and all players that want to settle down to this rather laid back and Zen type of existence round Bear Bay. There is plenty of land available to build on, or you may be interested in moving into one of the vacant properties in the village itself. If you wish to become a citizen, all we ask is that you are prepared to join in with the various projects and to help others both in and around the village. We are looking especially for players who are prepared to give a long term commitment to the village and the community around Bear Bay.\n</p>\n<p>We are closely associated with Serene Bear Landing on the other side of the bay and are considering joint projects with their mayor, Sillyma.\n</p>\n<p>If you are interested in applying for citizenship, please come and talk to Tealc, or PM him in game.\n</p>', 6),
(8093, 2239, 'Citizens', 'Citizens', 'Dragonhead Kehelekarakh Misterangry Nepulus Sumtinrother Yoplitein (alt of Misterangry) Ctrlaltdelete (holds deed for Shipyard of Flamgra\'in)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Dragonhead\" title=\"Player:Dragonhead\">Dragonhead</a></li>\n<li>Kehelekarakh</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Misterangry\" title=\"Player:Misterangry\">Misterangry</a></li>\n<li>Nepulus</li>\n<li>Sumtinrother</li>\n<li>Yoplitein (alt of Misterangry)</li>\n<li>Ctrlaltdelete (holds deed for Shipyard of Flamgra\'in)</li></ul>', 0),
(8094, 2239, 'Shipyard of Flamgra\'in', 'Shipyard_of_Flamgra.27in', 'Shipyard of Flamgra\'in was an 11x11 deed on the west coast of Flamgra\'in, owned by Ctrlaltdelete ( alt of Misterangry ). It is open for all residents of the island to use for boat keeping.', '<p>Shipyard of Flamgra\'in was an 11x11 deed on the west coast of Flamgra\'in, owned by Ctrlaltdelete (<i>alt of Misterangry</i>). It is open for all residents of the island to use for boat keeping.\n</p>', 1),
(8095, 2240, 'About Well of Souls', 'About_Well_of_Souls', 'Well of Souls was founded by Adje .\nIt is a hard working community focussed on infrastructure and mining. Well of Souls provides healing, food and water to passerbys.', '<p>Well of Souls was founded by <a href=\"/index.php/User:Adje\" title=\"User:Adje\">Adje</a>.\nIt is a hard working community focussed on infrastructure and mining.\n</p>\n<p><b>Well of Souls provides healing, food and water to passerbys.</b>\n</p>', 0),
(8096, 2243, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'On top of a mountain south of Darkenstone, high above the world, lies Wynnger Observatory. Far away from any settlement this is the perfect place to watch the stars.\nVisitors need to climb a path, dodge the Trolls from the troll spawn and summon Batolemaeus from his retirement to see the place.', '<p>On top of a mountain south of Darkenstone, high above the world, lies Wynnger Observatory. Far away from any settlement this is the perfect place to watch the stars.\nVisitors need to climb a path, dodge the Trolls from the troll spawn and summon Batolemaeus from his retirement to see the place.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(8097, 2243, 'Trade', 'Trade', 'Wynnger Observatory is selling Enlightenment. Buy two, get one free!', '<p>Wynnger Observatory is selling Enlightenment. Buy two, get one free!\n</p>', 1),
(8098, 2244, 'Description', 'Description', 'Re-founded in the Freedom Lands, Outer Heaven once again continues to strive for excellence within the community of Wurm. Part of the Fomorach Alliance, Outer Heaven once again has become a symbol of greatness amongst its peers. Leader Amikron - Digger , Excavator , Land Shaper , Miner , Lumberjack , Handyman , Mason , Carpenter', '<p>Re-founded in the Freedom Lands, Outer Heaven once again continues to strive for excellence within the community of Wurm. Part of the Fomorach Alliance, \n</p>\n<p>Outer Heaven once again has become a symbol of greatness amongst its peers.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Leader\">Leader</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Amikron\" title=\"Player:Amikron\">Amikron</a> - <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Digger\" title=\"Digger\">Digger</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Excavator\" title=\"Excavator\">Excavator</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Land_Shaper\" title=\"Land Shaper\">Land Shaper</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Miner\" title=\"Miner\">Miner</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lumberjack\" title=\"Lumberjack\">Lumberjack</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Handyman\" title=\"Handyman\">Handyman</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mason\" title=\"Mason\">Mason</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Carpenter\" title=\"Carpenter\">Carpenter</a></li></ul>', 0),
(8099, 2245, 'Description', 'Description', 'Pirate outpost, Size 5 homestead. Planted by cubeman\'s alt. Cool place to be. Mayor Sourceman', '<p>Pirate outpost, Size 5 homestead. Planted by cubeman\'s alt. Cool place to be.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Sourceman\" title=\"Player:Sourceman\">Sourceman</a></li></ul>', 0),
(8100, 2246, 'Description', 'Description', 'Potidaea was a size 20 village settled east of Freedom Market', '<p><b>Potidaea</b> was a size 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">village</a> settled east of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Freedom_Market\" title=\"Freedom Market\">Freedom Market</a>\n</p>', 0),
(8101, 2247, 'Background', 'Background', 'Rocksville is a reasonable sized deed situated half way up a mountain, north of Oreo .', '<p>Rocksville is a reasonable sized deed situated half way up a mountain, north of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oreo\" title=\"Oreo\">Oreo</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(8102, 2247, 'Villagers', 'Villagers', 'Syncaidius (Mayor) Cerberius (Syncaidius\' priest alt) Blarster', '<ul><li>Syncaidius (Mayor)</li>\n<li>Cerberius (Syncaidius\' priest alt)</li>\n<li>Blarster</li></ul>', 1),
(8103, 2248, 'Background', 'Background', 'Rockwood is a reasonable sized deed situated about 200 tiles south east of Merchant Town.', '<p>Rockwood is a reasonable sized deed situated about 200 tiles south east of Merchant Town.\n</p>', 0),
(8104, 2250, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sealand was a HotS village on the Wild server located on an artificial island north-east of the Shroud.', '<p>Sealand was a HotS village on the Wild server located on an artificial island north-east of the Shroud.\n</p>', 0),
(8105, 2251, 'History', 'History', 'Shadow Requiem was formed when the members of Darkwoods and Obsidia decided to merge and relocate. After extensive discussion, both sides deemed the act beneficial and created one of the larger BL settlements .', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shadow_Requiem\" title=\"Shadow Requiem\">Shadow Requiem</a> was formed when the members of Darkwoods and Obsidia decided to merge and relocate. After extensive discussion, both sides deemed the act beneficial and created one of the larger <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/BL\" title=\"BL\">BL</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Settlements\" title=\"Settlements\">settlements</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(8106, 2251, 'Contact', 'Contact', 'here', '<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://hots.ipbfree.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a>', 1),
(8107, 2251, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Kabill - [Excavator], [Handyman], [Mastermine], [Trollslayer] Elders Chromega - [Blacksmith], [Digger], [Goldsmith], [Handyman], [Keeper of Faith], [Trollslayer] Corbindallis - [Mason], [Trollslayer] Daiken - [Carpenter], [Excavator], [Handyman], [Mason], [Trollslayer] Zeblalt - Priest [Trollslayer] Citizens Crimsonwolf - Priest [Digger], [Handyman], [Lumberjack], [Miner], [Repairman], [Tanner], [Trollslayer], [Warrior] Davidbritsky - [Trollslayer] Dipse Dongiblioni Fez - [Dragonslayer], [Miner], [Warrior] Fieron - [Carpenter], [Digger], [Tanner], [Trollslayer] Fuel - [Digger], [Dragonslayer], [Handyman], [Keeper of Faith], [Lumberjack], [Miner], [Trollslayer], [Warrior] Glenskunk Imbill Mastex Mojo - [Carpenter], [Destroyer of Faith] Puzzle Raloc Shortass - [Ageless], [Destroyer of Faith] Tealmercury - [Digger] Vakai Zekedge - [Destroyer of Faith]', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Kabill\" title=\"Player:Kabill\">Kabill</a> - [Excavator], [Handyman], [Mastermine], [Trollslayer]</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Chromega\" title=\"User:Chromega\">Chromega</a> - [Blacksmith], [Digger], [Goldsmith], [Handyman], [Keeper of Faith], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li>Corbindallis - [Mason], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Daiken\" title=\"Player:Daiken\">Daiken</a> - [Carpenter], [Excavator], [Handyman], [Mason], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeblalt\" title=\"Player:Zeblalt\">Zeblalt</a> - <b>Priest</b> [Trollslayer]</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Crimsonwolf\" title=\"Player:Crimsonwolf\">Crimsonwolf</a> - <b>Priest</b> [Digger], [Handyman], [Lumberjack], [Miner], [Repairman], [Tanner], [Trollslayer], [Warrior]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Davidbritsky\" title=\"Player:Davidbritsky\">Davidbritsky</a> - [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Dipse\" title=\"Player:Dipse\">Dipse</a></li>\n<li>Dongiblioni</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fez\" title=\"Player:Fez\">Fez</a> - [Dragonslayer], [Miner], [Warrior]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fieron\" title=\"Player:Fieron\">Fieron</a> - [Carpenter], [Digger], [Tanner], [Trollslayer]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fuel\" title=\"Player:Fuel\">Fuel</a> - [Digger], [Dragonslayer], [Handyman], [Keeper of Faith], [Lumberjack], [Miner], [Trollslayer], [Warrior]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Glenskunk\" title=\"Player:Glenskunk\">Glenskunk</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Imbill\" title=\"Player:Imbill\">Imbill</a></li>\n<li>Mastex</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Mojo\" title=\"Player:Mojo\">Mojo</a> - [Carpenter], [Destroyer of Faith]</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Puzzle\" title=\"Player:Puzzle\">Puzzle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Raloc\" title=\"Player:Raloc\">Raloc</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Shortass\" title=\"Player:Shortass\">Shortass</a> - [Ageless], [Destroyer of Faith]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tealmercury\" title=\"Player:Tealmercury\">Tealmercury</a> - [Digger]</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Vakai\" title=\"Player:Vakai\">Vakai</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Zekedge\" title=\"Player:Zekedge\">Zekedge</a> - [Destroyer of Faith]</li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(8108, 2251, 'Raid Log', 'Raid_Log', 'Villages 12/4/2007 Caelohh proudly displays the 8 silver, 43 copper and 75 iron he found in the coffers of Independent Settlers. disbanded 6 hours later Homesteads 12/4/2007 Kabill proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Offtopica Wl Roadside Trade Post. 12/15/2007 Wossoo proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Rivendell Customs and Shelter. 12/22/2007 Kabill proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Kendrick\'s Laboratory. 12/22/2007 Fuel proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Valhalla. 12/23/2007 Crimsonwolf proudly displays the 19 copper and 8 iron he found in the coffers of Kendrick\'s Laboratory. disbanded due to upkeep 12/26/2007 Fuel proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Valhalla.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Villages\">Villages</span></h3>\n<ul><li>12/4/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Caelohh\" title=\"Player:Caelohh\">Caelohh</a> proudly displays the 8 silver, 43 copper and 75 iron he found in the coffers of Independent Settlers. <i>disbanded 6 hours later</i></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Homesteads\">Homesteads</span></h3>\n<ul><li>12/4/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Kabill\" title=\"Player:Kabill\">Kabill</a> proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Offtopica Wl Roadside Trade Post.</li>\n<li>12/15/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Wossoo\" title=\"Player:Wossoo\">Wossoo</a> proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Rivendell Customs and Shelter.</li>\n<li>12/22/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Kabill\" title=\"Player:Kabill\">Kabill</a> proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Kendrick\'s Laboratory.</li>\n<li>12/22/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fuel\" title=\"Player:Fuel\">Fuel</a> proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Valhalla.</li>\n<li>12/23/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Crimsonwolf\" title=\"Player:Crimsonwolf\">Crimsonwolf</a> proudly displays the 19 copper and 8 iron he found in the coffers of Kendrick\'s Laboratory. <i>disbanded due to upkeep</i></li>\n<li>12/26/2007 <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fuel\" title=\"Player:Fuel\">Fuel</a> proudly displays the 37 copper and 50 iron he found in the coffers of Valhalla.</li></ul>', 3),
(8109, 2251, 'Uniques Slain', 'Uniques_Slain', 'The 2nd Forest Giant. Forest Giant v2.0 Shadow Requiem ventured with Libilian Outlaws|LO to take down the mighty beast after the unique respawn, and Ryuu landed the final blow. The 2nd Red Dragon. Red Dragon v2.0 Shadow Requiem ventured with Libilian Outlaws|LO and some of the Home BLers to conquer the king of all uniques. Drenx landed the final blow.', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:102px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Forest_Giant.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"1015\" data-file-width=\"787\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"129\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/8a/Forest_Giant.jpg/100px-Forest_Giant.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/8a/Forest_Giant.jpg/150px-Forest_Giant.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/8a/Forest_Giant.jpg/200px-Forest_Giant.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Forest_Giant.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The 2nd Forest Giant.</div></div></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<br/><b>Forest Giant v2.0</b><br/>\nShadow Requiem ventured with Libilian Outlaws|LO to take down the mighty beast after the unique respawn, and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ryuu\" title=\"Player:Ryuu\">Ryuu</a> landed the final blow.\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:102px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Red_dragon1.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"464\" data-file-width=\"792\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"59\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/84/Red_dragon1.png/100px-Red_dragon1.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/84/Red_dragon1.png/150px-Red_dragon1.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/84/Red_dragon1.png/200px-Red_dragon1.png 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Red_dragon1.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The 2nd Red Dragon.</div></div></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<br/><b>Red Dragon v2.0</b><br/>\nShadow Requiem ventured with Libilian Outlaws|LO and some of the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Home\" title=\"Home\">Home</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/BL\" title=\"BL\">BLers</a> to conquer the king of all uniques. <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Drenx</a> landed the final blow.\n</p>', 4),
(8110, 2252, 'General Information', 'General_Information', 'Shantytown was an undeeded settlement located on the Wild Server. It was primarily known as a camp for refugees who haven\'t managed to settle in the Pirate Outpost . Shantytown was an independent village, only geographically associated with Pirate Outpost . Its full name was \"People\'s Socialist Republic of Shantytown\". However, the full name was used only in case of declaring wars, signing peace treaties and creating alliances. Shantytown is a peaceful Jenn-Kellon settlement, often described as \"Newtown of Wild\". Inhabitants of the village were always helpful, and always ready to aid newcomers. After Milp had decided to move onto a bigger project and moved away, most of the Shantytown citizens had already moved to other settlements. Often deeded unlike Shantytown. Milp and Sentinelxs had decided to work on the New Prypjat project.', '<p>Shantytown was an undeeded settlement located on the Wild Server. It was primarily known as a camp for refugees who haven\'t managed to settle in the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pirate_Outpost\" title=\"Pirate Outpost\">Pirate Outpost</a>. Shantytown was an independent village, only geographically associated with <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pirate_Outpost\" title=\"Pirate Outpost\">Pirate Outpost</a>. Its full name was \"People\'s Socialist Republic of Shantytown\". However, the full name was used only in case of declaring wars, signing peace treaties and creating alliances. Shantytown is a peaceful <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> settlement, often described as \"Newtown of Wild\". Inhabitants of the village were always helpful, and always ready to aid newcomers.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nAfter <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> had decided to move onto a bigger project and moved away, most of the Shantytown citizens had already moved to other settlements. Often deeded unlike Shantytown. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sentinelxs\" title=\"Player:Sentinelxs\">Sentinelxs</a> had decided to work on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/New_Prypjat\" title=\"New Prypjat\">New Prypjat</a> project.\n</p>', 0),
(8111, 2252, 'Location', 'Location', 'Shantytown was conveniently located in the north most tundra on the Wild map. The terrain around Shantytown was relatively free of trees, although the tundra was (and still is) surrounded with great pines and other fruit trees. Shantytown now lies in ruin, with the outlines of buildings and winding paths stretching across the tundra. Milp created his New Prypjat just south of the old location. Then Milp built his empire in the tundra making sure to preserve the location of Shantytown. Now Shantytown the tundra is being actively worked and walled off so that it may be preserved, protected and hunted privately.', '<p>Shantytown was conveniently located in the north most tundra on the Wild map. The terrain around Shantytown was relatively free of trees, although the tundra was (and still is) surrounded with great pines and other fruit trees. Shantytown now lies in ruin, with the outlines of buildings and winding paths stretching across the tundra. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> created his <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/New_Prypjat\" title=\"New Prypjat\">New Prypjat</a> just south of the old location. Then <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> built his empire in the tundra making sure to preserve the location of Shantytown. Now Shantytown the tundra is being actively worked and walled off so that it may be preserved, protected and hunted privately.\n</p>', 1),
(8112, 2252, 'Conditions', 'Conditions', 'Conditions in Shantytown were horrid. The settlement was covered in pits and valleys that were created by the new players and citizens of Shantytown. The same issue occurred in mines with there being winding paths and huge plummets including the entrance. Although space and help was given by the carefree citizens and leaders, the issue of food was huge, although Milp promised food, the citizens were often without food. Water was abundant as well but citizens had to walk down a very long mineshaft to get to it. Another problem that arrised was that citizens were unequipped for certain tasks. Such as making food. During one great chapter in history the citizens of Shantytown were told that no food would be supplied until a large wall was errected all the way around Shantytown. Some of the citizens complied with the order and started to make the wall. Others were angry with this order and rejected it. This created some problems when all the citizens had no food to eat and could not work. So the great event started where every able bodied man in Shantytown was helping make the devices and items required to make food. They stole a Large Anvil from an abandoned house in town, and began mining the ore in order to make a cauldron. The idea was to make soup, enought for everyone in the town. With some fine crafting skills from Sentinelxs the had made a cauldron. Scrounged meat and water from the local fountain were added and 1QL soup was produced.', '<p>Conditions in Shantytown were horrid. The settlement was covered in pits and valleys that were created by the new players and citizens of Shantytown. The same issue occurred in mines with there being winding paths and huge plummets including the entrance. Although space and help was given by the carefree citizens and leaders, the issue of food was huge, although <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> promised food, the citizens were often without food. Water was abundant as well but citizens had to walk down a very long mineshaft to get to it. \n</p>\n<p>Another problem that arrised was that citizens were unequipped for certain tasks. Such as making food. During one great chapter in history the citizens of Shantytown were told that no food would be supplied until a large wall was errected all the way around Shantytown. Some of the citizens complied with the order and started to make the wall. Others were angry with this order and rejected it. This created some problems when all the citizens had no food to eat and could not work. So the great event started where every able bodied man in Shantytown was helping make the devices and items required to make food. They stole a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Anvil\" title=\"Large Anvil\">Large Anvil</a> from an abandoned house in town, and began mining the ore in order to make a cauldron. The idea was to make soup, enought for everyone in the town. With some fine crafting skills from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sentinelxs\" title=\"Player:Sentinelxs\">Sentinelxs</a> the had made a cauldron. Scrounged meat and water from the local fountain were added and 1QL soup was produced.\n</p>', 2),
(8113, 2252, 'Citizens of Shantytown', 'Citizens_of_Shantytown', 'Mayor Milp / Kelp Shantytown Elder Citizens Tbot / Jackthehunter Slavik Aikhjarto Blofield Gulzan Ohlol Shantytown Citizens Foxhound Adborr / Adboar Ilurvslavvypoo Matalan Millan Sameo Fernando Ramma Afrodude Schiff Aljaud Tonxcz Sentinelxs Muffinman Archronos Hogue Jsm Ephemeral Evveron Titesitt', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> / <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Kelp\" title=\"Player:Kelp\">Kelp</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shantytown_Elder_Citizens\">Shantytown Elder Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Tbot\" title=\"Player:Tbot\">Tbot</a> / Jackthehunter</li>\n<li>Slavik</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Aikhjarto\" title=\"Player:Aikhjarto\">Aikhjarto</a></li>\n<li>Blofield</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Gulzan\" title=\"Player:Gulzan\">Gulzan</a></li>\n<li>Ohlol</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shantytown_Citizens\">Shantytown Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Foxhound</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Adborr\" title=\"Player:Adborr\">Adborr</a> / <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Adboar\" title=\"Player:Adboar\">Adboar</a></li>\n<li>Ilurvslavvypoo</li>\n<li>Matalan</li>\n<li>Millan</li>\n<li>Sameo</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fernando\" title=\"Player:Fernando\">Fernando</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ramma\" title=\"Player:Ramma\">Ramma</a></li>\n<li>Afrodude</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Schiff\" title=\"Player:Schiff\">Schiff</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Aljaud\" title=\"Player:Aljaud\">Aljaud</a></li>\n<li>Tonxcz</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sentinelxs\" title=\"Player:Sentinelxs\">Sentinelxs</a></li>\n<li>Muffinman</li>\n<li>Archronos</li>\n<li>Hogue</li>\n<li>Jsm</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ephemeral\" title=\"Player:Ephemeral\">Ephemeral</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Evveron\" title=\"Player:Evveron\">Evveron</a></li>\n<li>Titesitt</li></ul>', 3),
(8114, 2252, 'Enemies of Shantytown', 'Enemies_of_Shantytown', 'Curbstomp Hybridtheory Helmetsnipe During the last weeks of Shantytown \'s occupation, citizens from Pirate Outpost had been causing grief and general chaos. Citizens of Shantytown had taken offense and also had taken action against them. At one point raiding them and doing damage to their town, stealing and looting the town. After this both settlements had become enemy.', '<ul><li>Curbstomp</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Hybridtheory\" title=\"Player:Hybridtheory\">Hybridtheory</a></li>\n<li>Helmetsnipe</li></ul>\n<p>During the last weeks of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shantytown\" title=\"Shantytown\">Shantytown</a>\'s occupation, citizens from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pirate_Outpost\" title=\"Pirate Outpost\">Pirate Outpost</a> had been causing grief and general chaos. Citizens of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shantytown\" title=\"Shantytown\">Shantytown</a> had taken offense and also had taken action against them. At one point raiding them and doing damage to their town, stealing and looting the town. After this both settlements had become enemy.\n</p>', 4),
(8115, 2252, 'Random History Snipits', 'Random_History_Snipits', 'After Shantytown was abandoned, Milp took a lot of the relics and inside joke items from Shantytown and put them in his new town The original \"EATING OKAY / TAKING NAY!\" sign resides in New Prypjat . Sentinelxs \'s \"fail moat\" around his house still is visible at the sight, if you know where to look. Sameo (now goobles) Kyara fried chicken setup is still visible at the sight, if you know where to look. The mine is, and always will be fail. As the mine entrance is all wonky. Milp once created a gatehouse with one door, deemed \"Failhouse.\" Shantytown wasn\'t good enough for Milp . That\'s why he made his own deed else where.', '<ul><li>After Shantytown was abandoned, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> took a lot of the relics and inside joke items from Shantytown and put them in his new town</li>\n<li>The original \"EATING OKAY / TAKING NAY!\" sign resides in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/New_Prypjat\" title=\"New Prypjat\">New Prypjat</a>.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sentinelxs\" title=\"Player:Sentinelxs\">Sentinelxs</a>\'s \"fail moat\" around his house still is visible at the sight, if you know where to look.</li>\n<li>Sameo (now goobles) Kyara fried chicken setup is still visible at the sight, if you know where to look.</li>\n<li>The mine is, and always will be fail. As the mine entrance is all wonky.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a> once created a gatehouse with one door, deemed \"Failhouse.\"</li>\n<li>Shantytown wasn\'t good enough for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Milp\" title=\"Player:Milp\">Milp</a>. That\'s why he made his own deed else where.</li></ul>', 5),
(8116, 2253, 'Shaolin Monastery', 'Shaolin_Monastery', 'Shaolin Monastery is a Chán Buddhist temple in the Jenn-Kellon Province, legend goes there was a fierce storm, the following morning the temple appeared, as if it had always been there. it is said the doors of the temple are open to any weary traveler in need of aid or shelter. Not much is known about the monks or the temple, though it is said these monks practice a fighting style unknown in the lands based upon the movement and characteristics of animals. Each animal embodies a particular range of strategies and styles. It is said to take half a lifetime to master any one of the Shaolin Fighting styles. on Luck day in week 1 of the starfall of Silence in the year of 1009 the Shaolin Monastery fleeing to Horde of the Summoned after  betraying the Jenn-Kellon kingdom for their treacherous acts against humanity has allied itself with the emperor Disciples of The Shaolin Jacob Sunchun Helpbhotone Kuja Lordjustinian The Heirlooms of Shaolin Eye of Buddha  Lost to Mol-Rehan in the great fall of the Shaolin Monastery', '<p>Shaolin Monastery is a Chán Buddhist temple in the Jenn-Kellon Province, legend goes there was a fierce storm, the following morning the temple appeared, as if it had always been there. it is said the doors of the temple are open to any weary traveler in need of aid or shelter.\n</p>\n<p>Not much is known about the monks or the temple, though it is said these monks practice a fighting style unknown in the lands based upon the movement and characteristics of animals. Each animal embodies a particular range of strategies and styles. It is said to take half a lifetime to master any one of the Shaolin Fighting styles.\n</p>\n<p>on Luck day in week 1 of the starfall of Silence in the year of 1009 the Shaolin Monastery fleeing to <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a>  after  betraying the <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> kingdom for their treacherous acts against humanity has allied itself with the emperor \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Disciples_of_The_Shaolin\">Disciples of The Shaolin</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Jacob\" title=\"Player:Jacob\">Jacob</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Sunchun\" title=\"Player:Sunchun\">Sunchun</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Helpbhotone\" title=\"Player:Helpbhotone\">Helpbhotone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Kuja\" title=\"Player:Kuja\">Kuja</a></li>\n<li>Lordjustinian</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Heirlooms_of_Shaolin\">The Heirlooms of Shaolin</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Eye of Buddha  Lost to <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a> in the great fall of the Shaolin Monastery</li></ul>', 0),
(8117, 2254, 'Village Description', 'Village_Description', 'We\'re a new village on Freedom we settled during august 2009, ours goals to become a thriving self suffient village with access to as many raw materials and resources as possibly and hopefully trade resources and crafted materials with our neighbours and other people alike. We\'re primarily active in european timezones, with a population currently spreading over UK and Scandinavia. Any questions regarding the village can be directed to either Julepalme or fmrunga via ingame whispers.', '<p>We\'re a new village on Freedom we settled during august 2009, ours goals to become a thriving self suffient village with access to as many raw materials and resources as possibly and hopefully trade resources and crafted materials with our neighbours and other people alike.\n</p>\n<p>We\'re primarily active in european timezones, with a population currently spreading over UK and Scandinavia.\n</p>\n<p>Any questions regarding the village can be directed to either Julepalme or fmrunga via ingame whispers.\n</p>', 0),
(8118, 2254, 'Village Members', 'Village_Members', 'Mayor Julepalme Mayor of Silverhill Co-Mayor fmrunga Allied & Owner of Silverhill Port Citizens felleanderson spiritusante psychedemic defensa deruu rarati Baeralorn Ketamin', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Julepalme\" title=\"Player:Julepalme\">Julepalme</a> Mayor of Silverhill</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Co-Mayor\">Co-Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Fmrunga\" title=\"Player:Fmrunga\">fmrunga</a> Allied &amp; Owner of Silverhill Port</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li>felleanderson</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Spiritusante\" title=\"Player:Spiritusante\">spiritusante</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Psychedemic\" title=\"Player:Psychedemic\">psychedemic</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Defensa\" title=\"Player:Defensa\">defensa</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Deruu\" title=\"Player:Deruu\">deruu</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Rarati\" title=\"Player:Rarati\">rarati</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Baeralorn\" title=\"Player:Baeralorn\">Baeralorn</a></li>\n<li>Ketamin</li></ul>', 1),
(8119, 2254, 'Recruiting', 'Recruiting', 'We\'re a group of friends mostly.. but if you\'re eager to join we\'ll consider it, we\'re open to newcomers and hope to start a thriving village.', '<p>We\'re a group of friends mostly.. but if you\'re eager to join we\'ll consider it, we\'re open to newcomers and hope to start a thriving village.\n</p>', 2),
(8120, 2254, 'Location', 'Location', 'We\'re located at 21x 43y on the player made map of freedom isles, we\'ve applied to get on the map but its currently not quite there yet. were about 1-1½ hours sail away from samling in average wind conditions in a sailing boat.', '<p>We\'re located at 21x 43y on the player made map of freedom isles, we\'ve applied to get on the map but its currently not quite there yet. were about 1-1½ hours sail away from samling in average wind conditions in a sailing boat.\n</p>', 3),
(8121, 2254, 'Resources available', 'Resources_available', 'Clay (200 tiles north of us, either by packed dirt road or by boat at our neighbour apintp) Tar (On the SE Side of the bay, quick 2 minutes sail across the bay) Sand (Right next to our harbor) Wood (Pine, Maple and Cedar in large quantities) Moss (Currently deep in the woods south of us, but working on making it accessible by road) Ores (We have copper, tin and iron currently mineable and zinc has been prospected aswell, missing lead, silver & gold so far)', '<p>Clay (200 tiles north of us, either by packed dirt road or by boat at our neighbour apintp)\n</p>\n<p>Tar (On the SE Side of the bay, quick 2 minutes sail across the bay)\n</p>\n<p>Sand (Right next to our harbor)\n</p>\n<p>Wood (Pine, Maple and Cedar in large quantities)\n</p>\n<p>Moss (Currently deep in the woods south of us, but working on making it accessible by road)\n</p>\n<p>Ores (We have copper, tin and iron currently mineable and zinc has been prospected aswell, missing lead, silver &amp; gold so far)\n</p>', 4),
(8122, 2254, 'Wildlife', 'Wildlife', 'Our current area has 6 known animal lairs: troll, goblin, deer, unicorn, mountain lion and wild cat We currently have a thriving wild population of unicorn roaming around our general area. And heres a list of the creatures we see most often: wolves, dogs, deer, cows, lava spiders, huge spiders, unicorn and scorpions And less often: trolls, goblins, crocs, horses, pigs, pheasant, bears both black and brown.', '<p>Our current area has 6 known animal lairs: troll, goblin, deer, unicorn, mountain lion and wild cat\n</p>\n<p>We currently have a thriving wild population of unicorn roaming around our general area.\n</p>\n<p>And heres a list of the creatures we see most often: wolves, dogs, deer, cows, lava spiders, huge spiders, unicorn and scorpions\n</p>\n<p>And less often: trolls, goblins, crocs, horses, pigs, pheasant, bears both black and brown.\n</p>', 5),
(8123, 2254, 'Current projects', 'Current_projects', 'Fields and animal pens (50% done) Building and deoorating the harbor (90% done) Terraforming the village stage 1 (55% done) Terraforming the village stage 2 (0% done) Internal Roading between harbor, farm, mine and village (95% done) Citizen housing 2x3 stone houses. (5% done) Road north up coast to our neighbours, missing pavement and some slopes fixed (80% done) Road SW over the mountains to the SW bay area is another of our biggest projects to do´as we progress with the village, scouting completed successfully, road construction begun (5% done) Terraforming and digging a mine with 7x6 smithing/storage area and finding iron (Done)', '<p>Fields and animal pens (50% done)\n</p>\n<p>Building and deoorating the harbor (90% done)\n</p>\n<p>Terraforming the village stage 1 (55% done)\n</p>\n<p>Terraforming the village stage 2 (0% done)\n</p>\n<p>Internal Roading between harbor, farm, mine and village (95% done)\n</p>\n<p>Citizen housing 2x3 stone houses. (5% done)\n</p>\n<p>Road north up coast to our neighbours, missing pavement and some slopes fixed (80% done) \n</p>\n<p>Road SW over the mountains to the SW bay area is another of our biggest projects to do´as we progress with the village, scouting completed successfully, road construction begun (5% done)\n</p>\n<p>Terraforming and digging a mine with 7x6 smithing/storage area and finding iron (Done)\n</p>', 6),
(8124, 2255, 'Background', 'Background', 'More information soon!', '<p>More information soon!\n</p>', 0),
(8125, 2260, 'General Info', 'General_Info', 'The Pirate Outpost was founded during the end of the last beta map by Raloc and Starving(midget).  It was created under the impression that the players who joined should have unlimited freedom but always keeping the Pirate Outpost before all else.  In later times a more pirate like theme of looting and plundering was adopted and we became widely known for it (causing one of the biggest civil wars at its time). It is currently residing in the BMO Tundra, directly south of Kyara .', '<p>The Pirate Outpost was founded during the end of the last beta map by Raloc and Starving(midget).  It was created under the impression that the players who joined should have unlimited freedom but always keeping the Pirate Outpost before all else.  In later times a more pirate like theme of looting and plundering was adopted and we became widely known for it (causing one of the biggest civil wars at its time).\n</p>\n<p>It is currently residing in the BMO Tundra, directly south of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Kyara\" title=\"Kyara\">Kyara</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(8126, 2260, 'History', 'History', 'The Original Pirate Outpost was an idea formed during a 48 hour server downtime on the forums, it started as a simple idea as a town and slowly expanded on it.  In the 48 hours the server was down, the thread had grown to 25 pages and the idea was set and prepared to be executed.  The first one to join me in helping in this venture was Starvingmidget, who had an undying faith that we would do good.  We chose an island 15 minutes away from the largest town at the time ( Kyara ) and went about starting.  It soon grew, gaining several new members quickly (some notable mentions: Gedd, Crimsonwolf, Puzzle, Flimmy, Zelar being some of the few that started at Pirate Outpost and later moved on to other places) and a stone wall settlement being formed.  The announcement of Gold happened the day we finished the main walls and all hope was lost.  A few days later everyone stopped playing and the town decayed. Gold Ones Pirate Outpost was short lived, it started as Flimmy and Gedd joining myself (Raloc) trying to restart what we once had, we struggled to assemble a tower for our own good and to plant a deed, but the work flow was limited due to trying to juggle everything else and we soon conformed joining Leersum never to be seen again during that map', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Original_Pirate_Outpost\">The Original Pirate Outpost</span></h3>\n<p>was an idea formed during a 48 hour server downtime on the forums, it started as a simple idea as a town and slowly expanded on it.  In the 48 hours the server was down, the thread had grown to 25 pages and the idea was set and prepared to be executed.  The first one to join me in helping in this venture was Starvingmidget, who had an undying faith that we would do good.  We chose an island 15 minutes away from the largest town at the time (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Kyara\" title=\"Kyara\">Kyara</a>) and went about starting.  It soon grew, gaining several new members quickly (some notable mentions: Gedd, Crimsonwolf, Puzzle, Flimmy, Zelar being some of the few that started at Pirate Outpost and later moved on to other places) and a stone wall settlement being formed.  The announcement of Gold happened the day we finished the main walls and all hope was lost.  A few days later everyone stopped playing and the town decayed.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gold_Ones_Pirate_Outpost\">Gold Ones Pirate Outpost</span></h3>\n<p>was short lived, it started as Flimmy and Gedd joining myself (Raloc) trying to restart what we once had, we struggled to assemble a tower for our own good and to plant a deed, but the work flow was limited due to trying to juggle everything else and we soon conformed joining <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leersum\" title=\"Leersum\">Leersum</a> never to be seen again during that map\n</p>', 1),
(8127, 2260, 'Gold Two Pirate Outpost Endeavors', 'Gold_Two_Pirate_Outpost_Endeavors', 'The map reset allowed for the idea of Pirate Outpost to be revived, and we took the chance while it was there.  Shortly after the server was reset we chose a spot not far off from the Altar of Three this lasted for a few weeks until a griefing deed was placed outside our front door, making it impossible to leave (or plant our own deed) we struggled with the GM\'s trying to convince them it was illegal action (and coincidentally they built a tower behind us and rushed us with an enemy deed) but it never got through and we were forced to relocate. We attempted to create a island in the water not too far away, after a weeks worth of digging and dropping, we finally purchased a deed.  Upon trying to place it a land hogging homestead prevented us from planting again, we were on the verge of just quitting when it was suggested we should go and try to find an island and relive the times of the original Pirate Outpost, and so we did and headed north beyond Independent Settlers (the old one). and so the first main town was formed Island Pirate Outpost was formed (it was nicknamed thusly due to multiple Pirate Outposts) the first ever deeded Pirate Outpost.  It was quite successful and occupied the majority of the island we chose.  This Pirate Outpost lasted for some time, being the first big project most of us had some across. And during the time of Island Pirate Outpost, we gained several memorable figures including Imbill, Pvtryan, Kalinium, Awesomefusion, Tricks, Ishwoo, Digerati, all of which went on to play later.  This Pirate Outpost was ended after encouragement from some of the towns to start attacking enemy settlements, we went at night to try and attack one place we had found, a small house seemingly in the middle of nowhere.  After picking into it, taking all of the contents and leaving we learned that we were right next to Pirates Cove a Pirate Outpost knockoff and a child deed to Libilian Outlawz .  Well lo and behold, Libilian Outlawz caught wind and soon raided us into the ground thus ending that chapter of The Pirate Outpost. Tundra Pirate Outpost (dubbed thusly due to being planted on the tundra south of Kyara) was widely considered by Pirate Outpost members to be the most popular, most active and best Pirate Outpost that has ever existed.  It was the first size 10 deed that Pirate Outpost had, it was technically named \"Pirates of Brawlstow\" after a suggestion that the Pirate Outpost name was worn out.  This Pirate Outpost was highly influenced by the great Facepunch rush and thusly the deed was filled in 3 days flat.  Soon the Pirate Outpost expanded faster than the elders could handle and a split off town was founded, being named Shanty Town (which later grew into it\'s own town).  Upon growth the town members grew bored of ordinary village doings and ventured into the world of pillaging and looting, starting with looting the houses around the landing and expanding to larger places such as Iron Hill and others.  The other larger towns caught on and took action against Pirate Outpost, starting a constant state of civil war.  Soon after declaring full war, the other towns leveled out Pirate Outpost and we soon disbanded. Northshore Pirate Outpost was placed directly north of Kyara on (you guessed it) the shore was a small size five village as a last stitch hope to restart the former glory of what Pirate Outpost once was, it gained a few more memorable members such as Stickmaus, Gnomie, Fernando, Viperguy, Skiyootlaroso and Fpspike.  As time rolled on, it attempted to follow in the footsteps of the former glory of Tundra Pirate Outpost and soon was ended in a similar fashion but on a much much smaller scale.  It was later disbanded due to loss of interest from the members.', '<p>The map reset allowed for the idea of Pirate Outpost to be revived, and we took the chance while it was there.  Shortly after the server was reset we chose a spot not far off from the <a href=\"/index.php/Altar_of_Three\" title=\"Altar of Three\">Altar of Three</a> this lasted for a few weeks until a griefing deed was placed outside our front door, making it impossible to leave (or plant our own deed) we struggled with the GM\'s trying to convince them it was illegal action (and coincidentally they built a tower behind us and rushed us with an enemy deed) but it never got through and we were forced to relocate.\n</p>\n<p>We attempted to create a island in the water not too far away, after a weeks worth of digging and dropping, we finally purchased a deed.  Upon trying to place it a land hogging homestead prevented us from planting again, we were on the verge of just quitting when it was suggested we should go and try to find an island and relive the times of the original Pirate Outpost, and so we did and headed north beyond <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Independent_Settlers&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Independent Settlers (page does not exist)\">Independent Settlers</a>(the old one). and so the first main town was formed\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Island_Pirate_Outpost\">Island Pirate Outpost</span></h3>\n<p>was formed (it was nicknamed thusly due to multiple Pirate Outposts) the first ever deeded Pirate Outpost.  It was quite successful and occupied the majority of the island we chose.  This Pirate Outpost lasted for some time, being the first big project most of us had some across. And during the time of Island Pirate Outpost, we gained several memorable figures including Imbill, Pvtryan, Kalinium, Awesomefusion, Tricks, Ishwoo, Digerati, all of which went on to play later.  This Pirate Outpost was ended after encouragement from some of the towns to start attacking enemy settlements, we went at night to try and attack one place we had found, a small house seemingly in the middle of nowhere.  After picking into it, taking all of the contents and leaving we learned that we were right next to <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_settlement\" title=\"Undefined settlement\">Pirates Cove</a> a Pirate Outpost knockoff and a child deed to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Libilian_Outlawz\" title=\"Libilian Outlawz\">Libilian Outlawz</a>.  Well lo and behold, Libilian Outlawz caught wind and soon raided us into the ground thus ending that chapter of The Pirate Outpost.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tundra_Pirate_Outpost\">Tundra Pirate Outpost</span></h3>\n<p>(dubbed thusly due to being planted on the tundra south of Kyara) was widely considered by Pirate Outpost members to be the most popular, most active and best Pirate Outpost that has ever existed.  It was the first size 10 deed that Pirate Outpost had, it was technically named \"Pirates of Brawlstow\" after a suggestion that the Pirate Outpost name was worn out.  This Pirate Outpost was highly influenced by the great <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Facepunch\" title=\"Facepunch\">Facepunch</a> rush and thusly the deed was filled in 3 days flat.  Soon the Pirate Outpost expanded faster than the elders could handle and a split off town was founded, being named <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shantytown\" title=\"Shantytown\">Shanty Town</a> (which later grew into it\'s own town).  Upon growth the town members grew bored of ordinary village doings and ventured into the world of pillaging and looting, starting with looting the houses around the landing and expanding to larger places such as <a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_settlement\" title=\"Undefined settlement\">Iron Hill</a> and others.  The other larger towns caught on and took action against Pirate Outpost, starting a constant state of civil war.  Soon after declaring full war, the other towns leveled out Pirate Outpost and we soon disbanded.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Northshore_Pirate_Outpost\">Northshore Pirate Outpost</span></h3>\n<p>was placed directly north of Kyara on (you guessed it) the shore was a small size five village as a last stitch hope to restart the former glory of what Pirate Outpost once was, it gained a few more memorable members such as Stickmaus, Gnomie, Fernando, Viperguy, Skiyootlaroso and Fpspike.  As time rolled on, it attempted to follow in the footsteps of the former glory of Tundra Pirate Outpost and soon was ended in a similar fashion but on a much much smaller scale.  It was later disbanded due to loss of interest from the members.\n</p>', 2),
(8128, 2260, 'Current Pirate Outpost', 'Current_Pirate_Outpost', 'WILL FILL IN WHEN I FEEL LIKE BEING CLEVER', '<p>WILL FILL IN WHEN I FEEL LIKE BEING CLEVER\n</p>', 3),
(8129, 2261, 'History', 'History', '2012 Disbanded due to inactivity. October 4th, 2010 [21:39:39] It is 11:28:43 on Wrath day in week 4 of the starfall of the Leaf in the year of 1009.', '<p><b>2012</b>\nDisbanded due to inactivity.  \n</p>\n<p><b>October 4th, 2010</b>\n</p>\n<p>[21:39:39] It is 11:28:43 on Wrath day in week 4 of the starfall of the Leaf in the year of 1009.\n</p>', 0),
(8130, 2261, 'Location', 'Location', '8x43, Independence', '<p>8x43, Independence\n</p>', 1),
(8131, 2261, 'Population', 'Population', '4 (2) Mayors Marni Moot Citizens Purp Vilnayin', '<p>4 (2)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayors\">Mayors</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Marni\" title=\"Player:Marni\">Marni</a></li>\n<li>Moot</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Purp\" title=\"Player:Purp\">Purp</a></li>\n<li>Vilnayin</li></ul>', 2),
(8132, 2262, 'Tokyo', 'Tokyo', '\"None of us actually live in Japan.\"', '<p>\"None of us actually live in Japan.\"\n</p>', 0),
(8133, 2262, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Mikuso Citizens Posteh Evasion Azarelius Commonenemy', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Mikuso</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Posteh\" title=\"User:Posteh\">Posteh</a></li>\n<li>Evasion</li>\n<li>Azarelius</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Commonenemy\" title=\"User:Commonenemy\">Commonenemy</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8134, 2262, 'Basic Info', 'Basic_Info', 'We believe in Communism.  Everything is shared, all citizens have access to all buildings and locked chests.  Not recruiting.', '<p>We believe in Communism.  Everything is shared, all citizens have access to all buildings and locked chests.  Not recruiting.\n</p>', 2),
(8135, 2263, 'The Retreat of Tras', 'The_Retreat_of_Tras', 'Traslogan\'s Retreat is Traslogan\'s 3rd village(the 1st one went boom, the 2nd one got sold, so here\'s number 3). He is trying to promote his newcomer-friendly ways again by being situated closer to Freedom Market.\nThe village has all the resources it needs(close clay,tar,peat,marsh, and lots of iron and silver and copper). Our Forums : http://z15.invisionfree.com/Traslogans_Retreat/index.php?act=idx', '<p>Traslogan\'s Retreat is Traslogan\'s 3rd village(the 1st one went boom, the 2nd one got sold, so here\'s number 3). He is trying to promote his newcomer-friendly ways again by being situated closer to Freedom Market.\nThe village has all the resources it needs(close clay,tar,peat,marsh, and lots of iron and silver and copper).\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nOur Forums : <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://z15.invisionfree.com/Traslogans_Retreat/index.php?act=idx\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://z15.invisionfree.com/Traslogans_Retreat/index.php?act=idx</a>\n</p>', 0),
(8136, 2263, 'Residents(May require updating. NOT a 24/7 accurate list)', 'Residents.28May_require_updating._NOT_a_24.2F7_accurate_list.29', '( Bold text signifies a title) Traslogan Trollslayer\' , Community Assistant , Miner , Prime Minester - Mayor/Founder Paterso Trollslayer - Tras\' Ex-main account - Elder Storm - Villager Siharaj - Villager Sawu - Villager Joona Trollslayer - Villager appelstrudel - Villager Superlenny - Villager Mckillaboy - Villager Vorvadoss - Villager Niners - Villager Atrix - Villager Ryoki - Villager Krath - Villager Xtigermanxx - Villager Apathy - Villager Bladerunner - Villager Enolam - Villager Filberts - Villager Twinsen - Villager Deathrow - Villager Heraldo - Villager', '<p>(<b>Bold</b> text signifies a title)\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\">Traslogan</a> <b>Trollslayer\'<i>,</i></b><i>Community Assistant<b>,</b>Miner<b>, </b>Prime Minester</i> - <i>Mayor/Founder</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Traslogan\" title=\"User:Traslogan\">Paterso</a> <b>Trollslayer</b> - Tras\' Ex-main account - <i>Elder</i>\n</p>\n<p>Storm - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Siharaj - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Sawu - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Joona <b>Trollslayer</b>- Villager\n</p>\n<p>appelstrudel - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Superlenny - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Mckillaboy - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Vorvadoss - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Niners - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Atrix - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Ryoki - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Krath - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Xtigermanxx - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Apathy - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Bladerunner - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Enolam - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Filberts - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Twinsen - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Deathrow - Villager\n</p>\n<p>Heraldo - Villager\n</p>', 1),
(8137, 2263, 'Pictures from The Retreat', 'Pictures_from_The_Retreat', '', '<p><img alt=\"wurm201101161442.jpg\" src=\"http://i1212.photobucket.com/albums/cc441/Filberts/wurm201101161442.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm201101161447_1.png\" src=\"http://i1214.photobucket.com/albums/cc488/Traslogan/wurm201101161447_1.png\"/>\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"wurm201101161509_2.png\" src=\"http://i1214.photobucket.com/albums/cc488/Traslogan/wurm201101161509_2.png\"/>\n</p>', 2),
(8138, 2264, 'Traslogan\'s Retreat', 'Traslogan.27s_Retreat', 'The Deliverance Version of Traslogan\'s Retreat is Traslogan \'s Current Deed, and he claims to be reluctant to move again, as he has formed many deeds in the past but now wishes to settle down on his own. Villagers: Traslogan Translogan Paterso', '<p>The Deliverance Version of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Traslogan%27s_Retreat\" title=\"Traslogan\'s Retreat\">Traslogan\'s Retreat</a> is <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Traslogan\" title=\"Player:Traslogan\">Traslogan</a>\'s Current Deed, and he claims to be reluctant to move again, as he has formed many deeds in the past but now wishes to settle down on his own.\n</p>\n<p>Villagers:\n</p>\n<p>Traslogan \n</p>\n<p>Translogan\n</p>\n<p>Paterso\n</p>', 0),
(8139, 2267, 'Vanguard', 'Vanguard', 'Founded by Nevrax , Vanguard is a starting Jenn-Kellon Settlement on the Wild Server that is currently under construction. The location of Vanguard is currently not available for public procurement due to numerous risks. Vanguard is close allies with Woodscove if not an outpost or a smaller settlement somewhat connected with Woodscove .', '<p>Founded by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Nevrax\" title=\"Player:Nevrax\">Nevrax</a>, Vanguard is a starting <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">Settlement</a> on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wild_Server\" title=\"Wild Server\">Wild Server</a> that is currently under construction. The location of Vanguard is currently not available for public procurement due to numerous risks. Vanguard is close allies with <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Woodscove\" title=\"Woodscove\">Woodscove</a> if not an outpost or a smaller settlement somewhat connected with <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Woodscove\" title=\"Woodscove\">Woodscove</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(8140, 2267, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Name - Profession [Title(s)] Nevrax - Mayor [None] Elders Name - Profession [Title(s)] None Citizens Name - Profession [Title(s)] None', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h3>\n<p><i>Name - Profession [Title(s)]</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Nevrax\" title=\"Player:Nevrax\">Nevrax</a> - Mayor [None]</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<p><i>Name - Profession [Title(s)]</i>\n</p>\n<p>None\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p><i>Name - Profession [Title(s)]</i>\n</p>\n<p>None\n</p>', 1),
