(8483, 2353, 'Description', 'Description', 'It is a normal wide staircase with banisters on left made of standalone.', '<p><i>It is a normal wide staircase with banisters on left made of standalone.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(8484, 2353, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Follows the same requirements for multi-story housing and stone flooring: 21 carpentry required to plan a staircase on the first floor. See multi-story housing for additional skill requirements per floor. You must right-click on a finished floor with a hammer , mallet , or trowel and select Plan > Build Wide staircase with left banisters . Be careful not to create one against a wall, at the top or bottom level, as it\'s impossible to pass. Should you become stuck, the building owner may rotate the staircase to help you exit the confinement. Once the staircase is built the floor beneath it can be removed. Be careful when creating one against a wall, as planning a wall on the floor above will be more difficult. Wide staircases take up the entire tile; so you will not be able to walk around it on the upper or lower floor on that same tile. Vehicles may not be commanded up staircases, only those that can be dragged can ascend to another floor. Animals cannot be ridden up staircases, but may be led. You cannot use haul up or haul down with a staircase.', '<ul><li>Follows the same requirements for multi-story housing and stone flooring:\n<ul><li>21 <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> required to plan a staircase on the first floor. See <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Multi_story#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi story\">multi-story housing</a> for additional skill requirements per floor.</li></ul></li>\n<li>You must right-click on a finished <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Floor\" title=\"Floor\">floor</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and select <b>Plan &gt; Build Wide staircase with left banisters</b>. Be careful not to create one against a wall, at the top or bottom level, as it\'s impossible to pass. Should you become stuck, the building owner may rotate the staircase to help you exit the confinement.</li>\n<li>Once the staircase is built the floor beneath it can be removed.</li>\n<li>Be careful when creating one against a wall, as planning a wall on the floor above will be more difficult.</li>\n<li>Wide staircases take up the entire tile; so you will not be able to walk around it on the upper or lower floor on that same tile.</li>\n<li>Vehicles may not be commanded up staircases, only those that can be dragged can ascend to another floor.</li>\n<li>Animals cannot be ridden up staircases, but may be led.</li>\n<li>You cannot use haul up or haul down with a staircase.</li></ul>', 1);
