ing owner may rotate the staircase to help you exit the confinement.</li>\n<li>Once the staircase is built the floor beneath it can be removed.</li>\n<li>Be careful when creating one against a wall, as planning a wall on the floor above will be more difficult.</li>\n<li>Wide staircases take up the entire tile; so you will not be able to walk around it on the upper or lower floor on that same tile.</li>\n<li>Vehicles may not be commanded up staircases, only those that can be dragged can ascend to another floor.</li>\n<li>Animals cannot be ridden up staircases, but may be led.</li>\n<li>You cannot use haul up or haul down with a staircase.</li></ul>', 1),
(8488, 2354, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Openings Wide staircase with both banisters Wide staircase with left banisters Wide staircase Spiral staircase Spiral staircase with banisters Marble slab staircase Stone slab staircase Stone brick staircase Slate slab staircase Pottery brick staircase Wooden plank staircase Standalone staircase', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Openings\" title=\"Category:Openings\">Category:Openings</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wide_staircase_with_both_banisters\" title=\"Wide staircase with both banisters\">Wide staircase with both banisters</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wide_staircase_with_left_banisters\" title=\"Wide staircase with left banisters\">Wide staircase with left banisters</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wide_staircase\" title=\"Wide staircase\">Wide staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spiral_staircase\" title=\"Spiral staircase\">Spiral staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spiral_staircase_with_banisters\" title=\"Spiral staircase with banisters\">Spiral staircase with banisters</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_slab_staircase\" title=\"Marble slab staircase\">Marble slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_slab_staircase\" title=\"Stone slab staircase\">Stone slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick_staircase\" title=\"Stone brick staircase\">Stone brick staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Slate_slab_staircase\" title=\"Slate slab staircase\">Slate slab staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick_staircase\" title=\"Pottery brick staircase\">Pottery brick staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_plank_staircase\" title=\"Wooden plank staircase\">Wooden plank staircase</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Standalone_staircase\" title=\"Standalone staircase\">Standalone staircase</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8492, 2356, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door.', '<p><i>You see a door. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(8493, 2356, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob, for example trolls , or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob, for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>, or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(8494, 2356, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Plank and 1 Large nails in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Wooden portcullis . Continuation requires at least 1 plank in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">Plank</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">Large nails</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Wooden portcullis</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(8495, 2356, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(8496, 2356, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a plank before improving it. Activate a plank , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the plank is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(8497, 2356, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Wooden wall Wooden door Wooden double door Wooden window Wooden wide window Wooden portcullis Wooden canopy Wooden arch Wooden T arch Wooden arch right Wooden arch left', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_wall\" title=\"Wooden wall\">Wooden wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_door\" title=\"Wooden door\">Wooden door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_double_door\" title=\"Wooden double door\">Wooden double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_window\" title=\"Wooden window\">Wooden window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_wide_window\" title=\"Wooden wide window\">Wooden wide window</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Wooden portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_canopy\" title=\"Wooden canopy\">Wooden canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch\" title=\"Wooden arch\">Wooden arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_T_arch\" title=\"Wooden T arch\">Wooden T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_right\" title=\"Wooden arch right\">Wooden arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_arch_left\" title=\"Wooden arch left\">Wooden arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(8504, 1860, 'Description', 'Description', 'Smithing is everything related to the creation of metal items, usually created using metal lumps on a small anvil or large anvil . Metal lumps and items need to be glowing hot to be smithed. You can do this in any fire, but the forge is most effective. The quality of the item you create will be no more than 0.2 x skill (skill is the one associated with the item you are creating).\nFor example:  If you have 35.21 skill in jewelry making, the best you can get will be an item of quality 7.04. Note: This is the creation quality of the item, not the highest quality you can improve an item to. Improving items are greatly based off skill and the random number generator.', '<p>Smithing is everything related to the creation of metal items, usually created using <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps\" title=\"Metal lumps\">metal lumps</a> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_anvil\" title=\"Small anvil\">small anvil</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">large anvil</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Metal lumps and items need to be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Glowing\" title=\"Glowing\">glowing</a> hot to be smithed. You can do this in any fire, but the <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a> is most effective.\n</p>\n<p>The quality of the item you create will be no more than 0.2 x skill (skill is the one associated with the item you are creating).\nFor example:  If you have 35.21 skill in jewelry making, the best you can get will be an item of quality 7.04. <i>Note: This is the creation quality of the item, not the highest quality you can improve an item to. Improving items are greatly based off skill and the random number generator.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(8505, 1860, 'Tools', 'Tools', 'The following tools are needed for improving and finishing smithing items: Hammer Pelt Whetstone Water Metal lumps', '<p>The following tools are needed for improving and finishing smithing items:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">Hammer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelt</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Whetstone\" title=\"Whetstone\">Whetstone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps\" title=\"Metal lumps\">Metal lumps</a></li></ul>', 1),
(8506, 1860, 'Sub-Skills', 'Sub-Skills', 'Weapon smithing - Used in the creation of weapons such as swords and axes and bladed tools such as scythes and sickles . Blades smithing Weapon heads smithing Armour smithing - Used in the creation of armour for added protection against attacks. Chain armour smithing - Used in the creation of chain armour . Plate armour smithing - Used in the creation of plate armour . Shield smithing - Used in the creation of shields . Blacksmithing - Used to make items like nails or pots and pans. Locksmithing - Used in the creation of locks and lockpicks Metallurgy - Used in the creation of alloys like steel , bronze and brass Jewelry smithing - Used to make jewelry and statuettes.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Weapons\" title=\"Category:Weapons\">weapons</a> such as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Swords\" title=\"Category:Swords\">swords</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Axes\" title=\"Category:Axes\">axes</a>  and bladed tools such as <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickles</a>.\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Blades_smithing\" title=\"Blades smithing\">Blades smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_heads_smithing\" title=\"Weapon heads smithing\">Weapon heads smithing</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour_smithing\" title=\"Armour smithing\">Armour smithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Armour\" title=\"Category:Armour\">armour</a> for added protection against attacks.\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour_smithing\" title=\"Chain armour smithing\">Chain armour smithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">chain armour</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour_smithing\" title=\"Plate armour smithing\">Plate armour smithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">plate armour</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shield_smithing\" title=\"Shield smithing\">Shield smithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Shields\" title=\"Shields\">shields</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a> - Used to make items like nails or pots and pans.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Locksmithing\" title=\"Locksmithing\">Locksmithing</a> - Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Locksmithing_items\" title=\"Category:Locksmithing items\">locks</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lockpick\" title=\"Lockpick\">lockpicks</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Metallurgy\" title=\"Metallurgy\">Metallurgy</a> - Used in the creation of alloys like <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_lump\" title=\"Steel lump\">steel</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bronze_lump\" title=\"Bronze lump\">bronze</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Brass_lump\" title=\"Brass lump\">brass</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a> - Used to make jewelry and statuettes.</li></ul>', 2),
(8507, 1860, 'Items', 'Items', 'There are no items created directly by the smithing skill. See smithing items for a complete list of smithing items.', '<p>There are no items created directly by the smithing skill.\n</p>\n<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Smithing_items\" title=\"Category:Smithing items\">smithing items</a> for a complete list of smithing items.\n</p>', 3),
(8508, 1860, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing Body > Body strength Body > Body control', '<ul><li>Smithing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>', 4),
(8509, 1860, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Smith at 50 skill Tinker at 70 skill Master Smith at 90 skill Ill Tempered at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Smith at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Tinker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Smith at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Ill Tempered at 100 skill</li></ul>', 5),
(8510, 2359, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long length of rope with knotted loops to lead multiple animals.', '<p><i>A long length of rope with knotted loops to lead multiple animals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(8511, 2359, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A halter rope is used to lead up to 4 animals at once with one rope. Many creatures can be led without taming and these include: bison , bulls , calves , cows , chickens , hens , horses , roosters , pigs , and sheep . At PVP servers you can only lead 2 animals. If you are mounted, you can only lead 1 animal on PVP servers. Only the commander of a boat or cart can lead animals. Passengers are not able to lead animals. Some items may be hauled up and down ladders of a structure by using a rope or halter rope. Ropemaking skill at 25 and rope QL at 63 gives a 6% chance for success.', '<ul><li>A <b>halter rope</b> is used to lead up to 4 animals at once with one rope. Many creatures can be led without <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_taming\" title=\"Animal taming\">taming</a> and these include: <a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">bison</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">bulls</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Calf\" title=\"Calf\">calves</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cows\" title=\"Cows\">cows</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Chicken\" title=\"Chicken\">chickens</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hen\" title=\"Hen\">hens</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rooster\" title=\"Rooster\">roosters</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pig\" title=\"Pig\">pigs</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">sheep</a>.</li>\n<li>At PVP servers you can only lead 2 animals. If you are mounted, you can only lead 1 animal on PVP servers.</li>\n<li>Only the commander of a <a href=\"/index.php/Ship\" title=\"Ship\">boat</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Carts\" title=\"Carts\">cart</a> can lead animals. Passengers are not able to lead animals.</li>\n<li>Some items may be <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Hauled_items\" title=\"Category:Hauled items\">hauled up and down</a> ladders of a structure by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">rope</a> or halter rope.</li>\n<li>Ropemaking skill at 25 and rope QL at 63 gives a 6% chance for success.</li></ul>', 1),
(8512, 2359, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Thick rope Cordage rope Mooring rope', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Thick_rope\" title=\"Thick rope\">Thick rope</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cordage_rope\" title=\"Cordage rope\">Cordage rope</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mooring_rope\" title=\"Mooring rope\">Mooring rope</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8518, 2362, 'Digging', 'Digging', 'The concrete would only flow away. Occurs when trying to raise a rock tile that is greater than 40 slope. It only takes into consideration the 4 adjacent slope borders. The frozen soil is too hard to dig effectively. Occurs when there is tundra next to it. The <item> would flow down into a <structure/fence>. You are not allowed to drop <item> on <structures/fences> Occurs when trying to drop a dirt that is adjacent to a structure/fence in which the slope is more than 40. The object nearby prevents digging further down. Occurs when trying to dig down when a planted object, like a bulk storage bin or food storage bin, is on the tile. The road would be too steep to traverse. Occurs when trying to dig on a paved tile at a slope greater than 19. The water is too deep and would only dissolve the concrete. When using concrete to raise a tile below water the lowest height that the tile can be is 25. The water is too deep to cultivate here. Occurs when trying to cultivate a tile in which the northwest corner is not 0 dirts or more above the water table. The water is too deep or too shallow to dig using that tool. Occurs when trying to dredge from a cart or wagon between 2 and 6 dirts below the water table. The water is too deep to pack the dirt here. Occurs when trying to pack a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 0 dirts below the water table. The water is too deep to pave here. Occurs when trying to pave a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 0 dirts below the water table. The water is too deep or too shallow to dig using that tool. Occurs when trying to dig on a tile with a shovel that is more than 6 dirts below the water table. You can\'t flatten at that depth. Occurs when trying to flatten a tile in which is the involved tiles are 7 or more dirts below the water table. You can\'t level at that depth. Occurs when trying to level a tile in which the involved tiles are 7 or more dirts below the water table. The water is too deep and would only dissolve the concrete. Occurs when attempting to raise a rock tile with concrete in which the corner is more than 24 dirts below the water table. You are not allowed to drop dirt there. Cannot drop dirt on paved road when the corner is surrounded on all sides by trees or similar tiles. You are not skilled enough to dig in such steep slopes. Occurs when you are not skilled enough to dig on a slope. The max slope that you can dig is 3 times your digging skill. You cannot dig in such terrain. This message happens when the corner is surrounded by 3 or 4 tree or bush tiles. This message will also occur when trying to lower floorboards through a dig action. You hit rock. All the dirt above the rock layer in this tile corner has been dug away. You suddenly become very weak, and your arm muscles fail you. You just can not dig here it seems. You are trying to dig within a planned house. You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first. You need 10 digging to remove pavement. You need to be stronger to destroy pavement. Body strength of 20 and a digging skill of 10 is required for destroying pavement. You need to be stronger to dig on roads. You need 20 body strength to dig on roads. Your shovel fails to penetrate the earth no matter what you try. Weird. You are trying to dig in an area protected by the GMs. Find a different spot.', '<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<ul><li><i>The concrete would only flow away.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to raise a rock tile that is greater than 40 slope. It only takes into consideration the 4 adjacent slope borders.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The frozen soil is too hard to dig effectively.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when there is tundra next to it.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The &lt;item&gt; would flow down into a &lt;structure/fence&gt;. You are not allowed to drop &lt;item&gt; on &lt;structures/fences&gt;</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to drop a dirt that is adjacent to a structure/fence in which the slope is more than 40.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The object nearby prevents digging further down.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to dig down when a planted object, like a bulk storage bin or food storage bin, is on the tile.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The road would be too steep to traverse.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to dig on a paved tile at a slope greater than 19.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i> The water is too deep and would only dissolve the concrete.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>When using <a href=\"/index.php/Concrete\" title=\"Concrete\">concrete</a> to raise a tile below water the lowest height that the tile can be is 25.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to cultivate here.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to cultivate a tile in which the northwest corner is not 0 dirts or more above the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep or too shallow to dig using that tool.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to dredge from a cart or wagon between 2 and 6 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to pack the dirt here.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to pack a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 0 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to pave here.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to pave a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 0 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep or too shallow to dig using that tool.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to dig on a tile with a shovel that is more than 6 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You can\'t flatten at that depth.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to flatten a tile in which is the involved tiles are 7 or more dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You can\'t level at that depth.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to level a tile in which the involved tiles are 7 or more dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep and would only dissolve the concrete.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when attempting to raise a rock tile with concrete in which the corner is more than 24 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i> You are not allowed to drop dirt there.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Cannot drop dirt on paved road when the corner is surrounded on all sides by trees or similar tiles.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You are not skilled enough to dig in such steep slopes.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when you are not skilled enough to dig on a slope. The max slope that you can dig is 3 times your digging skill.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You cannot dig in such terrain.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>This message happens when the corner is surrounded by 3 or 4 tree or bush tiles.</dd>\n<dd>This message will also occur when trying to lower floorboards through a dig action.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You hit rock.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>All the dirt above the rock layer in this tile corner has been dug away.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You suddenly become very weak, and your arm muscles fail you. You just can not dig here it seems.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>You are trying to dig within a planned house.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>You need 10 digging to remove pavement.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You need to be stronger to destroy pavement.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Body strength of 20 and a digging skill of 10 is required for destroying pavement.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You need to be stronger to dig on roads.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>You need 20 body strength to dig on roads.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>Your shovel fails to penetrate the earth no matter what you try. Weird.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>You are trying to dig in an area protected by the GMs. Find a different spot.</dd></dl>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(8519, 2362, 'Planning/Building', 'Planning.2FBuilding', 'You can\'t build on water. Occurs when trying to plan a house on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table. The water is too deep. Occurs when trying to build a fence on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table. You cannot build here, there must be a gap around the building. Occurs when trying to plan a house in a cave that does not have a buffer around it when the cave is against the deed border. Also can occur when trying to plan a house in a cave when the house is off deed. See more: Cave Dwellings You need to build in connection with a finished neighboring floor, roof or wall. Occurs when trying to plan a roof or floor that is not adjacent to an already finished floor/roof/or lower wall. Finish the adjacent tiles first before you can plan this tile.', '<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<ul><li><i>You can\'t build on water.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to plan a house on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to build a fence on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You cannot build here, there must be a gap around the building.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to plan a house in a cave that does not have a buffer around it when the cave is against the deed border. Also can occur when trying to plan a house in a cave when the house is off deed.\n<dl><dd><b>See more:</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Guides:Build_house#Cave_dwellings\" title=\"Guides:Build house\">Cave Dwellings</a></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You need to build in connection with a finished neighboring floor, roof or wall.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to plan a roof or floor that is not adjacent to an already finished floor/roof/or lower wall. Finish the adjacent tiles first before you can plan this tile.</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(8520, 2362, 'Farming/Planting', 'Farming.2FPlanting', 'The ground is too moist here, so the <item> would rot. Occurs when trying to plant crops on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table. Also could present itself with the message The water is too deep. You cannot sow that <item> there. This type of crop can only grow in water of suitable depth Occurs when trying to sow reed or rice that is not a suitable depth. Reed and Rice can be planted in a depth between 1 dirts and 4 dirts below the water table. Can also present itself in the form of the message This type of crop can only grow in water of suitable depth. The water is too deep to plant the <item>. Occurs when trying to plant a crop on a tile in which the northwest corner of that tile is more than 0 dirts below the water table. You are not skilled enough to build in such steep slopes. Occurs when trying to build a fence on a tile border in which the slope is to high for your skill. The max slope you can build on is (3*√skill)+10.', '<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<ul><li><i>The ground is too moist here, so the &lt;item&gt; would rot.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to plant crops on a tile that is 1 or more dirts below the water table.</dd>\n<dd>Also could present itself with the message <i>The water is too deep. You cannot sow that &lt;item&gt; there.</i></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>This type of crop can only grow in water of suitable depth</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to sow reed or rice that is not a suitable depth. Reed and Rice can be planted in a depth between 1 dirts and 4 dirts below the water table.</dd>\n<dd>Can also present itself in the form of the message <i>This type of crop can only grow in water of suitable depth.</i></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to plant the &lt;item&gt;.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to plant a crop on a tile in which the northwest corner of that tile is more than 0 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You are not skilled enough to build in such steep slopes.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to build a fence on a tile border in which the slope is to high for your skill. The max slope you can build on is (3*√skill)+10.</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(8521, 2362, 'Mining', 'Mining', 'The water is too deep to mine. Occurs when trying to open a tunnel in which the northwest corner of the tile being mined is at or more than 12 dirts below the water table. The water is too deep to mine. Occurs when surface mining a tile in which the corner is more than 13 dirts below the water table. The water is too deep to prospect. Occurs when trying to prospect a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 13 dirts below the water table. You are too unskilled to mine here. Occurs when trying to mine a rock tile in which you are not skilled enough to mine. The max slope at which you can mine is 3x your mining skill. The mountainside would risk crumbling. You can\'t open a hole here. Occurs when attempting to tunnel into a rock that is greater than 270 slope. You cannot reach the ceiling. Occurs when trying to mine the cave ceiling that is more than 61 height away from the floor. The ceiling is too close. Occurs when using concrete to raise a floor tile that is less than 20 distance from the ceiling.', '<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to mine.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to open a tunnel in which the northwest corner of the tile being mined is at or more than 12 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to mine.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when surface mining a tile in which the corner is more than 13 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The water is too deep to prospect.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to prospect a tile in which the northwest corner is more than 13 dirts below the water table.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You are too unskilled to mine here.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to mine a rock tile in which you are not skilled enough to mine. The max slope at which you can mine is 3x your mining skill.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The mountainside would risk crumbling. You can\'t open a hole here.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when attempting to tunnel into a rock that is greater than 270 slope.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>You cannot reach the ceiling.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when trying to mine the cave ceiling that is more than 61 height away from the floor.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><i>The ceiling is too close.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Occurs when using concrete to raise a floor tile that is less than 20 distance from the ceiling.</dd></dl>\n</div>', 3),
(8534, 2365, 'Description', 'Description', 'A mask. A cosmetic item that was gifted to players who were non-premium and purchased premium as part of the 10 year anniversary of Wurm in 2016.', '<p><i>A mask.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A cosmetic item that was gifted to players who were non-premium and purchased premium as part of the 10 year anniversary of Wurm in 2016.\n</p>', 0),
(8535, 2366, 'Description', 'Description', 'A knapsack for keeping 10 years of Wurm, wogic and memories. Make sure not to burn it up!', '<p><i>A knapsack for keeping 10 years of Wurm, wogic and memories. Make sure not to burn it up!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(8536, 2366, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality , material, and rarity of the knapsack depends on the length of time the account has been premium since December 2013. It can be worn on the back slot of your character and holds 100 items. Knapsacks were given to premium players as a 10 Year Anniversary gift on June 09 2016', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, material, and rarity of the knapsack depends on the length of time the account has been premium since December 2013.</li>\n<li>It can be worn on the back slot of your character and holds 100 items.</li>\n<li>Knapsacks were given to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> players as a 10 Year Anniversary gift on June 09 2016</li></ul>', 1),
(8537, 2367, 'Description', 'Description', 'This champagne is at least 10 years old.', '<p><i>This champagne is at least 10 years old.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(8538, 2367, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'The Champagne can be drunk, which temporarily makes your character glow with the same colour as the rarity of the Champagne.', '<p>The Champagne can be drunk, which temporarily makes your character glow with the same colour as the rarity of the Champagne.\n</p>', 1),
(8539, 2367, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality and rarity of the Champagne depends on the length of time the account has been premium since December 2013.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> and rarity of the Champagne depends on the length of time the account has been premium since December 2013.</li></ul>', 2),
(8540, 2367, 'History', 'History', 'Champagne were given to premium players as a 10 Year Anniversary gift on June 09 2016', '<p>Champagne were given to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> players as a 10 Year Anniversary gift on June 09 2016\n</p>', 3),
(8563, 2376, 'Description', 'Description', 'Missions are randomly given tasks that are server specific.  They provide you with sleep bonus and karma . Turn on mission progress from the hud settings to see what current missions are available. For Epic Server, missions provide additional material, refer to Scenarios .', '<ul><li>Missions are randomly given tasks that are server specific.  They provide you with <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Karma\" title=\"Karma\">karma</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Turn on mission progress from the hud settings to see what current missions are available.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>For Epic Server, missions provide additional material, refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Scenarios\" title=\"Scenarios\">Scenarios</a>.</li></ul>', 0),
(8564, 2376, 'Requirements for Completing a Mission', 'Requirements_for_Completing_a_Mission', 'The only requirement is for the sacrifice missions. You will need to be at least a follower of any god and have enough faith to sacrifice. You do not have to be premium to partake in or complete the mission and you will still receive the karma and sleep bonus if other requirements are met. If the mission asks for a \"Decent\" item, this means it has to be 30 quality or higher. What religion you follow does not limit which mission you can be a part of.', '<ul><li>The only requirement is for the sacrifice missions. You will need to be at least a follower of any god and have enough faith to sacrifice.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You do not have to be premium to partake in or complete the mission and you will still receive the karma and sleep bonus if other requirements are met.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If the mission asks for a \"Decent\" item, this means it has to be 30 quality or higher.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>What religion you follow does not limit which mission you can be a part of.</li></ul>', 1),
(8565, 2376, 'Rewards', 'Rewards', 'Sleep bonus, variable by mission type and player contribution; capped at 30 minutes per contributor. Cannot take you past your usual sleep bonus cap, and is only rewarded if mission is successfully completed and NOT expired. Each mission provides 1000 karma total. If it is a single player mission, that one player will get 1000 karma for completing it. If it is a mission that requires 132 parts, for example, each part will give 1000/132 per part. For Epic, refer to Scenarios .', '<ul><li>Sleep bonus, variable by mission type and player contribution; capped at 30 minutes per contributor. Cannot take you past your usual sleep bonus cap, and is only rewarded if mission is successfully completed and NOT expired.</li>\n<li>Each mission provides 1000 karma total.</li>\n<li>If it is a single player mission, that one player will get 1000 karma for completing it.</li>\n<li>If it is a mission that requires 132 parts, for example, each part will give 1000/132 per part.</li>\n<li>For Epic, refer to  <a href=\"/index.php/Scenarios\" title=\"Scenarios\">Scenarios</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(8566, 2376, 'Types of Missions', 'Types_of_Missions', 'Slay X number of creatures: Kill X amount of a type of creature on the server. Slay traitor: Kill a specific creature with \"traitor\" at the end of their name. Sacrifice normal item: Sacrifice X amount of a type of item at an altar. These items must be \"Decent\", which is 30ql or higher. Sacrifice valrei item: Sacrifice X amount of Valrei object at an altar. These objects must be found and spawn randomly on the server. The name of the object doesn\'t matter, since you can use ANY valrei object for these missions. Unfortunately, they can spawn on deed and inside buildings. Build structure (Epic focus point): These are special structures that can only be built in specific locations. Only the person that completes it will get the rewards and be able to move it. They cannot be built on deed. Once built, they will not decay and then become a target for the ritual missions. They can be built in the Northwest, Southwest, and Southeast, but there has never been a mission to build them in the Northeast (unsure as if this is a bug or intended); There are only 3 of each type of structure that can be built on each server for the missions.  You can make them unfinished at the location and build more elsewhere but they will NOT become an epic focus point for future missions that way. Ritual: Easy to do mission that may or may not require an additional item to perform. Simply, click on the structure and perform ritual. Only one person per ritual and the number of people needed can vary from 1 or much more. Give item: Give a certain item to an avatar. The mission description tells you what deed it was last seen at but they can be dragged or move far from that location.  Ql does not matter on the item but a specific colour or type may. The missions can be ambiguous on the type of an item. The mission text may say common wool hat when it requires blue common wool hat. Create item: Produce the item given in the mission description. For items requiring multiple parts, priests cannot complete the mission without losing faith since they cannot continue building. Ql does not matter on the item but a specific colour or type may. The missions can be ambiguous on the type of an item. The mission text may say common wool hat when it requires blue common wool hat. Cut down tree: Cut down a specific tree on the server. The mission description will tell you what direction the tree will be from a deed in a quadrant of the server. WARNING: players might consider this griefing but since it is offdeed, there are no rules against it if it\'s for the mission. Only one person can ever complete this mission.  Partially chopping the tree does not progress the mission, it has to be completely cut down to know if you got it or not. Trees do have a sort of blue aura to them, signifying it is the tree to cut to complete the mission. NOTE: Particle Effects must be enabled for this aura to be displayed.', '<ul><li>Slay X number of creatures: Kill X amount of a type of creature on the server.</li>\n<li>Slay traitor: Kill a specific creature with \"traitor\" at the end of their name.</li>\n<li>Sacrifice normal item: Sacrifice X amount of a type of item at an altar. These items must be \"Decent\", which is 30ql or higher.</li>\n<li>Sacrifice valrei item: Sacrifice X amount of Valrei object at an altar. These objects must be found and spawn randomly on the server. The name of the object doesn\'t matter, since you can use ANY valrei object for these missions. Unfortunately, they can spawn on deed and inside buildings.</li>\n<li>Build structure (Epic focus point): These are special structures that can only be built in specific locations. Only the person that completes it will get the rewards and be able to move it. They cannot be built on deed. Once built, they will not decay and then become a target for the ritual missions. They can be built in the Northwest, Southwest, and Southeast, but there has never been a mission to build them in the Northeast (unsure as if this is a bug or intended); There are only 3 of each type of structure that can be built on each server for the missions.  You can make them unfinished at the location and build more elsewhere but they will NOT become an epic focus point for future missions that way.</li>\n<li>Ritual: Easy to do mission that may or may not require an additional item to perform. Simply, click on the structure and perform ritual. Only one person per ritual and the number of people needed can vary from 1 or much more.</li>\n<li>Give item: Give a certain item to an avatar. The mission description tells you what deed it was last seen at but they can be dragged or move far from that location.  Ql does not matter on the item but a specific colour or type may. The missions can be ambiguous on the type of an item. The mission text may say common wool hat when it requires blue common wool hat.</li>\n<li>Create item: Produce the item given in the mission description. For items requiring multiple parts, priests cannot complete the mission without losing faith since they cannot continue building. Ql does not matter on the item but a specific colour or type may. The missions can be ambiguous on the type of an item. The mission text may say common wool hat when it requires blue common wool hat.</li>\n<li>Cut down tree: Cut down a specific tree on the server. The mission description will tell you what direction the tree will be from a deed in a quadrant of the server. WARNING: players might consider this griefing but since it is offdeed, there are no rules against it if it\'s for the mission. Only one person can ever complete this mission.  Partially chopping the tree does not progress the mission, it has to be completely cut down to know if you got it or not.\n<ul><li>Trees <b>do</b> have a sort of blue aura to them, signifying it is the tree to cut to complete the mission.</li>\n<li>NOTE: Particle Effects must be enabled for this aura to be displayed.</li></ul></li></ul>', 3),
(8567, 2376, 'Issues to be concerned about', 'Issues_to_be_concerned_about', 'If a duplicate mission pops up, only the newest mission will get credited so that the new mission must be completed before the older one can. Sometimes a build mission will bug and it will say \'this cannot be completed at this time.\' These can be reported and reset by a GM and they know about this issue.', '<ul><li>If a duplicate mission pops up, only the newest mission will get credited so that the new mission must be completed before the older one can.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Sometimes a build mission will bug and it will say \'this cannot be completed at this time.\' These can be reported and reset by a GM and they know about this issue.</li></ul>', 4),
(8568, 2376, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You can view the current status of avatars in their mission by viewing the in-game Valrei map .', '<ul><li>You can view the current status of avatars in their mission by viewing the in-game <a href=\"/index.php/Valrei_map\" title=\"Valrei map\">Valrei map</a>.</li></ul>', 5),
(8621, 1071, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large closed wooden barrel with a tap, designed to hold lots of oil.', '<p><i>A large closed wooden barrel with a tap, designed to hold lots of oil.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(8622, 1071, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to store any liquid, a smaller alternative to the huge tub . Used with 1 or more spirit templars and olive oil to automatically fuel all lamps within a 24 tile perimeter of the deed. Some items may be placed on top of the barrel, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this. Once completed, they cannot be picked up, but can be moved by pushing/pulling. They can be loaded into a wagon as cargo, but not a large cart. You cannot create or move it onto a tile already containing one. Can hold 2250kg of liquid. Unlike a lantern , this item will not hold tar . Regarding the off-deed lamps: Should someone replace or refill off-deed lamps with tar, they will need to be refuelled with olive oil for the templar to resume lighting them. Also note that lamps will initially need to be filled by hand, for the barrel and templar to work.', '<ul><li>Used to store any liquid, a smaller alternative to the <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_tub\" title=\"Huge tub\">huge tub</a>.</li>\n<li>Used with 1 or more spirit templars and <a href=\"/index.php/Olive_oil\" title=\"Olive oil\">olive oil</a> to automatically fuel all lamps within a 24 tile perimeter of the deed.</li>\n<li>Some items may be placed on top of the barrel, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this.</li>\n<li>Once completed, they cannot be picked up, but can be moved by pushing/pulling.</li>\n<li>They can be loaded into a wagon as cargo, but not a large cart.</li>\n<li>You cannot create or move it onto a tile already containing one.</li>\n<li>Can hold 2250kg of liquid.</li>\n<li>Unlike a <a href=\"/index.php/Lantern\" title=\"Lantern\">lantern</a>, this item will not hold <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a>.</li>\n<li>Regarding the off-deed lamps:\n<ul><li>Should someone replace or refill off-deed lamps with tar, they will need to be refuelled with olive oil for the templar to resume lighting them.</li>\n<li>Also note that lamps will initially need to be filled by hand, for the barrel and templar to work.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(8629, 2396, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine tunic made from red cloth with leather trim and a decorative belt. Armour for your torso, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>A fine tunic made from red cloth with leather trim and a decorative belt.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your torso, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8630, 2396, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Requires a minimum of 10 skill in Cloth tailoring to create A higher quality cloth shirt increases your chance at creating. This piece uses the same slot as a cloth jacket , they cannot be worn together.', '<ul><li>Requires a minimum of 10 skill in <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">Cloth tailoring</a> to create</li>\n<li>A higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_shirt\" title=\"Cloth shirt\">cloth shirt</a> increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>This piece uses the same slot as a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_jacket\" title=\"Cloth jacket\">cloth jacket</a>, they cannot be worn together.</li></ul>', 1),
(8631, 2396, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8632, 2397, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine tunic made from green cloth with yellow trim and decorative belt. Armour for your torso, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>A fine tunic made from green cloth with yellow trim and decorative belt.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your torso, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8633, 2397, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality cloth shirt increases your chance at creating. This piece uses the same slot as a cloth jacket , they cannot be worn together.', '<ul><li>A higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_shirt\" title=\"Cloth shirt\">cloth shirt</a> increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>This piece uses the same slot as a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_jacket\" title=\"Cloth jacket\">cloth jacket</a>, they cannot be worn together.</li></ul>', 1),
(8634, 2397, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8635, 2398, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long, black vest fastened at the waist with a decorative belt. It could be improved with a string of cloth. Armour for your torso, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>A long, black vest fastened at the waist with a decorative belt. It could be improved with a string of cloth.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your torso, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8636, 2398, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality cloth shirt increases your chance at creating. This piece uses the same slot as a cloth jacket , they cannot be worn together. This is dyeable, but the color added doesn\'t show.', '<ul><li>A higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_shirt\" title=\"Cloth shirt\">cloth shirt</a> increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>This piece uses the same slot as a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_jacket\" title=\"Cloth jacket\">cloth jacket</a>, they cannot be worn together.</li>\n<li>This is dyeable, but the color added doesn\'t show.</li></ul>', 1),
(8637, 2398, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8644, 2400, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sleeves made from green fabric and leather with a yellow trim. Armour for your arms, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>Sleeves made from green fabric and leather with a yellow trim.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your arms, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8645, 2400, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality plain white cloth sleeve increases your chance at creating. One sleeve is needed for each arm.', '<ul><li>A higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_white_cloth_sleeve\" title=\"Plain white cloth sleeve\">plain white cloth sleeve</a> increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>One sleeve is needed for each arm.</li></ul>', 1),
(8646, 2400, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8647, 2401, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sleeves made from red fabric with leather trim at the wrists. Armour for your arms, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>Sleeves made from red fabric with leather trim at the wrists.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your arms, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8648, 2401, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality plain white cloth sleeve increases your chance at creating. One sleeve is needed for each arm.', '<ul><li>A higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_white_cloth_sleeve\" title=\"Plain white cloth sleeve\">plain white cloth sleeve</a> increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>One sleeve is needed for each arm.</li></ul>', 1),
(8649, 2401, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8650, 2402, 'Description', 'Description', 'Short striped trousers. Armour for your legs, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>Short striped trousers.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your legs, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8651, 2402, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Higher quality plain white cloth pants will increase your chance at creating.', '<ul><li>Higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_white_cloth_pants\" title=\"Plain white cloth pants\">plain white cloth pants</a> will increase your chance at creating.</li></ul>', 1),
(8652, 2402, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(8653, 2403, 'Description', 'Description', 'Leg protection sown from thick cloth. It could be improved with a string of cloth. Armour for your legs, so you won\'t get injured there as severely when being hit in combat . Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality , but has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.', '<p><i>Leg protection sown from thick cloth. It could be improved with a string of cloth.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a> for your legs, so you won\'t get <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injured</a> there as severely when <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">being hit</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a>. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a> is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, but has no penalty to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.\n</p>', 0),
(8654, 2403, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Higher quality plain white cloth pants will increase your chance at creating. This is dyeable, but the color added doesn\'t show.', '<ul><li>Higher quality <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_white_cloth_pants\" title=\"Plain white cloth pants\">plain white cloth pants</a> will increase your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>This is dyeable, but the color added doesn\'t show.</li></ul>', 1),
