(9308, 2574, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large war machine designed to knock down walls and doors, used by ramming the large log into the wall you wish to no longer exist.', '<p><i>A large war machine designed to knock down walls and doors, used by ramming the large log into the wall you wish to no longer exist.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(9309, 2574, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To use a battering ram, move or drag the battering ram into position, facing the wall or door to be destroyed. Then, with the battering ram in position very close to or against the object, select \"ram\" within its right-click menu. The battering ram will then ram the object with damage dealt upon each action as described below. Unlike many actions in Wurm, multiple requests to perform the ram action cannot be queued. Attempts to queue further actions beyond the initial one are met with a message of: \"You cannot use the battering ram right now as it is already being used.\" A minimum of 21 body strength is needed to use it. Uses the war machine skill, meaning the higher the skill, the faster the action timer. Can only be used by one person at a time and they must be close to use it. Citizens or allies with destroy wall permissions will deal bonus damage. Cannot be used on steep slopes. Ram does double damage to walls underground. Damage is determined by the ram quality and the skill. Checks a short area in front of the ram for anything to hit and will hit the first thing it finds. Battering rams cannot be loaded onto vehicles.', '<ul><li>To use a battering ram, move or drag the battering ram into position, facing the wall or door to be destroyed. Then, with the battering ram in position very close to or against the object, select \"ram\" within its right-click menu. The battering ram will then ram the object with damage dealt upon each action as described below.</li>\n<li>Unlike many actions in Wurm, multiple requests to perform the ram action cannot be queued. Attempts to queue further actions beyond the initial one are met with a message of: \"You cannot use the battering ram right now as it is already being used.\"</li>\n<li>A minimum of 21 body strength is needed to use it.</li>\n<li>Uses the war machine skill, meaning the higher the skill, the faster the action timer.</li>\n<li>Can only be used by one person at a time and they must be close to use it.</li>\n<li>Citizens or allies with destroy wall permissions will deal bonus damage.</li>\n<li>Cannot be used on steep slopes.</li>\n<li>Ram does double damage to walls underground.</li>\n<li>Damage is determined by the ram quality and the skill.</li>\n<li>Checks a short area in front of the ram for anything to hit and will hit the first thing it finds.</li>\n<li>Battering rams cannot be loaded onto vehicles.</li></ul>', 1),
(9310, 2574, 'Skills', 'Skills', 'Uses the War Machines skill', '<ul><li>Uses the War Machines skill</li></ul>', 2),
(9311, 2574, 'Characteristics trained', 'Characteristics_trained', 'See: Characteristics', '<p>See: <a href=\"/index.php/Characteristics\" title=\"Characteristics\">Characteristics</a>\n</p>', 3),
(9312, 2574, 'Titles', 'Titles', '? at 50 skill ? at 70 skill ? at 90 skill', '<ul><li> ? at 50 skill</li>\n<li> ? at 70 skill</li>\n<li> ? at 90 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(9313, 2575, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large and heavy four-sided pyramidal head that will provide quite the punch.', '<p><i>A large and heavy four-sided pyramidal head that will provide quite the punch.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(9314, 2575, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used for the construction of a Battering ram', '<p>Used for the construction of a <a href=\"/index.php/Battering_ram\" title=\"Battering ram\">Battering ram</a>\n</p>', 1),
(9315, 2575, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failing to make this piece will result in 1kg loss total from lump.', '<p>Failing to make this piece will result in 1kg loss total from lump.\n</p>', 2),
(9319, 2577, 'Description', 'Description', 'A vein of sand-sized minerals or rock grains, composed of quartz or feldspar, because these are the most common minerals in the Wurm\'s crust.', '<p><i>A vein of sand-sized minerals or rock grains, composed of quartz or feldspar, because these are the most common minerals in the Wurm\'s crust.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(9320, 2577, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Sandstone veins contain a random amount of shards between 1-10000.', '<ul><li>Sandstone veins contain a random amount of <a href=\"/index.php/Sandstone_shards\" title=\"Sandstone shards\">shards</a> between 1-10000.</li></ul>', 1),
(9321, 2577, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Masonry Stonecutting Mining Prospecting Analyze', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">Masonry</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stonecutting\" title=\"Stonecutting\">Stonecutting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mining</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">Prospecting</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Analyze\" title=\"Analyze\">Analyze</a></li></ul>', 2),
(9322, 2578, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a window', '<p><i>You see a window </i>\n</p>', 0),
(9323, 2578, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(9324, 2578, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Pottery brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Pottery window . Continuation requires at least 1 Pottery brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Pottery window</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(9325, 2578, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(9326, 2578, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Pottery brick before improving it. Activate a Pottery brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Pottery brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(9327, 2578, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Pottery brick wall Pottery window Pottery door Pottery double door Pottery oriel Pottery narrow window Pottery portcullis Pottery barred wall Pottery arched wall Pottery T arch Pottery arch left Pottery arch right', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick_wall\" title=\"Pottery brick wall\">Pottery brick wall</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Pottery window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_door\" title=\"Pottery door\">Pottery door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_double_door\" title=\"Pottery double door\">Pottery double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_oriel\" title=\"Pottery oriel\">Pottery oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_narrow_window\" title=\"Pottery narrow window\">Pottery narrow window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Pottery portcullis (wall)\">Pottery portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_barred_wall\" title=\"Pottery barred wall\">Pottery barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_arched_wall\" title=\"Pottery arched wall\">Pottery arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_T_arch\" title=\"Pottery T arch\">Pottery T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_arch_left\" title=\"Pottery arch left\">Pottery arch left</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_arch_right\" title=\"Pottery arch right\">Pottery arch right</a></li></ul>', 5),
(9328, 2579, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door', '<p><i>You see a door </i>\n</p>', 0),
(9329, 2579, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob (for example trolls ) or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob (for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>) or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(9330, 2579, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 2),
(9331, 2579, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Pottery brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Pottery door . Continuation requires at least 1 Pottery brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Pottery door</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 3),
(9332, 2579, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 4),
(9333, 2579, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Pottery brick before improving it. Activate a Pottery brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Pottery brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">Pottery brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
