(9695, 2619, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall.', '<p><i>You see a wall. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(9696, 2619, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(9697, 2619, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Rounded stone and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Rounded stone wall . Continuation requires at least 1 Rounded stone and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone\" title=\"Rounded stone\">Rounded stone</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Rounded stone wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone\" title=\"Rounded stone\">Rounded stone</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(9698, 2619, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(9699, 2619, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Rounded stone before improving it. Activate a Rounded stone , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Rounded stone is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone\" title=\"Rounded stone\">Rounded stone</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone\" title=\"Rounded stone\">Rounded stone</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone\" title=\"Rounded stone\">Rounded stone</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(9700, 2619, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Rounded stone wall Rounded stone window Rounded stone door Rounded stone double door Rounded stone oriel Rounded stone narrow window Rounded stone portcullis Rounded stone barred wall Rounded stone arched wall Rounded stone T arch Rounded stone arch right Rounded stone arch left', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Rounded stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_window\" title=\"Rounded stone window\">Rounded stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_door\" title=\"Rounded stone door\">Rounded stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_double_door\" title=\"Rounded stone double door\">Rounded stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_oriel\" title=\"Rounded stone oriel\">Rounded stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_narrow_window\" title=\"Rounded stone narrow window\">Rounded stone narrow window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Rounded stone portcullis (wall)\"> Rounded stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_barred_wall\" title=\"Rounded stone barred wall\">Rounded stone barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_arched_wall\" title=\"Rounded stone arched wall\">Rounded stone arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_T_arch\" title=\"Rounded stone T arch\">Rounded stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_arch_right\" title=\"Rounded stone arch right\">Rounded stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rounded_stone_arch_left\" title=\"Rounded stone arch left\">Rounded stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(9701, 2639, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tool consisting of a steel bar with a single curved end and flattened points.', '<p><i>A tool consisting of a steel bar with a single curved end and flattened points.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(9702, 2639, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A crowbar is a tool that can turn rendered walls back into their plain stone version. It is also used to remove catseyes and waystones from highways, paving from tunnel floors, cladding from mine walls, and removing mine doors (with permissions). A crowbar may be used as a weapon. The crowbar can also be used to destroy some structures and fences when other methods/tools are not available.', '<ul><li>A <b>crowbar</b> is a tool that can turn rendered walls back into their plain stone version.</li>\n<li>It is also used to remove <a href=\"/index.php/Catseye\" title=\"Catseye\">catseyes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Waystone\" title=\"Waystone\">waystones</a> from highways, paving from tunnel floors, cladding from mine walls, and removing mine doors (with permissions).</li>\n<li>A crowbar may be used as a weapon.</li>\n<li>The crowbar can also be used to destroy some structures and fences when other methods/tools are not available.</li></ul>', 1),
(9703, 2639, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Using Clay will change a plain stone wall back to rendered walls.', '<p>Using <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">Clay</a> will change a plain stone wall back to rendered walls. \n</p>', 2),
(9704, 2639, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Skills: Clubs Damage Type: Crushing and Piercing Wielding: One-hander .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Skills: <a href=\"/index.php/Clubs\" title=\"Clubs\">Clubs</a></li>\n<li>Damage Type: Crushing and Piercing</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 3),
(9705, 2640, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wooden contraption made from planks with a shaft to press in order to extract juice from fruits and vegetables. Utilized in conjunction with certain materials, a fruit press can be used to create oil and fruit juice.', '<p><i>A wooden contraption made from planks with a shaft to press in order to extract juice from fruits and vegetables.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Utilized in conjunction with certain materials, a fruit press can be used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Oil\" title=\"Oil\">oil</a> and fruit juice.\n</p>', 0),
(9706, 2640, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To use, activate the fruit press and then right-click the material intended to be pressed. From the resulting menu, select \"Create > Food > Fruit juice\". The chosen juice will then be created inside the fruit press. The fruit press can hold 2.00kg of juice, and any excess produced above this amount will be wasted. It is therefore recommended the produced juice/oil held within the fruit press be moved regularly to another container. Materials and Products Input Material Difficulty Base Weight of Input Material (One Unit) Input Material Used Up Per Press Resulting Output and Its Weight Blueberries 20 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Blueberry juice,   0.27 kg Cherries 15 0.20 kg 0.20 kg Cherry juice,   0.18 kg Apples 15 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Apple juice,   0.27 kg Grapes 10 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Grape juice,   0.27 kg Lemons 15 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Lemon juice,   0.27 kg Oranges 20 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Orange juice,   0.27 kg Lingonberries 20 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Lingonberry juice,   0.27 kg Olives 10 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Olive oil,   0.27 kg Strawberries 20 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Strawberry juice,   0.27 kg Raspberries 20 0.30 kg 0.30 kg Raspberry juice,   0.27 kg Pinenuts 35 0.20 kg 0.20 kg Pinenut oil,   0.18 kg Pineapples 25 0.50 kg 0.50 kg Pineapple juice,   0.45 kg Cotton seeds 25 0.10 kg 0.10 kg Cotton seed oil,   0.09 kg Fennel 40 0.05 kg 0.05 kg Fennel oil,   0.045 kg Hazelnuts 30 0.20 kg 0.20 kg Hazelnuts oil,   0.18 kg Walnuts 20 0.20 kg 0.20 kg Walnut oil,   0.18 kg Nutmeg 50 0.05 kg 0.05 kg Nutmeg oil,   0.045 kg Corn 15 0.10 kg 0.10 kg Corn oil,   0.09 kg Octopus ink sac ? 0.40 kg 0.20 kg Black ink ,   0.10 kg and Pig food , 0.05 kg', '<ul><li>To use, <a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">activate</a> the fruit press and then right-click the material intended to be pressed. From the resulting menu, select \"Create &gt; Food &gt; Fruit juice\". The chosen juice will then be created inside the fruit press.</li>\n<li>The fruit press can hold 2.00kg of juice, and any excess produced above this amount will be wasted. It is therefore recommended the produced juice/oil held within the fruit press be moved regularly to another container.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Materials_and_Products\">Materials and Products</span></h3>\n<table border=\"1px\" cellpadding=\"4\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"background: #f9f9f9;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Input Material</th>\n<th>Difficulty</th>\n<th>Base Weight of Input Material (One Unit)</th>\n<th>Input Material Used Up Per Press</th>\n<th>Resulting Output and Its Weight\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Blueberries\" title=\"Blueberries\">Blueberries</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Blueberry juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cherries\" title=\"Cherries\">Cherries</a></td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>Cherry juice,   0.18 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Apples\" title=\"Apples\">Apples</a></td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Apple juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Grapes\" title=\"Grapes\">Grapes</a></td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Grape juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lemons\" title=\"Lemons\">Lemons</a></td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Lemon juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oranges\" title=\"Oranges\">Oranges</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Orange juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Lingonberries\" title=\"Lingonberries\">Lingonberries</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Lingonberry juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Olives\" title=\"Olives\">Olives</a></td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Olive oil,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Strawberries\" title=\"Strawberries\">Strawberries</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Strawberry juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Raspberries\" title=\"Raspberries\">Raspberries</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>0.30 kg</td>\n<td>Raspberry juice,   0.27 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pinenuts\" title=\"Pinenuts\">Pinenuts</a></td>\n<td>35</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>Pinenut oil,   0.18 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pineapples</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>0.50 kg</td>\n<td>0.50 kg</td>\n<td>Pineapple juice,   0.45 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cotton_seeds\" title=\"Cotton seeds\">Cotton seeds</a></td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>0.10 kg</td>\n<td>0.10 kg</td>\n<td>Cotton seed oil,   0.09 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Fennel\" title=\"Fennel\">Fennel</a></td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>0.05 kg</td>\n<td>0.05 kg</td>\n<td>Fennel oil,   0.045 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Hazelnuts\" title=\"Hazelnuts\">Hazelnuts</a></td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>Hazelnuts oil,   0.18 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Walnuts\" title=\"Walnuts\">Walnuts</a></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td>Walnut oil,   0.18 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Nutmeg\" title=\"Nutmeg\">Nutmeg</a></td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>0.05 kg</td>\n<td>0.05 kg</td>\n<td>Nutmeg oil,   0.045 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corn\" title=\"Corn\">Corn</a></td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>0.10 kg</td>\n<td>0.10 kg</td>\n<td>Corn oil,   0.09 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Octopus_ink_sac\" title=\"Octopus ink sac\">Octopus ink sac</a></td>\n<td>?</td>\n<td>0.40 kg</td>\n<td>0.20 kg</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Black_ink\" title=\"Black ink\">Black ink</a>,   0.10 kg and <a href=\"/index.php/Pig_food\" title=\"Pig food\">Pig food</a>, 0.05 kg\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(9707, 2640, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'The last wood piece (sprout included) used in the creation process of the fruit press will determine its final woodtype. Creating oils and juices using the fruit press uses the beverages skill. A rare fruit press speeds the action timer and increases final product quality. Higher quality in a fruit press speeds the action timer and increases the chance of a skill-tick based on the action\'s difficulty.', '<ul><li>The last wood piece (sprout included) used in the creation process of the fruit press will determine its final woodtype.</li>\n<li>Creating oils and juices using the fruit press uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a> skill.</li>\n<li>A rare fruit press speeds the action timer and increases final product quality.</li>\n<li>Higher quality in a fruit press speeds the action timer and increases the chance of a skill-tick based on the action\'s difficulty.</li></ul>', 2),
(9708, 1206, 'Description', 'Description', 'Marble chiseled into a cubic shape. A high quality stone chisel increases the chance of successfully creating a marble brick as well as those of a higher quality. The quality of the marble shards determines the quality of the marble brick.', '<p><i>Marble chiseled into a cubic shape.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A high <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> stone chisel increases the chance of successfully creating a marble brick as well as those of a higher quality. The quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_shards\" title=\"Marble shards\">marble shards</a> determines the quality of the marble brick.\n</p>', 0),
(9709, 1206, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Building marble walls and houses. Improving and repairing marble slab floor . Creation of Brazier pillars . Marble bricks (pavement) .', '<ul><li>Building marble walls and houses.</li>\n<li>Improving and repairing <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_slab_floor\" title=\"Marble slab floor\">marble slab floor</a>.</li>\n<li>Creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_pillar\" title=\"Brazier pillar\">Brazier pillars</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_bricks_(pavement)\" title=\"Marble bricks (pavement)\">Marble bricks (pavement)</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(9710, 2642, 'Description', 'Description', 'Walking on pavement is the fastest way of traveling on foot (up to 17.3Km/h on a flat tile). Pavement can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 Body Strength and 10 Digging.', '<p>Walking on pavement is the fastest way of traveling on foot (up to 17.3Km/h on a flat tile). Pavement can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 Body Strength and 10 Digging. <br/>\n</p>', 0),
(9711, 2642, 'Paving', 'Paving', 'Activate a pottery brick Right-click a tile of packed dirt and select Pave > Pottery bricks . Note : You can also right-click a paved tile and select Re-pave > Tile or Nearest corner', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_brick\" title=\"Pottery brick\">pottery brick</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> and select <i><a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">Pave</a> &gt; Pottery bricks</i>.</li></ol>\n<p><i>Note</i>: You can also right-click a paved tile and select <i>Re-pave</i> &gt; <i>Tile</i> or <i>Nearest corner</i>\n</p>', 1),
(9712, 2642, 'Destroying pavement', 'Destroying_pavement', 'Activate a shovel Right-click a tile of pavement and select Destroy Pavement . Note: 20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy pavement.', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of pavement and select <i>Destroy Pavement</i>.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Note:</b> 20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy pavement.\n</p>', 2),
(9713, 2642, 'Messages', 'Messages', 'You need to be stronger to destroy pavement. 20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement. You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first. 10+ Digging is required to remove pavement. You need to be stronger to dig on roads. 20.10+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.', '<dl><dt>You need to be stronger to destroy pavement.</dt>\n<dd>20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first.</dt>\n<dd>10+ Digging is required to remove pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You need to be stronger to dig on roads.</dt>\n<dd>20.10+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.</dd></dl>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(9714, 2642, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Pottery brick paving: Lichen .', '<p>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Pottery brick paving: <a href=\"/index.php/Lichen\" title=\"Lichen\">Lichen</a>.\n</p>', 4),
(9715, 2642, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Pavement', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pavement\" title=\"Pavement\">Pavement</a></li></ul>', 5),
(9716, 2643, 'Description', 'Description', 'Walking on pavement is the fastest way of traveling on foot (up to 17.3Km/h on a flat tile). Pavement can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 Body Strength and 10 Digging.', '<p>Walking on pavement is the fastest way of traveling on foot (up to 17.3Km/h on a flat tile). Pavement can only be removed or terraformed by a player with 20 Body Strength and 10 Digging. <br/>\n</p>', 0),
(9717, 2643, 'Paving', 'Paving', 'Activate a sandstone brick Right-click a tile of packed dirt and select Pave > Sandstone bricks . Note : You can also right-click a paved tile and select Re-pave > Tile or Nearest corner', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Sandstone_brick\" title=\"Sandstone brick\">sandstone brick</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> and select <i><a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">Pave</a> &gt; Sandstone bricks</i>.</li></ol>\n<p><i>Note</i>: You can also right-click a paved tile and select <i>Re-pave</i> &gt; <i>Tile</i> or <i>Nearest corner</i>\n</p>', 1),
(9718, 2643, 'Destroying pavement', 'Destroying_pavement', 'Activate a shovel Right-click a tile of pavement and select Destroy Pavement . Note: 20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy pavement.', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of pavement and select <i>Destroy Pavement</i>.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Note:</b> 20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy pavement.\n</p>', 2),
(9719, 2643, 'Messages', 'Messages', 'You need to be stronger to destroy pavement. 20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement. You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first. 10+ Digging is required to remove pavement. You need to be stronger to dig on roads. 20.10+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.', '<dl><dt>You need to be stronger to destroy pavement.</dt>\n<dd>20+ Body Strength is required to destroy pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You can\'t figure out how to remove the stone. You must become a bit better at digging first.</dt>\n<dd>10+ Digging is required to remove pavement.</dd>\n<dt>You need to be stronger to dig on roads.</dt>\n<dd>20.10+ Body Strength is required to dig on roads.</dd></dl>', 3),
(9720, 2643, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Sandstone brick paving: Lichen .', '<ul><li>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Sandstone brick paving: <a href=\"/index.php/Lichen\" title=\"Lichen\">Lichen</a>.</li></ul>', 4),
