(10262, 2764, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Upon creation, the catseye will only use 0.01 kg of the eye used, regardless of its weight. Quality of the catseye is capped by the lesser of the quality of the blind catseye and your paving skill divided by 5. Can be stored in a bulk storage bin . Requires 20.1 paving and above 10ql to plant. Can be planted on reinforced cave tiles (actual pavement not necessary). When creating, the QL of the eye affects your success chance. When creating a highway , a waystone must be planted first before planting catseyes. Can be replaced by a waystone without regard to who originally planted it. Can be removed from the ground with a crowbar . Right-click the catseye and select Bash>Pry . The catseye will be damaged with each action until it is broken. Even Fo priests can create catseyes (and doing so increase their paving skill) and plant them. They cannot improve them. Improving catseyes gives paving skill', '<ul><li>Upon creation, the catseye will only use 0.01 kg of the eye used, regardless of its weight.</li>\n<li>Quality of the catseye is capped by the lesser of the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Blind_catseye\" title=\"Blind catseye\">blind catseye</a> and your <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> skill divided by 5.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a>.</li>\n<li>Requires 20.1 <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> and above 10ql to plant.</li>\n<li>Can be planted on reinforced cave tiles (actual pavement not necessary).</li>\n<li>When creating, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Eye\" title=\"Eye\">eye</a> affects your success chance.</li>\n<li>When creating a <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">highway</a>, a <a href=\"/index.php/Waystone\" title=\"Waystone\">waystone</a> must be planted first before planting catseyes.</li>\n<li>Can be replaced by a <a href=\"/index.php/Waystone\" title=\"Waystone\">waystone</a> without regard to who originally planted it.</li>\n<li>Can be removed from the ground with a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>.\n<ul><li>Right-click the catseye and select <i>Bash&gt;Pry</i>.</li>\n<li>The catseye will be damaged with each action until it is broken.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Even <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> priests can create catseyes (and doing so increase their <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> skill) and plant them. They cannot improve them.</li>\n<li>Improving catseyes gives <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> skill</li></ul>', 1),
(10263, 2765, 'Description', 'Description', 'A marker used in the middle of a highway , or it could be, if it had eyes.', '<p><i>A marker used in the middle of a <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">highway</a>, or it could be, if it had eyes.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10264, 2765, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to make a catseye for highways. Can be stored in a bulk storage bin . Quality is capped by the lesser of the quality of stone shards and your paving skill divided by 5. Even Fo priests can create blind catseyes (and doing so increase their paving skill).', '<ul><li>Used to make a <a href=\"/index.php/Catseye\" title=\"Catseye\">catseye</a> for highways.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a>.</li>\n<li>Quality is capped by the lesser of the quality of stone shards and your <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> skill divided by 5.</li>\n<li>Even <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> priests can create blind catseyes (and doing so increase their <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">paving</a> skill).</li></ul>', 1),
(10265, 2766, 'Description', 'Description', 'A marker to designate a junction in a highway.', '<p><i>A marker to designate a junction in a highway.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10266, 2766, 'Notes', 'Notes', '21 paving skill is required to create, continue creating, and install a waystone. Must be above 10ql to plant on a highway. Waystones are removed from a highway with either a crowbar or via replacement with a catseye . If connected to a wagoner container that must be picked up before the waystone can be removed or changed. To replace a waystone with a catseye, activate the catseye in your inventory, right-click the waystone, and select \"replace\". Note - you must be the person who planted the waystone in order to replace it in this way. To plant a waystone, activate the waystone in your inventory, right-click a tile corner, and select \"Plant\". The Allow Highways deed setting must be enabled to plant a waystone. Waystones can be picked up into the inventory after creation. If connected to a wagoner container that container must be picked up before the waystone can be removed or changed.', '<ul><li>21 paving skill is required to create, continue creating, and install a waystone.</li>\n<li>Must be above 10ql to plant on a highway.</li>\n<li>Waystones are removed from a <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">highway</a> with either a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a> or via replacement with a <a href=\"/index.php/Catseye\" title=\"Catseye\">catseye</a>. If connected to a wagoner container that must be picked up before the waystone can be removed or changed.</li>\n<li>To replace a waystone with a catseye, activate the catseye in your inventory, right-click the waystone, and select \"replace\". Note - you must be the person who planted the waystone in order to replace it in this way.</li>\n<li>To plant a waystone, activate the waystone in your inventory, right-click a tile corner, and select \"Plant\". The Allow Highways deed setting must be enabled to plant a waystone.</li>\n<li>Waystones can be picked up into the inventory after creation.</li>\n<li>If connected to a <a href=\"/index.php/Wagoner_container\" title=\"Wagoner container\">wagoner container</a> that container must be picked up before the waystone can be removed or changed.</li></ul>', 1),
(10267, 2766, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'In addition to typical menu items, right-clicking a waystone will also bring up the options to view protection , view links , and find route : View Protection: 30-second action that highlights protected, surrounding tiles in green. View Links: 30-second action that shows direction, with green arrows, to nearby waystones. Find Route: Brings up a dialogue box in which players can select a deed and then find directions to it. For this to work, the deed being searched must have a waystone in it and be a part of the common highway system (same-server only). The preferred route is the shortest distance in tiles, if the distance in tiles is the same between two points then the route with the least number of waystones on the way will be chosen.', '<ul><li>In addition to typical menu items, right-clicking a waystone will also bring up the options to <b>view protection</b>, <b>view links</b>, and <b>find route</b>:\n<ul><li><b>View Protection:</b> 30-second action that highlights protected, surrounding tiles in green.</li>\n<li><b>View Links:</b> 30-second action that shows direction, with green arrows, to nearby waystones.</li>\n<li><b>Find Route:</b> Brings up a dialogue box in which players can select a deed and then find directions to it. For this to work, the deed being searched must have a waystone in it and be a part of the common highway system (same-server only). The preferred route is the shortest distance in tiles, if the distance in tiles is the same between two points then the route with the least number of waystones on the way will be chosen.</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(10268, 2767, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a strong stone parapet.', '<p><i>You see a strong stone parapet. </i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(10269, 2767, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(10270, 2767, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Slate parapet with slate brick. Each slate brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a small barrel and a large barrel .  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a wooden parapet while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.', '<ul><li>Repair Slate parapet with slate brick. Each slate brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">small barrel</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">large barrel</a>.  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_parapet\" title=\"Wooden parapet\">wooden parapet</a> while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(10271, 2767, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(10272, 2768, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a strong stone parapet.', '<p><i>You see a strong stone parapet. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(10273, 2768, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(10274, 2768, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Sandstone parapet with Sandstone brick. Each Sandstone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a small barrel and a large barrel .  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a wooden parapet while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.', '<ul><li>Repair Sandstone parapet with Sandstone brick. Each Sandstone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">small barrel</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">large barrel</a>.  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_parapet\" title=\"Wooden parapet\">wooden parapet</a> while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(10275, 2768, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(10276, 2769, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a strong stone parapet.', '<p><i>You see a strong stone parapet. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(10277, 2769, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(10278, 2769, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Marble parapet with Marble brick. Each Marble brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a small barrel and a large barrel .  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a wooden parapet while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.', '<ul><li>Repair Marble parapet with Marble brick. Each Marble brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>A stone parapet which alternates between the height of a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">small barrel</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">large barrel</a>.  Can easily be seen over by an avatar.  Can only be built on building borders. It is not possible to shoot arrows over either a stone parapet or a <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_parapet\" title=\"Wooden parapet\">wooden parapet</a> while target shooting. However, it works just fine when aiming at a living target.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
