(10677, 2861, 'Description', 'Description', 'Spooky, scary shoulder pads. They send shivers down your spine.', '<p><i>Spooky, scary shoulder pads. They send shivers down your spine.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10678, 2861, 'Effects', 'Effects', 'No known buff, purely decoration.', '<ul><li>No known buff, purely decoration.</li></ul>', 1),
(10679, 2861, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'First obtained during Halloween 2017 by killing hostile creatures. Shoulder pads take damage when not in the player\'s inventory, on a merchant , in the mail or in a magic chest and cannot be repaired. Signature on the shoulder pad is from the mob that dropped it. i.e: \'a.ol.scent.crocodile\'. Could be obtained via Archaeology and slaying hostile mobs throughout the 2021 and 2022 Halloween Events. The archaeology version requires 5 pumpkin shoulder pad fragments to complete. Dye is applied to the leather shoulder area, but not to the pumpkin itself. If dyed, shoulderpads must be removed and re-equipped to show color.', '<ul><li>First obtained during Halloween 2017 by killing hostile creatures.</li>\n<li>Shoulder pads take damage when not in the player\'s inventory, on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Merchant\" title=\"Merchant\">merchant</a>, in the <a href=\"/index.php/Mail\" title=\"Mail\">mail</a> or in a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Magic_chest\" title=\"Magic chest\">magic chest</a> and cannot be repaired.</li>\n<li>Signature on the shoulder pad is from the mob that dropped it. <i>i.e: \'a.ol.scent.crocodile\'.</i></li>\n<li>Could be obtained via <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> and slaying hostile mobs throughout the 2021 and 2022 Halloween Events.</li>\n<li>The archaeology version requires 5 pumpkin shoulder pad fragments to complete.</li>\n<li>Dye is applied to the leather shoulder area, but not to the pumpkin itself.</li>\n<li>If dyed, shoulderpads must be removed and re-equipped to show color.</li></ul>', 2),
(10683, 2863, 'History of the Empire', 'History_of_the_Empire', 'The following is a complete history of the Empire of Mol Rehan on Chaos. It attempts to be as unbiased as possible, although it does present the war from MR\'s side. This section is a WIP. Feel free to contribute!', '<p>The following is a complete history of the Empire of Mol Rehan on Chaos. It attempts to be as unbiased as possible, although it does present the war from MR\'s side.\n</p>\n<p><b>This section is a WIP. Feel free to contribute!</b>\n</p>', 0),
(10684, 2863, 'Leadership Structure', 'Leadership_Structure', 'Kingdom Management Council Emperor Horton - the Emperor of the Empire of Mol Rehan, Horton, holds a special title as the symbolic leader of the kingdom. Horton holds executive, de-jure power over the kingdom, meaning that he normally does not preside over kingdom matters (only offering his advice) except for in times of crisis. Horton is a highly respected and seasoned member of the kingdom, once the mayor of Whosville and both the last and longest-serving chancellor of the Wild kingdom Mol-Rehan. War Chief Emoo - responsible for the day to day de-facto running of the kingdom and for chairing the Warlords, the War Chief can be regarded as the main leader of the kingdom. They also hold the in-game Chief title and the crown of the kingdom. War Chiefs are elected by the citizens of the Empire every 6 months (Normally in January and July.) Any citizen may stand for election and there is no limit on how many times a Chief may stand for re-election. Warlords The Warlords are a closed group of MR\'s most loyal and long-serving players. Its main focus is on planning PvP activities, but it also handles many other high-level kingdom issues. The Warlords system allows players who have contributed to the kingdom for a long time and who have proven their trust to have a say in the running of the most sensitive kingdom issues. The only real requirements for joining are maturity and ability to be trusted. Citizens All citizens of MR are entitled to have their opinion heard in front of the kingdom as a whole, regardless of its nature. Every citizen is entitled to one vote in the biannual War Chief election, and is also entitled to nominate themself for election if they so wish.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kingdom_Management_Council\">Kingdom Management Council</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Emperor <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Whos\" title=\"Player:Whos\">Horton</a></b> - the Emperor of the Empire of Mol Rehan, Horton, holds a special title as the symbolic leader of the kingdom. Horton holds executive, <i>de-jure</i> power over the kingdom, meaning that he normally does not preside over kingdom matters (only offering his advice) except for in times of crisis. Horton is a highly respected and seasoned member of the kingdom, once the mayor of Whosville and both the last and longest-serving chancellor of the Wild kingdom Mol-Rehan.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>War Chief <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Emoo\" title=\"Player:Emoo\">Emoo</a></b>- responsible for the day to day <i>de-facto</i> running of the kingdom and for chairing the Warlords, the War Chief can be regarded as the main leader of the kingdom. They also hold the in-game Chief title and the crown of the kingdom. War Chiefs are elected by the citizens of the Empire every 6 months (Normally in January and July.) Any citizen may stand for election and there is no limit on how many times a Chief may stand for re-election.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Warlords\">Warlords</span></h3>\n<p>The Warlords are a closed group of MR\'s most loyal and long-serving players. Its main focus is on planning PvP activities, but it also handles many other high-level kingdom issues. The Warlords system allows players who have contributed to the kingdom for a long time and who have proven their trust to have a say in the running of the most sensitive kingdom issues. The only real requirements for joining are maturity and ability to be trusted.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<p>All citizens of MR are entitled to have their opinion heard in front of the kingdom as a whole, regardless of its nature. Every citizen is entitled to one vote in the biannual War Chief election, and is also entitled to nominate themself for election if they so wish.\n</p>', 1),
(10685, 2863, 'Main Deeds', 'Main_Deeds', 'The Empire has a number of major deeds, with a list and description of them compiled below. This list will not attempt to include all MR deeds. House of Mol-Rehan Hom Nom Nom Nom Mayor: Horton HoM is MR\'s capital and most symbolic deed. Back in the old Wild days and after the fall of LO, MR\'s first major wardeed, HoM was the village that united the kingdom and kept it afloat. Some say that without HoM and the closure of the home servers, MR on Wild would have become non-existent. HoM is MR\'s largest deed. Arachnadelphia FOR THE WAR!!! Mayor: Robus Arachnadelphia has stood the test of time for many years as a major homeland deed in Mol Rehan. Constructed in the days of the Wild server, Arach still stands to this day as a strong and active deed. Azkaban Mayors: Kharm & Zivirt Azkaban is an eastern fortress, built on the ruins of the old HotS capital Dark Citadel, home to many players who benefit from both its proximity to the Freedom border and its friendly community comprised of new and old players alike. Eden No sanity allowed! Mayor: Febur Eden is by far the furthest west and most secluded deed on the Chaos server - although that doesn\'t mean it wasn\'t built for a fight. With huge walls and a number of veteran players housed inside, it has never been successfully attacked. Eden was also MR\'s stronghold in the brief period of the 3rd Whitelight. Fort Freedom Mayor: Madnezz Fort Freedom is a relatively new deed to the Empire, originally founded as a Freedom village south of starter town Hunter\'s Lodge . FF is now a strong and prominent central stronghold, with a large number of active players. FF is expected to play a key role in the continued growth of the Empire. Heaven\'s Canteen Mayor: Tommty An island fortress founded on the abandoned island previously known as Hell\'s Kitchen , HC is a strong MR deed poised on the edge of the Blacklight mainlands. Kratos Mayor: Emoo Founded by Emoo in the far East of the server, Kratos has been the Empire\'s PvP stronghold since the re-introduction of PvP gameplay to the server. A colossal and impressive mountain fortress, Kratos is the strongest deed in the Empire and arguably the strongest on the server, having never been successfully raided. The deed provided an important staging point for all of the Empire\'s territorial gains in the East of the server. Ravenholm Don\'t dare to question the ways of the Raven. Previous Mayor: Reincarnation/Balmore Mayor: Armyskin Ravenholm is another relatively new deed to the server, founded by long-standing and returned players Reincarnation and Taya, who both served as LO Mayor and MR Chancellor respectively in the glory days of Libilan Outlaws. Now, they offer another new take on PvP, with a large and friendly deed with a strong focus on recruiting new players to the Chaos server . Valley Cove Mayor: Epicphail/Felinas Valley Cove is a newly built town on the East of Chaos. Ruled over by the ever-friendly Epicphail, it\'s a popular destination for new players to the server, while also being home to numerous more experienced players who are always happy to pass on their knowledge.', '<p>The Empire has a number of major deeds, with a list and description of them compiled below. This list will not attempt to include all MR deeds.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Mol-Rehan\">House of Mol-Rehan</span></h4>\n<p><i>Hom Nom Nom Nom</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>Mayor: Horton</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php?title=House_of_Mol_Rehan\" rel=\"nofollow\">HoM</a> is MR\'s capital and most symbolic deed. Back in the old Wild days and after the fall of LO, MR\'s first major wardeed, HoM was the village that united the kingdom and kept it afloat. Some say that without HoM and the closure of the home servers, MR on Wild would have become non-existent. HoM is MR\'s largest deed.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Arachnadelphia\">Arachnadelphia</span></h4>\n<p><i>FOR THE WAR!!!</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>Mayor: Robus</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php?title=Arachnadelphia\" rel=\"nofollow\">Arachnadelphia</a> has stood the test of time for many years as a major homeland deed in Mol Rehan. Constructed in the days of the Wild server, Arach still stands to this day as a strong and active deed.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Azkaban\">Azkaban</span></h4>\n<p><i>Mayors: Kharm &amp; Zivirt</i>\n</p>\n<p>Azkaban is an eastern fortress, built on the ruins of the old HotS capital Dark Citadel, home to many players who benefit from both its proximity to the Freedom border and its friendly community comprised of new and old players alike.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Eden\">Eden</span></h4>\n<p><i>No sanity allowed!</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>Mayor: Febur</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php?title=Eden\" rel=\"nofollow\">Eden</a> is by far the furthest west and most secluded deed on the Chaos server - although that doesn\'t mean it wasn\'t built for a fight. With huge walls and a number of veteran players housed inside, it has never been successfully attacked. Eden was also MR\'s stronghold in the brief period of the 3rd Whitelight.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fort_Freedom\">Fort Freedom</span></h4>\n<p><i>Mayor: Madnezz</i>\n</p>\n<p>Fort Freedom is a relatively new deed to the Empire, originally founded as a Freedom village south of starter town <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hunter%27s_Lodge\" title=\"Hunter\'s Lodge\">Hunter\'s Lodge</a>. FF is now a strong and prominent central stronghold, with a large number of active players. FF is expected to play a key role in the continued growth of the Empire.\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Heaven\'s_Canteen\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Heaven.27s_Canteen\">Heaven\'s Canteen</span></h4>\n<p><i>Mayor: Tommty</i>\n</p>\n<p>An island fortress founded on the abandoned island previously known as <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php?title=Hell%27s_Kitchen\" rel=\"nofollow\">Hell\'s Kitchen</a>, HC is a strong MR deed poised on the edge of the Blacklight mainlands.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kratos\">Kratos</span></h4>\n<p><i>Mayor: Emoo</i>\n</p>\n<p>Founded by Emoo in the far East of the server, Kratos has been the Empire\'s PvP stronghold since the re-introduction of PvP gameplay to the server. A colossal and impressive mountain fortress, Kratos is the strongest deed in the Empire and arguably the strongest on the server, having never been successfully raided. The deed provided an important staging point for all of the Empire\'s territorial gains in the East of the server.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ravenholm\">Ravenholm</span></h4>\n<p><i>Don\'t dare to question the ways of the Raven.</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>Previous Mayor: Reincarnation/Balmore</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>Mayor: Armyskin</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php/Ravenholm\" rel=\"nofollow\">Ravenholm</a> is another relatively new deed to the server, founded by long-standing and returned players Reincarnation and Taya, who both served as LO Mayor and MR Chancellor respectively in the glory days of Libilan Outlaws. Now, they offer another new take on PvP, with a large and friendly deed with a strong focus on <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/92192-ravenholm-mr-chaos/\" rel=\"nofollow\">recruiting new players to the Chaos server</a>.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Valley_Cove\">Valley Cove</span></h4>\n<p><i>Mayor: Epicphail/Felinas</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/110966-valley-cove-mol-rehan-chaos/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Valley Cove</a>is a newly built town on the East of Chaos. Ruled over by the ever-friendly Epicphail, it\'s a popular destination for new players to the server, while also being home to numerous more experienced players who are always happy to pass on their knowledge.\n</p>', 2),
(10689, 1486, 'Description', 'Description', 'This looks like the collar bone from some animal. These are said to provide luck.', '<p><i>This looks like the collar bone from some animal. These are said to provide luck.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10690, 1486, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Bones are a butchering product from certain uniques . They can also be found by premium players by digging . Bones cannot be found by leveling or flattening. Only digging actions, including digging to pile, have a chance of producing one. On Elevation , Large treasure chests and Supply depots have a chance to contain a bone.', '<ul><li>Bones are a <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a> product from certain <a href=\"/index.php/Unique\" title=\"Unique\">uniques</a>.</li>\n<li>They can also be found by premium players by <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a>.\n<ul><li>Bones cannot be found by leveling or flattening. Only digging actions, including digging to pile, have a chance of producing one.</li></ul></li>\n<li>On <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Large_treasure_chest\" title=\"Large treasure chest\">Large treasure chests</a> and Supply depots have a chance to contain a bone.</li></ul>', 1),
(10691, 1486, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'They have a one-time use for transferring their rarity level onto another item. Item must be finished and must be an item that can be picked up/held in inventory. Cannot be used on coins. There is no timer for use of a strange bone. Please make sure you are rare-ing the right item.', '<ul><li>They have a one-time use for transferring their <a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">rarity level</a> onto another item.\n<ul><li>Item must be finished and must be an item that can be picked up/held in inventory.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Cannot be used on coins.</li>\n<li>There is no timer for use of a strange bone. Please make sure you are rare-ing the right item.</li></ul>', 2),
(10692, 1486, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Rarity system Unique Skull', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">Rarity system</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Unique\" title=\"Unique\">Unique</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Skull\" title=\"Skull\">Skull</a></li></ul>', 3),
(10701, 2868, 'Description', 'Description', 'A mouldy cow head, with some fleshy bits still attached to it.', '<p><i>A mouldy cow head, with some fleshy bits still attached to it.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10702, 2868, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Obtained from killing and butchering the Troll King . Obtained at 70ql. Cannot be dyed. Can be colored by applying an Adamantine Rune of Jackal . Example: A mouldy cow head, with some fleshy bits still attached to it. Colors: R≈121, G≈129, B≈3.', '<ul><li>Obtained from killing and butchering the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Troll_King\" title=\"Troll King\">Troll King</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Obtained at 70ql.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cannot be dyed.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Can be colored by applying an <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">Adamantine Rune of Jackal</a>. Example: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> A mouldy cow head, with some fleshy bits still attached to it. Colors: R≈121, G≈129, B≈3. </span></li></ul>', 1),
(10705, 2870, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sloppy looking headdress, the pinnacle of goblin craftsmanship.', '<p><i>A sloppy looking headdress, the pinnacle of goblin craftsmanship.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10706, 2870, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Obtained from killing and butchering the Goblin leader . Obtained at 55ql. Cannot be dyed.', '<ul><li>Obtained from killing and butchering the <a href=\"/index.php/Goblin_leader\" title=\"Goblin leader\">Goblin leader</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Obtained at 55ql.</li>\n<li>Cannot be dyed.</li></ul>', 1),
(10724, 2877, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Dishes Water Pig food', '<ul><li>Dishes</li>\n<li>Water</li>\n<li>Pig food</li></ul>', 0),
(10730, 2879, 'Description', 'Description', 'Bashing is the use of some item to violently strike and thus destroy some other item or structure.', '<p>Bashing is the use of some item to violently strike and thus destroy some other item or structure.\n</p>', 0),
(10731, 2879, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'You must have at least 21 body strength to bash. Activate the item with which you will do the bashing, then right-click the item to be bashed and select \"destroy\" or \"bash\".', '<ul><li>You must have at least 21 body strength to bash.</li>\n<li>Activate the item with which you will do the bashing, then right-click the item to be bashed and select \"destroy\" or \"bash\".</li></ul>', 1),
(10732, 2879, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Different items bash different things with varying efficacy. For example, it seems that carving knives work best in bashing rope fences and many wooden objects. Large mauls work well on stone items. Bashing is not an official skill nor does it carry a title of any sort. The quality of the item doing the bashing also seems to have a considerable effect on the efficacy of each bash action. Followers of some religions may find bashing to be a conflict. Toggling religious devotion is one way around this. On-deed, deed rules and permission settings apply and can thus prohibit or allow bashing. Wooden items made from oak receive a 25% bonus to resilience against bashing damage. Items made of lead provide a 20% bonus to the damage caused with each bash action. Some creatures are also able to bash and destroy certain structures. Bashing/destroying items can be done while moving. Bashing structures can not be done while moving. Various metals do more or less damage when bashing ranging from lead being the best and zinc being the worst. Bashing planted items will lower their effective quality by (Damage in decibles * Quality of item) Planted items lowered to 10 effective quality, or hit 70 damage, will become unplanted.', '<ul><li>Different items bash different things with varying efficacy. For example, it seems that carving knives work best in bashing rope fences and many wooden objects. Large mauls work well on stone items.</li>\n<li>Bashing is not an official skill nor does it carry a title of any sort.</li>\n<li>The quality of the item doing the bashing also seems to have a considerable effect on the efficacy of each bash action.</li>\n<li>Followers of some religions may find bashing to be a conflict. Toggling religious devotion is one way around this.</li>\n<li>On-deed, deed rules and permission settings apply and can thus prohibit or allow bashing.</li>\n<li>Wooden items made from oak receive a 25% bonus to resilience against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Items made of <a href=\"/index.php/Lead\" title=\"Lead\">lead</a> provide a 20% bonus to the damage caused with each bash action.</li>\n<li>Some creatures are also able to bash and destroy certain structures.</li>\n<li>Bashing/destroying items can be done while moving. Bashing structures can not be done while moving.</li>\n<li>Various metals do more or less damage when bashing ranging from <a href=\"/index.php/Lead\" title=\"Lead\">lead</a> being the best and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Zinc\" title=\"Zinc\">zinc</a> being the worst.</li>\n<li>Bashing planted items will lower their effective quality by (Damage in decibles * Quality of item)<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\"></ul>\n</li><li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Quality_vs_damage.png\"><img alt=\"Quality vs damage.png\" data-file-height=\"1331\" data-file-width=\"1486\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"107\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/Quality_vs_damage.png/120px-Quality_vs_damage.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/Quality_vs_damage.png/180px-Quality_vs_damage.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1a/Quality_vs_damage.png/240px-Quality_vs_damage.png 2x\" width=\"120\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<ul><li>Planted items lowered to 10 effective quality, or hit 70 damage, will become unplanted.</li></ul>', 2),
(10750, 2540, 'Description', 'Description', 'Some pieces of hardened wood gathered from a defeated rift. Can be crafted together with metal to create a rune that will attach to wooden items. Rift wood is used to create runes .', '<p><i>Some pieces of hardened wood gathered from a defeated rift. Can be crafted together with metal to create a rune that will attach to wooden items.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Rift wood</b> is used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">runes</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(10751, 2540, 'Aquisition', 'Aquisition', 'Woodcutting Rift wood can be obtained by cutting down a rift plant in the rift area after the rift has been closed. Gathering these efficiently requires a high woodcutting skill. Gathered rift wood is dropped directly into the inventory. A failed action results in a regular log on the ground with a random woodtype. Participation Rift wood is also randomly distributed to players according to their participation points together with the other rift rewards after the rift has been closed.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Woodcutting\">Woodcutting</span></h3>\n<p>Rift wood can be obtained by <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">cutting</a> down a <a href=\"/index.php/Rift_plant\" title=\"Rift plant\">rift plant</a> in the <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">rift</a> area after the rift has been closed. Gathering these efficiently requires a high <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">woodcutting</a> skill. Gathered rift wood is dropped directly into the inventory. A failed action results in a regular <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> on the ground with a random woodtype. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Participation\">Participation</span></h3>\n<p>Rift wood is also randomly distributed to players according to their participation points together with the other rift rewards after the rift has been closed.\n</p>', 1),
(10752, 2540, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Rift wood combined with a metal lump and devoted to a god creates a rune that can be attached to wooden items. Creating runes with rift wood uses fine carpentry . Rift wood used on a barrel filled with wort creates Rift Beer. Different Woodtypes determine the temporary affinity.', '<p>Rift wood combined with a metal <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lump\" title=\"Lump\">lump</a> and devoted to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/God\" title=\"God\">god</a> creates a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a> that can be attached to wooden items. Creating runes with rift wood uses <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Rift wood used on a barrel filled with wort creates Rift Beer. Different Woodtypes determine the temporary affinity.\n</p>', 2),
(10753, 2540, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The woodtype has no effect for runes. Woodtypes Include: Birch, Maple, Oak, Oleander, and Willow. Failure to create runes uses 0.01kg of the material. 0.20kg is needed to craft runes .', '<ul><li>The woodtype has no effect for runes.</li>\n<li>Woodtypes Include: Birch, Maple, Oak, Oleander, and Willow.</li>\n<li>Failure to create <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">runes</a> uses <b>0.01kg</b> of the material.</li>\n<li><b>0.20kg</b> is needed to craft <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">runes</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(10754, 2540, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Rift crystal Rift stone shard', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rift_crystal\" title=\"Rift crystal\">Rift crystal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rift_stone_shard\" title=\"Rift stone shard\">Rift stone shard</a></li></ul>', 4),
(10783, 2891, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This artifact is the only weapon used by these skills, which have no other function.', '<p>This <a href=\"/index.php/Artifact\" title=\"Artifact\">artifact</a> is the only weapon used by these skills, which have no other function.\n</p>', 0),
(10784, 2891, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Hammers Subskills Warhammer', '<ul><li>Hammers</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Warhammer\" title=\"Warhammer\">Warhammer</a></li></ul>', 1),
(10785, 2891, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Hammerer at 50 skill Assaulter at 70 skill Thor at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Hammerer at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Assaulter at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Thor at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(10786, 2892, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Hammers > Warhammer', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammers\" title=\"Hammers\">Hammers</a> &gt; Warhammer</li></ul>', 0),
(10787, 2892, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Sledgehammer at 50 skill Dwarf at 70 skill Stag King at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Sledgehammer at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Dwarf at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Stag King at 90 skill</li></ul>', 1),
(10794, 2895, 'Description', 'Description', 'A metal key with a few large teeth. It has some weird dents Used to lock or unlock different kinds of locks .', '<p><i>A metal key with a few large teeth. It has some weird dents</i>\n</p>\n<p>Used to lock or unlock different kinds of <a href=\"/index.php/Lock\" title=\"Lock\">locks</a>.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(10795, 2895, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the key form affects your success chance when creating. The quality of the copper lump affects the quality of the resulting key. Copies of keys made from copper will show up as key copy, copper to show it is a copy of a key rather than the original', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Key_form\" title=\"Key form\">key form</a> affects your success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The quality of the copper lump affects the quality of the resulting key.</li>\n<li>Copies of keys made from copper will show up as <i>key copy, copper</i> to show it is a copy of a key rather than the original</li></ul>', 1),
(10801, 2897, 'Description', 'Description', 'Lemons can be harvested from this tree with a sickle during the appropriate season .', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lemons\" title=\"Lemons\">Lemons</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> during the appropriate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(10802, 2897, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When in harvest season , lemons can be harvested from this tree with a sickle . These lemons can then be used in cooking , making beverages , and in transmutation liquid . When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: The tree has some fine yellow lemons. Lemon trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly. Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.', '<ul><li>When in harvest <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lemons\" title=\"Lemons\">lemons</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>. These lemons can then be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a>, making <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a>, and in <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquid</a>.</li>\n<li>When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining:  <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The tree has some fine yellow lemons.  </span></li>\n<li>Lemon trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly.</li>\n<li>Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.</li></ul>', 1),
(10803, 2897, 'Images', 'Images', 'Lemon tree in season', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 294.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 294.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 292.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"760\" data-file-width=\"742\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e4/Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg/439px-Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e4/Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg/659px-Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg 1.5x, /images/e/e4/Lemon_tree_fruit.jpg 2x\" width=\"293\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 273px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lemon tree in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(10804, 2897, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fruit Forestry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fruit\" title=\"Fruit\">Fruit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a></li></ul>', 3),
(10813, 2899, 'Description', 'Description', 'Oranges can be harvested from this tree with a sickle during the appropriate season .', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oranges\" title=\"Oranges\">Oranges</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> during the appropriate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(10814, 2899, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When in harvest season , oranges can be harvested from this tree with a sickle . These oranges can then be used in cooking , making beverages , and in transmutation liquid . When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: The tree has some fine oranges. Orange trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly. Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.', '<ul><li>When in harvest <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oranges\" title=\"Oranges\">oranges</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>. These oranges can then be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a>, making <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a>, and in <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquid</a>.</li>\n<li>When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The tree has some fine oranges. </span></li>\n<li>Orange trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly.</li>\n<li>Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.</li></ul>', 1),
(10815, 2899, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fruit Forestry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fruit\" title=\"Fruit\">Fruit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(10816, 2900, 'Description', 'Description', 'Cherry trees are known for producing delicious cherries in season.', '<p>Cherry trees are known for producing delicious cherries in season.\n</p>', 0),
(10817, 2900, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When in harvest season , cherries can be harvested from this tree with a sickle . These cherries can then be used in cooking , making beverages , and in transmutation liquid . Cherry trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly. Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.', '<ul><li>When in harvest <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cherries\" title=\"Cherries\">cherries</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>. These cherries can then be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a>, making <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a>, and in <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquid</a>.</li>\n<li>Cherry trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly.</li>\n<li>Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.</li></ul>', 1),
(10818, 2900, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fruit Forestry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fruit\" title=\"Fruit\">Fruit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(10822, 2809, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pair of bags that may be added to a saddle. Saddle bags can be placed in a saddle to allow horses to carry items.', '<p><i>A pair of bags that may be added to a saddle.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Saddle bags can be placed in a <a href=\"/index.php/Saddle\" title=\"Saddle\">saddle</a> to allow horses to carry items.\n</p>', 0),
(10823, 2809, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'They each have a volume of 100. 11 Pottery bowls fit in a saddlebag. Items in saddlebags count as 50% weight compared to having the item in your inventory while riding the horse.', '<ul><li>They each have a volume of 100.</li>\n<li>11 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">Pottery bowls</a> fit in a saddlebag.</li>\n<li>Items in saddlebags count as 50% weight compared to having the item in your inventory while riding the horse.</li></ul>', 1),
(10824, 2809, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Saddle', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Saddle\" title=\"Saddle\">Saddle</a></li></ul>', 2),
(10863, 2910, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cart designed to transport creature cages over land.', '<p><i>A cart designed to transport creature cages over land.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10864, 2910, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Creature transporters require 25 fine carpentry to start. 20.1 mind logic is needed to command the creature transporter. Will not hold anything but creature cages . Can be dragged by a player or have 2 animals hitched to it to pull it. Can carry a maximum of 4 cages. Can not be loaded on to a boat, wagon, nor large cart.', '<ul><li>Creature transporters require 25 <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a> to start.</li>\n<li>20.1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> is needed to command the creature transporter.</li>\n<li>Will not hold anything but <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">creature cages</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be dragged by a player or have 2 animals hitched to it to pull it.</li>\n<li>Can carry a maximum of 4 cages.</li>\n<li>Can not be loaded on to a boat, wagon, nor large cart.</li></ul>', 1),
(10865, 2910, 'To Load', 'To_Load', 'First, drag or move the transporter very close to the cage. Then embark on the transporter. From here, right click the cage and select \"Load Cargo\". 23 body strength is needed to use the load cargo function to load cages.', '<ul><li>First, drag or move the transporter very close to the cage. Then embark on the transporter. From here, right click the cage and select \"Load Cargo\".</li>\n<li>23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> is needed to use the <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">load cargo</a> function to load cages.</li></ul>', 2),
(10866, 2910, 'Hitchable Creatures', 'Hitchable_Creatures', 'Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a cart or wagon. Brown bears when tamed , young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Bulls Bisons Donkeys Hell horse , young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Horses Mules Trolls when dominated , young and adolescent Unicorns when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged Weta when on Jackal', '<p>Many of Wurm\'s creatures may be hitched to pull a cart or wagon.  \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">Brown bears</a> when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tame\" title=\"Tame\">tamed</a>, young and adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">Bulls</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bisons</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Donkey\" title=\"Donkey\">Donkeys</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">Hell horse</a>, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horses</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mule\" title=\"Mule\">Mules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Trolls</a> when <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">dominated</a>, young and adolescent</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">Unicorns</a> when tamed, young, adolescent, mature and the first stages of aged</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weta\" title=\"Weta\">Weta</a> when on Jackal</li></ul>', 3),
(10867, 2910, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Creature cage', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature cage</a></li></ul>', 4),
(10868, 2911, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cage to hold a creature. This cage is empty. A creature cage is a device that can load a creature into a ship and take it cross-server. Not to be confused with the Creature transporter .', '<p><i>A cage to hold a creature. This cage is empty.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A creature cage is a device that can load a creature into a ship and take it cross-server. Not to be confused with the <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_transporter\" title=\"Creature transporter\">Creature transporter</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(10869, 2911, 'General notes', 'General_notes', '60 Carpentry skill is required to create the cage and continue building it. 23 Body strength is required to load the cage onto a ship/creature transporter. Like all loaded containers, deed permissions come into play.', '<ul><li>60 <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill is required to create the cage and continue building it.</li>\n<li>23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a> is required to load the cage onto a ship/creature transporter.</li>\n<li>Like all loaded containers, deed <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> come into play.</li></ul>', 1),
(10870, 2911, 'Operation', 'Operation', 'To load (while leading animal): Right click cage -> Load creature. To unload (after unloading cage): Activate rope / halter rope > Right click cage > Open > Right click creature > Unload creature.', '<ul><li>To load (while leading animal): Right click cage -&gt; Load creature.</li>\n<li>To unload (after unloading cage): Activate <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">rope</a>/<a href=\"/index.php/Halter_rope\" title=\"Halter rope\">halter rope</a> &gt; Right click cage &gt; Open &gt; Right click creature &gt; Unload creature.</li></ul>', 2),
(10871, 2911, 'Concerning venerable animals', 'Concerning_venerable_animals', 'When loading a venerable animal, the message \"The venerable fat (animal name) is venerable, and may die if it crosses to another server\" will show. This simply means if the animal has not been cared for on the destination server, there is a very random, somewhat rare chance the animal could die as soon as it\'s unloaded. To reduce this risk, use an electrum rune \'s spell on the creature, which will reduce the creature\'s age.', '<p>When loading a venerable animal, the message <i>\"The venerable fat (animal name) is venerable, and may die if it crosses to another server\"</i> will show. This simply means if the animal has not been <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry#Caring\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">cared for</a> on the destination server, there is a very random, somewhat rare chance the animal could die as soon as it\'s unloaded.\n</p>\n<ul><li>To reduce this risk, use an <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Electrum\" title=\"Electrum\">electrum</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rune\" title=\"Rune\">rune</a>\'s spell on the creature, which will reduce the creature\'s age.</li></ul>', 3),
(10872, 2911, 'Notes', 'Notes', '1 creature per cage, no matter the size. You cannot load pregnant, hurt, or equipped animals (ones with horse shoes/bridle etc..). You can only lead and load one animal at a time. Max of 4 creature cages per tile. A caged animal damages the cage over time. A higher quality cage receives less damage. The animal will kick the cage in anger after being unloaded, causing more damage. You cannot repair or improve a cage if it\'s storing an animal. When a cage hits 80 damage, the animal will escape. A low QL cage can take 80 damage in under 48 hours. The cage can be pushed/pulled/rotated, with or without an animal. A rope/halter rope is needed to unload the animal from the cage. Only animals that are leadable can be stored in the cage. Note that some animals need to be tamed to be led. Animals with traits will keep them when crossing servers. Venerable animals run a (small) risk that they might die (if not cared for) on the destination server as soon as they\'re unloaded. However, they can be cared for as soon you pass the server border, even when loaded. Unlike vehicles, a branded animal will not transfer their permissions when crossing servers. Can be hauled up and down ladders with or without creature loaded. When you open the creature cage with a loaded animal, the ql shown for the animal, depicts the age of the animal in Wurm months.', '<ul><li>1 creature per cage, no matter the size.</li>\n<li>You cannot load pregnant, hurt, or equipped animals (ones with horse shoes/bridle etc..).</li>\n<li>You can only lead and load one animal at a time.</li>\n<li>Max of 4 creature cages per tile.</li>\n<li>A caged animal damages the cage over time. A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">quality</a> cage receives less damage.</li>\n<li>The animal will kick the cage in anger after being unloaded, causing more damage.</li>\n<li>You cannot repair or improve a cage if it\'s storing an animal.</li>\n<li>When a cage hits 80 damage, the animal will escape.</li>\n<li>A low QL cage can take 80 damage in under 48 hours.</li>\n<li>The cage can be pushed/pulled/rotated, with or without an animal.</li>\n<li>A rope/halter rope is needed to unload the animal from the cage.</li>\n<li>Only animals that are leadable can be stored in the cage. Note that some animals need to be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> to be led.</li>\n<li>Animals with traits will keep them when crossing servers.</li>\n<li>Venerable animals run a (small) risk that they might die (if not cared for) on the destination server as soon as they\'re unloaded. However, they can be cared for as soon you pass the server border, even when loaded.</li>\n<li>Unlike vehicles, a branded animal will <i><b>not</b></i> transfer their permissions when crossing servers.</li>\n<li>Can be hauled up and down ladders with or without creature loaded.</li>\n<li>When you open the creature cage with a loaded animal, the ql shown for the animal, depicts the age of the animal in Wurm months.</li></ul>', 4),
(10873, 2911, 'Vehicle load capacity', 'Vehicle_load_capacity', 'Vehicle Quantity Wagon 2 Cog 6 Corbita 5 Knarr 4 Caravel 8 Creature transporter 4', '<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"90\">Vehicle</th>\n<th>Quantity\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cog</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">Corbita</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">Knarr</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Caravel\" title=\"Caravel\">Caravel</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Creature_transporter\" title=\"Creature transporter\">Creature transporter</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(10874, 2911, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Creature transporter', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Creature_transporter\" title=\"Creature transporter\">Creature transporter</a></li></ul>', 6),
(10881, 2913, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small book with a dyeable cover. Can be used to hold papyrus or paper sheets .', '<p><i>A small book with a dyeable cover. Can be used to hold <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Papyrus\" title=\"Papyrus\">papyrus</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Paper_sheet\" title=\"Paper sheet\">paper sheets</a>.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10882, 2913, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Placeable as a decoration on furniture. Used to make Almanac , Archaeology journal or Atlas . Creation quality is capped at 1/5 of papyrusmaking skill. Improves with cloth tailoring tools and gives papyrusmaking skill. A book whose quality is 22 or less will hold 22 pages. If its quality is 23 or more, it will hold the number of pages equal to its quality. Rare books do not allow more pages to be stored than non-rares of the same quality. Paper, papyrus and reports will no longer decay inside books. A book can be given a title of up to 20 characters.', '<ul><li>Placeable as a decoration on furniture.</li>\n<li>Used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Almanac\" title=\"Almanac\">Almanac</a>,  <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">Archaeology journal</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Atlas\" title=\"Atlas\">Atlas</a>.</li>\n<li>Creation quality is capped at 1/5 of papyrusmaking skill.</li>\n<li>Improves with cloth tailoring tools and gives papyrusmaking skill.</li>\n<li>A book whose quality is 22 or less will hold 22 pages. If its quality is 23 or more, it will hold the number of pages equal to its quality.</li>\n<li>Rare books do not allow more pages to be stored than non-rares of the same quality.</li>\n<li>Paper, papyrus and reports will no longer decay inside books.</li>\n<li>A book can be given a title of up to 20 characters.</li></ul>', 1),
(10885, 2915, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sharp looking empty bookshelf to store your special writings.', '<p><i>A sharp looking empty bookshelf to store your special writings.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10886, 2915, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can hold up to 30 items including books. Can be picked up by hand. Cannot be loaded or dyed. Skill requirement: 25 Fine Carpentry. Able to have items placed on it, though these items will decay over time, even on deed.', '<ul><li>Can hold up to 30 items including books.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up by hand.</li>\n<li>Cannot be loaded or dyed.</li>\n<li>Skill requirement: 25 Fine Carpentry.</li>\n<li>Able to have items placed on it, though these items will decay over time, even on deed.</li></ul>', 1),
(10887, 2915, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Empty high bookshelf Low bookshelf High bookshelf', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empty_high_bookshelf\" title=\"Empty high bookshelf\">Empty high bookshelf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Low_bookshelf\" title=\"Low bookshelf\">Low bookshelf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/High_bookshelf\" title=\"High bookshelf\">High bookshelf</a></li></ul>', 2),
(10888, 2916, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sharp looking empty bookshelf to store your special writings.', '<p><i>A sharp looking empty bookshelf to store your special writings.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10889, 2916, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used as decoration.', '<ul><li>Used as decoration.</li></ul>', 1),
(10890, 2916, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can hold up to 41 items including books. Can be picked up. Cannot be loaded or dyed. Skill Requirement: 35 Fine Carpentry. Able to have items placed on it.', '<ul><li>Can hold up to 41 items including books.</li>\n<li>Can be picked up.</li>\n<li>Cannot be loaded or dyed.</li>\n<li>Skill Requirement: 35 Fine Carpentry.</li>\n<li>Able to have items placed on it.</li></ul>', 2),
(10891, 2916, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Empty low bookshelf Low bookshelf High bookshelf', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empty_low_bookshelf\" title=\"Empty low bookshelf\">Empty low bookshelf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Low_bookshelf\" title=\"Low bookshelf\">Low bookshelf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/High_bookshelf\" title=\"High bookshelf\">High bookshelf</a></li></ul>', 3),
(10901, 2919, 'Description', 'Description', 'You can almost feel the mask is alive with little shoots among the leaves.', '<p><i>You can almost feel the mask is alive with little shoots among the leaves.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10902, 2919, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The mask of rebirth is originally from the Midsummers event on Xanadu back in June 2017 One of many potential rewards through the 12th Anniversary of Wurm Archaeology event gift boxes. It does not decay when stored on-deed.', '<ul><li>The mask of rebirth is originally from the Midsummers event on Xanadu back in June 2017</li>\n<li>One of many potential rewards through the 12th Anniversary of Wurm Archaeology event gift boxes.</li>\n<li>It does not decay when stored on-deed.</li></ul>', 1),
(10908, 2917, 'Description', 'Description', 'A journal to safely keep reports of archaeological discoveries you have made.', '<p><i>A journal to safely keep reports of archaeological discoveries you have made.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10909, 2917, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Use a Book and 3 leather strips to make an Archaeology Journal. An unfinished journal will be created at 1/5 of your leatherworking skill with each following leather strip improving its quality until the journal is finished. The book\'s quality and also the finished journal can be improved but note that the book will use cloth tailoring tools but give papyrus skill and the journal will use leatherworking tools and also give leatherworking skill. Journals will now hold a number of reports up to the ql of the journal, with a minimum of 22. Placing a piece of paper or papyrus greater than 30ql inside the journal will automatically turn it into a blank report', '<ul><li>Use a <a href=\"/index.php/Book\" title=\"Book\">Book</a> and 3 leather strips to make an Archaeology Journal. An unfinished journal will be created at 1/5 of your leatherworking skill with each following leather strip improving its quality until the journal is finished.</li>\n<li>The book\'s quality and also the finished journal can be improved but note that the book will use cloth tailoring tools but give papyrus skill and the journal will use leatherworking tools and also give leatherworking skill.</li>\n<li>Journals will now hold a number of reports up to the ql of the journal, with a minimum of 22.</li>\n<li>Placing a piece of <a href=\"/index.php/Paper_sheet\" title=\"Paper sheet\">paper</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Papyrus\" title=\"Papyrus\">papyrus</a> greater than 30ql inside the journal will automatically turn it into a blank report</li></ul>', 1),
(10910, 2917, 'Using the Journal to Locate Hidden Caches and Old Deeds', 'Using_the_Journal_to_Locate_Hidden_Caches_and_Old_Deeds', 'Data will automatically record to reports/pages as it is found via the archaeological investigation process. With sufficient information in a report, you will get the message: [21:27:06] You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called *name of deed*. You feel confident you know exactly where *name of deed* once lay, and complete the location details in the report. The option to \"Get Direction\" will appear on that report from the right-click menu. \"Get Direction\" will show the player exactly where the center tile of that deed once stood. A player can then stand on that tile, once located, and utilize the same \"Get Direction\" command to then unearth a special cache from that prior deed. Simply follow the directions given while trying \"Get Direction\" on different tiles. Once located, this cache will hold a variety of unidentified archaeology fragments with a higher chance at statue fragments in addition to a small token attributed to that old deed. Once this cache is unearthed, the report used to find it will be consumed. The amount of fragments a player may find is determined by their archaeology skill and the report\'s quality with a minimum of 10 fragments . [18:44:30] You spot something glinting in the ground and start pulling it free... [18:44:44] As you discover a Rocky Coast hidden cache the report is crumpled up and ruined. [18:45:02] A small chest that rattles with the sound of some item fragments inside. It is made from birchwood. Ql: 37.456696, Dam: 0.0.', '<p>Data will automatically record to reports/pages as it is found via the archaeological investigation process. With sufficient information in a report, you will get the message: <i>[21:27:06] You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called *name of deed*. You feel confident you know exactly where *name of deed* once lay, and complete the location details in the report.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The option to \"Get Direction\" will appear on that report from the right-click menu. \"Get Direction\" will show the player exactly where the center tile of that deed once stood. A player can then stand on that tile, once located, and utilize the same \"Get Direction\" command to then unearth a special cache from that prior deed. Simply follow the directions given while trying \"Get Direction\" on different tiles. Once located, this cache will hold a variety of unidentified archaeology fragments with a higher chance at statue fragments in addition to a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_token\" title=\"Small token\">small token</a> attributed to that old deed. Once this cache is unearthed, the report used to find it will be consumed. The amount of fragments a player may find is determined by their archaeology skill and the report\'s quality with a minimum of 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a>.\n</p>\n<p><i>[18:44:30] You spot something glinting in the ground and start pulling it free...</i>\n<i>[18:44:44] As you discover a Rocky Coast hidden cache the report is crumpled up and ruined.</i>\n<i>[18:45:02] A small chest that rattles with the sound of some item fragments inside. It is made from birchwood. Ql: 37.456696, Dam: 0.0.</i>\n</p>', 2),
(10911, 2917, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'You do not need a pen, ink, or dye for any part of the use or making of an archaeology journal. Reports can also now be moved in and out of journals via drag and drop. Reports can only be read on the server that they were created on. On any other server you will get the message The report seems to be written in some foreign language. Perhaps it is meant for a village from some distant lands . Report quality dictates statue fragment count and the quality levels and numbers of the items found within the cache. A report can be traded and the other player will be able to find directions to the cache. Reports can be renamed. This allows you to tag a report with, for example, the server and location it came from.', '<ul><li>You do not need a pen, ink, or dye for any part of the use or making of an archaeology journal.</li>\n<li>Reports can also now be moved in and out of journals via drag and drop.</li>\n<li>Reports can only be read on the server that they were created on. On any other server you will get the message <i>The report seems to be written in some foreign language. Perhaps it is meant for a village from some distant lands</i>.</li>\n<li>Report quality dictates statue fragment count and the quality levels and numbers of the items found within the cache.</li>\n<li>A report can be traded and the other player will be able to find directions to the cache.</li>\n<li>Reports can be renamed. This allows you to tag a report with, for example, the server and location it came from.</li></ul>', 3),
(10912, 2917, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Archaeology Fragments Restoration Statues', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">Fragments</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">Restoration</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li></ul>', 4),
(10915, 1277, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin and long leather strip.', '<p><i>A thin and long leather strip.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10916, 1277, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Leather wound handle Lunchbox Tackle box Archaeology journal Almanac Atlas Bedroll Tortoise shield', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Leather_wound_handle\" title=\"Leather wound handle\">Leather wound handle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lunchbox\" title=\"Lunchbox\">Lunchbox</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tackle_box\" title=\"Tackle box\">Tackle box</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">Archaeology journal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Almanac\" title=\"Almanac\">Almanac</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Atlas\" title=\"Atlas\">Atlas</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bedroll\" title=\"Bedroll\">Bedroll</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tortoise_shield\" title=\"Tortoise shield\">Tortoise shield</a></li></ul>', 1),
(10924, 1733, 'Description', 'Description', 'This giant cherry wasn\'t mature when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. God food that may contain strange powers!', '<p><i>This giant cherry wasn\'t mature when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. God food that may contain strange powers!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10925, 1733, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Stoneskin (Ignore next 3 wounds taken) Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%) Costs 500 karma to cast.', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Stoneskin (Ignore next 3 wounds taken)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%)</li>\n<li>Costs 500 <a href=\"/index.php/Karma\" title=\"Karma\">karma</a> to cast.</li></ul>', 1),
(10926, 1733, 'Item use requirements', 'Item_use_requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.\n</p>', 2),
(10927, 1733, 'Messages', 'Messages', '[21:56:48] You start using the green cherry. [21:56:57] The cherry is very bitter. [21:57:08] The green cherry crumbles to dust.', '<p>[21:56:48] You start using the green cherry.<br/>\n[21:56:57] The cherry is very bitter.<br/>\n[21:57:08] The green cherry crumbles to dust.<br/>\n</p>', 3),
(10928, 1732, 'Description', 'Description', 'This giant cherry was fully ripe when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. It may take you there to join the deities!', '<p><i>This giant cherry was fully ripe when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. It may take you there to join the deities!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10929, 1732, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Karma Bolt (Causes infection wound on target) Spell granted: Forecast (Places traps around target) Resistance: Poison 15% (Decreases poison damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Physical 5% (Increases physical damage taken by 5%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Karma Bolt (Causes infection wound on target)</li>\n<li>Spell granted: Forecast (Places traps around target)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Poison 15% (Decreases poison damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Physical 5% (Increases physical damage taken by 5%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10930, 1732, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be high up towards the heavens, closer to the gods. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, at least 1000 slope above sea level.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be high up towards the heavens, closer to the gods.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, at least 1000 slope above sea level.\n</p>', 2),
(10931, 1730, 'Description', 'Description', 'This giant cherry was almost ripe when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. God food that may contain mystical powers!', '<p><i>This giant cherry was almost ripe when it was picked from the tree on Valrei, home of the gods. God food that may contain mystical powers!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10932, 1730, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Rust Monster (Attacker\'s weapon takes more damage) Resistance: Water 15% (Decreases water damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Disease 10% (Increases disease damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Rust Monster (Attacker\'s weapon takes more damage)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Water 15% (Decreases water damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Disease 10% (Increases disease damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10933, 1730, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be deep in the barren desert, where nothing ever grows. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, inside at least 51x51 desert area.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be deep in the barren desert, where nothing ever grows.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, inside at least 51x51 desert area.\n</p>', 2),
(10943, 2343, 'Description', 'Description', 'Orange red golden flames endorse the covers of this tome.', '<p><i>Orange red golden flames endorse the covers of this tome.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10944, 2343, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Incinerate (Damage over time spell, causing very light to light burn wounds each 10 seconds, damage and amount of ticks may vary - 750 karma to cast) Resistance: Fire 15% (Decreases Fire damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Bite 10% (Increases Bite damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Incinerate (Damage over time spell, causing very light to light burn wounds each 10 seconds, damage and amount of ticks may vary - 750 karma to cast)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Fire 15% (Decreases Fire damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Bite 10% (Increases Bite damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10945, 2343, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area.\n</p>', 2),
(10946, 1741, 'Description', 'Description', 'A black leather book with an etched silver owl, to be read by the wicked and twisted.', '<p><i>A black leather book with an etched silver owl, to be read by the wicked and twisted.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10947, 1741, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Karma Missile (Causes 4 acid wounds on the target) Resistance: Pierce 15% (Decreases pierce damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Bite 10% (Increases bite damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Karma Missile (Causes 4 acid wounds on the target)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Pierce 15% (Decreases pierce damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Bite 10% (Increases bite damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10948, 1741, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area inside a cave.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area inside a cave.\n</p>', 2),
(10952, 1740, 'Description', 'Description', 'A parchment roll inscribed with symbols that glow faintly as you eye them. You have a hard time refraining from reading as you feel it will change your inner being.', '<p><i>A parchment roll inscribed with symbols that glow faintly as you eye them. You have a hard time refraining from reading as you feel it will change your inner being.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10953, 1740, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Karma Slow (Slows attack speed) Resistance: Crush 15% (Decreases crush damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Slash 10% (Increases slash damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Karma Slow (Slows attack speed)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Crush 15% (Decreases crush damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Slash 10% (Increases slash damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10954, 1740, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.\n</p>', 2),
(10955, 1742, 'Description', 'Description', 'This crystal vial contains the paralyzing slime of Uttacha, a giant slug living leagues deep in the Shaded Depths of Valrei.', '<p><i>This crystal vial contains the paralyzing slime of Uttacha, a giant slug living leagues deep in the Shaded Depths of Valrei.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10956, 1742, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: True Strike (Next hit is 100% Crit) Resistance: Slash 15% (Decreases slash damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Crush 10% (Increases crush damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: True Strike (Next hit is 100% Crit)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Slash 15% (Decreases slash damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Crush 10% (Increases crush damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10957, 1742, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.\n</p>', 2),
(10958, 1735, 'Description', 'Description', 'This giant walnut has been picked on Valrei, home of the gods. Strange powers may dwelve within!', '<p><i>This giant walnut has been picked on Valrei, home of the gods. Strange powers may dwelve within!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(10959, 1735, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Lightning (Causes a head wound) Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Lightning (Causes a head wound)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(10960, 1735, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.\n</p>', 2),
(10977, 2946, 'Description', 'Description', 'A black hole with shimmering edges. It is unstable and will disappear in about 368 days, 19 hours and 49 minutes. Unstable source rifts were the result of an old bug where a fountain or other large complex object could be created inside of a smaller container, allowing the owner to store a considerable volume inside of a smaller space. The bug that allowed their creation has since been fixed and it is no longer possible to create these containers. As the name suggests, these items were unstable and were phased out of Wurm Online. It is strongly recommended for owners of these containers to relocate their contents before they are removed and their contents emptied into the container they are in or on the ground.', '<p><i>A black hole with shimmering edges. It is unstable and will disappear in about 368 days, 19 hours and 49 minutes.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Unstable source rifts</b> were the result of an old bug where a fountain or other large complex object could be created inside of a smaller container, allowing the owner to store a considerable volume inside of a smaller space. The bug that allowed their creation has since been fixed and it is no longer possible to create these containers. As the name suggests, these items were unstable and were phased out of Wurm Online. <b>It is strongly recommended for owners of these containers to relocate their contents before they are removed and their contents emptied into the container they are in or on the ground.</b>\n</p>', 0),
(10978, 2946, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Unstable source rifts still existed inside of their smaller container. These containers disappeared around November 9th, 2016. You could examine your Unstable source rift to see the time remaining until it disappears. When they disappeared, any items inside would either end up in the container they are in at that time or outside on the ground if they didn\'t fit. Rifts were made from magic and not from stone, so they could not be improved.', '<ul><li><b>Unstable source rifts</b> still existed inside of their smaller container.</li>\n<li>These containers disappeared around November 9th, 2016.</li>\n<li>You could examine your <b>Unstable source rift</b> to see the time remaining until it disappears.</li>\n<li>When they disappeared, any items inside would either end up in the container they are in at that time or outside on the ground if they didn\'t fit.</li>\n<li>Rifts were made from magic and not from stone, so they could not be improved.</li></ul>', 1),
(10979, 2881, 'Description', 'Description', 'A nice and cosy campfire. A campfire can be used to heat items like food and ore .', '<p><i>A nice and cosy campfire.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>campfire</b> can be used to heat items like <a href=\"/index.php/Food\" title=\"Food\">food</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">ore</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(10980, 2881, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'The quality of the kindling is the maximum quality of the campfire. Examine the campfire to see its quality. The higher the quality, the faster it will heat up anything put in it. The quality of the campfire will also be the quality of the ash it leaves behind. If you do not have a steel and flint , you can use a kindling on a wood scrap to create a crude campfire, with lower quality. You can create only one campfire per tile, an additional campfire created on the same tile will just fuel the existing campfire.', '<p>The quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Kindling\" title=\"Kindling\">kindling</a> is the maximum quality of the campfire. Examine the campfire to see its quality. The higher the quality, the faster it will heat up anything put in it. The quality of the campfire will also be the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Ash\" title=\"Ash\">ash</a> it leaves behind.\n</p>\n<p>If you do not have a <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_and_flint\" title=\"Steel and flint\">steel and flint</a>, you can use a kindling on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">wood scrap</a> to create a crude campfire, with lower quality.\n</p>\n<p>You can create only one campfire per tile, an additional campfire created on the same tile will just fuel the existing campfire.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(10981, 2881, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To extend the life of a fire, you need to add fuel to it. Activate a fuel item, for example a log or wood scrap , right-click the campfire, and select Burn . Alternatively, the fuel can also be left inside the campfire till the fuel decays from fire damage. The campfire caps out at 20 kg worth of fuel, so adding any more than that is a waste. You can examine a campfire to get an event message telling how long it will burn. If it says that it The fire burns steadily and will still burn for a long time , then it means that you have more than 10 real life minutes worth of fuel in it. If it says anything else, you\'d be wise to add more. Once all fuel has been used up, the campfire will turn into 0.10 kg of ash and all items inside are dropped on the tile the campfire was on. Snuffing A lit campfire can be snuffed: Right-click the campfire with the steel and flint activated (or alternatively, nothing activated), and select Snuff . The result is an unlit campfire which does not disappear for a long time even if empty. If you snuff a rare (or supreme) campfire, it will keep its special status (even after relighting later). Re-lighting An unlit campfire can be lit again: Put a kindling in your inventory, activate your steel and flint, right-click the campfire, and select Light . Creating a new campfire on a tile with an unlit campfire will light the existing one. The campfire will appear glowing but does not show any fire animation or smoke, in order to reduce the strain on your graphics card.', '<p>To extend the life of a fire, you need to add <a href=\"/index.php/Fuel\" title=\"Fuel\">fuel</a> to it. Activate a fuel item, for example a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">wood scrap</a>, right-click the campfire, and select <i>Burn</i>. Alternatively, the fuel can also be left inside the campfire till the fuel decays from fire damage.\n</p>\n<p>The campfire caps out at 20 kg worth of fuel, so adding any more than that is a waste.\n</p>\n<p>You can examine a campfire to get an event message telling how long it will burn. If it says that it <i>The fire burns steadily and will still burn for a long time</i>, then it means that you have more than 10 real life minutes worth of fuel in it. If it says anything else, you\'d be wise to add more.\n</p>\n<p>Once all fuel has been used up, the campfire will turn into 0.10 kg of ash and all items inside are dropped on the tile the campfire was on.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Snuffing\">Snuffing</span></h3>\n<p>A lit campfire can be snuffed: Right-click the campfire with the steel and flint activated (or alternatively, nothing activated), and select <i>Snuff</i>. The result is an unlit campfire which does not disappear for a long time even if empty.\n</p>\n<p>If you snuff a <a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">rare</a> (or supreme) campfire, it will keep its special status (even after relighting later).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Re-lighting\">Re-lighting</span></h3>\n<p>An unlit campfire can be lit again: Put a kindling in your inventory, activate your steel and flint, right-click the campfire, and select <i>Light</i>.\n</p>\n<p>Creating a new campfire on a tile with an unlit campfire will light the existing one. The campfire will appear glowing but does not show any fire animation or smoke, in order to reduce the strain on your graphics card.\n</p>', 2),
(10982, 2881, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A campfire may hold up to 18 ore. The quality of ore smelted in a campfire will be reduced by 20%. A 50QL ore will only yield a 40QL lump. A campfire adds 5 difficulty to cooking items compared to an oven , but 5 less than a forge . Creating a campfire will damage your steel and flint a bit, unlike when lighting up an oven or a forge. The quality of the material you fuel the fire with does not impact on the heating speed or lifespan of the fire, only the weight matters. It is said that a birchwood campfire burns the longest, however. Keep your fire in a \"..will burn for a long time\" state, because it will lose heating power when fuel begins to run low. At its final stages, it may very well be so weak that items inside will cool faster than they heat. Campfires may not be started within a structure. If you are after ash you need to create campfires on separate tiles and let them burn out.', '<ul><li>A campfire may hold up to 18 ore.</li>\n<li>The quality of ore smelted in a campfire will be reduced by 20%. A 50QL ore will only yield a 40QL lump.</li>\n<li>A campfire adds 5 difficulty to <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> items compared to an <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>, but 5 less than a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>.</li>\n<li>Creating a campfire will damage your steel and flint a bit, unlike when lighting up an oven or a forge.</li>\n<li>The quality of the material you fuel the fire with does not impact on the heating speed or lifespan of the fire, only the weight matters. It is said that a birchwood campfire burns the longest, however.</li>\n<li>Keep your fire in a \"..will burn for a long time\" state, because it will lose heating power when fuel begins to run low. At its final stages, it may very well be so weak that items inside will cool faster than they heat.</li>\n<li>Campfires may not be started within a structure.</li>\n<li>If you are after <a href=\"/index.php/Ash\" title=\"Ash\">ash</a> you need to create campfires on separate tiles and let them burn out.</li></ul>', 3),
(10983, 2881, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Container', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">Container</a></li></ul>', 4),
(10997, 2953, 'Description', 'Description', 'Kingdom Judges serve to choose a member of a Template Kingdom as the new leader of that kingdom. There are three Judges one for each kingdom. Lady of the lake - Jenn-Kellon equivalent Stone of the sword - Mol-Rehan equivalent Cobra king - Horde of the Summoned equivalent', '<p>Kingdom Judges serve to choose a member of a Template Kingdom as the new leader of that kingdom. There are three Judges one for each kingdom.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lady_of_the_lake\" title=\"Lady of the lake\">Lady of the lake</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> equivalent</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_of_the_sword\" title=\"Stone of the sword\">Stone of the sword</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a> equivalent</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cobra_king\" title=\"Cobra king\">Cobra king</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a> equivalent</li></ul>', 0),
(10999, 2954, 'Description', 'Description', 'A Template kingdom is one of the three original kingdoms in the game. All Player made kingdoms or PMK\' s must choose one of the three Template kingdoms to base their kingdom on. The kingdoms include: Jenn-Kellon Mol-Rehan Horde of the Summoned', '<p>A <b>Template kingdom</b> is one of the three original kingdoms in the game. All <a href=\"/index.php/Player_made_kingdom\" title=\"Player made kingdom\">Player made kingdoms</a> or <b>PMK\'</b>s must choose one of the three <b>Template kingdoms</b> to base their kingdom on.\n</p>\n<p>The kingdoms include:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a></li></ul>', 0),
(11013, 2956, 'Description', 'Description', 'A Royal crown serves as the helmet for the leader of either a Template kingdom or a Player made kingdom . The crown is equivalent of wearing a Great helm in protection of head and face and can be used by the player as a symbol of authority. If the leader is in a player made kingdom they can transfer the crown to another kingdom member to make that new person the chief of the kingdom.', '<p>A <b>Royal crown</b> serves as the helmet for the leader of either a <a href=\"/index.php/Template_kingdom\" title=\"Template kingdom\">Template kingdom</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Player_made_kingdom\" title=\"Player made kingdom\">Player made kingdom</a>. The crown is equivalent of wearing a <a href=\"/index.php/Great_helm\" title=\"Great helm\">Great helm</a> in protection of head and face and can be used by the player as a symbol of authority. If the leader is in a player made kingdom they can transfer the crown to another kingdom member to make that new person the chief of the kingdom.\n</p>', 0),
(11014, 2956, 'Obtaining', 'Obtaining', 'A Royal crown can be obtained two ways: 1. From being the founding member of a Player made kingdom 2. From the Kingdom judge, which would be either of the following: Jenn-Kellon - The Lady of the Lake Mol Rehan - Sword of the Stone Horde of the Summoned - Cobra King', '<p>A <b>Royal crown</b> can be obtained two ways:\n</p>\n<ul><li>1. From being the founding member of a Player made kingdom</li>\n<li>2. From the Kingdom judge, which would be either of the following:\n<ul><li>Jenn-Kellon - The Lady of the Lake</li>\n<li>Mol Rehan - Sword of the Stone</li>\n<li>Horde of the Summoned - Cobra King</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11015, 2956, 'Crowns', 'Crowns', 'Put crown image here Jenn-Kellon Crown Put crown image here Mol-Rehan Crown Put crown image here Horde of the Summoned Crown', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 185px\"><div style=\"width: 185px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height: 180px;\">Put crown image here</div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> Crown\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 185px\"><div style=\"width: 185px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height: 180px;\">Put crown image here</div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a> Crown\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 185px\"><div style=\"width: 185px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height: 180px;\">Put crown image here</div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a> Crown\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(11016, 1452, 'Description', 'Description', 'A crystal vial containing the vicious fumes of Sol that twisted the demons and fuels their madness.', '<p><i>A crystal vial containing the vicious fumes of Sol that twisted the demons and fuels their madness.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11017, 1452, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Karma Disease (650 karma cost to inflict a 19 damage \"infected\" wound) Resistance: Physical 10% (Decreases physical damage taken by 10%) Weakness: Poison 10% (Increases poison damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Karma Disease (650 karma cost to inflict a 19 damage \"infected\" wound)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Physical 10% (Decreases physical damage taken by 10%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Poison 10% (Increases poison damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(11018, 1452, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight. Can be used at any altar in 3x3 flat area, within a cave. Note: A normal metal bowl can be used in place of an altar to consume charges from sorcery tomes. The bowl has to be set on the ground, then activate the sorcery item to use on itself.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in 3x3 flat area, within a cave.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: A normal metal bowl can be used in place of an altar to consume charges from sorcery tomes. The bowl has to be set on the ground, then activate the sorcery item to use on itself.</li></ul>', 2),
(11019, 2960, 'Description', 'Description', 'Cloth rags.', '<p><i>Cloth rags.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11020, 2960, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Rags can be used as bandage. 1 rags will bandage a light wound.  Combine 2 rags to bandage a medium wound. Rags can also be used to spin more strings of cloth with a spindle.  Just as with spinning cotton, you need 0.20kg of rags to make 1 string of cloth and 0.10kg of rags.', '<p>Rags can be used as bandage. 1 rags will bandage a light wound.  Combine 2 rags to bandage a medium wound.\n</p>\n<p>Rags can also be used to spin more strings of cloth with a spindle.  Just as with spinning cotton, you need 0.20kg of rags to make 1 string of cloth and 0.10kg of rags.\n</p>', 1),
(11021, 2960, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Maximum weight of combining rags will not exceed 12.80 kg. Rags decay quickly. Rags can not be crafted but may be the result of failing at creating certain items.', '<ul><li>Maximum weight of combining rags will not exceed 12.80 kg.</li>\n<li>Rags decay quickly.</li>\n<li>Rags can not be crafted but may be the result of failing at creating certain items.</li></ul>', 2),
(11022, 2960, 'See also', 'See_also', 'First aid', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/First_aid\" title=\"First aid\">First aid</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11026, 2961, 'Description', 'Description', 'An alloy of gold and silver.', '<p><i>An alloy of gold and silver.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11027, 2961, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When creating, the QL of the gold affects your success chance. Any enchantments should be cast upon the gold lump. The quality of the silver is the maximum quality of the resulting lump. If you fail creating, you lose 0.01kg from both lumps. The gold and/or silver can be combined into one lump, as only the amount required is used. Even when both are combined, only one 0.10kg electrum lump is produced, however. Despite using 0.10kg of each lump to create the alloy, attempting to use exactly 0.10 results in an error because it\'s too little material: more than 0.10kg is needed to start the creation. This alloy has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>When creating, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">gold</a> affects your success chance.</li>\n<li>Any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Enchantments\" title=\"Enchantments\">enchantments</a> should be cast upon the gold lump.</li>\n<li>The quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">silver</a> is the maximum quality of the resulting lump.</li>\n<li>If you fail creating, you lose 0.01kg from both lumps.</li>\n<li>The gold and/or silver can be combined into one lump, as only the amount required is used. Even when both are combined, only one 0.10kg electrum lump is produced, however.</li>\n<li>Despite using 0.10kg of each lump to create the alloy, attempting to use exactly 0.10 results in an error because it\'s too little material: more than 0.10kg is needed to start the creation.</li>\n<li>This alloy has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11028, 2961, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See metal products list for items that can be made from electrum.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for items that can be made from electrum.</li></ul>', 2),
(11033, 1040, 'Description', 'Description', 'Some reed plants. It has very strong fibres.', '<p><i>Some reed plants. It has very strong fibres.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11034, 1040, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Reed plants can be gathered from natural reed tiles , which uses gardening skill. They can be gathered using shovel , sickle or scythe . Reed plants can also be harvested from a reed field , which uses farming skill. No tool is required to harvest. Reed plants can be foraged from Seaweed Resource nodes , and botanized from Swampy puddles , Wild grasses and Dune grasses . Reed plants are crushed to produce reed fibre , which then can be used to create papyrus sheets with a press . Crushing 0.5kg of reed plants will produce 0.1kg reed fibre. Reed plants are used to create reed pens . Reed plants are used to create thatch for a Thatched roof and/or to plant grass . Reed Plants are used as an ingredient to make Healing covers .', '<ul><li><b>Reed plants</b> can be gathered from natural reed <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>, which uses <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">gardening</a> skill. They can be gathered using <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythe</a>. <b>Reed plants</b> can also be harvested from a reed <a href=\"/index.php/Field\" title=\"Field\">field</a>, which uses <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a> skill. No tool is required to harvest.</li>\n<li><b>Reed plants</b> can be foraged from <a href=\"/index.php/Seaweed\" title=\"Seaweed\">Seaweed</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>, and botanized from <a href=\"/index.php/Swampy_puddle\" title=\"Swampy puddle\">Swampy puddles</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_grasses\" title=\"Wild grasses\">Wild grasses</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Dune_grass\" title=\"Dune grass\">Dune grasses</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Reed plants</b> are <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">crushed</a> to produce <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_fibre\" title=\"Reed fibre\">reed fibre</a>, which then can be used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Papyrus_sheet\" title=\"Papyrus sheet\">papyrus sheets</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Press\" title=\"Press\">press</a>. Crushing 0.5kg of reed plants will produce 0.1kg reed fibre.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Reed plants</b> are used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_pen\" title=\"Reed pen\">reed pens</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Reed plants</b> are used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Thatch\" title=\"Thatch\">thatch</a> for a <a href=\"/index.php/Thatched_roof\" title=\"Thatched roof\">Thatched roof</a> and/or to plant <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Reed Plants</b> are used as an ingredient to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">Healing covers</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11035, 1040, 'Method', 'Method', 'Reed tiles Reed plants can be gathered from medium, long and wild natural reed tiles . \nNote that medium reed produces 1 plant, tall produces 2 plants and wild produces 3 plants. The quality of the harvest is random. Tools aside from the sickle and scythe , however, do limit harvest quality to 20. The length of the reed can be examined : You see a patch of reed. The reed is short and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is medium and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is tall and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is wild and seem to like it here. Reed tiles can be harvested with a Sickle Shovel Scythe maybe more (needs testing) Reed fields Reed can be planted using reed seeds , which are picked from reed plants . Picking seeds will destroy the plant. No tool is required to harvest reed fields. The amount and quality of the harvest depends on the farming skill. Unlike other farm fields, reeds need to be sown underwater. Ideal depth is 3 dirts higher than maximum shovel depth. Pile of reed plants', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Reed_tiles\">Reed tiles</span></h3>\n<p><b>Reed plants</b> can be gathered from medium, long and wild natural <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_tile\" title=\"Reed tile\">reed tiles</a>. \nNote that medium reed produces 1 plant, tall produces 2 plants and wild produces 3 plants. The quality of the harvest is random. Tools aside from the <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythe</a>, however, do limit harvest quality to 20.\n</p>\n<p>The length of the reed can be <a href=\"/index.php/Examine\" title=\"Examine\">examined</a>:\n</p>\n<pre>You see a patch of reed. The reed is short and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is medium and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is tall and seem to like it here.\nYou see a patch of reed. The reed is wild and seem to like it here.\n</pre>\n<p>Reed tiles can be harvested with a\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">Shovel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a></li>\n<li>maybe more (needs testing)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Reed_fields\">Reed fields</span></h3>\n<p>Reed can be planted using <a href=\"/index.php/Reed_seeds\" title=\"Reed seeds\">reed seeds</a>, which are picked from <b>reed plants</b>. Picking seeds will destroy the plant. No tool is required to harvest reed fields. The amount and quality of the harvest depends on the <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a> skill. Unlike other farm fields, reeds need to be sown underwater. Ideal depth is 3 dirts higher than maximum shovel depth.\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:235px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_reed_plants.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"225\" data-file-width=\"233\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/f/fb/Pile_of_reed_plants.png\" width=\"233\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_reed_plants.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Pile of reed plants</div></div></div>', 2),
(11039, 1409, 'Description', 'Description', 'Some rice. Rice requires a lot of water to grow.', '<p><i>Some rice. Rice requires a lot of water to grow.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11040, 1409, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Can be used in many cooking recipes. Can be used with beverages skill to create rice wine.', '<ul><li>Can be used in many <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be used with <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a> skill to create rice wine.</li></ul>', 1),
(11041, 1409, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be found by botanizing from Swampy puddle , Wild grasses Resource nodes and Dune grass Resource nodes . Can be found by foraging from Seaweed Resource nodes . Rice requires a water depth of at least 1 and a maximum of 4. The \"Drink\" option in the context menu will first appear when at least one corner of a tile is one dirt below water. Another way to measure depth is with a shovel\'s maximum dig depth. Three dirts up from maximum shovel dig depth is the maximum planting depth (4 dirts below water) and six dirts up is the minimum planting depth (1 dirt below water). Sowing is possible if at least one corner is within the acceptable zone and the standard farming sloped tile restriction apply. A Rice field can be tended, harvested, and sown like other farm crops. Pile of rice Picture of rice field growing.', '<ul><li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Swampy_puddle\" title=\"Swampy puddle\">Swampy puddle</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_grasses\" title=\"Wild grasses\">Wild grasses</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Dune_grass\" title=\"Dune grass\">Dune grass</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Seaweed\" title=\"Seaweed\">Seaweed</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Rice requires a water depth of at least 1 and a maximum of 4. The \"Drink\" option in the <a href=\"/index.php/Context_menu\" title=\"Context menu\">context menu</a> will first appear when at least one corner of a tile is one dirt below water. Another way to measure depth is with a shovel\'s maximum dig depth. Three dirts up from maximum shovel dig depth is the maximum planting depth (4 dirts below water) and six dirts up is the minimum planting depth (1 dirt below water).</li>\n<li>Sowing is possible if at least one corner is within the acceptable zone and the standard <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a> sloped tile restriction apply.</li>\n<li>A Rice field can be tended, harvested, and sown like other <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farm</a> crops.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:252px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_rice.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"386\" data-file-width=\"361\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"267\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/66/Pile_of_rice.png/250px-Pile_of_rice.png\" srcset=\"/images/6/66/Pile_of_rice.png 1.5x\" width=\"250\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_rice.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Pile of rice</div></div></div>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rice-harvest.png\"><img alt=\"Rice-harvest.png\" data-file-height=\"591\" data-file-width=\"970\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"122\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/a4/Rice-harvest.png/200px-Rice-harvest.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/a4/Rice-harvest.png/300px-Rice-harvest.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/a4/Rice-harvest.png/400px-Rice-harvest.png 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\nPicture of rice field growing.\n</p>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(11045, 1056, 'List of known Achievements', 'List_of_known_Achievements', 'Achievements Achievement Description Rarity How to Unlock Abstinence You wouldn\'t mind something to eat. Really really really. Silver Fasting . Adamantine Item You created an adamantine item. Silver Create an item out of adamantine Adulterator You like wine Silver Make 100 liters of wine Almost impossible You\'ve manufactured something really special Diamond Create a fantastic item. Almost as good as an Axe There\'s always a way to bring down a tree. Silver Cut down a mature or older tree with something other than an axe. Ambitious You\'re not fooling around. You\'re doing things! Gold 100,000 actions performed (in total, not one play session). Angry Sailor Beware the Angry Sailor and his Belaying Pin Silver (?) Animal Care How nice of you to feed your pet Silver Feed any animal. Arachnophile You hate spiders Silver Kill lots of spiders (exact number unknown). Ascetic You are dying from famine Silver Food bar below 7% (no more fasting). Ashes to Ashes Most people avoid lava for good reasons Silver Die on a lava tile. Backstabber What\'s with everyone turning towards you all the time? Silver Defeat an opponent in combat while they face away from you (requires conformation). Baker You should wear a white cap silver Bake 100 bread. \"boat type\" Sailor Look, it floats! Silver Embark different types of boats as commander. \"boat type\" Maker You finished the \"boat type\" Silver Complete construction of different types of boats. Becalmer You\'ve killed an angry creature. Silver Kill a angry creature. Be Gentle Please You won a spar, hooray! Silver Win a spar. Bodhisattva Meditating cleans the mind and elevates your soul. Gold Meditate 2000 times. Brass Item You created a brass item Silver Craft an item from brass Bread Maker You can bake! Silver Bake bread Brilliant! You\'ve mined a brilliant gem Gold Mine a 90QL gem. Brilliant! You\'ve dug up a brilliant gem Gold Dig a 90QL gem. Bronze Item You created a bronze item. Silver Create an item from bronze Brother In Spars You\'re quite popular to spar against. Silver Participate in (?) spars. Bugged Rarity You were the victim of a weird achievement bug but survived Silver Any improving before Rarity achievement was fixed. Bumble Bee Are you in it for the honey, Honey? Gold Plant 500 flowers Burglar They can\'t keep you out! Silver Pick 5 locks . Cap\'n Aye aye, Cap\'n Silver Embark all the different types of boats as commander. Careful Identifier Care and attention to detail let you identify ancient items. Silver Completely clean and identify 50 fragments. Chief Mate Yarr Matey Silver Embark a boat x times Citizen Congratulations! You\'ve joined your first settlement! Silver Become a citizen of a settlement Cleanup Operation You are recycling things. Good. Silver Let 100 items \'decay\' in a trash heap Cleptomaniac Just... one... more... Silver Pick 50 locks . Clumsy Try to be more gentle when climbing Silver Fall down 125 times and take some damage. Concrete Shoes You\'ve discovered that swimming requires training Silver Death by drowning Cowboy Bovine is your thing. Silver Lead 3 bulls while riding a horse. Cyclops Ouch! The eye! Silver Take a hit to the face? Dead end Sometimes it\'s hard to survive while driving Silver Killed while on a cart. Death from above Oops!! That must have hurt! Silver Hit by flying debris (i.e. from a catapult) Debt Collector That\'s your money! Silver Drain a deed Decay Removal Services You could do this for a living. Unless you already are. Gold Repair 1250 fences, floors or walls. Deep Pockets You can\'t possibly carry more Silver Be encumbered and try to pick up something Defiler You have destroyed the holy altar Diamond Destroy the whitelight Deforestation There is something with you and trees Silver Cut down 1000 trees Die by the Rift You died in the Rift Area Silver Die inside the rift area. Dough Hands Ignorance and error are necessary to life, like bread and water. Gold Bake 500 bread(?) Drunken Sailor What shall we do with you? Silver Pilot a boat while drunk Environment Improval Engineer You take pride in repairing structures Silver Repair 250 fences, floors, or walls. Enviromental Hero You\'re a hero! You keep the world alive! Diamond Put 10000 items into a trash bin. Epic helper You did your part in helping the gods advance on their journey on Valrei. Silver Contribute towards a mission. Epic Finalizer You managed to finish that mission. Good job! Silver Complete a mission. Exceptional craftsmen You can do really fine things Silver Improve an item from under 50.00ql to above 50.00ql Experienced You have been premium for 9 months. Silver Have a total of 9 months of premium. Fire Extinguisher You\'re the nemesis of Lava creatures Gold Kill a certain (unknown) number of lava spiders. Flirtatious Your smiles can melt ice Silver flirt with 10 players. (Must be unique accounts) Fo\'s Favorite You start to become popular with the gods of nature Silver Plant 1000 trees. Foundation Pillar You\'ve been premium for 36 months Diamond Be premium for 36 months. Fragmental The ancients apparently used these tools too, who knew? Silver Recreate a tool from fragments Founder There\'s nothing like home Silver Found a deed Free Hugs You\'re the cuddly type Silver Use emote smile on another player Giant Fish You caught the rare one Gold Catch a very heavy and high-quality shark Ghost Others only notice a slight movement of the air but choose to look the other way Silver Successfully stealth 200 times Ghost of the Rift Warmasters You\'re scaring the Rift Warmasters Gold Unknown Glittered You\'ve been premium for 20 months Gold Be premium for 20 months Gold Digger Found the Gold. Now - what to do with it? Silver Mine gold. Gollum It came to me, my own, my love... my... preciousss. Silver Stealthing in a cave (with an equipped ring?) Gravedigger You put the dead to rest. Silver Bury a corpse. Good Work You excel in improving things Silver Succeed impr