<td>Tears of the Unicorn</td>\n<td>You are a slayer of beauty</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill 100 <a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">unicorns</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>To hell with it</td>\n<td>You\'ve killed the Hell Hound</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_hound\" title=\"Hell hound\">hell hound</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traitor</td>\n<td>And that poor guard was just doing his duty</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Guard\" title=\"Guard\">guard</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Troll King Assassination</td>\n<td>You\'ve killed the Troll King</td>\n<td>Gold</td>\n<td>Be engaged in combat with the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Troll_King\" title=\"Troll King\">Troll King</a> when it dies\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trolls killed</td>\n<td>You\'ve killed the fearsome Troll</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">troll</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unicorns Killed</td>\n<td>You\'ve slain the Unicorn</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">unicorn</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uttacha Spawn Slayer</td>\n<td>You\'ve killed the Uttacha Spawn</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Spawn_of_Uttacha\" title=\"Spawn of Uttacha\">Spawn of Uttacha</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Willbreaker</td>\n<td>You\'ve killed a hardened creature</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_conditions\" title=\"Animal conditions\">hardened</a> creature.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wolves killed</td>\n<td>You\'re a wolf slayer</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Black_wolf\" title=\"Black wolf\">wolf</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>You Cannot Pass</td>\n<td>You have defeated many Lava Fiends</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill 20 lava fiends.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Zombies killed</td>\n<td>Zombie! Zombie!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Kill a <a href=\"/index.php/Zombie\" title=\"Zombie\">zombie</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Zombie Hunter</td>\n<td>Apparently It\'s you or zombies</td>\n<td>Gold</td>\n<td>kill 50 <a href=\"/index.php/Zombie\" title=\"Zombie\">zombies</a>.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Event_Achievements\">Event Achievements</span></h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Achievement\n</th>\n<th>Description\n</th>\n<th>Rarity\n</th>\n<th>How to Unlock\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Independence Tourist</td>\n<td>You\'ve toured the sights of Independence!</td>\n<td>Iron</td>\n<td>Complete the Independence Sightseeing Race.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gopher for the Gods</td>\n<td>You finished the May 2016 Scavenger hunt... Either that or you\'re a rodent of some sort. One of the two anyhow</td>\n<td>Iron</td>\n<td>Complete the Independence May 2016 Treasure Hunt.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Geographer of the Isles</td>\n<td>You have successfully pieced together the locations to a treasure map</td>\n<td>Iron</td>\n<td>Complete the Pristine April 2016 event.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I survived the Labyrinth.</td>\n<td>Granted for completing the 2015 Labyrinth on Xanadu</td>\n<td>Iron</td>\n<td>Complete the famous Xanadu Labyrinth.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cooking_Achievements\">Cooking Achievements</span></h3>\n<p>(Hidden so it\'s not ruined for anyone)\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Achievement\n</th>\n<th>Description\n</th>\n<th>Rarity\n</th>\n<th>How to Unlock\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Beer</td>\n<td>Homebrew!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Brewing some beer.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Berry Pie</td>\n<td>Berry nice!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a berry pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Black Forest Gateau</td>\n<td>I want to get lost in this forest!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a Black Forest Gateau.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brewer</td>\n<td>Brewed one of each.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Ferment one of each brew\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chocoholic</td>\n<td>um, chocolate!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a chocolate cake\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cookies</td>\n<td>You say cookie, I say biscuit, lets om-nom-nom</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> cookies.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cottage Pie</td>\n<td>Just like my grandmother used to make!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a cottage pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Custard Creams</td>\n<td>When only the cream de la cream will do!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> some custard creams.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Custard Pie</td>\n<td>Phanton flam flinger</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a custard pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Distiller</td>\n<td>Distilled one of each!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Distill one of each alcohol\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fish pie</td>\n<td>You made that, sounds a bit fishy to me!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a> a fish pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fruit Pie</td>\n<td>Berry nice!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a berry pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gin</td>\n<td>As drunk on fine floating palaces everywhere.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Distilling gin.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gruel</td>\n<td>Please sir, can I have some more?</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a> gruel.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Insect Stew</td>\n<td>You begin to feel the speed of 6 legs come upon you.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a> an insect stew.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Meat pie</td>\n<td>Meat and gravy all in a pie!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a meat pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Moonshine</td>\n<td>Yeee-haw!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Distill some Moonshine.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pasta Maker</td>\n<td>Life is a combination of magic and pasta</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Unknown\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pie-Maker</td>\n<td>When you die, if you get a choice between going to regular heaven and pie heaven, choose pie heaven. It might be a trick, but if it\'s not, mmmmmm, boy.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Make one of each: Cottage, fish, raspberry, fruit, berry, custard, steak and ale, pork and meat.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pizza Maker</td>\n<td>Making the world a better place, one tomato-laden delight at a time.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Unknown\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pork pie</td>\n<td>Come here, piggy!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a Pork pie.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Raspberry Pi</td>\n<td>The code for this was intense!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a Raspberry Pi.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Simple pasta</td>\n<td>I make a pasta!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a> a Simple pasta.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Steak and ale pie</td>\n<td>um, beer!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">Baking</a> a Steak and ale pie\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sushi Maker</td>\n<td>Teach a man to fish, but not cook, and he\'ll make sushi.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Make some sushi.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vinegar</td>\n<td>Oops, that was not expected, maybe I can use it for cooking!</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Make some Vinegar.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vodka</td>\n<td>At least one letter away from water.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Distill some vodka.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Whisky</td>\n<td>Always carry a small flask of whiskey in case of snake bite.  Also, always carry a small snake.</td>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>Distill some Whisky.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(11046, 1056, 'Goals', 'Goals', 'Goals were added with the Steam client.The Goals tab in the main menu shows these in game or they can be viewed in Steam. Achievement How to unlock Wurmian Finish the tutorial Trollslayer Slay a troll Dragonslayer Help with slaying a Dragon Can you dig it? Create a tunnel in a rock face Architect Plan a structure Builder Complete a house Town Planner Complete 10 houses For the greater good Slay any creature Ecological disaster underway Slay 100 creatures Surface scratched Raise a skill to 20 Going strong Raise a skill to 50 Really getting stuck in Raise a skill to 70 Halfway There Raise a skill to 90 Wildlife? I\'ve seen some... Raise Fighting skill to 70 Bug squisher Slay a huge spider A really slow chase Slay a slow creature You\'re not so green Slay a greenish creature Champion amongst creatures Slay a champion creature Incoming! Slay a creature using a catapult Man\'s best friend Tame a creature Blackest heart in the land Slay a unicorn Bringing home the bacon Slay a pig They don\'t like it up \'em! Taunt a creature in combat Brave knight Ride a horse Faux knight Ride a cow Really brave knight Ride a brown bear Ploughing the ocean waves Pilot a boat. Or a ship! Building communities Join a village Don\'t make me turn this wagon around! Win a spar against another player I\'m not as think as you drunk I am! Get really drunk Forestry department? We don\'t need no stinking forestry department! Cut down 100 trees Undertaker Bury 100 corpses Forestry department recruit Plant 100 trees ...is my hand supposed to glow as well? Equip an enchanted weapon Celestial trash compactor Sacrifice 50 items Burrowing varmint! Destroy a cave wall Charlie Mops Brew some beer Hangover is now in pre-production Make some wine Heard a higher calling Become a follower of a deity Are you sure that\'s what animal husbandry means? Breed a creature Much bigger pockets Create a small cart Portable handbag Create a large cart Rower with boat, seeks stream for merriness Create a rowing boat All the colours of the rainbow Dye any item If looks could kill Dye a piece of armor Red goes faster Paint a vehicle Siesta Sleep in a bed Waiting game Plant a crop Quick, trouble the waters! Plan a bridge It takes a village Participate in a mission Now we\'re cooking with tar! Learn 250 cooking recipes Born to rune! Use a rune Every day, in every way... Improve items 1000 times Dude, sweeeeeeet! Collect some honey Eating for at least a day Catch a fish Absolutely divine! Find an underground source of water using a pendulum Pucker up! Kiss someone Bee whisperer Open a beehive Goblin slayer Make a skull cup Puppeteer Hold a puppet show Yo ho ho and a bottle of whatever this is Make some rum World famous author Write a book Beary good! Create a bear rug When life gives you lemons... Make some lemonade No archeologists inside Create a larder Lounge Lizard Create a royal lounge chaise Forest dweller Pick a mushroom Ratalicious! Cook a rat-on-a-stick Treasures of the sea Find a pearl Jaws Slay a shark I scream, you scream Make some ice cream It will only hurt for a little while... Brand an animal Early bird catches the wurm Search for a wurm Snowball fight! Throw a snowball Some Unique Blood Get the blood of a unique creature Rift Master Participate in a rift Ting-A-Ling Ring a Bell', '<p>Goals were added with the Steam client.The Goals tab in the <a href=\"/index.php/Interface_and_controls#Main_Menu\" title=\"Interface and controls\">main menu</a> shows these in game or they can be viewed in Steam.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Achievement\n</th>\n<th>How to unlock\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wurmian</td>\n<td>Finish the tutorial\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trollslayer</td>\n<td>Slay a troll\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dragonslayer</td>\n<td>Help with slaying a Dragon\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Can you dig it?</td>\n<td>Create a tunnel in a rock face\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Architect</td>\n<td>Plan a structure\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Builder</td>\n<td>Complete a house\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Town Planner</td>\n<td>Complete 10 houses\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>For the greater good</td>\n<td>Slay any creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ecological disaster underway</td>\n<td>Slay 100 creatures\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Surface scratched</td>\n<td>Raise a skill to 20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Going strong</td>\n<td>Raise a skill to 50\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Really getting stuck in</td>\n<td>Raise a skill to 70\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Halfway There</td>\n<td>Raise a skill to 90\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wildlife? I\'ve seen some...</td>\n<td>Raise Fighting skill to 70\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bug squisher</td>\n<td>Slay a huge spider\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A really slow chase</td>\n<td>Slay a slow creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>You\'re not so green</td>\n<td>Slay a greenish creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Champion amongst creatures</td>\n<td>Slay a champion creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Incoming!</td>\n<td>Slay a creature using a catapult\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Man\'s best friend</td>\n<td>Tame a creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Blackest heart in the land</td>\n<td>Slay a unicorn\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bringing home the bacon</td>\n<td>Slay a pig\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>They don\'t like it up \'em!</td>\n<td>Taunt a creature in combat\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brave knight</td>\n<td>Ride a horse\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Faux knight</td>\n<td>Ride a cow\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Really brave knight</td>\n<td>Ride a brown bear\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ploughing the ocean waves</td>\n<td>Pilot a boat. Or a ship!\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Building communities</td>\n<td>Join a village\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Don\'t make me turn this wagon around!</td>\n<td>Win a spar against another player\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I\'m not as think as you drunk I am!</td>\n<td>Get really drunk\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Forestry department? We don\'t need no stinking forestry department!</td>\n<td>Cut down 100 trees\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Undertaker</td>\n<td>Bury 100 corpses\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Forestry department recruit</td>\n<td>Plant 100 trees\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>...is my hand supposed to glow as well?</td>\n<td>Equip an enchanted weapon\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Celestial trash compactor</td>\n<td>Sacrifice 50 items\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Burrowing varmint!</td>\n<td>Destroy a cave wall\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Charlie Mops</td>\n<td>Brew some beer\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hangover is now in pre-production</td>\n<td>Make some wine\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Heard a higher calling</td>\n<td>Become a follower of a deity\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Are you sure that\'s what animal husbandry means?</td>\n<td>Breed a creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Much bigger pockets</td>\n<td>Create a small cart\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Portable handbag</td>\n<td>Create a large cart\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rower with boat, seeks stream for merriness</td>\n<td>Create a rowing boat\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>All the colours of the rainbow</td>\n<td>Dye any item\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>If looks could kill</td>\n<td>Dye a piece of armor\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Red goes faster</td>\n<td>Paint a vehicle\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Siesta</td>\n<td>Sleep in a bed\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Waiting game</td>\n<td>Plant a crop\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Quick, trouble the waters!</td>\n<td>Plan a bridge\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>It takes a village</td>\n<td>Participate in a mission\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Now we\'re cooking with tar!</td>\n<td>Learn 250 cooking recipes\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Born to rune!</td>\n<td>Use a rune\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Every day, in every way...</td>\n<td>Improve items 1000 times\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dude, sweeeeeeet!</td>\n<td>Collect some honey\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eating for at least a day</td>\n<td>Catch a fish\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Absolutely divine!</td>\n<td>Find an underground source of water using a pendulum\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pucker up!</td>\n<td>Kiss someone\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bee whisperer</td>\n<td>Open a beehive\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goblin slayer</td>\n<td>Make a skull cup\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Puppeteer</td>\n<td>Hold a puppet show\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Yo ho ho and a bottle of whatever this is</td>\n<td>Make some rum\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>World famous author</td>\n<td>Write a book\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Beary good!</td>\n<td>Create a bear rug\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>When life gives you lemons...</td>\n<td>Make some lemonade\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No archeologists inside</td>\n<td>Create a larder\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lounge Lizard</td>\n<td>Create a royal lounge chaise\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Forest dweller</td>\n<td>Pick a mushroom\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ratalicious!</td>\n<td>Cook a rat-on-a-stick\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Treasures of the sea</td>\n<td>Find a pearl\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Jaws</td>\n<td>Slay a shark\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I scream, you scream</td>\n<td>Make some ice cream\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>It will only hurt for a little while...</td>\n<td>Brand an animal\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Early bird catches the wurm</td>\n<td>Search for a wurm\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Snowball fight!</td>\n<td>Throw a snowball\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Some Unique Blood</td>\n<td>Get the blood of a unique creature\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rift Master</td>\n<td>Participate in a rift\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ting-A-Ling</td>\n<td>Ring a Bell\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(11047, 2970, 'Description', 'Description', 'A horned helmet that inspires respect. It looks dangerous, heavy and robust.', '<p><i>A horned helmet that inspires respect. It looks dangerous, heavy and robust.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11048, 2970, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A horned helmet is armour for your head and face which helps to prevent injuries in combat and falls. It\'s made of steel and gold and was obtained through a treasure hunt on Chaos and as a reward from Challenge servers. It protects the same parts of the body as the open helm and basinet helm .', '<ul><li>A horned helmet is <a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armour</a> for your head and face which helps to prevent <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">injuries</a> in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">combat</a> and falls.</li>\n<li>It\'s made of <a href=\"/index.php/Steel\" title=\"Steel\">steel</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">gold</a> and was obtained through a treasure hunt on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a> and as a reward from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Challenge\" title=\"Challenge\">Challenge</a> servers.</li>\n<li>It protects the same parts of the body as the <a href=\"/index.php/Open_helm\" title=\"Open helm\">open helm</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Basinet_helm\" title=\"Basinet helm\">basinet helm</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11049, 2970, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11050, 2971, 'Description', 'Description', 'Alcoholic beverages such as wine and beer can cause the player to become intoxicated or addicted. Intoxication and addiction have various bonuses and penalties, and some alcoholic beverages are stronger than others.', '<p>Alcoholic <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a> such as <a href=\"/index.php/Wine\" title=\"Wine\">wine</a> and beer can cause the <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> to become intoxicated or addicted.\n</p>\n<p>Intoxication and addiction have various bonuses and penalties, and some alcoholic beverages are stronger than others.\n</p>', 0),
(11051, 2971, 'Intoxication', 'Intoxication', 'A player\'s intoxication is increased by drinking alcoholic beverages, and reduces gradually over time. Alcohol strength Stronger forms of alcohol will contribute more to intoxication. Quality of the beverage increases its strength. Strength ranges from 100% to 150% of the base strength of the alcohol consumed, depending on quality. When drinking any beverage, 0.20 liters are consumed at a time, about once per second. If less than 0.20 liters is drunk at a time, the amount of intoxication is scaled. For example, drinking 0.10 liters will increase intoxication half as much as 0.20 liters. Levels and effects of intoxication Intoxication has numerous effects on the player and their actions, achieved at different levels of intoxication. When drinking alcohol, a message is given indicating the player\'s current level of intoxication, from 0% to 100%. \"You are tipsy.\" : 10% – 20% \"You are getting drunk.\" : 20% – 30% Starting at this level, drinking alcohol also increases alcohol addiction. \"You are drunk.\" : 30% – 60% Starting at some point within this range, the player begins taking 50% reduced damage from attacks. \"You are really really drunk.\" : 60% – 90% \"You can barely walk.\" : 90% – 95% Starting at this level, the player\'s walking speed is drastically reduced. Starting at this level, the player also has a chance to spill food or beverages instead of consuming them. This will destroy the entire item, or spill the entire contents of the beverage container, even a stationary container such as a well or fountain . \"You are setting some kind of record.\" : 95% – 100% \"You made it to the top! You are perfectly drunk!\" : 100% At this level, the Drunkard title is achieved. Some effects increase gradually with intoxication level: Increased item creation difficulty . Increased cooking difficulty . Increased Combat Rating bonus. After a certain threshold, this becomes an increasing Combat Rating penalty instead.', '<p>A player\'s intoxication is increased by drinking alcoholic beverages, and reduces gradually over time.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alcohol_strength\">Alcohol strength</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Stronger forms of alcohol will contribute more to intoxication.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">Quality</a> of the beverage increases its strength.\n<ul><li>Strength ranges from 100% to 150% of the base strength of the alcohol consumed, depending on quality.</li></ul></li>\n<li>When drinking any beverage, 0.20 liters are consumed at a time, about once per second.\n<ul><li>If less than 0.20 liters is drunk at a time, the amount of intoxication is scaled. For example, drinking 0.10 liters will increase intoxication half as much as 0.20 liters.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Levels_and_effects_of_intoxication\">Levels and effects of intoxication</span></h3>\n<p>Intoxication has numerous effects on the player and their actions, achieved at different levels of intoxication.\n</p>\n<p>When drinking alcohol, a message is given indicating the player\'s current level of intoxication, from 0% to 100%.\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>\"You are tipsy.\"</i>: 10% – 20%</li>\n<li><i>\"You are getting drunk.\"</i>: 20% – 30%\n<ul><li>Starting at this level, drinking alcohol also increases alcohol addiction.</li></ul></li>\n<li><i>\"You are drunk.\"</i>: 30% – 60%\n<ul><li>Starting at some point within this range, the player begins taking 50% reduced <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> from attacks.</li></ul></li>\n<li><i>\"You are really really drunk.\"</i>: 60% – 90%</li>\n<li><i>\"You can barely walk.\"</i>: 90% – 95%\n<ul><li>Starting at this level, the player\'s walking <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">speed</a> is drastically reduced.</li>\n<li>Starting at this level, the player also has a chance to spill food or beverages instead of consuming them. This will destroy the entire item, or spill the entire contents of the beverage container, even a stationary container such as a <a href=\"/index.php/Well\" title=\"Well\">well</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Fountain\" title=\"Fountain\">fountain</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li><i>\"You are setting some kind of record.\"</i>: 95% – 100%</li>\n<li><i>\"You made it to the top! You are perfectly drunk!\"</i>: 100%\n<ul><li>At this level, the <b>Drunkard</b> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Title\" title=\"Title\">title</a> is achieved.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\nSome effects increase gradually with intoxication level:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Increased item creation <a href=\"/index.php/Difficulty\" title=\"Difficulty\">difficulty</a>.</li>\n<li>Increased <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Difficulty\" title=\"Difficulty\">difficulty</a>.</li>\n<li>Increased <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">Combat Rating</a> bonus.\n<ul><li>After a certain threshold, this becomes an increasing Combat Rating <i>penalty</i> instead.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(11052, 2971, 'Addiction', 'Addiction', 'A player\'s alcohol addiction level is increased by drinking alcoholic beverages when beyond the \"tipsy\" stage of intoxication. Alcohol addiction level gradually decreases over time, but only when the player\'s intoxication level is 0%. In other words, the addiction level only goes down while the player is completely sober. This means the player may be susceptible to withdrawal. By reaching a high enough addiction level, the Alcoholic title is achieved. Withdrawal When completely sober (0% intoxication) and with a high addiction level, the player has a chance of randomly failing actions with the following message: \"You tremble and shake from withdrawal.\" This has no effect on some actions, and can have severe consequences for others, depending on the action being performed. If this occurs when improving, extremely high amounts of damage may be done to the item being improved.', '<p>A player\'s alcohol addiction level is increased by drinking alcoholic beverages when beyond the \"tipsy\" stage of intoxication.\n</p>\n<p>Alcohol addiction level gradually decreases over time, but only when the player\'s intoxication level is 0%. In other words, the addiction level only goes down while the player is completely sober. This means the player may be susceptible to withdrawal.\n</p>\n<ul><li>By reaching a high enough addiction level, the <b>Alcoholic</b> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Title\" title=\"Title\">title</a> is achieved.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Withdrawal\">Withdrawal</span></h3>\n<p>When completely sober (0% intoxication) and with a high addiction level, the player has a chance of randomly failing actions with the following message: <i>\"You tremble and shake from withdrawal.\"</i> This has no effect on some actions, and can have severe consequences for others, depending on the action being performed.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If this occurs when improving, extremely high amounts of damage may be done to the item being improved.</li></ul>', 2),
(11053, 2971, 'Achievements', 'Achievements', 'Various Achievements can be gained by performing tasks related to alcohol: Commanding a boat while intoxicated. Commanding a cart while intoxicated.', '<p>Various <a href=\"/index.php/Achievements\" title=\"Achievements\">Achievements</a> can be gained by performing tasks related to alcohol:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Commanding a boat while intoxicated.</li>\n<li>Commanding a cart while intoxicated.</li></ul>', 3),
(11054, 2971, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Praying has a small chance of removing any intoxication and addiction from the player, if they already have some level of addiction. Alcoholic beverages can be drunk regardless of thirst level.', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">Praying</a> has a small chance of removing any intoxication and addiction from the player, if they already have some level of addiction.</li>\n<li>Alcoholic beverages can be drunk regardless of <a href=\"/index.php/Thirst\" title=\"Thirst\">thirst</a> level.</li></ul>', 4),
(11068, 2975, 'Description', 'Description', 'Kyara is the capital of the Jenn Kellon Player made kingdom on the Chaos wild server, and was originally founded by Eaglef and Dreammaster on the 6th beta map. It\'s name was made up by Teseng. Kyara is the oldest surviving town in Wurm. This is the 7th version of Kyara. Jenn Kellon is currently at war with the Empire of Mol Rehan, but is not in a state of war against the Horde of the Summoned. Historical screenshots The first Kyara was situated between an ocean and the top of a mountain range. This was before climbing was implemented. The white square to the right of the large fields was the location of the first guard tower build in wurm. It took 1000 bricks, 1000 clays and 500 planks. Gallery The 3rd Kyara.  This was a short-lived map where Kyara settled on a seashore with a rocky headland. Gallery The 4th Kyara, on the last beta map (9th world), had 87 active citizens, and a size 100 deed. The walled area with the tower in the center of the picture was town center. On the upper left of the picture, the buildings with the tiny 1x1 sheds next to the two farms was the recruiting center. Kyara was receiving new recruits daily. Gallery The 5th Kyara was located on the homeserver in Gold-1. It was a size 10 deed and was near the unicorn spawn. At the end of Gold-1, it served mostly as a recruiting center for Kyara V6. Gallery The 6th Kyara was located on the wildserver in Gold-1, and was called Merkamanost. At the end of Gold-1 it had a large dirt wall and a thorn moat surrounding the town, and the only way inside was through a deeded cave system. You can see the early defenses and the start of the dirt wall in this screenshot. No screenshots of the finished Kyara V6 are currently available. Gallery', '<p>Kyara is the capital of the Jenn Kellon <a href=\"/index.php/Player_made_kingdom\" title=\"Player made kingdom\">Player made kingdom</a> on the Chaos wild server, and was originally founded by Eaglef and Dreammaster on the 6th beta map. It\'s name was made up by Teseng. Kyara is the oldest surviving town in Wurm. This is the 7th version of Kyara.\n</p>\n<p>Jenn Kellon is currently at war with the Empire of Mol Rehan, but is not in a state of war against the Horde of the Summoned.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Historical_screenshots\">Historical screenshots</span></h3>\n<table border=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-1.jpg\"><img alt=\"Kyara-1.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"768\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/37/Kyara-1.jpg/300px-Kyara-1.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/37/Kyara-1.jpg/450px-Kyara-1.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/37/Kyara-1.jpg/600px-Kyara-1.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-1.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div></td>\n<td>The first Kyara was situated between an ocean and the top of a mountain range. This was before climbing was implemented. The white square to the right of the large fields was the location of the first guard tower build in wurm. It took 1000 bricks, 1000 clays and 500 planks.\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.kyara.us/adoll/kyara/Kyara_2/images.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gallery</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-3.jpg\"><img alt=\"Kyara-3.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"768\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/da/Kyara-3.jpg/300px-Kyara-3.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/da/Kyara-3.jpg/450px-Kyara-3.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/da/Kyara-3.jpg/600px-Kyara-3.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-3.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div></td>\n<td>The 3rd Kyara.  This was a short-lived map where Kyara settled on a seashore with a rocky headland.\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.kyara.us/adoll/kyara/Kyara_3/images.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gallery</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-4.jpg\"><img alt=\"Kyara-4.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"707\" data-file-width=\"963\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"220\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b1/Kyara-4.jpg/300px-Kyara-4.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b1/Kyara-4.jpg/450px-Kyara-4.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/b1/Kyara-4.jpg/600px-Kyara-4.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-4.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div></td>\n<td>The 4th Kyara, on the last beta map (9th world), had 87 active citizens, and a size 100 deed. The walled area with the tower in the center of the picture was town center. On the upper left of the picture, the buildings with the tiny 1x1 sheds next to the two farms was the recruiting center. Kyara was receiving new recruits daily.\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.kyara.us/adoll/kyara/Kyara_4/images.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gallery</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-5.JPG\"><img alt=\"Kyara-5.JPG\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"768\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/44/Kyara-5.JPG/300px-Kyara-5.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/44/Kyara-5.JPG/450px-Kyara-5.JPG 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/44/Kyara-5.JPG/600px-Kyara-5.JPG 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-5.JPG\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div></td>\n<td>The 5th Kyara was located on the homeserver in Gold-1. It was a size 10 deed and was near the unicorn spawn. At the end of Gold-1, it served mostly as a recruiting center for Kyara V6.\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.kyara.us/adoll/kyara/Kyara_5/images.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gallery</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-6.JPG\"><img alt=\"Kyara-6.JPG\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"990\" data-file-width=\"1272\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"233\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/54/Kyara-6.JPG/300px-Kyara-6.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/54/Kyara-6.JPG/450px-Kyara-6.JPG 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/54/Kyara-6.JPG/600px-Kyara-6.JPG 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Kyara-6.JPG\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div></td>\n<td>The 6th Kyara was located on the wildserver in Gold-1, and was called Merkamanost. At the end of Gold-1 it had a large dirt wall and a thorn moat surrounding the town, and the only way inside was through a deeded cave system. You can see the early defenses and the start of the dirt wall in this screenshot. No screenshots of the finished Kyara V6 are currently available.\n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.kyara.us/adoll/kyara/Merk/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gallery</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 0),
(11069, 2975, 'People', 'People', 'Founders of Kyara Eaglef and Dreammaster Mayor of Kyara Duce Consuls of Kyara Adoll Dreammaster (presently on loan to Wurmonline team) Gavin Madt Manny (presently on loan to Wurmonline team) Miggy Nosyt Sqorpius Starving Wintermute Xallo Former Consuls Herme Inacron Ironlion Omegaforce Tehheretic Toni', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Founders_of_Kyara\">Founders of Kyara</span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Eaglef\" title=\"User:Eaglef\">Eaglef</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/User:Dreammaster\" title=\"User:Dreammaster\">Dreammaster</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor_of_Kyara\">Mayor of Kyara</span></h3>\n<p><a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=User:Duce&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"User:Duce (page does not exist)\">Duce</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Consuls_of_Kyara\">Consuls of Kyara</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Adoll\" title=\"User:Adoll\">Adoll</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Dreammaster\" title=\"User:Dreammaster\">Dreammaster</a> (presently on loan to Wurmonline team)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Gavin\" title=\"Player:Gavin\">Gavin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Madt\" title=\"User:Madt\">Madt</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Manny\" title=\"User:Manny\">Manny</a> (presently on loan to Wurmonline team)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Miggy\" title=\"Player:Miggy\">Miggy</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Nosyt\" title=\"Player:Nosyt\">Nosyt</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Sqorpius\" title=\"Player:Sqorpius\">Sqorpius</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Starving\" title=\"User:Starving\">Starving</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Wintermute</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Xallo\" title=\"Player:Xallo\">Xallo</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Former_Consuls\">Former Consuls</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Herme</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Inacron\" title=\"Player:Inacron\">Inacron</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ironlion\" title=\"Player:Ironlion\">Ironlion</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Omegaforce\" title=\"Player:Omegaforce\">Omegaforce</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Tehheretic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Toni\" title=\"Player:Toni\">Toni</a></li></ul>', 1),
(11075, 2977, 'Description', 'Description', 'An empty shelf good for placing items upon. Used for decoration when displaying items or organizing a room.', '<p><i>An empty shelf good for placing items upon.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Used for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Decoration\" title=\"Decoration\">decoration</a> when displaying items or organizing a room.\n</p>', 0),
(11076, 2977, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Must be dropped to continue building.', '<ul><li>Must be dropped to continue building.</li></ul>', 1),
(11077, 2977, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Shows wood type When riding (an animal or vehicle) or looking down through an opening, items can be placed on the top shelf but may poke through the floor above if taller than a pottery jar. When picked up and placed again, the items will stay where they were originally placed on the shelf.', '<ul><li>Shows wood type</li>\n<li>When riding (an animal or vehicle) or looking down through an opening, items can be placed on the top shelf but may poke through the floor above if taller than a pottery jar.</li>\n<li>When picked up and placed again, the items will stay where they were originally placed on the shelf.</li></ul>', 2),
(11078, 2977, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Bookshelf for additional types of shelf storage', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bookshelf\" title=\"Bookshelf\">Bookshelf</a> for additional types of shelf storage</li></ul>', 3),
(11087, 1447, 'Description', 'Description', 'Blood from special creatures is said to have magic enchanting powers. This came from the <creature type> Blood from unique creatures can be mixed with source salt to create potions that when applied to tools -- a process known as \"imbuing\" -- grant that tool a bonus to gathering or improving.', '<p><i>Blood from special creatures is said to have magic enchanting powers. This came from the &lt;creature type&gt;</i>\n</p>\n<p>Blood from <a href=\"/index.php/Unique\" title=\"Unique\">unique</a> creatures can be mixed with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a> to create potions that when applied to tools -- a process known as \"imbuing\" -- grant that tool a bonus to gathering or improving.\n</p>', 0),
(11088, 1447, 'Notes', 'Notes', '0.10 kg of blood is given to all premium characters in local when a unique is slain, whether or not you attacked the creature or landed a blow. Blood is not treated as a liquid by the game so it does not have to be held within a container . The effect gradually wears off with use. The greater the strength of imbuement, the longer the effects will last. Dispel will remove imbues from a tool, so use caution. Failure to create a potion or ointment will consume both the blood and the source salt. Salve of frost and potion of acid are disabled on Defiance server. Alternate potions are noted below.', '<ul><li>0.10 kg of blood is given to all <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> characters in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Local\" title=\"Local\">local</a> when a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Unique_creatures\" title=\"Category:Unique creatures\">unique</a> is slain, whether or not you attacked the creature or landed a blow.</li>\n<li>Blood is not treated as a liquid by the game so it does not have to be held within a <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">container</a>.</li>\n<li>The effect gradually wears off with use. The greater the strength of imbuement, the longer the effects will last.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">Dispel</a> will remove imbues from a tool, so use caution.</li>\n<li>Failure to create a potion or ointment will consume both the blood and the source salt.</li>\n<li>Salve of frost and potion of acid are disabled on <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a> server. Alternate potions are noted below.</li></ul>', 1),
(11089, 1447, 'Creatures and potions', 'Creatures_and_potions', 'Goblin leader - Potion of mining Kyklops - Potion of leatherworking Forest giant - Potion of woodcutting Troll king - Ointment of stonecutting Dragons Black dragon - Potion of carpentry Blue dragon - Potion of butchery Green dragon - Ointment of tailoring Red dragon - Potion of ropemaking White dragon - Oil of the blacksmith Hatchlings Black dragon hatchling - Oil of the armour smith Blue dragon hatchling - Fletching potion Green dragon hatchling - Potion of acid / Ointment of tailoring on Defiance Red dragon hatchling - Oil of the weapon smith White dragon hatchling - Salve of frost / Oil of the blacksmith on Defiance', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Goblin_leader\" title=\"Goblin leader\">Goblin leader</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_mining\" title=\"Potion of mining\">Potion of mining</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Kyklops\" title=\"Kyklops\">Kyklops</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_leatherworking\" title=\"Potion of leatherworking\">Potion of leatherworking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forest_giant\" title=\"Forest giant\">Forest giant</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_woodcutting\" title=\"Potion of woodcutting\">Potion of woodcutting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Troll_king\" title=\"Troll king\">Troll king</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Ointment_of_stonecutting\" title=\"Ointment of stonecutting\">Ointment of stonecutting</a></li></ul>\n<p><b>Dragons</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_dragon\" title=\"Black dragon\">Black dragon</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_carpentry\" title=\"Potion of carpentry\">Potion of carpentry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Blue_dragon\" title=\"Blue dragon\">Blue dragon</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_butchery\" title=\"Potion of butchery\">Potion of butchery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Green_dragon\" title=\"Green dragon\">Green dragon</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Ointment_of_tailoring\" title=\"Ointment of tailoring\">Ointment of tailoring</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Red_dragon\" title=\"Red dragon\">Red dragon</a> - <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_ropemaking\" title=\"Potion of ropemaking\">Potion of ropemaking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/White_dragon\" title=\"White dragon\">White dragon</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Oil_of_the_blacksmith\" title=\"Oil of the blacksmith\">Oil of the blacksmith</a></li></ul>\n<p><b>Hatchlings</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_dragon_hatchling\" title=\"Black dragon hatchling\">Black dragon hatchling</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Oil_of_the_armour_smith\" title=\"Oil of the armour smith\">Oil of the armour smith</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Blue_dragon_hatchling\" title=\"Blue dragon hatchling\">Blue dragon hatchling</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Fletching_potion\" title=\"Fletching potion\">Fletching potion</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Green_dragon_hatchling\" title=\"Green dragon hatchling\">Green dragon hatchling</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_acid\" title=\"Potion of acid\">Potion of acid</a>/ Ointment of tailoring on Defiance</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Red_dragon_hatchling\" title=\"Red dragon hatchling\">Red dragon hatchling</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Oil_of_the_weapon_smith\" title=\"Oil of the weapon smith\">Oil of the weapon smith</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/White_dragon_hatchling\" title=\"White dragon hatchling\">White dragon hatchling</a> - <a href=\"/index.php/Salve_of_frost\" title=\"Salve of frost\">Salve of frost</a>/ Oil of the blacksmith on Defiance</li></ul>', 2),
(11090, 1447, 'Imbuing', 'Imbuing', 'In order to imbue an item with potion you must activate the potion, right click the item, and choose \"Alchemy > Imbue\". The entire potion is consumed upon imbuement of an item. Potion quality has the largest effect the strength of the potion\'s imbuement, while skill in natural substances has a lesser effect. A single tool can be imbued by more than one type of ointment/potion imbue, e.g. blacksmithing and weaponsmithing both on one tool.', '<p>In order to imbue an item with potion you must activate the potion, right click the item, and choose \"Alchemy &gt; Imbue\".\n</p>\n<ul><li>The entire potion is consumed upon imbuement of an item.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Potion quality has the largest effect the strength of the potion\'s imbuement, while skill in <a href=\"/index.php/Natural_substances\" title=\"Natural substances\">natural substances</a> has a lesser effect.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>A single tool can be imbued by more than one type of ointment/potion imbue, e.g. blacksmithing and weaponsmithing both on one tool.</li></ul>', 3),
(11091, 1447, 'Skill imbuement', 'Skill_imbuement', 'Potions of a particular skill, such as a Fletching potion or Ointment of stonecutting will improve the results of using those skills in various ways: Better results in item creation . When creating items with an imbued tool, quality of results will be better on average, but will still have a maximum quality equal to that of the material. Higher quality resources . When gathering raw materials with an imbued tool, quality of materials will be better on average, and can therefore be higher than normal maximum quality based on skill and ore vein quality. Better item improvement . When improving an item with an imbued tool, the item will gain more quality and can be improved to a higher quality than your skill level would normally allow. Examining the imbued tool will show: It has been imbued with special abilities, and it improves (one of the following depending on type: [leather working, carpentry, mining, etc]) max ql [0-100]', '<p>Potions of a particular skill, such as a <b>Fletching potion</b> or <b>Ointment of stonecutting</b> will improve the results of using those skills in various ways:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Better results in item creation</b>. When creating items with an imbued tool, quality of results will be better on average, but will still have a maximum quality equal to that of the material.</li>\n<li><b>Higher quality resources</b>. When gathering raw materials with an imbued tool, quality of materials will be better on average, and can therefore be higher than normal maximum quality based on skill and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">ore</a> vein quality.</li>\n<li><b>Better item improvement</b>. When improving an item with an imbued tool, the item will gain more quality and can be improved to a higher quality than your skill level would normally allow.</li></ul>\n<p>Examining the imbued tool will show: <i>It has been imbued with special abilities, and it improves</i> (one of the following depending on type: [leather working, carpentry, mining, etc]) <i>max ql [0-100]</i>\n</p>', 4),
(11092, 2732, 'Description', 'Description', 'A metallic liquid mixed with tiny black flakes. Smear this on an item to protect it once from shattering during enchants.', '<p><i>A metallic liquid mixed with tiny black flakes. Smear this on an item to protect it once from shattering during enchants.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11093, 2732, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Metallic liquid is obtainable as a reward from participating in a Rift event and collecting rift points. Can only be applied to items held in inventory (and not archaeology statues). The imbue will start with 100 power, no matter what your actual skill are or the potion QL is as long as the action succeeds. The imbuing action requires a full \'original unit\' (0.144 KG) to imbue any item. It can properly consume part of a larger combined fluid weight and leave the leftovers intact. Will protect against items \"cracking\", completely negating the damage that would have been dealt, up to five times with each protection lowering the imbue power by 20. Will protect against a SINGLE item shatter event and afterwards completely remove the imbue from the item. As long as the item is imbued, it\'ll be protected. (IE 20 power imbue will still protect the same as a 100 power imbue) You cannot improve the imbue with a fresh potion, the effect must entirely be gone to reapply the metallic liquid. The liquid comes in a glass bottle with a custom name (Potion Bottle). Potion bottles will always be 10 QL. Metallic liquid can be removed with the Dispel spell, so use caution.', '<ul><li>Metallic liquid is obtainable as a reward from participating in a <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">Rift</a> event and collecting rift points.</li>\n<li>Can only be applied to items held in inventory (and not archaeology statues).</li>\n<li>The imbue will start with 100 power, no matter what your actual skill are or the potion QL is as long as the action succeeds.</li>\n<li>The imbuing action requires a full \'original unit\' (0.144 KG) to imbue any item. It can properly consume part of a larger combined fluid weight and leave the leftovers intact.</li>\n<li>Will protect against items \"cracking\", completely negating the damage that would have been dealt, up to five times with each protection lowering the imbue power by 20.</li>\n<li>Will protect against a SINGLE item shatter event and afterwards completely remove the imbue from the item. As long as the item is imbued, it\'ll be protected. (IE 20 power imbue will still protect the same as a 100 power imbue)</li>\n<li>You cannot improve the imbue with a fresh potion, the effect must entirely be gone to reapply the metallic liquid.</li>\n<li>The liquid comes in a glass bottle with a custom name (Potion Bottle). Potion bottles will always be 10 QL.</li>\n<li>Metallic liquid can be removed with the <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">Dispel</a> spell, so use caution.</li></ul>', 1),
(11094, 2732, 'Messages', 'Messages', 'You will get a message each time the metallic liquid takes effect, they are as follows: Protecting from a shatter: (orange text) \"The (item name) emits a strong deep sound of resonance and starts to shatter, but the Metallic Liquid protects the (item name)! The Metallic Liquid has dissipated.\" Protecting from damaging: (normal text) \"The (item name) emits a deep worrying sound of resonance, and a small crack wants to start forming, but the Metallic Liquid steps in and takes the damage instead!\" Dissipating after running out of Imbue Power: (orange text) \"The Metallic Liquid\'s strength has been depleted, and its protection has been removed from the (item name)\"', '<p>You will get a message each time the metallic liquid takes effect, they are as follows:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Protecting from a shatter:</b> <i>(orange text)</i> \"The (item name) emits a strong deep sound of resonance and starts to shatter, but the Metallic Liquid protects the (item name)! The Metallic Liquid has dissipated.\"</li>\n<li><b>Protecting from damaging:</b> <i>(normal text)</i> \"The (item name) emits a deep worrying sound of resonance, and a small crack wants to start forming, but the Metallic Liquid steps in and takes the damage instead!\"</li>\n<li><b>Dissipating after running out of Imbue Power:</b> <i>(orange text)</i> \"The Metallic Liquid\'s strength has been depleted, and its protection has been removed from the (item name)\"</li></ul>', 2),
(11095, 2982, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a glorious eagle.﻿', '<p><i>A statue of a glorious eagle.﻿</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11096, 2982, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 93 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 93 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.</li></ul>', 1),
(11097, 2982, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11098, 2983, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bale of cotton.', '<p><i>A bale of cotton.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(11099, 2983, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cotton can be used for bandaging wounds. Higher quality cotton helps the chance of success in this, while lower quality cotton will give better skill gains while healing. If you find yourself in the wilderness with wounds, you can forage for cotton on tiles. While injured, your chances of finding cotton while foraging are approximately doubled. Virtually any item in-game that is made from cotton can be utilized as a bandage if needed. Example: [18:04:15] You bandage the wound with a fishing net. If the item is combinable, it will only use the necessary portion to treat the wound, while non-combinable items, such as a ship\'s sail, for example, are completely used up in the bandaging action. Cotton is also used to make cloth tailoring items. Cotton seeds can be picked picking out from cotton, with each cotton producing one seed. The cotton is destroyed in the process. Cotton weighing less than 1.00 kg cannot be picked for seeds. No tools are necessary in any of the methods for acquiring/harvesting cotton. Cotton can be combined up to 64 kg per bale. Can be found by Foraging Animal burrow , Undergrowth and Critter nest Resource nodes . Can be found by Botanizing Low brush , Desert weeds , Dune grass , Alpine brush and Thicket Resource nodes', '<ul><li>Cotton can be used for <a href=\"/index.php/Bandage\" title=\"Bandage\">bandaging</a> wounds. Higher quality cotton helps the chance of success in this, while lower quality cotton will give better skill gains while healing.\n<ul><li>If you find yourself in the wilderness with wounds, you can <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forage\" title=\"Forage\">forage</a> for cotton on tiles.</li>\n<li>While injured, your chances of finding cotton while foraging are approximately doubled.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Virtually any item in-game that is made from cotton can be utilized as a bandage if needed. Example: <i>[18:04:15] You bandage the wound with a fishing net.</i> If the item is combinable, it will only use the necessary portion to treat the wound, while non-combinable items, such as a ship\'s sail, for example, are completely used up in the bandaging action.</li>\n<li>Cotton is also used to make cloth tailoring items.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cotton_seeds\" title=\"Cotton seeds\">Cotton seeds</a> can be picked <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">picking</a> out from cotton, with each cotton producing one seed. The cotton is destroyed in the process. Cotton weighing less than 1.00 kg cannot be picked for seeds.</li>\n<li>No tools are necessary in any of the methods for acquiring/harvesting cotton.</li>\n<li>Cotton can be <a href=\"/index.php/Combine\" title=\"Combine\">combined</a> up to 64 kg per bale.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_burrow\" title=\"Animal burrow\">Animal burrow</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Undergrowth\" title=\"Undergrowth\">Undergrowth</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Critter_nest\" title=\"Critter nest\">Critter nest</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Low_brush\" title=\"Low brush\">Low brush</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Desert_weeds\" title=\"Desert weeds\">Desert weeds</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Dune_grass\" title=\"Dune grass\">Dune grass</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Alpine_brush\" title=\"Alpine brush\">Alpine brush</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Thicket\" title=\"Thicket\">Thicket</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a></li></ul>', 1),
(11103, 1181, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine soft cap that has a strange shimmer. A wearable red cotton cap that comes at 99 quality .', '<p><i>A fine soft cap that has a strange shimmer.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A wearable red cotton cap that comes at 99 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(11104, 1181, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'The soft cap can be worn in place of other hats or armour in the head slot.', '<p>The soft cap can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Equip\" title=\"Equip\">worn</a> in place of other hats or armour in the head slot.\n</p>', 1),
(11105, 1181, 'History', 'History', 'Soft caps were given to premium players as a Christmas gift in 2012.', '<p>Soft caps were given to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> players as a Christmas gift in 2012.\n</p>', 2),
(11106, 1589, 'Description', 'Description', 'The leather hat to wear for all of your adventures. A hat worn on the head, made of leather and improvable like leather.', '<p><i>The leather hat to wear for all of your adventures.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A hat worn on the head, made of leather and improvable like leather.\n</p>', 0),
(11107, 1589, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Seafarer\'s Hat', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Seafarer\'s Hat</a></li></ul>', 1),
(11108, 1589, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This item does not provide armour protection. This item can be enchanted.', '<ul><li>This item does not provide armour protection.</li>\n<li>This item can be enchanted.</li></ul>', 2),
(11112, 2988, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a large, drooling one-eyed giant. Statue of a Kyklops is a decorative statue of a Kyklops, created from 46 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>A statue of a large, drooling one-eyed giant.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of a Kyklops</b> is a decorative statue of a Kyklops, created from 46 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>', 0),
(11113, 2988, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11114, 2988, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Kyklops', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Kyklops\" title=\"Kyklops\">Kyklops</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11142, 1630, 'Description', 'Description', 'These gigantic creatures travel huge distances looking for food, while singing their mysterious songs. This blue whale is a large, non-aggressive animal , found in the seas. Due to their blue, water-like color, they can be difficult to spot.', '<p><i>These gigantic creatures travel huge distances looking for food, while singing their mysterious songs.</i>\n</p>\n<p>This blue whale is a large, non-aggressive <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animal</a>, found in the seas. Due to their blue, water-like color, they can be difficult to spot.\n</p>', 0),
(11143, 1630, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Blue whales are stronger than crocodiles and weaker than trolls . They have very good armour and medium attack speed. 65+ fighting skill as well as QL60+ weapon and armour are recommended for fighting this creature. Blue whales spawn from deep water tiles only.', '<ul><li>Blue whales are stronger than <a href=\"/index.php/Crocodile\" title=\"Crocodile\">crocodiles</a> and weaker than <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>.</li>\n<li>They have very good armour and medium attack speed.</li>\n<li>65+ fighting skill as well as QL60+ weapon and armour are recommended for fighting this creature.</li>\n<li>Blue whales spawn from deep water tiles only.</li></ul>', 1),
(11144, 1736, 'Description', 'Description', 'The green leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.', '<p><i>The green leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11145, 1736, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Summon Worg (Summons a Worg ) (Costs 500karma to summon) Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Summon <a href=\"/index.php/Worg\" title=\"Worg\">Worg</a> (Summons a <a href=\"/index.php/Worg\" title=\"Worg\">Worg</a>) (Costs 500karma to summon)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Internal 15% (Decreases internal damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Fire 10% (Increases fire damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(11146, 1736, 'Item use requirements', 'Item_use_requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be close to a strong plant, so that you may connect to its life force.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, with at least one very old (or older) non-fruit tree.\n</p>', 2),
(11147, 2508, 'Description', 'Description', 'A flat piece of papyrus made from pressed reed fibre. It has a waxed coating! It is possible to inscribe on the waxed papyrus sheet if you know how.', '<p><i>A flat piece of papyrus made from pressed reed fibre. It has a waxed coating! It is possible to inscribe on the waxed papyrus sheet if you know how.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11148, 2508, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Waxed paper is primarily used to wrap food items to make them decay slower. The wrapping of prepared food items using waxed paper can be done by activating a waxed paper that is in the player\'s inventory and then right-clicking a prepared food item that is also in inventory, and then selecting \"wrap\". Wrapped food always decays slower, regardless of its stored location. Cannot be stored in a bulk storage bin.', '<ul><li>Waxed paper is primarily used to wrap food items to make them decay slower. The wrapping of prepared food items using waxed paper can be done by activating a waxed paper that is in the player\'s inventory and then right-clicking a prepared food item that is also in inventory, and then selecting \"wrap\".</li>\n<li>Wrapped food always decays slower, regardless of its stored location.</li>\n<li>Cannot be stored in a bulk storage bin.</li></ul>', 1),
(11149, 2990, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a mountain lion. Statue of Mountain Lion is a decorative statue of a ravenous Mountain Lion, created from 46 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>A statue of a mountain lion.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of Mountain Lion</b> is a decorative statue of a ravenous Mountain Lion, created from 46 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>', 0),
(11150, 2990, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11151, 2990, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Mountain Lion', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mountain_Lion\" title=\"Mountain Lion\">Mountain Lion</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11152, 1638, 'Description', 'Description', 'A vase with some sweet roses to a sweet friend. A decorative item of beautiful roses, each given with a quality of 100.', '<p><i>A vase with some sweet roses to a sweet friend.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A decorative item of beautiful roses, each given with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of 100.\n</p>', 0),
(11153, 1638, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A valentine is a decorative item that may be dropped on the ground. They do not form a pile when multiples are dropped on the same tile. Normal push/pull/rotate actions may be used to move the vase. Valentines take damage over time, but may be repaired by watering them. Activate a container holding water and right-click the valentine and select Water plant . This action will consume 0.10kg of water regardless of success or failure. You may water them on the ground, in your inventory, or from inside a container. Watering a valentine uses the gardening skill. You start watering the flowers. The watering action can fail, though failure does not cause more damage. You accidentally miss the pot and pour the water on the ground instead. For some inexplicable reason you poured all of the water on the ground, how you thought it would help you will never know. You spill water all over your clothes. When successfully watered, their damage is reduced to 0 without any quality lost. You successfully watered the flowers, they look healthier. After enough successful actions, the valentine cannot be watered any more. The flowers are in no need of watering.', '<p>A valentine is a decorative item that may be dropped on the ground. They do not form a pile when multiples are dropped on the same tile. Normal push/pull/rotate actions may be used to move the vase.\n</p>\n<p>Valentines take damage over time, but may be repaired by watering them. <b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">container</a> holding <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a> and <b>right-click</b> the valentine and select <b>Water plant</b>. This action will consume 0.10kg of water regardless of success or failure. You may water them on the ground, in your inventory, or from inside a container. Watering a valentine uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">gardening</a> skill.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You start watering the flowers. </span>\n</p>\n<p>The watering action can fail, though failure does not cause more damage.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You accidentally miss the pot and pour the water on the ground instead.<br/>\nFor some inexplicable reason you poured all of the water on the ground, how you thought it would help you will never know.<br/>\nYou spill water all over your clothes. </span>\n</p>\n<p>When successfully watered, their damage is reduced to 0 without any quality lost.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You successfully watered the flowers, they look healthier. </span>\n</p>\n<p>After enough successful actions, the valentine cannot be watered any more.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> The flowers are in no need of watering. </span>\n</p>', 1),
(11154, 1638, 'History', 'History', 'Valentines were redeemable for premium players on Valentine\'s Day in 2015 and 2018 by using the /redeemkey chat command : /redeemkey TXFX4VCF7B8W-ABGWDXESZWO3 (2015) /redeemkey XDH94OUQA4UL-ABZIM4ESSVSY (2018) A valentines materializes in your pocket.', '<p>Valentines were redeemable for premium players on Valentine\'s Day in 2015 and 2018 by using the <b>/redeemkey</b> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chat_command\" title=\"Chat command\">chat command</a>:\n</p>\n<p><code>/redeemkey TXFX4VCF7B8W-ABGWDXESZWO3</code> (2015)\n</p>\n<p><code>/redeemkey XDH94OUQA4UL-ABZIM4ESSVSY</code> (2018)\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> A valentines materializes in your pocket. </span>\n</p>', 2),
(11156, 3003, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Alpengeist , The Reborn', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Alpengeist\" title=\"User:Alpengeist\">Alpengeist</a>, The Reborn\n</p>', 0),
(11164, 2987, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a terrifying hell horse.', '<p><i>A statue of a terrifying hell horse.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11165, 2987, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 93 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 93 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11166, 2987, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Hell horse', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">Hell horse</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11167, 2995, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of the malevolent goddess Libila.﻿﻿﻿', '<p><i>A statue of the malevolent goddess Libila.﻿﻿﻿</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11168, 2995, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 66 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 66 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11169, 2995, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Libila', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11176, 2993, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of the benevolent goddess Vynora.', '<p><i>A statue of the benevolent goddess Vynora.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11177, 2993, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 66 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 66 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11178, 2993, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Vynora', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11179, 2991, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of an imposing drake.', '<p><i>A statue of an imposing drake.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11180, 2991, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding  127 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them. Creation of this statue uses restoration skill, but improvement uses blacksmithing tools, while giving stonecutting skill.', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding  127 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.</li>\n<li>Creation of this statue uses restoration skill, but improvement uses blacksmithing tools, while giving stonecutting skill.</li></ul>', 1),
(11181, 2991, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Drake', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Drake\" title=\"Drake\">Drake</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11182, 2989, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a beast seen appearing from rifts of jackal. Statue of Rift Beast is a decorative statue of a ravenous Rift Beast, created from 46 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>A statue of a beast seen appearing from rifts of jackal.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of Rift Beast</b> is a decorative statue of a ravenous Rift Beast, created from 46 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>', 0),
(11183, 2989, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11184, 2989, 'Images', 'Images', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rift_beast2.jpg\"><img alt=\"Rift beast2.jpg\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"169\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/6c/Rift_beast2.jpg/300px-Rift_beast2.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/6c/Rift_beast2.jpg/450px-Rift_beast2.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/6c/Rift_beast2.jpg/600px-Rift_beast2.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a>\n</p>', 2),
(11185, 2989, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11186, 2996, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of the forest god Fo.﻿﻿﻿', '<p><i>A statue of the forest god Fo.﻿﻿﻿</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11187, 2996, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 66 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 66 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.</li></ul>', 1),
(11188, 2996, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Fo', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11189, 2994, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of the warrior god Magranon.﻿﻿﻿', '<p><i>A statue of the warrior god Magranon.﻿﻿﻿</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11190, 2994, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 66 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 66 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11191, 2994, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Magranon', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11198, 3016, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a strong guard. Statue of Guard is a decorative statue of a noble guard, created from 93 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>A statue of a strong guard.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of Guard</b> is a decorative statue of a noble guard, created from 93 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>', 0),
(11199, 3016, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11200, 3016, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Tower Guard', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tower_Guard\" title=\"Tower Guard\">Tower Guard</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11201, 3017, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a mighty worg.', '<p><i>A statue of a mighty worg.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11202, 3017, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding 93 fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding 93 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(11203, 3017, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Worg', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Worg\" title=\"Worg\">Worg</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11211, 3023, 'Description', 'Description', 'The skinned-off facial region of a troll, fashioned into a detestable mask for the wearing.', '<p><i>The skinned-off facial region of a troll, fashioned into a detestable mask for the wearing.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11212, 3023, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Troll masks were among the possible drops given off by the killing of hunter creatures during the 2018 Halloween Event. Possible to obtain during the 2021 and 2022 Halloween Events, via Archaeology or slaying hostile mobs. The archaeology version requires 5 troll mask fragments to complete. Can be colored by Adamantine Jackal rune .', '<ul><li>Troll masks were among the possible drops given off by the killing of hunter <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a> during the 2018 Halloween Event.</li>\n<li>Possible to obtain during the 2021 and 2022 Halloween Events, via <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> or slaying hostile mobs.</li>\n<li>The archaeology version requires 5 troll mask fragments to complete.</li>\n<li>Can be colored by Adamantine Jackal <a href=\"/index.php/Runes#Properties\" title=\"Runes\">rune</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11216, 3021, 'Description', 'Description', 'A gruesome and scary mask with blood staining the front of it. It appears to have been fashioned from a face of a humanoid skull.', '<p><i>A gruesome and scary mask with blood staining the front of it. It appears to have been fashioned from a face of a humanoid skull. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(11217, 3021, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Skull masks can be made of a number of different materials including oleanderwood, gold, and silver. Each variant does give a different visual look based on that material. The maker signature will be that of the creature that dropped it. It was one of a number of possible drop rewards given off by the killing of hunter creatures during the 2018 Halloween Event, and possibly at other events as well (this needs additional confirmation). Obtainable as part of the 2021 Halloween Event, from slaying hostile mobs (excluding hell horse )', '<ul><li>Skull masks can be made of a number of different materials including oleanderwood, gold, and silver. Each variant does give a different visual look based on that material.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The maker signature will be that of the creature that dropped it.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>It was one of a number of possible drop rewards given off by the killing of hunter creatures during the 2018 Halloween Event, and possibly at other events as well (this needs additional confirmation).</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Obtainable as part of the 2021 Halloween Event, from slaying hostile mobs (excluding <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">hell horse</a>)</li></ul>', 1),
(11228, 3020, 'Description', 'Description', 'A blue colored wooden stick with a bunch of green leaves in a fan shape on one end. Symbols indicate that if you plant it at sea, an island will emerge!', '<p><i>A blue colored wooden stick with a bunch of green leaves in a fan shape on one end. Symbols indicate that if you plant it at sea, an island will emerge!</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11229, 3020, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate the wand by double-clicking, then right click the wand and two options should appear: Survey Tells you whether or not the wand can be used at this location. Activate After 60 seconds, the rock and dirt layer will be raised, forming a round island with a lava pit in the center. This action destroys the wand upon completion. Once the 60 second timer has started, the game will warn you that once the process is complete, there will be no way to undo the effects.', '<p>Activate the wand by double-clicking, then right click the wand and two options should appear:\n</p>\n<p><b>Survey</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Tells you whether or not the wand can be used at this location.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Activate</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>After 60 seconds, the rock and dirt layer will be raised, forming a round island with a lava pit in the center.\n<ul><li>This action destroys the wand upon completion.</li>\n<li>Once the 60 second timer has started, the game will warn you that <b>once the process is complete, there will be no way to undo the effects.</b></li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(11230, 3020, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Island can range in size about 150-250 slopes high and 35-45 wide. 20-25 slope of dirt on top of a rock layer. Needs to be a certain distance away from shore and deeds. The Wand of the seas was only attainable through winning the game on Freedom. But can still be obtained as a reward from winning the Valrei scenario on the EPIC cluster.', '<ul><li>Island can range in size about 150-250 slopes high and 35-45 wide.</li>\n<li>20-25 slope of dirt on top of a rock layer.</li>\n<li>Needs to be a certain distance away from shore and deeds.</li>\n<li>The Wand of the seas was only attainable through <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Personal_goals\" title=\"Personal goals\">winning the game</a> on Freedom.</li>\n<li>But can still be obtained as a reward from winning the <a href=\"/index.php/Scenarios\" title=\"Scenarios\">Valrei scenario</a> on the EPIC cluster.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n<a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Wand_of_seas_island.jpg\" title=\"Wand of Seas Island\"><img alt=\"Wand of Seas Island\" data-file-height=\"1019\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"265\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/87/Wand_of_seas_island.jpg/500px-Wand_of_seas_island.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/87/Wand_of_seas_island.jpg/750px-Wand_of_seas_island.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/87/Wand_of_seas_island.jpg/1000px-Wand_of_seas_island.jpg 2x\" width=\"500\"/></a>\n</p>', 2),
(11235, 3031, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small flask containing a syrupy golden substance.', '<p><i>A small flask containing a syrupy golden substance.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11236, 3031, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Potion created by mixing blue dragon blood with source salt .', '<p>Potion created by mixing <a href=\"/index.php/Blue_dragon\" title=\"Blue dragon\">blue dragon</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(11237, 3031, 'Imbuing', 'Imbuing', 'Activate the potion and right-click tool you want to imbue. Select \"Alchemy > Imbue\" from the menu.\nExamine the imbued tool to see what effect (ranging to 100) does the imbue have. Improving butchering products using imbued tool will be easier.', '<p>Activate the potion and right-click tool you want to imbue. Select \"Alchemy &gt; Imbue\" from the menu.\nExamine the imbued tool to see what effect (ranging to 100) does the imbue have.\n</p>\n<p>Improving <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a> products using imbued tool will be easier.\n</p>', 2),
(11238, 3031, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Power of the imbue effect will wear down slowly.', '<ul><li>Power of the imbue effect will wear down slowly.</li></ul>', 3),
(11239, 3032, 'Description', 'Description', 'A crystal ball once owned by the Puzzle King.', '<p><i>A crystal ball once owned by the Puzzle King.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11240, 3032, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A special item only known to be attainable through the successful completion of the Puzzle Labyrinth Adventure, which is a deed created by Faeran and Griphyth and documented by their videos on  their youtube channel FactionalFight. The labyrinth was built at the deed \"Puzzle Labyrinth\", just Northwest of Vrock Landing . Both premium and non-premium players can attain this item', '<ul><li>A special item only known to be attainable through the successful completion of the Puzzle Labyrinth Adventure, which is a deed created by Faeran and Griphyth and documented by their videos on  their youtube channel FactionalFight.</li>\n<li>The labyrinth was built at the deed \"Puzzle Labyrinth\", just Northwest of <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement:Vrock_Landing\" title=\"Settlement:Vrock Landing\">Vrock Landing</a>.</li>\n<li>Both premium and non-premium players can attain this item</li></ul>', 1),
(11241, 3032, 'Pictures', 'Pictures', 'Labyrinth Front:', '<ul><li>Labyrinth Front:</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Puzzlemaze.jpg\"><img alt=\"Puzzlemaze.jpg\" data-file-height=\"1017\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1017\" src=\"/images/2/2d/Puzzlemaze.jpg\" width=\"1920\"/></a>\n</p>', 2),
