(11662, 3152, 'Description', 'Description', 'A spell given to priests of Magranon at 30 Faith . This spell is used to enchant jewelry. Wearing jewelry with this enchantment will reduce the damage of all cold wounds suffered by the player.', '<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> given to <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> at 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a>.\n</p>\n<p>This spell is used to enchant jewelry. Wearing jewelry with this enchantment will reduce the damage of all cold wounds suffered by the player.\n</p>', 0),
(11663, 3152, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click a jewelry item Select Spells > Frost protection', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a jewelry item</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Frost protection</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11664, 3152, 'Jewelry damage enchantments', 'Jewelry_damage_enchantments', 'Several jewelry enchantments enhance damage done by the player wearing them, or decrease damage done to that player. Each enchantment applies to a specific type of damage. These enchantments apply to all possible sources of the specified damage type, whether it is a weapon, weapon enchantment, offensive spell, or other source. These enchantments conflict with each other as well as Nolocate , meaning you cannot enchant an item with more than one of these spells. Effectiveness The effectiveness of the enchantment is determined by both enchantment power and the quality level of the jewelry, each having equal importance. For example, a 50QL ring with a 25 power enchantment has the same effectiveness as a 25QL ring with a 50 power enchantment. Depending on QL and enchantment power, offensive enchantments increase that type of damage between 2.5% and 5%, and defensive enchantments decrease incoming damage of that type between 2.5% to 7.5%. Wearing multiple items with the same enchantment of this type will have diminishing returns. The total effectiveness of all items combined is multiplied by 2 / (1 + count) , where \"count\" refers to the number of the same enchantment equipped. In other words, having two of the same enchantment equipped will be 2/3 (66.7%) total effectiveness, and three of the same type will have 1/2 (50%) effectiveness. For example, two 50QL rings with the same 50-power enchantment will have a total effectiveness of 66.7 (2/3 of 100), and adding a third with the same QL and enchantment power would have a effectiveness of 75 (1/2 of 150). Table of enchantments Damage type Offensive Defensive Fire Blaze Fire protection Acid Corrosion Acid protection Cold Glacial Frost protection Poison Toxin Poison protection', '<p>Several <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Jewelry\" title=\"Jewelry\">jewelry</a> enchantments enhance damage done by the player wearing them, or decrease damage done to that player. Each enchantment applies to a specific type of damage.\n</p>\n<p>These enchantments apply to all possible sources of the specified damage type, whether it is a weapon, weapon enchantment, offensive spell, or other source.\n</p>\n<p>These enchantments conflict with each other as well as <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a>, meaning you cannot enchant an item with more than one of these spells.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Effectiveness\">Effectiveness</span></h3>\n<p>The effectiveness of the enchantment is determined by both enchantment power and the <a href=\"/index.php/Quality_level\" title=\"Quality level\">quality level</a> of the jewelry, each having equal importance. For example, a 50QL <a href=\"/index.php/Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> with a 25 power enchantment has the same effectiveness as a 25QL ring with a 50 power enchantment.\n</p>\n<p>Depending on QL and enchantment power, offensive enchantments increase that type of damage between 2.5% and 5%, and defensive enchantments decrease incoming damage of that type between 2.5% to 7.5%.\n</p>\n<p>Wearing multiple items with the same enchantment of this type will have diminishing returns. The total effectiveness of all items combined is multiplied by <i>2 / (1 + count)</i>, where \"count\" refers to the number of the same enchantment equipped. In other words, having two of the same enchantment equipped will be 2/3 (66.7%) total effectiveness, and three of the same type will have 1/2 (50%) effectiveness. For example, two 50QL rings with the same 50-power enchantment will have a total effectiveness of 66.7 (2/3 of 100), and adding a third with the same QL and enchantment power would have a effectiveness of 75 (1/2 of 150).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Table_of_enchantments\">Table of enchantments</span></h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Damage type\n</th>\n<th>Offensive\n</th>\n<th>Defensive\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Fire\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Blaze\" title=\"Blaze\">Blaze</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_protection\" title=\"Fire protection\">Fire protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Acid\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corrosion\" title=\"Corrosion\">Corrosion</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_protection\" title=\"Acid protection\">Acid protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Cold\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Glacial\" title=\"Glacial\">Glacial</a></td>\n<td><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Frost protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Poison\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Toxin\" title=\"Toxin\">Toxin</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Poison_protection\" title=\"Poison protection\">Poison protection</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(11669, 3154, 'Description', 'Description', 'A spell given to priests of Libila at 27 Faith . This spell is used to enchant jewelry. Wearing jewelry with this enchantment will reduce the damage of all poison wounds suffered by the player.', '<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> given to <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> at 27 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a>.\n</p>\n<p>This spell is used to enchant jewelry. Wearing jewelry with this enchantment will reduce the damage of all poison wounds suffered by the player.\n</p>', 0),
(11670, 3154, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click a jewelry item Select Spells > Poison protection', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a jewelry item</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Poison protection</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11671, 3154, 'Jewelry damage enchantments', 'Jewelry_damage_enchantments', 'Several jewelry enchantments enhance damage done by the player wearing them, or decrease damage done to that player. Each enchantment applies to a specific type of damage. These enchantments apply to all possible sources of the specified damage type, whether it is a weapon, weapon enchantment, offensive spell, or other source. These enchantments conflict with each other as well as Nolocate , meaning you cannot enchant an item with more than one of these spells. Effectiveness The effectiveness of the enchantment is determined by both enchantment power and the quality level of the jewelry, each having equal importance. For example, a 50QL ring with a 25 power enchantment has the same effectiveness as a 25QL ring with a 50 power enchantment. Depending on QL and enchantment power, offensive enchantments increase that type of damage between 2.5% and 5%, and defensive enchantments decrease incoming damage of that type between 2.5% to 7.5%. Wearing multiple items with the same enchantment of this type will have diminishing returns. The total effectiveness of all items combined is multiplied by 2 / (1 + count) , where \"count\" refers to the number of the same enchantment equipped. In other words, having two of the same enchantment equipped will be 2/3 (66.7%) total effectiveness, and three of the same type will have 1/2 (50%) effectiveness. For example, two 50QL rings with the same 50-power enchantment will have a total effectiveness of 66.7 (2/3 of 100), and adding a third with the same QL and enchantment power would have a effectiveness of 75 (1/2 of 150). Table of enchantments Damage type Offensive Defensive Fire Blaze Fire protection Acid Corrosion Acid protection Cold Glacial Frost protection Poison Toxin Poison protection', '<p>Several <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Jewelry\" title=\"Jewelry\">jewelry</a> enchantments enhance damage done by the player wearing them, or decrease damage done to that player. Each enchantment applies to a specific type of damage.\n</p>\n<p>These enchantments apply to all possible sources of the specified damage type, whether it is a weapon, weapon enchantment, offensive spell, or other source.\n</p>\n<p>These enchantments conflict with each other as well as <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a>, meaning you cannot enchant an item with more than one of these spells.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Effectiveness\">Effectiveness</span></h3>\n<p>The effectiveness of the enchantment is determined by both enchantment power and the <a href=\"/index.php/Quality_level\" title=\"Quality level\">quality level</a> of the jewelry, each having equal importance. For example, a 50QL <a href=\"/index.php/Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> with a 25 power enchantment has the same effectiveness as a 25QL ring with a 50 power enchantment.\n</p>\n<p>Depending on QL and enchantment power, offensive enchantments increase that type of damage between 2.5% and 5%, and defensive enchantments decrease incoming damage of that type between 2.5% to 7.5%.\n</p>\n<p>Wearing multiple items with the same enchantment of this type will have diminishing returns. The total effectiveness of all items combined is multiplied by <i>2 / (1 + count)</i>, where \"count\" refers to the number of the same enchantment equipped. In other words, having two of the same enchantment equipped will be 2/3 (66.7%) total effectiveness, and three of the same type will have 1/2 (50%) effectiveness. For example, two 50QL rings with the same 50-power enchantment will have a total effectiveness of 66.7 (2/3 of 100), and adding a third with the same QL and enchantment power would have a effectiveness of 75 (1/2 of 150).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Table_of_enchantments\">Table of enchantments</span></h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Damage type\n</th>\n<th>Offensive\n</th>\n<th>Defensive\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Fire\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Blaze\" title=\"Blaze\">Blaze</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_protection\" title=\"Fire protection\">Fire protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Acid\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Corrosion\" title=\"Corrosion\">Corrosion</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Acid_protection\" title=\"Acid protection\">Acid protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Cold\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Glacial\" title=\"Glacial\">Glacial</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Frost_protection\" title=\"Frost protection\">Frost protection</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Poison\n</th>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Toxin\" title=\"Toxin\">Toxin</a></td>\n<td><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Poison protection</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(11672, 3154, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Although the minimum Faith for this spell of 27, being a priest requires at least 30 Faith, so this spell is technically only available at 30 Faith and higher.', '<ul><li>Although the minimum Faith for this spell of 27, being a priest requires at least 30 Faith, so this spell is technically only available at 30 Faith and higher.</li></ul>', 3),
(11729, 3161, 'Description', 'Description', 'A delicate necklace made from a string of pearls with a black pearl in middle.', '<p><i>A delicate necklace made from a string of pearls with a black pearl in middle.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11730, 3161, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Pearls and black pearls are obtained from clams while fishing or (rarely) from a snowman statue instead of a snowball. The finished necklace cannot be improved, use high quality components when crafting to get better quality. The pearl necklace takes on the same model as the medallion necklace, when it is not worn.', '<ul><li>Pearls and black pearls are obtained from <a href=\"/index.php/Clam\" title=\"Clam\">clams</a> while fishing or (rarely) from a <a href=\"/index.php/Snowman_statue\" title=\"Snowman statue\">snowman statue</a> instead of a snowball.</li>\n<li>The finished necklace cannot be improved, use high quality components when crafting to get better quality.</li>\n<li>The pearl necklace takes on the same model as the medallion necklace, when it is not worn.</li></ul>', 1),
(11731, 3162, 'Description', 'Description', 'A dark green stinking troll. Always hungry. Always deadly.', '<p><i>A dark green stinking troll. Always hungry. Always deadly.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11732, 3162, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Trolls can cause large wounds using a huge shod club as well as bite with strong jaws. A minimum of 60 fighting skill with good equipment is recommended to fight one alone. They can pass through unlocked doors and gates and can climb ladders. They can traverse any tile steepness but will not enter water. If killed, they give the title \'Trollslayer\' (note: the player must record at least one hit on the troll before it dies in order to get the title). When dominated , they cannot destroy fences/stone/house walls. They can pull carts but only while dominated or when a zombie . They can rapidly regenerate and heal any wounds, despite severity. Trolls drop a 45ql, 15kg huge shod club upon death. They also pose a small chance to drop a non-rare, rare, supreme, or even a fantastic recipe . You can take a huge shod club from a dominated troll\'s inventory but not put it back in.  A shod clubless troll claws. \" [20:17:41] Adolescent greenish troll claws Aged huge spider extremely hard in the stomach and damages it. \"', '<ul><li>Trolls can cause large wounds using a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">huge shod club</a> as well as bite with strong jaws. A minimum of 60 fighting skill with good equipment is recommended to fight one alone.</li>\n<li>They can pass through unlocked doors and gates and can climb ladders.</li>\n<li>They can traverse any tile steepness but will not enter water.</li>\n<li>If killed, they give the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Title\" title=\"Title\">title</a> \'Trollslayer\' (note: the player must record at least one hit on the troll before it dies in order to get the title).</li>\n<li>When <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">dominated</a>, they cannot destroy fences/stone/house walls.</li>\n<li>They can pull carts but only while <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\"><i>dominated</i></a> or when a <a href=\"/index.php/Zombie\" title=\"Zombie\"><i>zombie</i></a>.</li>\n<li>They can rapidly regenerate and heal any wounds, despite severity.</li>\n<li>Trolls drop a 45ql, 15kg <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">huge shod club</a> upon death. They also pose a small chance to drop a non-rare, rare, supreme, or even a fantastic <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking#Recipes\" title=\"Cooking\">recipe</a>.</li>\n<li>You can take a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">huge shod club</a> from a <a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">dominated</a> troll\'s inventory but not put it back in.  A shod clubless troll claws. \"<i>[20:17:41] Adolescent greenish troll claws Aged huge spider extremely hard in the stomach and damages it.</i>\"</li></ul>', 1),
(11733, 3162, 'Images', 'Images', 'Today\'s common troll in its natural environment', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 226.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 226.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 224.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"967\" data-file-width=\"725\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/04/2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png/337px-2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/0/04/2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png/506px-2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/0/04/2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png/675px-2014-02-06_wiki_troll.png 2x\" width=\"225\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 205px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Today\'s common troll in its natural environment\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(11734, 3114, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a peaceful unicorn family. Statue of unicorn is a decorative statue of a unicorn parent and foal, created from 80 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>A statue of a peaceful unicorn family.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of unicorn</b> is a decorative statue of a unicorn parent and foal, created from 80 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(11735, 3114, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11736, 3114, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Unicorn', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn\" title=\"Unicorn\">Unicorn</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11737, 3164, 'Description', 'Description', '... Statue of Lava fiend is a decorative statue of a frightening lava fiend, created from 93 fragments found in the wild.', '<p><i>...</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Statue of Lava fiend</b> is a decorative statue of a frightening lava fiend, created from 93 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> found in the wild.\n</p>', 0),
(11738, 3164, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'These statues are made by finding fragments in the wild, using the archaeology skill, then combining them, which gives restoration skill. Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>These statues are made by finding <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> in the wild, using the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> skill, then combining them, which gives <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a> skill.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved once completed, with their corresponding materials.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \'Turn\' commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11739, 3164, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Statues Archaeology Lava fiend', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lava_fiend\" title=\"Lava fiend\">Lava fiend</a></li></ul>', 2),
(11745, 3166, 'Description', 'Description', 'A captured fly, should be good fishing with it.', '<p><i>A captured fly, should be good fishing with it.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11746, 3166, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Flies are caught using a pottery jar , with a bit of honey in it, on animals that require grooming . Animals can shy away regardless if led or not. Takes up the action of grooming . Time to next groom (availability of catching flies) can be seen by Inspecting animal. Takes .01kg of honey per fly. Fly will be inside pottery jar until taken out of. Is used as bait for fishing . Cannot be stored in a bsb . Can be stored in a tackle box .', '<ul><li>Flies are caught using a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_jar\" title=\"Pottery jar\">pottery jar</a>, with a bit of <a href=\"/index.php/Honey\" title=\"Honey\">honey</a> in it, on animals that require <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Groom\" title=\"Groom\">grooming</a>.</li>\n<li>Animals can shy away regardless if <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures#Leading\" title=\"Creatures\">led</a> or not.</li>\n<li>Takes up the action of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Groom\" title=\"Groom\">grooming</a>.</li>\n<li>Time to next <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Groom\" title=\"Groom\">groom</a> (availability of catching flies) can be seen by Inspecting animal.</li>\n<li>Takes .01kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Honey\" title=\"Honey\">honey</a> per fly.</li>\n<li>Fly will be inside <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_jar\" title=\"Pottery jar\">pottery jar</a> until taken out of.</li>\n<li>Is used as <a href=\"/index.php/Bait\" title=\"Bait\">bait</a> for <a href=\"/index.php/Fishing\" title=\"Fishing\">fishing</a>.</li>\n<li>Cannot be stored in a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bsb\" title=\"Bsb\">bsb</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Tackle_box\" title=\"Tackle box\">tackle box</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11747, 1557, 'Description', 'Description', '', '', 0),
(11748, 1557, 'Construction--Parts of the Bridge', 'Construction--Parts_of_the_Bridge', 'Wood bridge crown The center parts of a rope bridge. It is the crown of a wood bridge. Total items required 4 wooden beams 2 iron ribbons 3 large nails 22 planks 2 shafts 1 small nail Wood bridge abutment The section of the bridge that connects to the ground. Total items required 8 wooden beams 4 iron ribbons 4 large nails 22 planks 2 shafts 1 small nail Wood bridge support Total items required 16 wooden beams 8 iron ribbons 6 large nails 22 planks 2 shafts 1 small nail Wood bridge bracing Total items required 8 wooden beams 4 iron ribbons 4 large nails 22 planks 2 shafts 1 small nail', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wood_bridge_crown\">Wood bridge crown</span></h3>\n<p>The center parts of a rope bridge. <i>It is the crown of a wood bridge.</i>\n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beams</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ribbon\" title=\"Iron ribbon\">iron ribbons</a></li>\n<li>3 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a></li>\n<li>22 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shafts</a></li>\n<li>1 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Small_nail\" title=\"Small nail\">small nail</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wood_bridge_abutment\">Wood bridge abutment</span></h3>\n<p>The section of the bridge that connects to the ground. \n</p>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>8 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beams</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ribbon\" title=\"Iron ribbon\">iron ribbons</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a></li>\n<li>22 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shafts</a></li>\n<li>1 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Small_nail\" title=\"Small nail\">small nail</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wood_bridge_support\">Wood bridge support</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>16 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beams</a></li>\n<li>8 <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ribbon\" title=\"Iron ribbon\">iron ribbons</a></li>\n<li>6 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a></li>\n<li>22 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shafts</a></li>\n<li>1 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Small_nail\" title=\"Small nail\">small nail</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wood_bridge_bracing\">Wood bridge bracing</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p>Total items required\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<ul><li>8 <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_beam\" title=\"Wooden beam\">wooden beams</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ribbon\" title=\"Iron ribbon\">iron ribbons</a></li>\n<li>4 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a></li>\n<li>22 <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">planks</a></li>\n<li>2 <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shafts</a></li>\n<li>1 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Small_nail\" title=\"Small nail\">small nail</a></li></ul>\n</div></div>', 1),
(11749, 1557, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wood bridges do not finish with a wood type. They are simply \"wooden.\" Wood bridges are limited to 2 tiles wide. Foundations will vary based on bridge height Wooden bridge supports are 3 meters tall Wooden bridge extensions are 3 meters tall (each)', '<ul><li>Wood bridges do not finish with a wood type. They are simply \"wooden.\"</li>\n<li>Wood bridges are limited to 2 tiles wide.</li>\n<li>Foundations will vary based on bridge height</li>\n<li>Wooden bridge supports are 3 meters tall</li>\n<li>Wooden bridge extensions are 3 meters tall (each)</li></ul>', 2),
(11750, 1557, 'Images', 'Images', 'A Wood Bridge Built Inside A Cave', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Woodbridge.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/64/Woodbridge.jpg/800px-Woodbridge.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/64/Woodbridge.jpg/1200px-Woodbridge.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/64/Woodbridge.jpg/1600px-Woodbridge.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 514px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>A Wood Bridge Built Inside A Cave\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(11751, 1557, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Bridge', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bridge\" title=\"Bridge\">Bridge</a></li></ul>', 4),
(11760, 2992, 'Description', 'Description', 'Metallurgy is the skill that determines success and QL when creating metal alloys.', '<p>Metallurgy is the skill that determines success and QL when creating metal alloys.\n</p>', 0),
(11761, 2992, 'Alloy Recipes', 'Alloy_Recipes', 'Known creatable alloys are: Brass - created from Zinc and Copper Bronze - created from Tin and Copper Steel - created from Charcoal and Iron Electrum - created from Gold and Silver Success chance and average quality of metal created are affected by the first component of each alloy. Zinc for Brass Tin for Bronze Charcoal for Steel Gold for Electrum Max quality is substantially affected by the quality of the second component of each alloy. Iron for Steel Copper for Brass and Bronze Silver for Electrum', '<p>Known creatable alloys are:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brass_lump\" title=\"Brass lump\">Brass</a> - created from <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">Zinc</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bronze_lump\" title=\"Bronze lump\">Bronze</a> - created from <a href=\"/index.php/Tin_lump\" title=\"Tin lump\">Tin</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Steel_lump\" title=\"Steel lump\">Steel</a> - created from <a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal\" title=\"Charcoal\">Charcoal</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">Iron</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Electrum_lump\" title=\"Electrum lump\">Electrum</a> - created from <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">Gold</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">Silver</a></li></ul>\n<p>Success chance and average quality of metal created are affected by the first component of each alloy.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Zinc for Brass</li>\n<li>Tin for Bronze</li>\n<li>Charcoal for Steel</li>\n<li>Gold for Electrum</li></ul>\n<p>Max quality is substantially affected by the quality of the second component of each alloy. \n</p>\n<ul><li>Iron for Steel</li>\n<li>Copper for Brass and Bronze</li>\n<li>Silver for Electrum</li></ul>', 1),
(11762, 2992, 'Consumption Ratios', 'Consumption_Ratios', 'Brass 1.00 kg Zinc lump + 0.15 kg Copper lump = 0.10 kg Brass lump Bronze 0.50 kg Tin lump + 0.15 kg Copper lump = 0.10 kg Bronze lump Steel 0.20 kg Iron lump + 0.20 kg Charcoal = 0.40 kg Steel lump Electrum 0.10 kg Silver lump + 0.10 kg Gold lump = 0.10 kg Electrum lump. Note: Large lumps of both ingredients are easier to work with, as only the required portion is used with each successful creation.', '<ul><li>Brass\n<ul><li>1.00 kg Zinc lump + 0.15 kg Copper lump = 0.10 kg Brass lump</li></ul></li>\n<li>Bronze\n<ul><li>0.50 kg Tin lump + 0.15 kg Copper lump = 0.10 kg Bronze lump</li></ul></li>\n<li>Steel\n<ul><li>0.20 kg Iron lump + 0.20 kg Charcoal = 0.40 kg Steel lump</li></ul></li>\n<li>Electrum\n<ul><li>0.10 kg Silver lump + 0.10 kg Gold lump = 0.10 kg Electrum lump.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>Note: Large lumps of both ingredients are easier to work with, as only the required portion is used with each successful creation. \n</p>', 2),
(11763, 2992, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing > Metallurgy Body > Body control Body > Body strength', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; Metallurgy</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11764, 2992, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Smelter at 50 skill Metallurgist at 70 skill Master Metallurgist at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Smelter at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Metallurgist at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Metallurgist at 90 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(11765, 3170, 'Description', 'Description', 'Summon soul is a spell given to priests at 80 faith, although it requires 100 faith or linking to cast due to its 100 favor cost. The spell will summon (teleport) a player of your choice to your current location. They will need to be on the same server and will have to accept the summon. Does not work on servers with pvp enabled.', '<p><b>Summon soul</b> is a spell given to priests at 80 faith, although it requires 100 faith or <a href=\"/index.php/Linking\" title=\"Linking\">linking</a> to cast due to its 100 favor cost.\n</p>\n<p>The spell will summon (teleport) a player of your choice to your current location. They will need to be on the same <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Server\" title=\"Server\">server</a> and will have to accept the summon. Does not work on servers with <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pvp\" title=\"Pvp\">pvp</a> enabled.\n</p>', 0),
(11766, 3170, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click a tile . Select Spells > Summon soul', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Summon soul</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11817, 3171, 'Description', 'Description', 'Rift creatures are those creatures sent by the gods to fight at rifts and challenge the player\'s all. These creatures can only be found at active rifts and nowhere else in the lands of Wurm.', '<p>Rift creatures are those creatures sent by the gods to fight at rifts and challenge the player\'s all. \n</p>\n<p>These creatures can only be found at active rifts and nowhere else in the lands of Wurm.\n</p>', 0),
(11818, 3171, 'Rift beast', 'Rift_beast', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift beast', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Riftbeast.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"627\" data-file-width=\"679\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ae/Riftbeast.jpg/487px-Riftbeast.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/a/ae/Riftbeast.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"325\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 305px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift beast\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 1),
(11819, 3171, 'Rift ogre', 'Rift_ogre', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift ogre', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 366px\"><div style=\"width: 366px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 364px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Riftogre.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"793\" data-file-width=\"962\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/3d/Riftogre.jpg/546px-Riftogre.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/3d/Riftogre.jpg/819px-Riftogre.jpg 1.5x, /images/3/3d/Riftogre.jpg 2x\" width=\"364\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 344px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift ogre\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(11820, 3171, 'Rift ogre mage', 'Rift_ogre_mage', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift ogre mage', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 237.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 237.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 235.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Riftogremage.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"839\" data-file-width=\"658\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d6/Riftogremage.jpg/353px-Riftogremage.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d6/Riftogremage.jpg/529px-Riftogremage.jpg 1.5x, /images/d/d6/Riftogremage.jpg 2x\" width=\"236\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 216px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift ogre mage\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(11821, 3171, 'Rift caster', 'Rift_caster', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift caster ~Creature images coming~', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 448px\"><div style=\"width: 448px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 446px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rift_caster.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1045\" data-file-width=\"1552\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/29/Rift_caster.png/669px-Rift_caster.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/29/Rift_caster.png/1003px-Rift_caster.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/29/Rift_caster.png/1337px-Rift_caster.png 2x\" width=\"446\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 426px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift caster\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<ul><li>~Creature images coming~</li></ul>', 4),
(11822, 3171, 'Rift summoner', 'Rift_summoner', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift summoner', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 358.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 358.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 356.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Riftsummoner.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"903\" data-file-width=\"1074\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/6d/Riftsummoner.jpg/535px-Riftsummoner.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/6d/Riftsummoner.jpg/803px-Riftsummoner.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/6d/Riftsummoner.jpg/1071px-Riftsummoner.jpg 2x\" width=\"357\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 337px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift summoner\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 5),
(11823, 3171, 'Rift jackal', 'Rift_jackal', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Rift jackal', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 320.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Riftjackal.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"863\" data-file-width=\"923\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e0/Riftjackal.jpg/481px-Riftjackal.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e0/Riftjackal.jpg/722px-Riftjackal.jpg 1.5x, /images/e/e0/Riftjackal.jpg 2x\" width=\"321\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 301px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rift jackal\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 6),
(11824, 3171, 'Warmaster', 'Warmaster', 'Notes ~Creature notes coming~ Images Warmaster', '<p><b>Notes</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>~Creature notes coming~</li></ul>\n<p><b>Images</b>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 253.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 253.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 251.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Warmaster.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"756\" data-file-width=\"634\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/15/Warmaster.png/377px-Warmaster.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/15/Warmaster.png/566px-Warmaster.png 1.5x, /images/1/15/Warmaster.png 2x\" width=\"252\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 232px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Warmaster\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 7),
(11825, 3171, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Rift Fighting Death', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">Rift</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Death\" title=\"Death\">Death</a></li></ul>', 8),
(11850, 1535, 'Description', 'Description', 'This page explains completing tasks via the crafting window rather than manual crafting through the inventory.  To activate the crafting window select the far right button on the quickbar or enter the in-game options screen (default key is Esc) and select Crafting.', '<p>This page explains completing tasks via the crafting window rather than manual crafting through the inventory.  To activate the crafting window select the far right button on the <a href=\"/index.php/Quickbar\" title=\"Quickbar\">quickbar</a> or enter the in-game options screen (default key is Esc) and select Crafting.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(11851, 1535, 'Object Boxes', 'Object_Boxes', 'The upper section of the window focuses on the items or objects to be used in the crafting process.  Items may be added to these boxes by dragging them from an inventory window and releasing over one of the boxes or via the right-click menu on objects that cannot be picked up, such as tile borders or building walls.  Stacks of items may also be added by dragging the group header or by ctrl/shift selecting individual items before dragging. It is also possible to repair items in these boxes via the right-click menu. Clay When a clay item requires hand-moulding the hand button may be clicked (top left) one or more times to alternate which box the hand should be applied, if an object is already in one of the boxes the empty one will be populated.  If both boxes are in use then the leftmost box will be overwritten.  A hand may also be dragged and dropped from the body section of the inventory if this has been enabled. Large or fixed objects Large or non-inventory based items may be worked or continued upon in the window just as any other.  To add them to the boxes use the right-click interface on the object and add to crafting window .  An empty slot will be taken or the leftmost in the case of both being populated. Structures When the large or fixed object is a structure, you must drag the appropriate tool into the second box. The list will update to tell you the items you must have in your inventory in order to continue. When an object is used by the crafting window, it consumes the first available item of that type in your inventory, including items that are rare or better. Any item that you do not wish to be used in the crafting process should be removed from your inventory to prevent accidental use. Removing objects Clicking the red cross to the right of either box will remove whatever object has been assigned.  It is also possible to right click inside of the box and remove one or all items (in the case of a stack) from that box. Combining objects Selecting the button below the red cross will combine all items of the same type which have been entered into the box.  The total number of items in the stack are shown at the top right of the box.  Normal rules apply for combining objects such as the loss of spell effects, modifications to quality and monetary value. Statistics Quick statistics about the item are displayed in the areas below the item(s).', '<div class=\"floatright\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:CraftingWindowExpanded.jpg\"><img alt=\"CraftingWindowExpanded.jpg\" data-file-height=\"429\" data-file-width=\"643\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"429\" src=\"/images/b/ba/CraftingWindowExpanded.jpg\" width=\"643\"/></a></div>\n<p>The upper section of the window focuses on the items or objects to be used in the crafting process.  Items may be added to these boxes by dragging them from an inventory window and releasing over one of the boxes or via the right-click menu on objects that cannot be picked up, such as tile borders or building walls.  Stacks of items may also be added by dragging the group header or by ctrl/shift selecting individual items before dragging.\n</p>\n<p>It is also possible to repair items in these boxes via the right-click menu.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Clay\">Clay</span></h3>\n<p>When a clay item requires hand-moulding the hand button may be clicked (top left) one or more times to alternate which box the hand should be applied, if an object is already in one of the boxes the empty one will be populated.  If both boxes are in use then the leftmost box will be overwritten.  A hand may also be dragged and dropped from the body section of the inventory if this has been enabled.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Large_or_fixed_objects\">Large or fixed objects</span></h3>\n<p>Large or non-inventory based items may be worked or continued upon in the window just as any other.  To add them to the boxes use the right-click interface on the object and <i>add to crafting window</i>.  An empty slot will be taken or the leftmost in the case of both being populated.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Structures\">Structures</span></h3>\n<p>When the large or fixed object is a structure, you must drag the appropriate tool into the second box. The list will update to tell you the items you must have in your inventory in order to continue. When an object is used by the crafting window, it consumes the first available item of that type in your inventory, including items that are rare or better. Any item that you do not wish to be used in the crafting process should be removed from your inventory to prevent accidental use.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Removing_objects\">Removing objects</span></h3>\n<p>Clicking the red cross to the right of either box will remove whatever object has been assigned.  It is also possible to right click inside of the box and remove one or all items (in the case of a stack) from that box.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Combining_objects\">Combining objects</span></h3>\n<p>Selecting the button below the red cross will combine all items of the same type which have been entered into the box.  The total number of items in the stack are shown at the top right of the box.  Normal rules apply for <a href=\"/index.php/Combine\" title=\"Combine\">combining</a> objects such as the loss of spell effects, modifications to quality and monetary value.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statistics\">Statistics</span></h3>\n<p>Quick statistics about the item are displayed in the areas below the item(s).\n</p>', 1),
(11852, 1535, 'Crafting list', 'Crafting_list', 'The crafting list can be expanded by clicking the arrow to the middle right side of the window.  The list will show all possible crafts based on the items entered into the boxes, along with their craft probability based on your skills and the quality and damage of the items selected. Any items in red cannot yet be crafted by the character. Single clicking on any craftable item will add it to the middle box below the ingredients boxes. Double clicking on any item in the crafting list will automatically start crafting the item should all criteria be met (e.g. amount of source materials).', '<p>The crafting list can be expanded by clicking the arrow to the middle right side of the window.  The list will show all possible crafts based on the items entered into the boxes, along with their craft probability based on your skills and the quality and damage of the items selected.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Any items in red cannot yet be crafted by the character.</li>\n<li>Single clicking on any craftable item will add it to the middle box below the ingredients boxes.</li>\n<li>Double clicking on any item in the crafting list will automatically start crafting the item should all criteria be met (e.g. amount of source materials).</li></ul>', 2),
(11853, 1535, 'Action queue', 'Action_queue', 'The action queue is the last part to the main window which allows the player to control how many items will be attempted or how many actions will be taken when the create button is clicked or when an item is double clicked from the crafting list.  As with manual crafting the limit is based on the characters mind logic .  However it is possible to increase or decrease the number of attempts made up to and including the limit by selecting the up/down and min/max buttons. The number in the middle of the box shows the current and max number of actions permitted. The bar below is the progress indicator with description. The cancel button will end the current (not all) queue task, similar to the Esc button.', '<p>The <a href=\"/index.php/Action_queue\" title=\"Action queue\">action queue</a> is the last part to the main window which allows the player to control how many items will be attempted or how many actions will be taken when the <i>create</i> button is clicked or when an item is double clicked from the crafting list.  As with manual crafting the limit is based on the characters <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a>.  However it is possible to increase or decrease the number of attempts made up to and including the limit by selecting the up/down and min/max buttons.\n</p>\n<ul><li>The number in the middle of the box shows the current and max number of actions permitted.</li>\n<li>The bar below is the progress indicator with description.</li>\n<li>The <i>cancel</i> button will end the current (not all) queue task, similar to the Esc button.</li></ul>', 3),
(11854, 1535, 'Crafting Recipes', 'Crafting_Recipes', 'This is a pop-up list called by selecting the lower left hand button of the crafting window.  This displays all items that may be crafted regardless of the player skill, along with the skill required to make the item and the quantity required of each sub-item or ingredient. Search The search box in the lower left is set to default on search .  This will do a name search, finding all items that contain the word entered. Search category will look through the group headers and bring back all items belonging to that group. Search material will disregard the name and category but search for any items which are crafted using that material/tool as part of their recipe.  For example search using needle and all items which require a needle to complete or create them will be displayed. Navigation Double click a category/header to view only the recipes for that group.  There is no back button so bear that in mind when using search. Click the expand button (+) to drill down into its base parts, double clicking on any item will then enters the item name into the search box and runs the default search on the name.  No back button! Right click on an item at the top of the recipe tree to add starting items to crafting .  This cannot be done to sub-items; to do this first double click on the sub-item to make that the focus, then add.  Remember(!), there is no back button. Notes If the items required to begin or complete a craft are not available a message stating Your don\'t have that... will appear in both boxes on the main window. Some items are not included in the list such as the majority of alchemy recipes like healing covers or dyes , food related recipes or house walls, even though these may still be added and created via the crafting window.', '<p>This is a pop-up list called by selecting the lower left hand button of the crafting window.  This displays all items that may be crafted regardless of the player skill, along with the skill required to make the item and the quantity required of each sub-item or ingredient.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Search\">Search</span></h3>\n<ul><li>The search box in the lower left is set to default on <i>search</i>.  This will do a name search, finding all items that contain the word entered.</li>\n<li><i>Search category</i> will look through the group headers and bring back all items belonging to that group.</li>\n<li><i>Search material</i> will disregard the name and category but search for any items which are crafted using that material/tool as part of their recipe.  For example search using needle and all items which require a needle to complete or create them will be displayed.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Navigation\">Navigation</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Double click a category/header to view only the recipes for that group.  There is no back button so bear that in mind when using search.</li>\n<li>Click the expand button (+) to drill down into its base parts, double clicking on any item will then enters the item name into the search box and runs the default search on the name.  No back button!</li>\n<li>Right click on an item at the top of the recipe tree to <i>add starting items to crafting</i>.  This cannot be done to sub-items; to do this first double click on the sub-item to make that the focus, then add.  Remember(!), there is no back button.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h3>\n<ul><li>If the items required to begin or complete a craft are not available a message stating <i>Your don\'t have that...</i> will appear in both boxes on the main window.</li>\n<li>Some items are not included in the list such as the majority of <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> recipes like <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dyes</a>, food related recipes or house walls, even though these may still be added and created via the crafting window.</li></ul>', 4),
(11865, 3030, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small flask containing a syrupy golden substance.', '<p><i>A small flask containing a syrupy golden substance.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11866, 3030, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Potion created by mixing red dragon blood with source salt .', '<p>Potion created by mixing <a href=\"/index.php/Red_dragon\" title=\"Red dragon\">red dragon</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(11867, 3030, 'Imbuing', 'Imbuing', 'Activate the potion and right-click tool you want to imbue. Select \"Alchemy > Imbue\" from the menu.\nExamine the imbued tool to see what effect (ranging to 100) the imbue has on your tool. Improving ropemaking products using an imbued tool will be easier.', '<p>Activate the potion and right-click tool you want to imbue. Select \"Alchemy &gt; Imbue\" from the menu.\nExamine the imbued tool to see what effect (ranging to 100) the imbue has on your tool.\n</p>\n<p>Improving <a href=\"/index.php/Ropemaking\" title=\"Ropemaking\">ropemaking</a> products using an imbued tool will be easier.\n</p>', 2),
(11868, 3030, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Imbueing a rope tool will give you a bonus to QL creation. Power of the imbue effect will wear down slowly.', '<ul><li>Imbueing a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope_tool\" title=\"Rope tool\">rope tool</a> will give you a bonus to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> creation.</li>\n<li>Power of the imbue effect will wear down slowly.</li></ul>', 3),
(11869, 3191, 'Description', 'Description', 'Removes all beneficial spell effects from the target. Will not remove karma spell effects.', '<p>Removes all beneficial spell effects from the target. Will not remove karma spell effects.\n</p>', 0),
(11870, 3191, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette Right-click an item or person Select Spells > Purge', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click an item or person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Purge</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11874, 3193, 'Description', 'Description', 'Targets creatures. Deals 10,000 base damage and 300 bonus damage per power. Range of 12.5 tiles. Shares a spell resistance with Inferno and Worm brains .', '<p>Targets creatures. Deals 10,000 base damage and 300 bonus damage per power. Range of 12.5 tiles. Shares a spell resistance with <a href=\"/index.php/Inferno\" title=\"Inferno\">Inferno</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Worm_brains\" title=\"Worm brains\">Worm brains</a>.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(11875, 3193, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette Right-click an item or person Select Spells > Hypothermia', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click an item or person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Hypothermia</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11876, 3194, 'Description', 'Description', 'Deals 30,000 base damage and 75 bonus damage per power. Range of 12.5 tiles. Shares a spell resistance with Hypothermia and Worm brains .', '<p>Deals 30,000 base damage and 75 bonus damage per power. Range of 12.5 tiles. Shares a spell resistance with <a href=\"/index.php/Hypothermia\" title=\"Hypothermia\">Hypothermia</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Worm_brains\" title=\"Worm brains\">Worm brains</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(11877, 3194, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette Right-click an item or person Select Spells > Inferno', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click an item or person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Inferno</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11892, 3198, 'Description', 'Description', 'Heal is a spell gained at 40 faith by priests of Fo that grants the ability to heal oneself, a creature , or another player for a large amount of health. It costs 40 favor , has a difficulty of 30, and takes 29 seconds to cast. It heals between 40 to 200 total damage per cast, depending on the power of the cast, spread between multiple wounds if necessary. It has a range of 3 tiles.', '<p><b>Heal</b> is a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> gained at 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> by <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> that grants the ability to heal oneself, a <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creature</a>, or another <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> for a large amount of health. It costs 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a>, has a difficulty of 30, and takes 29 seconds to cast.\n</p>\n<p>It heals between 40 to 200 total damage per cast, depending on the power of the cast, spread between multiple wounds if necessary.\n</p>\n<p>It has a range of 3 tiles.\n</p>', 0),
(11893, 3198, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click one\'s body, a creature, or another player Select Spells > Heal', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click one\'s body, a creature, or another player</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Heal</i></li></ol>', 1),
(11894, 3198, 'Healing resistance', 'Healing_resistance', 'Healing spells and enchantments grant the healed player a healing resistance effect. This effect is applied based on how much health is healed, and will reduce all further healing on the target from any healing spells or enchantments. This includes healing spells as well as weapon enchantments that heal the player, such as Life transfer . The maximum duration of healing resistance is approximately 20 minutes, and the reduction scales linearly from that mark. For example, if you have 10 minutes of healing resistance remaining, you will receive heals at 50% normal effectiveness.', '<p>Healing spells and enchantments grant the healed <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> a healing resistance effect. This effect is applied based on how much health is healed, and will reduce all further healing on the target from any healing spells or enchantments. This includes healing spells as well as weapon enchantments that heal the player, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Life_transfer\" title=\"Life transfer\">Life transfer</a>.\n</p>\n<p>The maximum duration of healing resistance is approximately 20 minutes, and the reduction scales linearly from that mark. For example, if you have 10 minutes of healing resistance remaining, you will receive heals at 50% normal effectiveness.\n</p>', 2),
(11895, 3198, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Healing a Libila follower with a Fo healing spell will give the caster a severe faith penalty. Deals damage to zombie creatures.', '<ul><li>Healing a <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> follower with a Fo healing spell will give the caster a severe faith penalty.</li>\n<li>Deals damage to <a href=\"/index.php/Zombie\" title=\"Zombie\">zombie</a> creatures.</li></ul>', 3),
(11904, 1009, 'Description', 'Description', 'This fiery creature is rumoured to be the mounts of the demons of Sol.', '<p><i>This fiery creature is rumoured to be the mounts of the demons of Sol.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11905, 1009, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Counts as aggressive to tower guards and spirit templars . Even though red outlined they don\'t attack automatically, but they may attack unpredictably when not tamed. Rideable at 31 body control . As a mount they are ~5kmh faster than normal horses and more consistently use speed-related traits . Still attacks rider unless tamed. Recommended minimum skill for taming ~ 60, though it is possible to tame with difficulty at lower skill. Can be hitched up until the last aged stage . However, the hell horse will unhitch when they age up to Old at 30 months and become unruly. When tamed/ charmed : Can be cared for . Can be equipped like horses with saddle , bridle , horse shoes and barding . Has 35 body strength. Untamed hell horses hitched to a hitching post are docile and will not attack anything as long as they have food in their trough.', '<ul><li>Counts as aggressive to <a href=\"/index.php/Tower_guard\" title=\"Tower guard\">tower guards</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_templar\" title=\"Spirit templar\">spirit templars</a>.</li>\n<li>Even though red outlined they don\'t attack automatically, but they may attack unpredictably when not tamed.</li>\n<li>Rideable at 31 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">body control</a>.\n<ul><li>As a <a href=\"/index.php/Mounts\" title=\"Mounts\">mount</a> they are ~5kmh faster than normal <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a> and more consistently use speed-related <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Traits\" title=\"Traits\">traits</a>.</li>\n<li>Still attacks rider unless tamed.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Recommended minimum skill for <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_taming\" title=\"Animal taming\">taming</a> ~ 60, though it is possible to tame with difficulty at lower skill.</li>\n<li>Can be hitched up until <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">the last aged stage</a>. However, the hell horse will unhitch when they age up to Old at 30 months and become unruly.</li>\n<li>When tamed/<a href=\"/index.php/Charm_animal\" title=\"Charm animal\">charmed</a>:\n<ul><li>Can be <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry#caring\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">cared for</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be equipped like horses with <a href=\"/index.php/Saddle\" title=\"Saddle\">saddle</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bridle\" title=\"Bridle\">bridle</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Horse_shoe\" title=\"Horse shoe\">horse shoes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Barding\" title=\"Barding\">barding</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Has 35 body strength.</li>\n<li>Untamed hell horses hitched to a hitching post are docile and will not attack anything as long as they have food in their trough.</li></ul>', 1),
(11906, 1009, 'Breeding', 'Breeding', 'Bred hell horses have individual (but not unique) names randomly chosen at birth. They can have traits affecting their speed. Bred hell horses have 2 foal stages (young foal and adolescent foal) before they grow to young hell horses. All foals are bred, not wild. Color of bred hell horses will be inherited from their parents, with a very small chance of becoming an entirely different color at birth. Traits have a chance to be inherited from the parents. Both parents having a trait will help but does not guarantee that trait will be passed on.', '<ul><li>Bred hell horses have individual (but not unique) <a href=\"/index.php/Horse_names\" title=\"Horse names\">names</a> randomly chosen at birth. They can have traits affecting their speed.</li>\n<li>Bred hell horses have 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Foal\" title=\"Foal\">foal</a> stages (young foal and adolescent foal) before they grow to young hell horses. All foals are bred, not wild.</li>\n<li>Color of bred hell horses will be inherited from their parents, with a very small chance of becoming an entirely different color at birth.</li>\n<li>Traits have a chance to be inherited from the parents. Both parents having a trait will help but does not guarantee that trait will be passed on.</li></ul>', 2),
(11907, 1009, 'Colors', 'Colors', 'Hell horses can be found in a total of 8 colors, seen upon examining the creatures. Brown - Cinder Gold - Envious Black - Shadow White - Pestilential Grey - Ash Ebony Black - Molten - Gives a small speed boost (estimated at/near +2.5%) when riding (with speed traits) or pulling (with draft traits) Piebald Pinto - Nightshade Blood bay - Incandescent', '<p>Hell horses can be found in a total of 8 colors, seen upon examining the creatures. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\nBrown - Cinder  \n</p>\n<p>Gold - Envious \n</p>\n<p>Black - Shadow\n</p>\n<p>White - Pestilential  \n</p>\n<p>Grey - Ash  \n</p>\n<p>Ebony Black - Molten - Gives a small speed boost (estimated at/near +2.5%) when riding (with speed traits) or pulling (with draft traits) \n</p>\n<p>Piebald Pinto - Nightshade   \n</p>\n<p>Blood bay - Incandescent\n</p>', 3),
(11908, 1009, 'Combat', 'Combat', 'Hell horses deal burn damage with these attacks Kick. Bite Fire breath , 4 tile cone (Does not hurt rider.)', '<p>Hell horses deal burn damage with these attacks\n</p>\n<ul><li>Kick.</li>\n<li>Bite</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fire_breath\" title=\"Fire breath\">Fire breath</a>, 4 tile cone (Does not hurt rider.)</li></ul>', 4),
(11909, 1009, 'Images', 'Images', 'Cinder Envious Shadow Pestilential Ash Molten Nightshade Incandescent', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hellhorse_cinder.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/69/Hellhorse_cinder.jpeg/400px-Hellhorse_cinder.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/6/69/Hellhorse_cinder.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Cinder\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_horse_envious.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d5/Hell_horse_envious.jpeg/400px-Hell_horse_envious.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/d/d5/Hell_horse_envious.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Envious\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_horse_shadow.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/07/Hell_horse_shadow.jpeg/400px-Hell_horse_shadow.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/0/07/Hell_horse_shadow.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Shadow\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hellhorse_pestilential.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/49/Hellhorse_pestilential.jpeg/400px-Hellhorse_pestilential.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/4/49/Hellhorse_pestilential.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Pestilential\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_horse_ash.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/80/Hell_horse_ash.jpeg/400px-Hell_horse_ash.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/8/80/Hell_horse_ash.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Ash\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 269.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 269.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 267.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_horse_molten.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"374\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/6f/Hell_horse_molten.jpeg/401px-Hell_horse_molten.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/6/6f/Hell_horse_molten.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"268\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 248px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Molten\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_horse_nightshade.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/5c/Hell_horse_nightshade.jpeg/400px-Hell_horse_nightshade.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/5/5c/Hell_horse_nightshade.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Nightshade\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hellhorse_incandescent.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/24/Hellhorse_incandescent.jpeg/400px-Hellhorse_incandescent.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/2/24/Hellhorse_incandescent.jpeg 1.5x\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 247px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Incandescent\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 5),
(11910, 1009, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Horse names Horse', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse_names\" title=\"Horse names\">Horse names</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horse</a></li></ul>', 6),
(11911, 3165, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bright white unicorn with a slender twisted horn.', '<p><i>A bright white unicorn with a slender twisted horn.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11912, 3165, 'Breeding', 'Breeding', 'Bred unicorns have individual (but not unique) names randomly chosen at birth. They can have traits affecting their speed and other characteristics . Bred unicorns have 2 foal stages (young foal and adolescent foal) before they grow to young unicorns. Traits have a chance to be inherited from the parents. Both parents having a trait will help but does not guarantee that trait will be passed on.', '<ul><li>Bred unicorns have individual (but not unique) <a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn_names\" title=\"Unicorn names\">names</a> randomly chosen at birth. They can have traits affecting their speed and other <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_conditions\" title=\"Animal conditions\">characteristics</a>.</li>\n<li>Bred unicorns have 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Foal\" title=\"Foal\">foal</a> stages (young foal and adolescent foal) before they grow to young unicorns.</li>\n<li>Traits have a chance to be inherited from the parents. Both parents having a trait will help but does not guarantee that trait will be passed on.</li></ul>', 1),
(11913, 3165, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Unicorns are significantly faster than normal horses . Unicorns can be tamed with seeds, mixed grass, and other vegetation. A taming skill of 35+ is recommended for this, although successful taming has been seen at a taming skill of 13. 50 Taming (with 50 nature) appears to be the approximate cutoff where you will succeed taming actions more often than fail, allowing you to tame and maintain its status more effectively. Can be ridden when tame up to venerable stage, and can also hold a passenger. The passenger mount does not require any body control. Can be hitched up until the last aged stage . However, unicorns will unhitch when they age up to Old at 30 months and become unruly. Can be hitched when tamed, but will unhitch if it becomes untamed. Will be attacked by carnivorous animals and mobs. Have a body strength of 30. Can be equipped with saddle , bridle , and horse shoes (made of gold , silver , electrum or empyrean only) Unicorns spawn on grass , steppe , and mycelium tiles. Unicorns are highly resistant to disease and starvation/hunger issues faced by other animals while living in less than ideal conditions. They can still suffer from these issues but typically take much longer to experience them due to triggering conditions than most other animals.', '<ul><li>Unicorns are significantly faster than normal <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>.</li>\n<li>Unicorns can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> with seeds, mixed grass, and other vegetation. A taming skill of 35+ is recommended for this, although successful taming has been seen at a taming skill of 13.</li>\n<li>50 Taming (with 50 nature) appears to be the <i>approximate</i> cutoff where you will succeed taming actions more often than fail, allowing you to tame and maintain its status more effectively.</li>\n<li>Can be ridden when tame up to venerable stage, and can also hold a passenger. The passenger mount does not require any body control.</li>\n<li>Can be hitched up until the <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">last aged stage</a>. However, unicorns will unhitch when they age up to Old at 30 months and become unruly.</li>\n<li>Can be hitched when tamed, but will unhitch if it becomes untamed.</li>\n<li>Will be attacked by carnivorous animals and mobs.</li>\n<li>Have a body strength of 30.</li>\n<li>Can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Equip\" title=\"Equip\">equipped</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Saddle\" title=\"Saddle\">saddle</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bridle\" title=\"Bridle\">bridle</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Horse_shoe\" title=\"Horse shoe\">horse shoes</a> (made of <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">gold</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">silver</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Electrum_lump\" title=\"Electrum lump\">electrum</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Empyrean_lump\" title=\"Empyrean lump\">empyrean</a> only)</li>\n<li>Unicorns spawn on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Steppe\" title=\"Steppe\">steppe</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Mycelium\" title=\"Mycelium\">mycelium</a> tiles.</li>\n<li>Unicorns are highly resistant to disease and starvation/hunger issues faced by other animals while living in less than ideal conditions. They can still suffer from these issues but typically take much longer to experience them due to triggering conditions than most other animals.</li></ul>', 2),
(11914, 3165, 'Images', 'Images', 'Unicorn in the wild', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 382.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 382.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 380.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Unicorn.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"529\" data-file-width=\"805\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c4/Unicorn.jpg/571px-Unicorn.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/c/c4/Unicorn.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"381\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 361px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Unicorn in the wild\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(11915, 3165, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Unicorn names', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Unicorn_names\" title=\"Unicorn names\">Unicorn names</a></li></ul>', 4),
(11916, 2963, 'Description', 'Description', 'Each character is given a list of goals upon creation. These goals are randomly chosen from a pool and range from very simple to extremely difficult. To access personal goals, open the main menu and click on \"Hud settings\". From here, click on \"Personal Goals Window\".', '<p>Each character is given a list of goals upon creation. These goals are randomly chosen from a pool and range from very simple to extremely difficult.\n</p>\n<p>To access personal goals, open the main menu and click on \"Hud settings\". From here, click on \"Personal Goals Window\".\n</p>', 0),
(11917, 2963, 'Winning The Game', 'Winning_The_Game', 'Upon completion of all of a player\'s personal goals, they will receive a special title - Winner . They will then receive a random special item and will have their achievement announced and recorded in a number of places including on Twitter, Niarja, and in Global. Possible Item Rewards Any Sorcery item (except Key to the Heavens) Wand of the seas Huge egg', '<p>Upon completion of all of a player\'s personal goals, they will receive a special title - <b>Winner</b>. They will then receive a random special item and will have their achievement announced and recorded in a number of places including on Twitter, Niarja, and in Global.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Possible_Item_Rewards\">Possible Item Rewards</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Any Sorcery item (except Key to the Heavens)</li>\n<li>Wand of the seas</li>\n<li>Huge egg</li></ul>', 1),
(11918, 2963, 'List of Goals', 'List_of_Goals', 'This list is a work in progress. Name Rarity Destroy a structure by catapulting it Silver Defeat another player by using a huge club Silver Catch 200 Fish Silver Bake 20 loaves of bread Silver Create a fantastic item Diamond Pilot a Caravel Silver Pilot a Knarr Silver Plant 200 trees Silver Try swimming a bit Silver Slay the Forest Giant Gold Pilot a Rowboat Silver Create a supreme item Gold Take some falling damage Silver Join a settlement Silver Kill a Wolf Silver Finish the tutorial Silver Wear a ring, a necklace and a bracelet at the same time Silver Help in an Epic mission Silver Kill a Cave Bug Silver Pilot a Cog Silver Kill a Deer Silver Build a Knarr Silver Kill a Mountain Lion Silver Kill an Angry creature Silver Be overly forthcoming Silver Catch 1000 fish Gold Get out into the deep sea Silver Build a Sailboat Silver Kill 50 Zombies Gold Defeat another player using a crush weapon Silver Scare ten hens to death Silver Defeat another player using an axe Silver Climb up a really really high mountain Silver Kill 100 Lava Fiends Silver Build a Rowboat Silver Kill 20 Crocodile Silver Plant 200 hedges or flower beds Silver Kill a Fierce creature Silver Slay a bison Silver Improve an item beyond quality level 99 Diamond Slay the Goblin leader Gold Eat some really high quality food Silver Improve an item beyond your knowledge at quality level 30+ Silver Catch a cold Silver Kill 20 Lava Fiends Silver Kill an Alert creature Silver Pick 20 mushrooms Silver Kill a Greenish creature Silver Kill a Slow creature Silver Mine an exquisite gemstone Gold Kill the Cyclops Silver Kill a Raging creature Silver Kill a Lava Fiend Silver Improve an item beyond quality level 50 Silver Put 100 items in the trash bin Silver Repair 6250 fences, floors or walls Diamond Ride 4000 tiles in one session Silver Kill a Troll Silver Cut down a tree using a shovel Silver Cut down 1000 trees Silver Pilot a Rowboat and a Sailboat Silver Bury a corpse Silver Kill a Zombie Silver Repair 50 fences, floors or walls Silver Kill a Lurking creature Silver Slay the Troll King Gold Plant 5000 trees Gold Travel 500 tiles in one session Silver Build a well at a suitable spot Silver Kill a Unicorn Silver Slay a goblin Silver Smith a sword, a maul, an axe and a shield Silver Kill 100 Unicorns Silver Create a rare item Silver Slay a Hell Horse Silver Create 5000 liters of wine Diamond Slay a demon Silver Slay an incarnation of Libila Gold Slay an incarnation of Libila Gold Pie-maker Silver Perform 100000 actions Gold', '<p>This list is a work in progress.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"350\">Name\n</th>\n<th width=\"50\">Rarity\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Destroy a structure by catapulting it\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Defeat another player by using a huge club\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Catch 200 Fish\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bake 20 loaves of bread\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create a fantastic item\n</td>\n<td>Diamond\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pilot a Caravel\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pilot a Knarr\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plant 200 trees\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Try swimming a bit\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay the Forest Giant\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pilot a Rowboat\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create a supreme item\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Take some falling damage\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Join a settlement\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Wolf\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finish the tutorial\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wear a ring, a necklace and a bracelet at the same time\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Help in an Epic mission\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Cave Bug\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pilot a Cog\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Deer\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Build a Knarr\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Mountain Lion\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill an Angry creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Be overly forthcoming\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Catch 1000 fish\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get out into the deep sea\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Build a Sailboat\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill 50 Zombies\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Defeat another player using a crush weapon\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scare ten hens to death\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Defeat another player using an axe\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Climb up a really really high mountain\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill 100 Lava Fiends\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Build a Rowboat\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill 20 Crocodile\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plant 200 hedges or flower beds\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Fierce creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay a bison\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Improve an item beyond quality level 99\n</td>\n<td>Diamond\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay the Goblin leader\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eat some really high quality food\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Improve an item beyond your knowledge at quality level 30+\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Catch a cold\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill 20 Lava Fiends\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill an Alert creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pick 20 mushrooms\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Greenish creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Slow creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mine an exquisite gemstone\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill the Cyclops\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Raging creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Lava Fiend\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Improve an item beyond quality level 50\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Put 100 items in the trash bin\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Repair 6250 fences, floors or walls\n</td>\n<td>Diamond\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ride 4000 tiles in one session\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Troll\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cut down a tree using a shovel\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cut down 1000 trees\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pilot a Rowboat and a Sailboat\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bury a corpse\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Zombie\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Repair 50 fences, floors or walls\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Lurking creature\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay the Troll King\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plant 5000 trees\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Travel 500 tiles in one session\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Build a well at a suitable spot\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a Unicorn\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay a goblin\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Smith a sword, a maul, an axe and a shield\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill 100 Unicorns\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create a rare item\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay a Hell Horse\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create 5000 liters of wine\n</td>\n<td>Diamond\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay a demon\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay an incarnation of Libila\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slay an incarnation of Libila\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pie-maker\n</td>\n<td>Silver\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Perform 100000 actions\n</td>\n<td>Gold\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>', 2),
(11919, 2963, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Guides:Personal goals|Personal goals guide - Contains more detailed information on the personal goal system and rewards.', '<ul><li>Guides:Personal goals|Personal goals guide - Contains more detailed information on the personal goal system and rewards.</li></ul>', 3),
(11920, 3207, 'Description', 'Description', 'A walnut tree is a lumber and nut-bearing tree.', '<p>A walnut tree is a lumber and nut-bearing tree. \n</p>', 0),
(11921, 3207, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Walnuts come into season on these trees during weeks 1 through 4 of the starfall of Dancers and can then be harvested using a sickle. Prior to being in season, the message when the tree is examined will be: The walnuts will soon be ripe. Charcoal piles made from walnut will give a 10% bonus on the quality of the items it produces.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Walnuts\" title=\"Walnuts\">Walnuts</a> come into season on these trees during weeks 1 through 4 of the starfall of Dancers and can then be harvested using a sickle.</li>\n<li>Prior to being in season, the message when the tree is examined will be: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The walnuts will soon be ripe.  </span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal_pile\" title=\"Charcoal pile\">Charcoal piles</a> made from walnut will give a 10% bonus on the quality of the items it produces.</li></ul>', 1),
(11922, 3207, 'Images', 'Images', 'Walnut tree while in season', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 380px\"><div style=\"width: 380px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 378px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"974\" data-file-width=\"1228\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d1/Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg/567px-Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d1/Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg/851px-Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/d1/Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg/1135px-Walnut_tree_nuts.jpg 2x\" width=\"378\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 358px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Walnut tree while in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(11923, 3208, 'Description', 'Description', 'No known use for Chestnut trees yet except for lumber and harvesting Chestnuts .', '<p>No known use for Chestnut trees yet except for lumber and harvesting <a href=\"/index.php/Chestnuts\" title=\"Chestnuts\">Chestnuts</a>.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(11924, 3208, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Chestnuts can be harvested from the tree using a sickle during the appropriate season . These can be eaten and using in cooking recipes. When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: The tree has some interesting chestnuts.', '<ul><li>Chestnuts can be harvested from the tree using a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> during the appropriate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>. These can be eaten and using in cooking recipes.</li>\n<li>When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining:  <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The tree has some interesting chestnuts.  </span></li></ul>', 1),
(11925, 3208, 'Images', 'Images', 'Chestnut tree in season', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 334px\"><div style=\"width: 334px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 332px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Chestnut_tree_fruit.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"984\" data-file-width=\"1089\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/25/Chestnut_tree_fruit.png/498px-Chestnut_tree_fruit.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/25/Chestnut_tree_fruit.png/747px-Chestnut_tree_fruit.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/25/Chestnut_tree_fruit.png/996px-Chestnut_tree_fruit.png 2x\" width=\"332\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 312px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Chestnut tree in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(11926, 3209, 'Description', 'Description', 'A few handfuls of wheat. Wheat is pretty sensitive as a crop. It is normally used to turn into flour and bake with or to sow with.', '<p><i>A few handfuls of wheat. Wheat is pretty sensitive as a crop. It is normally used to turn into flour and bake with or to sow with.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11927, 3209, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wheat is a crop that can be milled to make flour for baking bread, or to tame and feed animals like hens or horses . Wheat can be used in healing covers with a potency of 1. Wheat can be found by botanizing from wild grasses resource nodes .', '<ul><li>Wheat is a <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">crop</a> that can be <a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">milled</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Flour\" title=\"Flour\">flour</a> for baking bread, or to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tame</a> and feed animals like <a href=\"/index.php/Hen\" title=\"Hen\">hens</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>.</li>\n<li>Wheat can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> with a potency of 1.</li>\n<li>Wheat can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_grasses\" title=\"Wild grasses\">wild grasses</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">resource nodes</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11928, 3210, 'What is an Impalong', 'What_is_an_Impalong', 'Impalongs are community events where many players gather to improve items, enchant weapons and tools, sermon, play games and have fun!\nHigher skilled players volunteer their time and skills to improve / enchant items for lower skilled players to aid them in their journey into this challenging world we all call home. Players or Alliances host an event for other players to come by and get items improved, usually to at least 70ql. Players that have priests also gather to have sermon circles and enchant weapons and tools, usually near the improving area. Some Impalongs offer lodging for staff, players and alts. Setting up Planning an Impalong takes a lot of time and resources. The Deeds are made to have access from water and land for easy travels. The main building houses the Forges , Ovens , Kilns , Altars , and storage containers for resources and items. Secured rooms providing bed(s) and storage, usually reserved ahead of time for proper permissions. Materials are gathered and stored in the hundreds sometimes thousands in a warehouse to be used throughout the event. Arenas and event areas are recommended for GMs to spawn creatures and have giveaways. Docks, enchanted fields, and Campgrounds (for tents) are recommended for travelers. Posting on the forums with a date, location, and a general idea of what will be happening at event. The Event Opening day, and how things work. Volunteered players ranging from all skills are assigned their improving range and stations. Players rename their items to their own name to be easily identified and then placed into the proper container to be improved. Items are enchanted depending on the availability of priests. Typical Games Players make up games to be played and are sometimes given prizes based on winning or answering correctly. You Got Fished Each player equips a fish and starts to duel, when the fish hits a specified body part, they win. Scavenger Hunt Several clues are hidden around the area of the impalong and players have to follow them to get to the end. Trivia Players are asked random trivia and first person to correctly responds wins. Devs and their shenanigans Enki and his minions Death is always around the corner Forge setup, everyone monkeying around', '<p>Impalongs are community events where many players gather to improve items, enchant weapons and tools, sermon, play games and have fun!\nHigher skilled players volunteer their time and skills to improve / enchant items for lower skilled players to aid them in their journey into this challenging world we all call home.\n</p>\n<p>Players or Alliances host an event for other players to come by and get items improved, usually to at least 70ql. Players that have priests also gather to have <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">sermon</a> circles and enchant weapons and tools, usually near the improving area. Some Impalongs offer lodging for staff, players and alts.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Setting_up\">Setting up</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Planning an Impalong takes a lot of time and resources.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">Deeds</a> are made to have access from water and land for easy travels.</li>\n<li>The main building houses the <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Ovens</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">Kilns</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">Altars</a>, and storage containers for resources and items.</li>\n<li>Secured rooms providing bed(s) and storage, usually reserved ahead of time for proper permissions.</li>\n<li>Materials are gathered and stored in the hundreds sometimes thousands in a warehouse to be used throughout the event.</li>\n<li>Arenas and event areas are recommended for GMs to spawn creatures and have giveaways.</li>\n<li>Docks, enchanted fields, and Campgrounds (for tents) are recommended for travelers.</li>\n<li>Posting on the forums with a date, location, and a general idea of what will be happening at event.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Event\">The Event</span></h3>\n<p><i>Opening day, and how things work.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Volunteered players ranging from all skills are assigned their improving range and stations.</li>\n<li>Players rename their items to their own name to be easily identified and then placed into the proper container to be improved.</li>\n<li>Items are enchanted depending on the availability of priests.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Typical_Games\">Typical Games</span></h3>\n<p><i>Players make up games to be played and are sometimes given prizes based on winning or answering correctly.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>You Got Fished</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>Each player equips a fish and starts to duel, when the fish hits a specified body part, they win.</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>Scavenger Hunt</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>Several clues are hidden around the area of the impalong and players have to follow them to get to the end.</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>Trivia</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>Players are asked random trivia and first person to correctly responds wins.</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:252px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Impalong_2018.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"751\" data-file-width=\"806\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"233\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/51/Impalong_2018.png/250px-Impalong_2018.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/51/Impalong_2018.png/375px-Impalong_2018.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/51/Impalong_2018.png/500px-Impalong_2018.png 2x\" width=\"250\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Impalong_2018.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Devs and their shenanigans</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:327px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Enki_and_the_minions.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"865\" data-file-width=\"1429\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"197\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/49/Enki_and_the_minions.png/325px-Enki_and_the_minions.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/49/Enki_and_the_minions.png/488px-Enki_and_the_minions.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/49/Enki_and_the_minions.png/650px-Enki_and_the_minions.png 2x\" width=\"325\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Enki_and_the_minions.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Enki and his minions</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"center\"><div class=\"thumb tnone\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:352px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Champ_dev_spiders.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"570\" data-file-width=\"1293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"154\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4f/Champ_dev_spiders.png/350px-Champ_dev_spiders.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/4f/Champ_dev_spiders.png/525px-Champ_dev_spiders.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/4f/Champ_dev_spiders.png/700px-Champ_dev_spiders.png 2x\" width=\"350\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Champ_dev_spiders.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Death is always around the corner</div></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"center\"><div class=\"thumb tnone\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Impalong,_monkeyin_around.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"675\" data-file-width=\"931\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"218\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/a7/Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png/300px-Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/a7/Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png/450px-Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/a7/Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png/600px-Impalong%2C_monkeyin_around.png 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Impalong,_monkeyin_around.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Forge setup, everyone monkeying around</div></div></div></div>', 0),
(11932, 1301, 'Fir Tree', 'Fir_Tree', 'No known use for Fir trees yet except for lumber.', '<p>No known use for Fir trees yet except for lumber.\n</p>', 0),
(11935, 1302, 'Description', 'Description', 'No known use for Linden trees yet except for lumber.', '<p>No known use for Linden trees yet except for lumber.\n</p>', 0),
(11938, 3217, 'Description', 'Description', 'The mask is made of light materials with a luxurious finish.', '<p><i>The mask is made of light materials with a luxurious finish.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11939, 3217, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A cosmetic item that was awarded to players during challenge server rounds. This item is also possible to be obtained discovering mask fragments with archaeology and reconstructing the mask with restoration .', '<ul><li>A cosmetic item that was awarded to players during challenge server rounds.</li>\n<li>This item is also possible to be obtained discovering mask fragments with <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> and reconstructing the mask with <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(11964, 3220, 'Description', 'Description', 'A simple yet functional cloth barding that will provide moderate protection, made in a way that allows colors.', '<p><i>A simple yet functional cloth barding that will provide moderate protection, made in a way that allows colors.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(11965, 3220, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'At 51 cloth tailoring skill, there is a 57% creation chance. Each failed creation attempt uses up 1.20 kg of cloth. Dyeing the main body of the barding using the \"Paint\" option uses 592 g of dye. Dyeing the pattern uses 177 g of dye. As it is made of cloth , it does very little to protect a horse. It is best used as decoration. Slows the mount a very small amount.', '<ul><li>At 51 <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> skill, there is a 57% creation chance. Each failed creation attempt uses up 1.20 kg of cloth.</li>\n<li>Dyeing the main body of the barding using the \"Paint\" option uses 592 g of dye. Dyeing the pattern uses 177 g of dye.</li>\n<li>As it is made of <a href=\"/index.php/Square_piece_of_cloth\" title=\"Square piece of cloth\">cloth</a>, it does very little to protect a horse. It is best used as decoration.</li>\n<li>Slows the mount a very small amount.</li></ul>', 1),
(11966, 3220, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Barding', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Barding\" title=\"Barding\">Barding</a>\n</p>', 2),
(11970, 3224, 'Features', 'Features', 'Shorter action times Highly increased skill gain Spawn with higher initial skills and selectable loadout', '<ul><li>Shorter action times</li>\n<li>Highly increased skill gain</li>\n<li>Spawn with higher initial skills and selectable loadout</li></ul>', 0),
(11971, 3224, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Characters are being moved back to Golden Valley after the rounds end. Winners of a prize will receive a tradeable code which can be redeemed in-game.', '<ul><li>Characters are being moved back to Golden Valley after the rounds end.</li>\n<li>Winners of a prize will receive a tradeable code which can be redeemed in-game.</li></ul>', 1),
(11972, 3225, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a portcullis.', '<p><i>You see a portcullis. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(11973, 3225, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11974, 3225, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Rounded stone portcullis (fence) with Rounded stone. Each Rounded stone will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. Intelligent monsters such as trolls are able to open unlocked gates. Gates can be locked with a gate lock , then controlled by deed permissions if applicable, as well as the key .', '<ul><li>Repair Rounded stone portcullis (fence) with Rounded stone. Each Rounded stone will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Intelligent monsters such as <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a> are able to open unlocked gates.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gates can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a>, then controlled by deed <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> if applicable, as well as the <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">key</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(11975, 3225, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11976, 3226, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a portcullis.', '<p><i>You see a portcullis. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(11977, 3226, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11978, 3226, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Sandstone portcullis (fence) with Sandstone brick. Each Sandstone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. Intelligent monsters such as trolls are able to open unlocked gates. Gates can be locked with a gate lock , then controlled by deed permissions if applicable, as well as the key .', '<ul><li>Repair Sandstone portcullis (fence) with Sandstone brick. Each Sandstone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Intelligent monsters such as <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a> are able to open unlocked gates.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gates can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a>, then controlled by deed <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> if applicable, as well as the <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">key</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(11979, 3226, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11980, 3227, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a portcullis.', '<p><i>You see a portcullis. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(11981, 3227, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11982, 3227, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Marble portcullis (fence) with Marble brick. Each Marble brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. Intelligent monsters such as trolls are able to open unlocked gates. Gates can be locked with a gate lock , then controlled by deed permissions if applicable, as well as the key .', '<ul><li>Repair Marble portcullis (fence) with Marble brick. Each Marble brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Intelligent monsters such as <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a> are able to open unlocked gates.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gates can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a>, then controlled by deed <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> if applicable, as well as the <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">key</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(11983, 3227, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(11984, 3228, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a portcullis.', '<p><i>You see a portcullis. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(11985, 3228, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(11986, 3228, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Rendered portcullis (fence) with clay. Each clay will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall. Intelligent monsters such as trolls are able to open unlocked gates. Gates can be locked with a gate lock , then controlled by deed permissions if applicable, as well as the key .', '<ul><li>Repair Rendered portcullis (fence) with clay. Each clay will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Intelligent monsters such as <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a> are able to open unlocked gates.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Gates can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a>, then controlled by deed <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> if applicable, as well as the <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">key</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
