(12028, 3246, 'Description', 'Description', 'An insect that lives on the moon Jackal .', '<p>An insect that lives on the moon <a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(12029, 3246, 'Notes', 'Notes', '', '', 1),
(12033, 3248, 'Description', 'Description', 'A perfectly black pearl.', '<p><i>A perfectly black pearl.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(12034, 3248, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Black pearls are only known to be produced by clams , and handily enough, the snowman statue on seldom occasion. They are very rare. The likelihood of harvesting a black pearl is largely skill-based. Higher fishing skill brings a much better chance. Black pearls can be made into pearl necklaces .', '<ul><li>Black pearls are only known to be produced by <a href=\"/index.php/Clam\" title=\"Clam\">clams</a>, and handily enough, the <a href=\"/index.php/Snowman_statue\" title=\"Snowman statue\">snowman statue</a> on seldom occasion. They are very rare.</li>\n<li>The likelihood of harvesting a black pearl is largely skill-based. Higher fishing skill brings a much better chance.</li>\n<li>Black pearls can be made into <a href=\"/index.php/Pearl_necklace\" title=\"Pearl necklace\">pearl necklaces</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(12035, 3137, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bit of cheese, ideal for fishing bait.', '<p><i>A bit of cheese, ideal for fishing bait.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(12036, 3137, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used as bait for fishing . Can be kept in a tackle box .', '<ul><li>Used as <a href=\"/index.php/Bait\" title=\"Bait\">bait</a> for <a href=\"/index.php/Fishing\" title=\"Fishing\">fishing</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be kept in a <a href=\"/index.php/Tackle_box\" title=\"Tackle box\">tackle box</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(12037, 3250, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large crustacean found only on the moon Jackal .', '<p>A large crustacean found only on the moon <a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(12038, 3250, 'Notes', 'Notes', '', '', 1),
(12039, 2618, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall', '<p><i>You see a wall </i>\n</p>', 0),
(12040, 2618, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(12041, 2618, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Marble brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Marble wall . Continuation requires at least 1 Marble brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">Marble brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Marble wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">Marble brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(12042, 2618, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(12043, 2618, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Marble brick before improving it. Activate a Marble brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Marble brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">Marble brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">Marble brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_brick\" title=\"Marble brick\">Marble brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(12044, 2618, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Marble wall Marble window Marble door Marble double door Marble oriel Marble narrow window Marble portcullis Marble barred wall Marble arched wall Marble T arch Marble arch right Marble arch left', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Marble wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_window\" title=\"Marble window\">Marble window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_door\" title=\"Marble door\">Marble door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_double_door\" title=\"Marble double door\">Marble double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_oriel\" title=\"Marble oriel\">Marble oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_narrow_window\" title=\"Marble narrow window\">Marble narrow window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Marble portcullis (wall)\">Marble portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_barred_wall\" title=\"Marble barred wall\">Marble barred wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_arched_wall\" title=\"Marble arched wall\">Marble arched wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_T_arch\" title=\"Marble T arch\">Marble T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_arch_right\" title=\"Marble arch right\">Marble arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Marble_arch_left\" title=\"Marble arch left\">Marble arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(12054, 3051, 'Description', 'Description', 'In loving memory of our friend and developer, Tich. You can barely make out the signature of its maker ___. A statue of a much beloved player and contributor stands in eternal remembrance.', '<p><i>In loving memory of our friend and developer, Tich. You can barely make out the signature of its maker ___.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A statue of a much beloved player and contributor stands in eternal remembrance.\n</p>', 0),
(12055, 3051, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A marble version of the Statue of Tich is created through stone cutting work, or by combining 80 archaeology fragments . A metallic version of the Statue of Tich is created via the assembly of 80 archaeology fragments . Statues can be improved with marble shards and stone chisel if marble, or the corresponding metal, if the metal version. Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>A marble version of the Statue of Tich is created through stone cutting work, or by combining 80 archaeology <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragments\" title=\"Fragments\">fragments</a>.</li>\n<li>A metallic version of the Statue of Tich is created via the assembly of 80 archaeology <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragments\" title=\"Fragments\">fragments</a>.</li>\n<li>Statues can be improved with <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_shards\" title=\"Marble shards\">marble shards</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a> if marble, or the corresponding metal, if the metal version.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\', \'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(12056, 3192, 'Description', 'Description', 'Enchant that serves as Libila’s version of Life transfer . However, the healing done is only 1/3rd of what Fo’s Life transfer grants. To counterbalance, Essence drain also deals a wound at 10% of base damage as internal damage to creature.', '<p>Enchant that serves as Libila’s version of <a href=\"/index.php/Life_transfer\" title=\"Life transfer\">Life transfer</a>. However, the healing done is only 1/3rd of what Fo’s Life transfer grants. To counterbalance, Essence drain also deals a wound at 10% of base damage as internal damage to creature.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(12057, 3192, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This spell will stack with Blessings of the dark , Circle of cunning , Demise spells , Mind stealer , Nimbleness , and Wind of ages . This spell will not stack with Bloodthirst , Flaming aura , Frostbrand , Rotting touch , Venom , or Life transfer', '<ul><li>This spell will stack with <a href=\"/index.php/Blessings_of_the_dark\" title=\"Blessings of the dark\">Blessings of the dark</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Circle_of_cunning\" title=\"Circle of cunning\">Circle of cunning</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Demise_spells\" title=\"Demise spells\">Demise spells</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_stealer\" title=\"Mind stealer\">Mind stealer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Nimbleness\" title=\"Nimbleness\">Nimbleness</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_ages\" title=\"Wind of ages\">Wind of ages</a>.</li>\n<li>This spell will <b>not</b> stack with <a href=\"/index.php/Bloodthirst\" title=\"Bloodthirst\">Bloodthirst</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Flaming_aura\" title=\"Flaming aura\">Flaming aura</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Frostbrand\" title=\"Frostbrand\">Frostbrand</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rotting_touch\" title=\"Rotting touch\">Rotting touch</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Venom\" title=\"Venom\">Venom</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Life_transfer\" title=\"Life transfer\">Life transfer</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(12058, 3192, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette Right-click an item or person Select Spells > Essence Drain', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click an item or person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Essence Drain</i></li></ol>', 2),
(12059, 2346, 'Description', 'Description', 'Usually only encountered under foggy conditions, this creature is often considered an Omen. The Fog spider is a dangerous, aggressive insect with eight legs and an appetite for players .', '<p><i>Usually only encountered under foggy conditions, this creature is often considered an Omen.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The Fog spider is a dangerous, aggressive <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">insect</a> with eight legs and an appetite for <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">players</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(12060, 2346, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Fog spiders run as fast as a player with no load. Younger and older spiders are slower. All spiders are known to pursue players for quite a distance. Fog spiders can teleport and phase through fences and walls. [16:46:48] Aged fog spider phases! Fog spiders have stun attacks and deal poison wounds. Fog spiders drop 1 kg of water upon death, which has no side effects when drinking. It is found in the corpse . Fog spiders were introduced into the game in late 2015 to honor former Game Master Oracle . He was known for teasing players in kingdom chat with warnings about (then fictional) fog spiders and then setting fog to near blackout levels.[ [1] ]', '<ul><li>Fog spiders run as fast as a player with no load. Younger and older spiders are slower.</li>\n<li>All spiders are known to pursue players for quite a distance.</li>\n<li>Fog spiders can teleport and phase through fences and walls. <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> [16:46:48] Aged fog spider phases! </span></li>\n<li>Fog spiders have stun attacks and deal poison wounds.</li>\n<li>Fog spiders drop 1 kg of water upon death, which has no side effects when drinking. It is found in the <a href=\"/index.php/Corpse\" title=\"Corpse\">corpse</a>.</li>\n<li>Fog spiders were introduced into the game in late 2015 to honor former Game Master <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Oracle\" title=\"Player:Oracle\">Oracle</a>. He was known for teasing players in kingdom chat with warnings about (then fictional) fog spiders and then setting fog to near blackout levels.[<a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/136026-news-89-watch-out-for-the-foggz\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>]</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Fogspider1.jpg\"><img alt=\"Fogspider1.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"576\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"169\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4e/Fogspider1.jpg/300px-Fogspider1.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/4e/Fogspider1.jpg/450px-Fogspider1.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/4e/Fogspider1.jpg/600px-Fogspider1.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Fogspider1.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div>', 1),
(12061, 2346, 'Fighting Tips', 'Fighting_Tips', 'Fog spiders, like all other animals, become stronger and bigger as they age. A young fog spider is weak, and does not aim well for the head. Older fog spiders are strong, cause a lot of damage per hit, and will aim for the head. (They also focus with more success)', '<ul><li>Fog spiders, like all other animals, become stronger and bigger as they age.</li>\n<li>A young fog spider is weak, and does not aim well for the head.</li>\n<li>Older fog spiders are strong, cause a lot of damage per hit, and will aim for the head. (They also focus with more success)</li></ul>', 2),
(12062, 2346, 'Phobia', 'Phobia', 'Spider graphics can be turned into blobs for those suffering from arachnophobia. To activate this, enable Phobia Mode in the advanced graphics tab before logging in to Wurm Online.', '<ul><li>Spider graphics can be turned into blobs for those suffering from arachnophobia. To activate this, enable Phobia Mode in the advanced graphics tab before logging in to Wurm Online.</li></ul>', 3),
(12115, 1561, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bridge made out of one of the types of bricks: marble, pottery, rendered, rounded, slate, or stone. It can be flat or arched.', '<p>A bridge made out of one of the types of bricks: marble, pottery, rendered, rounded, slate, or stone. It can be flat or arched. \n</p>', 0),
(12116, 1561, 'Parts of the bridge', 'Parts_of_the_bridge', 'Brick bridge - abutment Brick bridge - bracing Brick bridge - crown Brick bridge - double abutment Brick bridge - double bracing Brick bridge - floating Brick bridge - support Stone keystone', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_abutment\" title=\"Brick bridge - abutment\">Brick bridge - abutment</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_bracing\" title=\"Brick bridge - bracing\">Brick bridge - bracing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_crown\" title=\"Brick bridge - crown\">Brick bridge - crown</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_double_abutment\" title=\"Brick bridge - double abutment\">Brick bridge - double abutment</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_double_bracing\" title=\"Brick bridge - double bracing\">Brick bridge - double bracing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_floating\" title=\"Brick bridge - floating\">Brick bridge - floating</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brick_bridge_-_support\" title=\"Brick bridge - support\">Brick bridge - support</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_keystone\" title=\"Stone keystone\">Stone keystone</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(12117, 1561, 'Images', 'Images', 'Example of Brick Bridge, Rendered Version Example of Marble Brick Bridge Example of Slate Brick Bridge', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Brickbridge.1304.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/3c/Brickbridge.1304.jpg/800px-Brickbridge.1304.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/3c/Brickbridge.1304.jpg/1200px-Brickbridge.1304.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/3c/Brickbridge.1304.jpg/1600px-Brickbridge.1304.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 514px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Example of Brick Bridge, Rendered Version\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Marblebrickbridge.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/99/Marblebrickbridge.jpg/800px-Marblebrickbridge.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/99/Marblebrickbridge.jpg/1200px-Marblebrickbridge.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/9/99/Marblebrickbridge.jpg/1600px-Marblebrickbridge.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 514px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Example of Marble Brick Bridge\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 535.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 533.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Slatebrickbridge.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"1080\" data-file-width=\"1920\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7e/Slatebrickbridge.jpg/800px-Slatebrickbridge.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7e/Slatebrickbridge.jpg/1200px-Slatebrickbridge.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7e/Slatebrickbridge.jpg/1600px-Slatebrickbridge.jpg 2x\" width=\"534\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 514px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Example of Slate Brick Bridge\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(12118, 1561, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Bridge', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bridge\" title=\"Bridge\">Bridge</a></li></ul>', 3),
(12119, 3144, 'Description', 'Description', 'Every player has a journal with which to track various premade goals.', '<p>Every player has a journal with which to track various premade goals.\n</p>', 0),
(12120, 3144, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The journal is not craftable and cannot be lost. Every player has one from the very first moment of character creation. Successful completion of journal goals results in rewards, which can be seen by hovering over the heading of each section. Rewards include Titles and Sleep bonus buffs. Sections in the journal written in green text indicate completed sections. There are 10 sections of the journal. At first, only the first is displayed. After you complete 50% of the quests in a section, the next section will become visible. You don\'t need to have triggered the visibility of a section in order to complete a quest in that section. Sleep bonuses added by journal completions do not stack above your sleep bonus capacity. When claiming sleep bonus increases from journal entries, the capacity is 10 hours, the same as the developer given sleep bonus capicity. You can leave one goal in each section uncompleted and still complete that section. The journal is in no way related to the separate item, the archaeology journal .', '<ul><li>The journal is not craftable and cannot be lost. Every player has one from the very first moment of character creation.</li>\n<li>Successful completion of journal goals results in rewards, which can be seen by hovering over the heading of each section.</li>\n<li>Rewards include <a href=\"/index.php/Titles\" title=\"Titles\">Titles</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">Sleep bonus</a> buffs.</li>\n<li>Sections in the journal written in green text indicate completed sections.</li>\n<li>There are 10 sections of the journal. At first, only the first is displayed. After you complete 50% of the quests in a section, the next section will become visible. You don\'t need to have triggered the visibility of a section in order to complete a quest in that section.</li>\n<li>Sleep bonuses added by journal completions do not stack above your sleep bonus capacity.</li>\n<li>When claiming sleep bonus <b>increases</b> from journal entries, the capacity is 10 hours, the same as the developer given sleep bonus capicity.</li>\n<li>You can leave one goal in each section uncompleted and still complete that section.</li>\n<li>The journal is in no way related to the separate item, the <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">archaeology journal</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(12121, 3144, 'Journal Goals', 'Journal_Goals', 'Crafter journal First Steps: Chop down some trees Flatten a tile Create a mallet Mine iron Create some nails Plan a house Complete a house Improve a metal tool to 15ql Ride a cow Kill a creature Plant a crop Find a route Pick flowers Reward: Apprentice title and 1 hour of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). Finding the Path: Build a stone house wall Tame a creature Mine copper and tin Create a bronze lump Breed a creature Create a small cart Create a forge or oven Cook a breakfast Ride a horse Bandage a wound Plant a tree Find a rare coin Reward: Learned title and 1 hour of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). Gathering Stride Create a large cart Build a two story building Create a boat Cook a meal Catch a large fish Kill a spider Improve a tool to 50QL Harvest 5 cotton Ride a bear or bull Create a healing cover Make a rare item Sleep in a bed Join a meditation path Get to focus level 3 Epic Helper Reward: Experienced title and 2 hours of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). Paved With Stone Restore an item from fragments Slay a troll Open a wild beehive without being stung Study a tree or bush Improve a weapon to 50QL (doesn\'t need to be a weaponsmithing item) Get a skill to 50 Become a follower of a deity Plan a bridge Pilot a Knarr Spear a fish Make some wine Create a halter rope Get to focus level 5 Taunt a creature Write with Black Ink and a Reed Pen Reward: Skilled title and 2 hours of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). On the Highway - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Get a skill to 70 Improve a tool to 70QL Slay a greenish creature Get drunk Catch a disease Reach 30 faith Reach meditation path level 4 Build an underground house Obtain 15 titles Kill a creature with a catapult Build a guard tower Complete an almanac Harvest Lingonberries Reward: Accomplished title. glimmersteel or adamantine lump, and 3 hours of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). Picking up Speed - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Use a rune Slay each rift creature Reach meditation path level 7 Equip an enchanted weapon Discover an archaeology cache obtain 30 titles Ride a horse over 30km/h Create a wagon Harvest 50 herbs Help complete 10 missions Catch a huge fish Slay a champion creature Breed a Hostile Wild Champion Creature Reward: Proficient title, a choice of affinity , and 3 hours of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). The Winding Road - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Get a skill to 90 Obtain 60 titles Ride a Unicorn Slay a legendary creature Restore a statue from fragments Cook Billy Sheep Gruff Stew Improve an Armour Piece or Shield to 80QL Win 10 spars Reach meditation path level 9 Mine a tonne of high quality ore (1000kg of ore 80+ql) Create 10 Runes Get 10 skills to 50 Create a Moon Metal Item Reward: Talented title, increased maximum sleep bonus, and 6 hours of sleep bonus (on cluster of completion). Going the Distance - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Learn 250 cooking recipes Get 2000 total skill points Create 5 items from every metal (including moonmetals) Help with 50 missions Slay 50 champion creatures Use 50 runes Complete a colossus Dye 100 things Bandage 1000 wounds Discover 10 archaeology caches Get 70 fighting skill Get 70 in a sub-fighting skill Contribute to an Epic Mission Structure Reward: Professional title, 2.5% bonus skillgain, and 6 hours of sleep bonus(on cluster of completion). The Road Less Traveled - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Travel 7500km Complete 20 buildings Catch a 75KG fish Get 90 titles Slay 10 legendary creatures Destroy 25 veins via mining Reach level 11 meditation path Get 10 skills to 70 Restore 250 items from fragments Plant 2500 trees Equip a complete set of Drake armour Get 80 fighting skill Create a chess set Rewards: Expert title, 10% more rarity windows, and 6 hours of sleep bonus(on cluster of completion). Destinations Unknown - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Build a 10 story building Get a skill to 99 Get 5000 total skill points Learn 500 cooking recipes Help with 250 missions Get 120 titles Slay 20000 creatures Improve items 100000 times Close 100 rifts (You must have 20 participation points per rift) Perform 500000 actions Equip a complete set of enchanted scale armour Get 90 fighting skill Collect 10 chests from difficult treasure hunts Rewards: Master title, 10% more affinity windows, Master Cape, and 6 hours of sleep bonus(on cluster of completion). Basic training Basic Training: Carpentry - Complete at least 10 out of 11 goals Apprentice carpenter Create a set of carpentry tools Create a bed Plan a building of 10 or more tiles Sailboat maker Create 10 crates Creat 100 arrows Create a set of puppets Create items from each type of tree wood Create a rare carpentry item Improve a carpentry item to 30 ql Rewards: Novice Woodworker title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Smithing - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Apprentice smith Create a set of smithing tools Create 100 nails Create a lunchbox Create a set of god statuettes Create a set of chain armour Create a dioptra Create some lockpicks Create a charcoal pile Create a lump of each alloy Create an item of each base metal Create a rare smithing item Improve a smithing item to 30 ql Rewards: Novice metalworker title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Tailoring - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Apprentice tailor Create a set of tailoring tools Create a set of leather armour Create a set of cloth armour Create 100 strings of cloth or wool yarn Create a meditation rug Create a tapestry stand Create a set of tailored horse equipment Create a triangular sail Create an animal skin rug Create a cordage rope Create a rare tailoring or ropemaking item Improve a tailoring or ropemaking item to 30 ql Rewards: Novice Clothier title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Masonry - Complete at least 13 out of 14 goals Apprentice mason Create a set of masonry tools Create a forge and oven Create an open fireplace Create a coffin and gravestone Create 10 masonry fences Create 10 statues Build a stone house wall Render a wall or fence using clay Create a well Create an item of each stone Create a rare masonry item Improve a masonry item to 30 ql Rewards: Novice Bricklayer title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Pottery - Complete at least 9 out of 10 goals Apprentice potter Create a set of pottery tools Create an amphora Create 100 clay shingles or bricks Create 10 clay flowerpots Create 10 clay planters Create a measuring jug Use a kiln Create a rare pottery item Improve a pottery item to 30 ql Rewards: Novice Ceramist title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Terraforming - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Apprentice terraformer Create a set of terraforming tools Create a dredge Dig special resources Dig or mine a gem Mine for minerals Flatten or level a cave tile Flatter or level a tile border Prospect for silver or gold Analyze for traces of metal Plan an underground house Pave 10 tiles Mine, dig, or dredge a rare item Rewards: Novice Landscaper title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Cooking - Complete at least 11 out of 12 goals Apprentice cook Create a set of utensils Learn 50 cooking recipes Butcher animal skins Mill salt Use a wine barrel Bake a pie, tart, or cake Make fruit juice, olive oil, and cooking oil The smell of freshly baked bread Create butter Spit-roast an animal Make rare food Rewards: Novice Provisioner title, 2 hours sleep bonus Basic Training: Nature - Complete at least 12 out of 13 goals Apprentice Ecologist Create a set of agriculture tools Plant 10 trees Pick 10 bouquets of flowers Catch a clam Create a trellis Harvest seasonal products Farm vegetables Join a meditation path Breed a creature Milk a cow, bison, and sheep Find foraging and botanizing items Find a rare nature product Rewards: Novice Naturalist, 2 hours sleep bonus Treasure hunting Hunting for Clues - Complete at least 5 out of 6 goals Search via farming or harvest