dified Version, as the publisher.</dd>\n<dd><b>D.</b> Preserve all the copyright notices of the Document.</dd>\n<dd><b>E.</b> Add an appropriate copyright notice for your modifications adjacent to the other copyright notices.</dd>\n<dd><b>F.</b> Include, immediately after the copyright notices, a license notice giving the public permission to use the Modified Version under the terms of this License, in the form shown in the Addendum below.</dd>\n<dd><b>G.</b> Preserve in that license notice the full lists of Invariant Sections and required Cover Texts given in the Document\'s license notice.</dd>\n<dd><b>H.</b> Include an unaltered copy of this License.</dd>\n<dd><b>I.</b> Preserve the section Entitled \"History\", Preserve its Title, and add to it an item stating at least the title, year, new authors, and publisher of the Modified Version as given on the Title Page. If there is no section Entitled \"History\" in the Document, create one stating the title, year, authors, and publisher of the Document as given on its Title Page, then add an item describing the Modified Version as stated in the previous sentence.</dd>\n<dd><b>J.</b> Preserve the network location, if any, given in the Document for public access to a Transparent copy of the Document, and likewise the network locations given in the Document for previous versions it was based on. These may be placed in the \"History\" section. You may omit a network location for a work that was published at least four years before the Document itself, or if the original publisher of the version it refers to gives permission.</dd>\n<dd><b>K.</b> For any section Entitled \"Acknowledgements\" or \"Dedications\", Preserve the Title of the section, and preserve in the section all the substance and tone of each of the contributor acknowledgements and/or dedications given therein.</dd>\n<dd><b>L.</b> Preserve all the Invariant Sections of the Document, unaltered in their text and in their titles. Section numbers or the equivalent are not considered part of the section titles.</dd>\n<dd><b>M.</b> Delete any section Entitled \"Endorsements\". Such a section may not be included in the Modified Version.</dd>\n<dd><b>N.</b> Do not retitle any existing section to be Entitled \"Endorsements\" or to conflict in title with any Invariant Section.</dd>\n<dd><b>O.</b> Preserve any Warranty Disclaimers.</dd></dl>\n<p>If the Modified Version includes new front-matter sections or appendices that qualify as Secondary Sections and contain no material copied from the Document, you may at your option designate some or all of these sections as invariant. To do this, add their titles to the list of Invariant Sections in the Modified Version\'s license notice. These titles must be distinct from any other section titles. \n</p>\n<p>You may add a section Entitled \"Endorsements\", provided it contains nothing but endorsements of your Modified Version by various parties--for example, statements of peer review or that the text has been approved by an organization as the authoritative definition of a standard. \n</p>\n<p>You may add a passage of up to five words as a Front-Cover Text, and a passage of up to 25 words as a Back-Cover Text, to the end of the list of Cover Texts in the Modified Version. Only one passage of Front-Cover Text and one of Back-Cover Text may be added by (or through arrangements made by) any one entity. If the Document already includes a cover text for the same cover, previously added by you or by arrangement made by the same entity you are acting on behalf of, you may not add another; but you may replace the old one, on explicit permission from the previous publisher that added the old one. \n</p>\n<p>The author(s) and publisher(s) of the Document do not by this License give permission to use their names for publicity for or to assert or imply endorsement of any Modified Version. \n</p>', 4),
(13180, 3523, '5. COMBINING DOCUMENTS', '5._COMBINING_DOCUMENTS', 'You may combine the Document with other documents released under this License, under the terms defined in section 4 above for modified versions, provided that you include in the combination all of the Invariant Sections of all of the original documents, unmodified, and list them all as Invariant Sections of your combined work in its license notice, and that you preserve all their Warranty Disclaimers. The combined work need only contain one copy of this License, and multiple identical Invariant Sections may be replaced with a single copy. If there are multiple Invariant Sections with the same name but different contents, make the title of each such section unique by adding at the end of it, in parentheses, the name of the original author or publisher of that section if known, or else a unique number. Make the same adjustment to the section titles in the list of Invariant Sections in the license notice of the combined work. In the combination, you must combine any sections Entitled \"History\" in the various original documents, forming one section Entitled \"History\"; likewise combine any sections Entitled \"Acknowledgements\", and any sections Entitled \"Dedications\". You must delete all sections Entitled \"Endorsements.\"', '<p>You may combine the Document with other documents released under this License, under the terms defined in section 4 above for modified versions, provided that you include in the combination all of the Invariant Sections of all of the original documents, unmodified, and list them all as Invariant Sections of your combined work in its license notice, and that you preserve all their Warranty Disclaimers. \n</p>\n<p>The combined work need only contain one copy of this License, and multiple identical Invariant Sections may be replaced with a single copy. If there are multiple Invariant Sections with the same name but different contents, make the title of each such section unique by adding at the end of it, in parentheses, the name of the original author or publisher of that section if known, or else a unique number. Make the same adjustment to the section titles in the list of Invariant Sections in the license notice of the combined work. \n</p>\n<p>In the combination, you must combine any sections Entitled \"History\" in the various original documents, forming one section Entitled \"History\"; likewise combine any sections Entitled \"Acknowledgements\", and any sections Entitled \"Dedications\". You must delete all sections Entitled \"Endorsements.\" \n</p>', 5);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(13181, 3523, '6. COLLECTIONS OF DOCUMENTS', '6._COLLECTIONS_OF_DOCUMENTS', 'You may make a collection consisting of the Document and other documents released under this License, and replace the individual copies of this License in the various documents with a single copy that is included in the collection, provided that you follow the rules of this License for verbatim copying of each of the documents in all other respects. You may extract a single document from such a collection, and distribute it individually under this License, provided you insert a copy of this License into the extracted document, and follow this License in all other respects regarding verbatim copying of that document.', '<p>You may make a collection consisting of the Document and other documents released under this License, and replace the individual copies of this License in the various documents with a single copy that is included in the collection, provided that you follow the rules of this License for verbatim copying of each of the documents in all other respects. \n</p>\n<p>You may extract a single document from such a collection, and distribute it individually under this License, provided you insert a copy of this License into the extracted document, and follow this License in all other respects regarding verbatim copying of that document. \n</p>', 6),
(13182, 3523, '7. AGGREGATION WITH INDEPENDENT WORKS', '7._AGGREGATION_WITH_INDEPENDENT_WORKS', 'A compilation of the Document or its derivatives with other separate and independent documents or works, in or on a volume of a storage or distribution medium, is called an \"aggregate\" if the copyright resulting from the compilation is not used to limit the legal rights of the compilation\'s users beyond what the individual works permit. When the Document is included in an aggregate, this License does not apply to the other works in the aggregate which are not themselves derivative works of the Document. If the Cover Text requirement of section 3 is applicable to these copies of the Document, then if the Document is less than one half of the entire aggregate, the Document\'s Cover Texts may be placed on covers that bracket the Document within the aggregate, or the electronic equivalent of covers if the Document is in electronic form. Otherwise they must appear on printed covers that bracket the whole aggregate.', '<p>A compilation of the Document or its derivatives with other separate and independent documents or works, in or on a volume of a storage or distribution medium, is called an \"aggregate\" if the copyright resulting from the compilation is not used to limit the legal rights of the compilation\'s users beyond what the individual works permit. When the Document is included in an aggregate, this License does not apply to the other works in the aggregate which are not themselves derivative works of the Document. \n</p>\n<p>If the Cover Text requirement of section 3 is applicable to these copies of the Document, then if the Document is less than one half of the entire aggregate, the Document\'s Cover Texts may be placed on covers that bracket the Document within the aggregate, or the electronic equivalent of covers if the Document is in electronic form. Otherwise they must appear on printed covers that bracket the whole aggregate. \n</p>', 7),
(13183, 3523, '8. TRANSLATION', '8._TRANSLATION', 'Translation is considered a kind of modification, so you may distribute translations of the Document under the terms of section 4. Replacing Invariant Sections with translations requires special permission from their copyright holders, but you may include translations of some or all Invariant Sections in addition to the original versions of these Invariant Sections. You may include a translation of this License, and all the license notices in the Document, and any Warranty Disclaimers, provided that you also include the original English version of this License and the original versions of those notices and disclaimers. In case of a disagreement between the translation and the original version of this License or a notice or disclaimer, the original version will prevail. If a section in the Document is Entitled \"Acknowledgements\", \"Dedications\", or \"History\", the requirement (section 4) to Preserve its Title (section 1) will typically require changing the actual title.', '<p>Translation is considered a kind of modification, so you may distribute translations of the Document under the terms of section 4. Replacing Invariant Sections with translations requires special permission from their copyright holders, but you may include translations of some or all Invariant Sections in addition to the original versions of these Invariant Sections. You may include a translation of this License, and all the license notices in the Document, and any Warranty Disclaimers, provided that you also include the original English version of this License and the original versions of those notices and disclaimers. In case of a disagreement between the translation and the original version of this License or a notice or disclaimer, the original version will prevail. \n</p>\n<p>If a section in the Document is Entitled \"Acknowledgements\", \"Dedications\", or \"History\", the requirement (section 4) to Preserve its Title (section 1) will typically require changing the actual title. \n</p>', 8),
(13184, 3523, '9. TERMINATION', '9._TERMINATION', 'You may not copy, modify, sublicense, or distribute the Document except as expressly provided for under this License. Any other attempt to copy, modify, sublicense or distribute the Document is void, and will automatically terminate your rights under this License. However, parties who have received copies, or rights, from you under this License will not have their licenses terminated so long as such parties remain in full compliance.', '<p>You may not copy, modify, sublicense, or distribute the Document except as expressly provided for under this License. Any other attempt to copy, modify, sublicense or distribute the Document is void, and will automatically terminate your rights under this License. However, parties who have received copies, or rights, from you under this License will not have their licenses terminated so long as such parties remain in full compliance. \n</p>', 9),
(13185, 3523, '10. FUTURE REVISIONS OF THIS LICENSE', '10._FUTURE_REVISIONS_OF_THIS_LICENSE', 'The Free Software Foundation may publish new, revised versions of the GNU Free Documentation License from time to time. Such new versions will be similar in spirit to the present version, but may differ in detail to address new problems or concerns. See http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/ . Each version of the License is given a distinguishing version number. If the Document specifies that a particular numbered version of this License \"or any later version\" applies to it, you have the option of following the terms and conditions either of that specified version or of any later version that has been published (not as a draft) by the Free Software Foundation. If the Document does not specify a version number of this License, you may choose any version ever published (not as a draft) by the Free Software Foundation.', '<p>The Free Software Foundation may publish new, revised versions of the GNU Free Documentation License from time to time. Such new versions will be similar in spirit to the present version, but may differ in detail to address new problems or concerns. See <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/</a>. \n</p>\n<p>Each version of the License is given a distinguishing version number. If the Document specifies that a particular numbered version of this License \"or any later version\" applies to it, you have the option of following the terms and conditions either of that specified version or of any later version that has been published (not as a draft) by the Free Software Foundation. If the Document does not specify a version number of this License, you may choose any version ever published (not as a draft) by the Free Software Foundation.\n</p>', 10),
(13186, 3523, 'External links', 'External_links', 'GNU Free Documentation License (Wikipedia article on the license) Official GNU FDL webpage', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Free_Documentation_License\" rel=\"nofollow\">GNU Free Documentation License</a> (Wikipedia article on the license)</li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/fdl.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Official GNU FDL webpage</a></li></ul>', 11),
(13190, 3527, 'Description', 'Description', 'Creation chance is the percentage of a chance a player has to craft an item. This can be based on skill level, tool quality and material quality . Some items have a hard skill requirement before an item can be made, but many do not.', '<p>Creation chance is the percentage of a chance a player has to craft an item. This can be based on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> level, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tool\" title=\"Tool\">tool</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> and material <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>. Some items have a hard <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> requirement before an item can be made, but many do not.\n</p>', 0),
(13191, 3527, 'On the Wurmpedia', 'On_the_Wurmpedia', 'Creation chances from experimentation can be put in the Discussion section of each Wurmpedia page. Players can list their own experiences for use by CA help or other players looking for ideas. Creation percentages may vary wildly depending on the player\'s actions, so only hard limits should be listed on the main Wurmpedia pages.', '<p>Creation chances from experimentation can be put in the Discussion section of each Wurmpedia page. Players can list their own experiences for use by CA help or other players looking for ideas. Creation percentages may vary wildly depending on the player\'s actions, so only hard limits should be listed on the main Wurmpedia pages.\n</p>', 1),
(13192, 3299, 'Earning Marks', 'Earning_Marks', 'Marks are earned by the purchase of premium time at the following rates: 15 days from token (with 5 silver coins): 1000 marks. 30 days from token (with 10 silver coins): 3000 marks. 30 days from shop: 4500 marks. Any single purchase of six months premium time will award 3000 marks as a bonus.\nAny single purchase of twelve months premium time will award 6000 marks as a bonus.\nPurchases of silver coins from the shop will award 20 marks per silver coin purchased. Note: buying the first time premium special from the shop will not award marks.', '<p>Marks are earned by the purchase of premium time at the following rates:\n</p>\n<ul><li>15 days from token (with 5 silver coins): 1000 marks.</li>\n<li>30 days from token (with 10 silver coins): 3000 marks.</li>\n<li>30 days from shop: 4500 marks.</li></ul>\n<p>Any single purchase of six months premium time will award 3000 marks as a bonus.\nAny single purchase of twelve months premium time will award 6000 marks as a bonus.\nPurchases of silver coins from the shop will award 20 marks per silver coin purchased.\n</p>\n<p><b>Note: buying the first time premium special from the shop will not award marks.</b>\n</p>', 0),
(13193, 3299, 'Purchasing with Marks', 'Purchasing_with_Marks', 'You may only purchase from the shop while you are premium. Go to a token, right-click, and select Select Premium Awards . A screen will appear with the selections available. The Marks Shop interface Caution: Some shop items, such as Magical ink are not tradeable to other player accounts. See their respective wiki pages. Some options will give a random item, such as a random moon metal lump or random Jackal skin . Additionally, there will be monthly skins for weapons added to the shop, which are only available that month. Several trader items are also available, including the Rod of transmutation , Shaker orbs , and large and small magical chests, a complete list of items available is shown in the table below. Item name Cost (marks) Additional information Random moonmetal lump 3000 - Random ancient Jackal skin 3000 - Sleep powder 3000 - Monthly skin 4500 - Gift pack 4500 A random item from a premade table of possibilities including moonmetal , statues , and bones though sleep powder is the most common item rewarded. Shaker orb 6000 A shaker orb is used to collapse cave tiles , like the Strongwall spell. Random affinity 10000 Adds one random affinity. Wooden nameplate 18000 The player can change the name of one cared for animal (Regular Wurm rules about naming apply). Extra care for slot 22500 A player can care for one extra animal above your animal husbandry skill. Rod of transmutation 25000 The Rod of transmutation turns a normal cave rock tile into the vein of your choice. Magical ink 27000 Allows the player to change the name of an item. The player\'s name will be added to the item as well (Regular Wurm rules about naming apply). Faith swap 27000 Allows a priest to swap to another god without losing faith . Sleep bonus 27000 Adds one additional hour to your maximum sleep bonus limit. Small magical chest 30000 Provides greatly reduced decay on contents. Holds the same amount and types of items as a normal small chest . Golden mirror 35000 Allows a player to change their character\'s appearance and gender once. Meditation path change 36000 Allows a player to change their meditation path without losing the path progress. Large magical chest 42000 Provides greatly reduced decay on contents. Holds the same amount and types of items as a normal large chest . Magical tomes 54000 Previously only available as rare drops from uniques or as a reward for the old personal goals system. One random tome with one charge can be purchased. Available variants: Red tome of magic , Tome of incineration , Green tome of magic , Black tome of magic , Blue tome of magic , White tome of magic , Libram of the night', '<p>You may only purchase from the shop while you are premium. Go to a token, right-click, and select <b>Select Premium Awards</b>. A screen will appear with the selections available. \n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Marks_shop.JPG\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"568\" data-file-width=\"517\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/0d/Marks_shop.JPG/109px-Marks_shop.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/0/0d/Marks_shop.JPG/164px-Marks_shop.JPG 1.5x, /images/thumb/0/0d/Marks_shop.JPG/218px-Marks_shop.JPG 2x\" width=\"109\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>The Marks Shop interface\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<table style=\"background-color:#f8f8f8; -moz-border-radius:10px; width:50%; border:2px solid #e0e0e0; margin-left:0 auto; padding:5px; -moz-outline-style: outset; -moz-outline-radius: 10px; -moz-outline-color: #e0e0e0;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"30\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/30px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/45px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/60px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"30\"/></a></div>\n</td>\n<td><b>Caution:</b> Some shop items, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Magical_ink\" title=\"Magical ink\">Magical ink</a> are not tradeable to other player accounts. See their respective wiki pages.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Some options will give a random item, such as a random <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Moon_metal\" title=\"Moon metal\">moon metal</a> lump or random <a href=\"/index.php/Jackal#Jackal_points_and_rewards\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal skin</a>. Additionally, there will be monthly skins for weapons added to the shop, which are only available that month. Several <a href=\"/index.php/Trader#Item_stocks\" title=\"Trader\">trader items</a> are also available, including the <a href=\"/index.php/Rod_of_transmutation\" title=\"Rod of transmutation\">Rod of transmutation</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Shaker_orb\" title=\"Shaker orb\">Shaker orbs</a>, and large and small magical chests, a complete list of items available is shown in the table below.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"200\">Item name\n</th>\n<th width=\"10\">Cost (marks)\n</th>\n<th>Additional information\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Moon_metals\" title=\"Metal lumps\">moonmetal</a> lump\n</td>\n<td>3000\n</td>\n<td>-\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random <a href=\"/index.php/Jackal#Jackal_points_and_rewards\" title=\"Jackal\">ancient Jackal skin</a>\n</td>\n<td>3000\n</td>\n<td>-\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_powder\" title=\"Sleep powder\">Sleep powder</a>\n</td>\n<td>3000\n</td>\n<td>-\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Loyalty_program#Monthly_Skins\" title=\"Loyalty program\">Monthly skin</a>\n</td>\n<td>4500\n</td>\n<td>-\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Gift_pack\" title=\"Gift pack\">Gift pack</a>\n</td>\n<td>4500\n</td>\n<td>A random item from a premade table of possibilities including <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Moon_metals\" title=\"Metal lumps\">moonmetal</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration#Unique_Fragments\" title=\"Restoration\">statues</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Strange_bone\" title=\"Strange bone\">bones</a> though <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_powder\" title=\"Sleep powder\">sleep powder</a> is the most common item rewarded.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Shaker_orb\" title=\"Shaker orb\">Shaker orb</a>\n</td>\n<td>6000\n</td>\n<td>A shaker orb is used to collapse <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">cave</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>, like the <a href=\"/index.php/Strongwall\" title=\"Strongwall\">Strongwall</a> spell.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Random <a href=\"/index.php/Affinity\" title=\"Affinity\">affinity</a>\n</td>\n<td>10000\n</td>\n<td>Adds one random affinity.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_nameplate\" title=\"Wooden nameplate\">Wooden nameplate</a>\n</td>\n<td>18000\n</td>\n<td>The player can change the name of one cared for animal (Regular Wurm rules about naming apply).\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Extra <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry#Caring\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">care for</a> slot\n</td>\n<td>22500\n</td>\n<td>A player can care for one extra animal above your <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">animal husbandry</a> skill.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Rod_of_transmutation\" title=\"Rod of transmutation\">Rod of transmutation</a>\n</td>\n<td>25000\n</td>\n<td>The Rod of transmutation turns a normal cave rock tile into the vein of your choice.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Magical_ink\" title=\"Magical ink\">Magical ink</a>\n</td>\n<td>27000\n</td>\n<td>Allows the player to change the name of an item. The player\'s name will be added to the item as well (Regular Wurm rules about naming apply).\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Faith_swap\" title=\"Faith swap\">Faith swap</a>\n</td>\n<td>27000\n</td>\n<td>Allows a <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priest</a> to swap to another <a href=\"/index.php/Gods\" title=\"Gods\">god</a> without losing <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">Sleep bonus</a>\n</td>\n<td>27000\n</td>\n<td>Adds one additional hour to your maximum sleep bonus limit.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_magical_chest\" title=\"Small magical chest\">Small magical chest</a>\n</td>\n<td>30000\n</td>\n<td>Provides greatly reduced decay on contents. Holds the same amount and types of items as a normal <a href=\"/index.php/Small_chest\" title=\"Small chest\">small chest</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Golden_mirror\" title=\"Golden mirror\">Golden mirror</a>\n</td>\n<td>35000\n</td>\n<td>Allows a player to change their character\'s appearance and gender once.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Meditating#Path_Management_and_Advancement\" title=\"Meditating\">Meditation path</a> change\n</td>\n<td>36000\n</td>\n<td>Allows a player to change their meditation path without losing the path progress.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_magical_chest\" title=\"Large magical chest\">Large magical chest</a>\n</td>\n<td>42000\n</td>\n<td>Provides greatly reduced decay on contents. Holds the same amount and types of items as a normal <a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">large chest</a>.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Sorcery_items\" title=\"Category:Sorcery items\">Magical tomes</a>\n</td>\n<td>54000\n</td>\n<td>Previously only available as rare drops from <a href=\"/index.php/Unique\" title=\"Unique\">uniques</a> or as a reward for the old <a href=\"/index.php/Historical:Personal_goals\" title=\"Historical:Personal goals\">personal goals</a> system. One random tome with one <a href=\"/index.php/Sorcery#Usage\" title=\"Sorcery\">charge</a> can be purchased. Available variants: <a href=\"/index.php/Red_tome_of_magic\" title=\"Red tome of magic\">Red tome of magic</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Tome_of_incineration\" title=\"Tome of incineration\">Tome of incineration</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Green_tome_of_magic\" title=\"Green tome of magic\">Green tome of magic</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Black_tome_of_magic\" title=\"Black tome of magic\">Black tome of magic</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Blue_tome_of_magic\" title=\"Blue tome of magic\">Blue tome of magic</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/White_tome_of_magic\" title=\"White tome of magic\">White tome of magic</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Libram_of_the_night\" title=\"Libram of the night\">Libram of the night</a>\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(13194, 3299, 'Monthly Skins', 'Monthly_Skins', 'Each month, the Marks shop will offer a skin for armour or a weapon. These are different from the Jackal skins. Skins must be applied to a certain item, noted in parentheses, by right-clicking and applying. Warning: skins cannot be removed from an item after applying without destroying the skin.\nSkins are expendable (one use item), after being applied to their item they\'re removed from the inventory. When applying a different skin to an item, the currently applied skin will be destroyed. Note: Monthly skins may be rerun on the Silver shop . 2020 February 2020 Raider Shield (Medium wooden shield) A sturdy round wooden shield, also effective outside of raids. March 2020 Shield of the Ageless (Large metal shield) Once wielded by a mighty race, now forgotten. April 2020 Tower Shield (Large wooden shield) This shapely shield took the saying \"Don\'t be a square\" to its cold wooden heart. May 2020 Lómanian Cavalry Maul (Maul) Wielded with precision and an iron will it shall overcome any two- or four-legged obstacle. June 2020 Prodigious Longbow (Long bow) An old proverb is engraved into its shiny wood: \"True Aim, Goblin\'s Bane\" July 2020 Agile Bow (Bow) Best ye go, best ye go, outrun my bow August 2020 Fiendish Large Maul (Large maul) Crushing bones, crushing hearts September 2020 Bearded Hatchet (Hatchet) Excels in chopping wood, limbs and small critters that happen to wander by. October 2020 Goblinsbane (Long sword) Highly effective against goblins and other green, thieving vermin. November 2020 Mastercrafted Basinet Helm (Basinet helm) A finely worked piece of armour, fit for a king. December 2020 Candy Cane (Short sword) Delicious, give it a lick! 2021 January 2021 Goat Helm (Open helm) You ponder which nightmarish creature these appendages once belonged to. Absolutely terrifying. March 2021 Seafarer\'s Hat (Leather adventurer hat) Now where did the rum go? April 2021 Stag Helm (Open helm) They might call you bone-headed but at least that precious noggin is safe. May 2021 Executioner Hood (Studded leather cap) Best worn during mischievous activities or on bad hair days. June 2021 Trident (Metal spear) Poking three holes instead of one-The inventor must have been some kind of genius. July 2021 Blacksmith\'s Hammer (Hammer) The Blacksmith and his hammer - a love story based on true events. August 2021 Bulwark Shield (Large metal shield) Stand proud mine brothers, no turning back now! September 2021 Staff of the Dragon (Metal staff) A small dragon figurine is tightly wrapped around one end. When the light hits it just right it almost appears to be alive - Weird. October 2021 Seeker\'s Lantern (lantern) Once used by Vynora herself to illuminate the Void. November 2021 Skeleton Chest (large chest) A sturdy, roomy chest for keeping treasured possessions. Various bones of the last scoundrel who wandered too close are nailed to all corners. Better luck next time! December 2021 Claymore (two-handed sword) Make your clanmates turn blue with envy by wielding this glorious sword. 2022 January 2022 Dragon Statuette (Statuette) A tiny dragon guards the general area. You feel safer immediately. February 2022 Bear Army Statuette (Statuette) A proud warriorette seated upon her salmon-fueled battle mount. March 2022 Decorative Flowers (Pottery jar) Some lovely, fragrant flowers brighten up the room. April 2022 Statuette of the Avenger (Statuette) Not much is known about this noble creature other than that it has a great sense of fashion. May 2022 Messer (Longsword) No messering around with this sturdy single-edged sword! June 2022 Cactus Skin (Pottery planter) Yowch! Why, you little... July 2022 Raider Axe Skin (Medium Axe) All bets are off after the third keg of mead has run dry. August 2022 Bjarne Backpack Skin (Backpack) The bravest bear in all of Wurm always has your back! September 2022 Winged Helm (Open Helm) Invented by R. Plimey in 908 after an unfortunate horseback collision with an eagle. October 2022 Menacing Medium Maul Skin (Medium Maul) Deliver some satisfyingly spiky bonks to your enemies! November 2022 Sigvard\'s Wrath (Huge axe) Its former owner appears to be all tied up, might as well get some use out of it! December 2022 Festive Light of the Gods (Candelabra) As if by magic the center part starts to move. Certainly a sign of the gods! 2023 January 2023 Bucket Helm (Great Helm) fashionable and functional, with a solid metal liner for superior protection and blocking out the smells imbibed by its previous uses! February 2023 Dark Maul (Large maul) Dark Maul: Revenge is a dish best served with a maul. March 2023 Small cherry tree (Marble planter) A tiny cherry tree in perpetual bloom. Lovely! April 2023 Bunny Backpack (Backpack) A cute bunny backpack! Plenty of room for eggs and chocolate inside. May 2023 Harrowing Halberd (Halberd) Sharp, pointy things on a stick, an all-time classic. July 2023 Trusty Axe (Small axe) August 2023 Sol shield (Medium metal shield) A radiant and robust round metal shield , inspired by everyone\'s favorite fiery sky Sphere. September 2023 Small Knarr (Decorative ship) A detailed model of a knarr sits proudly on a polished wooden base. October 2023 Small Caravel (Decorative ship) A detailed model of a caravel sits proudly on a polished wooden base. November 2023 Libila\'s Liberator (Scythe) A menacing-looking scythe, reserved for tasks entirely unrelated to mowing grass or harvesting grains. December 2023 Santa Beard (Paper mask) A luxurious Santa beard meticulously handcrafted from the finest sheep\'s wool, providing a cozy feel and gentle warmth to your face. 2024 January 2024 Grimshadow (Butchering knife) An elegant weapon of silent death, its gleaming edge infused with the essence of darkness. February 2024 Thunderforge Anvil (Large anvil) A steadfast ally in the art of shaping metal. March 2024 Lapine Luminance Brazier (small brazier) A flickering beacon of comfort and style, the Lapine Luminance Brazier shines bright. April 2024 Companion Bird Hat (green common wool hat) Aah, spring is in the air! Some birdies seem to have found a new home and you certainly wouldn\'t want to disturb them. May 2024 Regal Bed (bed) Regal Bed: Snoozing the night away in this comfy bed - absolute bliss. August 2024 Dragon Lamp (torch lamp) Dragon Lamp: Let the mystical glow of dragon fire light up your surroundings. September 2024 Lindwyrm Bench (wooden bench) Lindwyrm Bench: A wooden bench featuring intricate carvings, inviting you to rest for a while. October 2024 Drinking Horn (water skin) Drinking Horn: Drink mead or other delectable beverages of choice in style! November 2024 Small Corbita (decorative ship) Small Corbita: A detailed model of a corbita sits proudly on a polished wooden base. December 2024 Hell Horse Rider (statuette) Hell Horse Rider Statuette: A brave rider and his fiery steed. 2025 February 2025 Merry Flowers (pottery jar) Merry Flowers: A beautiful flowering plant in a crimson vase. March 2025 Rose Arch Trellis (rose trellis) Rose Arch Trellis: Some climbing roses growing up a sturdy arch trellis with interwoven wooden panels. April 2025 Dragon Helm (great helm) Dragon Helm: An awe-inspiring specimen of a great helm. May 2025 Marvellous Mallet (wooden mallet) Marvellous Mallet: A meticulously crafted mallet, with walnut end plates and woven leather grip for increased comfort. June 2025 Orchard Bowl (pottery bowl) Orchard Bowl: An assortment of fruit tastefully arranged in a blue glazed pottery bowl. July 2025 Statue of the Renowned Warrior (Statuette) Statue of the Renowned Warrior: A statuette of an acclaimed hero, basking in glory. August 2025 Spacious Oven (oven) Spacious Oven: A spacious oven including a generous wooden worktop. October 2025 Small Thunderforge Anvil (small anvil) Small Thunderforge Anvil: The smaller, slightly less capable little brother of the mighty Thunderforge Anvil.', '<p>Each month, the Marks shop will offer a skin for armour or a weapon. These are different from the Jackal skins. Skins must be applied to a certain item, noted in parentheses, by right-clicking and applying. \n</p>\n<p>Warning: skins cannot be removed from an item after applying without destroying the skin.\nSkins are expendable (one use item), after being applied to their item they\'re removed from the inventory. When applying a different skin to an item, the currently applied skin will be destroyed.\n</p>\n<p>Note: Monthly skins may be rerun on the <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_shop\" title=\"Silver shop\">Silver shop</a>. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2020\">2020</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/fd/Monthlyskin.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>February 2020 <br/> <b>Raider Shield</b> (Medium wooden shield) <br/> <i>A sturdy round wooden shield, also effective outside of raids.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin2.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/f4/Monthlyskin2.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2020 <br/><b>Shield of the Ageless</b> (Large metal shield) <br/> <i>Once wielded by a mighty race, now forgotten.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin3.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/5/5c/Monthlyskin3.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2020 <br/><b>Tower Shield</b> (Large wooden shield) <br/><i>This shapely shield took the saying \"Don\'t be a square\" to its cold wooden heart.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin4.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/7/79/Monthlyskin4.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2020 <br/> <b>Lómanian Cavalry Maul</b> (Maul) <br/> <i>Wielded with precision and an iron will it shall overcome any two- or four-legged obstacle.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin5.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/a/ac/Monthlyskin5.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>June 2020 <br/> <b>Prodigious Longbow</b> (Long bow) <br/> <i>An old proverb is engraved into its shiny wood: \"True Aim, Goblin\'s Bane\" </i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin6.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/05/Monthlyskin6.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>July 2020 <br/> <b>Agile Bow</b> (Bow) <br/> <i>Best ye go, best ye go, outrun my bow</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin7.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/d/da/Monthlyskin7.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2020 <br/> <b>Fiendish Large Maul</b> (Large maul) <br/> <i>Crushing bones, crushing hearts</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin8.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/06/Monthlyskin8.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>September 2020 <br/> <b>Bearded Hatchet</b> (Hatchet) <br/> <i>Excels in chopping wood, limbs and small critters that happen to wander by.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin9.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/1/1e/Monthlyskin9.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2020 <br/> <b>Goblinsbane</b> (Long sword) <br/> <i>Highly effective against goblins and other green, thieving vermin.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin10.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/03/Monthlyskin10.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>November 2020 <br/> <b>Mastercrafted Basinet Helm</b> (Basinet helm) <br/><i>A finely worked piece of armour, fit for a king.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin11.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/2/2f/Monthlyskin11.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>December 2020 <br/> <b>Candy Cane</b> (Short sword) <br/> <i>Delicious, give it a lick!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2021\">2021</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin12.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/8/8f/Monthlyskin12.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>January 2021 <br/><b>Goat Helm</b> (Open helm) <br/> <i>You ponder which nightmarish creature these appendages once belonged to. Absolutely terrifying.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Monthlyskin13.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/4c/Monthlyskin13.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2021 <br/> <b>Seafarer\'s Hat</b> (Leather adventurer hat) <br/> <i>Now where did the rum go?</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 316.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 316.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 314.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:April2021Monthlyskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"295\" data-file-width=\"464\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/a/a0/April2021Monthlyskin.png\" width=\"315\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2021 <br/> <b>Stag Helm</b> (Open helm) <br/> <i>They might call you bone-headed but at least that precious noggin is safe.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 315.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 315.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 313.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:May2021Monthlyskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"249\" data-file-width=\"390\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/b/b0/May2021Monthlyskin.png\" width=\"314\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2021 <br/> <b>Executioner Hood</b> (Studded leather cap) <br/> <i>Best worn during mischievous activities or on bad hair days.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Trident.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/9a/Trident.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>June 2021 <br/> <b>Trident</b> (Metal spear) <br/> <i>Poking three holes instead of one-The inventor must have been some kind of genius.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 322px\"><div style=\"width: 322px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 320px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:July_2021_Monthly_skin_Blacksmiths_Hammer.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"229\" data-file-width=\"366\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/3/3f/July_2021_Monthly_skin_Blacksmiths_Hammer.png\" width=\"320\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>July 2021 <br/> <b>Blacksmith\'s Hammer</b> (Hammer) <br/> <i>The Blacksmith and his hammer - a love story based on true events.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 326px\"><div style=\"width: 326px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 324px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:August_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"231\" data-file-width=\"374\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/fc/August_skin.png\" width=\"324\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2021 <br/> <b>Bulwark Shield</b> (Large metal shield) <br/> <i>Stand proud mine brothers, no turning back now!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:September_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"224\" data-file-width=\"362\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/46/September_skin.png\" width=\"324\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>September 2021 <br/> <b>Staff of the Dragon</b> (Metal staff) <br/> <i>A small dragon figurine is tightly wrapped around one end. When the light hits it just right it almost appears to be alive - Weird.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 334.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 334.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 332.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Octlampskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"210\" data-file-width=\"349\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/8/87/Octlampskin.png\" width=\"333\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2021 <br/> <b>Seeker\'s Lantern</b> (lantern) <br/> <i>Once used by Vynora herself to illuminate the Void.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 334.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 334.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 332.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Skeleton_chest.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"295\" data-file-width=\"490\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/7/70/Skeleton_chest.png\" width=\"333\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>November 2021 <br/> <b>Skeleton Chest</b> (large chest) <br/> <i>A sturdy, roomy chest for keeping treasured possessions. Various bones of the last scoundrel who wandered too close are nailed to all corners. Better luck next time!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 332px\"><div style=\"width: 332px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 330px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Claymore_skin.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"467\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/fe/Claymore_skin.jpg\" width=\"330\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>December 2021 <br/> <b>Claymore</b> (two-handed sword) <br/> <i>Make your clanmates turn blue with envy by wielding this glorious sword.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2022\">2022</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 335.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 335.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 333.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Dragon_statuette.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"215\" data-file-width=\"358\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/9c/Dragon_statuette.png\" width=\"334\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>January 2022 <br/><b>Dragon Statuette</b> (Statuette) <br/> <i>A tiny dragon guards the general area. You feel safer immediately.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 268.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bear_statuette_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/e/ec/Bear_statuette_skin.png\" width=\"267\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>February 2022 <br/><b>Bear Army Statuette</b> (Statuette) <br/> <i>A proud warriorette seated upon her salmon-fueled battle mount.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 321.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Marchskin.JPG\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"346\" data-file-width=\"555\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e7/Marchskin.JPG/482px-Marchskin.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/e/e7/Marchskin.JPG 1.5x\" width=\"322\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2022 <br/><b>Decorative Flowers</b> (Pottery jar) <br/> <i>Some lovely, fragrant flowers brighten up the room.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 320.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:April_Skin.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"281\" data-file-width=\"450\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/05/April_Skin.jpg\" width=\"321\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2022 <br/><b>Statuette of the Avenger</b> (Statuette) <br/> <i>Not much is known about this noble creature other than that it has a great sense of fashion.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 329.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Messer_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"282\" data-file-width=\"464\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/7/73/Messer_skin.png\" width=\"330\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2022 <br/> <b>Messer</b> (Longsword) <br/> <i>No messering around with this sturdy single-edged sword!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Cactus_skin.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"460\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/6/68/Cactus_skin.jpeg\" width=\"326\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>June 2022 <br/> <b>Cactus Skin</b> (Pottery planter) <br/> <i>Yowch! Why, you little...</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Raid_Axe_Skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"254\" data-file-width=\"410\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/0b/Raid_Axe_Skin.png\" width=\"324\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>July 2022 <br/> <b>Raider Axe Skin</b> (Medium Axe) <br/> <i>All bets are off after the third keg of mead has run dry.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 332.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 332.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 330.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bjarne_backpack.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"279\" data-file-width=\"461\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/46/Bjarne_backpack.jpeg\" width=\"331\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2022 <br/> <b>Bjarne Backpack Skin</b> (Backpack) <br/> <i>The bravest bear in all of Wurm always has your back!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 334px\"><div style=\"width: 334px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 332px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Winged_helm.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"286\" data-file-width=\"474\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/6/62/Winged_helm.jpeg\" width=\"332\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>September 2022 <br/> <b>Winged Helm</b> (Open Helm) <br/> <i>Invented by R. Plimey in 908 after an unfortunate horseback collision with an eagle.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Menacing_Medium_Maul_Skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"329\" data-file-width=\"530\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c8/Menacing_Medium_Maul_Skin.png/484px-Menacing_Medium_Maul_Skin.png\" srcset=\"/images/c/c8/Menacing_Medium_Maul_Skin.png 1.5x\" width=\"323\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2022 <br/> <b>Menacing Medium Maul Skin</b> (Medium Maul) <br/> <i>Deliver some satisfyingly spiky bonks to your enemies!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 329.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Sigvard%27s_wrath_skin.jpeg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"466\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/a/aa/Sigvard%27s_wrath_skin.jpeg\" width=\"330\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>November 2022 <br/> <b>Sigvard\'s Wrath</b> (Huge axe) <br/> <i>Its former owner appears to be all tied up, might as well get some use out of it!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 328px\"><div style=\"width: 328px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 326px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Festive_candelabra.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"284\" data-file-width=\"463\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/6/65/Festive_candelabra.png\" width=\"326\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>December 2022 <br/> <b>Festive Light of the Gods</b> (Candelabra) <br/> <i>As if by magic the center part starts to move. Certainly a sign of the gods!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2023\">2023</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Buckethelmskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"226\" data-file-width=\"367\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/7/70/Buckethelmskin.png\" width=\"325\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>January 2023 <br/><b>Bucket Helm</b> (Great Helm) <br/> <i>fashionable and functional, with a solid metal liner for superior protection and blocking out the smells imbibed by its previous uses!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Dark_Maul.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"289\" data-file-width=\"466\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/1/19/Dark_Maul.png\" width=\"323\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>February 2023 <br/> <b>Dark Maul</b> (Large maul) <br/> <i>Dark Maul: Revenge is a dish best served with a maul.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 330.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 330.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 328.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Small_Cherry_Tree.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"286\" data-file-width=\"470\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/0a/Small_Cherry_Tree.png\" width=\"329\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2023 <br/> <b>Small cherry tree</b> (Marble planter) <br/> <i>A tiny cherry tree in perpetual bloom. Lovely!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 330px\"><div style=\"width: 330px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 328px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bunny_backpack_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"224\" data-file-width=\"367\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/4b/Bunny_backpack_skin.png\" width=\"328\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2023 <br/> <b>Bunny Backpack</b> (Backpack) <br/> <i>A cute bunny backpack! Plenty of room for eggs and chocolate inside.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 321.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 321.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 319.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Harrowing_halberd.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"289\" data-file-width=\"461\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/49/Harrowing_halberd.png\" width=\"320\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2023 <br/> <b>Harrowing Halberd</b> (Halberd) <br/> <i>Sharp, pointy things on a stick, an all-time classic.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 316.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 316.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 314.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Trusty_Axe_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"238\" data-file-width=\"374\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/2/22/Trusty_Axe_skin.png\" width=\"315\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>July 2023 <br/> <b>Trusty Axe</b> (Small axe) <br/>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 320px\"><div style=\"width: 320px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 318px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Sol_shield.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"234\" data-file-width=\"372\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/9b/Sol_shield.png\" width=\"318\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2023 <br/> <b>Sol shield</b> (Medium metal shield) <br/> <i>A radiant and robust round metal shield , inspired by everyone\'s favorite fiery sky Sphere.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 318px\"><div style=\"width: 318px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 316px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Smallknarrskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"238\" data-file-width=\"376\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/04/Smallknarrskin.png\" width=\"316\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>September 2023 <br/> <b>Small Knarr</b> (Decorative ship) <br/> <i>A detailed model of a knarr sits proudly on a polished wooden base.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 329.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 329.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 327.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Smallcaravelskin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"463\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/47/Smallcaravelskin.png\" width=\"328\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2023 <br/> <b>Small Caravel</b> (Decorative ship) <br/> <i>A detailed model of a caravel sits proudly on a polished wooden base.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 329.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 329.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 327.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Scythe_Skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"280\" data-file-width=\"458\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/4/4e/Scythe_Skin.png\" width=\"328\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>November 2023 <br/> <b>Libila\'s Liberator</b> (Scythe) <br/> <i>A menacing-looking scythe, reserved for tasks entirely unrelated to mowing grass or harvesting grains.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 328.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 328.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 326.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Santa_beard.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"280\" data-file-width=\"457\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/f5/Santa_beard.png\" width=\"327\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>December 2023 <br/> <b>Santa Beard</b> (Paper mask) <br/> <i>A luxurious Santa beard meticulously handcrafted from the finest sheep\'s wool, providing a cozy feel and gentle warmth to your face.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2024\">2024</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 326.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Grimshadow.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"285\" data-file-width=\"462\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/8/84/Grimshadow.png\" width=\"325\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>January 2024 <br/> <b>Grimshadow</b> (Butchering knife) <br/> <i>An elegant weapon of silent death, its gleaming edge infused with the essence of darkness.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 330px\"><div style=\"width: 330px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 328px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Large_anvil_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"284\" data-file-width=\"465\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/3/37/Large_anvil_skin.png\" width=\"328\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>February 2024 <br/> <b>Thunderforge Anvil</b> (Large anvil) <br/> <i>A steadfast ally in the art of shaping metal.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 314px\"><div style=\"width: 314px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 312px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Lapine_Luminance_Brazier.PNG\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"245\" data-file-width=\"382\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/d/d5/Lapine_Luminance_Brazier.PNG\" width=\"312\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2024 <br/> <b>Lapine Luminance Brazier </b> (small brazier) <br/> <i>A flickering beacon of comfort and style, the Lapine Luminance Brazier shines bright.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 321.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 321.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 319.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Companion_Bird_Hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"290\" data-file-width=\"463\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/8/8f/Companion_Bird_Hat.png\" width=\"320\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2024 <br/> <b>Companion Bird Hat</b>  (green common wool hat) <br/> <i>Aah, spring is in the air! Some birdies seem to have found a new home and you certainly wouldn\'t want to disturb them.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 328px\"><div style=\"width: 328px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 326px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Regal_bed.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"285\" data-file-width=\"464\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/92/Regal_bed.png\" width=\"326\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2024 <br/> <b>Regal Bed</b> (bed) <br/> <i>Regal Bed: Snoozing the night away in this comfy bed - absolute bliss.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 331.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 329.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Dragon_lamp.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"287\" data-file-width=\"472\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/2/2b/Dragon_lamp.png\" width=\"330\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2024 <br/> <b>Dragon Lamp</b> (torch lamp) <br/> <i>Dragon Lamp: Let the mystical glow of dragon fire light up your surroundings.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 326px\"><div style=\"width: 326px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 324px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Wooden_bench.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"288\" data-file-width=\"466\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/0/0d/Wooden_bench.png\" width=\"324\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>September 2024 <br/> <b>Lindwyrm Bench</b> (wooden bench) <br/> <i>Lindwyrm Bench: A wooden bench featuring intricate carvings, inviting you to rest for a while.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 321.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Drinking_horn.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"293\" data-file-width=\"470\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/d/db/Drinking_horn.png\" width=\"322\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2024 <br/> <b>Drinking Horn</b> (water skin) <br/> <i>Drinking Horn: Drink mead or other delectable beverages of choice in style!</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 330.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 330.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 328.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Small_corbita.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"285\" data-file-width=\"468\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/1/1e/Small_corbita.png\" width=\"329\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>November 2024 <br/> <b>Small Corbita</b> (decorative ship) <br/> <i>Small Corbita: A detailed model of a corbita sits proudly on a polished wooden base.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 322.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 320.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Hell_Horse_Rider_Statuette.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"293\" data-file-width=\"469\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/e/e4/Hell_Horse_Rider_Statuette.png\" width=\"321\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>December 2024 <br/> <b>Hell Horse Rider</b> (statuette) <br/> <i>Hell Horse Rider Statuette: A brave rider and his fiery steed.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"2025\">2025</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 323.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 321.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Merry_flowers.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"287\" data-file-width=\"461\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/e/e9/Merry_flowers.png\" width=\"322\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>February 2025 <br/> <b>Merry Flowers</b> (pottery jar) <br/> <i>Merry Flowers: A beautiful flowering plant in a crimson vase.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 324.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 322.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rose_trellis_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"290\" data-file-width=\"468\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/6/69/Rose_trellis_skin.png\" width=\"323\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>March 2025 <br/> <b>Rose Arch Trellis</b> (rose trellis) <br/> <i>Rose Arch Trellis: Some climbing roses growing up a sturdy arch trellis with interwoven wooden panels.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 320.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 320.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 318.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:DragonHelmSkin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"236\" data-file-width=\"376\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/9a/DragonHelmSkin.png\" width=\"319\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>April 2025 <br/> <b>Dragon Helm</b> (great helm) <br/> <i>Dragon Helm: An awe-inspiring specimen of a great helm.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Marvellous_Mallet.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"286\" data-file-width=\"465\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/e/e7/Marvellous_Mallet.png\" width=\"326\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>May 2025 <br/> <b>Marvellous Mallet</b> (wooden mallet) <br/> <i>Marvellous Mallet: A meticulously crafted mallet, with walnut end plates and woven leather grip for increased comfort.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 327.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Orchard_bowl.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"287\" data-file-width=\"467\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/1/19/Orchard_bowl.png\" width=\"326\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>June 2025 <br/> <b>Orchard Bowl</b> (pottery bowl) <br/> <i>Orchard Bowl: An assortment of fruit tastefully arranged in a blue glazed pottery bowl.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 318px\"><div style=\"width: 318px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 316px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Statue_of_the_Renowned_Warrior.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"239\" data-file-width=\"377\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/2/25/Statue_of_the_Renowned_Warrior.png\" width=\"316\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>July 2025 <br/> <b>Statue of the Renowned Warrior</b> (Statuette) <br/> <i>Statue of the Renowned Warrior: A statuette of an acclaimed hero, basking in glory.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 330px\"><div style=\"width: 330px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 328px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Oven_skin.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"464\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/f/f2/Oven_skin.png\" width=\"328\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>August 2025 <br/> <b>Spacious Oven</b> (oven) <br/> <i>Spacious Oven: A spacious oven including a generous wooden worktop.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 325.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 323.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Small_Thunderforge.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"283\" data-file-width=\"457\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/7/79/Small_Thunderforge.png\" width=\"324\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>October 2025 <br/> <b>Small Thunderforge Anvil</b> (small anvil) <br/> <i>Small Thunderforge Anvil: The smaller, slightly less capable little brother of the mighty Thunderforge Anvil.</i>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>', 2),
(13197, 3019, 'Description', 'Description', 'A black pointed hat accented with a leather belt and golden buckle. Perfect attire for turning villagers into newts..', '<p><i>A black pointed hat accented with a leather belt and golden buckle. Perfect attire for turning villagers into newts..</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(13198, 3019, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'First obtained from killing hunter mobs during 2018 Halloween. Signature on the hat is from the mob that dropped it. i.e: \'a.ol.scent.crocodile\'. Functions as leather armour. Obtainable as part of the Halloween 2021 and 2022 events, either from Archaeology or slaying hostile mobs (excluding hell horse ). The archaeology version requires 3 witch hat fragments to complete. Cannot be dyed', '<ul><li>First obtained from killing <a href=\"/index.php/Hunter_mob\" title=\"Hunter mob\">hunter mobs</a> during 2018 Halloween.</li>\n<li>Signature on the hat is from the mob that dropped it. <i>i.e: \'a.ol.scent.crocodile\'.</i></li>\n<li>Functions as leather armour.</li>\n<li>Obtainable as part of the Halloween 2021 and 2022 events, either from <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> or slaying hostile mobs (excluding <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">hell horse</a>).</li>\n<li>The archaeology version requires 3 witch hat fragments to complete.</li>\n<li>Cannot be dyed</li></ul>', 1),
(13216, 1595, 'Description', 'Description', 'A common wool hat for all weathers.', '<p><i>A common wool hat for all weathers.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(13217, 1595, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Hats replace armour pieces to the head and do not provide any protection. Requires minimum 5 cloth tailoring skill to create. Additionally, a minimum of 20 cloth tailoring skill is required to create the coloured versions.', '<ul><li>Hats replace <a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armour</a> pieces to the head and do not provide any protection.</li>\n<li>Requires minimum 5 <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> skill to create.</li>\n<li>Additionally, a minimum of 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> skill is required to create the coloured versions.</li></ul>', 1),
(13218, 1595, 'Variants', 'Variants', 'There are six variants of the common wool hat: regular, blue, brown, dark, green, and red. These are all created from the finished base hat and colored raw dying materials. They may not be colored by using pre-made dye. To color a hat it needs to first be dipped in water ; activate water from a container in the inventory and on the base hat right click > create .  The table below shows all materials required to create a dyed hat, including the initial water. Color Water 1.5kg Cochineal Copper lump Iron lump Tannin Woad Blue 3 2 Brown 3 3 2 1 Dark 1 1 1 Green 2 1 Red 3 2 Gallery Common wool hat Blue common wool hat Brown common wool hat Dark common wool hat Green common wool hat Red common wool hat', '<p>There are six variants of the common wool hat: regular, blue, brown, dark, green, and red. These are all created from the finished base hat and colored raw dying materials. They may not be colored by using pre-made dye.\n</p>\n<p>To color a hat it needs to first be dipped in <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>; activate water from a <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">container</a> in the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> and on the base hat <b>right click</b> &gt; <b>create</b>.  The table below shows all materials required to create a dyed hat, including the initial water.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th height=\"17\" width=\"90\">Color\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a> 1.5kg\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Cochineal\" title=\"Cochineal\">Cochineal</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper lump</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">Iron lump</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Tannin\" title=\"Tannin\">Tannin</a>\n</th>\n<th width=\"90\"><a href=\"/index.php/Woad\" title=\"Woad\">Woad</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Blue\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Brown\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Dark\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Green\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"17\">Red\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">3\n</td>\n<td align=\"CENTER\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 212px\"><div style=\"width: 212px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 210px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"289\" data-file-width=\"243\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/1/19/Common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"210\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 190px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 200px\"><div style=\"width: 200px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 198px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Blue_common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"293\" data-file-width=\"232\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/e/ef/Blue_common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"198\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 178px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Blue common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210px\"><div style=\"width: 210px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Brown_common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"287\" data-file-width=\"239\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/4/40/Brown_common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"208\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 188px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Brown common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 200px\"><div style=\"width: 200px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 198px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Dark_common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"295\" data-file-width=\"234\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/7/78/Dark_common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"198\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 178px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Dark common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 204.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 204.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 202.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green_common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"289\" data-file-width=\"234\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/b/b3/Green_common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"203\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 183px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Green common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 203.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 203.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 201.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Red_common_wool_hat.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"293\" data-file-width=\"236\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/4/4e/Red_common_wool_hat.png\" width=\"202\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 182px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Red common wool hat\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>', 2),
(13219, 1738, 'Description', 'Description', 'The blue leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.', '<p><i>The blue leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(13220, 1738, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Wall of Stone (click tile border to create a wall of stone, needs to be one tile to the right or left - 400 Karma to cast) Spell granted: Wall of Ice (click tile border to create a wall of ice, needs to be one tile to the right or left - 400 Karma to cast) Resistance: Cold 15% (Decreases cold damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Acid 10% (Increases Acid damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Wall of Stone (click tile border to create a wall of stone, needs to be one tile to the right or left - 400 Karma to cast)</li>\n<li>Spell granted: Wall of Ice (click tile border to create a wall of ice, needs to be one tile to the right or left - 400 Karma to cast)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Cold 15% (Decreases cold damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Acid 10% (Increases Acid damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(13221, 1738, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be standing in the cleansing shallow water.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, standing in shallow water.\n</p>', 2),
(13222, 1737, 'Description', 'Description', 'The black leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.', '<p><i>The black leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(13223, 1737, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Summon Skeletons (Summons a group of skeletons) (Costs 500karma to summon) Spell granted: Summon Wraith (Summons a Wraith) Resistance: Disease 15% (Decreases disease damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Water 10% (Increases water damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Summon Skeletons (Summons a group of skeletons) (Costs 500karma to summon)</li>\n<li>Spell granted: Summon Wraith (Summons a Wraith)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Disease 15% (Decreases disease damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Water 10% (Increases water damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(13224, 1737, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight. Can be used at any altar in 3x3 flat area, within a cave.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be in the darkness of caves, sheltered from sight.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in 3x3 flat area, within a cave.\n</p>', 2),
(13225, 1734, 'Description', 'Description', 'The red leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.', '<p><i>The red leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(13226, 1734, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Fireball (An AoE Fireball Attack) Resistance: Fire 15% (Decreases fire damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Internal 10% (Increases internal damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Fireball (An AoE Fireball Attack)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Fire 15% (Decreases fire damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Internal 10% (Increases internal damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(13227, 1734, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be deep in the barren desert, where nothing ever grows. Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, inside at least 51x51 sand area.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be deep in the barren desert, where nothing ever grows.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, inside at least 51x51 sand area.\n</p>', 2),
(13228, 1743, 'Description', 'Description', 'The white leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.', '<p><i>The white leather covers will reveal the secrets of high magic for the one who dares open them.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(13229, 1743, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Spell granted: Fire Wall (Summons a wall of fire on tile border) Spell granted: Ice Wall (Summons a wall of ice on tile border) Resistance: Bite 15% (Decreases bite damage taken by 15%) Weakness: Pierce 10% (Increases pierce damage taken by 10%)', '<ul><li>Spell granted: Fire Wall (Summons a wall of fire on tile border)</li>\n<li>Spell granted: Ice Wall (Summons a wall of ice on tile border)</li>\n<li>Resistance: Bite 15% (Decreases bite damage taken by 15%)</li>\n<li>Weakness: Pierce 10% (Increases pierce damage taken by 10%)</li></ul>', 1),
(13230, 1743, 'Item Use Requirements', 'Item_Use_Requirements', 'You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this. You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar. You need to be high up towards the heavens, closer to the gods.', '<blockquote>\n<p><i>You need to be standing in a 3x3 flat area in order to use this.<br/>You need to be in the vicinity of a holy altar.<br/>You need to be high up towards the heavens, closer to the gods.</i>\n</p>\n</blockquote>', 2),
(13231, 1743, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, at least 1000 slope above sea level.', '<ul><li>Can be used at any altar in a 3x3 flat area, at least 1000 slope above sea level.</li></ul>', 3),
(13232, 2792, 'Description', 'Description', 'Archaeology is a skill used in retrieving artifacts. It has one subskill of restoration . These skills are used for locating, identifying, and combining of fragments of different items from resources to weapons and more.', '<p>Archaeology is a skill used in retrieving artifacts. It has one subskill of <a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">restoration</a>. These skills are used for locating, identifying, and combining of fragments of different items from resources to weapons and more. \n</p>', 0),
(13233, 2792, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'The archaeology skill level helps determine what item or fragment you get when investigating tiles. It will also determine what and how much information you get on settlements that used to exist on or near the location investigated. The type of fragment you retrieve is determined based on: How many settlements have been on that tile in the past. How long the settlement(s) stood there. How long it has been since the settlement disbanded. Skill level. Each of these increase the difficulty of the action, but also increase the chances of finding uncommon item fragments, with the higher difficulties providing the most unique items. When finding a fragment, there may be a message in the event tab stating information on past settlement locations. The higher your skill level, the more information you may receive. You also need an archaeology journal and 30+ Ql paper to record records of the deed to get the cache. Investigation To investigate a tile, activate a trowel , right-click a tile and click Investigate . This will search the tile for fragments. At 20+ skill, a shovel may be used instead of a trowel, increasing the difficulty and timer length of the action. Some fragments are instantly identified upon discovery at this level with no further restoration work needed. At 30+ skill level, there is a chance to see the name of one of the settlements at that location: You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Sunnyvale. At 40+ skill, there is a chance to see the name of the last mayor: You can see signs of a single abandoned settlement here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, the settlement must have been called Splash Point. You find a scrap of washed out parchment signed by the last mayor, Badgirl. At 50+ skill level, there is a chance to see the name of the settlement\'s founder: You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Mordor. You recall this settlement, and remember the name of the founder as Gromclad. At 70+ skill level, there is a chance to see names of deeds in the area some tiles away and the time since abandonment of a deed: You spot some markers of an old settlement in the area. It looks like it may be close to the northeast from here. You find a small scrap of something that has the deed name on it... \'Kittenforest Paradise\'. At 80+ skill level, there is a chance to see the length of the period that a deed was occupied: You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Grindavik. You make a rough estimate that the settlement was inhabited for about 8 years, 2 months. In areas that are considered valuable, finding fragments is a bit easier at higher levels.', '<p>The archaeology skill level helps determine what item or fragment you get when investigating tiles. It will also determine what and how much information you get on settlements that used to exist on or near the location investigated.\n</p>\n<p>The type of fragment you retrieve is determined based on:\n</p>\n<ul><li>How many settlements have been on that tile in the past.</li>\n<li>How long the settlement(s) stood there.</li>\n<li>How long it has been since the settlement disbanded.</li>\n<li>Skill level.</li></ul>\n<p>Each of these increase the difficulty of the action, but also increase the chances of finding uncommon item fragments, with the higher difficulties providing the most unique items.\n</p>\n<p>When finding a fragment, there may be a message in the event tab stating information on past settlement locations. The higher your skill level, the more information you may receive. You also need an <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">archaeology journal</a> and 30+ Ql paper to record records of the deed to get the cache.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Investigation\">Investigation</span></h3>\n<p>To investigate a tile, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a>, right-click a tile and click <i>Investigate</i>. This will search the tile for fragments.\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 20+ skill, a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> may be used instead of a trowel, increasing the difficulty and timer length of the action. Some fragments are instantly identified upon discovery at this level with no further restoration work needed.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>At 30+ skill level, there is a chance to see the name of one of the settlements at that location:</li></ul>\n<p><i>You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Sunnyvale.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 40+ skill, there is a chance to see the name of the last mayor:</li></ul>\n<p><i>You can see signs of a single abandoned settlement here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, the settlement must have been called Splash Point. You find a scrap of washed out parchment signed by the last mayor, Badgirl.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 50+ skill level, there is a chance to see the name of the settlement\'s founder:</li></ul>\n<p><i>You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Mordor. You recall this settlement, and remember the name of the founder as Gromclad.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 70+ skill level, there is a chance to see names of deeds in the area some tiles away and the time since abandonment of a deed:</li></ul>\n<p><i>You spot some markers of an old settlement in the area. It looks like it may be close to the northeast from here. You find a small scrap of something that has the deed name on it... \'Kittenforest Paradise\'.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 80+ skill level, there is a chance to see the length of the period that a deed was occupied:</li></ul>\n<p><i>You can see multiple markers of abandoned settlements here. Based on your knowledge of the area and small hints you can find, one of the settlements must have been called Grindavik. You make a rough estimate that the settlement was inhabited for about 8 years, 2 months.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>In areas that are considered valuable, finding fragments is a bit easier at higher levels.</li></ul>', 1),
(13234, 2792, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Rarity of a fragment will always transfer over to the finished item becoming rare, despite the order by which the fragments are combined. When investigating only tiles that were part of a deed when the deed disbanded, count as part of that specific deed', '<ul><li>Rarity of a fragment will always transfer over to the finished item becoming rare, despite the order by which the fragments are combined.</li>\n<li>When investigating only tiles that were part of a deed when the deed disbanded, count as part of that specific deed</li></ul>', 2),
(13235, 2792, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Archaeology Mind > Mind logic Body > Body control Subskill Restoration', '<ul><li>Archaeology</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskill\">Subskill</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">Restoration</a></li></ul>', 3),
(13236, 2792, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Investigator at 50 skill Archaeologist at 70 skill Curator at 90 skill Witness to Decay at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Investigator at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Archaeologist at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Curator at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Witness to Decay at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(13237, 2792, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Restoration Archaeology journal (Cache info found here) Small token', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Restoration\" title=\"Restoration\">Restoration</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">Archaeology journal</a> (Cache info found here)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_token\" title=\"Small token\">Small token</a></li></ul>', 5),
(13259, 2436, 'Description', 'Description', 'Runes are items that can be used to give other items a bonus, or used one time to activate their effect. There are 65 different rune effects in Wurm, using combinations of 13 different metals and 5 possible gods available.', '<p>Runes are items that can be used to give other items a bonus, or used one time to activate their effect.\n</p>\n<p>There are 65 different rune effects in Wurm, using combinations of 13 different <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">metals</a> and 5 possible <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/God\" title=\"God\">gods</a> available.\n</p>', 0),
(13260, 2436, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Stone Rune of Vynora, Brass Runes are crafted by using different materials found at rifts ( rift crystal , rift stone shard , and rift wood ) combined with a lump of metal. The different combinations will create different rune types, each type giving a different effect. When crafting a rift resource with a lump of metal, you are given the option of 5 different rune types: Fo Magranon Vynora Libila Jackal Crystal runes use jewelry smithing to create. Stone runes use stonecutting , and wood runes use fine carpentry . Each god and metal combination creates a rune of a different effect; that is, a brass rune of Libila will not have the same effect as a brass rune of Magranon. Some may be similar in effect, with different strengths. Any player of any religion can make any rune of any god-type. However, creating runes of one\'s own corresponding god-type gives a bonus and is easier at creation. Jackal runes are, therefore, the most difficult to work with all the way around.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:202px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rune1.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"641\" data-file-width=\"869\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"148\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/Rune1.jpg/200px-Rune1.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/Rune1.jpg/300px-Rune1.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7d/Rune1.jpg/400px-Rune1.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rune1.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Stone Rune of Vynora, Brass</div></div></div>\n<p>Runes are crafted by using different materials found at <a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">rifts</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Rift_crystal\" title=\"Rift crystal\">rift crystal</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rift_stone_shard\" title=\"Rift stone shard\">rift stone shard</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Rift_wood\" title=\"Rift wood\">rift wood</a>) combined with a lump of metal. The different combinations will create different rune types, each type giving a different effect.\n</p>\n<p>When crafting a rift resource with a lump of metal, you are given the option of 5 different rune types:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal</a></li></ul>\n<p>Crystal runes use <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">jewelry smithing</a> to create. Stone runes use <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stonecutting\" title=\"Stonecutting\">stonecutting</a>, and wood runes use <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Each god and metal combination creates a rune of a different effect; that is, a brass rune of Libila will not have the same effect as a brass rune of Magranon. Some may be similar in effect, with different strengths. Any player of any religion can make any rune of any god-type. However, creating runes of one\'s own corresponding god-type gives a bonus and is easier at creation. Jackal runes are, therefore, the most difficult to work with all the way around.\n</p>', 1),
(13261, 2436, 'Effects', 'Effects', 'The combination of metal type and god type will determine the effect of a rune. The rift resource used will determine what the rune can be attached to or used on. Rift wood runes - can be used on wooden items, and use fine carpentry skill to create. Rift crystal runes - can be used on metal items, and use jewelry smithing skill to create. Rift stone runes - can be used on stone , pottery , cloth and leather items, and use stonecutting skill to create.', '<p>The combination of metal type and god type will determine the effect of a rune.\n</p>\n<p>The rift resource used will determine what the rune can be attached to or used on.\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>Rift wood runes</i> - can be used on <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">wooden</a> items, and use fine carpentry skill to create.</li>\n<li><i>Rift crystal runes</i> - can be used on metal items, and use jewelry smithing skill to create.</li>\n<li><i>Rift stone runes</i> - can be used on <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Masonry_items\" title=\"Category:Masonry items\">stone</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery\" title=\"Pottery\">pottery</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Cloth_tailoring_items\" title=\"Category:Cloth tailoring items\">cloth</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leather</a> items, and use stonecutting skill to create.</li></ul>', 2),
(13262, 2436, 'Properties (perks)', 'Properties_.28perks.29', 'Runes\' Properties List Metal Fo Jackal Libila Magranon Vynora The Scavenger** Adamantine 5% less enchant decay, 5% Enchant Success RAF 1x Random color on item RAJ 10% Less enchant decay RAL 10% Vehicle Speed RAM 7.5% Vehicle Speed, 5% Less decay RAV 10% enchant success, 10% less decay RAS Brass 5% More quality when imped, 5% higher gathering QL ( QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting ) RBrF \"Bright\" Glow RBrJ \"Okay\" Glow, 5% higher gather QL ( QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting ) RBrL 10% more quality when imped RBrM \"Slight\" Glow, 7.5% more quality when imped RBrV 10% less damage taken, 10% less weight RBrS Bronze 10% Wind Speed RBzF 1x Goat Shape (Spell) RBzJ 10% higher gather QL (any item) ( QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting ) RBzL 5% higher gather QL, 5% less enchant decay ( QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting ) RBzM 7.5% Wind Speed, 5% Vehicle Speed (any item) RBzV 10% more quality when imped, 10% less enchant decay RBzS Copper 1x Charm Animal (Spell) RCF 5% Higher improve chance, 5% Less Decay on contents RCJ 1x Locate Soul (Spell) RCL 5% Higher improve chance, 5% Increased rarity chance RCM 7.5% Higher improve chance RCV 10% Higher improve chance, 10% less QL loss from repairing RCS Electrum 1x Reduce creature\'s age * REF N/A REJ N/A REL N/A REM N/A REV ? RES Glimmersteel 10% skill level bonus *** RGsF 5% skill level bonus ***, 5% more quality when imped RGsJ 10% usage speed RGsL 5% usage speed, 5% skill level bonus *** RGsM 5% usage speed, 5% more quality when imped RGsV 10% usage speed, 10% shatter resistance RGsS Gold 10% chance to increase the effect of tending a field or harvesting a tree, bush, or trellis**** RGF 10% reduced size RGJ 5% raking/harvesting, 5% less weight (any item) RGL 5% reduced size, 5% less weight RGM 1x reveal creatures (Spell) RGV 10% less QL loss from repairing, 10% less damage taken RGS Iron 10% less fuel usage RIF 5% raking/harvesting, 5% less decay (any item) RIJ 1x light token (Spell) RIL 1x sunder (spell) RIM 5% less fuel usage, 5% less decay RIV 10% reduced size, 10% less enchant decay RIS Lead 5% less QL loss from repairing, 5% usage speed RLF 10% less volume RLJ 5% reduced volume, 5% usage speed RLL 10% less QL lost when repaired RLM 5% less QL lost when repaired, 5% increased volume RLV 10% reduced volume, 10% usage speed RLS Seryll 10% enchant success RSeF 5% enchant success, 5% less QL loss from repairing RSeJ 5% shatter resistance, 5% less QL loss from repairing RSeL 10% shatter resistance RSeM 5% shatter resistance, 5% enchant success RSeV 10% enchant success, 10% shatter resistance RseS Silver \"Okay glow\", 5% skill level bonus RSiF \"Okay glow\", 7.5% increased volume RSiJ 5% increased volume, 5% less decay on contents RSiL 10% increased volume RSiM 10% less decay on contents RSiV 10% increased volume, 10% less decay on contents RSiS Steel 5% less decay, 5% less damage taken RStF 10% less decay RStJ 5% less damage taken, 5% wind speed (any item) RStL 5% reduced decay, 5% more wind speed (any item) RStM 10% less damage taken RStV 10% less damage taken, 10% less decay RStS Tin 5% increased rarity chance, 5% less damage taken RTF 1x Second Wind (Spell) RTJ 5% increased rarity chance, 5% higher improve chance RTL 1x mole senses (Spell) RTM 10% increased rarity chance RTV 10% increased rarity chance,  10% higher improve chance RTS Zinc 1x morning fog (Spell) RZF 5% less weight, 5% vehicle speed (any item) RZJ 10% less weight RZL 5% increased size, 5% vehicle speed (any item) RZM 1x mend (Spell) RZV 10% less weight , 10% increased size RZS * Reduces age by a percentage of the current age. Creatures cannot be pregnant when the rune is used. The minimum age this can be used on is Aged (12 months). Does not work on aggressive animals until you tame / dominate / charm them. ** Runes of The Scavenger can be found on items recovered through Restoration , and cannot be created or attached to existing items. *** \"Skill level bonus\" reduces the distance of the skill\'s value from 100 by the percentage given, but only for the purpose of random skill checks. For example, a pickaxe with this rune would harvest slightly higher quality ore on average, but will not increase the maximum quality possible. **** When milking, harvesting a tree/trellis/wishing tree holy site, or searching for wurms/grubs/other fishing bait: chance for 1 extra action tick, giving you an extra item (or extra volume in the case of milk). When tending a field or large planter: a chance to have an extra effect roughly equivalent to an additional successful tending action on the field. Notes Runes for raking/gathering, gathering quality, and vehicle speed can be added to any material, regardless of their own material. Any rune with raking or gathering effects will also effect milking actions. (Spell Runes) Spell runes will not attach, if successful instead they will cast the listed spell 1 time. Spell runes are created in the same method as all other runes. Spell runes do not require any priest to activate or create.', '<table class=\"wikitable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"7\">Runes\' Properties List\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Metal\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Fo\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Jackal\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Libila\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Magranon\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Vynora\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">The Scavenger**\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Adamantine\n</th>\n<td>5% less enchant decay, 5% Enchant Success<br/>RAF\n</td>\n<td>1x Random color on item<br/>RAJ\n</td>\n<td>10% Less enchant decay<br/>RAL\n</td>\n<td>10% Vehicle Speed<br/>RAM\n</td>\n<td>7.5% Vehicle Speed, 5% Less decay<br/>RAV\n</td>\n<td>10% enchant success, 10% less decay<br/>RAS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Brass\n</th>\n<td>5% More quality when imped, 5% higher gathering QL (<b>QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting</b>)<br/>RBrF\n</td>\n<td>\"Bright\" Glow<br/>RBrJ\n</td>\n<td>\"Okay\" Glow, 5% higher gather QL (<b>QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting</b>)<br/>RBrL\n</td>\n<td>10% more quality when imped<br/>RBrM\n</td>\n<td>\"Slight\" Glow, 7.5% more quality when imped<br/>RBrV\n</td>\n<td>10% less damage taken, 10% less weight<br/>RBrS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Bronze\n</th>\n<td>10% Wind Speed<br/>RBzF\n</td>\n<td>1x Goat Shape (Spell)<br/>RBzJ\n</td>\n<td>10% higher gather QL (any item) (<b>QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting</b>)<br/>RBzL\n</td>\n<td>5% higher gather QL, 5% less enchant decay (<b>QL of gathered items does not exceed skill level for mining or woodcutting</b>)<br/>RBzM\n</td>\n<td>7.5% Wind Speed, 5% Vehicle Speed (any item)<br/>RBzV\n</td>\n<td>10% more quality when imped, 10% less enchant decay<br/>RBzS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Copper\n</th>\n<td>1x Charm Animal (Spell) <br/>RCF\n</td>\n<td>5% Higher improve chance, 5% Less Decay on contents<br/>RCJ\n</td>\n<td>1x Locate Soul (Spell)<br/>RCL\n</td>\n<td>5% Higher improve chance, 5% Increased rarity chance<br/>RCM\n</td>\n<td>7.5% Higher improve chance<br/>RCV\n</td>\n<td>10% Higher improve chance, 10% less QL loss from repairing<br/>RCS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Electrum\n</th>\n<td>1x Reduce creature\'s age *<br/>REF\n</td>\n<td>N/A<br/>REJ\n</td>\n<td>N/A<br/>REL\n</td>\n<td>N/A<br/>REM\n</td>\n<td>N/A<br/>REV\n</td>\n<td>?<br/>RES\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Glimmersteel\n</th>\n<td>10% skill level bonus ***<br/>RGsF\n</td>\n<td>5% skill level bonus ***, 5% more quality when imped<br/>RGsJ\n</td>\n<td>10% usage speed<br/>RGsL\n</td>\n<td>5% usage speed, 5% skill level bonus ***<br/>RGsM\n</td>\n<td>5% usage speed, 5% more quality when imped<br/>RGsV\n</td>\n<td>10% usage speed, 10% shatter resistance<br/>RGsS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Gold\n</th>\n<td>10% chance to increase the effect of tending a field or harvesting a tree, bush, or trellis****<br/>RGF\n</td>\n<td>10% reduced size<br/>RGJ\n</td>\n<td>5% raking/harvesting, 5% less weight (any item)<br/>RGL\n</td>\n<td>5% reduced size, 5% less weight<br/>RGM\n</td>\n<td>1x reveal creatures (Spell)<br/>RGV\n</td>\n<td>10% less QL loss from repairing, 10% less damage taken<br/>RGS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Iron\n</th>\n<td>10% less fuel usage<br/>RIF\n</td>\n<td>5% raking/harvesting, 5% less decay (any item)<br/>RIJ\n</td>\n<td>1x light token (Spell)<br/>RIL\n</td>\n<td>1x sunder (spell)<br/>RIM\n</td>\n<td>5% less fuel usage, 5% less decay<br/>RIV\n</td>\n<td>10% reduced size, 10% less enchant decay<br/>RIS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Lead\n</th>\n<td>5% less QL loss from repairing, 5% usage speed<br/>RLF\n</td>\n<td>10% less volume<br/>RLJ\n</td>\n<td>5% reduced volume, 5% usage speed<br/>RLL\n</td>\n<td>10% less QL lost when repaired<br/>RLM\n</td>\n<td>5% less QL lost when repaired, 5% increased volume<br/>RLV\n</td>\n<td>10% reduced volume, 10% usage speed<br/>RLS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Seryll\n</th>\n<td>10% enchant success<br/>RSeF\n</td>\n<td>5% enchant success, 5% less QL loss from repairing<br/>RSeJ\n</td>\n<td>5% shatter resistance, 5% less QL loss from repairing<br/>RSeL\n</td>\n<td>10% shatter resistance<br/>RSeM\n</td>\n<td>5% shatter resistance, 5% enchant success<br/>RSeV\n</td>\n<td>10% enchant success, 10% shatter resistance<br/>RseS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Silver\n</th>\n<td>\"Okay glow\", 5% skill level bonus<br/>RSiF\n</td>\n<td>\"Okay glow\", 7.5% increased volume<br/>RSiJ\n</td>\n<td>5% increased volume, 5% less decay on contents<br/>RSiL\n</td>\n<td>10% increased volume<br/>RSiM\n</td>\n<td>10% less decay on contents<br/>RSiV\n</td>\n<td>10% increased volume, 10% less decay on contents<br/>RSiS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Steel\n</th>\n<td>5% less decay, 5% less damage taken<br/>RStF\n</td>\n<td>10% less decay<br/>RStJ\n</td>\n<td>5% less damage taken, 5% wind speed (any item)<br/>RStL\n</td>\n<td>5% reduced decay, 5% more wind speed (any item)<br/>RStM\n</td>\n<td>10% less damage taken<br/>RStV\n</td>\n<td>10% less damage taken, 10% less decay<br/>RStS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Tin\n</th>\n<td>5% increased rarity chance, 5% less damage taken<br/>RTF\n</td>\n<td>1x Second Wind (Spell)<br/>RTJ\n</td>\n<td>5% increased rarity chance, 5% higher improve chance<br/>RTL\n</td>\n<td>1x mole senses (Spell)<br/>RTM\n</td>\n<td>10% increased rarity chance<br/>RTV\n</td>\n<td>10% increased rarity chance,  10% higher improve chance<br/>RTS\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Zinc\n</th>\n<td>1x morning fog (Spell)<br/>RZF\n</td>\n<td>5% less weight, 5% vehicle speed (any item)<br/>RZJ\n</td>\n<td>10% less weight<br/>RZL\n</td>\n<td>5% increased size, 5% vehicle speed (any item)<br/>RZM\n</td>\n<td>1x mend (Spell)<br/>RZV\n</td>\n<td>10% less weight , 10% increased size<br/>RZS\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<ul><li>* Reduces age by a percentage of the current age. Creatures cannot be pregnant when the rune is used. The minimum age this can be used on is Aged (12 months). Does not work on aggressive animals until you tame / dominate / charm them.</li>\n<li>** Runes of The Scavenger can be found on items recovered through <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology#Restoration\" title=\"Archaeology\">Restoration</a>, and cannot be created or attached to existing items.</li>\n<li>*** \"Skill level bonus\" reduces the distance of the skill\'s value from 100 by the percentage given, but only for the purpose of random skill checks. For example, a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a> with this rune would harvest slightly higher quality ore on average, but will not increase the maximum quality possible.</li>\n<li>**** When milking, harvesting a tree/trellis/wishing tree holy site, or searching for wurms/grubs/other fishing bait: chance for 1 extra action tick, giving you an extra item (or extra volume in the case of milk). When tending a field or large planter: a chance to have an extra effect roughly equivalent to an additional successful tending action on the field.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Runes for raking/gathering, gathering quality, and vehicle speed can be added to any material, regardless of their own material.</li>\n<li>Any rune with raking or gathering effects will also effect <a href=\"/index.php/Milking\" title=\"Milking\">milking</a> actions.</li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"(Spell_Runes)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\".28Spell_Runes.29\">(Spell Runes)</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Spell runes will not attach, if successful instead they will cast the listed spell 1 time.</li>\n<li>Spell runes are created in the same method as all other runes.</li>\n<li>Spell runes do not require any priest to activate or create.</li></ul>', 3),
(13263, 2436, 'Attaching', 'Attaching', 'Application of runes can usually be done by the owner. For vehicles, manage permission is required. Chance to successfully attach a rune depends on player Soul Depth and the Quality of the rune. Failure results in complete loss of the rune. The success chance one has to successfully attach a rune can be seen by activating the rune and right-clicking the object it will potentially be attached to. On-deed, the player doing the attaching must have improve/repair and pickup permissions . Can only attach them to completed items. Only one rune can be attached to an item. Attaching a new rune will replace the previous rune. If replacing the color change rune (Adamantine, Jackal), the color will remain on the item.', '<ul><li>Application of runes can usually be done by the owner. For vehicles, manage permission is required.</li>\n<li>Chance to successfully attach a rune depends on player <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Soul_Depth\" title=\"Soul Depth\">Soul Depth</a> and the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">Quality</a> of the rune. Failure results in complete loss of the rune. The success chance one has to successfully attach a rune can be seen by activating the rune and right-clicking the object it will potentially be attached to.</li>\n<li>On-deed, the player doing the attaching must have improve/repair and pickup <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a>.</li>\n<li>Can only attach them to completed items.</li>\n<li>Only one rune can be attached to an item.\n<ul><li>Attaching a new rune will replace the previous rune.</li>\n<li>If replacing the color change rune (Adamantine, Jackal), the color will remain on the item.</li></ul></li></ul>', 4),
(13264, 2436, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'Creation success will consume 0.2kg of the material, failure consumes 0.01kg. Runes decay dramatically fast outside of inventory. Runes are removed by a priest\'s dispel casting. Runes can also be replaced by attaching a new rune. Rune with \"Bright\" Glow effect (Crystal Brass Jackal rune) allows to use branding iron without heating it first. Runes with the Glow effect cannot be applied to items that can be lit, such as forges or smelters. Runes that increase volume will allow the affected container to hold more of items that already fit. Runes that increase size will allow the affected container to hold bigger items. They will also increase the amount of dye needed to paint that item. Any runes on weapon heads or spear heads will transfer over to the completed item when combined. Some Archeology items can be found with more than one rune on the item (up to 5 runes maximum).', '<ul><li>Creation success will consume 0.2kg of the material, failure consumes 0.01kg.</li>\n<li>Runes <b>decay</b> dramatically fast outside of inventory.</li>\n<li>Runes are <b>removed</b> by a priest\'s dispel casting.\n<ul><li>Runes can also be replaced by attaching a new rune.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Rune with \"Bright\" Glow effect (Crystal Brass Jackal rune) allows to use <a href=\"/index.php/Branding_iron\" title=\"Branding iron\">branding iron</a> without heating it first.</li>\n<li>Runes with the <i>Glow</i> effect cannot be applied to items that can be lit, such as forges or smelters.</li>\n<li>Runes that increase <i>volume</i> will allow the affected container to hold more of items that already fit.</li>\n<li>Runes that increase <i>size</i> will allow the affected container to hold bigger items. They will also increase the amount of <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a> needed to paint that item.</li>\n<li>Any runes on weapon heads or spear heads will transfer over to the completed item when combined.</li>\n<li>Some Archeology items can be found with more than one rune on the item (up to 5 runes maximum).</li></ul>', 5),
(13265, 2436, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Rift', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rift\" title=\"Rift\">Rift</a></li></ul>', 6),
(13297, 946, 'Description', 'Description', 'Skills on the Epic servers do not work as they do on the Classic servers.  They follow a \'curve\' where skill gain is faster at lower levels, and drops off the higher skills get.  The result is that players reach a certain level of skill more quickly, allowing new players to reach competitive levels more quickly, whilst retaining some benefit for more experienced players. Skills in the skill window are still listed at their non-curve level however. Due to The Curve the creation of certain items will unlock at a lower skill than listed on this wiki. Free accounts do not follow the curve on the Epic servers.  Once premium time has been bought the skills will follow The Curve, with no change to the listed skill. Skill gain is also faster at lower levels due to this curve.', '<p>Skills on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Epic\" title=\"Epic\">Epic servers</a> do not work as they do on the Classic servers.  They follow a \'curve\' where skill gain is faster at lower levels, and drops off the higher skills get.  The result is that players reach a certain level of skill more quickly, allowing new players to reach competitive levels more quickly, whilst retaining some benefit for more experienced players.\n</p>\n<p>Skills in the <a href=\"/index.php/Interface_and_controls#Skills\" title=\"Interface and controls\">skill window</a> are still listed at their non-curve level however.\n</p>\n<p>Due to The Curve the creation of certain items will unlock at a lower skill than listed on this wiki. \n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Account_types#Basic\" title=\"Account types\">Free accounts</a> do not follow the curve on the Epic servers.  Once premium time has been bought the skills will follow The Curve, with no change to the listed skill.\n</p>\n<p>Skill gain is also faster at lower levels due to this curve.\n</p>', 0),
(13298, 946, 'Formula', 'Formula', 'The Curve\'s formula is y = 2 x -( x /10)^2, where y is the \"effective skill\" and x is the raw skill number.  For example, at 50 raw skill in mining, one can get 75 max. ql of ore, since their effective skill is 2*50-(50/10)^2, which equals 75 effective skill. The reverse formula for this equation is -10*((100- y )^(1/2)-10) = x .', '<p>The Curve\'s formula is <i>y</i> = 2<i>x</i>-(<i>x</i>/10)^2, where <i>y</i> is the \"effective skill\" and <i>x</i> is the raw skill number.  For example, at 50 raw skill in mining, one can get 75 max. ql of ore, since their effective skill is 2*50-(50/10)^2, which equals 75 effective skill. The reverse formula for this equation is -10*((100-<i>y</i>)^(1/2)-10) = <i>x</i>.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(13299, 946, 'Exceptions', 'Exceptions', 'The following is an incomplete list of skills and abilities that do not follow the curve on the Epic servers: Main Fighting skill Combat rating Maximum house size 30 Masonry requirement to build stone or brick houses Faith Lockpicking Farming yields (harvest ql follows the curve) Digging slope Animal husbandry (ability to see traits follows the curve - ability to breed traits does not) Meditation Paving requirements for slate, marble, etc. Bow skill requirements for aiming at certain body parts Analyse Large crate and Wagon skill requirement', '<p>The following is an incomplete list of skills and abilities that <b>do not</b> follow the curve on the Epic servers:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Main <a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a> skill</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">Combat rating</a></li>\n<li>Maximum house size</li>\n<li>30 Masonry requirement to build stone or brick <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">houses</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lockpicking\" title=\"Lockpicking\">Lockpicking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Farming</a> yields (harvest ql follows the curve)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">Digging</a> slope</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">Animal husbandry</a> (ability to see traits follows the curve - ability to breed traits does not)</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Meditation\" title=\"Meditation\">Meditation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">Paving</a> requirements for slate, marble, etc.</li>\n<li>Bow skill requirements for aiming at certain body parts</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">Analyse</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a> skill requirement</li></ul>', 2),
(13300, 946, 'Helpful Tools', 'Helpful_Tools', 'WolframAlpha (Add \"if x is\" followed by skill to calculate a single value.) A Google search can show a graph of The Curve\'s formula as a graph .', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wolframalpha.com/input/?i=2x+-+%28x%2F10%29^2\" rel=\"nofollow\">WolframAlpha</a> (Add \"if x is\" followed by skill to calculate a single value.)</li>\n<li>A Google search can show a graph of The Curve\'s formula <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=2x-%28x%2F10%29^2+from+0+to+100\" rel=\"nofollow\">as a graph</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(13355, 3563, 'The aquatic life of Wurm', 'The_aquatic_life_of_Wurm', 'Yum! Fish make a tasty treat when cooked ! They can also be eaten raw.', '<p><i>Yum!</i> Fish make a tasty treat when <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooked</a>! They can also be eaten raw.\n</p>', 0),
(13356, 3563, 'Attributes', 'Attributes', 'All fish now have a set of attributes which determine where and when they are more likely to be caught: Preferred water type Minimum and maximum depth: if the depth of the water is between the min and max, then the fish is more likely to be caught; otherwise it’s harder the further away from either limit you are. Equipment Time of day: some fish like to feed in the morning, afternoon, evening or even at night. Morning (4:30-10:30) | Afternoon (10:30-16:30) | Evening (16:30-22:30) | Night (22:30-4:30). A higher number means the fish is more likely to feed at those times  (on a scale of 1-4). Bait: each fish has a favorite bait (on a scale of 1-10). Some it likes, others it is less likely to eat, and some it will never touch. Outside or in caves: some fish are only found underground. Rare fish can only be caught on special tiles (which are out at sea). Fishing height - how deep the fish swim. Water has several depths, allowing for fish to prefer a particular level Top - near the surface of the water Bottom - near the bottom of the water column Any - anywhere in the water column Water types Lake-Inland body of water at least 7 tiles radius. Fresh water. If a lake is connected to the sea by a canal of over 25 depth, it will count as Sea (salt water) whether above or below ground. Lake shallows-Enclosed inland body of water, shallower than 25 dirt. Fresh water. Pond-Inland body of water at least 2 tiles radius. Fresh water. Sea-Open water, not surrounded by land. Salt water. Sea shallows-Open water, shallower than 25 dirt. Salt water.', '<p>All fish now have a set of attributes which determine where and when they are more likely to be caught:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Preferred water type</li>\n<li>Minimum and maximum depth: if the depth of the water is between the min and max, then the fish is more likely to be caught; otherwise it’s harder the further away from either limit you are.</li>\n<li>Equipment</li>\n<li>Time of day: some fish like to feed in the morning, afternoon, evening or even at night. Morning (4:30-10:30) | Afternoon (10:30-16:30) | Evening (16:30-22:30) | Night (22:30-4:30). A higher number means the fish is more likely to feed at those times  (on a scale of 1-4).</li>\n<li>Bait: each fish has a favorite bait (on a scale of 1-10). Some it likes, others it is less likely to eat, and some it will never touch.</li>\n<li>Outside or in caves: some fish are only found underground. Rare fish can only be caught on special tiles (which are out at sea).</li>\n<li>Fishing height - how deep the fish swim. Water has several depths, allowing for fish to prefer a particular level\n<ul><li>Top - near the surface of the water</li>\n<li>Bottom - near the bottom of the water column</li>\n<li>Any - anywhere in the water column</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Water_types\">Water types</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Lake-Inland body of water at least 7 tiles radius. Fresh water. If a lake is connected to the sea by a canal of over 25 depth, it will count as Sea (salt water) whether above or below ground.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Lake shallows-Enclosed inland body of water, shallower than 25 dirt. Fresh water.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Pond-Inland body of water at least 2 tiles radius. Fresh water.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Sea-Open water, not surrounded by land. Salt water.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Sea shallows-Open water, shallower than 25 dirt. Salt water.</li></ul>', 1),
(13357, 3563, 'Known species', 'Known_species', 'Fish weight is based on its QL .\nFor each fish species there is a multiplier for this formula: QL * multiplier. \nFormula: weight divided by 3 and multiplied with the shown damage multiplier, then rounded down to one decimal. Your skill in fishing reduces the rod damage and the chance to break. Fish by water type Water type Fish Pond Carp, Minnow, Perch, Roach, Sardine, Trout Lake Carp, Catfish, Herring, Minnow, Perch, Pike, Roach, Salmon, Sardine, Smallmouth bass, Trout Lake shallows Minnow, Perch, Roach, Sardine Sea Blue shark, Catfish, Dorado, Herring, Marlin, Octopus, Sailfish, Salmon, Snook, Tuna, White shark, Smallmouth bass Sea shallows Minnow, Perch, Roach, Sardine Cave pond, Cave lake Loach, Minnow Cave sea Wurmfish Special fish tiles Blue shark, Marlin, Octopus, Sailfish, Tuna, White shark, Dorado Any water of any depth Sardine, Clam Fish by equipment type Equipment type Fish Net Clam, Sardine, Minnow, Perch, Roach Spear Brook trout, Carp, Catfish, Loach, Perch, Roach, Salmon Pole Carp, Minnow, Loach, Perch, Roach, Smallmouth Bass Light rod Brook trout, Carp, Catfish, Herring, Loach, Minnow, Perch, Pike, Roach, Salmon, Smallmouth Bass, Snook, Wurmfish Medium rod Brook trout, Carp, Catfish, Herring, Loach, Pike, Salmon, Snook Deep water rod Carp, Catfish, Dorado, Octopus, Snook, Tuna Professional rod Blue shark, Carp, Catfish, Dorado, Herring, Marlin, Octopus, Sailfish, Smallmouth Bass, Tuna, White shark, Wurmfish Fish information tables Blue shark Water types Sea Only surface Fishing height Any Special fish tiles only Swim depths 250-1000 Equipment Professional rod Fishing times Morning 4 Afternoon 3 Evening 4 Night 2 Baits Best: Sardines (none) 0 Cheese piece 1 Corn kernel 1 Dough Ball 1 Fish bait 0 Fly 0 Grub 1 Minnow 5 Perch 5 Roach 5 Sardines 10 Wheat Grain 1 Wurm 1 Weight at 10ql 4.00kg Multiplier by ql 0.4 Rod damage 1 Brook trout Water types Pond, Lake Only surface Fishing height Bottom Not special f