(15993, 4046, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a log before improving it. Activate a log (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the log is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>', 4),
(15994, 4046, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be sealed with 20 kgs of clay for a different look. Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a crowbar .', '<ul><li>Can be sealed with 20 kgs of <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> for a different look.</li>\n<li>Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(15995, 4046, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Log arch Log balcony Log canopy Log door Log double door Log double window Log double T arch Log T arch Log wall Log wide window Log window', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_arch\" title=\"Log arch\">Log arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_balcony\" title=\"Log balcony\">Log balcony</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_canopy\" title=\"Log canopy\">Log canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_door\" title=\"Log door\">Log door</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Log double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_double_window\" title=\"Log double window\">Log double window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_double_T_arch\" title=\"Log double T arch\">Log double T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_T_arch\" title=\"Log T arch\">Log T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_wall\" title=\"Log wall\">Log wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_wide_window\" title=\"Log wide window\">Log wide window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log_window\" title=\"Log window\">Log window</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 6),
(15996, 4056, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door.', '<p><i>You see a door. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(15997, 4056, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob, for example trolls , or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob, for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>, or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(15998, 4056, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 log and 1 peg in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Rustic log double door .', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Peg\" title=\"Peg\">peg</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Rustic log double door</b>.</li></ul>', 2),
(15999, 4056, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(16000, 4056, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a log before improving it. Activate a log (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the log is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>', 4),
(16001, 4056, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be sealed with 20 kgs of clay for a different look. Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a crowbar .', '<ul><li>Can be sealed with 20 kgs of <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> for a different look.</li>\n<li>Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(16002, 4056, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Rustic log arch Rustic log balcony Rustic log canopy Rustic log door Rustic log double door Rustic log double window Rustic log double T arch Rustic log T arch Rustic log wall Rustic log wide window Rustic log window', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_arch\" title=\"Rustic log arch\">Rustic log arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_balcony\" title=\"Rustic log balcony\">Rustic log balcony</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_canopy\" title=\"Rustic log canopy\">Rustic log canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_door\" title=\"Rustic log door\">Rustic log door</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Rustic log double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_double_window\" title=\"Rustic log double window\">Rustic log double window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_double_T_arch\" title=\"Rustic log double T arch\">Rustic log double T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_T_arch\" title=\"Rustic log T arch\">Rustic log T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_wall\" title=\"Rustic log wall\">Rustic log wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_wide_window\" title=\"Rustic log wide window\">Rustic log wide window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rustic_log_window\" title=\"Rustic log window\">Rustic log window</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 6),
(16003, 4079, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a door.', '<p><i>You see a door. </i>\n</p>', 0),
(16004, 4079, 'Locking', 'Locking', 'It can be locked with a door lock . Any humanoid mob, for example trolls , or player can pass through an unlocked door.', '<ul><li>It can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a>. Any humanoid mob, for example <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>, or player can pass through an unlocked door.</li></ul>', 1),
(16005, 4079, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 log and 1 peg in your inventory. Activate a mallet or hammer and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Hardwood log double door .', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Peg\" title=\"Peg\">peg</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Hardwood log double door</b>.</li></ul>', 2),
(16006, 4079, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(16007, 4079, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a log before improving it. Activate a log (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the log is affected by its damage and your Carpentry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> (minimum 16800 grams), right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>', 4),
(16008, 4079, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be sealed with 20 kgs of clay for a different look. Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a crowbar .', '<ul><li>Can be sealed with 20 kgs of <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a> for a different look.</li>\n<li>Clay can be removed from a sealed wall, by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(16009, 4079, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Hardwood log arch Hardwood log balcony Hardwood log canopy Hardwood log door Hardwood log double door Hardwood log double window Hardwood log double T arch Hardwood log T arch Hardwood log wall Hardwood log wide window Hardwood log window', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_arch\" title=\"Hardwood log arch\">Hardwood log arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_balcony\" title=\"Hardwood log balcony\">Hardwood log balcony</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_canopy\" title=\"Hardwood log canopy\">Hardwood log canopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_door\" title=\"Hardwood log door\">Hardwood log door</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Hardwood log double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_double_window\" title=\"Hardwood log double window\">Hardwood log double window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_double_T_arch\" title=\"Hardwood log double T arch\">Hardwood log double T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_T_arch\" title=\"Hardwood log T arch\">Hardwood log T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_wall\" title=\"Hardwood log wall\">Hardwood log wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_wide_window\" title=\"Hardwood log wide window\">Hardwood log wide window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hardwood_log_window\" title=\"Hardwood log window\">Hardwood log window</a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 6),
(16010, 4114, 'Description', 'Description', 'A spooky fang necklace.', '<p><i>A spooky fang necklace.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16011, 4114, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update. A decorative item obtained through Archaeology only during the annual Halloween event. Can be created by combining 3 fang necklace fragments.', '<ul><li>Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update.</li>\n<li>A decorative item obtained through <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> only during the annual Halloween event.</li>\n<li>Can be created by combining 3 fang necklace fragments.</li></ul>', 1),
(16012, 4115, 'Description', 'Description', 'Apparently this is bat country now.', '<p><i>Apparently this is bat country now.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16013, 4115, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update. A hangable decorative item obtained through Archaeology only during the annual Halloween event. Can be created by combining 8 Bat swarm fragments. Can be hung vertically from Ceilings .', '<ul><li>Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update.</li>\n<li>A hangable decorative item obtained through <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> only during the annual Halloween event.</li>\n<li>Can be created by combining 8 Bat swarm fragments.</li>\n<li>Can be hung vertically from <a href=\"/index.php/Ceilings\" title=\"Ceilings\">Ceilings</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16014, 4116, 'Description', 'Description', 'A Jack O\'Lantern which can be attached to various vehicles and ships, lighting the way.', '<p><i>A Jack O\'Lantern which can be attached to various vehicles and ships, lighting the way.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16015, 4116, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update. Can be attached to carts , wagons and some ships( small sailing boat and knarr ), obtained through Archaeology only during the annual Halloween event. Can be created by combining 5 Pumpkin lantern fragments.', '<ul><li>Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update.</li>\n<li>Can be attached to <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">carts</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagons</a> and some ships(<a href=\"/index.php/Small_sailing_boat\" title=\"Small sailing boat\">small sailing boat</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">knarr</a>), obtained through <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> only during the annual Halloween event.</li>\n<li>Can be created by combining 5 Pumpkin lantern fragments.</li></ul>', 1),
(16016, 4117, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tiny wraith stands guard. It seems unsure as to why it has been summoned.\'', '<p><i>A tiny wraith stands guard. It seems unsure as to why it has been summoned.\'</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16017, 4117, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update. A decorative item obtained through Archaeology only during the annual Halloween event. Can be created by combining 5 Tiny wraith fragments.', '<ul><li>Added as part of the Halloween 2025 update.</li>\n<li>A decorative item obtained through <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">Archaeology</a> only during the annual Halloween event.</li>\n<li>Can be created by combining 5 Tiny wraith fragments.</li></ul>', 1),
(16022, 4119, 'Description', 'Description', 'A coarse and flaking ember, said to have fallen from Sol itself. Striking this produces sparks of impossible heat, capable of starting fires without kindling.', '<p><i>A coarse and flaking ember, said to have fallen from Sol itself. Striking this produces sparks of impossible heat, capable of starting fires without kindling.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16023, 4119, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in place of a steel and flint , to start fires without kindling . Available from the Silver shop for 15 silver coins . First introduced in 2025. It is re-usable and can be dropped, but it is non-craftable. It is also possible to receive the Solar Cinder randomly from the gift pack in the Marks store at the token. As of lastest testing, this does not appear to give skill firemaking', '<ul><li>Used in place of a <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_and_flint\" title=\"Steel and flint\">steel and flint</a>, to start fires without <a href=\"/index.php/Kindling\" title=\"Kindling\">kindling</a>.</li>\n<li>Available from the <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_shop\" title=\"Silver shop\">Silver shop</a> for 15 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Silver_coin\" title=\"Silver coin\">silver coins</a>. First introduced in 2025.</li>\n<li>It is re-usable and can be dropped, but it is non-craftable.</li>\n<li>It is also possible to receive the Solar Cinder randomly from the gift pack in the Marks store at the token.</li>\n<li>As of lastest testing, this does not appear to give skill <a href=\"/index.php/Firemaking\" title=\"Firemaking\">firemaking</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16072, 1684, 'Description', 'Description', 'Santa Claus gives out gifts at several locations around christmas time. He gives gifts to all premium players who visit him.', '<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Santa Claus</a> gives out <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gifts\" title=\"Category:Gifts\">gifts</a> at several locations around christmas time. He gives gifts to all premium players who visit him.\n</p>', 0),
(16073, 1684, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'During the Christmas season, Santa Claus can be found located at all maps\' starter towns. His location can be seen from afar as it is marked with a multi-colored, ground-to-sky beacon/beam. He typically also brings along a julbord feast, stationed right next to him, from which players are welcome to eat as much as they like. For players unable to geographically reach Santa Claus, creating and using a Christmas tree at their own location provides the same gift-giving experience, minus the julbord feast. Santa and Christmas trees only respond to gift inquiries with a gift near to Christmas Day. This time period ranges from around one week before Christmas Day until about five days after it.', '<ul><li>During the Christmas season, Santa Claus can be found located at all maps\' starter towns. His location can be seen from afar as it is marked with a multi-colored, ground-to-sky beacon/beam.</li>\n<li>He typically also brings along a julbord feast, stationed right next to him, from which players are welcome to eat as much as they like.</li>\n<li>For players unable to geographically reach Santa Claus, creating and using a <a href=\"/index.php/Christmas_tree\" title=\"Christmas tree\">Christmas tree</a> at their own location provides the same gift-giving experience, minus the julbord feast.</li>\n<li>Santa and Christmas trees only respond to gift inquiries with a gift near to Christmas Day. This time period ranges from around one week before Christmas Day until about five days after it.</li></ul>', 1),
(16074, 1684, 'Previous gifts', 'Previous_gifts', 'On Christmas of 2005 he gave out a bag of keeping . On Christmas of 2006 he gave out a spyglass . On Christmas of 2007 he gave out a silver farwalker amulet . On Christmas of 2008 he gave out a sculpting wand . On Christmas of 2009 he gave out transmutation liquid . On Christmas of 2010 he gave out a box of fireworks . On Christmas of 2011 he gave out a garden gnome . On Christmas of 2012 he gave out a soft cap . On Christmas of 2013 he gave out a snow lantern . On Christmas of 2014 he gave out a yule goat . On Christmas of 2015 he gave out a yule reindeer . On Christmas of 2016 he gave out a picnic basket . On Christmas of 2017 he gave out saddle sacks . On Christmas of 2018 he gave out a snowman statue . On Christmas of 2019 he gave out a festive bedroll . On Christmas of 2021 he gave out a Jewelry Casket Skin . On Christmas of 2022 he gave out a Stocking . On Christmas of 2023 he gave out a Large sled , Merry wreath and Statue of elf . On Christmas of 2024 he gave out a figurine of Santa and a Hanging star lamp .', '<ul><li>On Christmas of 2005 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Bag_of_keeping\" title=\"Bag of keeping\">bag of keeping</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2006 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Spyglass\" title=\"Spyglass\">spyglass</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2007 he gave out a silver <a href=\"/index.php/Farwalker_amulet\" title=\"Farwalker amulet\">farwalker amulet</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2008 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Sculpting_wand\" title=\"Sculpting wand\">sculpting wand</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2009 he gave out <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquid</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2010 he gave out a box of <a href=\"/index.php/Fireworks\" title=\"Fireworks\">fireworks</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2011 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Garden_gnome\" title=\"Garden gnome\">garden gnome</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2012 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Soft_cap\" title=\"Soft cap\">soft cap</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2013 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Snow_lantern\" title=\"Snow lantern\">snow lantern</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2014 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Yule_goat\" title=\"Yule goat\">yule goat</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2015 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Yule_reindeer\" title=\"Yule reindeer\">yule reindeer</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2016 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Picnic_basket\" title=\"Picnic basket\">picnic basket</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2017 he gave out <a href=\"/index.php/Saddle_sacks\" title=\"Saddle sacks\">saddle sacks</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2018 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Snowman_statue\" title=\"Snowman statue\">snowman statue</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2019 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Festive_bedroll\" title=\"Festive bedroll\">festive bedroll</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2021 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_Casket_Skin\" title=\"Jewelry Casket Skin\">Jewelry Casket Skin</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2022 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Stocking\" title=\"Stocking\">Stocking</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2023 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_sled\" title=\"Large sled\">Large sled</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Merry_wreath\" title=\"Merry wreath\">Merry wreath</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Statue_of_elf\" title=\"Statue of elf\">Statue of elf</a>.</li>\n<li>On Christmas of 2024 he gave out a <a href=\"/index.php/Figurine_of_Santa\" title=\"Figurine of Santa\">figurine of Santa</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Hanging_star_lamp\" title=\"Hanging star lamp\">Hanging star lamp</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(16083, 4128, 'Patch Notes 13-JAN-2026', 'Patch_Notes_13-JAN-2026', 'Server Changelog New: Added a tree regrowth zone around the starter town on Guidance, increasing rate of tree spread and allowing trees to replace bushes. New: New title has been added for 100 skill in Toymaking. Congrats Hailiah! New: New title has been added for 100 skill in Axes. Congrats Rocklobster! Change: Portalling away from Defiance/Epic will no longer cause a 10 minute cooldown for portalling to other non-Defiance/Epic servers. Change: The Inspect Animal window now shows the same information regarding branding village, caretaker name, and taming loyalty that is shown when examining the creature. Change: Placing items now has the minimum 5-second timer regardless of item weight on-deed. This has the same requirements as the 1-second timer for Push and Pull: You must be within a village where you have Load permissions. Change: Goblin skulls, beer steins, skull cups, chess pieces, and bone fishing hooks will now decay. Goblin skulls, beer steins, chess pieces and skull cups have been made decorations, so they will not decay within settlements with at least 30 days of upkeep. Change: Cross-kingdom mail is now enabled on PvP servers. Bugfix: Fixed height clearance requirements for placing, pushing, and pulling items underneath bridges. You should now be able to move items underneath bridges as long as there is a reasonable amount of clearance *between the item and the bridge. Bugfix: Fixed a cause of the \"Could not find height to stop at\" error when placing or pushing items to the north or south. Bugfix: Fixed the Tunnel action sometimes not warning that there is an open caves diagonal to the new cave exit, or warning when it shouldn\'t. Bugfix: Dirt dug to a pile will now have normal pickup permissions applied as if the digging player were the one to drop it to the ground. Bugfix: Fixed an issue that could cause uniques to not die when killed. Bugfix: Deities should no longer block Destroy Roof actions. Bugfix: Caring for a caged creature now checks for things in the way between you and the cage, not between you and wherever the creature was prior to being caged. Bugfix: Fixed grammar of message received when calling guards through chat. Bugfix: Lighting bee smokers now takes the appropriate amount of time and gives skill, and once again requires it to be fueled. Bugfix: Vynora priests are no longer warned against destroying floors, walls, or fences, and will no longer suffer any Faith loss from performing these actions, as intended by the 2018 priest update. Bugfix: Planting a hedge or flower bed from inside a cave will no longer result in a bugged hedge or flower bed that cannot be interacted with properly. Existing bugged hedges and flower beds have been removed. Bugfix: Fixed not being able to take over enemy vehicles on PvP after the vehicle owner has changed kingdoms. Bugfix: Can no longer dominate hidden creatures Bugfix: Village role \"Drop\" permission is now checked when dragging items to containers on the ground. This is not applied to locked containers or vehicles, or containers inside them, since those have their own permissions. Bugfix: Fixed items being impossible to place along the ground if there is an item between the cursor and the target floor or bridge. Bugfix: Location required for structure-building missions should now be much more randomized, instead of frequently requiring the same location many times in a row. A message is now sent on PVE servers when starting to build an Epic mission structure that would not qualify for any current mission. The message is only informative, and does not prevent creating the item. Bugfix: Fixed items not updating their models when contents are added or removed, when the container is placed on another item or the Take action is used on contents. Bugfix: Corrected \"does not extend onto that tile\" bug when placing an item on walls or fences. Bugfix: Removed the ability to plan buggy walls underneath the bottom level of a house built on top of a dock. Client Changelog Change: Third person perspective will now cause the player to face the same direction the camera is facing, when the player is in combat. Change: Only movement related key presses will now quit out of board games, instead of just pressing any key. This should allow you to interact with the UI better while playing games, such as opening the chat by pressing a key. Bugfix: Fixed some particle effects attached to items scaling incorrectly, usually only visible when size runes are applied to the item. Bugfix: Fixed the camera spinning when entering board games in certain situations. Bugfix: Fixed player facing not updating in third person while mounted. Bugfix: Fixed mount movement being blocked when moving off surface floors onto cave entrances. Bugfix: Fixed some more instances of mount movement being blocked on floors incorrectly.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Server_Changelog\">Server Changelog</span></h3>\n<ul><li>New: Added a tree regrowth zone around the starter town on Guidance, increasing rate of tree spread and allowing trees to replace bushes.</li>\n<li>New: New title has been added for 100 skill in Toymaking. Congrats Hailiah!</li>\n<li>New: New title has been added for 100 skill in Axes. Congrats Rocklobster!</li>\n<li>Change: Portalling away from Defiance/Epic will no longer cause a 10 minute cooldown for portalling to other non-Defiance/Epic servers.</li>\n<li>Change: The Inspect Animal window now shows the same information regarding branding village, caretaker name, and taming loyalty that is shown when examining the creature.</li>\n<li>Change: Placing items now has the minimum 5-second timer regardless of item weight on-deed. This has the same requirements as the 1-second timer for Push and Pull: You must be within a village where you have Load permissions.</li>\n<li>Change: Goblin skulls, beer steins, skull cups, chess pieces, and bone fishing hooks will now decay. Goblin skulls, beer steins, chess pieces and skull cups have been made decorations, so they will not decay within settlements with at least 30 days of upkeep.</li>\n<li>Change: Cross-kingdom mail is now enabled on PvP servers.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed height clearance requirements for placing, pushing, and pulling items underneath bridges. You should now be able to move items underneath bridges as long as there is a reasonable amount of clearance *between the item and the bridge.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed a cause of the \"Could not find height to stop at\" error when placing or pushing items to the north or south.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed the Tunnel action sometimes not warning that there is an open caves diagonal to the new cave exit, or warning when it shouldn\'t.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Dirt dug to a pile will now have normal pickup permissions applied as if the digging player were the one to drop it to the ground.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed an issue that could cause uniques to not die when killed.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Deities should no longer block Destroy Roof actions.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Caring for a caged creature now checks for things in the way between you and the cage, not between you and wherever the creature was prior to being caged.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed grammar of message received when calling guards through chat.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Lighting bee smokers now takes the appropriate amount of time and gives skill, and once again requires it to be fueled.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Vynora priests are no longer warned against destroying floors, walls, or fences, and will no longer suffer any Faith loss from performing these actions, as intended by the 2018 priest update.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Planting a hedge or flower bed from inside a cave will no longer result in a bugged hedge or flower bed that cannot be interacted with properly. Existing bugged hedges and flower beds have been removed.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed not being able to take over enemy vehicles on PvP after the vehicle owner has changed kingdoms.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Can no longer dominate hidden creatures</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Village role \"Drop\" permission is now checked when dragging items to containers on the ground. This is not applied to locked containers or vehicles, or containers inside them, since those have their own permissions.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed items being impossible to place along the ground if there is an item between the cursor and the target floor or bridge.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Location required for structure-building missions should now be much more randomized, instead of frequently requiring the same location many times in a row. A message is now sent on PVE servers when starting to build an Epic mission structure that would not qualify for any current mission. The message is only informative, and does not prevent creating the item.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed items not updating their models when contents are added or removed, when the container is placed on another item or the Take action is used on contents.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Corrected \"does not extend onto that tile\" bug when placing an item on walls or fences.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Removed the ability to plan buggy walls underneath the bottom level of a house built on top of a dock.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Client_Changelog\">Client Changelog</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Change: Third person perspective will now cause the player to face the same direction the camera is facing, when the player is in combat.</li>\n<li>Change: Only movement related key presses will now quit out of board games, instead of just pressing any key. This should allow you to interact with the UI better while playing games, such as opening the chat by pressing a key.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed some particle effects attached to items scaling incorrectly, usually only visible when size runes are applied to the item.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed the camera spinning when entering board games in certain situations.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed player facing not updating in third person while mounted.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed mount movement being blocked when moving off surface floors onto cave entrances.</li>\n<li>Bugfix: Fixed some more instances of mount movement being blocked on floors incorrectly.</li></ul>', 0),
(16084, 4130, 'Description', 'Description', 'Alchemy is the skill used for creating healing items or substances out of natural resources such as botanized items.', '<p>Alchemy is the skill used for creating healing items or substances out of natural resources such as <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Botanize\" title=\"Botanize\">botanized</a> items.\n</p>', 0),
(16085, 4130, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Alchemy Mind > Mind logic Subskill Natural substances', '<ul><li>Alchemy</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskill\">Subskill</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Natural_substances\" title=\"Natural substances\">Natural substances</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16086, 4130, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Alchemist at 50 skill Chemist at 70 skill Shaman at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Alchemist at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Chemist at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Shaman at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(16087, 4130, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Natural substances items . Healing Natural substances Potions Sorcery Dye', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Natural_substances_items\" title=\"Category:Natural substances items\">Category:Natural substances items</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Healing\" title=\"Category:Healing\">Healing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Natural_substances\" title=\"Natural substances\">Natural substances</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Potions\" title=\"Category:Potions\">Potions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sorcery\" title=\"Sorcery\">Sorcery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">Dye</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16099, 4133, 'Description', 'Description', 'Made from ash and water, this is used when preparing leather. This has very low nutritional value. A mixture made through alchemy , used in the creation of leather , concrete , corrosive traps , and stamp erasers .', '<p><i>Made from ash and water, this is used when preparing leather. This has very low nutritional value.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A mixture made through <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a>, used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Leather\" title=\"Leather\">leather</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Concrete\" title=\"Concrete\">concrete</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Corrosive_trap\" title=\"Corrosive trap\">corrosive traps</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Stamp_eraser\" title=\"Stamp eraser\">stamp erasers</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16100, 4133, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Creating lye will consume all the water in the container, regardless of the amount of lye being made. Ash will be consumed at a ratio of 0.10 kg for every 1.00 kg of water. Quality of the lye is capped by the quality of the ash used and affected by your skill check success in natural substances . Failing to create lye wastes 0.10 kg of water and 0.10 kg of ash.', '<ul><li>Creating lye will consume all the <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a> in the container, regardless of the amount of lye being made. <a href=\"/index.php/Ash\" title=\"Ash\">Ash</a> will be consumed at a ratio of 0.10 kg for every 1.00 kg of water.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">Quality</a> of the lye is capped by the quality of the ash used and affected by your skill check success in <a href=\"/index.php/Natural_substances\" title=\"Natural substances\">natural substances</a>.</li>\n<li>Failing to create lye wastes 0.10 kg of water and 0.10 kg of ash.</li></ul>', 1),
(16101, 4133, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Lye is not edible. If you try to drink it, you get the message \"Eww.. the lye tastes funny and won\'t quench your thirst at all!\" Rare lye adds +1 to the QL of leather produced. Additional applications of rare lye need further research.', '<ul><li>Lye is not edible. If you try to drink it, you get the message \"Eww.. the lye tastes funny and won\'t quench your thirst at all!\"</li>\n<li>Rare lye adds +1 to the QL of leather produced. Additional applications of rare lye need further research.</li></ul>', 2),
(16121, 2779, 'Description', 'Description', 'A reddish chunk of rock containing many cavities lined with dark, metallic crystals.', '<p><i>A reddish chunk of rock containing many cavities lined with dark, metallic crystals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16122, 2779, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from iron veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 1.0 kg of iron lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of iron you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_vein\" title=\"Iron vein\">iron veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 1.0 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">iron lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of iron you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16135, 4145, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Stone', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone\" title=\"Stone\">Stone</a></li></ul>', 0),
(16136, 3235, 'Description', 'Description', 'Dig this tile with a shovel to get a heap of sand . Sand is used to make mortar with clay . \nDrop sand on a dirt tile to change it to sand.  Drop dirt on a sand tile to change it back to dirt. Sand has been used to prevent trees from growing, and is often used along highways to make the road more visible, and to make animals slower when crossing it. Depending on location, the following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Sand tiles: Desert weeds , Dune grass and Mineral debris . Submerged Sand tiles can also spawn Seaweed and Flotsam Resource nodes .', '<p>Dig this tile with a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> to get a <a href=\"/index.php/Heap_of_sand\" title=\"Heap of sand\">heap of sand</a>. Sand is used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a>. \nDrop sand on a <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> tile to change it to sand.  Drop dirt on a sand tile to change it back to dirt.\n</p>\n<p>Sand has been used to prevent trees from growing, and is often used along highways to make the road more visible, and to make animals slower when crossing it.\n</p>\n<p>Depending on location, the following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Sand tiles: <a href=\"/index.php/Desert_weeds\" title=\"Desert weeds\">Desert weeds</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Dune_grass\" title=\"Dune grass\">Dune grass</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a>.<br/>\nSubmerged Sand tiles can also spawn <a href=\"/index.php/Seaweed\" title=\"Seaweed\">Seaweed</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Flotsam\" title=\"Flotsam\">Flotsam</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16154, 3005, 'Description', 'Description', 'A crystalline chunk of clear quartz with golden clumps.', '<p><i>A crystalline chunk of clear quartz with golden clumps.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16155, 3005, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from gold veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 0.1 kg of gold lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of gold you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_vein\" title=\"Gold vein\">gold veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 0.1 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">gold lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of gold you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(16156, 3005, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Gold Lump', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gold_Lump\" title=\"Gold Lump\">Gold Lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16157, 3113, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick clump of large cubic grey metallic crystals.', '<p><i>A thick clump of large cubic grey metallic crystals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16158, 3113, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from lead veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 1.0 kg of lead lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of lead you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Lead_vein\" title=\"Lead vein\">lead veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 1.0 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Lead_lump\" title=\"Lead lump\">lead lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of lead you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(16159, 3113, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Lead lump', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lead_lump\" title=\"Lead lump\">Lead lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16160, 3024, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick clump of rock with metallic red and grey colours.', '<p><i>A thick clump of rock with metallic red and grey colours.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16161, 3024, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from silver veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 0.1 kg of silver lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of silver you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_vein\" title=\"Silver vein\">silver veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 0.1 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">silver lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of silver you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(16162, 3024, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Silver lump', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">Silver lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16188, 4164, 'Description', 'Description', 'Tannin acid made from acorns and water. Used with iron lump to create black dye .', '<p><i>Tannin acid made from acorns and water.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Used with <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">iron lump</a> to create black <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16189, 4164, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failure decreases the volume of water by 0.1 weight and decreases the quality of the acorn by 0.5 ql. Quality of the acorns will determine the maximum quality of the Tannin. (RNG still has a window on the quality of the Tannin)', '<ul><li>Failure decreases the volume of water by 0.1 weight and decreases the quality of the acorn by 0.5 ql.</li>\n<li>Quality of the acorns will determine the maximum quality of the Tannin. (RNG still has a window on the quality of the Tannin)</li></ul>', 1),
(16190, 4165, 'Description', 'Description', 'A yellow-flowered, no-joke, low growing plant with slender green leaves.', '<p><i>A yellow-flowered, no-joke, low growing plant with slender green leaves.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16191, 4165, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used to create blue dye . When planted in a pottery planter , can be harvested (picked) several times. Can be found by botanizing Low brush Resource nodes Can be found by botanizing Wildflowers Resource nodes It is significantly easier to find in Low brush Resource nodes.', '<ul><li>Can be used to create blue <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>.</li>\n<li>When planted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\">pottery planter</a>, can be harvested (picked) several times.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Low_brush\" title=\"Low brush\">Low brush</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a></li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>\n<ul><li>It is significantly easier to find in Low brush Resource nodes.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(16192, 4165, 'Images', 'Images', 'Woad in a pottery planter', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"585\" data-file-width=\"416\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e9/Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png/85px-Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e9/Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png/128px-Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e9/Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png/171px-Woad_planted_in_a_planter.png 2x\" width=\"85\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Woad in a pottery planter\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(16193, 2696, 'Description', 'Description', 'A clay jar hardened by fire.', '<p><i>A clay jar hardened by fire.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16194, 2696, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Decorative Flowers', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Decorative Flowers</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16195, 2696, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A pottery jar is created by heating a clay jar in a campfire , stone oven , forge , or kiln . Holds up to 2.00 kg of liquid. The jar can also hold non liquid items. A hardened pottery jar can no longer be improved, nor repaired. Can be sealed with a wax sealing kit to preserve contents from decay. Pottery jar is needed when creating a compass .', '<ul><li>A pottery jar is created by heating a <a href=\"/index.php/Clay_jar\" title=\"Clay jar\">clay jar</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_oven\" title=\"Stone oven\">stone oven</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">kiln</a>.</li>\n<li>Holds up to 2.00 kg of liquid.</li>\n<li>The jar can also hold non liquid items.</li>\n<li>A hardened pottery jar can no longer be improved, nor repaired.</li>\n<li>Can be sealed with a <a href=\"/index.php/Wax_sealing_kit\" title=\"Wax sealing kit\">wax sealing kit</a> to preserve contents from decay.</li>\n<li>Pottery jar is needed when creating a <a href=\"/index.php/Compass\" title=\"Compass\">compass</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(16196, 2696, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Pottery bowl Pottery flask', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">Pottery bowl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_flask\" title=\"Pottery flask\">Pottery flask</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16199, 2858, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Tileborder.jpeg\" title=\"A highlighted tile border\"><img alt=\"A highlighted tile border\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"470\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"160\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/9f/Tileborder.jpeg/200px-Tileborder.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/9f/Tileborder.jpeg/300px-Tileborder.jpeg 1.5x, /images/thumb/9/9f/Tileborder.jpeg/400px-Tileborder.jpeg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n<a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Tileborderflat.jpeg\" title=\"A highlighted flat tile border\"><img alt=\"A highlighted flat tile border\" data-file-height=\"364\" data-file-width=\"455\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"160\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/90/Tileborderflat.jpeg/200px-Tileborderflat.jpeg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/90/Tileborderflat.jpeg/300px-Tileborderflat.jpeg 1.5x, /images/thumb/9/90/Tileborderflat.jpeg/400px-Tileborderflat.jpeg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a>\n</p>', 0),
(16201, 1133, 'Description', 'Description', 'Fences are used to enclose your land or for decorative purposes.', '<p>Fences are used to enclose your land or for decorative purposes. \n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16202, 1133, 'Types of Fences', 'Types_of_Fences', 'Some of these restrict movement past, while others do not (for example, low rope fences can be crossed, and are therefore decorative only). Fences can be built on a maximum slope based on skill needed to build that fence. To build a fence activate a hammer or mallet and right click the tile border . Select Build and a fence type. Fences can be dyed with 1kg of dye per tile. Iron High iron fence Chain fence Iron fence Wooden Crude wooden fence High roundpole fence Low roundpole fence Palisade Wooden fence Wooden parapet Woven fence Palisade Stone Low stone wall Curb Stone and iron parapet Stone parapet Tall stone wall Stone fence Pottery Pottery fence Pottery iron fence Pottery parapet Pottery high iron fence Tall pottery wall Pottery chain fence Rounded Stone Rounded stone fence Rounded stone iron fence Rounded stone parapet Rounded stone high iron fence Tall rounded stone wall Rounded stone chain fence Slate Slate Fence Slate iron fence Slate parapet Slate high iron fence Tall slate stone wall Slate chain fence Marble Marble fence Marble iron fence Marble parapet Marble high iron fence Tall marble wall Marble chain fence Sandstone Sandstone fence Sandstone iron fence Sandstone parapet Sandstone high iron fence Tall sandstone wall Sandstone chain fence Rendered Rendered fence Rendered iron fence Rendered parapet Rendered high iron fence Tall rendered stone wall Rendered chain fence Rope and Shrubbery Camellia hedge Cedar hedge Oleander hedge Thorn hedge Rose hedge Maple hedge Lavender plantation High rope fence Low rope fence', '<p>Some of these restrict movement past, while others do not (for example, <a href=\"/index.php/Low_rope_fence\" title=\"Low rope fence\">low rope fences</a> can be crossed, and are therefore decorative only). \n</p>\n<p>Fences can be built on a <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> based on skill needed to build that fence. \n</p>\n<p>To build a fence activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> and right click the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile_border\" title=\"Tile border\">tile border</a>. Select <i>Build</i> and a fence type.\n</p>\n<p>Fences can be <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dyed</a> with 1kg of dye per tile. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Iron\">Iron</span></h3>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 202.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 202.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 200.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/High_iron_fence\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"851\" data-file-width=\"1138\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/46/High_iron_fence.jpg/301px-High_iron_fence.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/46/High_iron_fence.jpg/452px-High_iron_fence.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/46/High_iron_fence.jpg/602px-High_iron_fence.jpg 2x\" width=\"201\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 181px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>High iron fence\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 386px\"><div style=\"width: 386px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 384px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_fence\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"375\" data-file-width=\"959\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/a6/Chain_fence.png/576px-Chain_fence.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/a6/Chain_fence.png/865px-Chain_fence.png 1.5x, /images/a/a6/Chain_fence.png 2x\" width=\"384\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 364px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Chain fence\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 315.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 315.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 313.33333333333px;\"><div sty