rapper\" style=\"width: 356px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Lavender plantation\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 412.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 412.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 410.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/High_rope_fence\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"228\" data-file-width=\"624\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Highropefence.jpg/616px-Highropefence.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/1/1c/Highropefence.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"411\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 391px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>High rope fence\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 486px\"><div style=\"width: 486px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 484px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Low_rope_fence\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"160\" data-file-width=\"516\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/b/b5/Lowropefence.jpg\" width=\"484\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 464px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Low rope fence\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 1),
(16203, 1133, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Wall Category:Fences Gates Walls Mine doors House doors Empirical Evaluation of Fences Palisade', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wall\" title=\"Wall\">Wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Category:Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Gates</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Walls\" title=\"Category:Walls\">Walls</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mine_doors\" title=\"Category:Mine doors\">Mine doors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:House_doors\" title=\"Category:House doors\">House doors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Palisade\" title=\"Palisade\">Palisade</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16211, 4140, 'Description', 'Description', 'A white and pale green chunk of rock.', '<p><i>A white and pale green chunk of rock.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16212, 4140, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from copper veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 1.0 kg of copper lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of copper you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_vein\" title=\"Copper vein\">copper veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 1.0 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">copper lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of copper you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16213, 4140, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Copper lump', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16218, 4175, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tool for digging. Shovel is a versatile tool used mainly for digging and terraforming.', '<p><i>A tool for digging.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Shovel</b> is a versatile tool used mainly for digging and terraforming.\n</p>', 0),
(16219, 4175, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'When creating a shovel, the quality of the shaft affects success chance.\nThe quality of the shovel blade affects the initial quality of the shovel.', '<p>When creating a shovel, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> affects success chance.\nThe quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel_blade_(metal)\" title=\"Shovel blade (metal)\">shovel blade</a> affects the initial quality of the shovel.\n</p>', 1),
(16220, 4175, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Shovel is used to dig up clay , dirt , moss , peat , sand , and tar . Shovel is also the primary tool for terraforming , landscaping and building roads and packed dirt paths. With shovel you can \'Cultivate\' packed dirt, moss, grass, steppe or mycelium tiles into dirt suitable for farming . If your character has 10 digging and 20 body strength , you may use a shovel to destroy pavement such as cobblestone , gravel , stone slabs , or floor boards . Shovels can be used to disarm traps . You can cut down trees and bushes with a shovel, albeit much more slowly than with a hatchet . Shovels can be used to investigate tiles to search for archaeology fragments with 20+ skill in Archaeology - though with higher difficulty than using a trowel.', '<ul><li>Shovel is used to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dig\" title=\"Dig\">dig</a> up <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_dirt\" title=\"Pile of dirt\">dirt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">moss</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Peat\" title=\"Peat\">peat</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Heap_of_sand\" title=\"Heap of sand\">sand</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a>.</li>\n<li>Shovel is also the primary tool for <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">terraforming</a>, landscaping and building <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Roads\" title=\"Roads\">roads</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> paths.</li>\n<li>With shovel you can \'Cultivate\' packed dirt, moss, grass, steppe or mycelium tiles into dirt suitable for <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a>.</li>\n<li>If your character has 10 <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> and 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>, you may use a shovel to <a href=\"/index.php/Destroy_pavement\" title=\"Destroy pavement\">destroy pavement</a> such as <a href=\"/index.php/Cobblestone\" title=\"Cobblestone\">cobblestone</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Gravel\" title=\"Gravel\">gravel</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_slab\" title=\"Stone slab\">stone slabs</a>, or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Floor_boards\" title=\"Floor boards\">floor boards</a>.</li>\n<li>Shovels can be used to disarm <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">traps</a>.</li>\n<li>You can cut down trees and bushes with a shovel, albeit much more slowly than with a <a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">hatchet</a>.</li>\n<li>Shovels can be used to investigate tiles to search for <a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology\" title=\"Archaeology\">archaeology</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fragment\" title=\"Fragment\">fragments</a> with 20+ skill in Archaeology - though with higher difficulty than using a trowel.</li></ul>', 2),
(16221, 4175, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a shovel Miscellaneous items > Shovel When creating a shovel Smithing > Blacksmithing', '<p>When using a shovel\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Shovel</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a shovel\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16222, 4175, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Shoveler at 50 skill Packer at 70 skill Undertaker at 90 skill Ace Of Spades at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Shoveler at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Packer at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Undertaker at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Ace Of Spades at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(16223, 4175, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Crude shovel WARNING: The shovel given with the beginner set is made out of birchwood and is burnable. Take care as to not accidentally burn it to fuel a campfire, forge or oven! If you lose it in this way, you will have to either make a new one from scratch or ask other players for help in acquiring a new one.', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">Crude shovel</a>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>WARNING:</b> The shovel given with the beginner set is made out of birchwood and is burnable. Take care as to not accidentally burn it to fuel a campfire, forge or oven! If you lose it in this way, you will have to either make a new one from scratch or ask other players for help in acquiring a new one.\n</p>', 5),
(16224, 4176, 'Description', 'Description', 'Blended with water, this would produce lye. Ash is acquired either from a burnt out campfire , forge , oven , kiln , smelter , or charcoal pile . It is most often used as a component in the creation of lye .', '<p><i>Blended with water, this would produce lye.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Ash</b> is acquired either from a burnt out <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">kiln</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal_pile\" title=\"Charcoal pile\">charcoal pile</a>. It is most often used as a component in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">lye</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16225, 4176, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Adding logs to campfires will not increase the amount of ash created. Therefore, multiple fires are suggested for the purpose of bulk ash generation. To gather ash from a forge , oven , kiln , or smelter , activate a shovel , right-click the burning vessel that was recently used, and select \"clean\". At the 30-minute mark of a burn (real life minutes), enough material will have been consumed to create a collectable amount of ash. The actual act of gathering ash with a shovel from any such burning vessel utilizes the firemaking skill. The fire must be snuffed, before you can clean the item and collect ash. The QL of ash is capped at the QL of the item you are cleaning. You may get lower QL of ash due to RNG. Can be Foraged on Rubble Resource nodes .', '<ul><li>Adding <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a> will <b>not</b> increase the amount of ash created. Therefore, multiple fires are suggested for the purpose of bulk ash generation.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>To gather ash from a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">kiln</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a>, right-click the burning vessel that was recently used, and select \"clean\".</li>\n<li>At the 30-minute mark of a burn (real life minutes), enough material will have been consumed to create a collectable amount of ash. The actual act of gathering ash with a shovel from any such burning vessel utilizes the <a href=\"/index.php/Firemaking\" title=\"Firemaking\">firemaking</a> skill.</li>\n<li>The fire must be snuffed, before you can clean the item and collect ash.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of ash is capped at the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the item you are cleaning. You may get lower <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of ash due to RNG.</li>\n<li>Can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forage\" title=\"Forage\">Foraged</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Rubble\" title=\"Rubble\">Rubble</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16226, 4176, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Natural substances', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Natural_substances\" title=\"Natural substances\">Natural substances</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16242, 2535, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lump of pure iron.', '<p><i>A lump of pure iron.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16243, 2535, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting iron ore in a smelter , forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns  one 1.0kg iron lump per 20kg of iron ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ore\" title=\"Iron ore\">iron ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns  one 1.0kg iron lump per 20kg of iron ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(16244, 2535, 'Enchanting', 'Enchanting', 'Will be faster to use if enchanted with Wind of ages . Skill experience boost if enchanted with Circle of cunning Enchantments on iron lumps will degrade over time. You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one.', '<ul><li>Will be faster to use if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_ages\" title=\"Wind of ages\">Wind of ages</a>.</li>\n<li>Skill experience boost if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Circle_of_cunning\" title=\"Circle of cunning\">Circle of cunning</a></li>\n<li>Enchantments on iron lumps will degrade over time.</li>\n<li>You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one.</li></ul>', 2),
(16245, 2535, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The metal is considered an average material, and as such doesn\'t provide any special properties . Higher QL forges , campfires , and ovens will smelt the ore faster. To smelt you press \"open\" on the fire source and put the ore in the window.', '<ul><li>The metal is considered an average material, and as such doesn\'t provide any <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>.</li>\n<li>Higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">ovens</a> will smelt the ore faster.</li>\n<li>To smelt you press \"open\" on the fire source and put the ore in the window.</li></ul>', 3),
(16246, 2535, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Black dye requires iron. See List of iron products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from iron.', '<ul><li>Black <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a> requires iron.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Iron_products\" title=\"Category:Iron products\">List of iron products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from iron.</li></ul>', 4),
(16267, 4182, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long pole with a half meter long sharp blade, used for cutting grass or harvesting crops.', '<p><i>A long pole with a half meter long sharp blade, used for cutting grass or harvesting crops.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16268, 4182, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to harvest cereals . Can cut down trees . As a bladed weapon it can be used to butcher. A viable weapon with the same stats of a halberd . On a grass tile to make a cut grass tile, resulting in mixed grass or hay .', '<ul><li>Used to harvest <a href=\"/index.php/Cereals\" title=\"Cereals\">cereals</a>.</li>\n<li>Can cut down <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trees\" title=\"Trees\">trees</a>.</li>\n<li>As a bladed weapon it can be used to butcher.</li>\n<li>A viable weapon with the same stats of a <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">halberd</a>.</li>\n<li>On a grass tile to make a <a href=\"/index.php/Cut_grass\" title=\"Cut grass\">cut grass</a> tile, resulting in <a href=\"/index.php/Mixed_grass\" title=\"Mixed grass\">mixed grass</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Hay\" title=\"Hay\">hay</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16269, 4182, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.45 (Similar to the two handed sword) Attack Speed: 5 seconds (4 in aggressive mode) - Add 1 second on PVP servers Damage Type: Cutting Parry Rate: Rate uncertain, but capable of parrying. Wielding: Two-hander (can\'t use a shield with it)', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.45 (Similar to the two handed sword)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 5 seconds (4 in aggressive mode) - Add 1 second on PVP servers</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Rate uncertain, but capable of parrying.</li>\n<li>Wielding: Two-hander (can\'t use a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a> with it)</li></ul>', 2),
(16270, 4182, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.', '<ul><li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.</li></ul>', 3),
(16271, 4182, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a scythe Miscellaneous items > Scythe When creating a scythe Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a scythe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Scythe</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a scythe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(16272, 4182, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Harvester at 50 skill Reaper at 70 skill Hand of Libila at 90 skill Reaper of Souls at 100 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Harvester at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Reaper at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Hand of Libila at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Reaper of Souls at 100 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(16275, 4184, 'Description', 'Description', 'A kind of small hand-held scythe with a crescent-moon formed blade. The sickle is a tool used in forestry and gardening .', '<p><i>A kind of small hand-held scythe with a crescent-moon formed blade.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>sickle</b> is a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tool\" title=\"Tool\">tool</a> used in <a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">forestry</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">gardening</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16276, 4184, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Harvest fruit and other things from trees and bushes when in season . Pick flowers from certain grass tiles . At 15 Gardening mouse-overs will show the type of flowers growing. Pick sprouts from mature, old, and very old trees and bushes. Prune trees and bushes into younger stage. Can cut trees down. As it is bladed can be used as crude butchering knife and as a weapon.', '<ul><li>Harvest fruit and other things from <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bush\" title=\"Bush\">bushes</a> when in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>.</li>\n<li>Pick <a href=\"/index.php/Flower\" title=\"Flower\">flowers</a> from certain <a href=\"/index.php/Grass_tile\" title=\"Grass tile\">grass tiles</a>.</li>\n<li>At 15 <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">Gardening</a> mouse-overs will show the type of flowers growing.</li>\n<li>Pick <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">mature, old, and very old</a> trees and bushes.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry#pruning\" title=\"Forestry\">Prune</a> trees and bushes into younger stage.</li>\n<li>Can cut trees down.</li>\n<li>As it is bladed can be used as crude butchering knife and as a weapon.</li></ul>', 1),
(16277, 4184, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.30 (Stronger than a longsword, but weaker than a large axe) Attack Speed: 3 seconds (PvE), 4 seconds (PvP) Damage Type: Cutting Parry Rate: Low Wielding: One-hander', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.30 (Stronger than a longsword, but weaker than a large axe)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 3 seconds (PvE), 4 seconds (PvP)</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Low</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>', 2),
(16278, 4184, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Jackal sickle', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal sickle</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16279, 4184, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.', '<ul><li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.</li></ul>', 4),
(16280, 4184, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a sickle Miscellaneous items > Sickle When creating a sickle Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a sickle\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Sickle</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a sickle\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 5),
(16281, 4184, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Pruner at 50 skill Gatherer at 70 skill Fully Sickle at 90 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Pruner at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Gatherer at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Fully Sickle at 90 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 6),
(16288, 4186, 'Description', 'Description', 'A handful of oak acorns.', '<p><i>A handful of oak acorns.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16289, 4186, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be harvested from oak trees when in season. Can be found by foraging from Critter nest and Undergrowth Resource nodes . Can be used to create tannin for black dye . Can be used in creating healing covers . Can be used in taming or feeding animals that graze. Can not be used in cooking . Can not be used to plant oak trees , see sprouts .', '<ul><li>Can be harvested from oak trees when in season.</li>\n<li>Can be found by foraging from <a href=\"/index.php/Critter_nest\" title=\"Critter nest\">Critter nest</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Undergrowth\" title=\"Undergrowth\">Undergrowth</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Tannin\" title=\"Tannin\">tannin</a> for black <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be used in creating <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be used in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">taming</a> or feeding <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a> that graze.</li>\n<li>Can not be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a>.</li>\n<li>Can not be used to plant <a href=\"/index.php/Oak_tree\" title=\"Oak tree\">oak trees</a>, see <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sprouts\" title=\"Sprouts\">sprouts</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16331, 4078, 'Description', 'Description', 'A trader is a NPC who gives a discount to deed upkeep.', '<p>A <b>trader</b> is a <a href=\"/index.php/NPC\" title=\"NPC\">NPC</a> who gives a discount to deed upkeep.\n</p>', 0),
(16332, 4078, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Trader is placed by using a trader contract, which could be purchased from any other trader until July17th 2023 at a cost of 35s. Trader cannot be moved after it has been placed. Dismissing a trader will not return the contract to be placed again and the trader will be gone forever. Traders can only be placed on deeds and will disappear without refund if the deed disbands or is resized so the trader is outside the deed. Traders give a 20% discount on monthly deed upkeep and also sell a variety of goods. Traders cannot be placed underground. Traders no longer sells items - but can be used to access the silver store', '<ul><li>Trader is placed by using a trader contract, which could be purchased from any other trader until July17th 2023 at a cost of 35s.</li>\n<li>Trader cannot be moved after it has been placed. Dismissing a trader will not return the contract to be placed again and the trader will be gone forever.</li>\n<li>Traders can only be placed on deeds and will disappear without refund if the deed disbands or is resized so the trader is outside the deed.</li>\n<li>Traders give a 20% discount on monthly deed upkeep and also sell a variety of goods.</li>\n<li>Traders cannot be placed underground.</li>\n<li>Traders no longer sells items - but can be used to access the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Silver_store\" title=\"Silver store\">silver store</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16333, 4078, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Personal merchant', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Personal_merchant\" title=\"Personal merchant\">Personal merchant</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16334, 4202, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin, crescent moon formed blade for a sickle.', '<p><i>A thin, crescent moon formed blade for a sickle.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16335, 4202, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a sickle when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16336, 4202, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Often the first item a new player encounters with the the minimum required creation chance. The item requires a 6% chance of creation or greater to be displayed in the creation menu, and blades smithing of more than 1.00.', '<ul><li>Often the first item a new player encounters with the the minimum required creation chance.</li>\n<li>The item requires a 6% chance of creation or greater to be displayed in the creation menu, and <a href=\"/index.php/Blades_smithing\" title=\"Blades smithing\">blades smithing</a> of more than 1.00.</li></ul>', 2),
(16344, 1843, 'THE TOWN IS ALIVE', 'THE_TOWN_IS_ALIVE', 'Town founded by Pedro Deed Size- 100^^', '<p>Town founded by Pedro<br/>\nDeed Size- 100^^\n</p>', 0),
(16345, 1843, 'Members', 'Members', 'pedro - psyho - samotnyjoe - Jawelery, prospector, fighter, miner More will be added soon:] Screenshots Coming soon Special buildings More coming soon', '<ul><li>pedro - <br/></li>\n<li>psyho - <br/></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Samotnyjoe\" title=\"User:Samotnyjoe\">samotnyjoe</a> - Jawelery, prospector, fighter, miner<br/></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n<br/>\n<br/>\n<br/>\n<br/>\n<br/>\nMore will be added soon:]\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Screenshots\">Screenshots</span></h1>\n<p>Coming soon\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Special_buildings\">Special buildings</span></h1>\n<p>More coming soon\n</p>', 1),
(16349, 4208, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lot of dirt, enough to raise the ground somewhere.', '<p><i>A lot of dirt, enough to raise the ground somewhere.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(16350, 4208, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When simply dropped dirt will raise the nearest tile corner of the player dropping it. To create a pile of dirt on the ground without raising the terrain right click dirt in your inventory, then select Drop -> As Pile old method: drop at least 4 other items ( wood scraps are good for this) so that a pile of items is created, open the new pile and then drop the dirt into it. After dropping the dirt, take the wood scraps (or item you used) out. The same thing works for heap of sand . Dirt is used in the creation of kilns and charcoal piles . Dirt can now also be discarded by right-clicking it and choosing Discard.', '<ul><li>When simply dropped dirt will raise the nearest tile corner of the player dropping it.</li>\n<li>To create a pile of dirt on the ground without raising the terrain\n<ul><li>right click dirt in your inventory, then select <code>Drop -&gt; As Pile</code></li>\n<li>old method: drop at least 4 other items (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wood_scraps\" title=\"Wood scraps\">wood scraps</a> are good for this) so that a <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_items\" title=\"Pile of items\">pile of items</a> is created, open the new pile and then drop the dirt into it. After dropping the dirt, take the wood scraps (or item you used) out. The same thing works for <a href=\"/index.php/Heap_of_sand\" title=\"Heap of sand\">heap of sand</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Dirt is used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Kiln\" title=\"Kiln\">kilns</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal_pile\" title=\"Charcoal pile\">charcoal piles</a>.</li>\n<li>Dirt can now also be discarded by right-clicking it and choosing Discard.</li></ul>', 1),
(16353, 4210, 'Description', 'Description', 'A corpse is the result of the death of NPCs , creatures , tower guards , players , rift creatures , and uniques .', '<p>A <b>corpse</b> is the result of the death of <a href=\"/index.php/NPC\" title=\"NPC\">NPCs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Tower_guard\" title=\"Tower guard\">tower guards</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">players</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rift_creature\" title=\"Rift creature\">rift creatures</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Unique\" title=\"Unique\">uniques</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16354, 4210, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A corpse is used for (and left after) butchering . Burying a corpse gives a small amount of digging skill and if the corpse is a player then burying it can increase alignment by 1 point. A dirt tile must be least three dirts above rock or water at each corner to allow burying, and the player must use a shovel to do so. Burial of a corpse on a rock tile requires using a pickaxe instead. Corpses decay relatively quickly unless inside a cave . Once it has decayed, any items on the corpse will form a pile of items . Corpses may be also buried beneath a gravestone . Corpses cannot be renamed. Corpses cannot be mailed. You can spend karma to summon your corpse to your inventory. The spell locate soul can be used to locate the target player\'s corpse.', '<ul><li>A corpse is used for (and left after) <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a>.</li>\n<li>Burying a corpse gives a small amount of <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> skill and if the corpse is a player then burying it can increase <a href=\"/index.php/Alignment\" title=\"Alignment\">alignment</a> by 1 point. A dirt tile must be least three dirts above rock or water at each corner to allow burying, and the player must use a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> to do so. Burial of a corpse on a rock tile requires using a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a> instead.</li>\n<li>Corpses <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> relatively quickly unless inside a <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">cave</a>. Once it has decayed, any <a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">items</a> on the corpse will form a <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_items\" title=\"Pile of items\">pile of items</a>.</li>\n<li>Corpses may be also buried beneath a <a href=\"/index.php/Gravestone\" title=\"Gravestone\">gravestone</a>.</li>\n<li>Corpses cannot be renamed.</li>\n<li>Corpses cannot be mailed.</li>\n<li>You can spend <a href=\"/index.php/Karma\" title=\"Karma\">karma</a> to summon your corpse to your inventory.</li>\n<li>The spell <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_soul\" title=\"Locate soul\">locate soul</a> can be used to locate the target player\'s corpse.</li></ul>', 1),
(16355, 4210, 'Images', 'Images', 'Corpse of a player Corpse of a brown bear', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 575.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 575.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 573.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Corpse_human.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"715\" data-file-width=\"1366\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c5/Corpse_human.png/860px-Corpse_human.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c5/Corpse_human.png/1290px-Corpse_human.png 1.5x, /images/c/c5/Corpse_human.png 2x\" width=\"574\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 554px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Corpse of a <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a>\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 396.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 396.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 394.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Corpse.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"543\" data-file-width=\"714\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/86/Corpse.jpg/592px-Corpse.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/8/86/Corpse.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"395\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 375px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Corpse of a brown bear\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(16356, 4210, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Death Creatures Drown Suicide', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Death#Your_corpse\" title=\"Death\">Death</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">Creatures</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Drown\" title=\"Drown\">Drown</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Suicide\" title=\"Suicide\">Suicide</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16363, 4213, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pig is here, wallowing in the mud.', '<p><i>A pig is here, wallowing in the mud.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16364, 4213, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Pigs can be lead without taming, but are also good practice for early taming skill. Kick and bite attack. Eats any food laying on the ground near it, or in a pet bowl or trough . Effectively butchers corpses that lay around to eat the meat but does not bury the corpse. Pigs may be hitched on hitching post.', '<ul><li>Pigs can be lead without taming, but are also good practice for early taming skill.</li>\n<li>Kick and bite attack.</li>\n<li>Eats any food laying on the ground near it, or in a <a href=\"/index.php/Pet_bowl\" title=\"Pet bowl\">pet bowl</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trough\" title=\"Trough\">trough</a>.</li>\n<li>Effectively butchers corpses that lay around to eat the meat but does not bury the corpse.</li>\n<li>Pigs may be hitched on hitching post.</li></ul>', 1),
(16365, 4213, 'Pig model during Halloween', 'Pig_model_during_Halloween', '', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:202px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:H14_Pig.jpg\"><img alt=\"H14 Pig.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"336\" data-file-width=\"663\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"101\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/H14_Pig.jpg/200px-H14_Pig.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/H14_Pig.jpg/300px-H14_Pig.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7b/H14_Pig.jpg/400px-H14_Pig.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:H14_Pig.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div>', 2),
(16366, 4214, 'Description', 'Description', 'This large drooling one-eyed giant is obviously too stupid to feel any mercy. The Kyklops is a unique, one-eyed creature that roams the wilderness of Wurm.', '<p><i>This large drooling one-eyed giant is obviously too stupid to feel any mercy.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The Kyklops is a unique, one-eyed creature that roams the wilderness of Wurm. \n</p>', 0),
(16367, 4214, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The Kyklops cannot swim. It cannot be tamed. It cannot spawn on deeds. The Kyklops can pick up and throw players. The Kyklops is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying. The Kyklops, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in its path. Slaying the Kyklops will give the title \" Giantslayer \". When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Kyklops blood with source salt will create a potion of leatherworking .', '<ul><li>The Kyklops cannot swim.</li>\n<li>It cannot be tamed.</li>\n<li>It cannot spawn on deeds.</li>\n<li>The Kyklops can pick up and throw players.</li>\n<li>The Kyklops is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying.</li>\n<li>The Kyklops, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in its path.</li>\n<li>Slaying the Kyklops will give the title \"<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Giantslayer\" title=\"Giantslayer\">Giantslayer</a>\".</li>\n<li>When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Kyklops <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a> will create a <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_leatherworking\" title=\"Potion of leatherworking\">potion of leatherworking</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16396, 2548, 'Description', 'Description', 'Baking is the skill used to make breads, cakes, pies, and most foods that use a baking stone , cake tin , or pie dish as a container. Baking often requires several steps and skills, such as milling grain into flour , creating butter or other dairy food making products, and combining more than one baked good to make a final, large dessert. Baking is also the skill used in making endurance sandwiches .', '<p>Baking is the skill used to make breads, cakes, pies, and most foods that use a <a href=\"/index.php/Baking_stone\" title=\"Baking stone\">baking stone</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Cake_tin\" title=\"Cake tin\">cake tin</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Pie_dish\" title=\"Pie dish\">pie dish</a> as a container. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\nBaking often requires several steps and skills, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">milling</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grain\" title=\"Grain\">grain</a> into <a href=\"/index.php/Flour\" title=\"Flour\">flour</a>, creating butter or other <a href=\"/index.php/Dairy_food_making\" title=\"Dairy food making\">dairy food making</a> products, and combining more than one baked good to make a final, large dessert. Baking is also the skill used in making <a href=\"/index.php/Endurance_sandwich\" title=\"Endurance sandwich\">endurance sandwiches</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16397, 2548, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Cooking > Baking Mind > Mind logic Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a> &gt; Baking</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16398, 2548, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Boulanger at 50 skill Bakesale at 70 skill Confissier at 90 skill Breaking Bread at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Boulanger at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Bakesale at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Confissier at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Breaking Bread at 100 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(16399, 2548, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Baking items Cooking Baking Beverages Butchering Dairy food making Hot food cooking Milling', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Baking_items\" title=\"Category:Baking items\">Category:Baking items</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Baking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">Beverages</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">Butchering</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Dairy_food_making\" title=\"Dairy food making\">Dairy food making</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">Hot food cooking</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">Milling</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16422, 4230, 'Description', 'Description', 'A delicate necklace.', '<p><i>A delicate necklace.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16423, 4230, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Can be enchanted with the Nolocate spell.', '<ul><li>Can be enchanted with the <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a> spell.</li></ul>', 1),
(16424, 4230, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Worn on the neck. Uses only 0.01 kgs of lump when being improved.', '<ul><li>Worn on the neck.</li>\n<li>Uses only 0.01 kgs of lump when being improved.</li></ul>', 2),
(16425, 4230, 'Different types of necklaces', 'Different_types_of_necklaces', 'Gold necklace Silver necklace Electrum necklace', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Goldnecklace.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-width=\"450\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/3d/Goldnecklace.jpg/120px-Goldnecklace.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/3d/Goldnecklace.jpg/180px-Goldnecklace.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/3d/Goldnecklace.jpg/240px-Goldnecklace.jpg 2x\" width=\"120\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Gold necklace\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Silvernecklace.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-width=\"450\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/32/Silvernecklace.jpg/120px-Silvernecklace.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/32/Silvernecklace.jpg/180px-Silvernecklace.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/32/Silvernecklace.jpg/240px-Silvernecklace.jpg 2x\" width=\"120\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Silver necklace\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Electrumnecklace.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"314\" data-file-width=\"240\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/5b/Electrumnecklace.jpg/92px-Electrumnecklace.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/5b/Electrumnecklace.jpg/137px-Electrumnecklace.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/5b/Electrumnecklace.jpg/183px-Electrumnecklace.jpg 2x\" width=\"92\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Electrum necklace\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(16426, 4230, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Rift jewelry (Further types of necklaces represented here)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rift_jewelry\" title=\"Rift jewelry\">Rift jewelry</a> (Further types of necklaces represented here)</li></ul>', 4),
(16427, 2692, 'Description', 'Description', 'A beautiful candelabra. The number of arms on a candelabra varies depending on a number of factors, but mainly by the preferences of the designer. Apparently even fairly intelligent people sometimes fail to recognize the proper number which causes mild confusion.', '<p><i>A beautiful candelabra. The number of arms on a candelabra varies depending on a number of factors, but mainly by the preferences of the designer. Apparently even fairly intelligent people sometimes fail to recognize the proper number which causes mild confusion.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(16428, 2692, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Decorative lamps are stationary light sources that often require higher skill and more materials than street lamps. They can be planted much like a sign and can be picked up by the planter only. You need 10 digging skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 effective quality . Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to decay or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally. There\'s no limit to how many decorative lamps you can plant. When planted on a deed , candelabras will automatically snuff at night and re-light at sunrise, like other types of lamps. You need fuel them with candles to light them the first time, but they will not need refueling.', '<ul><li>Decorative lamps are stationary light sources that often require higher skill and more materials than street lamps. They can be planted much like a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Signs\" title=\"Category:Signs\">sign</a> and can be picked up by the planter only.</li>\n<li>You need 10 digging skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Effective_quality\" title=\"Effective quality\">effective quality</a>.</li>\n<li>Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally.</li>\n<li>There\'s no limit to how many decorative lamps you can plant.</li>\n<li>When planted on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">deed</a>, candelabras will automatically snuff at night and re-light at sunrise, like other types of lamps. You need fuel them with <a href=\"/index.php/Candle\" title=\"Candle\">candles</a> to light them the first time, but they will not need refueling.</li></ul>', 1),
(16429, 2692, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Candelabras are lit by candles made from animal fat or beeswax , instead of tar or oil. The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate. Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below. Can be made from any metal. No matter how many candles the model holds, you only need one to fill it. Needs at least jewelry smithing skill > 1 to create.', '<ul><li>Candelabras are lit by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Candles\" title=\"Candles\">candles</a> made from <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_fat\" title=\"Animal fat\">animal fat</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Beeswax\" title=\"Beeswax\">beeswax</a>, instead of tar or oil.</li>\n<li>The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate.</li>\n<li>Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below.</li>\n<li>Can be made from any metal.</li>\n<li>No matter how many candles the model holds, you only need one to fill it.</li>\n<li>Needs at least <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">jewelry smithing</a> skill &gt; 1 to create.</li></ul>', 2),
(16430, 2692, 'Decorative lamp types', 'Decorative_lamp_types', 'Brazier pillar Candelabra Small brazier', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Brazier_pillar\" title=\"Brazier pillar\">Brazier pillar</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Candelabra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_brazier\" title=\"Small brazier\">Small brazier</a></li></ul>', 3);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16431, 2692, 'Images', 'Images', 'Adamantine candelabra Brass candelabra Bronze candelabra Copper candelabra Electrum candelabra Glimmersteel candelabra Gold candelabra Iron candelabra Lead candelabra Seryll candelabra Silver candelabra Steel candelabra Tin candelabra Zinc candelabra', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:36.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Adamantine_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"591\" data-file-width=\"377\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"157\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Adamantine_candelabra.jpg/100px-Adamantine_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/bb/Adamantine_candelabra.jpg/150px-Adamantine_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/bb/Adamantine_candelabra.jpg/200px-Adamantine_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Adamantine candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:28px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Brass_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"607\" data-file-width=\"348\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"174\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/12/Brass_candelabra.jpg/100px-Brass_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/12/Brass_candelabra.jpg/150px-Brass_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/12/Brass_candelabra.jpg/200px-Brass_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Brass candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:30.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bronze_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"610\" data-file-width=\"360\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"169\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d6/Bronze_candelabra.jpg/100px-Bronze_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d6/Bronze_candelabra.jpg/150px-Bronze_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/d6/Bronze_candelabra.jpg/200px-Bronze_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Bronze candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:31px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Copper_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"644\" data-file-width=\"383\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"168\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/Copper_candelabra.jpg/100px-Copper_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/Copper_candelabra.jpg/150px-Copper_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/7d/Copper_candelabra.jpg/200px-Copper_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Copper candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:25.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Electrum_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"584\" data-file-width=\"327\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"179\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b4/Electrum_candelabra.jpg/100px-Electrum_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b4/Electrum_candelabra.jpg/150px-Electrum_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/b4/Electrum_candelabra.jpg/200px-Electrum_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Electrum candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Glimmer_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"687\" data-file-width=\"324\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/14/Glimmer_candelabra.jpg/94px-Glimmer_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/14/Glimmer_candelabra.jpg/141px-Glimmer_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/14/Glimmer_candelabra.jpg/188px-Glimmer_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"94\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Glimmersteel candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gold_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"671\" data-file-width=\"329\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/53/Gold_candelabra.jpg/98px-Gold_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/53/Gold_candelabra.jpg/147px-Gold_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/53/Gold_candelabra.jpg/196px-Gold_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"98\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Gold candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:22px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Iron_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"524\" data-file-width=\"281\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"186\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e6/Iron_candelabra.jpg/100px-Iron_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e6/Iron_candelabra.jpg/150px-Iron_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e6/Iron_candelabra.jpg/200px-Iron_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Iron candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Lead_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"628\" data-file-width=\"317\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"198\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/40/Lead_candelabra.jpg/100px-Lead_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/40/Lead_candelabra.jpg/150px-Lead_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/40/Lead_candelabra.jpg/200px-Lead_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Lead candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:26px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Seryll_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"635\" data-file-width=\"357\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"178\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/09/Seryll_candelabra.jpg/100px-Seryll_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/0/09/Seryll_candelabra.jpg/150px-Seryll_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/0/09/Seryll_candelabra.jpg/200px-Seryll_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Seryll candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:24px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Silver_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"618\" data-file-width=\"340\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"182\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/be/Silver_candelabra.jpg/100px-Silver_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/be/Silver_candelabra.jpg/150px-Silver_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/be/Silver_candelabra.jpg/200px-Silver_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Silver candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Steel_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"619\" data-file-width=\"298\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/2c/Steel_candelabra.jpg/96px-Steel_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/2c/Steel_candelabra.jpg/144px-Steel_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/2c/Steel_candelabra.jpg/192px-Steel_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"96\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Steel candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Tin_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"603\" data-file-width=\"322\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/62/Tin_candelabra.jpg/100px-Tin_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/62/Tin_candelabra.jpg/150px-Tin_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/62/Tin_candelabra.jpg/200px-Tin_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Tin candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 135px\"><div style=\"width: 135px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 130px;\"><div style=\"margin:19.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Zinc_candelabra.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"614\" data-file-width=\"321\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"191\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/45/Zinc_candelabra.jpg/100px-Zinc_candelabra.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/45/Zinc_candelabra.jpg/150px-Zinc_candelabra.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/45/Zinc_candelabra.jpg/200px-Zinc_candelabra.jpg 2x\" width=\"100\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<center>Zinc candelabra</center>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 4),
(16432, 4233, 'Description', 'Description', 'A finely carved statuette. A statuette is made of gold or silver, using jewelry smithing .\nIt can be used for decoration.', '<p><i>A finely carved statuette.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">statuette</a> is made of gold or silver, using <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">jewelry smithing</a>.\nIt can be used for decoration.\n</p>', 0),
(16433, 4233, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Dragon Statuette Bear army statuette Statuette of the avenger Statuette of the Renowned Warrior', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Dragon Statuette</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Bear army statuette</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Statuette of the avenger</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Statuette of the Renowned Warrior</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16434, 4233, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This basic statuette can not be used to channel spells.', '<ul><li>This basic statuette can not be used to channel spells.</li></ul>', 2),
(16435, 4233, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Statues Statuettes Jewelry smithing', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statues\" title=\"Statues\">Statues</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Statuettes\" title=\"Statuettes\">Statuettes</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16449, 1262, 'Description', 'Description', 'Willow trees are a larger species of tree that are fairly uncommon and are often spotted naturally growing near sources of water.', '<p>Willow trees are a larger species of tree that are fairly uncommon and are often spotted naturally growing near sources of water.\n</p>', 0),
(16450, 1262, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Willow wood is useful as it provides a significant bonus to bows made from it, decreasing the difficulty of successfully shooting the target. Willow fishing rods break less. Like Oaks , willows kill all other trees and bushes within two tiles of it while growing. Crops and flowers are all that can be grown within this radius. Willows kill all trees and bushes within one tile (including diagonal tiles) after they reach the mature stage and all those within two tiles after they reach the old stage. The other tree will only be killed when the willow moves to the next age level. Until then it will continue to grow and age as normal.', '<ul><li>Willow wood is useful as it provides a significant bonus to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bows\" title=\"Bows\">bows</a> made from it, decreasing the difficulty of successfully shooting the target.</li>\n<li>Willow <a href=\"/index.php/Fishing_rod\" title=\"Fishing rod\">fishing rods</a> break less.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Like <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">Oaks</a>, willows kill all other trees and bushes within two tiles of it while growing. Crops and flowers are all that can be grown within this radius. Willows kill all trees and bushes within one tile (including diagonal tiles) after they reach the mature stage and all those within two tiles after they reach the old stage. The other tree will only be killed when the willow moves to the next age level. Until then it will continue to grow and age as normal.</li></ul>', 1),
(16451, 1262, 'Tree Kill Zone', 'Tree_Kill_Zone', 'O O O O O O O O X X X X X O O X X X X X O O X X T X X O O X X X X X O O X X X X X O O O O O O O O T=Tree X =Kill zone from mature onwards X=Kill zone from old onwards O=Safe zone', '<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td>T</td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font></td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>X</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O</td>\n<td>O\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>T=Tree<br/>\n</p>\n<p><font color=\"red\"><b>X</b></font>=Kill zone from mature onwards<br/>\nX=Kill zone from old onwards<br/>\nO=Safe zone<br/>\n</p>', 2),
(16452, 1262, 'Images', 'Images', 'Screenshots A previous willow tree model.', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\" style=\"max-width: 486px;_width: 486px;\">\n<li class=\"gallerycaption\">Screenshots</li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Babywillow6bw.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"440\" data-file-width=\"576\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b7/Babywillow6bw.png/157px-Babywillow6bw.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b7/Babywillow6bw.png/236px-Babywillow6bw.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/b/b7/Babywillow6bw.png/314px-Babywillow6bw.png 2x\" width=\"157\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>A previous willow tree model.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(16458, 3778, 'Description', 'Description', 'This spell stores favor in gems , depending on the QL of the gem and your current amount of favor. You need at least 7.5 favor to begin to cast Vessel.  The cost of the cast is 5 favor.  Any remaining favor is stored in the gem and the priest may gain channeling skill.  \nOnce charged, the gem is renamed to \"Radiant [gem type].\"  Vessel cannot be cast on \"Radiant\" gems. No favor is stored if the gem is less than 10QL. Instead, the cast uses 5 favor and the priest may still gain channeling skill.  The gem loses 3QL or is destroyed if less than 3QL.', '<p>This spell stores <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> in <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gems</a>, depending on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the gem and your current amount of favor.\n</p>\n<p>You need at least 7.5 favor to begin to cast Vessel.  The cost of the cast is 5 favor.  Any remaining favor is stored in the gem and the priest may gain <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill.  \nOnce charged, the gem is renamed to \"Radiant [gem type].\"  Vessel cannot be cast on \"Radiant\" gems.\n</p>\n<p>No favor is stored if the gem is less than 10QL. Instead, the cast uses 5 favor and the priest may still gain channeling skill.  The gem loses 3QL or is destroyed if less than 3QL.\n</p>', 0),
(16459, 3778, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette of your god Right-click a gem Select Spells > Vessel', '<ol><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> of your god</li>\n<li>Right-click a gem</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Vessel</i></li></ol>', 1),
(16460, 3778, 'Using the gem', 'Using_the_gem', 'Right-click the gem Select Use When you use the gem it will lose QL in the amount of half the favor given.  A 25ql gem filled with 10 favor upon use will give 20 favor and the gem will fall to 15ql.  With no more favor stored, the gem is renamed back to its original gem type. Favor Used to Fill a Gem The amount of favor used to completely fill a gem is the QL plus 5.  For example, a 20QL gem would require 25 favor to fill completely. Favor Stored in Gem The amount of favor stored in a gem is double the amount used to fill the gem. Upon examining a gem the approximate amount of favor stored can be found from the power emitted. Favor Amount Message 1 - 10 It emits faint power. 10 - 16.50 * It emits some power. 16.50 * - 50 It emits power. 51 - 100 It emits quite a lot of power. 101 - 150 It emits very much power. 150+ It emits huge amounts of power ∗ The mark of denotation is somewhere between 16.38 and 16.65. It was averaged to 16.50 Example of storing and using Vessel Assume that the Priest has 50 Faith and a therefore a maximum of 50 Favor. The priest also has a gem of 25QL If the priest had 30 favor and cast vessel on the 25QL gem their favor would drop to 0 and the gem would be completely filled with power, as the favor to completely fill a gem is the QL plus 5 Favor. Now the priest, not wanting to wait to regain favor naturally uses the gem at once. \"You feel a rush of blood to your head as the power from the gem enters your body.\" The QL of the gem drops to almost 0 and the priests favor jumps up to 50. This is because the amount of favor used to fill the gem (not including the 5 used to cast) is doubled and given back to the priest.', '<ol><li>Right-click the gem</li>\n<li>Select <i>Use</i></li></ol>\n<p>When you use the gem it will lose QL in the amount of half the favor given.  A 25ql gem filled with 10 favor upon use will give 20 favor and the gem will fall to 15ql.  With no more favor stored, the gem is renamed back to its original gem type.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Favor_Used_to_Fill_a_Gem\">Favor Used to Fill a Gem</span></h4>\n<p>The amount of favor used to completely fill a gem is the QL plus 5.  For example, a 20QL gem would require 25 favor to fill completely.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Favor_Stored_in_Gem\">Favor Stored in Gem</span></h4>\n<p>The amount of favor stored in a gem is double the amount used to fill the gem.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nUpon examining a gem the <i>approximate</i> amount of favor stored can be found from the power emitted.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Favor Amount</th>\n<th>Message\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 - 10</td>\n<td>It emits faint power.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10 - 16.50<sup>*</sup></td>\n<td>It emits some power.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16.50<sup>*</sup> - 50</td>\n<td>It emits power.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>51 - 100</td>\n<td>It emits quite a lot of power.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>101 - 150</td>\n<td>It emits very much power.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>150+</td>\n<td>It emits huge amounts of power\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>∗ The mark of denotation is somewhere between 16.38 and 16.65. It was averaged to 16.50\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_of_storing_and_using_Vessel\">Example of storing and using Vessel</span></h4>\n<p>Assume that the Priest has 50 Faith and a therefore a maximum of 50 Favor. The priest also has a gem of 25QL\n</p>\n<p>If the priest had 30 favor and cast vessel on the 25QL gem their favor would drop to 0 and the gem would be completely filled with power, as the favor to completely fill a gem is the QL plus 5 Favor.\n</p>\n<p>Now the priest, not wanting to wait to regain favor naturally uses the gem at once. \"You feel a rush of blood to your head as the power from the gem enters your body.\" The QL of the gem drops to almost 0 and the priests favor jumps up to 50. This is because the amount of favor used to fill the gem (not including the 5 used to cast) is doubled and given back to the priest.\n</p>', 2),
(16461, 3778, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Although you can Vessel a gem only once, you can use it over and over until it\'s empty. A gem over 50ql can potentially fill your favor multiple times. You can repeatedly Vessel and use a gem if you don\'t fill it up completely. This is crucial when grinding channeling and getting the most casts out of a gem.\nFor example, if you start casting Vessel at 7.5 favor you will charge the gem with approximately 5 favor. (gaining 10 favor on use, reducing the QL by 5) This is ideal, however your natural favor gain will likely have the 1st tick after 7.49 fall between 7.5 an 8.1.  (Favor gained during the cast will count towards the favor charged into the gem) The longer you wait to cast and the more favor you have at the start of your cast will result in filling the gem with more favor. A Priest can not store a linked priest\'s favor when vesseling gems over 10ql. (You store your own, but not the linked priest\'s) \nHowever, the cost of the cast (5 Favor) will be taken from the linked priest.  This can be helpful when vesseling many gems that are less than 10QL, giving a larger favor pool to pull from.', '<p>Although you can Vessel a gem only once, you can use it over and over until it\'s empty. A gem over 50ql can potentially fill your favor multiple times.\n</p>\n<p>You can repeatedly Vessel and use a gem if you don\'t fill it up completely. This is crucial when grinding channeling and getting the most casts out of a gem.\nFor example, if you start casting Vessel at 7.5 favor you will charge the gem with approximately 5 favor. (gaining 10 favor on use, reducing the QL by 5)  \n</p>\n<ul><li>This is ideal, however your natural favor gain will likely have the 1st tick after 7.49 fall between 7.5 an 8.1.  (Favor gained during the cast will count towards the favor charged into the gem)</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The longer you wait to cast and the more favor you have at the start of your cast will result in filling the gem with more favor.</li></ul>\n<p>A Priest can not store a linked priest\'s favor when vesseling gems over 10ql. (You store your own, but not the linked priest\'s) \nHowever, the cost of the cast (5 Favor) will be taken from the linked priest.  This can be helpful when vesseling many gems that are less than 10QL, giving a larger favor pool to pull from.\n</p>', 3),
(16462, 4243, 'Description', 'Description', 'Huge club skill is gained by fighting with a huge shod club , a two-handed weapon collected from killing a troll . The parent skill is clubs .', '<p><b>Huge club</b> skill is gained by fighting with a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">huge shod club</a>, a two-handed weapon collected from killing a <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">troll</a>. The parent skill is <a href=\"/index.php/Clubs\" title=\"Clubs\">clubs</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16463, 4243, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Clubs > Huge club', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Clubs\" title=\"Clubs\">Clubs</a> &gt; Huge club</li></ul>', 1),
(16464, 4243, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Troll at 50 skill Forest Giant at 70 skill Kyklops at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Troll at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Forest Giant at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Kyklops at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(16465, 4243, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Huge shod club is the only weapon that uses this skill.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a> is the only weapon that uses this skill.</li></ul>', 3),
(16466, 4244, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large wooden sign.', '<p><i>A large wooden sign.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16467, 4244, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The higher the quality , the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 2 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select Rename to enter your message. You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign. To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select Plant. Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface.  Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move, or remove the sign. If you fail creation, both the nail and the plank are damaged.', '<ul><li>The higher the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 2 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select Rename to enter your message.</li>\n<li>You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign.</li>\n<li>To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select Plant. Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface.  Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move, or remove the sign.</li>\n<li>If you fail creation, both the nail and the plank are damaged.</li></ul>', 1),
(16468, 4244, 'Limitations', 'Limitations', 'Off deed signs You can only plant one sign per Wurm week (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed and can be picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below. On deed signs There are no limits to signs you plant within your deed.', '<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Off_deed_signs\">Off deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>You can only plant one sign per Wurm <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Week\" title=\"Week\">week</a> (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed and can be picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below. \n</p>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"On_deed_signs\">On deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>There are no limits to signs you plant within your deed.\n</p>', 2),
(16469, 4244, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Small sign Pointing sign Shop sign', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_sign\" title=\"Small sign\">Small sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pointing_sign\" title=\"Pointing sign\">Pointing sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shop_sign\" title=\"Shop sign\">Shop sign</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16470, 4245, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small wooden sign.', '<p><i>A small wooden sign.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16471, 4245, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The higher the quality , the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 1 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select Rename to enter your message.  The name of the sign will be displayed on mouse-over once planted. You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign. To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select Plant. Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface. Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move or remove the sign. The wood type of the sign is determined by the wood type of the shaft used to complete the small sign.', '<ul><li>The higher the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 1 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select Rename to enter your message.  The name of the sign will be displayed on mouse-over once planted.</li>\n<li>You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign.</li>\n<li>To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select Plant. Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface. Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move or remove the sign.</li>\n<li>The wood type of the sign is determined by the wood type of the shaft used to complete the small sign.</li></ul>', 1),
(16472, 4245, 'Limitations', 'Limitations', 'Off deed signs You can only plant one sign per Wurm week (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed and can be picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below. On deed signs These are no limits signs you plant within your deed.', '<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Off_deed_signs\">Off deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>You can only plant one sign per Wurm <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Week\" title=\"Week\">week</a> (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed and can be picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below.\n</p>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"On_deed_signs\">On deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>These are no limits signs you plant within your deed.\n</p>', 2),
(16473, 4245, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Large sign Pointing sign Shop sign', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_sign\" title=\"Large sign\">Large sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pointing_sign\" title=\"Pointing sign\">Pointing sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shop_sign\" title=\"Shop sign\">Shop sign</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16474, 4246, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wooden sign that is pointing towards something.', '<p><i>A wooden sign that is pointing towards something.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16475, 4246, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The higher the quality , the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 1 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select Rename to enter your message.  The name of the sign will be displayed on mouse-over once planted. You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign. To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select Plant . Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface. Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move or remove the sign. If you fail creation, both the nail and the plank are damaged.', '<ul><li>The higher the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, the more you can write on the sign, at a ratio of 1 letter per each whole quality. Right-click the sign at any time and select <i>Rename</i> to enter your message.  The name of the sign will be displayed on mouse-over once planted.</li>\n<li>You need a minimum of 10 digging skill to plant a sign.</li>\n<li>To plant the sign simply stand in place, right-click on the sign in your inventory and select <i>Plant</i>. Once planted the sign may be pushed, pulled or rotated by using the right-click interface. Only the player who planted the sign may rename, move or remove the sign.</li>\n<li>If you fail creation, both the nail and the plank are damaged.</li></ul>', 1),
(16476, 4246, 'Limitations', 'Limitations', 'Off deed signs You can only plant one sign per Wurm week (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below. On deed signs These are no limits to signs you plant within your deed.', '<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Off_deed_signs\">Off deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>You can only plant one sign per Wurm <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Week\" title=\"Week\">week</a> (21 real life hours). However, signs can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ damage and or are 10 quality and below. \n</p>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"On_deed_signs\">On deed signs</span></h5>\n<p>These are no limits to signs you plant within your deed.\n</p>', 2),
(16477, 4246, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Small sign Large sign Shop sign', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_sign\" title=\"Small sign\">Small sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_sign\" title=\"Large sign\">Large sign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shop_sign\" title=\"Shop sign\">Shop sign</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16495, 4250, 'Description', 'Description', 'A decorative stool.', '<p><i>A decorative stool.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16496, 4250, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A stool is used to sit on and decorate houses. It is fairly high and might look best with large dining tables or small square tables .', '<ul><li>A stool is used to sit on and decorate houses. It is fairly high and might look best with <a href=\"/index.php/Large_dining_table\" title=\"Large dining table\">large dining tables</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Small_square_table\" title=\"Small square table\">small square tables</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16500, 4252, '051230', '051230', '5 typos reported by Ellor fixed. Improving walls when not the writ holder should not be possible any longer. Inventory restrictions for botanize, harvest, forage, and pick sprout. Bug with loosing faith for eating or drinking fixed. Village guards should respawn correctly and head for the token more often when in caves. It is now possible to spawn at the token itself. An anti-cheat fix may happen to people who lag much. Hopefully it will not be noticeable. Erroneous outline colours on guards fixed. Bugs with huge altars fixed. Two new spells were added. One to all deities, and one to Libila and Vynora.', '<ul><li>5 typos reported by Ellor fixed.</li>\n<li>Improving walls when not the writ holder should not be possible any longer.</li>\n<li>Inventory restrictions for botanize, harvest, forage, and pick sprout.</li>\n<li>Bug with loosing faith for eating or drinking fixed.</li>\n<li>Village guards should respawn correctly and head for the token more often when in caves.</li>\n<li>It is now possible to spawn at the token itself.</li>\n<li>An anti-cheat fix may happen to people who lag much. Hopefully it will not be noticeable.</li>\n<li>Erroneous outline colours on guards fixed.</li>\n<li>Bugs with huge altars fixed.</li>\n<li>Two new spells were added. One to all deities, and one to Libila and Vynora.</li></ul>', 0),
(16501, 4252, '051222', '051222', 'Improving walls/fences is now limited by the item ql and the skill in combination instead of the best of those two. Unfinished items now need to be hot in order to finish. They should however keep their temperature at initial creation. Decaytime for certain liquids like sap, syrup and juice was far too low so they now last longer. More web interface methods.', '<ul><li>Improving walls/fences is now limited by the item ql and the skill in combination instead of the best of those two.</li>\n<li>Unfinished items now need to be hot in order to finish. They should however keep their temperature at initial creation.</li>\n<li>Decaytime for certain liquids like sap, syrup and juice was far too low so they now last longer.</li>\n<li>More web interface methods.</li></ul>', 1),
(16502, 4252, '051215', '051215', 'You may now remove colors/paints by using a metal brush.', '<ul><li>You may now remove colors/paints by using a metal brush.</li></ul>', 2),
(16503, 4252, '051214b', '051214b', 'Probable reconnect-hang bug fixed. You may now receive and use titles. Check the /title and /titles commands. A small bug with selecting titles exists, but can be avoided by clicking on the undesired title (or \'none\' option).', '<ul><li>Probable reconnect-hang bug fixed.</li>\n<li>You may now receive and use titles. Check the /title and /titles commands. A small bug with selecting titles exists, but can be avoided by clicking on the undesired title (or \'none\' option).</li></ul>', 3),
(16504, 4252, '051214', '051214', 'Campfire size increased to original size. Forges were made larger again. This will only affect new forges. Walls now load colors properly. Still debugging the anti-cheat system so some instability may still occur. Problem with opening of containers should be fixed.', '<ul><li>Campfire size increased to original size. Forges were made larger again. This will only affect new forges.</li>\n<li>Walls now load colors properly.</li>\n<li>Still debugging the anti-cheat system so some instability may still occur.</li>\n<li>Problem with opening of containers should be fixed.</li></ul>', 4),
(16505, 4252, '051213', '051213', 'Campfires now hold less items than forges. Fighting now correctly only gives skill when damage is dealt. Progress may need some tweaking. Autoban removed, instead insta-teleportation will happen when you move too fast. Dye making should work better with containers. Some small reputation fixes. Other small bugfixes.', '<ul><li>Campfires now hold less items than forges.</li>\n<li>Fighting now correctly only gives skill when damage is dealt. Progress may need some tweaking.</li>\n<li>Autoban removed, instead insta-teleportation will happen when you move too fast.</li>\n<li>Dye making should work better with containers.</li>\n<li>Some small reputation fixes.</li>\n<li>Other small bugfixes.</li></ul>', 5),
(16506, 4252, '051207', '051207', 'Drag and drop bug fixed, as well as some other for mortals non-noticeable ones.', '<ul><li>Drag and drop bug fixed, as well as some other for mortals non-noticeable ones.</li></ul>', 6),
(16507, 4252, '051206', '051206', 'Part of the movement cheat detection is now automated and will ban you. Fighting now correctly only gives skill when damage is dealt. Progress may need some tweaking. Various other more or less serious bugfixes, with dye, cotton seed picking and pumpkin crushing for instance.', '<ul><li>Part of the movement cheat detection is now automated and will ban you.</li>\n<li>Fighting now correctly only gives skill when damage is dealt. Progress may need some tweaking. Various other more or less serious bugfixes, with dye, cotton seed picking and pumpkin crushing for instance.</li></ul>', 7),
(16508, 4252, '051130', '051130', 'Colors! You may now find out how to create dyes with the basic colors. You may mix them by using drag and drop into containers (this will be simplified soon). Then you may use that dye to color some items and building walls. Reputation system added, and thieving. Non-HOTS people who want to steal things from villages or structures in their kingdom may now lose reputation if they are noticed. You start with reputation 100. When it reaches 0 you will be labeled Outlaw, and may be attacked by any player from your kingdom and they will receive no penalty for it. When your reputation goes below -100 you will also be attacked by kingdom guards. When your reputation goes below -200 you will convert to HOTS. \nYou may check your reputation using the command [i]/reputation[/i]. Reputation goes up with about 1 per hour, even if offline. Guards in a village may notice you and stop you from stealing in that village. Owners or guests of a structure and kingdom guards noticing you may stop you from stealing from an undeeded structure. The closer you are to someone stealing the lower that persons chances to steal are. Drinking, filling, eating and dragging is also protected by the reputation system. If you kill someone with positive reputation you will lose a large amount of reputation. If you die as non-HOTS while your reputation is negative, you will lose 5 times as much skill.', '<ul><li>Colors! You may now find out how to create dyes with the basic colors. You may mix them by using drag and drop into containers (this will be simplified soon). Then you may use that dye to color some items and building walls.</li>\n<li>Reputation system added, and thieving. Non-HOTS people who want to steal things from villages or structures in their kingdom may now lose reputation if they are noticed. You start with reputation 100.</li></ul>\n<p>When it reaches 0 you will be labeled Outlaw, and may be attacked by any player from your kingdom and they will receive no penalty for it. When your reputation goes below -100 you will also be attacked by kingdom guards. When your reputation goes below -200 you will convert to HOTS. \nYou may check your reputation using the command [i]/reputation[/i]. Reputation goes up with about 1 per hour, even if offline. Guards in a village may notice you and stop you from stealing in that village. Owners or guests of a structure and kingdom guards noticing you may stop you from stealing from an undeeded structure. The closer you are to someone stealing the lower that persons chances to steal are. Drinking, filling, eating and dragging is also protected by the reputation system. If you kill someone with positive reputation you will lose a large amount of reputation. If you die as non-HOTS while your reputation is negative, you will lose 5 times as much skill.\n</p>', 8),
(16509, 4252, '051124', '051124', 'Guards move quicker. Personal trader bugfix. They now work again, so you will receive the money you sell stuff for. Also, if you set a price that is what he will sell it for as well (ignoring any price modifier).', '<ul><li>Guards move quicker.</li>\n<li>Personal trader bugfix. They now work again, so you will receive the money you sell stuff for. Also, if you set a price that is what he will sell it for as well (ignoring any price modifier).</li></ul>', 9),
(16510, 4252, '051121', '051121', 'You now only gain skill in fights where real damage is dealt. So if a creature is hit hard enough, the next 20 seconds that creature and creatures fighting him may gain skill. Armour now takes only half the damage, so they last longer. Their effectiveness remains the same. House wall damage bug fixed. House walls now also have a 2 day grace period before they start decaying.', '<ul><li>You now only gain skill in fights where real damage is dealt. So if a creature is hit hard enough, the next 20 seconds that creature and creatures fighting him may gain skill.</li>\n<li>Armour now takes only half the damage, so they last longer. Their effectiveness remains the same.</li>\n<li>House wall damage bug fixed. House walls now also have a 2 day grace period before they start decaying.</li></ul>', 10),
(16511, 4252, '051116', '051116', 'Skillgain for basic characteristics like strength and also mining has slowed down some. You should now be able to lower upkeep at will. Tower guards should leave caves now. Disbanding homesteads now takes 1 hour for the mayor.', '<ul><li>Skillgain for basic characteristics like strength and also mining has slowed down some.</li>\n<li>You should now be able to lower upkeep at will.</li>\n<li>Tower guards should leave caves now.</li>\n<li>Disbanding homesteads now takes 1 hour for the mayor.</li></ul>', 11),
(16512, 4252, '051115', '051115', 'Decay time has increased for walls and fences in deeded (x10) and been halved in non-deeded, non-kingdom (x0.5) areas.', '<ul><li>Decay time has increased for walls and fences in deeded (x10) and been halved in non-deeded, non-kingdom (x0.5) areas.</li></ul>', 12),
(16513, 4252, '051107', '051107', 'Creatures should now leave the 1-tile caves. The amount of water you need to drink should have decreased. New guard towers should be improvable again. The \'Piles of Death\' that disconnected you should work again. The server now only sends 100 of the items in a pile and other containers on the ground. The damage weapon deals should be more even. Creatures do less damage. Creatures in caves should no longer walk through cave walls. Desecrating altars should be harder. Non-climbing creatures will avoid steep slopes. More cave entrances fixed.', '<ul><li>Creatures should now leave the 1-tile caves.</li>\n<li>The amount of water you need to drink should have decreased.</li>\n<li>New guard towers should be improvable again.</li>\n<li>The \'Piles of Death\' that disconnected you should work again. The server now only sends 100 of the items in a pile and other containers on the ground.</li>\n<li>The damage weapon deals should be more even. Creatures do less damage.</li>\n<li>Creatures in caves should no longer walk through cave walls.</li>\n<li>Desecrating altars should be harder.</li>\n<li>Non-climbing creatures will avoid steep slopes.</li>\n<li>More cave entrances fixed.</li></ul>', 13),
(16514, 4252, '051026', '051026', 'A bug that had reappeared with trading items fixed. Wall and fence damages and quality drop lowered for repairing.', '<ul><li>A bug that had reappeared with trading items fixed.</li>\n<li>Wall and fence damages and quality drop lowered for repairing.</li></ul>', 14),
(16515, 4252, '051024', '051024', 'You may now use the /stuck command if you become stuck in a tree. Guests may not trade with npcs any longer Fixed broken cave entrances.(I hope)', '<ul><li>You may now use the /stuck command if you become stuck in a tree.</li>\n<li>Guests may not trade with npcs any longer</li>\n<li>Fixed broken cave entrances.(I hope)</li></ul>', 15),
(16516, 4252, '051018', '051018', 'Gm chat bug fixed. Pigs are now leadable. Creatures regenerate stamina slower, and not while fighting.', '<ul><li>Gm chat bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Pigs are now leadable.</li>\n<li>Creatures regenerate stamina slower, and not while fighting.</li></ul>', 16),
(16517, 4252, '051017', '051017', 'Trading bug fixed Most animals now need food, so in order to slaughter fat cattle you will have to feed them fairly regularly. They will look for food in the vicinity.', '<ul><li>Trading bug fixed</li>\n<li>Most animals now need food, so in order to slaughter fat cattle you will have to feed them fairly regularly. They will look for food in the vicinity.</li></ul>', 17),
(16518, 4252, '051011', '051011', 'Creating walls with ql 100 exploit fixed. Their ql was lowered some but not totally, as a reward for reporting the exploit. Traders will no longer accept containers with items in them. Various other small, invisible bugs fixed.', '<ul><li>Creating walls with ql 100 exploit fixed. Their ql was lowered some but not totally, as a reward for reporting the exploit.</li>\n<li>Traders will no longer accept containers with items in them.</li>\n<li>Various other small, invisible bugs fixed.</li></ul>', 18),
(16519, 4252, '051010', '051010', 'Mining on cave entrances should no longer produce an impassable wall Multiple creatures appearing on cave entrances fix. Various other small fixes. Forge descriptions might still be buggy though. Trading changed. Due to the bug with liquids you now have to remove items from containers to receive full price for them.', '<ul><li>Mining on cave entrances should no longer produce an impassable wall</li>\n<li>Multiple creatures appearing on cave entrances fix.</li>\n<li>Various other small fixes. Forge descriptions might still be buggy though.</li>\n<li>Trading changed. Due to the bug with liquids you now have to remove items from containers to receive full price for them.</li></ul>', 19),
(16520, 4252, '051007', '051007', 'Fixed a server crash bug. Carts shouldn\'t become stuck in walls any longer. Weapon damage has changed some. Main difference is that tools were nerfed so they do less damage.', '<ul><li>Fixed a server crash bug.</li>\n<li>Carts shouldn\'t become stuck in walls any longer.</li>\n<li>Weapon damage has changed some. Main difference is that tools were nerfed so they do less damage.</li></ul>', 20),
(16521, 4252, '051006', '051006', 'The auto-healing feature that slowly removed the red damage in the stamina bar was removed. It caused you to have wounds but no damage. You may now check kingdom influence using the /kingdoms command in any chat window. Creatures should not become stuck at cave entrances any more.', '<ul><li>The auto-healing feature that slowly removed the red damage in the stamina bar was removed. It caused you to have wounds but no damage.</li>\n<li>You may now check kingdom influence using the /kingdoms command in any chat window.</li>\n<li>Creatures should not become stuck at cave entrances any more.</li></ul>', 21),
(16522, 4252, '051005', '051005', 'Tried to fix some holes that remained since last fix. Hopefully this did not ruin existing caves. Creatures should handle cave entrances better and hunt through them. Bug with items on cave entrances fixed.', '<ul><li>Tried to fix some holes that remained since last fix. Hopefully this did not ruin existing caves.</li>\n<li>Creatures should handle cave entrances better and hunt through them.</li>\n<li>Bug with items on cave entrances fixed.</li></ul>', 22),
(16523, 4252, '051003', '051003', 'Cave entrances now take about 25 mining operations to open. Demand should slowly rise for unpurchased items at traders, only purchased items did before:P. Deadly cave entrances were fixed. The caves were not properly saved before, so caves made during the weekend were lost. New fix for the 1 ore tile bug.', '<ul><li>Cave entrances now take about 25 mining operations to open.</li>\n<li>Demand should slowly rise for unpurchased items at traders, only purchased items did before:P.</li>\n<li>Deadly cave entrances were fixed. The caves were not properly saved before, so caves made during the weekend were lost.</li>\n<li>New fix for the 1 ore tile bug.</li></ul>', 23);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16524, 4252, '050929', '050929', 'Attacking a creature in a cave without danger should be fixed. You may no longer remove items from trade that are in traded containers. Building a fence while in the cave should work better. Fences near buildings shouldn\'t let creatures through any longer. Creatures should find their way out of caves better. You should now receive a free trader contract when expanding an existing size 5 village deed (not homestead). Bug with trader pricing fixed. Bug with non-passable water-level cave entrances fixed. You will no longer be invulnerable while reconnecting fighting. It should no longer be impossible to create fruit juice, and certain fruits are combinable. Items becoming invisible/disappearing when dying should be fixed.', '<ul><li>Attacking a creature in a cave without danger should be fixed.</li>\n<li>You may no longer remove items from trade that are in traded containers.</li>\n<li>Building a fence while in the cave should work better.</li>\n<li>Fences near buildings shouldn\'t let creatures through any longer.</li>\n<li>Creatures should find their way out of caves better.</li>\n<li>You should now receive a free trader contract when expanding an existing size 5 village deed (not homestead).</li>\n<li>Bug with trader pricing fixed.</li>\n<li>Bug with non-passable water-level cave entrances fixed.</li>\n<li>You will no longer be invulnerable while reconnecting fighting.</li>\n<li>It should no longer be impossible to create fruit juice, and certain fruits are combinable.</li>\n<li>Items becoming invisible/disappearing when dying should be fixed.</li></ul>', 24),
(16525, 4252, '050921b', '050921b', 'You may now drag carts in and out of caves. Fishing and drinking on cave walls fixed. Interacting with walls and fences should now work better when standing in the cave.', '<ul><li>You may now drag carts in and out of caves.</li>\n<li>Fishing and drinking on cave walls fixed.</li>\n<li>Interacting with walls and fences should now work better when standing in the cave.</li></ul>', 25),
(16526, 4252, '050921a', '050921a', 'Citizens of a village logging on when a citizen has started to disband the village will not automatically stop the disbanding any longer. Various bugs creating holes in caves fixed. Teleporting for gms should work better. Dropping items through walls in caves fixed. Invisible/floating players and creatures bug fixed (again).', '<ul><li>Citizens of a village logging on when a citizen has started to disband the village will not automatically stop the disbanding any longer.</li>\n<li>Various bugs creating holes in caves fixed.</li>\n<li>Teleporting for gms should work better.</li>\n<li>Dropping items through walls in caves fixed.</li>\n<li>Invisible/floating players and creatures bug fixed (again).</li></ul>', 26),
(16527, 4252, '050920', '050920', 'CAVES You may no longer find ore on the surface. When you mine on the surface you instead create an opening after a while. Lots of small bugs fixed as well. For instance: The erroneous positioning of players bug should be fixed. Trading exploits fixed. Some item related bugs like \'last log created size\'-bug and \'cannot drop slab\'-bug. Cloth shoes do not insta-decay any longer. Metal shouldn\'t become insta-cold when put in an unlit fireplace. Wall and Palisade damage taken increased some.', '<p>CAVES\n</p>\n<ul><li>You may no longer find ore on the surface. When you mine on the surface you instead create an opening after a while.</li>\n<li>Lots of small bugs fixed as well. For instance:</li>\n<li>The erroneous positioning of players bug should be fixed.</li>\n<li>Trading exploits fixed.</li>\n<li>Some item related bugs like \'last log created size\'-bug and \'cannot drop slab\'-bug.</li>\n<li>Cloth shoes do not insta-decay any longer. Metal shouldn\'t become insta-cold when put in an unlit fireplace.</li>\n<li>Wall and Palisade damage taken increased some.</li></ul>', 27),
(16528, 4252, '050907b', '050907b', 'The rare occurrence where players became visually misplaced should be fixed. Guards now shouldn\'t die in one hit. A few new creatures who serve a higher purpose have been introduced. Creatures now have age and may die from it eventually.', '<ul><li>The rare occurrence where players became visually misplaced should be fixed.</li>\n<li>Guards now shouldn\'t die in one hit.</li>\n<li>A few new creatures who serve a higher purpose have been introduced.</li>\n<li>Creatures now have age and may die from it eventually.</li></ul>', 28),
(16529, 4252, '050907a', '050907a', 'Bug with trading not ending if both participants did not offer anything fixed. There are bartenders in Newtown who feed and quench newbies thirst. Banks will start working again. All village tokens have to be manually replaced first though. New traders placed by a citizen of a village will pay tax and add to the village upkeep fund when they buy from foreigners. The \'floating players\' bug may still be in.', '<ul><li>Bug with trading not ending if both participants did not offer anything fixed.</li>\n<li>There are bartenders in Newtown who feed and quench newbies thirst.</li>\n<li>Banks will start working again. All village tokens have to be manually replaced first though.</li>\n<li>New traders placed by a citizen of a village will pay tax and add to the village upkeep fund when they buy from foreigners.</li>\n<li>The \'floating players\' bug may still be in.</li></ul>', 29),
(16530, 4252, '050906', '050906', 'Thanks to Johnwayne and Southernstar for not abusing but reporting a serious exploit. They have been duly rewarded. Containers and tiles will now not contain more than roughly 50 items. That goes for your inventory as well. There are several reasons behind this, most of which makes good sense. Walls, fences and items now endure much more damage dealt by weapons. Server disconnects should be reduced overall. The economy has changed drastically and traders should be more sensitive to supply and demand. Prices may be lower now, but will increase a lot over time as trader demands rise. Due to good weather, the creatures of Wurm have increased.', '<ul><li>Thanks to Johnwayne and Southernstar for not abusing but reporting a serious exploit. They have been duly rewarded.</li>\n<li>Containers and tiles will now not contain more than roughly 50 items. That goes for your inventory as well. There are several reasons behind this, most of which makes good sense.</li>\n<li>Walls, fences and items now endure much more damage dealt by weapons.</li>\n<li>Server disconnects should be reduced overall.</li>\n<li>The economy has changed drastically and traders should be more sensitive to supply and demand. Prices may be lower now, but will increase a lot over time as trader demands rise.</li>\n<li>Due to good weather, the creatures of Wurm have increased.</li></ul>', 30),
(16531, 4252, '050823', '050823', 'Armour penalties to movement is implemented. Old armour worn is not affected, since it would be too much database hassle to fix :O If you wear new armour it will affect your speed though. You can now fight again while moving, but it has a penalty. The duplicate wounds that appeared should be gone. You should now be able to pick up piles safely in villages where it is allowed. Weapon damage has tripled. Wooden items do much less damage. Positioning now affects combat for flanking and rear attacks as well as elevation. Shark attacks should no longer happen to dead people. You may now repair unfinished items.', '<ul><li>Armour penalties to movement is implemented. Old armour worn is not affected, since it would be too much database hassle to fix :O If you wear new armour it will affect your speed though.</li>\n<li>You can now fight again while moving, but it has a penalty.</li>\n<li>The duplicate wounds that appeared should be gone.</li>\n<li>You should now be able to pick up piles safely in villages where it is allowed.</li>\n<li>Weapon damage has tripled. Wooden items do much less damage.</li>\n<li>Positioning now affects combat for flanking and rear attacks as well as elevation.</li>\n<li>Shark attacks should no longer happen to dead people.</li>\n<li>You may now repair unfinished items.</li></ul>', 31),
(16532, 4252, '050819', '050819', 'A bug with containers that affected for instance piles and campfires were detected. All ash items had to be removed from the game. Possibly some items in campfires have disappeared because of the bug as well.', '<ul><li>A bug with containers that affected for instance piles and campfires were detected. All ash items had to be removed from the game. Possibly some items in campfires have disappeared because of the bug as well.</li></ul>', 32),
(16533, 4252, '050818', '050818', 'Fighting system very much remade. Creatures and weapons do other amounts of damage now. Take care while you try it out and read the forum posts. Planting a size 10+ village deed now gives you a trader contract for free. Fo healers will now be penalized severely for healing followers of Libila. The bug where no stamina was used when creating items fixed. A few bugs with cooking (mainly bugs with steaks) fixed. Bug with favor going up insta fixed. You now harvest maple sap with a bucket. An eerie surprise!', '<ul><li>Fighting system very much remade. Creatures and weapons do other amounts of damage now. Take care while you try it out and read the forum posts.</li>\n<li>Planting a size 10+ village deed now gives you a trader contract for free.</li>\n<li>Fo healers will now be penalized severely for healing followers of Libila.</li>\n<li>The bug where no stamina was used when creating items fixed.</li>\n<li>A few bugs with cooking (mainly bugs with steaks) fixed.</li>\n<li>Bug with favor going up insta fixed.</li>\n<li>You now harvest maple sap with a bucket.</li>\n<li>An eerie surprise!</li></ul>', 33),
(16534, 4252, '050809', '050809', 'Bushes and fruit trees may now be harvested. Pending the fighting system overlook, some items like shafts have been made twohanded. Kingdom change is now working again. Cooking is now harder if not performed in an oven. Some more stone decoration items added. Stonecutting is now a subskill to masonry, and replaces masonry for bricks and such. On this map, you will get stonecutting=masonry if you already have masonry. Improving and repairing fences should now yield higher skill gain.', '<ul><li>Bushes and fruit trees may now be harvested.</li>\n<li>Pending the fighting system overlook, some items like shafts have been made twohanded.</li>\n<li>Kingdom change is now working again.</li>\n<li>Cooking is now harder if not performed in an oven.</li>\n<li>Some more stone decoration items added. Stonecutting is now a subskill to masonry, and replaces masonry for bricks and such. On this map, you will get stonecutting=masonry if you already have masonry.</li>\n<li>Improving and repairing fences should now yield higher skill gain.</li></ul>', 34),
(16535, 4252, '050729b', '050729b', 'Your shovel/pickaxe may now get stuck while digging or mining. You have to move to free it. Hammers are now improvable again.', '<ul><li>Your shovel/pickaxe may now get stuck while digging or mining. You have to move to free it.</li>\n<li>Hammers are now improvable again.</li></ul>', 35),
(16536, 4252, '050729', '050729', 'Steeping is now properly called tempering. Don\'t ask where i got \'steeping\' from since it\'s used for tea. You now need to use a pelt instead of rags to polish things (thanks Inacron). Cats and rats have pelts. You now succeed in making the item on the first try 50% of the time instead of 20%. A bug with tempering where water turned into an inventory item fixed. The inventorys have been changed back. Objects like axes that need tempering but used to burn up should not burn any longer, so they can be tempered. While finishing an item, the improvement rate has been lowered by 0.5. Hammer heads and hammers can no longer be improved, since it caused annoying illogicalness.', '<ul><li>Steeping is now properly called tempering. Don\'t ask where i got \'steeping\' from since it\'s used for tea.</li>\n<li>You now need to use a pelt instead of rags to polish things (thanks Inacron). Cats and rats have pelts.</li>\n<li>You now succeed in making the item on the first try 50% of the time instead of 20%.</li>\n<li>A bug with tempering where water turned into an inventory item fixed. The inventorys have been changed back.</li>\n<li>Objects like axes that need tempering but used to burn up should not burn any longer, so they can be tempered.</li>\n<li>While finishing an item, the improvement rate has been lowered by 0.5.</li>\n<li>Hammer heads and hammers can no longer be improved, since it caused annoying illogicalness.</li></ul>', 36),
(16537, 4252, '050728b', '050728b', 'Skillgain is now 5 times slower. Skill gain rates have been altered for many skills that were too slow though. The bug that made it impossible to finish and improve items is fixed.', '<ul><li>Skillgain is now 5 times slower. Skill gain rates have been altered for many skills that were too slow though.</li>\n<li>The bug that made it impossible to finish and improve items is fixed.</li></ul>', 37),
(16538, 4252, '050728', '050728', 'Item creation and improvement is now more intricate. You will now sometimes need a tool to finish creating an item or improving an item. There is a 1 in 5 chance that you succed in making the item on the first try, so eventually you will manage to make it. In the 4 other cases you will end up with an \'unfinished (name)\', and will have to perform an action to finish it. Every use of a tool to finish the unfinished item will count as an improve. The reason for this is to encourage finishing those unfinished items. Examining the container you are cooking in should now give a good estimation of the difficulty of the meal. The lower the difficulty the easier the meal. Difficulties were also tweaked, since it really was too hard ;) :O :P :) . The \'ghost logs\' bug fixed. * The bug that made it impossible to move sometimes fixed. Most items will now start decaying after about 2 real days. Food starts decaying after roughly 2 ingame days. The bug where rafts disappear at creation is fixed', '<ul><li>Item creation and improvement is now more intricate. You will now sometimes need a tool to finish creating an item or improving an item. There is a 1 in 5 chance that you succed in making the item on the first try, so eventually you will manage to make it. In the 4 other cases you will end up with an \'unfinished (name)\', and will have to perform an action to finish it. Every use of a tool to finish the unfinished item will count as an improve. The reason for this is to encourage finishing those unfinished items.</li>\n<li>Examining the container you are cooking in should now give a good estimation of the difficulty of the meal. The lower the difficulty the easier the meal. Difficulties were also tweaked, since it really was too hard ;) :O :P :) .</li>\n<li>The \'ghost logs\' bug fixed. * The bug that made it impossible to move sometimes fixed.</li>\n<li>Most items will now start decaying after about 2 real days. Food starts decaying after roughly 2 ingame days.</li>\n<li>The bug where rafts disappear at creation is fixed</li></ul>', 38),
(16539, 4252, '050718b', '050718b', 'Reset skills to max 20 and 1 for base characteristics.', '<ul><li>Reset skills to max 20 and 1 for base characteristics.</li></ul>', 39),
(16540, 4252, '050718', '050718', 'The server was reset. All items, skills, structures, village are gone. The reason for this is that someone got hold of an old forum backup, and managed to crack some passwords. Since we do not match your player accounts to emails we could not replace those passwords. Limited skill gain per action to max 1. Fixed tracking that did not increase.', '<ul><li>The server was reset. All items, skills, structures, village are gone.</li>\n<li>The reason for this is that someone got hold of an old forum backup, and managed to crack some passwords. Since we do not match your player accounts to emails we could not replace those passwords.</li>\n<li>Limited skill gain per action to max 1.</li>\n<li>Fixed tracking that did not increase.</li></ul>', 40),
(16541, 4252, '050714', '050714', 'The \'You are not trading\' bug fixed. Heal now removes damage correctly. The price of metal art items like pendulums now is affected by their material.', '<ul><li>The \'You are not trading\' bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Heal now removes damage correctly.</li>\n<li>The price of metal art items like pendulums now is affected by their material.</li></ul>', 41),
(16542, 4252, '050712', '050712', 'Item damage should be more \'fluent\' so you may predict decay better. Batch combine should work now.', '<ul><li>Item damage should be more \'fluent\' so you may predict decay better.</li>\n<li>Batch combine should work now.</li></ul>', 42),
(16543, 4252, '050707', '050707', 'When you found a settlement, no other settlement must be within 100 tiles now, unless you are founding a homestead. The settlement may in that case opt to \'accept homesteads\' in which case you will be able to found the homestead within the area. Skill gain has been tweaked. Consider it a test for now. You now gain skill only when you succeed with a skill roll. You will gain skill either if you have very low skill, or you pass the skillroll fairly good. The reason for this change is to remove the incitement to fail with skill rolls by using low ql tools, thus creating lots of garbage. Outside items should decay at a much more even pace. This may have effect on server performance', '<ul><li>When you found a settlement, no other settlement must be within 100 tiles now, unless you are founding a homestead. The settlement may in that case opt to \'accept homesteads\' in which case you will be able to found the homestead within the area.</li>\n<li>Skill gain has been tweaked. Consider it a test for now. You now gain skill only when you succeed with a skill roll. You will gain skill either if you have very low skill, or you pass the skillroll fairly good. The reason for this change is to remove the incitement to fail with skill rolls by using low ql tools, thus creating lots of garbage.</li>\n<li>Outside items should decay at a much more even pace. This may have effect on server performance</li></ul>', 43),
(16544, 4252, 'Missing maybe', 'Missing_maybe', '', '', 44),
(16545, 4252, '050518', '050518', 'Kingdoms are now in. Kingdoms grow around villages and guard towers. Guards towers spawn guards that will hunt enemies within the kingdom border. On wild servers villages can only be built inside the kingdom (on home servers the whole server is the same kingdom), and not too close to each other. Towers can be built inside the kingdom or very far from any kingdom, and not too close to a village or other tower. Villages have a ticking upkeep now. Unless your village is payed for continuously it will be disbanded. The upkeep pays for spirit guards as well. There are three levels of upkeep that spawn one guardtype each. Guards respawn in regular intervals. Anyone may pay upkeep at the village token (village info) or at the guard management menu. You may now change sex to female using the command /gofemale. The change is permanent and irreversible. Healing spells now should remove the damage in the stamina bar as well. Citizen-less guards should stop hunting after a while. Respawning at the black altar now works. Guards repeatedly overkilling bug fixed. If you die in your own village or in an allied village, you now lose much less skill. Prospecting for gems is no longer possible;). You now may happen to find one whenever you mine. Cooking food quality is now calculated differently. It might be too hard still. * Pushing and pulling is now policed by guards. On different server types: Wurm will have two type of servers, \'Home\' and \'Wild\'. Home servers have one kingdom on the whole server. Wild servers host several kingdoms that fight for territory and resources. Since we are testing PvP/PvE this is currently a Wild server. On Home servers, GM\'s will act as a police force, protecting players from intra-kingdom griefing and will punish thieves if they are caught. On Wild servers, GM interaction is supposed to be kept to a minimum. Use /dev to report bugs and abuse.', '<ul><li>Kingdoms are now in. Kingdoms grow around villages and guard towers. Guards towers spawn guards that will hunt enemies within the kingdom border. On wild servers villages can only be built inside the kingdom (on home servers the whole server is the same kingdom), and not too close to each other. Towers can be built inside the kingdom or very far from any kingdom, and not too close to a village or other tower.</li>\n<li>Villages have a ticking upkeep now. Unless your village is payed for continuously it will be disbanded. The upkeep pays for spirit guards as well. There are three levels of upkeep that spawn one guardtype each. Guards respawn in regular intervals. Anyone may pay upkeep at the village token (village info) or at the guard management menu.</li>\n<li>You may now change sex to female using the command /gofemale. The change is permanent and irreversible.</li>\n<li>Healing spells now should remove the damage in the stamina bar as well.</li>\n<li>Citizen-less guards should stop hunting after a while.</li>\n<li>Respawning at the black altar now works.</li>\n<li>Guards repeatedly overkilling bug fixed.</li>\n<li>If you die in your own village or in an allied village, you now lose much less skill.</li>\n<li>Prospecting for gems is no longer possible;). You now may happen to find one whenever you mine.</li>\n<li>Cooking food quality is now calculated differently. It might be too hard still. * Pushing and pulling is now policed by guards.</li>\n<li>On different server types:</li>\n<li>Wurm will have two type of servers, \'Home\' and \'Wild\'. Home servers have one kingdom on the whole server. Wild servers host several kingdoms that fight for territory and resources.</li>\n<li>Since we are testing PvP/PvE this is currently a Wild server.</li>\n<li>On Home servers, GM\'s will act as a police force, protecting players from intra-kingdom griefing and will punish thieves if they are caught.</li>\n<li>On Wild servers, GM interaction is supposed to be kept to a minimum. Use /dev to report bugs and abuse.</li></ul>', 45),
(16546, 4252, '050426', '050426', 'Made it easier finding gems. You will however need 20+ prospecting skill to have a chance to prospect them. You may mine them by chance at any skill.', '<ul><li>Made it easier finding gems. You will however need 20+ prospecting skill to have a chance to prospect them. You may mine them by chance at any skill.</li></ul>', 46),
(16547, 4252, '050425', '050425', 'Model name bug fixed. You may now find (very rare) gems while mining. High prospecting will help. Prospecting now damages the pickaxe. You may now create satchels and backpacks. Armour chains are no longer ql-capped at skill/5. You may no longer improve them either. Fixed a bug with lootable corpses.', '<ul><li>Model name bug fixed.</li>\n<li>You may now find (very rare) gems while mining. High prospecting will help. Prospecting now damages the pickaxe.</li>\n<li>You may now create satchels and backpacks.</li>\n<li>Armour chains are no longer ql-capped at skill/5. You may no longer improve them either.</li>\n<li>Fixed a bug with lootable corpses.</li></ul>', 47),
(16548, 4252, '050424', '050424', '4 people had managed to run into a bug that gave them 100 faith. Bug fixed and their faith set to 10 instead. Some spell costs tweaked.', '<ul><li>4 people had managed to run into a bug that gave them 100 faith. Bug fixed and their faith set to 10 instead.</li>\n<li>Some spell costs tweaked.</li></ul>', 48),
(16549, 4252, '050421', '050421', 'Armour now takes half the damage it used to. Faith gain is back, but in a new shape. You must pray at altars to gain faith. Deities will only be pleased about 5 times per 24 hours, and with 20 minutes in between. Favor slowly rises automatically, faster when praying. High favor is very hard to attain, making for very potent spells later on. Spells have been adjusted accordingly. More spells will come soon. Dishes now need meat or fish to become really good. Bug with woodscraps fixed. Yoyo\'s should be available again.', '<ul><li>Armour now takes half the damage it used to.</li>\n<li>Faith gain is back, but in a new shape. You must pray at altars to gain faith. Deities will only be pleased about 5 times per 24 hours, and with 20 minutes in between.</li>\n<li>Favor slowly rises automatically, faster when praying. High favor is very hard to attain, making for very potent spells later on. Spells have been adjusted accordingly. More spells will come soon.</li>\n<li>Dishes now need meat or fish to become really good.</li>\n<li>Bug with woodscraps fixed. Yoyo\'s should be available again.</li></ul>', 49),
(16550, 4252, '050420', '050420', 'Bug with landscapes around willows and oaks being disrupted fixed. Faith gain put on hold pending new implementation.', '<ul><li>Bug with landscapes around willows and oaks being disrupted fixed.</li>\n<li>Faith gain put on hold pending new implementation.</li></ul>', 50),
(16551, 4252, '050419B', '050419B', 'Pvp is now allowed again. Non-libilans may not loot corpses from the same kingdom unless they issue the command /release corpse. /release corpse makes all your current corpses lootable by the same kingdom. When joining a village, your reputation is now cleared. Bug with moving forges and similar items fixed.', '<ul><li>Pvp is now allowed again.</li>\n<li>Non-libilans may not loot corpses from the same kingdom unless they issue the command /release corpse.</li>\n<li>/release corpse makes all your current corpses lootable by the same kingdom.</li>\n<li>When joining a village, your reputation is now cleared.</li>\n<li>Bug with moving forges and similar items fixed.</li></ul>', 51),
(16552, 4252, '050419', '050419', 'This week should be quite heavy with updates. In this update, kingdoms are supported. Attacking people from the same kingdom will give severe penalties (except for followers of Libila). You should only be able to interact with members of other kingdoms through local chat, fighting (still NOT allowed!), and emotes right now. Guards WILL attack players from other kingdoms. Charcoal piles and plate smithing now shows as a construction option for newbies. Tool skills are now rolled when creating items instead of simply giving a bonus, so you gain tool skill now but may fail more often. The friends and ignored lists have been reset, since I changed the save format. You may now join Libila and the Horde of the Summoned regardless of alignment. Your alignment will become negative permanently, and you may never return to the good side. Wound bug where you could not heal others while wounded fixed. Two handed weapons like huge axe, twohanded sword, large maul now needs to be wielded with both hands, and no shield may be used. If you are wielding two axes, remove one and the shield. Fighting using both is considered using an exploit and a bannable offence. Fruit trees produce less wood than normal trees. Bushes produce no wood. New items will now have the woodtype (although invisible in most cases). Old items are made from birch. Birch burns better than other woodtypes, cedar decays slower, oak takes less damage. Oak grows slower. Willows and oaks kill nearby trees. Wall and fence damage is now much more dependant on quality level when destroying, so improve them to at least above ql 20. Use /dev to report bugs and abuse.', '<ul><li>This week should be quite heavy with updates.</li>\n<li>In this update, kingdoms are supported. Attacking people from the same kingdom will give severe penalties (except for followers of Libila). You should only be able to interact with members of other kingdoms through local chat, fighting (still NOT allowed!), and emotes right now. Guards WILL attack players from other kingdoms.</li>\n<li>Charcoal piles and plate smithing now shows as a construction option for newbies.</li>\n<li>Tool skills are now rolled when creating items instead of simply giving a bonus, so you gain tool skill now but may fail more often.</li>\n<li>The friends and ignored lists have been reset, since I changed the save format.</li>\n<li>You may now join Libila and the Horde of the Summoned regardless of alignment. Your alignment will become negative permanently, and you may never return to the good side.</li>\n<li>Wound bug where you could not heal others while wounded fixed.</li>\n<li>Two handed weapons like huge axe, twohanded sword, large maul now needs to be wielded with both hands, and no shield may be used. If you are wielding two axes, remove one and the shield. Fighting using both is considered using an exploit and a bannable offence.</li>\n<li>Fruit trees produce less wood than normal trees. Bushes produce no wood. New items will now have the woodtype (although invisible in most cases). Old items are made from birch. Birch burns better than other woodtypes, cedar decays slower, oak takes less damage. Oak grows slower. Willows and oaks kill nearby trees.</li>\n<li>Wall and fence damage is now much more dependant on quality level when destroying, so improve them to at least above ql 20.</li></ul>\n<p>Use /dev to report bugs and abuse.\n</p>', 52),
(16553, 4252, '050406', '050406', 'Improving now works as intended. Practice dolls are capped at about 20 for fighting skillgain.', '<ul><li>Improving now works as intended.</li>\n<li>Practice dolls are capped at about 20 for fighting skillgain.</li></ul>', 53),
(16554, 4252, '050404', '050404', 'Clay items are now repair/improvable. Skill progression has been tweaked and should be faster in most cases. The bug that crashed the game was fixed. Democracies may no longer revoke citizenships. You may now select to no longer be a citizen of your village by using /revoke.', '<ul><li>Clay items are now repair/improvable.</li>\n<li>Skill progression has been tweaked and should be faster in most cases.</li>\n<li>The bug that crashed the game was fixed.</li>\n<li>Democracies may no longer revoke citizenships.</li>\n<li>You may now select to no longer be a citizen of your village by using /revoke.</li></ul>', 54),
(16555, 4252, '050403', '050403', 'Kingdom chat is now optional. Toggle it with /kchat. Creation menus bug fix. Fish sizes increased so endless amounts shouldn\'t fit in containers. Logs used in improving now is depleted, not damaged. Improving now requires 10 times less raw materials, and depletion is done upon finishing the action. Muting now stays between logins. Fishing rods now take some damage when a fish is caught.', '<ul><li>Kingdom chat is now optional. Toggle it with /kchat.</li>\n<li>Creation menus bug fix.</li>\n<li>Fish sizes increased so endless amounts shouldn\'t fit in containers.</li>\n<li>Logs used in improving now is depleted, not damaged.</li>\n<li>Improving now requires 10 times less raw materials, and depletion is done upon finishing the action.</li>\n<li>Muting now stays between logins.</li>\n<li>Fishing rods now take some damage when a fish is caught.</li></ul>', 55),
(16556, 4252, '050329', '050329', 'Improving items now use resources instead, and \'simple improvable\' items like weapons now start at a capped ql so you will have to improve them.', '<ul><li>Improving items now use resources instead, and \'simple improvable\' items like weapons now start at a capped ql so you will have to improve them.</li></ul>', 56),
(16557, 4252, '050329', '050329_2', 'Item creation bug fixed. Overall creation times have increased slightly. Endless amounts of items were created before. We\'re going to change the way items are created in the future.', '<ul><li>Item creation bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Overall creation times have increased slightly. Endless amounts of items were created before. We\'re going to change the way items are created in the future.</li></ul>', 57),
(16558, 4252, '050328b', '050328b', 'Woodcutting skill should progress faster. Newbies may now /shout. Fish weight is now considered when fishing. You may now no longer leave buildings through locked doors. Removed the initial cap for improvable items since it diminished the use of raw material ql. Improvable items instead takes longer to create. Skillgain for improving items tripled. Improving ql cap increased. All this is subject to change, don\'t panic.', '<ul><li>Woodcutting skill should progress faster.</li>\n<li>Newbies may now /shout.</li>\n<li>Fish weight is now considered when fishing.</li>\n<li>You may now no longer leave buildings through locked doors.</li>\n<li>Removed the initial cap for improvable items since it diminished the use of raw material ql. Improvable items instead takes longer to create. Skillgain for improving items tripled. Improving ql cap increased. All this is subject to change, don\'t panic.</li></ul>', 58),
(16559, 4252, '050328', '050328', 'Skills now normally update at the end of an action. Thus, progress has changed and may be flawed in some occasions. This will be trimmed in. Improving items now has a max limit quality level. Items should fit better in containers and cooked items shouldn\'t disappear without a dish appearing. A destroy option is now available on structure writs. Non-newbies may now /shout again. Armour now takes 5 times more damage.', '<ul><li>Skills now normally update at the end of an action. Thus, progress has changed and may be flawed in some occasions. This will be trimmed in.</li>\n<li>Improving items now has a max limit quality level.</li>\n<li>Items should fit better in containers and cooked items shouldn\'t disappear without a dish appearing.</li>\n<li>A destroy option is now available on structure writs.</li>\n<li>Non-newbies may now /shout again.</li>\n<li>Armour now takes 5 times more damage.</li></ul>', 59),
(16560, 4252, '050224', '050224', 'Name check was removed for the weekend pending a name-change implementation.', '<ul><li>Name check was removed for the weekend pending a name-change implementation.</li></ul>', 60),
(16561, 4252, '050223', '050223', 'The bug with containers that will not hold items or water fixed. Hot food quality now depends much more on cooking skill. Bug found with key copying. Still untested though. Mining and wall/fence building now takes longer time again to preserve the economy. Name censoring working now. Some of you may have lost your account due to this. We have no quick fix right now.', '<ul><li>The bug with containers that will not hold items or water fixed.</li>\n<li>Hot food quality now depends much more on cooking skill.</li>\n<li>Bug found with key copying. Still untested though.</li>\n<li>Mining and wall/fence building now takes longer time again to preserve the economy.</li>\n<li>Name censoring working now. Some of you may have lost your account due to this. We have no quick fix right now.</li></ul>', 61),
(16562, 4252, '050222', '050222', 'Various bug fixes from bugzilla. Some unique creatures to stay away from. More actions now take less time. You should not be able to insert large amounts of food into small containers any more. Damage to walls increased.', '<ul><li>Various bug fixes from bugzilla.</li>\n<li>Some unique creatures to stay away from.</li>\n<li>More actions now take less time.</li>\n<li>You should not be able to insert large amounts of food into small containers any more.</li>\n<li>Damage to walls increased.</li></ul>', 62),
(16563, 4252, '050216', '050216', 'Bug fixes: Charcoal piles work again. Wooden shields are now created from nails and planks. You now need skill to build steep fences. You may now improve metal altars using a chisel. Creatures should not enter houses. Still some pathfinding cleanup left though. Bug with increasing deed size fixed. Faith gain speed increased. Bury no longer gives faith. Creatures will be a bit more aggressive.', '<ul><li>Bug fixes:</li>\n<li>Charcoal piles work again.</li>\n<li>Wooden shields are now created from nails and planks.</li>\n<li>You now need skill to build steep fences.</li>\n<li>You may now improve metal altars using a chisel.</li>\n<li>Creatures should not enter houses. Still some pathfinding cleanup left though.</li>\n<li>Bug with increasing deed size fixed.</li>\n<li>Faith gain speed increased. Bury no longer gives faith.</li>\n<li>Creatures will be a bit more aggressive.</li></ul>', 63),
(16564, 4252, '050209', '050209', 'A few more fascist checks for dragging items that are inside a building while you have walked outside implemented. You may now drag liquid to and fill liquid containers that contain food only. Burning items and lighting fires through windows are now blocked.', '<ul><li>A few more fascist checks for dragging items that are inside a building while you have walked outside implemented.</li>\n<li>You may now drag liquid to and fill liquid containers that contain food only.</li>\n<li>Burning items and lighting fires through windows are now blocked.</li></ul>', 64),
(16565, 4252, '050206', '050206', 'Ghost structure bug fixed. Bears now look like cows instead of humans. Respawning bug fixed. Combine bug fixed. Drinking and eating now theft-protected.', '<ul><li>Ghost structure bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Bears now look like cows instead of humans.</li>\n<li>Respawning bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Combine bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Drinking and eating now theft-protected.</li></ul>', 65),
(16566, 4252, '050131', '050131', 'Foraged food now yields more. Forageable tiles are a little bit more sparse. Guests shouldn\'t be able to create water items outside containers anymore. You may now select where you want to spawn after a death. The command /respawn may come in handy at times. Animals should hunt less ferociously and may possibly be fooled. Behave like this, please: For different reasons we have turned off PvP. Since the future will hold different sides, you are now expected to act as if you were on the same side in a huge war. The future will allow same-side griefing but it will be severely penalized. Since neither both sides nor the penalty system is in place, griefers WILL be banned. Griefing now includes bullying, stealing, and menacing in general. Respect non-deeded settlements as if they were actually deeded and guarded when it comes to stealing, building, farming, terraforming etc. GM\'s are called upon to uphold the law. Use /dev to report abuse. Thank you for your patience!', '<ul><li>Foraged food now yields more. Forageable tiles are a little bit more sparse.</li>\n<li>Guests shouldn\'t be able to create water items outside containers anymore.</li>\n<li>You may now select where you want to spawn after a death. The command /respawn may come in handy at times.</li>\n<li>Animals should hunt less ferociously and may possibly be fooled.</li></ul>\n<p>Behave like this, please: For different reasons we have turned off PvP. Since the future will hold different sides, you are now expected to act as if you were on the same side in a huge war. The future will allow same-side griefing but it will be severely penalized. Since neither both sides nor the penalty system is in place, griefers WILL be banned. Griefing now includes bullying, stealing, and menacing in general. Respect non-deeded settlements as if they were actually deeded and guarded when it comes to stealing, building, farming, terraforming etc. GM\'s are called upon to uphold the law. Use /dev to report abuse. Thank you for your patience!\n</p>', 66),
(16567, 4252, '050125', '050125', 'Food system changed like this: All grass tiles yield forage once every 24 hours. Food you forage may feed you up to a certain limit due to its low quality. Raw fish and meat gives more, and cooked meals up to max. Your stamina level may go up to 4 times your food level.', '<ul><li>Food system changed like this:</li>\n<li>All grass tiles yield forage once every 24 hours.</li>\n<li>Food you forage may feed you up to a certain limit due to its low quality.</li>\n<li>Raw fish and meat gives more, and cooked meals up to max.</li>\n<li>Your stamina level may go up to 4 times your food level.</li></ul>', 67),
(16568, 4252, '050124', '050124', 'Welcome to a clean slate! We are testing newbie progress, so no deeds will be given out. You have a bank account at your disposal on the village token to protect some of your things. We are still going to add features not yet in, so don\'t expect everything to be totally smooth. Good luck and take care! Behave like this, please: Full PvP is in. This means you may in theory attack anyone. Your deity and local laws may prevent this though. Village diplomats may declare wars on other villages. When both parties have accepted they should then be able to attack each other with no penalties from their respective deity. A village that has been declared war upon has 24 hours to accept. As soon as they accept, the village war is on. You may not decline a village war declaration. Domains of deities give bonuses to their followers and others of the same alignment. This system should work, but a GMs word is law!', '<ul><li>Welcome to a clean slate!</li>\n<li>We are testing newbie progress, so no deeds will be given out.</li>\n<li>You have a bank account at your disposal on the village token to protect some of your things.</li>\n<li>We are still going to add features not yet in, so don\'t expect everything to be totally smooth.</li>\n<li>Good luck and take care!</li></ul>\n<p>Behave like this, please: Full PvP is in. This means you may in theory attack anyone. Your deity and local laws may prevent this though. Village diplomats may declare wars on other villages. When both parties have accepted they should then be able to attack each other with no penalties from their respective deity. A village that has been declared war upon has 24 hours to accept. As soon as they accept, the village war is on. You may not decline a village war declaration. Domains of deities give bonuses to their followers and others of the same alignment. This system should work, but a GMs word is law!\n</p>', 68),
(16569, 4252, '050111', '050111', 'Bug with excessive faith progress fixed. Clay decay time increased. Bandaging bug fixed so now you can bandage others again', '<ul><li>Bug with excessive faith progress fixed.</li>\n<li>Clay decay time increased.</li>\n<li>Bandaging bug fixed so now you can bandage others again</li></ul>', 69),
(16570, 4252, '050110', '050110', 'Piles and containers as well as carts should now be theft-protected. Food still not though. Creatures hunt again. Reputations go up slower. Small chance for critical hits to players are now in. No fighting should be totally safe anymore. We removed the teleport wands since they have proven to be extremely unbalanced.', '<ul><li>Piles and containers as well as carts should now be theft-protected. Food still not though.</li>\n<li>Creatures hunt again. Reputations go up slower.</li>\n<li>Small chance for critical hits to players are now in. No fighting should be totally safe anymore.</li>\n<li>We removed the teleport wands since they have proven to be extremely unbalanced.</li></ul>', 70),
(16571, 4252, '050107', '050107', 'Charcoal piles should work again. Farming ql is more proper again, and farming takes less time. Banks finally work. Bug with theft fixed. Faith for followers of Libila shouldn\'t decrease while attacking now.', '<ul><li>Charcoal piles should work again.</li>\n<li>Farming ql is more proper again, and farming takes less time.</li>\n<li>Banks finally work.</li>\n<li>Bug with theft fixed.</li>\n<li>Faith for followers of Libila shouldn\'t decrease while attacking now.</li></ul>', 71),
(16572, 4252, '050105', '050105', 'Fatigue is implemented. You receive 4 real hours per real day to perform \'fatiguing\' tasks. Fatiguing tasks are usually things that take time. The main reason behind fatigue is to prevent action queueing, but it also serves well in other departments. Some actions may seem stupid to crave fatigue like track, yoyoing or praying, but learn to save some fatigue for those tasks. You may pool up to 8 hours of fatigue. You receive 1 hour of fatigue every 6 hours. Type /fatigue to check how much time you have left. Stamina rises faster, hunger and thirst slower as a compensation. Pathfinding works better. Theft prevention is now implemented. Some deities will not allow you to pick up things in villages you are not at war with and where you are not citizen or ally, or in any structure where you are not guest. Guards also enforce this rule. Use the trade window to swap items as a standard. You may however drop things and pick them up again anywhere. You may of course also disobey your deity or take your chances with the guards. Use the legal and faith modes to do this. NOTE: To protect old items, you have to drop them once first. The server may lag, since items inside containers decay again. Faith now work like skills, and go up even slower. Switch tasks to see if you gain more faith if it stops moving. Unlit charcoal piles now decay slower. You may now make kindling from wood scrap(!). Harvests now yield slightly lower quality levels. Max ql is less also. Bears and wolves are now common in forests. They may wander into settlements but will not hunt into them.', '<ul><li>Fatigue is implemented. You receive 4 real hours per real day to perform \'fatiguing\' tasks. Fatiguing tasks are usually things that take time. The main reason behind fatigue is to prevent action queueing, but it also serves well in other departments. Some actions may seem stupid to crave fatigue like track, yoyoing or praying, but learn to save some fatigue for those tasks. You may pool up to 8 hours of fatigue. You receive 1 hour of fatigue every 6 hours. Type /fatigue to check how much time you have left. Stamina rises faster, hunger and thirst slower as a compensation.</li>\n<li>Pathfinding works better.</li>\n<li>Theft prevention is now implemented. Some deities will not allow you to pick up things in villages you are not at war with and where you are not citizen or ally, or in any structure where you are not guest. Guards also enforce this rule. Use the trade window to swap items as a standard. You may however drop things and pick them up again anywhere. You may of course also disobey your deity or take your chances with the guards. Use the legal and faith modes to do this. NOTE: To protect old items, you have to drop them once first.</li>\n<li>The server may lag, since items inside containers decay again.</li>\n<li>Faith now work like skills, and go up even slower. Switch tasks to see if you gain more faith if it stops moving.</li>\n<li>Unlit charcoal piles now decay slower.</li>\n<li>You may now make kindling from wood scrap(!).</li>\n<li>Harvests now yield slightly lower quality levels. Max ql is less also.</li>\n<li>Bears and wolves are now common in forests. They may wander into settlements but will not hunt into them.</li></ul>', 72),
(16580, 4256, 'Description', 'Description', 'A handful of a brightly red sticky substance. Cochineal is a butchering product obtainable from cave bugs and scorpions .', '<p><i>A handful of a brightly red sticky substance.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Cochineal is a butchering product obtainable from <a href=\"/index.php/Cave_bug\" title=\"Cave bug\">cave bugs</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Scorpion\" title=\"Scorpion\">scorpions</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16581, 4256, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in the creation of red dye . Used in the construction of a range pole . Used in some cooking recipes. Used in tailoring Used to create foundation pillars Used to create a Magranon puppet', '<ul><li>Used in the creation of red <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in the construction of a <a href=\"/index.php/Range_pole\" title=\"Range pole\">range pole</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Used in <a href=\"/index.php/Tailoring\" title=\"Tailoring\">tailoring</a></li>\n<li>Used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Foundation_pillar\" title=\"Foundation pillar\">foundation pillars</a></li>\n<li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon_puppet\" title=\"Magranon puppet\">Magranon puppet</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16582, 4256, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.', '<ul><li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>', 2),
(16583, 4257, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick fur, skinned from an animal. A butchered item obtained from black bears , brown bears or black wolves .', '<p><i>A thick fur, skinned from an animal.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Butchering_items\" title=\"Category:Butchering items\">butchered item</a> obtained from <a href=\"/index.php/Black_bear\" title=\"Black bear\">black bears</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">brown bears</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Black_wolf\" title=\"Black wolf\">black wolves</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(16584, 4257, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'It is used for creating beds and animal rugs .', '<p>It is used for creating <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">beds</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking#Rugs\" title=\"Leatherworking\">animal rugs</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(16585, 4257, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Brown bear fur weighs 4 kg and others 3 kg. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.', '<ul><li>Brown bear fur weighs 4 kg and others 3 kg.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16586, 4258, 'Description', 'Description', 'A paw from a butchered animal. A butchered item obtained from butchering animals .', '<p><i>A paw from a butchered animal.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Butchering_items\" title=\"Category:Butchering items\">butchered item</a> obtained from <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16587, 4258, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in some cooking recipes. Used to create a healing cover with a potency of 2.', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a> with a potency of 2.</li></ul>', 1),
(16588, 4258, 'Notes', 'Notes', '0.10 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage. A paw can be butchered from these animals: Black wolf Crocodile Dog Mountain lion', '<ul><li>0.10 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>\n<p>A <b>paw</b> can be butchered from these animals:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_wolf\" title=\"Black wolf\">Black wolf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crocodile\" title=\"Crocodile\">Crocodile</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Dog\" title=\"Dog\">Dog</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_lion\" title=\"Mountain lion\">Mountain lion</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16599, 4265, 'Description', 'Description', 'Black, greasy, sticky tar.', '<p><i>Black, greasy, sticky tar.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16600, 4265, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Fuel for forges , stone ovens , campfires , lanterns , lamps , and carved pumpkins Torch Boats Floor boards preservative (via the \"Tar\" action)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fuel\" title=\"Fuel\">Fuel</a> for <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_oven\" title=\"Stone oven\">stone ovens</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lantern\" title=\"Lantern\">lanterns</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lamp\" title=\"Lamp\">lamps</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Carved_pumpkin\" title=\"Carved pumpkin\">carved pumpkins</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Torch\" title=\"Torch\">Torch</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Boats\" title=\"Boats\">Boats</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Floor_board\" title=\"Floor board\">Floor boards</a> preservative (via the \"Tar\" action)</li></ul>', 1),
(16601, 4265, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Tar is created from charcoal piles , can be dug from tar pits or butchered from Spawn of Uttacha . Tar can also be found by Foraging at Bog muck Resource nodes . Tar tiles can be raised by dropping dirt or sand but they cannot be changed to a different tile type without using the transmutation liquids . They can be lowered with the level command if all corners are higher or level to an adjacent flat tile and your digging skill is at least 70.', '<ul><li><b>Tar</b> is created from <a href=\"/index.php/Charcoal_pile\" title=\"Charcoal pile\">charcoal piles</a>, can be <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">dug</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Tar_tile\" title=\"Tar tile\">tar pits</a> or butchered from <a href=\"/index.php/Spawn_of_Uttacha\" title=\"Spawn of Uttacha\">Spawn of Uttacha</a>.</li>\n<li>Tar can also be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> at <a href=\"/index.php/Bog_muck\" title=\"Bog muck\">Bog muck</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tar_tile\" title=\"Tar tile\">Tar tiles</a> can be raised by dropping <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sand\" title=\"Sand\">sand</a> but they cannot be changed to a different tile type without using the <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquids</a>.</li>\n<li>They can be lowered with the <a href=\"/index.php/Level\" title=\"Level\">level</a> command if all corners are higher or level to an adjacent flat tile and your <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> skill is at least 70.</li></ul>', 2),
(16602, 4265, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Peat', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Peat\" title=\"Peat\">Peat</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16605, 4267, 'Description', 'Description', 'Mend is a a spell available to a Vynora priests at 29 faith that allows players to remove damage from items. The spell reduces the damage of an item by up to 20 points and the quality by up to 2, and can be cast on some items that cannot normally be repaired. Reduction in quality depends on the amount of damage reduced. For example, if cast on an item with 10 damage, damage would be reduced by 10 and quality would be reduced by 1. Depending on repair skill level, can be more effective at repairing on normal items.', '<p><b>Mend</b> is a a spell available to a <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> at 29 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> that allows players to remove <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> from items.\n</p>\n<p>The spell reduces the <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> of an item by up to 20 points and the quality by up to 2, and can be cast on some items that cannot normally be repaired.\n</p>\n<p>Reduction in quality depends on the amount of damage reduced. For example, if cast on an item with 10 damage, damage would be reduced by 10 and quality would be reduced by 1.\n</p>\n<p><i>Depending on repair skill level, can be more effective at repairing on normal items.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16606, 4267, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate a Statuette , right-click an item and select Spells > Mend . You cannot cast mend on items of QL 2 or less. Instead you\'ll get an error message saying that the item ...would break under the power of the spell. Mend does not shatter items on failure. You cannot cast mend on items with 0 damage. Mend only items A non-exhaustive list of such that cannot be repaired , but can be mended. Compasses Logs Lumps Pelts Whetstones Pottery items Runes No repair or mend items A non-exhaustive list of items that cannot be repaired or mended. Food Small magical chest Starter tent Valrei item', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">Statuette</a>, <b>right-click</b> an item and select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Mend</i>.\n</p>\n<ul><li>You cannot cast mend on items of QL 2 or less. Instead you\'ll get an error message saying that the item <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> ...would break under the power of the spell. </span></li>\n<li>Mend does not shatter items on failure.</li>\n<li>You cannot cast mend on items with 0 damage.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mend_only_items\">Mend only items</span></h3>\n<p>A non-exhaustive list of such that <b>cannot be repaired</b>, but can be mended.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Compass\" title=\"Compass\">Compasses</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Logs\" title=\"Logs\">Logs</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lump\" title=\"Lump\">Lumps</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Whetstone\" title=\"Whetstone\">Whetstones</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pottery\" title=\"Pottery\">Pottery</a> items</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">Runes</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"No_repair_or_mend_items\">No repair or mend items</span></h3>\n<p>A non-exhaustive list of items that cannot be repaired or mended.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Food\" title=\"Food\">Food</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_magical_chest\" title=\"Small magical chest\">Small magical chest</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Starter_tent\" title=\"Starter tent\">Starter tent</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Valrei_item\" title=\"Valrei item\">Valrei item</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16626, 4271, 'Description', 'Description', 'A zombie is the raised spirit of a creature or player.  A zombie will act like a normal pet .', '<p>A zombie is the raised spirit of a <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creature</a> or player.  A zombie will act like a normal <a href=\"/index.php/Pet\" title=\"Pet\">pet</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16627, 4271, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A zombie can be made by priests of Libila with at least 40 faith by casting rebirth , or with the Scale of Libila . To raise a zombie, select a statuette of Libila, right-click a corpse, and select \"Rebirth\". The strength of a zombie may be somewhat weaker then the original. Zombies cannot log off with the owner and only live for 24 hours. Human and troll zombies can be equipped.', '<ul><li>A zombie can be made by <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> with at least 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> by casting <a href=\"/index.php/Rebirth\" title=\"Rebirth\">rebirth</a>, or with the <a href=\"/index.php/Scale_of_Libila\" title=\"Scale of Libila\">Scale of Libila</a>. To raise a zombie, select a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> of Libila, right-click a corpse, and select \"Rebirth\".</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The strength of a zombie may be somewhat weaker then the original.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Zombies cannot log off with the owner and only live for 24 hours.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Human and <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">troll</a> zombies can be equipped.</li></ul>', 1),
(16632, 4272, 'Description', 'Description', 'Reputation lowers when a player breaks a kingdom or village law within a deed . All players start with 100 reputation. If a player does something to loose reputation, it will slowly regenerate at about one point per real hour. Reputation does continue to increment while a player is offline. Reputation can be checked with the chat command /reputation . For instance, a player loses 35 reputation for stealing an item on PVP servers.', '<p><b>Reputation</b> lowers when a <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> breaks a <a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom\" title=\"Kingdom\">kingdom</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Village\" title=\"Village\">village</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed#Permissions\" title=\"Deed\">law</a> within a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">deed</a>.\n</p>\n<p>All players start with 100 reputation. If a player does something to loose reputation, it will slowly regenerate at about one point per real hour. \n</p>\n<p>Reputation does continue to increment while a player is offline. Reputation can be checked with the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chat_command\" title=\"Chat command\">chat command</a> <tt>/reputation</tt>.\n</p>\n<p>For instance, a player loses 35 reputation for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Steal\" title=\"Steal\">stealing</a> an item on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PVP\" title=\"PVP\">PVP</a> servers.\n</p>', 0),
(16633, 4272, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'If a player dies with less than 0 reputation, he or she will lose 5x the normal skill loss (a devastating 1.25 in skills). Player with negative reputation also can\'t join a village, this also include Black Light villages. If a player is a whitelighter and their reputation drops below -200, they will automatically become a blacklighter . This will use a convert . It is possible to change back to the White Light . This will also use a convert . Going blacklighter from reputation loss does not make you lose your kingdom title; it merely becomes inactive. You can still become a white lighter with -200 or lower reputation. Your village guards, should you be in a village with -200, will not attack you then.', '<ul><li>If a player dies with less than 0 reputation, he or she will lose 5x the normal <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> loss (a devastating 1.25 in skills).</li>\n<li>Player with negative reputation also can\'t join a village, this also include Black Light villages.</li>\n<li>If a player is a <a href=\"/index.php/Whitelighter\" title=\"Whitelighter\">whitelighter</a> and their reputation drops below -200, they will automatically become a <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">blacklighter</a>. <i>This will use a <a href=\"/index.php/Convert\" title=\"Convert\">convert</a></i>. It is possible to change back to the <a href=\"/index.php/White_Light\" title=\"White Light\">White Light</a>. <i>This will also use a convert</i>.</li>\n<li>Going <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">blacklighter</a> from reputation loss does not make you lose your kingdom title; it merely becomes inactive.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You can still become a white lighter with -200 or lower reputation. Your village guards, should you be in a village with -200, will not attack you then.</li></ul>', 1),
(16645, 4277, 'Description', 'Description', 'A comfortable armchair with a seat padded with cloth.', '<p><i>A comfortable armchair with a seat padded with cloth.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16646, 4277, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality shaft increases your chance for creating. Failure to create will damage both the shaft and plank. It can be picked up.', '<ul><li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> shaft increases your chance for creating.</li>\n<li>Failure to create will damage both the shaft and plank.</li>\n<li>It can be picked up.</li></ul>', 1),
(16647, 4277, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Chair Stool', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Chair\" title=\"Chair\">Chair</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stool\" title=\"Stool\">Stool</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16652, 4279, 'The Gnyffel', 'The_Gnyffel', 'The gnyffels are fictional critters invented by me back in...let me see...2002, most likely. They live at remote locations in the Andes mountains in large herds. Here, they live off the occasional passing caravan that they ambush. They use sand to camouflage their rather yellow bodies during raiding parties on caravan routes.', '<p>The gnyffels are fictional critters invented by me back in...let me see...2002, most likely. They live at remote locations in the Andes mountains in large herds. Here, they live off the occasional passing caravan that they ambush. They use sand to camouflage their rather yellow bodies during raiding parties on caravan routes.\n</p>', 0),
(16653, 4279, 'Image', 'Image', 'Very few have survived an encounter with the ferocious gnyffel, and thus the chances of a survivor being a talented artist are rather slim - hence the crude drawing (you didn\'t believe that for a second, did you? :/). [1]', '<p>Very few have survived an encounter with the ferocious gnyffel, and thus the chances of a survivor being a talented artist are rather slim - hence the crude drawing (you didn\'t believe that for a second, did you? :/).\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://img380.imageshack.us/img380/3948/gnyffel23ir.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>\n</p>', 1),
(16681, 4284, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a spell of Vynora . Cast on food, it will make the food item satisfy your character better. Spell available to priests of Vynora at 30 faith . Uses 10 favor to cast. The results vary, but you may keep casting until you get the result you like. Opulence is fantastic for raising channeling skill on a fresh priest character up until about 35.', '<p>This is a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>. Cast on food, it will make the food item satisfy your character better.\n</p>\n<p>Spell available to <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of Vynora at 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>. Uses 10 favor to cast. \n</p>\n<p>The results vary, but you may keep casting until you get the result you like. Opulence is fantastic for raising <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill on a fresh priest character up until about 35.\n</p>', 0),
(16682, 4284, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette of Vynora Right-click a food item Select Spells > Opulence', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette_of_Vynora\" title=\"Statuette of Vynora\">statuette of Vynora</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a food item</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Opulence</i></li></ol>', 1),
(16683, 4284, 'Warning', 'Warning', 'There is a chance that this spell will destroy the item. Opulence shatter rate is considered moderate - it ceases shattering items regularly after 25 skill.', '<p>There is a chance that this spell will destroy the item. Opulence shatter rate is considered <b>moderate</b> - it ceases shattering items regularly after 25 skill.\n</p>', 2),
(16717, 4292, 'Description', 'Description', 'Thin and pointy light green leaves in a small bundle.', '<p><i>Thin and pointy light green leaves in a small bundle.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16718, 4292, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used as a herb in some cooking recipes. Can be obtained by picking from an oleander bush or by botanizing on a Wildflowers node.', '<ul><li>Used as a <a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">herb</a> in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be obtained by picking from an <a href=\"/index.php/Oleander_bush\" title=\"Oleander bush\">oleander bush</a> or by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> node.</li></ul>', 1),
(16719, 4292, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Oleander bush', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Oleander_bush\" title=\"Oleander bush\">Oleander bush</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16720, 1263, 'Description', 'Description', 'A maple tree forest. Maple trees are useful trees that yield wood as well as the seasonal production of maple sap . Notes When in their harvesting season , maple sap can be harvested using a small bucket . Maple sap is then used to make maple syrup. Arrow shafts made from maplewood take less damage than those made from other wood types.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:402px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Newmaple.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"884\" data-file-width=\"1440\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"246\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1b/Newmaple.jpg/400px-Newmaple.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1b/Newmaple.jpg/600px-Newmaple.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1b/Newmaple.jpg/800px-Newmaple.jpg 2x\" width=\"400\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Newmaple.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>A maple tree forest.</div></div></div>\n<p>Maple trees are useful trees that yield <a href=\"/index.php/Wood\" title=\"Wood\">wood</a> as well as the seasonal production of <a href=\"/index.php/Maple_sap\" title=\"Maple sap\">maple sap</a>. \n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h1>\n<ul><li>When in their harvesting <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>, maple sap can be harvested using a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_bucket\" title=\"Small bucket\">small bucket</a>. Maple sap is then used to make maple syrup.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">Arrow shafts</a> made from maplewood take less damage than those made from other wood types.</li></ul>', 0),
(16721, 3546, 'Description', 'Description', 'Wine is a beverage made from maple syrup and grape juice. It is stored in a wine barrel to age over time. Blue grapes make red wine Green grapes make white wine.', '<p>Wine is a <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverage</a> made from maple syrup and grape juice. It is stored in a wine barrel to age over time.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Blue <a href=\"/index.php/Grapes\" title=\"Grapes\">grapes</a> make red wine</li>\n<li>Green <a href=\"/index.php/Grapes\" title=\"Grapes\">grapes</a> make white wine.</li></ul>', 0),
(16722, 3546, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Creating unfermented wine uses an equal amount of grape juice and maple syrup. The unfermented wine must then be placed in a wine barrel , and the barrel sealed with a wood scrap . The wine will then ferment over time. To seal the barrel, first activate the wood scrap , right click the wine barrel , and select Create -> Drink -> fermenting (white/red) wine Using a fruit tree wood scrap will result in vinegar instead of wine. Unlike most other items, wine quality goes up over time, as long as it stays in a sealed small barrel or wine barrel , although a wine barrel produces the best results.', '<ul><li>Creating unfermented wine uses an equal amount of grape juice and maple syrup.</li>\n<li>The unfermented wine must then be placed in a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wine_barrel\" title=\"Wine barrel\">wine barrel</a>, and the barrel sealed with a <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">wood scrap</a>. The wine will then ferment over time.\n<ul><li>To seal the barrel, first activate the <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">wood scrap</a>, right click the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wine_barrel\" title=\"Wine barrel\">wine barrel</a>, and select <b>Create</b> -&gt; <b>Drink</b> -&gt; <b>fermenting (white/red) wine</b></li>\n<li>Using a fruit tree wood scrap will result in vinegar instead of wine.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>Unlike most other items, wine <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> goes up over time, as long as it stays in a sealed <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">small barrel</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wine_barrel\" title=\"Wine barrel\">wine barrel</a>, although a wine barrel produces the best results.\n</p>', 1),
(16723, 3546, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Wine increases stamina and reduces thirst , with the effect multiplying in higher quality wine. Wine will also give a temporary random skill affinity , with the duration varying depending on quality and amount drank.', '<p>Wine increases <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stamina\" title=\"Stamina\">stamina</a> and reduces <a href=\"/index.php/Thirst\" title=\"Thirst\">thirst</a>, with the effect multiplying in higher quality wine.\n</p>\n<p>Wine will also give a temporary random skill <a href=\"/index.php/Affinity\" title=\"Affinity\">affinity</a>, with the duration varying depending on quality and amount drank.\n</p>', 2),
(16724, 3546, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wine is created in the container that the grape juice is in. If the total amount is greater than the container\'s volume, the extra wine will spill. Fermentation time is approximately 5-7 real days. After fermentation is complete, you may either leave it sealed with the woodscrap, or unseal the fermented wine barrel, and reseal with a peg for the aging process. Wood scrap is only necessary for fermentation. Food affinity for the wine will depend on wood type of the wood scrap used to seal. Fruit trees make vinegar. Wine will age better inside a building than outside (ie: where other items would have minimized decay, wine ages better). Best aging method known for wine is storing it in a oak wine barrel in a underground building on deed. Please note that a barrel of wine will not count for your achievements if you are offline or on another server when the fermentation finishes.', '<ul><li>Wine is created in the container that the grape juice is in. If the total amount is greater than the container\'s volume, the extra wine will spill.</li>\n<li>Fermentation time is approximately 5-7 real days.</li>\n<li>After fermentation is complete, you may either leave it sealed with the woodscrap, or unseal the fermented wine barrel, and reseal with a peg for the aging process. Wood scrap is only necessary for fermentation.</li>\n<li>Food affinity for the wine will depend on wood type of the wood scrap used to seal. Fruit trees make vinegar.</li>\n<li>Wine will age better inside a building than outside (ie: where other items would have minimized decay, wine ages better).</li>\n<li>Best aging method known for wine is storing it in a oak wine barrel in a underground building on deed.</li>\n<li>Please note that a barrel of wine will not count for your <a href=\"/index.php/Achievements\" title=\"Achievements\">achievements</a> if you are offline or on another server when the fermentation finishes.</li></ul>', 3),
(16725, 3546, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Alcohol', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Alcohol\" title=\"Alcohol\">Alcohol</a></li></ul>', 4),
(16743, 4299, 'Description', 'Description', 'A short but sturdy axe with a thick blade specially designed to cut down trees with but poor in combat.', '<p><i>A short but sturdy axe with a thick blade specially designed to cut down trees with but poor in combat.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16744, 4299, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Bearded Hatchet', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Bearded Hatchet</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16745, 4299, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'QL of shaft affects % chance to create. This item is a standard newbie tool. The newbie hatchet is made from birchwood, is not improvable, and will burn if put in any kind of fire ; take care as to not accidentally lose it in this way. Hatchets used to weigh 1.5 kg before the fight fix in late 2007. Hatchet is a small axe specifically made for woodcutting , and is much better at this task than any other type of axe. It is a poor weapon for fighting , however. The hatchet and saw are the only tools that give tool skill above 20 when cutting down trees with it. Other tool and weapon skills cannot be improved this way beyond 20; after that using them for cutting wood only gives woodcutting skill. Each tool comes with a skill based on the item itself. This skill effects how well you can use a hatchet. Higher skill improves the chance of getting higher quality trees or logs, although the maximum quality is determined by your woodcutting skill.', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> affects % chance to create.</li>\n<li>This item is a standard newbie tool. The newbie hatchet is made from birchwood, is not improvable, and will burn if put in any kind of <a href=\"/index.php/Fire\" title=\"Fire\">fire</a>; take care as to not accidentally lose it in this way.</li>\n<li>Hatchets used to weigh 1.5 kg before the fight fix in late 2007.</li>\n<li>Hatchet is a small <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Axes\" title=\"Category:Axes\">axe</a> specifically made for <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">woodcutting</a>, and is much better at this task than any other type of axe. It is a poor weapon for <a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">fighting</a>, however.</li>\n<li>The hatchet and <a href=\"/index.php/Saw\" title=\"Saw\">saw</a> are the only tools that give tool skill above 20 when cutting down trees with it. Other tool and weapon skills cannot be improved this way beyond 20; after that using them for cutting wood only gives woodcutting skill.</li>\n<li>Each tool comes with a skill based on the item itself. This skill effects how well you can use a hatchet. Higher skill improves the chance of getting higher quality trees or logs, although the maximum quality is determined by your woodcutting skill.</li></ul>', 2),
(16746, 4299, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a hatchet Miscellaneous items > Hatchet When creating a hatchet Smithing > Blacksmithing', '<p>When using a hatchet\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Hatchet</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a hatchet\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16747, 4299, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Woodsman at 50 skill Hewer at 70 skill Tomahawk at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Woodsman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Hewer at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Tomahawk at 90 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(16748, 4300, 'Description', 'Description', 'A green-brown watery liquid with a slightly smoky scent.', '<p><i>A green-brown watery liquid with a slightly smoky scent.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16749, 4300, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Tea is a liquid beverage that can be brewed using camellia , herbs or tea leaves.', '<p><b>Tea</b> is a <a href=\"/index.php/Liquid\" title=\"Liquid\">liquid</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Beverage\" title=\"Beverage\">beverage</a> that can be brewed using <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Camellia\" title=\"Camellia\">camellia</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Herbs\" title=\"Herbs\">herbs</a> or tea leaves.\n</p>', 1),
(16750, 4300, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Tea is a drink that contains caffeine . It can be used to increase your skill gains while using sleep bonus . The maximum caffeine effect is 100 which yields a 2x sleep bonus rate.', '<ul><li>Tea is a drink that contains <a href=\"/index.php/Caffeine\" title=\"Caffeine\">caffeine</a>.</li>\n<li>It can be used to increase your skill gains while using <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a>.</li>\n<li>The maximum <a href=\"/index.php/Caffeine\" title=\"Caffeine\">caffeine</a> effect is 100 which yields a 2x <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a> rate.</li></ul>', 2),
(16751, 4300, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The Camellia , herb or tea leaves QL and the beverages skill affect the QL of the tea made.', '<p>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Camellia\" title=\"Camellia\">Camellia</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">herb</a> or tea leaves <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> and the <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a> skill affect the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the tea made.\n</p>', 3),
(16752, 4300, 'Tools required', 'Tools_required', 'campfire , stone oven , Pottery bowl , teapot or cauldron', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_oven\" title=\"Stone oven\">stone oven</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">Pottery bowl</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Teapot\" title=\"Teapot\">teapot</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Cauldron\" title=\"Cauldron\">cauldron</a></li></ul>', 4),
(16753, 4300, 'Notes', 'Notes_2', 'If it\'s low quality (10ql or less), it will not be drinkable at all.', '<ul><li>If it\'s low quality (10ql or less), it will not be drinkable at all.</li></ul>', 5),
(16761, 4303, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge dark bowl with three feet and a metal hanger. A Cauldron is used to cook ingredients in.', '<p><i>A huge dark bowl with three feet and a metal hanger.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>Cauldron</b> is used to <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cook</a> ingredients in.\n</p>', 0),
(16762, 4303, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Place ingredients in the cauldron by dragging and dropping them. The cauldron acts as a container, holding items inside. To find out if the ingredients will create something, right-click on the cauldron and select Lore .', '<p>Place ingredients in the cauldron by dragging and dropping them. The cauldron acts as a container, holding items inside. To find out if the ingredients will create something, right-click on the cauldron and select <i>Lore</i>. \n</p>', 1),
(16763, 4303, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Holds up to 64 kg of liquid. The higher the quality, the quicker it heats up. The QL also affects the chance to get the maximum quality (capped by hot food cooking skill) of the food cooked in it.', '<ul><li>Holds up to 64 kg of liquid.</li>\n<li>The higher the quality, the quicker it <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Heat\" title=\"Heat\">heats</a> up.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> also affects the chance to get the maximum quality (capped by <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">hot food cooking</a> skill) of the <a href=\"/index.php/Food\" title=\"Food\">food</a> cooked in it.</li></ul>', 2),
(16764, 4303, 'Tips', 'Tips', 'Put metal scraps , lumps , or other small items in a cauldron to make more space in a forge .', '<ul><li>Put <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal_scrap\" title=\"Metal scrap\">metal scraps</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lumps\" title=\"Lumps\">lumps</a>, or other small items in a cauldron to make more space in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(16765, 4303, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Cooking utensils', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cooking_utensils\" title=\"Cooking utensils\">Cooking utensils</a></li></ul>', 4),
(16784, 2974, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sturdy bow that will fire pretty far with good accuracy.', '<p><i>A sturdy bow that will fire pretty far with good accuracy.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16785, 2974, 'Shooting', 'Shooting', 'This weapon is best used at 10 tiles range, or 40m when looking through a spyglass . It requires a minimum range of 5 tiles. Higher skill in this weapon gives more shooting options when used. Bows must be wielded in your hands to be fired. Bows are two handed weapons, and cannot be equipped unless both hands are empty and you aren\'t wearing a shield. See the archery page for more.', '<p>This weapon is best used at 10 tiles range, or 40m when looking through a <a href=\"/index.php/Spyglass\" title=\"Spyglass\">spyglass</a>. It requires a minimum range of 5 tiles. Higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> in this weapon gives more shooting options when used. \n</p>\n<p>Bows must be wielded in your hands to be fired. Bows are two handed weapons, and cannot be equipped unless both hands are empty and you aren\'t wearing a shield.\n</p>\n<p>See the <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a> page for more.\n</p>', 1),
(16786, 2974, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A bow is best made out of willow logs. Examining it will then say, \" The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility. \" Stringing with a bow string is needed to make the bow functional. Before that, examining it will say: \" An unstringed sturdy bow. \"  A bow must be unstrung in order to improve it. A reflex bow is best made out of willow logs. Examining it will then say, \"The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility.\" Iron bows exist in the game. These were a reward from a special historical event and are quite rare. They cannot be crafted. They look like regular wooden bows. Reflex Bow deals more damage than a Shortbow but less than a Longbow.', '<ul><li>A bow is best made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Willow\" title=\"Willow\">willow</a> logs. Examining it will then say, \"<i>The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility.</i>\"</li>\n<li>Stringing with a <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow string</a> is needed to make the bow functional. Before that, examining it will say: \"<i>An unstringed sturdy bow.</i>\"  A bow must be unstrung in order to improve it.</li>\n<li>A reflex bow is best made out of willow logs. Examining it will then say, \"The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility.\"</li>\n<li>Iron bows exist in the game. These were a reward from a special historical event and are quite rare. They cannot be crafted. They look like regular wooden bows.</li>\n<li>Reflex Bow deals more damage than a Shortbow but less than a Longbow.</li></ul>', 2),
(16787, 2974, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Agile Bow', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Agile Bow</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16788, 2974, 'Storage', 'Storage', 'Can be stored in a bow rack or in a regular large chest .', '<p>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_rack\" title=\"Bow rack\">bow rack</a> or in a regular <a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">large chest</a>.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(16789, 2974, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a bow Archery > Reflex bow Body > Body control When creating a bow Carpentry > Bowyery', '<p>When using a bow\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a> &gt; Reflex bow</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a bow\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Bowyery\" title=\"Bowyery\">Bowyery</a></li></ul>', 5),
(16790, 2974, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Bowman at 50 skill Skirmisher at 70 skill Ranger at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Bowman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Skirmisher at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Ranger at 90 skill</li></ul>', 6),
(16791, 2974, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Short bow Long bow', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_bow\" title=\"Short bow\">Short bow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_bow\" title=\"Long bow\">Long bow</a></li></ul>', 7),
(16815, 4314, 'Description', 'Description', 'Fletching is the skill used in the creation and improving of arrows .', '<p><b>Fletching</b> is the skill used in the creation and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Improving\" title=\"Improving\">improving</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Arrow\" title=\"Arrow\">arrows</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16816, 4314, 'Items', 'Items', 'Arrow shaft Arrows Hunting arrow War arrow Ballista dart', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">Arrow shaft</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Arrows\" title=\"Category:Arrows\">Arrows</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">Hunting arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">War arrow</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ballista_dart\" title=\"Ballista dart\">Ballista dart</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16817, 4314, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Top creation quality of an arrow can be calculated as (Fletching / 5). The items required for improving an arrow include: Carving knife , Mallet , File , Pelt , and Log . Hunting arrow are easy to make, but less used later. While improving individual arrows is efficient for leveling Fletchery, prioritize placing arrows in an arrow bundle first. This allows mass-improvement.', '<ul><li>Top creation quality of an arrow can be calculated as (Fletching / 5).</li>\n<li>The items required for improving an arrow include: <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">Carving knife</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">Mallet</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/File\" title=\"File\">File</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelt</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">Log</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">Hunting arrow</a> are easy to make, but less used later.</li>\n<li>While improving individual arrows is efficient for leveling Fletchery, prioritize placing arrows in an <a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_bundle\" title=\"Arrow bundle\">arrow bundle</a> first. This allows mass-improvement.</li></ul>', 2),
(16818, 4314, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Carpentry > Fletching Body > Body control Mind > Mind logic', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; Fletching</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16819, 4314, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Fletcher at 50 skill Arrowmaker at 70 skill Master Fletcher at 90 skill Quivering with Excitement at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Fletcher at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Arrowmaker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Fletcher at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Quivering with Excitement at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(16820, 4315, 'Description', 'Description', 'Bowyery is the skill in creating bows . Creating the arrows for bows is fletching . Bows are best made out of willow . The quality of the bow has an impact on the amount of damage done.', '<p><b>Bowyery</b> is the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> in creating <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bows\" title=\"Bows\">bows</a>. Creating the <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Arrows\" title=\"Category:Arrows\">arrows</a> for bows is <a href=\"/index.php/Fletching\" title=\"Fletching\">fletching</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Bows are best made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Willow\" title=\"Willow\">willow</a>. The quality of the bow has an impact on the amount of damage done.\n</p>', 0),
(16821, 4315, 'Items', 'Items', 'Long bow Reflex bow Short bow', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_bow\" title=\"Long bow\">Long bow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Reflex_bow\" title=\"Reflex bow\">Reflex bow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_bow\" title=\"Short bow\">Short bow</a></li></ul>', 1),
(16822, 4315, 'Skillgain Tips', 'Skillgain_Tips', 'At least one player has found the best way to grind bowery skill is to create 10 to 20 of a certain type of bow. There does not seem to be a skill difference between improving a normal bow or a short bow, so going with a short bow is easier, as it takes less skill to make. Once many bows have been made, improve them all to 10 QL , and then increase them all to 10+ bowery skill. You will quickly get to a point where you need to make more bows to imp, so always have some new ones handy. A toolbelt is VERY handy to have around. Fill bow rack first to streamline organization and efficiency. With two fully stocked bow racks, you can reach Bowyering level 50+ without making additional bows. Prioritize future-use bows types during selection, as with you are luck any achieving rare quality or higher.', '<p>At least one <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> has found the best way to grind bowery skill is to create 10 to 20 of a certain type of bow. There does not seem to be a skill difference between <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Improving\" title=\"Improving\">improving</a> a normal bow or a short bow, so going with a short bow is easier, as it takes less skill to make.\n</p>\n<p>Once many bows have been made, improve them all to 10<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a>, and then increase them all to 10+ bowery skill. You will quickly get to a point where you need to make more bows to imp, so always have some new ones handy. A <a href=\"/index.php/Toolbelt\" title=\"Toolbelt\">toolbelt</a> is VERY handy to have around.\n</p>\n<p>Fill <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_rack\" title=\"Bow rack\">bow rack</a> first to streamline organization and efficiency. With two fully stocked bow racks, you can reach Bowyering level 50+ without making additional bows. Prioritize future-use bows types during selection, as with you are luck any achieving <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rare\" title=\"Rare\">rare</a> quality or higher.\n</p>', 2),
(16823, 4315, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Carpentry > Bowyery Body > Body control Mind > Mind logic', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; Bowyery</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16824, 4315, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Bowmaker at 50 skill Able Bowmaker at 70 skill Master Bowmaker at 90 skill Bow Down at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Bowmaker at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Able Bowmaker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Bowmaker at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Bow Down at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(16825, 4315, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Bows Archery Carpentry Bowyery Fine carpentry Fletching Ship building Toy making', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Category:Bows\" title=\"Category:Bows\">Category:Bows</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Bowyery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">Fine carpentry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fletching\" title=\"Fletching\">Fletching</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ship_building\" title=\"Ship building\">Ship building</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Toy_making\" title=\"Toy making\">Toy making</a></li></ul></li></ul>', 5),
(16826, 4316, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wooden practice target made from planks and logs with a few circles around the bulls eye. An archery target is a board with numbered circles around a central bull\'s-eye, used for practicing archery and bow skills. It will score hits ranging from a measly 0 to a perfect 10.', '<p><i>A wooden practice target made from planks and logs with a few circles around the bulls eye.</i>\n</p>\n<p>An <b>archery target</b> is a board with numbered circles around a central bull\'s-eye, used for practicing <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bowyery_items\" title=\"Category:Bowyery items\">bow</a> skills. It will score hits ranging from a measly 0 to a perfect 10.\n</p>', 0),
(16827, 4316, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Training archery and bow skills.', '<ul><li>Training <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bowyery_items\" title=\"Category:Bowyery items\">bow</a> skills.</li></ul>', 1),
(16828, 4316, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'With an archery target, you can only gain archery skill up to 45. Upon reaching 45 archery skill, you won\'t gain any characteristics either. Individual bow skills have a maximum of 30, while shooting at an archery target. This is not limited to the main archery skill hitting the limit of 45. Drops from inventory upon completion. Can not be picked up. Arrows fired at the archery target will be on the same tile and can be retrieved if they do not break. Far less damage is imposed to the target if shot with arrow shafts instead of complete arrows. Can be loaded into large cart or wagon if the prerequisite of 23 body strength is met.', '<ul><li>With an archery target, you can only gain <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a> skill up to 45. Upon reaching 45 archery skill, you won\'t gain any characteristics either.</li>\n<li>Individual bow skills have a maximum of 30, while shooting at an archery target. This is not limited to the main archery skill hitting the limit of 45.</li>\n<li>Drops from inventory upon completion.</li>\n<li>Can not be picked up.</li>\n<li>Arrows fired at the archery target will be on the same tile and can be retrieved if they do not break.</li>\n<li>Far less damage is imposed to the target if shot with arrow shafts instead of complete arrows.</li>\n<li>Can be loaded into <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a> if the prerequisite of 23 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> is met.</li></ul>', 2),
(16831, 4318, 'Description', 'Description', 'The skill used in making ropes and bow strings using a rope tool and wemp fibre .', '<p>The <a href=\"/index.php/Skills\" title=\"Skills\">skill</a> used in making <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">ropes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow strings</a> using a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope_tool\" title=\"Rope tool\">rope tool</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a>. \n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16832, 4318, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the rope tool affects success chances when creating A high skill will raise the chance of getting maximum quality items The maximum quality is equal to the wemp fibre \'s effective quality As a regular player, the best way to grind ropemaking is to improve net traps , which uses a cloth tailoring tool set. As a priest, an excellent way to train ropemaking is to make bow strings , which only consume about 0.013kg of the wemp fibre .', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the rope tool affects success chances when creating</li>\n<li>A high skill will raise the chance of getting maximum <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> items</li>\n<li>The maximum quality is equal to the <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a>\'s effective quality</li>\n<li>As a regular player, the best way to grind ropemaking is to improve <a href=\"/index.php/Net_trap\" title=\"Net trap\">net traps</a>, which uses a <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> tool set.</li>\n<li>As a priest, an excellent way to train ropemaking is to make <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow strings</a>, which only consume about 0.013kg of the <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16833, 4318, 'Ropemaking Items', 'Ropemaking_Items', 'See Category:Ropemaking items', '<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Ropemaking_items\" title=\"Category:Ropemaking items\">Category:Ropemaking items</a>\n</p>', 2),
(16834, 4318, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Ropemaking Mind > Mind logic', '<ul><li>Ropemaking</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16835, 4318, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Ropemaker at 50 skill Renowned Ropemaker at 70 skill Hangman at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Ropemaker at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Renowned Ropemaker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Hangman at 90 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(16836, 4319, 'Description', 'Description', 'A quiver sown from leather, designed to be hanging across your back or from your hips.', '<p><i>A quiver sown from leather, designed to be hanging across your back or from your hips.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16837, 4319, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A quiver is a container that holds up to 41 arrows and is worn on your back or hips.', '<p>A <b>quiver</b> is a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Containers\" title=\"Category:Containers\">container</a> that holds up to 41 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arrows\" title=\"Arrows\">arrows</a> and is worn on your <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">back</a> or hips.\n</p>', 1),
(16838, 4319, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When shown on the player model, the quiver will not show arrows inside, even if the quiver does contain arrows.', '<p>When shown on the player model, the quiver will not show arrows inside, even if the quiver does contain arrows.\n</p>', 2),
(16839, 4319, 'Gallery', 'Gallery', '', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:43px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg\"><img alt=\"Wurmpedia Quiver Legs.jpg\" data-file-height=\"489\" data-file-width=\"472\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"124\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg/120px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg/180px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/7/77/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg/240px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Legs.jpg 2x\" width=\"120\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:31px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg\"><img alt=\"Wurmpedia Quiver Torso.jpg\" data-file-height=\"677\" data-file-width=\"550\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"148\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d3/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg/120px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d3/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg/180px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/d3/Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg/240px-Wurmpedia_Quiver_Torso.jpg 2x\" width=\"120\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 3),
(16840, 4320, 'Description', 'Description', 'Rough and clumsy, but pretty sharp scissors.', '<p><i>Rough and clumsy, but pretty sharp scissors.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16841, 4320, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Scissors are used in finishing and improving cloth tailoring items. Also used to turn short grass into lawn tiles. Used to shear sheep The quality of the active scissor blade affects the chance of creation success. The metal type of the passive (not activated) scissor blade determines the metal type of the finished product. The rarity of the selected (activated) scissor blade determines the rarity of the finished product.', '<ul><li><b>Scissors</b> are used in finishing and improving <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> items.</li>\n<li>Also used to turn short grass into <a href=\"/index.php/Lawn\" title=\"Lawn\">lawn</a> tiles.</li>\n<li>Used to shear <a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">sheep</a></li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the active scissor blade affects the chance of creation success.</li>\n<li>The metal type of the passive (not activated) scissor blade determines the metal type of the finished product.</li>\n<li>The rarity of the selected (activated) scissor blade determines the rarity of the finished product.</li></ul>', 1),
(16870, 4323, 'Description', 'Description', 'A spell of Magranon given to priests at level 39 faith even though the spell requires 40 favor .', '<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> given to <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> at level 39 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> even though the spell requires 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(16871, 4323, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Dominate works almost like taming , but has a lower rate of failure (based primarily on channeling skill and with a bonus provided by soul strength ). It can be used to dominate monsters without food as opposed to taming . The only creatures noted to be successfully dominated without the Crown of might are trolls , goblins , scorpions , hell scorpious , and lava fiends . Casting Dominate will not be interrupted by combat, even if the creature hits the casting player. Dominate lasts approximately 72 hours. When a creature is dominated, it will have a loyalty of 50. Pet will go offline when dominator logs off. Dominated creatures lose loyalty when hurt, like tamed creatures. The more powerful the creature the easier it becomes aggravated. You can take a huge shod club from a dominated troll inventory but cannot put it back on.', '<ul><li>Dominate works almost like <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">taming</a>, but has a lower rate of failure (based primarily on <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill and with a bonus provided by <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_strength\" title=\"Soul strength\">soul strength</a>). It can be used to dominate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Monster\" title=\"Monster\">monsters</a> without <a href=\"/index.php/Food\" title=\"Food\">food</a> as opposed to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">taming</a>.</li>\n<li>The only creatures noted to be successfully dominated without the <a href=\"/index.php/Crown_of_might\" title=\"Crown of might\">Crown of might</a> are <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Goblin\" title=\"Goblin\">goblins</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Scorpion\" title=\"Scorpion\">scorpions</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_scorpious\" title=\"Hell scorpious\">hell scorpious</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Lava_fiend\" title=\"Lava fiend\">lava fiends</a>.</li>\n<li>Casting Dominate will not be interrupted by combat, even if the creature hits the casting player.</li>\n<li>Dominate lasts approximately 72 hours.</li>\n<li>When a creature is dominated, it will have a loyalty of 50.</li>\n<li>Pet will go offline when dominator logs off.</li>\n<li>Dominated creatures lose loyalty when hurt, like tamed creatures. The more powerful the creature the easier it becomes aggravated.</li>\n<li>You can take a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">huge shod club</a> from a dominated <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">troll</a> inventory but cannot put it back on.</li></ul>', 1),
(16872, 4324, 'Description', 'Description', 'Decay is the erosion of objects over time in the form of gradually increasing damage . The decay rate depends on the item type, where the item is stored, the item\'s quality , and sometimes the item\'s material. Logs , stone shards or dirt for example will completely decay within days while other items may even last months and years. Items made from cedarwood decay slower. Damage from decay and other sources is displayed in the DMG column. Damage is also done to items from being used or failing an improvement attempt. There are various ways to reduce decay.', '<p><b>Decay</b> is the erosion of objects over time in the form of gradually increasing <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a>. The decay rate depends on the item type, where the item is stored, the item\'s <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>, and sometimes the item\'s material. <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">Logs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> for example will completely decay within days while other items may even last months and years. Items made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedarwood</a> decay slower.\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">Damage</a> from decay and other sources is displayed in the DMG column. Damage is also done to items from being used or failing an improvement attempt.\n</p>\n<p>There are various ways to reduce decay.\n</p>', 0),
(16873, 4324, 'Item decay modifiers', 'Item_decay_modifiers', 'Kingdom Kingdoms reduce wall decay by 2x. Non-kingdom zones have no reduced decay. Deeds Deeds decrease decay on walls of any kind by 10x, if the upkeep is higher than 7 days . Deeds stop the decay on walls of any kind if the upkeep is higher than 30 days. Deeds also stop decay on lamps, flags, and banners Houses Houses reduce item decay by 2x? Possibly 3x?. Some evidence that wood is 2x, and stone is 3x ... more testing needed. Containers Containers will reduce decay by 2x. Containers in houses might get both bonus. (Testing required) Bulk Storage Containers Bulk storage containers like Small and Large Crates , Bulk storage bins , Food storage bins , Bulk container units and Large pantry cupboards will prevent decay entirely, however, if they are not stored on a deed with at least 30 days of upkeep remaining then they will lose 5% of their contents every 28 days. Other Items made out of cedar wood decay slower (they have reduced decay tick frequency). Items with normal QL based decay that are made out of Oak or Steel will suffer 20% reduced damage per decay tick. Raw materials ( clay , dirt , logs , stone shards , meat etc) decay faster than finished materials ( weapons , tools , etc.) There is a 2-day period of no decay after a wall is finished. Items do not decay in inventories or on merchants (note that merchants can be threatened on Elevation ), with the exception of food items, lanterns, construction markers, torches, and huge shod clubs. Houses that are abandoned get greatly increased decay. A house is considered abandoned when the owner does not log in to the same server for more than 3 months (real life). An abandoned house within a perimeter will sustain an additional damage bonus. The decay rates for abandoned houses are currently unknown. Note: This calculation is server specific. If you have a building on a server that you do not visit for more than 3 months it will be treated as abandoned. For non-abandoned houses that are off deed the decay rate is (perish-ability/QL) total damage per decay tick. A stone house \'s walls/windows/doors perish-ability is 3, making its average decay per tick (3/wall QL). A wooden house \'s walls/windows/doors perish-ability is 10, making its average decay per tick (10/wall QL). Perimeter is treated the same with wilderness, thus do not reduce decay. Nor does it increase decay unless the owner of the structure has been away from the server for more than three months. At which time the building will begin to accumulate increased perimeter decay. This occurs in addition to the “abandoned” status decay increase.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kingdom\">Kingdom</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom\" title=\"Kingdom\">Kingdoms</a> reduce wall decay by 2x.</li>\n<li>Non-kingdom zones have no reduced decay.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Deeds\">Deeds</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">Deeds</a> decrease decay on <a href=\"/index.php/Wall\" title=\"Wall\">walls</a> of any kind by 10x, if the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Upkeep\" title=\"Upkeep\">upkeep</a> is higher than 7 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Day\" title=\"Day\">days</a>.</li>\n<li>Deeds stop the decay on walls of any kind if the upkeep is higher than 30 days.</li>\n<li>Deeds also stop decay on lamps, flags, and banners</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Houses\">Houses</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Houses reduce item decay by 2x? Possibly 3x?.   <i>Some evidence that wood is 2x, and stone is 3x ... more testing needed.</i></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Containers\">Containers</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">Containers</a> will reduce decay by 2x.</li>\n<li>Containers in houses might get both bonus. (Testing required)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bulk_Storage_Containers\">Bulk Storage Containers</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Bulk storage containers like Small and Large <a href=\"/index.php/Crate\" title=\"Crate\">Crates</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bins</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">Food storage bins</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_container_unit\" title=\"Bulk container unit\">Bulk container units</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Large_pantry_cupboard\" title=\"Large pantry cupboard\">Large pantry cupboards</a> will prevent decay entirely, however, if they are not stored on a deed with at least 30 days of upkeep remaining then they will lose 5% of their contents every 28 days.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other\">Other</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Items made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> wood decay slower (they have reduced decay tick frequency).</li>\n<li>Items with normal QL based decay that are made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">Oak</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Steel\" title=\"Steel\">Steel</a> will suffer 20% reduced damage per decay tick.</li>\n<li>Raw materials (<a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a>,<a href=\"/index.php/Meat\" title=\"Meat\">meat</a> etc) decay faster than finished materials (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Weapon\" title=\"Weapon\">weapons</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tool\" title=\"Tool\">tools</a>, etc.)</li>\n<li>There is a 2-day period of no decay after a wall is finished.</li>\n<li>Items do not decay in inventories or on merchants (note that merchants can be threatened on <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>), with the exception of food items, lanterns, construction markers, torches, and huge shod clubs.</li>\n<li>Houses that are abandoned get greatly increased decay. A house is considered abandoned when the owner does not log in to the same server for more than 3 months (real life). An abandoned house within a perimeter will sustain an additional damage bonus. The decay rates for abandoned houses are currently unknown.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><b>Note:</b> This calculation is server specific. If you have a building on a server that you do not visit for more than 3 months it will be treated as abandoned.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>For non-abandoned houses that are off deed the decay rate is (perish-ability/QL) total damage per decay tick.</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">stone house</a>\'s walls/windows/doors perish-ability is 3, making its average decay per tick (3/wall QL).</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">wooden house</a>\'s walls/windows/doors perish-ability is 10, making its average decay per tick (10/wall QL).</li>\n<li>Perimeter is treated the same with wilderness, thus do not reduce decay.\n<ul><li>Nor does it increase decay unless the owner of the structure has been away from the server for more than three months. At which time the building will begin to accumulate increased perimeter decay. This occurs in addition to the “abandoned” status decay increase.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(16874, 4324, 'Myths', 'Myths', 'Stacking a container inside another container does NOT improve the bonus Containers in the inventory do not modify the decay rate of their contents at all. Bless has no effect on decay. Its only use is to activate metal altars and to enchant planted lamps to stay lit on paved tiles. Wooden fences do not decay faster than stone fences (see: [1] ).', '<ul><li>Stacking a container inside another container does NOT improve the bonus</li>\n<li>Containers in the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> do not modify the decay rate of their contents at all.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bless\" title=\"Bless\">Bless</a> has no effect on decay. Its only use is to activate metal altars and to enchant planted <a href=\"/index.php/Lamp\" title=\"Lamp\">lamps</a> to stay lit on paved tiles.</li>\n<li>Wooden fences do not decay faster than stone fences (see: <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a>).</li></ul>', 2),
(16875, 4324, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'An item in a container, in a house, in kingdom territory probably multiplies the bonus, but this needs verifying. It is possible for items to \"miss\" their decay ticks for some period of time, and then experience \"catch up\" decay that can result in the destruction of very low ql items. Some items will actually give a local event notice when they completely decay to loss. [17:52:34] A stone shards crumbles to dust.', '<ul><li>An item in a container, in a house, in kingdom territory probably multiplies the bonus, but this needs verifying.</li>\n<li>It is possible for items to \"miss\" their decay ticks for some period of time, and then experience \"catch up\" decay that can result in the destruction of very low ql items.</li>\n<li>Some items will actually give a local event notice when they completely decay to loss. <i>[17:52:34] A stone shards crumbles to dust.</i></li></ul>', 3),
(16876, 4324, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Damage Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">Damage</a>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a>\n</p>', 4),
(16877, 3212, 'Description', 'Description', 'Cedar is a tree that is fabled for its valuable properties. Cedarwood items are known to decay slower. Notes Arrows with arrow shafts made from cedarwood are significantly easier to improve. Very old cedar trees are the tallest trees in the lands of Wurm.', '<p>Cedar is a tree that is fabled for its valuable properties. Cedarwood items are known to <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> slower.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h1>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arrows\" title=\"Arrows\">Arrows</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">arrow shafts</a> made from cedarwood are significantly easier to improve.</li>\n<li>Very old cedar trees are the tallest trees in the lands of Wurm.</li></ul>', 0),
(16878, 3681, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bright, long-blooming camellia flower.', '<p><i>A bright, long-blooming camellia flower.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16879, 3681, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be botanized on Wildflowers nodes. Used to make tea . Can be used in alchemy to make healing covers (healing potency 3). Grows to a medium height', '<ul><li>Can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Botanize\" title=\"Botanize\">botanized</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> nodes.</li>\n<li>Used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Tea\" title=\"Tea\">tea</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> (healing potency 3).</li>\n<li>Grows to a medium height</li></ul>', 1),
(16880, 3681, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Herbs', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Herbs\" title=\"Herbs\">Herbs</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16881, 2684, 'Description', 'Description', 'A Thorn bush This is a very large bush with sharp thorns. It cannot be harvested and is mainly used as a primitive defense against invaders.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:402px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Thorn_bush.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"400\" data-file-width=\"475\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"337\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/41/Thorn_bush.png/400px-Thorn_bush.png\" srcset=\"/images/4/41/Thorn_bush.png 1.5x\" width=\"400\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Thorn_bush.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>A Thorn bush</div></div></div>\n<p>This is a very large bush with sharp thorns. It cannot be harvested and is mainly used as a primitive defense against invaders.\n</p>', 0),
(16882, 2684, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Approximately one week after a thorn bush reaches old age, its thorns will cause cutting wounds to players on the same tile. Players with at least 40 faith in Fo will not be harmed by thorns. The Fo spell, Morning fog , also provides some protection. Enchanted thorn bushes do not inflict damage. Axes deal 50% less damage to these bushes than other bushes and trees. Thorns do not hurt passive or aggressive creatures.', '<ul><li>Approximately one week after a thorn bush reaches old age, its thorns will cause cutting <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wounds</a> to players on the same tile.</li>\n<li>Players with at least 40 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> in <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> will not be harmed by thorns. The Fo spell, <a href=\"/index.php/Morning_fog\" title=\"Morning fog\">Morning fog</a>, also provides some protection.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Enchanted_tree\" title=\"Enchanted tree\">Enchanted</a> thorn bushes do not inflict damage.</li>\n<li>Axes deal 50% less damage to these bushes than other bushes and trees.</li>\n<li>Thorns do not hurt passive or aggressive creatures.</li></ul>', 1),
(16907, 2677, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small bush with green leaves. A Grape bush', '<p>A small bush with green leaves. \n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Grape_bush.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"400\" data-file-width=\"406\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"296\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/0b/Grape_bush.png/300px-Grape_bush.png\" srcset=\"/images/0/0b/Grape_bush.png 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Grape_bush.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>A Grape bush</div></div></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(16908, 2677, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Grape bushes in the northern half of a map will provide green grapes, while ones in the southern half will provide blue grapes. When the bush is in season, you will see this message when examining: The bush has some juicy green grapes. in the northern part of the server and The bush has some juicy blue grapes. in the southern part of the server. You can find grapewood sprouts by picking them with a sickle from grape bushes or grape trellises. Grapes can be used to make wine and grape juice. They are also used in some cooking recipes.', '<ul><li>Grape bushes in the northern half of a map will provide green grapes, while ones in the southern half will provide blue grapes.</li>\n<li>When the bush is in season, you will see this message when examining: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The bush has some juicy green grapes.  </span> in the northern part of the server and <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The bush has some juicy blue grapes.  </span> in the southern part of the server.</li>\n<li>You can find grapewood <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a> by picking them with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> from grape bushes or grape trellises.</li>\n<li>Grapes can be used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Wine\" title=\"Wine\">wine</a> and grape juice. They are also used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li></ul>', 1),
(16909, 2677, 'Images', 'Images', 'Green grape bush in season Blue grape bush in season', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 183.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 183.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 181.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green_grapes_fruit.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"816\" data-file-width=\"739\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/40/Green_grapes_fruit.png/272px-Green_grapes_fruit.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/40/Green_grapes_fruit.png/407px-Green_grapes_fruit.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/40/Green_grapes_fruit.png/543px-Green_grapes_fruit.png 2x\" width=\"182\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 162px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Green grape bush in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 173.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 173.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 171.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Blue_grapes_fruit.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"666\" data-file-width=\"570\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4f/Blue_grapes_fruit.png/257px-Blue_grapes_fruit.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/4f/Blue_grapes_fruit.png/385px-Blue_grapes_fruit.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/4f/Blue_grapes_fruit.png/513px-Blue_grapes_fruit.png 2x\" width=\"172\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 152px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Blue grape bush in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(16910, 2683, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a high bush with many thorny roses. Rose flowers can be harvested from this bush with a sickle during the appropriate season . Rose bushes are notorious for spreading incredibly fast, hindering the growth of other plants by occupying potential space. Rose trellis may also be harvested for roses.', '<p>This is a high bush with many thorny roses. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rose_flower\" title=\"Rose flower\">Rose flowers</a> can be harvested from this bush with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> during the appropriate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>. Rose bushes are notorious for spreading incredibly fast, hindering the growth of other plants by occupying potential space. <a href=\"/index.php/Rose_trellis\" title=\"Rose trellis\">Rose trellis</a> may also be harvested for roses.\n</p>', 0),
(16911, 2683, 'Examine Message', 'Examine_Message', 'Prior to season message on examine: The bush has a couple of promising buds. When ready to harvest, the bush will show such by examining it: The bush has some beautiful flowers.', '<p>Prior to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seasons\" title=\"Seasons\">season</a> message on examine:\n</p>\n<p><i>The bush has a couple of promising buds.</i>\n</p>\n<p>When ready to harvest, the bush will show such by examining it: \n</p>\n<p><i>The bush has some beautiful flowers.</i>\n</p>', 1),
(16912, 2683, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'The flowers can be used in some cooking recipes. Flowers can be used also in alchemy to make healing covers (healing potency 1). Sprouts can be used to grow a hedge . (prime type)', '<ul><li>The flowers can be used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Flowers can be used also in <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> (healing potency 1).</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sprouts\" title=\"Sprouts\">Sprouts</a> can be used to grow a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hedge\" title=\"Hedge\">hedge</a>. (prime type)</li></ul>', 2),
(16913, 4332, 'Description', 'Description', 'Using the /suicide> or the /respawn chat command while still alive will open the Respawn dialog allowing you to kill yourself in order to respawn.', '<p>Using the <code>/suicide&gt;</code> or the  <code>/respawn</code> chat command while still alive will open the <b>Respawn</b> dialog allowing you to kill yourself in order to respawn.\n</p>', 0),
(16914, 4332, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A suicide will result in the typical player death and subsequent respawn options. Suicide off-deed results in the normal, death-related skill loss of 0.25 from several skills and 0.01 body strength. Suicide on-deed, however, results in full skill losses. There is a 5 minute cool-down timer between suicides. There is a requirement of 19.45 body strength to commit suicide.', '<ul><li>A suicide will result in the typical player <a href=\"/index.php/Death\" title=\"Death\">death</a> and subsequent <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Respawn\" title=\"Respawn\">respawn</a> options.</li>\n<li>Suicide off-deed results in the normal, death-related skill loss of 0.25 from several skills and 0.01 body strength. Suicide on-deed, however, results in full <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> losses.</li>\n<li>There is a 5 minute cool-down timer between suicides.</li>\n<li>There is a requirement of 19.45 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> to commit suicide.</li></ul>', 1),
(16915, 4332, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Respawn Death Tent Corpse', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Respawn\" title=\"Respawn\">Respawn</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Death\" title=\"Death\">Death</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tent\" title=\"Tent\">Tent</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Corpse\" title=\"Corpse\">Corpse</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16926, 4335, 'Description', 'Description', 'A few handfuls of rye. Rye grows pretty much anywhere and is easy to farm. It is normally used to turn into flour and bake with or to sow with.', '<p><i>A few handfuls of rye. Rye grows pretty much anywhere and is easy to farm. It is normally used to turn into flour and bake with or to sow with.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16927, 4335, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Rye is used to make flour for baking bread and to tame and feed animals such as hens , horses , and bulls . Rye can be found by botanizing from Wild grasses Resource nodes . Rye can be sown on dirt , to produce more rye. Rye is harvested with a scythe and ground into flour with a grindstone .', '<ul><li>Rye is used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Flour\" title=\"Flour\">flour</a> for baking bread and to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tame</a> and feed <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a> such as <a href=\"/index.php/Hen\" title=\"Hen\">hens</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">horses</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">bulls</a>.</li>\n<li>Rye can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_grasses\" title=\"Wild grasses\">Wild grasses</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Rye can be <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">sown</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt_tile\" title=\"Dirt tile\">dirt</a>, to produce more rye.</li>\n<li>Rye is <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">harvested</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythe</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">ground</a> into <a href=\"/index.php/Flour\" title=\"Flour\">flour</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Grindstone\" title=\"Grindstone\">grindstone</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16928, 4335, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Cereal', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cereal\" title=\"Cereal\">Cereal</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16929, 4335, 'Reference', 'Reference', '', '', 3),
(16930, 4336, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cob of corn. Corn will be hard to grow in this environment. It is normally used to cook and eat, or to sow with.', '<p><i>A cob of corn. Corn will be hard to grow in this environment. It is normally used to cook and eat, or to sow with.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16931, 4336, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used in cooking recipes. Can be used to create a healing cover with a potency of 1. Can be milled with a grindstone to create corn flour. Can be pressed with a fruit press to create corn oil which is a cooking oil . It can be found by botanizing on Wild grasses or farmed. 100 fit in a pottery bowl .', '<ul><li>Can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a> with a potency of 1.</li>\n<li>Can be milled with a <a href=\"/index.php/Grindstone\" title=\"Grindstone\">grindstone</a> to create corn flour.</li>\n<li>Can be pressed with a <a href=\"/index.php/Fruit_press\" title=\"Fruit press\">fruit press</a> to create corn oil which is a <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking_oil\" title=\"Cooking oil\">cooking oil</a>.</li>\n<li>It can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_grasses\" title=\"Wild grasses\">Wild grasses</a> or farmed.</li>\n<li>100 fit in a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">pottery bowl</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(16932, 4336, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Vegetable', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Vegetable\" title=\"Vegetable\">Vegetable</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16933, 4337, 'Description', 'Description', 'Ground cereals.', '<p><i>Ground cereals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16934, 4337, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Flour is made by milling grain like barley , oat , rye or wheat with a grindstone . Failure results in no loss of grain, only causes decrease in the quality of the grain. It can be mixed with water to turn it into dough for baking into a bread.', '<ul><li>Flour is made by <a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">milling</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grain\" title=\"Grain\">grain</a> like <a href=\"/index.php/Barley\" title=\"Barley\">barley</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oat\" title=\"Oat\">oat</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rye\" title=\"Rye\">rye</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Wheat\" title=\"Wheat\">wheat</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Grindstone\" title=\"Grindstone\">grindstone</a>.</li>\n<li>Failure results in no loss of grain, only causes decrease in the quality of the grain.</li>\n<li>It can be mixed with <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a> to turn it into dough for <a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">baking</a> into a bread.</li></ul>', 1),
(16935, 4337, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Grindstone Grain Milling', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Grindstone\" title=\"Grindstone\">Grindstone</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grain\" title=\"Grain\">Grain</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">Milling</a></li></ul>', 2),
(16947, 1872, 'Mayor / Co-Mayor', 'Mayor_.2F_Co-Mayor', 'Bleth ** Moved to Wild ** Azzu ** Moved to Wild **', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Bleth\" title=\"Player:Bleth\">Bleth</a>  ** Moved to Wild ** \n</p>\n<p>Azzu ** Moved to Wild **\n</p>', 0),
(16948, 4343, 'Description', 'Description', 'Morning fog is a spell which grants some protection from thorns . The protection is not permanent like a blessing ; it is temporary. How good a protection one receives from the spell can be seen under \"Hud Settings > Spell Effects\". This spell is great for grinding your channeling skill due to the very low favor cost.', '<p><b>Morning fog</b> is a spell which grants some protection from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Thorn\" title=\"Thorn\">thorns</a>. The protection is not permanent like a <a href=\"/index.php/Bless\" title=\"Bless\">blessing</a>; it is temporary. How good a protection one receives from the spell can be seen under \"Hud Settings &gt; Spell Effects\". This spell is great for grinding your <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill due to the very low favor cost.\n</p>', 0),
(16949, 4343, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette of Fo Right-click a creature or person Select Spells > Morning fog', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette_of_Fo\" title=\"Statuette of Fo\">statuette of Fo</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a creature or person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Morning fog</i></li></ol>', 1),
(16950, 4343, 'Event Window', 'Event_Window', 'Start: \"You start to cast \'Morning fog\' on yourself.\" Success:\"You cast \'Morning fog\' on yourself.\" \"You now have protection from thorns and lava.\" Better power recast: \"You will now receive improved protection from thorns and lava.\" Fail: [20:31:21] You fail to channel the \'Morning fog\'. Combat window message when not facing the creature you\'re casting on You must turn towards Fosnake in order to see it.', '<p>Start: \"You start to cast \'Morning fog\' on yourself.\"\n</p>\n<p>Success:\"You cast \'Morning fog\' on yourself.\" \"You now have protection from thorns and lava.\"\n</p>\n<p>Better power recast: \"You will now receive improved protection from thorns and lava.\"\n</p>\n<p>Fail: [20:31:21] You fail to channel the \'Morning fog\'.\n</p>\n<p>Combat window message when not facing the creature you\'re casting on <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You must turn towards Fosnake in order to see it. </span>\n</p>', 2),
(16956, 2731, 'Description', 'Description', 'Demise spells are weapon enchantments that increase damage against specific types of creatures by 3%. They cannot shatter the item they are cast upon.', '<p><b>Demise</b> spells are weapon enchantments that increase damage against specific types of creatures by 3%.\n</p>\n<p>They cannot shatter the item they are cast upon.\n</p>', 0),
(16957, 2731, 'Requirements', 'Requirements', 'Demise spells can be cast only on a weapon of a QL greater than 70. An existing demise enchantment is not affected if the weapon\'s quality later falls below 70 QL due to damage. Multiple demise enchantments cannot be stacked with each other or with salve of frost or potion of acid on the same weapon. Each Demise spell requires a different amount of favor; see the list below for the cost of each spell.', '<p>Demise spells can be cast only on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Weapon\" title=\"Weapon\">weapon</a> of a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> greater than 70. An existing demise enchantment is not affected if the weapon\'s quality later falls below 70 QL due to damage.\n</p>\n<p>Multiple demise enchantments cannot be stacked with each other or with <a href=\"/index.php/Salve_of_frost\" title=\"Salve of frost\">salve of frost</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_acid\" title=\"Potion of acid\">potion of acid</a> on the same weapon.\n</p>\n<p>Each Demise spell requires a different amount of favor; see the list below for the cost of each spell.\n</p>', 1),
(16958, 2731, 'Demise spells', 'Demise_spells', 'Animal demise : available to priests of Magranon, Vynora, and Libila at 43 faith, and costs 40 favor. +3% damage versus non- legendary \"animal\" creatures Examples: Wild cat , brown bear , hell horse , etc. Monster demise : available to priests of Libila, Magranon, and Vynora at 41 faith, and costs 40 favor. +3% damage versus non- legendary \"monster\" creatures Examples: Troll , goblin , hell scorpious , etc. Legendary demise : available to priests of Libila, Vynora, and Magranon at 51 faith, and costs 50 favor. +3% damage versus legendary creatures Examples: Black dragon , Kyklops , Troll king , etc. Human demise : available to priests of Libila and Vynora at 61 faith, , and costs 60 favor. +3% damage versus humans Examples: Other players , guards , etc. Does not affect \"humanoid\" creatures such as trolls .', '<ul><li><b>Animal demise</b>: available to priests of Magranon, Vynora, and Libila at 43 faith, and costs 40 favor.\n<ul><li>+3% damage versus non-<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Legendary\" title=\"Legendary\">legendary</a> \"animal\" creatures</li>\n<li>Examples: <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_cat\" title=\"Wild cat\">Wild cat</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">brown bear</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">hell horse</a>, etc.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Monster demise</b>: available to priests of Libila, Magranon, and Vynora at 41 faith, and costs 40 favor.\n<ul><li>+3% damage versus non-<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Legendary\" title=\"Legendary\">legendary</a> \"monster\" creatures</li>\n<li>Examples: <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Troll</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Goblin\" title=\"Goblin\">goblin</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hell_scorpious\" title=\"Hell scorpious\">hell scorpious</a>, etc.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Legendary demise</b>: available to priests of Libila, Vynora, and Magranon at 51 faith, and costs 50 favor.\n<ul><li>+3% damage versus <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Legendary\" title=\"Legendary\">legendary</a> creatures</li>\n<li>Examples: <a href=\"/index.php/Black_dragon\" title=\"Black dragon\">Black dragon</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Kyklops\" title=\"Kyklops\">Kyklops</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Troll_king\" title=\"Troll king\">Troll king</a>, etc.</li></ul></li>\n<li><b>Human demise</b>: available to priests of Libila and Vynora at 61 faith, , and costs 60 favor.\n<ul><li>+3% damage versus humans</li>\n<li>Examples: Other <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Players\" title=\"Players\">players</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Guards\" title=\"Guards\">guards</a>, etc.</li>\n<li>Does <i>not</i> affect \"humanoid\" creatures such as <a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">trolls</a>.</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(16959, 4346, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine hen proudly prods around here.', '<p><i>A fine hen proudly prods around here.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16960, 4346, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A hen is a farm animal that can be found in the wilderness. They can be white, black, or brown in color. They can be lead with a rope without being tamed . Hens do not graze in Wurm. When eating from a pile, they seem to eat roughly 10 seeds per RL day. Hens will lay eggs when fed and kept on the following types of tile: dirt , grass , Enchanted grass , Mycelium , moss , steppe , lawn , bushes (normal and enchanted), and crops . To hatch eggs, lay a fertile egg on a tile and allow it to decay. When it reaches 100 damage, there is a small chance that a chicken will emerge. Hens will be hunted down by carnivorous animals or mobs. Dies at aged stage unless cared for . You can have up to 13 hens loaded into a chicken coop for easy access to eggs. They can be fertile or infertile and will decay while in the chicken coop.', '<ul><li>A hen is a farm <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animal</a> that can be found in the wilderness.</li>\n<li>They can be white, black, or brown in color.</li>\n<li>They can be lead with a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">rope</a> without being <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a>.</li>\n<li>Hens do <i>not</i> graze in Wurm.\n<ul><li>When eating from a pile, they seem to eat roughly 10 seeds per RL day.</li>\n<li>Hens will lay <a href=\"/index.php/Egg\" title=\"Egg\">eggs</a> when fed and kept on the following types of tile: <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt_tile\" title=\"Dirt tile\">dirt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Grass_tile\" title=\"Grass tile\">grass</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Enchanted_grass\" title=\"Enchanted grass\">Enchanted grass</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mycelium\" title=\"Mycelium\">Mycelium</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">moss</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Steppe\" title=\"Steppe\">steppe</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lawn\" title=\"Lawn\">lawn</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bushes\" title=\"Bushes\">bushes</a> (normal and enchanted), and <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">crops</a>.</li></ul></li>\n<li>To hatch eggs, lay a <a href=\"/index.php/Egg\" title=\"Egg\">fertile egg</a> on a tile and allow it to decay. When it reaches 100 damage, there is a small chance that a chicken will emerge.</li>\n<li>Hens will be hunted down by carnivorous animals or mobs.</li>\n<li>Dies at <a href=\"/index.php/Age#Creatures\" title=\"Age\">aged</a> stage unless <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_husbandry#Caring\" title=\"Animal husbandry\">cared for</a>.</li>\n<li>You can have up to 13 hens loaded into a <a href=\"/index.php/Chicken_coop\" title=\"Chicken coop\">chicken coop</a> for easy access to eggs. They can be fertile or infertile and will decay while in the chicken coop.</li></ul>', 1),
(16964, 4348, 'Description', 'Description', 'A proud rooster struts around here.', '<p><i>A proud rooster struts around here.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(16965, 4348, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'They can be white, black, or brown in color. Roosters do not have to be tamed to be led with a rope. They are tamable with seeds. Uses a stabbing attack, but are very easy to kill. Dies at aged stage unless cared for.', '<ul><li>They can be white, black, or brown in color.</li>\n<li>Roosters do not have to be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> to be <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">led</a> with a rope.</li>\n<li>They are tamable with seeds.</li>\n<li>Uses a stabbing attack, but are very easy to kill.</li>\n<li>Dies at aged stage unless cared for.</li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(16966, 4348, 'Images', 'Images', 'Three Handsome Roosters', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 403.33333333333px\"><div style=\"width: 403.33333333333px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 401.33333333333px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Threeroosters.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"299\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/8/85/Threeroosters.jpg\" width=\"402\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 382px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Three Handsome Roosters\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(16967, 4348, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Chicken Hen', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Chicken\" title=\"Chicken\">Chicken</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hen\" title=\"Hen\">Hen</a></li></ul>', 3),
(16972, 4350, 'Description', 'Description', 'Alignment is a measure of how good you are to your god , 100 alignment being the maximum for Fo , Vynora and Magranon , -100 for Libila . An alignment of 0 is sufficient to be accepted as a Vynora or Magranon followers, however Fo requires an alignment of at least one or Fo will not accept the person as a follower. For followers with 20 or more faith, the following boosts of +2.5% to +10% characteristic gain are scaled by alignment: Deity Body strength Body stamina Body control Mind logic Mind speed Soul strength Soul depth Fo Vynora Magranon Libila For priests , a high alignment value increases chances to successfully cast spells while a low alignment value lowers the chances. Alignment is also said to affect your fighting ability, but it is unknown by how much. Warning: Priests who lost all their alignment towards their god will lose priesthood and their faith will drop to 0.', '<p>Alignment is a measure of how good you are to your <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/God\" title=\"God\">god</a>, 100 alignment being the maximum for <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a>, -100 for <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a>. An alignment of 0 is sufficient to be accepted as a Vynora or Magranon followers, however Fo requires an alignment of at least one or Fo will not accept the person as a follower.\n</p>\n<p>For followers with 20 or more faith, the following boosts of +2.5% to +10% characteristic gain are scaled by alignment:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Deity\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Body_stamina\" title=\"Body stamina\">Body stamina</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Mind_speed\" title=\"Mind speed\">Mind speed</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Soul_strength\" title=\"Soul strength\">Soul strength</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>For <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a>, a high alignment value increases chances to successfully cast <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spells</a> while a low alignment value lowers the chances. Alignment is also said to affect your fighting ability, but it is unknown by how much.\n</p>\n<p><b>Warning:</b> Priests who lost all their alignment towards their god will lose priesthood and their faith will drop to 0.\n</p>', 0),
(16973, 4350, 'Alignment gain and loss', 'Alignment_gain_and_loss', 'Alignment will automatically go towards 1 over time for whitelighters , and -1 for blacklighters . When alignment goes down, for whatever reason, it will drop at a value equal to 1-( Faith /200). Thus, at 0 faith one would lose 1.0 alignment and at 100 faith one would lose 0.5 alignment.  This loss is halved in local range to the White light for whitelighters. Gaining alignment points (either positive or negative) has a cool down timer. Once you have gained an alignment tick you must wait 30 minutes before you are able to gain again.  Note that alignment automatically drifting towards zero does not affect this timer. Altering your alignment These actions can effect your alignment: Action Direction Amount Notes Butchering a human corpse - 1 Burying a human corpse + 2 Listening to a confession +/- 1 Confessing to a priest +/- 5 Holding a sermon +/- 4 Listening to a sermon +/- 4 up to 4 depending on the number of listeners. Sermons can only move your alignment in the direction of your deity\'s alignment, not against. Converting someone to your religion +/- 1 Healing another player + 1 Casting Bless on players + 1 Possibly random Sacrificing items in an altar +/- 1 Exact favor amount requirement unknown Praying at the White Light on Chaos + 3 Praying at the Black Light on Chaos - 3 Desecrating an altar - 2 Killing of a whitelighter - 5 Killing of a blacklighter + 5 Plant a sprout or a flower + 1 Fo only Felling trees aged very old , or overaged + 1 Vynora only Starting a wall (first action on a new wall) + 1 Vynora only Mine + 0.5 Magranon only: Kill a creature + 0.5 Magranon only Kill a creature - 0.5 Libila only Alignment changes with a positive sign (+) indicate a gain for whitelighters and a loss for blacklighters.  A negative sign (-) is the opposite.', '<p>Alignment will automatically go towards 1 over time for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Whitelight\" title=\"Whitelight\">whitelighters</a>, and -1 for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Blacklight\" title=\"Blacklight\">blacklighters</a>.\n</p>\n<p>When alignment goes down, for whatever reason, it will drop at a value equal to 1-(<a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a>/200). Thus, at 0 faith one would lose 1.0 alignment and at 100 faith one would lose 0.5 alignment.  This loss is halved in local range to the White light for whitelighters.\n</p>\n<p>Gaining alignment points (either positive or negative) has a cool down timer. Once you have gained an alignment tick you must wait 30 minutes before you are able to gain again.  Note that alignment automatically drifting towards zero does not affect this timer.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Altering_your_alignment\">Altering your alignment</span></h3>\n<p>These actions can effect your alignment:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"250\">Action\n</th>\n<th width=\"50\">Direction\n</th>\n<th width=\"50\">Amount\n</th>\n<th width=\"200\">Notes\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">Butchering</a> a human corpse\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Burying a human corpse\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listening to a <a href=\"/index.php/Confession\" title=\"Confession\">confession</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Confessing to a priest\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">5\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Holding a <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">sermon</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listening to a sermon\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4\n</td>\n<td>up to 4 depending on the number of listeners. Sermons can only move your alignment in the direction of your deity\'s alignment, not against.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Convert\" title=\"Convert\">Converting</a> someone to your religion\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Healing\" title=\"Healing\">Healing</a> another player\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Casting <a href=\"/index.php/Bless\" title=\"Bless\">Bless</a> on players\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>Possibly random\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sacrificing items in an <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altar</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+/-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td>Exact favor amount requirement unknown\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Praying at the <a href=\"/index.php/White_Light\" title=\"White Light\">White Light</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Praying at the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_Light\" title=\"Black Light\">Black Light</a> on Chaos\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Desecrating an altar\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">2\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Killing of a whitelighter\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">5\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Killing of a blacklighter\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">5\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plant a sprout or a flower\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> only\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Felling trees aged <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">very old</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">overaged</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> only\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Starting a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall\" title=\"Wall\">wall</a> (first action on a new wall)\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> only\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mine\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.5\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> only:\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a creature\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">+\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.5\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> only\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kill a creature\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">-\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.5\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> only\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Alignment changes with a positive sign (+) indicate a gain for whitelighters and a loss for blacklighters.  A negative sign (-) is the opposite.\n</p>', 1),
(16988, 4353, 'Description', 'Description', 'A citizen of a settlement .', '<p>A citizen of a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">settlement</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(16989, 4353, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The mayor of the settlement (deed holder) can configure a unique set of permissions for any player or citizen. Upon death, a citizen can choose to re-spawn at the settlement they belong to rather than the default spawn-point/town. They may also choose to re-spawn on deeds allied to their own deed of citizenship if they are within 50 tiles of the allied deed token when they die. A citizen can choose to create or relocate their bank account to the settlement token but has the right to choose any deed token on the server as their bank. Citizens can use the /vote username command to vote for a new mayor in deeds set to run as democracies. 51% (the majority) of such citizen votes are needed to elect a new mayor. Other governance formats on deeds do not allow for such democratic changes of mayorship.', '<ul><li>The mayor of the settlement (deed holder) can configure a unique set of <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> for any player or citizen.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Upon death, a citizen can choose to re-spawn at the settlement they belong to rather than the default spawn-point/town. They may also choose to re-spawn on deeds allied to their own deed of citizenship if they are within 50 tiles of the allied deed token when they die.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>A citizen can choose to create or relocate their <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bank\" title=\"Bank\">bank</a> account to the settlement <a href=\"/index.php/Token\" title=\"Token\">token</a> but has the right to choose any deed token on the server as their bank.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Citizens can use the <i>/vote username</i> command to vote for a new mayor in deeds set to run as democracies. 51% (the majority) of such citizen votes are needed to elect a new mayor. Other governance formats on deeds do not allow for such democratic changes of mayorship.</li></ul>', 1),
(17028, 4360, 'Description', 'Description', 'The pheasant slowly paces here, vigilant as always.', '<p><i>The pheasant slowly paces here, vigilant as always.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17029, 4360, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Pheasants can\'t fly. They must be tamed with seeds before it can be led Slashing attack Can be bred with one male and one female. Pheasant will be hunted down by carnivorous animals or mobs', '<ul><li>Pheasants can\'t fly.</li>\n<li>They must be tamed with seeds before it can be <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures#Leading\" title=\"Creatures\">led</a></li>\n<li>Slashing attack</li>\n<li>Can be bred with one male and one female.</li>\n<li>Pheasant will be hunted down by carnivorous animals or mobs</li></ul>', 1),
(17030, 4360, 'Images', 'Images', 'Pheasant', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:252px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pheasant5yd.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"189\" data-file-width=\"338\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"140\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/ec/Pheasant5yd.png/250px-Pheasant5yd.png\" srcset=\"/images/e/ec/Pheasant5yd.png 1.5x\" width=\"250\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pheasant5yd.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Pheasant</div></div></div>', 2),
(17031, 4361, 'Description', 'Description', 'This bull looks pretty menacing.', '<p><i>This bull looks pretty menacing.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17032, 4361, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The bull is a farm animal that can be found in the wilderness. They can be bred with cows , resulting in calves . You can lead a bull with a rope without taming it. They will graze on a tile of grass or a tile of farmed field. They can eat your crops so be warned. Bulls can be hitched to a large cart as a draft animal. Minimum age to hitch is full sized young growth stage. Body control of 23 required to ride.', '<ul><li>The bull is a farm <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animal</a> that can be found in the wilderness. They can be bred with <a href=\"/index.php/Cow\" title=\"Cow\">cows</a>, resulting in <a href=\"/index.php/Calf\" title=\"Calf\">calves</a>.</li>\n<li>You can lead a bull with a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">rope</a> without <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">taming</a> it.</li>\n<li>They will graze on a tile of grass or a tile of farmed field. They can eat your crops so be warned.</li>\n<li>Bulls can be hitched to a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a> as a draft animal. Minimum age to hitch is full sized young growth stage.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a> of 23 required to ride.</li></ul>', 1),
(17037, 4363, 'Description', 'Description', 'Occasionally this dog will bark and scratch itself behind the ears.', '<p><i>Occasionally this dog will bark and scratch itself behind the ears.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17038, 4363, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Dogs are tamable animals . It can be tamed with almost any food, with no minimum taming skill recommended. Difficulty to kill is between a wild cat and a mountain lion . A dog will eat nearly any food items, similarly to a pig , dropped on the ground. A dog will eat the entirety of what you feed it. It leaves no leftovers even if it cannot consume as much as you feed it. A champion dog stands taller than a one-story house . A very good pet for beginners. Dogs will eat a corpse. The corpse will look butchered and butchering items will disappear along with it.', '<ul><li>Dogs are <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamable</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a>. It can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> with almost any food, with no minimum taming skill recommended.</li>\n<li>Difficulty to kill is between a <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_cat\" title=\"Wild cat\">wild cat</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_lion\" title=\"Mountain lion\">mountain lion</a>.</li>\n<li>A dog will eat nearly any food items, similarly to a <a href=\"/index.php/Pig\" title=\"Pig\">pig</a>, dropped on the ground. A dog will eat the entirety of what you feed it. It leaves no leftovers even if it cannot consume as much as you feed it.</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_conditions\" title=\"Animal conditions\">champion</a> dog stands taller than a one-story <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">house</a>.</li>\n<li>A very good <a href=\"/index.php/Pet\" title=\"Pet\">pet</a> for beginners.</li>\n<li>Dogs will eat a corpse. The corpse will look <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchered</a> and butchering items will disappear along with it.</li></ul>', 1),
(17039, 3533, 'Description', 'Description', 'The sack where a now deceased animal used to keep its urine.', '<p><i>The sack where a now deceased animal used to keep its urine.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17040, 3533, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in the construction of a cheese drill . Used in some cooking recipes. Used to create a healing cover with a potency of 2.', '<ul><li>Used in the construction of a <a href=\"/index.php/Cheese_drill\" title=\"Cheese drill\">cheese drill</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a> with a potency of 2.</li></ul>', 1),
(17041, 3533, 'Notes', 'Notes', '0.02kg is used in the creation of a healing cover. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage. A bladder can be butchered from these animals: Bison Bull Calf Cow Deer Dog Donkey Foal Hell horse Horse Lamb Ram Sheep', '<ul><li>0.02kg is used in the creation of a healing cover.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>\n<p>A <b>bladder</b> can be butchered from these animals:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bison</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">Bull</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Calf\" title=\"Calf\">Calf</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cow\" title=\"Cow\">Cow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Deer\" title=\"Deer\">Deer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Dog\" title=\"Dog\">Dog</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Donkey\" title=\"Donkey\">Donkey</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Foal\" title=\"Foal\">Foal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_horse\" title=\"Hell horse\">Hell horse</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horse</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lamb\" title=\"Lamb\">Lamb</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ram\" title=\"Ram\">Ram</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">Sheep</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17085, 1688, 'Description', 'Description', 'Four main kingdoms exist in the story of Wurm. Three of these kingdoms exist on the Epic cluster as well as one on the Freedom cluster. Also, there are player-made kingdoms ( PMK ) on the Elevation server in the Epic cluster and on the Chaos server in the Freedom cluster. To see the kingdom influence on your current server, use the /kingdoms chat command .', '<p>Four main kingdoms exist in the story of Wurm. Three of these kingdoms exist on the Epic cluster as well as one on the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> cluster. Also, there are player-made kingdoms (<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PMK\" title=\"PMK\">PMK</a>) on the <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> server in the Epic cluster and on the <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a> server in the Freedom cluster.\n</p>\n<p>To see the kingdom influence on your current server, use the <code>/kingdoms</code> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chat_command\" title=\"Chat command\">chat command</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(17086, 1688, 'Epic Server Kingdoms', 'Epic_Server_Kingdoms', 'Desertion : Home to the Whitelighter (WL) Kingdom of Mol-Rehan aka MR Serenity : Home to the Whitelighter (WL) Kingdom of Jenn-Kellon aka JK Affliction : Home to the Blacklighter (BL) Horde of the Summoned aka HOTS All kingdoms on the Epic servers are at war with each other by default. While all kingdoms are in conflict over land and power, the blacklight kingdom HotS fights the other whitelight kingdoms over religion . On the Elevation server, land must be claimed for the kingdom by building guard towers . When a guard tower is created, it claims the land around it for the kingdom, and it is then possible to build a settlement there. On Affliction, Desertion, and Serenity, land is already claimed for the default kingdom on the server, and guard towers are not required to place a deed. No enemy kingdom can claim land or place deeds on these three servers. If a player wishes to change their kingdom, they must be invited to join by a member of that kingdom.', '<ul><li>Desertion : Home to the <a href=\"/index.php/Whitelighter\" title=\"Whitelighter\">Whitelighter</a> (WL) <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Kingdom of Mol-Rehan</a> aka MR</li>\n<li>Serenity : Home to the <a href=\"/index.php/Whitelighter\" title=\"Whitelighter\">Whitelighter</a> (WL) <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Kingdom of Jenn-Kellon</a> aka JK</li>\n<li>Affliction : Home to the <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighter</a> (BL) <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a> aka HOTS</li></ul>\n<p>All kingdoms on the Epic servers are at war with each other by default. While all kingdoms are in conflict over land and power, the blacklight kingdom HotS fights the other whitelight kingdoms over <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religion</a>.\n</p>\n<p>On the <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> server, land must be claimed for the kingdom by building <a href=\"/index.php/Guard_tower\" title=\"Guard tower\">guard towers</a>. When a guard tower is created, it claims the land around it for the kingdom, and it is then possible to build a settlement there. On Affliction, Desertion, and Serenity, land is already claimed for the default kingdom on the server, and guard towers are not required to place a deed. No enemy kingdom can claim land or place deeds on these three servers.\n</p>\n<p>If a player wishes to change their kingdom, they must be invited to join by a member of that kingdom.\n</p>', 1),
(17087, 1688, 'Freedom Kingdom', 'Freedom_Kingdom', 'On the Freedom servers, there is only one kingdom: \"Freedom\". Thus, no inter-kingdom conflicts of any sort occur, and there is no need to claim land for your kingdom. It is, however, still possible to build guard towers, though they are not required to build settlements. The one exception to this is on the PvP Chaos server, where Player Made Kingdoms can be created.', '<p>On the Freedom servers, there is only one kingdom: \"Freedom\". Thus, no inter-kingdom conflicts of any sort occur, and there is no need to claim land for your kingdom. It is, however, still possible to build guard towers, though they are not required to build settlements.\n</p>\n<p>The one exception to this is on the PvP Chaos server, where Player Made Kingdoms can be created.\n</p>', 2),
(17088, 1688, 'Player Made Kingdoms', 'Player_Made_Kingdoms', 'In addition to the normal preset Kingdoms, players can create their own Player Made Kingdom on the Elevation or Chaos servers. PMK\'s are independent Kingdoms, created by declaring independence with a specific item on their settlement token.', '<p>In addition to the normal preset Kingdoms, players can create their own <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player_Made_Kingdom\" title=\"Player Made Kingdom\">Player Made Kingdom</a> on the Elevation or Chaos servers. PMK\'s are independent Kingdoms, created by declaring independence with a specific item on their settlement token.\n</p>', 3),
(17089, 1688, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'On the Golden Valley server all players are Freedom Isles, and new players may not venture onto the main server.', '<ul><li>On the Golden Valley server all players are Freedom Isles, and new players may not venture onto the main server.</li></ul>', 4),
(17090, 1688, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Convert Duel ring', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Convert\" title=\"Convert\">Convert</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Duel_ring\" title=\"Duel ring\">Duel ring</a></li></ul>', 5),
(17096, 4377, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large funny-coloured egg.', '<p><i>A large funny-coloured egg.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17097, 4377, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Easter eggs could be found around Easter before 2023 by foraging relevant tiles. Eggs may only be found by accounts with premium status and will appear directly in the player inventory once located.\nTo obtain the contents of an egg, right click it and select Open. From 2023, Decorative easter eggs replaced the egg you can find during Easter event.', '<p><b>Easter eggs</b> could be found around Easter before 2023 by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forage\" title=\"Forage\">foraging</a> relevant tiles. Eggs may only be found by accounts with premium status and will appear directly in the player inventory once located.\nTo obtain the contents of an egg, right click it and select Open.\n</p>\n<p>From 2023, <a href=\"/index.php/Decorative_easter_egg\" title=\"Decorative easter egg\">Decorative easter eggs</a> replaced the egg you can find during Easter event.\n</p>', 1),
(17098, 4377, 'History', 'History', 'Easter 2006 - The eggs were dropped by Easter Bunny . When decayed, they dropped gems , either a Crystal Diamond, or a Crystal Sapphire. Easter 2007 - No eggs had been added. Easter 2008 - The eggs dropped by the bunny decayed into high-quality cheese of various types, including buffalo and feta and also, more rarely, dropped gems. Easter 2009 - Eggs were foraged from grass tiles and turned into gems.  Other eggs were dropped by the Easter bunny; some were cheese or gems like the year before. Easter 2010 - No eggs had been added. Easter 2011 - Eggs are found by foraging and rummaging. Easter 2012 - Eggs are found by foraging. Easter 2013 - No eggs added (?) Easter 2014 - Eggs are found by foraging. Easter 2017 - Eggs can be redeemed with a key, still good for once per premium character /redeemkey 9VMY486QSC8D-QH84F6O8UMSN (2017) Easter 2020 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, and multiple Easter Bunny roaming. Easter 2021 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, resulting in a Spring flowers , and multiple Easter Bunny roaming. Easter 2022 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, and multiple Easter Bunny roaming.', '<ul><li>Easter 2006 - The eggs were dropped by <a href=\"/index.php/Easter_Bunny\" title=\"Easter Bunny\">Easter Bunny</a>. When decayed, they dropped <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gem\" title=\"Gem\">gems</a>, either a Crystal Diamond, or a Crystal Sapphire.</li>\n<li>Easter 2007 - No eggs had been added.</li>\n<li>Easter 2008 - The eggs dropped by the bunny decayed into high-quality cheese of various types, including buffalo and feta and also, more rarely, dropped gems.</li>\n<li>Easter 2009 - Eggs were <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forage\" title=\"Forage\">foraged</a> from grass tiles and turned into gems.  Other eggs were dropped by the Easter bunny; some were cheese or gems like the year before.</li>\n<li>Easter 2010 - No eggs had been added.</li>\n<li>Easter 2011 - Eggs are found by foraging and rummaging.</li>\n<li>Easter 2012 - Eggs are found by foraging.</li>\n<li>Easter 2013 - No eggs added (?)</li>\n<li>Easter 2014 - Eggs are found by foraging.</li>\n<li>Easter 2017 - Eggs can be redeemed with a key, still good for once per premium character /redeemkey 9VMY486QSC8D-QH84F6O8UMSN (2017)</li>\n<li>Easter 2020 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, and multiple <a href=\"/index.php/Easter_Bunny\" title=\"Easter Bunny\">Easter Bunny</a> roaming.</li>\n<li>Easter 2021 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, resulting in a <a href=\"/index.php/Spring_flowers\" title=\"Spring flowers\">Spring flowers</a>, and multiple <a href=\"/index.php/Easter_Bunny\" title=\"Easter Bunny\">Easter Bunny</a> roaming.</li>\n<li>Easter 2022 - One foraged easter egg per premium account, and multiple <a href=\"/index.php/Easter_Bunny\" title=\"Easter Bunny\">Easter Bunny</a> roaming.</li></ul>', 2),
(17099, 4377, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Decorative easter egg', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Decorative_easter_egg\" title=\"Decorative easter egg\">Decorative easter egg</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17100, 3401, 'Description', 'Description', 'Used to locate artifacts spread across the land.', '<p>Used to locate <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Artifact\" title=\"Category:Artifact\">artifacts</a> spread across the land.\n</p>', 0),
(17101, 3401, 'Use', 'Use', 'It is a completely random process to locate each item. It will tell you what direction, right, left, forward/front/ahead etc and a relative distance.\nVery far, far, pretty far, rather long distance, quite some distance, some distance, pretty close by, a stone throw away, practically standing on. (add more, and maybe some measure in km). It will also tell you if someone has found it, who is carrying it, and if they are in a village, what village they are in. If someone has left the artifact somewhere, it will tell you it is in the wild. If it is in a village, it will tell you what settlement it is in. If it is in a building, it will tell you the name of the building. The gold Charm of Fo has not yet been revealed. The gold Charm of Fo is very far away ahead of you to the left. The glass Orb of Doom is carried by Malvada. Malvada is in the settlement of Mist. If you try to use the spell on a PVE Freedom server the message The artifact was hidden from view by the gods. will appear in the event tab. There are no artifacts on PVE servers.', '<p>It is a completely random process to locate each item.\n</p>\n<p>It will tell you what direction, right, left, forward/front/ahead etc and a relative distance.\nVery far, far, pretty far, rather long distance, quite some distance, some distance, pretty close by, a stone throw away, practically standing on. (add more, and maybe some measure in km).\n</p>\n<p>It will also tell you if someone has found it, who is carrying it, and if they are in a village, what village they are in. If someone has left the artifact somewhere, it will tell you it is in the wild. If it is in a village, it will tell you what settlement it is in. If it is in a building, it will tell you the name of the building.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> The gold Charm of Fo has not yet been revealed. The gold Charm of Fo is very far away ahead of you to the left. </span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> The glass Orb of Doom is carried by Malvada. Malvada is in the settlement of Mist. </span>\n</p>\n<p>If you try to use the spell on a PVE Freedom server the message <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> The artifact was hidden from view by the gods. </span> will appear in the event tab. There are no artifacts on PVE servers.\n</p>', 1),
(17102, 3401, 'Distances', 'Distances', 'Distance Message 0 tiles You are practically standing on the <artifact>! 1-3 tiles The <artifact> is in front of you a stone\'s throw away! 4-5 tiles The <artifact> is in front of you very close. 6-9 tiles The <artifact> is in front of you pretty close by. 10-19 tiles The <artifact> is in front of you fairly close by. 20-49 tiles The <artifact> is some distance away in front of you. 50-199 tiles The <artifact> is quite some distance away in front of you. 200-499 tiles The <artifact> is rather a long distance away in front of you. 500-999 tiles The <artifact> is pretty far away in front of you. 1000> tiles The <artifact> is far away in front of you.', '<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Distance</th>\n<th>Message\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0 tiles</td>\n<td>You are practically standing on the &lt;artifact&gt;!\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1-3 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is in front of you a stone\'s throw away!\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4-5 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is in front of you very close.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6-9 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is in front of you pretty close by.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10-19 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is in front of you fairly close by.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>20-49 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is some distance away in front of you.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50-199 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is quite some distance away in front of you.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>200-499 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is rather a long distance away in front of you.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>500-999 tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is pretty far away in front of you.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1000&gt; tiles</td>\n<td>The &lt;artifact&gt; is far away in front of you.\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>', 2),
(17103, 3401, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click a tile Select Spells > Locate artifact', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a></li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Locate artifact</i></li></ol>', 3),
(17104, 3401, 'List of artifacts', 'List_of_artifacts', 'Vynora Eye of Vynora Mouth of Vynora Ear of Vynora Fo Finger of Fo Rod of Beguiling Charm of Fo Magranon Crown of Might Sword of Magranon Hammer of Magranon Libila Orb of doom Sceptre of ascension Scale of Libila', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Vynora\"><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Eye_of_Vynora\" title=\"Eye of Vynora\">Eye of Vynora</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mouth_of_Vynora\" title=\"Mouth of Vynora\">Mouth of Vynora</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ear_of_Vynora\" title=\"Ear of Vynora\">Ear of Vynora</a></li></ul></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fo\"><a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Finger_of_Fo\" title=\"Finger of Fo\">Finger of Fo</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rod_of_Beguiling\" title=\"Rod of Beguiling\">Rod of Beguiling</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Charm_of_Fo\" title=\"Charm of Fo\">Charm of Fo</a></li></ul></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Magranon\"><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Crown_of_Might\" title=\"Crown of Might\">Crown of Might</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sword_of_Magranon\" title=\"Sword of Magranon\">Sword of Magranon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammer_of_Magranon\" title=\"Hammer of Magranon\">Hammer of Magranon</a></li></ul></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Libila\"><a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Orb_of_doom\" title=\"Orb of doom\">Orb of doom</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sceptre_of_ascension\" title=\"Sceptre of ascension\">Sceptre of ascension</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Scale_of_Libila\" title=\"Scale of Libila\">Scale of Libila</a></li></ul></dd></dl>', 4),
(17105, 4379, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The location or carrier of an artifact may be determined using the Locate artifact spell. Each artifact has 30 charges. Every week 10 charges are removed. Activation|use removes 1 charge. When an artifact has 0 charges left it will disappear into the ground at a random location within the week unless recharged at either the White Light or Bone Altar . Recharging takes up to 4 minutes, can only be done one artifact at a time and emits a serverwide event message. Recharging is limited to specific times and days. Times are the 1st and 3rd week of each starfall, during either Awakening or Wrath day. Artifacts do not decay or take damage when used. May not be taken to any other server. You may not teleport whilst carrying an artifact. Artifacts drop on the ground upon leaving the world. Artifacts will drop on the tile on player death.', '<ul><li>The location or carrier of an artifact may be determined using the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>Each artifact has 30 charges. Every week 10 charges are removed. Activation|use removes 1 charge.</li>\n<li>When an artifact has 0 charges left it will disappear into the ground at a random location within the week unless recharged at either the <a href=\"/index.php/White_Light\" title=\"White Light\">White Light</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Bone_Altar\" title=\"Bone Altar\">Bone Altar</a>.</li>\n<li>Recharging takes up to 4 minutes, can only be done one artifact at a time and emits a serverwide event message.</li>\n<li>Recharging is limited to specific times and days. Times are the 1st and 3rd week of each starfall, during either Awakening or Wrath day.</li>\n<li>Artifacts do not decay or take damage when used.</li>\n<li>May not be taken to any other server.</li>\n<li>You may not teleport whilst carrying an artifact.</li>\n<li>Artifacts drop on the ground upon leaving the world.</li>\n<li>Artifacts will drop on the tile on player death.</li></ul>', 0),
(17106, 4379, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Artifacts', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Category:Artifacts\" title=\"Category:Artifacts\">Category:Artifacts</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17107, 2371, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge blue gem with a shimmering light inside.', '<p><i>A huge blue gem with a shimmering light inside.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17108, 2371, 'Item Use', 'Item_Use', 'Activation will cast the spells Locate Artifact and Locate soul . Detects through Nolocate spells.', '<ul><li>Activation will cast the spells <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Locate_Artifact\" title=\"Locate Artifact\">Locate Artifact</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_soul\" title=\"Locate soul\">Locate soul</a>. Detects through <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a> spells.</li></ul>', 1),
(17109, 2371, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Cooldown is 1 hour.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cooldown is 1 hour.</li></ul>', 2),
(17110, 2380, 'Description', 'Description', 'A slender, blue twisted crystal horn.', '<p><i>A slender, blue twisted crystal horn.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17111, 2380, 'Item Use', 'Item_Use', 'Gives 1 hour of sleep bonus. Refreshes the player. Gives Vynora followers Excel .', '<ul><li>Gives 1 hour of sleep bonus.</li>\n<li>Refreshes the player.</li>\n<li>Gives <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> followers <a href=\"/index.php/Excel\" title=\"Excel\">Excel</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17112, 2380, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Cooldown is 12 hours.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cooldown is 12 hours.</li></ul>', 2),
(17113, 2379, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large seashell made from blue crystal.', '<p><i>A large seashell made from blue crystal.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17114, 2379, 'Use', 'Use', 'Drops 1 gem, flint or salt 33% of the time and items are always over 70QL, with an average of 85ql. 57% of the time nothing happens. 10% of the time an anaconda appears. Must be used off-deed to work.', '<ul><li>Drops 1 gem, flint or salt 33% of the time and items are always over 70QL, with an average of 85ql.</li>\n<li>57% of the time nothing happens.</li>\n<li>10% of the time an <a href=\"/index.php/Anaconda\" title=\"Anaconda\">anaconda</a> appears.</li>\n<li>Must be used off-deed to work.</li></ul>', 1),
(17115, 2379, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Cooldown is 1 hour.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cooldown is 1 hour.</li></ul>', 2),
(17116, 2382, 'Description', 'Description', 'A very natural one foot long slender twig, except that it seems made from silver.', '<p><i>A very natural one foot long slender twig, except that it seems made from silver.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17117, 2382, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Having this item in inventory prevents wounds of every allied person in proximity from growing. This artifact can heal all your wounds in an instant, and give Fo followers Forest giant strength . One use per hour.', '<ul><li>Having this item in inventory prevents <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wounds</a> of every allied person in proximity from growing.</li>\n<li>This <a href=\"/index.php/Artifact\" title=\"Artifact\">artifact</a> can heal all your wounds in an instant, and give <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> followers <a href=\"/index.php/Forest_giant_strength\" title=\"Forest giant strength\">Forest giant strength</a>. One use per hour.</li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(17118, 2382, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>', 2),
(17119, 2381, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick heavy gold crown covered in green and red gems', '<p><i>A thick heavy gold crown covered in green and red gems</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17120, 2381, 'Item Use', 'Item_Use', 'Can be used to dominate monsters with a 10 second timer. When worn on the head it protects as a steel great helm and gives every allied person in proximity a non-stackable Combat rating bonus of 1. Activating gives Magranon followers Frantic charge and a small chance to spawn a Mountain gorilla .', '<ul><li>Can be used to dominate monsters with a 10 second timer.</li>\n<li>When worn on the head it protects as a steel great helm and gives every allied person in proximity a non-stackable <a href=\"/index.php/Combat_rating\" title=\"Combat rating\">Combat rating</a> bonus of 1.</li>\n<li>Activating gives <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> followers <a href=\"/index.php/Frantic_charge\" title=\"Frantic charge\">Frantic charge</a> and a small chance to spawn a <a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_gorilla\" title=\"Mountain gorilla\">Mountain gorilla</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17121, 2381, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>', 2),
(17124, 2375, 'Description', 'Description', 'A round crystal ball the size of your hand, with a treacherous red glow dancing amidst dark vapors inside.', '<p><i>A round crystal ball the size of your hand, with a treacherous red glow dancing amidst dark vapors inside.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17125, 2375, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The glass orb itself is 99QL and is worth a lords ransom : 2.5 Gold. Activation (use) starts a 20 second countdown, at the end of which a infected wound is dealt to all players and mobs within a 5x5 centred on the user, with chance to resist it completely based on soul strength . Ignores armor and can do up to 50 damage before DR. Has an extremely high chance to fail upon use, if it fails it will instead kill the user unless they resist it. Has a 1 hour cooldown between uses. Uses 10 charges.', '<ul><li>The glass orb itself is 99QL and is worth a lords ransom : 2.5 Gold.</li>\n<li>Activation (use) starts a 20 second countdown, at the end of which a infected <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wound</a> is dealt to all players and mobs within a 5x5 centred on the user, with chance to resist it completely based on <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_strength\" title=\"Soul strength\">soul strength</a>. Ignores armor and can do up to 50 damage before DR.</li>\n<li>Has an extremely high chance to fail upon use, if it fails it will instead kill the user unless they resist it.</li>\n<li>Has a 1 hour cooldown between uses. Uses 10 charges.</li></ul>', 1),
(17126, 2375, 'Examples of use', 'Examples_of_use', 'The Orb of Doom was used twice in early April 2012 during a battle on the Elevation Server of the Epic cluster in which The Mongol Empire killed (approximately) 44 players from all other kingdoms. At this point it  had a cooldown of only 10 minutes. [20:06:07] A pulse surges through the air. Moirai activates the Orb of Doom!  (Sending end) [20:06:27] A deadly field surges through the air from the location of Moirai and the Orb of Doom!   (Receiving end) [20:50:59] A pulse surges through the air. Moirai activates the Orb of Doom!  (Sending end) [14:29:21] Evarya uses her Orb of Doom! [14:29:21] Evarya is dead. R.I.P. (Failed use)', '<p>The Orb of Doom was used twice in early April 2012 during a battle on the Elevation Server of the Epic cluster in which The Mongol Empire killed (approximately) 44 players from all other kingdoms. At this point it  had a cooldown of only 10 minutes. \n</p>\n<p>[20:06:07] A pulse surges through the air. Moirai activates the Orb of Doom!  (Sending end)\n</p>\n<p>[20:06:27] A deadly field surges through the air from the location of Moirai and the Orb of Doom!   (Receiving end)\n</p>\n<p>[20:50:59] A pulse surges through the air. Moirai activates the Orb of Doom!  (Sending end)\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n[14:29:21] Evarya uses her Orb of Doom! [14:29:21] Evarya is dead. R.I.P. (Failed use)\n</p>', 2),
(17127, 2375, 'History', 'History', 'This artifact was first revealed on Wild (now Chaos ) by Jotz 7-15-2009', '<p>This artifact was first revealed on Wild (now <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>) by Jotz 7-15-2009\n</p>', 3),
(17128, 2369, 'Description', 'Description', 'A three foot long golden rod with a head covered with red gems.', '<p><i>A three foot long golden rod with a head covered with red gems.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17129, 2369, 'Use', 'Use', 'Carrying this rod in inventory gives a 20% weapon damage buff in PvP only. Does not effect other Artifacts. Activation sets Favor to 90% of your faith and gives Forest giant strength to Fo followers, and Phantasms to non-Fo followers.', '<ul><li>Carrying this rod in inventory gives a 20% weapon damage buff in PvP only. Does not effect other Artifacts.</li>\n<li>Activation sets <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">Favor</a> to 90% of your faith and gives <a href=\"/index.php/Forest_giant_strength\" title=\"Forest giant strength\">Forest giant strength</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> followers, and <a href=\"/index.php/Phantasms\" title=\"Phantasms\">Phantasms</a> to non-Fo followers.</li></ul>', 1),
(17130, 2369, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>', 2),
(17134, 2373, 'Description', 'Description', 'A ball made of twigs with a green gem inside.', '<p><i>A ball made of twigs with a green gem inside.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17135, 2373, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Using on an animal tames them instantly, with a guaranteed 50 power tame. Activating gives Fo followers Oakshell and has a small chance to spawn a Wild boar .', '<ul><li>Using on an animal tames them instantly, with a guaranteed 50 power tame.</li>\n<li>Activating gives <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> followers <a href=\"/index.php/Oakshell\" title=\"Oakshell\">Oakshell</a> and has a small chance to spawn a <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_boar\" title=\"Wild boar\">Wild boar</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17136, 2373, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Cooldown is 1 hour.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Cooldown is 1 hour.</li></ul>', 2),
(17137, 2370, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge brutal warhammer made totally from bronze.', '<p><i>A huge brutal warhammer made totally from bronze.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17138, 2370, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Extremely powerful weapon, although heavy and slow to use. Activation gives the message \"You feel the light of *your deity * shine upon you.\" Life transfer effect. Followers of Magranon get bonuses when using this weapon. Using gives Warhammer skill', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Extremely powerful weapon, although heavy and slow to use.</li>\n<li>Activation gives the message \"You feel the light of *your <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deity\" title=\"Deity\">deity</a>* shine upon you.\"</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Life_transfer\" title=\"Life transfer\">Life transfer</a> effect.</li>\n<li>Followers of Magranon get bonuses when using this weapon.</li>\n<li>Using gives <a href=\"/index.php/Warhammer\" title=\"Warhammer\">Warhammer</a> skill</li></ul>', 1),
(17155, 4394, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Fighting > Defensive fighting Mind > Mind speed Body > Body control', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a> &gt; Defensive fighting</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_speed\" title=\"Mind speed\">Mind speed</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>', 0),
(17156, 4394, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Defensive at 50 skill Steadfast at 70 skill Guardian at 90 skill Unyielding at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Defensive at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Steadfast at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Guardian at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Unyielding at 100 skill</li></ul>', 1),
(17157, 4394, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fighting Aggressive fighting Defensive fighting Normal fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Aggressive_fighting\" title=\"Aggressive fighting\">Aggressive fighting</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Defensive fighting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Normal_fighting\" title=\"Normal fighting\">Normal fighting</a></li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(17158, 4395, 'Description', 'Description', 'Weaponless fighting is the fighting ability to hit an opponent using fists and feet only, without a weapon .', '<p><b>Weaponless fighting</b> is the <a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">fighting</a> ability to hit an opponent using fists and feet only, without a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Weapon\" title=\"Weapon\">weapon</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(17159, 4395, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To fight weaponlessly with the hands, the player must not be holding (have equipped) a weapon. To fight weaponlessly with the feet (kicking), the player\'s waist and legs must be free and movable, thus the player must not be wearing pants. Skill is gained only through successful hits in which damage is also dealt. A hit that deals no damage offers no subsequent skill gain. It is not believed that wearing shoes or gloves has an effect on hit damage or the chance to hit. ~Further confirmation pending here~ The damage inflicted through weaponless fighting hits is greatly (but not totally) dependent on the player\'s strength . Weaponless fighting skill can only be gained for a maximum of 10 minutes per target. Upon reaching 10 minutes of weaponless fighting on a particular target, weaponless fighting skill will no longer be gained (cooldown period unknown). Another target may then be engaged for continued gains up to 10 minutes again with no limits on how many new targets may be engaged for further skillgain.', '<ul><li>To fight weaponlessly with the hands, the player must not be holding (have equipped) a weapon.</li>\n<li>To fight weaponlessly with the feet (kicking), the player\'s waist and legs must be free and movable, thus the player must not be wearing pants.</li>\n<li>Skill is gained only through successful hits in which damage is also dealt. A hit that deals no damage offers no subsequent skill gain.</li>\n<li>It is not believed that wearing shoes or gloves has an effect on hit damage or the chance to hit. ~Further confirmation pending here~</li>\n<li>The damage inflicted through weaponless fighting hits is greatly (but not totally) dependent on the player\'s <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">strength</a>.</li>\n<li>Weaponless fighting skill can only be gained for a maximum of 10 minutes per target. Upon reaching 10 minutes of weaponless fighting on a particular target, weaponless fighting skill will no longer be gained (cooldown period unknown). Another target may then be engaged for continued gains up to 10 minutes again with no limits on how many new targets may be engaged for further skillgain.</li></ul>', 1),
(17160, 4395, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Fighting > Weaponless fighting Body > Body control Mind > Mind speed', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a> &gt; Weaponless fighting</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_speed\" title=\"Mind speed\">Mind speed</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17161, 4395, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Lightweight at 50 skill Middleweight at 70 skill Heavyweight at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Lightweight at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Middleweight at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Heavyweight at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(17162, 4393, 'Description', 'Description', 'Aggressive fighting style is the opposite of defensive fighting . Higher damage is dealt (133% max) and two-handed weapon speed is increased by up to one second; however, defenses are reduced. This type of fighting works well when you fight with a group of people, but are not the one taking the hits and needing to defend yourself. You hit more often but parry less. Axes are considered good weapons for aggressive fighting, since they do not parry anyway. It can be toggled via the \"fight window\". If the fight window is not displayed it can be toggled through the menu by pressing the \"o\" key.', '<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Aggressive fighting</a> style is the opposite of <a href=\"/index.php/Defensive_fighting\" title=\"Defensive fighting\">defensive fighting</a>. Higher damage is dealt (133% max) and two-handed weapon speed is increased by up to one second; however, defenses are reduced. This type of fighting works well when you fight with a group of people, but are not the one taking the hits and needing to defend yourself. You hit more often but parry less. Axes are considered good weapons for aggressive fighting, since they do not parry anyway.\n</p>\n<p>It can be toggled via the \"fight window\". If the fight window is not displayed it can be toggled through the menu by pressing the \"o\" key.\n</p>', 0),
(17163, 4393, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Fighting > Aggressive fighting Body > Body control Mind > Mind speed', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a> &gt; Aggressive fighting</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_speed\" title=\"Mind speed\">Mind speed</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17164, 4393, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Feisty at 50 skill Belligerent at 70 skill Barbarian at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Feisty at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Belligerent at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Barbarian at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(17165, 4393, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Fighting Aggressive fighting Defensive fighting Normal fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Aggressive fighting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Defensive_fighting\" title=\"Defensive fighting\">Defensive fighting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Normal_fighting\" title=\"Normal fighting\">Normal fighting</a></li></ul></li></ul>', 3),
(17166, 4397, 'Description', 'Description', 'The prepared hide of an animal. Leather is created from the hide of a butchered animal. 0.10kg of lye is required to turn 3.00kg of hide into 3.00kg of leather. You may use larger quantities of both lye and hide , only the amount required will be used. The quality of the lye affects the creation chance.', '<p><i>The prepared hide of an animal.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Leather</b> is created from the <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_hide\" title=\"Animal hide\"> hide</a> of a <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchered</a> animal.\n</p>\n<p>0.10kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">lye</a> is required to turn 3.00kg of hide into 3.00kg of leather. You may use larger quantities of both <a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">lye</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_hide\" title=\"Animal hide\"> hide</a>, only the amount required will be used. The quality of the lye affects the creation chance.\n</p>', 0),
(17167, 4397, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Leather is used for creating and improving leatherworking items. Improving leather items is not limited by leather QL. This item is unique in this way.', '<p>Leather is used for creating and improving <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leatherworking</a> items. Improving leather items is not limited by leather QL. This item is unique in this way.\n</p>', 1),
(17168, 4397, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failure to produce leather will use 0.05kg of the lye and 0.30kg of the hide. You need a hide with a weight of at least 3.00kg to start.', '<ul><li>Failure to produce leather will use 0.05kg of the lye and 0.30kg of the hide.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>You need a hide with a weight of at least 3.00kg to start.</li></ul>', 2),
(17169, 4397, 'Other creation methods', 'Other_creation_methods', 'Please see Leather pieces for an alternative method of making leather.', '<p>Please see <a href=\"/index.php/Leather_pieces\" title=\"Leather pieces\">Leather pieces</a> for an alternative method of making leather.\n</p>', 3),
(17175, 4400, 'Description', 'Description', 'Small pieces of leather.', '<p><i>Small pieces of leather.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17176, 4400, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Leather pieces are created as a side-product of leatherworking or as a result of failing to create a leather item. They can be combined together and re-stitched into leather by using a needle on the pieces bundle and choosing Create>Resources>leather . Requires at least 4.5kg of leather pieces to create a 3kg piece of leather .', '<ul><li>Leather pieces are created as a side-product of <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">leatherworking</a> or as a result of failing to create a leather item. They can be combined together and re-stitched into <a href=\"/index.php/Leather\" title=\"Leather\">leather</a> by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Needle\" title=\"Needle\">needle</a> on the pieces bundle and choosing <i>Create&gt;Resources&gt;leather</i>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Requires at least 4.5kg of leather pieces to create a 3kg piece of <a href=\"/index.php/Leather\" title=\"Leather\">leather</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17177, 4401, 'Description', 'Description', 'A backpack made from leather with metal husks.', '<p><i>A backpack made from leather with metal husks.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17178, 4401, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Bjarne Backpack Bunny Backpack', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Bjarne Backpack </a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Bunny Backpack </a></li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(17179, 4401, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'By storing items in a backpack players are able to carry more than 100 items , which is the normal inventory limit, however, the weight of the items will still count towards your maximum weight limit (7 * body strength ). Like other leather items, a backpack will NOT take damage from being heated in a forge . This makes them useful when smithing (or cooking) in a forge since you can put more than 100 items in the forge plus you can sort the items easier. For cooking, a backpack will hold a maximum of 37 frying pans , 29 sauce pans or 8 pottery bowls .', '<ul><li>By storing items in a backpack players are able to carry more than 100 <a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">items</a>, which is the normal <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> limit, however, the weight of the items will still count towards your maximum <a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">weight</a> limit (7 * <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>).</li>\n<li>Like other leather items, a backpack will NOT take damage from being heated in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>. This makes them useful when smithing (or cooking) in a forge since you can put more than 100 items in the forge plus you can sort the items easier.</li>\n<li>For cooking, a backpack will hold a maximum of 37 <a href=\"/index.php/Frying_pan\" title=\"Frying pan\">frying pans</a>, 29 <a href=\"/index.php/Sauce_pan\" title=\"Sauce pan\">sauce pans</a> or 8 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">pottery bowls</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(17180, 4401, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Satchel Container', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Satchel\" title=\"Satchel\">Satchel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">Container</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17182, 4403, 'Description', 'Description', 'A glove made from leather.', '<p><i>A glove made from leather.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17183, 4403, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your hands. You will need one for each hand. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your hands. You will need one for each hand.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17184, 4403, 'Enchantments and runes', 'Enchantments_and_runes', 'Magical enchantments and runes on gloves affect actions that require hands: crafting clay items, improving clay items with the hand, forage, botanise. Since: Patch Notes 05-DEC-2023 Only magical effects such as runes and spell enchantments function for this purpose. For example, Wind of Ages will improve action speed and Circle of Cunning will improve skill gain. The glove is not being used as an actual tool, so it will not receive damage, and its quality, rarity, and material will have no impact on effectiveness. However, like a tool, enchantments will still decay from use. Enchantment/Rune effectiveness is averaged between both gloves. For example, having 100 Wind of Ages on one glove and 50 on the other will be equivalent to having 75 Wind of Ages on a tool, and having a rune on one glove but not the other will result in that rune being half as effective as usual.', '<ul><li>Magical enchantments and runes on gloves affect actions that require hands: crafting clay items, improving clay items with the hand, forage, botanise. Since: <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/199861-patch-notes-05-dec-2023/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Patch Notes 05-DEC-2023</a></li>\n<li>Only magical effects such as runes and spell enchantments function for this purpose. For example, Wind of Ages will improve action speed and Circle of Cunning will improve skill gain.</li>\n<li>The glove is not being used as an actual tool, so it will not receive damage, and its quality, rarity, and material will have no impact on effectiveness. However, like a tool, enchantments will still decay from use.</li>\n<li>Enchantment/Rune effectiveness is averaged between both gloves. For example, having 100 Wind of Ages on one glove and 50 on the other will be equivalent to having 75 Wind of Ages on a tool, and having a rune on one glove but not the other will result in that rune being half as effective as usual.</li></ul>', 2),
(17185, 4403, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17186, 4404, 'Description', 'Description', 'A jacket made from leather with wooden husks.', '<p><i>A jacket made from leather with wooden husks.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17187, 4404, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your torso. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your torso.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17188, 4404, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17198, 4408, 'Description', 'Description', 'A leather cap with ear flaps and a strap .', '<p><i>A leather cap with ear flaps and a strap</i>. \n</p>', 0),
(17199, 4408, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your head and face. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your head and face.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17200, 4408, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17211, 4411, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small square table.', '<p><i>A small square table.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17212, 4411, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot be picked up after completion. It is a fairly high table, reaching up to just below your chest. Able to have items placed on it.', '<ul><li>Cannot be picked up after completion.</li>\n<li>It is a fairly high table, reaching up to just below your chest.</li>\n<li>Able to have items placed on it.</li></ul>', 1),
(17221, 3075, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine pelt, skinned from an animal.', '<p><i>A fine pelt, skinned from an animal.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17222, 3075, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Butchered from animals. Used improving smithing and carpentry items. Cannot be repaired , except with Mend spell. Decay can be avoided by storing it in inventory , a bank , a merchant , or a Magic chest . Pelt quality directly affects the speed and success rate experienced while using the pelt. Table of animals that yield pelts of different weight below. Animal Weight (kg) Dog 0.6 Large rat 0.2 Mountain lion 0.4 Wild cat 0.8 The weight of a mountain lion pelt can be reduced by producing a mountain lion rug from part of it. After that operation it will weight 0.1', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">Butchered</a> from animals.</li>\n<li>Used improving smithing and carpentry items.</li>\n<li>Cannot be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Repair\" title=\"Repair\">repaired</a>, except with <a href=\"/index.php/Mend\" title=\"Mend\">Mend</a> spell. <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">Decay</a> can be avoided by storing it in <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a>, a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bank\" title=\"Bank\">bank</a>, a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Merchant\" title=\"Merchant\">merchant</a>, or a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Magic_chest\" title=\"Magic chest\">Magic chest</a>.</li>\n<li>Pelt quality directly affects the speed and success rate experienced while using the pelt.</li>\n<li>Table of animals that yield pelts of different weight below.</li></ul>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" width=\"100\">Animal</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">Weight</a> (kg)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Dog\" title=\"Dog\">Dog</a></td>\n<td>0.6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_rat\" title=\"Large rat\">Large rat</a></td>\n<td>0.2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_lion\" title=\"Mountain lion\">Mountain lion</a></td>\n<td>0.4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wild_cat\" title=\"Wild cat\">Wild cat</a></td>\n<td>0.8\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li>The weight of a mountain lion pelt can be reduced by producing a <a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_lion_rug\" title=\"Mountain lion rug\">mountain lion rug</a> from part of it. After that operation it will weight 0.1</li></ul>', 1),
(17228, 4415, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tool for working the fields.', '<p><i>A tool for working the fields.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17229, 4415, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used for farming fields. Can be used to cut down trees, though not recommended.', '<ul><li>Used for <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a> fields.</li>\n<li>Can be used to cut down trees, though not recommended.</li></ul>', 1),
(17230, 4415, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The newbie version from the starter kit is made of birchwood, cannot be improved, and will burn if placed in a fire. The QL of the rake slightly effects the timer. Maximum creation QL is 1/5 of blacksmithing skill.', '<ul><li>The newbie version from the starter kit is made of birchwood, cannot be improved, and will burn if placed in a fire.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the rake slightly effects the timer.</li>\n<li>Maximum creation QL is 1/5 of <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">blacksmithing</a> skill.</li></ul>', 2),
(17231, 4415, 'Skills & Characterics', 'Skills_.26_Characterics', 'When using a rake Miscellaneous items > Rake When creating a rake Smithing > Blacksmithing', '<p>When using a rake\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Rake</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a rake\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17232, 4415, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Cultivator at 50 skill Furrower at 70 skill Harrower at 90 skill We are farmers at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Cultivator at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Furrower at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Harrower at 90 skill</li>\n<li>We are farmers at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(17262, 4423, 'Description', 'Description', 'A very short and sharp curved blade on a shaft, used to carve in leather.', '<p><i>A very short and sharp curved blade on a shaft, used to carve in leather.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17263, 4423, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to improve leather items by cutting away excess leather.', '<ul><li>Used to <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improve</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_item\" title=\"Leather item\">leather items</a> by cutting away excess leather.</li></ul>', 1),
(17264, 4423, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Leatherworking', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking\" title=\"Leatherworking\">Leatherworking</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17270, 4426, 'Description', 'Description', 'A leather glove strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>A leather glove strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17271, 4426, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your hands. You will need one for each hand. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the glove and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your hands. You will need one for each hand.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the glove and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 1),
(17272, 4426, 'Enchantments and runes', 'Enchantments_and_runes', 'Magical enchantments and runes on gloves affect actions that require hands: crafting clay items, improving clay items with the hand, forage, botanise. Since: Patch Notes 05-DEC-2023 Only magical effects such as runes and spell enchantments function for this purpose. For example, Wind of Ages will improve action speed and Circle of Cunning will improve skill gain. The glove is not being used as an actual tool, so it will not receive damage, and its quality, rarity, and material will have no impact on effectiveness. However, like a tool, enchantments will still decay from use. Enchantment/Rune effectiveness is averaged between both gloves. For example, having 100 Wind of Ages on one glove and 50 on the other will be equivalent to having 75 Wind of Ages on a tool, and having a rune on one glove but not the other will result in that rune being half as effective as usual.', '<ul><li>Magical enchantments and runes on gloves affect actions that require hands: crafting clay items, improving clay items with the hand, forage, botanise. Since: <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/199861-patch-notes-05-dec-2023/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Patch Notes 05-DEC-2023</a></li>\n<li>Only magical effects such as runes and spell enchantments function for this purpose. For example, Wind of Ages will improve action speed and Circle of Cunning will improve skill gain.</li>\n<li>The glove is not being used as an actual tool, so it will not receive damage, and its quality, rarity, and material will have no impact on effectiveness. However, like a tool, enchantments will still decay from use.</li>\n<li>Enchantment/Rune effectiveness is averaged between both gloves. For example, having 100 Wind of Ages on one glove and 50 on the other will be equivalent to having 75 Wind of Ages on a tool, and having a rune on one glove but not the other will result in that rune being half as effective as usual.</li></ul>', 2),
(17273, 4426, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17274, 4427, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine leather jacket strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>A fine leather jacket strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17275, 4427, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your torso. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the jacket and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your torso.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the jacket and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 1),
(17276, 4427, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17277, 4428, 'Description', 'Description', 'Leg protection made from leather strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>Leg protection made from leather strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17278, 4428, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your legs. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the pants and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your legs.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the pants and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 1),
(17279, 4428, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17280, 4429, 'Description', 'Description', 'A leather boot strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>A leather boot strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17281, 4429, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your feet. You will need one for each foot. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the boot and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your feet. You will need one for each foot.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the boot and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 1),
(17282, 4429, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17283, 4430, 'Description', 'Description', 'Leather sewn into a cylinder to protect the arms and strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>Leather sewn into a cylinder to protect the arms and strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(17284, 4430, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the sleeve and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the sleeve and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 1),
(17285, 4430, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17286, 4431, 'Description', 'Description', 'A leather cap strengthened with metal studs.', '<p><i>A leather cap strengthened with metal studs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17287, 4431, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Executioner Hood', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Executioner Hood</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17288, 4431, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your head and face. Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as leather armour . Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between walking and attack speed. Failure during creation damages the cap and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets. Higher rivet quality will increase your chance of success when creating. The material type of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself. Rarity is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.', '<ul><li>Armour for your head and face.</li>\n<li>Studded leather armour generally provides a moderate amount of base defense with similar penalties as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leather_armour\" title=\"Category:Leather armour\">leather armour</a>. Studded leather armour represents a good common ground between <a href=\"/index.php/Speed\" title=\"Speed\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> during creation damages the cap and consumes 0.05 kg of rivets.</li>\n<li>Higher rivet <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> will increase your chance of success when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">material type</a> of the rivets currently has no effect on the armour itself.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Rarity\" title=\"Rarity\">Rarity</a> is lost when adding rivets as the process creates a new item.</li></ul>', 2),
(17289, 4431, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Leather armour Chain armour Plate armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour\" title=\"Chain armour\">Chain armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17302, 4436, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pendulum with a fine chain and a well-polished ball. A hanging weight which can be used for divination to find a water source which can be tapped by building a fountain or well on the indicated spot. There is no skill involved in doing this but the quality of the pendulum affects your divination chances.', '<p><i>A pendulum with a fine chain and a well-polished ball.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A hanging weight which can be used for <a href=\"/index.php/Water_divining\" title=\"Water divining\">divination</a> to find a water source which can be tapped by building a <a href=\"/index.php/Fountain\" title=\"Fountain\">fountain</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Well\" title=\"Well\">well</a> on the indicated spot. There is no skill involved in doing this but the quality of the pendulum affects your divination chances.\n</p>', 0),
(17303, 4436, 'Pendulum Spells', 'Pendulum_Spells', 'A pendulum can also have other functions if the appropriate spell has been cast upon it. These are: Lurker in the woods - Locates champion animals Lurker in the deep - Locates rare fishes Lurker in the dark - Locates nearby enemies', '<p>A pendulum can also have other functions if the appropriate spell has been cast upon it. These are:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_woods\" title=\"Lurker in the woods\">Lurker in the woods</a> - Locates champion animals</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_deep\" title=\"Lurker in the deep\">Lurker in the deep</a> - Locates rare fishes</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_dark\" title=\"Lurker in the dark\">Lurker in the dark</a> - Locates nearby enemies</li></ul>', 1),
(17304, 4436, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The QL of the chain affects chance of crafting success. The ball must be glowing hot. The material the ball is made from determines what type of material the pendulum is made of, and therefore determines what it can be improved with. Wind of ages is effective to decrease the action timer. In regards to Dispel enchanting practices, WOA is listed first and then Lurker effects. In regards to Lurker in the deep , The QL of the pendulum seems to affect the chance of getting a reading and the power level of the spell seems to affect the range at which fish are detected. Enchanting a pendulum with any lurker spell ( Lurker in the deep , Lurker in the woods , and Lurker in the dark ) will make the pendulum unable to find water. If you get the message \"You fail to make sense of the pendulum\", you have failed to get a reading and will need to try again. It may take a few attempts to get a reading, which is dependent on the QL of the pendulum.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the chain affects chance of crafting success.</li>\n<li>The ball must be glowing hot.</li>\n<li>The material the ball is made from determines what type of material the pendulum is made of, and therefore determines what it can be improved with.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_ages\" title=\"Wind of ages\">Wind of ages</a> is effective to decrease the action timer.</li>\n<li>In regards to <a href=\"/index.php/Dispel\" title=\"Dispel\">Dispel</a> enchanting practices, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/WOA\" title=\"WOA\">WOA</a> is listed first and then Lurker effects.</li>\n<li>In regards to <a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_deep\" title=\"Lurker in the deep\">Lurker in the deep</a>, The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the pendulum seems to affect the chance of getting a reading and the power level of the spell seems to affect the range at which <a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a> are detected.</li>\n<li>Enchanting a pendulum with any lurker spell ( <a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_deep\" title=\"Lurker in the deep\">Lurker in the deep</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_woods\" title=\"Lurker in the woods\">Lurker in the woods</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Lurker_in_the_dark\" title=\"Lurker in the dark\">Lurker in the dark</a> ) will make the pendulum unable to find water.</li>\n<li>If you get the message \"You fail to make sense of the pendulum\", you have failed to get a reading and will need to try again. It may take a few attempts to get a reading, which is dependent on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the pendulum.</li></ul>', 2),
(17305, 3199, 'Description', 'Description', 'A delicate tree sprout with a few tender leaves. A tree or a bush sprout used for some tools or for planting.', '<p><i>A delicate tree sprout with a few tender leaves.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Tree#Bushes\" title=\"Tree\">bush</a> sprout used for some tools or for planting.\n</p>', 0),
(17306, 3199, 'Method', 'Method', 'To pick a sprout: Activate a sickle , right click > Nature on tree or bush and select Pick sprout . Only trees aged mature to very old will produce a sprout, if a tree of this age does not hold a sprout then it\'s possible another player has already picked it. To plant a sprout: Activate the sprout, right click > Nature and select \'Plant naturally\' or \'Plant in center\' on a dirt or grass tile. The quality and damage of a sprout, and gardening skill, affects the chance of successfully planting it.', '<ul><li>To pick a sprout: Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>, <b>right click</b> &gt; <b>Nature</b> on tree or bush and select <b>Pick sprout</b>.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Only trees <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">aged</a> mature to very old will produce a sprout, if a tree of this age does not hold a sprout then it\'s possible another player has already picked it.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li>To <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">plant</a> a sprout: Activate the sprout, <b>right click</b> &gt; <b>Nature</b> and select \'Plant naturally\' or \'Plant in center\' on a <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a> tile.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> of a sprout, and <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">gardening</a> skill, affects the chance of successfully planting it.</dd></dl>', 1),
(17307, 3199, 'Other Uses', 'Other_Uses', 'Making a fruit press . Making a cheese drill . Planting hedges .', '<ul><li>Making a <a href=\"/index.php/Fruit_press\" title=\"Fruit press\">fruit press</a>.</li>\n<li>Making a <a href=\"/index.php/Cheese_drill\" title=\"Cheese drill\">cheese drill</a>.</li>\n<li>Planting <a href=\"/index.php/Hedges\" title=\"Hedges\">hedges</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(17308, 3199, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Sprout quality does not determine tree quality nor does it have any affect in growth rate. If a sprout is not picked, the tree will attempt to seed itself to a random nearby tile when it advances to the next stage of growth. If the tile is not \"available\" (grass or  flower tile) then the sprout is wasted. Not to be confused with a seedling .', '<ul><li>Sprout quality does not determine tree quality nor does it have any affect in growth rate.</li>\n<li>If a sprout is not picked, the tree will attempt to seed itself to a random nearby tile when it advances to the next stage of growth. If the tile is not \"available\" (grass or  flower tile) then the sprout is wasted.</li>\n<li>Not to be confused with a <a href=\"/index.php/Seedling\" title=\"Seedling\">seedling</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(17309, 3199, 'Skills used', 'Skills_used', 'Forestry (picking sprouts) Gardening (planting sprouts)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a> (picking sprouts)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">Gardening</a> (planting sprouts)</li></ul>', 4),
(17317, 1726, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a spell that can not only destroy normal altars , but it can also damage the Bone Altar and the Altar of Three , (referred to as \'huge\' altars in the spell list). This spell requires 20 favor to cast against normal altars, but 80 when cast against the Bone Altar or Altar of Three. It will give you rather nasty wounds if you fail in the cast.', '<p>This is a spell that can not only destroy normal <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altars</a>, but it can also damage the <a href=\"/index.php/Bone_Altar\" title=\"Bone Altar\">Bone Altar</a> and the <a href=\"/index.php/Altar_of_Three\" title=\"Altar of Three\">Altar of Three</a>, (referred to as \'huge\' altars in the spell list). This spell requires 20 favor to cast against normal altars, but 80 when cast against the Bone Altar or Altar of Three. It will give you rather nasty wounds if you fail in the cast.\n</p>', 0),
(17318, 1726, 'Destroying the main WL / BL altar', 'Destroying_the_main_WL_.2F_BL_altar', 'To be able to destroy the black or white main altar it is imperative that the following requirements are met : Enough followers of your faith with high faith. (5000 faith) Enough followers of your faith at the altar. Someone who can cast the spell or through the use of the right artifact . Priests must have 23 body strength', '<p>To be able to destroy the black or white main altar it is imperative that the following requirements are met :\n</p>\n<ul><li>Enough followers of your faith with high faith. (5000 faith)</li>\n<li>Enough followers of your faith at the altar.</li>\n<li>Someone who can cast the spell or <a href=\"/index.php/Sceptre_of_ascension\" title=\"Sceptre of ascension\">through the use</a> of the right <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Artifact\" title=\"Category:Artifact\">artifact</a>.</li>\n<li>Priests must have 23 body strength</li></ul>', 1),
(17336, 4405, 'Description', 'Description', 'Leg protection made from leather.', '<p><i>Leg protection made from leather.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17337, 4405, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your legs. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your legs.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17338, 4405, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17339, 2426, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sleeves made from plain white fabric.', '<p><i>Sleeves made from plain white fabric.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17340, 2426, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm. Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality. However, it has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate. A higher quality needle increases your chance at creating. Failure creating will consume 0.02 kg of square piece of cloth.', '<ul><li>Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm.</li>\n<li>Cloth armour is the weakest of all, with 40% damage reduction at 100 quality. However, it has no penalty to walking speed, and offers the highest evasion rate.</li>\n<li>A higher quality needle increases your chance at creating.</li>\n<li>Failure creating will consume 0.02 kg of square piece of cloth.</li></ul>', 1),
(17341, 2426, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Cloth armour Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17342, 4407, 'Description', 'Description', 'Leather sewn into a cylinder to protect the arms.', '<p><i>Leather sewn into a cylinder to protect the arms.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17343, 4407, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your arms. You will need one for each arm.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17344, 4407, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17345, 4406, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sturdy boot made from leather.', '<p><i>A sturdy boot made from leather.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17346, 4406, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Armour for your feet. You will need one for each foot. Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to walking and attack speed. A higher quality needle increases your success chance for creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to use some quality. Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage. Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.', '<ul><li>Armour for your feet. You will need one for each foot.</li>\n<li>Leather armour generally provides a low amount of base defense. However, it also has the smallest penalties to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">walking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Attack\" title=\"Attack\">attack</a> speed.</li>\n<li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needle increases your success chance for creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to use some quality.</li>\n<li>Offers a defense bonus against bashing damage.</li>\n<li>Suffers higher damage from cutting damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(17347, 4406, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Armour Armour types Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting#Armour_types\" title=\"Fighting\">Armour types</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17358, 2680, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cluster of small light blue flowers with a sweet scent.', '<p><i>A cluster of small light blue flowers with a sweet scent.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(17359, 2680, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in some cooking recipes. Can be used in alchemy to make healing covers (healing potency 2). Lavender flowers are gathered from mature or older lavender bushes or botanized from Wildflowers nodes.', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> (healing potency 2).</li>\n<li>Lavender flowers are gathered from mature or older <a href=\"/index.php/Lavender_bush\" title=\"Lavender bush\">lavender bushes</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Botanize\" title=\"Botanize\">botanized</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> nodes.</li></ul>', 1),
(17360, 4454, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see part of the lands of Wurm', '<p><i>You see part of the lands of Wurm</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17361, 4454, 'Benefits', 'Benefits', 'Walking on gravel is faster than walking on naturally occurring tiles, but slower than cobblestone or slabs. Gravel lanes and paths are usually used as a quick improvement over packed dirt or for aesthetic effect.', '<ul><li>Walking on gravel is faster than walking on naturally occurring tiles, but slower than cobblestone or slabs.</li>\n<li>Gravel lanes and paths are usually used as a quick improvement over <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> or for aesthetic effect.</li></ul>', 1),
(17362, 4454, 'Making gravel', 'Making_gravel', 'Activate a stone shards (20.00kg) Right-click a tile of packed dirt and select Pave . Note : You can also right-click a paved tile and select Re-pave > Tile or Nearest corner', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> (20.00kg)</li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Packed_dirt\" title=\"Packed dirt\">packed dirt</a> and select <a href=\"/index.php/Paving\" title=\"Paving\">Pave</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><i>Note</i>: You can also right-click a paved tile and select <i>Re-pave</i> &gt; <i>Tile</i> or <i>Nearest corner</i>\n</p>', 2),
(17363, 4454, 'Destroying gravel', 'Destroying_gravel', 'Activate a shovel Right-click a tile of cobblestone and select Destroy Pavement.', '<ul><li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a tile of cobblestone and select Destroy Pavement.</li></ul>', 3),
(17364, 4454, 'Notes', 'Notes', '20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy gravel. Vynora followers and priests will need to go \'unfaithful\' to destroy gravel. Gravel tiles have a chance of decaying if they are not walked on for an extended period of time. Outdoor gravel tiles do not amass collectible snow during the Wurm winter. The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Gravel: Mineral debris , Rubble , Snow pile , and Lichen .', '<ul><li>20 body strength and 10 digging skill is needed to destroy gravel.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Follower\" title=\"Follower\">followers</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> will need to go \'unfaithful\' to destroy gravel.</li>\n<li>Gravel tiles have a chance of decaying if they are not walked on for an extended period of time.</li>\n<li>Outdoor gravel tiles do not amass collectible snow during the Wurm winter.</li>\n<li>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Gravel: <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rubble\" title=\"Rubble\">Rubble</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Snow_pile\" title=\"Snow pile\">Snow pile</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Lichen\" title=\"Lichen\">Lichen</a>.</li></ul>', 4),
(17367, 4456, 'Icon', 'Icon', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Faithful.png\"><img alt=\"Faithful.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"31\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"32\" src=\"/images/2/21/Faithful.png\" width=\"31\"/></a>\n</p>', 0),
(17368, 4457, 'Icon', 'Icon', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Lawful.png\"><img alt=\"Lawful.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"31\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"32\" src=\"/images/1/10/Lawful.png\" width=\"31\"/></a>\n</p>', 0),
(17369, 4458, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'Mojang Specifications was the former name of the company that develops and runs Wurm Online, it\'s name is \"inspired\" by the swedish word Mojäng. The company has been renamed to Onetoofree AB, and then renamed once again to Code Club AB, as on 10/12/11. On what mojäng means in Swedish;\n\"Thingie is a good translation, it usually refers to a thingie of mechanical sort. Like, a little machine that looks like a trash bin and only jumps up and down, puffing out smoke. For instance.\" -- Svensson Mojang was run by a partnership of Rolf and Notch .', '<p>Mojang Specifications was the former name of the company that develops and runs Wurm Online, it\'s name is \"inspired\" by the swedish word Mojäng. The company has been renamed to Onetoofree AB, and then renamed once again to Code Club AB, as on 10/12/11. \n</p>\n<p>On what mojäng means in Swedish;\n\"Thingie is a good translation, it usually refers to a thingie of mechanical sort. Like, a little machine that looks like a trash bin and only jumps up and down, puffing out smoke. For instance.\" -- <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Svensson\" title=\"Player:Svensson\">Svensson</a>\n</p>\n<p>Mojang was run by a partnership of <a href=\"/index.php/User:Rolf\" title=\"User:Rolf\">Rolf</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/User:Notch\" title=\"User:Notch\">Notch</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(17409, 4469, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge yellow egg. This has a very low nutrition value\' These huge eggs are usually guarded by the dragons . They can be cracked open once they reach 80.01 damage.\nHuge eggs take damage quickly while in inventory. They are a food item.\nThey will automatically hatch if they reach 100 damage. You can taste or eat them. They will remain functional as long as they are not fully eaten.\nThey will not give timed affinity. If left on the ground, an animal could eat a huge egg. Dragon or Dragon hatchlings have a chance to hatch from them. The color is random.\nThe exact mortality rate is unknown.', '<p><i>A huge yellow egg. This has a very low nutrition value\'</i>\n</p>\n<p>These huge eggs are usually guarded by the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dragons\" title=\"Dragons\">dragons</a>. They can be cracked open once they reach 80.01 damage.\nHuge eggs take damage quickly while in inventory. They are a food item.\nThey will automatically hatch if they reach 100 damage.\n</p>\n<p>You can taste or eat them. They will remain functional as long as they are not fully eaten.\nThey will not give timed affinity.\n</p>\n<p>If left on the ground, an animal could eat a huge egg.\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/Dragon\" title=\"Dragon\">Dragon</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dragon\" title=\"Dragon\">Dragon hatchlings</a> have a chance to hatch from them. The color is random.\nThe exact mortality rate is unknown.\n</p>', 0),
(17410, 4470, 'Description', 'Description', 'Preaching is the skill used in converting other people to your religion , to hold sermons , and to take confessions . To convert someone using this skill, activate the statuette for your religion then right-click another person, and select religion->convert. Your target must have issued the command /invitations for this to work. To hold a sermon , activate the statuette then right-click an altar and select preach. New converts start with faith equal to one fifth of your preaching skill.', '<p>Preaching is the skill used in <a href=\"/index.php/Convert\" title=\"Convert\">converting</a> other people to your <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religion</a>, to hold <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">sermons</a>, and to take <a href=\"/index.php/Confession\" title=\"Confession\">confessions</a>. \n</p>\n<p>To convert someone using this skill, activate the <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> for your <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religion</a> then right-click another person, and select religion-&gt;convert. Your target must have issued the command <code>/invitations</code> for this to work.\n</p>\n<p>To hold a <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">sermon</a>, activate the <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> then right-click an altar and select preach.\n</p>\n<p>New converts start with <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> equal to one fifth of your preaching skill. \n</p>', 0),
(17411, 4470, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Religion > Preaching', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a> &gt; Preaching</li></ul>', 1),
(17412, 4470, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Preacher at 50 skill Orator at 70 skill Soothsayer at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Preacher at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Orator at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Soothsayer at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(17413, 4472, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large square dining table.', '<p><i>A large square dining table.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17414, 4472, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot be picked up after completion. It is a moderately high table at about hip height. It looks good with chairs , stools , and armchairs . Able to have items placed on it.', '<ul><li>Cannot be picked up after completion.</li>\n<li>It is a moderately high table at about hip height.</li>\n<li>It looks good with <a href=\"/index.php/Chair\" title=\"Chair\">chairs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stool\" title=\"Stool\">stools</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Armchair\" title=\"Armchair\">armchairs</a>.</li>\n<li>Able to have items placed on it.</li></ul>', 1),
(17417, 4474, 'Description', 'Description', 'The healing skill currently only has one sub-skill, first aid . The first aid skill is used with the common healing items, and the channeling skill is used if it is a healing spell . No skills are used when healing with mycelium .', '<p>The <b>healing skill</b> currently only has one sub-skill, <a href=\"/index.php/First_aid\" title=\"First aid\">first aid</a>. The first aid skill is used with the common healing items, and the <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill is used if it is a healing <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a>. No skills are used when healing with <a href=\"/index.php/Mycelium\" title=\"Mycelium\">mycelium</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(17418, 4474, 'Items Used', 'Items_Used', 'Bandage Farmer\'s salve Healing covers Water', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bandage\" title=\"Bandage\">Bandage</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Farmer%27s_salve\" title=\"Farmer\'s salve\">Farmer\'s salve</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">Healing covers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17419, 4474, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Healing Mind > Mind logic Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li>Healing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17420, 4474, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Healer at 50 skill Doctor at 70 skill Surgeon at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Healer at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Doctor at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Surgeon at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(17421, 4474, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Healing spells Healing guide Mycelium Wound', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Healing_spells\" title=\"Category:Healing spells\">Healing spells</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Guides:Healing_Guide\" title=\"Guides:Healing Guide\">Healing guide</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mycelium\" title=\"Mycelium\">Mycelium</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">Wound</a></li></ul>', 4),
(17434, 3498, 'Description', 'Description', 'A handful of small, red berries with a sour and sweet taste.', '<p><i>A handful of small, red berries with a sour and sweet taste.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17435, 3498, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Lingonberries can be found by botanizing on flotsam nodes or harvesting from lingonberry bushes in season. Lingonberries can be used in cooking and pressed using a fruit press to make juice.', '<ul><li>Lingonberries can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Flotsam\" title=\"Flotsam\">flotsam</a> nodes or harvesting from <a href=\"/index.php/Lingonberry_bush\" title=\"Lingonberry bush\">lingonberry bushes</a> in season.</li>\n<li>Lingonberries can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">cooking</a> and pressed using a <a href=\"/index.php/Fruit_press\" title=\"Fruit press\">fruit press</a> to make juice.</li></ul>', 1),
(17436, 3498, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Berry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Berry\" title=\"Berry\">Berry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17501, 4451, 'Description', 'Description', 'Skill gained while creating and improving both metal and wooden shields . Influences the success ratio and the quality of the outcome.', '<p>Skill gained while creating and improving both metal and wooden <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Shields\" title=\"Category:Shields\">shields</a>. Influences the success ratio and the quality of the outcome.\n</p>', 0),
(17502, 4451, 'Items', 'Items', 'See : Category:Shield smithing items', '<p>See : <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Shield_smithing_items\" title=\"Category:Shield smithing items\">Category:Shield smithing items</a>\n</p>', 1),
(17503, 4451, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing > Armour smithing > Shield smithing Body > Body strength Body > Body control', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Armour_smithing\" title=\"Armour smithing\">Armour smithing</a> &gt; Shield smithing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17504, 4451, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Shieldsmith at 50 skill Able Shieldsmith at 70 skill Master Shieldsmith at 90 skill Forge of the Shieldwall at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Shieldsmith at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Able Shieldsmith at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Shieldsmith at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Forge of the Shieldwall at 100 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(17505, 2389, 'Description', 'Description', 'Plate armour smithing is the craft of creating and improving plate armour for battle.  Skill level influences the success ratio and the quality of the outcome. Plate armour is created using metal lumps . This is also the skill used to create dragon scale armour .', '<p>Plate armour smithing is the craft of creating and improving <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">plate armour</a> for battle.  Skill level influences the success ratio and the quality of the outcome. Plate armour is created using <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal_lump\" title=\"Metal lump\">metal lumps</a>. This is also the skill used to create <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dragon_scale_armour\" title=\"Dragon scale armour\">dragon scale armour</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(17506, 2389, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wearing your plate armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding. For information about making steel , see the metallurgy page. Use your lowest quality lump for the creation of items. A minimum of 16.1 weight is required for a full suit with great helm. You can sort your lumps either by using containers or by using the \"sort by quality\" button on the forge\'s inventory menu. Using a lump more than about 10 quality higher than what you are improving can be wasteful. However using a lump only a few quality higher than the target lowers the chance to succeed, especially at higher qualities. For efficient grinding, gauntlets use the least amount of metal to make or improve. Great Helms use more lump but are far more useful and easier to sell or trade.', '<ul><li>Wearing your plate armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding.</li>\n<li>For information about making <a href=\"/index.php/Steel\" title=\"Steel\">steel</a>, see the <a href=\"/index.php/Metallurgy\" title=\"Metallurgy\">metallurgy</a> page.</li>\n<li>Use your lowest quality lump for the creation of items.</li>\n<li>A minimum of 16.1 weight is required for a full suit with great helm.</li>\n<li>You can sort your lumps either by using containers or by using the \"sort by quality\" button on the forge\'s inventory menu. Using a lump more than about 10 quality higher than what you are improving can be wasteful. However using a lump only a few quality higher than the target lowers the chance to succeed, especially at higher qualities.</li>\n<li>For efficient grinding, <a href=\"/index.php/Plate_gauntlet\" title=\"Plate gauntlet\">gauntlets</a> use the least amount of metal to make or improve. <a href=\"/index.php/Great_helm\" title=\"Great helm\">Great Helms</a> use more lump but are far more useful and easier to sell or trade.</li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(17507, 2389, 'Plate Armour & Dragon Scale Armour Variations', 'Plate_Armour_.26_Dragon_Scale_Armour_Variations', 'Dragon scale armour Plate armour Iron plate armour with open helm Iron plate armour with great helm Iron plate armour with basinet helm Steel plate armour with open helm Steel plate armour with great helm Steel plate armour with basinet helm Brass plate armour with open helm Brass plate armour with great helm Brass plate armour with basinet helm Bronze plate armour with open helm Bronze plate armour with great helm Bronze plate armour with basinet helm Copper plate armour with open helm Copper plate armour with great helm Copper plate armour with basinet helm Lead plate armour with open helm Lead plate armour with great helm Lead plate armour with basinet helm Tin plate armour with open helm Tin plate armour with great helm Tin plate armour with basinet helm Zinc plate armour with open helm Zinc plate armour with great helm Zinc plate armour with basinet helm Gold plate armour with open helm Gold plate armour with great helm Gold plate armour with basinet helm Silver plate armour with open helm Silver plate armour with great helm Silver plate armour with basinet helm Adamantine plate armour with open helm Adamantine plate armour with great helm Adamantine plate armour with basinet helm Glimmersteel plate armour with open helm Glimmersteel plate armour with great helm Glimmersteel plate armour with basinet helm Seryll plate armour with open helm Seryll plate armour with great helm Seryll plate armour with basinet helm', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Dragon_scale_armour\">Dragon scale armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n<a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Scalepics.png\" title=\"Comparison of different scale armour colors on male wurmian.\"><img alt=\"Comparison of different scale armour colors on male wurmian.\" data-file-height=\"295\" data-file-width=\"733\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"295\" src=\"/images/e/e1/Scalepics.png\" width=\"733\"/></a>\n</p>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Plate_armour\">Plate armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<pre><br/>\n</pre>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"991\" data-file-width=\"827\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e2/Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg/313px-Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e2/Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg/470px-Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e2/Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg/626px-Armormetals-plate-iron-open.jpg 2x\" width=\"209\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 189px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Iron plate armour with open helm\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"991\" data-file-width=\"827\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/51/Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg/313px-Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/51/Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg/470px-Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/51/Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg/626px-Armormetals-plate-iron-great.jpg 2x\" width=\"209\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 189px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Iron plate armour with great helm\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"991\" data-file-width=\"827\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/55/Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg/313px-Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/55/Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg/470px-Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/55/Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg/626px-Armormetals-plate-iron-basinet.jpg 2x\" width=\"209\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 189px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Iron plate armour with basinet helm\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"991\" data-file-width=\"827\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4e/Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg/313px-Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/4e/Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg/470px-Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/4/4e/Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg/626px-Armormetals-plate-steel-open.jpg 2x\" width=\"209\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 189px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Steel plate armour with open helm\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"ima