(17765, 4553, 'Description', 'Description', 'Mushrooms can be found growing in the grassy forests of Wurm .', '<p>Mushrooms can be found growing in the grassy forests of <a href=\"/index.php/Basic_Knowledge\" title=\"Basic Knowledge\">Wurm</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(17766, 4553, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mushrooms can be found growing on grass / tree / mycelium tiles or when foraging for vegetables. Mushrooms can also be grown in a large planter . Most mushrooms can be used in alchemy to make healing covers , used as a cooking ingredient, or eaten directly. Mushrooms can also be given to a follower of a deity when praying at an altar . You can use a spoon to make it into a container for cooking recipes.', '<ul><li>Mushrooms can be found growing on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass_tiles\" title=\"Grass tiles\">grass</a>/<a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a>/<a href=\"/index.php/Mycelium\" title=\"Mycelium\">mycelium</a> tiles or when <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> for vegetables.</li>\n<li>Mushrooms can also be grown in a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_planter\" title=\"Large planter\">large planter</a>.</li>\n<li>Most mushrooms can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a>, used as a <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> ingredient, or eaten directly.</li>\n<li>Mushrooms can also be given to a follower of a deity when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">praying</a> at an <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altar</a>.</li>\n<li>You can use a <a href=\"/index.php/Spoon\" title=\"Spoon\">spoon</a> to make it into a container for <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li></ul>', 1),
(17767, 4553, 'Types', 'Types', 'Color Healing potency Black 5 Green 4 Yellow 3 Blue 3 Brown 2 Red 0', '<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Color</th>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Healing_potency\" title=\"Healing potency\">Healing potency</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Black_mushroom\" title=\"Black mushroom\">Black</a></td>\n<td>5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Green_mushroom\" title=\"Green mushroom\">Green</a></td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Yellow_mushroom\" title=\"Yellow mushroom\">Yellow</a></td>\n<td>3\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Blue_mushroom\" title=\"Blue mushroom\">Blue</a></td>\n<td>3\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_mushroom\" title=\"Brown mushroom\">Brown</a></td>\n<td>2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Red_mushroom\" title=\"Red mushroom\">Red</a></td>\n<td>0\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(17768, 4553, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Berry Cereals Fruit Herb Nut Seed Spices Vegetable', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Berry\" title=\"Berry\">Berry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cereals\" title=\"Cereals\">Cereals</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fruit\" title=\"Fruit\">Fruit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">Herb</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Nut\" title=\"Nut\">Nut</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seed\" title=\"Seed\">Seed</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spices\" title=\"Spices\">Spices</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Vegetable\" title=\"Vegetable\">Vegetable</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17769, 4560, 'Description', 'Description', 'A strange agaric with a red leathery hat and a thin white foot.', '<p><i>A strange agaric with a red leathery hat and a thin white foot.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17770, 4560, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You can use a spoon to make it into a container for cooking recipes. Cannot be used in healing covers unlike the other mushrooms.', '<ul><li>You can use a <a href=\"/index.php/Spoon\" title=\"Spoon\">spoon</a> to make it into a container for <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Cannot be used in healing covers unlike the other mushrooms.</li></ul>', 1),
(17771, 4560, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Mushroom', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Mushroom\" title=\"Mushroom\">Mushroom</a>\n</p>', 2),
(17772, 4561, 'Types', 'Types', 'There are 3 types of Mauls , each with its own subskill. Small maul - 3s attack speed, weak damage Medium maul - 5s attack speed, medium damage Large maul - 6s attack speed, high damage', '<p>There are 3 types of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mauls\" title=\"Category:Mauls\">Mauls</a>, each with its own subskill.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a> - 3s attack speed, weak damage</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a> - 5s attack speed, medium damage</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a> - 6s attack speed, high damage</li></ul></dd></dl>', 0),
(17773, 4561, 'Characteristics trained', 'Characteristics_trained', 'See: Characteristics', '<p>See: <a href=\"/index.php/Characteristics\" title=\"Characteristics\">Characteristics</a>\n</p>', 1),
(17774, 4561, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Mauls Body > Body strength Subskills Mauls > Large maul Mauls > Medium maul Mauls > Small maul', '<ul><li>Mauls</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Mauls &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li>Mauls &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a></li>\n<li>Mauls &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17775, 4561, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Mauler at 50 skill Bonker at 70 skill Crusher at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Mauler at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Bonker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Crusher at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(17776, 4562, 'Types', 'Types', 'There are 4 types of axes , and each has its own sub-skill. Small axe - 3s attack speed, weak damage Large axe - 5s attack speed, medium damage Huge axe - slow speed, high damage Hatchet - made specifically for chopping wood', '<p>There are 4 types of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Axes\" title=\"Category:Axes\">axes</a>, and each has its own sub-skill.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a> - 3s attack speed, weak damage</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_axe\" title=\"Large axe\">Large axe</a> - 5s attack speed, medium damage</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a> - slow speed, high damage</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">Hatchet</a> - made specifically for chopping wood</li></ul></dd></dl>', 0),
(17777, 4562, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Axes Body > Body strength Subskills Small axe Large axe Huge axe Hatchet', '<ul><li>Axes</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_axe\" title=\"Large axe\">Large axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">Hatchet</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17778, 4562, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Axeman/Axewoman at 50 skill Berserker at 70 skill Fleshrender at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Axeman/Axewoman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Berserker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Fleshrender at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(17797, 4565, 'Description', 'Description', 'A herb with twig-like stems and small white flowers, as well as a very nice scent.', '<p><i>A herb with twig-like stems and small white flowers, as well as a very nice scent.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17798, 4565, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Rosemary is used in many cooking recipes. It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar. Also a very powerful ingredient for a healing cover , with a potency of 4. Can be found by botanizing from Mints and Wildflowers Resource nodes . Can be picked from a pottery planter -', '<ul><li>Rosemary is used in many <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar.</li>\n<li>Also a very powerful ingredient for a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a>, with a potency of 4.</li>\n<li>Can be found by botanizing from <a href=\"/index.php/Mints\" title=\"Mints\">Mints</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be picked from a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\">pottery planter</a>-</li></ul>', 1),
(17799, 4565, 'Images', 'Images', 'Rosemary planted in a pottery planter', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Rosemaryplanter.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/91/Rosemaryplanter.jpg/96px-Rosemaryplanter.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/91/Rosemaryplanter.jpg/144px-Rosemaryplanter.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/9/91/Rosemaryplanter.jpg/192px-Rosemaryplanter.jpg 2x\" width=\"96\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Rosemary planted in a pottery planter\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(17800, 4565, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Herb', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">Herb</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17827, 1019, 'Description', 'Description', 'Chaos is the oldest server in Wurm. It was originally called Wild.', '<p>Chaos is the oldest server in Wurm. It was originally called Wild. \n</p>', 0),
(17828, 1019, 'Spawn settlements', 'Spawn_settlements', 'Hunter\'s Lodge The Landing Gold Coast The Shroud', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Settlement:Hunter%27s_Lodge\" title=\"Settlement:Hunter\'s Lodge\">Hunter\'s Lodge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Settlement:The_Landing\" title=\"Settlement:The Landing\">The Landing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Settlement:Gold_Coast\" title=\"Settlement:Gold Coast\">Gold Coast</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Settlement:The_Shroud\" title=\"Settlement:The Shroud\">The Shroud</a></li></ul>', 1),
(17829, 1019, 'Travel', 'Travel', 'This island may be reached by sailing west from Deliverance , Independence , Exodus , and Celebration or by using plot course from any Southern Isles server. You are also able to travel any direction off Chaos using plot course with or without enemies in local.', '<p>This island may be reached by sailing west from <a href=\"/index.php/Deliverance\" title=\"Deliverance\">Deliverance</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Independence\" title=\"Independence\">Independence</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Exodus\" title=\"Exodus\">Exodus</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Celebration\" title=\"Celebration\">Celebration</a> or by using <a href=\"/index.php/Plot_course\" title=\"Plot course\">plot course</a> from any Southern Isles server. You are also able to travel any direction off Chaos using <a href=\"/index.php/Plot_course\" title=\"Plot course\">plot course</a> with or without enemies in local.\n</p>', 2),
(17830, 1019, 'Maps', 'Maps', 'In-game map Map dumps', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/File:Chaos_250.jpg\" title=\"File:Chaos 250.jpg\"> In-game map</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B6J_aGQ6URL8TkJpbllsR0s5UEE\" rel=\"nofollow\">Map dumps</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17831, 1019, 'Statistics', 'Statistics', 'Server status Server statistics See server graphs for the statistics of all servers.', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://chaos.game.wurmonline.com/battles/stats.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Server status</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://chaos.game.wurmonline.com/mrtg/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Server statistics</a></li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Server_graphs\" title=\"Server graphs\">server graphs</a> for the statistics of all servers.<i></i></li></ul>', 4),
(17842, 4574, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small pointy, slightly conical blade the length of a hand.', '<p><i>A small pointy, slightly conical blade the length of a hand.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17843, 4574, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct an awl when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct an <a href=\"/index.php/Awl\" title=\"Awl\">awl</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17848, 4576, 'Description', 'Description', 'Gems are precious stones which sometimes appear on the ground when digging (emeralds/star emeralds only) or mining (all gem types) in caves, in which their quality is capped by your mining skill and/or tile quality. They can also be received as a gift from the gods when praying as a priest of over 50 faith .', '<p><b>Gems</b> are precious stones which sometimes appear on the ground when <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> (emeralds/star emeralds only) or <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> (all gem types) in caves, in which their quality is capped by your mining skill and/or tile quality. They can also be received as a gift from the gods when praying as a priest of over 50 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(17849, 4576, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Gems can be either sold to another player for varying amounts of money or can be used by priests to \" vessel \" their favor , saving it for later use. Gems never decay, although \'using\' a vesselled gem to recover favor causes it to lose quality each time. The amount of QL lost is equal to the amount of favor taken to fill the priests favor bar divided by 2. E.g. a priest has 20 favor and 60 faith, the gem will provide 40 favor at a cost of 20 QL. Casting vessel on a gem under 10QL will lower the QL of the gem by 3, and store no favor - useful for grinding the channeling skill. All the \"common\" gems are equally rare and at equal qualities worth the same and store the same amount of favor. The Black/Star gems are rare versions of their respective \"common\" counterparts. All the \"rare\" gems are equally rare, and at equal qualities, they are worth the same and store the same amount of favor. Their value and ability to hold favor is double that of the common ones. Some unique gems were received from easter eggs in 2006. Another unique gem which is not found anymore is the Glass Crazy Diamond. Gems cannot be stored in any kind of bulk container. Consequently, many players opt to store them in chests, satchels, backpacks, etc.', '<ul><li>Gems can be either sold to another player for varying amounts of money or can be used by priests to \"<a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">vessel</a>\" their <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a>, saving it for later use.</li>\n<li>Gems never decay, although \'using\' a vesselled gem to recover favor causes it to lose quality each time. The amount of QL lost is equal to the amount of favor taken to fill the priests favor bar divided by 2. E.g. a priest has 20 favor and 60 faith, the gem will provide 40 favor at a cost of 20 QL. Casting vessel on a gem under 10QL will lower the QL of the gem by 3, and store no favor - useful for grinding the <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skill.</li>\n<li>All the \"common\" gems are equally rare and at equal qualities worth the same and store the same amount of favor.</li>\n<li>The Black/Star gems are rare versions of their respective \"common\" counterparts. All the \"rare\" gems are equally rare, and at equal qualities, they are worth the same and store the same amount of favor. Their value and ability to hold favor is double that of the common ones.</li>\n<li>Some unique gems were received from <a href=\"/index.php/Easter_egg\" title=\"Easter egg\">easter eggs</a> in 2006. Another unique gem which is not found anymore is the Glass Crazy Diamond.</li>\n<li>Gems cannot be stored in any kind of bulk container. Consequently, many players opt to store them in chests, satchels, backpacks, etc.</li></ul>', 1),
(17850, 4576, 'List of Wurm Gems', 'List_of_Wurm_Gems', 'Black opal Diamond Emerald Opal Ruby Sapphire Star diamond Star emerald Star ruby Star sapphire', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_opal\" title=\"Black opal\">Black opal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Diamond\" title=\"Diamond\">Diamond</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Emerald\" title=\"Emerald\">Emerald</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Opal\" title=\"Opal\">Opal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ruby\" title=\"Ruby\">Ruby</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sapphire\" title=\"Sapphire\">Sapphire</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Star_diamond\" title=\"Star diamond\">Star diamond</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Star_emerald\" title=\"Star emerald\">Star emerald</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Star_ruby\" title=\"Star ruby\">Star ruby</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Star_sapphire\" title=\"Star sapphire\">Star sapphire</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17851, 4255, 'Description', 'Description', 'The bent blade of a butchering knife.', '<p><i>The bent blade of a butchering knife.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17852, 4255, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to create a butchering knife when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering_knife\" title=\"Butchering knife\">butchering knife</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(17853, 4255, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Older versions weigh only 0.3 kg and can\'t be used anymore for creation of butchering knives .', '<ul><li>Older versions weigh only 0.3 kg and can\'t be used anymore for creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering_knife\" title=\"Butchering knife\">butchering knives</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(17870, 4582, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sprawling plant with coarse leaves.', '<p><i>A sprawling plant with coarse leaves.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17871, 4582, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Oregano is used in many cooking recipes. It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar. Oregano can be found by Botanizing at Mints and Desert weeds Resource nodes .', '<ul><li>Oregano is used in many <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar.</li>\n<li>Oregano can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> at <a href=\"/index.php/Mints\" title=\"Mints\">Mints</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Desert_weeds\" title=\"Desert weeds\">Desert weeds</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(17872, 4582, 'Images', 'Images', 'Oregano planted in a pottery planter', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:15px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Oreganoplanter.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e3/Oreganoplanter.jpg/96px-Oreganoplanter.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/e3/Oreganoplanter.jpg/144px-Oreganoplanter.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/e3/Oreganoplanter.jpg/192px-Oreganoplanter.jpg 2x\" width=\"96\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Oregano planted in a pottery planter\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(17873, 4582, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Herb', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">Herb</a></li></ul>', 3),
(17880, 2650, 'Description', 'Description', 'A handful of small, blue berries with a wonderful sweet taste.', '<p><i>A handful of small, blue berries with a wonderful sweet taste.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17881, 2650, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Blueberries can be found by foraging on Bog muck or botanizing on Briar patch or Swampy puddle Resource nodes or by harvesting from blueberry bushes in season. Blueberries can be used in cooking or to make juice.', '<ul><li>Blueberries can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Bog_muck\" title=\"Bog muck\">Bog muck</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Briar_patch\" title=\"Briar patch\">Briar patch</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Swampy_puddle\" title=\"Swampy puddle\">Swampy puddle</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> or by harvesting from <a href=\"/index.php/Blueberry_bush\" title=\"Blueberry bush\">blueberry bushes</a> in season.</li>\n<li>Blueberries can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">cooking</a> or to make juice.</li></ul>', 1),
(17882, 2650, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Berry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Berry\" title=\"Berry\">Berry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17883, 4586, 'Description', 'Description', 'Bluish purple flowers in loose, drooping clusters on short stalks.', '<p><i>Bluish purple flowers in loose, drooping clusters on short stalks.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17884, 4586, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Belladonna can be grown in and picked from a pottery planter . Can be found by Botanizing Nightshades and Wildflowers Resource nodes . It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar. Though poisonous in real life, belladonna is an herb in Wurm. Belladonna planted in a pottery planter', '<ul><li>Belladonna can be grown in and picked from a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\">pottery planter</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Nightshades\" title=\"Nightshades\">Nightshades</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wildflowers\" title=\"Wildflowers\">Wildflowers</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar.</li>\n<li>Though poisonous in real life, belladonna is an herb in Wurm.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:202px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Belladonnaplanter.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-width=\"400\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d2/Belladonnaplanter.jpg/200px-Belladonnaplanter.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/d2/Belladonnaplanter.jpg/300px-Belladonnaplanter.jpg 1.5x, /images/d/d2/Belladonnaplanter.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Belladonnaplanter.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Belladonna planted in a pottery planter</div></div></div>', 1),
(17885, 4586, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Herb', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">Herb</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17886, 4584, 'Description', 'Description', 'Large, glistening red hearts with tiny yellow seeds.', '<p><i>Large, glistening red hearts with tiny yellow seeds.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17887, 4584, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be found by botanizing from Low brush Resource nodes . Strawberry seeds can be picked out of strawberries, and each strawberry picked in this way produces one seed. Picking the seeds destroys the strawberries. Strawberries can be used in cooking recipes and in making juice.', '<ul><li>Can be found by botanizing from <a href=\"/index.php/Low_brush\" title=\"Low brush\">Low brush</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Strawberry_seed\" title=\"Strawberry seed\">Strawberry seeds</a> can be picked out of strawberries, and each strawberry picked in this way produces one seed. Picking the seeds destroys the strawberries.</li>\n<li>Strawberries can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">cooking</a> recipes and in making juice.</li></ul>', 1),
(17888, 4584, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Berry', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Berry\" title=\"Berry\">Berry</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17901, 4595, 'Story', 'Story', 'The White Light While the Archives lack any specific details of this battle. What is known\nis the Horde of the Summoned was led by Malvada , who supposedly was appointed\nto the post by none other than Libila herself. The objective was simple: Take\nthe infamous Steel Sceptre of Ascension to the Altar of Three and destroy it. Rendering the\nforces of Jenn-Kellon effectively useless without their beloved White Light. Now the records do not say as to how or why the plan was discovered. But a\ndefense force was quickly rallied up and camped a mere half-kilometer from\nthe White Light. When the Horde discovered that the element of surprise was\ngone, they attacked with a fury not seen for many a starfall. The battle could\nbe easily compared with the Battle of Armageddon that so many beliefs refer to\nin their texts. But for some reason unknown now, the Jenn-Kellon army was able to beat back\nthe rampaging Hordes and claimed victory. However, it isn\'t known of what became\nof the Steel Sceptre of Ascension. Either it stills lies somewhere buried under the blood of\nmany a fighter. Or worse, could\'ve been spirited away to await perhaps the fabled\nArmageddon War that may be yet to come....', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Altarof3.JPG\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"768\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/eb/Altarof3.JPG/300px-Altarof3.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/eb/Altarof3.JPG/450px-Altarof3.JPG 1.5x, /images/thumb/e/eb/Altarof3.JPG/600px-Altarof3.JPG 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Altarof3.JPG\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The White Light</div></div></div>\n<p>While the Archives lack any specific details of this battle. What is known\nis the Horde of the Summoned was led by <a href=\"/index.php/User:Malvada\" title=\"User:Malvada\">Malvada</a>, who supposedly was appointed\nto the post by none other than <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> herself. The objective was simple: Take\nthe infamous <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Steel_Sceptre_of_Ascension\" title=\"Steel Sceptre of Ascension\">Steel Sceptre of Ascension</a> to the <a href=\"/index.php/Altar_of_Three\" title=\"Altar of Three\">Altar of Three</a> and destroy it. Rendering the\nforces of Jenn-Kellon effectively useless without their beloved White Light. \n</p>\n<p>Now the records do not say as to how or why the plan was discovered. But a\ndefense force was quickly rallied up and camped a mere half-kilometer from\nthe White Light. When the Horde discovered that the element of surprise was\ngone, they attacked with a fury not seen for many a starfall. The battle could\nbe easily compared with the Battle of Armageddon that so many beliefs refer to\nin their texts.\n</p>\n<p>But for some reason unknown now, the Jenn-Kellon army was able to beat back\nthe rampaging Hordes and claimed victory. However, it isn\'t known of what became\nof the Steel Sceptre of Ascension. Either it stills lies somewhere buried under the blood of\nmany a fighter. Or worse, could\'ve been spirited away to await perhaps the fabled\nArmageddon War that may be yet to come....\n</p>', 0),
(17902, 4595, 'Review (WLers Point of View)', 'Review_.28WLers_Point_of_View.29', 'The initial plan by the BLers was to take out the White Light by using a artifact (Steel Sceptre of Ascension). While this is risky, success would mean the storyline would move forward. Once Malvada advertised the attack, the WLers ran towards the WL. First they planted a Homestead about 500m from the White Light (a rule of Wurm is no deeds shall be planted on the Lights themselves), this did three things: One it shifted the focus of the battle to the deed, and it forced the BLers into having to attack the deed because it acted like a castle. It could not be ignored, and lastly, gave the WLers an unfair advantage as they already outnumbered the BLers, but now they could respawn when they died, as their towns were allied with this deed. Once the deed was there, it spawned guards which gave the WLers even more of an advantage and spawned fighters to annoy the attackers. After a while the BLers broke onto the deed, drained it, killed everyone and took the final lives from Champions, leaving the BLers to skip merrily back to their land, while being pursued by the last Champion, who wanted a 1 on 1 fight with Malvada. Malvada won, which finalised the victory for the BLers.', '<p>The initial plan by the BLers was to take out the White Light by using a artifact (Steel Sceptre of Ascension). While this is risky, success would mean the storyline would move forward.\n</p>\n<p>Once Malvada advertised the attack, the WLers ran towards the WL. First they planted a Homestead about 500m from the White Light (a rule of Wurm is no deeds shall be planted on the Lights themselves), this did three things: One it shifted the focus of the battle to the deed, and it forced the BLers into having to attack the deed because it acted like a castle. It could not be ignored, and lastly, gave the WLers an unfair advantage as they already outnumbered the BLers, but now they could respawn when they died, as their towns were allied with this deed.\n</p>\n<p>Once the deed was there, it spawned guards which gave the WLers even more of an advantage and spawned fighters to annoy the attackers. After a while the BLers broke onto the deed, drained it, killed everyone and took the final lives from Champions, leaving the BLers to skip merrily back to their land, while being pursued by the last Champion, who wanted a 1 on 1 fight with Malvada. Malvada won, which finalised the victory for the BLers.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(17903, 4595, 'Review (BLers Point of View)', 'Review_.28BLers_Point_of_View.29', 'The majority of the warriors were from VCS, LO and FT and during this battle many champions fell, however more WLer than BLe\nThe force met at VCS, and went through NT towards the Light. Once they got close many WLers appeared. The BLers noticed the newly planted deed and ran towards it, then followed the hunting down of many of the WLers that were not on the deed, Hyenas were used to kill WLers on the deed and they quickly fell. However, they soon respawned on the deed and collected new weapons. They continued to kill the WLers as they respawned and then procceeded to take there weapons until eventually they would not have any. The BLers then moved towards the Whitelight, easily getting past the incomplete walls surrounding it, any WLers that tryed to get closed were killed quickly. However, the destruction of the WL was not going well, descrating the Altar was not doing as much damage as everyone had hoped. The BLers moved back towards the deed and, although many WL champions had fallen they we still outnumbered, howver winning the battle. Once all the WL Champions were down, and they were running out of weapons, the BLers pressed onto the deed. The Spirit Templars were dealt with. The deed was looted and the BLers returned to there homes. The BLers had won, however they had not managed to destroy the WL as planned. They did however come out better off as the WLers had lost lots of items and champions.', '<p>The majority of the warriors were from VCS, LO and FT and during this battle many champions fell, however more WLer than BLe\nThe force met at VCS, and went through NT towards the Light. Once they got close many WLers appeared. \n</p>\n<p>The BLers noticed the newly planted deed and ran towards it, then followed the hunting down of many of the WLers that were not on the deed, Hyenas were used to kill WLers on the deed and they quickly fell. However, they soon respawned on the deed and collected new weapons. They continued to kill the WLers as they respawned and then procceeded to take there weapons until eventually they would not have any. \n</p>\n<p>The BLers then moved towards the Whitelight, easily getting past the incomplete walls surrounding it, any WLers that tryed to get closed were killed quickly. However, the destruction of the WL was not going well, descrating the Altar was not doing as much damage as everyone had hoped. The BLers moved back towards the deed and, although many WL champions had fallen they we still outnumbered, howver winning the battle. Once all the WL Champions were down, and they were running out of weapons, the BLers pressed onto the deed. The Spirit Templars were dealt with. The deed was looted and the BLers returned to there homes.\n</p>\n<p>The BLers had won, however they had not managed to destroy the WL as planned. They did however come out better off as the WLers had lost lots of items and champions.\n</p>', 2),
(17941, 1315, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fruit, once probably picked from a tree.', '<p><i>A fruit, once probably picked from a tree.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17942, 1315, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in cooking and beverage recipes. Can be eaten to relieve a small amount of hunger. Harvested with a sickle from apple trees during apple season . Can be found by Botanizing on Thicket and Alpine brush Resource nodes . Though apples appear red on trees, they are always green apples.', '<ul><li>Used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Beverage\" title=\"Beverage\">beverage</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be eaten to relieve a small amount of hunger.</li>\n<li>Harvested with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Apple_tree\" title=\"Apple tree\">apple trees</a> during apple <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Thicket\" title=\"Thicket\">Thicket</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Alpine_brush\" title=\"Alpine brush\">Alpine brush</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Though apples appear red on trees, they are always green apples.</li></ul>', 1),
(17943, 1315, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Beverages Cooking Forestry Fruit', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">Beverages</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">Forestry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fruit\" title=\"Fruit\">Fruit</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17959, 2745, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large wooden barrel, strengthened by iron ribbons.', '<p><i>A large wooden barrel, strengthened by iron ribbons.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17960, 2745, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to store items and liquids. Cannot be loaded but can be taken into inventory Can be planted. Can be stored in a large barrel rack . Some items can be placed on top of a large barrel, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is picked up; a message in event log will notify the player of this. It has a liquid capacity of 250kg. Slows the decay of the items inside. It is the QL of the iron ribbon that determines the success rate. If you fail creating, the ribbon and plank used are both damaged. The last plank attached determines the wood type. Use cedar wood for the barrel itself to have reduced decay(this doesn\'t affect the contents). Unlike Small barrel it cannot be sealed. However Large pottery amphora can be sealed with a Wax sealing kit and fits 275kg.', '<ul><li>Used to store items and liquids.</li>\n<li>Cannot be loaded but can be taken into inventory</li>\n<li>Can be planted.</li>\n<li>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel_rack\" title=\"Large barrel rack\">large barrel rack</a>.</li>\n<li>Some items can be placed on top of a large barrel, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is picked up; a message in event log will notify the player of this.</li>\n<li>It has a liquid capacity of 250kg.</li>\n<li>Slows the decay of the items inside.</li>\n<li>It is the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ribbon\" title=\"Iron ribbon\">iron ribbon</a> that determines the success rate.</li>\n<li>If you fail creating, the ribbon and plank used are both damaged.</li>\n<li>The last plank attached determines the wood type.</li>\n<li>Use <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> wood for the barrel itself to have reduced decay(this doesn\'t affect the contents).</li>\n<li>Unlike <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">Small barrel</a> it cannot be sealed. However <a href=\"/index.php/Large_pottery_amphora\" title=\"Large pottery amphora\">Large pottery amphora</a> can be sealed with a <a href=\"/index.php/Wax_sealing_kit\" title=\"Wax sealing kit\">Wax sealing kit</a> and fits 275kg.</li></ul>', 1),
(17961, 2745, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Huge tub Small barrel Small wine barrel', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Huge_tub\" title=\"Huge tub\">Huge tub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">Small barrel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_wine_barrel\" title=\"Small wine barrel\">Small wine barrel</a></li></ul>', 2),
(17962, 2745, 'Images', 'Images', '.mw-parser-output .woodgrain-highlight-row{background-color:#a6a290} Large barrels with different wood types as labelled. The worn/decayed barrels are small barrels. Apple: Birch: Cedar: Cherry: Chestnut: Fir: Lemon: Linden: Maple: Oak: Oleander: Olive: Orange: Pine: Walnut: Willow: Worn: Decayed:', '<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120118\">.mw-parser-output .woodgrain-highlight-row{background-color:#a6a290}</style>\n<table align=\"center\" border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; style=\">\n<caption>Large barrels with different wood types as labelled. The worn/decayed barrels are small barrels.\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr class=\"woodgrain-highlight-row\">\n<th>Apple:\n</th>\n<th>Birch:\n</th>\n<th>Cedar:\n</th>\n<th>Cherry:\n</th>\n<th>Chestnut:\n</th>\n<th>Fir:\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Apple.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Apple.png\" data-file-height=\"284\" data-file-width=\"244\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"175\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/LargeBarrel-Apple.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Apple.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7d/LargeBarrel-Apple.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Apple.png 1.5x, /images/7/7d/LargeBarrel-Apple.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Birch.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Birch.png\" data-file-height=\"381\" data-file-width=\"263\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"217\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/2d/LargeBarrel-Birch.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Birch.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/2d/LargeBarrel-Birch.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Birch.png 1.5x, /images/2/2d/LargeBarrel-Birch.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Cedar.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Cedar.png\" data-file-height=\"377\" data-file-width=\"308\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"184\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/32/LargeBarrel-Cedar.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Cedar.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/32/LargeBarrel-Cedar.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Cedar.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/3/32/LargeBarrel-Cedar.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Cedar.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Cherry.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Cherry.png\" data-file-height=\"367\" data-file-width=\"366\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c0/LargeBarrel-Cherry.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Cherry.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c0/LargeBarrel-Cherry.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Cherry.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/c/c0/LargeBarrel-Cherry.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Cherry.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png\" data-file-height=\"413\" data-file-width=\"301\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"206\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1a/LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1a/LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Chestnut.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Fir.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Fir.png\" data-file-height=\"364\" data-file-width=\"276\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"198\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/18/LargeBarrel-Fir.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Fir.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/18/LargeBarrel-Fir.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Fir.png 1.5x, /images/1/18/LargeBarrel-Fir.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table align=\"center\" border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; style=\">\n<tbody><tr class=\"woodgrain-highlight-row\">\n<th>Lemon:\n</th>\n<th>Linden:\n</th>\n<th>Maple:\n</th>\n<th>Oak:\n</th>\n<th>Oleander:\n</th>\n<th>Olive:\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Lemon.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Lemon.png\" data-file-height=\"332\" data-file-width=\"258\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"193\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/6f/LargeBarrel-Lemon.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Lemon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/6f/LargeBarrel-Lemon.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Lemon.png 1.5x, /images/6/6f/LargeBarrel-Lemon.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Linden.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Linden.png\" data-file-height=\"356\" data-file-width=\"311\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"172\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/a0/LargeBarrel-Linden.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Linden.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/a0/LargeBarrel-Linden.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Linden.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/a/a0/LargeBarrel-Linden.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Linden.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Maple.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Maple.png\" data-file-height=\"374\" data-file-width=\"327\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"172\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1f/LargeBarrel-Maple.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Maple.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1f/LargeBarrel-Maple.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Maple.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1f/LargeBarrel-Maple.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Maple.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Oak.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Oak.png\" data-file-height=\"321\" data-file-width=\"282\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"171\" src=\"/images/thumb/a/ae/LargeBarrel-Oak.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Oak.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/a/ae/LargeBarrel-Oak.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Oak.png 1.5x, /images/a/ae/LargeBarrel-Oak.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG\" data-file-height=\"403\" data-file-width=\"407\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"149\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/89/LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG/150px-LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/89/LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG/225px-LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/89/LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG/300px-LargeBarrel-oleander.JPG 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Olive.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Olive.png\" data-file-height=\"367\" data-file-width=\"270\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"204\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/f5/LargeBarrel-Olive.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Olive.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/f5/LargeBarrel-Olive.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Olive.png 1.5x, /images/f/f5/LargeBarrel-Olive.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<table align=\"center\" border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; style=\">\n<tbody><tr class=\"woodgrain-highlight-row\">\n<th>Orange:\n</th>\n<th>Pine:\n</th>\n<th>Walnut:\n</th>\n<th>Willow:\n</th>\n<th>Worn:\n</th>\n<th>Decayed:\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Orange.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Orange.png\" data-file-height=\"329\" data-file-width=\"282\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"175\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/ea/LargeBarrel-Orange.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Orange.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/e/ea/LargeBarrel-Orange.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Orange.png 1.5x, /images/e/ea/LargeBarrel-Orange.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Pine.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Pine.png\" data-file-height=\"446\" data-file-width=\"360\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"186\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/51/LargeBarrel-Pine.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Pine.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/5/51/LargeBarrel-Pine.png/225px-LargeBarrel-Pine.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/5/51/LargeBarrel-Pine.png/300px-LargeBarrel-Pine.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Walnut.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Walnut.png\" data-file-height=\"284\" data-file-width=\"214\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"199\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/59/LargeBarrel-Walnut.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Walnut.png\" srcset=\"/images/5/59/LargeBarrel-Walnut.png 1.5x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:LargeBarrel-Willow.png\"><img alt=\"LargeBarrel-Willow.png\" data-file-height=\"250\" data-file-width=\"195\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"192\" src=\"/images/thumb/e/e4/LargeBarrel-Willow.png/150px-LargeBarrel-Willow.png\" srcset=\"/images/e/e4/LargeBarrel-Willow.png 1.5x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:SmallBarel-Worn.png\"><img alt=\"SmallBarel-Worn.png\" data-file-height=\"453\" data-file-width=\"396\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"172\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/f7/SmallBarel-Worn.png/150px-SmallBarel-Worn.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/f7/SmallBarel-Worn.png/225px-SmallBarel-Worn.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/f/f7/SmallBarel-Worn.png/300px-SmallBarel-Worn.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:SmallBarel-Decayed.png\"><img alt=\"SmallBarel-Decayed.png\" data-file-height=\"437\" data-file-width=\"308\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"213\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1b/SmallBarel-Decayed.png/150px-SmallBarel-Decayed.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1b/SmallBarel-Decayed.png/225px-SmallBarel-Decayed.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1b/SmallBarel-Decayed.png/300px-SmallBarel-Decayed.png 2x\" width=\"150\"/></a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3),
(17976, 4163, 'Description', 'Description', 'A heavy lump of dull grey lead.', '<p><i>A heavy lump of dull grey lead.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(17977, 4163, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting lead ore in a forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns 1.0kg lead lump per 20kg of lead ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Lead_ore\" title=\"Lead ore\">lead ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns 1.0kg <b>lead lump</b> per 20kg of lead ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(17978, 4163, 'Note', 'Note', 'This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(17979, 4163, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See List of Lead products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from lead. Used to create Larders .', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Lead_products\" title=\"Category:Lead products\">List of Lead products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from lead.</li>\n<li>Used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Larder\" title=\"Larder\">Larders</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18012, 2295, 'Description', 'Description', 'The Markets of Wurm are player made areas that can be populated with personal merchants from various players. These marketplaces work like bazaars of some games. But rather than having a Developer or GM run it, the players are in charge, to offer all fairness and player manipulation of the system. See also Inns .', '<p>The Markets of Wurm are player made areas that can be populated with <a href=\"/index.php/Personal_merchant\" title=\"Personal merchant\">personal merchants</a> from various players.\n</p>\n<p>These marketplaces work like bazaars of some games. But rather than having a Developer or GM run it, the players are in charge, to offer all fairness and player manipulation of the system. \n</p>\n<p>See also <a href=\"/index.php/Inn\" title=\"Inn\">Inns</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18013, 2295, 'Trade command', 'Trade_command', 'Right-click the person, merchant or trader you want to trade with, and choose Trade . A Trading window appears. Buying from a Personal Merchant Merchants\'s inventory is shown in \'<Merchant>\'s offer\' window top left. Drag items you want to the \'Your demand\' window below it. Drag money or selling items from your inventory into the \'Your offer\' window top right. Check \'You accept\'. If you offered a suitable amount, Merchant will accept also. If you offered more than the value of the items you bought, Merchant will give change. Trading items with another player To give Drag the item(s) you are offering from your inventory into the \'Your offer\' window top right. The other player sees it in \"<Player>\'s offer\" window, and must drag it to their demand window below it and check their \'You accept\' box. Check \'You accept\'. To receive You will see the other player\'s offer in \'<Player>\'s offer\' window top left. Drag the item(s) to the lower \'Your demand\' window and check \'You accept\'. The other player must check their \'You accept\' box also.', '<ul><li>Right-click the person, merchant or trader you want to trade with, and choose <b>Trade</b>. A Trading window appears.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Buying_from_a_Personal_Merchant\">Buying from a Personal Merchant</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Merchants\'s inventory is shown in \'&lt;Merchant&gt;\'s offer\' window top left. Drag items you want to the \'Your demand\' window below it.</li>\n<li>Drag money or selling items from your inventory into the \'Your offer\' window top right.</li>\n<li>Check \'You accept\'.</li></ul>\n<p>If you offered a suitable amount, Merchant will accept also. If you offered more than the value of the items you bought, Merchant will give change.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trading_items_with_another_player\">Trading items with another player</span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"To_give\">To give</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Drag the item(s) you are offering from your inventory into the \'Your offer\' window top right.</li>\n<li>The other player sees it in \"&lt;Player&gt;\'s offer\" window, and must drag it to their demand window below it and check their \'You accept\' box.</li>\n<li>Check \'You accept\'.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"To_receive\">To receive</span></h4>\n<ul><li>You will see the other player\'s offer in \'&lt;Player&gt;\'s offer\' window top left.</li>\n<li>Drag the item(s) to the lower \'Your demand\' window and check \'You accept\'.</li>\n<li>The other player must check their \'You accept\' box also.</li></ul>', 1),
(18014, 2295, 'Trade chat', 'Trade_chat', 'The Trade chat tab is a global chat used for advertising your intent to sell (WTS), buy (WTB), trade (WTT), or desire to price check something (PC). Only messages that begin with the abbreviations WTS, WTB, WTT, or PC are displayed in the chat window. Players answering your message will reply to you via private messages or direct in the trade chat by using \" @ <your username> \", which will only be visible to you. You may toggle this tab on and off in your profile settings . Read more : Chat | Profile | Private messages', '<p>The Trade chat tab is a <a href=\"/index.php/Chat#Global\" title=\"Chat\">global</a> chat used for advertising your intent to sell (WTS), buy (WTB), trade (WTT), or desire to price check something (PC). Only messages that begin with the abbreviations WTS, WTB, WTT, or PC are displayed in the chat window. Players answering your message will reply to you via <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PM\" title=\"PM\">private messages</a> or direct in the trade chat by using \"<code>@ &lt;your username&gt;</code>\", which will only be visible to you. You may toggle this tab on and off in your <a href=\"/index.php/Profile\" title=\"Profile\">profile settings</a>.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Trade_chat.jpg\" title=\"Trade chat\"><img alt=\"Trade chat\" data-file-height=\"200\" data-file-width=\"567\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/9/97/Trade_chat.jpg\" width=\"567\"/></a>\n</p>\n<p><b>Read more</b>: <a href=\"/index.php/Chat\" title=\"Chat\">Chat</a> | <a href=\"/index.php/Profile\" title=\"Profile\">Profile</a> | <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/PM\" title=\"PM\">Private messages</a>\n</p>', 2),
(18015, 2295, 'Player Trading', 'Player_Trading', 'Wurm offers a lot of different options for players to do business with one another. If you are interested in buying or selling something, you can post your request into the chat ingame, or make a separate thread for it in one of the marketplace sections on the forums in order to find your trading partner. You may also browse these forums for somebody who might already have posted about the item you wish to buy or sell, with whom you could immediately get in touch about the trade.', '<p>Wurm offers a lot of different options for players to do business with one another. If you are interested in buying or selling something, you can post your request into the chat ingame, or make a separate thread for it in one of the marketplace sections on the forums in order to find your trading partner. You may also browse these forums for somebody who might already have posted about the item you wish to buy or sell, with whom you could immediately get in touch about the trade. \n</p>', 3),
(18016, 2295, 'Server Cluster & The Forums', 'Server_Cluster_.26_The_Forums', 'Whether you are a new trader or someone who has already completed numerous transactions, the forums are your best friend when it comes to trading. Each server cluster has its own marketplace. The Freedom Isles Market is the largest within the game, offering several servers and a majority of people interested and willing to trade. The market on Epic and the market on Chaos are a little more complicated, since the cluster is PvP based and people do not easily trust one another. Most of the Chaos trades happen through the Freedom market, and it is recommended to stay cautious when trading with someone directly on Chaos. The Challenge market barely exists. It is therefore recommended for people who wish to trade with others to choose the Freedom cluster to do so. Within the forums, on each marketplace, you can find different boards to suit each of your inquiries. The Want To Buy board is available for you to post about anything you would like to find a seller for, anything you would like to purchase. The Want To Sell board is there for the opposite request and the right board to choose if you wish to sell some of your own items. Within the Auctions tab you can find items that are being auctioned to the highest bidder. If you have an item for which you expect to be getting a lot of interested buyers, you may consider posting an auction instead of a sales thread. Classified Ads is for you to post about your trades, services and item trades alike (if you offer both), and allows you to summarize all you have to offer in your very own topic to attract future customers.', '<p>Whether you are a new trader or someone who has already completed numerous transactions, the forums are your best friend when it comes to trading. Each server cluster has its own marketplace. The Freedom Isles Market is the largest within the game, offering several servers and a majority of people interested and willing to trade. The market on Epic and the market on Chaos are a little more complicated, since the cluster is PvP based and people do not easily trust one another. Most of the Chaos trades happen through the Freedom market, and it is recommended to stay cautious when trading with someone directly on Chaos. The Challenge market barely exists. It is therefore recommended for people who wish to trade with others to choose the Freedom cluster to do so. \n</p>\n<p>Within the forums, on each marketplace, you can find different boards to suit each of your inquiries. The Want To Buy board is available for you to post about anything you would like to find a seller for, anything you would like to purchase. The Want To Sell board is there for the opposite request and the right board to choose if you wish to sell some of your own items. Within the Auctions tab you can find items that are being auctioned to the highest bidder. If you have an item for which you expect to be getting a lot of interested buyers, you may consider posting an auction instead of a sales thread. Classified Ads is for you to post about your trades, services and item trades alike (if you offer both), and allows you to summarize all you have to offer in your very own topic to attract future customers. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(18017, 2295, 'Trading Process', 'Trading_Process', 'Finding Your Trade The obvious first step for every person interested in trading, is to choose a trade. It is difficult, and not recommended for somebody to begin with too many different things, as it is usually easier to cater to a specific one to begin with. As you master your first trade, there is nothing holding you back from expanding your range of service. When finding your trade, look at what you like to do ingame, and see if there is a market for something related, or if you can maybe even create a market for said thing. An example would be, if you like to tend to animals, you may consider breeding and selling your animals\' offspring. In existing markets, there are a lot of competitors for each trade, so it is not recommended to focus your trade on making as much money as possible, but to focus on making as much gain as possible within a price range that puts you ahead of your competitors and right into the trade market. The Markets In a game that is so focused on trades, a lot of markets currently exist. Here is a list of different groups and types of items that players frequently trade with, and that have established their own, obviously varying, price range. Bulk Materials - A lot of materials such as bricks, mortar, planks and more are being produced in bulk and sold per hundred or thousand. Rare/Supreme Items - Many players crave tools, weapons, decoration or other items of increased rarity. Animals - The biggest market within this category is definitely for horses. However, also all other animal types may sell to the right buyer. Enchanted Tools & Weapons - Priests of the gods are able to cast enchantments on items that, if high enough, quickly find a buyer. Ships - Difficult to make, a lot of people don\'t have the patience to build their own ships. Thus there is a steady market for useful ships. Setting The Price One of the most essential steps in the entire trading process is setting the right price for what you wish to sell. If you are uncertain, try to find equal sales of other people that have previously taken place, and check the price the items went for at that time. However, the market value of different items varies over time, and if the only topics you can find of equal sales are outdated, you might consider a PriceCheck. This option allows you to put PC (=Pricecheck) into the headline of your topic, in order to let players know you want to hear what they think the value for said items is. If you don\'t wish to do that, you might  ask possible buyers to make you an offer for the items, which you can either accept or decline. In those cases it is recommended to wait until multiple offers have arrived, in order for you to pick the best one. If you are certain about a price, make it known to the community that you will not sell for less than said price, as everybody loves to bargain. In the end, the right price will get you the money you deserve, but not force the player to get out of his budget to acquire your item.\nIn case of wanting to buy an item, the PC works just as well. You may also ask people to message you with offers - just like before - and pick one that you can trust is honest and not overpriced. You may also set a budget for your purchase, letting people know you will not pay more than said budget states. Finding Your Customer The next step is to make it known that you do wish to sell or buy. For that, it usually works best to create a thread in the forums. The thread should state whether you wish to buy or sell, what you wish to buy or sell, if you have a price in mind, and how you wish to organise delivery - whether pickup, C.O.D., or plain delivery, and whether this includes an extra fee. Customers might then PM you on the forums, ingame or with a reply to your thread to state their interest in trading with you, or share a thought they have about the transaction. Organising The Transaction There are three different ways for you to go about this. Cash On Delivery - C.O.D. You may have an item for sale, that fits into a mailbox. These items are the easiest to trade, as you can simply put them into a mailbox, select a recipient, check the C.O.D. tab, select a price, and send the item to your customer. The time it takes for the item to arrive depends on how high the enchantment on the mailbox is, and how far away your customer lives. You will be paid as soon as the customer receives the item.\nIn order to pick up an item sent to you via C.O.D., you simply go to a mailbox and receive the item. In order to successfully withdraw the item, you need the amount of money it costs to be in your bank, as it is automatically withdrawn from there. A courier fee of 1c per item applies (see mail for more details). Pickup You or your customer may choose Pickup for an option. That means that you either have to travel to your seller to pick up the item you wish to buy, or that your customer has to travel to you in order to pick up the item he wishes to buy. The likelihood of someone coming all the way to you to pick up their items depends on your location, the distance to them, and the value of the item. Delivery When selling an item, you may offer delivery. If you deliver to a location far away from you, you might consider applying delivery charges, which have to be discussed with your customer in advance. For bulk or loadable items, it is recommended to own a ship. However, if you are at a lake with a shallow canal to the outside sea, make sure you have a ship that is able to get through it. \nThe same applies to you if you wish for a seller to deliver to you - they may apply delivery charges just as well, so make sure to clarify on that before they make their way to you. Alternatively, you may use the new wagoner system which utilizes the highway system and an NPC to deliver the goods for you. Payment This is explained in detail below. It is the last step of the transaction with your customer, and often the most problematic one.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_Your_Trade\">Finding Your Trade</span></h3>\n<p>The obvious first step for every person interested in trading, is to choose a trade. It is difficult, and not recommended for somebody to begin with too many different things, as it is usually easier to cater to a specific one to begin with. As you master your first trade, there is nothing holding you back from expanding your range of service. When finding your trade, look at what you like to do ingame, and see if there is a market for something related, or if you can maybe even create a market for said thing. An example would be, if you like to tend to animals, you may consider breeding and selling your animals\' offspring. In existing markets, there are a lot of competitors for each trade, so it is not recommended to focus your trade on making as much money as possible, but to focus on making as much gain as possible within a price range that puts you ahead of your competitors and right into the trade market. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Markets\">The Markets</span></h3>\n<p>In a game that is so focused on trades, a lot of markets currently exist. Here is a list of different groups and types of items that players frequently trade with, and that have established their own, obviously varying, price range.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Bulk Materials - A lot of materials such as bricks, mortar, planks and more are being produced in bulk and sold per hundred or thousand.</li>\n<li>Rare/Supreme Items - Many players crave tools, weapons, decoration or other items of increased rarity.</li>\n<li>Animals - The biggest market within this category is definitely for horses. However, also all other animal types may sell to the right buyer.</li>\n<li>Enchanted Tools &amp; Weapons - Priests of the gods are able to cast enchantments on items that, if high enough, quickly find a buyer.</li>\n<li>Ships - Difficult to make, a lot of people don\'t have the patience to build their own ships. Thus there is a steady market for useful ships.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Setting_The_Price\">Setting The Price</span></h3>\n<p>One of the most essential steps in the entire trading process is setting the right price for what you wish to sell. If you are uncertain, try to find equal sales of other people that have previously taken place, and check the price the items went for at that time. However, the market value of different items varies over time, and if the only topics you can find of equal sales are outdated, you might consider a PriceCheck. This option allows you to put PC (=Pricecheck) into the headline of your topic, in order to let players know you want to hear what they think the value for said items is. If you don\'t wish to do that, you might  ask possible buyers to make you an offer for the items, which you can either accept or decline. In those cases it is recommended to wait until multiple offers have arrived, in order for you to pick the best one. If you are certain about a price, make it known to the community that you will not sell for less than said price, as everybody loves to bargain. In the end, the right price will get you the money you deserve, but not force the player to get out of his budget to acquire your item.\nIn case of wanting to buy an item, the PC works just as well. You may also ask people to message you with offers - just like before - and pick one that you can trust is honest and not overpriced. You may also set a budget for your purchase, letting people know you will not pay more than said budget states.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_Your_Customer\">Finding Your Customer</span></h3>\n<p>The next step is to make it known that you do wish to sell or buy. For that, it usually works best to create a thread in the forums. The thread should state whether you wish to buy or sell, what you wish to buy or sell, if you have a price in mind, and how you wish to organise delivery - whether pickup, C.O.D., or plain delivery, and whether this includes an extra fee. Customers might then PM you on the forums, ingame or with a reply to your thread to state their interest in trading with you, or share a thought they have about the transaction. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Organising_The_Transaction\">Organising The Transaction</span></h3>\n<p>There are three different ways for you to go about this. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cash_On_Delivery_-_C.O.D.\">Cash On Delivery - C.O.D.</span></h3>\n<p>You may have an item for sale, that fits into a mailbox. These items are the easiest to trade, as you can simply put them into a mailbox, select a recipient, check the C.O.D. tab, select a price, and send the item to your customer. The time it takes for the item to arrive depends on how high the enchantment on the mailbox is, and how far away your customer lives. You will be paid as soon as the customer receives the item.\nIn order to pick up an item sent to you via C.O.D., you simply go to a mailbox and receive the item. In order to successfully withdraw the item, you need the amount of money it costs to be in your bank, as it is automatically withdrawn from there. A courier fee of 1c per item applies (see <a href=\"/index.php/Mail\" title=\"Mail\">mail</a> for more details).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Pickup\">Pickup</span></h3>\n<p>You or your customer may choose Pickup for an option. That means that you either have to travel to your seller to pick up the item you wish to buy, or that your customer has to travel to you in order to pick up the item he wishes to buy. The likelihood of someone coming all the way to you to pick up their items depends on your location, the distance to them, and the value of the item. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Delivery\">Delivery</span></h3>\n<p>When selling an item, you may offer delivery. If you deliver to a location far away from you, you might consider applying delivery charges, which have to be discussed with your customer in advance. For bulk or loadable items, it is recommended to own a ship. However, if you are at a lake with a shallow canal to the outside sea, make sure you have a ship that is able to get through it. \nThe same applies to you if you wish for a seller to deliver to you - they may apply delivery charges just as well, so make sure to clarify on that before they make their way to you.\n</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you may use the new <a href=\"/index.php/Wagoner\" title=\"Wagoner\">wagoner</a> system which utilizes the <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">highway</a> system and an NPC to deliver the goods for you. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Payment\">Payment</span></h3>\n<p>This is explained in detail below. It is the last step of the transaction with your customer, and often the most problematic one. \n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 5),
(18018, 2295, 'Payment', 'Payment_2', 'Cash On Delivery (C.O.D.) The safest way to trade is via C.O.D.. You send the item to your buyer in a mailbox, and as they pick it up, you receive the money. If they do not pick it up, you will receive it back after a while. The money is automatically taken out of someone\'s bank account upon picking up the item. Ingame Currency You may also consider payment via ingame currency - usually silver. In an easy case, this can be traded for the actual item. For example, if you are selling armour to someone else, you can put the armour into the trade window, your partner puts the silver in, and upon closing the transaction you both have successfully received your items. If it concerns items that are not tradeable by window, it is usually a little bit more complicated. You may either find ways to lock your items and give the buyer the key upon receiving the money (For example, if you are selling mortar inside a BSB, you can lock it and trade the key to the bsb for the payment), or allow your customer to inspect the items, but ask him to pay before you unload them from your ship or other means of transport. The usual way in such cases is that players pay before receiving their items. Real Life Currency As of March 1st 2020, Wurm no longer allows trade with real life currency.', '<h3><span id=\"Cash_On_Delivery_(C.O.D.)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cash_On_Delivery_.28C.O.D..29\">Cash On Delivery (C.O.D.)</span></h3>\n<p>The safest way to trade is via C.O.D.. You send the item to your buyer in a mailbox, and as they pick it up, you receive the money. If they do not pick it up, you will receive it back after a while. The money is automatically taken out of someone\'s bank account upon picking up the item.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ingame_Currency\">Ingame Currency</span></h3>\n<p>You may also consider payment via ingame currency - usually silver. In an easy case, this can be traded for the actual item. For example, if you are selling armour to someone else, you can put the armour into the trade window, your partner puts the silver in, and upon closing the transaction you both have successfully received your items. If it concerns items that are not tradeable by window, it is usually a little bit more complicated. You may either find ways to lock your items and give the buyer the key upon receiving the money (For example, if you are selling mortar inside a BSB, you can lock it and trade the key to the bsb for the payment), or allow your customer to inspect the items, but ask him to pay before you unload them from your ship or other means of transport. The usual way in such cases is that players pay before receiving their items. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Real_Life_Currency\">Real Life Currency</span></h3>\n<p>As of March 1st 2020, Wurm no longer allows trade with real life currency.\n</p>', 6),
(18019, 2295, 'A Word Of Caution', 'A_Word_Of_Caution', 'While the Wurm community and staff try their best to prevent scams, no one but the people directly involved in the trade can be held responsible for the outcome of each transaction. Especially when trading via real life currency, that can become an issue. Scams are less than frequent, but they do happen, and you will wish to be as careful as possible to avoid that scenario. For that, there was an official warning to all players issued by the staff, which you are recommended to read. It is advised for you to trade only with people who have a reputation of completing successful trades, or who have someone respectable to back up their intentions as a first time trader. Make sure to take screenshots or even record your transactions and keep the results as proof for a successful transaction, or a scam just in case. If you are victim of a scam, issue a Support ticket and staff will attempt to support you in the matter as well as possible. However, as mentioned above, they can not issue refunds for payments made with out-of-game methods.', '<p>While the Wurm community and staff try their best to prevent scams, no one but the people directly involved in the trade can be held responsible for the outcome of each transaction. Especially when trading via real life currency, that can become an issue. Scams are less than frequent, but they do happen, and you will wish to be as careful as possible to avoid that scenario. For that, there was an official warning to all players issued by the staff, which you are recommended to read. It is advised for you to trade only with people who have a reputation of completing successful trades, or who have someone respectable to back up their intentions as a first time trader. \n</p>\n<p>Make sure to take screenshots or even record your transactions and keep the results as proof for a successful transaction, or a scam just in case. \n</p>\n<p>If you are victim of a scam, issue a Support ticket and staff will attempt to support you in the matter as well as possible. However, as mentioned above, they can not issue refunds for payments made with out-of-game methods.\n</p>', 7),
(18020, 4623, 'Shadow Requiem Citizen', 'Shadow_Requiem_Citizen', 'Wurm\'s resident Otaku. Blacklighter Alt Former elder of Ivalice and citizen of Serenity Port Titles - Timberman', '<p><i>Wurm\'s resident Otaku.</i>\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><b><a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighter</a> Alt</b></li>\n<li><b>Former elder of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ivalice\" title=\"Ivalice\">Ivalice</a> and citizen of <a class=\"new\" href=\"/index.php?title=Serenity_Port&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Serenity Port (page does not exist)\">Serenity Port</a></b></li>\n<li><b><a href=\"/index.php/Titles\" title=\"Titles\">Titles</a></b> - Timberman</li></ul></dd></dl>', 0),
(18021, 4118, 'Description', 'Description', 'A golden altar, with mystical carvings and inscriptions.', '<p><i>A golden altar, with mystical carvings and inscriptions.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18022, 4118, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failure to create the altar will use up 0.5 kg of gold Regardless of which god has domain over an area, any altar may be created in that area. Gold altars need to have the bless spell cast on them in order to be set to a specified deity. Stone and wooden altars , on the other hand, do not have this requirement. Improvement of the altar requires the standard jewelsmithing or blacksmithing tools. The use of heat here to make the altar \"glowing\" is not necessary as it is in most other smithing and metal-works endeavors. Any items placed on the altar do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do. All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory. For Benediction you will need anywhere from 13 to 20-some skill in Jewelry Smithing to make an altar. You must also have a premium account. Creation chance depends on your skill level and anvil quality.', '<ul><li>Failure to create the altar will use up 0.5 kg of gold</li>\n<li>Regardless of which god has domain over an area, any altar may be created in that area.</li>\n<li>Gold altars need to have the <a href=\"/index.php/Bless\" title=\"Bless\">bless</a> spell cast on them in order to be set to a specified deity. <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_altar\" title=\"Stone altar\">Stone</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_altar\" title=\"Wooden altar\">wooden altars</a>, on the other hand, do not have this requirement.</li>\n<li>Improvement of the altar requires the standard jewelsmithing or blacksmithing tools. The use of heat here to make the altar \"glowing\" is not necessary as it is in most other smithing and metal-works endeavors.</li>\n<li>Any items placed on the altar do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do.</li>\n<li>All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory.</li>\n<li>For Benediction you will need anywhere from 13 to 20-some skill in Jewelry Smithing to make an altar. You must also have a premium account.</li>\n<li>Creation chance depends on your skill level and anvil quality.</li></ul>', 1),
(18023, 4118, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Pray Sermons Sacrificing', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">Pray</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Faith#Sermons\" title=\"Faith\">Sermons</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sacrificing\" title=\"Sacrificing\">Sacrificing</a></li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18024, 4118, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Silver altar Wooden altar Stone altar Altar Religion Jewelry smithing', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Silver_altar\" title=\"Silver altar\">Silver altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_altar\" title=\"Wooden altar\">Wooden altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_altar\" title=\"Stone altar\">Stone altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">Altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18025, 4625, 'Description', 'Description', 'A metal altar made out of silver.', '<p><i>A metal altar made out of silver.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18026, 4625, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failure to create the altar will use up 0.5 kg of silver Regardless of which god has domain over an area, any altar may be created in that area. Silver altars need to have the bless spell cast on them in order to be set to a specified deity. Stone and wooden altars, on the other hand, do not have this requirement. Improvement of the altar requires the standard jewelsmithing or blacksmithing tools. The use of heat here to make the altar \"glowing\" is not necessary as it is in most other smithing and metal-works endeavors. Any items placed on the altar do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do. All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory.', '<ul><li>Failure to create the altar will use up 0.5 kg of silver</li>\n<li>Regardless of which god has domain over an area, any altar may be created in that area.</li>\n<li>Silver altars need to have the bless spell cast on them in order to be set to a specified deity. Stone and wooden altars, on the other hand, do not have this requirement.</li>\n<li>Improvement of the altar requires the standard jewelsmithing or blacksmithing tools. The use of heat here to make the altar \"glowing\" is not necessary as it is in most other smithing and metal-works endeavors.</li>\n<li>Any items placed on the altar do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do.</li>\n<li>All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory.</li></ul>', 1),
(18027, 4625, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Pray Sermons Sacrificing', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">Pray</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Faith#Sermons\" title=\"Faith\">Sermons</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sacrificing\" title=\"Sacrificing\">Sacrificing</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18028, 4625, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Gold altar Wooden altar Stone altar Altar Religion Jewelry smithing', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Gold_altar\" title=\"Gold altar\">Gold altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_altar\" title=\"Wooden altar\">Wooden altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_altar\" title=\"Stone altar\">Stone altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">Altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18040, 4631, 'Description', 'Description', 'A cosy bed with furs and sheets.', '<p><i>A cosy bed with furs and sheets.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18041, 4631, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You can logout in bed, accumulating useful sleep bonus the longer you are offline. Right-click the bed and select \'Bed\' > \'Sleep\'. A bed can only be slept on if it is inside a completed house. Otherwise the following message will display in your event window: The house is too windy to provide protection. To find out if a bed is available or who is sleeping in it, examine it. If the bed is occupied, it will say: Some kind of mysterious haze lingers over the <type of wood> bed, and you notice that the <type of wood> bed is occupied by the spirit of <playername> After the sleeper has accumulated the maximum sleep bonus (5 hours), the bed will be automatically freed up for other players to sleep in. If the bed is not on your own deed, there will be a 60 second timer to log out. Sleeping damages a bed, regardless of the house being on a deed or not. The quality of the head board affects the success chance when creating. The bed frame is damaged if you fail. Wood type is determined by the foot board . Beds can only be started inside a house. It does not have to be a finished house though. You could also build a new house around an existing bed. A bed cannot occupy the same tile as another bed or storage bin .  It can share a tile with a forge or oven. You can use furs larger than what the bed needs. When you add a fur, it will use one kilogram and give you back the rest. When finishing the bed, it will be placed perpendicular to you, with the pillow on left side. Can not be picked up by hand, but pushed, pulled, and turned. Can be loaded into any vehicle, except a small cart. Beds that do not have permissions set may be slept in by anyone who has a May Enter permission on the building where it\'s housed. Able to have items placed on it. There are two separate components of beds that can be dyed: the sheets and the wooden frame. Renting If you have manage item permissions of the house, you can rent beds to other players for coins , making it possible to earn money by running an inn . Right-click the bed and Select \'Bed\' > \'Rent 10 iron\' coins, \'Rent 25 iron\', \'Rent 50 iron\', \'Rent 1 copper\', \'Rent 10 copper\', \'Rent 1 silver\', \'Rent 10 silver\', or \'No rent\'. If you rent yourself a bed, the money will be withdrawn from your inventory and you will then logout to sleep.', '<ul><li>You can logout in bed, accumulating useful <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a> the longer you are offline. Right-click the bed and select \'Bed\' &gt; \'Sleep\'.</li>\n<li>A bed can only be slept on if it is inside a completed house. Otherwise the following message will display in your event window: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 10px 10px 10px 10px; display: block; width: 70%;\">The house is too windy to provide protection.</span></li>\n<li>To find out if a bed is available or who is sleeping in it, <a href=\"/index.php/Examine\" title=\"Examine\">examine</a> it. If the bed is occupied, it will say: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 10px 10px 10px 10px; display: block; width: 70%;\">Some kind of mysterious haze lingers over the <i>&lt;type of wood&gt;</i> bed, and you notice that the <i>&lt;type of wood&gt;</i> bed is occupied by the spirit of <i>&lt;playername&gt;</i></span></li>\n<li>After the sleeper has accumulated the maximum <a href=\"/index.php/Sleep_bonus\" title=\"Sleep bonus\">sleep bonus</a> (5 hours), the bed will be automatically freed up for other players to sleep in.</li>\n<li>If the bed is not on your own deed, there will be a 60 second timer to log out.</li>\n<li>Sleeping damages a bed, regardless of the house being on a deed or not.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Head_board\" title=\"Head board\">head board</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/index.php/Bed_frame\" title=\"Bed frame\">bed frame</a> is <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damaged</a> if you fail.</li>\n<li>Wood type is determined by the <a href=\"/index.php/Foot_board\" title=\"Foot board\">foot board</a>.</li>\n<li>Beds can only be started inside a house. It does not have to be a finished house though. You could also build a new house around an existing bed.</li>\n<li>A bed cannot occupy the same tile as another bed or <a href=\"/index.php/Storage_bin\" title=\"Storage bin\">storage bin</a>.  It can share a tile with a forge or oven.</li>\n<li>You can use furs larger than what the bed needs. When you add a fur, it will use one kilogram and give you back the rest.</li>\n<li>When finishing the bed, it will be placed perpendicular to you, with the pillow on left side.</li>\n<li>Can not be picked up by hand, but pushed, pulled, and turned.</li>\n<li>Can be <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">loaded</a> into any vehicle, except a small cart.</li>\n<li>Beds that do not have <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> set may be slept in by anyone who has a <b>May Enter</b> permission on the building where it\'s housed.</li>\n<li>Able to have items placed on it.</li>\n<li>There are two separate components of beds that can be dyed: the sheets and the wooden frame.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Renting\">Renting</span></h3>\n<ul><li>If you have manage item <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a> of the house, you can rent beds to other players for <a href=\"/index.php/Bank_of_Wurm\" title=\"Bank of Wurm\">coins</a>, making it possible to earn money by running an <a href=\"/index.php/Inn\" title=\"Inn\">inn</a>.\n<ul><li>Right-click the bed and Select \'Bed\' &gt; \'Rent 10 iron\' coins, \'Rent 25 iron\', \'Rent 50 iron\', \'Rent 1 copper\', \'Rent 10 copper\', \'Rent 1 silver\', \'Rent 10 silver\', or \'No rent\'.</li>\n<li>If you rent yourself a bed, the money will be withdrawn from your inventory and you will then logout to sleep.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(18042, 4631, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Canopy bed Straw bed Bedroll Festive bedroll', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Canopy_bed\" title=\"Canopy bed\">Canopy bed</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Straw_bed\" title=\"Straw bed\">Straw bed</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bedroll\" title=\"Bedroll\">Bedroll</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Festive_bedroll\" title=\"Festive bedroll\">Festive bedroll</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18045, 1910, 'Welcome to the Complete Database', 'Welcome_to_the_Complete_Database', 'The Complete Database is a reference to the whole of Wurm. Please select a category that you wish to look at. Feel free to edit and create pages! If you do, read the guidelines - click the link at the bottom of this page to read them. Items There is a list of all the items and information about them in this category. Skills There is a list of all the skills and information about them in this category. Resources A list of resources found in the game. These are raw materials like types of wood and ore. Bestiary A list of all the monsters that can be found. There are some pictures from travelers and fighters and information about each creature too. Terrain About the terrain, information about tile types and trees. Fighting About the fighting system. Religion About the different religions of Wurm such as Fo, Vynora, Magnaron and Libila. Kingdoms About the different kingdoms of Wurm like Jenn-Kellon. Servers About the different servers that Wurm offers. Currency About the currency and monetary system. Trade Trade in the world of Wurm. Lore Background story of the game. Highway About the highway system and its mechanics. Wurm Universe The space and time, and the land and sky of the Wurm Universe. What is the Complete Database? The Complete Database is a reference of Wurm items, resources, skills and basically everything to do with Wurm. It is organised in a neat fashion and made by the players of Wurm. This means you can edit it if you have some knowledge of Wurm that is not in this great database. But if you do, read the guidelines. See also the style guidelines for editing the wiki.', '<p>The Complete Database is a reference to the whole of Wurm. Please select a category that you wish to look at. Feel free to edit and create pages! If you do, read the guidelines - click the link at the bottom of this page to read them.\n</p>\n<dl><dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Items\" title=\"Category:Items\">Items</a></b></dt>\n<dd>There is a list of all the items and information about them in this category.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Skills\" title=\"Category:Skills\">Skills</a></b></dt>\n<dd>There is a list of all the skills and information about them in this category.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Resources\" title=\"Category:Resources\">Resources</a></b></dt>\n<dd>A list of resources found in the game. These are raw materials like types of wood and ore.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bestiary\" title=\"Category:Bestiary\">Bestiary</a></b></dt>\n<dd>A list of all the monsters that can be found. There are some pictures from travelers and fighters and information about each creature too.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Terrain\" title=\"Category:Terrain\">Terrain</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the terrain, information about tile types and trees.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the fighting system.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Religion\" title=\"Category:Religion\">Religion</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the different religions of Wurm such as Fo, Vynora, Magnaron and Libila.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Kingdoms\" title=\"Category:Kingdoms\">Kingdoms</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the different kingdoms of Wurm like Jenn-Kellon.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Servers\" title=\"Category:Servers\">Servers</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the different servers that Wurm offers.</dd>\n<dt><b><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Currency\" title=\"Currency\">Currency</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the currency and monetary system.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Trade\" title=\"Trade\">Trade</a></b></dt>\n<dd>Trade in the world of Wurm.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Lore\" title=\"Category:Lore\">Lore</a></b></dt>\n<dd>Background story of the game.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Highway\" title=\"Category:Highway\">Highway</a></b></dt>\n<dd>About the highway system and its mechanics.</dd>\n<dt><b><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Wurm_universe\" title=\"Category:Wurm universe\">Wurm Universe</a></b></dt>\n<dd>The space and time, and the land and sky of the Wurm Universe.</dd></dl>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<dl><dt><b>What is the Complete Database?</b></dt>\n<dd>The Complete Database is a reference of Wurm items, resources, skills and basically everything to do with Wurm. It is organised in a neat fashion and made by the players of Wurm. This means you can edit it if you have some knowledge of Wurm that is not in this great database. But if you do, read the guidelines.</dd></dl>\n<hr/>\n<p>See also the <a href=\"/index.php/Wurmpedia_editing_handbook\" title=\"Wurmpedia editing handbook\">style guidelines</a> for editing the wiki.\n</p>', 0),
(18046, 4005, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small wooden bucket.', '<p><i>A small wooden bucket.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18047, 4005, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Small buckets can be used for harvesting maple sap from maple trees, milking cows , sheep , or bison , and building a well . A small bucket may contain solids or liquids, but not both at once (with an exception to food items and liquids). Its capacity is 12 units of volume (not weight, its units are like a bulk storage bin ). A higher quality bucket will result in higher quality maple sap. It is the quality of the small nails that determine the success rate. Failure at creation results in damage to the plank and nails.', '<ul><li>Small buckets can be used for harvesting <a href=\"/index.php/Maple_sap\" title=\"Maple sap\">maple sap</a> from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Maple\" title=\"Maple\">maple</a> trees, <a href=\"/index.php/Milking\" title=\"Milking\">milking</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Cow\" title=\"Cow\">cows</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">sheep</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">bison</a>, and building a <a href=\"/index.php/Well\" title=\"Well\">well</a>.</li>\n<li>A small bucket may contain solids or liquids, but not both at once (with an exception to food items and liquids).</li>\n<li>Its capacity is 12 units of volume (not weight, its units are like a <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a>).</li>\n<li>A higher quality bucket will result in higher quality maple sap.</li>\n<li>It is the quality of the small nails that determine the success rate.</li>\n<li>Failure at creation results in damage to the plank and nails.</li></ul>', 1),
(18062, 4420, 'Item Storage', 'Item_Storage', 'Up to 5 items can be stored in a bank, though not all items can be stored (for example, logs are too large to fit). Containers must be empty when deposited. There is no decay on stored items. A character must designate a settlement token to use for bank actions. Items can only be deposited and withdrawn at the designated token. (It is not necessary to be a citizen of the settlement.) The bank can be moved to a different token at any time. The transition takes 24 real life hours, and the items inside are inaccessible during the process. If your bank account is at a deed which is disbanded , your bank account can be transferred to a new deed instantly. The item storage is not shared between servers. This means you can\'t access items you stored on a different server, but neither do they count towards the 5 item limit. Any food item will take immediate damage when trying to place in the bank. The Event window will state \"the (item) gets dirty.\"', '<p>Up to 5 items can be stored in a bank, though not all items can be stored (for example, logs are too large to fit). Containers must be empty when deposited. There is no <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> on stored items. \n</p>\n<p>A character must designate a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement_token\" title=\"Settlement token\">settlement token</a> to use for bank actions. Items can only be deposited and withdrawn at the designated token. (It is not necessary to be a citizen of the settlement.) The bank can be moved to a different token at any time. The transition takes 24 real life hours, and the items inside are inaccessible during the process. If your bank account is at a deed which is <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed#Disbanding\" title=\"Deed\">disbanded</a>, your bank account can be transferred to a new deed instantly.\n</p>\n<p>The item storage is not shared between servers. This means you can\'t access items you stored on a different server, but neither do they count towards the 5 item limit.\n</p>\n<p>Any food item will take immediate damage when trying to place in the bank. The Event window will state \"the (item) gets dirty.\"\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(18063, 4420, 'Money Storage', 'Money_Storage', 'You can also keep money in the bank. Money can only be deposited at the token designated for item storage (see above), but can be withdrawn at any settlement token. This means you do not have to withdraw money before going on a shopping trip, but you have to make it back safely if you sell something. Unlike items, deposited money is shared among servers. Money from the king (e.g. bought at the Wurm Store or from disbanding a settlement ) appears directly in your bank account, not in inventory .', '<p>You can also keep <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Money\" title=\"Money\">money</a> in the bank. Money can only be deposited at the token designated for item storage (see above), but can be withdrawn at any settlement token. This means you do not have to withdraw money before going on a shopping trip, but you have to make it back safely if you sell something.\n</p>\n<p>Unlike items, deposited money is shared among servers.\n</p>\n<p>Money from the king (e.g. bought at the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://store.wurmonline.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wurm Store</a> or from disbanding a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">settlement</a>) appears directly in your bank account, not in <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(18064, 4420, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Bank of Wurm', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bank_of_Wurm\" title=\"Bank of Wurm\">Bank of Wurm</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18082, 4646, 'Description', 'Description', 'The monstrously large type of scorpion found in woods and caves here is fairly aggressive.', '<p><i>The monstrously large type of scorpion found in woods and caves here is fairly aggressive.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18083, 4646, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Stronger than a bear or a huge spider . Fast attack speed. Does stinging (pierce), clawing (slash), and biting damage. Can sting 10 damage per hit on unarmoured body parts. Moves slowly and can be outrun fairly easily in most cases. They cannot be hitched to carts when dominated. Can be ridden with 25 Body Control.', '<ul><li>Stronger than a <a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">bear</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_spider\" title=\"Huge spider\">huge spider</a>.</li>\n<li>Fast attack speed.</li>\n<li>Does stinging (pierce), clawing (slash), and biting damage.</li>\n<li>Can sting 10 damage per hit on unarmoured body parts.</li>\n<li>Moves slowly and can be outrun fairly easily in most cases.</li>\n<li>They cannot be hitched to carts when dominated.</li>\n<li>Can be ridden with 25 Body Control.</li></ul>', 1),
(18084, 4646, 'Images', 'Images', '', '<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Scorpion_daylight.jpg\"><img alt=\"Scorpion daylight.jpg\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"277\" data-file-width=\"300\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"277\" src=\"/images/b/b8/Scorpion_daylight.jpg\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Scorpion_daylight.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div></div></div></div>', 2),
(18087, 4648, 'Description', 'Description', 'A clear liquid with a slightly sweet taste. Harvested from a maple tree with a bucket during the appropriate season .', '<p><i>A clear liquid with a slightly sweet taste.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Harvested from a <a href=\"/index.php/Maple_tree\" title=\"Maple tree\">maple tree</a> with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bucket\" title=\"Bucket\">bucket</a> during the appropriate <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18088, 4648, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Maple sap is turned into maple syrup by cooking it.\nIt may be cooked in a sauce pan or cauldron heated in a oven or campfire .', '<p><b>Maple sap</b> is turned into maple syrup by cooking it.\nIt may be cooked in a <a href=\"/index.php/Sauce_pan\" title=\"Sauce pan\">sauce pan</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Cauldron\" title=\"Cauldron\">cauldron</a> heated in a <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>. \n</p>', 1),
(18089, 4648, 'Harvest', 'Harvest', 'Higher forestry will yield more maple sap and increase the quality that the collected sap will be. 1 kg below 26 skill (maximum amount from Mature trees) 2 kg at 26 skill (maximum amount from younger stages of Old trees) 3 kg at 53 skill 4 kg at 80 skill', '<p>Higher <a href=\"/index.php/Forestry\" title=\"Forestry\">forestry</a> will yield more maple sap and increase the quality that the collected sap will be.\n</p>\n<ul><li>1 kg below 26 skill (maximum amount from Mature trees)</li>\n<li>2 kg at 26 skill (maximum amount from younger stages of Old trees)</li>\n<li>3 kg at 53 skill</li>\n<li>4 kg at 80 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(18090, 4648, 'Storage', 'Storage', 'Maple sap can be stowed in a small barrel.', '<p>Maple sap can be stowed in a small barrel.\n</p>', 3),
(18091, 4424, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin pointy blade on a shaft, used to make small holes.', '<p><i>A thin pointy blade on a shaft, used to make small holes.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18092, 4424, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to improve leather items by punching holes in them.', '<ul><li>Used to <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improve</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_item\" title=\"Leather item\">leather items</a> by punching holes in them.</li></ul>', 1),
(18102, 4652, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'This page contains links or descriptions of 3rd party websites, newspapers, magazines or television reviews of Wurm Online . Please do not add sites that only have a simple link to Wurm Online; the sites should have at least a simple description and a picture.', '<p>This page contains links or descriptions of 3rd party websites, newspapers, magazines or television reviews of <a href=\"/index.php/Main_Page\" title=\"Main Page\">Wurm Online</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Please do not add sites that only have a simple link to Wurm Online; the sites should have at least a simple description and a picture.\n</p>', 0),
(18103, 4652, 'Website Reviews', 'Website_Reviews', 'http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wurm_Online http://www.f13.net/index.php?itemid=151 http://www.boomtown.net/en_uk/articles/art.view.php?id=4984 http://www.gamerswithjobs.com/node/27230 http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/wurm-online-preview http://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2009/06/08/frontier-psychiatry-wurm-online-interview/', '<ul><li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wurm_Online\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wurm_Online</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.f13.net/index.php?itemid=151\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.f13.net/index.php?itemid=151</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.boomtown.net/en_uk/articles/art.view.php?id=4984\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.boomtown.net/en_uk/articles/art.view.php?id=4984</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.gamerswithjobs.com/node/27230\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.gamerswithjobs.com/node/27230</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/wurm-online-preview\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/wurm-online-preview</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2009/06/08/frontier-psychiatry-wurm-online-interview/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2009/06/08/frontier-psychiatry-wurm-online-interview/</a></li></ul>', 1),
(18104, 4652, 'Printed Reviews', 'Printed_Reviews', 'PC Gamer UK May 2009', '<p>PC Gamer UK May 2009\n</p>', 2),
(18105, 4652, 'Television Reviews', 'Television_Reviews', '', '', 3),
(18106, 4652, 'See Also', 'See_Also', '', '', 4),
(18107, 4142, 'Description', 'Description', 'A brown dirt-looking clump with regions of dark crystals.', '<p><i>A brown dirt-looking clump with regions of dark crystals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18108, 4142, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from tin veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 0.5 kg of tin lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of tin you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Tin_vein\" title=\"Tin vein\">tin veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 0.5 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Tin_lump\" title=\"Tin lump\">tin lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of tin you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18109, 4142, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Tin lump', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Tin_lump\" title=\"Tin lump\">Tin lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18110, 4141, 'Decoration', 'Decoration', 'A chunk of greenish brown glassy crystallines.', '<p><i>A chunk of greenish brown glassy crystallines.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18111, 4141, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mined from zinc veins found underground. Activate a pickaxe , right-click the vein and select Mine . The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a campfire , stone forge or smelter , will produce 1.0 kg of zinc lump . Ore can also be analysed to prospect underground. For information regarding the quality of zinc you may get from a vein, please refer to prospecting .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mined</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_vein\" title=\"Zinc vein\">zinc veins</a> found underground.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>, <b>right-click</b> the vein and select <b>Mine</b>.</li>\n<li>The result of 1 mining action (20 kg of ore), when smelted in a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_forge\" title=\"Stone forge\">stone forge</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">smelter</a>, will produce 1.0 kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">zinc lump</a>.</li>\n<li>Ore can also be <a href=\"/index.php/Analyse\" title=\"Analyse\">analysed</a> to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospect</a> underground.</li>\n<li>For information regarding the quality of zinc you may get from a vein, please refer to <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting#Vein_quality\" title=\"Prospecting\"> prospecting</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18112, 4141, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Zinc lump', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">Zinc lump</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18115, 4657, 'Description', 'Description', 'The parent skill when using butchering or carving knives.', '<p>The parent skill when using butchering or carving knives. \n</p>', 0),
(18116, 4657, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A low quality tool will produce higher skill gain for this skill.', '<ul><li>A low quality tool will produce higher skill gain for this skill.</li></ul>', 1),
(18117, 4657, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Knives Body > Body control Mind > Mind logic Subskills Carving knife Butchering knife', '<ul><li>Knives</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">Carving knife</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Butchering_knife\" title=\"Butchering knife\">Butchering knife</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18118, 4657, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Knifer at 50 skill Piercer at 70 skill Knife Specialist at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Knifer at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Piercer at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Knife Specialist at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18133, 4659, 'Description', 'Description', 'Chunky grains of white salt.', '<p><i>Chunky grains of white salt.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18134, 4659, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Salt can be found on certain ore and rock tiles while mining as well as milling rock salt , which is mined from rocksalt tiles. The maximum QL of the salt will be capped by your mining skill or the maximum QL of the rock/ore tile, whichever is lower. It can also be granted as a gift to a follower or priest when praying . You can also acquire salt by boiling salty water in a cauldron . 64 kg of salty water in a cauldron will produce 6 salt with 63.30 kg of water remaining. QL of salt depends on Hot food cooking skill, but not less than 10. If included in cooking recipes, salt reduces the decay by half. Salt is also used in the creation of animal rugs . It is a popular misconception that putting salt in a barrel with food decreases decay. This has been proven as untrue. If you have a prospecting skill of at least 40, you can prospect a tile and see if it contains salt. Placing a salt (or any food item) into your bank will cause it to immediately take some damage. The Event window will state \"the salt gets dirty.\"', '<ul><li>Salt can be found on certain <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">ore</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Rock_tile\" title=\"Rock tile\">rock tiles</a> while <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> as well as <a href=\"/index.php/Milling\" title=\"Milling\">milling</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Rock_salt_(shard)\" title=\"Rock salt (shard)\"> rock salt</a>, which is mined from <a href=\"/index.php/Rock_salt_(vein)\" title=\"Rock salt (vein)\">rocksalt</a> tiles. The maximum QL of the salt will be capped by your <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> skill or the maximum QL of the rock/ore tile, whichever is lower.</li>\n<li>It can also be granted as a gift to a <a href=\"/index.php/Follower\" title=\"Follower\">follower</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priest</a> when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">praying</a>.</li>\n<li>You can also acquire salt by boiling salty water in a <a href=\"/index.php/Cauldron\" title=\"Cauldron\">cauldron</a>. 64 kg of salty water in a cauldron will produce 6 salt with 63.30 kg of water remaining. QL of salt depends on <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">Hot food cooking</a> skill, but not less than 10.</li>\n<li>If included in cooking recipes, salt reduces the <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> by half.</li>\n<li>Salt is also used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking#Rugs\" title=\"Leatherworking\">animal rugs</a>.</li>\n<li>It is a popular misconception that putting salt in a barrel with food decreases decay. This has been proven as untrue.</li>\n<li>If you have a <a href=\"/index.php/Prospecting\" title=\"Prospecting\">prospecting</a> skill of at least 40, you can prospect a tile and see if it contains salt.</li>\n<li>Placing a salt (or any food item) into your <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bank\" title=\"Bank\">bank</a> will cause it to immediately take some damage. The Event window will state \"the salt gets dirty.\"</li></ul>', 1),
(18135, 4659, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Spices', '<p><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spices\" title=\"Spices\">Spices</a>\n</p>', 2),
(18136, 4660, 'Description', 'Description', 'Made for carving, this knife has a broad blade and half a hilt.', '<p><i>Made for carving, this knife has a broad blade and half a hilt.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18137, 4660, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used for carving wood, primarily in the creation or improvement of carpentry and fine carpentry items. The quality of both the blade and the handle affect the success rate. The quality of the blade caps the quality of the finished product. Can also be used for butchering but it\'s not good as a butchering knife . Very effective at destroying wooden house walls. Carving knife is both the item and the name of the skill gained when using a carving knife.', '<ul><li>Used for carving wood, primarily in the creation or improvement of <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Fine_carpentry\" title=\"Fine carpentry\">fine carpentry</a> items.</li>\n<li>The quality of <b>both</b> the blade and the handle affect the success rate.</li>\n<li>The quality of the blade caps the quality of the finished product.</li>\n<li>Can also be used for butchering but it\'s not good as a <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering_knife\" title=\"Butchering knife\">butchering knife</a>.</li>\n<li>Very effective at destroying wooden house walls.</li>\n<li>Carving knife is both the item and the name of the skill gained when using a carving knife.</li></ul>', 1),
(18138, 4660, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a carving knife Knives > carving knife Mind > Mind logic Body > Body control When creating a carving knife Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a carving knife\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Knives\" title=\"Knives\">Knives</a> &gt; carving knife</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a carving knife\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18139, 4660, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Stabber at 50 skill Carver at 70 skill Whittler at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Stabber at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Carver at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Whittler at 90 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18179, 1881, 'The telling of Old Guard', 'The_telling_of_Old_Guard', 'When the first wurmians came here this land was wild and dangerous. The few trained fighters there was had their hands full looking after new town and keeping the citizens there safe from the various beasts lurking in the woods. The tales from those who left and came back told of bounty and riches hardly imaginable to those who lived their monotonous lives in New Town. The safety of selling spindles and pottery bowls to Jake every night came with a price... and that price was adventure and excitement. It didn\'t take long before BaldEagleOG decided he to deserved better than carving spindles. He started systematically exploring his surroundings looking for a more fitting camp site. He soon decided that it was impossible to navigate the thick forrest, so he started looking for a way up to the top of Big Mountain. He knew that from up there he would be able to scout vast areas and find a brilliant spot for his next homestead, only to find it was hopeless since the mountain was surrounded by vertical cliffs all around. - One day I ran into a black wolf in the forrest. I was out of water and pretty damn tired, so i was lucky he was up wind from me. I started manouvering around him, but I soon realized he had me trapped in a small valley. Having nowhere else to turn i decided to get as far away as possible and hope for him to walk the other way. While looking for a place to rest up I stumbled on to a path that looked like it was in regular use. It was no animal trail, but people out here didn\'t necesarily mean friends. Since i was low on food and water, and had little of any value with me, except from my life I decided to take my chances. Just a few minutes down the trail i noticed it was ascending slightly, and up ahead i could see the trail raising above the treetops that was surrounding me. That blessed wolf! This was the first visit Bald ever made to Donner\'s Pass. Here he met Beowulf who had his settlement already set up halfway up to the top of Big Mountain. He led Bald to a viewpoint and Bald discovered that the forrest ha had tediously scouted for the past two days was all part of a huge valley. The size! The potential! BaldEagle and Beowulf gained each others trust, and soon enough they agreed it was a good idea for Bald to settle in the valley. They would be close enough in a time of crisis, yet have room to do their own things. An alliance was slowly forming. In time they both recruited help from travelers who had left New Time in boredom. They each built a separate camp - Donner\'s Pass and OldGuard. In time the ambition grew, and the manpower with it. Camps became villages and the valley was sealed of to stop any scavengers from exploiting the land. While the adventure moves forth the dream of prosperity has come to pass. Life in the Valley is plentifull, though demanding...', '<p>When the first wurmians came here this land was wild and dangerous. The few trained fighters there was had their hands full looking after new town and keeping the citizens there safe from the various beasts lurking in the woods. The tales from those who left and came back told of bounty and riches hardly imaginable to those who lived their monotonous lives in New Town. The safety of selling spindles and pottery bowls to Jake every night came with a price... and that price was adventure and excitement.\n</p>\n<p>It didn\'t take long before BaldEagleOG decided he to deserved better than carving spindles. He started systematically exploring his surroundings looking for a more fitting camp site. He soon decided that it was impossible to navigate the thick forrest, so he started looking for a way up to the top of Big Mountain. He knew that from up there he would be able to scout vast areas and find a brilliant spot for his next homestead, only to find it was hopeless since the mountain was surrounded by vertical cliffs all around.\n</p>\n<p>- One day I ran into a black wolf in the forrest. I was out of water and pretty damn tired, so i was lucky he was up wind from me. I started manouvering around him, but I soon realized he had me trapped in a small valley. Having nowhere else to turn i decided to get as far away as possible and hope for him to walk the other way. While looking for a place to rest up I stumbled on to a path that looked like it was in regular use. It was no animal trail, but people out here didn\'t necesarily mean friends. Since i was low on food and water, and had little of any value with me, except from my life I decided to take my chances. Just a few minutes down the trail i noticed it was ascending slightly, and up ahead i could see the trail raising above the treetops that was surrounding me. That blessed wolf!\n</p>\n<p>This was the first visit Bald ever made to Donner\'s Pass. Here he met Beowulf who had his settlement already set up halfway up to the top of Big Mountain. He led Bald to a viewpoint and Bald discovered that the forrest ha had tediously scouted for the past two days was all part of a huge valley. The size! The potential! BaldEagle and Beowulf gained each others trust, and soon enough they agreed it was a good idea for Bald to settle in the valley. They would be close enough in a time of crisis, yet have room to do their own things. An alliance was slowly forming.\n</p>\n<p>In time they both recruited help from travelers who had left New Time in boredom. They each built a separate camp - Donner\'s Pass and OldGuard. In time the ambition grew, and the manpower with it. Camps became villages and the valley was sealed of to stop any scavengers from exploiting the land.\n</p>\n<p>While the adventure moves forth the dream of prosperity has come to pass. Life in the Valley is plentifull, though demanding...\n</p>\n<hr/>', 0),
(18180, 1881, 'Members', 'Members', 'Elders Baldeagleog - OG Council Jobo Citizens Jinsei - OG Council Corvandee Neero Ostefisk Jenna Lokedott Mona Englishscott Cross Madt Priests Grym Riddlemaster Deemok', '<p><b>Elders</b><br/>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Baldeagleog\" title=\"User:Baldeagleog\">Baldeagleog</a> - OG Council <br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Jobo\" title=\"User:Jobo\">Jobo</a><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n<b>Citizens</b><br/>\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/index.php/User:Jinsei\" title=\"User:Jinsei\">Jinsei</a> - OG Council <br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Corvandee\" title=\"User:Corvandee\">Corvandee</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Neero\" title=\"User:Neero\">Neero</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Ostefisk\" title=\"User:Ostefisk\">Ostefisk</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Jenna\" title=\"User:Jenna\">Jenna</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Lokedott\" title=\"User:Lokedott\">Lokedott</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Mona\" title=\"User:Mona\">Mona</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Englishscott\" title=\"User:Englishscott\">Englishscott</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Cross\" title=\"User:Cross\">Cross</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Madt\" title=\"User:Madt\">Madt</a>\n</p>\n<p><b>Priests</b><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Grym\" title=\"User:Grym\">Grym</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Riddlemaster\" title=\"User:Riddlemaster\">Riddlemaster</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/User:Deemok\" title=\"User:Deemok\">Deemok</a><br/>\n</p>\n<hr/>', 1),
(18181, 1881, 'Current \"Trainees\" of OG', 'Current_.22Trainees.22_of_OG', 'Ildilas Thrandwil Junkyj Burningfury Zerosk Crazyman', '<dl><dd>Ildilas</dd>\n<dd>Thrandwil</dd>\n<dd>Junkyj</dd>\n<dd>Burningfury</dd>\n<dd>Zerosk</dd>\n<dd>Crazyman</dd></dl>', 2),
(18182, 1881, 'Recruiting', 'Recruiting', 'We are constantly on the watch for hard working, resourceful and dedicated players with common sense. Our current age-span is 18 to  mid 30\'s.\nIf you are interested in joining Old Guard you will simply have to get to know us. :) Be warned joining OG is a process unless you know us in real-life. You will have to prove to us you are industrious and trustworthy. Usually the process is something along the lines of: hang out and chat, be hired for chores in the valley, get permanent access to resources within the valley, become trainee  and offered a house within the valley, and eventually get access to the village itself. This process may take weeks, so don\'t quit your day job when you decide you want to become an OG too. No - you may not have an application form. You will simply have to hunt us down in-game.', '<p>We are constantly on the watch for hard working, resourceful and dedicated players with common sense. Our current age-span is 18 to  mid 30\'s.\nIf you are interested in joining Old Guard you will simply have to get to know us. :) Be warned joining OG is a process unless you know us in real-life. You will have to prove to us you are industrious and trustworthy. Usually the process is something along the lines of: hang out and chat, be hired for chores in the valley, get permanent access to resources within the valley, become trainee  and offered a house within the valley, and eventually get access to the village itself. This process may take weeks, so <i>don\'t quit your day job</i> when you decide you want to become an OG too.\n<b>No - you may not have an application form. You will simply have to hunt us down in-game.</b>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(18183, 1881, 'Projects', 'Projects', 'These are the projects we have spent numerous hours on. Some larger than others, some of greater public interest. Bald\'s pond. (Completed) Big Mountain tunnel access (Completed) Public Arena (Planned) Public Zoo (Planned) Valley Map (Pending)', '<p>These are the projects we have spent numerous hours on. Some larger than others, some of greater public interest.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>Bald\'s pond. <i>(Completed)</i></li>\n<li>Big Mountain tunnel access <i>(Completed)</i></li>\n<li>Public Arena <i>(Planned)</i></li>\n<li>Public Zoo <i>(Planned)</i></li>\n<li>Valley Map <i>(Pending)</i></li></ul></dd></dl>', 4),
(18184, 1881, 'Trade', 'Trade', 'We have Iron , Silver , Zinc , Tin , Lead and copper available for trade. Our stores have moved to the OG Bazaar. They will be undergoing some slight reconfigurations in the near future. Please stand by for updates. Feel free to contact us in-game for any requests.', '<p>We have <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">Iron</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">Silver</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">Zinc</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Tin_lump\" title=\"Tin lump\">Tin</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lead_lump\" title=\"Lead lump\">Lead</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">copper</a> available for trade.\n</p>\n<p>Our stores have moved to the OG Bazaar. They will be undergoing some slight reconfigurations in the near future. Please stand by for updates. Feel free to contact us in-game for any requests.\n</p>', 5),
(18185, 1881, 'Allies', 'Allies', 'Donners Pass Whosville', '<dl><dd><ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Donners_Pass\" title=\"Donners Pass\">Donners Pass</a></li>\n<li>Whosville</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 6),
(18186, 1881, 'Links', 'Links', 'info Beowulf put together for the n00bs OldGuard Forums', '<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=6618%7CUsefull\" rel=\"nofollow\">info Beowulf put together for the n00bs</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://oldguard.jconserv.net/index.php/\" rel=\"nofollow\">OldGuard Forums</a></li></ul>', 7),
(18193, 4673, 'Description', 'Description', 'The small, sharp blade of a carving knife.', '<p><i>The small, sharp blade of a carving knife.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18194, 4673, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a carving knife when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18195, 4673, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wooden handle quality determines chance of creation. Ten carving knife blades are required to create a knife trap .', '<ul><li>Wooden handle quality determines chance of creation.</li>\n<li>Ten carving knife blades are required to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Knife_trap\" title=\"Knife trap\">knife trap</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(18196, 4674, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sunder is a spell that priests of Magranon can use to cause damage to some items, including, but not limited to, any item that can be bashed by players. It deals up to 20 damage, with damage depending on the power of the cast. Higher damage and quality on the item will reduce damage taken. Heavier objects above 5kg will take reduced damage.', '<p>Sunder is a spell that <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> can use to cause <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> to some items, including, but not limited to, any item that can be bashed by players.\n</p>\n<p>It deals up to 20 damage, with damage depending on the power of the cast. Higher damage and quality on the item will reduce damage taken.\n</p>\n<p>Heavier objects above 5kg will take reduced damage.\n</p>', 0),
(18209, 4676, 'Description', 'Description', 'Can be cast on both aggressive and non-aggressive creatures. Will take the target down to very low health (typically \"dying\" status), but never kill it, with damage based on cast power. It\'s suspected to have the same effect as the Orb of doom , but where the artifact is a weapon of mass destruction, Smite only affects the target of the spell.', '<p>Can be cast on both aggressive and non-aggressive creatures.\n</p>\n<p>Will take the target down to very low health (typically \"dying\" status), but never kill it, with damage based on cast power.\n</p>\n<p>It\'s suspected to have the same effect as the <a href=\"/index.php/Orb_of_doom\" title=\"Orb of doom\">Orb of doom</a>, but where the artifact is a weapon of mass destruction, Smite only affects the target of the spell.\n</p>', 0),
(18210, 4676, 'Offensive spell resistance', 'Offensive_spell_resistance', 'Many offensive spells in the game now also have their own resistances. These function identically to the healing resistance above, but have much lower maximum duration for their resistance values. The duration of this effect is based on how much damage is done, and will reduce all further damage on the target from the same spell. The maximum duration of resistance various depending on the spell, and the reduction scales linearly from that mark. For example, if you have 1 minute of resistance remaining and the spell has a maximum resistance duration of 2 minutes, you will receive 50% normal damage from a further cast of that spell. Smite has a maximum resistance duration of 5 minutes.', '<p>Many offensive spells in the game now also have their own resistances. These function identically to the healing resistance above, but have much lower maximum duration for their resistance values. The duration of this effect is based on how much damage is done, and will reduce all further damage on the target from the same spell.\n</p>\n<p>The maximum duration of resistance various depending on the spell, and the reduction scales linearly from that mark. For example, if you have 1 minute of resistance remaining and the spell has a maximum resistance duration of 2 minutes, you will receive 50% normal damage from a further cast of that spell.\n</p>\n<p>Smite has a maximum resistance duration of 5 minutes.\n</p>', 1),
(18220, 3480, 'Description', 'Description', 'If you die , you may choose to respawn at different locations. All players have a infinite amount of respawns. You can choose to use the /respawn command while still alive. This will open the Respawn dialog and allow you to kill yourself in order to respawn. If the respawn window does not show after you die, type in /respawn into the chat window.', '<p>If you <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Die\" title=\"Die\">die</a>, you may choose to respawn at different locations. All players have a infinite amount of respawns. \n</p>\n<p>You can choose to use the <code>/respawn</code> command while still alive. This will open the <b>Respawn</b> dialog and allow you to kill yourself in order to respawn.\n</p>\n<p>If the respawn window does not show after you die, type in <code>/respawn</code> into the chat window. \n</p>', 0),
(18221, 3480, 'General Respawn Locations', 'General_Respawn_Locations', 'You can respawn at your kingdom\'s starter town of your current server . You can respawn at your village . You can respawn at a settlement you are allied with, if you died within 50 tiles of its token. You can respawn at your tent , if it is placed on the ground. On PVP servers, the tent must be placed in your kingdom\'s area of influence.', '<ul><li>You can respawn at your kingdom\'s starter town of your <a href=\"/index.php/Server_types\" title=\"Server types\">current server</a>.</li>\n<li>You can respawn at your <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">village</a>.</li>\n<li>You can respawn at a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">settlement</a> you are allied with, if you died within 50 tiles of its token.</li>\n<li>You can respawn at your <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tent\" title=\"Tent\">tent</a>, if it is placed on the ground. On PVP servers, the tent must be placed in your kingdom\'s area of influence.</li></ul>', 1),
(18222, 3480, 'Server Dependent Respawn Locations', 'Server_Dependent_Respawn_Locations', 'Epic cluster starting towns Desertion : Glittershore Affliction : Deadlake Serenity : Strongbox Elevation : Flamma (MR), Gloomshade (BL), High Hopes (JK) Southern Freedom Isles starting towns Independence : The Howl, Freedom Market, Haven\'s Landing Deliverance : Green Dog Exodus : Esert Celebration : Tap Dance Release : Sloping Sands Pristine : Blossom Xanadu : Glasshollow, Vrock Landing, Summerholt, Greymead, Whitefay, Linton, Lormere, Newspring, Esteron Chaos (PVP) : Non-premium players on Chaos are not given an option to respawn at a specific location. They will respawn on a random tile on the server. If KOS\'d at your own starter town, you will get the option to respawn \"Somewhere\". Hunter\'s Lodge: (Freedom default) The Landing: (Freedom) Gold Coast: (Freedom) The Shroud: ( Horde of the Summoned ) Northern Freedom Isles starting towns Harmony : Heartland, Harmony Bay Melody : Overture Cadence: Sonata, Encore Defiance (PVP) Rumble : (Mol-Rehan) Frontier : (Jenn-Kellon) Rotten Hollow : (Horde of the Summoned)', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Epic_cluster_starting_towns\">Epic cluster starting towns</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Desertion : Glittershore</li>\n<li>Affliction : Deadlake</li>\n<li>Serenity : Strongbox</li>\n<li>Elevation : Flamma (MR), Gloomshade (BL), High Hopes (JK)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Southern_Freedom_Isles_starting_towns\">Southern Freedom Isles starting towns</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Independence : The Howl, Freedom Market, Haven\'s Landing</li>\n<li>Deliverance : Green Dog</li>\n<li>Exodus : Esert</li>\n<li>Celebration : Tap Dance</li>\n<li>Release : Sloping Sands</li>\n<li>Pristine : Blossom</li>\n<li>Xanadu : Glasshollow, Vrock Landing, Summerholt, Greymead, Whitefay, Linton, Lormere, Newspring, Esteron</li>\n<li>Chaos (PVP) : Non-premium players on Chaos are not given an option to respawn at a specific location. They will respawn on a random tile on the server. If KOS\'d at your own starter town, you will get the option to respawn \"Somewhere\".\n<ul><li>Hunter\'s Lodge: (Freedom default)</li>\n<li>The Landing: (Freedom)</li>\n<li>Gold Coast: (Freedom)</li>\n<li>The Shroud: (<a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a>)</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Northern_Freedom_Isles_starting_towns\">Northern Freedom Isles starting towns</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Harmony : Heartland, Harmony Bay</li>\n<li>Melody : Overture</li>\n<li>Cadence: Sonata, Encore</li>\n<li>Defiance (PVP)\n<ul><li>Rumble : (Mol-Rehan)</li>\n<li>Frontier : (Jenn-Kellon)</li>\n<li>Rotten Hollow : (Horde of the Summoned)</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(18237, 4640, 'Description', 'Description', 'Milking is a skill used when milking cows , sheep , or bison .', '<p>Milking is a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> used when milking <a href=\"/index.php/Cow\" title=\"Cow\">cows</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Sheep\" title=\"Sheep\">sheep</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">bison</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18238, 4640, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To milk an animal, activate a container like a jar , a small bucket or a water skin , right-click the cow and choose Milk . An animal can be milked several times per day. Milk is always 100 QL , but combining damaged milk results in lower QL. Milk can be used to make cheese, butter, and cream. It is also an ingredient in many other cooking and baking recipes. The amount of milk produced depends on milking skill level and age of the animal: 1.00kg below 26 skill 2.00kg at 26 skill (maximum amount for Adolescent animals) 3.00kg at 53 skill (maximum amount for Mature animals) 4.00kg at 80 skill', '<ul><li>To milk an animal, <a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">container</a> like a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Jar\" title=\"Jar\">jar</a>, a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_bucket\" title=\"Small bucket\">small bucket</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Water_skin\" title=\"Water skin\">water skin</a>, right-click the cow and choose <b>Milk</b>.</li>\n<li>An animal can be milked several times per day.</li>\n<li>Milk is always 100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a>, but combining <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damaged</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Milk\" title=\"Milk\">milk</a> results in lower QL.</li>\n<li>Milk can be used to make cheese, butter, and cream. It is also an ingredient in many other <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Baking\" title=\"Baking\">baking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>The amount of milk produced depends on milking skill level and age of the animal:\n<ul><li>1.00kg below 26 skill</li>\n<li>2.00kg at 26 skill (maximum amount for Adolescent animals)</li>\n<li>3.00kg at 53 skill (maximum amount for Mature animals)</li>\n<li>4.00kg at 80 skill</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(18239, 4640, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Nature > Milking Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Nature\" title=\"Nature\">Nature</a> &gt; Milking</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18240, 4640, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Milkman/Milkmaid at 50 skill Milking Machine at 70 skill Cow Whisperer at 90 skill Udder Madness at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Milkman/Milkmaid at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Milking Machine at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Cow Whisperer at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Udder Madness at 100 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18248, 2804, 'Description', 'Description', 'A felled tree. Can be used in palisades or to make smaller logs from. It is made from [wood type].', '<p><i>A felled tree. Can be used in palisades or to make smaller logs from. It is made from [wood type].</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18249, 2804, 'Cuts to fell', 'Cuts_to_fell', 'As trees age they take more hits to cut down. At 85 Woodcutting and using a 85 ql hatchet an overage tree usually takes 2 hits to fall.', '<p>As trees age they take more hits to cut down.\n</p>\n<ul><li>At 85 <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">Woodcutting</a> and using a 85 ql hatchet an overage tree usually takes 2 hits to fall.</li></ul>', 1),
(18250, 2804, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A felled tree is primarily used for making logs , wooden palisade gates , palisades , keel sections and masts . The quality of the felled tree depends on the character\'s woodcutting skill as well as the quality of the hatchet used to fell it. A felled tree consumes 320 volume regardless of weight. A Hatchet is the most effective tool for cutting them down. Many medium size and larger bladed tools or weapons can, at a slower speed, cut down a tree. You can now right-click Felled Trees and select \'Discard\' to get rid of them immediately. Older trees (except shrivelled) produce a heavier felled tree.  See tree ages for more information. Age Weight Old (1) 106.67 kg Old (1), sprouting 120.00 kg Old (2) 133.33 kg Old (2), sprouting 146.67 kg Very old 160.00 kg Very old, sprouting 173.33 kg Overaged 186.67 kg', '<ul><li>A felled tree is primarily used for making <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_palisade_gate\" title=\"Wooden palisade gate\">wooden palisade gates</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Palisade\" title=\"Palisade\">palisades</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">keel sections</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Mast\" title=\"Mast\">masts</a>.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the felled tree depends on the character\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">woodcutting</a> skill as well as the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Axes\" title=\"Category:Axes\">hatchet</a> used to fell it.</li>\n<li>A felled tree consumes 320 <a href=\"/index.php/Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> regardless of weight.</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">Hatchet</a> is the most effective tool for cutting them down. Many medium size and larger bladed tools or weapons can, at a slower speed, cut down a tree.</li>\n<li>You can now right-click Felled Trees and select \'Discard\' to get rid of them immediately.</li>\n<li>Older <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a> (except shrivelled) produce a heavier felled tree.  See <a href=\"/index.php/Tree#Tree.2FBush_Ages\" title=\"Tree\">tree ages</a> for more information.</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"150\">Age\n</th>\n<th align=\"LEFT\" width=\"90\">Weight\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old (1)\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">106.67 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old (1), sprouting\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">120.00 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old (2)\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">133.33 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old (2), sprouting\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">146.67 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Very old\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">160.00 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Very old, sprouting\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">173.33 kg\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Overaged\n</td>\n<td align=\"LEFT\">186.67 kg\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(18251, 2804, 'Rare Functionality', 'Rare_Functionality', 'Note: Rare functionality is still not completely understood and is an exciting aspect of the game.  Most information listed is only an observation of one or more players rather than confirmed by developers. A rare felled tree will produce a few normal logs and a single rare log. The rare log is created from the last log cut from its trunk.', '<table style=\"background-color:#f8f8f8; -moz-border-radius:10px; width:50%; border:2px solid #e0e0e0; margin-left:0 auto; padding:5px; -moz-outline-style: outset; -moz-outline-radius: 10px; -moz-outline-color: #e0e0e0;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"30\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/30px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/45px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/60px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"30\"/></a></div>\n</td>\n<td><b>Note:</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">Rare</a> functionality is still not completely understood and is an exciting aspect of the game.  Most information listed is only an observation of one or more players rather than confirmed by developers.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li>A rare felled tree will produce a few normal logs and a single rare log. The rare log is created from the last log cut from its trunk.</li></ul>', 3),
(18252, 3353, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large heavy metal lock, ready to fit in a gate. Gate lock can be attached to a gate . It comes with a key of the same quality.', '<p><i>A large heavy metal lock, ready to fit in a gate.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Gate lock</b> can be attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate\" title=\"Gate\">gate</a>. It comes with a <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">key</a> of the same quality.\n</p>', 0),
(18253, 3353, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To attach a gate lock, activate the lock in your inventory, right-click the gate, and select Attach lock . You do not need to have the key in your inventory or be the lock\'s creator to do this.', '<p>To attach a gate lock, <a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">activate</a> the lock in your inventory, right-click the gate, and select <i>Attach lock</i>. You do not need to have the key in your inventory or be the lock\'s creator to do this.\n</p>', 1),
(18254, 3353, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When used, the gate\'s access options can be restricted with permissions . The key, created with the lock, acts as a manual way for an individual player to bypass the lock\'s permissions and gain quick access. Gate locks will not be removed if the gate is picked . Instead, the gate will remain unlocked for a limited time. Gate locks may be replaced with better quality locks by activating the new lock and right-clicking the gate. This may only be done by the character who attached the original lock. The quality of the metal lump used in creation caps the maximum quality of the produced lock.', '<ul><li>When used, the gate\'s access options can be restricted with <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Gates\" title=\"Permissions\">permissions</a>. The key, created with the lock, acts as a manual way for an individual player to bypass the lock\'s permissions and gain quick access.</li>\n<li>Gate locks will not be removed if the gate is <a href=\"/index.php/Lockpicking\" title=\"Lockpicking\">picked</a>. Instead, the gate will remain unlocked for a limited time.</li>\n<li>Gate locks may be replaced with better <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> locks by activating the new lock and right-clicking the gate. This may only be done by the character who attached the original lock.</li>\n<li>The quality of the metal lump used in creation caps the maximum quality of the produced lock.</li></ul>', 2),
(18255, 4656, 'Description', 'Description', 'A rugged metal blade on a shaft, used to make wood smoother.', '<p><i>A rugged metal blade on a shaft, used to make wood smoother.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18256, 4656, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A file is a tool mainly used in carpentry and its sub-skills for finishing and improving wooden items .', '<p>A <b>file</b> is a tool mainly used in <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> and its sub-skills for finishing and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Improving\" title=\"Improving\">improving</a> wooden <a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">items</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(18257, 4174, 'Description', 'Description', 'A saw, good for creating and sawing planks. Your basic metal saw. Used to make planks out of logs , kindling out of wood scrap , chop down trees and cut felled trees into logs .', '<p><i>A saw, good for creating and sawing planks.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Your basic metal saw. Used to make <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Planks\" title=\"Planks\">planks</a> out of <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Kindling\" title=\"Kindling\">kindling</a> out of <a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">wood scrap</a>, chop down <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a> and cut <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Felled_tree\" title=\"Felled tree\">felled trees</a> into <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18258, 4174, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The saw given with the starter set cannot be improved, but unlike most of the other starter tools it is not made of birchwood so will not be destroyed by fire. The saw and hatchet are the only tool that gives tool skill above 20 when cutting down trees with it. Other tool and weapon skills cannot be improved this way beyond 20; after that using them for cutting wood only gives woodcutting skill.', '<ul><li>The saw given with the starter set cannot be improved, but unlike most of the other starter tools it is not made of birchwood so will not be destroyed by fire.</li>\n<li>The saw and <a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">hatchet</a> are the only tool that gives tool skill above 20 when cutting down trees with it. Other tool and weapon skills cannot be improved this way beyond 20; after that using them for cutting wood only gives woodcutting skill.</li></ul>', 1),
(18259, 4174, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a saw Miscellaneous items > Saw When creating a saw Smithing > Blacksmithing', '<p>When using a saw\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Miscellaneous_items\" title=\"Miscellaneous items\">Miscellaneous items</a> &gt; Saw</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a saw\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18260, 4174, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'I\'m Sawry at 50 skill Chainsaw at 70 skill Jigsaw at 90 skill Tom Sawyer at 100 skill', '<ul><li>I\'m Sawry at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Chainsaw at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Jigsaw at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Tom Sawyer at 100 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18261, 4690, 'Description', 'Description', 'A piece of wood with tar and moss. It is made from [wood type].', '<p><i>A piece of wood with tar and moss. It is made from [wood type].</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18262, 4690, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Use a steel and flint on it to light it and it will provide light for at least 2* QL minutes.', '<ul><li>Use a <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_and_flint\" title=\"Steel and flint\">steel and flint</a> on it to light it and it will provide light for at least 2*<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> minutes.</li></ul>', 1),
(18263, 4690, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The torch\'s wood type will be the same as the shaft used to make it. Creation chance for the torch is determined by firemaking skill and tar quality. The finished torch\'s quality is influenced by firemaking skill, shaft quality, and moss quality. Sacrificing torches gives double favor to followers of Vynora.', '<ul><li>The torch\'s wood type will be the same as the shaft used to make it.</li>\n<li>Creation chance for the torch is determined by <a href=\"/index.php/Firemaking\" title=\"Firemaking\">firemaking</a> skill and <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a> quality.</li>\n<li>The finished torch\'s quality is influenced by firemaking skill, <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> quality, and <a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">moss</a> quality.</li>\n<li>Sacrificing torches gives double favor to followers of Vynora.</li></ul>', 2),
(18264, 4690, 'Other personal lamp options', 'Other_personal_lamp_options', 'Lantern Carved pumpkin Brass oil lamp Metal torch Candle Items with glow runes attached', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lantern\" title=\"Lantern\">Lantern</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Carved_pumpkin\" title=\"Carved pumpkin\">Carved pumpkin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brass_oil_lamp\" title=\"Brass oil lamp\">Brass oil lamp</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_torch\" title=\"Metal torch\">Metal torch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Candle\" title=\"Candle\">Candle</a></li>\n<li>Items with glow <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">runes</a> attached</li></ul>', 3),
(18265, 2033, 'Description', 'Description', 'A crude coffin made from stone with a heavy lid.', '<p><i>A crude coffin made from stone with a heavy lid.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18266, 2033, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'May be used to store anything from corpses to items.', '<p>May be used to store anything from corpses to items.\n</p>', 1),
(18267, 2033, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be made of stone, sandstone, marble and slate bricks and slab. Slab and brick must be of same material. Cannot be locked. Holds up to 500L. Brick quality determines the success rate. May be loaded . Some items may be placed on top of the coffin, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this. Coffins cannot be dyed.', '<ul><li>Can be made of stone, sandstone, marble and slate bricks and slab. Slab and brick must be of same material.</li>\n<li>Cannot be locked.</li>\n<li>Holds up to 500L.</li>\n<li>Brick quality determines the success rate.</li>\n<li>May be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Load\" title=\"Load\">loaded</a>.</li>\n<li>Some items may be placed on top of the coffin, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this.</li>\n<li>Coffins cannot be dyed.</li></ul>', 2),
(18268, 2372, 'Description', 'Description', 'A heavy two-handed sword of incredible quality made from steel and with a comfortable hilt of leather bound silver filigran.', '<p><i>A heavy two-handed sword of incredible quality made from steel and with a comfortable hilt of leather bound silver filigran.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18269, 2372, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This is a unique item currently found on Chaos , Defiance , and Elevation . It cannot be moved to any other server. To find its location or carrier, use the Locate artifact spell. It must be recharged regularly. It does not decay or take damage from use. Flaming aura effect. Can not be enchanted.', '<ul><li>This is a unique item currently found on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a>. It cannot be moved to any other server.</li>\n<li>To find its location or carrier, use the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_artifact\" title=\"Locate artifact\">Locate artifact</a> spell.</li>\n<li>It must be recharged regularly.</li>\n<li>It does not decay or take damage from use.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Flaming_aura\" title=\"Flaming aura\">Flaming aura</a> effect.</li>\n<li>Can not be enchanted.</li></ul>', 1),
(18274, 1727, 'Overview', 'Overview', 'Permissions & security are two topics fundamental to your enjoyment of Wurm Online. This article attempts to outline in great detail the mechanics available to players in order to maximize the security of their belongings and structures. See the talk page associated to this article for some basic advice and guidance. Manage permission from your Body menu To enter the management screen for one of the many permissions systems of Wurm Online right-click on any of the following and open the manage sub-menu. the body group header in the inventory or the body icon on the character window . the inventory header or any user-made group header Individual items may also be managed by right-clicking on them and selecting either Permissions > Manage Item , where Item would be the name of the item\'s type. If there would only be one option under Permissions , then the Manage Item option will be in the root menu. Read-only Permissions There are several areas where you may see read-only permissions. A read-only permission is when you can see what is set for that permission, but you are not able to make changes to it. For example, if the Settlement May Manage option has been ticked and you are not the mayor, or if you are viewing what your permissions are from Manage > Settlement > Info . The green check mark indicates that the permission is allowed . The red X mark indicates that the permission is disallowed . Common Permissions There are two common permissions across all of the management windows: Manage Item When you give this to someone, you are giving them near owner-like access to that item and all other permissions are automatically checked. This will place the item under their own personal management lists and allow them to remote manage it as if they were the owner, regardless of village and alliance settings. Manage Item does not give a person the ability to rename an item, only the owner can change an item\'s name. The settlement role permission Manage Allowed Objects gives any villager with it the ability to manage a settlement-managed item as if they had the Manage Item permission on that item. Deny All Allows you to completely exclude someone, even if other permissions would normally give them access. For example, if you tick Citizens of \"Settlement Name\" and then add a specific citizen and tick Deny All , they will have no access at all. This also overrides the settlement role permission Manage Allowed Objects , allowing you to selectively remove management permissions on a per-item basis. Permission Categories There are several groups of permissions available, depending on your current status and friends list. You can check the box for a category to apply that permission to everything inside of the category. This also applies to the Active Permissions category, where you can quickly tick the x and remove it to remove all permissions. Ticking the Citizens of \"Settlement\" group adds just that group, where as ticking the Citizens of my deed category will add each player individually. Alliance of \"Alliance Name\" also includes your village so you must set Citizens of \"Your Settlement\" to Deny All when you only wish for other alliance members outside of your village to have access. Trusted Friends Players in your Trusted friends category. See the Friends section. Friends Players in your Friends category. See the Friends section. Citizens of my deed A list of all citizens in your current settlement. Available Groups Blanket permission groups. Alliance of \"Alliance Name\" Represents all members of your current alliance, including your own village. See Alliance Permissions for more information. Citizens of \"Settlement Name\" Represents all citizens of your settlement. Kingdom of \"Kingdom Name\" Represents every member of your kingdom. On PvE servers, this will always be \'Freedom Isles\'. \"Everyone\" Represents player in the game. Manually Added This is where any names you add at the top of the form will show when they don\'t have any permissions assigned. Active Permissions This is a list of all permissions that are currently active. It will consist of both players and groups. Alliance Permissions Your villagers need Allow Actions on Allied Deeds in order for any alliance permissions to work for them. This means that if an alliance village has set permissions to allow the alliance to do things, such as May Enter , they will not be able to do so without that settlement permission checked in their role. Your villager can verify this by right-clicking on their body and going under Manage > Settlement > Info . There is a button that should say Show role for <role name> . They can click this and see a read-only view of their permissions. This applies to anything on and off-deed with the Alliance of \"Alliance Name\" permission group added. Not having this checked will treat that alliance member as a non-citizen on all alliance deeds. Friends Manage friends Your friends list has four categories: Trusted, Friends, Contacts, and Other. Only friends that are in the Trusted or Friends category will show in the permission management windows. These categories are quick and easy ways to add blanket permissions to a specific group of people by simply ticking the boxes for the entire group. This adds each name under the category to the permissions individually, which allows you to further customize your permissions. Note: The system is limited to a maximum of 1000 permissions added at a single time. This means that if your Trusted or Friends list has more than 1000 players in it, you will not be able to add the whole category at once. Read more : Manage Friends Locks & Keys The owner of an item or vehicle can unlock and replace locks without the need for keys. If you attach a lock and do not have all of the keys for that lock, you will see this error message: Security Warning: You do not have all the keys for that lock! . Anyone that has a key to the lock can access the locked item or vehicle, but they cannot unlock it, replace the lock, or manage any permissions if they do not have Manage Item set. Keys are entirely optional, with the choice to create copies remaining for situations where you may not wish to use the permission system. You may dispose of any unwanted keys by sacrificing them at an altar. Should you later decide that you would like a key, simply activate a new lock, right-click the item or vehicle, and click Replace Lock . Search Permissions Search permissions and result You may search for all the permissions a specific player has and choose which ones to edit. Open the Character Window and right-click on your body . Click on Manage > Search Permissions and a window will pop up asking you to enter a player\'s name. If the search finds that player listed in any permissions, it will give you a list indicating the name of the item, the type of item, and if they are the owner of it or not. You may tick the circle next to the item you wish to manage, and click Manage Permissions , or you may also click Remove all Permissions to quickly remove that player from all of the listed items. Permission History Permission history window The current owner or the mayor of a settlement-managed item may view the history of permission changes by right-clicking on the item and clicking on Permissions > History of Item , where item would be the type of item you are clicking on. This will show you a history of all permission changes and is preserved over changes in ownership. You may need to scroll the window horizontally to see longer lines, especially when many people or groups were added or removed at the same time.', '<p>Permissions &amp; security are two topics fundamental to your enjoyment of Wurm Online. This article attempts to outline in great detail the mechanics available to players in order to maximize the security of their belongings and structures. See the <a href=\"/index.php/Talk:Permissions\" title=\"Talk:Permissions\">talk page</a> associated to this article for some basic advice and guidance.\n</p>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:280px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Body_perrmission_menu.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-width=\"278\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/a/a5/Body_perrmission_menu.jpg\" width=\"278\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\">Manage permission from your Body menu</div></div></div>\n<p>To enter the management screen for one of the many permissions systems of Wurm Online <b>right-click</b> on any of the following and open the <b>manage</b> sub-menu.\n</p>\n<ul><li>the <b>body</b> group header in the <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> or</li>\n<li>the <b>body</b> icon on the <a href=\"/index.php/Character_window\" title=\"Character window\">character window</a>.</li>\n<li>the <b>inventory</b> header or</li>\n<li>any user-made <b>group</b> header</li></ul>\n<p>Individual items may also be managed by right-clicking on them and selecting either  <b>Permissions &gt; Manage Item</b>, where Item would be the name of the item\'s type. If there would only be one option under <i>Permissions</i>, then the <b>Manage Item</b> option will be in the root menu.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Read-only_Permissions\">Read-only Permissions</span></h3>\n<p>There are several areas where you may see read-only permissions. A read-only permission is when you can see what is set for that permission, but you are not able to make changes to it. For example, if the <b>Settlement May Manage</b> option has been ticked and you are not the mayor, or if you are viewing what your permissions are from <i>Manage &gt; Settlement &gt; Info</i>.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green_checkmark20x20.jpg\" title=\"inline\"><img alt=\"inline\" data-file-height=\"20\" data-file-width=\"20\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/c/cc/Green_checkmark20x20.jpg\" width=\"20\"/></a> The green check mark indicates that the permission is <b>allowed</b>.</li>\n<li><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Red_checkmark20x20.jpg\" title=\"inline\"><img alt=\"inline\" data-file-height=\"20\" data-file-width=\"20\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/1/16/Red_checkmark20x20.jpg\" width=\"20\"/></a> The red X mark indicates that the permission is <b>disallowed</b>.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Common_Permissions\">Common Permissions</span></h3>\n<p>There are two common permissions across all of the management windows:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>When you give this to someone, you are giving them near owner-like access to that item and all other permissions are automatically checked. This will place the item under their own personal management lists and allow them to remote manage it as if they were the owner, regardless of village and alliance settings. <b>Manage Item</b> does not give a person the ability to rename an item, only the owner can change an item\'s name. The settlement role permission <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> gives any villager with it the ability to manage a settlement-managed item as if they had the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that item.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Allows you to completely exclude someone, even if other permissions would normally give them access. For example, if you tick <b>Citizens of \"Settlement Name\"</b> and then add a specific citizen and tick <b>Deny All</b>, they will have no access at all. This also overrides the settlement role permission <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b>, allowing you to selectively remove management permissions on a per-item basis.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Permission_Categories\">Permission Categories</span></h3>\n<p>There are several groups of permissions available, depending on your current status and friends list. You can check the box for a category to apply that permission to everything inside of the category. This also applies to the <b>Active Permissions</b> category, where you can quickly tick the <i>x</i> and remove it to remove all permissions. Ticking the <b>Citizens of \"Settlement\"</b> group adds just that group, where as ticking the <b>Citizens of my deed</b> category will add each player individually. <b>Alliance of \"Alliance Name\"</b> also includes your village so you must set <b>Citizens of \"Your Settlement\"</b> to <b>Deny All</b> when you only wish for other alliance members outside of your village to have access.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Trusted Friends</dt>\n<dd>Players in your Trusted friends category. See the <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Friends\" title=\"Permissions\">Friends</a> section.</dd>\n<dt>Friends</dt>\n<dd>Players in your Friends category. See the <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Friends\" title=\"Permissions\">Friends</a> section.</dd>\n<dt>Citizens of my deed</dt>\n<dd>A list of all citizens in your current settlement.</dd>\n<dt>Available Groups</dt>\n<dd>Blanket permission groups.\n<dl><dt>Alliance of \"Alliance Name\"</dt>\n<dd>Represents all members of your current alliance, including your own village. See <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Alliance_Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">Alliance Permissions</a> for more information.</dd>\n<dt>Citizens of \"Settlement Name\"</dt>\n<dd>Represents all citizens of your settlement.</dd>\n<dt>Kingdom of \"Kingdom Name\"</dt>\n<dd>Represents every member of your kingdom. On PvE servers, this will always be \'Freedom Isles\'.</dd>\n<dt>\"Everyone\"</dt>\n<dd>Represents player in the game.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dt>Manually Added</dt>\n<dd>This is where any names you add at the top of the form will show when they don\'t have any permissions assigned.</dd>\n<dt>Active Permissions</dt>\n<dd>This is a list of all permissions that are currently active. It will consist of both players and groups.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alliance_Permissions\">Alliance Permissions</span></h3>\n<p>Your villagers need <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Allow Actions on Allied Deeds</a></b> in order for any alliance permissions to work for them. This means that if an alliance village has set permissions to allow the alliance to do things, such as <b>May Enter</b>, they will not be able to do so without that settlement permission checked in their role. Your villager can verify this by <b>right-clicking</b> on their <b>body</b> and going under <i>Manage &gt; Settlement &gt; Info</i>. There is a button that should say <i>Show role for &lt;role name&gt;</i>. They can click this and see a read-only view of their permissions.\n</p>\n<ul><li>This applies to anything on and off-deed with the<b>Alliance of \"Alliance Name\"</b> permission group added.</li>\n<li>Not having this checked will treat that alliance member as a non-citizen on all alliance deeds.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Friends\">Friends</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Manage_friends.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"303\" data-file-width=\"503\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"181\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Manage_friends.jpg/300px-Manage_friends.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Manage_friends.jpg/450px-Manage_friends.jpg 1.5x, /images/7/77/Manage_friends.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Manage_friends.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Manage friends</div></div></div>\n<p>Your <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Friends\" title=\"Friends\">friends</a> list has four categories: Trusted, Friends, Contacts, and Other. Only friends that are in the <b>Trusted</b> or <b>Friends</b> category will show in the permission management windows. These categories are quick and easy ways to add blanket permissions to a specific group of people by simply ticking the boxes for the entire group. This adds each name under the category to the permissions individually, which allows you to further customize your permissions.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><b>Note:</b> The system is limited to a maximum of 1000 permissions added at a single time. This means that if your Trusted or Friends list has more than 1000 players in it, you will not be able to add the whole category at once.</dd></dl>\n<p><b>Read more</b>: <a href=\"/index.php/Friend\" title=\"Friend\">Manage Friends</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Locks_&amp;_Keys\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Locks_.26_Keys\">Locks &amp; Keys</span></h3>\n<p>The owner of an item or vehicle can unlock and replace locks without the need for keys. If you attach a lock and do not have all of the keys for that lock, you will see this error message: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> Security Warning: You do not have all the keys for that lock! </span>. Anyone that has a key to the lock can access the locked item or vehicle, but they cannot unlock it, replace the lock, or manage any permissions if they do not have <b>Manage Item</b> set.\n</p>\n<p>Keys are entirely optional, with the choice to create copies remaining for situations where you may not wish to use the permission system. You may dispose of any unwanted keys by sacrificing them at an altar. Should you later decide that you would like a key, simply activate a new lock, <b>right-click</b> the item or vehicle, and click <b>Replace Lock</b>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Search_Permissions\">Search Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Search_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"365\" data-file-width=\"307\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"357\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/f8/Search_permissions.jpg/300px-Search_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/f/f8/Search_permissions.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Search_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Search permissions and result</div></div></div>\n<p>You may search for all the permissions a specific player has and choose which ones to edit. Open the <b>Character Window</b> and <b>right-click</b> on your <b>body</b>. Click on <i>Manage &gt; Search Permissions</i> and a window will pop up asking you to enter a player\'s name. If the search finds that player listed in any permissions, it will give you a list indicating the name of the item, the type of item, and if they are the owner of it or not. You may tick the circle next to the item you wish to manage, and click <b>Manage Permissions</b>, or you may also click <b>Remove all Permissions</b> to quickly remove that player from all of the listed items.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Permission_History\">Permission History</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Permission_history.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"323\" data-file-width=\"440\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"220\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/68/Permission_history.jpg/300px-Permission_history.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/6/68/Permission_history.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Permission_history.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Permission history window</div></div></div>\n<p>The current <b>owner</b> or the <b>mayor</b> of a settlement-managed item may view the history of permission changes by <b>right-clicking</b> on the item and clicking on <i>Permissions &gt; History of Item</i>, where item would be the type of item you are clicking on. This will show you a history of all permission changes and is preserved over changes in ownership. You may need to scroll the window horizontally to see longer lines, especially when many people or groups were added or removed at the same time.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18275, 1727, 'Animals', 'Animals', 'Animal management Animals must be branded by a deed to enable animal management. When branded, the owner defaults to the mayor of the deed that branded it. Like other managed items, Manage Allowed Objects does allows a villager the ability to manage branded animals. To access the management window, right-click on your body and click on Manage > Animals . This window shows you a list of all animals that you have tamed, are caring for, or that are branded on your deed. You may untame, stop caring for, or remove brands from this window. If the animal is branded, you may select the animal and click Give direction to . This will give you a message in the same way the Locate soul spell does and help direct you to your animal. To manage a specific animal, select the animal you wish to manage and click Manage Animal . You may also right-click on the animal you wish to manage and click on Manage Animal , which may be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options for that animal. Animal Notes Only available on PvE servers. The settlement role permission Attack Citizens for the branding settlement is needed to attack branded animals on or off-deed. The settlement role permission Tame/Charm/Dominate for the branding settlement is needed to tame branded animals on or off-deed. Removing a brand also deletes all settings and history associated with that animal. While taming or caring for an animal will show them in your list, neither will enable permission management. Branded animals can have their equipment managed by anyone with Manage Equipment enabled as if they had tamed it. The Lead settlement permission only allows a player to lead an animal, whereas May Ride set on the animal allows a player to lead and ride that animal. Branded animals may be given a nickname by the mayor of the deed that branded them. Example, if Runheart is given the nickname of \'Spot\': A aged fat runheart \'Spot\' grazes. Branded animals may be remote managed, even when off deed. Branded horses have the same protection when dead as when alive (until the next server restart), meaning only those who have permissions may take items from the corpse. Revoking permissions from someone riding the animal will not dismount them, but it will prevent them from riding the animal again once they disembark. The limit to the number of branded animals you can have is tiles / 11 . For example, for a 20 by 20 deed: 20x20 = 400 / 11 = 36 If deed permissions allow leading, it will override brand permissions while on deed. Animal Permissions Animal permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. Can Ride Allows riding of this animal. Can be Passenger Allows being a passenger of this animal. Manage Equipment Allows adding or removing equipment from the animal without taming it. Deny All Deny all access.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Animal_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"587\" data-file-width=\"558\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"316\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/62/Animal_management.jpg/300px-Animal_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/62/Animal_management.jpg/450px-Animal_management.jpg 1.5x, /images/6/62/Animal_management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Animal_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Animal management</div></div></div>\n<p>Animals must be branded by a deed to enable animal management. When branded, the owner defaults to the mayor of the deed that branded it. Like other managed items, <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> does allows a villager the ability to manage branded animals. To access the management window, <b>right-click</b> on your body and click on <i>Manage &gt; Animals</i>. This window shows you a list of all animals that you have tamed, are caring for, or that are branded on your deed. You may untame, stop caring for, or remove brands from this window. If the animal is branded, you may select the animal and click <b>Give direction to</b>. This will give you a message in the same way the <a href=\"/index.php/Locate_soul\" title=\"Locate soul\">Locate soul</a> spell does and help direct you to your animal. To manage a specific animal, select the animal you wish to manage and click <b>Manage Animal</b>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on the animal you wish to manage and click on <i>Manage Animal</i>, which may be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options for that animal.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Animal_Notes\">Animal Notes</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Only available on PvE servers.</li>\n<li>The settlement role permission <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#General\" title=\"Permissions\">Attack Citizens</a></b> for the branding settlement is needed to attack branded animals on or off-deed.</li>\n<li>The settlement role permission <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Animals_2\" title=\"Permissions\">Tame/Charm/Dominate</a></b> for the branding settlement is needed to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tame\" title=\"Tame\">tame</a> branded animals on or off-deed.</li>\n<li>Removing a brand also deletes all settings and history associated with that animal.</li>\n<li>While taming or caring for an animal will show them in your list, neither will enable permission management.</li>\n<li>Branded animals can have their equipment managed by anyone with <b>Manage Equipment</b> enabled as if they had tamed it.</li>\n<li>The <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Animals_2\" title=\"Permissions\">Lead</a></b> settlement permission only allows a player to lead an animal, whereas <b>May Ride</b> set on the animal allows a player to lead and ride that animal.</li>\n<li>Branded animals may be given a nickname by the mayor of the deed that branded them.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd>Example, if Runheart is given the nickname of \'Spot\': <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> A aged fat runheart \'Spot\' grazes. </span></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>Branded animals may be remote managed, even when off deed.</li>\n<li>Branded horses have the same protection when dead as when alive (until the next server restart), meaning only those who have permissions may take items from the corpse.</li>\n<li>Revoking permissions from someone riding the animal will not dismount them, but it will prevent them from riding the animal again once they disembark.</li>\n<li>The limit to the number of branded animals you can have is <tt>tiles / 11</tt>.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd>For example, for a 20 by 20 deed: <tt>20x20 = 400 / 11 = 36</tt></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>If deed permissions allow leading, it will override brand permissions while on deed.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Animal_Permissions\">Animal Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Animal_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"313\" data-file-width=\"524\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"179\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/26/Animal_permissions.jpg/300px-Animal_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/26/Animal_permissions.jpg/450px-Animal_permissions.jpg 1.5x, /images/2/26/Animal_permissions.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Animal_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Animal permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>Can Ride</dt>\n<dd>Allows riding of this animal.</dd>\n<dt>Can be Passenger</dt>\n<dd>Allows being a passenger of this animal.</dd>\n<dt>Manage Equipment</dt>\n<dd>Allows adding or removing equipment from the animal without taming it.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Deny all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 1),
(18276, 1727, 'Buildings & Doors', 'Buildings_.26_Doors', 'Buildings Building management You can manage buildings by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Buildings . You may also right-click on a building directly and select Manage Building . This will be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options on that building. You may only manage a building if you have been given the Manage Item permission on that building, have the Manage Allowed Objects settlement permission if the building is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the building. Owners of settlement-managed buildings without Manage Allowed Objects or Manage Item can only change the building\'s ownership. A building must have all first floor walls complete before permissions will work on that building, and doors must be locked with a door lock before they respect the May Enter permission. All other permissions are enforced without door locks. While building the initial walls of a building requires Build settlement permission, the Modify Building permission on the building itself is required to continue building by anyone but the owner once the walls are complete. The owner is the person who planned the structure. Owners of buildings that are not managed by a settlement, or mayors of settlement-managed buildings, may click on the Demolish button to completely destroy that building. This action cannot be undone. Building Notes Permissions on a building will override Settlement permissions . Only the current owner of a building may tick Settlement May Manage . Only the current owner of a building, or the mayor when Settlement May Manage is checked, can rename the building or its doors. Only the mayor may un-tick Settlement May Manage . You must have Pickup Items as well as May (Un)Load to load things from a building. You must have May Enter permissions in order to drop something inside a building. Container permissions override building permissions, allowing you to let someone take from a specific container without giving them Pickup Items on the building. If Settlement May Manage is set, the mayor is able to demolish a building instead of the actual owner. Any villager with Destroy Any Building may bash a building, regardless of ownership or settlement management. Building Permissions Building permissions Checking a building and pushing the Manage Permissions button will take you to a screen where the owner can re-name the building and change the ownership. The owner and any other players with direct or inherited manage permissions will also be able to view and modify all permissions linked to the building. Manage Item allows management of the permissions on the building May Enter allows entry through locked doors (if managed by the building) and the ability to improve and repair the building and its contents Modify Building allows destroying , building and rotating of floors, roofs. Deed permissions may be required to add or remove tiles Pickup Items allows taking , pushing , pulling , turning and hauling (overrides deed settings) Pickup Planted allows taking of planted items, requires the Pickup Items building permission Place Merchants allows placing of a merchant or trader and overrides the deed settings May (Un)Load allows the loading and unloading of items, overriding the deed settings. Requires Pickup Items for the target to load items they do not own and Pickup Planted for planted items. Deny All Does just that! Doors Door management You may manage doors by picking a building and clicking the Manage All Doors button. You may also manage a door directly by right-clicking on the door and clicking on Permissions > Manage Door . Door permissions are managed by the building\'s permissions by default. To manage individual door permissions, remove the check for Controlled By Building and Apply Changes . Doors can be named by typing a name into the box next to Name . You must be able to manage the building the door is attached to in order to manage the doors on that building. Door Notes Door permissions are only enabled when the door has a door lock attached. Doors default to Controlled By Building and anyone with Manage Item can toggle this option. Doors may only be renamed by the owner of the building, or the mayor when Settlement May Manage is checked. Door Permissions Door permissions Pass Door Allows passing through this door. Deny All Denies all access.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Buildings\">Buildings</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Building_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"267\" data-file-width=\"564\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"142\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/26/Building_management.jpg/300px-Building_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/26/Building_management.jpg/450px-Building_management.jpg 1.5x, /images/2/26/Building_management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Building_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Building management</div></div></div>\n<p>You can manage buildings by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Buildings</i>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on a building directly and select <i>Manage Building</i>. This will be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options on that building. You may only manage a building if you have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that building, have the <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> settlement permission if the building is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the building. Owners of settlement-managed buildings without <b>Manage Allowed Objects</b> or <b>Manage Item</b> can only change the building\'s ownership.\n</p>\n<p>A building must have all first floor walls complete before permissions will work on that building, and doors must be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a> before they respect the <b>May Enter</b> permission. All other permissions are enforced without door locks. While building the initial walls of a building requires <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Construction\" title=\"Permissions\">Build</a></b> settlement permission, the <b>Modify Building</b> permission on the building itself is required to continue building by anyone but the owner once the walls are complete. The owner is the person who planned the structure.\n</p>\n<p>Owners of buildings that are not managed by a settlement, or mayors of settlement-managed buildings, may click on the <b>Demolish</b> button to completely destroy that building. This action cannot be undone.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Building_Notes\">Building Notes</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Permissions on a building will override <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement\" title=\"Permissions\">Settlement permissions</a>.</li>\n<li>Only the current owner of a building may tick <b>Settlement May Manage</b>.</li>\n<li>Only the current owner of a building, or the mayor when <b>Settlement May Manage</b> is checked, can rename the building or its doors.</li>\n<li>Only the mayor may un-tick <b>Settlement May Manage</b>.</li>\n<li>You must have <b>Pickup Items</b> as well as <b>May (Un)Load</b> to load things from a building.</li>\n<li>You must have <b>May Enter</b> permissions in order to drop something inside a building.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Containers\" title=\"Permissions\">Container</a> permissions override building permissions, allowing you to let someone take from a specific container without giving them <b>Pickup Items</b> on the building.</li>\n<li>If <b>Settlement May Manage</b> is set, the mayor is able to demolish a building instead of the actual owner.</li>\n<li>Any villager with <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Destroy Any Building</a></b> may bash a building, regardless of ownership or settlement management.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Building_Permissions\">Building Permissions</span></h4>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Building_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"319\" data-file-width=\"600\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"160\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/93/Building_permissions.jpg/300px-Building_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/93/Building_permissions.jpg/450px-Building_permissions.jpg 1.5x, /images/9/93/Building_permissions.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Building_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Building permissions</div></div></div>\n<p>Checking a building and pushing the <b>Manage Permissions</b> button will take you to a screen where the <b>owner</b> can re-name the building and change the ownership. The owner and any other players with direct or inherited manage permissions will also be able to view and modify all permissions linked to the building.\n</p>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>allows <i>management of the permissions</i> on the building</dd>\n<dt>May Enter</dt>\n<dd>allows entry through locked doors (if managed by the building) and the ability to <i>improve</i> and <i>repair</i> the building and its contents</dd>\n<dt>Modify Building</dt>\n<dd>allows <i>destroying</i>, <i>building</i> and <i>rotating</i> of floors, roofs. Deed permissions may be required to add or remove tiles</dd>\n<dt>Pickup Items</dt>\n<dd>allows <i>taking</i>, <i>pushing</i>, <i>pulling</i>, <i>turning</i> and <i>hauling</i> (overrides deed settings)</dd>\n<dt>Pickup Planted</dt>\n<dd>allows <i>taking</i> of planted items, requires the <i>Pickup Items</i> building permission</dd>\n<dt>Place Merchants</dt>\n<dd>allows placing of a <i>merchant</i> or <i>trader</i> and overrides the deed settings</dd>\n<dt>May (Un)Load</dt>\n<dd>allows the <i>loading</i> and <i>unloading</i> of items, overriding the deed settings. Requires <i>Pickup Items</i> for the target to load items they do not own and <i>Pickup Planted</i> for planted items.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Does just that!</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Doors\">Doors</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Door_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"272\" data-file-width=\"477\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"171\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/98/Door_management.jpg/300px-Door_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/9/98/Door_management.jpg/450px-Door_management.jpg 1.5x, /images/9/98/Door_management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Door_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Door management</div></div></div>\n<p>You may manage doors by picking a building and clicking the <b>Manage All Doors</b> button. You may also manage a door directly by <b>right-clicking</b> on the door and clicking on <b>Permissions &gt; Manage Door</b>. Door permissions are managed by the building\'s permissions by default. To manage individual door permissions, remove the check for <b>Controlled By Building</b> and <b>Apply Changes</b>. Doors can be named by typing a name into the box next to <b>Name</b>. You must be able to manage the building the door is attached to in order to manage the doors on that building.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Door_Notes\">Door Notes</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Door permissions are only enabled when the door has a <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door lock</a> attached.</li>\n<li>Doors default to <b>Controlled By Building</b> and anyone with <b>Manage Item</b> can toggle this option.</li>\n<li>Doors may only be renamed by the owner of the building, or the mayor when <b>Settlement May Manage</b> is checked.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Door_Permissions\">Door Permissions</span></h4>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Door_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"317\" data-file-width=\"599\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"159\" src=\"/images/thumb/c/c4/Door_permissions.jpg/300px-Door_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/c/c4/Door_permissions.jpg/450px-Door_permissions.jpg 1.5x, /images/c/c4/Door_permissions.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Door_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Door permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Pass Door</dt>\n<dd>Allows passing through this door.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Denies all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 2),
(18277, 1727, 'Carts and Wagons', 'Carts_and_Wagons', 'A small padlock or large padlock is required to activate vehicle permissions. You can manage land vehicles by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Carts and Wagons . You may also right-click on an vehicle you own or have permission to manage and click Manage Item . Item will be whatever the type of vehicle it is that you are managing. This option may be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options on that item. You will only have the option to manage a vehicle if you are the owner or have been given the Manage Item permission on that vehicle. Cart and Wagon Notes Cart and Wagon Management The owner of a vehicle you may be using can change the name of that vehicle at any time or attach a lock to it thereby making it useless to anyone else, including locking you out of any items you may have inside the cart. If you have obtained a locked vehicle from another player who did not pass along the key to you, immediately replace the lock. Failing to do so can result in the owner of the key unlocking your vehicle at any time. Not all permissions will be visible on all vehicles. For example, small carts will not have Can Command or Can be Passenger . Only the owner may rename the vehicle. Cart and Wagon Permissions Cart and Wagon Permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. Can Command Allows commanding of this vehicle. Can be Passenger Allows being a passenger of this vehicle. Access Hold Allows access to the hold. May Drag Allows the vehicle to be dragged. Deny All Deny all access.', '<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Small_padlock\" title=\"Small padlock\">small padlock</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Large_padlock\" title=\"Large padlock\">large padlock</a> is required to activate vehicle permissions. You can manage land vehicles by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Carts and Wagons</i>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on an vehicle you own or have permission to manage and click <i>Manage Item</i>. Item will be whatever the type of vehicle it is that you are managing. This option may be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options on that item. You will only have the option to manage a vehicle if you are the owner or have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that vehicle.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cart_and_Wagon_Notes\">Cart and Wagon Notes</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"273\" data-file-width=\"477\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"172\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/80/Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg/300px-Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/80/Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg/450px-Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg 1.5x, /images/8/80/Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Cart_and_wagon_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Cart and Wagon Management</div></div></div>\n<ul><li>The owner of a vehicle you may be using can change the name of that vehicle at any time or attach a lock to it thereby making it useless to anyone else, including locking you out of any items you may have inside the cart.</li>\n<li>If you have obtained a locked vehicle from another player who did not pass along the key to you, immediately replace the lock. Failing to do so can result in the owner of the key unlocking your vehicle at any time.</li>\n<li>Not all permissions will be visible on all vehicles. For example, <a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">small carts</a> will not have <b>Can Command</b> or <b>Can be Passenger</b>.</li>\n<li>Only the owner may rename the vehicle.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cart_and_Wagon_Permissions\">Cart and Wagon Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Large_cart_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"352\" data-file-width=\"649\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"163\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/24/Large_cart_permissions.jpg/300px-Large_cart_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/24/Large_cart_permissions.jpg/450px-Large_cart_permissions.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/24/Large_cart_permissions.jpg/600px-Large_cart_permissions.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Large_cart_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Cart and Wagon Permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>Can Command</dt>\n<dd>Allows commanding of this vehicle.</dd>\n<dt>Can be Passenger</dt>\n<dd>Allows being a passenger of this vehicle.</dd>\n<dt>Access Hold</dt>\n<dd>Allows access to the hold.</dd>\n<dt>May Drag</dt>\n<dd>Allows the vehicle to be dragged.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Deny all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 3),
(18278, 1727, 'Gates', 'Gates', 'Gate management A gate must be locked with a gate lock for permissions to become active on it, though the mayor may rename the gate if it is managed by a settlement without a lock. You can manage gates by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Gates . You may also right-click on a gate directly and select Manage gate . This will be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options on that gate. You may only manage a gate if you have been given the Manage Item permission on that gate, have the Manage Allowed Objects settlement permission if the gate is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the gate. Owners of settlement-managed gates without Manage Allowed Objects or Manage Item can only change the gate\'s ownership. Gate Notes A gate created off-deed must have a lock attached in order to rename it or manage it in any way. The owner of a gate is whomever attached the lock. Anyone can attach a lock to an off-deed gate, but only citizens with Attach Lock can attach or replace locks on-deed. Settlement May Manage allows the mayor and any citizen with the Manage Allowed Objects permission to manage this item. Only the current owner may tick Settlement May Manage for off-deed gates, and only the mayor may remove the tick. A gate created on-deed defaults to Settlement May Manage . A lock is required to manage permissions, but the mayor can rename an gate without a lock. You cannot remove Settlement May Manage for on-deed gates. Locked off-deed gates without Settlement May Manage may be renamed by their current owner . Locked on-deed gates and off-deed gates with Settlement May Manage may only be renamed by the mayor of that settlement. Settlement-managed gates with no permissions ticked can be controlled by the settlement role permission May Pass Gates . Off-deed gates, even with Settlement May Manage , must be managed to allow citizens to pass. Anyone with a key to the current lock on the gate may unlock and pass through the gate. It is important to replace locks on gates that you extend your deed over, or when you are unsure as to who may have keys to it. Gate Permissions Gate permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. Pass Gate Allows entry through this gate even when its locked. (Un)Lock Gate Allows locking (and unlocking) of this gate. Deny All Deny all access.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gate_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"578\" data-file-width=\"587\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"295\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/Gate_management.jpg/300px-Gate_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/7b/Gate_management.jpg/450px-Gate_management.jpg 1.5x, /images/7/7b/Gate_management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gate_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Gate management</div></div></div>\n<p>A gate must be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a> for permissions to become active on it, though the mayor may rename the gate if it is managed by a settlement without a lock. You can manage gates by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Gates</i>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on a gate directly and select <i>Manage gate</i>. This will be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options on that gate. You may only manage a gate if you have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that gate, have the <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> settlement permission if the gate is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the gate. Owners of settlement-managed gates without <b>Manage Allowed Objects</b> or <b>Manage Item</b> can only change the gate\'s ownership.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gate_Notes\">Gate Notes</span></h3>\n<ul><li>A gate created off-deed must have a lock attached in order to rename it or manage it in any way.</li>\n<li>The <b>owner</b> of a gate is whomever attached the lock.</li>\n<li>Anyone can attach a lock to an off-deed gate, but only citizens with <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Item_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Attach Lock</a></b> can attach or replace locks on-deed.</li>\n<li><b>Settlement May Manage</b> allows the <b>mayor</b> and any citizen with the <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> permission to manage this item.</li>\n<li>Only the current <b>owner</b> may tick <b>Settlement May Manage</b> for off-deed gates, and only the <b>mayor</b> may remove the tick.</li>\n<li>A gate created on-deed defaults to <b>Settlement May Manage</b>. A lock is required to manage permissions, but the mayor can rename an gate without a lock.</li>\n<li>You cannot remove <b>Settlement May Manage</b> for on-deed gates.</li>\n<li>Locked off-deed gates without <b>Settlement May Manage</b> may be renamed by their current <b>owner</b>.</li>\n<li>Locked on-deed gates and off-deed gates with <b>Settlement May Manage</b> may only be renamed by the <b>mayor</b> of that settlement.</li>\n<li>Settlement-managed gates <i>with no permissions ticked</i> can be controlled by the settlement role permission <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#General\" title=\"Permissions\">May Pass Gates</a></b>.</li>\n<li>Off-deed gates, even with <b>Settlement May Manage</b>, must be managed to allow citizens to pass.</li>\n<li>Anyone with a key to the current lock on the gate may unlock and pass through the gate.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd><b>It is important to replace locks on gates that you extend your deed over, or when you are unsure as to who may have keys to it.</b></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gate_Permissions\">Gate Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gate_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"317\" data-file-width=\"427\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"223\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/63/Gate_permissions.jpg/300px-Gate_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/6/63/Gate_permissions.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Gate_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Gate permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>Pass Gate</dt>\n<dd>Allows entry through this gate even when its locked.</dd>\n<dt>(Un)Lock Gate</dt>\n<dd>Allows locking (and unlocking) of this gate.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Deny all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 4),
(18279, 1727, 'Mine Doors', 'Mine_Doors', 'Mine door management You can manage mine doors by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Mine Doors . You may also right-click on a mine door directly and select Manage Mine Door . This will be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options on that door. You may need to stand on the tile adjacent to a mine door in order for it to remain closed so you may right-click on it. You may only manage a mine door if you have been given the Manage Item permission on that door, have the Manage Allowed Objects settlement permission if the door is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the mine door. Owners of settlement-managed mine doors without Manage Allowed Objects or Manage Item can only change the mine door\'s ownership. Mine Door Notes The owner of the mine door is the player that installed it. When managed by the settlement, the mayor is treated as the owner. On-deed mine doors automatically set the Settlement May Manage flag, which cannot be removed while it remains on-deed. When a deed no longer covers a mine door, the Settlement May Manage flag is automatically removed, which the original owner may tick again if desired. Permissions are cleared whenever Settlement May Manage is removed. The owner, or the mayor if managed by a settlement, may rename a mine door. Pass / Deny permissions on mine doors apply only to entry into a mine from above ground. They do not apply to exiting a mine from the inside, which is always allowed. Mine Door Permissions Mine door permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. Pass Mine Door Allows passing through the mine door. Deny All Deny all access.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mine_door_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"260\" data-file-width=\"378\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"206\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/fc/Mine_door_management.jpg/300px-Mine_door_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/f/fc/Mine_door_management.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mine_door_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Mine door management</div></div></div>\n<p>You can manage mine doors by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Mine Doors</i>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on a mine door directly and select <i>Manage Mine Door</i>. This will be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options on that door. You may need to stand on the tile adjacent to a mine door in order for it to remain closed so you may right-click on it. You may only manage a mine door if you have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that door, have the <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> settlement permission if the door is managed by the settlement, or if you are the owner of the mine door. Owners of settlement-managed mine doors without <b>Manage Allowed Objects</b> or <b>Manage Item</b> can only change the mine door\'s ownership.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mine_Door_Notes\">Mine Door Notes</span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <b>owner</b> of the mine door is the player that installed it. When managed by the settlement, the mayor is treated as the owner.</li>\n<li>On-deed mine doors automatically set the <b>Settlement May Manage</b> flag, which cannot be removed while it remains on-deed.</li>\n<li>When a deed no longer covers a mine door, the <b>Settlement May Manage</b> flag is automatically removed, which the original owner may tick again if desired.</li>\n<li>Permissions are cleared whenever <b>Settlement May Manage</b> is removed.</li>\n<li>The owner, or the mayor if managed by a settlement, may rename a mine door.</li>\n<li>Pass / Deny permissions on mine doors apply only to <b>entry into a mine</b> from above ground. They do not apply to <b>exiting a mine</b> from the inside, which is always allowed.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mine_Door_Permissions\">Mine Door Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mine_door_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"312\" data-file-width=\"440\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"213\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/db/Mine_door_permissions.jpg/300px-Mine_door_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/d/db/Mine_door_permissions.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Mine_door_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Mine door permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>Pass Mine Door</dt>\n<dd>Allows passing through the mine door.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Deny all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 5);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18280, 1727, 'Settlement', 'Settlement', 'Manage Settlement from your body You can manage your settlement by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Settlement . This will bring up a list of various settlement options depending on your current permissions. The mayor may also use the settlement deed item in their inventory, and anyone can use the settlement token to both manage and view permissions of that settlement. Settlement Notes Manage settlement roles The Allow Actions on Allied Deeds permission is required in order to take advantage of a vehicles Allow Allies permissions to be enforced. If a role is given to a Trusted friend who also inherits the Citizens of my Deed roles the citizen permissions will take priority. It would be required to manually add the desired role for the player to the managed item if it differs from the citizen permission. The player can exist in more than one list; if different permissions are selected for the same player, they will end up with a merged set of permissions. Item-level permissions, including Deny All , can be used to override settlement-level permissions. Blue settings may only be set on citizen-type roles. Destroy Any Building is a citizen-only role. This will allow anyone with this permission the ability to bash any building, regardless of ownership. Settlement Permissions Role Management Animals Brand Allows branding of animals on deed. - Only for Citizen type roles. Breed Allows breeding of animals on deed. Butcher Allows butchering on deed. Groom Allows grooming of animals on deed. Lead Allows leading of animals on deed. Milk/Shear Allows milking of cows and shearing of sheep. Sacrifice Allows sacrificing of animals on deed. Tame / Charm / Dominate Allows taming of animals on deed. Charming and Dominating requires this and Cast Deity Spells . Construction Build Allows ability to color and continue on buildings and build fences and place mine doors. Destroy Fences Allows destruction of fences and gates. Destroy Items Allows destruction of items. Pick Locks Allows lockpicking of buildings, items and gates. Also requires Pickup permission to lockpick items. - Only for Citizen type roles. Plan Buildings Allows planning of buildings. Digging Cultivate Allows cultivating of packed tiles. Dig Clay/Tar/Peat/Moss Allows digging of resource tiles. Pack Allows packing of tiles. Terraform Allows terraforming (digging, leveling and flattening). Farming Harvest Fields Allows harvesting of fields. Sow Fields Allows sowing of fields. Tend Fields Allows tending of fields. Forestry/Gardening Chop Down Trees and Bushes Allows chopping down of all trees and bushes except the very old and overaged trees. Chop Down V.Old Trees Allows chopping down of very old and overaged trees. Also allows \' Wild growth \' spell on hedges, but that requires Cast Deity Spells privilege as well. Cut Grass Allows cutting of grass. Harvest Fruit Allows harvesting from trees and bushes. Make Lawn Allows ability to make lawn. Pick Sprouts Allows picking of sprouts from trees and bushes and also allows picking of flowers. Plant Flowers Allows planting of flowers, mixed grass and thatch. Plant Sprouts Allows planting of sprouts including hedges. Prune Allows pruning of trees and bushes including hedges. General Attack Citizens Allows attacking of citizens and allies of the settlement. Attack Non Citizens Allows attacking of non citizens which includes animals. Cast Deity Spells Allows use of deity spells on deed. Cast Sorcery Spells Allows use of sorcery spells on deed. Forage/Botanize Allows foraging and botanizing on deed. May Pass Gates Allows passing of gates that don\'t have any permissions set. May Place NPCs Allows placing of merchants and traders. Pave Allows adding or removing of paving on deed. Use Meditation Abilities Allows use of meditation abilities on deed. Item Management Attach Locks Allows attaching of locks on items on deed. - Only for Citizen type roles. Drop Allows dropping of items on deed. Improve/Repair Allows improving and repairing of items on deed. Load Allows loading of items on deed, also requires Pickup permissions or Pickup Planted permission. Pickup Allows picking up of items on deed. Pickup Planted Items Allows picking up of planted items on deed, also requires Pickup permission. Plant Item Allows planting and securing of items on deed. Pull/Push/Turn Allows pull, push, and turning of items on deed. UnLoad Allows unloading of items on deed. Mining Add/Remove Reinforcement Allows adding and removing of reinforced walls (needs Mine Rock ) and floors (needs Mine Floor ) on deed. Also used to control Disintegrate , which will also need Cast Deity Spells Mine Floor Allows mining of floors in cave on deed including leveling and flattening in caves. Mine Iron Veins Allows mining of iron veins on deed. Mine Other Veins Allows mining of other veins on deed. Mine Rock Allows mining of rock in caves on deed. Surface Mining Allows surface mining on deed. Tunnel Allows making tunnel entrances on deed. Settlement Management Only citizen-type roles may have these permissions set on them. They are not visible on non-citizen roles and cannot be enabled. If checked when creating a new non-citizen role, they will be removed once the role is saved. Allow Actions on Allied Deeds Allows actions on allied deeds using their ally role, if not set then they it will use their non-citizen. Destroy Any Buildings Allows demolition of any building. Invite Citizens Allows ability to invite non-citizens to join the settlement including using recruitment boards. Manage Allowed Objects Allows ability to manage allowed objects, that\'s buildings, gates, and mine doors that have the Settlement May Manage flag set. Manage Citizen Roles Allows ability to assign roles to citizens. Manage Guards Allows hiring guards to protect the settlement and uphold these rules. Manage Map Allows ability to add and remove village annotations on the map. Updating alliance annotations requires the manage politics permission as well. Manage Politics Allows ability to form and break alliances with other settlements, as well as declare war and make peace. Manage Reputations Allows ability to manage reputations. Manage Roles Allows managing of permissions in any role in which you have the corresponding permission in your role. Manage Settings Allows changing settlement settings. May Configure Twitter Allows ability to configure twitter settings. Resize Settlement Allows ability to change the size of the settlement.', '<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Body_settlement_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"417\" data-file-width=\"382\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"327\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/9b/Body_settlement_management.jpg/300px-Body_settlement_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/9/9b/Body_settlement_management.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Body_settlement_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Manage Settlement from your body</div></div></div>\n<p>You can manage your settlement by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Settlement</i>. This will bring up a list of various settlement options depending on your current permissions. The mayor may also use the <b>settlement deed</b> item in their inventory, and anyone can use the <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement_token\" title=\"Settlement token\">settlement token</a> to both manage and view permissions of that settlement.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Settlement_Notes\">Settlement Notes</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Settlement_roles.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"463\" data-file-width=\"466\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"298\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b4/Settlement_roles.jpg/300px-Settlement_roles.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b4/Settlement_roles.jpg/450px-Settlement_roles.jpg 1.5x, /images/b/b4/Settlement_roles.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Settlement_roles.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Manage settlement roles</div></div></div>\n<ul><li>The <i>Allow Actions on Allied Deeds</i> permission is required in order to take advantage of a vehicles <i>Allow Allies</i> permissions to be enforced.</li>\n<li>If a role is given to a <i>Trusted</i> friend who also inherits the <i>Citizens of my Deed</i> roles the citizen permissions will take priority. It would be required to manually add the desired role for the player to the managed item if it differs from the citizen permission. The player can exist in more than one list; if different permissions are selected for the same player, they will end up with a merged set of permissions.</li>\n<li>Item-level permissions, including <b>Deny All</b>, can be used to override settlement-level permissions.</li>\n<li><font color=\"#0000FF\">Blue</font> settings may only be set on citizen-type roles.</li>\n<li><font color=\"#FF6666\">Destroy Any Building</font> is a citizen-only role. This will allow anyone with this permission the ability to bash any building, regardless of ownership.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Settlement_Permissions\">Settlement Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Role_Management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"830\" data-file-width=\"661\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"377\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/18/Role_Management.jpg/300px-Role_Management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/18/Role_Management.jpg/450px-Role_Management.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/18/Role_Management.jpg/600px-Role_Management.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Role_Management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Role Management</div></div></div>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Animals_2\">Animals</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Brand</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows branding of animals on deed. - Only for Citizen type roles.</font></dd>\n<dt>Breed</dt>\n<dd>Allows breeding of animals on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Butcher</dt>\n<dd>Allows butchering on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Groom</dt>\n<dd>Allows grooming of animals on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Lead</dt>\n<dd>Allows leading of animals on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Milk/Shear</dt>\n<dd>Allows milking of cows and shearing of sheep.</dd>\n<dt>Sacrifice</dt>\n<dd>Allows sacrificing of animals on deed.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">Tame</a>/<a href=\"/index.php/Charm_animal\" title=\"Charm animal\">Charm</a>/<a href=\"/index.php/Dominate\" title=\"Dominate\">Dominate</a></dt>\n<dd>Allows taming of animals on deed. Charming and Dominating requires this and <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#General\" title=\"Permissions\">Cast Deity Spells</a></b>.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Construction\">Construction</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Build</dt>\n<dd>Allows ability to color and continue on buildings and build fences and place mine doors.</dd>\n<dt>Destroy Fences</dt>\n<dd>Allows destruction of fences and gates.</dd>\n<dt>Destroy Items</dt>\n<dd>Allows destruction of items.</dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Pick Locks</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows lockpicking of buildings, items and gates. Also requires <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Item_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Pickup</a></b> permission to lockpick items. - Only for Citizen type roles.</font></dd>\n<dt>Plan Buildings</dt>\n<dd>Allows planning of buildings.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Digging\">Digging</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Cultivate</dt>\n<dd>Allows cultivating of packed tiles.</dd>\n<dt>Dig Clay/Tar/Peat/Moss</dt>\n<dd>Allows digging of resource tiles.</dd>\n<dt>Pack</dt>\n<dd>Allows packing of tiles.</dd>\n<dt>Terraform</dt>\n<dd>Allows terraforming (digging, leveling and flattening).</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Farming\">Farming</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Harvest Fields</dt>\n<dd>Allows harvesting of fields.</dd>\n<dt>Sow Fields</dt>\n<dd>Allows sowing of fields.</dd>\n<dt>Tend Fields</dt>\n<dd>Allows tending of fields.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span id=\"Forestry/Gardening\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Forestry.2FGardening\">Forestry/Gardening</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Chop Down Trees and Bushes</dt>\n<dd>Allows chopping down of all trees and bushes except the very old and overaged trees.</dd>\n<dt>Chop Down V.Old Trees</dt>\n<dd>Allows chopping down of very old and overaged trees. Also allows \'<a href=\"/index.php/Wild_growth\" title=\"Wild growth\">Wild growth</a>\' spell on hedges, but that requires <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#General\" title=\"Permissions\">Cast Deity Spells</a></b> privilege as well.</dd>\n<dt>Cut Grass</dt>\n<dd>Allows cutting of grass.</dd>\n<dt>Harvest Fruit</dt>\n<dd>Allows harvesting from trees and bushes.</dd>\n<dt>Make Lawn</dt>\n<dd>Allows ability to make lawn.</dd>\n<dt>Pick Sprouts</dt>\n<dd>Allows picking of sprouts from trees and bushes and also allows picking of flowers.</dd>\n<dt>Plant Flowers</dt>\n<dd>Allows planting of flowers, mixed grass and thatch.</dd>\n<dt>Plant Sprouts</dt>\n<dd>Allows planting of sprouts including hedges.</dd>\n<dt>Prune</dt>\n<dd>Allows pruning of trees and bushes including hedges.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"General\">General</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Attack Citizens</dt>\n<dd>Allows attacking of citizens and allies of the settlement.</dd>\n<dt>Attack Non Citizens</dt>\n<dd>Allows attacking of non citizens which includes animals.</dd>\n<dt>Cast Deity Spells</dt>\n<dd>Allows use of deity spells on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Cast Sorcery Spells</dt>\n<dd>Allows use of sorcery spells on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Forage/Botanize</dt>\n<dd>Allows foraging and botanizing on deed.</dd>\n<dt>May Pass Gates</dt>\n<dd>Allows passing of gates that don\'t have any permissions set.</dd>\n<dt>May Place NPCs</dt>\n<dd>Allows placing of merchants and traders.</dd>\n<dt>Pave</dt>\n<dd>Allows adding or removing of paving on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Use Meditation Abilities</dt>\n<dd>Allows use of meditation abilities on deed.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Item_Management\">Item Management</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Attach Locks</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows attaching of locks on items on deed. - Only for Citizen type roles.</font></dd>\n<dt>Drop</dt>\n<dd>Allows dropping of items on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Improve/Repair</dt>\n<dd>Allows improving and repairing of items on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Load</dt>\n<dd>Allows loading of items on deed, also requires <b>Pickup</b> permissions or <b>Pickup Planted</b> permission.</dd>\n<dt>Pickup</dt>\n<dd>Allows picking up of items on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Pickup Planted Items</dt>\n<dd>Allows picking up of planted items on deed, also requires <b>Pickup</b> permission.</dd>\n<dt>Plant Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows planting and securing of items on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Pull/Push/Turn</dt>\n<dd>Allows pull, push, and turning of items on deed.</dd>\n<dt>UnLoad</dt>\n<dd>Allows unloading of items on deed.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mining\">Mining</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Add/Remove Reinforcement</dt>\n<dd>Allows adding and removing of reinforced walls (needs <b>Mine Rock</b>) and floors (needs <b>Mine Floor</b>) on deed. Also used to control <a href=\"/index.php/Disintegrate\" title=\"Disintegrate\">Disintegrate</a>, which will also need <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#General\" title=\"Permissions\">Cast Deity Spells</a></b></dd>\n<dt>Mine Floor</dt>\n<dd>Allows mining of floors in cave on deed including leveling and flattening in caves.</dd>\n<dt>Mine Iron Veins</dt>\n<dd>Allows mining of iron veins on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Mine Other Veins</dt>\n<dd>Allows mining of other veins on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Mine Rock</dt>\n<dd>Allows mining of rock in caves on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Surface Mining</dt>\n<dd>Allows surface mining on deed.</dd>\n<dt>Tunnel</dt>\n<dd>Allows making tunnel entrances on deed.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Settlement_Management\"><font color=\"#0000FF\">Settlement Management</font></span></h4>\n<ul><li>Only citizen-type roles may have these permissions set on them. They are not visible on non-citizen roles and cannot be enabled.</li>\n<li>If checked when creating a new non-citizen role, they will be removed once the role is saved.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allow Actions on Allied Deeds</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows actions on allied deeds using their ally role, if not set then they it will use their non-citizen.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#FF6666\">Destroy Any Buildings</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#FF6666\">Allows demolition of any building.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Invite Citizens</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to invite non-citizens to join the settlement including using recruitment boards.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Allowed Objects</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to manage allowed objects, that\'s buildings, gates, and mine doors that have the Settlement May Manage flag set.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Citizen Roles</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to assign roles to citizens.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Guards</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows hiring guards to protect the settlement and uphold these rules.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Map</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to add and remove village annotations on the map. Updating alliance annotations requires the manage politics permission as well.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Politics</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to form and break alliances with other settlements, as well as declare war and make peace.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Reputations</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to manage reputations.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Roles</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows managing of permissions in any role in which you have the corresponding permission in your role.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Manage Settings</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows changing settlement settings.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">May Configure Twitter</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to configure twitter settings.</font></dd>\n<dt><font color=\"#0000FF\">Resize Settlement</font></dt>\n<dd><font color=\"#0000FF\">Allows ability to change the size of the settlement.</font></dd></dl></dd></dl>', 6),
(18281, 1727, 'Ships', 'Ships', 'A boat lock is required to activate ship permissions. You can manage ships by right-clicking on your body and clicking on Manage > Ships . You may also right-click on an ship you own or have permission to manage and click Manage Ship . This option may be under the Permissions menu if there are multiple permission options on that ship. You will only have the option to manage a ship if you are the owner or have been given the Manage Item permission on that ship. Ship Notes Ship management Do not rely on permission categories , such as Alliance of \"Alliance Name\" or Citizens of \"Settlement Name\" for crossing server borders. Instead use named permissions. Unless you are the owner, have the key or have full manage rights to an item, taking it across server borders will leave you with an item that you can no longer manage or use. The owner of a vehicle can change the name of that vehicle at any time or attach a lock to it thereby making it useless to anyone else, including locking you out of any items you may have inside the cart. If you have obtained a locked vehicle from another player who did not pass along the key to you, immediately replace the lock. Failing to do so can result in the owner of the key unlocking your vehicle at any time. Commanding a boat cross server without explicit permissions will give an error message and prohibit the crossing. Keys are no longer required for unlocking or replacing a lock if you are the owner of the boat. Ship Permissions Ship permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. Can Command Allows commanding of this vehicle. Can be Passenger Allows being a passenger of this vehicle. Access Hold Allows access to the hold. May Drag Allows the vehicle to be dragged. Deny All Deny all access.', '<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Boat_lock\" title=\"Boat lock\">boat lock</a> is required to activate ship permissions. You can manage ships by <b>right-clicking</b> on your body and clicking on <i>Manage &gt; Ships</i>. You may also <b>right-click</b> on an ship you own or have permission to manage and click <i>Manage Ship</i>. This option may be under the <i>Permissions</i> menu if there are multiple permission options on that ship. You will only have the option to manage a ship if you are the owner or have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission on that ship.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ship_Notes\">Ship Notes</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Ship_management.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"233\" data-file-width=\"341\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"205\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/bd/Ship_management.jpg/300px-Ship_management.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/b/bd/Ship_management.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Ship_management.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Ship management</div></div></div>\n<ul><li>Do not rely on <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Permission_Categories\" title=\"Permissions\">permission categories</a>, such as <b>Alliance of \"Alliance Name\"</b> or <b>Citizens of \"Settlement Name\"</b> for crossing server borders. Instead use named permissions.</li>\n<li>Unless you are the owner, have the key or have full manage rights to an item, taking it across server borders will leave you with an item that you can no longer manage or use.</li>\n<li>The owner of a vehicle can change the name of that vehicle at any time or attach a lock to it thereby making it useless to anyone else, including locking you out of any items you may have inside the cart.</li>\n<li>If you have obtained a locked vehicle from another player who did not pass along the key to you, immediately replace the lock. Failing to do so can result in the owner of the key unlocking your vehicle at any time.</li>\n<li>Commanding a boat cross server without explicit permissions will give an error message and prohibit the crossing.</li>\n<li>Keys are no longer required for unlocking or replacing a lock if you are the owner of the boat.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ship_Permissions\">Ship Permissions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Ship_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"319\" data-file-width=\"499\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"192\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/47/Ship_permissions.jpg/300px-Ship_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/4/47/Ship_permissions.jpg/450px-Ship_permissions.jpg 1.5x, /images/4/47/Ship_permissions.jpg 2x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Ship_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Ship permissions</div></div></div>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>Can Command</dt>\n<dd>Allows commanding of this vehicle.</dd>\n<dt>Can be Passenger</dt>\n<dd>Allows being a passenger of this vehicle.</dd>\n<dt>Access Hold</dt>\n<dd>Allows access to the hold.</dd>\n<dt>May Drag</dt>\n<dd>Allows the vehicle to be dragged.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Deny all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 7),
(18282, 1727, 'Item Permissions', 'Item_Permissions', 'Item permissions cannot be managed remotely and must be done at the item you wish to manage. Containers Container permissions Containers require a small padlock or a large padlock to be attached in order to activate permissions. The owner of the container is the person who dropped it, planted it, or unloaded it, and only the owner may attach or replace a lock on a container. To manage a container, right-click on the container and click Permissions > Manage Item , where Item will be the type of container you are managing. You must be the owner or have been given the Manage Item permission in order to manage that container. Container Notes Only the owner may rename a container. Keys may still be used to access containers without the need to set up permissions. Keys are not required to modify a container\'s lock. Container Permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. May Open Allows access to this container. Deny All Denies all access. Beds Bed permissions You can manage a bed by right-clicking on the bed and clicking Permissions > Manage Bed . You must either be the owner of the building the bed is in, be able to manage the building, or have the Manage Item permission for that bed in order to manage it. Since Manage Allowed Objects allows for management of the building, it also allows for management of the beds inside settlement-managed buildings. Bed Notes Beds with no permissions default to allowing anyone with May Enter to sleep for free. Only the owner of the building, or the mayor of a settlement-managed building, may rename a bed or set rent on a bed. Free Sleep overrides any rent set on that bed. Bed Permissions Manage Item Allows managing of these permissions. May Use Bed Allows access to this bed. Free Sleep Allows this bed to be used for free. (Requires May Use Bed ) Deny All Denies all access.', '<p>Item permissions cannot be managed remotely and must be done at the item you wish to manage.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Containers\">Containers</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Container_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"314\" data-file-width=\"449\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"210\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/d6/Container_permissions.jpg/300px-Container_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/d/d6/Container_permissions.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Container_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Container permissions</div></div></div>\n<p>Containers require a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_padlock\" title=\"Small padlock\">small padlock</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_padlock\" title=\"Large padlock\">large padlock</a> to be attached in order to activate permissions. The owner of the container is the person who dropped it, planted it, or unloaded it, and only the owner may attach or replace a lock on a container. To manage a container, <b>right-click</b> on the container and click <i>Permissions &gt; Manage Item</i>, where Item will be the type of container you are managing. You must be the owner or have been given the <b>Manage Item</b> permission in order to manage that container.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Container_Notes\">Container Notes</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Only the owner may rename a container.</li>\n<li>Keys may still be used to access containers without the need to set up permissions.</li>\n<li>Keys are not required to modify a container\'s lock.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Container_Permissions\">Container Permissions</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>May Open</dt>\n<dd>Allows access to this container.</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Denies all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Beds\">Beds</span></h3>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bed_permissions.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"311\" data-file-width=\"448\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"208\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/05/Bed_permissions.jpg/300px-Bed_permissions.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/0/05/Bed_permissions.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Bed_permissions.jpg\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Bed permissions</div></div></div>\n<p>You can manage a bed by <b>right-clicking</b> on the bed and clicking <i>Permissions &gt; Manage Bed</i>. You must either be the owner of the building the bed is in, be able to manage the building, or have the <b>Manage Item</b> permission for that bed in order to manage it. Since <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Settlement_Management\" title=\"Permissions\">Manage Allowed Objects</a></b> allows for management of the building, it also allows for management of the beds inside settlement-managed buildings.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bed_Notes\">Bed Notes</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Beds with no permissions default to allowing anyone with <b><a href=\"/index.php/Permissions#Building_Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">May Enter</a></b> to sleep for free.</li>\n<li>Only the owner of the building, or the mayor of a settlement-managed building, may rename a bed or set rent on a bed.</li>\n<li><b>Free Sleep</b> overrides any rent set on that bed.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bed_Permissions\">Bed Permissions</span></h4>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Manage Item</dt>\n<dd>Allows managing of these permissions.</dd>\n<dt>May Use Bed</dt>\n<dd>Allows access to this bed.</dd>\n<dt>Free Sleep</dt>\n<dd>Allows this bed to be used for free. (Requires <b>May Use Bed</b>)</dd>\n<dt>Deny All</dt>\n<dd>Denies all access.</dd></dl></dd></dl>', 8),
(18283, 1727, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Here are a few key points to note when dealing with managed items. Some of these are referenced above within the relevant sections. Unless you are the owner, have the key or have full manage rights to an item, taking it across server borders will leave you with an item that you can no longer manage or use. If a role is given to a Trusted friend who also inherits the Citizens of my Deed roles the citizen permissions will take priority. It would be required to manually add the desired role for the player to the managed item if it differs from the citizen permission. The player can exist in more than one list; if different permissions are selected for the same player, they will end up with a merged set of permissions. Commanding a boat cross server without explicit permissions will give an error message and prohibit the crossing.', '<p>Here are a few key points to note when dealing with managed items. Some of these are referenced above within the relevant sections.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Unless you are the owner, have the key or have full manage rights to an item, taking it across server borders will leave you with an item that you can no longer manage or use.</li>\n<li>If a role is given to a <i>Trusted</i> friend who also inherits the <i>Citizens of my Deed</i> roles the citizen permissions will take priority. It would be required to manually add the desired role for the player to the managed item if it differs from the citizen permission. The player can exist in more than one list; if different permissions are selected for the same player, they will end up with a merged set of permissions.</li>\n<li>Commanding a boat cross server without explicit permissions will give an error message and prohibit the crossing.</li></ul>', 9),
(18284, 1469, 'Description', 'Description', 'Any player who follows one of the \" White Light Gods \": Fo , Magranon or Vynora . A player can become a Whitelighter if he or she journeys to the Altar of Three on the wild server, or joins either of the White Light kingdoms: Jenn-Kellon or Mol-Rehan . Players on the Freedom servers are restricted to the White Light Gods, and so could similarly be considered Whitelighters .', '<p>Any player who follows one of the \"<a href=\"/index.php/Altar_of_Three\" title=\"Altar of Three\">White Light Gods</a>\": <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>.\n</p>\n<p>A player can become a <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Whitelighter</a> if he or she journeys to the <a href=\"/index.php/Altar_of_Three\" title=\"Altar of Three\">Altar of Three</a> on the wild server, or joins either of the White Light kingdoms: <a href=\"/index.php/Jenn-Kellon\" title=\"Jenn-Kellon\">Jenn-Kellon</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a>. Players on the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> servers are restricted to the White Light Gods, and so could similarly be considered <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Whitelighters</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18285, 1469, 'Advantages', 'Advantages', 'As Whitelighters can follow a greater number of Gods , it could be argued that they collectively (through teamwork) have access to a greater variety of spells and enchantments than Blacklighters ; if they should later choose to become priests or priestesses.', '<ul><li>As <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Whitelighters</a> can follow a greater number of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Religion\" title=\"Category:Religion\">Gods</a>, it could be argued that they collectively (through teamwork) have access to a greater variety of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spells and enchantments</a> than <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighters</a>; if they should later choose to become <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> or priestesses.</li></ul>', 1),
(18286, 1469, 'Disadvantages', 'Disadvantages', 'Unlike the Blacklighters the White Light Gods frown on many sorts of actions, the least of which being theft, all the way to the dank pit of sin known as cannibalism. While this may not make much of a difference to someone who would follow these \"virtues\" to the letter, for someone who enjoys the darker things in life the rules laid down by the White Lighters can feel too constrained, and often leaves the person either; causing problems in their social circles due to their difference in moral values, and in more extreme circumstances a full renunciation of their White Light Religion.', '<ul><li>Unlike the <a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighters</a> the White Light Gods frown on many sorts of actions, the least of which being theft, all the way to the dank pit of sin known as cannibalism. While this may not make much of a difference to someone who would follow these \"virtues\" to the letter, for someone who enjoys the darker things in life the rules laid down by the White Lighters can feel too constrained, and often leaves the person either; causing problems in their social circles due to their difference in moral values, and in more extreme circumstances a full renunciation of their White Light Religion.</li></ul>', 2),
(18287, 1469, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Religion Blacklighter White light Black light', '<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Blacklighter\" title=\"Blacklighter\">Blacklighter</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/White_light\" title=\"White light\">White light</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Black_light\" title=\"Black light\">Black light</a></li></ul></dd></dl>', 3),
(18306, 2878, 'Description', 'Description', 'Black, sooty charcoal.', '<p><i>Black, sooty charcoal.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18307, 2878, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to make Steel lumps Making steel from combined pieces will only consume the necessary charcoal. Possible to split 1.5kg of butchered charcoal into 0.5kg pieces by putting it into a bulk storage bin , then removing said pieces. Charcoal can be butchered from these creatures: Hell hound Lava fiend Lava spider', '<ul><li>Used to make <a href=\"/index.php/Steel_lump\" title=\"Steel lump\">Steel lumps</a></li>\n<li>Making steel from combined pieces will only consume the necessary charcoal.</li>\n<li>Possible to split 1.5kg of butchered charcoal into 0.5kg pieces by putting it into a <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bin</a>, then removing said pieces.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Charcoal</b> can be butchered from these creatures:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Hell_hound\" title=\"Hell hound\">Hell hound</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lava_fiend\" title=\"Lava fiend\">Lava fiend</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lava_spider\" title=\"Lava spider\">Lava spider</a></li></ul>', 1),
(18312, 4701, 'Description', 'Description', 'A pile of items. Literally a pile of items. Each pile can hold only 100 items, not counting any\nthat are in containers , though the containers themselves are counted as items. Putting dirt into a pile of items and then removing the other items forms a pile of dirt , which does not raise the tiles below it, allowing for easy storage. 3 items must be on a tile to spawn a pile of items, which appears as a topless wooden box with tools inside it. The pile appears differently if items of a single type are in the pile.', '<p><i>A pile of items.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Literally a pile of items. Each pile can hold only 100 items, not counting any\nthat are in <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">containers</a>, though the containers themselves are counted as items. Putting <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> into a pile of items and then removing the other items forms a <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_dirt\" title=\"Pile of dirt\">pile of dirt</a>, which does not raise the tiles below it, allowing for easy storage. 3 items must be on a tile to spawn a pile of items, which appears as a topless wooden box with tools inside it. The pile appears differently if items of a single type are in the pile.\n</p>', 0),
(18316, 1238, 'Problems before pressing the play button', 'Problems_before_pressing_the_play_button', 'The game crashes before the login screen Make sure you are running an up to date client version. Make sure your Java version is up to date. The play button is grayed out Have you entered your character name correctly? Have you entered your password? Have you read and accepted the EULA? Has the pack update completed successfully? If the button remains greyed out, post a thread in the bug forum and ask for help. The pack update has failed (In version 2.7.0 or newer only) Press the \'show error log\' button and post the log in the bug forum. Attempt to download the packs manually. The packs can be downloaded using these links (Right click & then Save Target/Link As ): http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/graphics.jar http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/sound.jar Then, place the downloaded .jar files in the wurm/packs/ folder. Do not attempt to unzip the files. Make sure ALL files are downloaded and installed. If it still doesn\'t work: Make a post in the bug forum and wait for dev or GM assistance.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_game_crashes_before_the_login_screen\">The game crashes before the login screen</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Make sure you are running an up to date client version.</li>\n<li>Make sure your Java version is up to date.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_play_button_is_grayed_out\">The play button is grayed out</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Have you entered your character name correctly?</li>\n<li>Have you entered your password?</li>\n<li>Have you read and accepted the EULA?</li>\n<li>Has the pack update completed successfully?</li></ul>\n<p>If the button remains greyed out, post a thread in the bug forum and ask for help.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_pack_update_has_failed\">The pack update has failed</span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"color:red\">(In version 2.7.0 or newer only)</span> Press the \'show error log\' button and post the log in the bug forum.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Download-icon.gif\"><img alt=\"Download-icon.gif\" data-file-height=\"24\" data-file-width=\"24\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"24\" src=\"/images/c/c8/Download-icon.gif\" width=\"24\"/></a> <i>Attempt to download the packs manually.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The packs can be downloaded using these links (Right click &amp; then <tt>Save Target/Link As</tt>):\n</p>\n<div style=\"-moz-border-radius: 10px; background-color:#f8f8f8; border:2px solid #e0e0e0;margin-right:50%;\"><i></i>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/graphics.jar\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/graphics.jar</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/sound.jar\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/packs/sound.jar</a></li></ul>\n</div>\n<p>Then, place the downloaded .jar files in the wurm/packs/ folder.\n</p>\n<p><b>Do not attempt to unzip the files.</b>\n</p>\n<p>Make sure ALL files are downloaded and installed.\n</p>\n<p><b>If it still doesn\'t work:</b>\n</p>\n<p>Make a post in the bug forum and wait for dev or GM assistance.\n</p>', 0),
(18317, 1238, 'Problems after pressing play, before actually playing', 'Problems_after_pressing_play.2C_before_actually_playing', 'Grey game window when using a Macintosh Make sure you are using the JOGL+AWT renderer in game settings. Turn on \'Use nanoTime\' timer in the compatibility tab in the settings. The game crashes with a crash window Read the crash message at the top of the window (the part inside <brackets>). Check Client Log Messages if the message and a solution is listed. The game crashes without a crash window Locate the HS_ERR_PID crash log. It is usually on the desktop, but can be placed in other locations too. For Intel users Disable VBO (compatibility tab) If it still crashes, disable multidraw (compatibility tab) For ATI users Make sure you are using Catalyst 9.12 or newer . If your card is too old, use Catalyst 9.3 or older . Catalyst 9.4 through 9.11 have OpenGL memory leaks. Disable Catalyst AI Set antialiasing (AA) and anisotropic filtering (AF) to game-controlled. If it still fails Post your log file with description of the problem in the technical issues forums, and wait for developer, GM or other assistance. Link : http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/forum/26-technical-issues/ Mention that you used this page, and that your problem wasn\'t listed.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Grey_game_window_when_using_a_Macintosh\">Grey game window when using a Macintosh</span></h3>\n<p>Make sure you are using the JOGL+AWT renderer in game settings.\n</p>\n<p>Turn on \'Use nanoTime\' timer in the compatibility tab in the settings. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_game_crashes_with_a_crash_window\">The game crashes with a crash window</span></h3>\n<p>Read the crash message at the top of the window (the part inside &lt;brackets&gt;).\n</p>\n<ul><li>Check <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Client_Log_Messages\" title=\"Client Log Messages\">Client Log Messages</a> if the message and a solution is listed.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_game_crashes_without_a_crash_window\">The game crashes without a crash window</span></h3>\n<p>Locate the HS_ERR_PID crash log. It is usually on the desktop, but can be placed in other locations too.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"For_Intel_users\">For Intel users</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Disable VBO (compatibility tab)</li>\n<li>If it still crashes, disable multidraw (compatibility tab)</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"For_ATI_users\">For ATI users</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Make sure you are using Catalyst 9.12 <b>or newer</b>.\n<ul><li>If your card is too old, use Catalyst 9.3 <b>or older</b>.</li>\n<li>Catalyst 9.4 through 9.11 have OpenGL memory leaks.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Disable Catalyst AI</li>\n<li>Set antialiasing (AA) and anisotropic filtering (AF) to game-controlled.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"If_it_still_fails\">If it still fails</span></h4>\n<p>Post your log file with description of the problem in the technical issues forums, and wait for developer, GM or other assistance.\n</p>\n<pre> Link : <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/forum/26-technical-issues/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/forum/26-technical-issues/</a>\n</pre>\n<p>Mention that you used this page, and that your problem wasn\'t listed.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18318, 1238, 'Other technical issues', 'Other_technical_issues', '64bit Java If you\'re running a 64bit Windows you should run 64bit Java too. This will allow you to use more of the available system memory and it avoids certain crashes that may occur with 32bit Java. When you visit the Java download site with a 32bit web browser you will get the 32bit Java download by default. Visit the Java download site to download the 64bit version. If you don\'t need the 32bit version of Java you should uninstall Java completely and install only the 64bit version. This will prevent problems where the 32bit version is automaticly selected to run Wurm. Once you have the 64bit Java installed you can create a shortcut to start the Wurm client. Paste one of the following command lines as target for the shortcut. Stable client \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\javaws.exe\" http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp Unstable client \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\javaws.exe\" http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient_unstable.jnlp Texture problems on turkish computers The turkish language settings performs upper and lowercase conversion of the letters i and I differently than most languages. As a consequence the client can\'t find some textures and models and just display a red \"x\" on white ground instead. You can either change the language setting of your computer to a different language (eg. english) [1] or\nstart Wurm with an option to run with a different language setting [2] : Create a shortcut with the following command or run the command from the command prompt (Windows+R): C:\\Windows\\System32\\javaws.exe -J-Duser.country=us -J-Duser.language=en http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp Solutions in the forums Out of memory errors: [3] nVidia Optimus systems: [4]', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"64bit_Java\">64bit Java</span></h3>\n<p>If you\'re running a 64bit Windows you should run 64bit Java too. This will allow you to use more of the available system memory and it avoids certain crashes that may occur with 32bit Java.\n</p>\n<p>When you visit the Java download site with a 32bit web browser you will get the 32bit Java download by default. Visit the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://java.com/en/download/manual.jsp\" rel=\"nofollow\">Java download site</a> to download the 64bit version.\n</p>\n<p>If you don\'t need the 32bit version of Java you should uninstall Java completely and install only the 64bit version. This will prevent problems where the 32bit version is automaticly selected to run Wurm.\n</p>\n<p>Once you have the 64bit Java installed you can create a shortcut to start the Wurm client. Paste one of the following command lines as target for the shortcut. \n</p>\n<p><b>Stable client</b>\n</p>\n<pre>\"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\javaws.exe\" <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp</a>\n</pre>\n<p><b>Unstable client</b>\n</p>\n<pre>\"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\javaws.exe\" <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient_unstable.jnlp\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient_unstable.jnlp</a>\n</pre>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Texture_problems_on_turkish_computers\">Texture problems on turkish computers</span></h3>\n<p>The turkish language settings performs upper and lowercase conversion of the letters <i>i</i> and <i>I</i> differently than most languages. As a consequence the client can\'t find some textures and models and just display a red \"x\" on white ground instead.\n</p>\n<p>You can either change the language setting of your computer to a different language (eg. english) <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/72252-strange-texture-issues-since-3-months/#entry715617\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a> or\nstart Wurm with an option to run with a different language setting <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/93625-graphics-problem/#entry939516\" rel=\"nofollow\">[2]</a>:\n</p>\n<p>Create a shortcut with the following command or run the command from the command prompt (Windows+R):\n</p>\n<pre>C:\\Windows\\System32\\javaws.exe -J-Duser.country=us -J-Duser.language=en <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/client/wurmclient.jnlp</a>\n</pre>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions_in_the_forums\">Solutions in the forums</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Out of memory errors: <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/75790-how-do-i-fix-this-problem/#entry749327\" rel=\"nofollow\">[3]</a></li>\n<li>nVidia Optimus systems: <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/71698-2fps-and-crashing/#entry708815\" rel=\"nofollow\">[4]</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18319, 1238, 'Gameplay problems', 'Gameplay_problems', '', '', 3),
(18327, 2586, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wood chip carved into a hook with a stone as sink.', '<p><i>A wood chip carved into a hook with a stone as sink.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18328, 2586, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Drop into an empty fishing hook slot on a fishing line Wood type will affect how fast a fish turns up. The default is a modifier of 1, and each wood type modifier is additive to the default, so creating the right hook can nearly halve the time for a fish to turn up. The lower the modifier % in the chart below, the quicker the interval of time in which the fish turns up, i.e. the more effective the hook. (Example: Lemon/Orange is the preferred wood type for quickest results). Wood Type Modifier Cedar 90% Fir 85% Pine 95% Lemon and Orange 75% Apple 80% Oleander 80%', '<ul><li>Drop into an <b>empty fishing hook slot</b> on a fishing line</li>\n<li>Wood type will affect how fast a fish turns up. The default is a modifier of 1, and each wood type modifier is additive to the default, so creating the right hook can nearly halve the time for a fish to turn up. The lower the modifier % in the chart below, the quicker the interval of time in which the fish turns up, i.e. the more effective the hook. (Example: Lemon/Orange is the preferred wood type for quickest results).</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Wood Type</th>\n<th>Modifier\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cedar</td>\n<td>90%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fir</td>\n<td>85%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pine</td>\n<td>95%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lemon and Orange</td>\n<td>75%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Apple</td>\n<td>80%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Oleander</td>\n<td>80%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18329, 2586, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can sometimes be found by Foraging at Seaweed Resource nodes .', '<ul><li>Can sometimes be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> at <a href=\"/index.php/Seaweed\" title=\"Seaweed\">Seaweed</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(18330, 4309, 'Description', 'Description', 'An arrow with a thin straight head that can more easily be pulled out of a killed creature.', '<p><i>An arrow with a thin straight head that can more easily be pulled out of a killed creature.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18331, 4309, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'It has greater accuracy than a war arrow , but does less damage. The quality level of the arrow head affects creation success. Arrows made from maple or oak take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5). Arrows made from cedar are easier to improve. Upon creation failure, the arrow head and arrow shaft loses 0.5 QL .', '<ul><li>It has greater accuracy than a <a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">war arrow</a>, but does less damage.</li>\n<li>The quality level of the <a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow_head\" title=\"Hunting arrow head\">arrow head</a> affects creation success.</li>\n<li>Arrows made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Maple\" title=\"Maple\">maple</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">oak</a> take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5).</li>\n<li>Arrows made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> are easier to improve.</li>\n<li>Upon creation failure, the arrow head and arrow shaft loses 0.5 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18332, 4309, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'War arrow Archery Arrow bundle', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">War arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_bundle\" title=\"Arrow bundle\">Arrow bundle</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18351, 4312, 'Description', 'Description', 'A straight pointy arrow head without barbs. This arrow head is made out of any metal .', '<p><i>A straight pointy arrow head without barbs.</i>\n</p>\n<p>This arrow head is made out of any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal_lump\" title=\"Metal lump\">metal</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18352, 4312, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a hunting arrow when attached to an arrow shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">hunting arrow</a> when attached to an <a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">arrow shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18353, 4312, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'While a lump of 0.10 kg is required to craft, only 0.04 kg will be used per attempt.', '<ul><li>While a lump of 0.10 kg is required to craft, only 0.04 kg will be used per attempt.</li></ul>', 2),
(18354, 4312, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Arrow shaft Hunting arrow War arrow War arrow head Fletching Archery', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">Arrow shaft</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">Hunting arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">War arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow_head\" title=\"War arrow head\">War arrow head</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fletching\" title=\"Fletching\">Fletching</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18355, 2368, 'Description', 'Description', 'About ten metal nails, each one long as your hand. Used for creating wooden house walls , small rafts , market stalls and rope tools .', '<p><i>About ten metal nails, each one long as your hand.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Used for creating <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_house_wall\" title=\"Wooden house wall\">wooden house walls</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Small_raft\" title=\"Small raft\">small rafts</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Market_stall\" title=\"Market stall\">market stalls</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Rope_tool\" title=\"Rope tool\">rope tools</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18356, 2368, 'Tips', 'Tips', 'Nails are a component never used for improving , so it is a common practice to use lower quality iron to create. The finished item that the nails were used for can always be improved later on. Can be found by foraging on flotsam with high skill.', '<p>Nails are a component never used for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Improving\" title=\"Improving\">improving</a>, so it is a common practice to use lower <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> iron to create. The finished item that the nails were used for can always be improved later on.\n</p>\n<p>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Flotsam\" title=\"Flotsam\">flotsam</a> with high skill.\n</p>', 1),
(18357, 2063, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thick wooden hammerhead. A wooden mallet head, used to create a mallet together with a shaft .', '<p><i>A thick wooden hammerhead.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A wooden mallet head, used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> together with a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18365, 2479, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wide, flat blade that is tapped along the cut line to produce a groove.', '<p><i>A wide, flat blade that is tapped along the cut line to produce a groove.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18366, 2479, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a stone chisel when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18370, 4313, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin arrow head with vicious barbs. This arrow head is made of any metal .', '<p><i>A thin arrow head with vicious barbs.</i>\n</p>\n<p>This arrow head is made of any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal\" title=\"Metal\">metal</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18371, 4313, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a war arrow when attached to an arrow shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">war arrow</a> when attached to an <a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">arrow shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18372, 4313, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'While a lump of 0.10kg is required to craft, only 0.04kg will be used per attempt.', '<ul><li>While a lump of 0.10kg is required to craft, only 0.04kg will be used per attempt.</li></ul>', 2),
(18373, 4313, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Arrow shaft War arrow Hunting arrow Hunting arrow head Fletching Archery', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_shaft\" title=\"Arrow shaft\">Arrow shaft</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow\" title=\"War arrow\">War arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">Hunting arrow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow_head\" title=\"Hunting arrow head\">Hunting arrow head</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fletching\" title=\"Fletching\">Fletching</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18374, 4310, 'Description', 'Description', 'An arrow with barbs designed to inflict damage to anyone trying to pull the arrow out.', '<p><i>An arrow with barbs designed to inflict damage to anyone trying to pull the arrow out.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18375, 4310, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'It does more damage then a hunting arrow , but it is less accurate. The quality level of the arrow head affects creation success. Arrows made from maple take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5). Examine on maple arrow includes \"Maple arrows are smooth, uniform and take less damage than other arrows.\" Arrows made from oak take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5). Arrows made from cedar are easier to improve. Examine on Cedar arrow includes \"Cedar arrows are easier to make straight and smooth.\"', '<ul><li>It does more damage then a <a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">hunting arrow</a>, but it is less accurate.</li>\n<li>The quality level of the <a href=\"/index.php/War_arrow_head\" title=\"War arrow head\">arrow head</a> affects creation success.</li>\n<li>Arrows made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Maple\" title=\"Maple\">maple</a> take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5). Examine on maple arrow includes \"Maple arrows are smooth, uniform and take less damage than other arrows.\"</li>\n<li>Arrows made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">oak</a> take less damage (4 damage a shot instead of 5).</li>\n<li>Arrows made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> are easier to improve. Examine on Cedar arrow includes \"Cedar arrows are easier to make straight and smooth.\"</li></ul>', 1),
(18376, 4310, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Archery Arrow bundle Hunting arrow', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Arrow_bundle\" title=\"Arrow bundle\">Arrow bundle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hunting_arrow\" title=\"Hunting arrow\">Hunting arrow</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18377, 1807, 'Description', 'Description', 'A strong tall stone wall', '<p><i>A strong tall stone wall </i>\n</p>', 0),
(18378, 1807, 'Skill required', 'Skill_required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18379, 1807, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Repair Tall stone wall with stone brick. Each stone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill. At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.', '<ul><li>Repair Tall stone wall with stone brick. Each stone brick will repair up to 10 damage depending on quality and repairing skill.</li>\n<li>At 60 damage, cracks will form on the wall.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 2),
(18380, 1807, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fences Fence gates Empirical Evaluation of Fences', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">Fence gates</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Empirical_Evaluation_of_Fences\" title=\"Empirical Evaluation of Fences\">Empirical Evaluation of Fences</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18381, 4724, 'Description', 'Description', 'You see a wall', '<p><i>You see a wall </i>\n</p>', 0),
(18382, 4724, 'Skill Requirements', 'Skill_Requirements', 'At least 30 masonry skill is required to build stone walls. See multi-story housing for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.', '<ul><li>At least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill is required to build stone walls.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Multi-story_housing#Skill_needed\" title=\"Multi-story housing\">multi-story housing</a> for more information regarding skill requirements on additional floors.</li></ul>', 1),
(18383, 4724, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Have at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory. Activate a trowel and right-click on a wall plan . Select Build and then Stone wall . Continuation requires at least 1 Stone brick and 1 mortar in your inventory.', '<ul><li>Have at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Mortar\" title=\"Mortar\">mortar</a> in your inventory.</li>\n<li><b>Activate</b> a <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and <b>right-click</b> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>.</li>\n<li>Select <b>Build</b> and then <b>Stone wall</b>.</li>\n<li>Continuation requires at least 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> and 1 mortar in your inventory.</li></ul>', 2),
(18384, 4724, 'Modifying', 'Modifying', 'Pliers are used for modifying the wall into its trimless version, the Plain stone wall . Activate the tool and right-click the wall, then select Remove Decorations . You can turn walls to suit your needs by right-clicking them, and selecting Rotate wall .', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Pliers\" title=\"Pliers\">Pliers</a> are used for modifying the wall into its trimless version, the <a href=\"/index.php/Plain_stone_wall\" title=\"Plain stone wall\">Plain stone wall</a>.  <b>Activate</b> the tool and <b>right-click</b> the wall, then select <b>Remove Decorations</b>.</li>\n<li>You can turn walls to suit your needs by <b>right-clicking</b> them, and selecting <b>Rotate wall</b>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18385, 4724, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'You must repair any damage on the walls with a Stone brick before improving it. Activate a Stone brick , right-click the wall and select Repair or Improve . The effective quality of the Stone brick is affected by its damage and your masonry skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.', '<ul><li>You must <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repair</a> any <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> on the walls with a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> before <a href=\"/index.php/Improve\" title=\"Improve\">improving</a> it.</li>\n<li>Activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a>, right-click the wall and select <i>Repair</i> or <i>Improve</i>.</li>\n<li>The effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">Stone brick</a> is affected by its damage and your <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, it must be higher than the wall\'s current quality.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(18386, 4724, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Stone wall Stone door Stone portcullis Stone window Stone oriel Stone double door Stone T arch Stone arch right Stone arch left', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Stone wall</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_door\" title=\"Stone door\">Stone door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_portcullis_(wall)\" title=\"Stone portcullis (wall)\"> Stone portcullis</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_window\" title=\"Stone window\">Stone window</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_oriel\" title=\"Stone oriel\">Stone oriel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_double_door\" title=\"Stone double door\">Stone double door</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_T_arch\" title=\"Stone T arch\">Stone T arch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_arch_right\" title=\"Stone arch right\">Stone arch right</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_arch_left\" title=\"Stone arch left\">Stone arch left</a></li></ul>', 5),
(18390, 3045, 'Description', 'Description', 'A stone altar, with decorations depicting famous religious events.', '<p><i>A stone altar, with decorations depicting famous religious events.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18391, 3045, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You will need to be a follower or a priest of a god for the initial creation of an altar and to continue adding items to the altar. The altar is dedicated to the god of the character that finishes it, not the one that starts it. All altars can be created even within a different god\'s domain. All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory. The metal type of the bowl used in creation does not change the final appearance of the altar or its bowl. Any items placed on the altar as decoration do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do.', '<ul><li>You will need to be a <a href=\"/index.php/Follower\" title=\"Follower\">follower</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priest</a> of a <a href=\"/index.php/Gods\" title=\"Gods\">god</a> for the initial creation of an altar and to continue adding items to the altar.</li>\n<li>The altar is dedicated to the god of the character that finishes it, not the one that starts it.</li>\n<li>All altars can be created even within a different god\'s domain.</li>\n<li>All altars can be pushed/pulled/placed once created. They cannot be loaded onto a vehicle or picked-up into inventory.</li>\n<li>The metal type of the bowl used in creation does not change the final appearance of the altar or its bowl.</li>\n<li>Any items placed on the altar as decoration do not get sacrificed - only items placed inside the altar do.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Altar_types.png\"><img alt=\"Altar types.png\" data-file-height=\"128\" data-file-width=\"500\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"128\" src=\"/images/c/c7/Altar_types.png\" width=\"500\"/></a></div></div>', 1),
(18392, 3045, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Pray Sermons Sacrificing', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Praying\" title=\"Praying\">Pray</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Faith#Sermons\" title=\"Faith\">Sermons</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sacrificing\" title=\"Sacrificing\">Sacrificing</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18393, 3045, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Gold altar Silver altar Wooden altar Altar Religion', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Gold_altar\" title=\"Gold altar\">Gold altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Silver_altar\" title=\"Silver altar\">Silver altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_altar\" title=\"Wooden altar\">Wooden altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">Altar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">Religion</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18398, 4612, 'Description', 'Description', 'The heavy metal head for a maul.', '<p><i>The heavy metal head for a maul.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18399, 4612, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a small maul when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">small maul</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18404, 3638, 'Description', 'Description', 'A smooth heavy clump of metal on a shaft. A small maul is a weapon very similar in appearance to a hammer, except on a greater scale. It is used for bashing and bludgeoning things with, and is very effective against walls. The small maul is the smaller of 3 variants.', '<p><i>A smooth heavy clump of metal on a shaft.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A small maul is a weapon very similar in appearance to a hammer, except on a greater scale. It is used for bashing and bludgeoning things with, and is very effective against walls. The small maul is the smaller of 3 variants.\n</p>', 0),
(18405, 3638, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Skills: Mauls > Small maul Strength: 0.225 (Weaker than the small axe, but stronger than the short sword) Attack Speed: 3 seconds Damage Type: Mauling Parry Rate: Medium Wielding: One-hander', '<ul><li>Skills: <a href=\"/index.php/Mauls\" title=\"Mauls\">Mauls</a> &gt; Small maul</li>\n<li>Strength: 0.225 (Weaker than the small axe, but stronger than the short sword)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 3 seconds</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Mauling</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Medium</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>', 1),
(18406, 3638, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Exquisite', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Exquisite</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18407, 3638, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mauling damage is good vs armour units. Great at demolition as they are akin to what we know in real-life as a sledge hammer.', '<ul><li>Mauling damage is good vs armour units.</li>\n<li>Great at demolition as they are akin to what we know in real-life as a sledge hammer.</li></ul>', 3),
(18408, 3638, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a small maul Mauls > Small maul Body > Body strength When creating a small maul Smithing > Weapon smithing .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<p>When using a small maul\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mauls\" title=\"Mauls\">Mauls</a> &gt; Small maul</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a small maul \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 4),
(18414, 2355, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small lockable chest suitable for holding valuable items.', '<p><i>A small lockable chest suitable for holding valuable items.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18415, 2355, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Jewelry Casket Skin Everlasting Love chest skin', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_Casket_Skin\" title=\"Jewelry Casket Skin\">Jewelry Casket Skin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Everlasting_Love_chest_skin\" title=\"Everlasting Love chest skin\">Everlasting Love chest skin</a></li></ul>', 1),
(18416, 2355, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Final plank attached determines wood type and texture. May be carried in your inventory or can be placed in other containers. To lock, drop onto ground before applying lock. Can be locked with either a large padlock or a small padlock .', '<ul><li>Final plank attached determines wood type and texture.</li>\n<li>May be carried in your inventory or can be placed in other containers.</li>\n<li>To lock, drop onto ground before applying lock.</li>\n<li>Can be locked with either a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_padlock\" title=\"Large padlock\">large padlock</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_padlock\" title=\"Small padlock\">small padlock</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(18422, 2526, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small axe head.', '<p><i>A small axe head.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18423, 2526, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a small axe when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">small axe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18424, 2523, 'Description', 'Description', 'A short but sturdy axe with a thick blade.', '<p><i>A short but sturdy axe with a thick blade.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18425, 2523, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.250 (Stronger than the small maul) Attack Speed: 3 seconds Damage Type: Cutting Parry Rate: Low Wielding: One-hander', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.250 (Stronger than the small maul)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 3 seconds</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Low</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>', 1),
(18426, 2523, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Small axe', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Small axe</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18427, 2523, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'It is the lightest of four varieties of axe and as such will not do much damage in combat, although it is rather fast. Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20. The small axe is primarily a weapon. Much like the small maul and short sword, it sacrifices damage for increased accuracy, speed, and parry rate. The standard relationship between swords, mauls, and axes suggests that small axes most likely do more damage than short swords and small mauls, but perhaps parries less than both.', '<ul><li>It is the lightest of four varieties of axe and as such will not do much damage in combat, although it is rather fast.</li>\n<li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.</li>\n<li>The small axe is primarily a weapon. Much like the small maul and short sword, it sacrifices damage for increased accuracy, speed, and parry rate. The standard relationship between swords, mauls, and axes suggests that small axes most likely do more damage than short swords and small mauls, but perhaps parries less than both.</li></ul>', 3),
(18428, 2523, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a small axe Axes > Small axe Body > Body strength When creating a small axe Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a small axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Axes\" title=\"Axes\">Axes</a> &gt; Small axe</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a small axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(18429, 2523, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Small Axeman at 50 skill Hacker at 70 skill Ripper at 90 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Small Axeman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Hacker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Ripper at 90 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(18439, 897, 'Description', 'Description', 'Sub-skill of weapon smithing . This is the skill used in creating and improving weapon heads and arrow heads.', '<p>Sub-skill of <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">weapon smithing</a>. This is the skill used in creating and improving weapon heads and arrow heads. \n</p>', 0),
(18440, 897, 'Tools for creating and improving weapon heads smithing items', 'Tools_for_creating_and_improving_weapon_heads_smithing_items', 'Metal lumps (Creation material) Hammer Small anvil (Creation tool) Large anvil (Creation tool) Water Whetstone Pelt', '<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps\" title=\"Metal lumps\">Metal lumps</a> (Creation material)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">Hammer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_anvil\" title=\"Small anvil\">Small anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">Large anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Whetstone\" title=\"Whetstone\">Whetstone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelt</a></li></ul></dd></dl>', 1),
(18441, 897, 'Items', 'Items', 'See Category:Weapon heads smithing items', '<p>See <i><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Weapon_heads_smithing_items\" title=\"Category:Weapon heads smithing items\">Category:Weapon heads smithing items</a></i>\n</p>', 2),
(18442, 897, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing > Weapon smithing > Weapon heads smithing', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a> &gt; Weapon heads smithing</li></ul>', 3),
(18443, 897, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Hard Head at 50 skill Metal Head at 70 skill Head Smith at 90 skill Head Full of Dreams at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Hard Head at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Metal Head at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Head Smith at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Head Full of Dreams at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(18444, 3380, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long and slender sword.', '<p><i>A long and slender sword.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18445, 3380, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.275 (Slightly weaker than a sickle ) Attack Speed: 4 seconds Damage Type: Cutting and Piercing Parry Rate: High Wielding: One-hander', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.275 (Slightly weaker than a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 4 seconds</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting and Piercing</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: High</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18446, 3380, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Messer Goblinsbane Bastard long sword', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Messer</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Goblinsbane</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Bastard long sword</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18447, 3380, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'It is larger and slower than the short sword but faster and smaller than the two handed sword . It can be wielded in one hand and is better at parrying than other types of weapons such as mauls and axes . The QL of the handle plays a role in the success rate while crafting. A failed attempt will lower the quality level of the handle and damages the blade . Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20. The long sword uses the Longsword skill when used.', '<ul><li>It is larger and slower than the <a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">short sword</a> but faster and smaller than the <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">two handed sword</a>.</li>\n<li>It can be wielded in one hand and is better at parrying than other types of weapons such as <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Mauls\" title=\"Category:Mauls\">mauls</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Axes\" title=\"Category:Axes\">axes</a>.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Handle\" title=\"Handle\">handle</a> plays a role in the success rate while crafting. A failed attempt will lower the quality level of the handle and damages the <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword_blade\" title=\"Long sword blade\">blade</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20.</li>\n<li>The long sword uses the Longsword skill when used.</li></ul>', 3),
(18448, 3380, 'Skills & characteristics', 'Skills_.26_characteristics', 'When using a long sword Swords > Longsword Body > Body control When creating a long sword Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a long sword\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Swords\" title=\"Swords\">Swords</a> &gt; <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Longsword\" title=\"Longsword\">Longsword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a long sword\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(18449, 3380, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Long Swordsman at 50 skill Fighter at 70 skill Myrmidon at 90 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Long Swordsman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Fighter at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Myrmidon at 90 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(18456, 4481, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge spiked heavy clump of metal on a shaft. You\'ll need both hands free to wield this one.', '<p><i>A huge spiked heavy clump of metal on a shaft. You\'ll need both hands free to wield this one.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18457, 4481, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Skills: Mauls > Large maul Strength: 0.55 (Slightly weaker than a huge axe, but stronger than the two handed sword) Attack Speed: 6 seconds (5 in Aggressive Mode) Damage Type: Mauling Parry Rate: Medium Wielding: Two-hander (Unable to use a shield with it)', '<ul><li>Skills: <a href=\"/index.php/Mauls\" title=\"Mauls\">Mauls</a> &gt; Large maul</li>\n<li>Strength: 0.55 (Slightly weaker than a huge axe, but stronger than the two handed sword)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 6 seconds (5 in Aggressive Mode)</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Mauling</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Medium</li>\n<li>Wielding: Two-hander (Unable to use a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a> with it)</li></ul>', 1),
(18458, 4481, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Fiendish Large Maul', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Fiendish Large Maul</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18459, 4481, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The QL of the shaft affects the percentage chance of success. This weapon benefits greatly from Flaming aura enchants. Mauling damage is good vs armour units. Great at demolition as they are akin to what we know in real-life as a sledge hammer.', '<ul><li>The QL of the shaft affects the percentage chance of success.</li>\n<li>This weapon benefits greatly from <a href=\"/index.php/Flaming_aura\" title=\"Flaming aura\">Flaming aura</a> enchants.</li>\n<li>Mauling damage is good vs armour units.</li>\n<li>Great at demolition as they are akin to what we know in real-life as a sledge hammer.</li></ul>', 3),
(18460, 4481, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a large maul Mauls > Large maul Body > Body strength When creating a large maul Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a large maul\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mauls\" title=\"Mauls\">Mauls</a> &gt; Large maul</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a large maul \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18461, 4481, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Large Mauler at 50 skill Siegebreaker at 70 skill Hand of Magranon at 90 skill God/Godess of Thunder at 100 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Large Mauler at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Siegebreaker at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Hand of Magranon at 90 skill</li>\n<li>God/Godess of Thunder at 100 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(18462, 2319, 'Description', 'Description', 'A medium sized battle axe with a wooden shaft.', '<p><i>A medium sized battle axe with a wooden shaft.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18463, 2319, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.325 (Slightly stronger than a sickle) Attack Speed: 4 seconds Damage Type: Cutting Parry Rate: Low Wielding: One-hander', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.325 (Slightly stronger than a sickle)</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 4 seconds</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Low</li>\n<li>Wielding: One-hander</li></ul>', 1),
(18464, 2319, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Executioner', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Executioner</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18465, 2319, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20 woodcutting skill. After creation, the in-game item is referred to as \"Large axe.\" The skill used is also called Large axe in the in game skills box. Large axes deal cutting damage when used in battle. Large axes parry at 30% of the rate longswords do. Large axes are the fastest weapon in their class and do the least damage before armour modifiers. Large axes are used as a component of an axe trap .', '<ul><li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to skill the weapon up to 20 woodcutting skill.</li>\n<li>After creation, the in-game item is referred to as \"Large axe.\" The skill used is also called Large axe in the in game skills box.</li>\n<li>Large axes deal cutting damage when used in battle. Large axes parry at 30% of the rate longswords do. Large axes are the fastest weapon in their class and do the least damage before <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Armour\" title=\"Category:Armour\">armour</a> modifiers.</li>\n<li>Large axes are used as a component of an <a href=\"/index.php/Axe_trap\" title=\"Axe trap\">axe trap</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18466, 2319, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using an axe Axes > Large axe Body > Body strength When creating an axe Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using an axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Axes\" title=\"Axes\">Axes</a> &gt; Large axe</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating an axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(18467, 2319, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Large Axeman/woman at 50 skill Battleaxe at 70 skill Viking at 90 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Large Axeman/woman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Battleaxe at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Viking at 90 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(18468, 4181, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge axe with a heavy head and a wooden shaft. You\'ll need to wield it with both hands.', '<p><i>A huge axe with a heavy head and a wooden shaft. You\'ll need to wield it with both hands.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18469, 4181, 'Weapon Stats', 'Weapon_Stats', 'Strength: 0.60 Attack Speed: 6 seconds (10% faster in Aggressive Mode) Damage Type: Cutting Parry Rate: Low Wielding: Two-hander (Unable to use a shield with it)', '<ul><li>Strength: 0.60</li>\n<li>Attack Speed: 6 seconds (10% faster in Aggressive Mode)</li>\n<li>Damage Type: Cutting</li>\n<li>Parry Rate: Low</li>\n<li>Wielding: Two-hander (Unable to use a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shield\" title=\"Shield\">shield</a> with it)</li></ul>', 1),
(18470, 4181, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Bearded Huge Battle Axe Sigvard\'s Wrath', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Bearded Huge Battle Axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Loyalty_program\" title=\"Loyalty program\">Sigvard\'s Wrath</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18471, 4181, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This weapon is best used in the aggressive fighting stance. Can be used to chop trees/bushes to gain Huge axe skill from 1 to 20. Very effective in bashing down wooden house walls, wooden fence types, wooden mine doors, and any wood furniture.', '<ul><li>This weapon is best used in the <a href=\"/index.php/Aggressive_fighting\" title=\"Aggressive fighting\">aggressive fighting</a> stance.</li>\n<li>Can be used to chop trees/bushes to gain Huge axe skill from 1 to 20.</li>\n<li>Very effective in bashing down wooden house walls, wooden fence types, wooden mine doors, and any wood furniture.</li></ul>', 3),
(18472, 4181, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a huge axe Axes > Huge axe When creating a huge axe Smithing > Weapon smithing', '<p>When using a huge axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Axes\" title=\"Axes\">Axes</a> &gt; Huge axe</li></ul>\n<p>When creating a huge axe\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(18473, 4181, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Huge Axeman at 50 skill Headsman at 70 skill Axecutioner at 90 skill Legendary Decapitator at 100 skill .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center} Weapons: Short sword - Long sword - Two handed sword Small axe - Large Axe - Huge axe Small maul - Medium maul - Large maul Long spear - Spear - Staff (wooden) - Staff (metal) - Halberd Sickle - Scythe - Huge shod club', '<ul><li>Huge Axeman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Headsman at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Axecutioner at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Legendary Decapitator at 100 skill</li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120394\">.mw-parser-output .weaponlistbox{border-color:#000;text-align:center}</style>\n<div class=\"plainlist boxstyle weaponlistbox\"><b>Weapons:</b><br/>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">Short sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">Long sword</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_axe\" title=\"Small axe\">Small axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Large_Axe\" title=\"Large Axe\">Large Axe</a>\n- <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Huge axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_maul\" title=\"Small maul\">Small maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">Large maul</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Long_spear\" title=\"Long spear\">Long spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Spear\" title=\"Spear\">Spear</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(wooden)\" title=\"Staff (wooden)\">Staff (wooden)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Staff_(metal)\" title=\"Staff (metal)\">Staff (metal)</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Halberd\" title=\"Halberd\">Halberd</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">Sickle</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">Scythe</a>\n- <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_shod_club\" title=\"Huge shod club\">Huge shod club</a></li></ul></div>', 5),
(18474, 4617, 'Description', 'Description', 'The heavy spiked metal head for a maul.', '<p><i>The heavy spiked metal head for a maul.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18475, 4617, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a Medium maul when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_maul\" title=\"Medium maul\">Medium maul</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18476, 1010, 'Description', 'Description', 'The thick, heavy, spiked metal head for a maul. Large maul head is used for making an metal large maul .', '<p><i>The thick, heavy, spiked metal head for a maul.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Large maul head</b> is used for making an metal <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">large maul</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18480, 4298, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge axe head.', '<p><i>A huge axe head.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18481, 4298, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a huge axe when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_axe\" title=\"Huge axe\">huge axe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18482, 2388, 'Description', 'Description', 'The thick metal head for a hammer.', '<p><i>The thick metal head for a hammer.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18483, 2388, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a hammer when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18484, 2388, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be improved.', '<ul><li>Can be improved.</li></ul>', 2),
(18485, 3376, 'Description', 'Description', 'A blade for a longsword.', '<p><i>A blade for a longsword.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18486, 3376, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a long sword when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Long_sword\" title=\"Long sword\">long sword</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18487, 2530, 'Description', 'Description', 'Blade smithing is a sub-skill of weapon smithing that relates specifically to creating knives, swords , and other blades using a forge , hammer , anvil , and other smithing tools.', '<p>Blade smithing is a sub-skill of <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">weapon smithing</a> that relates specifically to creating knives, <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Swords\" title=\"Category:Swords\">swords</a>, and other blades using a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">anvil</a>, and other smithing tools.\n</p>', 0),
(18488, 2530, 'Tools Used', 'Tools_Used', 'Metal lumps , usually iron lump (Creation material) Hammer Small anvil (Creation tool) Large anvil (Creation tool) Water Whetstone Pelt', '<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps\" title=\"Metal lumps\">Metal lumps</a>, usually <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">iron lump</a> (Creation material)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">Hammer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_anvil\" title=\"Small anvil\">Small anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">Large anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Whetstone\" title=\"Whetstone\">Whetstone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelt</a></li></ul></dd></dl>', 1),
(18489, 2530, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing > Weapon smithing > Blades smithing Body > Body strength Body > Body control', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a> &gt; Blades smithing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18490, 2530, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Bladesmith at 50 skill Renowned Bladesmith at 70 skill Master Bladesmith at 90 skill Cutting Edge at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Bladesmith at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Renowned Bladesmith at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Bladesmith at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Cutting Edge at 100 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18491, 2530, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Blades smithing items Smithing Armour smithing Chain armour smithing Plate armour smithing Shield smithing Blacksmithing Jewelry smithing Locksmithing Metallurgy Weapon smithing Blades smithing Weapon heads smithing', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Blades_smithing_items\" title=\"Category:Blades smithing items\">Category:Blades smithing items</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour_smithing\" title=\"Armour smithing\">Armour smithing</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour_smithing\" title=\"Chain armour smithing\">Chain armour smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour_smithing\" title=\"Plate armour smithing\">Plate armour smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Shield_smithing\" title=\"Shield smithing\">Shield smithing</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">Blacksmithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">Jewelry smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Locksmithing\" title=\"Locksmithing\">Locksmithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Metallurgy\" title=\"Metallurgy\">Metallurgy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_smithing\" title=\"Weapon smithing\">Weapon smithing</a>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Blades smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_heads_smithing\" title=\"Weapon heads smithing\">Weapon heads smithing</a></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>', 4),
(18492, 2464, 'Description', 'Description', 'A blade for a shortsword.', '<p><i>A blade for a shortsword.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18493, 2464, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a short sword when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Short_sword\" title=\"Short sword\">short sword</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18494, 4639, 'Description', 'Description', 'A blade for a giant sword. A huge sword blade is used for creating a two handed sword .', '<p><i>A blade for a giant sword.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>huge sword blade</b> is used for creating a <a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">two handed sword</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18495, 4755, 'Description', 'Description', 'A very short and very sharp curved blade.', '<p><i>A very short and very sharp curved blade.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18496, 4755, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a leather knife when attached to a wooden handle .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Leather_knife\" title=\"Leather knife\">leather knife</a> when attached to a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wooden_handle\" title=\"Wooden handle\">wooden handle</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18497, 4416, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin blade for a rake.', '<p><i>A thin blade for a rake.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18498, 4416, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a rake when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Rake\" title=\"Rake\">rake</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18499, 4416, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Maximum creation QL is 1/5 blacksmithing skill.', '<ul><li>Maximum creation <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">QL</a> is 1/5 <a href=\"/index.php/Blacksmithing\" title=\"Blacksmithing\">blacksmithing</a> skill.</li></ul>', 2),
(18500, 4183, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin long blade for a scythe.', '<p><i>A thin long blade for a scythe.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18501, 4183, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a scythe when attached to a shaft . Used in the construction of a scythe trap .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in the construction of a <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe_trap\" title=\"Scythe trap\">scythe trap</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18502, 3682, 'Description', 'Description', 'A straight rugged metal blade. File blades are used to create an iron file with a wooden handle .', '<p><i>A straight rugged metal blade.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>File blades</b> are used to create an iron <a href=\"/index.php/File\" title=\"File\">file</a> with a wooden <a href=\"/index.php/Handle\" title=\"Handle\">handle</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18503, 4760, 'Description', 'Description', 'One half of a scissors.', '<p><i>One half of a scissors.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18504, 4760, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Two scissor blades are used to create a scissors .', '<p>Two <b>scissor blades</b> are used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Scissors\" title=\"Scissors\">scissors</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(18505, 4212, 'Description', 'Description', 'The black bear looks pretty kind, but has strong, highly curved claws ready to render you to pieces.', '<p><i>The black bear looks pretty kind, but has strong, highly curved claws ready to render you to pieces.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18506, 4212, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Black bear is a fierce animal to new players, but less so than its cousin brown bear . It can be killed by a well-equipped player without much fighting skill. It can be tamed with meat or fish . 20+ taming skill recommended. It is pretty rare and occasionally spawns in mines and from bear caves. It cannot swim.', '<ul><li><b>Black bear</b> is a fierce <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animal</a> to new players, but less so than its cousin <a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">brown bear</a>. It can be killed by a well-equipped player without much <a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">fighting</a> skill.</li>\n<li>It can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Meat\" title=\"Meat\">meat</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a>. 20+ taming skill recommended.</li>\n<li>It is pretty rare and occasionally spawns in mines and from bear caves.</li>\n<li>It cannot swim.</li></ul>', 1),
(18509, 2867, 'Description', 'Description', 'The brown bear has a distinctive hump on the shoulders, and long deadly claws on the front paws.', '<p><i>The brown bear has a distinctive hump on the shoulders, and long deadly claws on the front paws.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18510, 2867, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Brown bears are dangerous animals , slightly stronger than its black bear cousin. Do not try to run away from it into the water, because this bear can swim. It can be tamed with meat or fish (15+ taming skill recommended). Since brown bears can swim, one in the water is sometimes referred to as a Bearshark. Brown bears can only be hitched up to the last Aged stage . However, they can only be hitched if they are tamed. If they age and become unruly while hitched they will unhitch themselves. Brown bears can be used as a mount when tamed, if the player has a body control of 23 or higher. Brown bears seem to deal Bruise and Bite wounds, i.e Blunt and Bite damage.', '<ul><li>Brown bears are dangerous <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animals</a>, slightly stronger than its <a href=\"/index.php/Black_bear\" title=\"Black bear\">black bear</a> cousin.</li>\n<li>Do not try to run away from it into the water, because this bear can swim.</li>\n<li>It can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">tamed</a> with meat or fish (15+ taming skill recommended).</li>\n<li>Since brown bears can swim, one in the water is sometimes referred to as a Bearshark.</li>\n<li>Brown bears can only be hitched up to the <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">last Aged stage</a>. However, they can only be hitched if they are tamed. If they age and become unruly while hitched they will unhitch themselves.</li>\n<li>Brown bears can be used as a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mount\" title=\"Mount\">mount</a> when tamed, if the player has a <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">body control</a> of 23 or higher.</li>\n<li>Brown bears seem to deal Bruise and Bite wounds, i.e Blunt and Bite damage.</li></ul>', 1),
(18513, 4220, 'Description', 'Description', 'With an almost sad look upon its face, this filthy giant might be mistaken for a harmless huge baby. The Forest Giant is a unique creature that roams the forests of Wurm. The Forest Giant is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying. The Forest Giant is easily recognized due to its massive size and antlers. When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Forest Giant blood with source salt will create a Potion of woodcutting . Abilities The Forest Giant cannot swim. Cannot be tamed. The Forest Giant wields a 65ql huge club. The Forest Giant can pick up and throw players. The Forest Giant, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in it\'s path. Slaying the Forest Giant will give the title \" Giantslayer \".', '<p><i>With an almost sad look upon its face, this filthy giant might be mistaken for a harmless huge baby.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe Forest Giant is a unique creature that roams the forests of Wurm. The Forest Giant is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying. The Forest Giant is easily recognized due to its massive size and antlers. \n</p>\n<p>When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Forest Giant <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a> will create a <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_woodcutting\" title=\"Potion of woodcutting\">Potion of woodcutting</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Abilities\">Abilities</span></h3>\n<ul><li>The Forest Giant cannot swim.</li>\n<li>Cannot be tamed.</li>\n<li>The Forest Giant wields a 65ql huge club.</li>\n<li>The Forest Giant can pick up and throw players.</li>\n<li>The Forest Giant, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in it\'s path.</li>\n<li>Slaying the Forest Giant will give the title \"<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Giantslayer\" title=\"Giantslayer\">Giantslayer</a>\".</li></ul>', 0),
(18514, 4220, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot spawn on deeds.', '<ul><li>Cannot spawn on deeds.</li></ul>', 1),
(18515, 4219, 'Description', 'Description', 'Always on the brink of cackling wildly, this creature is possibly insane. The Goblin Leader is a unique creature that has a large group of goblins following him. The Goblin Leader is armed with a Short Sword and a Medium Metal Shield that it will use for attacking and parrying. When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Goblin Leader blood with source salt will create a potion of mining .', '<p><i>Always on the brink of cackling wildly, this creature is possibly insane.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe Goblin Leader is a unique creature that has a large group of <a href=\"/index.php/Goblin\" title=\"Goblin\">goblins</a> following him. The Goblin Leader is armed with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Short_Sword\" title=\"Short Sword\">Short Sword</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Medium_metal_shield\" title=\"Medium metal shield\">Medium Metal Shield</a> that it will use for attacking and parrying.\n</p>\n<p>When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Goblin Leader <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a> will create a <a href=\"/index.php/Potion_of_mining\" title=\"Potion of mining\">potion of mining</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18516, 4219, 'Abilities', 'Abilities', 'The Goblin Leader can swim. Cannot be tamed. The goblin carries a 45QL Short Sword and Medium Metal Shield. The Goblin Leader, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in its path. Slaying the Goblin Leader will give the title \" Fearless \".', '<ul><li>The Goblin Leader can swim.</li>\n<li>Cannot be tamed.</li>\n<li>The goblin carries a 45QL Short Sword and Medium Metal Shield.</li>\n<li>The Goblin Leader, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in its path.</li>\n<li>Slaying the Goblin Leader will give the title \"<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fearless\" title=\"Fearless\">Fearless</a>\".</li></ul>', 1),
(18517, 4219, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Drops Goblin_war_bonnet upon death. Cannot spawn on deeds.', '<ul><li>Drops <a href=\"/index.php/Goblin_war_bonnet\" title=\"Goblin war bonnet\">Goblin_war_bonnet</a> upon death.</li>\n<li>Cannot spawn on deeds.</li></ul>', 2),
(18518, 4362, 'Description', 'Description', 'Monstrously huge and fast, these spiders love to be played with. Huge spiders are dangerous, aggressive creatures with eight legs and an appetite for players .', '<p><i>Monstrously huge and fast, these spiders love to be played with.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Huge spiders are dangerous, aggressive <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a> with eight legs and an appetite for <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">players</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18519, 4362, 'Notes', 'Notes', '25 fighting skill with at least full studded leather armour and 30 QL weapons recommended. Aged spiders run as fast as a player with no load. Younger and older spiders are slower. All spiders are known to pursue players for quite a distance.', '<ul><li>25 <a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">fighting</a> skill with at least full studded leather armour and 30 QL weapons recommended.</li>\n<li>Aged spiders run as fast as a player with no load. Younger and older spiders are slower.</li>\n<li>All spiders are known to pursue players for quite a distance.</li></ul>', 1),
(18520, 4362, 'Fighting Tips', 'Fighting_Tips', 'Spiders, like all other animals, become stronger and bigger as they age. A young spider is weak, and does not aim well for the head. Older spiders are strong, cause a lot of damage per hit, and will aim for the head. They also focus with more success. They cannot chase you into water.', '<ul><li>Spiders, like all other animals, become stronger and bigger as they age.</li>\n<li>A young spider is weak, and does not aim well for the head.</li>\n<li>Older spiders are strong, cause a lot of damage per hit, and will aim for the head. They also focus with more success.</li>\n<li>They cannot chase you into water.</li></ul>', 2),
(18521, 4362, 'Phobia', 'Phobia', 'Spider graphics can be turned into blobs for those suffering from arachnophobia. To change this enable Phobia Mode in the advanced graphics tab before entering Wurm.', '<p>Spider graphics can be turned into blobs for those suffering from arachnophobia. To change this enable Phobia Mode in the advanced graphics tab before entering Wurm.\n</p>', 3),
(18524, 1216, 'Description', 'Description', 'This normally calm mountain gorilla may suddenly become a very fierce and dangerous foe if annoyed.', '<p><i>This normally calm mountain gorilla may suddenly become a very fierce and dangerous foe if annoyed.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18525, 1216, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Strength around a wild boar . Bashing attack. About 40 fighting skill with good armour recommended to take one solo. Expect some minor wounds. It is the religion animal of Magranon and will spawn near Holy sites of Magranon. It also spawns inside Mol-Rehan kingdoms on PvP . It will attack members of any kingdom other than the one it spawns in. Spirit guards of PMK\'s will attack them. Mountain gorillas spawn on Jackal as well.', '<ul><li>Strength around a <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_boar\" title=\"Wild boar\">wild boar</a>.</li>\n<li>Bashing attack.</li>\n<li>About 40 fighting skill with good armour recommended to take one solo. Expect some minor wounds.</li>\n<li>It is the religion animal of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> and will spawn near <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Holy_site\" title=\"Holy site\">Holy sites</a> of Magranon. It also spawns inside <a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a> kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. It will attack members of any kingdom other than the one it spawns in.</li>\n<li>Spirit guards of PMK\'s will attack them.</li>\n<li>Mountain gorillas spawn on <a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal</a> as well.</li></ul>', 1),
(18526, 4209, 'Description', 'Description', 'A hyena that has been infected with rabies.', '<p><i>A hyena that has been infected with rabies.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18527, 4209, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Non-aggressive except towards whitelight kingdoms on PVP servers. Despite the rabid descriptor, it doesn\'t give any kind of poison damage (You won\'t get rabies). Stronger than a wild boar . Slashing attack. 20 - 30 fight skill with full body armour recommended. You need 24 body control to ride zombie hyena', '<ul><li>Non-aggressive except towards whitelight kingdoms on PVP servers.</li>\n<li>Despite the rabid descriptor, it doesn\'t give any kind of poison damage (You won\'t get rabies).</li>\n<li>Stronger than a <a href=\"/index.php/Wild_boar\" title=\"Wild boar\">wild boar</a>.</li>\n<li>Slashing attack.</li>\n<li>20 - 30 fight skill with full body armour recommended.</li>\n<li>You need 24 body control to ride zombie hyena</li></ul>', 1),
(18530, 4218, 'Description', 'Description', 'This troll has a scary clever look in his eyes. He surely knows what he is doing. The Troll King is a unique creature that leads a large group of trolls around.', '<p><i>This troll has a scary clever look in his eyes. He surely knows what he is doing.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe Troll King is a unique creature that leads a large group of trolls around. \n</p>', 0),
(18531, 4218, 'Abilities', 'Abilities', 'It is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying. The Troll King is followed by a group of trolls. The Troll King, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in it\'s path.', '<ul><li>It is armed with a 65ql Huge Club that it will use for attacking and parrying.</li>\n<li>The Troll King is followed by a group of trolls.</li>\n<li>The Troll King, like any other unique, will break any wall or fence in it\'s path.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18532, 4218, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The Troll King and its followers are difficult to kill and very dangerous if encountered alone. It has a crown made out of a cow\'s head. When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Troll King blood with source salt will create a Ointment of Stone Cutting . It will also drop a Crown of the troll king upon death. *Slaying the Troll King will give the title \" Trollslayer \". Cannot spawn on deeds.', '<ul><li>The Troll King and its followers are difficult to kill and very dangerous if encountered alone.</li>\n<li>It has a crown made out of a cow\'s head.</li>\n<li>When slain, every premium player in local will receive blood. Mixing Troll King <a href=\"/index.php/Blood\" title=\"Blood\">blood</a> with <a href=\"/index.php/Source_salt\" title=\"Source salt\">source salt</a> will create a <a href=\"/index.php/Ointment_of_stonecutting\" title=\"Ointment of stonecutting\">Ointment of Stone Cutting</a>. It will also drop a <a href=\"/index.php/Crown_of_the_troll_king\" title=\"Crown of the troll king\">Crown of the troll king</a> upon death.</li>\n<li>*Slaying the Troll King will give the title \"<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trollslayer\" title=\"Trollslayer\">Trollslayer</a>\".</li>\n<li>Cannot spawn on deeds.</li></ul>', 2),
(18583, 1245, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lava tile comes from lava eruptions, which are extremely rare natural events and happen only on rock tiles , or when created by a follower of the Path of Power . Lava flows downhill, and its path can be changed by terraforming in front of it. Lava is the most dangerous tile in Wurm . It has the potential to kill in seconds if stood on it. Stay away or expect damage and potential loss of items and corpses !', '<p>A <b>lava</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> comes from lava eruptions, which are extremely rare natural events and happen only on <a href=\"/index.php/Rock_tile\" title=\"Rock tile\">rock tiles</a>, or when created by a follower of the <a href=\"/index.php/Path_of_Power\" title=\"Path of Power\">Path of Power</a>. Lava flows downhill, and its path can be changed by <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">terraforming</a> in front of it.\n</p>\n<p>Lava is the most dangerous tile in <a href=\"/index.php/Basic_Knowledge\" title=\"Basic Knowledge\">Wurm</a>. It has the potential to <a href=\"/index.php/Death\" title=\"Death\">kill</a> in seconds if stood on it. Stay away or expect <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> and potential loss of items and <a href=\"/index.php/Corpse\" title=\"Corpse\">corpses</a>!\n</p>', 0),
(18584, 1245, 'Erupt', 'Erupt', 'Follower of Path of Power level 7 receive the ability to erupt lava tiles and freeze back to rock tiles. Erupting a tile changes the rock tile to lava, and the rock/ore wall directly underneath into a lava wall. Freezing the above-ground lava tile will also freeze the lava wall beneath, changing it to rock, even if it was previously an ore tile. You can erupt stone tiles that are fully submerged in water. Cannot erupt on non-allied deed. When trying, you will see the message: Some psychological issue stops you from spawning lava here. An erupted tile\'s northwest corner might become slightly raised by 4 slopes if that said corner isn\'t too high compared to the rest of the tiles corners. (Exact slope unknown  but won\'t function at 150) Erupt cannot be used on a tile next to a cave entrance, above an empty mine tile, or above a reinforced mine wall. Trying to do so will initially tell you \"You start concentrating on the rock.\", but end up with \"Nothing happens\" - and this will not consume your daily usage of Erupt Nearby items such as altars and vehicles may prevent Erupt from working. Erupting requires that the tile is not in the domain of any god that isn\'t Magranon. In other words, it needs to be within Magranon\'s domain or no domain at all. A lava tile cannot be created on tiles adjacent to a settlement token.', '<ul><li>Follower of <a href=\"/index.php/Path_of_Power\" title=\"Path of Power\">Path of Power</a> level 7 receive the ability to erupt lava tiles and freeze back to rock tiles.</li>\n<li>Erupting a tile changes the rock tile to lava, and the rock/ore wall directly underneath into a lava wall. Freezing the above-ground lava tile will also freeze the lava wall beneath, changing it to rock, even if it was previously an ore tile.</li>\n<li>You can erupt stone tiles that are fully submerged in water.</li>\n<li>Cannot erupt on non-allied deed. When trying, you will see the message: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> Some psychological issue stops you from spawning lava here. </span></li>\n<li>An erupted tile\'s northwest corner might become slightly raised by 4 slopes if that said corner isn\'t too high compared to the rest of the tiles corners. (Exact slope unknown  but won\'t function at 150)</li>\n<li>Erupt cannot be used on a tile next to a cave entrance, above an empty mine tile, or above a reinforced mine wall. Trying to do so will initially tell you \"You start concentrating on the rock.\", but end up with \"Nothing happens\" - and this will not consume your daily usage of Erupt</li>\n<li>Nearby items such as altars and vehicles may prevent Erupt from working.</li>\n<li>Erupting requires that the tile is not in the domain of any god that isn\'t Magranon. In other words, it needs to be within Magranon\'s domain or no domain at all.</li>\n<li>A lava tile cannot be created on tiles adjacent to a settlement token.</li></ul>', 1),
(18585, 1245, 'Damage from lava', 'Damage_from_lava', 'Lava will rapidly cause major fire damage wounds to any creature standing on it. The Path of Power ability \"Elemental Immunity\" will prevent this damage if active, as with other elemental damage. Priests of Magranon with 35 faith receive the ability to walk on lava tiles without taking damage. Lava tiles cause damage to items left on top of them. All items take 1.00 damage approximately every 15 minutes. Items inside containers on the tile will not take damage, unless the container is destroyed and spills the items directly onto the lava. Lava tiles cause damage to fences on their northern and western tile borders, taking 1 damage approximately every second. Lava walls in caves are not harmful if touched. Hitched animals may still take damage by clipping through the lava wall and onto the tile. Animals lead over lava will take damage rapidly.', '<ul><li>Lava will rapidly cause major fire damage wounds to any creature standing on it.\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/index.php/Path_of_Power\" title=\"Path of Power\">Path of Power</a> ability \"Elemental Immunity\" will prevent this damage if active, as with other elemental damage.</li>\n<li>Priests of <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> with 35 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> receive the ability to walk on lava tiles without taking damage.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Lava tiles cause damage to items left on top of them.\n<ul><li>All items take 1.00 damage approximately every 15 minutes.</li>\n<li>Items inside containers on the tile will not take damage, unless the container is destroyed and spills the items directly onto the lava.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Lava tiles cause damage to fences on their northern and western tile borders, taking 1 damage approximately every second.</li>\n<li>Lava walls in caves are not harmful if touched.\n<ul><li>Hitched animals may still take damage by clipping through the lava wall and onto the tile.</li>\n<li>Animals lead over lava will take damage rapidly.</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(18586, 1245, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Lava fiends and lava spiders spawn on lava tiles. Over time, lava can freeze naturally, but has a smaller chance to spread to neighboring tiles instead. Spreading lava may affect non-rock tiles such as dirt, grass, bushes or even paved tiles, changing them to lava as well. When this lava freezes, the tile will become rock, effectively raising the rock layer on that tile. Enchanted trees will live forever and therefore block the lava spread forever. When spreading to nearby tiles, lava will only become a lava column beneath these tiles if the tile is not already mined out. Lava tiles consume anything on their north and west tile borders. Lava walls in caves act like solid walls and you cannot pass through them. Also, if you try to mine the wall it will give the message The rock is too hard to mine. The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on Lava tiles: Rubble', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lava_fiend\" title=\"Lava fiend\">Lava fiends</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Lava_spider\" title=\"Lava spider\">lava spiders</a> spawn on lava tiles.</li>\n<li>Over time, lava can freeze naturally, but has a smaller chance to spread to neighboring tiles instead.\n<ul><li>Spreading lava may affect non-rock tiles such as dirt, grass, bushes or even paved tiles, changing them to lava as well. When this lava freezes, the tile will become rock, effectively raising the rock layer on that tile.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Enchanted trees will live forever and therefore block the lava spread forever.</li>\n<li>When spreading to nearby tiles, lava will only become a lava column beneath these tiles if the tile is not already mined out.</li>\n<li>Lava tiles consume anything on their north and west tile borders.</li>\n<li>Lava walls in caves act like solid walls and you cannot pass through them. Also, if you try to mine the wall it will give the message <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> The rock is too hard to mine. </span></li>\n<li>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on Lava tiles: <a href=\"/index.php/Rubble\" title=\"Rubble\">Rubble</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18599, 1130, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wooden palisade gate is a gate made out of wood which can be locked with a gate lock . Palisade gates are stronger than wooden fence gates . The gate displays a plaque with the motto from the deed if on deeded land.', '<p>A <b>wooden palisade gate</b> is a gate made out of <a href=\"/index.php/Wood\" title=\"Wood\">wood</a> which can be locked with a <a href=\"/index.php/Gate_lock\" title=\"Gate lock\">gate lock</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Palisade gates are stronger than <a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_fence_gate\" title=\"Wooden fence gate\">wooden fence gates</a>.\n</p>\n<p>The gate displays a plaque with the motto from the deed if on deeded land.\n</p>', 0),
(18600, 1130, 'Skill Required', 'Skill_Required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(18601, 1130, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Palisade', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Palisade\" title=\"Palisade\">Palisade</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18602, 4234, 'Description', 'Description', 'A ring to put on your finger.', '<p><i>A ring to put on your finger.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18603, 4234, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Commonly made to improve jewelry smithing as it only requires below 0.01kg lump to improve per attempt. Used for sacrificing at an altar to boost favor quickly as a priest. Can be enchanted with the Nolocate spell. Moon metal rings (seryll, glimmersteel, adamantine) appear more vibrant in the dark (With a slight glow to the model). Seryll rings are commonly used to practice channeling because of seryll\'s shatter resistance Moon metal glow Adamantine ring Seryll ring Gold ring Silver ring', '<ul><li>Commonly made to improve <a href=\"/index.php/Jewelry_smithing\" title=\"Jewelry smithing\">jewelry smithing</a> as it only requires below 0.01kg lump to improve per attempt.</li>\n<li>Used for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sacrificing\" title=\"Sacrificing\">sacrificing</a> at an <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altar</a> to boost favor quickly as a priest.</li>\n<li>Can be enchanted with the <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a> spell.</li>\n<li>Moon metal rings (seryll, glimmersteel, adamantine) appear more vibrant in the dark (With a slight glow to the model).</li>\n<li>Seryll rings are commonly used to practice channeling because of seryll\'s shatter resistance</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\" style=\"max-width: 972px;_width: 972px;\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Moonmetalglow.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/87/Moonmetalglow.png/200px-Moonmetalglow.png\" srcset=\"/images/8/87/Moonmetalglow.png 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Moon metal glow\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:AdamantineRing.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/5/53/AdamantineRing.png/200px-AdamantineRing.png\" srcset=\"/images/5/53/AdamantineRing.png 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Adamantine ring\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Seryllring.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/3f/Seryllring.png/200px-Seryllring.png\" srcset=\"/images/3/3f/Seryllring.png 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Seryll ring\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Goldring.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/2b/Goldring.png/200px-Goldring.png\" srcset=\"/images/2/2b/Goldring.png 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Gold ring\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 235px\"><div style=\"width: 235px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 230px;\"><div style=\"margin:21.5px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Silverring.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"274\" data-file-width=\"293\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"187\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/36/Silverring.png/200px-Silverring.png\" srcset=\"/images/3/36/Silverring.png 1.5x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Silver ring\n</p>\n</div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 1),
(18614, 1918, 'Valley Of The Cursed Souls', 'Valley_Of_The_Cursed_Souls', '\"Oderint Dum Metuant.\" The Valley Of The Cursed Souls is a long standing Black Light town, loyal only to the goddess Libila and the combined effort to spread the control of the Horde of the Summoned over the wild . VCS established itself in the last map of beta with original founders Bismark And Malvado (a), some of its notable members were: Kai , Inacron , Erry, MalusSciurus , Fusspawn , Heven , Zeno and Riotz . The town has made the transition into gold with a few of the older core members still present. VCS was settled on the wild on the day of Sleep in week 1 of the starfall of Diamonds in the year 1000 by Arioch ( Fusspawn ) and Zeno . Since then Zeno has become full time patriarch and the town has continued to prosper well into gold. Any formal alliances or requests can be made to Zeno or any of the Elders, contact us in-game or on our IRC channel #VCS on irc.heavenlyplace.net (6667)', '<p>\"Oderint Dum Metuant.\"\n</p>\n<p><img alt=\"vcs1uy1.jpg\" src=\"http://img402.imageshack.us/img402/9246/vcs1uy1.jpg\"/>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nThe Valley Of The Cursed Souls is a long standing <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Black_Light\" title=\"Black Light\">Black Light</a> town, loyal only to the goddess <a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a> and the combined effort to spread the control of the <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a> over the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wild\" title=\"Wild\">wild</a>. VCS established itself in the last map of beta with original founders Bismark And Malvado (a), some of its notable members were: <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Kai\" title=\"Player:Kai\">Kai</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Inacron\" title=\"Player:Inacron\">Inacron</a>, Erry, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:MalusSciurus\" title=\"Player:MalusSciurus\">MalusSciurus</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fusspawn\" title=\"Player:Fusspawn\">Fusspawn</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Heven\" title=\"Player:Heven\">Heven</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeno\" title=\"Player:Zeno\">Zeno</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Riotz\" title=\"Player:Riotz\">Riotz</a>. The town has made the transition into gold with a few of the older core members still present.\n</p>\n<p>VCS was settled on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wild\" title=\"Wild\">wild</a> on the day of Sleep in week 1 of the starfall of Diamonds in the year 1000 by Arioch (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fusspawn\" title=\"Player:Fusspawn\">Fusspawn</a>) and <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeno\" title=\"Player:Zeno\">Zeno</a>. Since then <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeno\" title=\"Player:Zeno\">Zeno</a> has become full time patriarch and the town has continued to prosper well into gold.\n</p>\n<p>Any formal alliances or requests can be made to <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeno\" title=\"Player:Zeno\">Zeno</a> or any of the Elders, contact us in-game or on our IRC channel #VCS on irc.heavenlyplace.net (6667)\n</p>', 0),
(18615, 1918, 'Members', 'Members', 'Patriach Zeno Elders Riotz At0m Leve`Dara Citizens Benj Eddy NetEcho Arioch Inactive Citizens Fusspawn Rapty Opensource Yarrick Heven', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Patriach\">Patriach</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Zeno\" title=\"Player:Zeno\">Zeno</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elders\">Elders</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Riotz\" title=\"Player:Riotz\">Riotz</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:At0m\" title=\"Player:At0m\">At0m</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Levedara\" title=\"Player:Levedara\">Leve`Dara</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Benj\" title=\"Player:Benj\">Benj</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Eddy\" title=\"Player:Eddy\">Eddy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:NetEcho\" title=\"Player:NetEcho\">NetEcho</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Arioch\" title=\"Player:Arioch\">Arioch</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inactive_Citizens\">Inactive Citizens</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Fusspawn\" title=\"Player:Fusspawn\">Fusspawn</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Rapty\" title=\"Player:Rapty\">Rapty</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Opensource\" title=\"Player:Opensource\">Opensource</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Yarrick\" title=\"Player:Yarrick\">Yarrick</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Player:Heven\" title=\"Player:Heven\">Heven</a></li></ul>', 1),
(18616, 1918, 'Formal Alliances', 'Formal_Alliances', 'Cruorem Plaguewind Spire Candy Mountain Outpost', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cruorem\" title=\"Cruorem\">Cruorem</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plaguewind_Spire\" title=\"Plaguewind Spire\">Plaguewind Spire</a></li>\n<li>Candy Mountain Outpost</li></ul>', 2),
(18617, 4791, '061228', '061228', 'A bug with deeding the altars fixed. When the server crashes uncontrolled or must be hard booted you will now receive max sleep bonus (5 hours). A bug where artifacts were hidden in the rock in sloping environments fixed. Spyglasses are now nodrop so you will keep them when you die.', '<ul><li><i>A bug with deeding the altars fixed.</i></li>\n<li>When the server crashes uncontrolled or must be hard booted you will now receive max sleep bonus (5 hours).</li>\n<li><i>A bug where artifacts were hidden in the rock in sloping environments fixed.</i></li>\n<li>Spyglasses are now nodrop so you will keep them when you die.</li></ul>', 0),
(18618, 4791, '061223', '061223', 'A security hole was fixed. Outside items will now cool five times faster.', '<ul><li><i>A security hole was fixed.</i></li>\n<li>Outside items will now cool five times faster.</li></ul>', 1),
(18619, 4791, '061221', '061221', 'You will now be able to attack non-players at will again. The bug where you were teleported when sliding or climbing is temporarily fixed.', '<ul><li>You will now be able to attack non-players at will again.</li>\n<li><i>The bug where you were teleported when sliding or climbing is temporarily fixed.</i></li></ul>', 2),
(18620, 4791, '061220', '061220', 'Make sure to visit Santa Claus between the 24th-26th swedish time if you are a premium player. You may no longer attack people on the home server unless you have 20.5 body and soul strength. If this does not work well we will change it. The bug that disbanded Newtown and The Shroud was fixed. Two types of accounts now run the risk of being deleted: 1) Player accounts older than a week that never logged on. 2) Player accounts with three months of inactivitity and less than a days playing time. No accounts that is or has been premium will be deleted. It is virtually impossible to speed-cheat in Wurm now since the second part of the movementchecker has been fixed. Huge eggs may now be cracked open when the shell is thin enough. The woodtype bug is fixed.', '<ul><li>Make sure to visit Santa Claus between the 24th-26th swedish time if you are a premium player.</li>\n<li><i>You may no longer attack people on the home server unless you have 20.5 body and soul strength. If this does not work well we will change it.</i></li>\n<li>The bug that disbanded Newtown and The Shroud was fixed.</li>\n<li><i>Two types of accounts now run the risk of being deleted:</i></li></ul>\n<p><i>1) Player accounts older than a week that never logged on.</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>2) Player accounts with three months of inactivitity and less than a days playing time.</i>\n</p>\n<p><i>No accounts that is or has been premium will be deleted.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>It is virtually impossible to speed-cheat in Wurm now since the second part of the movementchecker has been fixed.</li>\n<li><i>Huge eggs may now be cracked open when the shell is thin enough.</i></li>\n<li>The woodtype bug is fixed.</li></ul>', 3),
(18621, 4791, '061213', '061213', 'Bug/exploit where you could give your personal merchant more items than supposed to fixed. The rendering bug should be gone for most people. Creatures now swim and rafts float. You should now be able to withdraw money even if your bank account is being transferred. Due to the amount of items tilling up the database decay damage now has a minimum value of 0.5 damage.', '<ul><li><i>Bug/exploit where you could give your personal merchant more items than supposed to fixed.</i></li>\n<li>The rendering bug should be gone for most people.</li>\n<li><i>Creatures now swim and rafts float.</i></li>\n<li>You should now be able to withdraw money even if your bank account is being transferred.</li>\n<li><i>Due to the amount of items tilling up the database decay damage now has a minimum value of 0.5 damage.</i></li></ul>', 4),
(18622, 4791, '061212', '061212', 'It items don\'t show on the ground, walk away maybe 5-20 or more tiles and return or try turning off culling in the client. The price of bow strings has slumped due to loss of demand. A bug with decay fixed.', '<ul><li><i>It items don\'t show on the ground, walk away maybe 5-20 or more tiles and return or try turning off culling in the client.</i></li>\n<li>The price of bow strings has slumped due to loss of demand.</li>\n<li><i>A bug with decay fixed.</i></li></ul>', 5),
(18623, 4791, '061207', '061207', 'The bug with temperature always showing as very warm for warmer items was fixed. A decay bug was fixed so some old items may panic-decay and disappear. Items and creatures should now be better positioned in height. Caves are now lit from outside by natural lighting. Caves and nights are darker. Olives now have a maturity season in the spring as well. Kingdom guards and merchants no longer use lanterns since oil is too expensive. Kingdom guards have been given orders to accept equipment again though. The deities have agreed to limit the power of their champions spells to 30 on the home servers in order to promote their heroism.', '<ul><li>The bug with temperature always showing as very warm for warmer items was fixed.</li>\n<li><i>A decay bug was fixed so some old items may panic-decay and disappear.</i></li>\n<li>Items and creatures should now be better positioned in height.</li>\n<li><i>Caves are now lit from outside by natural lighting. Caves and nights are darker.</i></li>\n<li>Olives now have a maturity season in the spring as well.</li>\n<li><i>Kingdom guards and merchants no longer use lanterns since oil is too expensive.</i></li>\n<li><i>Kingdom guards have been given orders to accept equipment again though.</i></li>\n<li>The deities have agreed to limit the power of their champions spells to 30 on the home servers in order to promote their heroism.</li></ul>', 6),
(18624, 4791, '061130', '061130', 'You will now need lanterns and torches to light the path in the dark. Fill lanterns with olive oil to make them burn. They will burn ql*2 minutes for torches, and a full lantern roughly 10 hours.', '<ul><li>You will now need lanterns and torches to light the path in the dark. Fill lanterns with olive oil to make them burn. They will burn ql*2 minutes for torches, and a full lantern roughly 10 hours.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 7),
(18625, 4791, '061122', '061122', 'Flattening in water is now easier. Flaming Aura had a severe bug, causing it to deal too much damage. Catapults may now make max 20 damage per shot to structures. Wooden palisade gates now take a little less damage from weapons. A bug where non-premium priests could still gain faith above 30 fixed.', '<ul><li>Flattening in water is now easier.</li>\n<li><i>Flaming Aura had a severe bug, causing it to deal too much damage.</i></li>\n<li>Catapults may now make max 20 damage per shot to structures.</li>\n<li><i>Wooden palisade gates now take a little less damage from weapons.</i></li>\n<li>A bug where non-premium priests could still gain faith above 30 fixed.</li></ul>', 8),
(18626, 4791, '061110', '061110', 'Some server bugfixes. The server memory leak is fixed as far as i can see, so the game should not become more laggy over time.', '<ul><li>Some server bugfixes.</li>\n<li><i>The server memory leak is fixed as far as i can see, so the game should not become more laggy over time.</i></li></ul>', 9),
(18627, 4791, '061104', '061104', 'The ql of the container, as well as the ql of the item itself now is involved in determining heat speed. Sleep bonus has changed so that you now get 1 minute of bonus per 24 minutes of sleep if you sleep more than one hour, up to max 5 hours bonus.', '<ul><li>The ql of the container, as well as the ql of the item itself now is involved in determining heat speed.</li>\n<li><i>Sleep bonus has changed so that you now get 1 minute of bonus per 24 minutes of sleep if you sleep more than one hour, up to max 5 hours bonus.</i></li></ul>', 10),
(18628, 4791, '061102', '061102', 'Forge/oven/fire qualitylevel is now correctly used when determining heat speed of items. Many raw material and scrap items are now recycled, and may not be banked. The banks have deemed them worthless and decided to throw such banked items on the garbage pile. Remove all your ore and logs from banks since they will also become recycled soon. Sleep bonus has changed upon request. You now recieve 1 hour bonus after 20 hours of sleep. Then 1 hour per next 24 hours up to max 5 hours.', '<ul><li>Forge/oven/fire qualitylevel is now correctly used when determining heat speed of items.</li>\n<li><i>Many raw material and scrap items are now recycled, and may not be banked. The banks have deemed them worthless and decided to throw such banked items on the garbage pile. Remove all your ore and logs from banks since they will also become recycled soon.</i></li>\n<li>Sleep bonus has changed upon request. You now recieve 1 hour bonus after 20 hours of sleep. Then 1 hour per next 24 hours up to max 5 hours.</li></ul>', 11),
(18629, 4791, '061018', '061018', 'Set the height limits of flattening and digging to 3*skill.', '<ul><li>Set the height limits of flattening and digging to 3*skill.</li></ul>', 12),
(18630, 4791, '061013', '061013', 'A lot of pretty minor bugfixes from bugzilla. Includes flattening, fishing, deed management.', '<ul><li>A lot of pretty minor bugfixes from bugzilla. Includes flattening, fishing, deed management.</li></ul>', 13),
(18631, 4791, '061008', '061008', 'Houses will now only provide theft protection if all walls are intact. The bug where roads still could not be flattened fixed. Minimum flattening difference at low skill is 1 yard now instead of 2 as per player request. Cave openings should not slope upwards any longer. Some internal checks implemented in order to eventually reduce lag.', '<ul><li>Houses will now only provide theft protection if all walls are intact.</li>\n<li><i>The bug where roads still could not be flattened fixed. Minimum flattening difference at low skill is 1 yard now instead of 2 as per player request.</i></li>\n<li>Cave openings should not slope upwards any longer.</li>\n<li><i>Some internal checks implemented in order to eventually reduce lag.</i></li></ul>', 14),
(18632, 4791, '061002', '061002', 'You may now drink fruit juice. The creation of carts and compasses has changed when it comes to what is destroyed. Flattening now should work better overall, but you will have to be the judge of that. You may now raise corners 3 times higher by flattening, so at 70 skill you may create 21 meters high slopes. You will now assemble and drop dirt automatically when flattening. You may now flatten tiles that could not be flattened before like roads. You may now make stone slab roads from stone slabs.', '<ul><li>You may now drink fruit juice.</li>\n<li>The creation of carts and compasses has changed when it comes to what is destroyed.</li>\n<li>Flattening now should work better overall, but you will have to be the judge of that.</li></ul>\n<p>You may now raise corners 3 times higher by flattening, so at 70 skill you may create 21 meters high slopes.\n</p>\n<p>You will now assemble and drop dirt automatically when flattening.\n</p>\n<p>You may now flatten tiles that could not be flattened before like roads.\n</p>\n<ul><li>You may now make stone slab roads from stone slabs.</li></ul>', 15),
(18633, 4791, '060929', '060929', 'Changes to flattening: You may now raise cobblestone and gravel. Skill needed increased. The problem where you could no longer farm was fixed.', '<ul><li>Changes to flattening: You may now raise cobblestone and gravel. Skill needed increased.</li>\n<li>The problem where you could no longer farm was fixed.</li></ul>', 16),
(18634, 4791, '060928', '060928', 'Traders no longer accept normal items to trade for deeds, since disbanding deeds yield money. The reason for this is that it ruins our business, which unfortunate since it would be a nice feature otherwise. Flattening has been revamped. Hopefully it is for the better, at least it is less buggy. You should be able to flatten in areas where you could not before, including close to water. Digging skill gain speed has been increased. Spell effects on items now slowly dissipates with use. The enchantment dissipates faster the lower the power of the effect. Omnivores and carnivores now will eat your dishes. Tweaked the difficulty of repairing walls and fences to make it easier. You may no longer /tell other players while muted.', '<ul><li>Traders no longer accept normal items to trade for deeds, since disbanding deeds yield money. The reason for this is that it ruins our business, which unfortunate since it would be a nice feature otherwise.</li>\n<li>Flattening has been revamped. Hopefully it is for the better, at least it is less buggy. You should be able to flatten in areas where you could not before, including close to water. Digging skill gain speed has been increased.</li>\n<li>Spell effects on items now slowly dissipates with use. The enchantment dissipates faster the lower the power of the effect.</li>\n<li>Omnivores and carnivores now will eat your dishes.</li>\n<li>Tweaked the difficulty of repairing walls and fences to make it easier.</li>\n<li>You may no longer /tell other players while muted.</li></ul>', 17),
(18635, 4791, '060923', '060923', 'Fixed a bug where creating items either became 0 or 100 percent.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug where creating items either became 0 or 100 percent.</li></ul>', 18),
(18636, 4791, '060922', '060922', 'Fixed the bug that crashed the server last night. Higher chance of lava eruptions You will now see normal information for beds with people sleeping in them. Cheese may now be used in cooking again You don\'t get thirsty as quick now. Wine and lemonade now give a boost to stamina. You may now make sandwiches. They don\'t last long but give a boost to stamina.', '<ul><li>Fixed the bug that crashed the server last night.</li>\n<li>Higher chance of lava eruptions</li>\n<li>You will now see normal information for beds with people sleeping in them.</li>\n<li>Cheese may now be used in cooking again</li>\n<li>You don\'t get thirsty as quick now. Wine and lemonade now give a boost to stamina.</li>\n<li>You may now make sandwiches. They don\'t last long but give a boost to stamina.</li></ul>', 19),
(18637, 4791, '060918', '060918', 'Fishing damage has changed so that it is more dependant on the type of fish. Damage is a bit higher on low quality rods, but lower when the line snaps. A bug with legal mode and stealing fixed. Lighting forges and ovens are now quicker. Signatures should now appear on certain unfinished items.', '<ul><li>Fishing damage has changed so that it is more dependant on the type of fish. Damage is a bit higher on low quality rods, but lower when the line snaps.</li>\n<li>A bug with legal mode and stealing fixed.</li>\n<li>Lighting forges and ovens are now quicker.</li>\n<li>Signatures should now appear on certain unfinished items.</li></ul>', 20),
(18638, 4791, '060913', '060913', 'Fixed a bug where you could not rent a bed unless you were holding an item. If you sleep less then 3 hours real time, your bed will still be available to you if you hired it. You now receive a question before going to sleep. Bug with setting sizes fixed. The sizes of cotton rags were also made smaller. Combine old rags to get the new size.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug where you could not rent a bed unless you were holding an item.</li>\n<li>If you sleep less then 3 hours real time, your bed will still be available to you if you hired it.</li>\n<li>You now receive a question before going to sleep.</li>\n<li>Bug with setting sizes fixed. The sizes of cotton rags were also made smaller. Combine old rags to get the new size.</li></ul>', 21),
(18639, 4791, '060912', '060912', 'Some model names changed for unfinished items so they will use the wrong models. It may take a while until the graphics packs are updated. Items should grow more appropriately when combined. Fields will now stay at full height a bit longer on average. The deities have agreed upon some religion reliefs: Magranon priests may now mine. Fo priests may now use healing covers. Vynora priests may now build roads. Magranon and libila priests may now use bows. More reliefs will come later, but this is a start.', '<ul><li>Some model names changed for unfinished items so they will use the wrong models. It may take a while until the graphics packs are updated.</li>\n<li>Items should grow more appropriately when combined.</li>\n<li>Fields will now stay at full height a bit longer on average.</li>\n<li>The deities have agreed upon some religion reliefs:\n<ul><li>Magranon priests may now mine.</li>\n<li>Fo priests may now use healing covers.</li>\n<li>Vynora priests may now build roads.</li>\n<li>Magranon and libila priests may now use bows.</li></ul></li>\n<li>More reliefs will come later, but this is a start.</li></ul>', 22),
(18640, 4791, '060911', '060911', 'The difficulty of repairing fences and walls are now more related to the damage, so it is harder the more damage they have. You may now move beds. Village alliances and wars now should be properly displayed in the village information.', '<ul><li>The difficulty of repairing fences and walls are now more related to the damage, so it is harder the more damage they have.</li>\n<li>You may now move beds.</li>\n<li>Village alliances and wars now should be properly displayed in the village information.</li></ul>', 23),
(18641, 4791, '060907', '060907', 'Fixed a few bugs with cultivating, player creation, and beds.', '<ul><li>Fixed a few bugs with cultivating, player creation, and beds.</li></ul>', 24),
(18642, 4791, '060906', '060906', 'You may now make beds inside houses. There will give bonus to skillgain and stamina regain if you sleep in them for more than one hour. Sleeping logs you off. You may also rent them if you own the house. You have to pay in cash to hire a bed. Half the amount will end up in the village upkeep if in a village, and half at the house owner. You may only hire one bed at a time. If you hire more, the previous will be made available to other. The bonus affects skillgain and stamina regeneration. You can check the bonus with the new /sleep command. You may now cultivate packed dirt in order to turn it back to normal dirt. Unfinished notake items can now be picked up again.', '<ul><li>You may now make beds inside houses. There will give bonus to skillgain and stamina regain if you sleep in them for more than one hour. Sleeping logs you off. You may also rent them if you own the house. You have to pay in cash to hire a bed. Half the amount will end up in the village upkeep if in a village, and half at the house owner. You may only hire one bed at a time. If you hire more, the previous will be made available to other. The bonus affects skillgain and stamina regeneration. You can check the bonus with the new /sleep command.</li>\n<li>You may now cultivate packed dirt in order to turn it back to normal dirt.</li>\n<li>Unfinished notake items can now be picked up again.</li></ul>', 25),
(18643, 4791, '060904', '060904', 'Bows now have signatures. Keys no longer have signatures.', '<ul><li>Bows now have signatures. Keys no longer have signatures.</li></ul>', 26),
(18644, 4791, '060831', '060831', 'Disbanding now returns 50% of the deed cost, and 50% of remaining upkeep to the deed holder. Citizens may stop the disbanding. Spiders are a bit less aggressive. Creatures now have a 180 degree field of view, but reacts if you walk too close behind them as well. Many item are now signed by their creator. Regaining lost skill after death should be 3 times quicker. You should now be able to lead your pet on deeds.', '<ul><li>Disbanding now returns 50% of the deed cost, and 50% of remaining upkeep to the deed holder. Citizens may stop the disbanding.</li>\n<li>Spiders are a bit less aggressive.</li>\n<li>Creatures now have a 180 degree field of view, but reacts if you walk too close behind them as well.</li>\n<li>Many item are now signed by their creator.</li>\n<li>Regaining lost skill after death should be 3 times quicker.</li>\n<li>You should now be able to lead your pet on deeds.</li></ul>', 27),
(18645, 4791, '060828', '060828', 'There are harsher reputation penalties for stealing and killing non-outlaws. Killing a non-outlaw now renders you an outlaw, loosing 125 reputation. It is no longer possible to push item out from deeds in order to steal them. Spiders on the wild server are back to very strong again due to popular demand, and they are a little bit stronger on home again as well. New unfinished \'more complicated\' items like barrels and watch towers will now behave more lile unfinished simple items like swords. You may now repair old unfinished \'complicated\' items. Woa now affects burying, fileting and butchering. Rye, wheat, corn and oat seeds weight more. Wemp weights more. You may now refer players with names over 20 characters long. Your playing time has been or will soon be reset since it was miscalculated. Item enchantments will now transfer between servers.', '<ul><li>There are harsher reputation penalties for stealing and killing non-outlaws. Killing a non-outlaw now renders you an outlaw, loosing 125 reputation.</li>\n<li>It is no longer possible to push item out from deeds in order to steal them.</li>\n<li>Spiders on the wild server are back to very strong again due to popular demand, and they are a little bit stronger on home again as well.</li>\n<li>New unfinished \'more complicated\' items like barrels and watch towers will now behave more lile unfinished simple items like swords. You may now repair old unfinished \'complicated\' items.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_Ages\" title=\"Wind of Ages\">Woa</a> now affects burying, fileting and butchering.</li>\n<li>Rye, wheat, corn and oat seeds weight more. Wemp weights more.</li>\n<li>You may now refer players with names over 20 characters long.</li>\n<li>Your playing time has been or will soon be reset since it was miscalculated.</li>\n<li>Item enchantments will now transfer between servers.</li></ul>', 28),
(18646, 4791, '060814', '060814', 'Referrals are in. You may now reward other players for bringing you to Wurm with the command /refer. Pigs had too thick hide. Spider do less damage. Guards should help each other a bit better now. You may now withdraw your money at any bank.', '<ul><li>Referrals are in. You may now reward other players for bringing you to Wurm with the command /refer.</li>\n<li>Pigs had too thick hide. Spider do less damage. Guards should help each other a bit better now.</li>\n<li>You may now withdraw your money at any bank.</li></ul>', 29),
(18647, 4791, '060810', '060810', 'The bug with locks was finally found. Most old locks can now be properly locked and unlocked. If they still don.', '<ul><li>The bug with locks was finally found. Most old locks can now be properly locked and unlocked. If they still don.</li></ul>', 30),
(18648, 4791, '060809', '060809', 'The message that the client is out of sync should appear much less frequently now and the game should run smoother again. You may now change upkeep plan even if there are no guards alive. The guard role will now show in village settings again.', '<ul><li>The message that the client is out of sync should appear much less frequently now and the game should run smoother again.</li>\n<li>You may now change upkeep plan even if there are no guards alive.</li>\n<li>The guard role will now show in village settings again.</li></ul>', 31),
(18649, 4791, '060808', '060808', 'The bug in the speed detection system fixed. Speed hacks are no longer a threat. Rather the opposite, since it is dangerous to use one. You may receive annoying warnings if the server is lagging. If those warnings become too common, these will be tweaked.', '<ul><li>The bug in the speed detection system fixed. Speed hacks are no longer a threat. Rather the opposite, since it is dangerous to use one. You may receive annoying warnings if the server is lagging. If those warnings become too common, these will be tweaked.</li></ul>', 32),
(18650, 4791, '060807', '060807', 'Fixed a graphical bug with multiple models showing when leaving a cave by a gate. Fixed the bug with keys not working with new locks or after changing server. Unfortunatly these newly made keys are unrelated to the newly made locks. Item naming fixed so that they don Bug with alliances not showing in the village info fixed. You now need 21 strength to fire, load or winch a catapult. Creating needles now uses up more material.', '<ul><li>Fixed a graphical bug with multiple models showing when leaving a cave by a gate.</li>\n<li><i>Fixed the bug with keys not working with new locks or after changing server. Unfortunatly these newly made keys are unrelated to the newly made locks.</i></li>\n<li>Item naming fixed so that they don</li>\n<li><i>Bug with alliances not showing in the village info fixed.</i></li>\n<li>You now need 21 strength to fire, load or winch a catapult.</li>\n<li><i>Creating needles now uses up more material.</i></li></ul>', 33),
(18651, 4791, '060802', '060802', 'Armour damage fix.', '<ul><li><i>Armour damage fix.</i></li></ul>', 34),
(18652, 4791, '060731', '060731', 'The database has been restructured in certain areas in order to solve the problems with the wild server. The change should have no visable effect, but the areas affected are house guests, structures, and keys. Due to a manual error recently created items on the wild server may have disappeared or changed place. Using catapults on houses with owners from the same kingdom now have more severe repercussions. Made it so that you can not trade liquids out of their containers. Picking seeds and crushing pumpkins are now policed.', '<ul><li><i>The database has been restructured in certain areas in order to solve the problems with the wild server. The change should have no visable effect, but the areas affected are house guests, structures, and keys. Due to a manual error recently created items on the wild server may have disappeared or changed place.</i></li>\n<li>Using catapults on houses with owners from the same kingdom now have more severe repercussions.</li>\n<li><i>Made it so that you can not trade liquids out of their containers.</i></li>\n<li>Picking seeds and crushing pumpkins are now policed.</li></ul>', 35),
(18653, 4791, '060728', '060728', 'The fix yesterday did not work, so in order to pin down why the database connection is suddenly being shut down, the game will shut down as well when it happens in order to get proper logs. Before the real message was rotated away due to the excess error logging that happened. This problem will hopefully be solved during the next few days.', '<ul><li>The fix yesterday did not work, so in order to pin down why the database connection is suddenly being shut down, the game will shut down as well when it happens in order to get proper logs. Before the real message was rotated away due to the excess error logging that happened.</li>\n<li>This problem will hopefully be solved during the next few days.</li></ul>', 36),
(18654, 4791, '060728', '060728_2', 'Upgraded kernel on the wild server, in an attempt to fix the instability.', '<ul><li><i>Upgraded kernel on the wild server, in an attempt to fix the instability.</i></li></ul>', 37),
(18655, 4791, '060726', '060726', 'A bug with updating passwords from the website caused the wild server to be down for about 10 hours. Premium players on that server have received 2 days compensation.', '<ul><li><i>A bug with updating passwords from the website caused the wild server to be down for about 10 hours. Premium players on that server have received 2 days compensation.</i></li></ul>', 38),
(18656, 4791, '060725', '060725', 'WARNING! Creatures now do different types of damage. Leather armour should become less prevalent since it is not as efficient against the various types of attacks. Fixed the table bug in the village settlement window. Fixed another bug with fence decay. A bug where armour speed modifiers were one step behind when you wore/removed armour has been fixed.', '<ul><li><i>WARNING! Creatures now do different types of damage. Leather armour should become less prevalent since it is not as efficient against the various types of attacks.</i></li>\n<li>Fixed the table bug in the village settlement window.</li>\n<li><i>Fixed another bug with fence decay.</i></li>\n<li>A bug where armour speed modifiers were one step behind when you wore/removed armour has been fixed.</li></ul>', 39),
(18657, 4791, '060719', '060719', 'Fixed a bug where repairing 0 damaged items made them receive damage.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug where repairing 0 damaged items made them receive damage.</li></ul>', 40),
(18658, 4791, '060718', '060718', 'Repair times were lowered. Fixed a bug with pricing that at rare occasions made certain items sell 1 iron cheaper then for wich they are purchased. Fixed a bug with trading where items traded with containers were not traded properly.', '<ul><li>Repair times were lowered.</li>\n<li><i> Fixed a bug with pricing that at rare occasions made certain items sell 1 iron cheaper</i></li></ul>\n<p>then for wich they are purchased. <i></i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Fixed a bug with trading where items traded with containers were not traded properly.</li></ul>', 41),
(18659, 4791, '060716', '060716', 'Fixed a bug with fence decay on eastern and southern village borders. You may no longer repair hot items that take damage from fires. You no longer get damage set to 0 for free after every repair Better looking village settings and personal trader price management windows. A bug with loosing link and invurnerability fixed. You are now vurnerable 3 minutes after you fight a creature, and 5 minutes after you fight a player. You may log off before though if in a safe area. The commands /attackers and /lotime might be useful Gate management window now shows the gate names properly.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug with fence decay on eastern and southern village borders.</li>\n<li><i>You may no longer repair hot items that take damage from fires. You no longer get damage set to 0 for free after every repair</i></li>\n<li>Better looking village settings and personal trader price management windows.</li>\n<li><i>A bug with loosing link and invurnerability fixed. You are now vurnerable 3 minutes after you fight a creature, and 5 minutes after you fight a player. You may log off before though if in a safe area. The commands /attackers and /lotime might be useful </i></li>\n<li>Gate management window now shows the gate names properly.</li></ul>', 42),
(18660, 4791, '060706', '060706', 'Due to the general problems after gold (and specifically the structure management bug), every paying player has received 1 week extra premium time. Creatures now age a bit faster. Max number of creatures increased. Bug with priest limitations fixed. The economy has been trimmed so traders should more often have money. The teleport bug when leaving caves with fences fixed. Fixed a bug with personal trader price management. Non-democracies may now revoke citizenship again. Manage citizens is now allowed on the token to those who may manage settings. Village settings window now scrolls left (still no table yet though).', '<ul><li>Due to the general problems after gold (and specifically the structure management bug), every paying player has received 1 week extra premium time.</li>\n<li><i>Creatures now age a bit faster. Max number of creatures increased.</i></li>\n<li>Bug with priest limitations fixed.</li>\n<li>The economy has been trimmed so traders should more often have money.</li>\n<li><i>The teleport bug when leaving caves with fences fixed.</i></li>\n<li>Fixed a bug with personal trader price management.</li>\n<li><i>Non-democracies may now revoke citizenship again. Manage citizens is now allowed on the token to those who may manage settings.</i></li>\n<li>Village settings window now scrolls left (still no table yet though).</li></ul>', 43),
(18661, 4791, '060630', '060630', 'Fixed other problems with the structure management window (the destroy bug) and the personal trader management window Archery targets are the only item that gives skill now when fired upon.', '<ul><li><i>Fixed other problems with the structure management window (the destroy bug) and the personal trader management window</i></li>\n<li>Archery targets are the only item that gives skill now when fired upon.</li></ul>', 44),
(18662, 4791, '060629', '060629', 'Fixed problems with various windows: Titles, structure management, bank management, spawning. Transfered some money to the wild server.', '<ul><li><i>Fixed problems with various windows: Titles, structure management, bank management, spawning.</i></li>\n<li>Transfered some money to the wild server.</li></ul>', 45),
(18663, 4791, '060627', '060627', 'New window system that does not use html. Most dialogs have been tested, but some errors may remain. Some may also look a bit weird now. Creature spawn rate lowered. Also a mysterious plague has hit boars, gorillas and hyenas. Bug with cave decay fixed so that weird holes no longer should emerge. Unused entrances also decay faster. A bug with time synchronization between the wild server and the login server fixed. No really bad effects should occur.', '<ul><li>New window system that does not use html. Most dialogs have been tested, but some errors may remain. Some may also look a bit weird now.</li>\n<li>Creature spawn rate lowered. Also a mysterious plague has hit boars, gorillas and hyenas.</li>\n<li>Bug with cave decay fixed so that weird holes no longer should emerge. Unused entrances also decay faster.</li>\n<li>A bug with time synchronization between the wild server and the login server fixed. No really bad effects should occur.</li></ul>', 46),
(18664, 4791, '060619', '060619', 'Fixed a bug with the rock layer. Uncovering rock by digging should be easier now again. Alchemy skillgain slowed down since it was too fast given the availability of the new wound covers. Fighting skills were equalled so they gain equally slow/quick in order to prepare for the future fighting system. Overall skillgain was also tweaked a bit.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug with the rock layer. Uncovering rock by digging should be easier now again.</li>\n<li>Alchemy skillgain slowed down since it was too fast given the availability of the new wound covers. Fighting skills were equalled so they gain equally slow/quick in order to prepare for the future fighting system. Overall skillgain was also tweaked a bit.</li></ul>', 47),
(18665, 4791, '060618', '060618', 'Unless you\'ve noticed already, it takes longer time to create a hole on the surface when mining, and it does not always yield rock shards. A bug with transferring wounds between servers fixed. Dragons did waaay too little damage. They were not the extremely tough creatures they were supposed to be. If you managed to kill one, congratulations.', '<ul><li>Unless you\'ve noticed already, it takes longer time to create a hole on the surface when mining, and it does not always yield rock shards. A bug with transferring wounds between servers fixed.</li>\n<li>Dragons did waaay too little damage. They were not the extremely tough creatures they were supposed to be. If you managed to kill one, congratulations.</li></ul>', 48),
(18666, 4791, '060614', '060614', 'Premium accounts now have received their sign-up bonus title and item. Set the title with the \'/titles\' command. Faith gain broke due to the fix and many players were reset to 1. All players with a deity are now set to faith 10. Most players will be capped at 30 anyways later on unless they decide to become priests. Faithgain was crazy before the \'fix\' anyways so 10 is probably reasonable.', '<ul><li>Premium accounts now have received their sign-up bonus title and item. Set the title with the \'/titles\' command.</li>\n<li>Faith gain broke due to the fix and many players were reset to 1. All players with a deity are now set to faith 10. Most players will be capped at 30 anyways later on unless they decide to become priests. Faithgain was crazy before the \'fix\' anyways so 10 is probably reasonable.</li></ul>', 49),
(18667, 4791, '060613', '060613', 'Bug found with creatures being out of position. Religion system fix:  At faith 10 anyone receive bonuses in your deity\'s domain.  Only priests can cast spells.  Faith 30 needed to become a priest.  You do not gain favour by praying any more. Favour slowly rises by time instead.  Spells almost always succeed.  Priests may NOT perform LOTS of normal actions, like mine, dig, repair, improve, mix alchemy etc. Fo priests may not initiate aggressive actions.  A priest may go unfaithful and still perform these actions and lose 0.1 faith. If they go below 30 faith they lose priesthood.  You need to be priest for a while if you want to become a champion of a deity and enjoy realdeath.  The effects of this system is to make priests and magic very rare, and possibly very powerful.  The prayer skill still remain but it does nothing and may be removed or reworked later. The channeling skill still helps if you are good at it, but it is also subject to change soon. Maybe even before anyone gets to use it.', '<ul><li>Bug found with creatures being out of position.</li>\n<li>Religion system fix:  At faith 10 anyone receive bonuses in your deity\'s domain.  Only priests can cast spells.  Faith 30 needed to become a priest.  You do not gain favour by praying any more. Favour slowly rises by time instead.  Spells almost always succeed.  Priests may NOT perform LOTS of normal actions, like mine, dig, repair, improve, mix alchemy etc. Fo priests may not initiate aggressive actions.  A priest may go unfaithful and still perform these actions and lose 0.1 faith. If they go below 30 faith they lose priesthood.  You need to be priest for a while if you want to become a champion of a deity and enjoy realdeath.  The effects of this system is to make priests and magic very rare, and possibly very powerful.  The prayer skill still remain but it does nothing and may be removed or reworked later. The channeling skill still helps if you are good at it, but it is also subject to change soon. Maybe even before anyone gets to use it.</li></ul>', 50),
(18668, 4791, '060608', '060608', 'A bug was fixed with the penalty for same-side attacking non-outlaws. The penalty was increased for home servers. In order to get to grips with the amount of thievery going on on the homeserver, the king now declares everyone an outlaw as soon as he or she is found stealing there. Bug with too much data sent when creatures moving fixed. Passing through fences should now happen much more seldom. Scrap material will no longer be yielded when failing to create something from scrap material. Bug with fighting affecting questions like \'who got the kill?\' fixed. Weapons belonging to monsters no longer take damage when fighting. Premium accounts now have twice the fatigue (12 hours added). Faithgain bugfix. Followers of Libila may not enter the homeserver for a while. People who convert to libila are now insta-transferred to the wild server. You may now create some natural healing treatments. It\'s missing from the official release notes, but opening a cave entrance now takes up to 60 mining actions, but yield less rock shards.', '<ul><li>A bug was fixed with the penalty for same-side attacking non-outlaws. The penalty was increased for home servers. In order to get to grips with the amount of thievery going on on the homeserver, the king now declares everyone an outlaw as soon as he or she is found stealing there.</li>\n<li>Bug with too much data sent when creatures moving fixed.</li>\n<li>Passing through fences should now happen much more seldom.</li>\n<li>Scrap material will no longer be yielded when failing to create something from scrap material.</li>\n<li>Bug with fighting affecting questions like \'who got the kill?\' fixed.</li>\n<li>Weapons belonging to monsters no longer take damage when fighting.</li>\n<li>Premium accounts now have twice the fatigue (12 hours added).</li>\n<li>Faithgain bugfix.</li>\n<li>Followers of Libila may not enter the homeserver for a while. People who convert to libila are now insta-transferred to the wild server.</li>\n<li>You may now create some natural healing treatments.</li></ul>\n<p><em>It\'s missing from the official release notes, but opening a cave entrance now takes up to 60 mining actions, but yield less rock shards.</em>\n</p>', 51);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18669, 4791, '060608', '060608_2', 'Tunneling now fails later when tunneling on ore. Water quality bug fixed. Flattening gravel/cobblestone fix. Spiders now has shorter vision.', '<ul><li>Tunneling now fails later when tunneling on ore.</li>\n<li>Water quality bug fixed.</li>\n<li>Flattening gravel/cobblestone fix.</li>\n<li>Spiders now has shorter vision.</li></ul>', 52),
(18670, 4791, '060606b', '060606b', 'Creatures will no longer spawn right beside you. You may now retrieve lower denominations from the bank as well. Fixed some issues with digging.', '<ul><li>Creatures will no longer spawn right beside you.</li>\n<li>You may now retrieve lower denominations from the bank as well.</li>\n<li>Fixed some issues with digging.</li></ul>', 53),
(18671, 4791, '060606 (Gold!)', '060606_.28Gold.21.29', 'Some initial game play tips: Try to collaborate. Doing it all yourself is very time consuming. Use the bartenders at the starting points for free food. Don\'t wander off too far from the starting points. Note: No spells are available for now, and faith will no longer rise above 30. This is pending the religion fix where priests are very limited in their actions. Planned feature number 1: Some kind of natural healing, like salves. Planned features numbers 2 and 3: Religion fix and fighting system fixes.', '<ul><li>Some initial game play tips:</li>\n<li>Try to collaborate. Doing it all yourself is very time consuming.</li>\n<li>Use the bartenders at the starting points for free food.</li>\n<li>Don\'t wander off too far from the starting points.</li>\n<li>Note: No spells are available for now, and faith will no longer rise above 30.\n<ul><li>This is pending the religion fix where priests are very limited in their actions.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Planned feature number 1: Some kind of natural healing, like salves.</li>\n<li>Planned features numbers 2 and 3: Religion fix and fighting system fixes.</li></ul>', 54),
(18672, 4791, '060531', '060531', 'Note: The home server is still considered a test server! No account guarantees are given. No GM supported expected. Etc. THIS IS UNTESTED: You should now be able to leave the server while carrying deeds, merchant contracts, and writs. These should not accompany you to the next server, but reappear when you return. Verify that it works before you head south yourself. BLs should no longer be able to enter the home server. Beware of sharks!', '<ul><li>Note: The home server is still considered a test server! No account guarantees are given. No GM supported expected. Etc.</li>\n<li>THIS IS UNTESTED: You should now be able to leave the server while carrying deeds, merchant contracts, and writs. These should not accompany you to the next server, but reappear when you return. Verify that it works before you head south yourself.</li>\n<li>BLs should no longer be able to enter the home server. Beware of sharks!</li></ul>', 55),
(18673, 4791, '60530', '60530', 'Falling damage on login should be much rarer. You should now be able to leave the server with unused deeds. You will not be able to return to the wild from the home server for a while. We are testing some premier account functionalities. You may now build plan on cobblestone and it is now terraformable. You may no longer create lockpicks until you have sufficient locksmithing. Also you need to have high ql picks to pick high ql locks.', '<ul><li>Falling damage on login should be much rarer.</li>\n<li>You should now be able to leave the server with unused deeds.</li>\n<li>You will not be able to return to the wild from the home server for a while. We are testing some premier account functionalities.</li>\n<li>You may now build plan on cobblestone and it is now terraformable.</li>\n<li>You may no longer create lockpicks until you have sufficient locksmithing. Also you need to have high ql picks to pick high ql locks.</li></ul>', 56),
(18674, 4791, '060529', '060529', 'It is now easier to mine cave floor and roof. You may now dig on dirt again..', '<ul><li>It is now easier to mine cave floor and roof.</li>\n<li>You may now dig on dirt again..</li></ul>', 57),
(18675, 4791, '060526b', '060526b', 'Updates to the qos scheme fixing some bugs.', '<ul><li>Updates to the qos scheme fixing some bugs.</li></ul>', 58),
(18676, 4791, '060526', '060526', 'We are testing a \'quality of service\' scheme, which means creature positions are updated less often. We will see how it goes. Fountains and statues and some other items are now created on ground. Shields are now created in inventory. Prospecting on surface rock now gives better quality messages. Fire effects that don\'t go away should be fixed. Creatures that don\'t climb should no longer spawn on steep slopes or on high mountain tops.', '<ul><li>We are testing a \'quality of service\' scheme, which means creature positions are updated less often. We will see how it goes.</li>\n<li>Fountains and statues and some other items are now created on ground. Shields are now created in inventory.</li>\n<li>Prospecting on surface rock now gives better quality messages.</li>\n<li>Fire effects that don\'t go away should be fixed.</li>\n<li>Creatures that don\'t climb should no longer spawn on steep slopes or on high mountain tops.</li></ul>', 59),
(18677, 4791, '060525', '060525', 'You may now cast \'break altar\' on normal altars', '<ul><li>You may now cast \'break altar\' on normal altars</li></ul>', 60),
(18678, 4791, '060523', '060523', 'You may no longer disband enemy deeds directly, only via drain coffers. Bandaging wounds should yield more accurate health back. Village spirits will now blink to their target. If you swim out to sea and encounter waves, proceed at your own risk. You may lose items, skills or even permadie. Hens will lay fewer eggs. Kill off the chickens please. Such creatures now should die even faster.', '<ul><li>You may no longer disband enemy deeds directly, only via drain coffers.</li>\n<li>Bandaging wounds should yield more accurate health back.</li>\n<li>Village spirits will now blink to their target.</li>\n<li>If you swim out to sea and encounter waves, proceed at your own risk. You may lose items, skills or even permadie.</li>\n<li>Hens will lay fewer eggs. Kill off the chickens please. Such creatures now should die even faster.</li></ul>', 61),
(18679, 4791, '060521', '060521', 'Gems now appear in piles. A tile can now only contain one campfire. One-item piles should appear only as a result of removing items from a tile. You may now pick your own locks and gates without upsetting your deity. You will receive no skill though since there is no risk involved. Items no longer yield too high amounts of temperature when burnt in fires. Examining a village token will tell you how many guards are alive. The bug where you could create cave openings with diagonal lowest corners is fixed, so you won\'t be able to mine on those. Chickens and other very weak creatures die very easily now.', '<ul><li>Gems now appear in piles.</li>\n<li>A tile can now only contain one campfire.</li>\n<li>One-item piles should appear only as a result of removing items from a tile.</li>\n<li>You may now pick your own locks and gates without upsetting your deity. You will receive no skill though since there is no risk involved.</li>\n<li>Items no longer yield too high amounts of temperature when burnt in fires.</li>\n<li>Examining a village token will tell you how many guards are alive.</li>\n<li>The bug where you could create cave openings with diagonal lowest corners is fixed, so you won\'t be able to mine on those.</li>\n<li>Chickens and other very weak creatures die very easily now.</li></ul>', 62),
(18680, 4791, '060517', '060517', 'You may now loot the corpses of outlaws. Invitations to join a kingdom or to join a religion now requires the target player to type /invitations in order to accept them.', '<ul><li>You may now loot the corpses of outlaws.</li>\n<li>Invitations to join a kingdom or to join a religion now requires the target player to type /invitations in order to accept them.</li></ul>', 63),
(18681, 4791, '060516', '060516', 'The huge altars will no longer receive negative damage, and heal once every ten minutes. Moving your bank account now works properly. Items in banks shouldn\'t crumble when you remove them. Any white light religion may now sacrifice at the Altar of Three.', '<ul><li>The huge altars will no longer receive negative damage, and heal once every ten minutes.</li>\n<li>Moving your bank account now works properly. Items in banks shouldn\'t crumble when you remove them.</li>\n<li>Any white light religion may now sacrifice at the Altar of Three.</li></ul>', 64),
(18682, 4791, '060514', '060514', 'Pets that you are leading no longer should go through gates or doors that you cannot enter.', '<ul><li>Pets that you are leading no longer should go through gates or doors that you cannot enter.</li></ul>', 65),
(18683, 4791, '060510', '060510', 'Faith gain was also increased. Bows should not start spamming you when the string breaks. Corpse models should change when butchered (if a model exists). Leather items now use material when improving.', '<ul><li>Faith gain was also increased.</li>\n<li>Bows should not start spamming you when the string breaks.</li>\n<li>Corpse models should change when butchered (if a model exists).</li>\n<li>Leather items now use material when improving.</li></ul>', 66),
(18684, 4791, '060508', '060508', 'Livestock now have shorter lifespan. Skills.. now rise at.. 12 TIMES FASTER, so this last month will roughly resemble one year of playing.. promised child! Steaks are now more properly called meals. Another bug with trying to destroy the huge altars using artifacts was found. The first successful server transfer has occured. Rolf swimmed from his homeserver to the wurm server. He had an extra body when he arrived, but otherwise everything looked well.', '<ul><li>Livestock now have shorter lifespan.</li>\n<li>Skills.. now rise at.. 12 TIMES FASTER, so this last month will roughly resemble one year of playing.. promised child!</li>\n<li>Steaks are now more properly called meals.</li>\n<li>Another bug with trying to destroy the huge altars using artifacts was found.</li>\n<li>The first successful server transfer has occured. Rolf swimmed from his homeserver to the wurm server. He had an extra body when he arrived, but otherwise everything looked well.</li></ul>', 67),
(18685, 4791, '060506', '060506', 'Bug with artifacts spamming a message fixed. They now correctly drop when the player carrying it logs off. Bugs with lockpicking fixed. You should no longer be able to lock doors with padlocks or gatelocks, and chests with gatelocks. Guard towers should be tile-aligned now. The door ends up behind you!', '<ul><li>Bug with artifacts spamming a message fixed. They now correctly drop when the player carrying it logs off.</li>\n<li>Bugs with lockpicking fixed.</li>\n<li>You should no longer be able to lock doors with padlocks or gatelocks, and chests with gatelocks.</li>\n<li>Guard towers should be tile-aligned now. The door ends up behind you!</li></ul>', 68),
(18686, 4791, '060504', '060504', 'Artifacts now take no damage. Artifacts now load on the ground where the owner was if they were in the possession of someone when the server starts. The Orb of Doom and the Magranon spell Smite no longer instakills. They will however put you very near death. Unique creatures usually have innate abilites that reduces this effect. You may now create and use lockpicks. A building door should stay open 10 minutes. Scale of Libila bug fix. Rod of Beguiling now has a use. You now need to have higher favor than the target player to bless someone.', '<ul><li>Artifacts now take no damage. Artifacts now load on the ground where the owner was if they were in the possession of someone when the server starts.</li>\n<li>The Orb of Doom and the Magranon spell Smite no longer instakills. They will however put you very near death. Unique creatures usually have innate abilites that reduces this effect.</li>\n<li>You may now create and use lockpicks. A building door should stay open 10 minutes.</li>\n<li>Scale of Libila bug fix. Rod of Beguiling now has a use. You now need to have higher favor than the target player to bless someone.</li></ul>', 69),
(18687, 4791, '060430', '060430', 'The bug with faith gain fixed.', '<ul><li>The bug with faith gain fixed.</li></ul>', 70),
(18688, 4791, '060426', '060426', 'Newbie items except the backpack will now stay in inventory when you die. The drawback is that they cannot be improved. Fences on the south and east side of villages now have village decay rate. You may no longer drain coffers as long as there are guards alive. Enemies may no longer pass gates on a deed. A bug with village gates was fixed. Fence and palisade gates now take more damage from attacks than the standard types of fence and palisade. Food bar fixed. You receive no penalties unless you are hungry. If you are full you will use up less stamina when working (making steaks valuable).', '<ul><li>Newbie items except the backpack will now stay in inventory when you die. The drawback is that they cannot be improved.</li>\n<li>Fences on the south and east side of villages now have village decay rate.</li>\n<li>You may no longer drain coffers as long as there are guards alive.</li>\n<li>Enemies may no longer pass gates on a deed. A bug with village gates was fixed. Fence and palisade gates now take more damage from attacks than the standard types of fence and palisade.</li>\n<li>Food bar fixed. You receive no penalties unless you are hungry. If you are full you will use up less stamina when working (making steaks valuable).</li></ul>', 71),
(18689, 4791, '060425', '060425', 'Some issues with irresponsive pets solved. Be aware that they are generally more alert when not being led. Get price now returns a more sensible value. Bug with dropping corpses where the owner became the person who dropped it fixed. You may now also always loot corpses from corpses.', '<ul><li>Some issues with irresponsive pets solved. Be aware that they are generally more alert when not being led.</li>\n<li>Get price now returns a more sensible value.</li>\n<li>Bug with dropping corpses where the owner became the person who dropped it fixed. You may now also always loot corpses from corpses.</li></ul>', 72),
(18690, 4791, '060420', '060420', 'You now get no deed skill loss bonus if suiciding on a deed. If you have realdeath (a champion of a deity), you have 50% of that suicide not counting towards your real deaths. A clarification to end certain rumours: A bonus for Magranon players is that at high faith and with enough favor left, they have about 75% chance to keep items and skills at death. Hopefully less login-lag will occur due to a better way of loading skills.', '<ul><li>You now get no deed skill loss bonus if suiciding on a deed. If you have realdeath (a champion of a deity), you have 50% of that suicide not counting towards your real deaths.</li>\n<li>A clarification to end certain rumours: A bonus for Magranon players is that at high faith and with enough favor left, they have about 75% chance to keep items and skills at death.</li>\n<li>Hopefully less login-lag will occur due to a better way of loading skills.</li></ul>', 73),
(18691, 4791, '060418', '060418', 'Trolls have come up with a way to make deadlier clubs, as well as improved armour so take care. Some bugs with attacking BL deed guards as a WL and stealing from BL houses fixed.', '<ul><li>Trolls have come up with a way to make deadlier clubs, as well as improved armour so take care.</li>\n<li>Some bugs with attacking BL deed guards as a WL and stealing from BL houses fixed.</li></ul>', 74),
(18692, 4791, '060412', '060412', 'You should no longer be killed by aggressive animals who walk up to you while you are linkless. Some new creatures! When becoming champion you will now receive bonus up to max skill 80 in certain religious skills (unless you already had higher). This since you have 3 lives now. If current upkeep will last more than 28 days, no decay should occur to fences and walls on a deed. Number of allowed roles on a deed has been increased to 12 again. Large deeds will need to manage citizens in a few more steps. The deed rules on attacking other players should now work correct.', '<ul><li>You should no longer be killed by aggressive animals who walk up to you while you are linkless.</li>\n<li>Some new creatures!</li>\n<li>When becoming champion you will now receive bonus up to max skill 80 in certain religious skills (unless you already had higher). This since you have 3 lives now.</li>\n<li>If current upkeep will last more than 28 days, no decay should occur to fences and walls on a deed.</li>\n<li>Number of allowed roles on a deed has been increased to 12 again. Large deeds will need to manage citizens in a few more steps.</li>\n<li>The deed rules on attacking other players should now work correct.</li></ul>', 75),
(18693, 4791, '060410', '060410', 'You may now gain shield skill when bashing with it. Citizen management should work better for large deeds. The number of available roles had to be lowered to 8 (old roles remain for now). Fo received a new spell that works on creatures. Currently not on self, but that will be fixed', '<ul><li>You may now gain shield skill when bashing with it.</li>\n<li>Citizen management should work better for large deeds. The number of available roles had to be lowered to 8 (old roles remain for now).</li>\n<li>Fo received a new spell that works on creatures. Currently not on self, but that will be fixed</li></ul>', 76),
(18694, 4791, '060405', '060405', 'Crush weapons now do much less damage versus cloth and leather armour. Other weapons now do more damage. You may now receive a negative bonus to fighting if your weapon skill is too low. Before it could only be positive. Pets should now swim when lead. Various small typos fixed.', '<ul><li>Crush weapons now do much less damage versus cloth and leather armour. Other weapons now do more damage. You may now receive a negative bonus to fighting if your weapon skill is too low. Before it could only be positive.</li>\n<li>Pets should now swim when lead.</li>\n<li>Various small typos fixed.</li></ul>', 77),
(18695, 4791, '060403', '060403', 'Deed guards should not all run after dominated creatures. Thanks to all of you who fell for our little jest with the chests! The competition was over on the 2nd of april, swedish time with no winner.', '<ul><li>Deed guards should not all run after dominated creatures.</li>\n<li>Thanks to all of you who fell for our little jest with the chests! The competition was over on the 2nd of april, swedish time with no winner.</li></ul>', 78),
(18696, 4791, '060401', '060401', 'April fool Gold competition Since we are coming close to going gold, we have decided to run a competition while we wait. One random creature in the game has been given magical properties. If you step up within two tiles of that creature and say I am a chest, give me my gold. you will receive and be announced as the winner of the Prize. The Prize consists of a fine Teleport Wand, a Bag of Keeping, and 2 gold (all of which you will be able to keep when we go gold). The server history log found on deed tokens will show if a winner has been declared. GMs are not allowed to participate, but chat moderators are. Good luck everyone! You now only gain skill from attacking opposing kingdom deed guards. Items no longer decay in banks.', '<ul><li>April fool Gold competition</li>\n<li>Since we are coming close to going gold, we have decided to run a competition while we wait. One random creature in the game has been given magical properties. If you step up within two tiles of that creature and say I am a chest, give me my gold. you will receive and be announced as the winner of the Prize. The Prize consists of a fine Teleport Wand, a Bag of Keeping, and 2 gold (all of which you will be able to keep when we go gold). The server history log found on deed tokens will show if a winner has been declared. GMs are not allowed to participate, but chat moderators are. Good luck everyone!</li>\n<li>You now only gain skill from attacking opposing kingdom deed guards.</li>\n<li>Items no longer decay in banks.</li></ul>', 79),
(18697, 4791, '060330', '060330', 'Various bugfixes, for instance with dough. Kingdom and deed guards should be a bit easier to cope with again.', '<ul><li>Various bugfixes, for instance with dough. Kingdom and deed guards should be a bit easier to cope with again.</li></ul>', 80),
(18698, 4791, '060328', '060328', 'Kingdom guards will only hunt near their tower now. Corpses will now fit in new coffins. A bug with enchantment effects being lost between reboots fixed. A new command, /attackers shows the creatures who attacked you the last 5 minutes. If a player is there should be able to attack him/her without a penalty to skills/faith. You now need 20.5 body control to steal things.', '<ul><li>Kingdom guards will only hunt near their tower now.</li>\n<li>Corpses will now fit in new coffins.</li>\n<li>A bug with enchantment effects being lost between reboots fixed.</li>\n<li>A new command, /attackers shows the creatures who attacked you the last 5 minutes. If a player is there should be able to attack him/her without a penalty to skills/faith.</li>\n<li>You now need 20.5 body control to steal things.</li></ul>', 81),
(18699, 4791, '060327', '060327', 'The extreme repairtimes were lessened. Armour strength were lowered again for most creatures. Archery targets can no longer be picked up. Champions of deities now have 3 chances before realdeath kicks in. Dough now should use less water when created.', '<ul><li>The extreme repairtimes were lessened.</li>\n<li>Armour strength were lowered again for most creatures.</li>\n<li>Archery targets can no longer be picked up.</li>\n<li>Champions of deities now have 3 chances before realdeath kicks in.</li>\n<li>Dough now should use less water when created.</li></ul>', 82),
(18700, 4791, '060325', '060325', 'Removed the bug that crashed the game tonight.', '<ul><li>Removed the bug that crashed the game tonight.</li></ul>', 83),
(18701, 4791, '060324', '060324', 'Practicing targets work now. We will test the new creature armour rates over the weekend. No time to fix anyways. Feedback after. Good luck!', '<ul><li>Practicing targets work now. We will test the new creature armour rates over the weekend. No time to fix anyways. Feedback after. Good luck!</li></ul>', 84),
(18702, 4791, '060322', '060322', 'You may now \'drain coffers\' from an enemy village once every 24 hours. If the village has more than one week of upkeep left, you will drain and receive a fraction of the monthly upkeep (drain about 15% and receive 7.5%). In order to prevent that villages always keep less than a weeks upkeep, structure decay will kick in at normal rate if upkeep left is less than one week. Bowstrings may now snap, and you may unstring your bow. Bows may only be improved if they have no string. Arrows should break less often, and hitting something should be much easier. Creatures now have better armour, as they are using armour types. You will now deflect arrows with your shield. A fraction of the defending creatures body control also now adds to the difficulty to hit. You can no longer shoot if you are in deep water. Repairing now takes longer time for very heavy items.', '<ul><li>You may now \'drain coffers\' from an enemy village once every 24 hours. If the village has more than one week of upkeep left, you will drain and receive a fraction of the monthly upkeep (drain about 15% and receive 7.5%). In order to prevent that villages always keep less than a weeks upkeep, structure decay will kick in at normal rate if upkeep left is less than one week.</li>\n<li>Bowstrings may now snap, and you may unstring your bow. Bows may only be improved if they have no string.</li>\n<li>Arrows should break less often, and hitting something should be much easier.</li>\n<li>Creatures now have better armour, as they are using armour types.</li>\n<li>You will now deflect arrows with your shield. A fraction of the defending creatures body control also now adds to the difficulty to hit.</li>\n<li>You can no longer shoot if you are in deep water.</li>\n<li>Repairing now takes longer time for very heavy items.</li></ul>', 85),
(18703, 4791, '060321', '060321', 'Bows can now be stringed. Arrow shafts and arrow heads now are not repairable and should be quicker to make. Notes on archery:  Archery is hard to learn. It is supposed only to be usable against creatures with fair skill and good equipment.\nTo gain skill quickest, practice with hunting arrows that have no penalties. All bows have a \'best distance\'. That distance is 20, 40, and 80 meters (or roughly 5, 10 and 20 tiles) for the bows. Shooting at shorter or longer ranges will affect the difficulty.\nArrows will be shot in the following order: 1. from quiver worn on body, 2. from quiver in inventory (or if 1 is found but is empty), 3. arrow held in hand, 4. arrow in inventory. If a quiver is found at 2 but it is empty, no arrow will be shot. This should give you good control over which arrows are shot.  Arrows are fired in the following order: 1. War arrows, 2. Hunting arrows, 3. shafts.  War arrows do more damage, but are slightly harder to hit with. Shafts do little damage and are hardest to hit with. All three religions should now be able to pray at the Altar of Three. Bugfixes with /ranks. A bug where the finished item received the wrong material was fixed.', '<ul><li>Bows can now be stringed. Arrow shafts and arrow heads now are not repairable and should be quicker to make.</li></ul>\n<p>Notes on archery:  Archery is hard to learn. It is supposed only to be usable against creatures with fair skill and good equipment.\nTo gain skill quickest, practice with hunting arrows that have no penalties.\n</p>\n<p>All bows have a \'best distance\'. That distance is 20, 40, and 80 meters (or roughly 5, 10 and 20 tiles) for the bows.\n</p>\n<p>Shooting at shorter or longer ranges will affect the difficulty.\nArrows will be shot in the following order: 1. from quiver worn on body, 2. from quiver in inventory (or if 1 is found but is empty), 3. arrow held in hand, 4. arrow in inventory.\n</p>\n<p>If a quiver is found at 2 but it is empty, no arrow will be shot. This should give you good control over which arrows are shot.  Arrows are fired in the following order: 1. War arrows, 2. Hunting arrows, 3. shafts.  War arrows do more damage, but are slightly harder to hit with. Shafts do little damage and are hardest to hit with. \n</p>\n<ul><li>All three religions should now be able to pray at the Altar of Three.</li>\n<li>Bugfixes with /ranks.</li>\n<li>A bug where the finished item received the wrong material was fixed.</li></ul>', 86),
(18704, 4791, '060320', '060320', 'Archery/Bowyery/Fletching is in. Some wood materials are better suited than other. Examine will give a clue. Smithing now has a title. The time to log out when in enemy kingdoms is now set to 2 minutes if you have not been involved in battle.', '<ul><li>Archery/Bowyery/Fletching is in. Some wood materials are better suited than other. Examine will give a clue.</li>\n<li>Smithing now has a title.</li>\n<li>The time to log out when in enemy kingdoms is now set to 2 minutes if you have not been involved in battle.</li></ul>', 87),
(18705, 4791, '060314', '060314', 'Fixed a bug that made armour disappear if you dragged it to your hands.', '<ul><li>Fixed a bug that made armour disappear if you dragged it to your hands.</li></ul>', 88),
(18706, 4791, '060313', '060313', 'Village guards should no longer suddenly become non-citizens. Item creation and pre-finished improving now is affected by Wind of ages. Building new house walls are now slightly slower, while repairing them is faster instead. Removed some money from some very rich players that were obviously inherited from old exploits. The bug where it was possible to become killed twice in a row should be fixed.', '<ul><li>Village guards should no longer suddenly become non-citizens.</li>\n<li>Item creation and pre-finished improving now is affected by Wind of ages.</li>\n<li>Building new house walls are now slightly slower, while repairing them is faster instead.</li>\n<li>Removed some money from some very rich players that were obviously inherited from old exploits.</li>\n<li>The bug where it was possible to become killed twice in a row should be fixed.</li></ul>', 89),
(18707, 4791, '060309', '060309', 'Zombies should no longer be insta-agg when created. Stealing in villages of the opposite kingdom no longer upsets your deity. Creatures should find their way in caves better. Wind of ages cast on tools now affects improvement times.', '<ul><li>Zombies should no longer be insta-agg when created.</li>\n<li>Stealing in villages of the opposite kingdom no longer upsets your deity.</li>\n<li>Creatures should find their way in caves better.</li>\n<li>Wind of ages cast on tools now affects improvement times.</li></ul>', 90),
(18708, 4791, '060307', '060307', 'Guards should not start hunting enemies outside the deed, and not assign all guards either. Managing gates have been moved from the village settings management interface. The village settings management should work better.', '<ul><li>Guards should not start hunting enemies outside the deed, and not assign all guards either.</li>\n<li>Managing gates have been moved from the village settings management interface. The village settings management should work better.</li></ul>', 91),
(18709, 4791, '060306', '060306', 'Holding/wearing armour should give more correct messages. Enchantments and the spell Sunder may no longer target locked items. Mycelium now should have a harder time surviving outside HOTS. You should now start to get warnings in village chat one week from when your village is disbanded. Newbies now wear items when they are created. More fixes with updating the color outlines of creatures. Dropping an item in a container in a barrel now should put the item in the correct container.', '<ul><li>Holding/wearing armour should give more correct messages.</li>\n<li>Enchantments and the spell Sunder may no longer target locked items.</li>\n<li>Mycelium now should have a harder time surviving outside HOTS.</li>\n<li>You should now start to get warnings in village chat one week from when your village is disbanded.</li>\n<li>Newbies now wear items when they are created.</li>\n<li>More fixes with updating the color outlines of creatures.</li>\n<li>Dropping an item in a container in a barrel now should put the item in the correct container.</li></ul>', 92),
(18710, 4791, '060303', '060303', 'Bug with kingdom guards not attacking fixed. Nobody gains skill from kingdom guards until a better solution is figured out. Reason was that you could gain too easy skill on them since they respawn and are fairly weak. IMPORTANT: You are now only invulnerable when logging off in your own kingdom! Outside it also takes 3 minutes to leave the world unless you have fought, in which case it takes 5 minutes. Check /lotime to see how long it takes until you leave the world.', '<ul><li>Bug with kingdom guards not attacking fixed. Nobody gains skill from kingdom guards until a better solution is figured out. Reason was that you could gain too easy skill on them since they respawn and are fairly weak.</li>\n<li>IMPORTANT: You are now only invulnerable when logging off in your own kingdom! Outside it also takes 3 minutes to leave the world unless you have fought, in which case it takes 5 minutes. Check /lotime to see how long it takes until you leave the world.</li></ul>', 93),
(18711, 4791, '060302', '060302', 'Tunneling while in the cave should generate fewer buggy shudders. You will now get a warning if a deep shaft will emerge. HOTS now gain no skill fighting kingdom guards, since they theoretically provide endless training with no risk involved. Attitude (the red/green/blue aura) has been reprogrammed, and should better reflect whether a creature will attack. New traders now start out with very little money instead of one gold as they used to. They will receive money distributed by the king instead. Guards spamming that they will help each other should be reduced. Pumpkins now should work for steaks. Cooking containers should no longer have less space after a few dishes.', '<ul><li>Tunneling while in the cave should generate fewer buggy shudders. You will now get a warning if a deep shaft will emerge.</li>\n<li>HOTS now gain no skill fighting kingdom guards, since they theoretically provide endless training with no risk involved.</li>\n<li>Attitude (the red/green/blue aura) has been reprogrammed, and should better reflect whether a creature will attack.</li>\n<li>New traders now start out with very little money instead of one gold as they used to. They will receive money distributed by the king instead.</li>\n<li>Guards spamming that they will help each other should be reduced.</li>\n<li>Pumpkins now should work for steaks.</li>\n<li>Cooking containers should no longer have less space after a few dishes.</li></ul>', 94),
(18712, 4791, '060227', '060227', 'Steaks now properly need to be made in a frying pan. Meat or fish with some appropriate vegetable, and no liquid. Creatures and guards should now ignore you when you are invulnerable. You are no longer invulnerable in hostile villages, when you log on or off. Spell levels have changed. Items may now only be taken from a cart or raft by the person dragging it if it is dragged. Vynora has some new spells that improves items. Libila has one as well. They may destroy the item depending on item quality, so try them out on something cheap. Drain health now heals wounds if you have any. Pets now are tame longer than 24 hours. Sorry. Pickaxes are now in the miscellaneous skill group instead of axes. Weapon group skills increase faster, except axes. You no longer parry with axes. Creatures should leave caves more frequently. A bug with stealing fixed.', '<ul><li>Steaks now properly need to be made in a frying pan. Meat or fish with some appropriate vegetable, and no liquid.</li>\n<li>Creatures and guards should now ignore you when you are invulnerable.</li>\n<li>You are no longer invulnerable in hostile villages, when you log on or off.</li>\n<li>Spell levels have changed.</li>\n<li>Items may now only be taken from a cart or raft by the person dragging it if it is dragged.</li>\n<li>Vynora has some new spells that improves items. Libila has one as well. They may destroy the item depending on item quality, so try them out on something cheap.</li>\n<li>Drain health now heals wounds if you have any.</li>\n<li>Pets now are tame longer than 24 hours. Sorry.</li>\n<li>Pickaxes are now in the miscellaneous skill group instead of axes. Weapon group skills increase faster, except axes. You no longer parry with axes.</li>\n<li>Creatures should leave caves more frequently.</li>\n<li>A bug with stealing fixed.</li></ul>', 95),
(18713, 4791, '060222', '060222', 'A bug with pets made some of them disappear. It should work now though, but you have to find new pets if you lost yours. Giving away pets works now. Very strong aggressive creatures will now break down walls and fences near them if they are disturbed by them.', '<ul><li>A bug with pets made some of them disappear. It should work now though, but you have to find new pets if you lost yours.</li>\n<li>Giving away pets works now.</li>\n<li>Very strong aggressive creatures will now break down walls and fences near them if they are disturbed by them.</li></ul>', 96),
(18714, 4791, '060220', '060220', 'Fumbling with repairing walls and fences will no longer insta-destroy them (was a bug). Taming carnivores with a corpse only works if the corpse is fairly undamaged. Small problem when being teleported near doors fixed. Followers of Libila now get less stamina drain when moving on mycelium. Tamed animals (not dominated or zombies) will now leave the world when you do (as soon as it has quit fighting), unless you order it to stay online. Fixed a bug with village voting.', '<ul><li>Fumbling with repairing walls and fences will no longer insta-destroy them (was a bug).</li>\n<li>Taming carnivores with a corpse only works if the corpse is fairly undamaged.</li>\n<li>Small problem when being teleported near doors fixed.</li>\n<li>Followers of Libila now get less stamina drain when moving on mycelium.</li>\n<li>Tamed animals (not dominated or zombies) will now leave the world when you do (as soon as it has quit fighting), unless you order it to stay online.</li>\n<li>Fixed a bug with village voting.</li></ul>', 97),
(18715, 4791, '060217', '060217', 'Fighting skills have been restored for those who lost them. Thorns will no longer damage GMs and are tougher to cut down. Bug with stealing items from deeds fixed.', '<ul><li>Fighting skills have been restored for those who lost them.</li>\n<li>Thorns will no longer damage GMs and are tougher to cut down.</li>\n<li>Bug with stealing items from deeds fixed.</li></ul>', 98),
(18716, 4791, '060216', '060216', 'More on pets: Bug where the pet did not fight back fixed.\nTaming should now work on deeds.\nYou can now give away pets to friendly players.\nPets should now have blue outlines to people from the same kingdom with positive reputation.\nUsually non-aggressive creatures may now attack you if you fail your taming skill.\nUnicorns are much harder to tame. Beware of old thorn bushes! Followers of Fo may pass unhindered if faithful enough. Stamina drain is a bit higher when moving. Followers with high faith are inspired in their deities favored terrains, and tire less there. Vynora get bonus on roads, Magranon on rock, and Fo on grass, dirt, trees. Followers of Vynora with high faith have slower skill decay (they already get bonus when learning all skills if they have enough favor). Followers of Magranon now receive skill bonuses in fighting if faith and favor are high. Village and Area (i.e Server) history are now gathered properly and may be found on the village tokens. Found a bug where unexpected shuddering occured when mining south.', '<ul><li>More on pets:</li></ul>\n<p>Bug where the pet did not fight back fixed.\nTaming should now work on deeds.\nYou can now give away pets to friendly players.\nPets should now have blue outlines to people from the same kingdom with positive reputation.\nUsually non-aggressive creatures may now attack you if you fail your taming skill.\nUnicorns are much harder to tame.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Beware of old thorn bushes! Followers of Fo may pass unhindered if faithful enough.</li>\n<li>Stamina drain is a bit higher when moving. Followers with high faith are inspired in their deities favored terrains, and tire less there. Vynora get bonus on roads, Magranon on rock, and Fo on grass, dirt, trees.</li>\n<li>Followers of Vynora with high faith have slower skill decay (they already get bonus when learning all skills if they have enough favor). Followers of Magranon now receive skill bonuses in fighting if faith and favor are high.</li>\n<li>Village and Area (i.e Server) history are now gathered properly and may be found on the village tokens.</li>\n<li>Found a bug where unexpected shuddering occured when mining south.</li></ul>', 99),
(18717, 4791, '060214', '060214', 'Bugfixes for pets: They should now be much harder to tame.\nYou now need food and stamina to tame pets.\nReborn pets are now more menacingly called Zombies. Old pets keep their names though.\nZombies should still alert the village guards when raised, but the attack should cease immediately.\nPets should not be able to attack themselves.\nUsing a pet to grief same-side players now results in skill-loss.\nCows and other creatures should now hunt at least a little.\nPets should now find their way a bit better.\nZombies should be more aggressive.\nZombies now have a lifespan of about 1 rl day.\nYou should no longer be able to trade with Zombies.', '<ul><li>Bugfixes for pets:</li></ul>\n<p>They should now be much harder to tame.\nYou now need food and stamina to tame pets.\nReborn pets are now more menacingly called Zombies. Old pets keep their names though.\nZombies should still alert the village guards when raised, but the attack should cease immediately.\nPets should not be able to attack themselves.\nUsing a pet to grief same-side players now results in skill-loss.\nCows and other creatures should now hunt at least a little.\nPets should now find their way a bit better.\nZombies should be more aggressive.\nZombies now have a lifespan of about 1 rl day.\nYou should no longer be able to trade with Zombies.\n</p>', 100),
(18718, 4791, '060213', '060213', 'Pets! Everyone may now tame animals. Followers of Libila have a harder time though. Followers of Libila may raise souls from corpses with a spell. These creatures may be equipped if human. \nTheir skills are lower than the original creature. \nFollowers of Magranon may dominate monsters, even the dragons (good luck). \nFollowers of Vynora will receive something special as well later/soon. \nYou may lead pets with ropes. Pets will attack and be attacked by creatures that would attack you. \nIf you log off, your pet should be safe from same kingdom village and kingdom guards. \nIf the animal is an aggressive creature, it will attack people with negative reputation or from other kingdoms. \nThis means they may work as watchdogs. Pets will stay logged on for now when you leave the game. Praying now goes faster overall, but the initial amount you receive is limited. Enchantments now work on items with ql 70+ instead of 90+.', '<ul><li>Pets! Everyone may now tame animals. Followers of Libila have a harder time though.</li></ul>\n<p>Followers of Libila may raise souls from corpses with a spell. These creatures may be equipped if human. \nTheir skills are lower than the original creature. \nFollowers of Magranon may dominate monsters, even the dragons (good luck). \nFollowers of Vynora will receive something special as well later/soon. \nYou may lead pets with ropes. Pets will attack and be attacked by creatures that would attack you. \nIf you log off, your pet should be safe from same kingdom village and kingdom guards. \nIf the animal is an aggressive creature, it will attack people with negative reputation or from other kingdoms. \nThis means they may work as watchdogs. Pets will stay logged on for now when you leave the game. \n</p>\n<ul><li>Praying now goes faster overall, but the initial amount you receive is limited.</li>\n<li>Enchantments now work on items with ql 70+ instead of 90+.</li></ul>', 101),
(18719, 4791, '060206', '060206', 'Casting spells, taunting and shieldbashing should now be interrupted if the target dies. Excessive wall/fence damage on unguarded deeds fixed. Spellcasting through windows is prevented for now. Mining graphical bugs should no longer be possible. Some players may now receive the possibility to mute other players to regulate foul language in kingdom chats, so keep it clean.', '<ul><li>Casting spells, taunting and shieldbashing should now be interrupted if the target dies.</li>\n<li>Excessive wall/fence damage on unguarded deeds fixed.</li>\n<li>Spellcasting through windows is prevented for now.</li>\n<li>Mining graphical bugs should no longer be possible.</li>\n<li>Some players may now receive the possibility to mute other players to regulate foul language in kingdom chats, so keep it clean.</li></ul>', 102),
(18720, 4791, '060131b', '060131b', 'Mining should work better now, and yield some more information. A reason for disappearing items fixed.', '<ul><li>Mining should work better now, and yield some more information.</li>\n<li>A reason for disappearing items fixed.</li></ul>', 103),
(18721, 4791, '060131', '060131', 'Debugging. A few reboots with bug fixes may occur after this one. Dye now uses up more scrap material. * Attacking a village wall or fence now should draw the guards out. Respawning guards should look for enemies more efficiently now.', '<ul><li>Debugging. A few reboots with bug fixes may occur after this one.</li>\n<li>Dye now uses up more scrap material. * Attacking a village wall or fence now should draw the guards out.</li>\n<li>Respawning guards should look for enemies more efficiently now.</li></ul>', 104),
(18722, 4791, '060128', '060128', 'Creatures should now enter unfinished buildings Fixed an interesting bug with mining flint. Thanks, Swisscheese.', '<ul><li>Creatures should now enter unfinished buildings</li>\n<li>Fixed an interesting bug with mining flint. Thanks, Swisscheese.</li></ul>', 105),
(18723, 4791, '060126', '060126', 'Two types of fish only no longer yield a steak. Found a bug with tunneling. Deed guards may now walk through walls and doors. Disappearing item bugs fixed, and a bug where creatures could become irresponsive. You should now be able to find flint, so you can create steel and flints.', '<ul><li>Two types of fish only no longer yield a steak.</li>\n<li>Found a bug with tunneling.</li>\n<li>Deed guards may now walk through walls and doors.</li>\n<li>Disappearing item bugs fixed, and a bug where creatures could become irresponsive.</li>\n<li>You should now be able to find flint, so you can create steel and flints.</li></ul>', 106),
(18724, 4791, '060124', '060124', 'Most fruits are now combinable. Steaks can now be made also from corn, or onion, or bread. Dog statues can now be painted as well. New color outlines fix. The bug where players could not move after login fixed. Creatures stuck underground should be destroyed.', '<ul><li>Most fruits are now combinable.</li>\n<li>Steaks can now be made also from corn, or onion, or bread.</li>\n<li>Dog statues can now be painted as well.</li>\n<li>New color outlines fix.</li>\n<li>The bug where players could not move after login fixed.</li>\n<li>Creatures stuck underground should be destroyed.</li></ul>', 107),
(18725, 4791, '060123', '060123', 'Pigs now eat pig food:P. Some items that were unusable on ground now should be usable. Disconnects at log on should be more rare, at the cost of a bit slower initial terrain rendering. You now need pumpkin or potato to make steaks. Color outlines fix for aggressive creatures from other kingdoms.', '<ul><li>Pigs now eat pig food:P.</li>\n<li>Some items that were unusable on ground now should be usable.</li>\n<li>Disconnects at log on should be more rare, at the cost of a bit slower initial terrain rendering.</li>\n<li>You now need pumpkin or potato to make steaks.</li>\n<li>Color outlines fix for aggressive creatures from other kingdoms.</li></ul>', 108),
(18726, 4791, '060118', '060118', 'Trader demands tweaked a bit. Expect much less cave-ins. It should now be possible to use the /stuck command more then once. Banked containers now show up when you open the bank. A cause for lag may be fixed. Leading cows out of caves does not make them untouchable. Ores will now respawn in a regional fashion, so certain ores will be more common in certain areas. This will work for caveins and new maps. Practice dolls, ovens and other items will now show what is needed to improve or finish them.', '<ul><li>Trader demands tweaked a bit.</li>\n<li>Expect much less cave-ins.</li>\n<li>It should now be possible to use the /stuck command more then once.</li>\n<li>Banked containers now show up when you open the bank.</li>\n<li>A cause for lag may be fixed.</li>\n<li>Leading cows out of caves does not make them untouchable.</li>\n<li>Ores will now respawn in a regional fashion, so certain ores will be more common in certain areas. This will work for caveins and new maps.</li>\n<li>Practice dolls, ovens and other items will now show what is needed to improve or finish them.</li></ul>', 109),
(18727, 4791, '060116', '060116', 'When villages disband, all the gates are unlocked Cave decay has been slowed down, and corrected. Now reinforcing both walls on the side of a passage stops decay for the center tile, as will reinforcing all three walls around a dead end. Reminder: You can not be killed by cave decay. People seem to think so. Bug fixed where if you used only a weapon in your left hand it increased barehand fighting. Note that your primary weapon should always be in your right hand. You will use your left hand much less often. You now have a small chance to parry with your left hand weapon as well. You may now correctly change kingdoms up to 3 times instead of 1. Money has been redistributed between the traders and the king to test the economy.', '<ul><li>When villages disband, all the gates are unlocked</li>\n<li>Cave decay has been slowed down, and corrected. Now reinforcing both walls on the side of a passage stops decay for the center tile, as will reinforcing all three walls around a dead end.</li></ul>\n<p>Reminder: You can not be killed by cave decay. People seem to think so.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Bug fixed where if you used only a weapon in your left hand it increased barehand fighting. Note that your primary weapon should always be in your right hand. You will use your left hand much less often. You now have a small chance to parry with your left hand weapon as well.</li>\n<li>You may now correctly change kingdoms up to 3 times instead of 1.</li>\n<li>Money has been redistributed between the traders and the king to test the economy.</li></ul>', 110),
(18728, 4791, '060112', '060112', 'Bug with door locks fixed. They will now always be locked when you attach them. Possible cause for creatures disappearing underground fixed.', '<ul><li>Bug with door locks fixed. They will now always be locked when you attach them.</li>\n<li>Possible cause for creatures disappearing underground fixed.</li></ul>', 111);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18729, 4791, '060111', '060111', 'If you reconnect inside a cave wall the game will try put you on a safe tile nearby, so it should be extremely uncommon. One possible cause for periodic lag removed. Bug with tempering fixed. Various other small bugs and improvements.', '<ul><li>If you reconnect inside a cave wall the game will try put you on a safe tile nearby, so it should be extremely uncommon.</li>\n<li>One possible cause for periodic lag removed.</li>\n<li>Bug with tempering fixed.</li>\n<li>Various other small bugs and improvements.</li></ul>', 112),
(18730, 4791, '060110', '060110', 'Cave decay is now implented. This means: Always bring a pickaxe, food and drink when going underground. You won\'t get killed by it right now, but items will be destroyed. The decay rate is fairly slow. Minerals may respawn. Reinforcing walls help. Large chambers decay quicker. Entrances may also cave in. Stamina-regen-movement delay removed, and fighting-stamina-regen-delay set to 2 seconds. You may now plan a new structure after 4 days unless your old structure becomes finished before that. Golden altars should now be improvable again. Prices of armour chains and cloth strings now better reflect similar product prices.', '<ul><li>Cave decay is now implented. This means: Always bring a pickaxe, food and drink when going underground. You won\'t get killed by it right now, but items will be destroyed.</li></ul>\n<p>The decay rate is fairly slow. Minerals may respawn. Reinforcing walls help. Large chambers decay quicker. Entrances may also cave in. \n</p>\n<ul><li>Stamina-regen-movement delay removed, and fighting-stamina-regen-delay set to 2 seconds.</li>\n<li>You may now plan a new structure after 4 days unless your old structure becomes finished before that.</li>\n<li>Golden altars should now be improvable again.</li>\n<li>Prices of armour chains and cloth strings now better reflect similar product prices.</li></ul>', 113),
(18731, 4791, '060105b', '060105b', 'Fighting skillgain bug fixed.', '<ul><li>Fighting skillgain bug fixed.</li></ul>', 114),
(18732, 4791, '060105', '060105', 'FIGHTING SKILL UP AND RUNNING AGAIN. The old skills were not restored, since they were \'dirty\' and we want to test skill progress and balance with this system. You now gain no fighting skill if your stamina is at the bottom, or if you or your opponent fight barehanded with a skill over 20. If you have killed your opponent during the last hour you gain a lot less skill also. Expect further tweaks to this system. Lost bodyparts should reappear. Guards skills have been centered around 30, 50 and 80 for the various guard types. Catapult bug fixes, including the very broken aiming algorithm and the too high damage dealt. Skillgain changed a bit, so that you will now gain skill less often for very easy tasks.', '<ul><li>FIGHTING SKILL UP AND RUNNING AGAIN. The old skills were not restored, since they were \'dirty\' and we want to test skill progress and balance with this system. You now gain no fighting skill if your stamina is at the bottom, or if you or your opponent fight barehanded with a skill over 20. If you have killed your opponent during the last hour you gain a lot less skill also. Expect further tweaks to this system.</li>\n<li>Lost bodyparts should reappear.</li>\n<li>Guards skills have been centered around 30, 50 and 80 for the various guard types.</li>\n<li>Catapult bug fixes, including the very broken aiming algorithm and the too high damage dealt.</li>\n<li>Skillgain changed a bit, so that you will now gain skill less often for very easy tasks.</li></ul>', 115),
(18733, 4791, '060103', '060103', 'FIGHTING SKILL RESET. Most fighting related skills capped at 30 until we have a satisfying solution to afk skillgain. You may no longer use catapults to shoot your live bodyparts away. New lag code is in place. It should be unnoticable for the most part. You who catapulted your bodyparts: login again if you are messed up. It should work.', '<ul><li>FIGHTING SKILL RESET. Most fighting related skills capped at 30 until we have a satisfying solution to afk skillgain.</li>\n<li>You may no longer use catapults to shoot your live bodyparts away.</li>\n<li>New lag code is in place. It should be unnoticable for the most part.</li>\n<li>You who catapulted your bodyparts: login again if you are messed up. It should work.</li></ul>', 116),
(18734, 4791, '060102', '060102', 'Fighting has changed some: Mauls are now slower than axes and swords. Swords are much better at parrying, and take less damage when parrying. Axe and sword damage has been adjusted upwards. You no longer gain skill if either the attacker or the defender is link-less. Prices for combined items now correctly affect trader demand. Consecutive teleports due to a lag teleport should not be as common. Walking through wall plans should no longer render a teleport. Metal altars no longer require heating to be finished or improved. Citizens that may destroy walls and fences now should be able to perform these actions a lot quicker within their own village. Improving walls should be possible again like before but only for finished walls. A bug made it so only the deed owner could continue building on a house. Fixed. There is now a small catapult available.', '<ul><li>Fighting has changed some: Mauls are now slower than axes and swords. Swords are much better at parrying, and take less damage when parrying. Axe and sword damage has been adjusted upwards. You no longer gain skill if either the attacker or the defender is link-less.</li>\n<li>Prices for combined items now correctly affect trader demand. Consecutive teleports due to a lag teleport should not be as common.</li>\n<li>Walking through wall plans should no longer render a teleport. Metal altars no longer require heating to be finished or improved.</li>\n<li>Citizens that may destroy walls and fences now should be able to perform these actions a lot quicker within their own village. Improving walls should be possible again like before but only for finished walls.</li>\n<li>A bug made it so only the deed owner could continue building on a house. Fixed.</li>\n<li>There is now a small catapult available.</li></ul>', 117),
(18735, 4629, 'Description', 'Description', 'The foot part of a bed, consisting of two feet joined by planks.', '<p><i>The foot part of a bed, consisting of two feet joined by planks.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18736, 4629, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the small nails affects the success chance when creating. The small nails used to create the foot board are damaged if you fail and the plank is also damaged. Wood type is determined by the type of the last wooden piece attached.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Small_nails\" title=\"Small nails\">small nails</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The small nails used to create the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">foot board</a> are damaged if you fail and the plank is also damaged.</li>\n<li>Wood type is determined by the type of the last wooden piece attached.</li></ul>', 1),
(18737, 4628, 'Description', 'Description', 'The head part of a bed, consisting of two feet joined by planks.', '<p><i>The head part of a bed, consisting of two feet joined by planks.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18738, 4628, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to create a bed .', '<ul><li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">bed</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18739, 4628, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the small nails affects the success chance when creating. The small nails used to create the head board are damaged if you fail and the plank is also damaged.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Small_nails\" title=\"Small nails\">small nails</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The small nails used to create the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">head board</a> are damaged if you fail and the plank is also damaged.</li></ul>', 2),
(18740, 4630, 'Description', 'Description', 'The sleeping part of a bed, lacking the feet that keeps you above the moisture and rats.', '<p><i>The sleeping part of a bed, lacking the feet that keeps you above the moisture and rats.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18741, 4630, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to create a bed .', '<ul><li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">bed</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18742, 4630, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the large nails affects the success chance when creating. The large nails and plank used to create the bed frame are damaged if you fail.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a> used to create the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">bed frame</a> are damaged if you fail.</li></ul>', 2),
(18746, 1243, 'Description', 'Description', 'Fine carpentry consists of the more difficult carpentry functions such as creating barrels and carts. Fine carpentry is a sub-skill of carpentry .', '<p>Fine carpentry consists of the more difficult carpentry functions such as creating barrels and carts.\n</p>\n<p>Fine carpentry is a sub-skill of <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(18747, 1243, 'Items', 'Items', 'See Fine carpentry items', '<p>See <i><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fine_carpentry_items\" title=\"Category:Fine carpentry items\"> Fine carpentry items</a></i>\n</p>', 1),
(18748, 1243, 'Minimum Creation Requirements', 'Minimum_Creation_Requirements', 'Item name Minimum fine carpentry level Archery tower 40 Alchemist\'s cupboard 20 Armchair 1 Armour stand 1 Axe display 1 Ballista 60 Battering ram 1 Bed 1 Bed frame 1 Bee hive 25 Bow rack 1 Bulk container unit 50 Canopy bed 65 Cartography table 20 Chair 1 Cheese drill 1 Chicken coop 50 Coffer 24 Creature transporter 25 Crow\'s nest 1 Cupboard 40 Decorative ship 1 Empty high bookshelf 35 Empty low bookshelf 25 Explorer tent 1 Fine high chair 60 Fishing rod 1 Fishing rod rack 1 Floor loom 1 Foot board 1 Fruit press 1 Head board 1 High bookshelf 35 High chair 50 Huge oil barrel 1 Huge tub 1 Ink brush 1 Larder 1 Large bar table 25 Large barrel 1 Large cart 1 Large chest 1 Large dining table 1 Large pantry cupboard 50 Large sign 1 Leggat 1 Lounge chair 40 Low bookshelf 25 Machine mount 60 Market stall 1 Medium fishing reel 1 Military tent 1 Pauper\'s high chair 40 Pavilion 1 Pet bowl 1 Pointing sign 1 Polearms rack 1 Press 1 Rope tool 1 Round table 1 Royal lounge chaise 70 Royal throne 70 Saddle rack 1 Shield rack 1 Ship transporter 15 Shop sign 1 Small barrel 1 Small bedside table 25 Small bucket 1 Small cart 1 Small catapult 1 Small chest 1 Small sign 1 Small square table 1 Small tripod table 30 Small wheel 1 Small wheel axle 1 Small wine barrel 1 Spinning wheel 30 Spirit house 1 Spirit mansion 1 Stamp box 1 Stool 1 Strange device 40 Sword display 1 Tapestry stand 1 Trebuchet 80 Wagon 40 Wardrobe 55 Weapons rack 1 Wood reel 1 Wooden altar 1 Wooden bench 35 Note that even with the above mentioned skill, you might not be able to craft an item. Tool quality also impacts the chances.', '<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Item name</th>\n<th>Minimum fine carpentry level\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Archery_tower\" title=\"Archery tower\">Archery tower</a></td>\n<td>40\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Alchemist%27s_cupboard\" title=\"Alchemist\'s cup