.php/Wooden_altar\" title=\"Wooden altar\">Wooden altar</a></td>\n<td>1\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_bench\" title=\"Wooden bench\">Wooden bench</a></td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Note that even with the above mentioned skill, you might not be able to craft an item. Tool quality also impacts the chances.\n</p>', 2),
(18749, 1243, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Carpentry > Fine carpentry Body > Body control Mind > Mind logic', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; Fine carpentry</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>', 3),
(18750, 1243, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Fine Carpenter at 50 skill Renowned Fine Carpenter at 70 skill Mighty Fine Carpenter at 90 skill Mighty Fine Splinter at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Fine Carpenter at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Renowned Fine Carpenter at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Mighty Fine Carpenter at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Mighty Fine Splinter at 100 skill</li></ul>', 4),
(18757, 1127, 'Description', 'Description', 'Bow strings are needed for using bows and for creating bow traps . They are made out of wemp fibre using a rope tool.', '<p>Bow strings are needed for using <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bows\" title=\"Bows\">bows</a> and for creating <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_trap\" title=\"Bow trap\">bow traps</a>. They are made out of <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a> using a rope tool. \n</p>', 0),
(18758, 1127, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The quality of the bow string can affect the hit chance of the bow. Higher quality also reduces the chance that the string breaks when the bow is used. The highest quality bow string one can make ultimately depends on the quality level of the wemp used. For example, with 99ql wemp, yet a relatively low quality rope tool and low ropemaking skill, one still has a chance at making a 99ql bow string. Bow string is also a widely favored choice for training the Ropemaking skill, as it only uses 0.013kg of wemp fibre with each attempt.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the bow string can affect the hit chance of the bow. Higher quality also reduces the chance that the string breaks when the bow is used.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The highest quality bow string one can make ultimately depends on the quality level of the wemp used. For example, with 99ql wemp, yet a relatively low quality rope tool and low ropemaking skill, one still has a chance at making a 99ql bow string.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Bow string is also a widely favored choice for training the Ropemaking skill, as it only uses 0.013kg of wemp fibre with each attempt.</li></ul>', 1),
(18759, 1938, 'Description', 'Description', 'Stone cutting skill involves creating bricks, statues, and other items purely of stone. Stone cutting is a sub-skill of masonry .', '<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Stone cutting</a> skill involves creating bricks, statues, and other items purely of stone.\n</p>\n<p>Stone cutting is a sub-skill of <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(18760, 1938, 'Items', 'Items', 'See: Category:Stone cutting items', '<p>See: <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Stone_cutting_items\" title=\"Category:Stone cutting items\">Category:Stone cutting items</a>\n</p>', 1),
(18761, 1938, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Masonry > Stone cutting Body > Body strength Mind > Mind logic', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">Masonry</a> &gt; Stone cutting</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li></ul>', 2),
(18762, 1938, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Sculptor at 50 skill Artist at 70 skill Michelangelo at 90 skill Chiseled to perfection at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Sculptor at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Artist at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Michelangelo at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Chiseled to perfection at 100 skill</li></ul>', 3),
(18763, 1759, 'Description', 'Description', 'A real sized statue of a small cute boy.', '<p><i>A real sized statue of a small cute boy.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18764, 1759, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statues can be improved with stone or marble shards and a stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.', '<ul><li>Statues can be improved with stone or marble shards and a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.</li></ul>', 1),
(18765, 1747, 'Description', 'Description', 'A statue of a large guard dog, fairly menacing yet lovingly portrayed.', '<p><i>A statue of a large guard dog, fairly menacing yet lovingly portrayed.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18766, 1747, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statues can be improved with stone shards and stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.', '<ul><li>Statues can be improved with <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.</li></ul>', 1),
(18767, 1758, 'Description', 'Description', 'A real sized statue of a small cute girl.', '<p><i>A real sized statue of a small cute girl.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18768, 1758, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statues can be improved with stone or marble shards and a stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.', '<ul><li>Statues can be improved with stone or marble shards and a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength is required for loading them.</li></ul>', 1),
(18769, 1752, 'Description', 'Description', 'A beautiful almost man-sized statue of a nymph, wearing only a thin robe as garment.', '<p><i>A beautiful almost man-sized statue of a nymph, wearing only a thin robe as garment.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18770, 1752, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statues can be improved with stone shards or marble shards and a stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\',\'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the \'Place\' command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li>Statues can be improved with <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Marble_shards\" title=\"Marble shards\">marble shards</a> and a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\',\'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the \'Place\' command.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(18771, 1762, 'Description', 'Description', 'A huge ugly troll, about one and a half times your size.', '<p><i>A huge ugly troll, about one and a half times your size.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18772, 1762, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statue of troll is a fairly large decorative statue and therefore a minimum of 23.6 body strength is required to hold the combined stone shards required to create. Statues can be improved with stone shards and stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\',\'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the \'Place\' command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).', '<ul><li><b>Statue of troll</b> is a fairly large decorative statue and therefore a minimum of 23.6 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> is required to hold the combined stone shards required to create.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Statues can be improved with <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with \'Push\',\'Pull\' and \"Turn\" commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the \'Place\' command.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons (23 body strength required for loading them).</li></ul>', 1),
(18773, 1754, 'Description', 'Description', 'A horrifying statue of a demon, complete with horns, claws, sharp teeth, mad piercing eyes and the tail curled around one of its goat legs.', '<p><i>A horrifying statue of a demon, complete with horns, claws, sharp teeth, mad piercing eyes and the tail curled around one of its goat legs.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18774, 1754, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Statues can be improved with stone shards and stone chisel . Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move>Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command. Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.', '<ul><li>Statues can be improved with <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a>.</li>\n<li>Statues cannot be picked up by hand once finished, but can be moved with Move&gt;Push, Pull, and Turn commands. They can also be moved to the center of a tile, or placed in a certain spot using the Place command.</li>\n<li>Statues can be loaded into large carts or wagons. 23 body strength required for loading.</li></ul>', 1),
(18775, 4193, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small lump of pure gold.', '<p><i>A small lump of pure gold.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18776, 4193, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting gold ore in a forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns one 0.1kg gold lump per 20kg of gold ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_ore\" title=\"Gold ore\">gold ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns one 0.1kg gold lump per 20kg of gold ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(18777, 4193, 'Enchanting', 'Enchanting', 'Will be faster to use if enchanted with Wind of ages . Skill experience boost if enchanted with Circle of cunning Enchantments on gold lumps will degrade over time. You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one.', '<ul><li>Will be faster to use if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Wind_of_ages\" title=\"Wind of ages\">Wind of ages</a>.</li>\n<li>Skill experience boost if enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Circle_of_cunning\" title=\"Circle of cunning\">Circle of cunning</a></li>\n<li>Enchantments on gold lumps will degrade over time.</li>\n<li>You can keep using the enchantments by combining more lump into the enchanted one.</li></ul>', 2),
(18778, 4193, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be foraged from Mineral debris nodes. Gold items are worth more to a trader than their equivalence in silver. Higher QL forges , campfires , and ovens will smelt the ore faster. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>Can be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forage\" title=\"Forage\">foraged</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a> nodes.</li>\n<li>Gold items are worth more to a <a href=\"/index.php/Trader\" title=\"Trader\">trader</a> than their equivalence in silver.</li>\n<li>Higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">ovens</a> will smelt the ore faster.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18779, 4193, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See List of gold products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from gold.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gold_products\" title=\"Category:Gold products\">List of gold products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from gold.</li></ul>', 4),
(18780, 4192, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small lump of pure silver. Silver lump comes from the melting silver ore . This process returns 0.1kg of silver lump per 20kg of silver ore.', '<p><i>A small lump of pure silver.</i>\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Silver lump</a> comes from the melting <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_ore\" title=\"Silver ore\">silver ore</a>. This process returns 0.1kg of silver lump per 20kg of silver ore.\n</p>', 0),
(18781, 4192, 'Method', 'Method', 'To create a silver lump you\'ll need 20 kg of silver ore and a heat source (could be a forge or a campfire ). You must put the silver ore into the heat source and wait till it is glowing from heat. This might take anywhere from 10 minutes to nearly an hour, depending on the quality of the silver ore and the quality of the fire. Once the silver ore is glowing from heat it will turn into a 0.1kg silver lump , which can then be used on either a large anvil or small anvil .', '<p>To create a silver lump you\'ll need 20 kg of silver ore and a heat source (could be a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>). You must put the silver ore into the heat source and wait till it is <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Glowing\" title=\"Glowing\">glowing</a> from heat. This might take anywhere from 10 minutes to nearly an hour, depending on the quality of the silver ore and the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the fire. Once the silver ore is glowing from heat it will turn into a 0.1kg <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">silver lump</a>, which can then be used on either a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">large anvil</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Small_anvil\" title=\"Small anvil\">small anvil</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(18782, 4192, 'Note', 'Note', 'This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron . Low quality Silver lumps can be foraged from Mineral debris Resource nodes .', '<ul><li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li>\n<li>Low quality Silver lumps can be foraged from <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(18783, 4192, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See List of Silver products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from silver.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Silver_products\" title=\"Category:Silver products\">List of Silver products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from silver.</li></ul>', 3),
(18784, 4191, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lump of pure red copper.', '<p><i>A lump of pure red copper.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18785, 4191, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting copper ore in a forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns 1.0kg of copper lump per 20kg of copper ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_ore\" title=\"Copper ore\">copper ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns 1.0kg of <b>copper lump</b> per 20kg of copper ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(18786, 4191, 'Note', 'Note', 'This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(18787, 4191, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Green dye requires copper. See List of Copper products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from copper.', '<ul><li>Green <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a> requires copper.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Copper_products\" title=\"Category:Copper products\">List of Copper products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from copper.</li></ul>', 3),
(18788, 2789, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lump of light tin.', '<p><i>A lump of light tin.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18789, 2789, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting tin ore in a forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns 0.5kg of tin lump per 20kg of tin ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Tin_ore\" title=\"Tin ore\">tin ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns 0.5kg of <b>tin lump</b> per 20kg of tin ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(18790, 2789, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to create bronze when combined with copper . See List of Tin products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from tin.', '<ul><li>Used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Bronze_lump\" title=\"Bronze lump\">bronze</a> when combined with <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">copper</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Tin_products\" title=\"Category:Tin products\">List of Tin products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from tin.</li></ul>', 2),
(18791, 2789, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Higher QL forges , campfires , and ovens will smelt the ore faster. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>Higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">ovens</a> will smelt the ore faster.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18792, 2791, 'Description', 'Description', 'A grey and white lump of zinc.', '<p><i>A grey and white lump of zinc.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18793, 2791, 'Creation', 'Creation', 'Produced by smelting zinc ore in a forge , campfire , or oven . Smelting returns 1.0kg of zinc lump per 20kg of zinc ore.', '<ul><li>Produced by smelting <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_ore\" title=\"Zinc ore\">zinc ore</a> in a <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forge</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfire</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">oven</a>.</li>\n<li>Smelting returns 1.0kg of <b>zinc lump</b> per 20kg of zinc ore.</li></ul>', 1),
(18794, 2791, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to create brass when combined with copper . Used to create white dye when combined with water . See list of Zinc products See metal products list for more items that can be made from zinc.', '<ul><li>Used to create <a href=\"/index.php/Brass_lump\" title=\"Brass lump\">brass</a> when combined with <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">copper</a>.</li>\n<li>Used to create white <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a> when combined with <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Zinc_products\" title=\"Category:Zinc products\">list of Zinc products</a></li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from zinc.</li></ul>', 2),
(18795, 2791, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Higher QL forges , campfires , and ovens will smelt the ore faster. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>Higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Campfire\" title=\"Campfire\">campfires</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">ovens</a> will smelt the ore faster.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 3),
(18796, 4195, 'Description', 'Description', 'A heavy lump of dark steel. Tools made from steel take 20% less damage from use than similar quality iron versions.', '<p><i>A heavy lump of dark steel.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Tools made from steel take 20% less damage from use than similar quality iron versions.\n</p>', 0),
(18797, 4195, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A minimum of 0.20kg for both iron and coal is needed for creation. For both materials, regardless of how large a bundle may be, only 0.20kg is used. A success consumes 0.20kg iron and 0.20kg of coal and results in a 0.40kg steel lump. A failed attempt decreases both the charcoal and the iron lumps\' weight by 0.04kg. The quality of the charcoal affects the success chance as well as the likelihood the lump will be high quality. The quality of the iron lump caps the quality of the steel lump. Only the charcoal needs to be glowing hot. Any enchantments should be cast upon the charcoal. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>A minimum of 0.20kg for both iron and coal is needed for creation. For both materials, regardless of how large a bundle may be, only 0.20kg is used.</li>\n<li>A success consumes 0.20kg iron and 0.20kg of coal and results in a 0.40kg steel lump.</li>\n<li>A failed attempt decreases both the charcoal and the iron lumps\' weight by 0.04kg.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the charcoal affects the success chance as well as the likelihood the lump will be high quality.</li>\n<li>The quality of the iron lump caps the quality of the steel lump.</li>\n<li>Only the charcoal needs to be glowing hot.</li>\n<li>Any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Enchantments\" title=\"Enchantments\">enchantments</a> should be cast upon the charcoal.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18798, 4195, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See List of steel products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from steel.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Steel_products\" title=\"Category:Steel products\">List of steel products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from steel.</li></ul>', 2),
(18799, 3176, 'Description', 'Description', 'A shiny yellowy red lump of brass.', '<p><i>A shiny yellowy red lump of brass.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18800, 3176, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When creating, the QL of the zinc affects your success chance. Any enchantments should be cast upon the zinc lump. The quality of the copper affects the maximum quality of the resulting lump, but since brass gets a 10% creation bonus, even to itself, it will come out higher than the ql of the copper. If you fail creating, you lose 0.01kg from both lumps. The copper and/or zinc can be combined into one lump, as only the amount required is used. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>When creating, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">zinc</a> affects your success chance.</li>\n<li>Any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Enchantments\" title=\"Enchantments\">enchantments</a> should be cast upon the zinc lump.</li>\n<li>The quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">copper</a> affects the maximum quality of the resulting lump, but since brass gets a 10% creation bonus, even to itself, it will come out higher than the ql of the copper.</li>\n<li>If you fail creating, you lose 0.01kg from both lumps.</li>\n<li>The copper and/or zinc can be combined into one lump, as only the amount required is used.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18801, 3176, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category: Brass products . Category:Any-metal_products for more items that can be made from brass.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Brass_products\" title=\"Category:Brass products\">Category: Brass products</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">Category:Any-metal_products</a> for more items that can be made from brass.</li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(18802, 3173, 'Description', 'Description', 'A red glistening lump of bronze.', '<p><i>A red glistening lump of bronze.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(18803, 3173, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The copper can be combined into one lump as only the amount required is used. The quality of the copper determines the maximum quality of the resulting bronze lumps. Since bronze has a 5% creation bonus, even to itself, the resulting lump will be higher than the copper ql. Any enchantments should be cast upon the tin lump. This metal has some special properties , especially when compared to iron .', '<ul><li>The copper can be combined into one lump as only the amount required is used.</li>\n<li>The quality of the copper determines the maximum quality of the resulting bronze lumps. Since bronze has a 5% creation bonus, even to itself, the resulting lump will be higher than the copper ql.</li>\n<li>Any <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Enchantments\" title=\"Enchantments\">enchantments</a> should be cast upon the tin lump.</li>\n<li>This metal has some <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal lumps\">special properties</a>, especially when compared to <a href=\"/index.php/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(18804, 3173, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'See list of bronze products . See metal products list for more items that can be made from bronze.', '<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bronze_products\" title=\"Category:Bronze products\">list of bronze products</a>.</li>\n<li>See <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">metal products list</a> for more items that can be made from bronze.</li></ul>', 2),
(18805, 2866, 'Description', 'Description', 'A metal lump is the melted form of a metal resource usually made by melting the ore form but, in the case of metallurgy , resources from the combined form of two materials.', '<p>A <b>metal lump</b> is the melted form of a metal resource usually made by melting the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">ore</a> form but, in the case of <a href=\"/index.php/Metallurgy\" title=\"Metallurgy\">metallurgy</a>, resources from the combined form of two materials.\n</p>', 0),
(18806, 2866, 'Base metals', 'Base_metals', 'Iron lump ( list of products ) Copper lump ( list of products ) Silver lump ( list of products ) Gold lump ( list of products ) Tin lump ( list of products ) Zinc lump ( list of products ) Lead lump ( list of products ) Empyrean lump ( list of products )', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">Iron lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Iron_products\" title=\"Category:Iron products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Copper_lump\" title=\"Copper lump\">Copper lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Copper_products\" title=\"Category:Copper products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">Silver lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Silver_products\" title=\"Category:Silver products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">Gold lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gold_products\" title=\"Category:Gold products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tin_lump\" title=\"Tin lump\">Tin lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Tin_products\" title=\"Category:Tin products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Zinc_lump\" title=\"Zinc lump\">Zinc lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Zinc_products\" title=\"Category:Zinc products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lead_lump\" title=\"Lead lump\">Lead lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Lead_products\" title=\"Category:Lead products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Empyrean_lump\" title=\"Empyrean lump\">Empyrean lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Any-metal_products\" title=\"Category:Any-metal products\">list of products</a>)</li></ul>', 1),
(18807, 2866, 'Metallurgy metals (Alloys)', 'Metallurgy_metals_.28Alloys.29', 'Steel lump ( list of products ) Brass lump ( list of products ) Bronze lump ( list of products ) Electrum lump ( list of products )', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Steel_lump\" title=\"Steel lump\">Steel lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Steel_products\" title=\"Category:Steel products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brass_lump\" title=\"Brass lump\">Brass lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Brass_products\" title=\"Category:Brass products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bronze_lump\" title=\"Bronze lump\">Bronze lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bronze_products\" title=\"Category:Bronze products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Electrum_lump\" title=\"Electrum lump\">Electrum lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Electrum_products\" title=\"Category:Electrum products\">list of products</a>)</li></ul>', 2),
(18808, 2866, 'Moon metals', 'Moon_metals', 'Glimmersteel lump ( list of products ) Adamantine lump ( list of products ) Seryll lump ( list of products )', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Glimmersteel_lump\" title=\"Glimmersteel lump\">Glimmersteel lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Glimmersteel_products\" title=\"Category:Glimmersteel products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Adamantine_lump\" title=\"Adamantine lump\">Adamantine lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Adamantine_products\" title=\"Category:Adamantine products\">list of products</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Seryll_lump\" title=\"Seryll lump\">Seryll lump</a> (<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Seryll_products\" title=\"Category:Seryll products\">list of products</a>)</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(18809, 2866, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'An enchanted lump can be combined with unenchanted lumps to maintain the enchant. Activate the enchanted lump, and combine with others. Regardless of metal type, lump ql affects how long it takes for a lump to heat to a glowing hot temperature as well as how long it actually holds that temperature. Higher ql lumps will heat up faster.', '<ul><li>An enchanted lump can be combined with unenchanted lumps to maintain the enchant. Activate the enchanted lump, and combine with others.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Regardless of metal type, lump ql affects how long it takes for a lump to heat to a glowing hot temperature as well as how long it actually holds that temperature. Higher ql lumps will heat up faster.</li></ul>', 4),
(18810, 2866, 'Table of properties', 'Table_of_properties', 'Armour Material Damage Reduction Movement Glance Adamantine 5.00% 5.00% Brass 1.00% Bronze 1.00% Copper -1.00% 1.00% -2.00% Electrum 0.50% -1.00% 2.00% Empyrean 2.00% Glimmersteel 5.00% 10.00% Gold -1.00% -5.00% 2.50% Iron Lead -2.50% -2.50% Seryll 5.00% 10.00% Silver -0.75% -2.00% 1.00% Steel 2.50% Tin -1.75% 2.00% Zinc -2.00% 2.50% Weapon Material Attack Speed Damage Dealt Armour Damage Parry Rate Extra Wound Extra Wound Type Adamantine 10.00% Brass -1.00% 5.00% Bronze -1.50% 7.50% Copper -35.00% 30.00% Poison Electrum -2.50% 5% ( Hunter creatures) Glimmersteel 10.00% Empyrean 7.5% ( Hunter creatures) 5.00% Gold -5.00% -2.50% 5.00% Iron Lead -50.00% 75.00% Poison Seryll 5.00% 5.00% Silver 10.00% ( Hunter creatures) -2.50% Steel 2.50% Tin 4.00% -7.50% -5.00% Zinc 5.00% -10.00% General Material Price Modifier Damage Taken Decay Damage Shatter Resistance Imp Speed Creation QL Repair Speed Adamantine 8x -60% -60% 15% 10% Brass 6x -5% -5% 2.50% 10% Bronze 5x -10% -15% 5% 2.50% Copper 5x 15% -5% 5% -7.50% Electrum 9x -10% -20% 15% Empyrean 9x -15% -15% 25% -15% -5% Glimmersteel 10x -40% -40% 25% 5% Gold 10x 20% -60% 20% -5% Iron Lead 0.75x 30% -20% 10% 5% -10% Seryll 12x -50% -50% 100% 5% Silver 8x 2.50% -30% 10% Steel 2.5x -20% -30% 2.50% Tin 20% -7.50% 2.50% 5% -2.50% Zinc 0.90x 25% 20% 7.50% -5% Special Material Lockpicking Bonus Holy Items (Statuettes) Unicorn Shoes Anchor Effectiveness Pendulum AOE Bash Damage Created Item QL Adamantine 5% 150% 15% 7.50% 10% Brass 90% 2.50% 5% Bronze 85% 5% 2.50% Copper -5% 95% -5% -10% Electrum YES YES 100% 7.50% 10% Empyrean 2.5% YES YES 115% 17.5% 7.5% Glimmersteel 5% 125% 20% 10% 10% Gold -2.50% YES YES 170% 10% 10% Iron 85% Lead -5% 100% -10% 20% Seryll 5% YES 125% 25% 7.50% Silver 2.50% YES YES 97.50% 5% 10% Steel 5% 85% 2.50% 5% Tin -2.50% 80% -5% -10% Zinc -2.50% 75% -5% -15%', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Armour\">Armour</span></h3>\n<table class=\"wikit