>17.800\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><b>Shields</b>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Object\n</th>\n<th>Amount, kg\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_metal_shield\" title=\"Large metal shield\">Large metal shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>0.304\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Large_wooden_shield\" title=\"Large wooden shield\">Large wooden shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>0.304\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Medium_metal_shield\" title=\"Medium metal shield\">Medium metal shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>0.180\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Medium_wooden_shield\" title=\"Medium wooden shield\">Medium wooden shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>Wood: 0.180 Stripes: 0.054\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_metal_shield\" title=\"Small metal shield\">Small metal shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>0.068\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_wooden_shield\" title=\"Small wooden shield\">Small wooden shield</a>\n</td>\n<td>0.068\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Walls\">Walls</span></h3>\n<div class=\"mw-collapsible-content\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Object\n</th>\n<th>Amount, kg\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/House_Wall\" title=\"House Wall\">House Wall</a>\n</td>\n<td>1.000\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>', 4),
(20208, 1336, 'Removal', 'Removal', 'On most items with only one dyeable area, dye is removed by using a metal brush on it. Lye is used to remove dye from cloth, leather, and drake hide armour . If the item has dual dyeable areas: Dye on the wooden area is removed by using a metal brush on it. Dye on the secondary (cloth) area is removed by using lye equal to half of the amount of dye needed in the first place: Bed - 0.331 kg Armchair - 0.032 kg Caravel - 33.000 kg Cog - 5.473 kg Corbita - 9.385 kg Knarr - 25.440 kg Small sailing boat - 0.750 kg', '<p>On most items with only one dyeable area, dye is removed by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_brush\" title=\"Metal brush\">metal brush</a> on it.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">Lye</a> is used to remove dye from cloth, leather, and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Drake_hide_armour\" title=\"Drake hide armour\">drake hide armour</a>.</li>\n<li>If the item has dual dyeable areas:\n<ul><li>Dye on the wooden area is removed by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Metal_brush\" title=\"Metal brush\">metal brush</a> on it.</li>\n<li>Dye on the secondary (cloth) area is removed by using <a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">lye</a> equal to half of the amount of dye needed in the first place:\n<ul><li>Bed - 0.331 kg</li>\n<li>Armchair - 0.032 kg</li>\n<li>Caravel - 33.000 kg</li>\n<li>Cog - 5.473 kg</li>\n<li>Corbita - 9.385 kg</li>\n<li>Knarr - 25.440 kg</li>\n<li>Small sailing boat - 0.750 kg</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>', 5),
(20209, 1336, 'Image', 'Image', 'Example of Dyed items.', '<p>Example of Dyed items.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Statuebarreldyed.png\"><img alt=\"Statuebarreldyed.png\" data-file-height=\"448\" data-file-width=\"1763\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"163\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/0c/Statuebarreldyed.png/640px-Statuebarreldyed.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/0/0c/Statuebarreldyed.png/960px-Statuebarreldyed.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/0/0c/Statuebarreldyed.png/1280px-Statuebarreldyed.png 2x\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</p>', 6),
(20210, 4260, 'Description', 'Description', 'This sharp tooth was taken as a trophy. A butchered item obtained from butchering creatures .', '<p><i>This sharp tooth was taken as a trophy.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Butchering_items\" title=\"Category:Butchering items\">butchered item</a> obtained from <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(20211, 4260, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in some cooking recipes. Used to create a healing cover with a potency of 4.', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a> with a potency of 4.</li></ul>', 1),
(20212, 4260, 'Notes', 'Notes', '0.01 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage. Creatures that yield teeth Animal Weight (kg) Anaconda 0.05 Black bear 0.03 Brown bear 0.04 Dragon 0.05 Goblin leader 0.03 Mountain gorilla 0.04 Pig 0.03 Troll 0.04 Wild boar 0.03', '<ul><li>0.01 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<caption>Creatures that yield teeth\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"150\">Animal\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\"><a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">Weight</a> (kg)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Anaconda\" title=\"Anaconda\">Anaconda</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.05\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Black_bear\" title=\"Black bear\">Black bear</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.03\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Brown_bear\" title=\"Brown bear\">Brown bear</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.04\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Dragon\" title=\"Dragon\">Dragon</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.05\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Goblin_leader\" title=\"Goblin leader\">Goblin leader</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.03\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Mountain_gorilla\" title=\"Mountain gorilla\">Mountain gorilla</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.04\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Pig\" title=\"Pig\">Pig</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.03\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Troll\" title=\"Troll\">Troll</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.04\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wild_boar\" title=\"Wild boar\">Wild boar</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">0.03\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(20249, 5157, 'Description', 'Description', 'Wurm has very advanced item (or object ) management. Almost all items are player -made from raw materials gathered or extracted from the surrounding nature or creatures .', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Basic_Knowledge\" title=\"Basic Knowledge\">Wurm</a> has very advanced <b>item</b> (or <b>object</b>) management. Almost all items are <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a>-made from raw materials gathered or extracted from the surrounding nature or <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(20250, 5157, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Every item has weight , damage , quality level , size/volume, possible temperature , possible enchantments , a custom description, and other types of data that can make every item very unique and almost seem alive. Items can be used to build other items and structures like houses , guard towers , roads , and many other things. Some items are used to improve the quality level of other items.', '<ul><li>Every item has <a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">weight</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Quality_level\" title=\"Quality level\">quality level</a>, size/volume, possible <a href=\"/index.php/Temperature\" title=\"Temperature\">temperature</a>, possible <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Enchantment\" title=\"Enchantment\">enchantments</a>, a custom description, and other types of data that can make every item very unique and almost seem alive.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Items can be used to build other items and structures like <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">houses</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Guard_tower\" title=\"Guard tower\">guard towers</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Road\" title=\"Road\">roads</a>, and many other things.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Some items are used to improve the quality level of other items.</li></ul>', 1),
(20251, 5161, 'Description', 'Description', 'Apple trees are known for producing succulent, juicy apples in Wurm.', '<p>Apple trees are known for producing succulent, juicy apples in Wurm.\n</p>', 0),
(20252, 5161, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When in harvest season , apples can be harvested from this tree with a sickle . These apples can then be used in cooking , making beverages , and in transmutation liquid . When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: The tree has some fine green apples. Apple trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly. Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.', '<ul><li>When in harvest <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Season\" title=\"Season\">season</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Apples\" title=\"Apples\">apples</a> can be harvested from this tree with a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>. These apples can then be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a>, making <a href=\"/index.php/Beverages\" title=\"Beverages\">beverages</a>, and in <a href=\"/index.php/Transmutation_liquid\" title=\"Transmutation liquid\">transmutation liquid</a>.</li>\n<li>When the tree is in season, you will see this message when examining: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  The tree has some fine green apples.  </span></li>\n<li>Apple trees are known for germinating and spreading to nearby tiles quickly.</li>\n<li>Like all fruit trees, they yield very little wood when chopped. Old to overaged trees give a 3.2 to 5.6 kg log.</li></ul>', 1),
(20253, 5161, 'Images', 'Images', 'Apple tree in season', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 234px\"><div style=\"width: 234px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 232px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Apple_tree_fruit.png\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"919\" data-file-width=\"711\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"300\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/82/Apple_tree_fruit.png/348px-Apple_tree_fruit.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/8/82/Apple_tree_fruit.png/522px-Apple_tree_fruit.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/8/82/Apple_tree_fruit.png/696px-Apple_tree_fruit.png 2x\" width=\"232\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 212px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Apple tree in season\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 2),
(20254, 5162, 'Description', 'Description', 'A field of crops for farming .  Use a rake to farm the field to clear weeds.  You can harvest some crops without a tool, while others require a scythe . Crops with yellow tips are ripe and will yield produce when harvested. Harvesting a field before it is ripe will yield a reduced amount of lower quality produce. Digging or flattening nearby will destroy the field tile, leaving a dirt tile. The following types of Resource nodes can spawn on a Field tile: Animal burrow and Mineral debris .', '<p>A field of crops for <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">farming</a>.  Use a <a href=\"/index.php/Rake\" title=\"Rake\">rake</a> to farm the field to clear weeds.  You can harvest some crops without a tool, while others require a <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe\" title=\"Scythe\">scythe</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Crops with yellow tips are ripe and will yield produce when harvested. Harvesting a field before it is ripe will yield a reduced amount of lower quality produce.\n</p>\n<p>Digging or flattening nearby will destroy the field tile, leaving a dirt tile.\n</p>\n<p>The following types of <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> can spawn on a Field tile: <a href=\"/index.php/Animal_burrow\" title=\"Animal burrow\">Animal burrow</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a>.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(20255, 5162, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Farming Large planter', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">Farming</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_planter\" title=\"Large planter\">Large planter</a></li></ul>', 1),
(20256, 4248, 'Description', 'Description', 'Damage is used to illustrate the concepts of wear-and-tear on items . Items can accumulate damage through decay , usage, improvement failures or players and creatures destroying the item. If an item reaches 100 damage it is destroyed. Damage on some items can be fixed by repairing or mending them. However, damage on some items like food can not be fixed at all. Damage on them is permanent. Damage reduces the effective QL of an item to QL * (1 - DMG/100) . Example: A QL 20.8 log with 26.0 damage will only give QL 15.4 kindling .', '<p><b>Damage</b> is used to illustrate the concepts of wear-and-tear on <a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">items</a>. \n</p>\n<ul><li>Items can accumulate damage through <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a>, usage, improvement failures or players and creatures destroying the item.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If an item reaches 100 damage it is destroyed. Damage on some items can be fixed by <a href=\"/index.php/Repairing\" title=\"Repairing\">repairing</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mend\" title=\"Mend\">mending</a> them.\n<ul><li>However, damage on some items like food can not be fixed at all. Damage on them is permanent.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li>Damage reduces the effective <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of an item to <b>QL * (1 - DMG/100)</b>. Example: A QL 20.8 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a> with 26.0 damage will only give QL 15.4 <a href=\"/index.php/Kindling\" title=\"Kindling\">kindling</a>.</li></ul>', 0),
(20257, 4248, 'Decay', 'Decay', 'Decay is the process of accumulating damage over time. The decay rate depends on the item type and where the item is stored. Logs , stone shards or dirt for example will completely decay within days while other items may even last months and years. Items made from cedar trees decay slower. However containers made from cedar do NOT protect their content better. Items on deed, in buildings or in containers will decay slower. Items in inventory will generally decay slower or will not decay at all. An exception to this rule is food. Meals, for example, decay faster in inventory than anywhere else, unless placed in a picnic basket or lunchbox . Some items can be stored in bulk storage bins and food storage bins . Items in those special containers are exempt from decay but 5% of the content is lost every month, unless it is on a settlement .', '<p><b>Decay</b> is the process of accumulating damage over time. The decay rate depends on the item type and where the item is stored. <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">Logs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> for example will completely decay within days while other items may even last months and years. Items made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> trees decay slower. However containers made from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cedar\" title=\"Cedar\">cedar</a> do NOT protect their content better.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Items on deed, in buildings or in <a href=\"/index.php/Container\" title=\"Container\">containers</a> will decay slower.</li>\n<li>Items in <a href=\"/index.php/Inventory\" title=\"Inventory\">inventory</a> will generally decay slower or will not decay at all. An exception to this rule is food. Meals, for example, decay faster in inventory than anywhere else, unless placed in a <a href=\"/index.php/Picnic_basket\" title=\"Picnic basket\">picnic basket</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Lunchbox\" title=\"Lunchbox\">lunchbox</a>.</li>\n<li>Some items can be stored in <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bins</a>  and <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">food storage bins</a>. Items in those special containers are exempt from decay but 5% of the content is lost every month, unless it is on a <a href=\"/index.php/Settlement\" title=\"Settlement\">settlement</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(20258, 4248, 'Usage Damage', 'Usage_Damage', 'Usage damage is often referred to as just damage . Every time an item is used in an action it may get damaged a bit. Items made out of oaken wood or steel receive 20% less usage damage (stacks with the reduction from rarity ).', '<p>Usage damage is often referred to as just <b>damage</b>. Every time an item is used in an action it may get damaged a bit. Items made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">oaken</a> wood or <a href=\"/index.php/Steel\" title=\"Steel\">steel</a> receive 20% less usage damage (stacks with the reduction from <a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">rarity</a>).\n</p>', 2),
(20259, 4248, 'Destroying', 'Destroying', 'Many immobile items like walls , fences , forges , ovens , looms , beds , coffins , huge tubs , large barrels , large chests , bulk storage bins and food storage bins can be destroyed by players. You need 21 body strength and a heavy tool like large maul for it. Mayors get a bonus when bashing structures on deed, and do more damage. Some creatures may damage boats and carts in combat.', '<p>Many immobile items like <a href=\"/index.php/Wall\" title=\"Wall\">walls</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Fence\" title=\"Fence\">fences</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">forges</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">ovens</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Loom\" title=\"Loom\">looms</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">beds</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Coffin\" title=\"Coffin\">coffins</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Huge_tub\" title=\"Huge tub\">huge tubs</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">large barrels</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">large chests</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bins</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Food_storage_bin\" title=\"Food storage bin\">food storage bins</a> can be destroyed by players. You need 21 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> and a heavy tool like <a href=\"/index.php/Large_maul\" title=\"Large maul\">large maul</a> for it. Mayors get a bonus when bashing structures on deed, and do more damage.\n</p>\n<p>Some creatures may damage <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Boats\" title=\"Boats\">boats</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Cart\" title=\"Cart\">carts</a> in combat.\n</p>', 3),
(20260, 4248, 'Wounds', 'Wounds', 'Should your character sustain damage, you will suffer one or more wounds of various severity. You can heal them by casting healing spells (see religion ) or by using cotton as first aid . Healing covers will speed up the healing process, and are required for more severe wounds to stop bleeding, or getting worse.', '<p>Should your character sustain damage, you will suffer one or more <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wounds</a> of various severity. You can heal them by casting healing <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spells</a> (see <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religion</a>) or by using <a href=\"/index.php/Cotton\" title=\"Cotton\">cotton</a> as <a href=\"/index.php/First_aid\" title=\"First aid\">first aid</a>. <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">Healing covers</a> will speed up the healing process, and are required for more severe wounds to stop bleeding, or getting worse.\n</p>', 4),
(20261, 4248, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Decay', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">Decay</a>\n</p>', 5);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(20287, 5167, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When outside(not in a cave) with a shovel or pickaxe activated, the slope of a tile border (or whether it is flat) will show by hovering the mouse over it. When inside a cave with a pickaxe activated, the slope of a tile border (or whether it is flat) will show by hovering the mouse over it. At 0 skill you can only see the slopes of the tile you are standing on. For every 15 digging or mining skill (depending on whether shovel or pickaxe is selected) the distance at which you can see slopes increases by 1 tile. The slope can also be shown inside a tunnel with concrete activated. Maximum slope before starting to fall down is 23 or 24, but a player can get hurt walking down if the slope is over 20, depending on body strength , how much the player is carrying or dragging, etc. At around 30 slope the player will be required to climb in order to move uphill. Horses can scale slopes up to 40 when ridden or pulling large carts and wagons .', '<ul><li>When outside(not in a cave) with a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a> activated, the slope of a tile border (or whether it is flat) will show by hovering the mouse over it.</li>\n<li>When inside a cave with a pickaxe activated, the slope of a tile border (or whether it is flat) will show by hovering the mouse over it.</li>\n<li>At 0 skill you can only see the slopes of the tile you are standing on. For every 15 <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> skill (depending on whether shovel or pickaxe is selected) the distance at which you can see slopes increases by 1 tile.</li>\n<li>The slope can also be shown inside a tunnel with <a href=\"/index.php/Concrete\" title=\"Concrete\">concrete</a> activated.</li>\n<li>Maximum slope before starting to fall down is 23 or 24, but a <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a> can get hurt walking down if the slope is over 20, depending on <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a>, how much the player is <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Encumbrance\" title=\"Encumbrance\">carrying</a> or dragging, etc.</li>\n<li>At around 30 slope the player will be required to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Climb\" title=\"Climb\">climb</a> in order to move uphill.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horses</a> can scale slopes up to 40 when ridden or pulling <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large carts</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagons</a>.</li></ul>', 0),
(20288, 5167, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Digging Mining Concrete Maximum slope Weight Diagonal slope', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">Digging</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">Mining</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Concrete\" title=\"Concrete\">Concrete</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">Maximum slope</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">Weight</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Diagonal_slope\" title=\"Diagonal slope\">Diagonal slope</a></li></ul>', 1),
(20303, 1390, 'Description', 'Description', 'You can send mail to other players in the game via spirit containers which have been enchanted by priests/priestesses of Fo or Libila with the spells Courier or Dark messenger . Mailboxes do receive damage and can be destroyed by decay, causing the cast on it to disappear.', '<p>You can send mail to other players in the game via spirit containers which have been enchanted by priests/priestesses of Fo or Libila with the spells <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">Courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a>.\n</p>\n<p>Mailboxes do receive damage and can be destroyed by decay, causing the cast on it to disappear.\n</p>', 0),
(20304, 1390, 'Types of spirit containers', 'Types_of_spirit_containers', 'There is no difference in operation between the various spirit containers. Spirit house - fine carpentry Spirit mansion - fine carpentry Spirit cottage - masonry Spirit castle - masonry', '<p>There is no difference in operation between the various spirit containers.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_house\" title=\"Spirit house\">Spirit house</a> - <i>fine carpentry</i></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_mansion\" title=\"Spirit mansion\">Spirit mansion</a> - <i>fine carpentry</i></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_cottage\" title=\"Spirit cottage\">Spirit cottage</a> - <i>masonry</i></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_castle\" title=\"Spirit castle\">Spirit castle</a> - <i>masonry</i></li></ul>', 1),
(20305, 1390, 'Mail between servers', 'Mail_between_servers', 'You cannot send an item to a member of an enemy kingdom on Chaos or on Epic servers. You get the message: \"You may not trade with the enemy.\" You cannot send items between Freedom or Epic servers and the Jackal server. You cannot send items between North and South Freedom clusters. NOTICE:  Items will be mailed to the server the recipient is currently present on. It can only be retrieved from that server.', '<ul><li>You cannot send an item to a member of an enemy <a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom\" title=\"Kingdom\">kingdom</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a> or on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Epic\" title=\"Epic\">Epic</a> servers. You get the message: \"You may not trade with the enemy.\"</li>\n<li>You cannot send items between Freedom or Epic servers and the Jackal server.</li>\n<li>You cannot send items between North and South Freedom clusters.</li>\n<li><b>NOTICE:  Items will be mailed to the server the recipient is currently present on. It can only be retrieved from that server.</b></li></ul>', 2),
(20306, 1390, 'Sending process', 'Sending_process', 'To send the mail, Drop the item(s) into any spirit container, then right-click the container, and select Send . There are two dialogues that will control how the items are sent. The first allows you to specify the name of the recipient, and what items should be sent using C.O.D. (cash on delivery).  It also allows to skip the second dialog. The second dialogue allows you to see how much the delivery charge will be, and to specify the C.O.D. amount you will charge the recipient if applicable.', '<p>To send the mail, \n</p>\n<ol><li>Drop the item(s) into any spirit container, then right-click the container, and select <i>Send</i>.</li>\n<li>There are two dialogues that will control how the items are sent.\n<ol><li>The first allows you to specify the name of the recipient, and what items should be sent using C.O.D. (cash on delivery).  It also allows to skip the second dialog.</li>\n<li>The second dialogue allows you to see how much the delivery charge will be, and to specify the C.O.D. amount you will charge the recipient if applicable.</li></ol></li></ol>', 3),
(20307, 1390, 'Receiving process', 'Receiving_process', 'When you login, you will receive a message if you have any mail. You sense imps speaking your name and saying you have 1 mail waiting to be picked up. To receive or check for mail, right-click any spirit container and select Check . If an item is sent as Cash On Delivery you need to have the money in your bank to cover the delivery charge before you can receive the items. You also have the option to return the items to the sender.', '<p>When you login, you will receive a message if you have any mail. <i>You sense imps speaking your name and saying you have 1 mail waiting to be picked up.</i>\n</p>\n<p>To receive or check for mail, right-click any spirit container and select <i>Check</i>. If an item is sent as <i>Cash On Delivery</i> you need to have the money in your bank to cover the delivery charge before you can receive the items.  \n</p>\n<p>You also have the option to return the items to the sender.  \n</p>', 4),
(20308, 1390, 'Non-retrieved items', 'Non-retrieved_items', 'If the recipient does not pick up their mail within two weeks, they are automatically returned-to-sender. The returned items will go back to the server the sender was on at the time it was sent. The sender will not receive a mail notification unless they enter that server. If the original sender does not pick up the returned items within two weeks, they are destroyed. If the recipient uses return-to-sender and the original sender does not pick up the items within 7 days, they are destroyed. If a merchant disbands due to 3 months of inactivity of its owner, then their contents will be mailed to the owner with a 6 month expiry period. There is no way to extract items from the mail system if you are not the recipient ! If you are sending something valuable, ensure that the recipient is available to pick it up before you send it.  If you return an item to the sender, it would be good manners to contact them to ensure they retrieve it before the two week deadline.', '<p>If the recipient does not pick up their mail within two weeks, they are automatically returned-to-sender.  \n</p>\n<p>The returned items will go back to the server the sender was on at the time it was sent. The sender will not receive a mail notification unless they enter that server.\n</p>\n<p>If the original sender does not pick up the returned items within two weeks, they are destroyed. \n</p>\n<p>If the recipient uses return-to-sender and the original sender does not pick up the items within 7 days, they are destroyed.\n</p>\n<p>If a merchant disbands due to 3 months of inactivity of its owner, then their contents will be mailed to the owner with a 6 month expiry period.\n</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><b>There is no way to extract items from the mail system if you are not the recipient !</b></span>\n</p>\n<p><b>If you are sending something valuable, ensure that the recipient is available to pick it up before you send it.  If you return an item to the sender, it would be good manners to contact them to ensure they retrieve it before the two week deadline.</b>\n</p>', 5),
(20309, 1390, 'Postage charges', 'Postage_charges', 'The postage is 1 copper per item for same or cross-server mailing. The postage fee is taken from the bank account of the sender as the items are sent, unless they are C.O.D., in which case it is taken from the recipient when received. Exceptions An inscribed papyrus sheet or paper sheet is 1 iron to mail. Combined items (such as metal lumps, wood scraps, liquids, etc) are 1 copper per 5 kg.', '<p>The postage is 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Bank_of_Wurm\" title=\"Bank of Wurm\">copper</a> per item for same or cross-server mailing. The postage fee is taken from the bank account of the sender as the items are sent, unless they are C.O.D., in which case it is taken from the recipient when received.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</span></h3>\n<ul><li>An inscribed <a href=\"/index.php/Papyrus_sheet\" title=\"Papyrus sheet\">papyrus sheet</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Paper_sheet\" title=\"Paper sheet\">paper sheet</a> is 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Bank_of_Wurm\" title=\"Bank of Wurm\">iron</a> to mail.</li>\n<li>Combined items (such as metal lumps, wood scraps, liquids, etc) are 1 copper per 5 kg.</li></ul>', 6),
(20310, 1390, 'Delivery times', 'Delivery_times', 'Any items sent via mailbox have a predetermined time for mailing, based on the power of the enchant of the sending mailbox .\nthe timer is 101 minus power in minutes. Examples: 1 power will take 100 minutes. 50 power will take 51 minutes. 99 power will take 2 minutes. 101 or higher power will be instant.', '<p>Any items sent via <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mailbox\" title=\"Mailbox\">mailbox</a> have a predetermined time for mailing, based on the power of the enchant of the sending <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mailbox\" title=\"Mailbox\">mailbox</a>.\nthe timer is 101 minus power in minutes.\n</p>\n<p>Examples:\n</p>\n<ul><li>1 power will take 100 minutes.</li>\n<li>50 power will take 51 minutes.</li>\n<li>99 power will take 2 minutes.</li>\n<li>101 or higher power will be instant.</li></ul>', 7),
(20311, 1390, 'Can be sent', 'Can_be_sent', 'Almanac (1c plus 1i per report inside) Archaeology journal (1c plus 1i per report inside) Armour pieces (including Barding ) Atlas (1c plus 1c per map inside) Backpack (and everything that can fit in one) Birdcage Book (1c plus 1i per sheet inside) Buoy Butchering knife Candelabra Carving knife Cauldron (and everything that can fit in one) Crude tools (all) Dredge Explorer tent Fence bars File Fireworks Fishing net Hammer Hatchet Horse shoe Huge axe Lantern Large anvil Large brazier bowl Large maul Large pottery amphora Longsword Mallet Meditation rug Metal lump (1c / 5kg if combined) Military tent Mooring anchor Needle Pelt Pickaxe Picnic basket Pile of dirt Practice doll Rake Reflex bow Saddle Saw Scythe Shields (all of them are mailable) Short bow Short sword Shovel Sickle Small anvil Small axe Small barrel or small wine barrel Small magical chest Small pottery amphora Small tortoise shell ** Smelting pot Snowman statue ** Spindle Square sail Steel and flint Still ** Stone chisel Stone shards Strip of leather Triangular sail (and all smaller than it, like square piece of cloth ) Troll mask Trowel Two handed sword Waystone Whetstone Witchs hat Yellow potion **Can be sent but were tested with a runed mailbox. Must still be tested with non-runed mailboxes.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Almanac\" title=\"Almanac\">Almanac</a> (1c plus 1i per report inside)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Archaeology_journal\" title=\"Archaeology journal\">Archaeology journal</a> (1c plus 1i per report inside)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">Armour pieces</a> (including <a href=\"/index.php/Barding\" title=\"Barding\">Barding</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Atlas\" title=\"Atlas\">Atlas</a> (1c plus 1c per map inside)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Backpack\" title=\"Backpack\">Backpack</a> (and everything that can fit in one)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Birdcage\" title=\"Birdcage\">Birdcage</a></li>\n<li><