ign: center;\">9\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">Small cart</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">756\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">60\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D L\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">16\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">40\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">9\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_raft\" title=\"Small raft\">Small raft</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">756\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">60\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D I\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">16\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">40\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">9\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Small_sailing_boat\" title=\"Small sailing boat\">Small sailing boat</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">756\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">140\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D L\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">16\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">40\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">9\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">20800\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">240\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">L\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">27\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">20\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">12\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">100\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">100\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">100\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">65\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Legend\">Legend</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Volume = the total amount of physical space a container takes up as well as offers internally for storage purposes.</li>\n<li>Weight = the total weight of the container without any items inside.</li>\n<li>Move: D = can be dragged, I = Can be picked up into inventory, L= Can be loaded</li>\n<li> ? = Data required</li></ul>', 0),
(20372, 4981, 'Container features', 'Container_features', 'Performing actions with containers All containers, including the inventory and inventory groups, can be activated like other items. Some actions have special functionality when a container is activated, and will choose the first valid item in the container when performing the action. These actions currently include: Sowing seeds Planting herbs and spices in pottery planters Planting sprouts , flowers , and other plants Taming and feeding creatures For example, if a satchel is activated and it happens to contain seeds, multiple sowing actions can be queued with the satchel activated and each action will automatically use a different seed item. When a container is on the toolbelt, the number of items inside the container will be shown on its toolbelt icon. By clicking the toolbelt slot again, or pressing the hotkey for that slot, the activated item will toggle between the container itself and the first item inside the container.', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Performing_actions_with_containers\">Performing actions with containers</span></h3>\n<p>All containers, including the inventory and inventory groups, can be activated like other items. Some actions have special functionality when a container is activated, and will choose the first valid item in the container when performing the action. These actions currently include:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Sowing <a href=\"/index.php/Seeds\" title=\"Seeds\">seeds</a></li>\n<li>Planting <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Herbs\" title=\"Herbs\">herbs</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spices\" title=\"Spices\">spices</a> in <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_planter\" title=\"Pottery planter\">pottery planters</a></li>\n<li>Planting <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sprouts\" title=\"Sprouts\">sprouts</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Flowers\" title=\"Flowers\">flowers</a>, and other plants</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">Taming</a> and feeding <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a></li></ul>\n<p>For example, if a satchel is activated and it happens to contain seeds, multiple sowing actions can be queued with the satchel activated and each action will automatically use a different seed item.\n</p>\n<p>When a container is on the toolbelt, the number of items inside the container will be shown on its toolbelt icon. By clicking the toolbelt slot again, or pressing the hotkey for that slot, the activated item will toggle between the container itself and the first item inside the container.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(20373, 4981, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'To effectively gauge how much of an item a particular container may hold, simply divide that container\'s volume, given in the chart above, by the volume that a single unit of that item takes up. The resulting number represents how many of that item will then actually fit in the desired container.', '<ul><li>To effectively gauge how much of an item a particular container may hold, simply divide that container\'s volume, given in the chart above, by the volume that a single unit of that item takes up. The resulting number represents how many of that item will then actually fit in the desired container.</li></ul>', 2),
(20374, 4981, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Decay', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">Decay</a></li></ul>', 3),
(20380, 5186, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A higher quality needles increases your success chance when creating. Failure when creating causes the leather to lose some quality.', '<ul><li>A higher <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> needles increases your success chance when creating.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Failure\" title=\"Failure\">Failure</a> when creating causes the leather to lose some quality.</li></ul>', 0),
(20397, 1028, 'Description', 'Description', 'These are the wall types you can build on a house. Fences may also be considered a type of wall and may be built inside houses.\nTo build a wall activate a hammer , mallet , or trowel and right-click a wall plan . Select Build and a wall type.\nWalls can be dyed with 1kg (1000g) of dye per section.', '<p>These are the wall types you can build on a house. <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Fences\" title=\"Category:Fences\">Fences</a> may also be considered a type of wall and may be built inside houses.\nTo build a wall activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">hammer</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a>, or <a href=\"/index.php/Trowel\" title=\"Trowel\">trowel</a> and right-click a <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_plan\" title=\"Wall plan\">wall plan</a>. Select <i>Build</i> and a wall type.\nWalls can be dyed with 1kg (1000g) of dye per section. \n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(20398, 1028, 'Types of walls', 'Types_of_walls', 'Solid walls block actions and movement and provide no visibility. Doors allow a player to walk or ride a cart into or through a building. Windows are walls with some form of opening for visibility and allow certain actions, such as archery, while blocking movement. Arched walls allow movement and some actions but cannot be locked and closed like doors ; however, you can build a gate or fence inside them. High gates do not fit inside an arched wall. Timber Walls Timber framed arched wall Timber framed arch left/right Timber framed T arch Timber framed balcony Timber framed door Timber framed double door Timber framed jetty Timber framed wall Timber framed window Wooden Walls Wooden arched wall Wooden arch left/right Wooden t arch Wooden canopy Wooden door Wooden double door Wooden portcullis Wooden house wall Wooden window Wooden wide window Log Walls Log arch Log balcony Log canopy Log door Log double door Log double T arch Log T arch Log wall Log window Log double window Log wide window Hardwood Log Walls Hardwood log arch Hardwood log balcony Hardwood log canopy Hardwood log door Hardwood log double door Hardwood log double T arch Hardwood log T arch Hardwood log wall Hardwood log window Hardwood log double window Hardwood log wide window Bark Log Walls Bark log arch Bark log balcony Bark log canopy Bark log door Bark log double door Bark log double T arch Bark log T arch Bark log wall Bark log window Bark log double window Bark log wide window Rustic Log Walls Rustic log arch Rustic log balcony Rustic log canopy Rustic log door Rustic log double door Rustic log double T arch Rustic log T arch Rustic log wall Rustic log window Rustic log double window Rustic log wide window Marble Walls Marble arched wall Marble arch left/right Marble t arch Marble door Marble double door Marble oriel Marble portcullis Marble wall Marble barred wall Marble window Marble window narrow Plain Stone Walls Plain stone arched wall Plain stone arch left/right Plain stone T arch Plain stone door Plain stone double door Plain stone oriel Plain stone portcullis Plain stone wall Plain stone barred wall Plain stone window Plain narrow stone window Pottery Walls Pottery arched wall Pottery arch left/right Pottery T arch Pottery door Pottery double door Pottery oriel Pottery portcullis Pottery house wall Pottery barred wall Pottery window Pottery narrow window Rendered Walls Rendered arched wall Rendered arch left/right Rendered T arch Rendered door Rendered double door Rendered oriel Rendered portcullis Rendered house wall Rendered barred wall Rendered window Rendered narrow window Rounded Stone Walls Rounded stone arched wall Rounded stone arch left/right Rounded stone t arch Rounded stone door Rounded stone double door Rounded stone oriel Rounded stone portcullis Rounded stone house wall Rounded stone barred wall Rounded stone window Rounded stone narrow window Sandstone Walls Sandstone arched wall Sandstone arch left/right Sandstone t arch sandstone door sandstone double door Sandstone oriel Sandstone portcullis Sandstone house wall Sandstone barred wall Sandstone window Sandstone narrow window Slate Walls Slate arched wall Slate arch left/right Slate t arch Slate door Slate double door Slate oriel Slate portcullis Slate house wall Slate barred wall Slate window Slate narrow window Stone Walls Stone arched wall Stone arch left/right Stone t arch Stone door Stone double door Stone oriel Stone portcullis Stone house wall Stone window', '<ul><li>Solid walls block actions and movement and provide no visibility.</li>\n<li>Doors allow a player to walk or ride a cart into or through a building.</li>\n<li>Windows are walls with some form of opening for visibility and allow certain actions, such as archery, while blocking movement.</li>\n<li>Arched walls allow movement and some actions but cannot be locked and closed like <a href=\"/index.php/Category:House_doors\" title=\"Category:House doors\">doors</a>; however, you can build a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Gates\" title=\"Category:Gates\">gate</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fences\" title=\"Fences\">fence</a> inside them. High gates do not fit inside an arched wall.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Timber_Walls\">Timber Walls</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 202px\"><div style=\"width: 202px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 200px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arched_wall\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"600\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/d/db/Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg/300px-Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/d/db/Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg/451px-Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/d/db/Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg/600px-Timber_framed_arched_wall.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 180px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Timber framed arched wall\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 202px\"><div style=\"width: 202px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 200px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a href=\"/index.php/Timber_framed_arch_left\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"600\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"150\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/67/Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg/300px-Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/67/Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg/451px-Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/6/67/Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg/600px-Timber_framed_left_arch.jpg 2x\" width=\"200\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 180px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Timber framed arch left/right\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</di