(20406, 2852, 'Description', 'Description', 'A palisade is a tall wall made of felled trees .', '<p>A <b>palisade</b> is a tall wall made of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Felled_tree\" title=\"Felled tree\">felled trees</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(20407, 2852, 'Skill Required', 'Skill_Required', 'To calculate the maximum slope you can build on, based on your carpentry or masonry skill, use the following formula submitted by Ketza : Max slope = (3 * √ skill) + 10 Skill Max Slope 6 17 8 18 9 19 12 20 14 21 16 22 19 23 22 24 25 25 29 26 33 27 36 28 41 29 45 30 49 31 54 32 59 33 64 34 70 35 75 36 81 37 88 38 94 39 Note: Maximum slope is rounded down', '<p>To calculate the <a href=\"/index.php/Maximum_slope\" title=\"Maximum slope\">maximum slope</a> you can build on, based on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> skill, use the following formula submitted by <a href=\"/index.php/Player:Ketza\" title=\"Player:Ketza\">Ketza</a>:\n</p>\n<p><i>Max slope = (3 *</i> √<i>skill) + 10</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Skill\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\">Max Slope\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>17\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>18\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>19\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td>21\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>22\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>23\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>24\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>25\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>29</td>\n<td>26\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>27\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>36</td>\n<td>28\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>41</td>\n<td>29\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>49</td>\n<td>31\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>54</td>\n<td>32\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>59</td>\n<td>33\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>64</td>\n<td>34\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>35\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>75</td>\n<td>36\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>81</td>\n<td>37\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>88</td>\n<td>38\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>94</td>\n<td>39\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Note:</b> Maximum slope is rounded <i>down</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(20408, 2852, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Wooden palisade gate', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wooden_palisade_gate\" title=\"Wooden palisade gate\">Wooden palisade gate</a></li></ul>', 2),
(20412, 5193, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wall plan is the frame of an incomplete building, this is the first step to building a house .', '<p>A <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">wall plan</a> is the frame of an incomplete building, this is the first step to building a <a href=\"/index.php/House\" title=\"House\">house</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(20413, 5193, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'To start planning a structure, activate a mallet or iron hammer , right-click a tile and select Plan building . You can extend the wall plan by additional tiles, depending on your carpentry skill. Each tile and each piece of wall needs 1 point in carpentry. To remove a wall plan from a tile, right-click the tile and select Remove plan here . A wall plan without any walls attached will generally decay within 24 hours. House tiles can now only be planned on perfectly flat ground ( slope of 0 dirts). The maximum length of a house is 20 tiles in one direction. Once you have the desired shape of your house, right-click the wooden frame and select Finalize build plan . This will create a house and it will also be added to your list of manageable buildings. You can manage the name, door locks , and friends of the house with if you have anyone on your friends list . You are not required to complete a building before you are allowed to build or plan another one, however if you wish to do so you must wait until a server reset.', '<p>To start planning a structure, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">mallet</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron_hammer\" title=\"Iron hammer\">iron hammer</a>, right-click a <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> and select <i>Plan building</i>. You can extend the wall plan by additional tiles, depending on your <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> skill. Each tile and each piece of wall needs 1 point in carpentry.\n</p>\n<p>To remove a wall plan from a tile, right-click the tile and select <i>Remove plan here</i>. A wall plan without any walls attached will generally decay within 24 hours.\n</p>\n<p>House tiles can now only be planned on perfectly flat ground (<a href=\"/index.php/Slope\" title=\"Slope\">slope</a> of 0 dirts). The maximum length of a house is 20 tiles in one direction.\n</p>\n<p>Once you have the desired shape of your house, right-click the wooden frame and select <i>Finalize build plan</i>. This will create a house and it will also be added to your list of manageable buildings. You can manage the name, <a href=\"/index.php/Door_lock\" title=\"Door lock\">door locks</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Friend\" title=\"Friend\">friends</a> of the house with if you have anyone on your <a href=\"/index.php/Friend\" title=\"Friend\">friends list</a>.\n</p>\n<p>You are not required to complete a building before you are allowed to build or plan another one, however if you wish to do so you must wait until a server reset.\n</p>', 1),
(20414, 5193, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Planning tools for calculating carpentry and material requirements. Walls for a list of walls available', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Toolkits\" title=\"Toolkits\">Planning tools</a> for calculating carpentry and material requirements.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Walls\" title=\"Category:Walls\">Walls</a> for a list of walls available</li></ul>', 2),
(20415, 4227, 'Description', 'Description', 'Swords deal both cutting and piercing damage. They attack relatively fast, and have a good chance to parry. Higher skill in swords increases both hit chances and parry chances. Swords skill helps with all types of swords, but the sub-skills for each sword type only help when using that type of sword.', '<p>Swords deal both cutting and piercing damage. They attack relatively fast, and have a good chance to parry. Higher skill in swords increases both hit chances and parry chances. Swords skill helps with all types of swords, but the sub-skills for each sword type only help when using that type of sword.\n</p>', 0),
(20416, 4227, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Swords Body > Body control Subskills Shortsword Longsword Two handed sword', '<ul><li>Swords</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shortsword\" title=\"Shortsword\">Shortsword</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Longsword\" title=\"Longsword\">Longsword</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Two_handed_sword\" title=\"Two handed sword\">Two handed sword</a></li></ul>', 1),
(20417, 4227, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Swordsman at 50 skill Duelist at 70 skill Swordsmaster at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Swordsman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Duelist at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Swordsmaster at 90 skill</li></ul>', 2),
(20418, 5049, 'Description', 'Description', 'Armour is equipment worn to protect against damage, at the cost of movement speed. Different types of armour are effective against different attack types.', '<p>Armour is equipment worn to protect against damage, at the cost of movement speed. Different types of armour are effective against different attack types.\n</p>', 0),
(20419, 5049, 'Effective ql curve', 'Effective_ql_curve', 'Armour up to quality 70 has an effective ql curve. Actual QL Effective QL 1 20 10 34.7 20 43.6 30 50.4 40 56.1 50 61.2 60 65.8 70 70 80 80 90 90 100 100', '<p>Armour up to quality 70 has an effective ql curve. \n</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Actual QL\n</th>\n<th>Effective QL\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>20\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>34.7\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>43.6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>50.4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>56.1\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>61.2\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>65.8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>70\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>80</td>\n<td>80\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>90\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>100\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(20420, 5049, 'Comparison', 'Comparison', 'Metal types have properties which may affect damage reduction or other aspects of armour. Damage reduction scales with quality level. Each level of rarity adds 3% to damage reduction: Rare: +3% Supreme: +6% Fantastic: +9% Armour type Base Damage Reduction Walking speed penalty Casting/archery buff Weight (kg) Weight Class Unarmoured N/A 0% +30% 0.00 no Cloth 40% 0% +30% 1.80 light Leather 60% 10.9% +30% 3.20 light Studded leather 62.5% 14.5% +0% 4.90 light Chain 62.5% 21.6% -15% 8.20 medium Plate armour 65% 27.0% -30% 20.50 heavy Drake hide armour 65% 9.6% -30% 3.20 medium Dragon scale armour 70% 5.4% -30% 5.80 heavy For spellcasting/archery buff, defaults to the heaviest type of armour that is worn.  Leather with a chain gauntlet will default to chain.  Helmets bypass this rule.', '<ul><li>Metal types have <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Metal_properties#Table_of_properties\" title=\"Metal properties\">properties</a> which may affect damage reduction or other aspects of armour.</li>\n<li>Damage reduction scales with quality level.</li>\n<li>Each level of rarity adds 3% to damage reduction:\n<ul><li>Rare: +3%</li>\n<li>Supreme: +6%</li>\n<li>Fantastic: +9%</li></ul></li></ul>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Armour type\n</th>\n<th>Base Damage Reduction\n</th>\n<th>Walking speed penalty\n</th>\n<th>Casting/archery buff\n</th>\n<th>Weight (kg)\n</th>\n<th>Weight Class\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Unarmoured\n</th>\n<td>N/A</td>\n<td>0%</td>\n<td>+30%</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n<td>no\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth</a>\n</th>\n<td>40%</td>\n<td>0%</td>\n<td>+30%</td>\n<td>1.80</td>\n<td>light\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>60%</td>\n<td>10.9%</td>\n<td>+30%</td>\n<td>3.20</td>\n<td>light\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Studded_leather_armour\" title=\"Studded leather armour\">Studded leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>62.5%</td>\n<td>14.5%</td>\n<td>+0%</td>\n<td>4.90</td>\n<td>light\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour_smithing\" title=\"Chain armour smithing\">Chain</a>\n</th>\n<td>62.5%</td>\n<td>21.6%</td>\n<td>-15%</td>\n<td>8.20</td>\n<td>medium\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate armour</a>\n</th>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>27.0%</td>\n<td>-30%</td>\n<td>20.50</td>\n<td>heavy\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Drake_hide_armour\" title=\"Drake hide armour\">Drake hide armour</a>\n</th>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>9.6%</td>\n<td>-30%</td>\n<td>3.20</td>\n<td>medium\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dragon_scale_armour\" title=\"Dragon scale armour\">Dragon scale armour</a>\n</th>\n<td>70%</td>\n<td>5.4%</td>\n<td>-30%</td>\n<td>5.80</td>\n<td>heavy\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li>For spellcasting/archery buff, defaults to the heaviest type of armour that is worn.  Leather with a chain gauntlet will default to chain.  Helmets bypass this rule.</li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(20421, 5049, 'Attack type protection', 'Attack_type_protection', 'Different types of armour are stronger or weaker against certain types of damage. Additionally, certain materials are best suited for armour purposes. See the following tables for more: Damage Reduction Armour type Acid Bite Burn Cold Crush Pierce Slash Chain 100% 107.5% 107.5% 92.5% 107.5% 92.5% 100% Cloth 100% 80% 80% 120% 120% 100% 80% Dragon scale 100% 100% 105% 95% 95% 105% 100% Drake hide 95% 100% 100% 105% 105% 100% 95% Leather 90% 90% 110% 100% 100% 90% 110% Plate 105% 105% 95% 100% 95% 100% 105% Studded leather 90% 105% 100% 110% 100% 110% 90% These values modify the base Damage Reduction values, given in the comparison table below. The higher the percentage, the more protection an armour has against that attack type. The lower the percentage, the less protection an armour has against that attack type. 100% = no modifier. Glance Rate Armour type Acid Bite Burn Cold Crush Pierce Slash Chain 25% 65% 65% 15% 30% 30% 65% Cloth 65% 35% 15% 65% 55% 40% 40% Dragon scale 25% 45% 55% 25% 35% 65% 50% Drake hide 50% 55% 25% 65% 60% 25% 40% Leather 40% 35% 15% 65% 55% 35% 35% Plate 35% 50% 35% 35% 30% 65% 30% Studded leather 50% 50% 15% 65% 65% 30% 30% These values determine the chance that an attack will glance, causing no damage. Additional Metal Armour Properties Material Damage Reduction Movement Glance Adamantine 5.00% 5.00% Brass 1.00% Bronze 1.00% Copper -1.00% 1.00% -2.00% Electrum 0.50% -1.00% 2.00% Empyrean 2.00% Glimmersteel 5.00% 10.00% Gold -1.00% -5.00% 2.50% Iron Lead -2.50% -2.50% Seryll 5.00% 10.00% Silver -0.75% -2.00% 1.00% Steel 2.50% Tin -1.75% 2.00% Zinc -2.00% 2.50%', '<p>Different types of armour are stronger or weaker against certain types of damage. Additionally, certain materials are best suited for armour purposes. See the following tables for more:\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Damage_Reduction\">Damage Reduction</span></h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Armour type\n</th>\n<th>Acid\n</th>\n<th>Bite\n</th>\n<th>Burn\n</th>\n<th>Cold\n</th>\n<th>Crush\n</th>\n<th>Pierce\n</th>\n<th>Slash\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour_smithing\" title=\"Chain armour smithing\">Chain</a>\n</th>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>107.5%</td>\n<td>107.5%</td>\n<td>92.5%</td>\n<td>107.5%</td>\n<td>92.5%</td>\n<td>100%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth</a>\n</th>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>80%</td>\n<td>80%</td>\n<td>120%</td>\n<td>120%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>80%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dragon_scale_armour\" title=\"Dragon scale armour\">Dragon scale</a>\n</th>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>95%</td>\n<td>95%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>100%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Drake_hide_armour\" title=\"Category:Drake hide armour\">Drake hide</a>\n</th>\n<td>95%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>95%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>90%</td>\n<td>90%</td>\n<td>110%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>90%</td>\n<td>110%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate</a>\n</th>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>95%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>95%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>105%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Studded_leather_armour\" title=\"Studded leather armour\">Studded leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>90%</td>\n<td>105%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>110%</td>\n<td>100%</td>\n<td>110%</td>\n<td>90%\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<ul><li>These values modify the base Damage Reduction values, given in the comparison table below.</li>\n<li>The higher the percentage, the more protection an armour has against that attack type.</li>\n<li>The lower the percentage, the less protection an armour has against that attack type.</li>\n<li>100% = no modifier.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Glance_Rate\">Glance Rate</span></h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Armour type\n</th>\n<th>Acid\n</th>\n<th>Bite\n</th>\n<th>Burn\n</th>\n<th>Cold\n</th>\n<th>Crush\n</th>\n<th>Pierce\n</th>\n<th>Slash\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Chain_armour_smithing\" title=\"Chain armour smithing\">Chain</a>\n</th>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>65%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Cloth_armour\" title=\"Cloth armour\">Cloth</a>\n</th>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>55%</td>\n<td>40%</td>\n<td>40%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Dragon_scale_armour\" title=\"Dragon scale armour\">Dragon scale</a>\n</th>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>45%</td>\n<td>55%</td>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>50%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Drake_hide_armour\" title=\"Category:Drake hide armour\">Drake hide</a>\n</th>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>55%</td>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>60%</td>\n<td>25%</td>\n<td>40%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Leather_armour\" title=\"Leather armour\">Leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>40%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>55%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>35%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Plate_armour\" title=\"Plate armour\">Plate</a>\n</th>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>30%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Studded_leather_armour\" title=\"Studded leather armour\">Studded leather</a>\n</th>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>65%</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>30%\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<ul><li>These values determine the chance that an attack will glance, causing no damage.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Additional Metal Armour Properties</b>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Material\n</th>\n<th>Damage Reduction</th>\n<th>Movement</th>\n<th>Glance\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Adamantine</td>\n<td>5.00%</td>\n<td>5.00%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brass</td>\n<td>1.00%</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bronze</td>\n<td>1.00%</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Copper</td>\n<td>-1.00%</td>\n<td>1.00%</td>\n<td>-2.00%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electrum</td>\n<td>0.50%</td>\n<td>-1.00%</td>\n<td>2.00%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Empyrean</td>\n<td>2.00%</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Glimmersteel</td>\n<td>5.00%</td>\n<td>10.00%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold</td>\n<td>-1.00%</td>\n<td>-5.00%</td>\n<td>2.50%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Iron</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lead</td>\n<td>-2.50%</td>\n<td>-2.50%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Seryll</td>\n<td>5.00%</td>\n<td>10.00%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Silver</td>\n<td>-0.75%</td>\n<td>-2.00%</td>\n<td>1.00%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Steel</td>\n<td>2.50%</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tin</td>\n<td>-1.75%</td>\n<td>2.00%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Zinc</td>\n<td>-2.00%</td>\n<td>2.50%</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3);
