>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>35</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>3\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sludge</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td>2,000</td>\n<td>5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"6\"><a href=\"/index.php/Mol-Rehan\" title=\"Mol-Rehan\">Mol-Rehan</a></td>\n<td>Burning swamp</td>\n<td>Low left, low, low right</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>43</td>\n<td>12,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cricket</td>\n<td>High left, high, high right</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>8,000</td>\n<td>2,000</td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Faithpush</td>\n<td>Low left, low, low right</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>27</td>\n<td>6,000</td>\n<td>8,000</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prod</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>55</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rampant delusion</td>\n<td>Left, right</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>8,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sensitive warden</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"6\"><a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a></td>\n<td>Dragontail</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>14,000</td>\n<td>3,000</td>\n<td>7\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Horse\'s ass</td>\n<td>Left, right</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>35</td>\n<td>12,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mask of defiance</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>65</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>9\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Moist hind</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>55</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slow scorpio</td>\n<td>Low left, low, low right</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>14,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>7\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wanderer</td>\n<td>Low left, low right</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>14,000</td>\n<td>13,000</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"6\"><a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom Isles</a></td>\n<td>Cold clouds</td>\n<td>High left, high, high right</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>16,000</td>\n<td>10,000</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eyesocket</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>45</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Low rider</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>19</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td>2,000</td>\n<td>5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Red flood</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>55</td>\n<td>15,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sharp twig</td>\n<td>Left, right</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>8,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Snakebite</td>\n<td>Low left, low, low right</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>43</td>\n<td>12,000</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>7\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(20876, 5281, 'Description', 'Description', 'An over 3 meters long muscle, this grey-green snake is formidable. An anaconda is a long, dangerous snake that spawns primarily in areas within the influence of Vynora and at Holy sites of Vynora. They have been known to spawn elsewhere on occasion. When idle, it is curled up on the ground like a rope , keeping a very low profile. Due to its green color, it is even harder to spot on grass , and most likely to be stepped on. An anaconda is very strong (some say about the strength of a scorpion ). Its bite causes medium wounds when in lower quality armour . Anacondas are rather slow and without being encumbered , it can be outrun easily, although it can chase for quite a while. It has a large target radius - before you see it, it will have seen you!', '<p><i>An over 3 meters long muscle, this grey-green snake is formidable.</i>\n</p>\n<p>An <b>anaconda</b> is a long, dangerous snake that spawns primarily in areas within the influence of <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> and at <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Holy_site\" title=\"Holy site\">Holy sites</a> of Vynora. They have been known to spawn elsewhere on occasion. When idle, it is curled up on the ground like a <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">rope</a>, keeping a very low profile. Due to its green color, it is even harder to spot on <a href=\"/index.php/Grass_tile\" title=\"Grass tile\">grass</a>, and most likely to be stepped on.\n</p>\n<p>An anaconda is very strong (some say about the strength of a <a href=\"/index.php/Scorpion\" title=\"Scorpion\">scorpion</a>). Its bite causes medium <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wounds</a> when in lower <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armour</a>. Anacondas are rather slow and without <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength#Carrying_capacity\" title=\"Body strength\">being encumbered</a>, it can be outrun easily, although it can chase for quite a while. It has a large target radius - before you see it, it will have seen you!\n</p>', 0),
(20877, 5281, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Spirit guards do not attack anacondas when in the influence area of an altar of a White light deity . Its speed is affected by its age . It is possible to pen an anaconda, as they do not bash fences. An anaconda looking at its dinner', '<ul><li>Spirit guards do not attack anacondas when in the influence area of an <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altar</a> of a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/White_light\" title=\"White light\">White light</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Gods\" title=\"Gods\">deity</a>.</li>\n<li>Its speed is affected by its <a href=\"/index.php/Age\" title=\"Age\">age</a>.</li>\n<li>It is possible to pen an anaconda, as they do not bash fences.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"thumb tleft\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:302px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Anaconda1.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"387\" data-file-width=\"390\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"298\" src=\"/images/thumb/4/4a/Anaconda1.png/300px-Anaconda1.png\" srcset=\"/images/4/4a/Anaconda1.png 1.5x\" width=\"300\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Anaconda1.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>An anaconda looking at its dinner</div></div></div>', 1),
(20889, 1068, 'Description', 'Description', 'To move about unseen, unheard, unnoticed', '<p>To move about unseen, unheard, unnoticed\n</p>', 0),
(20890, 1068, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To engage Stealth, you have to drag the Stealth icon onto the Quickbar , and then press the Stealth button on the Quickbar. Body Control gives a better success at stealthing. You must be at least one tile away from another creature or player to try to stealth. It appears to be easier to stealth on tree tiles and more difficult on road tiles. It is possible to completely disappear from local when in stealth mode. However, if another player in local has higher body control, you will fall out of stealth mode. It is possible to be completely invisible to other players and creatures when in stealth mode. Your name will still be visible in village and alliance chat. You move slower when in stealth. The actual amount of speed reduction here needs to be more fully researched. It is easier to stealth at nighttime. Moving on or across roads has a greater chance to unstealth you. Talking in the local chat tab will unstealth you. Using certain abilities such as Refresh will unstealth you. High mind logic players will have a chance to see you through your Stealth .', '<ul><li>To engage Stealth, you have to drag the Stealth icon onto the <a href=\"/index.php/Quickbar\" title=\"Quickbar\">Quickbar</a>, and then press the Stealth button on the Quickbar.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Body_Control\" title=\"Body Control\">Body Control</a> gives a better success at stealthing.</li>\n<li>You must be at least one tile away from another creature or player to try to stealth.</li>\n<li>It appears to be easier to stealth on tree tiles and more difficult on road tiles.</li>\n<li>It is possible to completely disappear from local when in stealth mode. However, if another player in local has higher body control, you will fall out of stealth mode.</li>\n<li>It is possible to be completely invisible to other players and creatures when in stealth mode.\n<ul><li>Your name will still be visible in village and alliance chat.</li></ul></li>\n<li>You move slower when in stealth. The actual amount of speed reduction here needs to be more fully researched.</li>\n<li>It is easier to stealth at nighttime.</li>\n<li>Moving on or across roads has a greater chance to unstealth you.</li>\n<li>Talking in the local chat tab will unstealth you.</li>\n<li>Using certain abilities such as <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Refresh\" title=\"Refresh\">Refresh</a> will unstealth you.</li>\n<li>High <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> players will have a chance to see you through your <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Stealth</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(20891, 1068, 'Icon', 'Icon', '', '<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Stealth.png\"><img alt=\"Stealth.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"31\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"32\" src=\"/images/1/19/Stealth.png\" width=\"31\"/></a>\n</p>', 2),
(20892, 4235, 'Description', 'Description', 'A slender bracelet.', '<p><i>A slender bracelet.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(20893, 4235, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Can be worn on the arm. Can be enchanted with the Nolocate spell. Equipping a bracelet removes your sleeve, but cannot be seen on your character. Rift bracelets can be equipped in the arm slots. Two of the same kind must be worn in order to receive the bonus.', '<ul><li>Can be worn on the arm.</li>\n<li>Can be enchanted with the <a href=\"/index.php/Nolocate\" title=\"Nolocate\">Nolocate</a> spell.</li>\n<li>Equipping a bracelet removes your sleeve, but cannot be seen on your character.</li>\n<li>Rift bracelets can be equipped in the arm slots. Two of the same kind must be worn in order to receive the bonus.</li></ul>', 1),
(20912, 5290, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fashionable wooden mailbox that looks like a rich mansion. - If enchanted - Courier or Dark Messenger has been cast on it, so it seems to be possessed by something.', '<p><i>A fashionable wooden mailbox that looks like a rich mansion.</i> - If enchanted - <i>Courier or Dark Messenger has been cast on it, so it seems to be possessed by something.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(20913, 5290, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Once enchanted with Courier or Dark messenger by a priest , the mailbox can be used to transport mail to other players. The quality of the cast will affect how fast mail travels from the mailbox. The mailboxes used to send and receive must both be enchanted. A failure on casting cannot shatter the mailbox.  Enchanting multiple times has a chance of improving the cast without any risk. The quality of the finished mailbox does not affect the mail system but will reduce the decay rate of the mailbox itself. May not be loaded or picked up after completion, but may be pushed.', '<ul><li>Once enchanted with <a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">Courier</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dark_messenger\" title=\"Dark messenger\">Dark messenger</a> by a <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priest</a>, the mailbox can be used to transport <a href=\"/index.php/Mail\" title=\"Mail\">mail</a> to other players. The quality of the cast will affect how fast mail travels from the mailbox.</li>\n<li>The mailboxes used to send and receive must both be enchanted.</li>\n<li>A failure on casting cannot shatter the mailbox.  Enchanting multiple times has a chance of improving the cast without any risk.</li>\n<li>The quality of the finished mailbox does not affect the mail system but will reduce the decay rate of the mailbox itself.</li>\n<li>May not be loaded or picked up after completion, but may be pushed.</li></ul>', 1),
(20914, 5290, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Mail Spirit house Spirit cottage Spirit castle', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mail\" title=\"Mail\">Mail</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_house\" title=\"Spirit house\">Spirit house</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_cottage\" title=\"Spirit cottage\">Spirit cottage</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spirit_castle\" title=\"Spirit castle\">Spirit castle</a></li></ul>', 2),
(20915, 5291, 'Description', 'Description', 'Collected from a creature\'s belly, this can be used to create candles and in cooking.', '<p><i>Collected from a creature\'s belly, this can be used to create candles and in cooking.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(20916, 5291, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in some cooking recipes and in creating candles and farmer\'s salve . Can be obtained by butchering animals, including starving animals. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage. Creatures that yield fat Animal Weight (kg) Bison 4.00 Black wolf 3.00 Bull 4.00 Calf 3.00 Cow 4.00 Deer 4.00 Dog 3.00 Foal 3.00 Hen 1.00 Horse 4.00 Pheasant 1.00 Pig 3.00 Rooster 1.00 Seal 2.00 Wild boar 3.00', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes and in creating <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Candles\" title=\"Candles\">candles</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Farmer%27s_salve\" title=\"Farmer\'s salve\">farmer\'s salve</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be obtained by butchering animals, including starving animals.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n<caption>Creatures that yield fat\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th width=\"100\">Animal\n</th>\n<th width=\"100\"><a href=\"/index.php/Weight\" title=\"Weight\">Weight</a> (kg)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Bison\" title=\"Bison\">Bison</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Black_wolf\" title=\"Black wolf\">Black wolf</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Bull\" title=\"Bull\">Bull</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Calf\" title=\"Calf\">Calf</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Cow\" title=\"Cow\">Cow</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Deer\" title=\"Deer\">Deer</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Dog\" title=\"Dog\">Dog</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Foal\" title=\"Foal\">Foal</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Hen\" title=\"Hen\">Hen</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Horse\" title=\"Horse\">Horse</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Pheasant\" title=\"Pheasant\">Pheasant</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Pig\" title=\"Pig\">Pig</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Rooster\" title=\"Rooster\">Rooster</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Seal\" title=\"Seal\">Seal</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">2.00\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/index.php/Wild_boar\" title=\"Wild boar\">Wild boar</a>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3.00\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 1),
(20917, 5291, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fat Cooking', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fat\" title=\"Fat\">Fat</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">Cooking</a></li></ul>', 2),
(20921, 5293, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Animal fat', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Animal_fat\" title=\"Animal fat\">Animal fat</a></li></ul>', 0),
(20930, 5292, 'Description', 'Description', 'A candle made from tallow repeatedly dipped around a cloth wick.', '<p><i>A candle made from tallow repeatedly dipped around a cloth wick.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(20931, 5292, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Candles will emit light upon being lit. They lose quality over time.  They are also part of candelabra and Snow lantern . On success, 1.00kg of fat and 0.08kg of string is consumed to create a 0.05kg candle. If you fail creating a candle, you use 0.005 of the animal fat and 0.01 of the string of cloth. The quality of animal fat determines the chance to create a candle. The quality of the string of cloth used determines the quality of the candle. A candle\'s quality is no more than the quality of the string of cloth. Candles burn at a rate of .5QL per minute. Cannot be stored in a Bsb .', '<ul><li>Candles will emit light upon being lit. They lose quality over time.  They are also part of <a href=\"/index.php/Candelabra\" title=\"Candelabra\">candelabra</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Snow_lantern\" title=\"Snow lantern\">Snow lantern</a>.</li>\n<li>On success, 1.00kg of fat and 0.08kg of string is consumed to create a 0.05kg candle.</li>\n<li>If you fail creating a candle, you use 0.005 of the animal fat and 0.01 of the string of cloth.</li>\n<li>The quality of animal fat determines the chance to create a candle.</li>\n<li>The quality of the string of cloth used determines the quality of the candle. A candle\'s quality is no more than the quality of the string of cloth.</li>\n<li>Candles burn at a rate of .5QL per minute.</li>\n<li>Cannot be stored in a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Bsb\" title=\"Bsb\">Bsb</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(20932, 5292, 'Other personal lamp options', 'Other_personal_lamp_options', 'Lantern Carved pumpkin Torch Brass oil lamp Metal torch Items with glow runes attached', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Lantern\" title=\"Lantern\">Lantern</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Carved_pumpkin\" title=\"Carved pumpkin\">Carved pumpkin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Torch\" title=\"Torch\">Torch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Brass_oil_lamp\" title=\"Brass oil lamp\">Brass oil lamp</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_torch\" title=\"Metal torch\">Metal torch</a></li>\n<li>Items with glow <a href=\"/index.php/Runes\" title=\"Runes\">runes</a> attached</li></ul>', 2),
(20933, 1272, 'Description', 'Description', 'A couple of feathers and pearls attached to a few looped silver strings. Given out with at 99 quality and with each use this is reduced by 1.', '<p><i>A couple of feathers and pearls attached to a few looped silver strings.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Given out with at 99 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> and with each use this is reduced by 1.\n</p>', 0),
(20934, 1272, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'When used, the amulet will give the player the unstoppable condition for 30 seconds, increasing their movement speed, each use lowers the quality by 1.', '<p>When used, the amulet will give the player the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Unstoppable\" title=\"Unstoppable\">unstoppable</a> condition for 30 seconds, increasing their movement speed, each use lowers the quality by 1.\n</p>', 1),
(20935, 1272, 'History', 'History', 'A gift from Santa to premium players in 2007.', '<p>A gift from Santa to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> players in 2007.\n</p>', 2),
(20936, 1272, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A no-drop item.', '<ul><li>A <a href=\"/index.php/Nodrop\" title=\"Nodrop\">no-drop</a> item.</li></ul>', 3),
(21002, 5307, 'Description', 'Description', 'A ship  with square sails steered by two side rudders connected to each other.', '<p><i>A ship  with square sails steered by two side rudders connected to each other.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21003, 5307, 'Vessel details', 'Vessel_details', 'Requires 21.05 mind logic to be able to command it. Passengers: 1 captain + 6 crew. Maximum speed: 28 km/h (in a gale ) Hold Capacity: 49 large crates. see #Loadable Items and #Useful Quantities for more info. Creature Cage Capacity: 5 Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt. Weight: 1400kg (20 body strength minimum to drag). Size: 5 tiles by 2 tiles Height: 25 dirt from water level to deck', '<ul><li>Requires 21.05 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to be able to command it.</li>\n<li>Passengers: 1 captain + 6 crew.</li>\n<li>Maximum speed: 28 km/h (in a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gale\" title=\"Gale\">gale</a>)</li>\n<li>Hold Capacity: 49 large crates. see <a href=\"#Loadable_Items\">#Loadable Items</a> and <a href=\"#Useful_Quantities\">#Useful Quantities</a> for more info.</li>\n<li>Creature Cage Capacity: 5</li>\n<li>Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt.</li>\n<li>Weight: 1400kg (20 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> minimum to drag).</li>\n<li>Size: 5 tiles by 2 tiles</li>\n<li>Height: 25 dirt from water level to deck</li></ul>', 1),
(21004, 5307, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The QL of the keel section that is active is what effects creation chance. Ships with a quality of less than 10 cannot be commanded. This includes ships whose damage percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality). Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again. Ships cannot be hauled up ladders Last wood piece determines final wood type. Example, adding walnut peg as the final piece will complete the Corbita as a walnut Corbita.', '<ul><li>The QL of the keel section that is active is what effects creation chance.</li>\n<li>Ships with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of less than 10 cannot be commanded.\n<ul><li>This includes ships whose <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality).</li>\n<li>Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Ships cannot be hauled up ladders</li>\n<li>Last wood piece determines final wood type. Example, adding walnut peg as the final piece will complete the Corbita as a walnut Corbita.</li></ul>', 2),
(21005, 5307, 'Loadable Items', 'Loadable_Items', 'List is a work in progress. Forge Oven Large crate - 49 Small crate - 85 Wagon Bulk storage bin - 5', '<p><i>List is a work in progress.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Oven</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a> - 49</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a> - 85</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a> - 5</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(21006, 5307, 'Useful Quantities', 'Useful_Quantities', 'can fit 1 wagon with 4 Creature Cages and 6 Large Crates . can fit 2 Large Carts with 4 Creature Cages and at least 18 Large Crates .', '<ul><li>can fit 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a> with 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a> and 6 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large Crates</a>.</li>\n<li>can fit 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large Carts</a> with 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a> and at least 18 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large Crates</a>.</li></ul>', 4),
(21007, 5307, 'Non-loadable items', 'Non-loadable_items', 'See Load cargo for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type. .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto} Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.', '<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">Load cargo</a> for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120390\">.mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto}</style>\n<div class=\"boxstyle infoboxbox\">\n<div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"24\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/24px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/36px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/48px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"24\"/></a></div>\n<span><strong>Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.</strong></span></div>', 5),
(21008, 5308, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sturdy one-masted merchant ship with a flat bottom. A medium difficulty ship, the cog requires fewer sails but more wooden materials than the corbita and is harder to create. One large advantage it has over the similarly-sized corbita is that the second passenger to board is put into the crow\'s nest , giving them a great view of the surrounding area. Cogs are great merchant ships as they are a large size, not difficult to build and as a result inexpensive to buy. They are good for long journeys but are impractical for short hops, especially in light winds.', '<p><i>A sturdy one-masted merchant ship with a flat bottom.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A medium difficulty ship, the cog requires fewer sails but more wooden materials than the <a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">corbita</a> and is harder to create. One large advantage it has over the similarly-sized corbita is that the second passenger to board is put into the <a href=\"/index.php/Crow%27s_nest\" title=\"Crow\'s nest\">crow\'s nest</a>, giving them a great view of the surrounding area.\n</p>\n<p>Cogs are great merchant ships as they are a large size, not difficult to build and as a result inexpensive to buy. They are good for long journeys but are impractical for short hops, especially in light winds.\n</p>', 0),
(21009, 5308, 'Vessel details', 'Vessel_details', 'Requires 22 mind logic to be able to command it. Passengers: 1 captain + 8 crew. Maximum speed: 33.22 km/h (solo, with a gale in the back) Hold Capacity: 29 large crates. see #Loadable Items and #Useful Quantities for more info. Creature Cage Capacity: 6 Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt. Size: ~ 5 tiles long and 2 tiles wide Height: 40 dirt from water level to deck(?) and ~ 170 dirt from waterlevel to top', '<ul><li>Requires 22 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to be able to command it.</li>\n<li>Passengers: 1 captain + 8 crew.</li>\n<li>Maximum speed: 33.22 km/h (solo, with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gale\" title=\"Gale\">gale</a> in the back)</li>\n<li>Hold Capacity: 29 large crates. see <a href=\"#Loadable_Items\">#Loadable Items</a> and <a href=\"#Useful_Quantities\">#Useful Quantities</a> for more info.</li>\n<li>Creature Cage Capacity: 6</li>\n<li>Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt.</li>\n<li>Size: ~ 5 tiles long and 2 tiles wide</li>\n<li>Height: 40 dirt from water level to deck(?) and ~ 170 dirt from waterlevel to top</li></ul>', 1),
(21010, 5308, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Ships with a quality of less than 10 cannot be commanded. This includes ships whose damage percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality). Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again. The quality of each of the keel sections affects the chance of being created. Ships cannot be hauled up ladders', '<ul><li>Ships with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of less than 10 cannot be commanded.\n<ul><li>This includes ships whose <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality).</li>\n<li>Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again.</li></ul></li>\n<li>The quality of each of the keel sections affects the chance of being created.</li>\n<li>Ships cannot be hauled up ladders</li></ul>', 2),
(21011, 5308, 'Loadable Items', 'Loadable_Items', 'List is a work in progress. Forge - 13 Oven Large crate - 29 Small crate - 51 Bulk storage bin - 3 Creature cage - 4 Tested. 11 small rafts 1 large chest 2 forges', '<p><i>List is a work in progress.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forge</a> - 13</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Oven</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a> - 29</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a> - 51</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a> - 3</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature cage</a> - 4</li></ul>\n<p><i>Tested.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li>11 small rafts</li>\n<li>1 large chest</li>\n<li>2 forges</li></ul>', 3),
(21012, 5308, 'Useful Quantities', 'Useful_Quantities', 'can fit 2 Large Carts with 4 Creature Cages . cannot fit 1 wagon even when empty.', '<ul><li>can fit 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large Carts</a> with 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a>.</li>\n<li>cannot fit 1 wagon even when empty.</li></ul>', 4),
(21013, 5308, 'Non-loadable items', 'Non-loadable_items', 'See Load cargo for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type. .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto} Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.', '<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">Load cargo</a> for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120390\">.mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto}</style>\n<div class=\"boxstyle infoboxbox\">\n<div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"24\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/24px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/36px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/48px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"24\"/></a></div>\n<span><strong>Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.</strong></span></div>', 5),
(21014, 5309, 'Description', 'Description', 'A ship with a clinker-built hull assembled with iron rivets, and one mast with a square yard sail. In insufficient winds it is rowed with oars. The side rudder is on the starboard side.', '<p><i>A ship with a clinker-built hull assembled with iron rivets, and one mast with a square yard sail. In insufficient winds it is rowed with oars. The side rudder is on the starboard side.</i>\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(21015, 5309, 'Vessel details', 'Vessel_details', 'Requires 23 mind logic to be able to command Passengers: 1 captain + 12 crew Maximum speed: 27 km/h (solo, with a gale in the back) Hold Capacity: 43 large crates. see #Loadable Items and #Useful Quantities for more info. Creature Cage Capacity: 4 Minimum passable depth: 5 dirt 29 body strength minimum to drag. Size: 4 tiles by 1 tiles Height: 8 dirt from water level to deck(?)', '<ul><li>Requires 23 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to be able to command</li>\n<li>Passengers: 1 captain + 12 crew</li>\n<li>Maximum speed: 27 km/h (solo, with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gale\" title=\"Gale\">gale</a> in the back)</li>\n<li>Hold Capacity: 43 large crates. see <a href=\"#Loadable_Items\">#Loadable Items</a> and <a href=\"#Useful_Quantities\">#Useful Quantities</a> for more info.</li>\n<li>Creature Cage Capacity: 4</li>\n<li>Minimum passable depth: 5 dirt</li>\n<li>29 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> minimum to drag.</li>\n<li>Size: 4 tiles by 1 tiles</li>\n<li>Height: 8 dirt from water level to deck(?)</li></ul>', 1),
(21016, 5309, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Ships with a quality of less than 10 cannot be commanded. This includes ships whose damage percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality). Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again. One of the most difficult ships to build. Higher quality of parts being attached improves chance of success. Knarrs show in the creation list when cogs are between 13% and 14%, and corbitas are at 25% To view creation chance see keel section . Ships cannot be hauled up ladders Last wood piece determines final wood type. Example, adding walnut peg as the final piece will complete the Knarr as a walnut boat.', '<ul><li>Ships with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of less than 10 cannot be commanded.\n<ul><li>This includes ships whose <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality).</li>\n<li>Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again.</li></ul></li>\n<li>One of the most difficult ships to build. Higher quality of parts being attached improves chance of success.</li>\n<li>Knarrs show in the creation list when <a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">cogs</a> are between 13% and 14%, and <a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">corbitas</a> are at 25%</li>\n<li>To view creation chance see <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">keel section</a>.</li>\n<li>Ships cannot be hauled up ladders</li>\n<li>Last wood piece determines final wood type. Example, adding walnut peg as the final piece will complete the Knarr as a walnut boat.</li></ul>', 2),
(21017, 5309, 'Loadable Items', 'Loadable_Items', 'List is a work in progress. Large crate - 43 (max of 12900 items) Small crate - 75 (max of 11250 items) Bulk storage bin - 4 Wagon (+4 Large crate) Large cart Small cart Forge Oven Large chest Bed Creature cage - 4 Smelter', '<p><i>List is a work in progress.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a> - 43 (max of 12900 items)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a> - 75 (max of 11250 items)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a> - 4</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a> (+4 Large crate)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large cart</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">Small cart</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Oven</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">Large chest</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">Bed</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature cage</a> - 4</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">Smelter</a></li></ul>', 3),
(21018, 5309, 'Useful Quantities', 'Useful_Quantities', 'Can fit 100 felled trees. Can fit 43 large crates and 1 small crate . Can fit 4 bulk storage bins and 6 large crates . Can fit 1 wagon and 4 Creature Cages can fit 2 Large Carts with 4 Creature Cages and at least 18 Large Crates . can fit 1 Smelter , 1 wagon , and 2 Creature Cages', '<ul><li>Can fit 100 felled trees.</li>\n<li>Can fit 43 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a> and 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">small crate</a>.</li>\n<li>Can fit 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">bulk storage bins</a> and 6 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">large crates</a>.</li>\n<li>Can fit 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a> and 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a></li>\n<li>can fit 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">Large Carts</a> with 4 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a> and at least 18 <a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large Crates</a>.</li>\n<li>can fit 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Smelter\" title=\"Smelter\">Smelter</a>, 1 <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagon</a>, and 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Creature_cage\" title=\"Creature cage\">Creature Cages</a></li></ul>', 4),
(21019, 5309, 'Non-loadable items', 'Non-loadable_items', 'See Load cargo for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type.', '<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">Load cargo</a> for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type.\n</p>', 5),
(21020, 5310, 'Description', 'Description', 'An impressive merchant ship.', '<p><i>An impressive merchant ship.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21021, 5310, 'Vessel details', 'Vessel_details', 'Requires 24 mind logic to be able to command it. Passengers: 1 captain + 13 crew. Maximum speed: 30.88km/h (solo, with a gale in the back). Hold Capacity: 62 large crates. see #Loadable Items for more info. Creature Cage Capacity: 8 Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt. 35 body strength minimum to drag. Hull size: 5 x 2 tiles Overall length: 6 x 2 tiles. Height: 35 dirt from water level to deck(?).', '<ul><li>Requires 24 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to be able to command it.</li>\n<li>Passengers: 1 captain + 13 crew.</li>\n<li>Maximum speed: 30.88km/h (solo, with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gale\" title=\"Gale\">gale</a> in the back).</li>\n<li>Hold Capacity: 62 large crates. see <a href=\"#Loadable_Items\">#Loadable Items</a> for more info.</li>\n<li>Creature Cage Capacity: 8</li>\n<li>Minimum passable depth: 20 dirt.</li>\n<li>35 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">body strength</a> minimum to drag.</li>\n<li>Hull size: 5 x 2 tiles</li>\n<li>Overall length: 6 x 2 tiles.</li>\n<li>Height: 35 dirt from water level to deck(?).</li></ul>', 1),
(21022, 5310, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You do not have to have 35 strength to avoid beaching the boat - so long as it is not moored, you can still push and pull the boat off of a reef. Ships with a quality of less than 10 cannot be commanded. This includes ships whose damage percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality). Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again. The most difficult ships to build. Higher quality parts improves chance of success. Ships cannot be hauled up ladders Can be loaded with a wagon or a large cart, and enough animals to drive them.', '<ul><li>You do not have to have 35 strength to avoid beaching the boat - so long as it is not moored, you can still push and pull the boat off of a reef.</li>\n<li>Ships with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of less than 10 cannot be commanded.\n<ul><li>This includes ships whose <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality).</li>\n<li>Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again.</li></ul></li>\n<li>The most difficult ships to build. Higher quality parts improves chance of success.</li>\n<li>Ships cannot be hauled up ladders</li>\n<li>Can be loaded with a wagon or a large cart, and enough animals to drive them.</li></ul>', 2),
(21023, 5310, 'Loadable Items', 'Loadable_Items', 'List is a work in progress. Forge Oven Large crate - 62 Small crate - 100 Bulk storage bin - 6 Wagon and 2 Bulk storage bin', '<p><i>List is a work in progress.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Forge\" title=\"Forge\">Forge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oven\" title=\"Oven\">Oven</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_crate\" title=\"Large crate\">Large crate</a> - 62</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_crate\" title=\"Small crate\">Small crate</a> - 100</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a> - 6</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">Wagon</a> and 2 <a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a></li></ul>', 3),
(21024, 5310, 'Non-loadable items', 'Non-loadable_items', 'See Load cargo for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type. .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto} Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.', '<p>See <a href=\"/index.php/Load_cargo\" title=\"Load cargo\">Load cargo</a> for exhaustive list of loadable/non-loadable items by smallest vehicle type.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120390\">.mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto}</style>\n<div class=\"boxstyle infoboxbox\">\n<div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"24\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/24px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/36px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/48px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"24\"/></a></div>\n<span><strong>Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.</strong></span></div>', 4),
(21028, 5312, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a standard oar, about the length of a tall man.', '<p><i>This is a standard oar, about the length of a tall man.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21029, 5312, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in creation of: Rowing boats Small sailing boats Corbitas Cogs Knarrs Caravels', '<ul><li>Used in creation of:</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rowing_boat\" title=\"Rowing boat\">Rowing boats</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_sailing_boat\" title=\"Small sailing boat\">Small sailing boats</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">Corbitas</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cogs</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">Knarrs</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Caravel\" title=\"Caravel\">Caravels</a></li></ul></dd></dl>', 1),
(21030, 5312, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The QL of the saw affects success of creation. Making an oar will only consume 8.0kg of the log , leaving the remainder intact.', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Saw\" title=\"Saw\">saw</a> affects success of creation.</li>\n<li>Making an oar will only consume 8.0kg of the <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a>, leaving the remainder intact.</li></ul>', 2),
(21031, 5313, 'Uses', 'Uses', 'Caravel Cog Corbita Knarr', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Caravel\" title=\"Caravel\">Caravel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cog</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Corbita\" title=\"Corbita\">Corbita</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Knarr\" title=\"Knarr\">Knarr</a></li></ul>', 0),
(21032, 5304, 'Description', 'Description', 'Ship building consists of making ships and the parts needed to construct them. Ship building is a sub-skill of carpentry .', '<p>Ship building consists of making ships and the parts needed to construct them.\n</p>\n<p>Ship building is a sub-skill of <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a>. \n</p>', 0),
(21033, 5304, 'Items', 'Items', 'See: Category:Ship building items See also ship for information about using ships. Ownership The person attaching the last piece to a boat will become the owner. Boats can be managed by the owner to have various permissions, like allowing all friends to command the boat, or to transfer ownership to another player. Ownership can be taken from another player on the Epic cluster and the Chaos server, but not on any other server in the Freedom cluster. To take ownership of a boat you must board the boat as captain whilst the current owner is an enemy. Creation Some ship building items are impossible to create with 0 skill, but at least seat and hull plank should be available to get the initial 1 skill. If you\'re making your first ever boat it is recommended to not make the keels as the first item. You should start by making hull plank , tenon , peg , and belaying pin . Then you make some of the more complicated pieces like oar or seat , and you improve those as far as you can to get your ship building skill up. Once your skill has reached 10-15, you may create the keel sections with decent success rate. All ships are started by using a keel section on a keel section . (Note: Each keel section weighs 60kg. Therefore you must be able to carry 120kg in order to start a ship.) For more detailed information on creation chance for the various ship types, see Keel section . Weight in parentheses is raw material weight required to create. Hatchet on Felled Tree Keel section (90.00kg) Small mast (72.00kg) Medium mast (96.00kg) Large mast (120.00kg) Tall mast (148.00kg) Saw on Log Seat (24.00kg) Hull plank (8.00kg) Oar (8.00kg) Deck board (5.60kg) Carving Knife on Log Tenon (1.40kg) Large tackle (13.00kg) Small tackle (6.50kg) Carving Knife on Shaft Belaying pin (0.65kg) Pegs (0.10kg) are a vital part of ship building, but count as regular carpentry items. Multiple Parts Rudder Ship helm Stern Crow\'s nest Rig', '<p>See:<a href=\"/index.php/Category:Ship_building_items\" title=\"Category:Ship building items\">Category:Ship building items</a>\n</p>\n<p>See also <a href=\"/index.php/Ship\" title=\"Ship\">ship</a> for information about using ships. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ownership\">Ownership</span></h3>\n<ul><li>The person attaching the last piece to a boat will become the owner.</li>\n<li>Boats can be managed by the owner to have various permissions, like allowing all friends to command the boat, or to transfer ownership to another player.</li>\n<li>Ownership can be taken from another player on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Epic\" title=\"Epic\">Epic</a> cluster and the <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a> server, but not on any other server in the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> cluster. To take ownership of a boat you must board the boat as captain whilst the current owner is an enemy.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Creation\">Creation</span></h3>\n<p>Some ship building items are impossible to create with 0 skill, but at least <a href=\"/index.php/Seat\" title=\"Seat\">seat</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Hull_plank\" title=\"Hull plank\">hull plank</a> should be available to get the initial 1 skill.\n</p>\n<p>If you\'re making your first ever boat it is recommended to not make the keels as the first item. You should start by making <a href=\"/index.php/Hull_plank\" title=\"Hull plank\">hull plank</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Tenon\" title=\"Tenon\">tenon</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Peg\" title=\"Peg\">peg</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Belaying_pin\" title=\"Belaying pin\">belaying pin</a>. Then you make some of the more complicated pieces like <a href=\"/index.php/Oar\" title=\"Oar\">oar</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Seat\" title=\"Seat\">seat</a>, and you improve those as far as you can to get your <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">ship building</a> skill up. Once your skill has reached 10-15, you may create the <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">keel sections</a> with decent success rate.\n</p>\n<p>All ships are started by using a <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">keel section</a> on a <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">keel section</a>. (Note: Each keel section weighs 60kg. Therefore you must be able to carry 120kg in order to start a ship.)\n</p>\n<p>For more detailed information on creation chance for the various ship types, see <a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">Keel section</a>.\n</p>\n<p><b>Weight in parentheses is raw material weight required to create.</b>\n</p>\n<p><b>Hatchet on Felled Tree</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Keel_section\" title=\"Keel section\">Keel section</a> (90.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_mast\" title=\"Small mast\">Small mast</a> (72.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Medium_mast\" title=\"Medium mast\">Medium mast</a> (96.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_mast\" title=\"Large mast\">Large mast</a> (120.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tall_mast\" title=\"Tall mast\">Tall mast</a> (148.00kg)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Saw on Log</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Seat\" title=\"Seat\">Seat</a> (24.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hull_plank\" title=\"Hull plank\">Hull plank</a> (8.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Oar\" title=\"Oar\">Oar</a> (8.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Deck_board\" title=\"Deck board\">Deck board</a> (5.60kg)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Carving Knife on Log</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Tenon\" title=\"Tenon\">Tenon</a> (1.40kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_tackle\" title=\"Large tackle\">Large tackle</a> (13.00kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_tackle\" title=\"Small tackle\">Small tackle</a> (6.50kg)</li></ul>\n<p><b>Carving Knife on Shaft</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Belaying_pin\" title=\"Belaying pin\">Belaying pin</a> (0.65kg)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Peg\" title=\"Peg\">Pegs</a> (0.10kg) are a vital part of ship building, but count as regular <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> items.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Multiple Parts</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Rudder\" title=\"Rudder\">Rudder</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ship_helm\" title=\"Ship helm\">Ship helm</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stern\" title=\"Stern\">Stern</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crow%27s_nest\" title=\"Crow\'s nest\">Crow\'s nest</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rig\" title=\"Rig\">Rig</a></li></ul>', 1),
(21034, 5304, 'Ship details overview', 'Ship_details_overview', 'Component Weight Imp S. Cart L. Cart Crude canoe Rowing boat Small sailing boat Corbita Cog Knarr Caravel Skill to Start NA NA NA NA 1 1 5 7 15 23 34 Occupants NA NA NA NA 2 3 5 7 9 13 14 Cargo Volume (kg) NA NA 760 ? 0 760 760 >20,000 >20,000 >20,000 >20,000 Mind logic NA NA NA 20.1 <20 <20 20.1 21.05 22 23 24 Body strength NA NA NA NA <20 <20 <20 20 <20 ~29 35 Keel section 60 yes no yes 0 3 3 4 4 5 5 Stern 120 yes unfinished unfinished 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 Rudder 13 yes unfinished yes 0 0 0 2 1 1 1 Ship helm 20 yes unfinished yes 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 Hull plank 8 no no yes 0 50 50 200 300 400 400 Seat 20 yes no yes 0 4 4 0 0 0 0 Deck board 4 no yes yes 0 0 0 40 60 80 80 Oar 5 yes no yes 1 2 2 2 2 10 10 Belaying pin 0.5 no yes yes 0 0 4 10 10 10 10 Tenon 1 no yes yes 0 50 50 200 200 200 300 Peg 0.1 no yes yes 6 50 50 400 400 400 600 Rivets 0.2 no yes yes 0 0 0 0 0 200 0 Tar 2 no yes yes 0 10 10 50 50 100 150 Rope 0.5 no yes yes 0 1 0 0 0 0 0 Mooring rope 0.5 no yes yes 0 0 1 4 4 4 8 Thick rope 5.5 no yes yes 0 0 2 8 8 8 12 Triangular rig 0 no unfinished yes 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 Square rig 86 no unfinished unfinished 0 0 0 1 0 0 1 Spinnaker rig 66 no unfinished yes 0 0 0 1 0 0 1 Square yard rig 106 no unfinished unfinished 0 0 0 0 0 1 0 Large square rig 106 no unfinished unfinished 0 0 0 0 1 0 0 Tall square rig 166 no unfinished unfinished 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 For details regarding completed vessel statistics you may also want to see the Vessel Details Table .', '<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Component\n</th>\n<th>Weight</th>\n<th>Imp</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">S. Cart</a></th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">L. Cart</a></th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_canoe\" title=\"Crude canoe\">Crude canoe</a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Rowing_boat\" title=\"Rowing 