ter\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div></td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Green-check.png\"><img alt=\"Green-check.png\" data-file-height=\"32\" data-file-width=\"32\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"20\" src=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/20px-Green-check.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/b/b3/Green-check.png/30px-Green-check.png 1.5x, /images/b/b3/Green-check.png 2x\" style=\"vertical-align: middle\" width=\"20\"/></a></div></div></td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3),
(21747, 5463, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A 5 QL bow trap produced a 2.15 damage wound (un armoured ) A 15QL stick trap produced a 5.5 damage wound (unarmoured) A 50QL stick trap produced two 20 damage wounds (unarmoured) When a trap is set on a dirt or cave floor tile, it is impossible to be detected by examining; this appears to be a bizarre glitch. Traps once set only last a few days. Preferable to stockpile and set as needed. Damage enhancer enchants, such as Rotting touch , do work on traps. Terraforming on tiles that are trapped does not effect the trap. If a trap is set on a tree tile and the tree advances in age (Young to Mature for example) the trap will be destroyed. Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>A 5<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> bow trap produced a 2.15 damage <a href=\"/index.php/Wound\" title=\"Wound\">wound</a> (un<a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armoured</a>)</li>\n<li>A 15QL stick trap produced a 5.5 damage wound (unarmoured)</li>\n<li>A 50QL stick trap produced two 20 damage wounds (unarmoured)</li>\n<li>When a trap is set on a <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Cave_floor\" title=\"Cave floor\">cave floor</a> tile, it is impossible to be detected by examining; this appears to be a bizarre glitch.</li>\n<li>Traps once set only last a few days. Preferable to stockpile and set as needed.</li>\n<li>Damage enhancer enchants, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Rotting_touch\" title=\"Rotting touch\">Rotting touch</a>, do work on traps.</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Terraforming\" title=\"Terraforming\">Terraforming</a> on tiles that are trapped does not effect the trap.</li>\n<li>If a trap is set on a tree tile and the tree advances in age (Young to Mature for example) the trap will be destroyed.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 4),
(21748, 5463, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Thievery > Traps', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Thievery\" title=\"Thievery\">Thievery</a> &gt; Traps</li></ul>', 5),
(21749, 5463, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'It\'s a Trap at 50 skill Trapper at 70 skill Snare Artist at 90 skill', '<ul><li>It\'s a Trap at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Trapper at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Snare Artist at 90 skill</li></ul>', 6),
(21771, 5465, 'Description', 'Description', 'A trap made from ropes and a sharp deadly pole.', '<p><i>A trap made from ropes and a sharp deadly pole.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21772, 5465, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This trap type can be set up on tree tiles . Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>This <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">trap</a> type can be set up on <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 1),
(21773, 5466, 'Description', 'Description', 'A bow mounted on a wooden frame, poised to shoot anyone who triggers it.', '<p><i>A bow mounted on a wooden frame, poised to shoot anyone who triggers it.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21774, 5466, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This trap type can be set up on tree tiles . Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>This <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">trap</a> type can be set up on <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 1),
(21775, 5467, 'Description', 'Description', 'The trap is made from a strong wooden frame, and a spring that triggers a heavy axe. The axe trap is a trap used to deal heavy damage.', '<p><i>The trap is made from a strong wooden frame, and a spring that triggers a heavy axe.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>axe trap</b> is a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">trap</a> used to deal heavy damage.\n</p>', 0),
(21776, 5467, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'Creation success is influenced by the active large nails . Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the plank; failure in continuing will damage the item being added. These are extremely difficult to make and continue, at least 55 carpentry is advised, 75 carpentry, 50 ql large nails = 70% creation chance The success rate is highly dependent on the quality of the material.', '<ul><li>Creation success is influenced by the active <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a>.</li>\n<li>Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the plank; failure in continuing will damage the item being added.</li>\n<li>These are extremely difficult to make and continue, at least 55 carpentry is advised,\n<ul><li>75 carpentry, 50 ql large nails = 70% creation chance</li></ul></li>\n<li>The success rate is highly dependent on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the material.</li></ul>', 1),
(21777, 5467, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'Improvement uses the carpentry skill and items: file , carving knife , pelt , and log Higher quality traps deal more damage', '<ul><li>Improvement uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> skill and items: <a href=\"/index.php/File\" title=\"File\">file</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">pelt</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a></li>\n<li>Higher quality traps deal more <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a></li></ul>', 2),
(21778, 5467, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Axe traps are placed on tree and bush tiles, the traps skill affects the placement chance.', '<p>Axe traps are placed on <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">bush</a> tiles, the <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">traps</a> skill affects the placement chance.\n</p>', 3),
(21779, 5467, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The trap\'s volume is very large; a single trap is too big to fit in a small cart. Improving these is a good way to train carpentry. The axe trap is suspected to be among the most deadly traps, sided closely with the scythe trap Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>The trap\'s volume is very large; a single trap is too big to fit in a small cart.</li>\n<li>Improving these is a good way to train carpentry.</li>\n<li>The <b>axe trap</b> is suspected to be among the most deadly traps, sided closely with the <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe_trap\" title=\"Scythe trap\">scythe trap</a></li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 4),
(21780, 5468, 'Description', 'Description', 'A lot of small knife blades are fitted on a wooden frame that springs to life as someone steps on its trigger plate.', '<p><i>A lot of small knife blades are fitted on a wooden frame that springs to life as someone steps on its trigger plate.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21781, 5468, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'This trap type can be set up on grass or dirt tiles . Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>This <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">trap</a> type can be set up on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tiles</a>.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 1),
(21782, 5469, 'Description', 'Description', '\"A devious trap made from sharp sticks that will be hard to detect in the grass\" Trigger message: \"A stick trap triggers and hits you with full force!\" The stick trap is a trap used to slow players by damaging the legs.', '<p>\"A devious trap made from sharp sticks that will be hard to detect in the grass\"\n</p>\n<p>Trigger message: <i>\"A stick trap triggers and hits you with full force!\"</i>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>stick trap</b> is a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">trap</a> used to slow players by damaging the legs.\n</p>', 0),
(21783, 5469, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'Creation success is influenced by the active large nails . Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the plank ; failure in continuing will damage the item being added. These are moderately easy to start and continue; about 20 carpentry is recommended. The success rate is highly dependent on the quality of the material.', '<ul><li>Creation success is influenced by the active <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a>.</li>\n<li>Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the <a href=\"/index.php/Plank\" title=\"Plank\">plank</a>; failure in continuing will damage the item being added.</li>\n<li>These are moderately easy to start and continue; about 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> is recommended.</li>\n<li>The success rate is highly dependent on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the material.</li></ul>', 1),
(21784, 5469, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'Improvement uses the carpentry skill and items: carving knife , pelt , file , and log . Higher quality traps deal more damage .', '<ul><li>Improvement uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">carpentry</a> skill and items: <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">pelt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/File\" title=\"File\">file</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a>.</li>\n<li>Higher quality traps deal more <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(21785, 5469, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Stick are placed on grass and dirt tiles, the traps skill affects the placement chance. Failed trap setting message: \"Sadly, you fail to set the trap correctly. The trap triggers and is destroyed. \"', '<ul><li>Stick are placed on <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Grass\" title=\"Grass\">grass</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Dirt\" title=\"Dirt\">dirt</a> tiles, the <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">traps</a> skill affects the placement chance.</li>\n<li>Failed trap setting message: <i>\"Sadly, you fail to set the trap correctly. The trap triggers and is destroyed.</i>\"</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 3),
(21786, 5469, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The trap\'s volume is very large (50kg); a single trap is too big to fit in a small cart. Improving these is an adequate way to train carpentry. These are arguably the easiest traps to create, at least in the availability of parts. An unarmored player can take two leg wounds of up to 20 damage each from a 50QL stick trap. Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>The trap\'s volume is very large (50kg); a single trap is too big to fit in a small cart.</li>\n<li>Improving these is an adequate way to train carpentry.</li>\n<li>These are arguably the easiest traps to create, at least in the availability of parts.</li>\n<li>An unarmored player can take two leg wounds of up to 20 damage each from a 50QL stick trap.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 4),
(21787, 5470, 'Description', 'Description', 'This trap contains fragile pottery flasks full of corrosive liquid. The corrosive trap is a trap used to deal damage, presumably, to the head.', '<p><i>This trap contains fragile pottery flasks full of corrosive liquid.</i>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>corrosive trap</b> is a trap used to deal damage, presumably, to the head.\n</p>', 0),
(21788, 5470, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'Creation success is influenced by the active large nails . Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the plank; failure in continuing will damage the item being added. These are fairly easy traps to create, about 20 pottery is recommended The success rate is highly dependent on the quality of the material being used.', '<ul><li>Creation success is influenced by the active <a href=\"/index.php/Large_nails\" title=\"Large nails\">large nails</a>.</li>\n<li>Failure in creating will damage both the large nails and the plank; failure in continuing will damage the item being added.</li>\n<li>These are fairly easy traps to create, about 20 <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery\" title=\"Pottery\">pottery</a> is recommended</li>\n<li>The success rate is highly dependent on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the material being used.</li></ul>', 1),
(21789, 5470, 'Improving', 'Improving', 'Improvement uses the pottery skill and items: clay shaper , water , clay , hand , and spatula Higher quality traps deal more damage', '<ul><li>Improvement uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery\" title=\"Pottery\">pottery</a> skill and items: <a href=\"/index.php/Clay_shaper\" title=\"Clay shaper\">clay shaper</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Clay\" title=\"Clay\">clay</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Hand\" title=\"Hand\">hand</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Spatula\" title=\"Spatula\">spatula</a></li>\n<li>Higher quality traps deal more <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a></li></ul>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(21790, 5470, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Corrosive traps are placed on tree and bush tiles, the traps skill affects the placement chance.', '<p>Corrosive traps are placed on <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">tree</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">bush</a> tiles, the <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">traps</a> skill affects the placement chance.\n</p>', 3),
(21791, 5470, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Unlike most traps, the corrosive trap will fit in a small cart. Improving these is an adequate way to train pottery. Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>Unlike most traps, the <b>corrosive trap</b> will fit in a small cart.</li>\n<li>Improving these is an adequate way to train pottery.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 4),
(21792, 5477, 'Description', 'Description', 'A large axe head fit for a hatchet. A hatchet head is used for making a hatchet .', '<p><i>A large axe head fit for a hatchet.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>hatchet head</b> is used for making a <a href=\"/index.php/Hatchet\" title=\"Hatchet\">hatchet</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(21793, 5478, 'Description', 'Description', '\"You will now detect hidden dangers.\" Lasts roughly 2.5 minutes per power, when it wears off you will get this event. \"You are no longer affected by Sixth sense.\" It is known to alert the affected to the presence of traps in the immediate vicinity (1-2 tiles). It does so by an orange \'TRAP!\' message displayed in event. No further information on the trap is divulged. Can be cast on all creatures, but is known only to have an effect on humans. Sixth sense yields little channeling skillgain on successful casts at nearly any skill level, and is a poor choice for skilling priests accordingly.', '<p><i>\"You will now detect hidden dangers.\"</i>\n</p>\n<p>Lasts roughly 2.5 minutes per power, when it wears off you will get this event.\n</p>\n<p><i>\"You are no longer affected by Sixth sense.\"</i>\n</p>\n<p>It is known to alert the affected to the presence of traps in the immediate vicinity (1-2 tiles). It does so by an orange \'TRAP!\' message displayed in event. No further information on the trap is divulged. Can be cast on all creatures, but is known only to have an effect on humans.\n</p>\n<p>Sixth sense yields little <a href=\"/index.php/Channeling\" title=\"Channeling\">channeling</a> skillgain on successful casts at nearly any skill level, and is a poor choice for skilling priests accordingly.\n</p>', 0),
(21794, 5478, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate a statuette of your god Right-click a person Select Spells > Sixth Sense', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> a <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> of your god</li>\n<li>Right-click a person</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Sixth Sense</i></li></ol>', 1),
(21806, 5480, 'Description', 'Description', 'A very deadly trap, this one is made from a scythe blade hidden in masonry disguised as a rock.', '<p><i>A very deadly trap, this one is made from a scythe blade hidden in masonry disguised as a rock.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21807, 5480, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to deal heavy damage when placed on rock and cave tiles.', '<ul><li>Used to deal heavy damage when placed on <a href=\"/index.php/Rock\" title=\"Rock\">rock</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">cave</a> tiles.</li></ul>', 1),
(21808, 5480, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Creation success is influenced by the active stone brick . Failure in creating will damage both the stone brick and the clay; failure in continuing will damage the item being added. These are difficult to make and continue, around 50 masonry is recommended. The success rate is highly dependent on the QL of the material. The traps skill affects the placement chance. The trap\'s volume is very large; a single trap is too big to fit in a small cart . Improving these is a very good way to train masonry. Suspected to be one of the deadliest traps, sided closely by the axe trap . The unfinished trap is much heavier than the finished trap. Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on PvP . Traps on PvE will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.', '<ul><li>Creation success is influenced by the active <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a>.</li>\n<li>Failure in creating will damage both the stone brick and the clay; failure in continuing will damage the item being added.</li>\n<li>These are difficult to make and continue, around 50 <a href=\"/index.php/Masonry\" title=\"Masonry\">masonry</a> is recommended.</li>\n<li>The success rate is highly dependent on the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/QL\" title=\"QL\">QL</a> of the material.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/index.php/Traps\" title=\"Traps\">traps</a> skill affects the placement chance.</li>\n<li>The trap\'s volume is very large; a single trap is too big to fit in a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">small cart</a>.</li>\n<li>Improving these is a very good way to train masonry.</li>\n<li>Suspected to be one of the deadliest traps, sided closely by the <a href=\"/index.php/Axe_trap\" title=\"Axe trap\">axe trap</a>.</li>\n<li>The unfinished trap is much heavier than the finished trap.</li>\n<li>Traps affect hostile mobs, enemy kingdom/village players and any animals or mobs of enemy kingdoms on <a href=\"/index.php/PvP\" title=\"PvP\">PvP</a>. Traps on <a href=\"/index.php/PvE\" title=\"PvE\">PvE</a> will harm hostile creatures but do not harm players or branded animals/mobs.</li></ul>', 2),
(21809, 5431, 'See also', 'See_also', 'User:Dashiva/Hunger , effects of hunger, thirst, and stamina Spell effects', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/User:Dashiva/Hunger\" title=\"User:Dashiva/Hunger\">User:Dashiva/Hunger</a>, effects of hunger, thirst, and stamina</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Spell_effects\" title=\"Spell effects\">Spell effects</a></li></ul>', 0),
(21810, 5483, 'Description', 'Description', 'A strong spring capable of generating a severe punch when unleashed.', '<p><i>A strong spring capable of generating a severe punch when unleashed.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21811, 5483, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct axe , man , and scythe traps .', '<ul><li>Used to construct <a href=\"/index.php/Axe_trap\" title=\"Axe trap\">axe</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Man_trap\" title=\"Man trap\">man</a>, and <a href=\"/index.php/Scythe_trap\" title=\"Scythe trap\">scythe</a> <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">traps</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(21833, 5339, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tackle used together with a rope will provide a powerful pull. This is the large beefy type.', '<p><i>A tackle used together with a rope will provide a powerful pull. This is the large beefy type.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21834, 5339, 'Used for', 'Used_for', 'Square rig Square yard rig Tall square rig Pile of large tackle', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Square_rig\" title=\"Square rig\">Square rig</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Square_yard_rig\" title=\"Square yard rig\">Square yard rig</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tall_square_rig\" title=\"Tall square rig\">Tall square rig</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:252px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_large_tackle.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"294\" data-file-width=\"326\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"225\" src=\"/images/thumb/8/8c/Pile_of_large_tackle.png/250px-Pile_of_large_tackle.png\" srcset=\"/images/8/8c/Pile_of_large_tackle.png 1.5x\" width=\"250\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Pile_of_large_tackle.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Pile of large tackle</div></div></div>', 1),
(21837, 5461, 'Description', 'Description', 'A grey stone well with a bucket.', '<p><i>A grey stone well with a bucket.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(21838, 5461, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'A well is a stone structure that holds up to 125kg of liquid, and automatically refills itself with water frequently when placed above an underground water source, found with divining .', '<p>A well is a stone structure that holds up to 125kg of liquid, and automatically refills itself with <a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">water</a> frequently when placed above an underground water source, found with <a href=\"/index.php/Water_divining\" title=\"Water divining\">divining</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(21839, 5461, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'The quality of the stone brick affects the success chance when creating. No matter the size of the first clay (as long as its 2 kg or higher), the entire clay lump will be used up. Adding clay just subtracts 2kg from a lump, however. The quality of the clay affects the initial quality of the well. If you fail creating, both the brick and the clay are damaged. The rendered well requires 1 additional clay. The well can be improved .', '<ul><li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">stone brick</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>No matter the size of the first clay (as long as its 2 kg or higher), the entire clay lump will be used up. Adding clay just subtracts 2kg from a lump, however.</li>\n<li>The quality of the clay affects the initial quality of the well.</li>\n<li>If you fail creating, both the brick and the clay are damaged.</li>\n<li>The rendered well requires 1 additional clay.</li>\n<li>The well can be <a href=\"/index.php/Improving_Guide\" title=\"Improving Guide\">improved</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(21840, 5461, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'Once built, it usually takes around 15 minutes for the well to fill. Water is typically refilled within minutes of depletion. Courier can be cast on wells to make them into a Wishing well . Wells will also function on upper stories or underground tiles, located above or below ground level. Can be loaded onto a large cart if empty but not held in inventory. Wells cannot be dyed. They can, however, be color-runed. Some items can be placed on top of the well, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this.', '<ul><li>Once built, it usually takes around 15 minutes for the well to fill.</li>\n<li>Water is typically refilled within minutes of depletion.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Courier\" title=\"Courier\">Courier</a> can be cast on wells to make them into a <a href=\"/index.php/Wishing_well\" title=\"Wishing well\">Wishing well</a>.</li>\n<li>Wells will also function on upper <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Multi_story\" title=\"Multi story\">stories</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Cave\" title=\"Cave\">underground</a> tiles, located above or below ground level.</li>\n<li>Can be loaded onto a large cart if empty but not held in inventory.</li>\n<li>Wells cannot be dyed. They can, however, be color-runed.</li>\n<li>Some items can be placed on top of the well, as decoration. Since the item is a container already, any items placed on it will be dropped on the ground when it is loaded; a message in event log will notify the player of this.</li></ul>', 3),
(21841, 5461, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Fountain Wishing well Well material types', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fountain\" title=\"Fountain\">Fountain</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wishing_well\" title=\"Wishing well\">Wishing well</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"center\"><div class=\"thumb tnone\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:1002px;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Well_types.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-file-height=\"525\" data-file-width=\"1964\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"267\" src=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Well_types.png/1000px-Well_types.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/7/77/Well_types.png/1500px-Well_types.png 1.5x, /images/7/77/Well_types.png 2x\" width=\"1000\"/></a> <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a class=\"internal\" href=\"/index.php/File:Well_types.png\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>Well material types</div></div></div></div>', 4),
(21842, 2176, 'Description', 'Description', 'Forestry is the skill used when: Cutting sprouts from trees and bushes Harvesting from bushes and trees when they are in season Pruning trees', '<p>Forestry is the skill used when:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Cutting <a href=\"/index.php/Sprout\" title=\"Sprout\">sprouts</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Bushes\" title=\"Category:Bushes\">bushes</a></li>\n<li>Harvesting from bushes and trees when they are in <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seasons\" title=\"Seasons\">season</a></li>\n<li>Pruning trees</li></ul>', 0),
(21843, 2176, 'Picking Sprouts', 'Picking_Sprouts', 'To pick an available sprout, activate a sickle , right-click the bush or tree tile, and click Pick sprout . Trees and bushes only have sprouts at certain ages. A forestry skill of 15 or more allows the player to see the age of trees and whether they\'re sprouting on the tile you are standing on. At a forestry skill of 30, this increases to one tile away and by simply hovering the mouse over the tile in question. The range at which players can recognize such plant features from afar increases every 15 skill points gained in forestry from that point on. For example, 45 forestry allows identification from up to two tiles away, 60 allows at three tiles, and so on. Planting sprouts is part of Gardening .', '<ul><li>To pick an available sprout, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>, right-click the bush or tree tile, and click <i>Pick sprout</i>. Trees and bushes only have sprouts at certain ages.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>A forestry skill of 15 or more allows the player to see the age of trees and whether they\'re sprouting on the tile you are standing on.</li>\n<li>At a forestry skill of 30, this increases to one tile away and by simply hovering the mouse over the tile in question.</li>\n<li>The range at which players can recognize such plant features from afar increases every 15 skill points gained in forestry from that point on. For example, 45 forestry allows identification from up to two tiles away, 60 allows at three tiles, and so on.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Planting sprouts is part of <a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">Gardening</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(21844, 2176, 'Harvesting', 'Harvesting', 'To harvest, activate a sickle , right-click the bush or tree tile, and click Harvest . Trees and bushes can only be harvested when mature or older, and must be in season . Examining the tree or bush will tell you if it\'s ready to be harvested, almost ready, or is in season but has been harvested already. With enough skill, hovering the mouse over it will also tell you if it can be harvested. The amount of goods harvested depends on the player\'s forestry skill level and the age of the tree or bush: 1 below 26 skill (maximum amount from mature trees) 2 at 26 skill (maximum amount from younger stages of old trees) 3 at 53 skill 4 at 80 skill', '<ul><li>To harvest, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Sickle\" title=\"Sickle\">sickle</a>, right-click the bush or tree tile, and click <i>Harvest</i>. Trees and bushes can only be harvested when mature or older, and must be <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seasons\" title=\"Seasons\">in season</a>.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Examining the tree or bush will tell you if it\'s ready to be harvested, almost ready, or is in season but has been harvested already. With enough skill, hovering the mouse over it will also tell you if it can be harvested.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The amount of goods harvested depends on the player\'s forestry skill level and the age of the tree or bush:</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>1 below 26 skill (maximum amount from mature trees)</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>2 at 26 skill (maximum amount from younger stages of old trees)</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>3 at 53 skill</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>4 at 80 skill</li></ul></dd></dl>', 2),
(21845, 2176, 'Pruning', 'Pruning', 'Very old trees with sprouts, some young and mature trees, and overaged trees can be pruned with a sickle to reduce their age. Unsuccessful pruning gives the message \"You make a lot of errors and need to take a break\" , but you can try again until you succeed.', '<ul><li>Very old trees with sprouts, some young and mature trees, and overaged trees can be pruned with a sickle to reduce their age.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Unsuccessful pruning gives the message <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> \"You make a lot of errors and need to take a break\" </span>, but you can try again until you succeed.</li></ul>', 3),
(21846, 2176, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Nature > Forestry Mind > Mind logic Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Nature\" title=\"Nature\">Nature</a> &gt; Forestry</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 4),
(21847, 2176, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Forester at 50 skill Arboriculturist at 70 skill Arbophiliac at 90 skill Lorax at 100 skill', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Forester\" title=\"Forester\">Forester</a> at 50 skill</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arboriculturist\" title=\"Arboriculturist\">Arboriculturist</a> at 70 skill</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Arbophiliac\" title=\"Arbophiliac\">Arbophiliac</a> at 90 skill</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Lorax\" title=\"Lorax\">Lorax</a> at 100 skill</li></ul>', 5),
(21848, 2176, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Gardening', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Gardening\" title=\"Gardening\">Gardening</a></li></ul>', 6),
(21927, 5501, 'Multiple targets', 'Multiple_targets', 'The target is generally the sole focus of the player \'s offensive capabilities, whereas the player will attempt to defend all incoming attacks whether the aggressor is targeted or not. Normally, if a player has no target selected, any aggression from creatures is met with automatic targeting and retaliation. However, if a player targets one creature afar and is attacked by another, this is not the case - the target will not change. This introduces the possibility that the player will accidentally just stand there doing no attacks. The player will also not be able to change his aim or shield bash in this circumstance. Be aware of what is targeted Note: You show off some moves means you have no target or the target is out of melee range.', '<p>The <i>target</i> is generally the sole focus of the <a href=\"/index.php/Player\" title=\"Player\">player</a>\'s offensive capabilities, whereas the player will attempt to defend all incoming attacks whether the aggressor is targeted or not. Normally, if a player has no target selected, any aggression from creatures is met with automatic targeting and retaliation. <b>However, if a player targets one creature afar and is attacked by another, this is not the case - the target will not change. This introduces the possibility that the player will accidentally just stand there doing no attacks.</b> The player will also not be able to change his aim or shield bash in this circumstance.\n</p>\n<p><b> Be aware of what is targeted </b>\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Note:</b> <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You show off some moves </span> means you have no target or the target is out of melee range.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(21928, 5501, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Fighting', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a></li></ul>', 1),
(21937, 1995, 'Government', 'Government', 'Despite Wurm\'s capitalist tendencies, the concept of Bromunism prevails in New Broleans.  Nothing is ever done without communal approval, and most brojects are undertaken for the good of society.  Citizens are allowed private property, but generally share time or material if someone else has greater need.', '<p>Despite Wurm\'s capitalist tendencies, the concept of Bromunism prevails in New Broleans.  Nothing is ever done without communal approval, and most brojects are undertaken for the good of society.  Citizens are allowed private property, but generally share time or material if someone else has greater need.\n</p>', 0),
(21938, 1995, 'Brojects', 'Brojects', 'Completed HUGE BLACK COG Bay path Settlement of Dat Hill Pending Completion Brolympus Grimdark Cave The Brolossus - Statue of Libroty Cog 2: Large Hadron Coglider', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completed\">Completed</span></h4>\n<dl><dd>HUGE BLACK <a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">COG</a></dd>\n<dd>Bay path</dd>\n<dd>Settlement of Dat Hill</dd></dl>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Pending_Completion\">Pending Completion</span></h4>\n<dl><dd>Brolympus</dd>\n<dd>Grimdark <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mine\" title=\"Mine\">Cave</a></dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Colossus\" title=\"Colossus\">The Brolossus</a> - Statue of Libroty</dd>\n<dd><a href=\"/index.php/Cog\" title=\"Cog\">Cog</a> 2: Large Hadron Coglider</dd></dl>', 1),
