(24268, 6106, 'A second experiment', 'A_second_experiment', 'About 3 years after this first experiment, a second experiment was set up on Deliverance. 6 different fences of 20ql were built: Woven Fence, Crude Wooden Fence, Wooden Fence, Low Stone Wall, Tall Stone Wall and Iron Fence. The damage was noted each day for 6 months, and here are the results, collected between February and July 2013 by [Yaga ]: The previous results could be confirmed: within statistical limits all fence types show the same rate of decay. (The minor spread at higher damages was mainly due to slight ql differences.)', '<p>About 3 years after this first experiment, a second experiment was set up on Deliverance. 6 different fences of 20ql were built: Woven Fence, Crude Wooden Fence, Wooden Fence, Low Stone Wall, Tall Stone Wall and Iron Fence. The damage was noted each day for 6 months, and here are the results, collected between February and July 2013 by <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.wurmpedia.com/index.php/Player:Yaga\" rel=\"nofollow\">[Yaga</a>]:\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://img94.imageshack.us/img94/926/zo6r.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Click here for results\"><img alt=\"Click here for results\" data-file-height=\"545\" data-file-width=\"1024\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"545\" src=\"/images/2/2a/FenceDecayFinal.jpg\" width=\"1024\"/></a>\n</p>\n<p>The previous results could be confirmed: within statistical limits all fence types show the same rate of decay. (The minor spread at higher damages was mainly due to slight ql differences.)\n</p>', 1),
(24272, 916, 'Introduction', 'Introduction', 'House of Mol Rehan is the new capital city of the kingdom Mol Rehan , it is ruled by Chancellor Horton . This size 100 deed is found East of Gold Coast . House of Mol Rehan provides exceptional protection for all players who seek a safe haven, housing the strongest fighters and champions in the kingdom. This town is new and is seeking players who are interested in being involved in the construction of Mol-Rehan\'s mighty new capital city. See this topic [1] for more info, and if you\'d like to join post here!', '<p>House of Mol Rehan is the new capital city of the kingdom <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Mol_Rehan\" title=\"Mol Rehan\">Mol Rehan</a>, it is ruled by Chancellor <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Horton\" title=\"User:Horton\">Horton</a>. This size 100 deed is found East of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gold_Coast\" title=\"Gold Coast\">Gold Coast</a>. House of Mol Rehan provides exceptional protection for all players who seek a safe haven, housing the strongest fighters and champions in the kingdom. This town is new and is seeking players who are interested in being involved in the construction of Mol-Rehan\'s mighty new capital city.\n</p>\n<p>See this topic <a class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://wurmonline.com/forum/index.php?topic=33469.0\" rel=\"nofollow\">[1]</a> for more info, and if you\'d like to join post here!\n</p>', 0),
(24273, 916, 'Members', 'Members', 'Mayor Horton Citizens Baddbob Bigears Brobert Caliphae Candee Coolecoola Donte Dskaggsgv Gadget Garrettwaden Gisewindblae Horst Howl Infinitai Jamius Jberg Jonneh Jellyman Keltonf Killgod Mimiga Mobius Nicodemus Ourlord Ourqueen Pow Scoobyx Sericares Siriuslighting Stabius Tunakee Vanakala Violet Xiao Zarmazarmax Zotte Founders - Those who helped make planting the deed possible. Banedon Wintersolstice Horton Maximustehgreat Violetann Nadroj Dadd Tommty/Mimiga Clover Jberg Rudie Gaeron Alyeska Arwen Yurik', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mayor\">Mayor</span></h4>\n<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/User:Horton\" title=\"User:Horton\">Horton</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Citizens\">Citizens</span></h4>\n<ul><li>Baddbob</li>\n<li>Bigears</li>\n<li>Brobert</li>\n<li>Caliphae</li>\n<li>Candee</li>\n<li>Coolecoola</li>\n<li>Donte</li>\n<li>Dskaggsgv</li>\n<li>Gadget</li>\n<li>Garrettwaden</li>\n<li>Gisewindblae</li>\n<li>Horst</li>\n<li>Howl</li>\n<li>Infinitai</li>\n<li>Jamius</li>\n<li>Jberg</li>\n<li>Jonneh</li>\n<li>Jellyman</li>\n<li>Keltonf</li>\n<li>Killgod</li>\n<li>Mimiga</li>\n<li>Mobius</li>\n<li>Nicodemus</li>\n<li>Ourlord</li>\n<li>Ourqueen</li>\n<li>Pow</li>\n<li>Scoobyx</li>\n<li>Sericares</li>\n<li>Siriuslighting</li>\n<li>Stabius</li>\n<li>Tunakee</li>\n<li>Vanakala</li>\n<li>Violet</li>\n<li>Xiao</li>\n<li>Zarmazarmax</li>\n<li>Zotte</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Founders_-_Those_who_helped_make_planting_the_deed_possible.\">Founders - Those who helped make planting the deed possible.</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Banedon</li>\n<li>Wintersolstice</li>\n<li>Horton</li>\n<li>Maximustehgreat</li>\n<li>Violetann</li>\n<li>Nadroj</li>\n<li>Dadd</li>\n<li>Tommty/Mimiga</li>\n<li>Clover</li>\n<li>Jberg</li>\n<li>Rudie</li>\n<li>Gaeron</li>\n<li>Alyeska</li>\n<li>Arwen</li>\n<li>Yurik</li></ul>', 1),
(24274, 916, 'Screenshots', 'Screenshots', 'Will be added.', '<p>Will be added.\n</p>', 2),
(24275, 6109, 'Description', 'Description', 'Someone is planning a building project here.', '<p><i>Someone is planning a building project here.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24276, 6109, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Unlike deed markers, these do not decay within an hour. It is just dropped in place, not planted like a sign. It cannot be improved. Construction markers cannot be repaired or improved. Off-deed, they can decay within 3 to 4 days.', '<ul><li>Unlike deed markers, these do not decay within an hour.</li>\n<li>It is just dropped in place, not planted like a sign. It cannot be improved.</li>\n<li>Construction markers cannot be repaired or improved. Off-deed, they can decay within 3 to 4 days.</li></ul>', 1),
(24277, 1421, 'Description', 'Description', 'Divining for water allows the detection of water sources beneath the surface using a pendulum .', '<p>Divining for water allows the detection of water sources beneath the surface using a <a href=\"/index.php/Pendulum\" title=\"Pendulum\">pendulum</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(24278, 1421, 'Method', 'Method', 'Stand on a tile and right-click the pendulum in your inventory, then select use.', '<p>Stand on a tile and right-click the pendulum in your inventory, then select use.\n</p>', 1),
(24279, 1421, 'Outcomes', 'Outcomes', 'The pendulum seems dead. There is no water nearby (or a false negative) You think you detect some faint tugs in the pendulum. There is water nearby (5 to ~10) The pendulum is starting to move, indicating a flow of energy somewhere in this area. There is water closer (3 to 4) The pendulum is swinging in a circle, the area must have a buried water source within a few paces. There is water very close (2) The pendulum swings rapidly back and forth! You are close to a water source! You are within approximately one tile of water (1) The pendulum now swings frantically! There is something here! You are standing on a water source (0)', '<dl><dt>The pendulum seems dead. </dt>\n<dd>There is no water nearby (or a false negative)</dd>\n<dt>You think you detect some faint tugs in the pendulum. </dt>\n<dd>There is water nearby (5 to ~10)</dd>\n<dt>The pendulum is starting to move, indicating a flow of energy somewhere in this area. </dt>\n<dd>There is water closer (3 to 4)</dd>\n<dt>The pendulum is swinging in a circle, the area must have a buried water source within a few paces. </dt>\n<dd>There is water very close (2)</dd>\n<dt>The pendulum swings rapidly back and forth! You are close to a water source! </dt>\n<dd>You are within approximately one tile of water (1)</dd>\n<dt>The pendulum now swings frantically! There is something here! </dt>\n<dd>You are standing on a water source (0)</dd></dl>', 2),
(24280, 1421, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'water sources will automatically fill up wells , fountains , ornate fountains and wall fountains placed on them, but not immediately. It can take up to ten minutes to be filled up. divining doesn\'t require or use any skills. divining can produce false negatives but not false positives (\"seem dead\" results can be false but if you find water in another try, it\'s really there). The water source will function even if the well or fountain is in a mine or upper floors of a building, as long as it is on the water source tile. A higher quality pendulum will be less likely to give false negatives, take less damage through use and will reduce the action timer slightly. A pendulum enchanted with one of the Lurker spells will not work for water source tile divination as their function is changed to locate other things instead by the enchantment.', '<ul><li>water sources will automatically fill up <a href=\"/index.php/Well\" title=\"Well\">wells</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Fountain_(container)\" title=\"Fountain (container)\">fountains</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Ornate_fountain\" title=\"Ornate fountain\">ornate fountains</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wall_fountain\" title=\"Wall fountain\">wall fountains</a> placed on them, but not immediately. It can take up to ten minutes to be filled up.</li>\n<li>divining doesn\'t require or use any skills.</li>\n<li>divining can produce false negatives but not false positives (\"seem dead\" results can be false but if you find water in another try, it\'s really there).</li>\n<li>The water source will function even if the well or fountain is in a mine or upper floors of a building, as long as it is on the water source tile.</li>\n<li>A higher quality pendulum will be less likely to give false negatives, take less damage through use and will reduce the action timer slightly.</li>\n<li>A pendulum enchanted with one of the Lurker spells will not work for water source tile divination as their function is changed to locate other things instead by the enchantment.</li></ul>', 3),
(24281, 6114, 'Current Status', 'Current_Status', 'Currently living on the Chaos server and being Emoo\'s loyal lover and companion through life.', '<p>Currently living on the <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a> server and being Emoo\'s loyal lover and companion through life.\n</p>', 0),
(24282, 6114, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Master bowmaker 26th January 2014 @ [02:36:43] You have just received the title \'Master bowmaker\'! Repairman 6th January 2014 @ [01:39:19] You have just received the title \'Repairman\'! Master Shieldsmith 23rd December 2013 @ [02:09:03] You have just received the title \'Master Shieldsmith\'! Able Shieldsmith 9th May 2013 @ [17:29:58] You have just received the title \'Able Shieldsmith\'! Shieldsmith 23rd April 2013 @ [11:14:23] You have just received the title \'Shieldsmith\'! Mastermine 16th April 2013 @ [18:01:50] You have just received the title \'Mastermine\'! Tim the Toolman 14th April 2013 @ [01:21:05] You have just received the title \'Tim the Toolman\'! King of the Hunt Was not online when the title was given. Prime Minester 3rd March 2013 @ [00:49:52] You have just received the title \'Prime Minester\'! Michelangelo 19th February 2013 @ [03:04:56] You have just received the title \'Michelangelo\'! Master Mason 19th February 2013 @ [01:02:02] You have just received the title \'Master Mason\'! Master of the Hunt Was not online when the title was given. Shieldsman 7th February 2013 @ [15:49:20] You have just received the title \'Shieldsman\'! Leader of the Hunt Was not online when the title was given. Mercenary 6th January 2013 @ [08:52:53] You have just received the title \'Mercenary\'! Bloodhound of the Hunt Was not online when the title was given. Lumberjack 21th December 2012 @ [01:34:20] You have just received the title \'Lumberjack\'! Soldier 20th December 2012 @ [00:10:01] You have just received the title \'Soldier\'! Participant of the Hunt Was not online when the title was given. Artist 18th October 2012 @ [20:05:02] You have just received the title \'Artist\'! Able Bowmaker 22nd September 2012 @ [20:15:12] You have just received the title \'Able Bowmaker\'! Renowned Carpenter 17th September 2012 @ [21:01:42] You have just received the title \'Renowned Carpenter\'! Bowmaker 1st September 2012 @ [15:03:21] You hav