yer:Mazterzdemon\">Mazterzdemon</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Mouchard\" title=\"Player:Mouchard\">Mouchard</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Movu</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Penta\" title=\"Player:Penta\">Penta</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Poolsclosed\" title=\"Player:Poolsclosed\">Poolsclosed</a> - banned<br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Remelia\" title=\"Player:Remelia\">Remelia</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Roflkittens\" title=\"Player:Roflkittens\">Roflkittens</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Rulerofwax\" title=\"Player:Rulerofwax\">Rulerofwax</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Silverhammers\" title=\"Player:Silverhammers\">Silverhammers</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Sparkysgal</a><br/>\n<a href=\"/index.php/Undefined_player\" title=\"Undefined player\">Starhero</a><br/>\n<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Player:Wauld\" title=\"Player:Wauld\">Wauld</a><br/>\n<br/>\n</p>', 1),
(24347, 6133, '~Drains~', '.7EDrains.7E', 'Jan 28th 2011 [06:27:42] You start to search for gold in the coffers of Hots Zoo. [06:28:12] You find 37 copper and 50 iron in the coffers of Hots Zoo.', '<p>Jan 28th 2011<br/>\n[06:27:42] You start to search for gold in the coffers of Hots Zoo.<br/>\n[06:28:12] You find 37 copper and 50 iron in the coffers of Hots Zoo.\n</p>', 2),
(24348, 1129, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Chests', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Chests\" title=\"Chests\">Chests</a></li></ul>', 0),
(24349, 4970, 'Description', 'Description', 'Wurm sports different kingdoms and different religions . A player may, within limits, change between each kingdom and religion. Choosing a new kingdom/religion may be done in different ways.', '<p>Wurm sports different <a href=\"/index.php/Kingdom\" title=\"Kingdom\">kingdoms</a> and different <a href=\"/index.php/Religion\" title=\"Religion\">religions</a>. A player may, within limits, change between each kingdom and religion. Choosing a new kingdom/religion may be done in different ways.\n</p>', 0),
(24350, 4970, 'Changing Kingdom', 'Changing_Kingdom', 'You can change Kingdom either by a player converting you, or by converting to Libila, which automatically changes you to the Horde of the Summoned Kingdom. You must toggle \'/invitations\' command for this option to be available to whoever is converting you. Use \'/converts\' command to see when you can change kingdom. You can only change kingdom once every 14 days unless you are HoTS.  HoTS must wait for 28 days before a change.', '<p>You can change Kingdom either by a player converting you, or by converting to Libila, which automatically changes you to the <a href=\"/index.php/Horde_of_the_Summoned\" title=\"Horde of the Summoned\">Horde of the Summoned</a> Kingdom. You must toggle \'/invitations\' <a href=\"/index.php/Chat_commands\" title=\"Chat commands\">command</a> for this option to be available to whoever is converting you.\n</p>\n<p>Use \'/converts\' command to see when you can change kingdom. You can only change kingdom once every 14 days unless you are HoTS.  HoTS must wait for 28 days before a change.\n</p>', 1),
(24351, 4970, 'Changing Religion', 'Changing_Religion', 'There are three ways of converting to a faith. Any follower of a deity can convert other players, provided they have the statuette of their god. On freedom isles (PVE servers), players can join a religion by talking to the religious advisor NPC at starter towns. On Chaos , Elevation or Defiance , you may convert to a religion by approaching one of the great altars and reading an inscription. Either way, you must satisfy the requirements of the faith. Conversion by Follower The follower or priest must activate the statuette of their God and right click on you, selecting convert under the religion tab. You must have toggled /invitations for this option to be available. You may only be converted once every 7 days, and must have a Body skill of 1.5 or above to get converted by another player. When being converted by a Priest your starting faith will be equal to 1/5th of his preaching. Conversion by Npc (PVE Servers Only) non followers can join a religion by right clicking the religious advisor npc at a starter town and choosing the \"Become a follower\" option. followers with 30 faith can do the same to become priest. Conversion by Altar (Pvp Only) On Chaos , Elevation or Defiance , you may convert to a religion by approaching one of the great altars and reading an inscription. To convert to a White Light God ( Vynora , Fo or Magranon ) you must go to the Altar of Three and right click on the altar, select Inscriptions, then select Read inscription 1, 2 or 3 respectively. For the Black Light God ( Libila ) you must go to the Bone Altar, right click on the altar and its inscription. NOTE: It was previously stated you need 1 alignment to convert - This has been tested and proven false. Vynora does not require +1 alignment. Fo does require a +1 alignment, otherwise in the event window it states Fo would never accept the player as a follower.', '<p>There are three ways of converting to a faith. \n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li>Any follower of a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deity\" title=\"Deity\">deity</a> can convert other players, provided they have the <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a> of their god.</li>\n<li>On freedom isles (PVE servers), players can join a religion by talking to the religious advisor NPC at starter towns.</li>\n<li>On <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, you may convert to a religion by approaching one of the great altars and reading an inscription.</li></ul></dd></dl>\n<p>Either way, you must satisfy the requirements of the faith.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conversion_by_Follower\">Conversion by Follower</span></h4>\n<p>The follower or priest must activate the statuette of their God and right click on you, selecting convert under the religion tab. You must have toggled /invitations for this option to be available. You may only be converted once every 7 days, and must have a <a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> skill of 1.5 or above to get converted by another player. \n</p>\n<ul><li>When being converted by a Priest your starting faith will be equal to 1/5th of his preaching.</li></ul>\n<h4><span id=\"Conversion_by_Npc_(PVE_Servers_Only)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conversion_by_Npc_.28PVE_Servers_Only.29\">Conversion by Npc (PVE Servers Only)</span></h4>\n<ul><li>non followers can join a religion by right clicking the religious advisor npc at a starter town and choosing the \"Become a follower\" option.</li>\n<li>followers with 30 faith can do the same to become priest.</li></ul>\n<h4><span id=\"Conversion_by_Altar_(Pvp_Only)\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conversion_by_Altar_.28Pvp_Only.29\">Conversion by Altar (Pvp Only)</span></h4>\n<p>On <a href=\"/index.php/Chaos\" title=\"Chaos\">Chaos</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a>, you may convert to a religion by approaching one of the great altars and reading an inscription. To convert to a White Light God (<a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a>) you must go to the Altar of Three and right click on the altar, select Inscriptions, then select Read inscription 1, 2 or 3 respectively. For the Black Light God (<a href=\"/index.php/Libila\" title=\"Libila\">Libila</a>) you must go to the Bone Altar, right click on the altar and its inscription.\n</p>\n<p>NOTE: It was previously stated you need 1 alignment to convert - This has been tested and proven false.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Vynora does not require +1 alignment. Fo does require a +1 alignment, otherwise in the event window it states Fo would never accept the player as a follower.</li></ul>', 2),
(24352, 4970, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'There is a 7 day cool down between being converted between religions.', '<ul><li>There is a 7 day cool down between being converted between religions.</li></ul>', 3),
(24357, 6137, 'Description', 'Description', 'A glittering diamond. A Diamond is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A glittering diamond.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nA Diamond is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24358, 6137, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. A diamond is used in the creation of the sacrificial knife .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>A diamond is used in the creation of the <a href=\"/index.php/Sacrificial_knife\" title=\"Sacrificial knife\">sacrificial knife</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24359, 6138, 'Description', 'Description', 'A beautiful, forest green emerald. A Emerald is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A beautiful, forest green emerald.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nA Emerald is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24360, 6138, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>', 1),
(24361, 6139, 'Description', 'Description', 'A dark green, blue and black opal. A Opal is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A dark green, blue and black opal.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nA Opal is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24362, 6139, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>', 1),
(24363, 6140, 'Description', 'Description', 'A passionately red ruby. A Ruby is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A passionately red ruby.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nA Ruby is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24364, 6140, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Rubies are used in creating the sacrificial knife .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Rubies are used in creating the <a href=\"/index.php/Sacrificial_knife\" title=\"Sacrificial knife\">sacrificial knife</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24365, 6141, 'Description', 'Description', 'A shiny sky blue sapphire. A Sapphire is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A shiny sky blue sapphire.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nA Sapphire is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(24366, 6141, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Sapphires are used in the creation of the sacrificial knife .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Sapphires are used in the creation of the <a href=\"/index.php/Sacrificial_knife\" title=\"Sacrificial knife\">sacrificial knife</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24367, 4518, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long twisted horn from an animal. A butchered item obtained from butchering unicorns.', '<p><i>A long twisted horn from an animal.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Butchering_items\" title=\"Category:Butchering items\">butchered item</a> obtained from <a href=\"/index.php/Butchering\" title=\"Butchering\">butchering</a> unicorns.\n</p>', 0),
(24368, 4518, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in some cooking recipes. Used to create a healing cover with a potency of 5.', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a> with a potency of 5.</li></ul>', 1),
(24369, 4518, 'Notes', 'Notes', '0.30 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover. Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.', '<ul><li>0.30 kg is used in the creation of a healing cover.</li>\n<li>Butchered products decay extremely fast outside of bulk storage.</li></ul>', 2),
(24370, 6143, 'Description', 'Description', 'A deep blue shining sapphire. This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star). A Star sapphire is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p><i>A deep blue shining sapphire.</i>\n</p>\n<p>This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star).\n</p>\n<p>A Star sapphire is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24371, 6143, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Can also be used to create a Sapphire staff .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Can also be used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Sapphire_staff\" title=\"Sapphire staff\">Sapphire staff</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(24372, 6144, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a rare gem which is worth twice as much to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star). A Star ruby is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p>This is a rare gem which is worth twice as much to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star).\n</p>\n<p>A Star ruby is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24373, 6144, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Can also be used to create a Ruby staff .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Can also be used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Ruby_staff\" title=\"Ruby staff\">Ruby staff</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(24374, 6145, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star). A Star emerald is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p>This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star).\n</p>\n<p>A Star emerald is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24375, 6145, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. It can also be used to create an emerald staff .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul><li>It can also be used to create an <a href=\"/index.php/Emerald_staff\" title=\"Emerald staff\">emerald staff</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24376, 6146, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star). A Star diamond is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p>This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star).\n</p>\n<p>A Star diamond is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24377, 6146, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Can also be used to create a Diamond staff .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Can also be used to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Diamond_staff\" title=\"Diamond staff\">Diamond staff</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(24378, 6147, 'Description', 'Description', 'This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star). A Black opal is a shiny precious gem that can appear on the ground after a mining action.', '<p>This is a rare gem which is twice as much worth to a trader and stores twice as much favor as it\'s more common counterpart (non-black|star).  \n</p>\n<p>A Black opal is a shiny precious <a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">gem</a> that can appear on the ground after a <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mining</a> action.\n</p>', 0),
(24379, 6147, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the tile mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower. Priests can cast Vessel on gems to store favor for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the faith of the priest. Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant. Can also be used to create an Opal staff .', '<ul><li>The maximum quality of the gem depends on the quality of the <a href=\"/index.php/Tile\" title=\"Tile\">tile</a> mined or your mining skill - whichever is lower.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">Priests</a> can cast <a href=\"/index.php/Vessel\" title=\"Vessel\">Vessel</a> on gems to store <a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> for later use. The amount of favor stored depends on the quality of the gem and the <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> of the priest.</li>\n<li>Storing favor in a gem causes it to become Radiant.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<p>Can also be used to create an <a href=\"/index.php/Opal_staff\" title=\"Opal staff\">Opal staff</a>.\n</p>', 1),
(24383, 1636, 'Description', 'Description', 'A thin metal sheet. A metal sheet is a thin strong piece of metal, used to make a metal mine door.', '<p><i>A thin metal sheet.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>metal sheet</b> is a thin strong piece of metal, used to make a metal mine door.\n</p>', 0),
(24384, 1636, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Once created it cannot be improved.', '<ul><li>Once created it cannot be improved.</li></ul>', 1),
(24385, 1636, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Gold sheet: Used for gold mine door and Colossus of Vynora . Needs 6.00 kg gold lump or bigger. Silver sheet: A thick dark silver sheet. Used for silver mine door , Colossus of Fo and Colossus of Magranon . Needs 6.00 kg silver lump or bigger. Steel sheet: Used for steel mine door . Iron: No known use. Copper sheet: Still , Colossus of Libila Lead sheet: Lunchbox Tin sheet: Lunchbox', '<ul><li>Gold sheet: Used for <a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(gold)\" title=\"Mine door (gold)\">gold mine door</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Vynora\" title=\"Colossus of Vynora\">Colossus of Vynora</a>. Needs 6.00 kg gold lump or bigger.</li>\n<li>Silver sheet: <i>A thick dark silver sheet.</i> Used for <a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(silver)\" title=\"Mine door (silver)\">silver mine door</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Fo\" title=\"Colossus of Fo\">Colossus of Fo</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Magranon\" title=\"Colossus of Magranon\">Colossus of Magranon</a>. Needs 6.00 kg silver lump or bigger.</li>\n<li>Steel sheet: Used for <a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(steel)\" title=\"Mine door (steel)\">steel mine door</a>.</li>\n<li>Iron: No known use.</li>\n<li>Copper sheet: <a href=\"/index.php/Still\" title=\"Still\">Still</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Colossus_of_Libila\" title=\"Colossus of Libila\">Colossus of Libila</a></li>\n<li>Lead sheet: <a href=\"/index.php/Lunchbox\" title=\"Lunchbox\">Lunchbox</a></li>\n<li>Tin sheet: <a href=\"/index.php/Lunchbox\" title=\"Lunchbox\">Lunchbox</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24386, 5801, 'Description', 'Description', 'A fine soft sheet.', '<p><i>A fine soft sheet.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24387, 5801, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'A cotton sheet is made of square piece of cloth . Sheets are used when creating beds and wagons . The quality of the needle affects the success chance when creating. The weight of the square piece of cloth is reduced by 10% on failure. Sheets can be very hard to make with low skill. It is recommended to grind cloth tailoring on something easier before attempting to make a sheet. With no failures, a sheet will require 1.5 kg square piece of cloth = 1.5 kg string of cloth = 1.5 kg cotton . Can be dyed for decorative purposes, but this dye will not transfer to anything made with that sheet (wagon, bed, etc).', '<ul><li>A cotton sheet is made of <a href=\"/index.php/Square_piece_of_cloth\" title=\"Square piece of cloth\">square piece of cloth</a>. Sheets are used when creating <a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">beds</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Wagon\" title=\"Wagon\">wagons</a>.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Needle\" title=\"Needle\">needle</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>The weight of the square piece of cloth is reduced by 10% on failure.</li>\n<li>Sheets can be very hard to make with low skill. It is recommended to grind <a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">cloth tailoring</a> on something easier before attempting to make a sheet.</li>\n<li>With no failures, a sheet will require 1.5 kg square piece of cloth = 1.5 kg <a href=\"/index.php/String_of_cloth\" title=\"String of cloth\">string of cloth</a> = 1.5 kg <a href=\"/index.php/Cotton\" title=\"Cotton\">cotton</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be dyed for decorative purposes, but this dye will not transfer to anything made with that sheet (wagon, bed, etc).</li></ul>', 1),
(24388, 1246, 'Description', 'Description', 'Magranon spell available to priests at 50 faith . An enchantment spell castable on altars . Requires linking with multiple priests to be possible. The spell is available to cast once the deity\'s favor is full. Only prayers and sermons that could cause valid faith gains increase deity favor, which is used to charge rite spells . If you are capped at the 30 or 100 faith caps, you can still provide to the deity favor as long as you have the valid timing available. Missions also provide some deity favor, scaled on the difficulty of the mission.', '<p><a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> spell available to <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> at 50 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>. An enchantment <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> castable on <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altars</a>. Requires <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Link\" title=\"Link\">linking</a> with multiple priests to be possible.\n</p>\n<p>The spell is available to cast once the deity\'s favor is full. Only prayers and sermons that could cause valid faith gains increase deity favor, which is used to charge <a href=\"/index.php/Rite_spells\" title=\"Rite spells\">rite spells</a>. If you are capped at the 30 or 100 faith caps, you can still provide to the deity favor as long as you have the valid timing available. Missions also provide some deity favor, scaled on the difficulty of the mission. \n</p>', 0),
(24389, 1246, 'Effects', 'Effects', 'Priests and followers gain 0.2% body stamina towards 100 and 5 hours of sleep bonus through a single prayer. This benefit can be experienced up to 24 hours from the cast by praying and having at least 30 faith . Buildings, fences, and bridges inside Magranon\'s domain are repaired, up to full damage. Meteor showers will begin throughout the duration of the spell, for the server it is cast on. All meteorites have a chance of giving lumps of empyrean iron when mined. *Meteor showers will occur and boulder-like meteorites will land across the server which have random metal type and can be mined directly for lumps. \n   *All metals except alloys and moonmetals will be possible\n   *Difficulty of mining meteorites will be lower than mining an equivalent vein in a cave, leading to higher average quality of metals.\n   *Meteorites will not change terrain, and will avoid landing on highways, deeds, structures, and deep water. Magranon followers get 100 water, 100 food, and 50 nutrition boost (up to 50 nutrition), with the event message: You feel a sudden surge of energy!.', '<ul><li>Priests and followers gain 0.2% <a href=\"/index.php/Body_stamina\" title=\"Body stamina\">body stamina</a> towards 100 and 5 hours of sleep bonus through a single prayer. This benefit can be experienced up to 24 hours from the cast by praying and having at least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>.</li>\n<li>Buildings, fences, and bridges inside Magranon\'s domain are repaired, up to full damage.</li>\n<li>Meteor showers will begin throughout the duration of the spell, for the server it is cast on.</li>\n<li>All meteorites have a chance of giving lumps of empyrean iron when mined.</li></ul>\n<pre>   *Meteor showers will occur and boulder-like meteorites will land across the server which have random metal type and can be mined directly for lumps. \n   *All metals except alloys and moonmetals will be possible\n   *Difficulty of mining meteorites will be lower than mining an equivalent vein in a cave, leading to higher average quality of metals.\n   *Meteorites will not change terrain, and will avoid landing on highways, deeds, structures, and deep water.\n</pre>\n<ul><li>Magranon followers get 100 water, 100 food, and 50 nutrition boost (up to 50 nutrition), with the event message: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You feel a sudden surge of energy!. </span></li></ul>', 1),
(24390, 1246, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The spell will disappear from list after a successful cast. The cooldown for this spell is similar to that of other global spells. To make sure that the spell has cooled down, start the Sermon and wait for the 30th second of the timer. Message indicate if the ritual is already ready to be performed: You sense that Magranon is brimming with power. Maybe you can channel it somehow? ; example of message for not cooled down yet: You explain how Magranon is strong but still needs you to work faithfully so that she may manifest her powers.', '<ul><li>The spell will disappear from list after a successful cast. The cooldown for this spell is similar to that of other global spells.</li>\n<li>To make sure that the spell has cooled down, start the <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">Sermon</a> and wait for the 30th second of the timer. Message indicate if the ritual is already ready to be performed: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You sense that Magranon is brimming with power. Maybe you can channel it somehow? </span>; example of message for not cooled down yet: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You explain how Magranon is strong but still needs you to work faithfully so that she may manifest her powers. </span></li></ul>', 2),
(24391, 1246, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Holy crop Rite of spring Rite of death Rite spells', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Holy_crop\" title=\"Holy crop\">Holy crop</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_spring\" title=\"Rite of spring\">Rite of spring</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_death\" title=\"Rite of death\">Rite of death</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_spells\" title=\"Rite spells\">Rite spells</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24392, 1246, 'Castings', 'Castings', 'Wurm Year 1008 Cast on 08/29/10 18:40:01 GMT (day of Sleep in week 3 of the Snake\'s starfall) Location: Magranon Sands, West beach of Samling Main Caster: Emperorchong (Metaldragon) Linkers (Participators): Arn, Draugr, Harvick, Iorail, Majesty & Gorm GMs Witnessing: Emu & Pomona Wurm Year 1013 Cast 03/20/11 14:26:38 EST Location: Akhenaten Main Caster: Arcadia (Thorgot) Linkers (Participators): Draugr, Gorm (Draugr), Raheed (Perdaetor), Ahkmag Wurm Year 1020 Cast on 01/29/12 09:47:05 EST Location: Dragonfoot (Magranon Prayer Group) Main Caster: Arcadia (Thorgot) Linkers (Participators): Padremaronno, Lumpygravy, Braum, Dichiara, Erah, Zhentil Wurm Year 1024 - Deliverance Cast on 01/07/2012 20:12 GMT. [22:12:16] Majesty casts \'Ritual of the Sun\' on an altar of Magranon. [22:12:16] You feel a sudden surge of energy! Location: Greendog Main Caster: Majesty ( Dopeymcdope , 18 attempts over 2 days) Failed Caster the day before: Gurkin (Figs)(4 attempts) Linkers for both days (Participators): Sincor ( Axeblade ), Gurkin (Figs), Sandtrix, Vilesh(Yetian), Gram, Dulcien ( Stargrace ), Rumo (Tekari) Forums: link Wurm Year 1028 - Deliverance Cast on 09/22/2012 19:15 UCT. Location: Puzzle Plaza market Main Caster: Majesty ( Dopeymcdope ) Linkers (Participators): Sincor ( Axeblade ), Marshie (Jesslynn), Praxxe, Kabalarian (Chulirac), Orago, Kameo, Rog, Rumo (Tekari), Valfreya Forums: link Wurm Year 1029 - Exodus Cast on 09/02/2013 20:10 GMT. Location: Arrowhead Main Caster: Melody Linkers (Participators): Vigilant, Redrum, Notyouravgscrub, Chort Wurm Year 1029 - Independence Cast on 09/02/2013 23:03 GMT. Location: Akhenaten Main Caster: Arcadia ( Thorgot ) Linkers (Participators): Vigilant, Notyouravgscrub, Chort, Melody Wurm Year 1030 - Celebration, Exodus, Deliverance, Independence Cast on 03/27/2013 15:47, 17:10, 19:22, 20:45 GMT. Location: Beargazi, Arrowhead, a mountainside, Ryddinjorn Main Caster: Vigilant (Skren), Melody, Notyouravgscrub (Skren), Arcadia ( Thorgot ) Linkers (Participators): Chort, Arcadia, Notyouravgscrub, Melody, Vigilant. (Skren and Noizhead added material support.) Wurm Year 1035 - Independence Cast on 10/02/13 09:17 EST. Location: Raider Nation Main Caster: Dani Linkers (Participators): Daneyko, Braum, Solingen Wurm Year 1036 - Independence Cast on 14/12/13 16:48:26 GMT+1 Location: Wolpertinger Ranch Main Caster: Bombi Linkers (Participators): Magira, Marinus and Vraccas', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1008\">Wurm Year 1008</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 08/29/10 18:40:01 GMT (day of Sleep in week 3 of the Snake\'s starfall)</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Magranon Sands, West beach of Samling</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Emperorchong (Metaldragon)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Arn, Draugr, Harvick, Iorail, Majesty &amp; Gorm</li>\n<li>GMs Witnessing: Emu &amp; Pomona</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1013\">Wurm Year 1013</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> 03/20/11 14:26:38 EST</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Akhenaten</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Arcadia (Thorgot)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Draugr, Gorm (Draugr), Raheed (Perdaetor), Ahkmag</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1020\">Wurm Year 1020</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 01/29/12 09:47:05 EST</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Dragonfoot (Magranon Prayer Group)</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Arcadia (Thorgot)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Padremaronno, Lumpygravy, Braum, Dichiara, Erah, Zhentil</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1024_-_Deliverance\">Wurm Year 1024 - Deliverance</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 01/07/2012 20:12 GMT.</li>\n<li>[22:12:16] Majesty casts \'Ritual of the Sun\' on an altar of Magranon.</li>\n<li>[22:12:16] You feel a sudden surge of energy!</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Greendog</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Majesty (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Dopeymcdope\" title=\"Player:Dopeymcdope\">Dopeymcdope</a>, 18 attempts over 2 days)</li>\n<li><b>Failed Caster the day before:</b> Gurkin (Figs)(4 attempts)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers for both days (Participators):</b> Sincor (<a href=\"/index.php/User:Axeblade\" title=\"User:Axeblade\">Axeblade</a>), Gurkin (Figs), Sandtrix, Vilesh(Yetian), Gram, Dulcien (<a href=\"/index.php/User:Stargrace\" title=\"User:Stargrace\">Stargrace</a>), Rumo (Tekari)</li>\n<li><b>Forums:</b> <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/62350-the-big-mass-ros-rots-hocr-20-is-done/#entry615491\" rel=\"nofollow\">link</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1028_-_Deliverance\">Wurm Year 1028 - Deliverance</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 09/22/2012 19:15 UCT.</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Puzzle Plaza market</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Majesty (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Dopeymcdope\" title=\"Player:Dopeymcdope\">Dopeymcdope</a>)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Sincor (<a href=\"/index.php/User:Axeblade\" title=\"User:Axeblade\">Axeblade</a>), Marshie (Jesslynn), Praxxe, Kabalarian (Chulirac), Orago, Kameo, Rog, Rumo (Tekari), Valfreya</li>\n<li><b>Forums:</b> <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/62350-the-big-mass-ros-rots-hocr-20-is-done/#entry615491\" rel=\"nofollow\">link</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1029_-_Exodus\">Wurm Year 1029 - Exodus</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 09/02/2013 20:10 GMT.</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Arrowhead</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Melody</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Vigilant, Redrum, Notyouravgscrub, Chort</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1029_-_Independence\">Wurm Year 1029 - Independence</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 09/02/2013 23:03 GMT.</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Akhenaten</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Arcadia (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Thorgot\" title=\"Player:Thorgot\">Thorgot</a>)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Vigilant, Notyouravgscrub, Chort, Melody</li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Wurm_Year_1030_-_Celebration,_Exodus,_Deliverance,_Independence\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1030_-_Celebration.2C_Exodus.2C_Deliverance.2C_Independence\">Wurm Year 1030 - Celebration, Exodus, Deliverance, Independence</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 03/27/2013 15:47, 17:10, 19:22, 20:45 GMT.</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Beargazi, Arrowhead, a mountainside, Ryddinjorn</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Vigilant (Skren), Melody, Notyouravgscrub (Skren), Arcadia (<a href=\"/index.php/Player:Thorgot\" title=\"Player:Thorgot\">Thorgot</a>)</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Chort, Arcadia, Notyouravgscrub, Melody, Vigilant. (Skren and Noizhead added material support.)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1035_-_Independence\">Wurm Year 1035 - Independence</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 10/02/13 09:17 EST.</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Raider Nation</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Dani</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Daneyko, Braum, Solingen</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wurm_Year_1036_-_Independence\">Wurm Year 1036 - Independence</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Cast</b> on 14/12/13 16:48:26 GMT+1</li>\n<li><b>Location:</b> Wolpertinger Ranch</li>\n<li><b>Main Caster:</b> Bombi</li>\n<li><b>Linkers (Participators):</b> Magira, Marinus and Vraccas</li></ul>', 4),
(24393, 3392, 'Description', 'Description', 'A spell available to Fo priests at 50 faith . An enchantment spell castable on altars . Requires linking with multiple priests due to the amount of favor required. The spell is available to cast once the deity\'s favor is full. Only prayers and sermons that could cause valid faith gains increase deity favor, which is used to charge rite spells. If you are capped at the 30 or 100 faith caps, you can still provide to the deity favor as long as you have the valid timing available. Missions also provide some deity favor, scaled on the difficulty of the mission.', '<p>A spell available to <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Priest\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> at 50 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>. An enchantment <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Spells\" title=\"Category:Spells\">spell</a> castable on <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altars</a>. Requires <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Link\" title=\"Link\">linking</a> with multiple priests due to the amount of favor required.\n</p>\n<p>The spell is available to cast once the deity\'s favor is full. Only prayers and sermons that could cause valid faith gains increase deity favor, which is used to charge rite spells. If you are capped at the 30 or 100 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a> caps, you can still provide to the deity favor as long as you have the valid timing available. Missions also provide some deity favor, scaled on the difficulty of the mission.\n</p>', 0),
(24394, 3392, 'Effects', 'Effects', 'Priests and followers gain 0.2% soul depth towards 100 and 5 hours of sleep bonus through a single prayer. This benefit can be experienced up to 24 hours from the cast by praying and having at least 30 faith . Flower spawns will increase. Grass will grow faster. Increases farm yield by 0-2, depending on the strength of the cast Instantly casts Genesis on all applicable creatures within the domain of Fo. 10% less difficulty when taming animals during the event.', '<ul><li>Priests and followers gain 0.2% <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">soul depth</a> towards 100 and 5 hours of sleep bonus through a single prayer. This benefit can be experienced up to 24 hours from the cast by praying and having at least 30 <a href=\"/index.php/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">faith</a>.</li>\n<li>Flower spawns will increase.</li>\n<li>Grass will grow faster.</li>\n<li>Increases farm yield by 0-2, depending on the strength of the cast</li>\n<li>Instantly casts <a href=\"/index.php/Genesis\" title=\"Genesis\">Genesis</a> on all applicable creatures within the domain of Fo.</li>\n<li>10% less difficulty when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taming\" title=\"Taming\">taming</a> animals during the event.</li></ul>', 1),
(24395, 3392, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The spell will disappear from list after a successful cast. The cooldown for this spell is similar to that of other global spells (See: Rite of spring , Ritual of the sun , Rite of death ). To make sure that the spell has cooled down, start the Sermon and wait for the 30th second of the timer. Message indicate if the ritual is already ready to be performed: You sense that Fo is brimming with power. Maybe you can channel it somehow? ; example of message for not cooled down yet: You explain how Fo is strong but still needs you to work faithfully so that she may manifest her powers.', '<ul><li>The spell will disappear from list after a successful cast. The cooldown for this spell is similar to that of other global spells (See: <a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_spring\" title=\"Rite of spring\">Rite of spring</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Ritual_of_the_sun\" title=\"Ritual of the sun\">Ritual of the sun</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_death\" title=\"Rite of death\">Rite of death</a>).</li>\n<li>To make sure that the spell has cooled down, start the <a href=\"/index.php/Sermon\" title=\"Sermon\">Sermon</a> and wait for the 30th second of the timer. Message indicate if the ritual is already ready to be performed: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You sense that Fo is brimming with power. Maybe you can channel it somehow? </span>; example of message for not cooled down yet: <span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You explain how Fo is strong but still needs you to work faithfully so that she may manifest her powers. </span></li></ul>', 2),
(24396, 3392, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Ritual of the sun Rite of death Rite of spring Rite spells', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Ritual_of_the_sun\" title=\"Ritual of the sun\">Ritual of the sun</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_death\" title=\"Rite of death\">Rite of death</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_of_spring\" title=\"Rite of spring\">Rite of spring</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rite_spells\" title=\"Rite spells\">Rite spells</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24397, 6154, 'Description', 'Description', 'A gift box with nice decorations. Ability to create item removed from game, see here: http://www.wurmonline.com/2014/01/08/slew-of-bugfixes/ The gift box was a player-made gift that could be addressed to other players. Unfortunately it became widely abused to avoid decay on many items, especially food, which devs found to be undesired behavior.', '<p><i>A gift box with nice decorations.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Ability to create item removed from game, see here: <a class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.wurmonline.com/2014/01/08/slew-of-bugfixes/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.wurmonline.com/2014/01/08/slew-of-bugfixes/</a></b>\n</p>\n<p>The <b>gift box</b> was a player-made gift that could be addressed to other players. Unfortunately it became widely abused to avoid decay on many items, especially food, which devs found to be undesired behavior.\n</p>', 0),
(24398, 6154, 'Creation/Wrapping Method', 'Creation.2FWrapping_Method', 'First, activate a wood scrap, right-click the item to be wrapped into a present, and select \"Wrap\". Next, \'rename\' the gift box with the name of the recipient. The gift itself will then carry the name: \"From creator to receiver\". Wrapping Event Text: You start to wrap the <item> in a nice package. You will have to destroy the package to retrieve it afterwards.\nYou create a box side.\nYou create another box side.\nYou create yet another box side.\nYou create the last box side.\nYou create a bottom.\nYou create a top.\nYou paint the package.\nYou add some decoration and put the < item > in it.', '<ul><li>First, activate a wood scrap, right-click the item to be wrapped into a present, and select \"Wrap\". Next, \'rename\' the gift box with the name of the recipient. The gift itself will then carry the name: \"From creator to receiver\".</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Wrapping Event Text:</li></ul>\n<pre>You start to wrap the &lt;item&gt; in a nice package. You will have to destroy the package to retrieve it afterwards.\nYou create a box side.\nYou create another box side.\nYou create yet another box side.\nYou create the last box side.\nYou create a bottom.\nYou create a top.\nYou paint the package.\nYou add some decoration and put the &lt;<a href=\"/index.php/Item\" title=\"Item\">item</a>&gt; in it.\n</pre>', 1),
(24399, 6154, 'Additional Notes', 'Additional_Notes', 'To open the gift box, right-click it and select \"Open\". Opening will destroy the box, while just the contents will remain. Only the named recipient or the creator can open the box in this way. Players with long names were reported to have problems opening the box. It was therefore suggested that players experiment with the process before wrapping something of considerable value. The gift box is created at a quality of 99. It decays slowly, only if left off-deed, and it cannot be repaired or improved. The gift box will always say, \"It is made from birchwood\" , despite the wood scrap type used in creation. Items unable to be gift wrapped include: wood scrap, edible items, ores, lumps, rock shards, and leather. Gift boxes will not burn if placed in a fire, forge, or oven. Instead, they will glow red, much like a metal lump, not incurring any decay/fire damage. However, players can use a gift box as fuel by selecting the \"burn\" option on the burning vessel with the gift box activated. The results of this action are not yet confirmed. Players can destroy a gift box in a trash heap, along with its contents. Gift boxes can no longer cross server borders, either via ship, or through the mail. An examine action performed on some of the gift boxes will then refresh them and allow the intended recipient to open them.', '<ul><li>To open the gift box, right-click it and select \"Open\". Opening will destroy the box, while just the contents will remain. Only the named recipient or the creator can open the box in this way.</li>\n<li>Players with long names were reported to have problems opening the box. It was therefore suggested that players experiment with the process before wrapping something of considerable value.</li>\n<li>The gift box is created at a quality of 99. It decays slowly, only if left off-deed, and it cannot be repaired or improved.</li>\n<li>The gift box will always say, <i>\"It is made from birchwood\"</i>, despite the wood scrap type used in creation.</li>\n<li>Items unable to be gift wrapped include: wood scrap, edible items, ores, lumps, rock shards, and leather.</li>\n<li>Gift boxes will not burn if placed in a fire, forge, or oven. Instead, they will glow red, much like a metal lump, not incurring any decay/fire damage. However, players can use a gift box as fuel by selecting the \"burn\" option on the burning vessel with the gift box activated. The results of this action are not yet confirmed.</li>\n<li>Players can destroy a gift box in a trash heap, along with its contents.</li>\n<li>Gift boxes can no longer cross server borders, either via ship, or through the mail.</li>\n<li>An <i>examine</i> action performed on some of the gift boxes will then refresh them and allow the intended recipient to open them.</li></ul>', 2),
(24400, 3195, 'Description', 'Description', 'A decorative lamp head on a wooden pole.', '<p><i>A decorative lamp head on a wooden pole.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24401, 3195, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Street lamps are stationary light sources. They are planted much like a sign and can be picked up by the planter only. Hanging lamps can also be placed on walls. You need 10 digging skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 effective quality . Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to decay or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally. There\'s no limit to how many street lamps you can plant. When planted on a deed , lamps will be automatically lit during night and unlit during the day. They do respond to manual control and when snuffed, will stay dark at night. This is also true after planting, so you need fuel to light them the first time, but after that will not need to refuel them.', '<ul><li>Street lamps are stationary light sources. They are planted much like a <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Signs\" title=\"Category:Signs\">sign</a> and can be picked up by the planter only.</li>\n<li>Hanging lamps can also be placed on walls.</li>\n<li>You need 10 <a href=\"/index.php/Digging\" title=\"Digging\">digging</a> skill to plant a lamp, and the lamp must have at least 10 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Effective_quality\" title=\"Effective quality\">effective quality</a>.</li>\n<li>Planted lamps that fall below 10 effective quality due to <a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">decay</a> or other damage become unplanted, and can be picked up normally.</li>\n<li>There\'s no limit to how many street lamps you can plant.</li>\n<li>When planted on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">deed</a>, lamps will be automatically lit during night and unlit during the day. They do respond to manual control and when snuffed, will stay dark at night. This is also true after planting, so you need fuel to light them the first time, but after that will not need to refuel them.</li></ul>', 1),
(24402, 3195, 'Blessed lamps', 'Blessed_lamps', 'Off deed lamps will stay lit until out of fuel, unless they are blessed by any priest. Blessed lamps planted off deed on pavement tiles or bridges will auto-light in the evening and consume no fuel as long as they are fueled and lit initially. Blessed lamps planted on or off deed on reinforced cave tiles will remain lit continually.', '<ul><li>Off deed lamps will stay lit until out of fuel, unless they are <a href=\"/index.php/Bless\" title=\"Bless\">blessed</a> by any priest.</li>\n<li>Blessed lamps planted off deed on pavement tiles or bridges will auto-light in the evening and consume no fuel as long as they are fueled and lit initially.</li>\n<li>Blessed lamps planted on or off deed on reinforced cave tiles will remain lit continually.</li></ul>', 2),
(24403, 3195, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'When creating, the quality of the log affects your success chance. When combining a street lamp head with a log, the entire log is consumed even if it is more than the required weight. Street lamps need 0.125kg of tar or olive oil as fuel to fill to max capacity. All street lamps can be dyed with 100g of dye . The dye will only affect the colour of the light the lamp emits, not the lamp itself. The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate. Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below. Despite being called \"hanging lamps, iron\" in the crafting menu , hanging lamps can be created from any metal. The finished model will differ in appearance, depending on the metal used for the hanging lamp head .', '<ul><li>When creating, the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the log affects your success chance.</li>\n<li>When combining a street lamp head with a log, the entire log is consumed even if it is more than the required weight.</li>\n<li>Street lamps need 0.125kg of <a href=\"/index.php/Tar\" title=\"Tar\">tar</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Olive_oil\" title=\"Olive oil\">olive oil</a> as fuel to fill to max capacity.</li>\n<li>All street lamps can be dyed with 100g of <a href=\"/index.php/Dye\" title=\"Dye\">dye</a>. The dye will only affect the colour of the light the lamp emits, not the lamp itself.</li>\n<li>The lamp quality determines how far the lamp will illuminate.</li>\n<li>Lamps can be bashed off deed as well as picked up if they have 70+ dmg and/or are 10 quality and below.</li>\n<li>Despite being called \"hanging lamps, iron\" in the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Crafting_menu\" title=\"Crafting menu\">crafting menu</a>, hanging lamps can be created from any metal. The finished model will differ in appearance, depending on the metal used for the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Hanging_lamp_head\" title=\"Hanging lamp head\">hanging lamp head</a>.</li></ul>', 3);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
