(24526, 6043, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Bulk storage bin Decay', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Bulk_storage_bin\" title=\"Bulk storage bin\">Bulk storage bin</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Decay\" title=\"Decay\">Decay</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24527, 5713, 'Description', 'Description', 'The art of doing something . Normally initiated by the right click interface.', '<p>The art of <i>doing something</i>. Normally initiated by the right click interface.\n</p>', 0),
(24528, 5713, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Fighting is not considered an action (apart from activities such as focusing or taunting ). The number of actions able to be queued depends on mind logic . Actions take a certain amount of time, based on stamina level and the skill level relevant to the action. You can see how much time the action has left under the Event Window.', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Fighting\" title=\"Fighting\">Fighting</a> is not considered an action (apart from activities such as <a href=\"/index.php/Focus\" title=\"Focus\">focusing</a> or <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Taunt\" title=\"Taunt\">taunting</a>).</li>\n<li>The number of actions able to be <a href=\"/index.php/Action_queue\" title=\"Action queue\">queued</a> depends on <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a>.</li>\n<li>Actions take a certain amount of time, based on stamina level and the skill level relevant to the action. You can see how much time the action has left under the Event Window.</li></ul>', 1),
(24529, 5713, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Action queue', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Action_queue\" title=\"Action queue\">Action queue</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24540, 3287, 'Description', 'Description', 'A door that looks very similar to the rock around here. Stone mine door is an item used to limit access to a mine.  It conceals the opening as to not be readily apparent to the passerby by making it look like the rest of the nearby rock.', '<p><i>A door that looks very similar to the rock around here.</i>\n</p>\n<p><b>Stone mine door</b> is an item used to limit access to a mine.  It conceals the opening as to not be readily apparent to the passerby by making it look like the rest of the nearby rock.\n</p>', 0),
(24541, 3287, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate the mine door, right-click a mine entrance tile border and select build door . The resulting door has 100 strength for every full QL of the item.', '<p>Activate the mine door, right-click a mine entrance tile border and select <i>build door</i>. The resulting door has 100 strength for every full QL of the item.\n</p>', 1),
(24542, 3287, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90. Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed perimeter does NOT protect mine doors. If you wish to place a fence around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door. On Elevation and Defiance servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed. Right-click on the door to manage the permissions. Requires 21 mining skill to attach. Otherwise the message \"You do not know how to do that effectively\" appear. Substantially more difficult to create than any other cut stone object. A 20 quality stone chisel and 20 skill in stone cutting is sufficient to create a stone mine door. Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the Manage Item permission with a crowbar . If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it. At least 21 Body strength is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears. Decays over time off deed (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0). Can be improved if not installed. Fits in a large cart , but not in a small cart .', '<ul><li><b>Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90.</b></li>\n<li><b>Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> does NOT protect mine doors.</b></li>\n<li>If you wish to place a <a href=\"/index.php/Fence\" title=\"Fence\">fence</a> around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door.</li>\n<li>On <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a> servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed.</li>\n<li>Right-click on the door to manage the permissions.</li>\n<li>Requires 21 mining skill to attach. Otherwise the message \"You do not know how to do that effectively\" appear.</li>\n<li>Substantially more difficult to create than any other cut stone object.</li>\n<li>A 20 quality <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a> and 20 skill in <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_cutting\" title=\"Stone cutting\">stone cutting</a> is sufficient to create a stone mine door.</li>\n<li>Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the <b>Manage Item</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permission</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>. If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it.</li>\n<li>At least 21 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a> is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears.</li>\n<li>Decays over time off deed (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0).</li>\n<li>Can be improved if not installed.</li>\n<li>Fits in a <a href=\"/index.php/Large_cart\" title=\"Large cart\">large cart</a>, but not in a <a href=\"/index.php/Small_cart\" title=\"Small cart\">small cart</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(24543, 3287, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Mine door (wood) Mine door (gold) Mine door (silver) Mine door (steel)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(wood)\" title=\"Mine door (wood)\">Mine door (wood)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(gold)\" title=\"Mine door (gold)\">Mine door (gold)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(silver)\" title=\"Mine door (silver)\">Mine door (silver)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(steel)\" title=\"Mine door (steel)\">Mine door (steel)</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24544, 6098, 'Description', 'Description', 'A door made from the purest silver. A silver mine door is an item used to limit access to a mine.', '<p><i>A door made from the purest silver.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>silver mine door</b> is an item used to limit access to a mine.\n</p>', 0),
(24545, 6098, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate the mine door, right click a mine tile border and select Build door .', '<ul><li>Activate the mine door, right click a mine tile border and select <i>Build door</i>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24546, 6098, 'Maintenance', 'Maintenance', 'Once installed, the silver mine door slowly loses strength if off deed. To keep it from decaying, it has to be repaired. To repair the silver mine door, activate a silver lump , right click the mine door and select Improve . The lump does not need to be glowing hot to be used. The maximum strength you can improve a silver mine door to depends on the silver lump and your blacksmithing skill. The formula is 100 * (Lump QL / 4 + Blacksmithing skill / 2). Each improvement uses 0.1 kg of the silver lump and raises the strength of the mine door by a fifth of the difference between current strength and maximum strength. The following graph shows the decay of a silver mine door over the course of over a year. The Mine door has been repaired a few times since.\nThe decay has been about 28 strength per day on average over the whole period of 400 days.', '<p>Once installed, the silver mine door slowly loses strength if off deed. To keep it from decaying, it has to be repaired. To repair the silver mine door, activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">silver lump</a>, right click the mine door and select <i>Improve</i>. The lump does not need to be glowing hot to be used.\n</p>\n<p>The maximum strength you can improve a silver mine door to depends on the silver lump and your blacksmithing skill. The formula is 100 * (Lump QL / 4 + Blacksmithing skill / 2). \n</p>\n<p>Each improvement uses 0.1 kg of the silver lump and raises the strength of the mine door by a fifth of the difference between current strength and maximum strength.\n</p>\n<p>The following graph shows the decay of a silver mine door over the course of over a year. The Mine door has been repaired a few times since.\nThe decay has been about 28 strength per day on average over the whole period of 400 days.\n</p>\n<p><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Silver_mine_door_decay.png\" title=\"Decay of a Silver mine door\"><img alt=\"Decay of a Silver mine door\" data-file-height=\"337\" data-file-width=\"951\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"337\" src=\"/images/9/98/Silver_mine_door_decay.png\" width=\"951\"/></a>\n</p>', 2);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(24547, 6098, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90. Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed perimeter does NOT protect mine doors. If you wish to place a fence around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door. On Elevation and Defiance servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed. Right-click on the door to manage the permissions. Needs a high blacksmithing skill with a high QL door lock to start. Very hard to start and continue at low skill, though there is no hard coded limit. Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the Manage Item permission with a crowbar . If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it. At least 21 Body strength is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears. Decays only off deed over time (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0).', '<ul><li><b>Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90.</b></li>\n<li><b>Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> does NOT protect mine doors.</b></li>\n<li>If you wish to place a <a href=\"/index.php/Fence\" title=\"Fence\">fence</a> around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door.</li>\n<li>On <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a> servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed.</li>\n<li>Right-click on the door to manage the permissions.</li>\n<li>Needs a high blacksmithing skill with a high QL door lock to start.</li>\n<li>Very hard to start and continue at low skill, though there is no hard coded limit.</li>\n<li>Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the <b>Manage Item</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permission</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>. If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it.</li>\n<li>At least 21 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a> is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears.</li>\n<li>Decays only off deed over time (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0).</li></ul>', 3),
(24548, 6098, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Mine door (gold) Mine door (stone) Mine door (steel) Mine door (wood)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(gold)\" title=\"Mine door (gold)\">Mine door (gold)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(stone)\" title=\"Mine door (stone)\">Mine door (stone)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(steel)\" title=\"Mine door (steel)\">Mine door (steel)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(wood)\" title=\"Mine door (wood)\">Mine door (wood)</a></li></ul>', 4),
(24549, 6118, 'Description', 'Description', 'A door made from the purest gold . An item used to limit access to a mine.', '<p><i>A door made from the purest <a href=\"/index.php/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">gold</a>.</i>\n</p>\n<p>An item used to limit access to a mine.\n</p>', 0),
(24550, 6118, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Activate the mine door, right click a mine tile border and select build door .', '<ul><li>Activate the mine door, right click a mine tile border and select <i>build door</i>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24551, 6118, 'Maintenance', 'Maintenance', 'Once installed the gold mine door slowly loses strength if off deed. To keep it from decaying it has to be repaired. To repair the gold mine door activate a gold lump , right click the mine door and select Improve . Each improvement uses 0.1kg of the gold lump and raises the strength of the mine door.', '<p>Once installed the gold mine door slowly loses strength if off deed. To keep it from decaying it has to be repaired. To repair the gold mine door activate a <a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">gold lump</a>, right click the mine door and select <i>Improve</i>. \n</p>\n<p>Each improvement uses 0.1kg of the gold lump and raises the strength of the mine door.\n</p>', 2),
(24552, 6118, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90. Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed perimeter does NOT protect mine doors. If you wish to place a fence around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door. On Elevation and Defiance servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed. Right-click on the door to manage the permissions. Needs a high blacksmithing skill with a high ql door lock to start. Very hard to start and continue, though there is no hard coded limit. (Estimated to take ~2 hours at 70 blacksmithing, with equal-quality materials) Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the Manage Item permission with a crowbar . If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it. At least 21 Body strength is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears. Decays only off deed over time (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0).', '<ul><li><b>Mine doors cannot be placed on entrances with a slope of greater than 90.</b></li>\n<li><b>Remember that off-deed mine doors can be bashed by other players, so your mine is not entirely safe just because it has a mine door attached. A deed <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> does NOT protect mine doors.</b></li>\n<li>If you wish to place a <a href=\"/index.php/Fence\" title=\"Fence\">fence</a> around a mine entrance this should be done before attaching a mine door.</li>\n<li>On <a href=\"/index.php/Elevation\" title=\"Elevation\">Elevation</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Defiance\" title=\"Defiance\">Defiance</a> servers, there must be a minimum of 3 tiles between mine doors and only 4 mine doors in an 11x11 area. There is a check in a 5 tile radius around the door being placed.</li>\n<li>Right-click on the door to manage the permissions.</li>\n<li>Needs a high blacksmithing skill with a high ql door lock to start.</li>\n<li>Very hard to start and continue, though there is no hard coded limit. (Estimated to take ~2 hours at 70 blacksmithing, with equal-quality materials)</li>\n<li>Can be removed by the owner or anyone with the <b>Manage Item</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">permission</a> with a <a href=\"/index.php/Crowbar\" title=\"Crowbar\">crowbar</a>. If on deed, only citizens of that deed can remove it.</li>\n<li>At least 21 <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a> is required to remove a mine door. Otherwise the message \"You are too weak to do that.\" appears.</li>\n<li>Decays only off deed over time (loses strength and disappears when it drops to 0).</li></ul>', 3),
(24553, 6118, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Mine door (silver) Mine door (stone) Mine door (steel) Mine door (wood)', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(silver)\" title=\"Mine door (silver)\">Mine door (silver)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(stone)\" title=\"Mine door (stone)\">Mine door (stone)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(steel)\" title=\"Mine door (steel)\">Mine door (steel)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mine_door_(wood)\" title=\"Mine door (wood)\">Mine door (wood)</a></li></ul>', 4),
(24554, 2514, 'Description', 'Description', 'Foraging is the skill used when searching Resource nodes for a wide variety of resources , including seeds and various food items.', '<p><b>Foraging</b> is the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Skill\" title=\"Skill\">skill</a> used when searching <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> for a wide variety of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Resources\" title=\"Resources\">resources</a>, including <a href=\"/index.php/Seeds\" title=\"Seeds\">seeds</a> and various food items.\n</p>', 0),
(24555, 2514, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Foraging a node will deplete it, causing it to disappear. Resource nodes spawn randomly, and can take up to a few days for more to appear. Different tile types and location, season, player condition, and other possible variables affect the percentage and type of items that can be botanized. See the Resource nodes page for more details on these modifiers. Higher skill adds a flat value increasing the number of items you find. (see Resource nodes page) You have a chance to obtain rare coin while botanizing. Foraging can be done while mounted/driving a vehicle. Foraging can be done while moving, so long as you do not move too far away (two tiles) from the tile you are currently working', '<ul><li>Foraging a node will deplete it, causing it to disappear.</li>\n<li>Resource nodes spawn randomly, and can take up to a few days for more to appear.</li>\n<li>Different tile types and location, season, player condition, and other possible variables affect the percentage and type of items that can be botanized. See the <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> page for more details on these modifiers.</li>\n<li>Higher skill adds a flat value increasing the number of items you find. (see <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> page)</li>\n<li>You have a chance to obtain rare <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Coin\" title=\"Coin\">coin</a> while botanizing.</li>\n<li>Foraging can be done while mounted/driving a vehicle.</li>\n<li>Foraging can be done while moving, so long as you do not move too far away (two tiles) from the tile you are currently working</li></ul>', 1),
(24556, 2514, 'Items', 'Items', 'Resources Branch Berries Cacao beans Green coffee beans Cotton Egg Feathers Fish Fishing hook Flint Gems Gold lumps Grub Hops seedling Ivy seedling Iron Rock Jewelry Liquor barrels and bottles Logs Marble shard Moss Mushrooms Nails Nettles Nuts Ore Pearl Stone shards Reed plants Rock salt Ropes Sandstone shards Seedlings Seeds (crop) Shafts Silver lump Slate shard Sprouts Square piece of cloth Stone shard Tea seeds Wemp fibre Wemp plants Woad Wood scrap Shipbuilding resources Wool', '<table width=\"100%\">\n<tbody><tr valign=\"top\">\n<td>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\"><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Resources\" title=\"Resources\">Resources</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Branch\" title=\"Branch\">Branch</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Berries\" title=\"Berries\">Berries</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cacao_beans\" title=\"Cacao beans\">Cacao beans</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Green_coffee_beans\" title=\"Green coffee beans\">Green coffee beans</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Cotton\" title=\"Cotton\">Cotton</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Egg\" title=\"Egg\">Egg</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Feathers\" title=\"Feathers\">Feathers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">Fish</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Fishing_hook\" title=\"Fishing hook\">Fishing hook</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Flint\" title=\"Flint\">Flint</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Gems\" title=\"Gems\">Gems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Gold_lump\" title=\"Gold lump\">Gold lumps</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Grub\" title=\"Grub\">Grub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hops_seedling\" title=\"Hops seedling\">Hops seedling</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Ivy_seedling\" title=\"Ivy seedling\">Ivy seedling</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron_Rock\" title=\"Iron Rock\">Iron Rock</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Jewelry\" title=\"Jewelry\">Jewelry</a></li>\n<li>Liquor barrels and bottles</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">Logs</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Marble_shard\" title=\"Marble shard\">Marble shard</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Moss\" title=\"Moss\">Moss</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mushroom\" title=\"Mushroom\">Mushrooms</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Nails\" title=\"Nails\">Nails</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Nettles\" title=\"Nettles\">Nettles</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Nuts\" title=\"Nuts\">Nuts</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">Ore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pearl\" title=\"Pearl\">Pearl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">Stone shards</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Reed_plants\" title=\"Reed plants\">Reed plants</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rock_salt_(shard)\" title=\"Rock salt (shard)\"> Rock salt</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Ropes\" title=\"Ropes\">Ropes</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Sandstone_shards\" title=\"Sandstone shards\">Sandstone shards</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Seedlings\" title=\"Seedlings\">Seedlings</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Seeds\" title=\"Seeds\">Seeds</a> (crop)</li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shafts\" title=\"Shafts\">Shafts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Silver_lump\" title=\"Silver lump\">Silver lump</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Slate_shard\" title=\"Slate shard\">Slate shard</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sprouts\" title=\"Sprouts\">Sprouts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Square_piece_of_cloth\" title=\"Square piece of cloth\">Square piece of cloth</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Stone_shard\" title=\"Stone shard\">Stone shard</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tea_seeds\" title=\"Tea seeds\">Tea seeds</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">Wemp fibre</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_plants\" title=\"Wemp plants\">Wemp plants</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Woad\" title=\"Woad\">Woad</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wood_scrap\" title=\"Wood scrap\">Wood scrap</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Shipbuilding_resources\" title=\"Shipbuilding resources\">Shipbuilding resources</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Wool\" title=\"Wool\">Wool</a></li></ul>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 2),
(24557, 2514, 'Messages while foraging', 'Messages_while_foraging', 'You\'ve found all that you can here. There is nothing more to be foraged on the node.', '<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> You\'ve found all that you can here. </span> There is nothing more to be foraged on the node. <br/>\n</p>', 3),
(24558, 2514, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Nature > Foraging Soul > Soul depth', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Nature\" title=\"Nature\">Nature</a> &gt; Foraging</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Soul\" title=\"Soul\">Soul</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Soul_depth\" title=\"Soul depth\">Soul depth</a></li></ul>', 4),
(24559, 2514, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Forager at 50 skill Plant Gatherer at 70 skill Master of Plants at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Forager at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Plant Gatherer at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master of Plants at 90 skill</li></ul>', 5),
(24560, 2514, 'Images', 'Images', 'A player foraging on a grass tile', '<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 192.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 192.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 190.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Forage_-_botanize.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"414\" data-file-width=\"395\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"200\" src=\"/images/thumb/9/94/Forage_-_botanize.jpg/286px-Forage_-_botanize.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/9/94/Forage_-_botanize.jpg 1.5x\" width=\"191\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 171px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>A player foraging on a grass tile\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>', 6),
(24561, 2514, 'See also', 'See_also', 'Botanizing Node resources Resource nodes', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Node_resources\" title=\"Node resources\">Node resources</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a></li></ul>', 7),
(24567, 6192, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small vaguely reddish rock containing a few cavities lined with dark, metallic crystals.', '<p><i>A small vaguely reddish rock containing a few cavities lined with dark, metallic crystals.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24568, 6192, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be found by Foraging at Mineral debris , Rubble , Bog muck and Lichen Resource nodes . Iron rocks can be smelted into iron lumps , just like iron ore , and give 0.8kg of iron for each 3kg of iron rock. Iron rocks can be combined.', '<ul><li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> at <a href=\"/index.php/Mineral_debris\" title=\"Mineral debris\">Mineral debris</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Rubble\" title=\"Rubble\">Rubble</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Bog_muck\" title=\"Bog muck\">Bog muck</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Lichen\" title=\"Lichen\">Lichen</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Iron rocks can be smelted into <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">iron lumps</a>, just like <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_ore\" title=\"Iron ore\">iron ore</a>, and give 0.8kg of iron for each 3kg of iron rock. Iron rocks can be combined.</li></ul>', 1),
(24569, 6194, 'Description', 'Description', 'A tool for digging. A crude shovel can be made from a stone crude shovel blade and a crude shaft, if you have lost your iron shovel . You can\'t repair a crude shovel. You can also use it to cut down trees but you won\'t be able to chop up felled trees with it (you will need to cut a mature tree to get a log).', '<p><i>A tool for digging.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>crude shovel</b> can be made from a stone crude shovel blade and a crude shaft, if you have lost your iron <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a>.\n</p>\n<p>You can\'t repair a crude shovel.<br/>You can also use it to <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">cut down trees</a> but you won\'t be able to chop up <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Felled_tree\" title=\"Felled tree\">felled trees</a> with it (you will need to cut a mature tree to get a log).\n</p>', 0),
(24570, 6194, 'Creating', 'Creating', 'A normal chopped wood shaft can be used besides a crude shaft.', '<ul><li>A normal chopped wood <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> can be used besides a crude shaft.</li></ul>', 1),
(24571, 6194, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot be improved. Cannot be used for burying corpses', '<ul><li>Cannot be improved.</li>\n<li>Cannot be used for burying corpses</li></ul>', 2),
(24572, 6194, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Crude tools Crude axe Crude knife Crude pickaxe', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_tools\" title=\"Crude tools\">Crude tools</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe\" title=\"Crude axe\">Crude axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">Crude knife</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\">Crude pickaxe</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24576, 6197, 'Description', 'Description', 'A one step long wooden branch that could be used to create a shaft.', '<p><i>A one step long wooden branch that could be used to create a shaft.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24577, 6197, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used in the creation of crude tools and to create shafts . Used in some cooking recipes. Can be found by Foraging Undergrowth and Rotting wood Resource nodes . Can be found by Botanizing Briar patch Resource nodes . Branches are found most easily by searching Resource nodes on tree tiles. The quality of the branch is based on your foraging skill. Branches can be discarded by right-clicking, and selecting \'Discard\'. This will dispose of them immediately.', '<ul><li>Used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Crude_Tools\" title=\"Category:Crude Tools\">crude tools</a> and to create <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shafts</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">Foraging</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Undergrowth\" title=\"Undergrowth\">Undergrowth</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Rotting_wood\" title=\"Rotting wood\">Rotting wood</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">Botanizing</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Briar_patch\" title=\"Briar patch\">Briar patch</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Branches are found most easily by searching Resource nodes on tree tiles.</li>\n<li>The quality of the branch is based on your foraging skill.</li>\n<li>Branches can be discarded by right-clicking, and selecting \'Discard\'. This will dispose of them immediately.</li></ul>', 1),
(24580, 6199, 'Description', 'Description', 'A hard, sharp piece of rock fastened to a shaft.', '<p><i>A hard, sharp piece of rock fastened to a shaft.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24581, 6199, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Either a crude knife or a carving knife can be used to carve a crude shaft from a branch . Only a carving knife can create a shaft from a log ; a crude knife will not work. Either a crude knife or a stone chisel can be used to create a crude pickaxe head from stone shards . A crude pickaxe of stone can be made from simple rummaged and foraged materials if you have lost your iron pickaxe . Cannot be improved or repaired. You can also use it to cut down trees but you won\'t be able to chop up felled trees with it. A crude axe is recommended.', '<ul><li>Either a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">crude knife</a> or a <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a> can be used to carve a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shaft\" title=\"Crude shaft\">crude shaft</a> from a <a href=\"/index.php/Branch\" title=\"Branch\">branch</a>.</li>\n<li>Only a <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">carving knife</a> can create a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a> from a <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">log</a>; a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">crude knife</a> will not work.</li>\n<li>Either a crude knife or a <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_chisel\" title=\"Stone chisel\">stone chisel</a> can be used to create a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe_head_(crude)\" title=\"Pickaxe head (crude)\">crude pickaxe head</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a>.</li>\n<li>A <b>crude pickaxe</b> of stone can be made from simple <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">rummaged and foraged</a> materials if you have lost your iron <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>.</li>\n<li>Cannot be improved or repaired.</li>\n<li>You can also use it to <a href=\"/index.php/Woodcutting\" title=\"Woodcutting\">cut down trees</a> but you won\'t be able to chop up felled trees with it. A <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe\" title=\"Crude axe\">crude axe</a> is recommended.</li></ul>', 1),
(24582, 6199, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Crude tools Crude axe Crude knife Crude shovel', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_tools\" title=\"Crude tools\">Crude tools</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe\" title=\"Crude axe\">Crude axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_knife\" title=\"Crude knife\">Crude knife</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">Crude shovel</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24583, 3525, 'Description', 'Description', 'Some wemp plants. It has very strong fibres.', '<p><i>Some wemp plants. It has very strong fibres.</i>\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(24584, 3525, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Wemp plants are crushed to produce wemp fibre . Wemp fibre is used for creating ropes and bow strings . Crushing 0.7kg of wemp plants will produce 0.5kg wemp fibre.', '<ul><li><b>Wemp plants</b> are crushed to produce <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a>. Wemp fibre is used for creating <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">ropes</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow strings</a>.\n<ul><li>Crushing 0.7kg of wemp plants will produce 0.5kg wemp fibre.</li></ul></li></ul>', 1),
(24585, 3525, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'You can also find wemp plants by foraging on Undergrowth or botanizing on Low brush .', '<ul><li>You can also find wemp plants by <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Undergrowth\" title=\"Undergrowth\">Undergrowth</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> on <a href=\"/index.php/Low_brush\" title=\"Low brush\">Low brush</a>.</li></ul>', 2),
(24586, 6191, 'Description', 'Description', 'This piece of rock can barely be called a knife but it will do the trick. A crude knife made from iron rock and rock shards, this knife has a broad blade and half a hilt.\nIt can be used to make a crude shaft , if you have lost your other tools.', '<p><i>This piece of rock can barely be called a knife but it will do the trick.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>crude knife</b> made from iron rock and rock shards, this knife has a broad blade and half a hilt.\nIt can be used to make a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shaft\" title=\"Crude shaft\">crude shaft</a>, if you have lost your other tools.\n</p>', 0),
(24587, 6191, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Cannot be improved or repaired. Can be used to butcher corpses. Uses the Carving knife skill.', '<ul><li>Cannot be improved or repaired.</li>\n<li>Can be used to butcher corpses.</li>\n<li>Uses the <a href=\"/index.php/Carving_knife\" title=\"Carving knife\">Carving knife</a> skill.</li></ul>', 1),
(24588, 6191, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Crude tools Crude axe Crude pickaxe Crude shovel', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_tools\" title=\"Crude tools\">Crude tools</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_axe\" title=\"Crude axe\">Crude axe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\">Crude pickaxe</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">Crude shovel</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24589, 6195, 'Description', 'Description', 'A one step long crooked wooden shaft that could be used to create a very simple tool or a weapon. It is made from [wood type]. A shaft made from a branch . This type of shaft can only be used in the creation of crude tools , such as crude shovels or crude pickaxes .', '<p><i>A one step long crooked wooden shaft that could be used to create a very simple tool or a weapon. It is made from [wood type].</i>\n</p>\n<p>A shaft made from a <a href=\"/index.php/Branch\" title=\"Branch\">branch</a>. This type of shaft can only be used in the creation of <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Crude_Tools\" title=\"Category:Crude Tools\">crude tools</a>, such as <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">crude shovels</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\"> crude pickaxes</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(24592, 2451, 'Description', 'Description', 'Skill used in creating weapons and tools that use weapon blades. It is the slowest skill to raise in the game besides characteristics skills.', '<p>Skill used in creating <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Weapons\" title=\"Category:Weapons\">weapons</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Tools\" title=\"Category:Tools\">tools</a> that use weapon blades. It is the slowest skill to raise in the game besides characteristics skills.\n</p>', 0),
(24593, 2451, 'Tools for creating and improving weaponsmithing items', 'Tools_for_creating_and_improving_weaponsmithing_items', 'Metal lumps , usually iron lump (Creation material) Hammer Small anvil (Creation tool) Large anvil (Creation tool) Water Whetstone Pelt', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Metal_lumps\" title=\"Metal lumps\">Metal lumps</a>, usually <a href=\"/index.php/Iron_lump\" title=\"Iron lump\">iron lump</a> (Creation material)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Hammer\" title=\"Hammer\">Hammer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Small_anvil\" title=\"Small anvil\">Small anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_anvil\" title=\"Large anvil\">Large anvil</a> (Creation tool)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Water\" title=\"Water\">Water</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Whetstone\" title=\"Whetstone\">Whetstone</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Pelt\" title=\"Pelt\">Pelt</a></li></ul>', 1),
(24594, 2451, 'Items', 'Items', 'See: Category:Weapon smithing items', '<p>See: <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Weapon_smithing_items\" title=\"Category:Weapon smithing items\">Category:Weapon smithing items</a>\n</p>', 2),
(24595, 2451, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Water won\'t benefit from Circle of cunning when improving', '<ul><li>Water won\'t benefit from <a href=\"/index.php/Circle_of_cunning\" title=\"Circle of cunning\">Circle of cunning</a> when improving</li></ul>', 3),
(24596, 2451, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Smithing > Weapon smithing Body > Body control Body > Body strength Subskills Blades smithing Weapon heads smithing', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Smithing\" title=\"Smithing\">Smithing</a> &gt; Weapon smithing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_strength\" title=\"Body strength\">Body strength</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subskills\">Subskills</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Blades_smithing\" title=\"Blades smithing\">Blades smithing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapon_heads_smithing\" title=\"Weapon heads smithing\">Weapon heads smithing</a></li></ul>', 4),
(24597, 2451, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Weaponsmith at 50 skill Arms master at 70 skill Master Weaponsmith at 90 skill Accessory to Murder at 100 skill', '<ul><li>Weaponsmith at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Arms master at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Weaponsmith at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Accessory to Murder at 100 skill</li></ul>', 5),
(24598, 2934, 'Description', 'Description', 'Chain armour smithing is the skill used to make chainmail armour for humans and horses.', '<p>Chain armour smithing is the skill used to make chainmail armour for humans and horses. \n</p>', 0),
(24599, 2934, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Wearing your chain armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding. Some items, particularly the pants and jacket, are difficult to create. They will not show up in the create menu unless you have a good anvil and/or high skill. Chain armour can be made from any metal. For speed comparisons check armour . Wearing your chain armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving chain armour smithing items, including barding.', '<ul><li>Wearing your chain armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding.</li>\n<li>Some items, particularly the pants and jacket, are difficult to create. They will not show up in the create menu unless you have a good anvil and/or high skill.</li>\n<li>Chain armour can be made from any metal.</li>\n<li>For speed comparisons check <a href=\"/index.php/Armour\" title=\"Armour\">armour</a>.</li>\n<li>Wearing your chain armour smithing title gives a bonus while improving chain armour smithing items, including barding.</li></ul>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(24600, 2934, 'Chain Armour Variations', 'Chain_Armour_Variations', 'Chain Armour Iron chain armour Steel chain armour Brass chain armour Bronze chain armour Copper chain armour Lead chain armour Tin chain armour Zinc chain armour Gold chain armour Silver chain armour Adamantine chain armour Glimmersteel chain armour Seryll chain armour Creation requirements: Chain coif 0.40 kg Chain jacket 2.20 kg Chain sleeve 0.70 kg Chain gauntlet 0.30 kg Chain pants 2.20 kg Chain boot 0.70 kg Full Set	        8.20 kg Chain Barding Adamantine chain barding Brass chain barding Bronze chain barding Copper chain barding Electrum chain barding Glimmersteel chain barding Gold chain barding Iron chain barding Lead chain barding Seryll chain barding Silver chain barding Steel chain barding Tin chain barding Zinc chain barding', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chain_Armour\">Chain Armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 208.66666666667px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"991\" data-file-width=\"827\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/2/28/Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg/313px-Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/2/28/Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg/470px-Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg 1.5x, /images/thumb/2/28/Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg/626px-Armormetals-chain-iron.jpg 2x\" width=\"209\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 189px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Iron chain armour\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\"><div style=\"width: 210.66666666667px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 20