orum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/177782-melody-community-map/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Forum Thread</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cadence.yaga.host\" rel=\"nofollow\">Map by Morbidae</a>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forum.wurmonline.com/index.php?/topic/191415-new-cadence-community-map//\" rel=\"nofollow\">Forum Thread</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"left\">\n<td><b>Other maps</b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.wurmnode.com/server/harmony/map\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wurmnode</a></li></ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.wurmnode.com/server/melody/map\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wurmnode</a></li></ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.wurmnode.com/server/cadence/map\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wurmnode</a></li></ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p> \n</p>\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<table align=\"left\" class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:25px; text-align: center; float:none;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th> </th>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:135%\">Moons</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\">\n<th>Moon</th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Jackal\" title=\"Jackal\">Jackal</a></th>\n<th><a href=\"/index.php/Valrei\" title=\"Valrei\">Valrei</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr align=\"left\" style=\"width:10%;\">\n<td><b>Official Maps</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:45%;\">\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1DY_NVqYwQNiJ0p-3_rmw5EbtYXPJovfC\" rel=\"nofollow\">Map dumps</a></li>\n<li>Jackal is a moon of our homeland, Wurm. Most of Jackal is still wholly unexplored. Around the spawn town of Camp Freedom there are both familiar and unfamiliar animals and trees. In the distance a land that seems to be corrupted looms.</li></ul>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:45%;\">\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/File:Valrei_map.jpg\" title=\"File:Valrei map.jpg\"> In-game map</a></li>\n<li>Valrei is the setting for the Gods scenarios relating to <a href=\"/index.php/Scenarios\" title=\"Scenarios\">Epic missions</a>.<br/>The current Valrei map may be seen by opening the Valrei map in game or by viewing the player-made map below.</li></ul>\n</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"left\" style=\"width:10%;\">\n<td><b>Community Maps</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:45%;\"> \n</td>\n<td>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://strikelimit.co.uk/Valrei/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Valrei map by Jekev and Mthec</a></li></ul>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 0);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(24763, 2549, 'Catacombs - Offline servers and other resources no longer available', 'Catacombs_-_Offline_servers_and_other_resources_no_longer_available', 'Golden Valley Server Golden Valley was historically the tutorial/non-premium server before the tutorial was moved to Haven. Travel to these lands is no longer possible. Golden Valley Community Map by Atlas Golden Valley by Xsamuraizx - Updated: 4/20/2010 New Dawn Map - Shows an accurate representation of the New Dawn deed with a few key features close by. Created by Xsamuraizx. Golden Valley Community Map - Created by Atlas 12/16/2022 Gold 1 Home server map dump , 10th world - Mapdump made by Notch of home server captured a few months before the Wurmageddon . Servermap4 (Gold 1) - 10th world, homeserver. Loganmom\'s map with newer towns being added. Alpha / Beta maps Wild001 2007 Map Dump Navigation maps Southern Freedom Cluster (Note: The cluster map shows geographic relations should plot-free sailing have the player cross server borders. Plotting course, on the other hand, alleviates the geographic relations/positioning visually seen in the cluster map.)', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Golden_Valley_Server\">Golden Valley Server</span></h4>\n<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<p><i>Golden Valley was historically the tutorial/non-premium server before the tutorial was moved to Haven. Travel to these lands is no longer possible.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://prosperific.github.io/wurm-online-golden-valley-map/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Golden Valley Community Map by Atlas</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151107015025/http://img407.imageshack.us/img407/2149/newgoldenvalleyfreedomb.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">Golden Valley by Xsamuraizx</a> - Updated: 4/20/2010</li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZhELuJj.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\">New Dawn Map</a> - Shows an accurate representation of the New Dawn deed with a few key features close by. Created by Xsamuraizx.</li>\n<li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://prosperific.github.io/wurm-online-golden-valley-map/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Golden Valley Community Map</a> - Created by Atlas 12/16/2022</li></ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gold_1\">Gold 1</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160629163634/http://wurmgold.awardspace.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Home server map dump</a>, 10th world - Mapdump made by <a href=\"/index.php/User:Notch\" title=\"User:Notch\">Notch</a> of home server captured a few months before the <a href=\"/index.php/Wurmageddon\" title=\"Wurmageddon\">Wurmageddon</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Historical:Servermap4_(Gold_1)\" title=\"Historical:Servermap4 (Gold 1)\">Servermap4 (Gold 1)</a> - 10th world, homeserver. Loganmom\'s map with newer towns being added.</li></ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span id=\"Alpha_/_Beta_maps\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alpha_.2F_Beta_maps\">Alpha / Beta maps</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20151107015020/http://www.nickersonm.com/wurm/mapping/wild001-map.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">Wild001 2007 Map Dump</a></li></ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Navigation_maps\">Navigation maps</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<ul><li><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/49ny4u0v6lstgwo/freedom.png?dl=0\" rel=\"nofollow\">Southern Freedom Cluster</a> (Note: The cluster map shows geographic relations should plot-free sailing have the player cross server borders. Plotting course, on the other hand, alleviates the geographic relations/positioning visually seen in the cluster map.)</li></ul>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(24764, 2549, 'Astronomical research archive', 'Astronomical_research_archive', 'Wurm Universe , Physics and Astronomical Research AstroResearch 1 , 14/09 986, 8th world AstroResearch 2 , 22/07 988, 9th world Moons , 9th world', '<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Wurm_Universe\" title=\"Wurm Universe\">Wurm Universe</a>, Physics and Astronomical Research</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/AstroResearch_1\" title=\"AstroResearch 1\">AstroResearch 1</a>, 14/09 986, 8th world</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/AstroResearch_2\" title=\"AstroResearch 2\">AstroResearch 2</a>, 22/07 988, 9th world</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Moons\" title=\"Moons\">Moons</a>, 9th world</li></ul>\n</div>', 2),
(24765, 2549, 'Miscellaneous', 'Miscellaneous', 'See this article if you are seeking information on the in-game World map. Scale for the topographical﻿ markings is 250 dirt/slope.', '<div class=\"toccolours\" style=\"width:center\">\n<ul><li>See <a href=\"/index.php/World_map\" title=\"World map\">this article</a> if you are seeking information on the in-game World map.</li>\n<li>Scale for the topographical﻿ markings is 250 dirt/slope.</li></ul>\n</div>', 3),
(24769, 6231, 'Description', 'Description', 'Turns an animal into a loyal companion ( pet ). The spell is an aggressive spell. The animal you cast the spell on will attack you even if it was non-aggressive. However, the casting process will not be interrupted by combat, even if the creature hits the caster. The spell can charm animals in situations where taming is not possible: animals can be charmed if they are in deep water or on a deed.  There is no need to go unfaithful or unlawful when charming on deed.', '<p>Turns an <a href=\"/index.php/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">animal</a> into a loyal companion (<a href=\"/index.php/Pet\" title=\"Pet\">pet</a>).\n</p>\n<p>The spell is an aggressive spell. The animal you cast the spell on will attack you even if it was non-aggressive. However, the casting process will not be interrupted by combat, even if the creature hits the caster.\n</p>\n<p>The spell can charm animals in situations where taming is not possible: animals can be charmed if they are in deep water or on a deed.  There is no need to go unfaithful or unlawful when charming on deed.\n</p>', 0),
(24770, 6231, 'Method', 'Method', 'Activate your deity\'s statuette Right-click a creature Select Spells > Charm animal', '<ol><li><a href=\"/index.php/Activate\" title=\"Activate\">Activate</a> your deity\'s <a href=\"/index.php/Statuette\" title=\"Statuette\">statuette</a></li>\n<li>Right-click a creature</li>\n<li>Select <i>Spells</i> &gt; <i>Charm animal</i></li></ol>', 1),
(24771, 6231, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'To charm an animal on deed, a player needs permissions on that deed to: Charm/Tame/Dominate Cast Deity Spells Attack citizens.', '<ul><li>To charm an animal on deed, a player needs permissions on that deed to:\n<ul><li>Charm/Tame/Dominate</li>\n<li>Cast Deity Spells</li>\n<li>Attack citizens.</li></ul></li></ul>', 2),
(24772, 2635, 'Description', 'Description', 'A rope making tool, a small handheld spinning wheel with three large nails. A rope tool is used for ropemaking , the art of making various types of ropes as well as bow strings from wemp fibre .', '<p><i>A rope making tool, a small handheld spinning wheel with three large nails.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A <b>rope tool</b> is used for <a href=\"/index.php/Ropemaking\" title=\"Ropemaking\">ropemaking</a>, the art of making various types of <a href=\"/index.php/Rope\" title=\"Rope\">ropes</a> as well as <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow strings</a> from <a href=\"/index.php/Wemp_fibre\" title=\"Wemp fibre\">wemp fibre</a>.\n</p>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 0),
(24773, 2635, 'Rare Functionality', 'Rare_Functionality', 'Note: Rare functionality is still not completely understood and is an exciting aspect of the game.  Most information listed is only an observation of one or more players rather than confirmed by developers. Rare rope tools can create products with a higher QL than the wemp fiber. (Up to +1 QL)', '<table style=\"background-color:#f8f8f8; -moz-border-radius:10px; width:50%; border:2px solid #e0e0e0; margin-left:0 auto; padding:5px; -moz-outline-style: outset; -moz-outline-radius: 10px; -moz-outline-color: #e0e0e0;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"30\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/30px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/45px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/60px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"30\"/></a></div>\n</td>\n<td><b>Note:</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Rarity_system\" title=\"Rarity system\">Rare</a> functionality is still not completely understood and is an exciting aspect of the game.  Most information listed is only an observation of one or more players rather than confirmed by developers.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Rare rope tools can create products with a higher QL than the wemp fiber. (Up to +1 QL)\n</p>', 1),
(24774, 2635, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Failure to create results in damage to the plank and shaft. The wood type is dictated by the wooden type activated OR what\'s in the second box while using the crafting window during creation. For example: If you activate shaft and right click plank, the unfinished rope tool will be of the shaft\'s wood type. Like with many other tools a high QL rope tool will increase chance of success (important with the harder types of rope).', '<ul><li>Failure to create results in damage to the plank and shaft.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/index.php/Wood\" title=\"Wood\">wood</a> type is dictated by the wooden type activated OR what\'s in the second box while using the crafting window during creation. For example: If you activate shaft and right click plank, the unfinished rope tool will be of the shaft\'s wood type.</li>\n<li>Like with many other tools a high QL rope tool will increase chance of success (important with the harder types of rope).</li></ul>', 2),
(24775, 3187, 'Description', 'Description', 'KoS (Kill on Sight) is a feature used by deed owners to keep criminals and other undesired players off of their land. When a player is placed on a deed\'s kill on sight list, spirit templars will attack them if they attempt to enter the deed, and tower guards will attack them once they enter the deed\'s perimeter (if their tower is nearby).', '<p><b>KoS</b> (Kill on Sight) is a feature used by <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Deed\" title=\"Deed\">deed</a> owners to keep criminals and other undesired players off of their land.\n</p>\n<p>When a player is placed on a deed\'s kill on sight list, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Spirit_Templars\" title=\"Spirit Templars\">spirit templars</a> will attack them if they attempt to enter the deed, and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Guards\" title=\"Guards\">tower guards</a> will attack them once they enter the deed\'s perimeter (if their tower is nearby).\n</p>', 0),
(24776, 3187, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Kill on sight is accessed at the deed token by selecting Manage Reputations . In order to gain the effect of KoS, the player\'s name must have a reputation below -30, set to permanent. KoS can also occur automatically when someone violates the laws of the settlement on the Chaos Server or attacks the guards on a settlement on any server. KoS is a drastic way to keep players away and should not be used to block roads or exclude everyone from an area on the Freedom server. It is considered to be in bad taste to KoS without reason and can be devastating for anyone who wanders on deed and is killed without reason. Using the guards to ambush people to steal their items on the Freedom Server constitutes griefing, a ban-able rules offense. KoS may not be used if the deed or perimeter has a highway going through it.', '<ul><li>Kill on sight is accessed at the deed token by selecting <i>Manage Reputations</i>. In order to gain the effect of KoS, the player\'s name must have a reputation below -30, set to permanent. KoS can also occur automatically when someone violates the laws of the settlement on the Chaos Server or attacks the guards on a settlement on any server.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>KoS is a drastic way to keep players away and should not be used to block roads or exclude everyone from an area on the <a href=\"/index.php/Freedom\" title=\"Freedom\">Freedom</a> server. It is considered to be in bad taste to KoS without reason and can be devastating for anyone who wanders on deed and is killed without reason. Using the guards to ambush people to steal their items on the Freedom Server constitutes griefing, a ban-able rules offense.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>KoS may not be used if the deed or perimeter has a <a href=\"/index.php/Highway\" title=\"Highway\">highway</a> going through it.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(24777, 3187, 'A Triggered KoS on Freedom: Process of Events', 'A_Triggered_KoS_on_Freedom:_Process_of_Events', 'KoS first gives KoS\'ed players a popup warning when they enter the perimeter or deed the first time. If they enter the perimeter, they get an event window warning. If they enter the deed, a three-minute countdown timer starts, and it pauses when they leave. They also get an event window warning that they are in that countdown frame. After the three minutes are up, they are on permanant KoS, just like before. The timer resets only if they are removed from KoS and added back again later.', '<ol><li>KoS first gives KoS\'ed players a popup warning when they enter the perimeter or deed the first time.</li>\n<li>If they enter the perimeter, they get an event window warning.</li>\n<li>If they enter the deed, a three-minute countdown timer starts, and it pauses when they leave.</li>\n<li>They also get an event window warning that they are in that countdown frame.</li>\n<li>After the three minutes are up, they are on permanant KoS, just like before.</li>\n<li>The timer resets only if they are removed from KoS and added back again later.</li></ol>', 2),
(24778, 3187, 'Example KoS Event Messages', 'Example_KoS_Event_Messages', 'Perimeter Breech [18:29:38] You are now within the hostile perimeter of Port Side and will be attacked by kingdom guards. Deed Breech, KoS on Countdown [12:05:48] You must leave the settlement of Port Side immediately or you will be attacked by the guards! Perimeter Breech, KoS on Countdown [12:04:18] Make sure to stay out of Port Side since you soon will be killed on sight there! General KoS Alarm [18:29:38] Portsideinviter raises the village alarm! [18:29:38] A horn sounds and the gates are locked. Port Side is put on alert!', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Perimeter_Breech\">Perimeter Breech</span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  [18:29:38] You are now within the hostile perimeter of Port Side and will be attacked by kingdom guards. </span>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Deed_Breech,_KoS_on_Countdown\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Deed_Breech.2C_KoS_on_Countdown\">Deed Breech, KoS on Countdown</span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\"> [12:05:48] You must leave the settlement of Port Side immediately or you will be attacked by the guards! </span>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Perimeter_Breech,_KoS_on_Countdown\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Perimeter_Breech.2C_KoS_on_Countdown\">Perimeter Breech, KoS on Countdown</span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  [12:04:18] Make sure to stay out of Port Side since you soon will be killed on sight there! </span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"General_KoS_Alarm\">General KoS Alarm</span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"color: #fff; font-family: Sans-Serif; font-size: 0.85em; border: 1px rgb(0, 0, 0) solid; background: rgb(75, 62, 48); line-height: 1.3em; -webkit-border-radius: 5px; -moz-border-radius: 5px; border-radius: 5px; -moz-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); -webkit-box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 1px rgb(101, 101, 101); padding: 2px 10px 2px 10px; display: inline-block;\">  [18:29:38] Portsideinviter raises the village alarm! [18:29:38] A horn sounds and the gates are locked. Port Side is put on alert! </span>\n</p>', 3),
(24779, 4515, 'Description', 'Description', 'Dum de da, Dum de Da, Dum de Da dill - I love to climb up Sassafras Hill.', '<p><i>Dum de da, Dum de Da, Dum de Da dill - I love to climb up Sassafras Hill.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24780, 4515, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be found by botanizing from Alpine brush and Thicket Resource nodes . Used in many cooking recipes. It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar. When used in a healing cover , it has a potency of 2. Cannot be planted.', '<ul><li>Can be found by botanizing from <a href=\"/index.php/Alpine_brush\" title=\"Alpine brush\">Alpine brush</a>  and <a href=\"/index.php/Thicket\" title=\"Thicket\">Thicket</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>.</li>\n<li>Used in many <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>It can be eaten by itself to fill a tiny amount of the hunger bar.</li>\n<li>When used in a <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing cover</a>, it has a potency of 2.</li>\n<li>Cannot be planted.</li></ul>', 1),
(24781, 4515, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Herb', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">Herb</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24782, 4251, 'Description', 'Description', 'A potato. Potatoes can be pretty hard to grow to edible size.', '<p><i>A potato. Potatoes can be pretty hard to grow to edible size.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24783, 4251, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be used in cooking recipes. It can be found by botanizing or foraging on certain Resource nodes tiles. Can be sown . 51 fit in a pottery bowl .', '<ul><li>Can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Hot_food_cooking\" title=\"Hot food cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>It can be found by <a href=\"/index.php/Botanizing\" title=\"Botanizing\">botanizing</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">foraging</a> on certain <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a> tiles.</li>\n<li>Can be <a href=\"/index.php/Farming\" title=\"Farming\">sown</a>.</li>\n<li>51 fit in a <a href=\"/index.php/Pottery_bowl\" title=\"Pottery bowl\">pottery bowl</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24784, 4251, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Node resources', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Node_resources\" title=\"Node resources\">Node resources</a></li></ul>', 2),
(24785, 4024, 'Description', 'Description', 'A long slender bow that must be fired pretty far for good accuracy. It will then provide a hefty punch.', '<p><i>A long slender bow that must be fired pretty far for good accuracy. It will then provide a hefty punch.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24786, 4024, 'Shooting', 'Shooting', 'This weapon is best used at 20 tiles range, or 80 m when looking through a spyglass . It requires a minimum range of 10 tiles. Higher skill in this weapon gives more shooting options when used. \nThe long bow has the furthest range of hand-held weapons in game. Long bows at a long range can give very nasty wounds with a good enough bow. The maximum range seems to be 50 tiles from the target unless aided by a spyglass. Bows must be wielded in your hands to be fired. Bows are two handed weapons, and cannot be equipped unless both hands are empty and you aren\'t wearing a shield. See the archery page for more.', '<p>This weapon is best used at 20 tiles range, or 80 m when looking through a <a href=\"/index.php/Spyglass\" title=\"Spyglass\">spyglass</a>. It requires a minimum range of 10 tiles. Higher skill in this weapon gives more shooting options when used. \nThe long bow has the furthest range of hand-held weapons in game. Long bows at a long range can give very nasty wounds with a good enough bow. The maximum range seems to be 50 tiles from the target unless aided by a spyglass.\n</p>\n<p>Bows must be wielded in your hands to be fired. Bows are two handed weapons, and cannot be equipped unless both hands are empty and you aren\'t wearing a shield.\n</p>\n<p>See the <a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">archery</a> page for more.\n</p>', 1),
(24787, 4024, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Stringing with a bow string is needed to make the bow functional. Before that, examining it will say: \" A long but unstringed slender bow. \"  The bow must be unstrung in order to improve it. A Long bow is best made out of willow . Examining it will then say, \" The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility. \" Longbow deals the highest damage.', '<ul><li>Stringing with a <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_string\" title=\"Bow string\">bow string</a> is needed to make the bow functional. Before that, examining it will say: \"<i>A long but unstringed slender bow.</i>\"  The bow must be unstrung in order to improve it.</li>\n<li>A Long bow is best made out of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Willow\" title=\"Willow\">willow</a>. Examining it will then say, \"<i>The willow wood used in this bow gives it good strength yet supreme flexibility.</i>\"</li>\n<li>Longbow deals the highest damage.</li></ul>', 2),
(24788, 4024, 'Skins applicable', 'Skins_applicable', 'Prodigious Longbow', '<ul><li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Item_skin_token\" title=\"Item skin token\">Prodigious Longbow</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24789, 4024, 'Storage', 'Storage', 'Can be stored in a bow rack .  Does not fit in a regular large chest .', '<p>Can be stored in a <a href=\"/index.php/Bow_rack\" title=\"Bow rack\">bow rack</a>.  Does not fit in a regular <a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">large chest</a>.\n</p>', 4),
(24790, 4024, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'When using a long bow Archery > Longbow Body > Body control When creating a long bow Carpentry > Bowyery', '<p>When using a long bow\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Archery\" title=\"Archery\">Archery</a> &gt; Longbow</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>\n<p>When creating a long bow\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Carpentry\" title=\"Carpentry\">Carpentry</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Bowyery\" title=\"Bowyery\">Bowyery</a></li></ul>', 5),
(24791, 4024, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Longbowman at 50 skill Marksman at 70 skill Robin Hood at 90 skill', '<ul><li>Longbowman at 50 skill</li>\n<li>Marksman at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Robin Hood at 90 skill</li></ul>', 6),
(24792, 4024, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Reflex bow Short bow', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Reflex_bow\" title=\"Reflex bow\">Reflex bow</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Short_bow\" title=\"Short bow\">Short bow</a></li></ul>', 7),
(24793, 1035, 'Description', 'Description', 'A blade used to make a shovel .', '<p>A blade used to make a <a href=\"/index.php/Shovel\" title=\"Shovel\">shovel</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(24794, 6196, 'Description', 'Description', 'A sort of stone blade that maybe would make a shovel were it not for the lack of a shaft.', '<p><i>A sort of stone blade that maybe would make a shovel were it not for the lack of a shaft.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24795, 6196, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a crude shovel when attached to a crude shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shovel\" title=\"Crude shovel\">crude shovel</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_shaft\" title=\"Crude shaft\">crude shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24796, 1034, 'Description', 'Description', 'The strong iron head of a pick.', '<p><i>The strong iron head of a pick.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24797, 1034, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a pickaxe when attached to a shaft . If rare, when activated and used with a shaft, the result is guaranteed to be a rare pickaxe.', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li>\n<li>If rare, when activated and used with a shaft, the result is guaranteed to be a rare pickaxe.</li></ul>', 1),
(24798, 1383, 'Description', 'Description', 'A piece of hard stone roughly shaped into a pickaxe blade. A crude pickaxe head of stone can be made from simple rummaged or mined stone shards to create a crude pickaxe if you have lost your iron pickaxe .', '<p><i> A piece of hard stone roughly shaped into a pickaxe blade.</i>\n</p>\n<p>A crude <b>pickaxe head</b> of stone can be made from simple <a href=\"/index.php/Foraging\" title=\"Foraging\">rummaged</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Mining\" title=\"Mining\">mined</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> to create a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\">crude pickaxe</a> if you have lost your iron <a href=\"/index.php/Pickaxe\" title=\"Pickaxe\">pickaxe</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(24799, 1383, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used to construct a crude pickaxe when attached to a shaft .', '<ul><li>Used to construct a <a href=\"/index.php/Crude_pickaxe\" title=\"Crude pickaxe\">crude pickaxe</a> when attached to a <a href=\"/index.php/Shaft\" title=\"Shaft\">shaft</a>.</li></ul>', 1),
(24800, 3410, 'Description', 'Description', 'The skill of creating leather or drake hide items.', '<p>The skill of creating leather or drake hide items.\n</p>', 0),
(24801, 3410, 'Tools Used', 'Tools_Used', 'Needle Leather knife Iron awl Mallet Leather Lye Animal hide Drake hide Rivets Mouth bit', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Needle\" title=\"Needle\">Needle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Leather_knife\" title=\"Leather knife\">Leather knife</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Iron_awl\" title=\"Iron awl\">Iron awl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mallet\" title=\"Mallet\">Mallet</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Leather\" title=\"Leather\">Leather</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Lye\" title=\"Lye\">Lye</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Animal_hide\" title=\"Animal hide\">Animal hide</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Drake_hide\" title=\"Drake hide\">Drake hide</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Rivets\" title=\"Rivets\">Rivets</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mouth_bit\" title=\"Mouth bit\">Mouth bit</a></li></ul>', 1),
(24802, 3410, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Improving leather items is not limited by the ql of the leather used to improve. Wearing your leatherworking title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding and any items that can be equipped on a horse.', '<ul><li>Improving leather items is not limited by the ql of the leather used to improve.</li>\n<li>Wearing your leatherworking title gives a bonus while improving armour items, including barding and any items that can be equipped on a horse.</li></ul>', 2),
(24803, 3410, 'Skills & Characteristics', 'Skills_.26_Characteristics', 'Tailoring > Leatherworking Mind > Mind logic Body > Body control', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Tailoring\" title=\"Tailoring\">Tailoring</a> &gt; Leatherworking</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Mind\" title=\"Mind\">Mind</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">Mind logic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Body\" title=\"Body\">Body</a> &gt; <a href=\"/index.php/Body_control\" title=\"Body control\">Body control</a></li></ul>', 3),
(24804, 3410, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Tanner at 50 skill High Tanner at 70 skill Master Tanner at 90 skill Master/Mistress of the Hide at 100 skill First to reach this skill is Willow at 3-5-15\n [22:01:44] <Willow> here you go guys  [14:02:51] Your title is now Mistress of the Hide.', '<ul><li>Tanner at 50 skill</li>\n<li>High Tanner at 70 skill</li>\n<li>Master Tanner at 90 skill</li>\n<li>Master/Mistress of the Hide at 100 skill</li></ul>\n<pre> First to reach this skill is Willow at 3-5-15\n [22:01:44] &lt;Willow&gt; here you go guys  [14:02:51] Your title is now Mistress of the Hide.\n</pre>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 4),
(24805, 3410, 'Leatherworking Item Variations', 'Leatherworking_Item_Variations', 'Drake Hide Armour Black drake hide armour Leather Armour Leather armour Studded Leather Armour Studded leather armour Leather Barding Leather barding', '<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Drake_Hide_Armour\">Drake Hide Armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 282px\"><div style=\"width: 282px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 280px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Drake_hide_armour.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"715\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/0/07/Drake_hide_armour.jpg/420px-Drake_hide_armour.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/0/07/Drake_hide_armour.jpg/630px-Drake_hide_armour.jpg 1.5x, /images/0/07/Drake_hide_armour.jpg 2x\" width=\"280\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 260px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Black drake hide armour\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Leather_Armour\">Leather Armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 282px\"><div style=\"width: 282px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 280px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Leather_armour.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"715\" data-file-width=\"800\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/3/3b/Leather_armour.jpg/420px-Leather_armour.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/3/3b/Leather_armour.jpg/630px-Leather_armour.jpg 1.5x, /images/3/3b/Leather_armour.jpg 2x\" width=\"280\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 260px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Leather armour\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Studded_Leather_Armour\">Studded Leather Armour</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 238px\"><div style=\"width: 238px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 236px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Studded_leather_armour.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"720\" data-file-width=\"680\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/f/f5/Studded_leather_armour.jpg/354px-Studded_leather_armour.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/f/f5/Studded_leather_armour.jpg/532px-Studded_leather_armour.jpg 1.5x, /images/f/f5/Studded_leather_armour.jpg 2x\" width=\"236\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 216px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Studded leather armour\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Leather_Barding\">Leather Barding</span></h3>\n<div class=\"toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"width:relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-packed-hover\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 268px\"><div style=\"width: 268px\">\n<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 266px;\"><div style=\"margin:0px auto;\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Leatherbarding.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" data-file-height=\"609\" data-file-width=\"648\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"250\" src=\"/images/thumb/6/61/Leatherbarding.jpg/399px-Leatherbarding.jpg\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/6/61/Leatherbarding.jpg/599px-Leatherbarding.jpg 1.5x, /images/6/61/Leatherbarding.jpg 2x\" width=\"266\"/></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytextwrapper\" style=\"width: 246px\"><div class=\"gallerytext\">\n<p>Leather barding\n</p>\n</div></div>\n</div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>', 5),
(24806, 3410, 'See Also', 'See_Also', 'Category:Leatherworking items Leatherworking Skill Tips Tailoring Cloth tailoring Leatherworking', '<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Category:Leatherworking_items\" title=\"Category:Leatherworking items\">Category:Leatherworking items</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Leatherworking_Skill_Tips\" title=\"Leatherworking Skill Tips\">Leatherworking Skill Tips</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Tailoring\" title=\"Tailoring\">Tailoring</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Cloth_tailoring\" title=\"Cloth tailoring\">Cloth tailoring</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Leatherworking</a></li></ul></li></ul>', 6),
(24807, 3479, 'Description', 'Description', 'A wooden tube made from planks with a shaft to press in order to separate the whey from the curd, and to press the curd into a mould.', '<p><i>A wooden tube made from planks with a shaft to press in order to separate the whey from the curd, and to press the curd into a mould.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24808, 3479, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to create cheese from milk . The quality of the bladder affects the success chance when creating. Both the shaft used to create the cheese drill and the bladder are damaged (fairly heavily) if you fail. 0.02 kg is consumed from the bladder on creation success.', '<ul><li>Used to create cheese from <a href=\"/index.php/Milk\" title=\"Milk\">milk</a>.</li>\n<li>The <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of the <a href=\"/index.php/Bladder\" title=\"Bladder\">bladder</a> affects the success chance when creating.</li>\n<li>Both the shaft used to create the cheese drill and the bladder are damaged (fairly heavily) if you fail.</li>\n<li>0.02 kg is consumed from the bladder on creation success.</li></ul>', 1),
(24809, 1248, 'Description', 'Description', 'A small sailing boat that will accommodate up to five people. They are very useful as personal ships for normal journeys. They don\'t have large holds, but can easily carry smaller items like fish and tools . Small barrels are good for expanding their hold capacity. They can still sustain a speed of about 6-8km/h in low winds, making them \"all-round\" server travel boats.', '<p><i>A small sailing boat that will accommodate up to five people.</i>\n</p>\n<p>They are very useful as personal ships for normal journeys. They don\'t have large holds, but can easily carry smaller items like <a href=\"/index.php/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a> and <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Tools\" title=\"Tools\">tools</a>. <a href=\"/index.php/Small_barrel\" title=\"Small barrel\">Small barrels</a> are good for expanding their hold capacity. They can still sustain a speed of about 6-8km/h in low winds, making them \"all-round\" server travel boats.\n</p>', 0),
(24810, 1248, 'Vessel Details', 'Vessel_Details', 'Requires 20.10 mind logic to be able to command it, so having premium at least once is required. Passengers: 1 captain + 4 crew Maximum speed: 21.34 km/h Hold Capacity: see #Loadable Items and #Useful Quantities Cannot hold rafts Minimum passable depth: 5 dirt. Everybody can drag. Size: 2 tiles by 1 tile. Height: 3 dirt from water level to deck', '<ul><li>Requires 20.10 <a href=\"/index.php/Mind_logic\" title=\"Mind logic\">mind logic</a> to be able to command it, so having <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Premium\" title=\"Premium\">premium</a> at least once is required.</li>\n<li>Passengers: 1 captain + 4 crew</li>\n<li>Maximum speed: 21.34 km/h</li>\n<li>Hold Capacity: see <a href=\"#Loadable_Items\">#Loadable Items</a> and <a href=\"#Useful_Quantities\">#Useful Quantities</a>\n<ul><li>Cannot hold <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Raft\" title=\"Raft\">rafts</a></li></ul></li>\n<li>Minimum passable depth: 5 dirt.</li>\n<li>Everybody can drag.</li>\n<li>Size: 2 tiles by 1 tile.</li>\n<li>Height: 3 dirt from water level to deck</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n</p>', 1),
(24811, 1248, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'The second smallest boat possible to make (excluding the raft , which isn\'t a true ship). Ships with a quality of less than 10 cannot be commanded. This includes ships whose damage percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality). Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again. Quality of active keel section affects success chance for creation. Ships cannot be hauled up ladders', '<ul><li>The second smallest boat possible to make (excluding the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Raft\" title=\"Raft\">raft</a>, which isn\'t a true ship).</li>\n<li>Ships with a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a> of less than 10 cannot be commanded.\n<ul><li>This includes ships whose <a href=\"/index.php/Damage\" title=\"Damage\">damage</a> percentage would calculate to bring the quality below 10 (eg. a 12 quality ship with 17 damage calculates to a ship below 10 quality).</li>\n<li>Repairing a ship can sometimes result in the ship retaining a quality above 10, thus being commandable once again.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Quality of active keel section affects success chance for creation.</li>\n<li>Ships cannot be hauled up ladders</li></ul>', 2),
(24812, 1248, 'Loadable Containers', 'Loadable_Containers', 'List is a work in progress. Large chest - 2 Bed - 1 Weapons rack - 2 Large barrel - 3 Bulk storage bins and crates will not fit in the small sailing boat.', '<p><i>List is a work in progress.</i>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_chest\" title=\"Large chest\">Large chest</a> - 2</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Bed\" title=\"Bed\">Bed</a> - 1</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Weapons_rack\" title=\"Weapons rack\">Weapons rack</a> - 2</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Large_barrel\" title=\"Large barrel\">Large barrel</a> - 3</li>\n<li>Bulk storage bins and crates will not fit in the small sailing boat.</li></ul>', 3),
(24813, 1248, 'Useful Quantities', 'Useful_Quantities', 'The following are the maximum hard-coded amounts of certain items a Small sailing boat can hold due to their volume or other factors (weight has no say here). 40 standard units (20 kg) of dirt , sand , stone shards or ore . 67 peat 94 bricks 7 slabs 9 logs 2 felled trees 100 planks .mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both} .mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto} Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.', '<p>The following are the maximum hard-coded amounts of certain items a Small sailing boat can hold due to their volume or other factors (weight has no say here).\n</p>\n<ul><li>40 standard units (20 kg) of <a href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_dirt\" title=\"Pile of dirt\">dirt</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Heap_of_sand\" title=\"Heap of sand\">sand</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_shards\" title=\"Stone shards\">stone shards</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Category:Ores\" title=\"Category:Ores\">ore</a>.</li>\n<li>67 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Pile_of_peat\" title=\"Pile of peat\">peat</a></li>\n<li>94 <a href=\"/index.php/Stone_brick\" title=\"Stone brick\">bricks</a></li>\n<li>7 <a href=\"/index.php/Slab\" title=\"Slab\">slabs</a></li>\n<li>9 <a href=\"/index.php/Log\" title=\"Log\">logs</a></li>\n<li>2 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Felled_tree\" title=\"Felled tree\">felled trees</a></li>\n<li>100 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Planks\" title=\"Planks\">planks</a></li></ul>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120347\">.mw-parser-output .boxstyle{margin:2px auto;padding:3px;width:60%;border:2px solid black;text-align:left;border-radius:10px;border-collapse:separate;box-shadow:2px 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);clear:both}.mw-parser-output .boxstyle::after{content:\"\";display:block;clear:both}</style>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r120390\">.mw-parser-output .infoboxbox{border-color:#E0E0E0;background-color:#F8F8F8;width:auto}</style>\n<div class=\"boxstyle infoboxbox\">\n<div class=\"floatleft\"><a class=\"image\" href=\"/index.php/File:Information_icon.png\"><img alt=\"Information icon.png\" data-file-height=\"62\" data-file-width=\"62\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"24\" src=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/24px-Information_icon.png\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/36px-Information_icon.png 1.5x, /images/thumb/1/1c/Information_icon.png/48px-Information_icon.png 2x\" width=\"24\"/></a></div>\n<span><strong>Boat speeds are relative and depend greatly on weather conditions.</strong></span></div>', 4),
(24814, 3502, 'Description', 'Description', 'A crimson rose, token of eternal love.', '<p><i>A crimson rose, token of eternal love.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24815, 3502, 'Usage', 'Usage', 'Used in some cooking recipes. Can be used in alchemy to make healing covers (healing potency 1).', '<ul><li>Used in some <a href=\"/index.php/Cooking\" title=\"Cooking\">cooking</a> recipes.</li>\n<li>Can be used in <a href=\"/index.php/Alchemy\" title=\"Alchemy\">alchemy</a> to make <a href=\"/index.php/Healing_cover\" title=\"Healing cover\">healing covers</a> (healing potency 1).</li></ul>', 1),
(24816, 3502, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Can be found by botanizing from Briar patch and Mints Resource nodes . You get this message when gathering them from a node You are pierced by the sharp thorns!', '<ul><li>Can be found by botanizing from <a href=\"/index.php/Briar_patch\" title=\"Briar patch\">Briar patch</a> and <a href=\"/index.php/Mints\" title=\"Mints\">Mints</a> <a href=\"/index.php/Resource_nodes\" title=\"Resource nodes\">Resource nodes</a>. You get this message when gathering them from a node <i>You are pierced by the sharp thorns!</i></li></ul>', 2),
(24817, 6052, 'Description', 'Description', 'A simple trash heap with a base made from planks. Things sure rot away quickly in there.', '<p><i>A simple trash heap with a base made from planks. Things sure rot away quickly in there.</i>\n</p>', 0),
(24818, 6052, 'Notes', 'Notes', 'Used to dispose of unwanted items. It must be a decayable item; for instance gems , locks , and original keys do not decay. Hull planks and bulk bins will not fit. Holds up to 100 items. Damaged items placed in the heap will decay within an hour. Undamaged items will receive 0.10 damage in the first hour, then decay completely in the second hour. Note that the decay above is instantaneous.  You cannot use the trash heap to deliberately damage items, and remove them before they are destroyed. Fluids in containers do not get decay damage at all, but are gone when the container is lost. When creating, the last plank added determines wood type. Can not be picked up. Requires a runed wagon to load.', '<ul><li>Used to dispose of unwanted items.</li>\n<li>It must be a decayable item; for instance <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Gem\" title=\"Gem\">gems</a>, <a href=\"/index.php/Lock\" title=\"Lock\">locks</a>, and original <a href=\"/index.php/Key\" title=\"Key\">keys</a> do not decay.</li>\n<li>Hull planks and bulk bins will not fit.</li>\n<li>Holds up to 100 items.</li>\n<li>Damaged items placed in the heap will decay within an hour.</li>\n<li>Undamaged items will receive 0.10 damage in the first hour, then decay completely in the second hour.</li>\n<li>Note that the decay above is instantaneous.  You cannot use the trash heap to deliberately damage items, and remove them before they are destroyed.</li>\n<li>Fluids in containers do not get decay damage at all, but are gone when the container is lost.</li>\n<li>When creating, the last plank added determines wood type.</li>\n<li>Can not be picked up. Requires a runed wagon to load.</li></ul>', 1),
(24819, 964, 'Description', 'Description', 'The Path of Love is one of the paths you can join by meditating .', '<p>The <b>Path of Love</b> is one of the paths you can join by <a href=\"/index.php/Meditating\" title=\"Meditating\">meditating</a>.\n</p>', 0),
(24820, 964, 'Path of Love tiles', 'Path_of_Love_tiles', 'Love path tiles are usually found near water on flat or flattish grass with flowers around. You can create your own love path tile by flattening a low area close to open water and planting flowers on all of the tiles. The rules for a tile to become a special tile are: There must be water closer than 20 tiles away. Usually the love tile will appear 5 or more tiles from water. There must be at least 4 tiles with flowers within a radius of 2 tiles around the special tile (forming a 5 x 5 area). The special tile must not be 10 dirts steeper than surrounding tiles. Grass (with or without flowers) must be predominant within a radius of 2 tiles around the special tile. Once planted, test each tile to see if it\'s \"special\" as the Love Tile does not have to be in the center of the area. If flowers or grass tiles are ever removed, the special tile may vanish. It must then be recreated, and may show up in a different spot than before. Be aware that sprouts spreading from trees and grazing animals can remove the flowers and therefore destroy the Path of Love special tile. As with all paths, meditating on the tile gives the message \"This is indeed a special place\" after meditation is complete, and shows that you have found a special tile that belongs to a path. Sometimes, it is needed to meditate on the same tile several times to get the \"special tile\" message.', '<p>Love path tiles are usually found near water on flat or flattish grass with flowers around.\n</p>\n<p>You can create your own love path tile by flattening a low area close to open water and planting flowers on all of the tiles. The rules for a tile to become a special tile are:\n</p>\n<ul><li>There must be water closer than 20 tiles away. Usually the love tile will appear 5 or more tiles from water.</li>\n<li>There must be at least 4 tiles with flowers within a radius of 2 tiles around the special tile (forming a 5 x 5 area).</li>\n<li>The special tile must not be 10 dirts steeper than surrounding tiles.</li>\n<li>Grass (with or without flowers) must be predominant within a radius of 2 tiles around the special tile.</li></ul>\n<p>Once planted, test each tile to see if it\'s \"special\" as the Love Tile does not have to be in the center of the area. If flowers or grass tiles are ever removed, the special tile may vanish. It must then be recreated, and may show up in a different spot than before.\n</p>\n<p>Be aware that sprouts spreading from trees and grazing animals can remove the flowers and therefore destroy the Path of Love special tile.\n</p>\n<p>As with all paths, meditating on the tile gives the message \"This is indeed a special place\" after meditation is complete, and shows that you have found a special tile that belongs to a path. Sometimes, it is needed to meditate on the same tile several times to get the \"special tile\" message.\n</p>', 1);
INSERT INTO `page_sections` (`id`, `page_id`, `heading`, `heading_id`, `content_text`, `content_html`, `section_order`) VALUES
(24821, 964, 'Bonus', 'Bonus', 'Refresh Gained at level 4 You get the option on other players at the fourth rank on the path of love. This will restore the players food, water and stamina 100% and give them 99% nutrition. This can be used once every 18 real world hours. Note: You need to be a premium character now to refresh other players. You can refresh yourself by double clicking the health bar to bring up the paper doll, selecting body in the bottom left corner and choosing \'Refresh\'. The refresh ability does not work on animals. Refreshing a player: You send (playername) a warm thought. Receiving a refresh: (playername) emits a positive wave of energy in your direction! Refreshing yourself: You send yourself a warm thought! Enchant Gained at level 7 You get the option on grass and trees tiles. The tile is transformed into an enchanted grass or enchanted tree tile. When you enchant the tile event says \"You let your love change the area\". It can be used once every 18 hours. Love Effect Gained at level 9 Love Effect turns all aggressive mobs (including uniques) in your local to \'friendly status\' with green highlight, so you can walk past them without being attacked.\nThe ability does not work in PvP (tamed/dominated pets). If you are fighting an animal and use this ability while sticking around, you will auto-attack back, which makes it continue fighting. Backing off and no-targeting should fix it. Usable once every 18 hours. The effect covers your local area (80 tiles in all directions) and it lasts for 3 minutes. When activated: \'You feel the love stream towards you\' (green text) When deactivating: \'The stream of love fades\' (orange text) Watch the event tab carefully for the fading effect message, it can happen that animals/monsters keep the green highlight even after the effect ran out. Relogging or embarking a cart/horse from one tile away (forcing client to reload) fixes this. Healing Hands Gained at level 11. Healing Hands is a passive ability that gives the player a 50% bonus to healing actions. This means that the healer will apply up to 50% extra healing when bandaging themselves or other players. They will also receive 50% more health from Life Transfer weapons. Mouse-Over Description: \"Improves the effectiveness of healing actions and natural regeneration by a factor of 1.5\" Recall Home Gained at level 12 You get the option on your Body (in your inventory). This will instantly teleport you back to the token at your deed. Can be used once every 12 hours. This cooldown is lowered by 1 hour for every level past 12. It only works if you have been part of the village for more than 24 hours. Only transports the player character; any mount, cart or boat is left behind. You close your eyes and let your spirit fly home. Final Breath Gained at level 13 Your willpower now gives you the ability to deal a powerful short range blow to the enemies. Final Breath deals medium poison wounds on the opponent. You sharpen your thoughts into a shining arrow of energy with which you assault Venerable troll.\nYou thought pulse Venerable troll extremely hard in the chest and harm it.\nVenom enters Venerable troll as you thought pulse him.\nYou see an ominous dark aura around throbbing ache at the chest. Final Breath has a 2 hour cooldown.', '<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Refresh\">Refresh</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 4\n</p>\n<p>You get the option on other players at the fourth rank on the path of love. This will restore the players food, water and stamina 100% and give them 99% nutrition. This can be used once every 18 real world hours. Note: You need to be a premium character now to refresh other players. You can refresh yourself by double clicking the health bar to bring up the paper doll, selecting body in the bottom left corner and choosing \'Refresh\'. The refresh ability does not work on animals.\n</p>\n<p>Refreshing a player: <i>You send (playername) a warm thought.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Receiving a refresh: <i>(playername) emits a positive wave of energy in your direction!</i>\n</p>\n<p>Refreshing yourself: <i>You send yourself a warm thought!</i>\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Enchant\">Enchant</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 7\n</p>\n<p>You get the option on grass and trees tiles. The tile is transformed into an <a href=\"/index.php/Enchanted_grass\" title=\"Enchanted grass\">enchanted grass</a> or <a href=\"/index.php/Enchanted_tree\" title=\"Enchanted tree\">enchanted tree</a> tile. When you enchant the tile event says \"You let your love change the area\". It can be used once every 18 hours.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Love_Effect\">Love Effect</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 9\n</p>\n<p>Love Effect turns all aggressive mobs (including uniques) in your local to \'friendly status\' with green highlight, so you can walk past them without being attacked.\nThe ability does not work in PvP (tamed/dominated pets). If you are fighting an animal and use this ability while sticking around, you will auto-attack back, which makes it continue fighting. Backing off and no-targeting should fix it. Usable once every 18 hours.\n</p>\n<p>The effect covers your local area (80 tiles in all directions) and it lasts for 3 minutes.\n</p>\n<p>When activated: \'You feel the love stream towards you\' (green text)<br/>\nWhen deactivating: \'The stream of love fades\' (orange text)\n</p>\n<p><br/>\nWatch the event tab carefully for the fading effect message, it can happen that animals/monsters keep the green highlight even after the effect ran out.\n</p>\n<p>Relogging or embarking a cart/horse from one tile away (forcing client to reload) fixes this.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Healing_Hands\">Healing Hands</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 11.\n</p>\n<p>Healing Hands is a passive ability that gives the player a 50% bonus to healing actions. This means that the healer will apply up to 50% extra healing when bandaging themselves or other players. They will also receive 50% more health from Life Transfer weapons.\n</p>\n<p>Mouse-Over Description: \"Improves the effectiveness of healing actions and natural regeneration by a factor of 1.5\"\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Recall_Home\">Recall Home</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 12\n</p>\n<p>\nYou get the option on your Body (in your inventory). This will instantly teleport you back to the token at your deed. </p>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<ul><li><p> Can be used once every 12 hours. <br/> This cooldown is lowered by 1 hour for every level past 12.</p></li>\n<li>It only works if you have been part of the village for more than 24 hours.</li>\n<li>Only transports the player character; any mount, cart or boat is left behind.</li></ul>\n<p><br/>\n<i>You close your eyes and let your spirit fly home.</i>\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Final_Breath\">Final Breath</span></h4>\n<p>Gained at level 13\n</p>\n<p><i>Your willpower now gives you the ability to deal a powerful short range blow to the enemies.</i>\n</p>\n<p>Final Breath deals medium poison wounds on the opponent.\n</p>\n<pre>You sharpen your thoughts into a shining arrow of energy with which you assault Venerable troll.\nYou thought pulse Venerable troll extremely hard in the chest and harm it.\nVenom enters Venerable troll as you thought pulse him.\nYou see an ominous dark aura around throbbing ache at the chest.\n</pre>\n<p>Final Breath has a 2 hour cooldown.\n</p>', 2),
(24822, 964, 'Titles', 'Titles', 'Level Skill Path of Love Titles 0 15 Uninitiated 1 15 Initiate 2 15 Nice 3 15 Gentle 4 15 Warm 5 15 Goodhearted 6 20 Giving 7 30 Rock 8 40 Splendid 9 50 Protector 10 60 Respectful 11 70 Saint 12 80 12th Deva 13 90 13th Deva 14 90 14th Deva 15 90 15th Deva 16 90 16th Deva', '<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\" cellspacing=\"2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Level\n</th>\n<th>Skill</th>\n<th>Path of Love Titles\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Uninitiated\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Initiate\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Nice\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Gentle\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Warm\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5\n</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Goodhearted\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6\n</td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>Giving\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7\n</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>Rock\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8\n</td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>Splendid\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9\n</td>\n<td>50</td>\n<td>Protector\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10\n</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td>Respectful\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11\n</td>\n<td>70</td>\n<td>Saint\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12\n</td>\n<td>80</td>\n<td>12th Deva\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13\n</td>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>13th Deva\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14\n</td>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>14th Deva\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>15\n</td>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>15th Deva\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16\n</td>\n<td>90</td>\n<td>16th Deva\n</td></tr></tbody></table>', 3),
(24823, 964, 'Questions & Answers', 'Questions_.26_Answers', 'The answers for the path questions can be found here .', '<p>The answers for the path questions can be found <a href=\"/index.php/Meditating_answers\" title=\"Meditating answers\">here</a>.\n</p>', 4),
(24829, 3238, 'Description', 'Description', 'All items in Wurm have a base value which depends on the item type and the effective item quality . The base value is used for: the Get price , favor gain when sacrificing at an altar .', '<p>All items in Wurm have a base value which depends on the item type and the effective item <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Quality\" title=\"Quality\">quality</a>. The base value is used for:\n</p>\n<ul><li>the <i>Get price</i>,</li>\n<li><a href=\"/index.php/Favor\" title=\"Favor\">favor</a> gain when <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/index.php/Sacrificing\" title=\"Sacrificing\">sacrificing</a> at an <a href=\"/index.php/Altar\" title=\"Altar\">altar</a>.</li></ul>', 0),
(24830, 3238, 'Favor', 'Favor', 'Priests can gain favor for sacrificing items in an altar. The amount of favor awarded is 1 favor per 500 irons sacrificed. The amount of favor can be calculated with the formula: favor = c * QL² * ( 1/500i ) which is equivalent to favor = c * QL² * 0.002 A variant of that formula is: favor = cf * (QL/10)² The table below lists the constant cf which is calculated as: cf = c / 5i Note: Magranon priests get twice the favor from sacrificing metal items, while Vynora priests get twice the favor from sacrificing wooden items, and Fo priests get twice the favor from cloth items.', '<p>Priests can gain favor for sacrificing items in an altar. The amount of favor awarded is 1 favor per 500 irons sacrificed.\n</p>\n<p>The amount of favor can be calculated with the formula:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>favor = c * QL² * ( 1/500i )</i> which is equivalent to <i>favor = c * QL² * 0.002</i></li></ul>\n<p>A variant of that formula is:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>favor = cf * (QL/10)²</i></li></ul>\n<p>The table below lists the constant <i>cf</i> which is calculated as:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>cf = c / 5i</i></li></ul>\n<p><b>Note:</b> <a href=\"/index.php/Magranon\" title=\"Magranon\">Magranon</a> priests get twice the favor from sacrificing metal items, while <a href=\"/index.php/Vynora\" title=\"Vynora\">Vynora</a> priests get twice the favor from sacrificing wooden items, and <a href=\"/index.php/Fo\" title=\"Fo\">Fo</a> priests get twice the favor from cloth items.\n</p>', 1),
(24831, 3238, 'Item type constants', 'Item_type_constants', 'The following table lists the item type constants for some items. The constants can be used with those formulas: Get price (irons) = c * QL² Favor = c * QL² * 0.002 Get price (irons) = c2 * (QL/10)² Favor = cf * (QL/10)² Item type constants Item c (irons) c2 (irons) cf Gems 5.00 500 1 Statuette of gods, gold 10.00 1,000 2 Statuette of gods, silver 8.00 800 1.6 Statuette , gold 5.00 500 1 Candelabra , gold 5.00 500 1 Candelabra , silver 4.00 400 0.8 Necklace , gold 3.50 350 0.7 Necklace , silver 2.75 275 0.55 Ring , gold 2.50 250 0.5 Ring , silver 2.00 200 0.4 Bracelet , gold 1.00 100 0.2 Bracelet , silver 0.80 80 0.16 Pendulum , gold 2.00 200 0.4 Pendulum , silver 1.60 160 0.32 Pendulum , iron 0.20 20 0.04 Cordage rope 1.30 130 0.26 Mooring rope 0.50 50 0.1 Rope 0.065 6.5 0.013 Thick rope 0.65 65 0.13 Boat lock 0.50 50 0.1 Door lock 0.50 50 0.1 Large padlock 0.25 25 0.05 File 0.50 50 0.1 Spindle 0.50 50 0.1 Yoyo 0.50 50 0.1 Mallet 0.05 5 0.01 Needle , iron 0.05 5 0.01 Pickaxe 0.005 0.5 0.001 Shovel 0.005 0.5 0.001 Square piece of cloth 0.50 50 0.1 Satchel 0.009 0.9 0.0018 Water skin 0.50 50 0.1 Spear 1.50 150 0.3 Long spear 0.50 50 0.1 Steel staff 0.50 50 0.1 Halberd 0.50 50 0.1 Long sword , iron 0.50 50 0.1 Small axe , iron 0.50 50 0.1 Gauntlet, steel 0.50 50 0.1 Large shield, iron 0.50 50 0.1 Shield, iron 0.50 50 0.1 Small shield, wood 0.50 50 0.1 Armour chains 0.05 5 0.01 Compass 0.50 50 0.1 Pottery Jar 0.50 50 0.1', '<p>The following table lists the item type constants for some items. The constants can be used with those formulas:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>Get price (irons) = c * QL²</i></li>\n<li><i>Favor = c * QL² * 0.002</i></li>\n<li><i>Get price (irons) = c2 * (QL/10)²</i></li>\n<li><i>Favor = cf * (QL/10)²</i></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"border:1px solid black;\">\n<caption><b>Item type constants</b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>c (irons)</th>\n<th>c2 (irons)</t